to indicate stress or placed above a vowel to indicate a special pronunciation [accent mark]</p><p><i>v.</i> to stress, single out as important [accentuate, emphasise, emphasize, punctuate, stress]</p><p><i>v.</i> put stress on [accentuate, stress]</p><p><b>diakritički znak koji se koristi za naglašavanje naglaska ili stavlja iznad samoglasnika kako bi se označio poseban izgovor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a diacritical mark used to indicate stress or placed above a vowel to indicate a special pronunciation [accent]</p><p><b>akcent, isticati, izgovarati, naglasak, naglasiti, naglasni, naglašavanje, podvlačiti, naglasne (od &quot;accent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of syllables) bearing the principle stress, usually accompanied by a change in pitch [tonic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> bearing a stress or accent [stressed]</p><p><b>akcent, isticati, izgovarati, naglasak, naglasiti, naglasni, naglašavanje, podvlačiti, naglasne (od &quot;accent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving special importance or significance to something [accentuation, emphasizing]</p><p><b>mala ptica poput vrapca iz planinskih regija Evroazije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small sparrow-like songbird of mountainous regions of Eurasia</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s naglaskom ili stresom, (od stiha) koji ima metrički sustav zasnovan na naglasku umjesto slogova ili količine (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to accent or stress</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of verse) having a metric system based on stress rather than syllables or quantity</p><p><b>sustav naglaska koji se koristi u određenom jeziku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of accentuation used in a particular language [prosodic system]</p><p><b>akcentirati, istaći, naglasiti, podvući, istaknuti, isticati, naglašavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to stress, single out as important [accent, emphasise, emphasize, punctuate, stress]</p><p><i>v.</i> put stress on [accent, stress]</p><p><b>AKCENTUACIJA, frekvencija korekcije, frekventna korekcija, isticanje, naglašavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use or application of an accent</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving special importance or significance to something [accenting, emphasizing]</p><p><b>akceptirati, dopustiti, preuzeti, prihvaćati, prihvati, prihvatiti, prijem, primiti, pristati, usvojiti, uvažiti, odobravati, odobriti, pristajati- pristati, primati, uzeti, uzimati, pripustiti, pripuštati, pustiti, puštati, preuzimati, usvajati, uvažavati, zaprimati, zaprimiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> consider or hold as true</p><p><i>v.</i> receive willingly something given or offered [have, take]</p><p><i>v.</i> give an affirmative reply to [consent, go for]</p><p><i>v.</i> react favorably to</p><p><i>v.</i> admit into a group or community [admit, take, take on]</p><p><i>v.</i> take on as one's own the expenses or debts of another person [assume, bear, take over]</p><p><i>v.</i> tolerate or accommodate oneself to [live with, swallow]</p><p><i>v.</i> be designed to hold or take [take]</p><p><i>v.</i> receive (a report) officially, as from a committee</p><p><i>v.</i> make use of or accept for some purpose [take]</p><p><i>v.</i> be sexually responsive to, used of a female domesticated mammal</p><p><b>mogućnost prijema, prihvatljivost, prihvatljivosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> satisfactoriness by virtue of conforming to approved standards [acceptableness]</p><p><b>dopustiv, prihvatljiv, prijatan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of acceptance or satisfactory</p><p><i>adj.</i> judged to be in conformity with approved usage</p><p><i>adj.</i> meeting requirements [decent, satisfactory]</p><p><i>adj.</i> adequate for the purpose</p><p><b>dopustiv, prihvatljiv, prijatan (od &quot;acceptable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> satisfactoriness by virtue of conforming to approved standards [acceptability]</p><p><b>na prihvatljiv (ali ne izvanredan) način (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an acceptable (but not outstanding) manner [so-so, tolerably]</p><p><b>akcept, akt o prihvaćanju, naklonost, odobravanje, odobrenje, prihvaćanja, prihvaćanje, prihvat, primanje, pristanak, suglasan, suglasni, suglasnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mental attitude that something is believable and should be accepted as true [credence]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of accepting with approval [acceptation, adoption, espousal]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being acceptable and accepted</p><p><i>n.</i> (contract law) words signifying consent to the terms of an offer (thereby creating a contract)</p><p><i>n.</i> banking: a time draft drawn on and accepted by a bank [banker's acceptance]</p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to tolerate or accept people or situations [sufferance, toleration]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of taking something that is offered</p><p><b>U slučaju da je proizvod ili proizvod koji se prodaje u Uniji ili u SAD-u, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvedeni u Uniji ili u Uniji, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, ne smije biti predmetom zahtjeva za izdavanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statistical procedure for accepting or rejecting a batch of merchandise or documents</p><p><b>voljno prihvaćanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> accepting willingly [acceptive]</p><p><b>povoljan prijem, prihvaćanje, pristanak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acceptance as true or valid</p><p><i>n.</i> the accepted meaning of a word [word meaning, word sense]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of accepting with approval [acceptance, adoption, espousal]</p><p><b>prihvaćen, prihvatili</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> generally approved or compelling recognition [recognised, recognized]</p><p><b>prihvaćanje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tolerating without protest</p><p><b>skloni prihvatiti umjesto odbijati, voljno prihvaćanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined to accept rather than reject</p><p><i>adj.</i> accepting willingly [acceptant]</p><p><b>akceptant</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) in the formation of a coordinate bond it is the compound to which electrons are donated</p><p><i>n.</i> the person (or institution) who accepts a check or draft and becomes responsible for paying the party named in the draft when it matures</p><p><b>RNK molekule prisutne u stanici (u najmanje 20 vrsta, svaka vrsta sposobna za kombinaciju s određenom aminokiselinom) koje vežu pravu aminokiselinu za proteinni lanac koji se sintetizira u ribosom stanice (prema uputama kodiranim u mRNK) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> RNA molecules present in the cell (in at least 20 varieties, each variety capable of combining with a specific amino acid) that attach the correct amino acid to the protein chain that is being synthesized at the ribosome of the cell (according to directions coded in the mRNA) [soluble RNA, tRNA, transfer RNA]</p><p><b>dohvat, dostup, dostupnost, priključni, prilaz, prilazni, pristup, pristupačnost, pristupiti, prolaz, raspolagati, uvid, prilazak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the right to enter [accession, admission, admittance, entree]</p><p><i>n.</i> the right to obtain or make use of or take advantage of something (as services or membership)</p><p><i>n.</i> a way of entering or leaving [approach]</p><p><i>n.</i> a code (a series of characters or digits) that must be entered in some way (typed or dialed or spoken) to get the use of something (a telephone line or a computer or a local area network etc.) [access code]</p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) the operation of reading or writing stored information [memory access]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of approaching or entering</p><p><i>v.</i> obtain or retrieve from a storage device</p><p><i>v.</i> reach or gain access to [get at]</p><p><b>pristupna šifra, pristupni kod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a code (a series of characters or digits) that must be entered in some way (typed or dialed or spoken) to get the use of something (a telephone line or a computer or a local area network etc.) [access]</p><p><b>kratka cesta koja daje pristup brzom putu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short road giving access to an expressway [slip road]</p><p><b>vrijeme pristup, vrijeme pristupa</b></p><p><i>n.</