ive]</p><p><b>akuzativ</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the case of nouns serving as the direct object of a verb [accusative, objective case]</p><p><b>posebno označava oblik progona u kojem je netko javno optužen i suđen za zločin i u kojem sudac nije i tužitelj (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> specifically indicating a form of prosecution in which one is publicly accused of and tried for a crime and in which the judge is not also the prosecutor</p><p><b>sadrži ili izražava optužbu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing or expressing accusation [accusative, accusing, accusive]</p><p><b>okriviti, optužiti, tužiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bring an accusation against [criminate, impeach, incriminate]</p><p><i>v.</i> blame for, make a claim of wrongdoing or misbehavior against [charge]</p><p><b>okrivljen, okrivljeni, okrivljenik, optužen, optužena, optuženik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a defendant in a criminal proceeding</p><p><b>tužitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who imputes guilt or blame</p><p><b>okriviti, optužiti, tužiti (od &quot;accuse&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing or expressing accusation [accusative, accusatory, accusive]</p><p><b>na optužujući način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an accusing manner</p><p><b>sadrži ili izražava optužbu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing or expressing accusation [accusative, accusatory, accusing]</p><p><b>navići se, naviknuti, priučiti, priviknuti, navikavati se, naviknuti se, privikavati se, priviknuti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make psychologically or physically used (to something) [habituate]</p><p><b>navikao, naviknut, običan, uobičajen, priviknut</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> commonly used or practiced [customary, habitual, wonted]</p><p><b>u naviku ili prilagođen za (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in the habit of or adapted to [used to]</p><p><b>as, as servis, kec, mala količina, mrvica, sportski as, Super!, adept, genij, majstor, virtuoz, vunderkind</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the smallest whole number or a numeral representing this number [1, I, one, single, uni