dgement, recognition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a short note recognizing a source of information or of a quoted passage [citation, cite, credit, mention, quotation, reference]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement acknowledging something or someone [acknowledgement]</p><p><b>Glavno strateško sjedište NATO-a u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a major strategic headquarters of NATO located in the United States [Allied Command Atlantic]</p><p><b>imaginarna crta paralelna ekvatoru gdje magnetna igla nema dubinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary line paralleling the equator where a magnetic needle has no dip [magnetic equator]</p><p><b>najviša točka, vrh, vrhunac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the highest level or degree attainable [elevation, height, meridian, peak, pinnacle, summit, superlative, tiptop, top]</p><p><i>n.</i> the highest point (of something) [apex, peak, vertex]</p><p><b>akna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inflammatory disease involving the sebaceous glands of the skin</p><p><b>bolest kože odraslih (često žena) kod koje se krvni sudovi lica povećavaju što rezultira crvenom pojavom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skin disease of adults (more often women) in which blood vessels of the face enlarge resulting in a flushed appearance [rosacea]</p><p><b>najčešći oblik akni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the most common form of acne</p><p><b>(od kože) sa oštećenjima kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of complexion) blemished by imperfections of the skin [pimpled, pimply, pustulate]</p><p><b>koji liče na akne (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling acne</p><p><b>podklasa Sporozoa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a subclass of Sporozoa [subclass Acnidosporidia]</p><p><b>mali rod stabala i grmova koji sadrže vrlo toksične glikozide za srce (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of trees and shrubs containing strongly toxic cardiac glycosides [Acokanthera, genus Acocanthera, genus Acokanthera]</p><p><b>srednjo veličine grmljavca iz Južne Afrike s gustim kožnim zimzeljenim lišćama i bijelim ili ružičastim cvijeć