</p><p><b>aktivacija, aktiviranje, pobuđivanje, pokretanje, potaknuće, uključenje, upućivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stimulation of activity in an organism or chemical</p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of causing to have energy and be active [activating, energizing]</p><p><i>n.</i> making active and effective (as a bomb)</p><p><b>aktivacijska energija, energija aktivacije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the energy that an atomic system must acquire before a process (such as an emission or reaction) can occur [energy of activation]</p><p><b>aktivator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) any agency bringing about activation</p><p><b>aktivan, aktive, djelatan, energičan, pokretljiv, pokretljivi, pravi, radan, radni, radno stanje, stvaran, vrijedan, zaposlen, živ, aktivni, aktivnima, aktivno, aktivnog, aktiv, živahan, otvoren, vrijedeći</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chemical agent capable of activity [active agent]</p><p><i>n.</i> the voice used to indicate that the grammatical subject of the verb is performing the action or causing the happening denoted by the verb [active voice]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is a participating member of an organization</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to become more severe or wider in scope</p><p><i>adj.</i> engaged in or ready for military or naval operations [combat-ready, fighting]</p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed to take action or effectuate change</p><p><i>adj.</i> taking part in an activity [participating]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by energetic activity</p><p><i>adj.</i> exerting influence or producing a change or effect</p><p><i>adj.</i> full of activity or engaged in continuous activity</p><p><i>adj.</i> in operation [alive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of the sun) characterized by an increased occurrence of sunspots and flares and radio emissions</p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing that the subject of the sentence has the semantic function of actor: "Hemingway favors active constructions"</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of verbs (e.g. `to run') and participial adjectives (e.g. `running' in `running water')) expressing action rather than a state of being [dynamic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of e.g. volcanos) capable of erupting</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of e.g. volcanos) erupting or liable to erupt</p><p><i>adj.</i> engaged in full-time work</p><p><b>kemijski agens sposoban za aktivnost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chemical agent capable of activity [active]</p><p><b>Službeni sustav za zaštitu od zračne odbrane: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> air defense by the use aircraft or missiles or artillery or electronic countermeasures</p><p><b>aplikacija koja se trenutno pokreće i u prvom planu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an application that is currently running and in the foreground</p><p><b>rodilac u kojem se majka potiče da aktivno sudjeluje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> childbirth during which the mother is encouraged to be an active participant</p><p><b>građanin koji ima aktivnu ulogu u zajednici (kao što je prevencija kriminala i nadzor susjedstva) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a citizen who takes an active role in the community (as in crime prevention and neighborhood watch)</p><p><b>oblik stečenog imuniteta u kojem tijelo proizvodi vlastita antitijela protiv antigena koji uzrokuju bolest. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of acquired immunity in which the body produces its own antibodies against disease-causing antigens</p><p><b>s masenim kapacitetom od 300 W do 2000 W, ali ne više od 300 W, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a type of LCD screen used for some portable computers</p><p><b>placebo koji se koristi u eksperimentalnim testovima lijeka koji ima primjetne nuspojave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a placebo used in experimental tests of a drug that has noticeable side effects</p><p><b>dio enzima ili antitela gdje se događa kemijska reakcija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of an enzyme or antibody where the chemical reaction occurs</p><p><b>aktivni prijenos, aktivni transport</b></p><p><i>n.</i> transport of a substance (as a protein or drug) across a cell membrane against the concentration gradient</p><p><b>povjerenje u kojem povjerenik mora obavljati određene dužnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trust in which the trustee must perform certain duties</p><p><b>aktiv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the voice used to indicate that the grammatical subject of the verb is performing the action or causing the happening denoted by the verb [active]</p><p><b>aktivno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an active manner</p><p><b>aktivnost, djelovanje, činjenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being active [action, activity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being active [activity]</p><p><b>odjeće za sport ili za običnu nošenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> attire worn for sport or for casual wear [athletic wear, sportswear]</p><p><b>aktivizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a policy of taking direct action to achieve a political or social goal</p><p><b>aktivist, aktivista, aktivistica, aktivistice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a militant reformer [militant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> advocating or engaged in activism [activistic]</p><p><b>aktivist, aktivista, aktivistica, aktivistice (od &quot;activist&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> advocating or engaged in activism [activist]</p><p><b>akcija, aktivnost, djelatnost, djelovanje, energičan rad, poduzetnost, preduzimljivos, rad, djelatnosti, djelovanja, radnja, činjenje, tjelesna funkcija, tjelesni proces, prirodni proces</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any specific behavior</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being active [action, activeness]</p><p><i>n.</i> an organic process that takes place in the body [bodily function, bodily process, body process]</p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) the capacity of a substance to take part in a chemical reaction</p><p><i>n.</i> a process existing in or produced by nature (rather than by the intent of human beings) [action, natural action, natural process]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being active [activeness]</p><p><b>proteinski kompleks u mišićnim vlaknima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a protein complex in muscle fibers</p><p><b>akter, glumac, glumica, protagonist, sudionik, tužitelj, učesnik, histrion</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a theatrical performer [histrion, player, role player, thespian]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who acts and gets things done [doer, worker]</p><p><b>poslovni agent za glumca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a business agent for an actor [theatrical agent]</p><p><b>pomoćnik glumca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wardrobe assistant for an actor [dresser]</p><p><b>riječi koje čine dijalog predstave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> words making up the dialogue of a play [speech, words]</p><p><b>glumac, glumica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a female actor</p><p><b>akti, apostolska djela, djela, akte</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book describing the development of the early church from Christ's Ascension to Paul's sojourn at Rome [Acts of the Apostles]</p><p><b>knjiga iz Novog zavjeta koja opisuje razvoj rane crkve od Kristovog uzašašća na nebo do Pavlovog boravka u Rimu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book describing the development of the early church from Christ's Ascension to Paul's sojourn at Rome [Acts]</p><p><b>aktualan, aktuelno, efektivan, efektivni, faktičan, pravi, realan, sadašnji, stvaran, stvarni ključ, suvremen, trenutan, trenutni, zbiljski, actualno, aktualni, prav, stvarni, stvarno, postojeći, prezentan, prisutan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> presently existing in fact and not merely potential or possible [existent]</p><p><i>adj.</i> taking place in reality</p><p><i>adj.</i> being or reflecting the essential or genuine character of something [genuine, literal, real]</p><p><i>adj.</i> existing in act or fact [factual]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being or existing at the present moment</p><p><b>(zakonom) naknada za štetu za koju se može lako dokazati da se dogodila i za koju je povrijeđena strana ima pravo na naknadu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) compensation for losses that can readily be proven to have occurred and for which the injured party has the right to be compensated [compensatory damages, general damages]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je iznajmljen