gent]</p><p><b>nerazoriv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> consisting of or having the hardness of adamant</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the hardness of a diamond</p><p><i>adj.</i> impervious to pleas, persuasion, requests, reason [adamant, inexorable, intransigent]</p><p><b>čvrsto, tvrdoglavo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> inflexibly</p><p><b>Američki revolucionarni vođa i patriota, Šesti predsjednik Sjedinjenih Američkih Država, Drugi predsjednik Sjedinjenih Država (1735-1826), planinski vrh u jugozapadnom Washingtonu u Cascade Rangeu (visina 12.307 stopa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American Revolutionary leader and patriot [Sam Adams, Samuel Adams]</p><p><i>n.</i> 6th President of the United States [John Quincy Adams, President Adams, President John Quincy Adams]</p><p><i>n.</i> 2nd President of the United States (1735-1826) [John Adams, President Adams, President John Adams]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain peak in southwestern Washington in the Cascade Range (12,307 feet high) [Mount Adams]</p><p><b>ponavljajući se nagli napadi nesvjesnosti uzrokovani poremećenom provodivosti impulsa koji reguliše otkucaje srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> recurrent sudden attacks of unconsciousness caused by impaired conduction of the impulse that regulates the heartbeat [Stokes-Adams syndrome, atrioventricular block, heart block]</p><p><b>Adana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in southern Turkey on the Seyhan River [Seyhan]</p><p><b>Baobaba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> baobab [genus Adansonia]</p><p><b>Afričko stablo s izuzetno debelim deblom i plodovima koji liče na bundevu i imaju jestivu pulpu zvanu majmunski kruh (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> African tree having an exceedingly thick trunk and fruit that resembles a gourd and has an edible pulp called monkey bread [baobab, monkey-bread tree]</p><p><b>Australsko stablo s ugodno kislim plodom koji liči na bundevu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree having an agreeably acid fruit that resembles a gourd [cream-of-tartar tree, sour gourd]</p><p><b>babilonski polubog ili prvi