ology) the responsive adjustment of a sense organ (as the eye) to varying conditions (as of light)</p><p><b>o prilagodbi ili o njoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to adaptation</p><p><b>koji imaju sposobnost prilagođavanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a capacity for adaptation [adaptive]</p><p><b>adaptiran, podešen, preuređen, prilagodio, prilagođen, prilagođena, prilagođeni, primijenjen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> changed in order to improve or made more fit for a particular purpose [altered]</p><p><b>adapter, adaptera, adaptor, pretvarač, prilagodnik, prilagođivač, uređaj za prilagodbu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musician who adapts a composition for particular voices or instruments or for another style of performance [arranger, transcriber]</p><p><i>n.</i> device that enables something to be used in a way different from that for which it was intended or makes different pieces of apparatus compatible [adaptor]</p><p><b>privikavanje, prilagodba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of adapting to something (such as environmental conditions) [adaptation, adjustment]</p><p><b>adaptabilan, adaptibilan, adaptivan, adaptivnog, prilagodljiv, prilagodljivi, snalažljiv, adaptivni, adaptivno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a capacity for adaptation [adaptative]</p><p><b>Razvoj mnogih različitih oblika iz prvobitno homogene grupe organizama kako ispunjavaju različite ekološke niše (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the development of many different forms from an originally homogeneous group of organisms as they fill different ecological niches</p><p><b>uređaj koji omogućuje neku stvar da se koristi na način koji se razlikuje od onoga za koji je namijenjen ili čini različite dijelove aparata kompatibilnim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> device that enables something to be used in a way different from that for which it was intended or makes different pieces of apparatus compatible [adapter]</p><p><b>Šesti mjesec civilne godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sixth month of the civil year</p><p><b>uklj