rgije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ester of adenosine that is converted to ATP for energy storage [ADP]</p><p><b>nukleotid koji se nalazi u mišićnim stanicama i važan je za metabolizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nucleotide found in muscle cells and important in metabolism [AMP, adenylic acid]</p><p><b>adenozin trifosfat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nucleotide derived from adenosine that occurs in muscle tissue [ATP]</p><p><b>poremećaj žlijezda tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disorder of the glands of the body [gland disease, glandular disease, glandular disorder]</p><p><b>Afričke antilope: puku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> African antelopes: puku [genus Adenota]</p><p><b>afrička antilopa bliska vodenicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an African antelope closely related to the waterbuck [puku]</p><p><b>adenovirus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a group of viruses including those that in humans cause upper respiratory infections or infectious pinkeye</p><p><b>nukleotid koji se nalazi u mišićnim stanicama i važan je za metabolizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nucleotide found in muscle cells and important in metabolism [AMP, adenosine monophosphate]</p><p><b>iskusan, obaviješten, poznavalac, pristalica, sljedbenik, stručan, stručnjak, umješan, upućen, vičan, vješt, adept, genij, majstor, virtuoz, vunderkind, dobar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is dazzlingly skilled in any field [ace, champion, genius, hotshot, maven, mavin, sensation, star, superstar, virtuoso, whiz, whizz, wiz, wizard]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing knowledge and skill and aptitude [expert, good, practiced, proficient, skilful, skillful]</p><p><b>upućenost, snalažljivost, spretnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> skillful performance or ability without difficulty [adroitness, deftness, facility, quickness]</p><p><b>adekvatnost, dostatnost, dovoljnost, kompetentnost, opravdanost, osnovanost, podešenost, podudaranje, prikladnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being able to meet a need satisfactorily: "he questioned the adequacy of the usual sentimental interpretation of the Golden Rule" [adequateness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being sufficient for the end in view [sufficiency]</p><p><b>adekvatan, dovoljan, koji odgovara, odgovarajući, podesan, prikladan, prikladni, podoban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the requisite qualities or resources to meet a task [equal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> sufficient for the purpose [enough]</p><p><i>adj.</i> about average [fair to middling, passable, tolerable]</p><p><b>koji imaju potrebne kvalitete za (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the requisite qualities for [capable, equal to, up to]</p><p><b>adekvatno, dovoljno, odgovarajuće, odgovarajući, odgovarajuć</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an adequate manner or to an adequate degree</p><p><b>adekvatan, dovoljan, koji odgovara, odgovarajući, podesan, prikladan, prikladni (od &quot;adequate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being able to meet a need satisfactorily: "he questioned the adequacy of the usual sentimental interpretation of the Golden Rule" [adequacy]</p><p><b>mineral koji je mješavina ugljovodonika i koji se javlja u kombinaciji s naftom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a waxy mineral that is a mixture of hydrocarbons and occurs in association with petroleum [earth wax, mineral wax, ozocerite, ozokerite]</p><p><b>vitamin B koji je bitan za metabolizam aminokiselina i skroba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is essential for metabolism of amino acids and starch [pyridoxal, pyridoxamine, pyridoxine, vitamin B6]</p><p><b>tamno sivo ekstruzivno kamenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dark greyish extrusive rock</p><p><b>hormon koji se luči iz pozadinske hipofize (trgovinski naziv Pitressin) i također iz živčanih završetaka u hipotalamu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hormone secreted by the posterior pituitary gland (trade name Pitressin) and also by nerve endings in the hypothalamus [Pitressin, antidiuretic hormone, vasopressin]</p><p><b>stanje (uglavnom kod dječaka) koje se karakterizira poremećajima ponašanja i učenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a condition (mostly in boys) characterized by behavioral and learning disorders [ADD, MBD, attention deficit disorder, attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, hyperkinetic syndrome, minimal brain damage, minimal brain dysfunction]</p><p><b>biti uz, držati se, ostajati vjeran, prianjati, prianjati za nešto, pričvrstiti, pridržavati se, prijanjati, priljubiti, pristajati, priljubiti se, priljubljivati se, prionuti, pripiti se, privezati se, pričvrstiti se, pričvršćivati se, vezati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be compatible or in accordance with</p><p><i>v.</i> follow through or carry out a plan without deviation</p><p><i>v.</i> come or be in close contact with [cleave, cling, cohere, stick]</p><p><i>v.</i> be a devoted follower or supporter [stick]</p><p><i>v.</i> be loyal to [stand by, stick, stick by]</p><p><i>v.</i> stick to firmly [bind, bond, hold fast, stick, stick to]</p><p><b>adherencija, odanost, prianjanje, pridržavanje, prijanjanje, privrženost, vjernost, zakvačanje, zakvačenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> faithful support for a cause or political party or religion [adhesion, attachment]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of sticking together (as of glue and wood) or the joining of surfaces of different composition [adhesion, adhesiveness, bond]</p><p><b>koji prianja, ljepljiv, pristalica, pristaša, sljedbenik, koji prijanja, učenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who believes and helps to spread the doctrine of another [disciple]</p><p><i>adj.</i> sticking fast</p><p><b>adhezija, adsorbirana voda, odanost nečemu, prianjanje, prijanjanje, privrženost, zakvačanje, zakvačenje, odanost, vjernost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal union of bodily tissues</p><p><i>n.</i> a fibrous band of scar tissue that binds together normally separate anatomical structures</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of sticking together (as of glue and wood) or the joining of surfaces of different composition [adherence, adhesiveness, bond]</p><p><i>n.</i> faithful support for a cause or political party or religion [adherence, attachment]</p><p><b>adhezijski ugovor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a contract that heavily restricts one party while leaving the other free (as some standard form printed contracts) [contract of adhesion]</p><p><b>adhezija, adhezijski, adhezivan, adhezivni, lepljiv, ljepilo, ljepljiv, adhesivni, keljilo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance that unites or bonds surfaces together [adhesive agent, adhesive material]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to adhere</p><p><b>ljepilo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance that unites or bonds surfaces together [adhesive, adhesive material]</p><p><b>zavoj koji se sastoji od medicinske obloge od obične apsorpcijske gaze koja se drži na mjestu plastičnom ili tkaninskom traku prekrivenom lepilom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bandage consisting of a medical dressing of plain absorbent gauze held in place by a plastic or fabric tape coated with adhesive</p><p><b>frikcija, trenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the friction between a body and the surface on which it moves (as between an automobile tire and the road) [grip, traction]</p><p><b>ljepilo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance that unites or bonds surfaces together [adhesive, adhesive agent]</p><p><b>flaster, medicinski flaster</b></p><p><i>n.</i> adhesive tape used in dressing wounds [plaster, sticking plaster]</p><p><b>ljepljiva traka, samoljepljiva traka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tape coated with adhesive</p><p><b>adhezivnost, prionjivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of sticking together (as of glue and wood) or the joining of surfaces of different composition [adherence, adhesion, bond]</p><p><b>organizacija s malom ili nikakvom strukturom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organization with little or no structure</p><p><b>Glavni sveti tekst sikhizma sadrži himne i poeziju kao i učenja prvih pet gurua. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principal sacred text of Sikhism contains hymns and poetry as well as the teachings of the first five gurus [Granth, Granth Sahib]</p><p><b>adijabatički, adijabat