><i>n.</i> the segment of the public that is easily influenced by mass media (chiefly British)</p><p><b>izmjeriti, odmjeriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> determine the quantity of someone's share</p><p><b>dati, potpomoći, pridonijeti, primijeniti, rukovodilac, rukovoditi, staviti u upotrebu, ukazati, upravljati, upravnik, vršiti, vršiti obavlja, dati lijek, i, prepisati, provođenje, davati, dijeliti, podijeliti, porazdijeliti, porazdjeljivati, razdati, razdavati, razdijeliti, razdjeljivati, udijeliti, udjeljivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> work in an administrative capacity [administrate]</p><p><i>v.</i> perform (a church sacrament) ritually</p><p><i>v.</i> administer or bestow, as in small portions [allot, deal, deal out, dish out, dispense, distribute, dole out, lot, mete out, parcel out, shell out]</p><p><i>v.</i> give or apply (medications) [dispense]</p><p><i>v.</i> direct the taking of</p><p><b>koji se može primjenjivati ili upravljati (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being administered or managed</p><p><b>rukovoditi, upravljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> work in an administrative capacity [administer]</p><p><b>administracija, direkcija, ministarstvo, rukovođenje, uprava, uprave, upravljanje, vlada, vlast, administrativno, uređenje, upravna vlast, predsjednički mandat, predsjedništvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a method of tending to or managing the affairs of a some group of people (especially the group's business affairs) [disposal]</p><p><i>n.</i> the persons (or committees or departments etc.) who make up a body for the purpose of administering something [brass, establishment, governance, governing body, organisation, organization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of administering medication [giving medication]</p><p><i>n.</i> the tenure of a president [presidency, presidential term]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of governing [governance, governing, government, government activity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of meting out justice according to the law [judicature]</p><p><b>administrativan, administra