i detalji koji se moraju brinuti i zadaće koje se moraju obavljati u vođenju organizacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tiresome but essential details that must be taken care of and tasks that must be performed in running an organization</p><p><b>Divna izvrsnost. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> admirable excellence [admirableness, wonderfulness]</p><p><b>divan, izvrstan, krasan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deserving of the highest esteem or admiration</p><p><i>adj.</i> inspiring admiration or approval</p><p><b>divan, izvrstan, krasan (od &quot;admirable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> admirable excellence [admirability, wonderfulness]</p><p><b>zadivljujuće, zapanjujuće, divno, krasno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an admirable manner [commendable, laudably, praiseworthily]</p><p><b>admiral, admiralski brod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the supreme commander of a fleet [full admiral]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several brightly colored butterflies</p><p><b>istraživač i američki mornarički časnik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> explorer and United States naval officer [Byrd, Richard E. Byrd, Richard Evelyn Byrd]</p><p><b>američki mornarički časnik sjećan na pobjedu u zalivu Manila u španjolsko-američkom ratu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a United States naval officer remembered for his victory at Manila Bay in the Spanish-American War [Dewey, George Dewey]</p><p><b>Engleski admiral koji je porazio francusku flotu Napoleona ali je smrtno ranjen u Trafalgaru (1758-1805) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English admiral who defeated the French fleets of Napoleon but was mortally wounded at Trafalgar (1758-1805) [Horatio Nelson, Lord Nelson, Nelson, Viscount Nelson]</p><p><b>Američki admiral pacifičke flote tijekom Drugog svjetskog rata koji je koristio nosače zrakoplova za uništavanje japanske mornarice (1885-1966) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States admiral of the Pacific fleet during World War II who used aircraft carriers to destroy the Japanese navy (1885-1966) [Chester Nimitz, Chester William Nimitz, Nimitz]</p><p><b>admira