ic [Motrin, Nuprin, ibuprofen, isobutylphenyl propionic acid]</p><p><b>opravdanost, uputnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being advisable</p><p><b>podesan, pogodan, poželjan, preporučljiv, uputan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of being recommended or suggested</p><p><b>izvijestiti, obavijestiti, preporučiti, priopćiti, savjetovati, izvjestiti, posavjetovati, preporučivati, predlagati, predložiti, sugerirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give advice to [counsel, rede]</p><p><i>v.</i> inform (somebody) of something [apprise, apprize, give notice, notify, send word]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a proposal, declare a plan for something [propose, suggest]</p><p><b>najavljen, promišljen, savjetovan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the benefit of careful prior consideration or counsel [well-advised]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having received information</p><p><b>promišljeno, razumno, svjesno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with intention [by choice, by design, deliberately, designedly, intentionally, on purpose, purposely]</p><p><b>netko tko prima savjete (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who receives advice</p><p><b>rasprava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> careful consideration [deliberation, weighing]</p><p><b>konzultant, savjetnik, savjetodavac, stručni savjetnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert who gives advice [advisor, consultant]</p><p><b>savjetnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert who gives advice [adviser, consultant]</p><p><b>savjetodavan, savjetodavni, savjetodavno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an announcement that usually advises or warns the public of some threat</p><p><i>adj.</i> giving advice [consultative, consultatory, consultive]</p><p><b>savjetodavni odbor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a board appointed to advise the chief administrator [planning board]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, "služba" znači: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a consulting service in which a CPA develops findings and conclusions and recommendations that are presented to the client for consideration and decision making</p><p><b>advo