jek (trademarks Aleve i Anaprox i Aflaxen) koji se bori protiv boli i upale (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (trademarks Aleve and Anaprox and Aflaxen) that fights pain and inflammation [Aleve, Anaprox, naproxen sodium]</p><p><b>nepostojan svijetleći (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> shining unsteadily [flickering]</p><p><b>koji plovi, na brodu, na moru, na vodi, ploveći, plutajući, u jeku, u pokretu, u toku</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> aimlessly drifting [adrift, aimless, directionless, planless, rudderless, undirected]</p><p><i>adj.</i> borne on the water</p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with water [awash, flooded, inundated, overflowing]</p><p><b>uzbuđen u očekivanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> excited in anticipation [nervous]</p><p><b>na nogama, pješice, pješke, u pokretu, u radu, u toku</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> traveling by foot</p><p><i>adj.</i> currently in progress [underway]</p><p><i>adv.</i> on foot</p><p><b>gore spomenuti, spomenut</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being the one previously mentioned or spoken of [aforesaid, said]</p><p><b>gore spomenuto, gore rečeni, gore spomenuti, prije spomenut, prijerečeni, gore pomenuti, spomenut</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being the one previously mentioned or spoken of [aforementioned, said]</p><p><b>umišljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> with planning and intention [planned, plotted]</p><p><b>posebno brodskih linija itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> especially of a ship's lines etc [foul, fouled]</p><p><b>neobično velika količina ovog fetoprotein u fetusu može signalizirati abnormalnost neuronske cijevi (kao što je spina bifida ili anencefalija) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormally large amount of this fetoprotein in the fetus can signal an abnormality of the neural tube (as spina bifida or anencephaly) [alpha fetoprotein, alpha foetoprotein]</p><p><b>bojati se nečega, plašio, prestrašen, uplašen, preplašen, ustrašen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> filled with fear or apprehension</p><p><i>adj.</i> filled with regret or concern</p><p><i>adj.</i> feeling worry or concern or insecurity</p><p><i>adj.</i> having feelings of aversion or unwillingness</p><p><b>afrički rod biljaka iz obitelji Zingiberaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an African genus of plants of the family Zingiberaceae [genus Aframomum]</p><p><b>biljka iz zapadne Afrike koja nosi žestoka sjemena paprike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> West African plant bearing pungent peppery seeds [Guinea grains, Guinea pepper, grains of paradise, melagueta pepper]</p><p><b>velika obitelj srodnih jezika koji se govore u Aziji i Africi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large family of related languages spoken both in Asia and Africa [Afrasian language, Afro-Asiatic, Afroasiatic, Afroasiatic language, Hamito-Semitic]</p><p><b>velika obitelj srodnih jezika koji se govore u Aziji i Africi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large family of related languages spoken both in Asia and Africa [Afrasian, Afro-Asiatic, Afroasiatic, Afroasiatic language, Hamito-Semitic]</p><p><b>iznova, nanovo, opet, ponovo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> again but in a new or different way [anew]</p><p><b>Afrika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the second largest continent</p><p><b>afrikanac, Afrikanka, afrički, afrikanski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Africa</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the nations of Africa or their peoples</p><p><b>ne-standardni oblik američkog engleskog koji karakteristično govore Afroamerikanci u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nonstandard form of American English characteristically spoken by African Americans in the United States [AAVE, African American Vernacular English, Black English, Black English Vernacular, Black Vernacular, Black Vernacular English, Ebonics]</p><p><b>ne-standardni oblik američkog engleskog koji karakteristično govore Afroamerikanci u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nonstandard form of American English characteristically spoken by African Americans in the United States [AAVE, African American English, Black English, Black English Vernacular, Black Vernacular, Black Vernacular English, Ebonics]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bowstring hemp of South Africa [African hemp, Sansevieria guineensis]</p><p><b>kameleon pronađen u Africi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chameleon found in Africa [Chamaeleo chamaeleon]</p><p><b>Žaba bez jezika porijeklom iz Afrike. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tongueless frog native to Africa [Xenopus laevis]</p><p><b>mala široko rasprostranjena drvena zmija južne Afrike u crnim i narandžastim prugama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small widely distributed arboreal snake of southern Africa banded in black and orange [Aspidelaps lubricus]</p><p><b>bilo koja zemlja koja okupira afrički kontinent (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any one of the countries occupying the African continent [African nation]</p><p><b>opasan krokodil široko rasprostranjen u Africi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dangerous crocodile widely distributed in Africa [Crocodylus niloticus, Nile crocodile]</p><p><b>grm iz jugozapadnog Mediterana s žutim cvjetovima nalik maramurici, Ostali proizvodi od biljaka ili biljaka od biljaka ili biljaka od biljaka ili biljaka od biljaka ili biljaka od biljaka, bilo koja od nekoliko biljaka rod Arctotis s cvjetovima nalik margaridama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub of southwestern Mediterranean region having yellow daisylike flowers [Lonas annua, Lonas inodora, yellow ageratum]</p><p><i>n.</i> African or Asiatic herbs with daisylike flowers</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several plants of the genus Arctotis having daisylike flowers</p><p><b>afrički slon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elephant native to Africa having enormous flapping ears and ivory tusks [Loxodonta africana]</p><p><b>obično domaći sivi papagaj s crno-crnim repom i bijelim licem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commonly domesticated grey parrot with red-and-black tail and white face [African grey, Psittacus erithacus]</p><p><b>obični majmun savane sa zelenkasto-sivom leđom i žutim repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common savannah monkey with greenish-grey back and yellow tail [Cercopithecus aethiops sabaeus, green monkey]</p><p><b>obično domaći sivi papagaj s crno-crnim repom i bijelim licem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commonly domesticated grey parrot with red-and-black tail and white face [African gray, Psittacus erithacus]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1., veliki grm Južne Afrike s mnogim vidljivim dlakavim granama s velikim dlakavim lišcima i grmovima vidljivih bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bowstring hemp of South Africa [African bowstring hemp, Sansevieria guineensis]</p><p><i>n.</i> large shrub of South Africa having many conspicuously hairy branches with large hairy leaves and clusters of conspicuous white flowers [Sparmannia africana]</p><p><b>dvostruko drvo iz tropske Afrike i južne Azije s plavobijelom trnčanošću, s plavim ili bijelim cvjetovima i svijetlo crvenim bojama nalik bojama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> woolly-stemmed biennial arborescent shrub of tropical Africa and southern Asia having silvery-white prickly branches, clusters of blue or white flowers, and bright red berries resembling holly berries [Solanum giganteum]</p><p><b>snažan sisavac poput psa iz južne i istočne Afrike koji lovi u velikim čoparima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a powerful doglike mammal of southern and eastern Africa that hunts in large packs [Cape hunting dog, Lycaon pictus, hyena dog]</p><p><b>Afrička biljka s svijetlo zelenim zimzelenim lišćama i čvorovima mnogih obično duboko ljubičastog plavog cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> African plant with bright green evergreen leaves and umbels of many usually deep violet-blue flowers [African tulip, Agapanthus africanus, blue African lily]</p><p><b>višegodišnje južnoafričke trave s gusto skupljenim krhkim stabljikama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial South African grass having densely clumped flimsy stems [Eragrostis curvula, weeping love grass]</p><p><b>afričko drvo s tvrdim teškim bezmirnim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> African tree having hard heavy odorless wood</p><p><b>Grupa od 100 g. do 100 g. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stout branching annual with large yellow to orange flower heads [Aztec marigold, Tagetes erecta, big marigold]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijska žitarica čija semena daju pomalo gorko brašno, osnovno jelo na Istoku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian cereal grass whose seed yield a somewhat bitter flour, a staple in the Orient [Eleusine coracana, coracan, corakan, finger millet, kurakkan, ragee, ragi]</p><p><b>uništava krokodilova jaja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> destroys crocodile eggs [Varanus niloticus]</p><p><b>bilo koja zemlja koja okupira afrički kontinent (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any one of the countries occupying the African continent [African country]</p><p><b>afrički palmi za ulje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> oil palm of Africa [Elaeis guineensis]</p><p><b>mala grmljava afrička stabla s tvrdim drvetom koja se koristi kao drvo za bojenje koje daje crvenu boju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrubby African tree with hard wood used as a dyewood yielding a red dye [Baphia nitida, camwood]</p><p><b>Afričko drvo koje ima prilično lagano drvo koje miriše na cedar i koje je različite boje od ružičaste do crvenkasto smeđe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> African tree having rather lightweight cedar-scented wood varying in color from pink to reddish brown [Entandrophragma cylindricum, cedar mahogany, sapele mahogany]</p><p><b>listovi grma Catha edulis koji se žvače kao duhan ili se koriste za pravljenje čaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the leaves of the shrub Catha edulis which are chewed like tobacco or used to make tea [Arabian tea, cat, kat, khat, qat, quat]</p><p><b>Afrička biljka s svijetlo zelenim zimzelenim lišćama i čvorovima mnogih obično duboko ljubičastog plavog cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> African plant with bright green evergreen leaves and umbels of many usually deep violet-blue flowers [African lily, Agapanthus africanus, blue African lily]</p><p><b>tropska afrička biljka