e love]</p><p><i>n.</i> a religious meal shared as a sign of love and fellowship [love feast]</p><p><i>adj.</i> with the mouth wide open as in wonder or awe [gaping]</p><p><b>nesebična ljubav jedne osobe prema drugoj bez spolnih implikacija (posebno ljubav koja je duhovne prirode) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> selfless love of one person for another without sexual implications (especially love that is spiritual in nature) [agape]</p><p><b>rod Psittacidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Psittacidae [genus Agapornis]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta uzgoja koja koristi agar kao želatni sredstvo, s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 g/cm2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any culture medium that uses agar as the gelling agent [nutrient agar]</p><p><i>n.</i> a colloidal extract of algae [agar-agar]</p><p><b>agar-agar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colloidal extract of algae [agar]</p><p><b>vrbov plutnjak, pečurka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungus used in the preparation of punk for fuses [Fomes igniarius]</p><p><i>n.</i> a saprophytic fungus of the order Agaricales having an umbrellalike cap with gills on the underside</p><p><b>Velika obitelj uključujući mnoge poznate gljive (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large family including many familiar mushrooms [family Agaricaceae]</p><p><b>tipične gljivice iz podpodjele Basidiomycota (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> typical gilled mushrooms belonging to the subdivision Basidiomycota [order Agaricales]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Agaricaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of Agaricaceae [genus Agaricus]</p><p><b>lipika, lokvić, poljska pečurka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coarse edible mushroom with a hollow stem and a broad white cap [horse mushroom]</p><p><b>uobičajena jestiva gljiva koja se prirodno nalazi u vlažnom otvorenom tlu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common edible mushroom found naturally in moist open soil [field mushroom, meadow mushroom]</p><p><b>Američki prirodnjak (rođen u Švicarskoj) koji je proučavao fosile riba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States naturalist (born in Switzerland) who studied fossil fish [Jean Louis Rodolphe Agassiz, Louis Agassiz]</p><p><b>Velika izop (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> giant hyssop [genus Agastache]</p><p><b>Čvrsta biljka iz Sjeverne Amerike s mirisom od fenikala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> much-branched North American herb with an odor like fennel [anise hyssop]</p><p><b>Vječna biljka iz Meksika koja je rasla u crvenokrasne cvijeće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect perennial of Mexico having rose to crimson flowers [Mexican hyssop]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka s čvrstima stabljikama i žuto-zelenim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect perennial with stout stems and yellow-green flowers [yellow giant hyssop]</p><p><b>Ahat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an impure form of quartz consisting of banded chalcedony</p><p><b>linija, red, redak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> space for one line of print (one column wide and 1/14 inch deep) used to measure advertising [line]</p><p><b>keramika koja je vinska i mrljana da liči na agat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pottery that is veined and mottled to resemble agate</p><p><b>Agatha Christie</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prolific English writer of detective stories (1890-1976) [Christie, Dame Agatha Mary Clarissa Christie]</p><p><b>šumska borovaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> kauri pine [genus Agathis]</p><p><b>izvorno iz Molukskih otočića i Filipina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> native to the Moluccas and Philippines [Agathis dammara, amboina pine, amboyna pine]</p><p><b>Visoko drvo na Novom Zelandu s bijelim drvetom s ravnim zrnama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall timber tree of New Zealand having white straight-grained wood [kauri, kaury]</p><p><b>izvorno iz Molukskih otočića i Filipina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> native to the Moluccas and Philippines [Agathis alba, amboina pine, amboyna pine]</p><p><b>Novozelandsko stablo s sjajnim lišćama i ljuskom crvenkasto-smeđom kore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> New Zealand tree with glossy leaves and scaly reddish-brown bark [red kauri]</p><p><b>Australsko drvo koje liči na kauri, ali je mnogo