ed as if in fear or wonder [staring]</p><p><b>rod s jednom vrstom koja je brzo rastuća uzlazna loza s gomoljastim korijenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus with one species that is a rapidly growing climbing vine with tuberous roots [genus Agdestis]</p><p><b>Azijski epitet za Reju ili Cibele (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic epithet for Rhea or Cybele</p><p><b>dob, doba, dugi rok, dugo vrijeme, era, godine, godine života, starost, godište, odležati, period, pokoljenje, postarati se, razdoblje, uzrast, vijek, vječnost, stariti, starjeti, dobi, dobna, dobne, starosna, starosno, uzraste, povijesno razdoblje, dugo, dugo vremena, godinama, kasne godine života, staračka dob, starije godine, treća dob, ostarjeti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> how long something has existed</p><p><i>n.</i> an era of history having some distinctive feature [historic period]</p><p><i>n.</i> a time of life (usually defined in years) at which some particular qualification or power arises [eld]</p><p><i>n.</i> a prolonged period of time [long time, years]</p><p><i>n.</i> a late time of life [eld, geezerhood, old age, years]</p><p><i>v.</i> begin to seem older</p><p><i>v.</i> grow old or older [get on, maturate, mature, senesce]</p><p><i>v.</i> make older</p><p><b>dobna grupa, dobna skupina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of people having approximately the same age [age group, cohort]</p><p><b>osobe u istom starosnom rasponu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people in the same age range</p><p><b>dobna grupa, dobna skupina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of people having approximately the same age [age bracket, cohort]</p><p><b>dobna granica, starosna granica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> regulation establishing the maximum age for doing something or holding some position</p><p><b>prosječna dob u kojoj se očekuje da se pojave određene performanse (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the average age at which particular performances are expected to appear</p><p><b>minimalna dob za brak bez pristanka roditelja ili minimalna dob za seksualne odnose 