n [qui vive]</p><p><i>n.</i> a warning serves to make you more alert to danger [alerting]</p><p><i>n.</i> an automatic signal (usually a sound) warning of danger [alarm, alarum, warning signal]</p><p><i>v.</i> warn or arouse to a sense of danger or call to a state of preparedness [alarm]</p><p><i>adj.</i> engaged in or accustomed to close observation [watchful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> quick and energetic [brisk, lively, merry, rattling, snappy, spanking, zippy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> mentally perceptive and responsive [alive, awake]</p><p><b>dežurstvo, pozornost, upozoravanje, uzbunjivanje, signal u pozdrava nj a, signal upozoravanja, signal uzbunjivanja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of readiness to respond [alertness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a warning serves to make you more alert to danger [alert]</p><p><b>alarm, alarmirati, budan, budnost, događaj koji zahtijeva trenutačnu pažnju, dovesti u stanje pripravnosti, hitar, na oprezu, oprez, oprezan, pozornost, spreman, spremnost, stanje pripravnosti, upozorenje, upozoriti, uzbuna, znak na uzbunu, živahan (od &quot;alert&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in mentally perceptive and responsive way</p><p><b>oprez, opreznost, pozornost, živahnost, budnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of paying close and continuous attention [vigilance, wakefulness, watchfulness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a state of readiness to respond [alerting]</p><p><i>n.</i> lively attentiveness [on the qui vive, sharp-sightedness]</p><p><b>Talijanski slikar mitoloških i religijskih slika (1444-1510) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian painter of mythological and religious paintings (1444-1510) [Botticelli, Sandro Botticelli]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1534. do 1549. koji je ekskomunicirao Henryja VIII. iz Engleske 1538. i pokrenuo Tridentanski koncil 1545. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1534 to 1549 who excommunicated Henry VIII of England in 1538 and initiated the Council of Trent in 1545 [Paul III]</p><p><b>Talijanski romanopisac i pjesnik (1785-1873) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.