ls of showy pinkish-purple lily-like flowers [Peruvian lily, lily of the Incas]</p><p><b>jedna od mnogih obitelji ili podobitelji u koje neki sustavi klasifikacije podjeljuju Liliaceae, ali nisu široko prihvaćeni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of many families or subfamilies into which some classification systems subdivide the Liliaceae but not widely accepted [family Alstroemeriaceae]</p><p><b>alt, EL, altituda, elevacija, visina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> angular distance above the horizon (especially of a celestial object) [EL, altitude, elevation]</p><p><b>ramipril</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ACE inhibitor (trade name Altace) used to treat high blood pressure or in some patients who have had a heart attack [ramipril]</p><p><b>Altaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain range in central Asia that extends a thousand miles from Kazakhstan eastward into western Mongolia and northern China [Altay Mountains]</p><p><b>bilo koji član naroda koji govori jezik u Altajskom jezičkom sastavu, grupa srodnih jezika koji se govore u Aziji i jugoistočnoj Europi, od ili se odnosi na ili napisan u Altaic (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any member of the peoples speaking a language in the Altaic language group</p><p><i>n.</i> a group of related languages spoken in Asia and southeastern Europe [Altaic language]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or written in Altaic</p><p><b>grupa srodnih jezika koji se govore u Aziji i jugoistočnoj Europi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of related languages spoken in Asia and southeastern Europe [Altaic]</p><p><b>Dvostruka zvijezda 15,7 svjetlosnih godina od Zemlje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> double star 15.7 light years from Earth</p><p><b>oltar, oltari, oltaru, žrtvenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the table in Christian churches where communion is given [Lord's table, communion table]</p><p><i>n.</i> a raised structure on which gifts or sacrifices to a god are made</p><p><b>dječak služi kao akolyte (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a boy serving as an acolyte</p><p><b>misno vino</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used in a communion service [sacramental wine]</p><p><b>oltarna pala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a painted or carved screen placed above and behind an altar or communion table [reredos]</p><p><b>Altaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain range in central Asia that extends a thousand miles from Kazakhstan eastward into western Mongolia and northern China [Altai Mountains]</p><p><b>instrument koji mjeri visinu i azimut nebeskih tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instrument that measures the altitude and azimuth of celestial bodies</p><p><b>izmijeniti, mijenjati, mijenjeti, oltar, preinačavati, preinačiti, promijeniti, promijeniti se, promjeniti kurs, žrtvenik, varirati, interpolirati, jaloviti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to change [change, modify]</p><p><i>v.</i> become different in some particular way, without permanently losing one's or its former characteristics or essence [change, vary]</p><p><i>v.</i> make an alteration to</p><p><i>v.</i> insert words into texts, often falsifying it thereby [falsify, interpolate]</p><p><i>v.</i> remove the ovaries of [castrate, neuter, spay]</p><p><b>alter ego</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a very close and trusted friend who seems almost a part of yourself</p><p><b>kvaliteta da se može mijenjati. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being alterable</p><p><b>izmjenljiv, preinačiv, promjenljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being changed or altered in some characteristic</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of the punishment ordered by a court) capable of being changed to one less severe</p><p><b>alteracija, alteracije, ispravak, izmjena, preinačenje, preklapanje, promjena, promjena ugovora o osiguranju života, rekonstrukcija, skretanje, mijena, modifikacija, prepravljanje, prilagodba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that occurs when something passes from one state or phase to another [change, modification]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making something different (as e.g. the size of a garment) [adjustment, modification]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of revising or altering (involving reconsideration and modification) [revision]</p><p><b>izmjeničan, promjenjiv, terapijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to cure or restore to health [curative, healing, remedial, sanative, therapeutic]</p><p><b>prepirati s, prepirati se, svađati se, porječkati se, posvaditi se, posvađati se, prepucavati se, rječkati se, sporiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> have a disagreement over something [argufy, dispute, quarrel, scrap]</p><p><b>prepirka, svađa, sukob</b></p><p><i>n.</i> noisy quarrel [affray, fracas]</p><p><b>izmijenjen, primijenjen, promijenjen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> changed in form or character without becoming something else</p><p><i>adj.</i> having testicles or ovaries removed [neutered]</p><p><i>adj.</i> changed in order to improve or made more fit for a particular purpose [adapted]</p><p><b>ažuriranje, mijenjanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sterilization of an animal [fixing, neutering]</p><p><b>rodni nizkih biljaka tropske Amerike i Australije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of low herbs of tropical America and Australia [genus Alternanthera]</p><p><b>Brojna južnoamerička vodena trava s lištima poput trave i kratkim šiljcima bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prolific South American aquatic weed having grasslike leaves and short spikes of white flowers [alligator grass, alligator weed]</p><p><b>alternativni, alternativno, alternirati, dopunski, izmenjivati se, izmjeničan, izmjenični, izmjenjivati, izmjenjivati se, mijenjati peri, mijenjati period, mijenjati periodično, mijenjati se, naizmeničan, naizmjeničan, naizmjenično, rezervni, varijanta, zamjenik, zamjenjivati, zastupnički zamjenik, zamjena, dublirati, alternativan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who takes the place of another person [replacement, surrogate]</p><p><i>v.</i> go back and forth [jump]</p><p><i>v.</i> exchange people temporarily to fulfill certain jobs and functions</p><p><i>v.</i> be an understudy or alternate for a role [understudy]</p><p><i>v.</i> reverse (a direction, attitude, or course of action) [flip, flip-flop, interchange, switch, tack]</p><p><i>v.</i> do something in turns [take turns]</p><p><i>adj.</i> every second one of a series</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving or used in place of another [alternative, substitute]</p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring by turns [alternating]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of leaves and branches etc</p><p><b>naizmjence, naizmjeničan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an alternating sequence or position</p><p><b>izmjenična, izmjenični, naizmjenice, naizmjeničan, naizmjenično</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a current) reversing direction</p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring by turns [alternate]</p><p><b>izmjenična struja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electric current that reverses direction sinusoidally [AC, alternating electric current]</p><p><b>električna struja koja sinusoidno okreće smjer (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electric current that reverses direction sinusoidally [AC, alternating current]</p><p><b>alternacija, alternacije, alterniranje, izmenjivanje, izmjenjivanje, promjena, promjena kursa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> successive change from one thing or state to another and back again</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, "sastavljanje" znači: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the alternation of two or more different forms in the life cycle of a plant or animal [heterogenesis, xenogenesis]</p><p><b>alternativa, alternativan, alternativni, alternativu, izbor, koji isključuje drugo, naizmjeničan, varijanta, zamjenska, zamjenski, mogućnost, opcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of a number of things from which only one can be chosen [choice, option]</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving or used in place of another [alternate, substitute]</p><p><i>adj.</i> necessitating a choice between mutually exclusive possibilities</p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to unconventional choices</p><p><b>metoda rađanja koja izbjegava uplitanje u visokotehnološku medicinu u korist prirodnih i kućnih okruženja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a method of childbirth that avoids intrusive high-tech medicine in favor of more natural and homely settings [alternative birthing]</p><p><b>metoda rađanja koja izbjegava uplitanje u visokotehnološku medicinu u korist prirodnih i kućnih okruženja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a method of childbirth that avoids intrusive high-tech medicine in favor of more natural and homely settings [alternative birth]</p><p><b>Energija koja se proizvodi iz izvora koji ne troše prirodne resurse ili štete okolišu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> energy derived from sources that do not use up natural resources or harm the environment</p><p><b>alternativna medicina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of medicine without the use of drugs</p><p><b>Pitanje koje se temelji na činjenicama koje su toliko odvojene da je teško utvrditi na koje se činjenice osoba želi osloniti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pleading that alleges facts so separate that it is difficult to determine which facts the person intends to rely on [pleading in the alternative]</p><p><b>alternativan, alternativno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in place of, or as an alternative to [instead, or else]</p><p><b>alternator, generator, generator izmjeničnog napona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an old term for an electric generator that produces alternating current (especially in automobiles)</p><p><b>bilo koje od različitih biljaka rodova Althaea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Althaea [althea, hollyhock]</p><p><b>bilo koje od različitih biljaka rodova Althaea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Althaea [althaea, hollyhock]</p><p><b>Tenisačica iz Sjedinjenih Država koja je bila prva crna žena koja je osvojila sve glavne svjetske singl titule (1927-2003) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States tennis player who was the first Black woman player to win all the major world singles titles (1927-2003) [Gibson]</p><p><b>Europska višegodišnja biljka naturalizirana u Sjedinjenim Državama s trokutnim ovatičnim listovima i lilakavo-ružičastom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European perennial plant naturalized in United States having triangular ovate leaves and lilac-pink flowers [marsh mallow, white mallow]</p><p><b>biljka s krajnjim rascemama od blesavih bijeli do ružičastih ili ljubičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant with terminal racemes of showy white to pink or purple flowers [Alcea rosea, rose mallow]</p><p><b>altimetar, visinometar, visinomjar, visinomjer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instrument that measures the height above ground</p><p><b>vrlo visoka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very high</p><p><b>dubina, nadmorska visina, nadmorska visine, nadvišenja, ugao, uzvišenja, visina, visine, visinski, visoki položaj, vrh, znamenitost, nadmorskoj visini, ALT, EL, altituda, elevacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> elevation especially above sea level or above the earth's surface [height]</p><p><i>n.</i> the perpendicular distance from the base of a geometric figure to the opposite vertex (or side if parallel)</p><p><i>n.</i> angular distance above the horizon (especially of a celestial object) [ALT, EL, elevation]</p><p><b>učinci (kao što su krvarenje iz nosa ili mučnina) nedostatka kisika u krvi i tkivima na velikim visinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> effects (as nosebleed or nausea) of oxygen deficiency in the blood and tissues at high altitudes</p><p><b>u vezi s visinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to altitude</p><p><b>Neograničeno visoko (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> indefinitely high</p><p><b>alt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a singer whose voice lies in the alto clef</p><p><i>n.</i> the lowest female singing voice [contralto]</p><p><i>n.</i> the highest adult male singing voice [countertenor]</p><p><i>n.</i> (of a musical instrument) the second highest instrument in a family of musical instruments</p><p><i>n.</i> the pitch range of the lowest female voice</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or being the lowest female voice [contralto]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or being the highest male voice [countertenor]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a musical instrument) second highest m