ing to the United States of America or its people or language or culture</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of the continents and islands of the Americas</p><p><b>široko uzgajana američka biljka s zelenkasto-bijelom cvjetom na visokom stabljku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated American monocarpic plant with greenish-white flowers on a tall stalk [Agave americana]</p><p><b>veliki aligator jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large alligator of the southeastern United States [Alligator mississipiensis]</p><p><b>tropske američke biljke s bazalnim rozetama vlaknastih lišća u obliku mača i cvijeća u visokim šiljcima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American plants with basal rosettes of fibrous sword-shaped leaves and flowers in tall spikes [agave, century plant]</p><p><b>malo listno drvo ili grm iz istočne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small deciduous clump-forming tree or shrub of eastern United States [Aralia spinosa, Hercules'-club, devil's walking stick]</p><p><b>Antilopski preždrljivac s malom granatiranom rogom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fleet antelope-like ruminant of western North American plains with small branched horns [Antilocapra americana, prongbuck, pronghorn, pronghorn antelope]</p><p><b>mala zimzelena biljka sa istočne Sjeverne Amerike koja ima sitna lišća na ravnim granama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small evergreen of eastern North America having tiny scalelike leaves on flattened branchlets [Thuja occidentalis, northern white cedar, white cedar]</p><p><b>biljka s bijelim cvjetovima iz zapadnoindijske regije čiji korijen daje škrob od korijena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white-flowered West Indian plant whose root yields arrowroot starch [Maranta arundinaceae, arrowroot, obedience plant]</p><p><b>Škrlatni špin iz Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender aspen native to North America [American quaking aspen, Populus tremuloides]</p><p><b>vrsta jazvice porijeklom iz Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><