no, neki, nekog, neodređeni član</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an associate degree in nursing [Associate in Nursing]</p><p><b>Nefud</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a desert in northern Saudi Arabia that is noted for its red sand and violent winds [An Nefud, Nafud, Nefud]</p><p><b>Nefud</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a desert in northern Saudi Arabia that is noted for its red sand and violent winds [An Nafud, Nafud, Nefud]</p><p><b>crtice, uspomene, zbirka anegdota o nekom čovjeku, zbirka izreka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mother of the ancient Irish gods</p><p><i>n.</i> a collection of anecdotes about a person or place</p><p><b>Ribe s trunskim perajima iz Afrike i južne Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small freshwater spiny-finned fishes of Africa and southern Asia [family Anabantidae]</p><p><b>protestantski pokret iz 16. stoljeća koji je vjerovao u prvenstvo Biblije, krstio samo vjernike, ne bebe i vjerovao u potpunu odvajanje crkve i države (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Protestant movement in the 16th century that believed in the primacy of the Bible, baptised only believers, not infants, and believed in complete separation of church and state</p><p><b>pristalica anabaptizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> adherent of Anabaptism</p><p><b>protestantska sekta koja ne želi krštenje djece i krsti samo vjernike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Protestant sect denying infant baptism and baptising only believers</p><p><b>tip rod porodice Anabantidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the type genus of the family Anabantidae [genus Anabas]</p><p><b>mala čvorka iz Indije čije su žlijezde modifikovane kako bi joj omogućile disanje zraka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small perch of India whose gills are modified to allow it to breathe air [A. testudineus, climbing perch]</p><p><b>od struje zraka ili vjetra (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of an air current or wind</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u razdoblju suše ne može osigurati da se životinje ne bi više razvijale, potrebno je utvrditi razinu u kojoj se životinje mogu ponovno razvijati. (MT)</b></p><p><i>