d at a time when it could not have existed or occurred [misdating, mistiming]</p><p><i>n.</i> an artifact that belongs to another time</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who seems to be displaced in time</p><p><b>anakronističan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> chronologically misplaced [anachronic, anachronous]</p><p><b>na anakronistički način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an anachronistic manner</p><p><b>anakronističan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> chronologically misplaced [anachronic, anachronistic]</p><p><b>analgetik za blagi bol, ali ne i za upalu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an analgesic for mild pain but not for inflammation [Datril, Panadol, Phenaphen, Tempra, Tylenol, acetaminophen]</p><p><b>dolina i rijeka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of valleys and rivers</p><p><b>(psihoanaliza) odnos obilježen snažnom ovisnošću o drugima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychoanalysis) relationship marked by strong dependence on others</p><p><b>Odnosi koji su karakterizirani snažnom ovisnošću jedne osobe o drugoj ili su povezani s njima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or related to relationships that are characterized by the strong dependence of one person on another</p><p><b>anaklitička depresija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> severe and progressive depression in infants who lose their mother and do not get a suitable substitute</p><p><b>nagla promjena unutar rečenice iz jedne sintaktičke strukture u drugu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abrupt change within a sentence from one syntactic structure to another [anacoluthon]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s sintaksnim nedosljednostima vrste poznate kao anacoluthons (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or related to syntactic inconsistencies of the sort known as anacoluthons</p><p><b>nagla promjena unutar rečenice iz jedne sintaktičke strukture u drugu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abrupt change within a sentence from one syntactic structure to another [anacoluthia]</p><p><b>anakonda, Eunectes murinus, velika anakonda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large arboreal boa of tropical South America [Eunectes