ension [bodybuilding, muscle building, musclebuilding]</p><p><b>anaeroban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> living or active in the absence of free oxygen [anaerobic]</p><p><b>anestezija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> loss of bodily sensation with or without loss of consciousness [anesthesia]</p><p><b>anestezija, anestetik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that causes temporary loss of bodily sensations [anaesthetic agent, anesthetic, anesthetic agent]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or producing insensibility [anesthetic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by insensibility [anesthetic]</p><p><b>anestetik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that causes temporary loss of bodily sensations [anaesthetic, anesthetic, anesthetic agent]</p><p><b>anestezirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> administer an anesthetic drug to [anaesthetize, anesthetise, anesthetize, put out, put under]</p><p><b>anestetičar, anesteziolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist who administers an anesthetic to a patient before he is treated [anesthesiologist, anesthetist]</p><p><b>anestezirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> administer an anesthetic drug to [anaesthetise, anesthetise, anesthetize, put out, put under]</p><p><b>uglavnom biljke iz Starog svijeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chiefly Old World herbs [genus Anagallis]</p><p><b>biljka s crvenom ili bijelom ili ljubičastim cvjetovima koji se zatvaraju prilikom približavanja kišnog vremena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herb with scarlet or white or purple blossoms that close at approach of rainy weather [poor man's weatherglass, red pimpernel, scarlet pimpernel]</p><p><b>mala plazava europska biljka sa osjetljivim ružičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small creeping European herb having delicate pink flowers [bog pimpernel]</p><p><b>motovi čije su ličinke brašna motovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> moth whose larvae are flour moths [genus Anagasta]</p><p><b>mali moljak čije ličinke oštećuju pohranjeno zrno i brašno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small moth whose larvae damage stored grain and flour [Mediterranean flour mot