 [androgenetic]</p><p><b>u slučaju da se u embrionu ne nalaze samo očinski hromozomi, u slučaju da se u embrionu ne nalaze samo očinski hromozomi, u slučaju da se u embrionu ne nalaze samo očinski hromozomi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> male parthenogenesis in which the embryo contains only paternal chromosomes due to the failure of the egg nucleus to participate in fertilization [androgenesis]</p><p><b>Ženski glas s muškim kvalitetima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman's voice with male qualities</p><p><b>koji imaju i muške i ženske spolne osobine i organe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one having both male and female sexual characteristics and organs [epicene, epicene person, gynandromorph, hermaphrodite, intersex]</p><p><b>androgin, dvospolac</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or exhibiting both female and male sex organs but with a predominantly female appearance</p><p><i>adj.</i> having both male and female characteristics</p><p><b>androginija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> showing characteristics of both sexes [bisexuality, hermaphroditism]</p><p><b>android, humanoid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an automaton that resembles a human being [humanoid, mechanical man]</p><p><b>Andromeda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> broad-leaved evergreen Asiatic shrub with glossy leaves and drooping clusters of white flowers [Japanese andromeda, Pieris japonica, lily-of-the-valley tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several shrubs of the genus Andromeda having leathery leaves and clusters of small flowers</p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) an Ethiopian princess and daughter of Cassiopeia</p><p><i>n.</i> a constellation in the northern hemisphere between Cassiopeia and Pegasus</p><p><b>spiralna galaksija u sazvežđu Andromeda koja je vidljiva golim okom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spiral galaxy in the constellation of Andromeda that is visible to the naked eye</p><p><b>Zeleni grm s visokom vrstom bijelog ili ružičastog cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wiry evergreen shrub having pendent clusters of white or pink flowers [bog rosemar