<p><b>pigment koji se nalazi u životinjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pigment occurring in animals</p><p><b>proizvod životinjskoga podrijetla, životinjski produkt, životinjski proizvod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a product made from animal material</p><p><b>psihologija životinja, zoopsihologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of psychology concerned with the behavior of animals [comparative psychology]</p><p><b>zoolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in the branch of biology dealing with animals [zoologist]</p><p><b>životinjska koža, koža</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the outer covering of an animal</p><p><b>S druge strane, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one form in which body fuel is stored [glycogen]</p><p><b>zanatlija koji se ispeče i montira kože životinja za prikaz (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a craftsman who stuffs and mounts the skins of animals for display [stuffer, taxidermist]</p><p><b>životinjsko tkivo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tissue in the bodies of animals</p><p><b>Toxin sličan bakterijskim toksinima po svojim antigenim svojstvima koji se nalazi u tekućinama određenih životinja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxin resembling bacterial toxins in its antigenic properties that is found in the fluids of certain animals [zootoxin]</p><p><b>osoba koja trenira ili izlaga životinje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who trains or exhibits animals [handler]</p><p><b>životinjski patogen koji je virus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an animal pathogen that is a virus</p><p><b>obožavanje životinja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the worship of animals [zoolatry]</p><p><b>mikroorganizam kao što su ameba ili paramecium (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> microscopic organism such as an amoeba or paramecium [animalculum]</p><p><b>mikroorganizam kao što su ameba ili paramecium (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> microscopic organism such as an amoeba or paramecium [animalcule]</p><p><b>carstvo Animalia, carstvo životinja, životinje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> taxonomic kingdom comprising all living or extinct animals [animal kingdom, kingdom Animalia]</p><p><b>čin koji čini ljude okrutnim ili kojima nedostaju normalne ljudske osobine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an act that makes people cruel or lacking normal human qualities [animalization, brutalisation, brutalization]</p><p><b>predstavljaju u obliku životinje, učiniti brutalan, bezosjećajni ili nehuman, postati brutalan ili neosjetljiv i bezosjećajan (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> represent in the form of an animal [animalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make brutal, unfeeling, or inhuman [animalize, brutalise, brutalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> become brutal or insensitive and unfeeling [animalize, brutalise, brutalize]</p><p><b>Nauka da su ljudska bića čisto životinjska prirode i da nemaju duhovnu prirodu., zaokupljenost zadovoljavanjem fizičkih želja i apetita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine that human beings are purely animal in nature and lacking a spiritual nature</p><p><i>n.</i> preoccupation with satisfaction of physical drives and appetites [physicality]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s životinjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to animalism</p><p><b>animalnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the physical (or animal) side of a person as opposed to the spirit or intellect [animal nature]</p><p><b>Slika u obliku životinje, čin koji čini ljude okrutnim ili kojima nedostaju normalne ljudske osobine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a depiction in the form of an animal</p><p><i>n.</i> an act that makes people cruel or lacking normal human qualities [animalisation, brutalisation, brutalization]</p><p><b>predstavljaju u obliku životinje, učiniti brutalan, bezosjećajni ili nehuman, postati brutalan ili neosjetljiv i bezosjećajan (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> represent in the form of an animal [animalise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make brutal, unfeeling, or inhuman [animalise, brutalise, brutalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> become brutal or insensitive and unfeeling [animalise, brutalise, brutalize]</p><p><b>animirati, nadahnut, nadahnuti, obodriti, oduševiti, ohrabriti, oživiti, pokrenuti, vedar, živ, živahan, bodriti, inspirirati, nadahnjivati, pobuditi, pobuđivati, potaknuti, poticati, stimulirati, krijepiti, obodrivati, okrepljivati, okrijepiti, oživjeti, oživljavati, razveseliti, razveseljavati, oživotvoriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> heighten or intensify [enliven, exalt, inspire, invigorate]</p><p><i>v.</i> give lifelike qualities to [animise, animize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make lively [enliven, invigorate, liven, liven up]</p><p><i>v.</i> give new life or energy to [quicken, reanimate, recreate, renovate, repair, revive, revivify, vivify]</p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to the class of nouns that denote living beings</p><p><i>adj.</i> endowed with animal life as distinguished from plant life</p><p><i>adj.</i> endowed with feeling and unstructured consciousness [sentient]</p><p><b>životinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a living organism characterized by voluntary movement [animal, beast, brute, creature, fauna]</p><p><b>živa stvar, živo biće, živuća stvar, živuće biće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a living (or once living) entity [living thing]</p><p><b>animiran, animirani, animirani film, crtani film, oživljeni, živahan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having life or vigor or spirit [alive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> made to appear to move as living creatures do</p><p><b>crtani film</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a film made by photographing a series of cartoon drawings to give the illusion of movement when projected in rapid sequence [cartoon, toon]</p><p><b>Sredozemski ovs za koji se smatra da je izvor modernog uzgojnog ovsa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mediterranean oat held to be progenitor of modern cultivated oat [Avene sterilis, wild red oat]</p><p><b>animiran, animirani, animirani film, crtani film, oživljeni, živahan (od &quot;animated&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an animated manner</p><p><b>animirati, nadahnut, nadahnuti, obodriti, oduševiti, ohrabriti, oživiti, pokrenuti, vedar, živ, živahan (od &quot;animate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being animated [aliveness, liveness]</p><p><b>animirati, nadahnut, nadahnuti, obodriti, oduševiti, ohrabriti, oživiti, pokrenuti, vedar, živ, živahan (od &quot;animate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> giving spirit and vivacity [enlivening]</p><p><b>animacija, oživljavanje, oživljavanje slika, svježina, veselost, živahnost, življenje, život, vitalitet, vitalnost, životna snaga, životnost, aktivnost, animiranost, elan, energičnost, oživljenje, polet, razigranost, živost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of living or the state of being alive [aliveness, life, living]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being able to survive and grow [vitality]</p><p><i>n.</i> quality of being active or spirited or alive and vigorous [brio, invigoration, spiritedness, vivification]</p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of giving vitality and vigour to something [invigoration, vivification]</p><p><i>n.</i> the making of animated cartoons</p><p><i>n.</i> general activity and motion [liveliness]</p><p><b>pripisivanje svijesti i osobnosti prirodnim pojavama kao što su oluje i potresi te predmetima kao što su biljke i kamenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the attribution of consciousness and personality to natural phenomena such as thunderstorms and earthquakes and to objects such as plants and stones</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s animatizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to animatism</p><p><b>animator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who imparts energy and vitality and spirit to other people [energiser, energizer, vitaliser, vitalizer]</p><p><i>n.</i> the technician who produces animated cartoons</p><p><b>Izgradnja robota koji izgledaju kao životinje (razvijen za Disneyland) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the construction of robots to look like animals (developed for Disneyland)</p><p><b>tvrdi kopal dobiven od afričkog stabla, s masenim udjelom polipropilena veći od 0,5% i, stil animacije razvijen u Japanu, karakteriziran stiliziranom obojenom umjetnošću i često temama za odrasle (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hard copal derived from an African tree [Zanzibar copal]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various resins or oleoresins [gum anime]</p><p><i>n.</i> a style of animation developed in Japan, characterized by stylized colorful art and often adult themes</p><p><b>animirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give lifelike qualities to [animate, animize]</p><p><b>animizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine that all natural objects and the universe itself have souls</p><p><b>onaj koji prihvaća doktrinu animizma, o ili koji se odnose na nauk o animizmu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who accepts the doctrine of animism</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to the doctrine of animism [animistic]</p><p><b>o ili koji se odnose na nauk o animizmu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to the doctrine of animism [animist]</p><p><b>animirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give lifelike qualities to [animate, animise]</p><p><b>mržnja, neprijateljstvo, zloba, animozitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of ill will arousing active hostility [animus, bad blood]</p><p><b>muška duša, preduvjerenje, zlonamjernost, animozitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of ill will arousing active hostility [animosity, bad blood]</p><p><b>anion</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a negatively charged ion</p><p><b>anion (od &quot;anion&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a class of synthetic detergents in which the molecules do not ionize in aqueous solutions [anionic detergent, non-ionic detergent]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to anions</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% masenog dianaxa, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound characterized by an active anion</p><p><b>razred sintetičkih deterdženta čiji se molekuli ne ionizuju u vodenim rastvorima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a class of synthetic detergents in which the molecules do not ionize in aqueous solutions [anionic, non-ionic detergent]</p><p><b>anis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> native to Egypt but cultivated widely for its aromatic seeds and the oil from them used medicinally and as a flavoring in cookery [Pimpinella anisum, anise plant]</p><p><i>n.</i> liquorice-flavored seeds, used medicinally and in cooking and liquors [anise seed, aniseed]</p><p><b>Piškot napravljen bez maslaca i aromatiziran s aniznim sjemenom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cookie made without butter and flavored with anise seed</p><p><b>Čvrsta biljka iz Sjeverne Amerike s mirisom od fenikala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> much-branched North American herb with an odor like fennel [Agastache foeniculum]</p><p><b>anis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> native to Egypt but cultivated widely for its aromatic seeds and the oil from them used medicinally and as a flavoring in cookery [Pimpinella anisum, anise]</p><p><b>Sjemenke s okusom slatkiše, koje se koriste u medicini i kuhanju i pića (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> liquorice-flavored seeds, used medicinally and in cooking and liquors [anise, aniseed]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko zimzelenih grmova i malih stabala roda Illicium (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several evergreen shrubs and small trees of the genus Illicium</p><p><b>miris anisa (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> smelling of anise</p><p><b>anis (od &quot;anise&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> liquorice-flavored seeds, used medicinally and in cooking and liquors [anise, anise seed]</p><p><b>vidni defekt u kojem se oblik i veličina očnog slika razlikuju u oba oka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> visual defect in which the shape and size of an ocular image differ in the two eyes</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na ili je karakterističan za vizualni defekt aniseikoniju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of the visual defect aniseikonia</p><p><b>anisovac, aniseta, anisovača</b></p><p><i>n.</i> liquorice-flavored usually colorless sweet liqueur made from aniseed [anisette de Bordeaux]</p><p><b>aniseta, anisovac, anisovača</b></p><p><i>n.</i> liquorice-flavored usually colorless sweet liqueur made from aniseed [anisette]</p><p><b>bilo od par različitih gameta posebno onih različitih u veličini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of a pair of unlike gametes especially those unlike in size</p><p><b>koji se odnose na bilo koji od parova različitih (anizogamskih) gameta koji se spajaju u spolnom razmnožavanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to either of a pair of dissimilar (anisogamic) gametes combining in sexual reproduction</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na vrstu spolnog razmnožavanja u kojem su gamete u određenom pogledu različite (u veličini ili obliku) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a type of sexual reproduction in which the gametes are dissimilar in some respect (as size or shape) [anisogamous]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na vrstu spolnog razmnožavanja u kojem su gamete u određenom pogledu različite (u veličini ili obliku) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a type of sexual reproduction in which the gametes are dissimilar in some respect (as size or shape) [anisogamic]</p><p><b>(biologija) razmnožavanje spajanjem dva različita gameta (posebno različite veličine) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) reproduction by the union or fusion of two differing gametes (especially differing in size)</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having unsymmetrical parts or unequal dimensions or measurements [unsymmetrical]</p><p><b>anizometropija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> difference in the refractive power of the two eyes</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na razliku u refrakcijskoj snazi dva oka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a difference in the refractive power of the two eyes</p><p><b>uši (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dragonflies [suborder Anisoptera]</p><p><b>rod Haemulidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Haemulidae [genus Anisotremus]</p><p><b>tamno siva hrana riba pronađena iz Louisiane i Floride prema jugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dusky grey food fish found from Louisiana and Florida southward [black margate, pompon]</p><p><b>crni i zlatni grunt pronađen od Bermuda do Kariba do Brazila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> black and gold grunt found from Bermuda to Caribbean to Brazil [pork-fish, porkfish]</p><p><b>anizotropan, neizotropan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not invariant with respect to direction</p><p><b>u anisotropnom obliku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an anisotropic manner</p><p><b>anizotropija, anizotropija stijena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being anisotropic</p><p><b>bivša provincija u zapadnoj Francuskoj u dolini Loare, kruška sa čvrstim mesom i zelenom kožom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former province of western France in the Loire valley</p><p><i>n.</i> a pear with firm flesh and a green skin</p><p><b>Glavni grad Turske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital of Turkey [Angora, Turkish capital, capital of Turkey]</p><p><b>članak, članak na nozi, gležanj, zglob, articulatio talocruralis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gliding joint between the distal ends of the tibia and fibula and the proximal end of the talus [ankle joint, articulatio talocruralis, mortise joint]</p><p><b>čep koji se nosi za jačanje gležnja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brace worn to strengthen the ankle</p><p><b>ukras koji se nosi oko gležnja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ornament worn around the ankle [anklet]</p><p><b>articulatio talocruralis, gležanj, članak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gliding joint between the distal ends of the tibia and fibula and the proximal end of the talus [ankle, articulatio talocruralis, mortise joint]</p><p><b>dolazi samo do gležnja ili koljena (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> coming only to the ankle or knee [knee-deep]</p><p><b>kost u gležnju koja se artikulira s kostom noge kako bi formirala zglob gležnja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bone in the ankle that articulates with the leg bones to form the ankle jo