n termites [Orycteropus afer, aardvark, anteater]</p><p><b>bilo koje od različitih tamnih ptica Južne Amerike koje se hrane mravima neke slijede vojske mravlje roje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various dull-colored South American birds that feeding on ants some following army ant swarms [antbird]</p><p><b>izlučuje tvar nalik medu koju jedu mravi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> excretes a honeylike substance eaten by ants</p><p><b>mravolovac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the larva of any of several insects [antlion, doodlebug]</p><p><i>n.</i> winged insect resembling a dragonfly [antlion, antlion fly]</p><p><b>Čunjevi koji su površinski slični čunjevima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antbirds superficially resembling shrikes</p><p><b>vrsta mravlja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of antbird</p><p><b>lijek (trgovinski naziv Antabuse) koji se koristi za liječenje alkoholizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug (trade name Antabuse) used in the treatment of alcoholism [disulfiram]</p><p><b>antacid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agent that counteracts or neutralizes acidity (especially in the stomach) [alkaliser, alkalizer, antiacid, gastric antacid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> acting to neutralize acid (especially in the stomach)</p><p><b>djelovati protiv, izazvati neprijateljstvo od (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> act in opposition to [antagonize, counteract]</p><p><i>v.</i> provoke the hostility of [antagonize]</p><p><b>antagonizam, neprijateljstvo, otpor, protivljenje, mržnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of deep-seated ill-will [enmity, hostility]</p><p><i>n.</i> the relation between opposing principles or forces or factors</p><p><i>n.</i> an actively expressed feeling of dislike and hostility</p><p><i>n.</i> (biochemistry) interference in or inhibition of the physiological action of a chemical substance by another having a similar structure</p><p><b>antagonist, antagonista, antagonističan, antagonistični, neprijatelj, protivnik, suparnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who offers opposition [adversary, opponent, opposer, resister]</p><p><i>n.</i> a muscle that relaxes while another contracts</p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that neutralizes or counteracts the effects of another drug</p><p><b>antagonistički, antagonizam, neprijateljski, odbojni, protivan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> indicating opposition or resistance [counter]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by antagonism or antipathy [antipathetic, antipathetical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> arousing animosity or hostility</p><p><i>adj.</i> used especially of drugs or muscles that counteract or neutralize each other's effect [incompatible]</p><p><i>adj.</i> incapable of harmonious association</p><p><b>(fiziologija) mišić koji se suprotstavlja djelovanju drugog mišića. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physiology) a muscle that opposes the action of another</p><p><b>na antagonistički način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an antagonistic manner</p><p><b>biti neprijateljski raspoložen, biti protiv, izazivati neprijateljstvo, opirati se, protiviti se, stvarati otpor, suprotstavljati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> provoke the hostility of [antagonise]</p><p><i>v.</i> act in opposition to [antagonise, counteract]</p><p><b>Grad u južnoj Turskoj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in southern Turkey [Antakya, Antioch]</p><p><b>Grad u južnoj Turskoj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in southern Turkey [Antakiya, Antioch]</p><p><b>Antalya</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port city in southwestern Turkey on the Gulf of Antalya [Adalia]</p><p><b>Antananarivo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Madagascar [capital of Madagascar]</p><p><b>tačka suprotna u smjeru od sunčevog vrha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the point opposite in direction from the solar apex</p><p><b>antartički, Antartik, južni pol, antarktik, antarktički</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the region around the south pole: Antarctica and surrounding waters [Antarctic Zone, South Frigid Zone]</p><p><i>adj.</i> at or near the south pole [south-polar]</p><p><b>linija geografske širine sjeverno od južnog pola (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a line