ng disease caused by inhaling coal dust [black lung, black lung disease, coal miner's lung]</p><p><b>antraks, crni prišt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a highly infectious animal disease (especially cattle and sheep) [splenic fever]</p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of humans that is not communicable</p><p><b>vrsta bacilusa koja uzrokuje antraks kod ljudi i životinja (goveđe i svinje i ovce i zečevi i miševi i morske svinje) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a species of bacillus that causes anthrax in humans and in animals (cattle and swine and sheep and rabbits and mice and guinea pigs) [Bacillus anthracis]</p><p><b>oblik infekcije antraksom dobivene udisanjem prašine koja sadrži Bacillus anthracis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of anthrax infection acquired by inhalation of dust containing Bacillus anthracis [inhalation anthrax, pulmonary anthrax, ragpicker's disease, ragsorter's disease, woolsorter's disease, woolsorter's pneumonia]</p><p><b>mali crno-crveno-bijeli tepih bube (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small black and red and white carpet beetle [buffalo carpet beetle]</p><p><b>Červil: iz Europe, Sjeverne Afrike i Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chervil: of Europe, North Africa and Asia [genus Anthriscus]</p><p><b>krasuljica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic annual Old World herb cultivated for its finely divided and often curly leaves for use especially in soups and salads [beaked parsley, chervil]</p><p><b>gruba uspravna dvostruko biljka iz Starog svijeta koja je uvedena kao korov u istočnoj Sjevernoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coarse erect biennial Old World herb introduced as a weed in eastern North America [cow parsley, wild chervil]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na čovječanstvo ili razdoblje postojanja čovječanstva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to mankind or the period of mankind's existence [anthropical]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na čovječanstvo ili razdoblje postojanja čovječanstva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to mankind or the period of mankind's existence [anthropic]</p><p><b>antropocentrični</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> human-centered</p><p><b>sklonost procjenjivati stvarnost isključivo u smislu ljudskih vrijednosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inclination to evaluate reality exclusively in terms of human values [anthropocentrism]</p><p><b>sklonost procjenjivati stvarnost isključivo u smislu ljudskih vrijednosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inclination to evaluate reality exclusively in terms of human values [anthropocentricity]</p><p><b>evoluciju ili genezu ljudske rase. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the evolution or genesis of the human race [anthropogeny]</p><p><b>o proučavanju porijekla i razvoja ljudskih bića ili o njemu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the study of the origins and development of human beings [anthropogenic]</p><p><b>antropogeni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the study of the origins and development of human beings [anthropogenetic]</p><p><b>evoluciju ili genezu ljudske rase. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the evolution or genesis of the human race [anthropogenesis]</p><p><b>antropoid, antropoidni, majmunoliki, antropoidan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> person who resembles a nonhuman primate [ape]</p><p><i>n.</i> any member of the suborder Anthropoidea including monkeys and apes and hominids</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling apes [anthropoidal, apelike]</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling human beings [manlike]</p><p><b>čovjekoliki majmun</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any tailless ape of the families Pongidae and Hylobatidae</p><p><b>koji liče na majmune. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling apes [anthropoid, apelike]</p><p><b>majmuni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monkeys [suborder Anthropoidea]</p><p><b>Obožavanje ljudskih bića. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the worship of human beings [worship of man]</p><p><b>antropološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or concerned with the science of anthropology</p><p><b>antropolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a social scientist who specializes in anthropology</p><p><b>antropologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the social science that