><i>n.</i> (Christianity) the adversary of Christ (or Christianity) mentioned in the New Testament</p><p><b>Onaj koji predviđa, Oznaka željanog očekivanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who anticipates [anticipator]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by eager anticipation [anticipative, expectant]</p><p><b>anticipirati, očekivati, opomenuti, predosjetiti, preduhitriti, predusresti, predvidjeti, predviđati, prethoditi, pripremiti se na, unaprijed uzeti u obzir, upozoriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> regard something as probable or likely [expect]</p><p><i>v.</i> act in advance of [counter, foresee, forestall]</p><p><i>v.</i> realize beforehand [foreknow, foresee, previse]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a prediction about [call, forebode, foretell, predict, prognosticate, promise]</p><p><i>v.</i> be excited or anxious about [look for, look to]</p><p><i>v.</i> be a forerunner of or occur earlier than</p><p><b>anticipativan, predvidljiv, predviđen, unaprijed očekivan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> expected hopefully [awaited, hoped-for]</p><p><b>anticipacija, iščekivanje, predosjećanje, predviđanje, pretjecanje, upozorenje, isčekivanje, očekivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expectation [expectancy]</p><p><i>n.</i> something expected (as on the basis of a norm) [expectancy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of predicting (as by reasoning about the future) [prediction, prevision]</p><p><i>n.</i> anticipating with confidence of fulfillment [expectation]</p><p><b>anticipativan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by eager anticipation [anticipant, expectant]</p><p><b>anticipator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who anticipates [anticipant]</p><p><b>anticipativan, preduhitriv, prethodni, preuranjen, upozoravajući</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in anticipation [prevenient]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je ugovorno povlačenje učinjeno prije izvršenja zahtjeva za izvršavanje, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a breach of contract committed prior to the time of required performance [constructive breach]</p><p><b>Od ili u vezi s naglom promjenom od impresivnog do smiješnog s