j i violinista (1675-1741) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian baroque composer and violinist (1675-1741) [Antonio Vivaldi, Vivaldi]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1691. do 1700. koji je ukinuo nepotizam unutar crkvene hijerarhije i bio je svetski voljen zbog svoje dobročinstva i pobožnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1691 to 1700 who abolished nepotism within the church hierarchy and was universally loved for his charity and piety [Innocent XII]</p><p><b>Talijanski proizvođač violina koji je razvio modernu violinu i stvorio violine bez premca u kvaliteti tona (1644?-1737) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian violin maker who developed the modern violin and created violins of unequaled tonal quality (1644?-1737) [Antonius Stradivarius, Stradivari, Stradivarius]</p><p><b>Talijanski barokni skladatelj i violinista (1675-1741) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian baroque composer and violinist (1675-1741) [Antonio Lucio Vivaldi, Vivaldi]</p><p><b>Rimski general pod Julijem Cezarom u galskim ratovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Roman general under Julius Caesar in the Gallic wars [Anthony, Antony, Marcus Antonius, Mark Anthony, Mark Antony]</p><p><b>Rimski car (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Emperor of Rome</p><p><b>Talijanski proizvođač violina koji je razvio modernu violinu i stvorio violine bez premca u kvaliteti tona (1644?-1737) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian violin maker who developed the modern violin and created violins of unequaled tonal quality (1644?-1737) [Antonio Stradivari, Stradivari, Stradivarius]</p><p><b>Rimski general pod Julijem Cezarom u galskim ratovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Roman general under Julius Caesar in the Gallic wars [Anthony, Antonius, Marcus Antonius, Mark Anthony, Mark Antony]</p><p><b>Američki plesač i koreograf (rođen u Engleskoj) (1909-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States dancer and choreographer (born in England) (1909-1987) [Tudor]</p><p><b>antonim, nasuprotnica, odveznica, protuznačnica, suprotnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a word