tively permanent state of worry and nervousness occurring in a variety of mental disorders, usually accompanied by compulsive behavior or attacks of panic [anxiousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a vague unpleasant emotion that is experienced in anticipation of some (usually ill-defined) misfortune</p><p><b>iznenadna akutna epizoda intenzivne anksioznosti i osjećaja panike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden acute episode of intense anxiety and feelings of panic</p><p><b>naziv za različite mentalne poremećaje u kojima je ozbiljna anksioznost glavni simptom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cover term for a variety of mental disorders in which severe anxiety is a salient symptom</p><p><b>oblik histerije koji ima obilježja i poremećaja konverzije i anksiozne neuroze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of hysteria having features of both conversion disorder and anxiety neurosis</p><p><b>karakterizira se difuznom anksioznošću i često somatskim manifestacijama straha. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> characterized by diffuse anxiety and often somatic manifestations of fear</p><p><b>anksioznost koja se odlikuje hroničnom anksioznošću i simptomima kao što su napetost, znojenje, drhtanje, vrtoglavica ili razdražljivost itd. koja traje više od šest mjeseci. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anxiety disorder characterized by chronic free-floating anxiety and such symptoms as tension or sweating or trembling or lightheadedness or irritability etc that has lasted for more than six months [GAD, generalized anxiety disorder]</p><p><b>uspavač koji se koristi za ublažavanje anksioznosti i smanjenje napetosti i razdražljivosti., ublažavanje anksioznosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tranquilizer used to relieve anxiety and reduce tension and irritability [antianxiety drug, anxiolytic drug, minor tranquilizer, minor tranquilliser, minor tranquillizer]</p><p><i>adj.</i> anxiety relieving</p><p><b>uspavač koji se koristi za ublažavanje anksioznosti i smanjenje napetosti i razdražljivosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tranquilizer used to relieve anxiety and reduce tension and irritability [antianxiety drug, anxiolytic, minor tranquilizer, minor tranquilliser, minor tranquillizer]</p><p><b>koji žudi, mučan, nemiran, nestrpljivo, uzbuđen, uznemiren, zabrinut, željan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> eagerly desirous [dying]</p><p><i>adj.</i> causing or fraught with or showing anxiety [nervous, queasy, uneasy, unquiet]</p><p><b>uznemireno, zabrinuto</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with anxiety or apprehension [apprehensively, uneasily]</p><p><b>tjeskoba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychiatry) a relatively permanent state of worry and nervousness occurring in a variety of mental disorders, usually accompanied by compulsive behavior or attacks of panic [anxiety]</p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of mild anxiety about possible developments [disquiet]</p><p><b>bilo kakav, bilo kakvu, bilo koje, bilo kojeg, bilo koji, bilo kojoj, bilo što, ikakav, ikakvih, ikoji, ikoliko, išta, itko, jedan, kojekakav, koji bilo, ma, ma koje, ma koji, neki, nekoliko, nešto, nijedno, nikakav, nikoji, svaki, svatko, što, svaka, svako</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> one or some or every or all without specification [whatever, whatsoever]</p><p><i>adv.</i> to any degree or extent</p><p><b>U ovom trenutku ili od sada. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at the present or from now on [anymore]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u pitanju prijava za preuzimanje, primatelj se poziva na zahtjev za preuzimanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a takeover bid where the acquirer offers to buy any and all shares outstanding</p><p><b>bilo kako, nekako, pa ipak, svakako, svakojako, u, u svakom slučaju, unatoč tome, u svakom slučaj, ionako, svejedno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement [anyway, anyways, at any rate, in any case, in any event]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in any way whatsoever [anyway]</p><p><b>ne više</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at the present or from now on [any longer]</p><p><b>na ili u ili na bilo koje mjesto (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> a