buka i šećera, Torta ispunjena rezanim jabukama i šećerom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small open pie filled with sliced apples and sugar</p><p><i>n.</i> a tart filled with sliced apples and sugar</p><p><b>jabuka, stablo jabuke</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any tree of the genus Malus especially those bearing firm rounded edible fruits</p><p><b>Proizvodnja s punjenjem jabuka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> turnover with an apple filling</p><p><b>miris jabuke (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> smelling of apples</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the general shape of an apple</p><p><b>s površinom od oko 10 mm ili više, ali ne više od 10 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the approximate size of an apple</p><p><b>Planiranje koje se prekida kad netko ̋poremetiti karticu s jabukama', ručni kolica s koje se prodaju jabuke i drugo voće na ulici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the planning that is disrupted when someone `upsets the applecart'</p><p><i>n.</i> a handcart from which apples and other fruit are sold in the street</p><p><b>jabukovača</b></p><p><i>n.</i> distilled from hard cider</p><p><b>Menta s stabljikama s mirisom jabuka iz južne i zapadne Europe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mint with apple-scented stems of southern and western Europe [Mentha rotundifolia, Mentha suaveolens, apple mint]</p><p><b>prazne riječi, umak od jabuka, zaslađena kaša od kuhanih jabuka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> puree of stewed apples usually sweetened and spiced [apple sauce]</p><p><i>n.</i> nonsensical talk or writing [codswallop, folderol, rubbish, trash, tripe, trumpery, wish-wash]</p><p><b>Vlažna začinjena torta s sokom od jabuke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> moist spicy cake containing applesauce</p><p><b>aplet, applet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Java application</p><p><b>Edward Appleton</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English physicist remembered for his studies of the ionosphere (1892-1966) [Edward Appleton, Sir Edward Victor Appleton]</p><p><i>n.</i> a town in eastern Wisconsin</p><p><b>Najviši reg