p><p><b>dušična kiselina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acid used especially in the production of fertilizers and explosives and rocket fuels [nitric acid]</p><p><b>zlatotopka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a yellow fuming corrosive mixture of nitric and hydrochloric acid that dissolves metals (including gold) [nitrohydrochloric acid]</p><p><b>od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestica ili od čestice ili od čestice do čestice ili od čestice ili od čestice ili od čestice ili od česti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> strong distilled liquor or brandy [ardent spirits]</p><p><b>uređaj (trgovinski naziv Aqua-Lung) koji omogućuje roniocima disanje pod vodom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device (trade name Aqua-Lung) that lets divers breathe under water [aqualung, scuba]</p><p><b>za ribarstvo ili s njim povezanim (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to aquiculture [aquicultural, hydroponic]</p><p><b>akvakultura</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rearing aquatic animals or cultivating aquatic plants for food</p><p><b>akvalung</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device (trade name Aqua-Lung) that lets divers breathe under water [Aqua-Lung, scuba]</p><p><b>akvamarin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a transparent variety of beryl that is blue green in color</p><p><i>n.</i> a shade of blue tinged with green [aqua, cobalt blue, greenish blue, peacock blue, turquoise]</p><p><b>akvanaut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an underwater swimmer equipped with a face mask and foot fins and either a snorkel or an air cylinder [skin-diver]</p><p><i>n.</i> a skilled worker who can live in underwater installations and participate in scientific research [oceanaut]</p><p><b>morbidni strah od utapanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a morbid fear of drowning</p><p><b>neuobičajeno se boji vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> abnormally afraid of water [hydrophobic]</p><p><b>akvaplan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a board that is pulled by a speedboat as a person stands on it and skims over the top of the water</p><p><i>v.</i> rise up onto a thin film of water between the tires and road so that there is no more contact with the road</p><p><i>v.</i> ride on an aquaplane</p><p><b>akvarij, akvarijum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tank or pool or bowl filled with water for keeping live fish and underwater animals [fish tank, marine museum]</p><p><b>vodenjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (astrology) a person who is born while the sun is in Aquarius [Water Bearer]</p><p><i>n.</i> a zodiacal constellation in the southern hemisphere</p><p><i>n.</i> the eleventh sign of the zodiac [Aquarius the Water Bearer, Water Bearer]</p><p><b>Jedanaesti znak zodijaka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the eleventh sign of the zodiac [Aquarius, Water Bearer]</p><p><b>voden, vodeni, vodena biljka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant that lives in or on water</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or consisting of or being in water</p><p><i>adj.</i> operating or living or growing in water</p><p><b>ptica vodarica, vodena ptica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wading and swimming and diving birds of either fresh or salt water</p><p><b>vodena paprat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ferns that grow in water [water fern]</p><p><b>kitovi i delfini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> whales and dolphins</p><p><b>vodena biljka, hidrofit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant that grows partly or wholly in water whether rooted in the mud, as a lotus, or floating without anchorage, as the water hyacinth [hydrophyte, hydrophytic plant, water plant]</p><p><b>vodeni kralježnjaci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> animal living wholly or chiefly in or on water</p><p><b>vodeni sport</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sports that involve bodies of water [water sport]</p><p><b>akvatinta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an etching made by a process that makes it resemble a water color</p><p><i>n.</i> a method of etching that imitates the broad washes of a water color</p><p><i>v.</i> etch in aquatint</p><p><b>Skandinavski alkohol obično sa okusom s semenom kamena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Scandinavian liquor usually flavored with caraway seeds [akvavit]</p><p><b>akvadukt, akvedukt, kanal, vodovod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conduit that resembles a bridge but carries water over a valley</p><p><b>kanal koji povezuje treću i četvrtu klijetku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a canal connecting the third and fourth ventricles [Sylvian aqueduct, cerebral aqueduct]</p><p><b>nataložen, voden, vodenast, vodnjikav, vodonosni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> similar to or containing or dissolved in water</p><p><i>adj.</i> produced by the action of water [sedimentary]</p><p><b>očna vodica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the limpid fluid within the eyeball between the cornea and the lens [aqueous humour]</p><p><b>čista tekućina unutar očnog jabuča između rožnice i sočiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the limpid fluid within the eyeball between the cornea and the lens [aqueous humor]</p><p><b>rastvor u vodi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solution in water</p><p><b>za ribarstvo ili s njim povezanim (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to aquiculture [aquacultural, hydroponic]</p><p><b>metoda uzgoja biljaka (bez tla) u vodi koja sadrži rastvorene hranljive tvari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a technique of growing plants (without soil) in water containing dissolved nutrients [hydroponics, tank farming]</p><p><b>vodonosnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> underground bed or layer yielding ground water for wells and springs etc</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s vodonosnim slojem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an aquifer</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjeni grmovi i stabla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed shrubs and trees [family Aquifoliaceae, holly family]</p><p><b>sazvežđe u Mliječnom putu u blizini Labudova., Glavni grad provincije Abruzzi u središnjoj Italiji, rod Accipitridae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a constellation in the Milky Way near Cygnus</p><p><i>n.</i> the provincial capital of the Abruzzi region in central Italy [Aquila degli Abruzzi, L'Aquila]</p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Accipitridae [genus Aquila]</p><p><b>veliki orao planinskih područja sjeverne hemisfere s zlatno smeđom glavom i vratom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large eagle of mountainous regions of the northern hemisphere having a golden-brown head and neck [golden eagle]</p><p><b>Glavni grad provincije Abruzzi u središnjoj Italiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the provincial capital of the Abruzzi region in central Italy [Aquila, L'Aquila]</p><p><b>brunasti orao iz Afrike i dijelova Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brownish eagle of Africa and parts of Asia [tawny eagle]</p><p><b>biljka iz roda Aquilegia s nepravilnim, navidnim, podignutim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant of the genus Aquilegia having irregular showy spurred flowers [aquilegia, columbine]</p><p><b>biljka iz roda Aquilegia s nepravilnim, navidnim, podignutim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant of the genus Aquilegia having irregular showy spurred flowers [aquilege, columbine]</p><p><b>kolumbina od Stjenovitih planina s dugim plavim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> columbine of the Rocky Mountains having long-spurred blue flowers [Aquilegia scopulorum calcarea, blue columbine]</p><p><b>kolumbina iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s dugim crvenim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> columbine of eastern North America having long-spurred red flowers [honeysuckle, meeting house]</p><p><b>kolumbina od Stjenovitih planina s dugim plavim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> columbine of the Rocky Mountains having long-spurred blue flowers [Aquilegia caerulea, blue columbine]</p><p><b>u obliku od šarene ili crvene boje, s masnim udelom od 30 mm do 40 mm, ali ne većim od 50 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common European columbine having variously colored (white or blue to purple or red) short-spurred flowers [granny's bonnets]</p><p><b>orlovski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> curved down like an eagle's beak [hooked]</p><p><b>(Rimska katolička crkva) Talijanski teolog i doktor crkve koji se sjeća za svoj pokušaj pomirenja vjere i razuma u sveobuhvatnoj teologiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) Italian theologian and Doctor of the Church who is remembered for his attempt to reconcile faith and reason in a comprehensive theology [Saint Thomas, Saint Thomas Aquinas, St. Thomas, St. Thomas Aquinas, Thomas Aquinas]</p><p><b>Akvitanija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a region of southwestern France between Bordeaux and the Pyrenees [Aquitania]</p><p><b>regija jugozapadne Francuske između Bordea i Pirineja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a region of southwestern France between Bordeaux and the Pyrenees [Aquitaine]</p><p><b>Oklahoma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless and odorless inert gas [argon, atomic number 18]</p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of surface area equal to 100 square meters [are]</p><p><i>n.</i> a state in south central United States [Ark., Arkansas, Land of Opportunity]</p><p><b>Dahna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a desert in southern Saudi Arabia [Dahna, Great Sandy Desert, Rub al-Khali]</p><p><b>sazvežđe na južnoj hemisferi u blizini Telescopiuma i Norme., čokoladice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a constellation in the southern hemisphere near Telescopium and Norma</p><p><i>n.</i> macaws [genus Ara]</p><p><b>Arapin, Arapkinja, arapski, arapski konj, Arap, arabljanin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a Semitic people originally from the Arabian peninsula and surrounding territories who speaks Arabic and who inhabits much of the Middle East and northern Africa [Arabian]</p><p><i>n.</i> a spirited graceful and intelligent riding horse native to Arabia [Arabian]</p><p><b>šeik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the leader of an Arab village or family [sheik, sheikh, tribal sheik, tribal sheikh]</p><p><b>Arapska liga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an international organization of independent Arab states formed in 1945 to promote cultural and economic and military and political and social cooperation</p><p><b>Arapska Republika Egipat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic in northeastern Africa known as the United Arab Republic until 1971 [Egypt, United Arab Republic]</p><p><b>Palestinska međunarodna teroristička organizacija koja se odvojila od PLO-a 1974. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Palestinian international terrorist organization that split from the PLO in 1974 [ANO, Abu Nidal Organization, Black September, Fatah-RC, Fatah Revolutionary Council, Revolutionary Organization of Socialist Muslims]</p><p><b>etničko manjino koje potječe od Berbera i Arapa i živi u sjevernoj Africi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ethnic minority descended from Berbers and Arabs and living in northern Africa [Berbers]</p><p><b>Egipat i Sirija napali su Izrael u listopadu 1973. (na Jom Kipur), Napetost između Arapa i Izraela izbila je u kratkom ratu u lipnju 1967. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Egypt and Syria attacked Israel in October 1973 (on Yom Kippur) [Yom Kippur War]</p><p><i>n.</i> tension between Arabs and Israeli erupted into a brief war in June 1967 [Six-Day War, Six Day War]</p><p><b>arabeska</b></p><p><i>n.</i> position in which the dancer has one leg raised behind and arms outstretched in a conventional pose</p><p><i>n.</i> an ornament that interlaces simulated foliage in an intricate design</p><p><b>Arabija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a peninsula between the Red Sea and the Persian Gulf [Arabian Peninsula]</p><p><b>Arapkinja, arapski, arapskom, Arapin, arabljanin, Arabijac, Arabljanka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a Semitic people originally from the Arabian peninsula and surrounding territories who speaks Arabic and who inhabits much of the Middle East and northern Africa [Arab]</p><p><i>n.</i> a spirited graceful and intelligent riding horse native to Arabia [Arab]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or associated with Arabia or its people</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Arabian horses</p><p><b>Camelus dromedarius, arapska deva, dromedar, jednogrba deva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one-humped camel of the hot deserts of northern Africa and southwestern Asia [Camelus dromedarius, dromedary]</p><p><b>Šumovi iz sjeveroistočne tropske Afrike, široko uzgajani u tropskim ili blizu tropskim područjima zbog sjemena koja čine većinu komercijalne kave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby tree of northeastern tropical Africa widely cultivated in tropical or near tropical regions for its seed which form most of the commercial coffee [Coffea arabica]</p><p><b>pustinja u Egiptu između rijeke Nila i Crvenog mora, pustinja na Arapskom poluostrvu u jugozapadnoj Aziji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a desert in Egypt between the Nile River and the Red Sea [Eastern Desert]</p><p><i>n.</i> a desert on the Arabian Peninsula in southwestern Asia [Great Arabian Desert]</p><p><b>Plitko rame Arapskog mora između Irana i Arapskog poluotoka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shallow arm of the Arabian Sea between Iran and the Arabian peninsula [Persian Gulf]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijska vječnozelena loza koja se uzgaja zbog svojih bogatih mirisnih bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian evergreen vine cultivated for its profuse fragrant white flowers [Jasminum sambac]</p><p><b>arapske noći, hiljadu jedna noć</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collection of folktales in Arabic dating from the 10th century [Arabian Nights' Entertainment, Thousand and One Nights]</p><p><b>zbirka narodnih priča na arapskom iz 10. stoljeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collection of folktales in Arabic dating from the 10th century [Arabian Nights, Thousand and One Nights]</p><p><b>poluostrvo između Crvenog mora i Persijskog zaljeva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a peninsula between the Red Sea and the Persian Gulf [Arabia]</p><p><b>Arapsko more</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a northwestern arm of the Indian Ocean between India and Arabia</p><p><b>listovi grma Catha edulis koji se žvače kao duhan ili se koriste za pravljenje čaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the leaves of the shrub Catha edulis which are chewed like tobacco or used to make tea [African tea, cat, kat, khat, qat, quat]</p><p><b>arapski, arapski jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Semitic language of the Arabs [Arabic language]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of Arabs</p><p><b>abeceda od 28 znakova izvedena iz aramejskog i korištena za pisanje arapskih jezika (i pozajmljena za pisanje urdskog) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the alphabet of 28 characters derived from Aramaic and used for writing Arabic languages (and borrowed for writing Urdu)</p><p><b>arapski jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Semitic language of the Arabs [Arabic]</p><p><b>Svaka oznaka mora biti označena s: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the symbols 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,0 [Hindu-Arabic numeral, Hindu numeral]</p><p><b>biljka od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od biljke od bil (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of the mustard family having white or yellow or purplish flowers [genus Arabidopsis]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je ova biljka u pitanju, ona se može koristiti za proizvodnju biljaka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small noninvasive cross-pollinating plant with white flowers</p><p><b>mala invazivna samopoužnjavajuća korova sa malim bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small invasive self-pollinating weed with small white flowers [mouse-ear cress]</p><p><b>kvaliteta zemljišta koja je prikladna za uzgoj; (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of land that is appropriate for cultivation</p><p><b>godišnje do višegodišnje drvene biljke iz umjerene Sjeverne Amerike, Europe i Azije: krastavca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual to perennial woody herbs of temperate North America, Europe and Asia: rockcress [genus Arabis]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički kameni krest s vrlo dugim zakrivljenim čipkama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American rock cress having very long curved pods [sicklepod]</p><p><b>ili rod Arabis: čvrsta kresta široko rasprostranjena diljem Europe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> or genus Arabis: erect cress widely distributed throughout Europe [Turritis glabra, tower cress, tower mustard]</p><p><b>Europski krest s čvrstim uspravnim stabljikama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European cress having stiff erect stems [tower cress, tower mustard]</p><p><b>učenjak koji se specijalizirao za arapske jezike i kulturu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scholar who specializes in Arab languages and culture</p><p><b>koji se ore, obradiv, oranica, plodan, plodna zemlja</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of farmland) capable of being farmed productively [cultivable, cultivatable, tillable]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na biljku iz obitelji Araceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a plant of the family Araceae [aroid]</p><p><b>rod biljaka s čunjama koje sazrevaju pod zemljom (vidi kikiriki) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of plants with pods that ripen underground (see peanut) [genus Arachis]</p><p><b>široko uzgajana američka biljka uzgajana u tropskim i toplim područjima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated American plant cultivated in tropical and warm regions [peanut, peanut vine]</p><p><b>arahnid, paučnjaci, paučnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> air-breathing arthropods characterized by simple eyes and four pairs of legs [arachnoid]</p><p><b>Velika klasa članonožnih uključujući paukove i krpelje i škorpije i tatinog dugonoge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large class of arthropods including spiders and ticks and scorpions and daddy longlegs [class Arachnida]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na ili sliči na pripadnika klase Arachnida (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or resembling a member of the class Arachnida [arachnoid, spiderlike, spiderly, spidery]</p><p><b>arahnid, paučnjaci, paučnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the middle of the 3 meninges [arachnoid membrane]</p><p><i>n.</i> air-breathing arthropods characterized by simple eyes and four pairs of legs [arachnid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or resembling a member of the class Arachnida [arachnidian, spiderlike, spiderly, spidery]</p><p><b>sredini tri moždanog crijeva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the middle of the 3 meninges [arachnoid]</p><p><b>morbidni strah od pauka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a morbid fear of spiders</p><p><b>Palestinski državnik koji je bio predsjednik Palestine Liberation Organization (1929-2004) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Palestinian statesman who was chairman of the Palestine Liberation Organization (1929-2004) [Yasser Arafat]</p><p><b>dio zapadnog Tihog oceana sjeverno od Australije i južno od Nove Gvineje i istočnih otočja Indonezije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a part of the western Pacific Ocean to the north of Australia and to the south of New Guinea and the eastern islands of Indonesia</p><p><b>Aragon, Katalonija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French writer who generalized surrealism to literature (1897-1982) [Louis Aragon]</p><p><i>n.</i> a region of northeastern Spain</p><p><b>Aragonit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mineral form of crystalline calcium carbonate</p><p><b>rijeka u središnjem Brazilu koja teče na sjeveru (sa mnogim slapovima) da se pridruži rijeci Tocantins (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in central Brazil that flows generally northward (with many falls) to join the Tocantins River [Araguaia River, Araguaya, Araguaya River]</p><p><b>rijeka u središnjem Brazilu koja teče na sjeveru (sa mnogim slapovima) da se pridruži rijeci Tocantins (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in central Brazil that flows generally northward (with many falls) to join the Tocantins River [Araguaia, Araguaya, Araguaya River]</p><p><b>rijeka u središnjem Brazilu koja teče na sjeveru (sa mnogim slapovima) da se pridruži rijeci Tocantins (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in central Brazil that flows generally northward (with many falls) to join the Tocantins River [Araguaia, Araguaia River, Araguaya River]</p><p><b>rijeka u središnjem Brazilu koja teče na sjeveru (sa mnogim slapovima) da se pridruži rijeci Tocantins (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in central Brazil that flows generally northward (with many falls) to join the Tocantins River [Araguaia, Araguaia River, Araguaya]</p><p><b>arak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various strong liquors distilled from the fermented sap of toddy palms or from fermented molasses [arrack]</p><p><b>jezero na istoku Kaspijskog mora koje se nalazi između Kazahstana i Uzbekistana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lake to the east of the Caspian Sea lying between Kazakhstan and Uzbekistan [Lake Aral]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Araceae [order Arales]</p><p><b>Svaka biljka iz roda Aralia (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Aralia</p><p><b>ljeplovita azijska grmljava grmljava ili mala stabla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous clump-forming Asian shrub or small tree [Japanese angelica tree]</p><p><b>biljka s crnim plodovima i ljekovitim ljuskom iz istočne i središnje Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bristly herb of eastern and central North America having black fruit and medicinal bark [bristly sarsaparilla, bristly sarsparilla, dwarf elder]</p><p><b>Uvođenje u uporabu u proizvodnji i proizvodnji proizvoda iz poglavlja II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common perennial herb having aromatic roots used as a substitute for sarsaparilla [false sarsaparilla, wild sarsaparilla, wild sarsparilla]</p><p><b>neoružana drvena rizomata višegodišnja biljka koja se od divljih sarsaparilla razlikuje aromatičnijim korijenima i panikiranim čvorom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unarmed woody rhizomatous perennial plant distinguished from wild sarsaparilla by more aromatic roots and panicled umbels [American spikenard, life-of-man, petty morel]</p><p><b>malo listno drvo ili grm iz istočne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small deciduous clump-forming tree or shrub of eastern United States [American angelica tree, Hercules'-club, devil's walking stick]</p><p><b>sličan američkom drvetu anđelike ali manje trnastih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to American angelica tree but less prickly [Chinese angelica, Chinese angelica tree]</p><p><b>uglavnom tropska stabla i grmovi i liane: rodovi Panax i Hedera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mostly tropical trees and shrubs and lianas: genera Panax and Hedera [family Araliaceae, ivy family]</p><p><b>Biblijsko ime za drevnu Siriju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the biblical name for ancient Syria</p><p><b>Ruski skladatelj (rođen u Armeniji) čija djela su romantična i odražavaju njegov interes za narodnu glazbu (1903-1978) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Russian composer (born in Armenia) whose works are romantic and reflect his interest in folk music (1903-1978) [Aram Khachaturian, Khachaturian]</p><p><b>Jermenski skladatelj koji je uključio orijentalnu narodnu glazbu (1903-1978) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Armenian composer who incorporated oriental folk music (1903-1978) [Kachaturian]</p><p><b>Ruski skladatelj (rođen u Armeniji) čija djela su romantična i odražavaju njegov interes za narodnu glazbu (1903-1978) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Russian composer (born in Armenia) whose works are romantic and reflect his interest in folk music (1903-1978) [Aram Ilich Khachaturian, Khachaturian]</p><p><b>član jedne od grupa semitskih naroda koji su naseljavali Aram i dijelove Mezopotamije od 11. do 8. stoljeća prije Krista, o ili u vezi s Aram ili s njenim stanovnicima ili njihovom kulturom ili jezikom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of one of a group of Semitic peoples inhabiting Aram and parts of Mesopotamia from the 11th to the 8th century BC [Aramean]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Aram or to its inhabitants or their culture or their language [Aramean]</p><p><b>Semitski jezik koji je izvorno pripadala drevnoj aramejskoj zajednici, ali ga još uvijek govore drugi ljudi u jugozapadnoj Aziji., abecedni (ili možda silabički) pisac koji se koristio od 9. stoljeća prije Krista za pisanje aramejskog jezika, od ili u vezi sa drevnim aramejskim jezicima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Semitic language originally of the ancient Arameans but still spoken by other people in southwestern Asia</p><p><i>n.</i> an alphabetical (or perhaps syllabic) script used since the 9th century BC to write the Aramaic language [Aramaic script]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the ancient Aramaic languages</p><p><b>abecedni (ili možda silabički) pisac koji se koristio od 9. stoljeća prije Krista za pisanje aramejskog jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alphabetical (or perhaps syllabic) script used since the 9th century BC to write the Aramaic language [Aramaic]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (b) ovog članka, za proizvode koji sadrže: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edible seaweed with a mild flavor</p><p><b>član jedne od grupa semitskih naroda koji su naseljavali Aram i dijelove Mezopotamije od 11. do 8. stoljeća prije Krista, o ili u vezi s Aram ili s njenim stanovnicima ili njihovom kulturom ili jezikom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of one of a group of Semitic peoples inhabiting Aram and parts of Mesopotamia from the 11th to the 8th century BC [Aramaean]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Aram or to its inhabitants or their culture or their language [Aramaean]</p><p><b>rod velikih smeđih ptica s dugim kljunom koje žive u toplim močvarnim područjima zapadne polutke: kurlan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of large brown long-billed wading birds found in warm swampy regions of the western hemisphere: courlan [genus Aramus]</p><p><b>ptica u vodi iz Južne i Srednje Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wading bird of South America and Central America [courlan]</p><p><b>Vodič na Floridi, Kubi i Jamajci s spušteni čvor i karakterističnim glasom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wading bird of Florida, Cuba and Jamaica having a drooping bill and a distinctive wailing call [limpkin]</p><p><b>tri mala otoka koja pripadaju Irskoj na ulazu u zaljev Galway (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> three small islands belonging to Ireland at the entrance to Galway Bay</p><p><b>rod paukova koji se bave tkanjem kugla uključujući obične vrtne pauke i pauke u stajama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of orb-weaving spiders including common garden spiders and barn spiders [Araneus, genus Aranea, genus Araneus]</p><p><b>pauk koji se često nalazi u evropskim vrtovima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spider common in European gardens [garden spider]</p><p><b>pauci, red Araneae, red Araneida, red paukova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spiders [Araneida, order Araneae, order Araneida]</p><p><b>pauci, red Araneae, red Araneida, red paukova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spiders [Araneae, order Araneae, order Araneida]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na ili sliči na pauka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or resembling a spider [araneidan]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na ili sliči na pauka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or resembling a spider [araneidal]</p><p><b>rod paukova koji se bave tkanjem kugla uključujući obične vrtne pauke i pauke u stajama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of orb-weaving spiders including common garden spiders and barn spiders [Aranea, genus Aranea, genus Araneus]</p><p><b>narandžasti i smeđi pauk sa tamno prugavim nogama koji svakodnevno previja mrežu kugle (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an orange and tan spider with darkly banded legs that spins an orb web daily [barn spider]</p><p><b>Treč koji je sličan Brahmanu ali koji će čitati ili objašnjavati ankoriti u tišini šume. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a treatise resembling a Brahmana but to be read or expounded by anchorites in the quiet of the forest</p><p><b>član plemena Indijanaca koji su nekada živjeli u istočnom Coloradu i Wyomingu (sada žive u Oklahomi i Wyomingu), Algonkijski jezik koji govore Arapaho. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a tribe of Plains Indians formerly inhabiting eastern Colorado and Wyoming (now living in Oklahoma and Wyoming) [Arapahoe]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Algonquian language spoken by the Arapaho [Arapahoe]</p><p><b>član plemena Indijanaca koji su nekada živjeli u istočnom Coloradu i Wyomingu (sada žive u Oklahomi i Wyomingu), Algonkijski jezik koji govore Arapaho. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a tribe of Plains Indians formerly inhabiting eastern Colorado and Wyoming (now living in Oklahoma and Wyoming) [Arapaho]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Algonquian language spoken by the Arapaho [Arapaho]</p><p><b>Ararat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mountain peak that Noah's ark landed on as the waters of the great flood receded [Mount Ararat, Mt. Ararat]</p><p><b>Brazilsko drvo s lijepo označenim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Brazilian tree with handsomely marked wood [Centrolobium robustum]</p><p><b>gorko žuti prah koji se koristi za liječenje kožnih bolesti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bitter yellow powder used to treat skin diseases [Goa powder, chrysarobin]</p><p><b>rijeka koja izlazi u sjeveroistočnoj Turskoj (u blizini izvora Eufrata) i teče na istoku kroz Armeniju do Kaspijskog mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river that rises in northeastern Turkey (near the source of the Euphrates) and flows generally eastward through Armenia to the Caspian Sea [Araxes]</p><p><b>rijeka koja izlazi u sjevernoj Kolumbiji i teče na istoku do rijeke Orinoco u središnjoj Venezueli (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river that rises in northern Colombia and flows generally eastward to the Orinoco in central Venezuela</p><p><b>bilo koje od nekoliko visokih južnoameričkih ili australijskih stabala s velikim čunjama i jestivim sjemenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several tall South American or Australian trees with large cones and edible seeds</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (c) ovog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large Chilean evergreen conifer having intertwined branches and bearing edible nuts [chile pine, monkey puzzle]</p><p><b>Australski igloviti stabla s dva inča sjemenki okus kao pečeni kesteni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian conifer bearing two-inch seeds tasting like roasted chestnuts [bunya bunya, bunya bunya tree]</p><p><b>vrlo visoka zimzelena stabla iz Nove Kaledonije i Nove Hebride slična boru sa otoka Norfolk (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very tall evergreen of New Caledonia and the New Hebrides similar to norfolk island pine [new caledonian pine]</p><p><b>Pinar Australije i Nove Gvineje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pine of Australia and New Guinea [Moreton Bay pine, hoop pine]</p><p><b>zelena biljka iz Australije i otoka Norfolk u južnom Pacifiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen of Australia and Norfolk Island in the South Pacific [Araucaria heterophylla, norfolk island pine]</p><p><b>Visoka, uvijek zelena, konusno-noseća stabla iz Južne Amerike i Australije s širokim kožnim listovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall evergreen cone-bearing trees of South America and Australia with broad leathery leaves [Araucariaceae, family Araucariaceae]</p><p><b>zelena biljka iz Australije i otoka Norfolk u južnom Pacifiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen of Australia and Norfolk Island in the South Pacific [Araucaria excelsa, norfolk island pine]</p><p><b>Visoka, uvijek zelena, konusno-noseća stabla iz Južne Amerike i Australije s širokim kožnim listovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall evergreen cone-bearing trees of South America and Australia with broad leathery leaves [araucaria family, family Araucariaceae]</p><p><b>malen rod južnoameričkih zimzelenih vinove loze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of South American evergreen vines [genus Araujia]</p><p><b>robusni grm s parfemnim bijelim ili ružičastim cvijećem s ravnim ljetnicama koje hvataju noćne moljke i zadržavaju ih do zore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> robust twining shrub having racemes of fragrant white or pink flowers with flat spreading terminal petals that trap nocturnal moths and hold them until dawn [cruel plant]</p><p><b>anti- TNF spojevi (trgovinski naziv Arava) koji se uzimaju oralno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anti-TNF compound (trade name Arava) that is given orally [leflunomide]</p><p><b>član široko rasprostranjene grupe Indijanaca koji žive na sjeveroistoku Južne Amerike., obitelj južnoameričkih indijskih jezika koji se govore na sjeveroistoku Južne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a widespread group of Amerindians living in northeastern South America [Arawakan]</p><p><i>n.</i> a family of South American Indian languages spoken in northeastern South America [Arawakan]</p><p><b>član široko rasprostranjene grupe Indijanaca koji žive na sjeveroistoku Južne Amerike., obitelj južnoameričkih indijskih jezika koji se govore na sjeveroistoku Južne Amerike, naroda koji govore aravakski jezik ili koji su povezani s njima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a widespread group of Amerindians living in northeastern South America [Arawak]</p><p><i>n.</i> a family of South American Indian languages spoken in northeastern South America [Arawak]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the peoples who speak the language of the Arawak</p><p><b>Keltsko božanstvo koje je bilo gospodar Annwfn (drugi svijet ili zemlja vila) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Celtic deity who was the lord of Annwfn (the other world or the land of fairies)</p><p><b>rijeka koja izlazi u sjeveroistočnoj Turskoj (u blizini izvora Eufrata) i teče na istoku kroz Armeniju do Kaspijskog mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river that rises in northeastern Turkey (near the source of the Euphrates) and flows generally eastward through Armenia to the Caspian Sea [Aras]</p><p><b>osoba koja se bavi arbitražom (koja kupuje vrijednosne papire na jednom tržištu za neposrednu prodju na drugom u nadi da će profitirati od cijene razlike) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who engages in arbitrage (who purchases securities in one market for immediate resale in another in the hope of profiting from the price differential) [arbitrager, arbitrageur]</p><p><b>arbitar, samostrel</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an engine that provided medieval artillery used during sieges [arbalist, ballista, bricole, catapult, mangonel, onager, trebuchet, trebucket]</p><p><b>motor koji je pružao srednjovjekovni topništvo korišteno tijekom opsada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an engine that provided medieval artillery used during sieges [arbalest, ballista, bricole, catapult, mangonel, onager, trebuchet, trebucket]</p><p><b>arbitar, izabrani sudac, izabrani sudija, posrednik, sudac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone with the power to settle matters at will [supreme authority]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone chosen to judge and decide a disputed issue [arbitrator, umpire]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je to potrebno za određivanje pravne osnove za postupak arbitraže, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> appropriate for or subject to settlement by arbitration</p><p><b>arbitraža, financijska arbitraža, kupoprodajna valuta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of hedged investment meant to capture slight differences in price</p><p><i>v.</i> practice arbitrage, as in the stock market</p><p><b>arbitraža, financijska arbitraža, kupoprodajna valuta (od &quot;arbitrage&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who engages in arbitrage (who purchases securities in one market for immediate resale in another in the hope of profiting from the price differential) [arb, arbitrageur]</p><p><b>osoba koja se bavi arbitražom (koja kupuje vrijednosne papire na jednom tržištu za neposrednu prodju na drugom u nadi da će profitirati od cijene razlike) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who engages in arbitrage (who purchases securities in one market for immediate resale in another in the hope of profiting from the price differential) [arb, arbitrager]</p><p><b>arbitražni, izbrani, arbitražna</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or resulting from arbitration [arbitrational]</p><p><b>Čin odlučivanja kao arbitar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of deciding as an arbiter [arbitration, arbitrement]</p><p><b>proizvoljno, samovoljno, slučajno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a random manner [at random, every which way, haphazardly, indiscriminately, randomly, willy-nilly]</p><p><b>samovolja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of acting unpredictably and more from whim or caprice than from reason or judgment [capriciousness, flightiness, whimsey, whimsicality, whimsy]</p><p><b>despotski, neobuzdan, neosnovan, proizvoljan, samovoljan, samovoljnom, svojeglav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> based on or subject to individual discretion or preference or sometimes impulse or caprice</p><p><b>arbitrirati, presuditi, suditi, posredovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> act between parties with a view to reconciling differences [intercede, intermediate, liaise, mediate]</p><p><b>arbitraža, arbitražni postupak, arbitriranje, odluka, presuda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) the hearing and determination of a dispute by an impartial referee agreed to by both parties (often used to settle disputes between labor and management)</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of deciding as an arbiter [arbitrament, arbitrement]</p><p><b>arbitražna klauzula, klauzula arbitraže</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a clause in a contract providing for arbitration of disputes arising under the contract</p><p><b>U slučaju arbitraže ili arbitraže u kojoj se sudski postupak odnosi na arbitražu ili koja proizlazi iz nje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or resulting from arbitration [arbitral]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or having the authority to arbitrate</p><p><b>arbitar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone chosen to judge and decide a disputed issue [arbiter, umpire]</p><p><b>Čin odlučivanja kao arbitar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of deciding as an arbiter [arbitrament, arbitration]</p><p><b>drvo, osovina, transmisija, vratilo, vreteno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree (as opposed to shrub)</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various rotating shafts that serve as axes for larger rotating parts [mandrel, mandril, spindle]</p><p><i>n.</i> a framework that supports climbing plants [arbour, bower, pergola]</p><p><b>Dan za sadnju stabala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a day designated for planting trees</p><p><b>u drveću. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> abounding in trees [arboreous, woodsy, woody]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili formirane od drveća (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or formed by trees [arboreal, arborical, arborous]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili formirane od drveća, koji žive ili često žive na drveću, koji je sličan drvetu po obliku i strukturi grana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or formed by trees [arborary, arborical, arborous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> inhabiting or frequenting trees [arboreous, tree-living]</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a tree in form and branching structure [arboreous, arborescent, arboresque, arboriform, dendriform, dendroid, dendroidal, tree-shaped, treelike]</p><p><b>žuti-pomičasti smeđi salamander iz kalifornijskih šuma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> yellow-spotted brown salamander of California woodlands [Aneides lugubris]</p><p><b>drven, pošumljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inhabiting or frequenting trees [arboreal, tree-living]</p><p><i>adj.</i> abounding in trees [arboraceous, woodsy, woody]</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a tree in form and branching structure [arboreal, arborescent, arboresque, arboriform, dendriform, dendroid, dendroidal, tree-shaped, treelike]</p><p><b>koji je sličan drvetu po obliku i strukturi grana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a tree in form and branching structure [arboreal, arboreous, arboresque, arboriform, dendriform, dendroid, dendroidal, tree-shaped, treelike]</p><p><b>s oblikom ili karakteristikama drveta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having the shape or characteristics of a tree</p><p><b>koji je sličan drvetu po obliku i strukturi grana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a tree in form and branching structure [arboreal, arboreous, arborescent, arboriform, dendriform, dendroid, dendroidal, tree-shaped, treelike]</p><p><b>arboretum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a facility where trees and shrubs are cultivated for exhibition [botanical garden]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili formirane od drveća (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or formed by trees [arborary, arboreal, arborous]</p><p><b>šumogojstvo, uzgajanje drveća i grmlja, uzgajanje ukrasnog drveća i grmlja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tending of and caring for trees [tree farming]</p><p><b>netko obučen u šumarstvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone trained in forestry [forester, tree farmer]</p><p><b>koji je sličan drvetu po obliku i strukturi grana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a tree in form and branching structure [arboreal, arboreous, arborescent, arboresque, dendriform, dendroid, dendroidal, tree-shaped, treelike]</p><p><b>Izrasli su kao drveće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> branch out like trees [arborize]</p><p><b>specijalista za liječenje oštećenih stabala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in treating damaged trees [tree surgeon]</p><p><b>Izrasli su kao drveće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> branch out like trees [arborise]</p><p><b>obožavanje stabala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the worship of trees [tree-worship]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili formirane od drveća (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or formed by trees [arborary, arboreal, arborical]</p><p><b>Velika heterogena grupa RNK virusa koja se može podijeliti u grupe na temelju viriona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large heterogeneous group of RNA viruses divisible into groups on the basis of the virions [arbovirus]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko azijskih i sjevernoameričkih iglavca rodova Thuja i Thujopsis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several Asian and North American conifers of the genera Thuja and Thujopsis</p><p><b>hladnjak, sjenica, sjenica u vrtu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fra