ring secret or mysterious knowledge</p><p><b>Talijanski violinist i skladatelj violinskih koncerata (1653-1713) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian violinist and composer of violin concertos (1653-1713) [Corelli]</p><p><b>eliksir, skrovit, tajna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> information known only to a special group [secret]</p><p><b>obrnuta funkcija kosina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inverse function of the cosine [arc cosine, arccosine, inverse cosine]</p><p><b>kut koji ima kosekant jednako određenom broju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the angle that has a cosecant equal to a given number [arc cosecant, inverse cosecant]</p><p><b>obrnuta funkcija kosina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inverse function of the cosine [arc cosine, arccos, inverse cosine]</p><p><b>obrnuta funkcija cotangenta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inverse function of the cotangent [arc cotangent, inverse cotangent]</p><p><b>stupanj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measure for arcs and angles [degree]</p><p><b>arkus, duga, električni luk, lučni, luk, luka, svjetlosni luk, svod (od &quot;arc&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> forming or resembling an arch [arched, arching, arciform, arcuate, bowed]</p><p><b>amebni protozoj s chitinoznom ljuskom nalik kišobranu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an amoeba-like protozoan with a chitinous shell resembling an umbrella</p><p><b>Prirodni i slatkovodni protozoi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soil and freshwater protozoa [family Arcellidae]</p><p><b>rod uglavnom američkih biljaka paraziti na igličnim stablima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of chiefly American plants parasitic on conifers [genus Arceuthobium]</p><p><b>mala biljka s lišćama poput ljuske na crvenkasto smeđim stabljikama i plodovima poput bobica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small herb with scalelike leaves on reddish-brown stems and berrylike fruits [American mistletoe]</p><p><b>glavni, lučni, lučni nosač, luk, lukav, plameni svod, prepreden, slavoluk, spojiti lukom, strop, svinuti u obliku luka, svod, zasvoditi, lukom, lučnim, plameni svo, nad-, nadsvođen prolaz, nadsvoditi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a curved shape in the vertical plane that spans an opening</p><p><i>n.</i> a curved bony structure supporting or enclosing organs (especially the inner sides of the feet)</p><p><i>n.</i> a passageway under a curved masonry construction [archway]</p><p><i>n.</i> (architecture) a masonry construction (usually curved) for spanning an opening and supporting the weight above it</p><p><i>v.</i> form an arch or curve [arc, curve]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of behavior or attitude) characteristic of those who treat others with condescension [condescending, patronising, patronizing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> naughtily or annoyingly playful [impish, implike, mischievous, pixilated, prankish, puckish, wicked]</p><p><b>nadsvoditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> form an arch over [overarch]</p><p><b>podupiranje za luk stopala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a support for the arch of the foot</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s najranijim poznatim stijenama formiranim tijekom prekambrijskog eona (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the earliest known rocks formed during the Precambrian Eon [archean]</p><p><b>smatraju drevnim oblicima života koji su evoluirali odvojeno od bakterija i plavo-zelenih algi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> considered ancient life forms that evolved separately from bacteria and blue-green algae [archaebacterium, archaeobacteria, archeobacteria]</p><p><b>smatraju drevnim oblicima života koji su evoluirali odvojeno od bakterija i plavo-zelenih algi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> considered ancient life forms that evolved separately from bacteria and blue-green algae [archaebacteria, archaeobacteria, archeobacteria]</p><p><b>smatraju drevnim oblicima života koji su evoluirali odvojeno od bakterija i plavo-zelenih algi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> considered ancient life forms that evolved separately from bacteria and blue-green algae [archaebacteria, archaebacterium, archeobacteria]</p><p><b>arheološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> related to or dealing with or devoted to archaeology [archaeological, archeologic, archeological]</p><p><b>arheološki, arheološke, arheološko, arheološkom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> related to or dealing with or devoted to archaeology [archaeologic, archeologic, archeological]</p><p><b>arheolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anthropologist who studies prehistoric people and their culture [archeologist]</p><p><b>arheologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of anthropology that studies prehistoric people and their cultures [archeology]</p><p><b>izumrla primitivna zubičasta ptica iz perioda Jura s dugim pernatim repom i šupljim kostima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct primitive toothed bird of the Jurassic period having a long feathered tail and hollow bones [Archaeopteryx lithographica, archeopteryx]</p><p><b>izumrla primitivna zubičasta ptica iz perioda Jura s dugim pernatim repom i šupljim kostima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct primitive toothed bird of the Jurassic period having a long feathered tail and hollow bones [archaeopteryx, archeopteryx]</p><p><b>izumrla primitivna ptica sa zubima s dugim perjenim repom i tri slobodna kandžica na svakom krilu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct primitive toothed bird with a long feathered tail and three free clawed digits on each wing</p><p><b>primitivne fosilne ptice poput gmizavaca iz Jure ili ranog krede (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> primitive reptile-like fossil birds of the Jurassic or early Cretaceous [subclass Archaeornithes]</p><p><b>Vrijeme od 3.800 milijuna godina do prije 2.500 milijuna godina., od ili pripadaju ranijim od dvije divizije predkambrijskog doba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time from 3,800 million years to 2,500 million years ago [Archaeozoic aeon, Archean, Archean aeon, Archean eon, Archeozoic, Archeozoic eon]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or belonging to earlier of two divisions of the Precambrian era [archeozoic]</p><p><b>Vrijeme od 3.800 milijuna godina do prije 2.500 milijuna godina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time from 3,800 million years to 2,500 million years ago [Archaeozoic, Archean, Archean aeon, Archean eon, Archeozoic, Archeozoic eon]</p><p><b>Arhaik, arhaičan, arhaizmi, starinski, staromodan, zastareo, zastario, antikni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> so extremely old as seeming to belong to an earlier period [antediluvian, antiquated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> little evolved from or characteristic of an earlier ancestral type [primitive]</p><p><b>arhaizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of an archaic expression [archaism]</p><p><b>dati arhaičan izgled karaktera na (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give an archaic appearance of character to [archaize]</p><p><b>arhaizam, archaism</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of an archaic expression [archaicism]</p><p><b>Osoba koja se arhaizira., stručnjak ili sakupljač starina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who archaizes</p><p><i>n.</i> an expert or collector of antiquities [antiquarian, antiquary]</p><p><b>imitacija arhaičnog stila ili načina (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> imitative of an archaic style or manner</p><p><b>dati arhaičan izgled karaktera na (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give an archaic appearance of character to [archaise]</p><p><b>arhanđeo, arhanđel, arkanđeo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an angel ranked above the highest rank in the celestial hierarchy</p><p><i>n.</i> a biennial cultivated herb [Angelica Archangelica, garden angelica]</p><p><b>arhanđeo, arhanđel (od &quot;archangel&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or resembling archangels [archangelical]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili nalik arhanđelima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or resembling archangels [archangelic]</p><p><b>arhiepiskop, mitropolit, nadbiskup, nadbiskupa, arheopiskop</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bishop of highest rank</p><p><b>arhiepiskopija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the territorial jurisdiction of an archbishop</p><p><b>arhiđakon, archiđakona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Anglican Church) an ecclesiastical dignitary usually ranking just below a bishop</p><p><b>arhiđakonat, arhiđakonstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the territorial juris