eroes who sailed with Jason in search of the Golden Fleece</p><p><i>n.</i> cephalopod mollusk of warm seas whose females have delicate papery spiral shells [Argonauta argo, nautilus, paper nautilus]</p><p><b>vrsta rod porodice Argonautidae: paper nautilus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the family Argonautidae: paper nautilus [genus Argonauta]</p><p><b>indijska lađica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cephalopod mollusk of warm seas whose females have delicate papery spiral shells [Argonaut, nautilus, paper nautilus]</p><p><b>u obliku od poluprovodnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> represented solely by the genus Argonauta [family Argonautidae]</p><p><b>Američka operacija u Prvom svjetskom ratu (1918) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an American operation in World War I (1918) [Argonne Forest, Meuse, Meuse-Argonne, Meuse-Argonne operation, Meuse River]</p><p><b>Američka operacija u Prvom svjetskom ratu (1918) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an American operation in World War I (1918) [Argonne, Meuse, Meuse-Argonne, Meuse-Argonne operation, Meuse River]</p><p><b>inertni plin, plemeniti plin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the chemically inert gaseous elements of the helium group in the periodic table [inert gas, noble gas]</p><p><b>drevni grad u jugoistočnoj Grčkoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient city in southeastern Greece</p><p><b>jedan ili više velikih trgovačkih brodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one or more large merchant ships</p><p><b>argo, šatrovački jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a characteristic language of a particular group (as among thieves) [cant, jargon, lingo, patois, slang, vernacular]</p><p><b>sporan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being supported by argument</p><p><i>adj.</i> open to argument or debate [debatable, disputable, moot]</p><p><b>dokazivo, moguće, nedvojbeno, uvjerljivo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> as can be shown by argument</p><p><b>argumentirati, diskutirati, dokazivati, objašnjavati se, prepirati se, prosuditi, raspravljati, razuvjeriti, svađati se, uvjeravati, uvjeriti, ob