eed to between opponents so they can discuss peace terms [cease-fire, truce]</p><p><b>pravni praznik u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a legal holiday in the United States [November 11, Veterans' Day, Veterans Day]</p><p><b>bez grana, bez ruke, bezruk, goloruk, nenaoružan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having no arms</p><p><b>mali zaljev, narukvica, rukavac, rukavac rijeke, zaštitni rukav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a band worn around the arm for decoration [arm band]</p><p><b>slično ruci. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling an arm</p><p><b>veliki ormar ili ormar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large wardrobe or cabinet</p><p><b>heraldika, oklopne jedinice, oružarnica, štit, zaštitni oklop, znak, znanost o grbovima, oklop, ljuštura, pokrov</b></p><p><i>n.</i> protective covering made of metal and used in combat [armour]</p><p><i>n.</i> a military unit consisting of armored fighting vehicles [armour]</p><p><i>n.</i> tough more-or-less rigid protective covering of an animal or plant [armour]</p><p><i>v.</i> equip with armor [armour]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 85%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> specially hardened steel plate used to protect fortifications or vehicles from enemy fire [armor plating, armour plate, plate armor, plate armour]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 85%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> specially hardened steel plate used to protect fortifications or vehicles from enemy fire [armor plate, armour plate, plate armor, plate armour]</p><p><b>Škvar koji nosi oklop viteza. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a squire carrying the armor of a knight [armiger]</p><p><b>s masnim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili većim (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with heavy steel [armor-plated, armour-clad, armour-plated, steel-plated]</p><p><b>s masnim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili većim (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with heavy steel [armor-clad, armour-clad, armour-plated, steel-plated]</p><p><b>škrob (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> horseradish [genus Armora