p><p><i>adj.</i> commanding attention [sensational, stunning]</p><p><b>žitarica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> oat grass [genus Arrhenatherum]</p><p><b>hrupna višegodišnja evroazijska trava slična ovsima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coarse perennial Eurasian grass resembling oat [French rye, evergreen grass, false oat, tall meadow grass, tall oat grass]</p><p><b>Švedski kemičar i fizičar poznat po svojoj teoriji kemijske disocijacije (1859-1927) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Swedish chemist and physicist noted for his theory of chemical dissociation (1859-1927) [Svante August Arrhenius]</p><p><b>(hemija) teorija koja opisuje vodene rastvore u smislu kiselina (koji se disoziiraju da daju vodikove ione) i baza (koji se disoziiraju da daju hidroksilne ione) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) theory that describes aqueous solutions in terms of acids (which dissociate to give hydrogen ions) and bases (which dissociate to give hydroxyl ions) [theory of dissociation, theory of electrolytic dissociation]</p><p><b>aritmija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal rate of muscle contractions in the heart [cardiac arrhythmia]</p><p><b>bez stalnog ritma, bez obzira na ritam. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking a steady rhythm [jerking, jerky]</p><p><i>adj.</i> without regard for rhythm [arrhythmical]</p><p><b>bez obzira na ritam. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> without regard for rhythm [arrhythmic]</p><p><b>rezerva, s rezervom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unstated doubt that prevents you from accepting something wholeheartedly [mental reservation, reservation]</p><p><b>dolazak, dolazni, novorođenče, prispijeće, stizanje, upadni, dostignuće, postignuće, postizanje, uspjeh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> accomplishment of an objective [reaching]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of arriving at a certain place</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who arrives (or has arrived) [arriver, comer]</p><p><b>Vrata na kojima putnici iskrcavaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gate where passengers disembark</p><p><b>vrijeme kada se javni prijevoz planira stići na određenu destinaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time at which a public conveyance is scheduled to arrive at a given destination [time of arrival]</p><p><b>doći, dolaziti, donijeti, doputovati, nastupiti, prispjeti, pristići, stići, stigli, dospjeti, dospeti, doletjeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> reach a destination [come, get]</p><p><i>v.</i> succeed in a big way [get in, go far, make it]</p><p><b>doći do, stići do, u, dohvatiti, dokučiti, dokučivati, dopirati, doprijeti, dosegnuti, doseći, dosizati, dostizati, dostići, hvatati, postizati, postići, prispjeti, pristizati, stizati, stići</b></p><p><i>v.</i> reach a destination, either real or abstract [attain, gain, hit, make, reach]</p><p><b>Posljednja riječ. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a farewell remark [adieu, adios, au revoir, auf wiedersehen, bye, bye-bye, cheerio, good-by, good-bye, good day, goodby, goodbye, sayonara, so long]</p><p><b>dolazak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who arrives (or has arrived) [arrival, comer]</p><p><b>osoba koja je iznenada napredovala u ekonomskom položaju, ali nije dobila društveno prihvaćanje drugih u toj klasi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who has suddenly risen to a higher economic status but has not gained social acceptance of others in that class [nouveau-riche, parvenu, upstart]</p><p><b>jedinica za težinu koja se koristi u nekim zemljama koje govore španjolski, tekuća mjera (sa različitim vrijednostima) koja se koristi u nekim zemljama koje govore španjolski jezik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of weight used in some Spanish speaking countries</p><p><i>n.</i> a liquid measure (with different values) used in some Spanish speaking countries</p><p><b>arogancija, bezobraznost, drskost, nadutost, oholost, osionost, osornost, arogantnost, bahatost, nadmenost, naduvenost, taština, umišljenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> overbearing pride evidenced by a superior manner toward inferiors [haughtiness, hauteur, high-handedness, lordliness]</p><p><b>arogantan, bahat, bezobrazan, bezobziran, drzak, nabusit, nadut, ohol, osoran, umišljen, uobražen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing feelings of unwarranted importance out of overbearing pride [chesty, self-important]</p><p><b>bahato, bezobrazno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an arrogant manner</p><p><b>prisvojiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> demand as being one's due or property [claim, lay claim]</p><p><i>v.</i> make undue claims to having [assign]</p><p><i>v.</i> seize and take control without authority and possibly with force [assume, seize, take over, usurp]</p><p><b>nepravedno, konfiskacija, pljenidba, zapljena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> seizure by the government [confiscation]</p><p><b>osoba koja se zbog domišljatosti pretjerano poziva na prava ili prednosti na koje nema pravo ili na kvalitete koje nema (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who through conceit makes pretentious claims to rights or advantages that he or she is not entitled to or to qualities that he or she does not possess</p><p><b>puščica, strelica, strijela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mark to indicate a direction or relation [pointer]</p><p><i>n.</i> a projectile with a straight thin shaft and an arrowhead on one end and stabilizing vanes on the other</p><p><b>vodena biljka iz roda Peltandra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an aquatic plant of the genus Peltandra</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u ovom slučaju ne primjenjuje ovaj standard, u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje ovaj standard, u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje ovaj standard, u slučaju da se primjenjuje druga metoda, u slučaju da se primjenjuje druga metoda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tufted perennial found in shallow water or marshland [Triglochin maritima]</p><p><b>različite vrste aster (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of aster</p><p><b>Ubližno srodno južnom drvetu strelice, listovi padajući grm iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s plavo-crnim bojama i čvrstom fleksibilnom drvetom koje se nekada koristilo za izradu strela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> closely related to southern arrow wood [Viburnum recognitum]</p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrub of eastern North America having blue-black berries and tough pliant wood formerly used to make arrows [Viburnum dentatum, southern arrow wood]</p><p><b>rod monocotyledonous boginjskog bilja red Naiadales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of monocotyledonous bog herbs of order Naiadales [Juncaginaceae, Scheuchzeriaceae, family Juncaginaceae, family Scheuchzeriaceae]</p><p><b>Kao glava strijela bez podloga. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a leaf shape) like an arrow head without flaring base lobes [sagittate, sagittiform]</p><p><b>Oštro oštro ili ubodajuća vrh strijele (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the pointed head or striking tip of an arrow</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka s oštrim zubima, trokutastih lišća na listnatim stabljikama s gomilom žutih cvjetnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial with sharply toothed triangular leaves on leafy stems bearing a cluster of yellow flower heads [Senecio triangularis]</p><p><b>indijska maranta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nutritive starch obtained from the root of the arrowroot plant</p><p><i>n.</i> white-flowered West Indian plant whose root yields arrowroot starch [American arrowroot, Maranta arundinaceae, obedience plant]</p><p><i>n.</i> canna grown especially for its edible rootstock from which arrowroot starch is obtained [Canna edulis, Canna indica, achira, indian shot]</p><p><b>tropske višegodišnje biljke s obično škrobnim rizomima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical perennial herbs with usually starchy rhizomes [Marantaceae, family Marantaceae]</p><p><b>Napravio je strijele. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a maker of arrows</p><p><b>bilo koji crv Chaetognatha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any worm of the Chaetognatha [chaetognath]</p><p><b>potok ili potok (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stream or brook</p><p><b>šumovita vrba sa zapada Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby willow of the western United States [Salix lasiolepis]</p><p><b>Riž i piletina skuhana zajedno španjolski stil (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rice and chicken cooked together