e who kills a prominent political figure) who kills by a surprise attack and often is hired to do the deed [assassinator, bravo]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a secret order of Muslims (founded in the 12th century) who terrorized and killed Christian Crusaders</p><p><b>Pravi insekt: dugonogi grabljivac koji živi uglavnom na drugim insektima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a true bug: long-legged predacious bug living mostly on other insects [reduviid]</p><p><b>ubiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> murder</p><p><i>v.</i> destroy or damage seriously, as of someone's reputation</p><p><b>ubijen, umoren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> murdered by surprise attack for political reasons</p><p><b>atentat, ubojstvo, umorstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an attack intended to ruin someone's reputation [blackwash, character assassination]</p><p><i>n.</i> murder of a public figure by surprise attack</p><p><b>ubojica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a murderer (especially one who kills a prominent political figure) who kills by a surprise attack and often is hired to do the deed [assassin, bravo]</p><p><b>juriš, jurišati, jurišni, napad, napadaj, napadati, napasti, uvreda, nasrtaj, obeščastiti, silovati, kritizirati, nasrnuti, nasrtati, obarati se, oboriti se, okomiti se, okomljivati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> close fighting during the culmination of a military attack</p><p><i>n.</i> a threatened or attempted physical attack by someone who appears to be able to cause bodily harm if not stopped</p><p><i>n.</i> thoroughbred that won the triple crown in 1946</p><p><i>n.</i> the crime of forcing a person to submit to sexual intercourse against his or her will [rape, ravishment, violation]</p><p><i>v.</i> attack someone physically or emotionally [assail, attack, set on]</p><p><i>v.</i> force (someone) to have sex against their will [dishonor, dishonour, outrage, rape, ravish, violate]</p><p><i>v.</i> attack in speech or writing [assail, attack, lash out, round, snipe]</p><p><b>fizički nasrtaj, tvorni napadaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an assault 