ocation, allotment, apportioning, apportionment, parceling, parcelling]</p><p><b>dobiven, dodan, dodani, dodijeljen, određen, pridružen, propisan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> appointed to a post or duty</p><p><b>asignatar, cesionar, opunomoćenik, zastupnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) the party to whom something is assigned (e.g., someone to whom a right or property is legally transferred)</p><p><b>dodjeljivanje, određivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of distributing something to designated places or persons [assignment]</p><p><b>asignacija, cesija, dodjela, dodjeljivanje, dodjeljivanje (frekvencija ili kanala), doznaka, imenovanje, izdvajanje, namjena, naznačavanje, određivanje, prijenos, raspodjela, upućivanje, zadatak, zaduženje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a duty that you are assigned to perform (especially in the armed forces) [duty assignment]</p><p><i>n.</i> the instrument by which a claim or right or interest or property is transferred from one person to another</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of distributing something to designated places or persons [assigning]</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a transfer of property by deed of conveyance [grant]</p><p><i>n.</i> an undertaking that you have been assigned to do (as by an instructor)</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of putting a person into a non-elective position [appointment, designation, naming]</p><p><b>ustupnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) the party who makes an assignment</p><p><b>asignant, uputitelj</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to be absorbed and incorporated into body tissues</p><p><b>apsorbirati, asimilirati, izjednačiti, izjednačiti se, navići se, prilagoditi se, primiti, usporediti, asimilirati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> take up mentally [absorb, ingest, take in]</p><p><i>v.</i> become similar to one's environment</p><p><i>v.</i> make similar</p><p><i>v.</i> take (gas, light or heat) into a solution [imbibe]</p><p><i>v.</i> become similar in sound</p><p><b>apsorbirati, asimilirati, izjednačiti, izjednačiti se, navići se, prilagoditi se, primiti, usporediti (od &quot;assimilate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of taking (gas, light, or liquids) into a solution [assimilative, assimilatory]</p><p><b>asimilacija, izjednačavanje, integracija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being assimilated</p><p><i>n.</i> the social process of absorbing one cultural group into harmony with another [absorption]</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of absorbing nutrients into the body after digestion [absorption]</p><p><i>n.</i> a linguistic process by which a sound becomes similar to an adjacent sound</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of assimilating new ideas into an existing cognitive structure [acculturation]</p><p><i>n.</i> in the theories of Jean Piaget: the application of a general schema to a particular instance</p><p><b>asimilacijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of mentally absorbing</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of taking (gas, light, or liquids) into a solution [assimilating, assimilatory]</p><p><b>naučnik, učenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone (especially a child) who learns (as from a teacher) or takes up knowledge or beliefs [learner, scholar]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm i (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of taking (gas, light, or liquids) into a solution [assimilating, assimilative]</p><p><b>asistencija, asistirati, biti od pomoći, pomagati, pomažemo, pomoći, pomogle, pomogli, potaknuti, prisustvovati, učestvovati, pomaganje, pomoć, dvoriti, poslužiti, posluživati, raditi, služiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of contributing to the fulfillment of a need or furtherance of an effort or purpose [aid, assistance, help]</p><p><i>n.</i> (sports) the act of enabling another player to make a good play</p><p><i>v.</i> give help or assistance [aid, help]</p><p><i>v.</i> act as an assistant in a subordinate or supportive function</p><p><i>v.</i> work for or be a servant to [attend, attend to, serve, wait on]</p><p><b>asistencija, podrška, pomaganje, pomoć, pomoći, savjetovanje, sudjelovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity o