 Roman Catholic Church of the Virgin Mary's being taken up into heaven when her earthly life ended [Assumption of Mary, August 15]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Christianity) the taking up of the body and soul of the Virgin Mary when her earthly life had ended</p><p><i>n.</i> audacious (even arrogant) behavior that you have no right to [effrontery, presumption, presumptuousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of assuming or taking for granted</p><p><b>Velika gospa, Uzašašće Blažene Djevice Marije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> celebration in the Roman Catholic Church of the Virgin Mary's being taken up into heaven when her earthly life ended [Assumption, August 15]</p><p><b>arogantan, drzak</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> excessively forward [assuming, presumptuous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> accepted as real or true without proof</p><p><b>drevni asirski grad na rijeku Tigris i tradicionalni glavni grad Asirije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Assyrian city on the Tigris and traditional capital of Assyria [Ashur, Asur]</p><p><b>garancija, jamstvo, jemstvo, obećanje, osiguranja, osiguranje, osiguranje života, samopouzdanje, sigurnost, uvjeravanje, životno osiguranje, prisega, zakletva, uvjerenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> freedom from doubt [authority, confidence, self-assurance, self-confidence, sureness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a binding commitment to do or give or refrain from something [pledge]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement intended to inspire confidence</p><p><i>n.</i> a British term for some kinds of insurance</p><p><b>Asurbanipal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of Assyria who built a magnificent palace and library at Nineveh (668-627 BC) [Ashurbanipal, Asurbanipal]</p><p><b>obećati, osigurati, uvjeravati, uvjeriti, zajamčiti, osiguravati, obećavati, obvezati se, obvezivati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make certain of [ensure, guarantee, insure, secure]</p><p><i>v.</i> inform positively and with certainty and confidence [tell]</p><p><i>v.</i> assure somebody of the truth of something with the intention of giving the listener confidence</p><p><i>v.</i> be careful or certain to do something [ascertain, check, control, ensure, insure, see, see to it]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to feel sure [reassure]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a promise or commitment [promise]</p><p><b>osiguran, siguran, siguran za, uvjeren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by assurance</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by certainty or security</p><p><b>naravno, nesumnjivo, sigurno, uvjereno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without a doubt</p><p><b>osiguran, siguran, siguran za, uvjeren (od &quot;assured&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> great coolness and composure under strain [aplomb, cool, poise, sang-froid]</p><p><b>uzdižu se iz mora., raste ili se širi prema gore (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> rising from the sea</p><p><i>adj.</i> growing or extending upward</p><p><b>uvjerljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> giving confidence</p><p><b>Asirija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient kingdom in northern Mesopotamia which is in present-day Iraq</p><p><b>stanovnik drevne Asire, jezik modernog Iraka, jezik Asirca iz drevne Mezopotamije koji je nestao (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inhabitant of ancient Assyria</p><p><i>n.</i> the language of modern Iraq [Assyrian Neo-Aramaic]</p><p><i>n.</i> an extinct language of the Assyrians in ancient Mesopotamia [Assyrian Akkadian]</p><p><b>jezik Asirca iz drevne Mezopotamije koji je nestao (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extinct language of the Assyrians in ancient Mesopotamia [Assyrian]</p><p><b>jezik modernog Iraka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the language of modern Iraq [Assyrian]</p><p><b>asiriologija, asirologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> archeology of the ancient Assyrians</p><p><b>uši (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crayfish [Astacura, family Astacidae]</p><p><b>uši (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crayfish [Astacidae, family Astacidae]</p><p><b>vrsta rod porodice Astacidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the family Astacidae [genus Astacus]</p><p><b>Američki plesač i filmski glumac poznat po svom originalnom i gracioznom stepu (1899-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States dancer and cinema actor noted for his original and graceful tap dancing (1899-1987) [Fred Astaire]</p><p><b>Astana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> remote city of Kazakhstan that (ostensibly for security reasons) was made the capital in 1998 [Akmola, capital of Kazakhstan]</p><p><b>drevna fenička boginja ljubavi i plodnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Phoenician goddess of love and fertility [Ashtoreth]</p><p><b>nesposobnost stajanja zbog mišićne neskladnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inability to stand due to muscular incoordination</p><p><b>astatičan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not static or stable</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arrangement of coils used in sensitive electrical instruments</p><p><b>ima pokretni magnet i astatičke tulume raspoređene kako bi poništile učinak Zemljino magnetno polje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> has a moving magnet and astatic coils arranged to cancel the effect of the Earth's magnetic field</p><p><b>astat, astatin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a highly unstable radioactive element (the heaviest of the halogen series) [At, atomic number 85]</p><p><b>astra, lijepa kata</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various chiefly fall-blooming herbs of the genus Aster with showy daisylike flowers</p><p><i>n.</i> star-shaped structure formed in the cytoplasm of a cell having fibers like rays that surround the centrosome during mitosis</p><p><b>Severnoamerička višegodišnja biljka s izgleda okruglim lišćama i blesavim bijelim ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American perennial with apparently whorled leaves and showy white purple-tinged flowers [whorled aster]</p><p><b>obična sjevernoamerička višegodišnja biljka s lišćama poput travnjaka i malim bijelim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common North American perennial with heathlike foliage and small white flower heads [heath aster]</p><p><b>višegodišnji drveni aster iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial wood aster of eastern North America [heart-leaved aster]</p><p><b>Uročnjak od drveta s bijelim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhizomatous perennial wood aster of eastern North America with white flowers [white wood aster]</p><p><b>tvrda višegodišnja biljka sa malim linearnim lišćama i brojnim malim bijelim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stiff perennial of the eastern United States having small linear leaves and numerous tiny white flower heads [bushy aster]</p><p><b>Česta višegodišnja biljka s velikom gromom, s lišćem poput travnjaka i malim zvijezdano-bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common much-branched North American perennial with heathlike foliage and small starry white flowers [heath aster]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka sa bijelim cvjetovima iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of western North America having white flowers [white prairie aster]</p><p><b>biljke s glavama koje se sastoje od mnogih cvjetnica: aster (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plants with heads composed of many florets: aster [Asteraceae, Compositae, family Asteraceae, family Compositae]</p><p><b>žičasta višegodišnja biljka sa čvrstih, uspravnih, grubih stabljika, linearnih lišća i velikih ljubičastih cvijeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wiry tufted perennial of the eastern United States with stiff erect rough stems, linear leaves and large violet flowers [stiff aster]</p><p><b>Dvostruko cvjetanje s početkom cvjetanja iz južne i jugoistočne Europe s cvjetnim vrhovima sličnim cvjetovima zlatne trake (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> early-flowering perennial of southern and southeastern Europe with flower heads resembling those of goldenrod [Linosyris vulgaris, goldilocks, goldilocks aster]</p><p><b>Uro od šumovitih biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tufted perennial wood aster of North America [large-leaved aster]</p><p><b>Uobičajena višegodišnja biljka iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s navidnim ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common perennial of eastern North America having showy purplish flowers [New England aster]</p><p><b>Uročnjava iz Sjeverne Amerike s malim jesenjim ljubičastim ili ružičastim ili bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American perennial herb having small autumn-blooming purple or pink or white flowers [Michaelmas daisy, New York aster]</p><p><b>Čvrsta višegodišnja biljka s pločama i pločama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tufted rigid North American perennial with loose clusters of white flowers [upland white aster]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država koja obično ima plave cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of southeastern United States having usually blue flowers [Short's aster]</p><p><b>Obični europski aster koji raste u solnim močvarama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common European aster that grows in salt marshes [sea aster, sea starwort]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za proizvode iz kategorije II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> violet-flowered perennial aster of central United States having solitary heads [prairie aster]</p><p><b>biljke s glavama koje se sastoje od mnogih cvjetnica: aster (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plants with heads composed of many florets: aster [Compositae, aster family, family Asteraceae, family Compositae]</p><p><b>gubitak sposobnosti prepoznavanja predmeta prilikom rukovanja njima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loss of the ability to recognize objects by handling them [tactile agnosia]</p><p><b>(od nekih kristala, posebno dragulja) s zvijezdama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of some crystals especially gemstones) exhibiting asterism</p><p><b>porodica svojte asterida</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of more or less advanced dicotyledonous herbs and some trees and shrubs</p><p><b>rod svojte asterida</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of more or less advanced dicotyledonous herbs and some trees and shrubs</p><p><b>skupina uglavnom simpatičnih biljaka i nekih stabala i grmova uglavnom s 2 spojena karpela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of mostly sympetalous herbs and some trees and shrubs mostly with 2 fused carpels [subclass Asteridae]</p><p><b>kraniometrijska točka na spoju lamboidne šavure i okcipitomastoidne i parietomastoidne šavure (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the craniometric point at the junction of the lamboid suture and the occipitomastoid suture and the parietomastoid suture</p><p><b>asterisk, staviti zvjezdicu, zvjezdica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a star-shaped character * used in printing [star]</p><p><i>v.</i> mark with an asterisk [star]</p><p><b>asterisk, staviti zvjezdicu, zvjezdica (od &quot;asterisk&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked with an asterisk [starred]</p><p><b>zviježđe</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (mineralogy) a star-shaped figure with six rays that is seen in some crystal structures under reflected or transmitted light</p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) a cluster of stars (or a small constellation)</p><p><b>koji se odnose na zvijezde ili sazvežđa (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to asterisms or constellations</p><p><b>krmom, na krmi, prema krmi, s traga, straga</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> stern foremost or backward</p><p><i>adv.</i> at or near or toward the stern of a ship or tail of an airplane [abaft, aft]</p><p><i>adv.</i> (of a ship or an airplane) behind</p><p><b>ne povezano s prsnom kostom ili prsnom kostom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not connected to the sternum or breastbone</p><p><b>asteriod, asteroid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous small celestial bodies composed of rock and metal that move around the sun (mainly between the orbits of Mars and Jupiter)</p><p><i>adj.</i> shaped like a star [star-shaped]</p><p><b>asteroidni pojas</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the region of interplanetary space between Mars and Jupiter where most asteroids are found</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili nalik asteroidu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or resembling an asteroid</p><p><b>morske zvijezde (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sea stars [class Asteroidea]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) jedna od 7 Plejada