ny celestial body</p><p><i>n.</i> a distinctive but intangible quality surrounding a person or thing [air, aura]</p><p><b>atmosferski, atmosferska, atmosfersko</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or located in the atmosphere [atmospherical]</p><p><b>atmosferski uvjeti, vremenski uvjeti, vrijeme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the atmospheric conditions that comprise the state of the atmosphere in terms of temperature and wind and clouds and precipitation [conditions, weather, weather condition]</p><p><b>električni praznici u atmosferi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electrical discharges in the atmosphere</p><p><b>atmosferska pojava, atmosferski fenomen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a physical phenomenon associated with the atmosphere</p><p><b>pritisak koji vrši atmosfera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the pressure exerted by the atmosphere [air pressure, pressure]</p><p><b>atmosfera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the weather or climate at some place [atmosphere]</p><p><b>zvuk škricanja ili ščepanja uzrokovan električnim smetnjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crackling or hissing noise caused by electrical interference [atmospherics, static]</p><p><b>atmosferski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or located in the atmosphere [atmospheric]</p><p><b>atmosferska pražnjenja, atmosferske smetnje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crackling or hissing noise caused by electrical interference [atmospheric static, static]</p><p><b>jesti kao kaša ili kao tanka kaša (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> eaten as mush or as a thin gruel</p><p><b>atol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an island consisting of a circular coral reef surrounding a lagoon</p><p><b>atom, atomski, atomska, atomske, djelić, djeličak, komadičak, zrnce, zrno, čestica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics and chemistry) the smallest component of an element having the chemical properties of the element</p><p><i>n.</i> (nontechnical usage) a tiny piece of anything [corpuscle, molecule, mote, particle, speck]</p><p><b>atomska bomba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear weapon in which enormous energy is released by nuclear fission (splitting the nuclei of a heavy element like uranium 235 or plutonium 239) [A-bomb, atomic bomb, fission bomb, plutonium bomb]</p><p><b>znanstveni instrument koji povećava kinetičku energiju napunjenih čestica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scientific instrument that increases the kinetic energy of charged particles [accelerator, particle accelerator]</p><p><b>atomska bomba</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bomb with atomic weapons [nuke]</p><p><b>atomiski, atomski, nuklearan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or comprising atoms</p><p><i>adj.</i> (weapons) deriving destructive energy from the release of atomic energy [nuclear]</p><p><i>adj.</i> immeasurably small</p><p><b>atomska bomba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear weapon in which enormous energy is released by nuclear fission (splitting the nuclei of a heavy element like uranium 235 or plutonium 239) [A-bomb, atom bomb, fission bomb, plutonium bomb]</p><p><b>časovnik koji dobiva svoju vremensku skali iz vibracija atoma ili molekula (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a timepiece that derives its time scale from the vibration of atoms or molecules</p><p><b>oralna doza radioaktivne tvari koja se koristi u liječenju i dijagnostici raka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oral dose of radioactive substance used in treatment and diagnosis of cancer</p><p><b>atomska energija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the energy released by a nuclear reaction [nuclear energy]</p><p><b>bivša izvršna agencija (od 1946. do 1974.) koja je bila odgovorna za istraživanje atomske energije i njene mirne upotrebe u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former executive agency (from 1946 to 1974) that was responsible for research into atomic energy and its peacetime uses in the United States [AEC]</p><p><b>Eksplozija atomske bombe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the explosion of an atomic bomb [nuclear explosion]</p><p><b>(kemija) masa atoma kemijskog elementa izražena u jedinicama atomske mase (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) the mass of an atom of a chemical element expressed in atomic mass units [atomic weight, relative atomic mass]</p><p><b>Jedinica za masno izražavanje masa atoma ili molekula (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unit of mass for expressing masses of atoms or molecules</p><p><b>redoslijed elementa u Mendelejevoj tabeli elemenata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the order of an element in Mendeleyev's table of the elements</p><p><b>Ne-metalni univalentni element koji je obično bezbojan i bez mirisa, vrlo zapaljivi diatomski plin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nonmetallic univalent element that is normally a colorless and odorless highly flammable diatomic gas [H, hydrogen]</p><p><b>bezbojan, bez mirisa plinasti element koji u vakuumskoj cijevi daje crveno svjetlo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless odorless gaseous element that give a red glow in a vacuum tube [Ne, neon]</p><p><b>Fm, atomski broj 100, fermij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radioactive transuranic metallic element produced by bombarding plutonium with neutrons [Fm, fermium]</p><p><b>Md, atomski broj 101, mendelevij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radioactive transuranic element synthesized by bombarding einsteinium with alpha particles (Md is the current symbol for mendelevium but Mv was formerly the symbol) [Md, Mv, mendelevium]</p><p><b>radioaktivni transuranski element sintetiziran bombardiranjem kurija ugljikovim jonima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radioactive transuranic element synthesized by bombarding curium with carbon ions [No, nobelium]</p><p><b>Lw, atomski broj 103, lawrencij, lorensij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radioactive transuranic element synthesized from californium [Lr, lawrencium]</p><p><b>Rf, atomski broj 104, ruthefordij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radioactive transuranic element which has been synthesized [Rf, Unq, element 104, rutherfordium, unnilquadium]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a transuranic element [Db, dubnium, element 105, hahnium]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a transuranic el