navanja ili razumijevanja značenja izgovorenih riječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inability to recognize or understand the meaning of spoken words</p><p><b>oštećenje razumijevanja govornog jezika koje nije uzrokovano gubitkom sluha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an impairment in understanding spoken language that is not attributable to hearing loss [acoustic aphasia, word deafness]</p><p><b>Svaka komponenta sluha uključujući vanjsko, srednje i unutarnje uho. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> all of the components of the organ of hearing including the outer and middle and inner ears</p><p><b>Kortikalno područje koje prima slušne informacije iz medijalnog genikularnog tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cortical area that receives auditory information from the medial geniculate body [auditory cortex]</p><p><b>u bilo kojem od prolaza u vanjskom uhu od sluznice do timpanske membrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of the passages in the outer ear from the auricle to the tympanic membrane [acoustic meatus, auditory meatus, ear canal, external auditory canal]</p><p><b>dio mozga (u prevoju moždane kore temporalnog režnja na obje strane mozga) koji prima impulse iz uha putem slušnog živca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of the brain (in a fold of the cerebral cortex of the temporal lobe on both sides of the brain) that receives impulses from the ear by way of the auditory nerve</p><p><b>auditorna komunikacija, slušna komunikacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> communication that relies on hearing</p><p><b>slušna kora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cortical area that receives auditory information from the medial geniculate body [auditory area]</p><p><b>iluzorno slušno shvaćanje čudnih neverbalnih zvukova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> illusory auditory perception of strange nonverbal sounds [acousma]</p><p><b>Neobična oštrina sluha zbog povećane razdražljivosti senzornog neuronskog mehanizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal acuteness of hearing due to increased irritability of the sensory neural mechanism [hyperacusia, hyperacusis]</p><p><b>mentalna slika koja je slična slušnoj percepciji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mental image that is similar to an auditory perception</p><p><b>u bilo kojem od prolaza u vanjskom uhu od sluznice do timpanske membrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of the passages in the outer ear from the auricle to the tympanic membrane [acoustic meatus, auditory canal, ear canal, external auditory canal]</p><p><b>sposobnost slušanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to hear [audition, auditory sense, hearing, sense of hearing]</p><p><b>slušni živac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a composite sensory nerve supplying the hair cells of the vestibular organ and the hair cells of the cochlea [acoustic nerve, eighth cranial nerve, nervus vestibulocochlearis, vestibulocochlear nerve]</p><p><b>slušna koščica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ossicles of the middle ear that transmit acoustic vibrations from the eardrum to the inner ear</p><p><b>percepcija zvuka kao značajnog fenomena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the perception of sound as a meaningful phenomenon [sound perception]</p><p><b>sluh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the subjective sensation of hearing something [sound]</p><p><b>sposobnost slušanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to hear [audition, auditory modality, hearing, sense of hearing]</p><p><b>Osjetni sustav za sluh (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sensory system for hearing</p><p><b>bilo koja od parnih cijevi koje povezuju srednje uho s nosopharynxom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of the paired tubes connecting the middle ears to the nasopharynx [Eustachian tube]</p><p><b>Ornitolog i umjetnik iz Sjedinjenih Država (rođen na Haitiju) poznat po slikama ptica Amerike (1785-1851) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States ornithologist and artist (born in Haiti) noted for his paintings of birds of America (1785-1851) [John James Audubon]</p><p><b>obični čvor zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common warbler of western North America [Audubon's warbler, Dendroica auduboni]</p>