os primigenius, urus]</p><p><b>polarna svjetlost, zora, aurora, božica jutra</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first light of day [break of day, break of the day, cockcrow, dawn, dawning, daybreak, dayspring, first light, morning, sunrise, sunup]</p><p><i>n.</i> an atmospheric phenomenon consisting of bands of light caused by charged solar particles following the earth's magnetic lines of force</p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman mythology) goddess of the dawn</p><p><b>aurora na južnoj hemisferi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the aurora of the southern hemisphere [southern lights]</p><p><b>aurora na sjevernoj hemisferi, polarna svjetlost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the aurora of the northern hemisphere [northern lights]</p><p><b>ionosferski, jutarnji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the atmospheric phenomenon auroras</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of the dawn [aurorean]</p><p><b>karakteristika zore (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of the dawn [auroral]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medical instrument consisting of a magnifying lens and light [auriscope, otoscope]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s zlatom ili koje sadrže ili su izvedene od zlata (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or containing or derived from gold [auric]</p><p><b>nacistički koncentracijski logor za Židove u jugozapadnoj Poljskoj tijekom Drugog svjetskog rata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Nazi concentration camp for Jews in southwestern Poland during World War II</p><p><b>pregled</b></p><p><i>v.</i> examine by auscultation</p><p><b>auskultatorno, oskultacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> listening to sounds within the body (usually with a stethoscope)</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s auskultiranjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to auscultation</p><p><b>(stari Rim) vjerski dužnosnik koji je tumačio znakove kako bi vodio javni sustav (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (ancient Rome) a religious official who interpreted omens to guide public policy [augur]</p><p><b>označavaju, kao što je znak ili znak, Počnite na način koji vam donosi sreću. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> indicate, as with a sign or an omen [augur, betoken, bode, forecast, foreshadow, foretell, omen, portend, predict, prefigure, presage, prognosticate]</p><p><i>v.</i> commence in a manner calculated to bring good luck</p><p><b>gatanje, okrilje, predznak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a favorable omen</p><p><b>okrilje, pokroviteljstvo, predviđanje, predznak, egida, patronat, zaštitništvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> kindly endorsement and guidance [aegis, protection]</p><p><b>povoljan, sretan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> auguring favorable circumstances and good luck</p><p><b>povoljan, sretan (od &quot;auspicious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an auspicious manner [propitiously]</p><p><b>povoljan, sretan (od &quot;auspicious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the favorable quality of strongly indicating a successful result [propitiousness]</p><p><b>rodom ili stanovnikom Australije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Australia [Australian]</p><p><b>Engleska romanopisac poznat po svojim pronicljivim portretima obitelji srednje klase (1775-1817) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English novelist noted for her insightful portrayals of middle-class families (1775-1817) [Jane Austen]</p><p><b>austenit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solid solution of ferric carbide or carbon in iron</p><p><b>austenitičan, austenitik</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> composed of austenite</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom mangansa od 10 do 14%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a steel with a relatively large component (10-14%) of manganese [manganese steel]</p><p><b>austenitni čelik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> steel that has enough nickel and chromium or manganese to retain austenite at atmospheric temperatures</p><p><b>asketski, isposnički, jednostavan, ljut, mrk, opor, oštar, ozbiljan, strog</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> severely simple [severe, stark, stern]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a stern or strict bearing or demeanor [stern]</p><p><i>adj.</i> practicing great self-denial [ascetic, ascetical, spartan]</p><p><b>asketski, isposnički, jednostavan, ljut, mrk, opor, oštar, ozbiljan, strog (od &quot;austere&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an austere fashion</p><p><b>asketski, isposnički, jednostavan, ljut, mrk, opor, oštar, ozbiljan, strog (od &quot;austere&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extreme plainness [severeness, severity]</p><p><b>jednostavnost, neprijaznost, oporost, strogost, surovost, askeza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of great self-denial (especially refraining from worldly pleasures) [asceticism, nonindulgence]</p><p><b>grad u Češkoj Republici, odlučujuća bitka tijekom Napoleonskih kampanja (1805) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in Czech Republic</p><p><i>n.</i> a decisive battle during the Napoleonic campaigns (1805) [battle of Austerlitz]</p><p><b>Glavni grad države Texas na rijeci Colorado (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> state capital of Texas on the Colorado River [capital of Texas]</p><p><b>jedan od rimokatoličkih pustinjaka Sv. Augustina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the Roman Catholic hermits of Saint Augustine</p><p><b>Augustinski red. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Augustinian monastic order</p><p><b>južni, obrazac brodarskog ugovora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Argentina</p><p><i>adj.</i> of the south or coming from the south</p><p><b>lanc malih otoka u Francuskoj Polineziji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chain of small islands in French Polynesia [Tubuai Islands]</p><p><b>Australazija, Oceanija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australia, New Zealand, and neighboring islands in the South Pacific</p><p><b>australazijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or found in Australasia</p><p><b>Australia, Australija, Australija.</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nation occupying the whole of the Australian continent [Commonwealth of Australia]</p><p><i>n.</i> the smallest continent</p><p><b>Australac, Australka, australski, Australijanac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Australia [Aussie]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Austronesian languages spoken by Aus