ettle tree]</p><p><b>bilo koje od nekoliko visokih australskih stabala rod Laportea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several tall Australian trees of the genus Laportea [Australian nettle]</p><p><b>Južnoafrička zimzelena djelimično drvena loza uzgajana zbog svojih grama ružičastih ljubičastih cvijeća koje slijede jestivi čunjevi poput graha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African evergreen partly woody vine grown for its clusters of rosy purple flowers followed by edible pods like snap beans [Dipogon lignosus, Dolichos lignosus]</p><p><b>obično australsko stablo koje se široko uzgaja kao ukrasno u tropskim područjima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common Australian tree widely grown as an ornamental in tropical regions [Casuarina equisetfolia]</p><p><b>biljka koja ima zelenu vrč i čep s šarenama i s crvenim rubovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a carnivorous perennial herb having a green pitcher and hinged lid both with red edges [Cephalotus follicularis]</p><p><b>Visoka australska trska poput trske koja se ponekad koristi za sijeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall Australian reedlike grass sometimes used for hay [Calamagrostic quadriseta]</p><p><b>vrsta morskih lavova pronađena u Australiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of sea lion found in Australia [Zalophus lobatus]</p><p><b>jedna od nekoliko država koje čine Australiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the several states constituting Australia</p><p><b>duge noge, tri prsta, ptica u bračastih močvarama Australije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> long-legged three-toed wading bird of brackish marshes of Australia [stilt]</p><p><b>zelena stabla iz Australije koja daje tamno žuto drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen of Australia yielding a dark yellow wood [Rhodosphaera rhodanthema, Rhus rhodanthema]</p><p><b>biljka koja se nalazi u području područja s velikim brojem špilja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sedgelike spring-flowering herb having clustered flowers covered with woolly hairs [Anigozanthus manglesii, kangaroo's-foot, kangaroo's paw, kangaroo-foot plant, kangaroo paw]</p><p><b>mala sivo-žičasta vrsta terijera iz Australije slična kairn (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small greyish wire-haired breed of terrier from Australia similar to the cairn</p><p><b>mala australska golubica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Australian dove [Stictopelia cuneata, turtledove]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko izumrlih humanoidnih dvostrogih primata s relativno malim mozgom iz roda Australopithecus, od ili pripadaju rodu hominida Australopithecus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several extinct humanlike bipedal primates with relatively small brains of the genus Australopithecus</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or belonging to the hominid genus Australopithecus</p><p><b>australopitek</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct genus of African hominid [genus Australopithecus]</p><p><b>fosilije pronađene u Etiopiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fossils found in Ethiopia</p><p><b>gracijalni hominid južne Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gracile hominid of southern Africa</p><p><b>hominid s velikim zubima iz istočne Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large-toothed hominid of eastern Africa</p><p><b>veliki zubni hominid južne Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large-toothed hominid of southern Africa</p><p><b>Austrija, austrijski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountainous republic in central Europe [Oesterreich, Republic of Austria]</p><p><b>Austro-Ugarska</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a geographical area in central and eastern Europe</p><p><b>Austrijanac, Austrijanka, austrijski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Austria</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Austria or its people or culture</p><p><b>glavni grad i najveći grad Austrije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Austria [Vienna, capital of Austria]</p><p><b>monetarna jedinica u Austriji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Austria</p><p><b>nekada osnovna jedinica novca u Austriji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> formerly the basic unit of money in Austria [schilling]</p><p><b>vrsta graška porije