ti autentičnost, identificirati, ovjeravati, ovjeriti, ovjeroviti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> establish the authenticity of something</p><p><b>ovjeren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> established as genuine [attested, documented]</p><p><b>autorizacija, ovjera, ovjera vjerodostojnosti, provjera, provjera autentičnosti, provjera identiteta, provjera valjanosti, utvrđivanje istinitosti, utvrđivanje vjerodostojnosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mark on an article of trade to indicate its origin and authenticity [assay-mark, hallmark]</p><p><i>n.</i> validating the authenticity of something or someone [certification]</p><p><b>provjeritelj (vjerodostojnosti), provjeritelj vjerodostojnosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who determines authenticity (as of works of art) or who guarantees validity [appraiser]</p><p><b>autentične, autentičnost, ispravnost, istinitost, izvornost, vjerodostojnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> undisputed credibility [genuineness, legitimacy]</p><p><b>autor, autorica, književnik, krivac, pisac, programer, stvaralac, tvorac, začetnik, autora, spisatelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> writes (books or stories or articles or the like) professionally (for pay) [writer]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who originates or causes or initiates something [generator, source]</p><p><i>v.</i> be the author of</p><p><b>ime koje se pojavljuje na naslovnoj stranici kako bi se identificirao autor djela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the name that appears on the by-line to identify the author of a work [writer's name]</p><p><b>Žena autorka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman author</p><p><b>autorski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or by or typical of an author [auctorial]</p><p><b>jezik za stvaranje, jezik za stvaranje višemedijskog materijala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> software that can be used to develop interactive computer programs without the technically demanding task of computer programming</p><p><b>odobrenje, ovlast, ovlaštenje, autorizacija, opunomoćenje, punomoć</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a document giving an official instruction or command [authorization, mandate]</p><p><i>n.</i> the power or right to give orders or make decisions [authority, authorization, dominance, potency, say-so]</p><p><i>n.</i> official permission or approval [authority, authorization, sanction]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of conferring legality or sanction or formal warrant [authorization, empowerment]</p><p><b>autorizirati, dopustiti, odobriti, ovlastiti, opunomoćiti, amenovati, dopuštati, dozvoliti, dozvoljavati, odobravati, ozakoniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give or delegate power or authority to [authorize, empower]</p><p><i>v.</i> grant authorization or clearance for [authorize, clear, pass]</p><p><b>dopušten, odobren, ovlašten</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> endowed with authority [authorized]</p><p><i>adj.</i> sanctioned by established authority [authoritative, authorized]</p><p><b>autorizirati, dopustiti, odobriti, ovlastiti (od &quot;authorise&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an authority who authorizes (people or actions) [authorizer]</p><p><b>autoritaran, autoritativac, autoritarna, autoritarni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who behaves in a tyrannical manner [dictator]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of an absolute ruler or absolute rule [autocratic, despotic, dictatorial, tyrannic, tyrannical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> expecting unquestioning obedience [dictatorial, overbearing]</p><p><b>autoritarni režim</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government that concentrates political power in an authority not responsible to the people [authoritarian state]</p><p><b>Vlada koja koncentriše političku moć u autoritetu koji nije odgovoran ljudima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government that concentrates political power in an authority not responsible to the people [authoritarian regime]</p><p><b>autoritarnost, autoritarizam, despotizam, diktatura, staljinizam, totalitarizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of government in which the ruler is an absolute dictator (not restricted by a constitution or laws or opposition etc.) [Caesarism, Stalinism, absolutism, despotism, dictatorship, monocracy, one-man rule, shogunate, totalitarianism, tyranny]</p><p><b>autoritativan, mjerodavan, zapovjednički, zvaničan, utjecajan, važan, klasičan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having authority or ascendancy or influence [important]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of recognized authority or excellence [definitive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> sanctioned by established authority [authorised, authorized]</p><p><b>autoritativno, zvanično</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an authoritative and magisterial manner [magisterially]</p><p><b>državna tijela, institucijama, institucije, nadležno tijelo, organ vlasti, službe, uprava, uprave, vlast, vlasti, vlastima, vlašću, režim, vlada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the organization that is the governing authority of a political unit [government, regime]</p><p><b>autoritet, direkcija, ingerencije, mjerodavnost, moć, nadležnost, nalog, ovlast, ovlaštenik, ovlaštenje, punomoć, punovažnost, rukovodstvo, tijelo, uprava, ustanova, vlast, vlasti, uprave, agencija, odjel, ured, vladina agencija, temeljna knjiga, temeljno djelo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the power or right to give orders or make decisions [authorisation, authorization, dominance, potency, say-so]</p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) persons who exercise (administrative) control over others</p><p><i>n.</i> an expert whose views are taken as definitive</p><p><i>n.</i> freedom from doubt [assurance, confidence, self-assurance, self-confidence, sureness]</p><p><i>n.</i> an administrative unit of government [agency, bureau, federal agency, government agency, office]</p><p><i>n.</i> official permission or approval [authorisation, authorization, sanction]</p><p><i>n.</i> an authoritative written work</p><p><b>netko tko je smatran autoriteta od strane nekoga drugog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is regarded as an authority by someone else</p><p><b>autorizacija, autorizacijski, dopuštenje, dozvola, odobrenje, ovlast, ovlaštenje, punomoć, raspodjela, opunomoćenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a document giving an official instruction or command [authorisation, mandate]</p><p><i>n.</i> the power or right to give orders or make decisions [authorisation, authority, dominance, potency, say-so]</p><p><i>n.</i> official permission or approval [authorisation, authority, sanction]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of conferring legality or sanction or formal warrant [authorisation, empowerment]</p><p><b>autorizirati, dopustiti, objasniti, odobriti, opunomočiti, opunomoćiti, ovlastiti, ozakoniti, pravdati, amenovati, dopuštati, dozvoliti, dozvoljavati, odobravati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> grant authorization or clearance for [authorise, clear, pass]</p><p><i>v.</i> give or delegate power or authority to [authorise, empower]</p><p><b>autoriziran, dopušten, dopušteno, nadležan, odobren, opunomoćen, ovlašten, ovlašteni, ozakonjen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> endowed with authority [authorised]</p><p><i>adj.</i> sanctioned by established authority [authorised, authoritative]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom (b) ovog članka, društvo može imati: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the maximum number of shares authorized under the terms of a corporation's articles of incorporation [authorized stock, capital stock]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom (b) ovog članka, društvo može imati: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the maximum number of shares authorized under the terms of a corporation's articles of incorporation [authorized shares, capital stock]</p><p><b>Engleski prijevod Biblije izdan 1611. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an English translation of the Bible published in 1611 [King James Bible, King James Version]</p><p><b>opunomoćitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an authority who authorizes (people or actions) [authoriser]</p><p><b>autorstvo, začetništvo, pisanje, pisano stvaralaštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of creating written works [composition, penning, writing]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of initiating a new idea or theory or writing [paternity]</p><p><b>autizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychiatry) an abnormal absorption with the self</p><p><b>autistički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of or affected with autism</p><p><b>auto, automatski, automatsko podešavanje, automobil, automobilski, samo-</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a motor vehicle with four wheels [automobile, car, machine, motorcar]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an accessory for an automobile</p><p><b>tvrtka koja proizvodi i prodaje automobile. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a company that makes and sells automobiles [car company]</p><p><b>tvornica u kojoj se proizvode automobili. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a factory where automobiles are manufactured [automobile factory, car factory]</p><p><b>socijalna kontrola ostvarena kao manifestacija vlastite volje ili opće suglasnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> social control achieved as a manifestation of self-will or general consent</p><p><b>osobni kredit za kupovinu automobila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a personal loan to purchase an automobile [automobile loan, car loan]</p><p><b>Poduzeće koje se bavi proizvodnjom automobila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a business engaged in the manufacture of automobiles [auto manufacturer, automaker, car maker, car manufacturer, carmaker]</p><p><b>Poduzeće koje se bavi proizvodnjom automobila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a business engaged in the manufacture of automobiles [auto maker, automaker, car maker, car manufacturer, carmaker]</p><p><b>Znanost izrade i popravke automobila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the craft of building and repairing automobiles</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a component of an automobile [car part]</p><p><b>trka između (obično visoko-izvršavajućih) automobila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a race between (usually high-performance) automobiles [automobile race, car race]</p><p><b>automobilizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sport of racing automobiles [car racing]</p><p><b>guma koja se sas