oda, neovisnost, samodovoljnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> immunity from arbitrary exercise of authority: political independence [liberty]</p><p><i>n.</i> personal independence [self-direction, self-reliance, self-sufficiency]</p><p><b>biljka sposobna sintetizirati vlastitu hranu iz jednostavnih organskih tvari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant capable of synthesizing its own food from simple organic substances [autophytic plant, autotroph, autotrophic organism]</p><p><b>od ili povezanih s organizmama (kao što su zelene biljke) koji mogu proizvoditi složena organska hranljiva jedinjenja iz jednostavnih anorganskih izvora fotosintezom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to organisms (as green plants) that can make complex organic nutritive compounds from simple inorganic sources by photosynthesis [autotrophic]</p><p><b>biljka sposobna sintetizirati vlastitu hranu iz jednostavnih organskih tvari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant capable of synthesizing its own food from simple organic substances [autophyte, autotroph, autotrophic organism]</p><p><b>automatski pilot, sprava koja održava kurs broda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cognitive state in which you act without self-awareness [automatic pilot]</p><p><i>n.</i> a navigational device that automatically keeps ships or planes or spacecraft on a steady course [automatic pilot, robot pilot]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili uključen u autoplastiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or involved in autoplasty</p><p><b>tkivo koje se uzima iz jednog mjesta i presađuje na drugo mjesto na istoj osobi, operacija popravka tkiva iz drugog dijela tijela pacijenta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tissue that is taken from one site and grafted to another site on the same person [autograft]</p><p><i>n.</i> surgical repair by using tissue from another part of the patient's own body</p><p><b>autopsija, obdukcija, seciranje leša</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an examination and dissection of a dead body to determine cause of death or the changes produced by diseas