errymaking [bacchanalian, bacchic, carousing, orgiastic]</p><p><b>orgija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an orgiastic festival in ancient Greece in honor of Dionysus (= Bacchus) [Dionysia]</p><p><i>n.</i> a wild gathering involving excessive drinking and promiscuity [bacchanal, debauch, debauchery, drunken revelry, orgy, riot, saturnalia]</p><p><b>bakantski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> used of riotously drunken merrymaking [bacchanal, bacchic, carousing, orgiastic]</p><p><b>bakant</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who engages in drinking bouts [bacchanal, drunken reveler, drunken reveller]</p><p><i>n.</i> a drunken reveller [bacchanal]</p><p><i>n.</i> (classical mythology) a priest or votary of Bacchus</p><p><b>bakantkinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (classical mythology) a priestess or votary of Bacchus</p><p><b>bakant (od &quot;bacchant&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or resembling a bacchanalian reveler</p><p><b>grmovi na zapadnoj hemisferi koji često imaju cveće koje miriše na med i nakon toga imaju šećerne glave poput trnja s malenim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubs of western hemisphere often having honey-scented flowers followed by silky thistlelike heads of tiny fruits [genus Baccharis]</p><p><b>grm solenih močvara istočne i južne središnje Sjeverne Amerike i Zapadne Indije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shrub of salt marshes of eastern and south central North America and West Indies [consumption weed, cotton-seed tree, groundsel bush, groundsel tree]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjen zimzelena grm od jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s glavama cvijeća u listovitom paniclu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely spreading evergreen shrub of southwestern United States with flower heads in a leafy panicle [chaparral broom, coyote brush, coyote bush, kidney wort]</p><p><b>Kalifornijskog grma s tankim listovitim izdancima koji su važni za browsing za jeleena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> California shrub with slender leafy shoots that are important browse for mule deer [mule fat]</p><p><b>ko