ali ljudi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Magadhan language spoken by the Bengali people [Bengali]</p><p><b>muslimanska republika u južnoj Aziji graniči s Indijom na sjeveru i zapadu i istoku i Bengalskim zaljevom na jugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Muslim republic in southern Asia bordered by India to the north and west and east and the Bay of Bengal to the south [Bangladesh, East Pakistan, People's Republic of Bangladesh]</p><p><b>Bangladeš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Muslim republic in southern Asia bordered by India to the north and west and east and the Bay of Bengal to the south [Bangla Desh, East Pakistan, People's Republic of Bangladesh]</p><p><b>rodom ili stanovnikom Bangladeša, od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Bangladeš ili njegov narod ili jezik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Bangladesh</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Bangladesh or its people or language [East Pakistani]</p><p><b>monetarna jedinica u Bangladešu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Bangladesh</p><p><b>grivna, narukvica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> jewelry worn around the wrist for decoration [bracelet]</p><p><i>n.</i> cheap showy jewelry or ornament on clothing [bauble, fallal, gaud, gewgaw, novelty, trinket]</p><p><b>grad u istočnom središnjem Mainu na rijeci Penobscot, Univerzitetski grad na sjeverozapadu Walesa na Menai tjesnacu, Grad u jugoistočnom dijelu Sjeverne Irske. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in east central Maine on the Penobscot River</p><p><i>n.</i> a university town in northwestern Wales on the Menai Strait</p><p><i>n.</i> a town in southeastern Northern Ireland</p><p><b>trkaći konj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a horse bred for racing [race horse, racehorse]</p><p><b>Bangui</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of the Central African Republic [capital of Central Africa]</p><p><b>Drvo u istočnoj Indiji koje izlazi iz zraka i koje raste u zemlju i stvara dodatna debla., Ovu je uzela moja žena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian tree t