nding activities [banking company, banking concern, depository financial institution]</p><p><i>n.</i> a long ridge or pile</p><p><i>n.</i> an arrangement of similar objects in a row or in tiers</p><p><i>n.</i> a supply or stock held in reserve for future use (especially in emergencies)</p><p><i>n.</i> the funds held by a gambling house or the dealer in some gambling games</p><p><i>n.</i> a slope in the turn of a road or track [camber, cant]</p><p><i>n.</i> a container (usually with a slot in the top) for keeping money at home [coin bank, money box, savings bank]</p><p><i>n.</i> a building in which the business of banking transacted [bank building]</p><p><i>n.</i> a flight maneuver</p><p><i>v.</i> tip laterally</p><p><i>v.</i> enclose with a bank</p><p><i>v.</i> do business with a bank or keep an account at a bank</p><p><i>v.</i> act as the banker in a game or in gambling</p><p><i>v.</i> be in the banking business</p><p><i>v.</i> put into a bank account [deposit]</p><p><i>v.</i> cover with ashes so to control the rate of burning</p><p><i>v.</i> have faith or confidence in [bet, calculate, count, depend, look, reckon, rely, swear]</p><p><b>bankovni račun</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fund that a customer has entrusted to a bank and from which the customer can make withdrawals</p><p><b>novčanica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of paper money (especially one issued by a central bank) [Federal Reserve note, bank note, banker's bill, banknote, bill, government note, greenback, note]</p><p><b>banka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a building in which the business of banking transacted [bank]</p><p><b>kreditna kartica koju je izdala banka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a credit card issued by a bank</p><p><b>Povelja o radu banke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a charter authorizing the operation of a bank</p><p><b>ček</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a written order directing a bank to pay money [check, cheque]</p><p><b>bankarski službenik, banknovni činovnik, bankovni činovnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an employee of a bank who 