ana kada su banke zatvorene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several weekdays when banks are closed</p><p><b>Identifikacijski broj koji se sastoji od dvostrukog koda dodijeljenog bankama i uštedničkim udruženjima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an identification number consisting of a two-part code assigned to banks and savings associations [ABA transit number, BIN]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je kreditni račun u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, to znači da se kreditni račun ne može koristiti za plaćanje kreditnih računa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the maximum credit that a customer is allowed [credit line, line, line of credit, personal credit line, personal line of credit]</p><p><b>zajam od banke</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loan made by a bank</p><p><b>upravitelj podružnice banke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> manager of a branch office of a bank</p><p><b>Švalka iz sjeverne hemisfere koja se gnijezda u tunelima iskopanim u glini ili pesku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> swallow of the northern hemisphere that nests in tunnels dug in clay or sand banks [Riparia riparia, bank swallow, sand martin]</p><p><b>banknota, novčanica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of paper money (especially one issued by a central bank) [Federal Reserve note, bank bill, banker's bill, banknote, bill, government note, greenback, note]</p><p><b>Centralna banka Engleske i Walesa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the central bank of England and Wales</p><p><b>Centralna banka Japana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the central bank of Japan</p><p><b>Svaka država članica može odrediti da je to u skladu s člankom 5. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the discount rate fixed by a central bank</p><p><b>pljačkaš banke</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a robber of banks</p><p><b>Koordinirani postupci ulagača koji pokušavaju povući novac iz banke jer misle da će propasti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the concerted action of depositors who try to withdraw their money from a bank because they think it will fail</p><p><b>k