ce of paper money (especially one issued by a central bank) [Federal Reserve note, bank bill, bank note, banknote, bill, government note, greenback, note]</p><p><b>"Kreditno pismo" znači akreditiv izdan od strane banke ili ekspresne tvrtke koji se plaća na prijenos bilo kojem dopisniku izdavatelja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a letter of credit issued by a bank or express company that is payable on presentation to any correspondent of the issuer [traveler's check, traveller's check]</p><p><b>bankovna mjenica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a draft drawn by a bank against funds deposited in another bank [bank draft]</p><p><b>neograničena američka glumica (1903-1968) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> uninhibited United States actress (1903-1968) [Tallulah Bankhead]</p><p><b>divovski brodski crvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> giant shipworms [genus Bankia]</p><p><b>divovski brodski crv sa pacifičke obale Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> giant shipworm of the Pacific coast of North America [giant northwest shipworm]</p><p><b>bankarski, bankarstvo, bankovni, bankovni poslovi, krivina puta, kut zaokreta, obavljanje bankovnih poslova, ugao zaokreta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> engaging in the business of keeping money for savings and checking accounts or for exchange or for issuing loans and credit etc.</p><p><i>n.</i> transacting business with a bank</p><p><b>banka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a financial institution that accepts deposits and channels the money into lending activities [bank, banking concern, depository financial institution]</p><p><b>banka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a financial institution that accepts deposits and channels the money into lending activities [bank, banking company, depository financial institution]</p><p><b>bilo koji kockanje u kojem se klade protiv kockarnice ili distributera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any gambling game in which bets are laid against the gambling house or the dealer</p><p><b>banke zajedno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> banks collectively [banking system]</p><p><b>bankarski sustav, bankovni sustav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> banks collectively [banking industry]</p><p><b>banknota, novčanica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of paper money (especially one issued by a central bank) [Federal Reserve note, bank bill, bank note, banker's bill, bill, government note, greenback, note]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog, osigurati dovoljno sredstava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a roll of currency notes (often taken as the resources of a person or business etc.) [roll]</p><p><i>v.</i> provide with sufficient funds</p><p><b>bankrot, bankrotirati, otići u stečaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who has insufficient assets to cover their debts [insolvent]</p><p><i>v.</i> reduce to bankruptcy [break, ruin, smash]</p><p><i>adj.</i> financially ruined [belly-up]</p><p><b>bankrot, stečaj, stečajni, stečajnom, propast, steeaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of complete lack of some abstract property</p><p><i>n.</i> inability to discharge all your debts as they come due [failure]</p><p><i>n.</i> a legal process intended to insure equality among the creditors of a corporation declared to be insolvent</p><p><b>banaka, bankama, banke</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English botanist who accompanied Captain Cook on his first voyage to the Pacific Ocean (1743-1820) [Sir Joseph Banks]</p><p><b>bilo koji grm ili drvo iz roda Banksia s alternativnim kožnim listovima, žutim cvjetovima često u najozbiljnije glave i koničnim plodovima s krilatim sjemenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any shrub or tree of the genus Banksia having alternate leathery leaves apetalous yellow flowers often in showy heads and conelike fruit with 