dependence of Scotland</p><p><b>javna najava o predlaženom braku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a public announcement of a proposed marriage</p><p><b>banket, domjenak, gozba, gostiti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ceremonial dinner party for many people [feast]</p><p><i>n.</i> a meal that is well prepared and greatly enjoyed [feast, spread]</p><p><i>v.</i> provide a feast or banquet for [feast, junket]</p><p><i>v.</i> partake in a feast or banquet [feast, junket]</p><p><b>pjesma (ponekad improvizirana) koju pjevaju gosti na banketu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a song (sometimes improvised) sung by guests at a banquet [scolion]</p><p><b>banket, domjenak, gozba (od &quot;banquet&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> eating an elaborate meal (often accompanied by entertainment) [feasting]</p><p><b>čepirana klanica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an upholstered bench</p><p><b>duh koji navješćuje smrt u kući, glasnica smrti, vila vjesnica smrti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Irish folklore) a female spirit who wails to warn of impending death [banshie]</p><p><b>(Irski folklor) ženski duh koji je zažalio upozoravajući na prijeteću smrt (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Irish folklore) a female spirit who wails to warn of impending death [banshee]</p><p><b>bilo koje od različitih malih pasmina ptica, vrlo mali (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various small breeds of fowl</p><p><i>adj.</i> very small [diminutive, flyspeck, lilliputian, midget, petite, tiny]</p><p><b>Teži 115-126 funti., amaterski boksač koji ne teži više od 119 funti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> weighs 115-126 pounds</p><p><i>n.</i> an amateur boxer who weighs no more than 119 pounds</p><p><b>divlji vol Malejskog arhipelaga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wild ox of the Malay Archipelago [Bos banteng, banting, tsine]</p><p><b>ćaskati, podsmijevati, šala, zadirkivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> light teasing repartee [backchat, give-and-take, raillery]</p><p><i>v.</i> be silly or tease one another [chaff, jolly, josh, kid]</p><p><b>ćaskati, podsmijevati, šala, zadirkivati (od &