i na Barbadu, od ili povezane s ili karakteristične za Barbados ili njegove stanovnike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Barbados</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Barbados or its inhabitants</p><p><b>Barbados</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a parliamentary democracy on the island of Barbados</p><p><i>n.</i> easternmost of the West Indies about 300 miles to the north of Venezuela</p><p><b>tropski američki grm s jestivom kiselom crvenom voćem nalik trešnje, kiselo crveno ili žuto voće poput trešnje tropskog američkog grma vrlo bogato vitaminom C. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American shrub bearing edible acid red fruit resembling cherries [Malpighia glabra, Surinam cherry, West Indian cherry, acerola]</p><p><i>n.</i> acid red or yellow cherry-like fruit of a tropical American shrub very rich in vitamin C [West Indian cherry, acerola, surinam cherry]</p><p><b>osnovna jedinica novca na Barbadu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Barbados</p><p><b>Zapadni indijski drveni planinari s trnastima stabljikama i brojnim mirisnim bijelim cvjetovima u panicama, a zatim malim žutim do narandžastim plodovima, Sljedeći članak: Priloga I. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> West Indian woody climber with spiny stems and numerous fragrant white flowers in panicles followed by small yellow to orange fruits [Barbados-gooseberry vine, Pereskia aculeata]</p><p><i>n.</i> small yellow to orange fruit of the Barbados gooseberry cactus used in desserts and preserves and jellies [blade apple]</p><p><b>Nazvana po kući na Barbadu gdje je otkrivena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> named for a country house in Barbados where it was discovered [Adiantum tenerum farleyense, Farley maidenhair, Farley maidenhair fern, glory fern]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijsko stablo s žuto-bijelom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian tree with racemes of yellow-white flowers [Adenanthera pavonina, coral-wood, coralwood, peacock flower fence, red sandalwood]</p><p><b>Zapadni indijski