ng]</p><p><b>Oštro prezivanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a severe scolding [castigation, chewing out, dressing down, earful, going-over, upbraiding]</p><p><b>crvenkastosmeđ, goniti, grupa, klisura, lajanje, lajati, lavež, ležište, lovor, odjeljak, okvir, otvorena ćelija, prazan prostor, prečka, stalak, stativa, tjerati, udubljenje, uvala, uvale, zaljev, zaton, zona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an indentation of a shoreline larger than a cove but smaller than a gulf [embayment]</p><p><i>n.</i> the sound of a hound on the scent</p><p><i>n.</i> small Mediterranean evergreen tree with small blackish berries and glossy aromatic leaves used for flavoring in cooking [Laurus nobilis, bay laurel, bay tree, true laurel]</p><p><i>n.</i> a compartment on a ship between decks</p><p><i>n.</i> a compartment in an aircraft used for some specific purpose</p><p><i>n.</i> a small recess opening off a larger room [alcove]</p><p><i>n.</i> a horse of a moderate reddish-brown color</p><p><i>v.</i> utter in deep prolonged tones</p><p><i>v.</i> bark with prolonged noises, of dogs [quest]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of animals especially a horse) of a moderate reddish-brown color</p><p><b>bilo koja od različitih trava iz roda Eragrostis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various grasses of the genus Eragrostis [love grass]</p><p><b>Sredozemsko zeleno stablo s crnim bojama i blistavim aromatičnim lištima koje se koristi za okus u kuhanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Mediterranean evergreen tree with small blackish berries and glossy aromatic leaves used for flavoring in cooking [Laurus nobilis, bay, bay tree, true laurel]</p><p><b>lovorov list, lovor-list</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dried leaf of the bay laurel</p><p><b>mali riš Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small lynx of North America [Lynx rufus, bobcat]</p><p><b>uvijekzeleno aromatično grmlje iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država koje ima male tvrde bobice gusto prekrivene bijelim voskom koji se koristi za svijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen aromatic shrubby tree of southeastern United States having small hard berries thickly coated with white wax used for candles [Myrica cerifera, puckerbush]</p><p><b>ruka Indijskog oceana na istoku Indije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arm of the Indian Ocean to the east of India</p><p><b>ruka Atlantskog oceana u zapadnoj Europi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arm of the Atlantic Ocean in western Europe</p><p><b>dio Meksičkog zaliva zapadno od Jukatana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a part of the Gulf of Mexico to the west of Yucatan [Golfo de Campeche, Gulf of Campeche]</p><p><b>zaljev Sjevernog Atlantika između New Brunswicka i Nove Škotske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bay of the North Atlantic between New Brunswick and Nova Scotia</p><p><b>ruka Tirenskog mora u Napulju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arm of the Tyrrhenian Sea at Naples</p><p><b>Ulaz u Kara more u zapadnom Sibiru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inlet of the Kara Sea in western Siberia [Gulf of Ob]</p><p><b>aromatska tekućina prvobitno dobivena destilacijom listova borovnice s rumom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an aromatic liquid originally obtained by distilling the leaves of the bayberry tree with rum</p><p><b>mišićni odjeljak malog izbora plitkih školjka, mala školjka koja živi u plitkim vodama i blatnim ravnicama na atlantskoj obali Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> muscle of small choice shallow-water scallops</p><p><i>n.</i> a small scallop inhabiting shallow waters and mud flats of the Atlantic coast of North America [Pecten irradians]</p><p><b>država u Novoj Engleskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in New England [MA, Mass., Massachusetts, Old Colony]</p><p><b>rodom ili prebivalištem u Massachusettsu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or resident of Massachusetts</p><p><b>Sredozemsko zeleno stablo s crnim bojama i blistavim aromatičnim lištima koje se koristi za okus u kuhanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Mediterranean evergreen tree with small blackish berries and glossy aromatic leaves used for flavoring in cooking [Laurus nobilis, bay, bay laurel, true laurel]</p><p><b>Europska vrba s sjajnim kožnim lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European willow tree with shining leathery leaves [Salix pentandra, laurel willow]</p><p><b>slang za guzicu, prozor koji izlazi iz vanjskog zida kuće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slang for a paunch [corporation, pot, potbelly, tummy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a window that sticks out from the outside wall of a house [bow window]</p><p><b>(antički) vijenc od lovornih listova nosio na glavi kao simbol pobjede (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (antiquity) a wreath of laurel foliage worn on the head as an emblem of victory [laurel, laurel wreath]</p><p><b>grm ili drvo iz južnog Floride do Srednje i Južne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub or small tree of southern Florida to Central and South America [Capparis flexuosa, caper tree]</p><p><b>Drvo u zapadnoj Indiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> West Indian tree [Jamaica bayberry, Pimenta acris, bayberry, wild cinnamon]</p><p><b>Indijski ptica-tkanar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common Indian weaverbird [Ploceus philippinus]</p><p><b>Francuski vojnik za kojeg se govorilo da je neustrašivi i vitezovi (1473-1524) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French soldier said to be fearless and chivalrous (1473-1524) [Chevalier de Bayard, Pierre Terrail, Pierre de Terrail, Seigneur de Bayard]</p><p><b>Zakletva na vjernost emiru. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oath of allegiance to an emir</p><p><b>Drvo u zapadnoj Indiji, ljeplovita aromatična grmlja iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s sivo-zeleno voskom obloženih bobica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> West Indian tree [Jamaica bayberry, Pimenta acris, bay-rum tree, wild cinnamon]</p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous aromatic shrub of eastern North America with grey-green wax-coated berries [Myrica pensylvanica, candleberry, swamp candleberry, waxberry]</p><p><b>Mirto (Myrta spp.) - mirisni zeleni vosak dobiven od voskovog mirta i korišten za pravljenje svijeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fragrant green wax obtained from the