, husky, strapping]</p><p><b>košnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any workplace where people are very busy</p><p><i>n.</i> a structure that provides a natural habitation for bees [hive]</p><p><i>n.</i> a hairdo resembling a beehive</p><p><i>n.</i> a man-made receptacle that houses a swarm of bees [hive]</p><p><b>država u zapadnim Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in the western United States [Mormon State, UT, Ut., Utah]</p><p><b>pčelar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a farmer who keeps bees for their honey [apiarist, apiculturist]</p><p><b>hranidba pčela, pčelarstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cultivation of bees on a commercial scale for the production of honey [apiculture]</p><p><b>najkraći put</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the most direct route</p><p><b>(Judao-kršćanske i islamske religije) glavni duh zla i protivnik Boga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judeo-Christian and Islamic religions) chief spirit of evil and adversary of God [Devil, Lucifer, Old Nick, Prince of Darkness, Satan, the Tempter]</p><p><b>bip, kratki zvučni signal, upravljački znak u ASCII znakovniku, brujati, gakati, potrubiti, treštati, trubiti, zabrujati, zatrubiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short high tone produced as a signal or warning [bleep]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a loud noise [blare, claxon, honk, toot]</p><p><i>v.</i> call, summon, or alert with a beeper</p><p><b>dojavljivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electronic device that generates a series of beeps when the person carrying it is being paged [pager]</p><p><b>piva, pivo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a general name for alcoholic beverages made by fermenting a cereal (or mixture of cereals) flavored with hops</p><p><b>bačva koja drži pivo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a barrel that holds beer [beer keg]</p><p><b>Boca koja drži pivo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bottle that holds beer</p><p><b>konzerva koja drži pivo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a can that holds beer</p><p><b>pivopija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone whose favorite drink is beer or ale [ale drinker]</p><p><b>Taverna s otvorenim prostorom (obično nalik vrtu) u kojoj se služe pivo i druga alkoholna pića (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tavern with an outdoor area (usually resembling a garden) where beer and other alcoholic drinks are served</p><p><b>relativno velika čaša za serviranje piva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relatively large glass for serving beer</p><p><b>pivnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hall or barroom featuring beer and (usually) entertainment</p><p><b>bačva koja drži pivo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a barrel that holds beer [beer barrel]</p><p><b>netko tko prirađuje pivo ili pivo od slada i hmelja i vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who brews beer or ale from malt and hops and water [brewer]</p><p><b>kapljični podnožjak pod čašu piva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drip mat placed under a glass of beer</p><p><b>krigla</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mug intended for serving beer [stein]</p><p><b>Engleski pisac i karikaturist (1872-1956) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English writer and caricaturist (1872-1956) [Max Beerbohm, Sir Henry Maxmilian Beerbohm]</p><p><b>miris piva (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> smelling of beer</p><p><b>pčelinji vosak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a yellow to brown wax secreted by honeybees to build honeycombs</p><p><i>v.</i> cover with beeswax</p><p><b>cikla, repa, šećerna repa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> biennial Eurasian plant usually having a swollen edible root [Beta vulgaris, common beet]</p><p><i>n.</i> round red root vegetable [beetroot]</p><p><b>larva molja koja jede lišće cvekle i drugih povrća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> moth larva that eats foliage of beets and other vegetables [Spodoptera exigua]</p><p><b>bolest biljaka cvekle (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of beet plants</p><p><b>list cikle</b></p><p><i>n.</i> young leaves of the beetroot</p><p><b>šećer od šećerne repe</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sugar made from sugar beets</p><p><i>n.</i> sugar from sugar beets used as sweetening agent</p><p><b>Njemački skladatelj instrumentalne glazbe (posebno simfonijske i komorne glazbe), Beethovenova gla