, priličiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> accord or comport with [beseem, suit]</p><p><b>primjereno za: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> appropriate to</p><p><b>U skladu s onim što je prikladno ili prikladno za okolnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in accordance with what is appropriate or suitable for the circumstances [appropriately, duly, fitly, fittingly, properly, suitably]</p><p><b>pomračiti, pomračivati, pomutiti, pomućivati, zamagliti, zamagljivati, zamračiti, zamračivati, zamutiti, zamućivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make less visible or unclear [becloud, cloud, fog, haze over, mist, obnubilate, obscure]</p><p><b>Opušteni alkoholnim pićem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> stupefied by alcoholic drink [befuddled]</p><p><b>prevariti, nasamariti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a fool or dupe of [fool, gull]</p><p><i>v.</i> fool or hoax [cod, dupe, fool, gull, put on, put one across, put one over, slang, take in]</p><p><b>prevariti (od &quot;befool&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> derision of someone or something as foolish or absurd or inconsistent [stultification]</p><p><b>ispred, naprijed, pred, prije, ranije, sprijeda</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> earlier in time [earlier]</p><p><i>adv.</i> at or in the front [ahead, in front]</p><p><b>prije kršćanske ere. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> before the Christian era [B.C., BC]</p><p><b>uskoro</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in the near future [presently, shortly, soon]</p><p><b>na vrijeme, prethodno, prije toga, prije vremena, ranije, unaprijed, blagovremeno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being ahead of time or need [advance]</p><p><i>adv.</i> ahead of time [ahead, in advance]</p><p><b>ukaljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> spot, stain, or pollute [defile, foul, maculate]</p><p><b>ukaljati (od &quot;befoul&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made dirty or foul [fouled]</p><p><b>stanje zagađenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being polluted [defilement, pollution]</p><p><b>podržavati, pomoći, prijateljski, sprijateljiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become friends with</p><p><b>zbuniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be confusing or perplexing to [bedevil, confound, confuse, discombobulate, fox, fuddle, throw]</p><p><i>v.</i> make stupid with alcohol [fuddle]</p><p><b>zbunjen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> stupefied by alcoholic drink [befogged]</p><p><i>adj.</i> perplexed by many conflicting situations or statements [at sea, baffled, bemused, bewildered, confounded, confused, lost, mazed, mixed-up]</p><p><i>adj.</i> confused and vague [addled, muddled, muzzy, woolly, woolly-headed, wooly, wooly-minded]</p><p><b>zbunjenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> confusion resulting from failure to understand [bafflement, bemusement, bewilderment, mystification, obfuscation, puzzlement]</p><p><b>moliti, prositi, tražiti, moljakati, prosjačiti, žicariti, žicati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> call upon in supplication [implore, pray]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a solicitation or entreaty for something [solicit, tap]</p><p><i>v.</i> ask to obtain free</p><p><i>v.</i> dodge, avoid answering, or take for granted</p><p><b>tražiti dozvolu da se oslobodi angažmana (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> ask for permission to be released from an engagement [excuse]</p><p><b>dati povoda, začeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make (offspring) by reproduction [bring forth, engender, father, generate, get, mother, sire]</p><p><b>otac, tata</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a male parent (also used as a term of address to your father) [father, male parent]</p><p><b>jadnik, prosjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pauper who lives by begging [mendicant]</p><p><i>v.</i> be beyond the resources of</p><p><i>v.</i> reduce to beggary [pauperise, pauperize]</p><p><b>Biljke iz Euroazije i Sjeverne Amerike koje imaju male bodljikave oraščice koje se drže odjeće, bilo koja od različitih tropskih i subtropskih biljaka s trifolijatnim listovima i grubo ljepljivim dijelovima ili podnožjima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian and North American plants having small prickly nutlets that stick to clothing [beggar's lice]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various tropical and subtropical plants having trifoliate l