rategy, beggar-my-neighbour strategy]</p><p><b>politika promoviranja sebe na račun drugih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a policy of promoting oneself at the expense of others [beggar-my-neighbor policy, beggar-my-neighbor strategy, beggar-my-neighbour policy]</p><p><b>Sjeme borovnice, bilo koja od nekoliko biljaka rodu Bidens s žutim cvijećem i trnastima plodovima koji se drže krzna i odjeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the seed of bur marigolds [Spanish needles]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several plants of the genus Bidens having yellow flowers and prickly fruits that cling to fur and clothing [beggar's-ticks, bur marigold, burr marigold, sticktight]</p><p><b>jadnik, prosjak (od &quot;beggar&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by poverty befitting a beggar [mean]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of sums of money) so small in amount as to deserve contempt [mean]</p><p><b>Čovjek koji je prosjak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who is a beggar</p><p><b>U Južnoj Americi uzgajana za hranjenje životinja i za poboljšanje tla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> West Indian forage plant cultivated in southern United States as forage and to improve soil [Desmodium purpureum, Desmodium tortuosum]</p><p><b>Žena koja je prosjačica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman who is a beggar</p><p><b>prijava novca ili hrane (posebno na ulici od strane osobe koja izgleda bez novca), Stanje prosjaka ili prosjaka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solicitation for money or food (especially in the street by an apparently penniless person) [begging, mendicancy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being a beggar or mendicant [mendicancy, mendicity]</p><p><b>prijava novca ili hrane (posebno na ulici od strane osobe koja izgleda bez novca) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solicitation for money or food (especially in the street by an apparently penniless person) [beggary, mendicancy]</p><p><b>pozlatiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> decorate with, or as if with, gold leaf or liquid gold [engild, gild]</p><p><b>otpočeti, početi, počinjati, započeti, počnete, krenuti, kretati, startati, stati, započinjati, začeti, začinjati, otpočinjati, inicirati, pokrenuti, pokretati, zametnuti, otvarati, otvoriti, načeti, načinjati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Israeli statesman (born in Russia) who (as prime minister of Israel) negotiated a peace treaty with Anwar Sadat (then the president of Egypt) (1913-1992) [Menachem Begin]</p><p><i>v.</i> take the first step or steps in carrying out an action [commence, get, get down, set about, set out, start, start out]</p><p><i>v.</i> have a beginning, in a temporal, spatial, or evaluative sense [start]</p><p><i>v.</i> set in motion, cause to start [commence, lead off, start]</p><p><i>v.</i> begin to speak or say</p><p><i>v.</i> be the first item or point, constitute the beginning or start, come first in a series</p><p><i>v.</i> have a beginning, of a temporal event</p><p><i>v.</i> have a beginning characterized in some specified way [start]</p><p><i>v.</i> begin an event that is implied and limited by the nature or inherent function of the direct object [start]</p><p><i>v.</i> achieve or accomplish in the least degree, usually used in the negative</p><p><i>v.</i> begin to speak, understand, read, and write a language</p><p><b>početnica, početnik, osnivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone new to a field or activity [initiate, novice, tiro, tyro]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who founds or establishes some institution [father, founder, founding father]</p><p><b>početak, početkom, počinjanje, počinjati, početka, početku, početni, počinjala, pokret, start, vrijeme polaska, vrijeme početka, vrijeme počinjanja, ishodište, izvor, korijen, pokretanje, začetak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the event consisting of the start of something</p><p><i>n.</i> the time at which something is supposed to begin [commencement, first, get-go, kickoff, offset, outset, showtime, start, starting time]</p><p><i>n.</i> the first part or section of something</p><p><i>n.</i> the place where something begins, where it springs into being [origin, root, rootage, source]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of starting something [commencement, start]</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to begin [first]</p><p><b>aliteracija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> use of the same consonant at the beginning of each stressed syllable in a line of verse [alliteration, head rhyme, initial rhyme]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih biljaka iz roda Begonia koje se uzgajaju zbog svojih atraktivnih blistavih asimetričnih listova i obojenih cvijeća u obično terminalnim cimetama ili racemama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous plants of the genus Begonia grown for their attractive glossy asymmetrical leaves and colorful flowers in usually terminal cymes or racemes</p><p><b>hibridna zimskocvjetna begonija koja se uzgaja zbog svojih mnogih velikih ružičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hybrid winter-blooming begonia grown for its many large pink flowers [Christmas begonia, blooming-fool begonia]</p><p><b>Južnoameričke begonije s vlaknastim korijenima s istaknutim bazalnim režnjama lišća koji ukazuju na anđeoska krila i raseme koralno-crvenih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South American fibrous-rooted begonias having prominent basal leaf lobes suggesting angels' wings and racemes of coral-red flowers [angel-wing begonia]</p><p><b>u obliku od poluploče ili od poluploče, od kojih je jedna od vrsta: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tuberous or semi-tuberous South African begonia having shallowly lobed ovate leaves and small white flowers [grape-leaf begonia, maple-leaf begonia]</p><p><b>Rizomatous begonia s okruglim mesnim lištima crvenkaste boje ispod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhizomatous begonia with roundish fleshy leaves reddish colored beneath [Begonia feastii, beefsteak begonia, kidney begonia]</p><p><b>monoecious sućutne biljke ili grmovi iz tropskih i toplih regija, posebno Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monoecious succulent herbs or shrubs of tropical and warm regions especially America [Begoniaceae, family Begoniaceae]</p><p><b>Rizomatous begonia s okruglim mesnim lištima crvenkaste boje ispod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhizomatous begonia with roundish fleshy leaves reddish colored beneath [Begonia erythrophylla, beefsteak begonia, kidney begonia]</p><p><b>Rizomatous begonia s lištima s šiljatim režnjevima koji podsjećaju na zvijezde i ružičaste cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhizomatous begonia having leaves with pointed lobes suggestive of stars and pink flowers [star-leaf begonia, star begonia]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih obično rizomatnih hibridnih begonija koje potiču od istočnoindijske biljke s grubim teksturiranim listovima s masnim i bronzanim uzorcima i ljubičastom i crveno-sjedom s neopažavanim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous usually rhizomatous hybrid begonias derived from an East Indian plant having rough-textured leaves patterned in silver and bronze and purple and red-brown with inconspicuous flowers [beefsteak geranium, king begonia, painted-leaf begonia, rex begonia]</p><p><b>hibridna begonija s vlaknastom korijenom s širokim ovatičnim zelenim do bronznocrvenim listovima i malim grmovima bijelih ili ružičastih ili crvenih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hybrid fibrous-rooted begonia having broad-ovate green to bronze-red leaves and small clusters of white or pink or red flowers [wax begonia]</p><p><b>Srednji-tuberna begonija s peltatnim lišćama i ružičastom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> semi-tuberous begonia having peltate leaves and rose-pink flowers [Socotra begonia]</p><p><b>bilo koji od brojnih hibridnih begonija s gomoljastim korijenima i cvjetovima različitih boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous hybrid begonias having tuberous roots and variously colored flowers [hybrid tuberous begonia]</p><p><b>monoecious sućutne biljke ili grmovi iz tropskih i toplih regija, posebno Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monoecious succulent herbs or shrubs of tropical and warm regions especially America [begonia family, family Begoniaceae]</p><p><b>(od potomstva) koje je stvoreno od potomstva, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of offspring) generated by procreation</p><p><b>blatiti, kaljati, mazati, mrljati, okaljati, onečistiti, onečišćavati, onečišćivati, prljati, ublatiti, ukaljati, umrljati, uprljati, zablatiti, zamazati, zaprljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make soiled, filthy, or dirty [bemire, colly, dirty, grime, soil]</p><p><b>guste prekrivene ukorenjenim prljavštinom ili sokom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> thickly covered with ingrained dirt or soot [dingy, grimy, grubby, grungy, raunchy]</p><p><b>nerado davati, zavidjeti, žaliti, zamjerati, zamjeriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be envious of [envy]</p><p><i>v.</i> wish ill or allow unwillingly [resent]</p><p><b>obmanuti, prevariti, varati, zabavljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> influence by slyness [hoodwink, juggle]</p><p><i>v.</i> attract [becharm, bewitch, captivate, capture, catch, charm, enamor, enamour, enchant, entrance, fascinate, trance]</p><p><b>ispunjen čudo i zadovoljstvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> filled with wonder and delight [captivated, charmed, delighted, enthralled, entranced]</p><p><b>razbibriga, razonoda, zabava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> magnetic personal charm [animal magnetism, bewitchery]</p><p><i>n.</i> an entertainment that provokes pleased interest and distracts you from worries and vexations [distraction]</p><p><b>varalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who leads you to believe something that is not true [cheat, cheater, deceiver, slicker, trickster]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who charms others (usually by personal attractiveness) [charmer]</p><p><b>čaroban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> highly attractive and able to arouse hope or desire [alluring, enticing, tempting]</p><p><i>adj.</i> misleading by means of pleasant or alluring methods</p><p><b>(Rimska katolička crkva) članka redovnog sestrinstva (jedno od nekoliko koje je osnovana u Nizozemskoj u 12. i 13. stoljeću), glazba napisana u bolero ritmu beguine plesa, plesni ples koji je nastao u Francuskoj Zapadnoj Indiji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) a member of a lay sisterhood (one of several founded in the Netherlands in the 12th and 13th centuries)</p><p><i>n.</i> music written in the bolero rhythm of the beguine dance</p><p><i>n.</i> a ballroom dance that originated in the French West Indies</p><p><b>begum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Muslim woman of high rank in India or Pakistan</p><p><b>interes, korist, prednost, u ime</b></p><p><i>n.</i> as the agent of or on someone's part (usually expressed as `on behalf of' rather than `in behalf of')</p><p><i>n.</i> for someone's benefit (usually expressed as `in behalf' rather than `on behalf' and usually with a possessive)</p><p><b>nastupati, nastupiti, ponašati, ponašati se, postupati, vladati se, ponijeti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> behave in a certain manner [act, do]</p><p><i>v.</i> behave in a certain manner [acquit, bear, carry, comport, conduct, deport]</p><p><i>v.</i> behave well or properly [comport]</p><p><b>karakteristika, ponašanje, postupak, reagiranje, režim, vladanje, akcija, reakcija, ophođenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> manner of acting or controlling yourself [behaviour, conduct, doings]</p><p><i>n.</i> the action or reaction of something (as a machine or substance) under specified circumstances [behaviour]</p><p><i>n.</i> (behavioral attributes) the way a person behaves toward other people [behaviour, conduct, demeanor, demeanour, deportment]</p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) the aggregate of the responses or reactions or movements made by an organism in any situation [behaviour]</p><p><b>Psihološka terapija koja nastoji ugasiti ili inhibirati abnormalno ili neadekvatno ponašanje jačanjem željenog ponašanja i ugasiti neželjeno ponašanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> psychotherapy that seeks to extinguish or inhibit abnormal or maladaptive behavior by reinforcing desired behavior and extinguishing undesired behavior [behavior therapy]</p><p><b>Psihološka terapija koja nastoji ugasiti ili inhibirati abnormalno ili neadekvatno ponašanje jačanjem željenog ponašanja i ugasiti neželjeno ponašanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> psychotherapy that seeks to extinguish or inhibit abnormal or maladaptive behavior by reinforcing desired behavior and extinguishing undesired behavior [behavior modification]</p><p><b>ponašanja, vezano za ponašanje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to behavior [behavioural]</p><p><b>biheviorizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an approach to psychology that emphasizes observable measurable behavior [behavioristic psychology, behaviourism, behaviouristic psychology]</p><p><b>psiholog koji podržava behaviorizam, od ili u vezi s behaviorizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a psychologist who subscribes to behaviorism [behaviourist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to behaviorism [behavioristic, behaviourist, behaviouristic]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s behaviorizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to behaviorism [behaviorist, behaviourist, behaviouristic]</p><p><b>biheviorizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an approach to psychology that emphasizes observable measurable behavior [behaviorism, behaviourism, behaviouristic psychology]</p><p><b>karakteristika, ophođenje, ponašanje, postupak, reagiranje, režim, vladanje, akcija, reakcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the action or reaction of something (as a machine or substance) under specified circumstances [behavior]</p><p><i>n.</i> (behavioral attributes) the way a person behaves toward other people [behavior, conduct, demeanor, demeanour, deportment]</p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) the aggregate of the responses or reactions or movements made by an organism in any situation [behavior]</p><p><i>n.</i> manner of acting or controlling yourself [behavior, conduct, doings]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na ponašanje ili vladanje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to behavior [behavioral]</p><p><b>biheviorizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an approach to psychology that emphasizes observable measurable behavior [behaviorism, behavioristic psychology, behaviouristic psychology]</p><p><b>psiholog koji podržava behaviorizam, od ili u vezi s behaviorizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a psychologist who subscribes to behaviorism [behaviorist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to behaviorism [behaviorist, behavioristic, behaviouristic]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s behaviorizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to behaviorism [behaviorist, behavioristic, behaviourist]</p><p><b>biheviorizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an approach to psychology that emphasizes observable measurable behavior [behaviorism, behavioristic psychology, behaviourism]</p><p><b>odsjeći glavu, dekapitirati, obezglaviti, odrubiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cut the head of [decapitate, decollate]</p><p><b>odsjeći glavu (od &quot;behead&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having had the head cut off [decapitated]</p><p><b>odsjeći glavu (od &quot;behead&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> execution by cutting off the victim's head [decapitation]</p><p><i>n.</i> killing by cutting off the head [decapitation]</p><p><b>divovska životinja, gigant, monstrum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone or something that is abnormally large and powerful [colossus, giant, goliath, monster]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person of exceptional importance and reputation [colossus, giant, heavyweight, titan]</p><p><b>amanet, zavjet, naredba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an authoritative command or request</p><p><b>iza, natrag, otraga, pozadi, sa zadnje strane, straga, stražnjica, u pozadini, za, zakašnjeli, debelo meso, dupe, guzica, rit, zadnjica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fleshy part of the human body that you sit on [arse, ass, backside, bottom, bum, buns, butt, buttocks, can, derriere, fanny, fundament, hind end, hindquarters, keister, nates, posterior, prat, rear, rear end, rump, seat, stern, tail, tail end, tooshie, tush]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the lower score or lagging position in a contest</p><p><i>adv.</i> in or to or toward the rear</p><p><i>adv.</i> remaining in a place or condition that has been left or departed from</p><p><i>adv.</i> of timepieces [slow]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in or into an inferior position</p><p><i>adv.</i> in debt [behindhand, in arrears]</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to samo jedna od vrsta iz članka 3. stavka 1. točke (a) ovog članka, to se ne primjenjuje na sve druge proizvode. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> designed and carried out secretly or confidentially [sub-rosa, under-the-table]</p><p><b>Kasni od rasporeda., u dugovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> behind schedule</p><p><i>adv.</i> in debt [behind, in arrears]</p><p><b>Njemački mističar i teozof koji je osnovao modernu teozofiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German mystic and theosophist who founded modern theosophy [Boehm, Boehme, Bohme, Jakob Behmen, Jakob Boehm, Jakob Boehme, Jakob Bohme]</p><p><b>mistično teološko učenje Jakova Boehmeja koje je utjecalo na kvakere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mystical theological doctrine of Jakob Boehme that influenced the Quakers [Boehmenism]</p><p><b>gledati, motriti, opaziti, promatrati, promatriti, vidjeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> see with attention [lay eyes on]</p><p><b>zahvalan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> under a moral obligation to someone</p><p><b>gledalac, promatrač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who becomes aware (of things or events) through the senses [observer, perceiver, percipient]</p><p><b>vid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perception by means of the eyes [seeing, visual perception]</p><p><b>odgovarati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be appropriate or necessary [behove]</p><p><b>biti prikladno ili potrebno (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be appropriate or necessary [behoove]</p><p><b>Njemački arhitekt poznat po jednostavnim utilitarnim tvornicama (1868-1940) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German architect known for his simple utilitarian factory buildings (1868-1940) [Peter Behrens]</p><p><b>Danski istraživač koji je za Ruse istraživao sjeverni Tihi ocean i otkrio Beringov moreuz (1681-1741) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Danish explorer who explored the northern Pacific Ocean for the Russians and discovered the Bering Strait (1681-1741) [Bering, Vitus Behring, Vitus Bering]</p><p><b>bež, drap</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a very light brown [ecru]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a light greyish-brown color</p><p><b>šećerni prsten</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) glazed yeast-raised doughnut-shaped roll with hard crust [bagel]</p><p><b>duboko pržena krofna sa kvascem na kojoj je napunjen slatkišnim šećerom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deep-fried, yeast-raised doughnut dusted with confectioners' sugar [French fritter]</p><p><b>Peking</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capital of the People's Republic of China in the Hebei province in northeastern China [Peiping, Peking, capital of Red China]</p><p><b>Dialekt kineskog jezika koji se govori u Pekingu i koji je prihvaćen kao službeni jezik za cijelu Kinu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the dialect of Chinese spoken in Beijing and adopted as the official language for all of China [Mandarin, Mandarin Chinese, Mandarin dialect]</p><p><b>budući, postojanje, postojeći, sadašnji, stvor, stvorenje, suština, biće, bitak, egzistencija, egzistiranje, opstojanje, organizam, živo biće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state or fact of existing [beingness, existence, face of the earth]</p><p><i>n.</i> a living thing that has (or can develop) the ability to act or function independently [organism]</p><p><b>egzistencija, egzistiranje, opstojanje, postojanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state or fact of existing [being, existence, face of the earth]</p><p><b>lučki grad u istočnom Mozambiku na Mozambiku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port city in eastern Mozambique on the Mozambique Channel</p><p><b>Bejrut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capital and largest city of Lebanon [Bayrut, capital of Lebanon]</p><p><b>ukrasiti ili ukrasiti dragim kamenjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> adorn or decorate with precious stones [jewel]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm,, Babilonski bog zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a logarithmic unit of sound intensity equal to 10 decibels [B]</p><p><i>n.</i> Babylonian god of the earth</p><p><b>Apokrifa koja se sastoji od teksta koji je dodan Danijelovoj knjizi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Apocryphal book consisting of text added to the Book of Daniel</p><p><b>stil operne pjesme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a style of operatic singing</p><p><b>duhovit ili pametan čovjek s dobrim umom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a witty or clever person with a fine mind</p><p><b>glavni babilonski bog. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the chief Babylonian god [Baal Merodach, Marduk, Merodach]</p><p><b>Mađarski skladatelj i pijanist koji je sakupljao mađarsku narodnu glazbu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Hungarian composer and pianist who collected Hungarian folk music [Bartok]</p><p><b>Američki filmski glumac (rođen u Mađarskoj) poznat po glumi čudovišta (1884-1956) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film actor (born in Hungary) noted for portraying monsters (1884-1956) [Bela Lugosi, Lugosi]</p><p><b>Američki filmski glumac (rođen u Mađarskoj) poznat po glumi čudovišta (1884-1956) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film actor (born in Hungary) noted for portraying monsters (1884-1956) [Bela Ferenc Blasko, Lugosi]</p><p><b>da radi na ili do apsurdne dužine, verbalno napadaju oštrim kritikom, Udari glasno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to work at or to absurd length [belabour]</p><p><i>v.</i> attack verbally with harsh criticism [belabour]</p><p><i>v.</i> beat soundly [belabour]</p><p><b>istući, izmlatiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to work at or to absurd length [belabor]</p><p><i>v.</i> beat soundly [belabor]</p><p><i>v.</i> attack verbally with harsh criticism [belabor]</p><p><b>u obliku krastavca ili krastavca, od vrste: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monocotyledonous genus of the family Iridaceae [genus Belamcanda]</p><p><b>vrtna biljka čija kapsula otkriva kad zrije masa sjemena nalik borovnici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> garden plant whose capsule discloses when ripe a mass of seeds resembling a blackberry [blackberry-lily, leopard lily]</p><p><b>Bjelorusija, Bjelarus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked republic in eastern Europe [Belorussia, Byelarus, Byelorussia, Republic of Belarus, White Russia]</p><p><b>bjeloruski, Belorus, Beloruskinja, Bjelorus, Bjeloruskinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Slavic language spoken in Belarus [Byelorussian, White Russian]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to Belarus or to the people or culture of Belarus</p><p><b>monetarna jedinica u Bjelorusiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Belarus</p><p><b>zakasnio, zakasnjeli</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> after the expected or usual time [late, tardy]</p><p><b>kasno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> later than usual or than expected [late, tardily]</p><p><b>lzvor je niz od više od 200 otoka dug oko 400 milja u zapadnom središnjem Pacifiku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chain of more than 200 islands about 400 miles long in the western central Pacific Ocean [Palau, Palau Islands, Pelew]</p><p><b>namotati, osiguranje, osiguravati, pričvrstiti, svezati, zakačiti, zakvačiti konopcem, zavezati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something to which a mountain climber's rope can be secured</p><p><i>v.</i> turn a rope round an object or person in order to secure it or him</p><p><i>v.</i> fasten a boat to a bitt, pin, or cleat</p><p><b>drveni ili metalni šip na koji se može pričvrstiti konopac (kao na brodu ili u planinarenju) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wood or metal bar to which a rope can be secured (as on a ship or in mountain climbing)</p><p><b>podrignuti, podrigivanje, eksplodirati, eruptirati, rigati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reflex that expels gas noisily from the stomach through the mouth [belching, burp, burping, eructation]</p><p><i>v.</i> expel gas from the stomach [bubble, burp, eruct]</p><p><i>v.</i> become active and spew forth lava and rocks [erupt, extravasate]</p><p><b>podrigivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the forceful expulsion of something from inside</p><p><i>n.</i> a reflex that expels gas noisily from the stomach through the mouth [belch, burp, burping, eructation]</p><p><b>ružna zlobna stara žena., žena u godinama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ugly evil-looking old woman [beldame, crone, hag, witch]</p><p><i>n.</i> a woman of advanced age [beldame]</p><p><b>ružna zlobna stara žena., žena u godinama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ugly evil-looking old woman [beldam, crone, hag, witch]</p><p><i>n.</i> a woman of advanced age [beldam]</p><p><b>dražiti, gnjaviti, ismijavati, izazivati, kinjiti, maltretirati, mučiti, razdraživati, salijetati, uznemirivati, zadirkivati, zafrkavati, zezati, šikanirati, opkoliti, opkoljavati, opsjedati, opsjednuti, opsjesti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> annoy persistently [badger, bug, pester, tease]</p><p><i>v.</i> surround so as to force to give up [besiege, circumvent, hem in, surround]</p><p><b>opsada, opsjedanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the action of an armed force that surrounds a fortified place and isolates it while continuing to attack [besieging, military blockade, siege]</p><p><b>lučki grad u sjevernom Brazilu u delti Amazona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> port city in northern Brazil in the Amazon delta [Feliz Lusitania, Para, Santa Maria de Belem, St. Mary of Bethlehem]</p><p><b>Konusni fosil kalčastog oblika, sa konomskom šupljinom na jednom kraju i konusnom šupljinom na drugom kraju, koji sadrži (kada nije razbijen) mali komoran fragmokon iz ljuske bilo kojeg od brojnih izumrlih glavonožnih životinja iz obitelji Belemnitidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conical calcareous fossil tapering to a point at one end and with a conical cavity at the other end containing (when unbroken) a small chambered phragmocone from the shell of any of numerous extinct cephalopods of the family Belemnitidae</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s belemnitima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to belemnites</p><p><b>obitelj izumrlih mezozojskih glavonožnih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of extinct Mesozoic cephalopods [family Belemnitidae]</p><p><b>red izumrlih dibranchiate cefalopoda koji su povezani s preživjelim spirulama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> order of extinct dibranchiate cephalopods related to the surviving spirulas [order Belemnoidea]</p><p><b