ose-colored flowers [Erica tetralix, cross-leaved heath]</p><p><i>n.</i> common low European shrub with purple-red flowers [Erica cinerea, fine-leaved heath, heather bell]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bell-shaped glass cover used to protect and display delicate objects or to cover scientific apparatus or to contain gases [bell glass]</p><p><b>plavocrvena crna ptica s zvonom poput zvona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bluish black fruit-eating bird with a bell-like call [currawong]</p><p><b>od bronze sa 3 ili 4 dijela bakra do 1 dijela metala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bronze with 3 or 4 parts copper to 1 part tin</p><p><b>smrčkovica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a morel whose fertile portion resembles a bell and is attached to the stipe only at the top [Verpa]</p><p><b>biljka s velikim blagim debelim zidovima obično zvonoličnim plodovima, Slatka paprika u obliku zvona u zelenim ili crvenim ili žutim ili narandžastim ili crnim vrstama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant bearing large mild thick-walled usually bell-shaped fruits [Capsicum annuum grossum, paprika, pimento, pimiento, sweet pepper, sweet pepper plant]</p><p><i>n.</i> large bell-shaped sweet pepper in green or red or yellow or orange or black varieties</p><p><b>dugme koje se pritisne da bi se zvono zvonilo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a button that is pushed to ring a bell</p><p><b>zvončara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who rings church bells (as for summoning the congregation) [ringer, toller]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who plays musical handbells</p><p><i>n.</i> something that exactly succeeds in achieving its goal [bull's eye, home run, mark]</p><p><b>agitiranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sound of someone playing a set of bells</p><p><i>n.</i> persuasion of voters in a political campaign [canvassing, electioneering]</p><p><i>n.</i> playing a set of bells that are (usually) hung in a tower [carillon, carillon playing]</p><p><b>sjedalo koje ima oblik zvona (na nekim st