 [benevolence]</p><p><b>semantička uloga namijenjenog primatelja koji koristi od događaja označenog glagolom u rečenici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the semantic role of the intended recipient who benefits from the happening denoted by the verb in the clause [beneficiary]</p><p><b>dobročinitelj, dobročnitelj, dobrotvor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who helps people or institutions (especially with financial help) [helper]</p><p><b>Žena dobrotvornica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman benefactor</p><p><b>koji ima pozitivan ili blagotvoran utjecaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> exerting a favorable or beneficent influence</p><p><b>crkveni položaj koji daje prihod svom nositelju, Dajte im korist. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an endowed church office giving income to its holder [ecclesiastical benefice]</p><p><i>v.</i> endow with a benefice</p><p><b>imaju korist (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a benefice</p><p><b>Dobro se ponašaš., osobina koja je dobra ili korisna ili darežljiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> doing good</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being kind or helpful or generous</p><p><b>dobrohotan, dobrotvoran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> doing or producing good</p><p><i>adj.</i> generous in assistance to the poor [benevolent, eleemosynary, philanthropic]</p><p><b>blagotvoran, dobrotvoran, koristan, povoljan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> promoting or enhancing well-being [good]</p><p><b>blagotvoran, dobrotvoran, koristan, povoljan (od &quot;beneficial&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a beneficial manner</p><p><b>korisnicom, korisnik, nadarbinski, užitnik, užitnik dohodaka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the recipient of funds or other benefits [donee]</p><p><i>n.</i> the semantic role of the intended recipient who benefits from the happening denoted by the verb in the clause [benefactive role]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or arising from a benefice</p><p><b>Proces (ruda ili druge sirovine), kao što je redukcija (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> process (ores or other raw materials), as by reduction</p><p><b>bogaćenje, ob