><i>n.</i> pollution that is rendered harmless by natural processes and so causes no permanent harm</p><p><b>razgraditi se prirodno djelovanjem bioloških agensa (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> break down naturally through the action of biological agents</p><p><b>biološka raznolikost, biološka raznovrsnost, bioraznolikost, kvaliteta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the diversity of plant and animal life in a particular habitat (or in the world as a whole)</p><p><b>električni pojavi kod životinja ili biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electric phenomena in animals or plants</p><p><b>biotehnika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of engineering science in which biological science is used to study the relation between workers and their environments [biotechnology, ergonomics]</p><p><b>bioetika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of ethics that studies moral values in the biomedical sciences</p><p><b>biološka povratna sprega, biološka povratna veza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a training program in which a person is given information about physiological processes (heart rate or blood pressure) that is not normally available with the goal of gaining conscious control of them</p><p><b>vitamin koji održava otpornost staničnih i kapilarnih zidova na prodiranje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vitamin that maintains the resistance of cell and capillary walls to permeation [citrin, vitamin P]</p><p><b>biogeneza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> production of a chemical compound by a living organism [biosynthesis]</p><p><i>n.</i> the production of living organisms from other living organisms [biogeny]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s proizvodnjom živih organizama iz drugih živih organizama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the production of living organisms from other living organisms</p><p><b>proizvodi živim organizmima ili biološkim procesima, neophodna za održavanje osnovnih životnih procesa (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> produced by living organisms or biological processes</p><p><i>adj.</i> essential for maintaining the fundamental li