ect that is present at birth [congenital abnormality, congenital anomaly, congenital defect, congenital disorder]</p><p><b>redovito ponavljajući grčevi bolova koji su karakteristični za porođaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a regularly recurrent spasm of pain that is characteristic of childbirth [labor pains, labour pains]</p><p><b>ograničavanje broja rođenih djece (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> limiting the number of children born [birth control, family planning]</p><p><b>odnos živorođenčadi u području prema stanovništvu tog područja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio of live births in an area to the population of that area [birthrate, fertility, fertility rate, natality]</p><p><b>fizička ozljeda djeteta tijekom poroda, Emocionalna ozljeda naneta djetetu događajima koji se događaju pri rođenju i za koje se tvrdi da se pojavljuju u simboličnom obliku kod pacijenata s mentalnom bolešću. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> physical injury to an infant during the birth process</p><p><i>n.</i> emotional injury inflicted on an infant by events incident to birth that is alleged to appear in symbolic form in patients with mental illness</p><p><b>socijalni reformator koji se zalaže za kontrolu rađanja i planiranje obitelji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a social reformer who advocates birth control and family planning [birth-control reformer]</p><p><b>socijalni reformator koji se zalaže za kontrolu rađanja i planiranje obitelji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a social reformer who advocates birth control and family planning [birth-control campaigner]</p><p><b>datum rođenja, rođendan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anniversary of the day on which a person was born (or the celebration of it)</p><p><i>n.</i> the date on which a person was born [natal day]</p><p><b>rođendanska torta, rođendanski kolač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> decorated cake served at a birthday party</p><p><b>čestitka za rođendan, rođendanska karta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a card expressing a birthday greeting</p><p><b>dar koji se daje na proslavu rođendana osobe.