everal fruits of cultivated cherry trees that have sweet flesh [sweet cherry]</p><p><b>Veliki sjevernoamerički divlji trešnje s okruglim crnim kislim jestivim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large North American wild cherry with round black sour edible fruit [Prunus serotina, black cherry, rum cherry]</p><p><b>tetrijeb</b></p><p><i>n.</i> male black grouse [blackcock]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički čvor koji se nalazi od Mainea i Ontarija do Wisconsina i južno do Georgije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American bugbane found from Maine and Ontario to Wisconsin and south to Georgia [Cimicifuga racemosa, black snakeroot, rattle-top]</p><p><b>komedija koja koristi crni humor. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comedy that uses black humor</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički popel s velikim zaobljenim listovima sa škrobom i drvenim drvetom, pamuk sa zapadnog dijelu Sjeverne Amerike s tamno zelenim lištima iznad koje sjaje, a ispod hrđavih ili srebrnih lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American poplar with large rounded scalloped leaves and brownish bark and wood [Populus heterophylla, downy poplar, swamp cottonwood, swamp poplar]</p><p><i>n.</i> cottonwood of western North America with dark green leaves shining above and rusty or silvery beneath [Populus trichocarpa, Western balsam poplar]</p><p><b>-Sranje koje je crno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crappie that is black [Pomoxis nigromaculatus]</p><p><b>crni ribiz, ribiz-crni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated current bearing edible black aromatic berries [European black currant, Ribes nigrum]</p><p><i>n.</i> small black berries used in jams and jellies</p><p><b>Australsko stablo s malim ravnim ljuskama kao lištima i brojnim tamno smeđim sjemenom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree with small flattened scales as leaves and numerous dark brown seed [Callitris calcarata, Callitris endlicheri, red cypress pine]</p><p><b>Epidemijski oblik bubonske kuge koji je doživljavao u srednjem vijeku kada je ubio gotovo polovinu stanovništva zapad