ly spoken by African Americans in the United States [AAVE, African American English, African American Vernacular English, Black English, Black Vernacular, Black Vernacular English, Ebonics]</p><p><b>oteklu modricu uzrokovanu udarom u oko, loš ugled., nesrećan događaj koji ometa ili ometa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a swollen bruise caused by a blow to the eye [mouse, shiner]</p><p><i>n.</i> a bad reputation</p><p><i>n.</i> an unfortunate happening that hinders or impedes [blow, reversal, reverse, setback]</p><p><b>naziv za vrstu Sarcosomataceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common name for a variety of Sarcosomataceae</p><p><b>zastava obično sa bijelom lubanjom i križanim kostima na crnoj pozadini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flag usually bearing a white skull and crossbones on a black background [Jolly Roger, blackjack, pirate flag]</p><p><b>mala crno-tvrda mišica koja grize i ima vodene ličinke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small blackish stout-bodied biting fly having aquatic larvae [blackfly, buffalo gnat]</p><p><b>planinski šumski region u jugozapadnom Njemačkoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hilly forest region in southwestern Germany [Schwarzwald]</p><p><b>crvena lisica u boji kada je krzna uglavnom crna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> red fox in the color phase when its pelt is mostly black</p><p><b>rimokatolički redovnik koji nosi crni ogrtač dominikanskog reda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Roman Catholic friar wearing the black mantle of the Dominican order [Blackfriar, Dominican, friar preacher]</p><p><b>biljka iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država koja ima tamno ljubičaste zvonolike cvijeće obilježeno zelenom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herb of southwestern United States having dark purple bell-shaped flowers mottled with green [Fritillaria biflora, mission bells]</p><p><b>pasmina (posebno zapadnih obalnih područja Sjeverne Amerike) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pasture grass (especially of western coastal regions of North America) [Bouteloua eriopoda]</p><p><b>nizko čvrsta, mnogo-ogrančana trnasta grmlja koja se nalazi u alkalnim zemljištima zapadne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low hardy much-branched spiny shrub common in alkaline soils of western America [Sarcobatus vermiculatus, greasewood]</p><p><b>mali tetrijeb, tetrijeb ruševac, tetrijeb ružavac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grouse of which the male is bluish-black</p><p><b>kolumnarno stablo iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s vodoravnim udovima i malim lišćama koje se pojavljuju kasno u proljeće i imaju sjajnu boju početkom jeseni, mali mallee s grubom tamnom ljuskom prema guzici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> columnar tree of eastern North America having horizontal limbs and small leaves that emerge late in spring and have brilliant color in early fall [Nyssa sylvatica, pepperidge, sour gum]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small mallee with rough dark-colored bark toward the butt [Eucalytus stellulata, black mallee, black sally]</p><p><b>Tajno terorističko društvo u SAD-u početkom 20. stoljeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a secret terrorist society in the United States early in the 20th century</p><p><b>listno stablo iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika, Ustavni listnat grm s mraženim tamnoplavim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous tree of southeastern United States and Mexico [Bumelia lanuginosa, chittamwood, chittimwood, false buckthorn, shittimwood]</p><p><i>n.</i> upright deciduous shrub having frosted dark-blue fruit [Viburnum prunifolium]</p><p><b>Vođa Sauka koji je 1832. vodio ratnike Fox i Sauka protiv Sjedinjenih Država (1767-1838) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Sauk leader who in 1832 led Fox and Sauk warriors against the United States (1767-1838) [Makataimeshekiakiak]</p><p><b>Helleborus niger, crni kukurijek, crnoglavac, kukurijek božićnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slightly hairy perennial having deep green leathery leaves and flowers that are ultimately purplish-green [Helleborus orientalis, lenten rose]</p><p><i>n.</i> European evergreen plant with white or purplish rose-like winter-blooming flowers [Christmas rose, Helleborus niger, winter rose]</p><p><b>velika zimzelena stabla zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large evergreen of western United States [Tsuga mertensiana, mountain hemlock]</p><p><b>otrovna smrdljiva biljka Starog svijeta s ljepljivim dlakavim lišcima i žuto-sjednim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> poisonous fetid Old World herb having sticky hairy leaves and yellow-brown flowers [Hyoscyamus niger, henbane, stinking nightshade]</p><p><b>crni orah</b></p><p><i>n.</i> smooth-barked North American hickory with 7 to 9 leaflets bearing a hard-shelled edible nut [Carya tomentosa, big-bud hickory, mockernut, mockernut hickory, white-heart hickory]</p><p><i>n.</i> an American hickory tree having bitter nuts [Carya glabra, brown hickory, pignut, pignut hickory]</p><p><i>n.</i> North American walnut tree with hard dark wood and edible nut [Juglans nigra, black walnut, black walnut tree]</p><p><b>planine u jugozapadnoj Južnoj Dakoti i sjeveroistočnom Wyomingu, planine u zapadnoj Južnoj Dakoti i sjeveroistočnom Wyomingu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mountains in southwestern South Dakota and northeastern Wyoming</p><p><i>n.</i> mountains in western South Dakota and northeastern Wyoming</p><p><b>crna rupa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a region of space resulting from the collapse of a star</p><p><b>tamnica u tvrđavi u Kalkuti gdje je preko noći držalo 146 engleskih zatvorenika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dungeon (20 feet square) in a fort in Calcutta where as many as 146 English prisoners were held overnight by Siraj-ud-daula</p><p><b>Vrba starog svijeta s svjetlo zelenim lišćama uzgajana za upotrebu u košari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World willow with light green leaves cultivated for use in basketry [Salix amygdalina, Salix triandra, almond willow]</p><p><b>Europska biljka sa lošim mirisom, s ružnim listovima i krugovima tamno ljubičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ill-smelling European herb with rugose leaves and whorls of dark purple flowers [Ballota nigra, black archangel, fetid horehound, stinking horehound]</p><p><b>nizak grm iz istočne Sjedinjenih Država koji donosi blistavo crno jestivo voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low shrub of the eastern United States bearing shiny black edible fruit [Gaylussacia baccata]</p><p><b>suprotstavljanje morbidnih i farsičnih elemenata (u pisanju ili drami) kako bi se postigao uznemirujući učinak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the juxtaposition of morbid and farcical elements (in writing or drama) to give a disturbing effect [black humour]</p><p><b>suprotstavljanje morbidnih i farsičnih elemenata (u pisanju ili drami) kako bi se postigao uznemirujući učinak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the juxtaposition of morbid and farcical elements (in writing or drama) to give a disturbing effect [black humor]</p><p><b>tanak sloj leda (kao od zamrzavanja magle) na putu ili pločniku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin coating of ice (as from freezing mist) on a road or sidewalk</p><p><b>General Sjedinjenih Država koji je zapovijedao američkim snagama u Europi tijekom Prvog svjetskog rata (1860-1948) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States general who commanded the American forces in Europe during World War I (1860-1948) [John Joseph Pershing, Pershing]</p><p><b>mrka lunja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dark Old World kite feeding chiefly on carrion [Milvus migrans]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka s tvrdim stubovima i ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a weedy perennial with tough wiry stems and purple flowers [Centaurea nigra, hardheads, lesser knapweed]</p><p><b>bolest šljive i trešnje karakterizirana crnim izbočinama na granama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> disease of plum and cherry trees characterized by black excrescences on the branches</p><p><b>srednjovelika škrobnica iz Kanade i sjeverne Sjedinjenih Država uključujući Aljasku s širokom koničnom krunom i hrđavo-sjedom ljuskom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized larch of Canada and northern United States including Alaska having a broad conic crown and rust-brown scaly bark [American larch, Larix laricina, tamarack]</p><p><b>grafit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used as a lubricant and as a moderator in nuclear reactors [graphite, plumbago]</p><p><b>teška pisaca u upotrebi od 15. do 18. stoljeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heavy typeface in use from 15th to 18th centuries [Gothic]</p><p><b>čvrsto drvo crnog skakavaca, veliko trnovo drvo iz istočnih i središnjih Sjedinjenih Država koje ima čipane složene lišće i spuštene trnje bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> strong stiff wood of a black-locust tree</p><p><i>n.</i> large thorny tree of eastern and central United States having pinnately compound leaves and drooping racemes of white flowers [Robinia pseudoacacia, yellow locust]</p><p><b>mješavina kalomela i limewater koji se koristi na sifilitične rane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mixture of calomel and limewater that is used on syphilitic sores [blackwash]</p><p><b>Europska biljka pomalo slična celeru koja se široko prirodila u obalnim područjima Britanije i često se uzgaja kao biljka za uzgoj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European herb somewhat resembling celery widely naturalized in Britain coastal regions and often cultivated as a potherb [Alexander, Alexanders, Smyrnium olusatrum, horse parsley]</p><p><b>bolest pluća uzrokovana udisanjem ugljenskog prašine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lung disease caused by inhaling coal dust [anthracosis, black lung disease, coal miner's lung]</p><p><b>bolest pluća uzrokovana udisanjem ugljenskog prašine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lung disease caused by inhaling coal dust [anthracosis, black lung, coal miner's lung]</p><p><b>crna magija, okultizam, vračanje, čarobnjaštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the belief in magical spells that harness occult forces or evil spirits to produce unnatural effects in the world [black art, necromancy, sorcery]</p><p><b>Sjevernozelandsko drvo s gustim tvrdim svjetlo smeđim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> northern Zealand tree having dense hard light-brown wood [Olea cunninghamii]</p><p><b>mali mallee s grubom tamnom ljuskom prema guzici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small mallee with rough dark-colored bark toward the butt [Eucalytus stellulata, black gum, black sally]</p><p><b>vrlo otrovna južnoafrička mamba koja se plaši zbog svoje brzine i spremnosti da ugrize. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a highly venomous southern African mamba dreaded because of its quickness and readiness to bite [Dendroaspis augusticeps]</p><p><b>Australijsko drvo koje podsjeća na crnu mangrovnu šumu Zapadne Indije i Floride., mangrov u Zapadnoj Indiji i južnoj obali Floride (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Australian tree resembling the black mangrove of the West Indies and Florida [Aegiceras majus]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mangrove of the West Indies and the southern Florida coast [Avicennia marina]</p><p><b>tamno siva hrana riba pronađena iz Louisiane i Floride prema jugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dusky grey food fish found from Louisiana and Florida southward [Anisotremus surinamensis, pompon]</p><p><b>crna marica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> van used by police to transport prisoners [paddy wagon, patrol wagon, police van, police wagon, wagon]</p><p><i>n.</i> a form of whist in which players avoid winning tricks containing hearts or the queen of spades [hearts]</p><p><b>crna burza, crno tržište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people who engage in illicit trade</p><p><i>n.</i> an illegal market in which goods or currencies are bought and sold in violation of rationing or controls</p><p><i>v.</i> deal in illegally, such as arms or liquor [run]</p><p><b>osoba koja se nezakonito bavi trgovinom rijetkim ili kontroliranim robama, Dogovor na crnom tržištu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who engages illegally in trade in scarce or controlled commodities</p><p><i>v.</i> deal on the black market</p><p><b>Ribe velike divljačke u Tihom oceanu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large game fish in the Pacific Ocean [Makaira marlina, Makaira mazara]</p><p><b>Europska biljka s malim žutim cvijećem i zakrivljenim cr