black background [Jolly Roger, black flag, pirate flag]</p><p><i>n.</i> a gambling game using cards [twenty-one, vingt-et-un]</p><p><i>v.</i> exert pressure on someone through threats [blackmail, pressure]</p><p><b>obično grmljevo listno stablo iz središnje i jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država koje ima tamnu koricu i široke trolobne (klubu) lišće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common scrubby deciduous tree of central and southeastern United States having dark bark and broad three-lobed (club-shaped) leaves [Quercus marilandica, blackjack, jack oak]</p><p><b>grafit</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cover with graphite</p><p><b>lopov, lupež, štrajkbreher, štrajkolomac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who works (or provides workers) during a strike [rat, scab, strikebreaker]</p><p><i>v.</i> take the place of work of someone on strike [fink, rat, scab]</p><p><b>crna lista</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a list of people who are out of favor [black book, shitlist]</p><p><i>v.</i> put on a blacklist so as to banish or cause to be boycotted</p><p><b>otkupnina, ucijeniti, ucjena, ucjenjivanje, ucjenjivati, ucjenjuju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extortion of money by threats to divulge discrediting information</p><p><i>v.</i> exert pressure on someone through threats [blackjack, pressure]</p><p><i>v.</i> obtain through threats</p><p><b>otkupnina, ucijeniti, ucjena, ucjenjivanje, ucjenjivati, ucjenjuju (od &quot;blackmail&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a criminal who extorts money from someone by threatening to expose embarrassing information about them [extortioner, extortionist]</p><p><b>Ribe s crnim ustima i žlijezdnim šupljinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small marine fish with black mouth and gill cavity [Synagrops bellus]</p><p><b>crnilo, mračnost, tmina, crna, crna boja, mrak, tama</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality or state of the achromatic color of least lightness (bearing the least resemblance to white) [black, inkiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> total absence of light [black, lightlessness, pitch blackness, total darkness]</p><p>