 [blue cheese dressing]</p><p><b>jestiva agarica koja je bleda ljubičasta kad je mlada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> edible agaric that is pale lilac when young [Clitocybe nuda]</p><p><b>grad u sjevernom Alžiru na podnožju planina Atlas jugozapadno od Alžira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in northern Algeria at the foot of the Atlas Mountains to the southwest of Algiers</p><p><b>Britanski admiral (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British admiral [Captain Bligh, William Bligh]</p><p><b>malen rod zimzelenih stabala i grmova iz zapadne Afrike s mesnim kapsularnim plodovima s tri semena jestivi kada nisu ni nezreli ni prezreli (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of western African evergreen trees and shrubs bearing fleshy capsular three-seeded fruits edible when neither unripe nor overripe [genus Blighia]</p><p><b>široko uzgajana u tropskim i subtropskim područjima zbog svojih mirisnih cvijeća i obojenih plodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated in tropical and subtropical regions for its fragrant flowers and colorful fruits [akee, akee tree]</p><p><b>bolest biljaka, kvariti, lisna uš, štetiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state or condition being blighted</p><p><i>n.</i> any plant disease resulting in withering without rotting</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to suffer a blight [plague]</p><p><b>faza požarne bolesti u kojoj se pojavljuju tumori (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a phase of fire blight in which cankers appear</p><p><b>bolest biljaka, kvariti, lisna uš, štetiti (od &quot;blight&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affected by blight [spoilt]</p><p><b>gnjavator, dečko, drug, klinac, lik, prijatelj, tip</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a persistently annoying person [cuss, gadfly, pest, pesterer]</p><p><i>n.</i> a boy or man [bloke, chap, cuss, fella, feller, fellow, gent, lad]</p><p><b>slang termin za Veliku Britaniju koji koriste britanske trupe koje služe u inozemstvu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slang term for Great Britain used by British troops serving abroad</p><p><b>rana koja bi uzrokovala da se engleski vojnik vrati kući iz službe u inozemstvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wound that would cause an English soldier to be sent home from service abroad</p><p><b>cepelin, mali upravljivi zrakoplov, zatucani reakcionar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any elderly pompous reactionary ultranationalistic person (after the cartoon character created by Sir David Low) [Colonel Blimp]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small nonrigid airship used for observation or as a barrage balloon [sausage, sausage balloon]</p><p><b>Pompastno ultra konzervativni i nacionalistički. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pompously ultraconservative and nationalistic</p><p><b>na slijepo, prijevara, slijep, slijepih, zastor, zavjesa, zaslon, oslijepiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people who have severe visual impairments, considered as a group</p><p><i>n.</i> a hiding place sometimes used by hunters (especially duck hunters)</p><p><i>n.</i> a protective covering that keeps things out or hinders sight [screen]</p><p><i>n.</i> something intended to misrepresent the true nature of an activity [subterfuge]</p><p><i>v.</i> render unable to see</p><p><i>v.</i> make blind by putting the eyes out</p><p><i>v.</i> make dim by comparison or conceal [dim]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unable to see [unsighted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unable or unwilling to perceive or understand</p><p><i>adj.</i> not based on reason or evidence [unreasoning]</p><p><b>Ulica s samo jednim ulazom ili izlazom, (figurativno) postupak koji nije produktivan i ne nudi nadu za poboljšanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a street with only one way in or out [cul de sac, dead-end street, impasse]</p><p><i>n.</i> (figurative) a course of action that is unproductive and offers no hope of improvement</p><p><b>krivulja ili zakret na cesti koju ne možete vidjeti dok vozite (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a curve or bend in the road that you cannot see around as you are driving [blind curve]</p><p><b>Ugao ulice koji ne možete vidjeti dok vozite (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a street corner that you cannot see around as you are driving</p><p><b>krivulja ili zakret na cesti koju ne možete vidjeti dok vozite (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a curve or bend in the road that you cannot see around as you are driving [blind bend]</p><p><b>sudionik u sastanku u slijepo (nekoga koga upoznajete prvi put kada imate sastanak s njim), Izlaz s strancem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a participant in a blind date (someone you meet for the first time when you have a date with them)</p><p><i>n.</i> a date with a stranger</p><p><b>jako pijan. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very drunk [besotted, blotto, cockeyed, crocked, fuddled, loaded, pie-eyed, pissed, pixilated, plastered, slopped, sloshed, smashed, soaked, soused, sozzled, squiffy, stiff, tight, wet]</p><p><b>vodeni salamander u obliku jegulje s dva para vrlo malih stopala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aquatic eel-shaped salamander having two pairs of very small feet [amphiuma, congo eel, congo snake]</p><p><b>koristeći samo instrumente za let zrakoplova jer ne možete vidjeti kroz oblake ili maglu itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> using only instruments for flying an aircraft because you cannot see through clouds or mists etc. [blind landing]</p><p><b>sličan Gentiani andrewsii, ali s većim cvjetovima, Gencijan iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s cijevičastom plavom ili bijelom cvjetom koji se malo otvara ili uopće ne otvara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to Gentiana andrewsii but with larger flowers [Gentiana clausa, closed gentian]</p><p><i>n.</i> gentian of eastern North America having tubular blue or white flowers that open little if at all [Gentiana andrewsii, bottle gentian, closed gentian]</p><p><b>šupljina u kojoj počinje debelo crijevo i u koju se otvara ileum (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cavity in which the large intestine begins and into which the ileum opens [caecum, cecum]</p><p><b>koristeći samo instrumente za let zrakoplova jer ne možete vidjeti kroz oblake ili maglu itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> using only instruments for flying an aircraft because you cannot see through clouds or mists etc. [blind flying]</p><p><b>osoba s teškim oštećenjem vida (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person with a severe visual impairment</p><p><b>strana na kojoj je vaše vidno stanje ograničeno ili onemogućeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the side on which your vision is limited or obstructed</p><p><b>crvljakava zmija sa ostalim očima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wormlike burrowing snake of warm regions having vestigial eyes [worm snake]</p><p><b>predmet o kojem ne znate ili imate predrasude i ne možete dobro suditi, točka u kojoj vidni živc ulazi u mrežnicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a subject about which you are ignorant or prejudiced and fail to exercise good judgment</p><p><i>n.</i> the point where the optic nerve enters the retina [optic disc, optic disk]</p><p><b>bolest središnjeg živčanog sustava koja pogotovo pogađa konje i stoku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of the central nervous system affecting especially horses and cattle [staggers]</p><p><b>šavovi koji se ne mogu lako vidjeti ili primijetiti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stitching that is not easily seen or noticed</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s član (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trust that enables a person to avoid possible conflict of interest by transferring assets to a fiduciary</p><p><b>oslijepljen, zaslijepljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deprived of sight</p><p><b>naočnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> blind consisting of a leather eyepatch sewn to the side of the halter that prevents a horse from seeing something on either side [blinker, winker]</p><p><b>vezanih očiju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cloth used to cover the eyes</p><p><i>v.</i> cover the eyes of (someone) to prevent him from seeing</p><p><i>adj.</i> wearing a blindfold [blindfolded]</p><p><b>zavezan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> wearing a blindfold [blindfold]</p><p><b>zagušenje filtra, zagušenje sita</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> shining intensely [blazing, dazzling, fulgent, glaring, glary]</p><p><b>slijepo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without seeing or looking</p><p><i>adv.</i> without preparation or reflection</p><p><b>dječja igra u kojoj se igrač sa zavezanim očima pokušava uhvatiti i identificirati druge igrače (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a children's game in which a blindfolded player tries to catch and identify other players [blindman's buff]</p><p><b>dječja igra u kojoj se igrač sa zavezanim očima pokušava uhvatiti i identificirati druge igrače (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a children's game in which a blindfolded player tries to catch and identify other players [blindman's bluff]</p><p><b>slijepoća, sljepilo, sljepoća</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being blind or lacking sight [cecity, sightlessness]</p><p><b>Započeti neobavezno, posebno s štetnim posljedicama, napad ili udarac na ili s strane gdje je pogled napadnutog osoba zaprtan (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> catch unawares, especially with harmful consequences</p><p><i>v.</i> attack or hit on or from the side where the attacked person's view is obstructed</p><p><b>mali kopalički evropski gušter bez nogu s sitnim očima, bilo koji od malih tankih bezgranačnih crvljaka iz reda Gymnophiona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small burrowing legless European lizard with tiny eyes [Anguis fragilis, slowworm]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of the small slender limbless burrowing wormlike amphibians of the order Gymnophiona [caecilian]</p><p><b>odvojeni od drugih proizvoda iz poglavlja II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flashy, ostentatious jewelry [bling bling]</p><p><b>odvojeni od drugih proizvoda iz poglavlja II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flashy, ostentatious jewelry [bling]</p><p><b>Ruski palačinke od brašna i kvasca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Russian pancake of buckwheat flour and yeast [bliny]</p><p><b>bljeskanje svjetlosnog signala, migati, svjetlucati, treperiti, treptati, žmigati, žmiriti, žmirkati, trenuti, trepnuti, zažmiriti, bljeskati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reflex that closes and opens the eyes rapidly [blinking, eye blink, nictation, nictitation, wink, winking]</p><p><i>v.</i> briefly shut the eyes [nictate, nictitate, wink]</p><p><i>v.</i> keep back by blinking [blink away, wink]</p><p><i>v.</i> gleam or glow intermittently [flash, twinkle, wink, winkle]</p><p><b>Držite se uzdržavanjem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> keep back by blinking [blink, wink]</p><p><b>djelić sekunde, otkucaj srca, tren, tren oka, trenutak, treptaj oka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a very short time (as the time it takes the eye to blink or the heart to beat) [New York minute, flash, heartbeat, instant, jiffy, split second, trice, twinkling, wink]</p><p><b>bljeskalica, signalna lampa, žmigavac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light that flashes on and off [flasher]</p><p><i>n.</i> a blinking light on a motor vehicle that indicates the direction in which the vehicle is about to turn [trafficator, turn indicator, turn signal]</p><p><i>n.</i> blind consisting of a leather eyepatch sewn to the side of the halter that prevents a horse from seeing something on either side [blinder, winker]</p><p><i>v.</i> put blinders on (a horse)</p><p><b>migajući, trepćući, trepereći, treperenje, žmigajući, žmirkav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reflex that closes and opens the eyes rapidly [blink, eye blink, nictation, nictitation, wink, winking]</p><p><i>adj.</i> closing the eyes intermittently and rapidly [winking]</p><p><i>adj.</i> informal intensifiers [bally, bloody, blooming, crashing, flaming, fucking]</p><p><b>mala indijska salata sjevernih regija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Indian lettuce of northern regions [Montia lamprosperma, blinks, water chickweed]</p><p><b>bljeskanje svjetlosnog signala, migati, svjetlucati, treperiti, treptati, žmigati, žmiriti, žmirkati (od &quot;blink&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Indian lettuce of northern regions [Montia lamprosperma, blinking chickweed, water chickweed]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) tanak palačinke preokrenuti oko punjenja i pržena ili pečena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) thin pancake folded around a filling and fried or baked [blintze]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) tanak palačinke preokrenuti oko punjenja i pržena ili pečena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) thin pancake folded around a filling and fried or baked [blintz]</p><p><b>Ruski palačinke od brašna i kvasca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Russian pancake of buckwheat flour and yeast [blini]</p><p><b>jeka, oznaka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden minor shock or meaningless interruption</p><p><i>n.</i> a radar echo displayed so as to show the position of a reflecting surface [pip, radar target]</p><p><b>blaženstvo, ushićenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of extreme happiness [blissfulness, cloud nine, seventh heaven, walking on air]</p><p><b>blažen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> completely happy and contented</p><p><b>blaženo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a blissful manner</p><p><b>blaženstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of extreme happiness [bliss, cloud nine, seventh heaven, walking on air]</p><p><b>činkavi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chinch bugs [genus Blissus]</p><p><b>mali crno-bijeli insekt koji se hrani žitnicama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small black-and-white insect that feeds on cereal grasses [chinch bug]</p><p><b>antenski poklopac, blister, čir, mjehur, plik, prištić, žulj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flaw on a surface resulting when an applied substance does not adhere (as an air bubble in a coat of paint)</p><p><i>n.</i> (botany) a swelling on a plant similar to that on the skin</p><p><i>n.</i> (pathology) an elevation of the skin filled with serous fluid [bleb, bulla]</p><p><i>v.</i> get blistered [vesicate]</p><p><i>v.</i> subject to harsh criticism [scald, whip]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause blisters to form on</p><p><b>Bube koji proizvode izlučivanje koje stvara mjehuriće na koži (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> beetle that produces a secretion that blisters the skin [meloid]</p><p><b>bolest škotskog bora, bolest čajnih biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of Scotch pines</p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of tea plants</p><p><b>blister-bakar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an impure form of copper having a black blistered surface</p><p><b>U slučaju proizvoda koji se upotrebljava za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> packaging in which a product is sealed between a cardboard backing and clear plastic cover [bubble pack]</p><p><b>hrđa ribiza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several diseases of pines caused by rust fungi of the genus Cronartium and marked by destructive invasion of bark and sapwood and producing blisters externally [white-pine rust, white pine blister rust]</p><p><i>n.</i> fungus causing white pine blister rust and having a complex life cycle requiring a plant of genus Ribes as alternate host [Cronartium ribicola]</p><p><b>bubrenje, stvaranje mjehura</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the formation of vesicles in or beneath the skin [vesication, vesiculation]</p><p><i>adj.</i> harsh or corrosive in tone [acerb, acerbic, acid, acrid, bitter, caustic, sulfurous, sulphurous, virulent, vitriolic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> hot enough to raise (or as if to raise) blisters [blistery]</p><p><i>adj.</i> very fast [hot, red-hot]</p><p><b>Toxicni ratni plin s sulfidnim spojevima koji stvara mjehuriće i napada oči i pluća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic war gas with sulfide based compounds that raises blisters and attacks the eyes and lungs [dichloroethyl sulfide, mustard agent, mustard gas, sulfur mustard]</p><p><b>dovoljno vruće da podiže (ili kao da podiže) mjehuriće, prekrivena malim mjehurima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> hot enough to raise (or as if to raise) blisters [blistering]</p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with small blisters [blebby]</p><p><b>pun života, veseo</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking or showing a lack of due concern</p><p><i>adj.</i> carefree and happy and lighthearted [blithesome, light-hearted, lighthearted, lightsome]</p><p><b>sretno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a joyous manner [gayly, happily, jubilantly, merrily, mirthfully]</p><p><b>pun života, veseo (od &quot;blithe&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of spontaneous good spirits [cheerfulness]</p><p><b>blebetati, lupetati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to talk foolishly [babble, blather, blether, smatter]</p><p><b>Bez brige i sretna i blage volje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> carefree and happy and lighthearted [blithe, light-hearted, lighthearted, lightsome]</p><p><b>diplomu iz književnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bachelor's degree in literature [Bachelor of Literature]</p><p><b>blic, izvesti blic, zračni napad, blitzkrieg</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (American football) defensive players try to break through the offensive line [linebacker blitzing, safety blitz]</p><p><i>n.</i> a swift and violent military offensive with intensive aerial bombardment [blitzkrieg]</p><p><i>v.</i> attack suddenly and without warning</p><p><b>blitzkrieg</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a swift and violent military offensive with intensive aerial bombardment [blitz]</p><p><i>v.</i> fight a quick and surprising war</p><p><b>Američki pijanist i skladatelj opera i glazbenih predstava (1905-1964) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States pianist and composer of operas and musical plays (1905-1964) [Marc Blitzstein]</p><p><b>Danska pisateljica koja je živela u Keniji 19 godina i poznata je po svojim spisima o Africi (1885-1962) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Danish writer who lived in Kenya for 19 years and is remembered for her writings about Africa (1885-1962) [Baroness Karen Blixen, Dinesen, Isak Dinesen, Karen Blixen]</p><p><b>mećava, snježna mećava, snježna oluja, vijavica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a storm with widespread snowfall accompanied by strong winds [snowstorm]</p><p><i>n.</i> a series of unexpected and unpleasant occurrences [rash]</p><p><b>nabreknuti, nadimati, nadimati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> swelling of the rumen or intestinal tract of domestic animals caused by excessive gas</p><p><i>v.</i> become bloated or swollen or puff up</p><p><i>v.</i> make bloated or swollen</p><p><b>nabreknuti, nadimati (od &quot;bloat&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large fatty herring lightly salted and briefly smoked</p><p><b>grudica, kap, nula, nula (kriket), zabrljati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an indistinct shapeless form</p><p><i>v.</i> make a spot or mark onto [blot, fleck, spot]</p><p><b>blok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of countries in special alliance [axis]</p><p><b>beta- blokator (trgovinski naziv Blocadren) koji se daje nakon srčanog udara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a beta blocker (trade name Blocadren) administered after heart attacks [timolol]</p><p><b>Američki skladatelj (rođen u Švicarskoj) koji je komponirao simfonije i kamernu glazbu i zbornu glazbu te klavirsku sonatu i operu (1880-1959) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States composer (born in Switzerland) who composed symphonies and chamber music and choral music and a piano sonata and an opera (1880-1959) [Ernest Bloch]</p><p><b>blok, blok kuća, blokirati, brvno, čvor, dijeliti na blokove, dijeljenje na blokove, grupa kuća, klada, klišej, politički blok, skupina, spriječiti, začepiti, zakloniti, zakrčiti, zastoj, zatvoriti, zaustaviti, četvrt, zapreka, zaprjeka, blokada, kvart, kocka, kvadar, dio, komad, niz, red, dizalica s koloturom, kolotur, prepreka, začepljenje, prepriječiti, zabarikadirati, omesti, ometati, sprečavati, zatvarati, začepljivati, zaboraviti, zaboravljati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solid piece of something (usually having flat rectangular sides)</p><p><i>n.</i> a rectangular area in a city surrounded by streets and usually containing several buildings [city block]</p><p><i>n.</i> a three-dimensional shape with six square or rectangular sides [cube]</p><p><i>n.</i> a number or quantity of related things dealt with as a unit</p><p><i>n.</i> housing in a large building that is divided into separate units</p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a sector or group of sectors that function as the smallest data unit permitted</p><p><i>n.</i> an inability to remember or think of something you normally can do [mental block]</p><p><i>n.</i> a simple machine consisting of a wheel with a groove in which a rope can run to change the direction or point of application of a force applied to the rope [pulley, pulley-block, pulley block]</p><p><i>n.</i> a metal casting containing the cylinders and cooling ducts of an engine [cylinder block, engine block]</p><p><i>n.</i> an obstruction in a pipe or tube [blockage, closure, occlusion, stop, stoppage]</p><p><i>n.</i> a platform from which an auctioneer sells [auction block]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of obstructing or deflecting someone's movements [blocking]</p><p><i>v.</i> render unsuitable for passage [bar, barricade, block off, block up, blockade, stop]</p><p><i>v.</i> hinder or prevent the progress or accomplishment of [blockade, embarrass, hinder, obstruct, stymie, stymy]</p><p><i>v.</i> stop from happening or developing [halt, kibosh, stop]</p><p><i>v.</i> interfere with or prevent the reception of signals [jam]</p><p><i>v.</i> run on a block system</p><p><i>v.</i> interrupt the normal function of by means of anesthesia</p><p><i>v.</i> shut out from view or get in the way so as to hide from sight [obstruct]</p><p><i>v.</i> stamp or emboss a title or design on a book with a block</p><p><i>v.</i> obstruct [choke up, lug, stuff]</p><p><i>v.</i> block passage through [close up, impede, jam, obstruct, obturate, occlude]</p><p><i>v.</i> support, secure, or raise with a block</p><p><i>v.</i> impede the movement of (an opponent or a ball) [deflect, parry]</p><p><i>v.</i> be unable to remember [blank out, draw a blank, forget]</p><p><i>v.</i> shape by using a block</p><p><i>v.</i> shape into a block or blocks</p><p><i>v.</i> prohibit the conversion or use of (assets) [freeze, immobilise, immobilize]</p><p><b>Anestezija područja koj