mus saltatrix]</p><p><i>n.</i> fatty bluish flesh of bluefish</p><p><b>važna jestiva sunčanica iz istočnih i središnjih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> important edible sunfish of eastern and central United States [Lepomis macrochirus]</p><p><b>bluegrass</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various grasses of the genus Poa [blue grass]</p><p><i>n.</i> an area in central Kentucky noted for its bluegrass and thoroughbred horses [Bluegrass Country, Bluegrass Region]</p><p><i>n.</i> a type of country music played at a rapid tempo on banjos and guitars</p><p><b>područje u središnjem Kentuckyju poznato po svojim konjima plavog trava i čistokrvnih konja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an area in central Kentucky noted for its bluegrass and thoroughbred horses [Bluegrass, Bluegrass Region]</p><p><b>područje u središnjem Kentuckyju poznato po svojim konjima plavog trava i čistokrvnih konja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an area in central Kentucky noted for its bluegrass and thoroughbred horses [Bluegrass, Bluegrass Country]</p><p><b>država u istočnom središnjem dijelu Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in east central United States [KY, Ken., Kentucky]</p><p><b>rođen ili boravak u Kentuckyju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or resident of Kentucky [Kentuckian]</p><p><b>Mali atlantski krst koji ima sjajnu plavu glavu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Atlantic wrasse the male of which has a brilliant blue head [Thalassoma bifasciatum]</p><p><b>azuran, ključ, modar, modro, modro obojiti, plav, plavetan, plavetnilo, plavo, sjetan, tužan, plava, plave, plavi, plavoj, plavom (od &quot;blue&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used to whiten laundry or hair or give it a bluish tinge [blue, bluing]</p><p><i>n.</i> a process that makes something blue (or bluish) [bluing]</p><p><b>od boje između zelene i ljubičaste boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of the color intermediate between green and violet [blue, bluish]</p><p><b>malo polusvetlo grmlje iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država koje ima dla