čan, srčano, strm, vrletan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with boldness, in a bold manner</p><p><b>smjelost, bezobrazluk, bezobraština, drskost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being willing to undertake things that involve risk or danger [daring, hardihood, hardiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> impudent aggressiveness [brass, cheek, face, nerve]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of standing out strongly and distinctly [strikingness]</p><p><b>deblo, stablo, torzo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soft oily clay used as a pigment (especially a reddish brown pigment)</p><p><i>n.</i> the main stem of a tree [tree trunk, trunk]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Chadic language spoken in northern Nigeria and closely related to Hausa [Bolanci]</p><p><b>bolero</b></p><p><i>n.</i> music written in the rhythm of the bolero dance</p><p><i>n.</i> a short jacket</p><p><i>n.</i> a Spanish dance in triple time accompanied by guitar and castanets</p><p><b>obitelj mesnih gljiva s porama koji se lako odvajaju od čaše i često jedni od drugih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of fleshy fungi having the germ pores easily separating from the cup and often from each other [family Boletaceae]</p><p><b>vrganjevka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any fungus of the family Boletaceae</p><p><b>rod gljiva iz obitelji Boletaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of fungi belonging to the family Boletaceae [genus Boletellus]</p><p><b>gljiva s dugim grubo obrijano mrežnim stabljkom i rimoznom areolatnom površinom kapljice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus with a long coarsely shaggy reticulate stalk and a rimose areolate cap surface</p><p><b>vrsta rod Boletaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of Boletaceae [genus Boletus]</p><p><b>zlatača</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus convex cap and a dingy yellow under surface and a dry stalk</p><p><b>Hrana za jestivo i za izbor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edible and choice fungus</p><p><b>gljiva s crvenim kapom i crvenim grubo mrežnim stabljkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus with a red cap and a red coarsely reticulate stalk [Frost's bolete]</p><p><b>kovara, ludoglavka, smeđi vrganj, vrganjica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a poisonous fungus with a dingy yellow cap and orange red undersurface and a cylindrical reticulate stalk</p><p><b>gljiva koja je jestiva kada je mlada i svježa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus that is edible when young and fresh</p><p><b>gljiva koja ima bijelu kapu kada je mlada, ali kasnije postaje prljavo smeđa i stabljka iste boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus that has an off-white cap when it is young but later becomes dingy brown and a stalk of the same color</p><p><b>lijepa ali otrovna bolete (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a beautiful but poisonous bolete</p><p><b>jestiva gljiva s široko konveksnim crno-sjedom kapom i površinom pore koja je žuta kada je mlada i tamni s godinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edible fungus with a broadly convex blackish brown cap and a pore surface that is yellow when young and darkens with age</p><p><b>gljiva s hrđavo crvenim kapom i bijelom površinom pora koja postaje žuta s godinama i blijedožuto žuto stabljike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus with a rusty red cap and a white pore surface that becomes yellow with age and a pale yellow stalk</p><p><b>gljiva s baršunastom stabljkom i obično prljavim smeđim kapom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus with a velvety stalk and usually a dingy brown cap</p><p><b>jedljiva (ali ne i izabrana) gljiva koja se nalazi na tlu pod tvrdim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edible (but not choice) fungus found on soil under hardwoods</p><p><b>Hladna i ukusna gljiva koja ima smeđu kapa sa zelenkasto žutom pod površinom i stabljkom koji postaje tamno crven s godinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edible and choice fungus that has a brown cap with greenish yellow under surface and a stalk that become dull red with age</p><p><b>Druga supruga Henryja VIII i majka Elizabeth I. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the second wife of Henry VIII and mother of Elizabeth I [Anne Boleyn]</p><p><b>bolid, meteor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> 