></p><p><i>n.</i> a female bound to serve without wages [bondswoman, bondwoman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a female slave [bondswoman, bondwoman]</p><p><b>rob</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a male bound to serve without wages [bondsman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a male slave [bondsman]</p><p><b>kmet, rob, sluga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a male slave [bondman]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who signs a bond as surety for someone else [bondswoman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a male bound to serve without wages [bondman]</p><p><b>netko tko potpisuje obveznicu kao jamstvo za nekoga drugog, Žena koja služi bez plaće., robinja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who signs a bond as surety for someone else [bondsman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a female bound to serve without wages [bondmaid, bondwoman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a female slave [bondmaid, bondwoman]</p><p><b>lijepo stablo iz središnje i istočne Sjeverne Amerike s velikim bipinatnim lišćama i zelenobranim cvijećem s velikim drvenim smeđim čunjama čija se sjemena koriste kao zamjena za kavu, tropsko stablo s velikim trnastima sjemenama koje liče na grah i koriste se za nakit i krunicu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> handsome tree of central and eastern North America having large bipinnate leaves and green-white flowers followed by large woody brown pods whose seeds are used as a coffee substitute [Gymnocladus dioica, Kentucky coffee tree, chicot]</p><p><i>n.</i> tropical tree with large prickly pods of seeds that resemble beans and are used for jewelry and rosaries [Caesalpinia bonduc, Caesalpinia bonducella, bonduc tree]</p><p><b>tvrdo sjajno sivo sjeme drveta bonduc (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hard shiny grey seed of a bonduc tree [nicker nut, nicker seed]</p><p><b>tropsko stablo s velikim trnastima sjemenama koje liče na grah i koriste se za nakit i krunicu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical tree with large prickly pods of seeds that resemble beans and are used for jewelry and rosaries [Caesalpinia bonduc, Caesalpinia bonducella, bonduc]</p><p><b>ropkinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a female bound to serve without wages [bondmaid, bondswoman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a female slave [bondmaid, bondswoman]</p><p><b>kost, kostur, koštani, koštani sustav, riblja kost, koštano tkivo, štrebati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rigid connective tissue that makes up the skeleton of vertebrates [os]</p><p><i>n.</i> the porous calcified substance from which bones are made [osseous tissue]</p><p><i>n.</i> a shade of white the color of bleached bones [ivory, off-white, pearl]</p><p><i>v.</i> study intensively, as before an exam [bone up, cram, drum, get up, grind away, mug up, swot, swot up]</p><p><i>v.</i> remove the bones from [debone]</p><p><i>adj.</i> consisting of or made up of bone</p><p><b>Starija osoba mjerena usporedbom razvoja kostiju (kao što je prikazano rendgenskim zrake) s razvojem kostiju prosječne osobe poznate hronološke dobi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person's age measured by matching their bone development (as shown by X rays) with bone development of an average person of known chronological age</p><p><b>pepeo ostaje kada kosti izgore. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ash left when bones burn</p><p><b>koštani ugljen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> black substance containing char in the form of carbonized bone [animal black, animal charcoal, bone char]</p><p><b>stanica koja je dio kosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cell that is part of a bone</p><p><b>crna tvar koja sadrži ugljen u obliku ugljenirane kosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> black substance containing char in the form of carbonized bone [animal black, animal charcoal, bone black]</p><p><b>fine porcelane koje sadrže kostni pepeo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fine porcelain that contains bone ash</p><p><b>bez tragova vlage. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> without a trace of moisture [bone-dry]</p><p><b>masnoće u kostima ekstrahirano rastvaračima ili kuhanjem ili parenjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fatty matter in bones extracted with solvents or by boiling or steaming</p><p><b>koštana moždina, koštana srž</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fatty network of connective tissue that fills the cavities of bones [marrow]</p><p><i>n.</i> very tender and very nutritious tissue from marrowbones [marrow]</p><p><b>predmet spora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the subject of a dispute</p><p><b>tekući dio kostne masti, ulje tamne boje i loše mirisa dobiveno ugljenom kostiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the liquid portion of bone fat</p><p><i>n.</i> dark-colored ill-smelling oil obtained by carbonizing bone [Dippel's oil]</p><p><b>spavin uzrokovan kostnim rastom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spavin caused by a bony growth</p><p><b>štrebati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> study intensively, as before an exam [bone, cram, drum, get up, grind away, mug up, swot, swot up]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je proizvod izravno proizveden iz materijala koji se koristi za proizvodnju, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (b) ovog članka, to je: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small porous bowl made of bone ash used in assaying to separate precious metals from e.g. lead [cupel, refractory pot]</p><p><b>(od životinja) oklopljene kostima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of animals) armored with bone</p><p><b>bez tragova vlage. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> without a trace of moisture [bone dry]</p><p><b>stanica iz koje se razvije kost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cell from which bone develops [osteoblast]</p><p><b>dvostrukojake biljjedne dinosaure s kostnim krunama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bipedal herbivorous dinosaurs with bony crowns</p><p><b>Ustavno lijen ili lijen. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constitutionally lazy or idle [bone-lazy]</p><p><b>Ustavno lijen ili lijen. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constitutionally lazy or idle [bone-idle]</p><p><b>nakon što su se kosti uklonile, s masom od 0,15 mm ili većom od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having had the bones removed [deboned]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having bones as specified</p><p><b>tanka srebrna morska riba koja se nalazi u tropskim blatočnim ravnicama i mangrovskim lagunama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender silvery marine fish found in tropical mud flats and mangrove lagoons [Albula vulpes]</p><p><b>Glup osoba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stupid person [blockhead, dumbass, dunce, dunderhead, fuckhead, hammerhead, knucklehead, loggerhead, lunkhead, muttonhead, numskull, shithead]</p><p><b>(koristi se neformalno) glup (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used informally) stupid [blockheaded, duncical, duncish, fatheaded, loggerheaded, thick, thick-skulled, thickheaded, wooden-headed]</p><p><b>bez kostiju</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being without a bone or bones</p><p><b>mala kost. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small bone [ossicle, ossiculum]</p><p><b>sliku kostiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling bone</p><p><b>gnojilo od mletih kostiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fertilizer made of ground bones</p><p><b>neuspjeh, kiks</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an embarrassing mistake [bloomer, blooper, blunder, boo-boo, botch, bungle, flub, foul-up, fuckup, pratfall]</p><p><b>kosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (used in the plural) a percussion instrument consisting of a pair of hollow pieces of wood or bone (usually held between the thumb and fingers) that are made to click together (as by Spanish dancers) in rhythm with the dance [castanets, clappers, finger cymbals]</p><p><b>Europska biljka s malim bijelim, ružičastim ili ljubičastim cvijećem, višegodišnje biljke iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s bijelom vrhovima cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European herb having small white, pink or purple flowers [Symphytum officinale, common comfrey]</p><p><i>n.</i> perennial herb of southeastern United States having white-rayed flower heads [Eupatorium perfoliatum, agueweed, thoroughwort]</p><p><b>netko (ne nužno licencirani liječnik) koji popravlja slomljene kosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone (not necessarily a licensed physician) who sets broken bones</p><p><b>bilo koje vozilo na kotačima koje je razvaljeno i neugodno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any wheeled vehicle that is dilapidated and uncomfortable</p><p><b>planina u Andima u Argentini (visina 22 546 stopa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain in the Andes in Argentina (22,546 feet high)</p><p><b>s posebno mnogim ili istaknutim kostima, biti vrlo mršav (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having bones especially many or prominent bones [bony]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being very thin [bony, scraggly, scraggy, scrawny, skinny, underweight, weedy]</p><p><b>lomača, vatra</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large outdoor fire that is lighted as a signal or in celebration [balefire]</p><p><b>Ovakve noći se spaljuju slike Guy Fawkesa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> effigies of Guy Fawkes are burned on this night [Guy Fawkes Night]</p><p><b>tupi rezonancijski zvuk kao zvono., Zvonite glasno i duboko. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dull resonant sound as of a bell</p><p><i>v.</i> ring loudly and deeply</p><p><b>mali bubanj., velika šumska antilopa iz središnje Afrike s crvenkasto-smeđom kožom s bijelim prugama i spiralnim rogovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small drum [bongo drum]</p><p><i>n.</i> large forest antelope of central Africa having a reddish-brown coat with white stripes and spiral horns [Boocercus eurycerus, Tragelaphus eurycerus]</p><p><b>mali bubanj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small drum [bongo]</p><p><b>(Francuski) sreća i dobro humor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (French) happiness and good humor</p><p><b>Njemački luteranski teolog i pastor čiji su radovi povezani s kršćanstvom u modernom svijetu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German Lutheran theologian and pastor whose works concern Christianity in the modern world [Dietrich Bonhoeffer]</p><p><b>biti ljubazan i pristupačan (lakše razgovarati s njim) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to be friendly and approachable (easy to talk to) [affability, affableness, amiability, amiableness, geniality]</p><p><b>ugostitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) Anglo-Saxon missionary who was sent to Frisia and Germany to spread the Christian faith [Apostle of Germany, Saint Boniface, St. Boniface, Winfred, Wynfrith]</p><p><i>n.</i> the