 way [bosie ball, googly, wrong 'un]</p><p><b>loptica za kriket koja se igra kao da se razbija na jedan način, ali zapravo se razbija na suprotan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cricket ball bowled as if to break one way that actually breaks in the opposite way [bosie, googly, wrong 'un]</p><p><b>rijetka hronična progresivna encefalitis uzrokovana virusom ospica i uglavnom se javlja kod djece i mladih odraslih osoba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rare chronic progressive encephalitis caused by the measles virus and occurring primarily in children and young adults [Dawson's encephalitis, SSPE, Van Bogaert encephalitis, inclusion body encephalitis, sclerosing leukoencephalitis, subacute inclusion body encephalitis, subacute sclerosing leukoencephalitis, subacute sclerosing panencephalitis]</p><p><b>malo šumovito područje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small wooded area</p><p><b>Mogući rani Homo sapiens predstavljen lubanjom pronađenom u Transvaalu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> possible early Homo sapiens represented by a cranium found in the Transvaal</p><p><b>koji pripadaju ili su povezani s ili slične Boskop čovjeku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging or relating to or resembling Boskop man</p><p><b>od čelika ili čelika, s masenim udjelom čelika od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with or consisting of bushes or thickets [brushy]</p><p><b>planinska republika u južnoj središnjoj Europi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountainous republic of south-central Europe [Bosnia, Bosnia-Herzegovina, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Republic of Bosnia and Herzegovina]</p><p><b>Bosna, Bosne</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the northern part of Bosnia-Herzegovina</p><p><i>n.</i> a mountainous republic of south-central Europe [Bosna i Hercegovina, Bosnia-Herzegovina, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Republic of Bosnia and Herzegovina]</p><p><b>BiH, Bosna, Bosna i Hercegovina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountainous republic of south-central Europe [Bosna i Hercegovina, Bosnia, Bosnia-Herzegovina, Republic of Bosnia and Herzegovi