tulinum koja uzrokuje botulizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> potent bacterial toxin produced by the bacterium Clostridium botulinum that causes botulism [botulin, botulinus toxin]</p><p><b>u obliku čestice ili čestice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shell of puff paste [patty shell]</p><p><b>od pređe od 50 g ili više, ali ne više od 50 g, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fabric of uneven yarn that has an uneven knobby effect</p><p><b>spavaća soba za dame ili privatni dnevni boravak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lady's bedroom or private sitting room</p><p><b>ženski frizuru u kojoj kosa daje oteklom izgled, biti napuhan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman's hairstyle in which the hair gives a puffy appearance</p><p><i>adj.</i> being puffed out [puffy]</p><p><b>opera s sretnim završetkom i u kojoj se dio teksta govori (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> opera with a happy ending and in which some of the text is spoken [comic opera, opera bouffe, opera comique]</p><p><b>Određene vrste: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental tropical woody vines [genus Bougainvillaea, genus Bougainvillea]</p><p><b>Francuski istraživač koji je u pratnji znanstvenika plovio oko svijeta (1729-1811), Najveći od Salomonovih otoka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French explorer who circumnavigated the globe accompanied by scientists (1729-1811) [Louis Antoine de Bougainville]</p><p><i>n.</i> the largest of the Solomon Islands</p><p><b>Depresija na dnu Tihog oceana između Nove Gvineje i Salomonovih otoka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a depression in the floor of the Pacific Ocean between New Guinea and the Solomon Islands</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko južnoameričkih ukrasnih drvenih vinove loze roda Bougainvillea s briljantno crvenom ili ljubičasto-crvenom cvjetnom bractom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several South American ornamental woody vines of the genus Bougainvillea having brilliant red or purple flower bracts</p><p><b>Brazilska loza koja stalno cvjeta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Brazilian vine that tends to flower continuously [paper flower]</p><p><b>debela, debeo, grana, kupili, kupljen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the larger branches of a tree</p><p><b>debela, debeo, grana, kupili, kupljen (od &quot;bough&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having boughs (of trees)</p><p><b>bez grana, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having no boughs (of trees)</p><p><b>kupljena (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> purchased [store-bought]</p><p><b>Sute ili gulaš od ribljeg i školjkovitog mesa s paradižnima, lukom ili purem, začinjeni safronom, češnjakom i biljkama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> highly seasoned Mediterranean soup or stew made of several kinds of fish and shellfish with tomatoes and onions or leeks and seasoned with saffron and garlic and herbs</p><p><b>čista začinjena juha. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a clear seasoned broth</p><p><b>u obliku od 1 kg ili više, ali ne više od 1 kg, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cube of evaporated seasoned meat extract</p><p><b>glondža, kameni blok, oblutak, stijena, šljunak, gromada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large smooth mass of rock detached from its place of origin [bowlder]</p><p><i>n.</i> a town in north central Colorado</p><p><b>Ne-stratificirana zemlja nastala od glečera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unstratified soil deposited by a glacier [till]</p><p><b>paprika iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s blijedozelenim lišćama i mirisom sijena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fern of eastern North America with pale green fronds and an aroma like hay [Dennstaedtia punctilobula, hay-scented, hay-scented fern, scented fern]</p><p><b>glondža, kameni blok, oblutak, stijena, šljunak (od &quot;boulder&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> abounding in rocks or stones [bouldery, rocky, stony]</p><p><b>koje su u stijenama ili kamenima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> abounding in rocks or stones [bouldered, rocky, stony]</p><p><b>dekorativni uređaj za namještaj s inkrustiranim dijelovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inlaid furniture decoration [boulle, buhl]</p><p><b>avenija, bulevar, šetalište, ulica, široka ulica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wide street or thoroughfare [avenue]</p><p><b>posjetitelj gradskog bulevar (posebno u Parizu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a visitor of a city boulevard (especially in Paris)</p><p><b>Francuski skladatelj serijske glazbe (rođen 1925.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French composer of serial music (born in 1925) [Pierre Boulez]</p><p><b>dekorativni uređaj za namještaj s inkrustiranim dijelovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inlaid furniture decoration [boule, buhl]</p><p><b>o d skok (kontakta), odbijanje lopte, odbijati (se), skakati, odskakutati, odskočiti, odskok, poskakivati, praskati, odbijati se, odskakati, skok, titranje (slike), vibracija, odraz lopte, odskakivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of a substance that is able to rebound [bounciness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a light, self-propelled movement upwards or forwards [bound, leap, leaping, saltation, spring]</p><p><i>n.</i> rebounding from an impact (or series of impacts) [bouncing]</p><p><i>v.</i> spring back [bound, rebound, recoil, resile, reverberate, ricochet, spring, take a hop]</p><p><i>v.</i> hit something so that it bounces</p><p><i>v.</i> move up and down repeatedly [jounce]</p><p><i>v.</i> come back after being refused</p><p><i>v.</i> leap suddenly</p><p><i>v.</i> refuse to accept and send back</p><p><i>v.</i> eject from the premises</p><p><b>odbiti se natrag, odskočiti natrag</b></p><p><i>v.</i> improve in health [get over, get well]</p><p><b>Odbijanje lopte tako da postane van (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bounce a ball so that it becomes an out</p><p><b>izbacivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person whose duty is to throw troublemakers out of a bar or public meeting [chucker-out]</p><p><b>kvaliteta tvari koja može odbiti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of a substance that is able to rebound [bounce]</p><p><b>odskakanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rebounding from an impact (or series of impacts) [bounce]</p><p><i>adj.</i> vigorously healthy</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by lively action [bouncy, peppy, spirited, zippy]</p><p><b>biljka 