d by a willingness to give freely [bounty]</p><p><b>darežljivost, dobrostivost, dobrota, poklon (od &quot;bounty&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> rewarded or able to be rewarded by a bounty</p><p><b>bogat, bogatoga, darežljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> given or giving freely [big, bighearted, bounteous, freehanded, giving, handsome, liberal, openhanded]</p><p><i>adj.</i> producing in abundance [plentiful]</p><p><b>bogat, bogatoga, darežljiv (od &quot;bountiful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a bountiful manner [bounteously, plenteously, plentifully]</p><p><b>bogat, bogatoga, darežljiv (od &quot;bountiful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of copious abundance [amplitude, bounty]</p><p><b>darežljivost, dobrostivost, dobrota, poklon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> payment or reward (especially from a government) for acts such as catching criminals or killing predatory animals or enlisting in the military [premium]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of copious abundance [amplitude, bountifulness]</p><p><i>n.</i> generosity evidenced by a willingness to give freely [bounteousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a ship of the British navy [H.M.S. Bounty]</p><p><b>lovac na ucjene</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who pursues fugitives or criminals for whom a reward is offered</p><p><i>n.</i> a hunter who kills predatory wild animals in order to collect a bounty</p><p><b>aranžman, aroma vina, buket, kita, kita cvijeća, kitica, miris, stručak, aroma, miomiris</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arrangement of flowers that is usually given as a present [corsage, nosegay, posy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a pleasingly sweet olfactory property [fragrance, fragrancy, redolence, sweetness]</p><p><b>bourbon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reactionary politician in the United States (usually from the South)</p><p><i>n.</i> whiskey distilled from a mash of corn and malt and rye and aged in charred oak barrels</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the European royal family that ruled France</p><p><i>n.</i> a European royal line that ruled in France (from 1589-1793) and