>v.</i> solder together by using hard solder with a high melting point</p><p><b>bakarni, bestidan, bezobrazan, drzak, mesingan</b></p><p><i>v.</i> face with defiance or impudence</p><p><i>adj.</i> unrestrained by convention or propriety [audacious, bald-faced, barefaced, bodacious, brassy, brazen-faced, insolent]</p><p><i>adj.</i> made of or resembling brass (as in color or hardness)</p><p><b>Neobuzdan konvencijom ili pristojnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> unrestrained by convention or propriety [audacious, bald-faced, barefaced, bodacious, brassy, brazen, insolent]</p><p><b>bakarni, bestidan, bezobrazan, drzak, mesingan (od &quot;brazen&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a brazen manner</p><p><b>drskost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> behavior marked by a bold defiance of the proprieties and lack of shame [shamelessness]</p><p><b>grijalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large metal container in which coal or charcoal is burned [brasier]</p><p><b>Brazil</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the largest Latin American country and the largest Portuguese speaking country in the world [Brasil, Federative Republic of Brazil]</p><p><i>n.</i> three-sided tropical American nut with white oily meat and hard brown shell [brazil nut]</p><p><b>brazilski orah, orah-brazilski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall South American tree bearing brazil nuts [Bertholletia excelsa, brazil-nut tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> three-sided tropical American nut with white oily meat and hard brown shell [brazil]</p><p><b>Visoko južnoameričko stablo koje nosi brazilske orahe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall South American tree bearing brazil nuts [Bertholletia excelsa, brazil nut]</p><p><b>Brazilac, Brazilka, brazilski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Brazil</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Brazil or the people of Brazil</p><p><b>Glavni grad Brazila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital of Brazil [Brasilia, capital of Brazil]</p><p><b>Južnoameričko stablo s plodovima sličnim pravim guava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South Ameri