ki zanat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the craft of laying bricks</p><p><b>ima malu elastičnost (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having little elasticity [brickly, brittle]</p><p><b>cigla, opeka (od &quot;brick&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having little elasticity [brickle, brittle]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju električnih vozila od željeza ili električne energije ne smiju se upotrebljavati: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> building material consisting of bricks laid with mortar between them</p><p><b>zidanje ciglom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> masonry done with bricks and mortar</p><p><b>ciglana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a place where bricks are made and sold [brickfield]</p><p><b>Izgradnja nečega od bilo kojeg materijala koji su dostupni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> construction of something by whatver material are available</p><p><b>motor koji je pružao srednjovjekovni topništvo korišteno tijekom opsada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an engine that provided medieval artillery used during sieges [arbalest, arbalist, ballista, catapult, mangonel, onager, trebuchet, trebucket]</p><p><b>svadba, svadben, svadbeni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> archaic terms for a wedding or wedding feast [espousal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a wedding [nuptial, spousal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to a bride</p><p><b>vjenčana haljina, vjenčanica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gown worn by the bride at a wedding [wedding dress, wedding gown]</p><p><b>Čileanski zimzeleni grm s osjetljivim šiljcima malih bijelih cvijeća, grm s obilnim malim bijelim cvjetovima na proljeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chilean evergreen shrub having delicate spikes of small white flowers [Francoa ramosa, bridal-wreath]</p><p><i>n.</i> shrub having copious small white flowers in spring [Saint Peter's wreath, Spiraea prunifolia, St. Peter's wreath, bridal-wreath]</p><p><b>Čileanski zimzeleni grm s osjetljivim šiljcima malih bijelih cvijeća, grm s obilnim malim bijelim cvjetovima na proljeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chilean evergreen shrub having delicate