wn, let down, lower, take down]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause the downfall of [overthrow, overturn, subvert]</p><p><i>v.</i> impose something unpleasant [impose, inflict, visit]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to come to the ground [land, put down]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be enthusiastic</p><p><i>v.</i> cut down on [cut, cut back, cut down, reduce, trim, trim back, trim down]</p><p><b>donijeti, donositi, generirati, izazivati, izazvati, proizvesti, proizvoditi, prouzrokovati, prouzročiti, stvarati, stvoriti, uzrokovati, izlagati, izložiti, iznijeti, iznositi, izvlačiti, izvući, pokazati, pokazivati, predočavati, predočiti, prezentirati, prikazati, prikazivati, rađati, roditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bring into existence [generate]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring out for display [produce]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring forth or yield [produce]</p><p><i>v.</i> make (offspring) by reproduction [beget, engender, father, generate, get, mother, sire]</p><p><b>dogurati, gurati, gurnuti, maknuti, micati, pogurati, poguravati, pogurivati, pogurnuti, pomaknuti, pomicati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to move forward [advance]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring forward for consideration [call up]</p><p><b>da bude razumljiv i jasan, zaraditi kao plaću ili plaću (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make understandable and clear</p><p><i>v.</i> earn as a salary or wage [take home]</p><p><b>pobijediti, pobjeđivati, uspijevati, uspjeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> attain success or reach a desired goal [come through, deliver the goods, succeed, win]</p><p><i>v.</i> supply means of subsistence [provide]</p><p><b>donijeti, donijeti (rezultat), predvesti, unijeti, uvesti, dobaviti, dobavljati, dohvatiti, dohvaćati, donositi, dosezati, doseći, namaknuti, namicati, postizati, postići, pribaviti, pribavljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bring in a new person or object into a familiar environment [introduce]</p><p><i>v.</i> earn on some commercial or business transaction [clear, earn, gain, make, pull in, realise, realize, take in]</p><p><i>v.</i> be sold for a certain price [bring, fetch]</p><p><i>v.</i> submit (a verdict) to a court</p><p><i>v.</i> transmit</p><p><b>spašavati, uspeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be successful [carry off, manage, negociate, pull off]</p><p><b>inducirati, izazivati, proizvesti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to arise [induce]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring onto the market or release [bring out, produce]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to appear</p><p><b>uzrok da se preduzme određena djelovanja, obično se koristi u negativnom smislu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to undertake a certain action, usually used in the negative</p><p><b>izvesti, štampati, iznijeti, iznositi, izvlačiti, izvući, objelodaniti, objelodanjivati, otkriti, otkrivati, prikazati, prikazivati, razotkriti, razotkrivati, objaviti, objavljivati, proizvesti, odati, odavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make visible [reveal, unveil]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring out of a specific state [let out]</p><p><i>v.</i> prepare and issue for public distribution or sale [issue, publish, put out, release]</p><p><i>v.</i> direct attention to, as if by means of contrast [set off]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring onto the market or release [bring on, produce]</p><p><i>v.</i> encourage to be less reserved</p><p><i>v.</i> take out of a container or enclosed space [get out]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring before the public for the first time, as of an actor, song, etc. [introduce]</p><p><i>v.</i> make known to the public information that was previously known only to a few people or that was meant to be kept a secret [break, disclose, discover, divulge, expose, give away, let on, let out, reveal, uncover, unwrap]</p><p><b>izvesti izvan tijela za operaciju, organa (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bring outside the body for surgery, of organs [exteriorize]</p><p><b>Izjava ili postupak, Vraćanje svijesti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to adopt an opinion or course of action [bring around]</p><p><i>v.</i> return to consciousness [bring around, bring back, bring to]</p><p><b>spasiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bring into safety [carry through, pull through, save]</p><p><b>podsjetiti, urazumiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> return to consciousness [bring around, bring back, bring round]</p><p><b>staviti u rad ili dovesti u djelovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bring into operation or effect</p><p><b>dovesti, gajiti, iznijeti, odgajati, odgojiti, staviti, dignuti, dizati, dići, podignuti, podizati, podići, uzdignuti, uzdizati, uzdići, iznositi, načeti, načinjati, pokrenuti, pokretati, početi, počinjati, započeti, započinjati, začeti, začinjati, spomenuti, spominjati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> summon into action or bring into existence, often as if by magic [arouse, call down, call forth, conjure, conjure up, evoke, invoke, put forward, raise, stir]</p><p><i>v.</i> look after a child until it is an adult [nurture, parent, raise, rear]</p><p><i>v.</i> promote from a lower position or rank</p><p><i>v.</i> raise from a lower to a higher position [elevate, get up, lift, raise]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to come to a sudden stop</p><p><i>v.</i> put forward for consideration or discussion [raise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make reference to [advert, cite, mention, name, refer]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to load (an operating system) and start the initial processes [boot, reboot]</p><p><b>donosi, donositi, donošenje, dovođenje, uvođenje, doprema, dopremanje, dostava, dostavljanje, isporuka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of delivering or distributing something (as goods or mail) [delivery]</p><p><b>Čin približavanja ili spajanja, posebno rezanih rubova tkiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of bringing near or bringing together especially the cut edges of tissue [approximation]</p><p><b>odgajanje, odgoj, podizanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> helping someone grow up to be an accepted member of the community [breeding, fosterage, fostering, nurture, raising, rearing, upbringing]</p><p><b>salinitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relative proportion of salt in a solution [salinity]</p><p><b>patlidžan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hairy upright herb native to southeastern Asia but widely cultivated for its large glossy edible fruit commonly used as a vegetable [Solanum melongena, aubergine, eggplant, eggplant bush, garden egg, mad apple]</p><p><b>granica, ivica, prag, rub</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a region marking a boundary [threshold, verge]</p><p><i>n.</i> the edge of a steep place</p><p><i>n.</i> the limit beyond which something happens or changes [verge]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, "zaštita" znači zaštita od opasnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the policy of pushing a dangerous situation to the brink of disaster (to the limits of safety)</p><p><b>Američki antropolog koji je prvi pokušao sustavnu klasifikaciju indijskih jezika (1837-1899) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States anthropologist who was the first to attempt a systematic classification of Native American languages (1837-1899) [Daniel Garrison Brinton]</p><p><b>slano</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any very large body of (salt) water [main]</p><p><i>adj.</i> slightly salty (especially from containing a mixture of seawater and fresh water) [brackish]</p><p><b>aktivnost, animiranost, elan, energičnost, oživljenje, polet, razigranost, svježina, živahnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> quality of being active or spirited or alive and vigorous [animation, invigoration, spiritedness, vivification]</p><p><b>lagana rolica bogata jajima i maslacem i pomalo slatka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light roll rich with eggs and butter and somewhat sweet</p><p><b>Vina rod Bryonia s velikim lišćama i malim cvijećem koja daje kisel sok s emetičkim i pročišćavajućim svojstvima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vine of the genus Bryonia having large leaves and small flowers and yielding acrid juice with emetic and purgative properties [bryony]</p><p><b>antiasidi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antacid</p><p><b>briket, briketirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a block made from charcoal or coal dust and burned as fuel [briquette]</p><p><b>briket, briketirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a block made from charcoal or coal dust and burned as fuel [briquet]</p><p><b>Židovski obred obrezivanja dječaka na osmi dan života (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Jewish rite of circumcision performed on a male child on the eighth day of his life [Berit, Berith, Briss, Brith]</p><p><b>"Strajnost" je snaga koja se može primijeniti na proizvodnju električne energije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the shattering or crushing effect of a sudden release of energy as in an explosion</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to primjenjuje se na proizvodnju i proizvodnju goriva i goriva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the power (the shattering effect) of an explosive</p><p><b>Glavni i najveći grad države Queensland (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capital and largest city of Queensland state</p><p><b>Australsko stablo s tvrdim bijelim drvetom i sjajnim zelenim lišćama s bijelim cvijećem, a zatim s jednosemnim sjajnim plavim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree having hard white timber and glossy green leaves with white flowers followed by one-seeded glossy blue fruit [Elaeocarpus grandis, blue fig, quandong, quandong tree, silver quandong tree]</p><p><b>bodar, brz, krepak, okretan, oštar, svjež, živahan</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become brisk [brisk up, brisken]</p><p><i>adj.</i> quick and energetic [alert, lively, merry, rattling, snappy, spanking, zippy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> imparting vitality and energy [bracing, fresh, refreshful, refreshing, tonic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> very active</p><p><b>Postati brz. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become brisk [brisk, brisken]</p><p><b>Postati brz. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become brisk [brisk, brisk up]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je proizvod proizveden iz goveđe hrane, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvod se može koristiti samo za proizvodnju goveđe hrane. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cut of meat from the breast or lower chest especially of beef</p><p><b>okretan, ubrzano, živahan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a brisk manner</p><p><b>bodar, brz, krepak, okretan, oštar, svjež, živahan (od &quot;brisk&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> liveliness and eagerness [alacrity, smartness]</p><p><b>mala masna evropska riba, Srednja cijena za proizvodnju: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small fatty European fish [sprat]</p><p><i>n.</i> small herring processed like a sardine [Clupea sprattus, sprat]</p><p><b>Židovski obred obrezivanja dječaka na osmi dan života (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Jewish rite of circumcision performed on a male child on the eighth day of his life [Berit, Berith, Bris, Brith]</p><p><b>čekinja, ježiti se, ljutiti se, nakostriješiti, nakostriješiti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stiff fiber (coarse hair or filament)</p><p><i>n.</i> a stiff hair</p><p><i>v.</i> be in a state of movement or action [abound, burst]</p><p><i>v.</i> rise up as in fear [stand up, uprise]</p><p><i>v.</i> have or be thickly covered with or as if with bristles</p><p><i>v.</i> react in an offended or angry manner</p><p><b>pokazuju ljutnju ili ogorčenost (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> show anger or indignation [bridle at, bridle up, bristle up]</p><p><b>četkica napravljena od kratkih čvrstih dlaka životinje ili biljke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brush that is made with the short stiff hairs of an animal or plant</p><p><b>Svaka paprika iz roda Trichomanes koja ima velike pinnatifične, često prozirne lišće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any fern of the genus Trichomanes having large pinnatifid often translucent fronds [filmy fern]</p><p><b>travnjake i šume s velikim ukrasnim šiljcima s dugim četkama ispod svakog šiljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grasses of grasslands and woodlands having large gracefully arching spikes with long bristles beneath each spikelet [bristlegrass]</p><p><b>pokazuju ljutnju ili ogorčenost (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> show anger or indignation [bridle at, bridle up, bristle at]</p><p><b>Vrste kao četkice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pointed like bristles</p><p><b>Piramidalna jelka sa jugozapadne Kalifornije s trnastima oštricama lišća i konusnim ljuskama s dugim šiljcima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pyramidal fir of southwestern California having spiny pointed leaves and cone scales with long spines [Abies bracteata, Abies venusta, Santa Lucia fir]</p><p><b>mali sporo rastući planinski bor zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (Rocky Mountains) s gustim granama s puklom hrđavo-sjedom kore i kratkim iglama u gomilama od 5 i šiljastim ljuskama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small slow-growing upland pine of western United States (Rocky Mountains) having dense branches with fissured rust-brown bark and short needles in bunches of 5 and thorn-tipped cone scales [Pinus aristata, Rocky Mountain bristlecone pine]</p><p><b>čekinjav, naježen, nakostrušen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or covered with protective barbs or quills or spines or thorns or setae etc. [barbed, barbellate, briary, briery, bristly, burred, burry, prickly, setaceous, setose, spiny, thorny]</p><p><b>travnjake i šume s velikim ukrasnim šiljcima s dugim četkama ispod svakog šiljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grasses of grasslands and woodlands having large gracefully arching spikes with long bristles beneath each spikelet [bristle grass]</p><p><b>kao čipka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a bristle</p><p><b>mali insekt bez krila s dugim bristlicnim repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small wingless insect with a long bristlelike tail</p><p><b>kvaliteta pokrivanja trnima ili trnima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being covered with prickly thorns or spines [prickliness, spininess, thorniness]</p><p><b>bodljikav, čekinjast</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very irritable [prickly, splenetic, waspish]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or covered with protective barbs or quills or spines or thorns or setae etc. [barbed, barbellate, briary, briery, bristled, burred, burry, prickly, setaceous, setose, spiny, thorny]</p><p><b>veliki grm ili malo drvo iz istočne Sjedinjenih Država s šipkastim stabljikama i velikim grmovima ružičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large shrub or small tree of the eastern United States having bristly stems and large clusters of pink flowers [Robinia hispida, moss locust, rose acacia]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjen europski korov s trnastima lišcima u obliku jezika i žutim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widespread European weed with spiny tongue-shaped leaves and yellow flowers [Picris echioides, bitterweed, bugloss, oxtongue]</p><p><b>biljka s crnim plodovima i ljekovitim ljuskom iz istočne i središnje Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bristly herb of eastern and central North America having black fruit and medicinal bark [Aralia hispida, bristly sarsparilla, dwarf elder]</p><p><b>biljka s crnim plodovima i ljekovitim ljuskom iz istočne i središnje Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bristly herb of eastern and central North America having black fruit and medicinal bark [Aralia hispida, bristly sarsaparilla, dwarf elder]</p><p><b>Bristol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industrial city and port in southwestern England near the mouth of the River Avon</p><p><b>Uliv u Atlantskom oceanu između južnog Walesa i jugozapadne Engleske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inlet of the Atlantic Ocean between southern Wales and southwestern England</p><p><b>u Velikoj Britaniji ili u toj zemlji, U slučaju da je to potrebno za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije II., Minutni rakovi koji čine hranu za kitove. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Great Britain [Britisher, Briton]</p><p><i>n.</i> the young of a herring or sprat or similar fish [britt]</p><p><i>n.</i> minute crustaceans forming food for right whales [britt]</p><p><b>Britanija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monarchy in northwestern Europe occupying most of the British Isles [Great Britain, U.K., UK, United Kingdom, United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alloy similar to pewter</p><p><b>Britanije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of Britain</p><p><b>(koristi se u množini) neformalni izraz za gaće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (use