n olivelike fruits [Buckleya distichophylla]</p><p><b>parazitski grm iz istočne Sjedinjenih Država s suprotnim lištima i beznačajnim zelenkastim cvijećima s masnim, tupim zelenim plodovima nalik maslinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> parasitic shrub of the eastern United States having opposite leaves and insignificant greenish flowers followed by oily dull green olivelike fruits [buckleya]</p><p><b>Američki arhitekt koji je izumio geodeznu kupola (1895-1983) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States architect who invented the geodesic dome (1895-1983) [Fuller, R. Buckminster Fuller, Richard Buckminster Fuller]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od 99,99% ili više, ali ne više od 99,99% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spheroidal fullerene [buckyball]</p><p><b>platno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coarse cotton fabric stiffened with glue</p><p><i>v.</i> stiffen with or as with buckram</p><p><i>adj.</i> rigidly formal [starchy, stiff]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a saw that is set in a frame in the shape of an H</p><p><b>besplatno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> free of charge</p><p><b>sačma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small lead shot for shotgun shells [bird shot, duck shot]</p><p><b>jelenska koža</b></p><p><i>n.</i> horse of a light yellowish dun color with dark mane and tail</p><p><i>n.</i> a soft yellowish suede leather originally from deerskin but now usually from sheepskin</p><p><b>jelenska koža (od &quot;buckskin&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (used in the plural) breeches made of buckskin</p><p><b>uskolisni trputac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shrub or shrubby tree of the genus Rhamnus</p><p><i>n.</i> any shrub or small tree of the genus Bumelia</p><p><i>n.</i> an Old World plantain with long narrow ribbed leaves widely established in temperate regions [English plantain, Plantago lanceolata, narrow-leaved plantain, ribgrass, ribwort, ripple-grass]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 1. točkom (a) ovog poglavlja upotrebljavaju proizvodi iz kategorije 9a ili 9a, točka (a) ovog poglavlja ne smije se primjenjivati na proizvode iz kategorije 9a ili 9a. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fruit of various buckthorns yielding dyes or pigments [yellow berry]</p><p><b>Drveće i grmovi obično trnasti s drupastih plodova, mnogi s ljekovitim učinkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trees and shrubs usually thorny bearing drupaceous fruit many having medicinal value [Rhamnaceae, family Rhamnaceae]</p><p><b>veliki izbočni prednji zub (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large projecting front tooth</p><p><b>heljda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the genus Fagopyrum [Fagopyrum esculentum, Polygonum fagopyrum]</p><p><i>n.</i> grain ground into flour</p><p><b>palačinke napravljene od brašna. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pancake made with buckwheat flour</p><p><b>rod biljaka reda Polygonales uglavnom iz sjeverne umjerene zone (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of plants of order Polygonales chiefly of the north temperate zone [Polygonaceae, family Polygonaceae]</p><p><b>stablo niskoližnih obalnih područja jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s sjajnim lištima i rasemi mirisnih bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree of low-lying coastal areas of southeastern United States having glossy leaves and racemes of fragrant white flowers [Cliftonia monophylla, titi]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od 99,99% ili više, ali ne više od 99,99% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spheroidal fullerene [buckminsterfullerene]</p><p><b>seljak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a country person [peasant, provincial]</p><p><i>n.</i> a short poem descriptive of rural or pastoral life [eclogue, idyl, idyll]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used with regard to idealized country life) idyllically rustic [arcadian, pastoral]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to shepherds or herdsmen or devoted to raising sheep or cattle [pastoral]</p><p><b>Bukurešt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> national capital and largest city of Romania in southeastern Romania [Bucharest, Bucharesti, capital of Romania]</p><p><b>oko, pup, pupolja