egah, budgerigar, budgie, grass parakeet, lovebird, shell parakeet]</p><p><b>budžet, proračun, proračuna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sum of money allocated for a particular purpose</p><p><i>n.</i> a summary of intended expenditures along with proposals for how to meet them</p><p><i>v.</i> make a budget</p><p><b>Zakon o smanjenju proračunskih troškova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of reducing budgeted expenditures</p><p><b>budžetski deficit, proračunski deficit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an excess of expenditures over revenues</p><p><b>izračunao dovoljno novca za (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> calculate enough money for</p><p><b>troškovi održavanja imovine (npr. plaćanje poreza na imovinu i komunalnih usluga te osiguranja) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the expense of maintaining property (e.g., paying property taxes and utilities and insurance) [operating cost, operating expense, overhead]</p><p><b>budžetski, proračunska, proračunski, proračunskim</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a budget</p><p><b>papigica, tigrica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Australian parakeet usually light green with black and yellow markings in the wild but bred in many colors [Melopsittacus undulatus, budgereegah, budgerigar, budgerygah, grass parakeet, lovebird, shell parakeet]</p><p><b>Gnu koze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gnu goats [genus Budorcas]</p><p><b>velika gota, vrlo čvrsto građena, iz istočnog Himalaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large heavily built goat antelope of eastern Himalayan area [gnu goat, takin]</p><p><b>bitka u Meksikanskom ratu 1847. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pitched battle in the Mexican War in 1847</p><p><b>Buenos Aires</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capital and largest city of Argentina [capital of Argentina]</p><p><b>koža, koža bika, polirati, usjajiti, fan, ljubitelj, obožavatelj, pristaša, politirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ardent follower and admirer [devotee, fan, lover]</p><p><i>n.</i> a soft thick undyed leather from the skins of e.g. buffalo or oxen</p><p><i>n.</i> bare skin</p><p><i>n.</i> a medium to dark tan color [caramel, caramel brown, raw sienna, yellowish brown]</p><p><i>n.</i> an implement consisting of soft material mounted on a block [buffer]</p><p><i>v.</i> strike, beat repeatedly [buffet]</p><p><i>v.</i> polish and make shiny [burnish, furbish]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of the yellowish-beige color of buff leather</p><p><b>od crne boje, odbojene s crvenom bojom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of brown tinged with buff</p><p><b>ima bledu boju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a buff color [buff-coloured]</p><p><b>ima bledu boju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a buff color [buff-colored]</p><p><b>bivol, bizon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large shaggy-haired brown bison of North American plains [American bison, American buffalo, Bison bison]</p><p><i>n.</i> a city on Lake Erie in western New York (near Niagara Falls)</p><p><i>n.</i> meat from an American bison</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several Old World animals resembling oxen including, e.g., water buffalo [Old World buffalo]</p><p><i>v.</i> intimidate or overawe</p><p><b>Američki showman poznat po svom Wild West Showu (1846-1917) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States showman famous for his Wild West Show (1846-1917) [Buffalo Bill Cody, Cody, William F. Cody, William Frederick Cody]</p><p><b>Američki showman poznat po svom Wild West Showu (1846-1917) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States showman famous for his Wild West Show (1846-1917) [Buffalo Bill, Cody, William F. Cody, William Frederick Cody]</p><p><b>spektakularno prikazivanje koje je 1883. godine organizovao William F. Cody koje je uključivalo jahanje konja i strijeljenje na velikoj razini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spectacular show organized in 1883 by William F. Cody that featured horseback riding and marksmanship on a large scale [Wild West Show]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička noćna šuma s trnastim lišćem i žutim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American nightshade with prickly foliage and racemose yellow flowers [Solanum rostratum]</p><p><b>mali crn