ct in a computer program, system, or machine [glitch]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small hidden microphone</p><p><i>n.</i> insects with sucking mouthparts and forewings thickened and leathery at the base [hemipteran, hemipteron, hemipterous insect]</p><p><i>n.</i> a minute life form (especially a disease-causing bacterium) [germ, microbe]</p><p><i>v.</i> annoy persistently [badger, beleaguer, pester, tease]</p><p><i>v.</i> tap a telephone or telegraph wire to get information [intercept, tap, wiretap]</p><p><b>isturiti, izbočiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bulge outward [bulge, bulge out, come out, pop, pop out, protrude, start]</p><p><b>entomolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a zoologist who studies insects [bugologist, entomologist]</p><p><b>zamišljeno čudovište koje se koristi za plašenje djece., razlog za zabrinutost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary monster used to frighten children [bogeyman, booger, boogeyman, bugbear]</p><p><i>n.</i> a source of concern</p><p><b>država Ugande i mjesto bivšeg Bantu kraljevstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of Uganda and site of a former Bantu kingdom</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička biljka s velikim listovima i žutkastozelenim cvijećem koja raste u rasceme, biljka rodova Cimicifuga s cvjetovima u dugim rascima ili panicama za koje se izvješćuje da su neokusne za insekte (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American plant having large leaves and yellowish green flowers growing in racemes [American hellebore, Indian poke, Veratrum viride, white hellebore]</p><p><i>n.</i> a plant of the genus Cimicifuga having flowers in long racemes or panicles reported to be distasteful to insects</p><p><b>Baba Roga, bauk, goblin koji jede zločestu djecu, problem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary monster used to frighten children [bogeyman, booger, boogeyman, bugaboo]</p><p><i>n.</i> an object of dread or apprehension [hobgoblin]</p><p><b>S odjeljkom za upravljanje sustavima za upravljanje informacijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having hidden electronic eavesdropping devices<