bles over other growth [Rubus australis, Rubus cissoides, lawyer bush, lawyerbush]</p><p><b>liga timova koji ne pripadaju glavnoj ligi (posebno bejzbolu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a league of teams that do not belong to a major league (especially baseball) [minor league, minors]</p><p><b>igrač u bejzbol timu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a player on a minor-league baseball team [minor leaguer]</p><p><b>godišnji s tamnožutim cvijećem manji od običnog vrtnog nasturtiuma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual with deep yellow flowers smaller than the common garden nasturtium [Tropaeolum minus]</p><p><b>Rast prema van. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> grow outward</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka iz roda Thermopsis koja ima trifolijalna lišća i žute ili ljubičaste cvjetove racemose (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Thermopsis having trifoliate leaves and yellow or purple racemose flowers</p><p><b>Zlatno žuti cvet koji se često uzgaja u jugozapadnim dijelovima SAD-a i Meksika zbog mirisnih zlatno žutih cvijeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen shrub of southwestern United States and Mexico often cultivated for its fragrant golden yellow flowers [tree poppy]</p><p><b>afrička šriketa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an African shrike</p><p><b>aktivni sivi titmice zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> active grey titmice of western North America [bushtit]</p><p><b>Europski ljubičastocvetni s tankim stabljikama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European purple-flowered with slender stems [Vicia sepium]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko biljaka rodova Browallia uzgajanih zbog svojih plavih ili ljubičastih ili bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several herbs of the genus Browallia cultivated for their blue or violet or white flowers [browallia]</p><p><b>mala južnoafrička stabla sa kremasto-žutim mirisnim cvijećem koja obično rastu na obali potoka, mala listovita stabla iz Transvala s šiljkama žutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small South African tree having creamy yellow fragrant flowers usually growing on stream banks [Combretum erythrophyllum]</p><p><i>n.</i> small deciduous tree of the Transvaal having spikes of yellow flowers [Combretum appiculatum]</p><p><b>Ne najkvalitetnije ili najsofisticiranije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not of the highest quality or sophistication [bush]</p><p><b>Agilicni noćni afrički lemur s dugim repom, guste dlakave krzna i velikim očima i ušima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> agile long-tailed nocturnal African lemur with dense woolly fur and large eyes and ears [bush baby, galago]</p><p><b>Antilope sa bijelim oznakama poput opreme i iskrivljenim rogovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antelope with white markings like a harness and twisted horns [Tragelaphus scriptus, guib]</p><p><b>blazinica ležaja, cjevčica, čahura, grm, guštik, slavina, šikara, utičnica, zatvarač, žbun, žbunje (od &quot;bush&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very tired [all in, beat, dead]</p><p><b>bušel, mjera za količinu, krpiti, obnavljati, obnoviti, popraviti, popravljati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a United States dry measure equal to 4 pecks or 2152.42 cubic inches</p><p><i>n.</i> a British imperial capacity measure (liquid or dry) equal to 4 pecks</p><p><i>v.</i> restore by replacing a part or putting together what is torn or broken [doctor, fix, furbish up, mend, repair, restore, touch on]</p><p><b>košara dovoljno velika da primi špilj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a basket large enough to hold a bushel</p><p><b>Bushido</b></p><p><i>n.</i> traditional code of the Japanese samurai which stressed courage and loyalty and self-discipline and simple living</p><p><b>čahura, izolacijaska cijev, izolacijska cijev, izolacijska cjevčica, izolator, izvod, jaram, umetak, utičnica, utikača kutija, utikačka kutija, vođica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an insulating liner in an opening through which conductors pass</p><p><i>n.</i> a cylindrical metal lining used to reduce friction [cylindrical lining]</p><p><b>nomadski lovci i sakupljači koji žive u južnoj Africi, stanovnik australijske šume. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nomadic hunters and gatherers who live in southern Africa [Khoisan]</p><p><i>n.</i> a dweller in the Australian bush country</p><p><b>Zeleni grm ili drvo iz Južne Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen shrub or tree of South Africa [Acocanthera oppositifolia, Acocanthera venenata, ordeal tree]</p><p><b>Američki izumitelj koji je 1775. godine dizajnirao potopnicu koja je bila neučinkovita, ali mu je kasnije zaslužila priznanje kao pionir podmornice (1742-1824) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American inventor who in 1775 designed a man-propelled submarine that was ineffectual but subsequently earned him recognition as a submarine pioneer (1742-1824) [David Bushnell, Father of the Submarine]</p><p><b>aktivni sivi titmice zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> active grey titmice of western North America [bush tit]</p><p><b>vrebati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> wait in hiding to attack [ambuscade, ambush, lie in wait, lurk, scupper, waylay]</p><p><i>v.</i> live in the bush as a fugitive or as a guerilla</p><p><i>v.</i> cut one's way through the woods or bush</p><p><b>vrebati (od &quot;bushwhack&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disparaging term for an unsophisticated person [hillbilly]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Confederate guerrilla during the American Civil War</p><p><b>vrebati (od &quot;bushwhack&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lying in ambush</p><p><b>čupav, grmovit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> used of hair [shaggy, shaggy-coated, shaggy-haired]</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a bush in being thickly branched and spreading</p><p><b>tvrda višegodišnja biljka sa malim linearnim lišćama i brojnim malim bijelim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stiff perennial of the eastern United States having small linear leaves and numerous tiny white flower heads [Aster dumosus]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko hroničara rodova Neotoma iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s grmljivim repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several bushy-tailed rodents of the genus Neotoma of western North America [Neotoma cinerea, pack rat, packrat, trade rat]</p><p><b>užurbano</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a busy manner</p><p><b>biznis, djelatnost, djelovanje, gospodarstvo, komercijalan, poduzeće, poduzetništvo, portfelj, posao, poslovan, poslovanje, poslovati, poslovni, promet, radni, trgovina, tvrtka, zanimanje, zaposlenost, djelatnosti, djelovanju, poslovanja, poslovna, poslovne, poslovnih, poslovnim, poslovno, poslovnog, trgovački posao, branša, glavni cilj, klijentela, epizoda, točka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a commercial or industrial enterprise and the people who constitute it [business concern, business organisation, business organization, concern]</p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of providing goods and services involving financial and commercial and industrial aspects [business enterprise, commercial enterprise]</p><p><i>n.</i> the principal activity in your life that you do to earn money [job, line, line of work, occupation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a rightful concern or responsibility</p><p><i>n.</i> an immediate objective</p><p><i>n.</i> the volume of commercial activity</p><p><i>n.</i> business concerns collectively [business sector]</p><p><i>n.</i> customers collectively [clientele, patronage]</p><p><i>n.</i> incidental activity performed by an actor for dramatic effect [byplay, stage business]</p><p><b>poslovanje, komercijalna djelatnost, poslovna djetanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> activity undertaken as part of a commercial enterprise [commercial activity]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je to potrebno za obavljanje poslovanja, podnositelj zahtjeva može zatražiti: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the address at which a business is located</p><p><b>Agent koji vodi poslovne poslove za drugog. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agent who handles business affairs for another</p><p><b>posjetnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a card on which are printed the person's name and business affiliation</p><p><b>škola za podučavanje poslovnih i trgovinskih aspekata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school for teaching the clerical aspects of business and commerce</p><p><b>Sredstva za upravljanje poslovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of individuals who manage businesses [businessmen]</p><p><b>biznis, posao</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a commercial or industrial enterprise and the people who constitute it [business, business organisation, business organization, concern]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (a) Uredbe (EU) br. 575/2013 za sve države članice u kojima se primjenjuje ovaj članak, za sve države članice u kojima se primjenjuje ovaj članak, primjenjuje se sljedeći odredbi: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> recurring fluctuations in economic activity consisting of recession and recovery and growth and decline [trade cycle]</p><p><b>obrada poslovnih podataka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> data processing in accounting or business management [administrative data processing]</p><p><b>posao</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a particular instance of buying or selling [deal, trade]</p><p><b>porezni otpis za troškove poslovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tax write-off for expenses of doing business</p><p><b>podjela poslovnog društva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a division of a business firm</p><p><b>središnje područje ili trgovački centar grada ili grada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the central area or commercial center of a town or city [downtown]</p><p><b>urednik novina odgovoran za poslovne vijesti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the newspaper editor responsible for business news</p><p><b>biznis, poduzetništvo, posao</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of providing goods and services involving financial and commercial and industrial aspects [business, commercial enterprise]</p><p><b>poslovni prostor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an establishment (a factory or an assembly plant or retail store or warehouse etc.) where business is conducted, goods are made or stored or processed or where services are rendered [place of business]</p><p><b>dužnosnik, menadžer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an executive in a business corporation [corporate executive]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 12. stavkom 1. točkom (a) Uredbe (EU) br. 1303/2013 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ordinary and necessary expenses incurred in a taxpayer's business or trade [trade expense]</p><p><b>poduzeće, firma, kompanija, tvrtka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the members of a business organization that owns or operates one or more establishments [firm, house]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, "poduzeća" znači društva koja se bave proizvodnjom proizvoda ili usluga. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statistical compilation that provides a context for economic or financial conditions</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ovog članka, u (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> insurance that provides protection for the loss of profits and continuing fixed expenses resulting from a break in commercial activities due to the occurrence of a peril</p><p><b>tajkun</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a very wealthy or powerful businessman [baron, big businessman, king, magnate, mogul, power, top executive, tycoon]</p><p><b>poslovno pismo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a letter dealing with business</p><p><b>Službeni radni radni staž u industriji ili trgovini ili profesionalnim djelatnostima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a career in industrial or commercial or professional activities [professional life]</p><p><b>poslovna linija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a particular kind of product or merchandise [line, line of business, line of merchandise, line of products, product line]</p><p><b>Službeni račun: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bank loan granted for the use of a business [commercial loan]</p><p><b>poslovni ručak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lunch (usually at a restaurant) where business is discussed and the cost is charged as a business expense</p><p><b>vijesti o poduzećima i ulaganjima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> news about businesses and investments</p><p><b>poslovnica, kancelarija, poslovni prostor, ured</b></p><p><i>n.</i> place of business where professional or clerical duties are performed [office]</p><p><b>biznis, posao</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a commercial or industrial enterprise and the people who constitute it [business, business concern, business organization, concern]</p><p><b>biznis, posao</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a commercial or industrial enterprise and the people who constitute it [business, business concern, business organisation, concern]</p><p><b>osobe koje posluju (posebno poslovni rukovodioci) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people who transact business (especially business executives) [businesspeople]</p><p><b>poslovni odnos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relation between different business enterprises</p><p><b>*account, business relationship, raeun</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a formal contractual relationship established to provide for regular banking or brokerage or business services [account]</p><p><b>Srednja škola koja nudi studije koje vode do diplome magistra poslovne administracije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graduate school offering study leading to a degree of Master in Business Administration</p><p><b>poslovne brige kolektivno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> business concerns collectively [business]</p><p><b>poslovno odijelo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a suit of clothes traditionally worn by businessmen</p><p><b>putnik čiji troškovi su plaćeni od strane posla za koje radi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a traveler whose expenses are paid by the business he works for</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to primjenjivo u svim državama članicama, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, poduzeća koja su u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog članka mogu imati:, Ne odvraćajući pažnju od cilja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> exhibiting methodical and systematic characteristics that would be useful in business</p><p><i>adj.</i> not distracted by anything unrelated to the goal [earnest]</p><p><b>biznismen, poslovan čovjek, poslovni čovjek, privrednik, poduzetnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person engaged in commercial or industrial business (especially an owner or executive) [man of affairs]</p><p><b>poslovni ljudi, poslovnih ljudi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of individuals who manage businesses [business community]</p><p><b>osobe koje posluju (posebno poslovni rukovodioci) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people who transact business (especially business executives) [business people]</p><p><b>biznismen, poduzetnik, poslovni čovjek</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a capitalist who engages in industrial commercial enterprise [bourgeois]</p><p><b>poslovna žena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a female businessperson</p><p><b>svirati glazbu na javnom mjestu i tražiti novac za to (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> play music in a public place and solicit money for it</p><p><b>ulični svirač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who entertains people for money in public places (as by singing or dancing), usually while asking for money</p><p><b>gležnjača, gležnjerica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a boot reaching halfway up to the knee [combat boot, desert boot, half boot, top boot]</p><p><b>Broj putnika ili količina tereta koji autobus može prevoziti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quantity of cargo or the number of passengers that a bus can carry</p><p><b>vozač autobusa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who drives a bus [bus driver]</p><p><b>praznik gdje radite iste stvari koje radite na poslu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a holiday where you do the same things you do at work</p><p><b>lijek (trgovinski naziv BuSpar) koji je posebno dizajniran za anksioznost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug (trade name BuSpar) designed specifically for anxiety [buspirone]</p><p><b>lijek (trgovinski naziv BuSpar) koji je posebno dizajniran za anksioznost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug (trade na