tle, hustle]</p><p><b>dahom, užurban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of energetic and noisy activity</p><p><b>bujnih grudi, prsata, sisata</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a woman's body) having a large bosom and pleasing curves [bosomy, buxom, curvaceous, curvy, full-bosomed, sonsie, sonsy, stacked, voluptuous, well-endowed]</p><p><b>čeprkati, dati posao, marljiv, okupiran, prometan, radan, radin, užurban, vrijedan, zaposlen, zaposliti, zauzet, zauzeto, baviti se, okupirati se, zanimati se, zaposliti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> keep busy with [occupy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> actively or fully engaged or occupied</p><p><i>adj.</i> overcrowded or cluttered with detail [fussy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> intrusive in a meddling or offensive manner [busybodied, interfering, meddlesome, meddling, officious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> crowded with or characterized by much activity</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of facilities such as telephones or lavatories) unavailable for use by anyone else or indicating unavailability [engaged, in use]</p><p><b>osoba koja je budna i energična (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alert and energetic person [eager beaver, live wire, sharpie, sharpy]</p><p><b>njuškalo, trčkaralo, zabadalo, zabadati (od &quot;busybody&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> intrusive in a meddling or offensive manner [busy, interfering, meddlesome, meddling, officious]</p><p><b>njuškalo, trčkaralo, zabadalo, zabadati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who meddles in the affairs of others [nosey-parker, nosy-parker, quidnunc]</p><p><b>poduzetnost, zauzetost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being or appearing to be actively engaged in an activity [hum]</p><p><b>aktivno radno djelo male vrijednosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> active work of little value [make-work]</p><p><b>a, ali, ama, iako, ipak, kakogod, ma, mada, nego, no, osim, osim da, pak, samo, tek, već, zamjerka</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> and nothing more [just, merely, only, simply]</p><p><b>bijeli kristalni ester koji se nanosi na sluznice kao lokalni anestetik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</