 koja pokriva gležanj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shoe covering the ankle</p><p><b>koji ima kalcij</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> derived from or containing calcium or lime</p><p><b>uzgajanje ili život u zemljištu bogatom vapnom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> growing or living in soil rich in lime</p><p><b>kalciferol, kolekalciferol, vitamin D</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fat-soluble vitamin that prevents rickets [D, cholecalciferol, ergocalciferol, viosterol, vitamin D]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> bearing or producing or containing calcium or calcium carbonate or calcite</p><p><b>koji uključuju ili proizlaze iz kalcifikacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving or resulting from calcification</p><p><b>kalcifikacija, kalcit, ovapnjenje, pretvarati u vapno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a process that impregnates something with calcium (or calcium salts)</p><p><i>n.</i> tissue hardened by deposition of lime salts</p><p><i>n.</i> an inflexible and unchanging state</p><p><b>uzgoj ili život u kiselom tlu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> growing or living in acid soil</p><p><b>ovapniti, pretvoriti u vapno, stvrdnuti, zakrečiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become impregnated with calcium salts</p><p><i>v.</i> become inflexible and unchanging</p><p><i>v.</i> turn into lime</p><p><i>v.</i> convert into lime</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,25% ili više, ali ne više od 0,25%,, prekrivanje kalciminom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a water-base paint containing zinc oxide and glue and coloring</p><p><i>v.</i> cover with calcimine</p><p><b>kaljenje, oksidacija, pečenje, pretvarati u vapno, žarenje, kalcinacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the conversion of metals into their oxides as a result of heating to a high temperature</p><p><b>oksidirati, pretvarati u vapno</b></p><p><i>v.</i> heat a substance so that it oxidizes or reduces</p><p><b>vapno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white crystalline oxide used in the production of calcium hydroxide [burnt lime, calcium oxide, calx, fluxing lime, lime, quicklime, unslaked lime]</p><p><b>Kakit, kalcit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common mineral consisting of crystallized calcium carbonate</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili sadržavaju kalcit (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or containing calcite</p><p><b>kalcitonin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thyroid hormone that tends to lower the level of calcium in the blood plasma and inhibit resorption of bone [thyrocalcitonin]</p><p><b>kalcij, kalcijev, kalcijeva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white metallic element that burns with a brilliant light [Ca, atomic number 20]</p><p><b>bikarbonat koji je glavni uzrok tvrde vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bicarbonate that is a major cause of hard water</p><p><b>bilo koji od lijekova koji blokiraju protok elektrolita kalcija (ili u provodljivosti živčanih stanica ili kontrakcije glatkih mišića srca) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a class of drugs that block the flow of the electrolyte calcium (either in nerve cell conduction or smooth muscle contraction of the heart) [calcium-channel blocker]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena (POP) od 1,5% ili više, ali ne više od 2,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a grey salt of calcium (CaC) used in making acetylene</p><p><b>kalcijev karbonat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt found in nature as chalk or calcite or aragonite or limestone</p><p><b>slijepa sol (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deliquescent salt</p><p><b>u obliku kalčana, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a caustic substance produced by heating limestone [calcium hydroxide, caustic lime, hydrated lime, lime, lime hydrate, slaked lime]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% masenog dianafta (CAS RN 1344-26-8) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a saltlike binary compound (CaH2) used as a reducing agent and source of hydrogen [hydrolith]</p><p><b>u obliku kalčana, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a caustic substance produced by heating limestone [calcium hydrate, caustic lime, hydrated lime, lime, lime hydrate, slaked lime]</p><p><b>bilo koji kalcijum hipo