serving to heat [calefactory]</p><p><b>služeći na toplinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to heat [calefactive]</p><p><b>kalendar, kalendarski, kalendarskoj, pregled</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of timekeeping that defines the beginning and length and divisions of the year</p><p><i>n.</i> a list or register of events (appointments or social events or court cases etc)</p><p><i>n.</i> a tabular array of the days (usually for one year)</p><p><i>v.</i> enter into a calendar</p><p><b>civilni dan, kalendarski dan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a day reckoned from midnight to midnight [civil day]</p><p><b>prirodno planiranje obitelji u kojem se pretpostavlja da se ovulacija događa 14 dana prije početka menstruacije (predpostavlja se da se plodno razdoblje proteže od 10. dana do 18. dana njenog ciklusa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> natural family planning in which ovulation is assumed to occur 14 days before the onset of a period (the fertile period would be assumed to extend from day 10 through day 18 of her cycle) [calendar method of birth control, rhythm, rhythm method, rhythm method of birth control]</p><p><b>prirodno planiranje obitelji u kojem se pretpostavlja da se ovulacija događa 14 dana prije početka menstruacije (predpostavlja se da se plodno razdoblje proteže od 10. dana do 18. dana njenog ciklusa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> natural family planning in which ovulation is assumed to occur 14 days before the onset of a period (the fertile period would be assumed to extend from day 10 through day 18 of her cycle) [calendar method, rhythm, rhythm method, rhythm method of birth control]</p><p><b>kalendarski mjesec, mjesec</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the twelve divisions of the calendar year [month]</p><p><b>kalendarski tjedan, sedmica, tjedan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a period of seven consecutive days starting on Sunday [week]</p><p><b>građanska godina, kalendarska godina, svjetovna godina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the year (reckoned from January 1 to December 31) according to Gregorian calendar [civil year]</p><p><b>kalendar, kalender, mašina glačali, stroj glačalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a machine that smooths or glazes paper or cloth by pressing it between plates or passing it through rollers</p><p><i>v.</i> press between rollers or plates so as to smooth, glaze, or thin into sheets</p><p><b>kalendar, kalender, mašina glačali, stroj glačalica (od &quot;calender&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of paper and fabric and leather) having a surface made smooth and shiny especially by pressing between rollers [glossy]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je to potrebno za određivanje vrijednosti, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, točka (b) ovog Pravilnika može se upotrebljavati za određivanje vrijednosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of or used in a calendar or time measurement [calendrical]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je to potrebno za određivanje vrijednosti, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, točka (b) ovog Pravilnika može se upotrebljavati za određivanje vrijednosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of or used in a calendar or time measurement [calendric]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih uglavnom jednogodišnjih biljaka iz roda Calendula široko uzgajanih zbog žutih ili narandžastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous chiefly annual herbs of the genus Calendula widely cultivated for their yellow or orange flowers</p><p><b>neven</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the common European annual marigold [Scotch marigold, common marigold, pot marigold, ruddles]</p><p><b>Zimična jednogodišnja biljka s slabim stablom koja je izvorno iz mediteranske regije i dugo se nalazi na jugu Sjedinjenih Država. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a weak-stemmed winter annual native to Mediterranean region for long established in southern United States [Lathyrus hirsutus, rough pea, singletary pea, wild winterpea]</p><p><b>lane, lisni mišić na nozi, list, list na nozi, mladi kit, mlado, priglup čovjek, tele, teleća 