 down]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be calm or quiet as by administering a sedative to [sedate, tranquilize, tranquillise, tranquillize]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not agitated [serene, tranquil, unagitated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of weather) free from storm or wind</p><p><b>Vjetar brzinom manjom od 1 čvor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wind moving at less than 1 knot [calm]</p><p><b>smiriti se, primiriti se, primirivati se, smirivati se, stišati se, umiriti se, umirivati se, upokojiti se, smiriti, smirivati, stišati, utišati, utihnuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become quiet or calm, especially after a state of agitation [calm, chill out, cool it, cool off, settle down, simmer down]</p><p><i>v.</i> make calm or still [calm, lull, quiet, quieten, still, tranquilize, tranquillise, tranquillize]</p><p><i>v.</i> become quiet or less intensive [lull]</p><p><b>bez vjetra, hladnokrvan, miran, mirno, smiren, staložen, tišina, umiriti se, utišati (od &quot;calm&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of appeasing (as by acceding to the demands of) [appeasement]</p><p><b>mirno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with self-possession (especially in times of stress)</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a sedate manner [sedately]</p><p><b>bez vjetra, hladnokrvan, miran, mirno, smiren, staložen, tišina, umiriti se, utišati (od &quot;calm&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> steadiness of mind under stress [calm, composure, equanimity]</p><p><i>n.</i> an absence of strong winds or rain</p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of calm</p><p><b>obična višegodišnja planinara umjerenih regija Evroazije i Sjeverne Amerike s gustim izduženim grmovima cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common perennial climber of temperate regions of Eurasia and North America having dense elongate clusters of flowers [Vicia cracca, bird vetch, tufted vetch]</p><p><b>rod tropskih američkih stabala iz obitelji Sapotaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of tropical American trees of the family Sapotaceae [genus Calocarpum]</p><p><b>tropsko američko stablo koje ima drvo poput mahagonija i slatko j