ible agaric with a brown fruiting body that is often compound [pig's ears]</p><p><b>dlakava lisičarka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mildly poisonous fungus with a fruiting body shaped like a hollow trumpet [floccose chanterelle]</p><p><b>bilo koji kut oka gdje se susreću gornje i donje kapke. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of the corners of the eye where the upper and lower eyelids meet</p><p><b>crkvena himna, Pjesma nad pjesmama</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hymn derived from the Bible</p><p><b>knjiga Starog zavjeta koja se sastoji od zbirke ljubavnih pjesama koje se tradicionalno pripisuju Salomonu, ali koje je zapravo napisano mnogo kasnije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Old Testament book consisting of a collection of love poems traditionally attributed to Solomon but actually written much later [Canticles, Song of Solomon, Song of Songs]</p><p><b>U kojem je Isus bio? (Luka 2:29-32) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the prayer of Simeon (Luke 2:29-32) [Nunc dimittis]</p><p><b>crkvena himna, Pjesma nad pjesmama (od &quot;canticle&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Old Testament book consisting of a collection of love poems traditionally attributed to Solomon but actually written much later [Canticle of Canticles, Song of Solomon, Song of Songs]</p><p><b>konzola, prosta greda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> projecting horizontal beam fixed at one end only</p><p><i>v.</i> project as a cantilever</p><p><i>v.</i> construct with girders and beams such that only one end is fixed</p><p><b>most izgrađen od dva kantilevera koji se susreću u sredini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bridge constructed of two cantilevers that meet in the middle</p><p><b>recitirati uz glazbenu intonaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> recite with musical intonation [chant, intonate, intone]</p><p><b>liturgijsko pjevanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> liturgical chanting</p><p><b>zadnja strana sjedala za sedlo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the back of a saddle seat</p><p><b>najviši dio (obično melodija) u pjesmi za zbor, Glavni dio duge pjesme. (MT)</b></p><p>