ide]</p><p><b>uzimanje iz različitih biljaka i korištenje za stimulaciju srca u slučajevima srčane insuficijencije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> obtained from a number of plants and used to stimulate the heart in cases of heart failure [cardiac glucoside]</p><p><b>nedostatak protoka krvi u srčane mišiće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inadequate blood flow to the heart muscles [coronary insufficiency]</p><p><b>hitna procedura koja koristi ritmičku kompresiju srca (ili kroz prsni zid ili, tijekom operacije, izravno na srce) u pokušaju održavanja cirkulacije tijekom srčanog zastoja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an emergency procedure that employs rhythmic compression of the heart (either through the chest wall or, during surgery, directly to the heart) in an attempt to maintain circulation during cardiac arrest [heart massage]</p><p><b>monitor srčane aktivnosti, srčani monitor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of electronic equipment for continual observation of the function of the heart [heart monitor]</p><p><b>abnormalni zvuk srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal sound of the heart [heart murmur, murmur]</p><p><b>mišićno tkivo srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the muscle tissue of the heart [heart muscle]</p><p><b>količina krvi koja se iz pumpa iz komora u određenom vremenskom razdoblju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of blood pumped out by the ventricles in a given period of time</p><p><b>srčani stimulator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialized bit of heart tissue that controls the heartbeat [SA node, pacemaker, sinoatrial node]</p><p><b>nervni pleksus koji opskrbljuje srce i obližnje strukture (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plexus of nerves supplying the heart and nearby structures [plexus cardiacus]</p><p><b>hitna procedura koja se sastoji od vanjske masaže srca i umjetnog disanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an emergency procedure consisting of external cardiac massage and artificial respiration [CPR, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, kiss of life, mouth-to-mouth resuscitation]</p><p><b>ritam kucajućeg srca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the rhythm of a beating heart [heart rhythm]</p><p><b>ventil između distalnog kraja jednjaka i želuca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the valve between the distal end of the esophagus and the stomach</p><p><b>mehanička kompresija srca koja je posljedica velike količine tekućine koja se skuplja u perikardnom prostoru i ograničava normalan raspon kretanja srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mechanical compression of the heart resulting from large amounts of fluid collecting in the pericardial space and limiting the heart's normal range of motion</p><p><b>ventil za kontrolu jednokrevetnog protoka krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a valve to control one-way flow of blood [heart valve]</p><p><b>Cardiff</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Wales</p><p><b>kratki pleteni kaputić, vunena jakna, vuneni džemper, kardigan, pletena vesta, vesta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> knitted jacket that is fastened up the front with buttons or a zipper</p><p><i>n.</i> slightly bowlegged variety of corgi having rounded ears and a long tail [Cardigan Welsh corgi]</p><p><b>Korgije s kratkim nogama, okruglim ušima i dugim repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slightly bowlegged variety of corgi having rounded ears and a long tail [Cardigan]</p><p><b>u obliku srca, s peščanom kopnom, dvoslojne školjke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> somewhat heart-shaped sand-burrowing bivalve mollusks [family Cardiidae]</p><p><b>bitan, glavni, kardinal, kardinalni, osnovni, prost (broj), svjetlocrven</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) one of a group of more than 100 prominent bishops in the Sacred College who advise the Pope and elect new Popes</p><p><i>n.</i> the number of elements in a mathematical set [cardinal number]</p><p><i>n.</i> a variable color averaging a vivid red [carmine]</p><p><i>n.</i> crested thick-billed North American finch having bright red plumage in the male [Cardinalis cardinalis, Richmondena Cardinalis, cardinal grosbeak, redbird]</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving as an essential component [central, fundamental, key, primal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being or denoting a numerical quantity but not order</p><p><b>Talijanski kardinal i teolog (1542. - 1621.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian cardinal and theologian (1542-1621) [Bellarmine, Bellarmino, Roberto Francesco Romolo Bellarmine]</p><p><b>glavna točka horizonta, glavna točka obzora, kardinalna točka horizonta, kardinalna točka obzora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the four main compass points</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička lobelija s sjajnim crvenim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American lobelia having brilliant red flowers [Indian pink, Lobelia cardinalis]</p><p><b>Punočastog sjevernoameričkog pimpeka s crvenim perjem u mužjaku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crested thick-billed North American finch having bright red plumage in the male [Cardinalis cardinalis, Richmondena Cardinalis, cardinal, redbird]</p><p><b>Engleski svećenik i teolog koji je (zajedno s Johnom Kebleom i Edwardom Puseyjem) osnovao Oxfordski pokret (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English prelate and theologian who (with John Keble and Edward Pusey) founded the Oxford movement [John Henry Newman, Newman]</p><p><b>glavni broj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the number of elements in a mathematical set [cardinal]</p><p><b>Francuski svećenik i državnik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French prelate and statesman [Armand Jean du Plessis, Duc de Richelieu, Richelieu]</p><p><b>mala žarko crvena i plava akvarijska riba iz potoka u Brazilu i Kolumbiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small bright red and blue aquarium fish from streams in Brazil and Colombia [Paracheirodon axelrodi]</p><p><b>bilo koji od glavnih venskih kanala kod primitivnih odraslih kralježnjaka i embriona viših kralježnjaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the major venous channels in primitive adult vertebrates and in embryos of higher vertebrates</p><p><b>glavna vrlina, kardinalna vrlina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the seven preeminent virtues</p><p><b>kardinal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) the body of all cardinals of the church [College of Cardinals, Sacred College, Sacred College of Cardinals]</p><p><i>n.</i> the office of cardinal [cardinalship]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, za ribolov u području Unije za koje se primjenjuje članak 2. točka (a) ovog članka, za ribolov u području Unije za koje se primjenjuje članak 2. točka (a) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći odredbi: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small red fishes of coral reefs and inshore tropical waters</p><p><b>Punočastog sjevernoameričkog pimpeka s crvenim perjem u mužjaku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crested thick-billed North American finch having bright red plumage in the male [Richmondena Cardinalis, cardinal, cardinal grosbeak, redbird]</p><p><b>kardinalni broj, kardinalnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (mathematics) the number of elements in a set or group (considered as a property of that grouping)</p><p><b>kardinal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the office of cardinal [cardinalate]</p><p><b>šok uzrokovan srčanim zastojom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shock caused by cardiac arrest</p><p><b>kardiogram</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graphical recording of the cardiac cycle produced by an electrocardiograph [ECG, EKG, electrocardiogram]</p><p><b>EKG, elektrokardiograf, kardiograf</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medical instrument that records electric currents associated with contractions of the heart [electrocardiograph]</p><p><i>n.</i> a medical instrument that measures the mechanical force of cardiac contractions and the amount of blood passing through the heart during a specified period by measuring the recoil of the body as blood is pumped from the ventricles [ballistocardiograph]</p><p><b>EKG, elektrokardiograf, kardiograf (od &quot;cardiograph&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a cardiograph</p><p><b>dijagnostički postupak koji se sastoji u elektroničkom snimanju aktivnosti srca kardiografom (i stvaranju kardiograma) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> diagnostic procedure consisting of recording the activity of the heart electronically with a cardiograph (and producing a cardiogram) [electrocardiography]</p><p><b>epicikloid u kojem je valjani krug jednak fiksnom krugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an epicycloid in which the rolling circle equals the fixed circle</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a directional microphone with a cardioid pattern of sensitivity [cardioid mike]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a directional microphone with a cardioid pattern of sensitivity [cardioid microphone]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili korištene u ili praktikuju kardiologiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or used in or practicing cardiology</p><p><b>kardiolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in cardiology [heart specialist, heart surgeon]</p><p><b>kardiologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of medicine dealing with the heart and its diseases</p><p><b>abnormalno proširenje srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal enlargement of the heart [enlarged heart, megacardia, megalocardia]</p><p><b>- poremećaj (obično nepoznatog porijekla) srčanog mišića (miokarda) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disorder (usually of unknown origin) of the heart muscle (myocardium) [myocardiopathy]</p><p><b>bolest srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of the heart [heart disease]</p><p><b>koji utječu na srce i pluća i njihove funkcije ili su povezani s njima ili ih utječu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or affecting both the heart and the lungs and their functions [cardiorespiratory]</p><p><b>odsutnost sistole (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> absence of systole [asystole, cardiac arrest]</p><p><b>vježbe namijenjene jačanju cirkulacijskog sustava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> exercise intended to strengthen the circulatory system</p><p><b>hitna procedura koja se sastoji od vanjske masaže srca i umjetnog disanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an emergency procedure consisting of external cardiac massage and artificial respiration [CPR, cardiac resuscitation, kiss of life, mouth-to-mouth resuscitation]</p><p><b>koji utječu na srce i pluća i njihove funkcije ili su povezani s njima ili ih utječu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or affecting both the heart and the lungs and their functions [cardiopulmonary]</p><p><b>spazam srčanog sphinctera (između jednjaka i želuca) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spasm of the cardiac sphincter (between the esophagus and the stomach)</p><p><b>biljke ili grmovi s bijelom mrljom u obliku srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tendril-climbing herbs or shrubs whose seeds have a white heart-shaped spot [genus Cardiospermum]</p><p><b>biljni vinogradi iz tropske Amerike i Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herbaceous vine of tropical America and Africa [heartseed]</p><p><b>drvena višegodišnja planina s velikim ukrasnim sjemenama koje liče na balone (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> woody perennial climbing plant with large ornamental seed pods that resemble balloons [balloon vine, heart pea]</p><p><b>kardiovaskularni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or involving the heart and blood vessels</p><p><b>bolest srca i krvožilnoga sustava, kardiovaskularne bolesti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of the heart or blood vessels</p><p><b>srčano-žilni sustav, kardiovaskularni sistem, kardiovaskularni sustav, krvožilni sistem, krvožilni sustav, srčano-žilni sistem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the organs and tissues involved in circulating blood and lymph through the body [circulatory system]</p><p><b>upale srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the heart</p><p><b>vrsta rodovi obitelji Cardiidae: štakorice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the family Cardiidae: cockles [genus Cardium]</p><p><b>uobičajena jestiva evropska škrga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common edible European cockle [edible cockle]</p><p><b>kalcijum blokator (trgovinski naziv Cardizem) koji se koristi za liječenje hipertenzije ili angine ili srčane insuficijencije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a calcium blocker (trade name Cardizem) used in treating hypertension or angina or heart failure [diltiazem]</p><p><b>artičok divlji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> southern European plant having spiny leaves and purple flowers cultivated for its edible leafstalks and roots [Cynara cardunculus]</p><p><i>n.</i> only parts eaten are roots and especially stalks (blanched and used as celery)</p><p><b>prostorija za kockanje na kartama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a room for gambling on card games</p><p><b>kartica, karticama, kartice, kartaška igra</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a game played with playing cards [card game]</p><p><b>profesionalni igrač karata koji živi od varanja u kartnim igrama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a professional card player who makes a living by cheating at card games [card shark, card sharp, card sharper, cardsharper, sharper, sharpie, sharpy]</p><p><b>profesionalni igrač karata koji živi od varanja u kartnim igrama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a professional card player who makes a living by cheating at card games [card shark, card sharp, card sharper, cardsharp, sharper, sharpie, sharpy]</p><p><b>Talijanski pjesnik koji se smatra nacionalnim pjesnikom moderne Italije (1835-1907) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian poet considered the national poet of modern Italy (1835-1907) [Giosue Carducci]</p><p><b>U nekim klasifikacijama za podgrupu ptičica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used in some classifications for a subgroup of finches [subfamily Carduelinae]</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama smatra se tipskim rodom podobitelji Carduelinae iz obitelji Fringillidae: zlatne škrilje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications considered the type genus of a subfamily Carduelinae of the family Fringillidae: goldfinches [genus Carduelis]</p><p><b>juričica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Old World finch whose male has a red breast and forehead [linnet, lintwhite]</p><p><b>Carduelis carduelis, češljugar, štiglić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small European finch having a crimson face and yellow-and-black wings [goldfinch]</p><p><b>Južnoamerička vrsta crvene pfinke s crnom glavom, krilima i repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South American species of scarlet finch with black head and wings and tail [red siskin]</p><p><b>mala škrinka poput škrinka s crvenom krunom i ružičastim grudima i guzicom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small siskin-like finch with a red crown and a rosy breast and rump [redpoll]</p><p><b>mala škrinka poput siskin s crvenom krunom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small siskin-like finch with a red crown [redpoll]</p><p><b>mala žuto-crna evroazijska pfinka sa oštrim kljunom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small yellow-and-black Eurasian finch with a sharp beak [siskin]</p><p><b>lijek protiv hipertenzije (trgovinski naziv Cardura) koji djeluje tako da opušta krvne žile tako da krv lakše prolazi kroz njih. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antihypertensive drug (trade name Cardura) that works by relaxing blood vessels so that blood passes through them more easily [doxazosin]</p><p><b>rod jednogodišnjih ili višegodišnjih bodljikaca Starog svijeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of annual or perennial Old World prickly thistles [genus Carduus]</p><p><b>Europska dvostruka u Sjevernoj Americi s glavama cvijeća u guštima na krajevima grana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European biennial introduced in North America having flower heads in crowded clusters at ends of branches [welted thistle]</p><p><b>Eurasijska višegodišnja biljka naturalizirana u istočnoj Sjevernoj Americi s vrlo trnastim bijelom pamučnim lišćem i nagnutim muškovitim crvenim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian perennial naturalized in eastern North America having very spiny white cottony foliage and nodding musky crimson flower heads [musk thistle, nodding thistle]</p><p><b>biti zabrinut, briga, brinuti, brinuti se, čuvati se, mariti, njega, obazirati se, pažnja, pobrinuti se, pozor, pozornost, skrb, staranje, starati se, zabrinutost, zaštita, brigu, brine, njezi, njegovanje, pomoć, oprez, opreznost, predostrožnost, skrbništvo, starateljstvo, održavanje, njegovati, paziti, skrbiti, skrbiti se, čuvati, htjeti, voljeti, željeti, ravnati, rukovoditi, upravljati, voditi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the work of providing treatment for or attending to someone or something [aid, attention, tending]</p><p><i>n.</i> judiciousness in avoiding harm or danger [caution, forethought, precaution]</p><p><i>n.</i> an anxious feeling [concern, fear]</p><p><i>n.</i> a cause for feeling concern</p><p><i>n.</i> attention and management implying responsibility for safety [charge, guardianship, tutelage]</p><p><i>n.</i> activity involved in maintaining something in good working order [maintenance, upkeep]</p><p><i>v.</i> feel concern or interest</p><p><i>v.</i> provide care for [give care]</p><p><i>v.</i> prefer or wish to do something [like, wish]</p><p><i>v.</i> be in charge of, act on, or dispose of [deal, handle, manage]</p><p><i>v.</i> be concerned with [worry]</p><p><b>Ne pokazuju brigu ili zanimanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> show no concern or interest [give a damn, give a hang, give a hoot]</p><p><b>pružanje zdravstvene skrbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the provision of health care [health care delivery, healthcare delivery]</p><p><b>brinuti se za, mariti, očuvati, pobrinuti se o, postarati se o, voljeti, sviđati se, brinuti se, liječiti, njegovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> have a liking, fondness, or taste (for)</p><p><i>v.</i> be fond of [cherish, hold dear, treasure]</p><p><i>v.</i> provide treatment for [treat]</p><p><b>opterećeni brigama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> burdened by cares [heavy-laden]</p><p><b>zbrinut</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having needed care and attention</p><p><b>nagnuti brod, nagnuti brod zbog popravka, ljuljati se, njihati se, oteturati, posrnuti, posrtati, teturati, zaljuljati se, zanijeti se, zanjihati se, zanositi se, zateturati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pitching dangerously to one side [rock, sway, tilt]</p><p><i>v.</i> walk as if unable to control one's movements [keel, lurch, reel, stagger, swag]</p><p><i>v.</i> move sideways or in an unsteady way [shift, tilt, wobble]</p><p><b>brzi kas, galop, galopirati, karijera, karijere, poziv, služba, trka, zanimanje, zvanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the particular occupation for which you are trained [calling, vocation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the general progression of your working or professional life [life history]</p><p><i>v.</i> move headlong at high speed</p><p><b>savjetovanje o mogućnostima karijere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> counseling on career opportunities</p><p><b>Žena koja je karijeristkinja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman who is a careerist</p><p><b>Čovjek koji je karijerist. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who is a careerist</p><p><b>praksa unapređenja karijere na račun osobnog integriteta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of advancing your career at the expense of your personal integrity</p><p><b>profesionalni koji želi unaprijediti svoju karijeru na bilo koji način i često na račun vlastitog integriteta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a professional who is intent on furthering his or her career by any possible means and often at the expense of their own integrity</p><p><b>bezbrižan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> free of trouble and worry and care [unworried]</p><p><i>adj.</i> cheerfully irresponsible [devil-may-care, freewheeling, happy-go-lucky, harum-scarum, slaphappy]</p><p><b>bezbrižnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cheerful feeling you have when nothing is troubling you [insouciance, lightheartedness, lightsomeness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being without worry or responsibility</p><p><b>brižan, brižljiv, obazriv, oprezan, pažljiv, pažljivom, pomnjiv, predostrožan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> exercising caution or showing care or attention</p><p><i>adj.</i> cautiously attentive [heedful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unhurried and with care and dignity [deliberate, measured]</p><p><i>adj.</i> full of cares or anxiety</p><p><i>adj.</i> mindful of the future in spending money [thrifty]</p><p><b>brižljivo, oprezno, pažljivo, pažnjom, pomno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> taking care or paying attention</p><p><i>adv.</i> as if with kid gloves [cautiously]</p><p><b>brižljivost, brižnost, oprez, opreznost, pažljivost, pedantnost, pomnjivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being cautious [caution, cautiousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being careful and painstaking</p><p><b>medicinski radnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who helps in identifying or preventing or treating illness or disability [PCP, health care provider, health professional, primary care provider]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is responsible for attending to the needs of a child or dependent adult</p><p><b>aljkav, bezbrižan, nehatan, nemaran, neobazriv, nepažljiv, zapušten</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by lack of attention or consideration or forethought or thoroughness</p><p><i>adj.</i> effortless and unstudied</p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually followed by `of') without due thought or consideration [regardless]</p><p><b>bezbrižno, nemarno, nepažljivo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without care or concern [heedlessly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without caution or prudence [incautiously]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a rakish manner [raffishly, rakishly]</p><p><b>bezbrižnost, nehat, nehaj, nehajnost, nemar, nemarnost, neopreznost, nepromišljenost, aljkavost, nebriga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of not being careful or taking pains [sloppiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> failure to act with the prudence that a reasonable person would exercise under the same circumstances [neglect, negligence, nonperformance]</p><p><b>pripadnik finskog naroda koji živi u Kareliji u sjeverozapadnoj Europi Rusije, Finski jezik kojim govore stanovnici Karelije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Finnish people living in Karelia in northwestern European Russia [Karelian]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Finnic language spoken by the people of Karelia [Karelian]</p><p><b>cjelivati, gladiti, maziti, milovanje, poljubac, pomilovati, dragati, grliti, milova