ine or verse</p><p><b>vječnozelena grmlja ili drvo na otoku Catalina (Kalifornija) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen shrub or small tree found on Catalina Island (California) [Prunus lyonii]</p><p><b>otok u Pacifiku uz jugozapadnu obalu Kalifornije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an island resort in the Pacific off the southwestern coast of California [Santa Catalina]</p><p><b>katalog, katalogizirati, spisak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a book or pamphlet containing an enumeration of things [catalogue]</p><p><i>n.</i> a complete list of things [catalogue]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a catalogue, compile a catalogue [catalogue]</p><p><i>v.</i> make an itemized list or catalog of [catalogue]</p><p><b>kupnja robe koja se šalje poštom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> buying goods to be shipped through the mail [mail-order buying]</p><p><b>skup kontrolnih izjava koje su stavljene u knjižnicu i koje se mogu preuzeti po imenu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a set of control statements that have been placed in a library and can be retrieved by name</p><p><b>katalog, katalogizirati, spisak (od &quot;catalog&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a librarian who classifies publications according to a categorial system [cataloguer]</p><p><b>cjenik, katalog, kataloški, kataloškog, popis, spisak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a complete list of things [catalog]</p><p><i>n.</i> a book or pamphlet containing an enumeration of things [catalog]</p><p><i>v.</i> make an itemized list or catalog of [catalog]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a catalogue, compile a catalogue [catalog]</p><p><b>popisivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a librarian who classifies publications according to a categorial system [cataloger]</p><p><b>Katalonija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a region of northeastern Spain</p><p><b>drvo roda Catalpa s velikim lišcima i bijelim cvijećem s dugim tankim strudama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree of the genus Catalpa with large leaves and white flowers followed by long slender pods [Indian bean]</p><p><b>drvo katalpa iz južnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><