ra]</p><p><b>prekinuti, prestao, prestati, završiti se, obustaviti, obustavljati, okončati, okončavati, prekidati, prestajati, stati, zaustaviti, zaustavljati, završavati, završiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (`cease' is a noun only in the phrase `without cease') end</p><p><i>v.</i> put an end to a state or an activity [discontinue, give up, lay off, quit, stop]</p><p><i>v.</i> have an end, in a temporal, spatial, or quantitative sense [end, finish, stop, terminate]</p><p><b>(zakon) pravni lijek koji se izdaje kako bi se stranci zabranila obavljanje ili nastavak obavljanja određene djelatnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a judicial remedy issued in order to prohibit a party from doing or continuing to do a certain activity [enjoining, enjoinment, injunction]</p><p><b>prekid vatre, primirje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of peace agreed to between opponents so they can discuss peace terms [armistice, truce]</p><p><b>besprekidan, neprestan, konstantan, neprekidan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> uninterrupted in time and indefinitely long continuing [constant, incessant, never-ending, perpetual, unceasing, unremitting]</p><p><b>besprekidan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with unflagging resolve [continuously, endlessly, incessantly, unceasingly, unendingly]</p><p><b>besprekidan, neprestan (od &quot;ceaseless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of something that continues without end or interruption [continuousness, incessancy, incessantness]</p><p><b>Svi majmuni Novog svijeta osim marmozetova i tamarina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> all the New World monkeys except marmosets and tamarins [family Cebidae]</p><p><b>važna luka na otoku Cebu na Filipinima, jedno od otoka Visayan u središnjem dijelu Filipina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an important seaport on the island of Cebu in the Philippines [Cebu City]</p><p><i>n.</i> one of the Visayan islands of the central Philippines</p><p><b>važna luka na otoku Cebu na Filipinima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an important seaport on the island of Cebu in the Philippines [Cebu]</p><p><b>tvrdo vlakno koje se koristi za izradu grube niti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hard fiber used in making coarse twine [cantala, manila maguey]</p><p><b>stanovnik otoka Cebu, jezik naroda Cebu na Filipinima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inhabitant of the island of Cebu</p><p><i>n.</i> language of the people of Cebu in the Philippines [Cebuano]</p><p><b>jezik naroda Cebu na Filipinima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> language of the people of Cebu in the Philippines [Cebuan]</p><p><b>Pitice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pygmy marmosets [genus Cebuella]</p><p><b>Najmanji majmun. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the smallest monkey [pygmy marmoset]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Cebidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Cebidae [genus Cebus]</p><p><b>majmun iz Srednje i Južne Amerike s gustim kosom na glavi koja liči na monaški kapuljač (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monkey of Central America and South America having thick hair on the head that resembles a monk's cowl [capuchin, ringtail]</p><p><b>od ili nalik cecumu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or like a cecum [caecal]</p><p><b>crvuljak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vestigial process that extends from the lower end of the cecum and that resembles a small pouch [appendix, vermiform appendix, vermiform process]</p><p><b>žuljni komarici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gall midges [family Cecidomyidae]</p><p><b>Američki filmski redatelj poznat po svojim ekstravagantnim i spektakularnim epskim produkcijama (1881-1959) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film maker remembered for his extravagant and spectacular epic productions (1881-1959) [Cecil Blount DeMille, DeMille]</p><p><b>Američki filmski redatelj poznat po svojim ekstravagantnim i spektakularnim epskim produkcijama (1881-1959) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film maker remembered for his extravagant and spectacular epic productions (1881-1959) [Cecil B. DeMille, DeMille]</p><p><b>Engleski fizičar koji je otkrio pion (prvi poznati mezon) koji je subatomska čestica koja drži jezgro zajedn