osporin (trgovinski naziv Rocephin) koji se koristi za tešku infekciju pluća ili grla ili ušiju ili mokraćnog trakta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a parenteral cephalosporin (trade name Rocephin) used for severe infection of the lungs or throat or ears or urinary tract [Rocephin]</p><p><b>cefalosporin koji se može davati parenteralno (trgovinski naziv Zinacef) ili oralno u obliku tableta (trgovinski naziv Ceftin) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cephalosporin that can be given parenterally (trade name Zinacef) or orally by tablets (trade name Ceftin) [Ceftin, Zinacef]</p><p><b>tropska američka stabla s palmatno složenim lišćama i najozbiljnijim zvonovitim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American trees with palmately compound leaves and showy bell-shaped flowers [genus Ceiba]</p><p><b>masivno tropsko stablo sa dubokim grebenima na masivnom deblu i nosivim velikim strukom sjemenki prekrivenim svilovitom nitom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> massive tropical tree with deep ridges on its massive trunk and bearing large pods of seeds covered with silky floss [Bombay ceiba, God tree, ceiba tree, kapok, silk-cotton tree, white silk-cotton tree]</p><p><b>masivno tropsko stablo sa dubokim grebenima na masivnom deblu i nosivim velikim strukom sjemenki prekrivenim svilovitom nitom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> massive tropical tree with deep ridges on its massive trunk and bearing large pods of seeds covered with silky floss [Bombay ceiba, Ceiba pentandra, God tree, kapok, silk-cotton tree, white silk-cotton tree]</p><p><b>mala južnoamerička trnasta stabla s tamnocrvenom i crvenom crvenom cvjetom samostalna ili u skupovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small South American spiny tree with dark crimson and scarlet flowers solitary or clustered [Erythrina crista-galli, common coral tree, cry-baby tree, crybaby tree]</p><p><b>neformalno društveno okupljanje na kojem se izvodi škotska ili irska narodna glazba i pjevanje i narodni ples i pričanje priča (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an informal social gathering at which there is Scottish or Irish folk music and singing and folk dancing and story telling</p><p><b>donji pojas, gornja granica, maksimalna visina leta, plafon, prečanica stropa, strop, tavanica, vršni, granica, krov</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the overhead upper surface of a covered space</p><p><i>n.</i> (meteorology) altitude of the lowest layer of clouds</p><p><i>n.</i> an upper limit on what is allowed [cap, roof]</p><p><i>n.</i> maximum altitude at which a plane can fly (under specified conditions)</p><p><b>donji pojas, gornja granica, maksimalna visina leta, plafon, prečanica stropa, strop, tavanica, vršni (od &quot;ceiling&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> provided with a ceiling especially the overhead interior surface</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička godišnja biljka s obično žutim ili narandžastom cvjetom, višegodišnje biljke s granatnim drvenim stablom i svijetlo žutim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American annual plant with usually yellow or orange flowers [Impatiens capensis, jewelweed, lady's earrings, orange balsam, touch-me-not]</p><p><i>n.</i> perennial herb with branched woody stock and bright yellow flowers [Chelidonium majus, greater celandine, swallow wort, swallowwort]</p><p><b>višegodišnje biljke porijeklom iz šumarskih područja istočne Sjedinjenih Država s žutim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial herb native to woodland of the eastern United States having yellow flowers [Stylophorum diphyllum, wood poppy]</p><p><b>drveće i grmovi i drvene loze obično s plodovima svijetle boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trees and shrubs and woody vines usually having bright-colored fruits [family Celastraceae, spindle-tree family, staff-tree family]</p><p><b>ukrasna azijska loza s najozbiljnije narandžasto-žuto voće s crvenom arilom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental Asiatic vine with showy orange-yellow fruit with a scarlet aril [Celastrus orbiculatus, Japan bittersweet, Japanese bittersweet, oriental bittersweet]</p><p><b>rod drvenih vinove loze i uspravnih grmlja (tipni rod Celastraceae) koji je izvorno nastanjen uglavnom u Aziji i Australiji: uključuje gorko-slatko (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of woody vines and erect shrubs (type genus of the Celastraceae) that is native chiefly to Asia and Australia: includes bittersweet [genus Celastrus]</p><p><b>ukrasna azijska loza s najozbiljnije narandžasto-žuto voće s crvenom arilom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental Asiatic vine with showy orange-yellow fruit with a scarlet aril [Celastric articulatus, Japan bittersweet, Japanese bittersweet, oriental bittersweet]</p><p><b>u obliku žutih kapsula koje sadrže crveno crveno sjeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> twining shrub of North America having yellow capsules enclosing scarlet seeds [American bittersweet, bittersweet, climbing bittersweet, false bittersweet, shrubby bittersweet, staff vine, waxwork]</p><p><b>Sulawesi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountainous island in eastern Indonesia [Sulawesi]</p><p><b>misnik, svećenik koji služi misu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is celebrating [celebrater, celebrator]</p><p><i>n.</i> an officiating priest celebrating the Eucharist</p><p><b>praznovati, proslava, proslavili, proslaviti, proslavljati, slaviti, svetkovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> behave as expected during of holidays or rites [keep, observe]</p><p><i>v.</i> have a celebration [fete]</p><p><i>v.</i> assign great social importance to [lionise, lionize]</p><p><b>koji se slavi, opjevanih, slavljen, uvažen, poznat</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> widely known and esteemed [famed, famous, far-famed, illustrious, notable, noted, renowned]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having an illustrious past [historied, storied]</p><p><b>praznovati, proslava, proslavili, proslaviti, proslavljati, slaviti (od &quot;celebrate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is celebrating [celebrant, celebrator]</p><p><b>obilježavanje, proslava, slavlje, zabava, svečanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a joyful occasion for special festivities to mark some happy event [jubilation]</p><p><i>