</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant with an elongated head of broad stalked leaves resembling celery [Brassica rapa pekinensis, Chinese cabbage, napa, pe-tsai]</p><p><i>n.</i> elongated head of crisp celery-like stalks and light green leaves [Chinese cabbage, Chinese celery]</p><p><b>Australazijanski vječnozelena ivorska stabla s gracioznom glavom lišća nalik celeru koji se sastoji od filodnih stabla na osovini listova nalik ljuski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australasian evergreen conifer having a graceful head of foliage resembling celery that is composed of phyllodes borne in the axils of scalelike leaves</p><p><b>celerov korijen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grown for its thickened edible aromatic root [Apium graveolens rapaceum, celeriac, knob celery, root celery, turnip-rooted celery]</p><p><i>n.</i> thickened edible aromatic root of a variety of celery plant [celeriac]</p><p><b>sjemena i sol (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ground celery seed and salt</p><p><b>Sjeme biljke celera koje se koristi kao začin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> seed of the celery plant used as seasoning</p><p><b>štapovi selera posječeni na male štapove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> celery stalks cut into small sticks</p><p><b>Srednji visoki bor tasmanijski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium tall celery pine of Tasmania [Phyllocladus asplenifolius, celery-topped pine]</p><p><b>godišnje biljke koje rastu na močvarnim mjestima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual herb growing in marshy places [Ranunculus sceleratus, cursed crowfoot]</p><p><b>Srednji visoki bor tasmanijski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium tall celery pine of Tasmania [Phyllocladus asplenifolius, celery top pine]</p><p><b>čelesta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musical instrument consisting of graduated steel plates that are struck by hammers activated by a keyboard</p><p><b>božanski, nebeski, rajski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the sky [heavenly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or inhabiting a divine heaven [heavenly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of heaven or the spirit [ethereal, supernal]</p><p><b>nebesko tijelo, svemirsko tijelo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> natural objects visible in the sky [heavenly body]</p><p><b>Rečenice koje se koriste za označavanje raja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> phrases used to refer to Heaven [City of God, Heavenly City, Holy City]</p><p><b>Veliki krug na nebeskoj kugli na pola između nebeskih polova. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the great circle on the celestial sphere midway between the celestial poles [equinoctial, equinoctial circle, equinoctial line]</p><p><b>celestijani globus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a globe that is a spherical model of the heavens</p><p><b>metoda kontrole leta rakete ili svemirske letjelice pomoću položaja nebeskih tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a method of controlling the flight of a missile or spacecraft by reference to the positions of celestial bodies</p><p><b>nebeska hijerarhija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the collective body of angels</p><p><b>Veliki krug na nebeskoj kugli čija ravnica prolazi kroz razumni horizont i centar Zemlje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the great circle on the celestial sphere whose plane passes through the sensible horizon and the center of the Earth [horizon]</p><p><b>(astronomija) ugaona udaljenosti nebeskog tijela sjeverno ili južno od nebeskog ekvatora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) the angular distance of a celestial body north or to the south of the celestial equator [dec, declination]</p><p><b>(astronomija) ekvatorijalna koordinata koja određuje kut, mjeren prema istoku duž nebeskog ekvatora, od proljetne jednodnevice do presjeka satnog kruga koji prolazi kroz objekt na nebu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) the equatorial coordinate specifying the angle, measured eastward along the celestial equator, from the vernal equinox to the intersection of the hour circle that passes through an object in the sky [RA, right ascension]</p><p><b>grana astronomije koja se bavi primjenom Newtonovih zakona kretanja na kretanje nebeskih tijela. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of astronomy concerned with the application of Newton's laws of motion to the motions of heavenly bodies</p><p><b>astronomska navigacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> navigating according to the positions of the stars [astronavigation]</p><p><b>orbita</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the (usually elliptical) path described by one celestial body in its revolution about another [orbit]</p><p><b>točka na nebu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a point in the heavens (on the celestial sphere)</p><p><b>jedna od dvije točke preseka Zemljine osi i nebeske sfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of two points of intersection of the Earth's axis and the celestial sphere [pole]</p><p><b>nebeski svod, nebo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the apparent surface of the imaginary sphere on which celestial bodies appear to be projected [empyrean, firmament, heavens, sphere, vault of heaven, welkin]</p><p><b>celestit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mineral consisting of strontium sulphate</p><p><b>koji pripadaju ili su propisani za celiakiju, od ili u ili pripadaju šupljini trbuha (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to or prescribed for celiac disease</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or in or belonging to the cavity of the abdomen [coeliac]</p><p><b>celiačna arterija, celijačna arterija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery that originates from the abdominal aorta just below the diaphragm and branches into the left gastric artery and the common hepatic artery and the splenic artery [arteria celiaca, celiac trunk, truncus celiacus]</p><p><b>celijakija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disorder in children and adults</p><p><b>arterija koja potječe iz abdominalne aorte odmah ispod dijafragme i odvija se u lijevu želučanu arteriju i zajedničku jetru i srčanu arteriju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery that originates from the abdominal aorta just below the diaphragm and branches into the left gastric artery and the common hepatic artery and the splenic artery [arteria celiaca, celiac artery, truncus celiacus]</p><p><b>beženstvo, celibat, neženstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unmarried status</p>