s form the fundamental structural and functional units of all living organisms [cell theory]</p><p><b>stanična membrana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin membrane (a double layer of lipids) enclosing the cytoplasm of a cell [cytomembrane, plasma membrane]</p><p><b>stanična jezgra, stani na jezgra., jezgra</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a part of the cell containing DNA and RNA and responsible for growth and reproduction [karyon, nucleus]</p><p><b>Specijalizirani dio stanice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialized part of a cell [cell organelle, organelle]</p><p><b>Specijalizirani dio stanice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialized part of a cell [cell organ, organelle]</p><p><b>nazvati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> call up by using a cellular phone</p><p><b>(biologija) teorija da stanice čine temeljne strukturne i funkcionalne jedinice svih živih organizama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) the theory that cells form the fundamental structural and functional units of all living organisms [cell doctrine]</p><p><b>čvrsti sloj polisaharida koji okružuje membranu biljnih i prokariotskih stanica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rigid layer of polysaccharides enclosing the membrane of plant and prokaryotic cells</p><p><b>nedostatak stanica (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking cells</p><p><b>slično ćeliji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a cell</p><p><b>imunološki odgovor (uglavnom protiv virusnih ili gljivičnih invazija ili transplantacije tkiva) koji uključuje T stanice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an immune response (chiefly against viral or fungal invasions or transplanted tissue) that involves T cells</p><p><b>konoba, podrum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lowermost portion of a structure partly or wholly below ground level [basement]</p><p><i>n.</i> an excavation where root vegetables are stored [root cellar]</p><p><i>n.</i> storage space where wines are stored [wine cellar]</p><p><b>podrum(i)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a charge for storing goods in a cellar</p><p><i>n.</i> a storage area in a cellar</p><p><b>odje