ape]</p><p><b>celulozni triacetat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cellulose acetate that is relatively slow to burn [triacetate]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,25% ili više, ali ne više od 0,25%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cellulose ester obtained by treating cellulose with caustic soda [viscose]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena veći od 0,5% i (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plastic made from cellulose (or a derivative of cellulose)</p><p><b>od ili sadržavaju ili su izrađeni od celuloze (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or containing or made from cellulose</p><p><b>šupljina u mezodermu embriona koja kod ljudi dovodi do pleuralne šupljine i perikardne šupljine i peritonealne šupljine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cavity in the mesoderm of an embryo that gives rise in humans to the pleural cavity and pericardial cavity and peritoneal cavity [celoma, coelom]</p><p><b>šupljina u mezodermu embriona koja kod ljudi dovodi do pleuralne šupljine i perikardne šupljine i peritonealne šupljine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cavity in the mesoderm of an embryo that gives rise in humans to the pleural cavity and pericardial cavity and peritoneal cavity [celom, coelom]</p><p><b>Gornji dio: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> weedy annual with spikes of silver-white flowers [red fox]</p><p><b>vrtna godišnja s perjem nalik šiljcima crvenih ili žutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> garden annual with featherlike spikes of red or yellow flowers [Celosia cristata, cockscomb, common cockscomb]</p><p><b>vrtna godišnja s perjem nalik šiljcima crvenih ili žutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> garden annual with featherlike spikes of red or yellow flowers [Celosia argentea cristata, cockscomb, common cockscomb]</p><p><b>Anders Celsius, Celzij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Swedish astronomer who devised the centigrade thermometer (1701-1744) [Anders Celsius]</p><p><b>Celzijusova ljestvica, Celzijusova skala, međunarodna ljestvica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a temperature scale that defines the freezing point of water as 0 degrees and the boiling point of water as 100 degrees [centigrade scale, international scale]</p><p><b>član europskog naroda koji je nekada okupirao Britaniju, Španjolsku i Galiju prije rimskog doba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a European people who once occupied Britain and Spain and Gaul prior to Roman times [Kelt]</p><p><b>keltski, Keltsko, keltsku</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a branch of the Indo-European languages that (judging from inscriptions and place names) was spread widely over Europe in the pre-Christian era [Celtic language]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of the Celts [Gaelic]</p><p><b>Latinski križ s prstenom oko raskrsnice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Latin cross with a ring surrounding the intersection</p><p><b>Bog koji su obožavali Kelti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deity worshipped by the Celts</p><p><b>grana indoeuropskih jezika koja je (s obzirom na natpise i imena mjesta) bila široko raširena po Europi u predkršćanskom dobu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a branch of the Indo-European languages that (judging from inscriptions and place names) was spread widely over Europe in the pre-Christian era [Celtic]</p><p><b>veliki rod stabala i grmova s bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large genus of trees and shrubs with berrylike fruit [genus Celtis]</p><p><b>Celtis australis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bright green deciduous shade tree of southern Europe [European hackberry, Mediterranean hackberry]</p><p><b>lišće lišće s malim crnim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shade tree with small black berries [sugarberry]</p><p><b>veliko lišće koje se nalazi u sjeni južne Sjedinjenih Država s malim crvenokrasnim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large deciduous shade tree of southern United States with small deep purple berries [American hackberry]</p><p><b>u obliku od šuma ili od žitarica ili od žitarica ili od žitarica ili od žitarica ili od žitarica ili od žitarica ili od žitarica ili od žitarica ili od žitara ili od žitara ili od žitara ili od žitara ili od žita