om iglom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (surgery) the act of puncturing a body cavity or organ with a hollow needle in order to draw out fluid</p><p><b>sto stupnjeva, stupanj Celzijeva toplomjera</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a temperature scale on which the freezing point of water is 0 degrees and the boiling point of water is 100 degrees</p><p><b>Celzijusova ljestvica, Celzijusova skala, međunarodna ljestvica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a temperature scale that defines the freezing point of water as 0 degrees and the boiling point of water as 100 degrees [Celsius scale, international scale]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thermometer calibrated in degrees centigrade</p><p><b>(statistika) bilo koji od 99 numeriranih točaka koji dijele uređeni skup ocjena na 100 dijelova od kojih svaki sadrži jedan stotni dio ukupnog broja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (statistics) any of the 99 numbered points that divide an ordered set of scores into 100 parts each of which contains one-hundredth of the total [percentile]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a metric unit of volume equal to one hundredth of a liter [centilitre, cl]</p><p><b>centilitar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a metric unit of volume equal to one hundredth of a liter [centiliter, cl]</p><p><b>peni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fractional monetary unit of several countries: France and Algeria and Belgium and Burkina Faso and Burundi and Cameroon and Chad and the Congo and Gabon and Haiti and the Ivory Coast and Luxembourg and Mali and Morocco and Niger and Rwanda and Senegal and Switzerland and Togo</p><p><i>n.</i> a coin worth one-hundredth of the value of the basic unit [cent, penny]</p><p><b>centimetar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a metric unit of length equal to one hundredth of a meter [centimetre, cm]</p><p><b>centimetar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a metric unit of length equal to one hundredth of a meter [centimeter, 