use-eared chickweed [genus Cerastium]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjen u Arktiku i planinama u Europi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widespread in the Arctic and on mountains in Europe [Alpine mouse-ear, Arctic mouse-ear]</p><p><b>guste tufted višegodišnje chickweed sjeverno umjerenoga područja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> densely tufted perennial chickweed of north temperate zone [field chickweed, field mouse-ear]</p><p><b>čokolada s dlakavim srebrno sivim lišcima i prilično velikim bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chickweed with hairy silver-grey leaves and rather large white flowers [love-in-a-mist, snow-in-summer]</p><p><b>tvrda medicinska pasta od maslaca ili ulja pomiješane s voskom ili smolom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hard medicated paste made of lard or oil mixed with wax or resin</p><p><b>keratin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fibrous scleroprotein that occurs in the outer layer of the skin and in horny tissues such as hair, feathers, nails, and hooves [keratin]</p><p><b>Sredozemski voćni muhe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mediterranean fruit flies [genus Ceratitis]</p><p><b>mala crno-bijela muha koja oštećuje citruse i druga voća implantacijom jaja koja se izležu unutar voća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small black-and-white fly that damages citrus and other fruits by implanting eggs that hatch inside the fruit [Mediterranean fruit fly, medfly]</p><p><b>riblje pluća s rogovitim grebenima na zubima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lungfishes having hornlike ridges on the teeth [family Ceratodontidae]</p><p><b>izumrle plućne ribe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct lungfish</p><p><b>šarobnice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> carobs [genus Ceratonia]</p><p><b>zelena mediteranska stabla s jestivim čunjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen Mediterranean tree with edible pods [algarroba, carob, carob bean tree, carob tree]</p><p><b>u obliku poluploče od vrste C. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dicotyledonous genus of the family Cunoniaceae [genus Ceratopetalum]</p><p><b>Australsko drvo ili grm s crvenim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree or shrub with red flowers [Christmas bush, Christmas tree]</p><p><b>u istoj površini s rodom Ceratophyllum: hornwort (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coextensive with the genus Ceratophyllum: hornworts [family Ceratophyllaceae]</p><p><b>koji čine obitelj Ceratophyllaceae: rogovice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> constituting the family Ceratophyllaceae: hornworts [genus Ceratophyllum]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Ceratopogonidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Ceratopogonidae [genus Ceratopogon]</p><p><b>ubijajuće guske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> biting midges [family Ceratopogonidae]</p><p><b>dinosauri sa rogovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> horned dinosaurs [suborder Ceratopsia]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko četveronožnih biljnih dinosaura s ogromnim kljunom lubanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several four-footed herbivorous dinosaurs with enormous beaked skulls [horned dinosaur]</p><p><b>Američki dinosauri ceratopsijski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American ceratopsian dinosaurs [family Ceratopsidae]</p><p><b>vodeni paprike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> water ferns [genus Ceratopteris]</p><p><b>vodeni paprika iz tropske Amerike često se koristi u akvarijima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aquatic fern of tropical America often used in aquariums [floating fern, water sprite]</p><p><b>Pteropod (Pteropodus) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pantropical aquatic fern [floating fern]</p><p><b>primitivni srednji teropod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> primitive medium-sized theropod [ceratosaurus]</p><p><b>primitivni srednji teropod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> primitive medium-sized theropod [ceratosaur]</p><p><b>gljivice s ugljikovom peritecijom s dugim vratom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungi having carbonous perithecia with long necks [family Ceratostomataceae]</p><p><b>rod gljiva koji formiraju kontinuirane hialinske spore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of fungi forming continuous hyaline spores [genus Ceratostomella]</p><p><b>gljivica koja uzrokuje holandsku bolest