rubs and trees of eastern Asia, southern Europe and the United States [genus Cercis]</p><p><b>malo grmlje istočne Sjeverne Amerike slično drvetu Judas koji obično ima ružičaste cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrubby tree of eastern North America similar to the Judas tree having usually pink flowers [redbud]</p><p><b>grm zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s ružičastim ili crvenokrasnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub of western United States having pink or crimson flowers [California redbud, western redbud]</p><p><b>Mangobeys (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mangabeys [genus Cercocebus]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> froghoppers or spittlebugs [family Cercopidae]</p><p><b>Majmuni Starog svijeta: guenon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World monkeys: guenon [family Cercopithecidae]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Cercopithecidae: guenoni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Cercopithecidae: guenons [genus Cercopithecus]</p><p><b>Bijeli i maslinovito-zeleni istočnoafrički majmun s dugim bijelim grmovima kose pored lica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white and olive green East African monkey with long white tufts of hair beside the face [grivet]</p><p><b>Južnoafrički majmun s crnim licem i rukama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African monkey with black face and hands [vervet, vervet monkey]</p><p><b>obični majmun savane sa zelenkasto-sivom leđom i žutim repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common savannah monkey with greenish-grey back and yellow tail [African green monkey, green monkey]</p><p><b>najmanji guenonski majmun (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> smallest guenon monkey [talapoin]</p><p><b>form rod nesposobnih gljiva koji su paraziti lišća s dugim tankim sporama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> form genus of imperfect fungi that are leaf parasites with long slender spores [genus Cercospora]</p><p><b>gljivica koja uzrokuje žutu mrlju (bolest šećerne trske u Australiji) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungus causing yellow spot (a sugarcane disease in Australia) [yellow spot fungus]</p><p><b>form rod nesposobnih gljiva bez pigmenta u sporama i konidioforima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> form genus of imperfect fungi lacking pigment in the spores and conidiophores [genus Cercosporella]</p><p><b>mesno, vosko pokriće na dnu gornjeg kljunu nekih ptica, Zavijte se u cereklot. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fleshy, waxy covering at the base of the upper beak of some birds</p><p><i>v.</i> wrap up in a cerecloth</p><p><b>zobene pahuljice, žitarica, žitarice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grass whose starchy grains are used as food: wheat [cereal grass]</p><p><i>n.</i> foodstuff prepared from the starchy grains of cereal grasses [food grain, grain]</p><p><i>n.</i> a breakfast food prepared from grain</p><p><i>adj.</i> made of grain or relating to grain or the plants that produce it</p><p><b>čaja za držanje žitarica za doručak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bowl for holding breakfast cereal</p><p><b>papirna kutija u kojoj se prodaju žitarice za doručak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a paper box in which breakfast cereals are sold</p><p><b>U slučaju da je proizvodnja u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka u potpunosti završena, točka (b) ovog članka ne primjenjuje se na proizvodnju u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grass whose starchy grains are used as food: wheat [cereal]</p><p><b>Avena sativa, ovas, zob</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated in temperate regions for its edible grains [Avena sativa]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili su povezani s malenim mozakom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or associated with the cerebellum</p><p><b>arterija koja opskrbljuje mozak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery that supplies the cerebellum [arteria cerebelli]</p><p><b>ili od dva bočna režnja mozak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two lateral lobes of the cerebellum</p><p><b>vene koje isušuju mozak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the veins draining the cerebellum [vena cerebellum]</p><p><b>mali mozak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a major division of the vertebrate brain</p><p><b>cerebralan, moždani, cerebralne, cerebralni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving intelligence rather than emotions or instinct [intellectual]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the cerebrum or brain</p><p><b>aneurizma krvne arterije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an aneurysm of the carotid artery</p><p><b>kanal koji povezuje treću i četvrtu klijetku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a canal connecting the third and fourth ventricles [Sylvian aqueduct, aqueductus cerebri]</p><p><b>bilo koja od arterija koja isporučuje krv u moždani korteks (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the arteries supplying blood to the cerebral cortex [arteria cerebri]</p><p><b>moždana kora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the layer of unmyelinated neurons (the grey matter) forming the cortex of the cerebrum [cerebral mantle, cortex, pallium]</p><p><b>smrt pri nedostatku disanja i drugih refleksnih funkcija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> death when respiration and other reflexes are absent [brain death]</p><p><b>oteklina mozga zbog apsorpcije vode u neuropilu i bijeloj materiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> swelling of the brain due to the uptake of water in the neuropile and white matter [brain edema]</p><p><b>polutka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either half of the cerebrum [hemisphere]</p><p><b>krvarenje iz puknute krvne žile u mozgu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bleeding from a ruptured blood vessel in the brain</p><p><b>sloj neurona bez mijelina (siva tvar) koji formira moždani korteks (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the layer of unmyelinated neurons (the grey matter) forming the cortex of the cerebrum [cerebral cortex, cortex, pallium]</p><p><b>cerebralna paraliza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loss or deficiency of motor control with involuntary spasms caused by permanent brain damage present at birth [spastic paralysis]</p><p><b>Grom mijeliniranih neurona koji se spajaju u različite dijelove mozga. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bundle of myelinated neurons joining different parts of the brain [peduncle]</p><p><b>krvni ugrušak u moždanoj arteriji ili veni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blood clot in a cerebral artery or vein</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko vena koje služe moždanoj hemisferi mozga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several veins serving the cerebral hemispheres of the brain [vena cerebri]</p><p><b>cerebralan, moždani, cerebralne, cerebralni (od &quot;cerebral&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an intellectual manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> in the brain</p><p><b>misliti, mozgati, premišljati se, promisliti, promišljati, promozgati, prosuditi, prosuđivati, rasuditi, rasuđivati, razmisliti, razmišljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> use or exercise the mind or one's power of reason in order to make inferences, decisions, or arrive at a solution or judgments [cogitate, think]</p><p><b>mišljenje, razmišljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of using your mind to consider something carefully [intellection, mentation, thinking, thought, thought process]</p><p><b>upale mozga i kičmene moždine i njihovih moždanih moždanih žlijezda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the brain and spinal cord and their meninges [encephalomeningitis, meningoencephalitis]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s mozgom i kičmenom moždinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the brain and spinal cord</p><p><b>meningitis uzrokovan bakterijama i često smrtonosan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> meningitis caused by bacteria and often fatal [brain fever, cerebrospinal meningitis, epidemic meningitis]</p><p><b>CSF, cerebrospinalni likvor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> clear liquid produced in the ventricles of the brain [spinal fluid]</p><p><b>meningitis uzrokovan bakterijama i često smrtonosan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> meningitis caused by bacteria and often fatal [brain fever, cerebrospinal fever, epidemic meningitis]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s mozgom i krvnim sudovima koji ga opskrbljuju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the brain and the blood vessels that supply it</p><p><b>apopleksija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden loss of consciousness resulting when the 