> liable to be accused, or cause for such liability [indictable]</p><p><b>okrivljen, optužen, pod naponom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a particle or body or system</p><p><i>adj.</i> fraught with great emotion [supercharged]</p><p><i>adj.</i> supplied with carbon dioxide [aerated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of producing violent emotion or arousing controversy</p><p><b>radnik zaposlen za eksplozivne eksplozive (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a workman employed to blast with explosives [blaster]</p><p><b>ispravljač za punjenje, prijenosnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> formerly a strong swift horse ridden into battle [courser]</p><p><i>n.</i> a device that can hold a rechargeable battery by means of an electrical cable [battery charger]</p><p><b>Chari, Shari</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an African river that flows northwest into Lake Chad [Chari River, Shari, Shari River]</p><p><b>Chari, Shari</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an African river that flows northwest into Lake Chad [Chari, Shari, Shari River]</p><p><b>grupa nilsko-saharskih jezika koji se govore u dijelovima Sudana i Zaira i Ugande i Tanzanije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of Nilo-Saharan language spoken in parts of the Sudan and Zaire and Uganda and Tanzania</p><p><b>Chari, Shari (od &quot;chari&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with great caution</p><p><b>Boa zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> boas of western North America [genus Charina]</p><p><b>Boe travnjaka i šuma zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> boa of grasslands and woodlands of western North America [rubber boa, tow-headed snake]</p><p><b>Chari, Shari (od &quot;chari&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being cautious and watchful [wariness]</p><p><b>bojna kola, kola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light four-wheel horse-drawn ceremonial carriage</p><p><i>n.</i> a two-wheeled horse-drawn battle vehicle</p><p><i>v.</i> transport in a chariot</p><p><i>v.</i> ride in a chariot</p><p><b>trka između drevnih kočija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a race between ancient chariots</p><p><b>vozač bojnih kola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the driver of a chariot</p><p><i>n.</i> a conspicuous constellation in the northern hemisphere [Auriga]</p><p><b>karizma, magnetizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a personal attractiveness or interestingness that enables you to influence others [personal appeal, personal magnetism]</p><p><b>karizmatičan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> possessing an extraordinary ability to attract [magnetic]</p><p><b>bolećiv, dobrotvoran, izdašan, benevolentan, dobar, dobrohotan, dobronamjeran, dobrostiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characterized by charity</p><p><i>adj.</i> full of love and generosity</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing or motivated by sympathy and understanding and generosity [benevolent, good-hearted, kindly, large-hearted, openhearted, sympathetic]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u pitanju društvo koje je osnovano u dobrotvorne ili vjerske ili obrazovne ili znanstvene svrhe, u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, društvo može biti: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trust created for charitable or religious or educational or scientific purposes [public trust]</p><p><b>bolećiv, dobrotvoran, izdašan (od &quot;charitable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> generosity as manifested by practicing charity (as for the poor or unfortunate)</p><p><b>dobrostivo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a charitable manner</p><p><b>Caritas, dobročinstvo, dobrotvorna organizacija, dobrotvorna priredba, dobrotvorno društvo, dobrotvornost, karitas, milosrđe, mislosrđe, bratska ljubav, ljubav, ljubav prema bližnjem, milost, dobrotvorstvo, dobrotvorna ustanova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a foundation created to promote the public good (not for assistance to any particular individuals)</p><p><i>n.</i> a kindly and lenient attitude toward people [brotherly love]</p><p><i>n.</i> an activity or gift that benefits the public at large</p><p><i>n.</i> pinnate-leaved European perennial having bright blue or white flowers [Greek valerian, Jacob's ladder, Polemonium caeruleum, Polemonium van-bruntiae, Polymonium caeruleum van-bruntiae]</p><p><i>n.</i> an institution set up to provide help to the needy</p><p><b>Slučaj za socijalnog radnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a case for a welfare worker [welfare case]</p><p><b>Neprekidni košarkaški pogodak sa linije krivice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unhindered basketball shot from the foul line [charity throw, charity toss, foul shot, free throw, penalty free throw]</p><p><b>Neprekidni košarkaški pogodak sa linije krivice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unhindered basketball shot from the foul line [charity shot, charity toss, foul shot, free throw, penalty free throw]</p><p><b>Neprekidni košarkaški pogodak sa linije krivice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unhindered basketball shot from the foul line [charity shot, charity throw, foul shot, free throw, penalty free throw]</p><p><b>bučna lažna serenada (izrada udarajući lonac i čajnik) novonaplavenom paru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a noisy mock serenade (made by banging pans and kettles) to a newly married couple [belling, callathump, callithump, chivaree, shivaree]</p><p><b>varalica, vrač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flamboyant deceiver [mountebank]</p><p><b>šarlatanstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the dishonesty of a charlatan [quackery]</p><p><b>Karlo Veliki</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of the Franks and Holy Roman Emperor [Carolus, Charles, Charles I, Charles the Great]</p><p><b>Grad u jugozapadnom Belgiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> city in southwestern Belgium</p><p><b>Kralj Francuske od 1560. do 1574. čije je vladavine dominirala njegova majka Katarina de Medicis (1550-1574), Kralj Francuske koji je počeo svoju vladavinu s većim dijelom sjeverne Francuske pod engleskom kontrolom, Kao Karlo II. bio je car Svetoga Rimskog Carstva i kao Karlo I. bio je kralj Francuske (823-877), Kralj Engleske i Škotske i Irske tijekom Restauracije (1630-1685), sin Jamesa I koji je bio kralj Engleske, Škotske i Irske, najstariji sin Elizabete II i nasljednik engleskog prijestolja (rođen 1948.), Francuski fizičar i autor Karlovog zakona koji je predvidio Gay-Lussacov zakon (1746-1823), kralj Franaka i car Svetoga Rimskog carstva, Rijeka u istočnom Massachusettsu koja se uliva u Boston Harbor i koja odvaja Cambridge od Bostona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> King of France from 1560 to 1574 whose reign was dominated by his mother Catherine de Medicis (1550-1574) [Charles IX]</p><p><i>n.</i> King of France who began his reign with most of northern France under English control [Charles VII]</p><p><i>n.</i> as Charles II he was Holy Roman Emperor and as Charles I he was king of France (823-877) [Charles I, Charles II, Charles the Bald]</p><p><i>n.</i> King of England and Scotland and Ireland during the Restoration (1630-1685) [Charles II]</p><p><i>n.</i> son of James I who was King of England and Scotland and Ireland [Charles I, Charles Stuart]</p><p><i>n.</i> the eldest son of Elizabeth II and heir to the English throne (born in 1948) [Prince Charles]</p><p><i>n.</i> French physicist and author of Charles's law which anticipated Gay-Lussac's law (1746-1823) [Jacques Alexandre Cesar Charles, Jacques Charles]</p><p><i>n.</i> king of the Franks and Holy Roman Emperor [Carolus, Charlemagne, Charles I, Charles the Great]</p><p><i>n.</i> a river in eastern Massachusetts that empties into Boston Harbor and that separates Cambridge from Boston [Charles River]</p><p><b>Američki avijator koji je 1927. godine prvi samostalni let bez zaustavljanja preko Atlantskog oceana (1902-1974) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States aviator who in 1927 made the first solo nonstop flight across the Atlantic Ocean (1902-1974) [Charles Augustus Lindbergh, Charles Lindbergh, Lindbergh, Lucky Lindy]</p><p><b>Charles de Gaulle</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French general and statesman who became very popular during World War II as the leader of the Free French forces in exile (1890-1970) [Charles de Gaulle, General Charles de Gaulle, General de Gaulle, de Gaulle]</p><p><b>Francuski fizičar poznat po svojim otkrićima u 