od komandom Ulysse S. Granta su pobijedile vojsku Konfederacije pod Braxtonom Braggom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in eastern Tennessee</p><p><i>n.</i> in the American Civil War (1863) the Union armies of Hooker, Thomas, and Sherman under the command of Ulysses S. Grant won a decisive victory over the Confederate Army under Braxton Bragg [battle of Chattanooga]</p><p><b>pokretna imovina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> personal as opposed to real property [movable, personal chattel]</p><p><b>Pozajmicu za kupnju nekih osobnih stvari. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loan to buy some personal item</p><p><b>brbljarija, brbljati, cvrkutanje, čavrljanje, ćaskanje, ćaskati, lupetati, naklapati, torokati, zveketanje, cvokotati, klepetati, klopotati, škljocati, škrgutati, ćakulati, čavrljati, klafrati, laprdati, zvocati, ćeretati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> noisy talk [cackle, yack, yak, yakety-yak]</p><p><i>n.</i> the rapid series of noises made by the parts of a machine [chattering]</p><p><i>n.</i> the high-pitched continuing noise made by animals (birds or monkeys) [chattering]</p><p><i>v.</i> click repeatedly or uncontrollably [click]</p><p><i>v.</i> cut unevenly with a chattering tool</p><p><i>v.</i> talk socially without exchanging too much information [chaffer, chat, chew the fat, chit-chat, chitchat, claver, confab, confabulate, gossip, jaw, natter, shoot the breeze, visit]</p><p><i>v.</i> speak (about unimportant matters) rapidly and incessantly [blab, blabber, clack, gabble, gibber, maunder, palaver, piffle, prate, prattle, tattle, tittle-tattle, twaddle]</p><p><i>v.</i> make noise as if chattering away</p><p><b>Oznake na ledenoj stijeni uzrokovane kretanjem glečera, S druge strane, za proizvodnju proizvoda od čelika ili čelika od čelika ili čelika, osim za proizvodnju proizvoda od čelika ili čelika od čelika ili čelika, s masenim udjelom čelika ili čelika od čelika ili čelika od čelika ili čelika od čelika ili čelika, s masenim udjelom čelika ili čelika od čelika ili čelika od čelika ili čelika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marks on a glaciated rock caused by the movement of a glacier</p><p><i>n.</i> a mark made by a chattering tool on the surface of a workpiece</p><p><b>Orhideja koja raste uz potoke ili jezera u zapadnoj Sjevernoj Americi s lišnim stabljikama i 1 zelenkasto-smeđi i ružičasto cvijeće u osovini svakog gornjeg lišća, Neprijatni, glupi i govorni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orchid growing along streams or ponds of western North America having leafy stems and 1 greenish-brown and pinkish flower in the axil of each upper leaf [Epipactis gigantea, giant helleborine, stream orchid]</p><p><i>n.</i> an obnoxious and foolish and loquacious talker [babbler, chatterer, magpie, prater, spouter]</p><p><b>brbljavac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an obnoxious and foolish and loquacious talker [babbler, chatterbox, magpie, prater, spouter]</p><p><i>n.</i> passerine bird of New World tropics [cotinga]</p><p><b>cvokotanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the rapid series of noises made by the parts of a machine [chatter]</p><p><i>n.</i> the high-pitched continuing noise made by animals (birds or monkeys) [chatter]</p><p><b>govorljiv (od &quot;chatty&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a chatty manner [volubly]</p><p><b>govorljiv, brbljiv, pričljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of trivial conversation [gabby, garrulous, loquacious, talkative, talky]</p><p><i>adj.</i> prone to friendly informal communication [gossipy, newsy]</p><p><b>Engleski pjesnik, poznat kao autor Canterbury Tales (1340-1400) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English poet remembered as author of the Canterbury Tales (1340-1400) [Geoffrey Chaucer]</p><p><b>kofer, šofer, vozač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man paid to drive a privately owned car</p><p><i>v.</i> drive someone in a vehicle [drive around]</p><p><b>Žena vozač. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman chauffeur</p><p><b>Istočnoindijsko stablo s masnim sjemenima daje ulje chaulmoogra koje se koristi za liječenje guba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian tree with oily seeds yield cha