lar, dog collar, neckband]</p><p><i>n.</i> a high tight collar [neck ruff, ruff, ruffle]</p><p><b>Britanski sleng (datirani) za zatvor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British slang (dated) for a prison [choky]</p><p><b>gušenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a condition caused by blocking the airways to the lungs (as with food or swelling of the larynx)</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of suffocating (someone) by constricting the windpipe [strangling, strangulation, throttling]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom energije od 1,15 kVA ili većim, ali ne većim od 2,15 kVA, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coil of low resistance and high inductance used in electrical circuits to pass direct current and attenuate alternating current [choke, choke coil]</p><p><b>Britanski sleng (datirani) za zatvor, Tako čvrsto da se guši. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British slang (dated) for a prison [chokey]</p><p><i>adj.</i> so tight as to tend to choke</p><p><b>radiografski pregled žučnih kanala nakon ubrizgavanja kontrastnog medija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> roentgenographic examination of the bile ducts after a contrast medium has been injected</p><p><b>upale žučnih kanala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the bile ducts</p><p><b>kalciferol, kolekalciferol, vitamin D</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fat-soluble vitamin that prevents rickets [D, calciferol, ergocalciferol, viosterol, vitamin D]</p><p><b>kolecistektomija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical removal of the gall bladder (usually for relief of gallstone pain)</p><p><b>kolecistitis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the gall bladder</p><p><b>hormon iz gastrointestinalnog sustava koji stimulira lučnični enzim i smanjenje i pražnjenje žučne mjehurice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gastrointestinal hormone that stimulates the secretion of pancreatic enzymes and the contraction and emptying of the gall bladder</p><p><b>prisutnost žučnih kamenja u žučnom mjehuru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the presence of gallstones in the gallbladder</p><p><b>uklanjanje žučnih kamenja kroz rez u žučnom mjeh