al from the Alberta region of Canada</p><p><b>S više od 50 kVA, ali ne više od 150 kVA (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instrument for accurate measurements of small intervals of time</p><p><b>bilo kakva promjena u normalnoj strukturi ili broju hromozoma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any change in the normal structure or number of chromosomes [chromosomal aberration, chromosomal anomaly, chromosonal disorder]</p><p><b>kukuljica, lutka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pupa of a moth or butterfly enclosed in a cocoon</p><p><b>krizantema</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the flower of a chrysanthemum plant</p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous perennial Old World herbs having showy brightly colored flower heads of the genera Chrysanthemum, Argyranthemum, Dendranthema, Tanacetum</p><p><b>dvostruko travlje s žutim cvjetovima poput gumbova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tansy-scented Eurasian perennial herb with buttonlike yellow flowers [Tanacetum balsamita, alecost, balsam herb, bible leaf, costmary, mint geranium]</p><p><b>s bijelom cvjetom, s balkanskim površinom, čiji su listovi s pinatom bijelog i svilovitog oblika ispod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white-flowered pyrethrum of Balkan area whose pinnate leaves are white and silky-hairy below [Dalmatia pyrethrum, Dalmatian pyrethrum, Tanacetum cinerariifolium, pyrethrum]</p><p><b>ljetnoputna vrtna višegodišnja biljka azijskog podrijetla s fino podijeljenim aromatičnim listovima i bijelim do ružičastog ljubičastog cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spring-flowering garden perennial of Asiatic origin having finely divided aromatic leaves and white to pink-purple flowers [Tanacetum coccineum, painted daisy, pyrethrum]</p><p><b>Broj biljaka: od 300 do 300 g. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby annual of the Mediterranean region with yellowish-white flowers [crown daisy]</p><p><b>uzgajan zbog svojih sočnih jestivih listova koji se koriste u azijskoj kuhinji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grown for its succulent edible leaves used in Asian cooking [chop-suey greens, shun giku, tong ho]<