p><i>adj.</i> closely encircling [encompassing, surrounding]</p><p><b>ležeći oko ili izvan rubova ili rubova (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lying around or just outside the edges or outskirts</p><p><b>diakritički znak (^) postavljen iznad samoglasnika u nekim jezicima kako bi se označio poseban fonetski kvalitet (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a diacritical mark (^) placed above a vowel in some languages to indicate a special phonetic quality</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko parnih zakrivljenih arterija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several paired curving arteries</p><p><b>arterija koja opskrbljuje zglob kuka i mišiće bedra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery that supplies the hip joint and thigh muscles [arteria circumflexa femoris]</p><p><b>ili dvije vene koje prate arterije istog imena koje služe kuk i bedro (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two veins that accompany arteries of the same name serving the hip and thigh [vena circumflexus femoris]</p><p><b>arterija koja opskrbljuje zglob ramena i mišiće ramena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery that supplies the shoulder joint and shoulder muscles [arteria circumflexa humeri]</p><p><b>arterija koja opskrbljuje donje zidove trbuha i kožu i mišić sartorius (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery that supplies the lower abdominal walls and skin and the sartorius muscle [arteria circumflexa ilium]</p><p><b>prati arteriju istog imena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> accompanies the artery of the same name [vena circumflexa ilium]</p><p><b>arterija koja služi mišićima ramena i skapulera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery that serves the muscles of the shoulder and scapular area [arteria circumflexa scapulae]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko zakrivljenih paralelnih vena koje prate arterije istog imena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several curved parallel veins accompanying arteries of the same name [vena circumflexa]</p><p><b>oblijevati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> spread something around something</p><p><b>okolišanje, rječitost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a style that involves indirect ways of expressing things [ambage, periphrasis]</p><p><i>n.</i> an indirect way of expressing something [indirect expression]</p><p><b>Krugovi i nepotrebno riječito (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> roundabout and unnecessarily wordy [ambagious, circumlocutory, periphrastic]</p><p><b>Krugovi i nepotrebno riječito (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> roundabout and unnecessarily wordy [ambagious, circumlocutious, periphrastic]</p><p><b>oploviti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> travel around, either by plane or ship [compass]</p><p><b>putovanje oko nečega (brodom ili zrakoplovom) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> traveling around something (by ship or plane)</p><p><b>(nebeskog tijela) neprekidno vidljiv iznad horizonta tijekom cijelog 360 stupnjeva dnevnog putovanja, nalazi se ili se nalazi u cijelom polarnom području (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a celestial body) continually visible above the horizon during the entire 360 degrees of daily travel</p><p><i>adj.</i> located or found throughout a polar region</p><p><b>ograničiti, opisati oko, označiti krug</b></p><p><i>v.</i> draw a line around</p><p><i>v.</i> restrict or confine within limits [confine to, limit]</p><p><i>v.</i> to draw a geometric figure around another figure so that the two are in contact but do not intersect</p><p><b>opisan oko</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> subject to limits or subjected to limits [limited]</p><p><b>ograničavanje, ograničenje, okruživanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of circumscribing</p><p><b>oprezan, razborit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> heedful of potential consequences [discreet]</p><p><b>znati kako izbjeći sramotu ili nevolju, osobina biti oprezan i razborit (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> knowing how to avoid embarrassment or distress [discreetness, discretion, prudence]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being circumspect and prudent [caution]</p><p><b>oprezan, razborit (od &quot;circumspect&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a cagey manner [cagily]</p><p><b>okolnost, prilika, slučaj, popratna pojava, utjecaj, kontekst, podatak, stvar, uvjet, činjenica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a condition that accompanies or influences some event or activity</p><p><i>n.</i> the set of facts or circumstances that surround a situation or event [context, setting]</p><p><i>n.</i> information that should be kept in mind when making a decision [condition, consideration]</p><p><i>n.</i> formal ceremony about important occasions</p><p><b>mogućnosti, okolnosti, prilikama, prilike, kob, sreća, sudba, sudbina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> your overall circumstances or condition in life (including everything that happens to you) [destiny, fate, fortune, lot, luck, portion]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person's financial situation (good or bad)</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> fully detailed and specific about particulars</p><p><b>dokazi koji pružaju samo osnovu za zaključivanje o spornoj činjenici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evidence providing only a basis for inference about the fact in dispute [indirect evidence]</p><p><b>prema okolnostima., u pogledu okolnosti, u najmanju detalju., bez unaprijed planiranja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> according to circumstances</p><p><i>adv.</i> insofar as the circumstances are concerned</p><p><i>adv.</i> in minute detail [minutely]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without advance planning [accidentally, by chance, unexpectedly]</p><p><b>dati posredni dokaz za (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give circumstantial evidence for</p><p><b>opkopati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> surround with or as if with a rampart or other fortification</p><p><b>izbjegnuti, nadmudriti, premostiti, prevariti, zaobići, opkoliti, opkoljavati, opsjedati, opsjednuti, opsjesti, izvrdati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> surround so as to force to give up [beleaguer, besiege, hem in, surround]</p><p><i>v.</i> beat through cleverness and wit [beat, outfox, outsmart, outwit, overreach]</p><p><i>v.</i> avoid or try to avoid fulfilling, answering, or performing (duties, questions, or issues) [dodge, duck, elude, evade, fudge, hedge, parry, put off, sidestep, skirt]</p><p><b>izbjegavanje, nadmudrivanje, zaobilazak, zaobilaženje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of evading by going around</p><p><b>Vjetar ili okret u obrtima, posebno u unutrašnjoj spirali, kao u puževu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> wind or turn in volutions, especially in an inward spiral, as of snail</p><p><b>okretanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of turning or winding or folding around a central axis</p><p><b>okretati se, okrenuti, okretati, rotirati, zaokrenuti, zaokretati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to turn on an axis or center [rotate]</p><p><b>cirkus, okrugao trg</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a travelling company of entertainers</p><p><i>n.</i> a performance given by a traveling company of acrobats, clowns, and trained animals</p><p><i>n.</i> a frenetic disorganized (and often comic) disturbance suggestive of a large public entertainment [carnival]</p><p><i>n.</i> (antiquity) an open-air stadium for chariot races and gladiatorial games</p><p><i>n.</i> an arena consisting of an oval or circular area enclosed by tiers of seats and usually covered by a tent</p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of haws comprising the harriers [genus Circus]</p><p><b>akrobat koji izvodi akrobatske podloge u cirkusu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acrobat who performs acrobatic feats in a circus</p><p><b>Harrier Starog svijeta koji često dolazi u močvarne regije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World harrier frequenting marshy regions [marsh harrier]</p><p><b>Uobičajena štaparica iz Sjeverne Amerike i Europe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common harrier of North America and Europe [hen harrier, marsh hawk, northern harrier]</p><p><b>brunasti europski harrier (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brownish European harrier [Montagu's harrier]</p><p><b>Kanvasni šator za smještaj publike na cirkuskoj predstavi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a canvas tent to house the audience at a circus performance [big top, round top, top]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> candlewood of Mexico and southwestern California having tall columnar stems and bearing honey-scented creamy yellow flowers [Fouquieria columnaris, Idria columnaris, boojum tree]</p><p><b>cirk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a steep-walled semicircular basin in a mountain [corrie, cwm]</p><p><b>ciroza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chronic disease interfering with the normal functioning of the liver [cirrhosis of the liver]</p><p><b>ciroza jetre</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chronic disease interfering with the normal functioning of the liver [cirrhosis]</p><p><b>obično zavijena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> usually coiled [cirrus]</p><p><b>morski rakovi s pernatim dodanim dijelovima za hvatanje hrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marine crustaceans with feathery food-catching appendages [barnacle, cirripede]</p><p><b>morski rakovi s pernatim dodanim dijelovima za hvatanje hrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marine crustaceans with feathery food-catching appendages [barnacle, cirriped]</p><p><b>škrge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> barnacles [subclass Cirripedia]</p><p><b>oblak na velikoj visini koji se sastoji od niza redovito raspoređenih malih oblaka koji liče na valove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cloud at a high altitude consisting of a series of regularly arranged small clouds resembling ripples [cirrocumulus cloud]</p><p><b>oblak na velikoj visini koji se sastoji od niza redovito raspoređenih malih oblaka koji liče na valove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cloud at a high altitude consisting of a series of regularly arranged small clouds resembling ripples [cirrocumulus]</p><p><b>tanak ravnomjeran sloj maglovitih oblaka na velikoj visini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin uniform layer of hazy cloud at high altitude [cirrostratus cloud]</p><p><b>tanak ravnomjeran sloj maglovitih oblaka na velikoj visini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin uniform layer of hazy cloud at high altitude [cirrostratus]</p><p><b>hvataljka, vitica, cirus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> usually coiled [cirrhus]</p><p><i>n.</i> a wispy white cloud (usually of fine ice crystals) at a high altitude (4 to 8 miles) [cirrus cloud]</p><p><i>n.</i> a slender flexible animal appendage as on barnacles or crinoids or many insects</p><p><b>cirus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wispy white cloud (usually of fine ice crystals) at a high altitude (4 to 8 miles) [cirrus]</p><p><b>u obliku žitarica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plume thistles [genus Cirsium]</p><p><b>Europski bodljik prirodni u Sjedinjenim Državama i Kanadi gdje je štetna korova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European thistle naturalized in United States and Canada where it is a pernicious weed [Canada thistle, creeping thistle]</p><p><b>čvrsti sjevernoamerički bodljik s ljubičasto-ružičastim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stout North American thistle with purplish-pink flower heads [field thistle]</p><p><b>Udio u kategoriji "Srbija" (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> woolly thistle of western and central Europe and Balkan Peninsula [European woolly thistle]</p><p><b>Čvrstak zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s bijelim vletnim listovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thistle of western North America having white woolly leaves [woolly thistle]</p><p><b>višegodišnji stoloniferni bodljik sjeverne Europe s lanceolatičnim bazalnim listovima i obično samostalnim glavama crvenkasto-fijaznih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial stoloniferous thistle of northern Europe with lanceolate basal leaves and usually solitary heads of reddish-purple flowers [Cirsium heterophylum, melancholy thistle]</p><p><b>višegodišnji stoloniferni bodljik sjeverne Europe s lanceolatičnim bazalnim listovima i obično samostalnim glavama crvenkasto-fijaznih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial stoloniferous thistle of northern Europe with lanceolate basal leaves and usually solitary heads of reddish-purple flowers [Cirsium helenioides, melancholy thistle]</p><p><b>Europski bodljik s prilično velikim glavama i trnastima lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European thistle with rather large heads and prickly leaves [Cirsium vulgare, boar thistle, bull thistle, spear thistle]</p><p><b>Srednje i jugozapadna Europa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of central and southwestern Europe [brook thistle]</p><p><b>Europski bodljik s prilično velikim glavama i trnastima lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European thistle with rather large heads and prickly leaves [Cirsium lanceolatum, boar thistle, bull thistle, spear thistle]</p><p><b>CIS, CSP</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alliance made up of states that had been Soviet Socialist Republics in the Soviet Union prior to its dissolution in Dec 1991 [Commonwealth of Independent States]</p><p><b>na talijanskoj ili rimskoj strani Alpa (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> on the Italian or Roman side of the Alps [ultramontane]</p><p><b>Agencija kanadske vlade koja ujedinjuje obavještajne jedinice kanadskih agencija za provedbu zakona., (računovodstvo) vrsta računalne arhitekture koja ima veliki broj instrukcija hard kodiranih u CPU čip (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agency of the Canadian government that unifies the intelligence units of Canadian law enforcement agencies [Criminal Intelligence Services of Canada]</p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a kind of computer architecture that has a large number of instructions hard coded into the CPU chip [complex instruction set computer, complex instruction set computing]</p><p><b>riblje vrste u hladnoćnoj vodi ulovljene u jezeru Superior i sjeverno, važna hrana za ribe hladnih dubokih jezera Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cold-water fish caught in Lake Superior and northward [lake herring]</p><p><i>n.</i> important food fish of cold deep lakes of North America [Coregonus artedi, lake herring]</p><p><b>smješten između Zemlje i Mjeseca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated between the earth and the moon [sublunar, sublunary]</p><p><b>na ovoj strani planine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> on this (the speaker's) side of the mountains</p><p><b>mekušac</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having unsuitable feminine qualities [effeminate, emasculate, epicene, sissified, sissy, sissyish]</p><p><b>biljke iz područja s umjerenim temperaturama, posebno mediteranske zone (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubs or woody herbs of temperate regions especially Mediterranean [family Cistaceae, rockrose family]</p><p><b>trapist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> member of an order of monks noted for austerity and a vow of silence [Trappist]</p><p><b>bazen za vodu, cisterna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sac or cavity containing fluid especially lymph or cerebrospinal fluid [cisterna]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tank that holds the water used to flush a toilet [water tank]</p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial reservoir for storing liquids</p><p><b>vreća ili šupljina koja sadrži tekućinu, posebno limfu ili moždano-spinalnu tekućinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sac or cavity containing fluid especially lymph or cerebrospinal fluid [cistern]</p><p><b>Boreći se u močvarnim močvarama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marsh wrens [genus Cistothorus]</p><p><b>Američki štap koji živi u visokim trske krevete (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American wren that inhabits tall reed beds [long-billed marsh wren]</p><p><b>mala američka škrga koja živi na vlažnim lijevim livama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small American wren inhabiting wet sedgy meadows [sedge wren, short-billed marsh wren]</p><p><b>(genetika) segment DNK koji je uključen u proizvodnju lanca polipeptida (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) a segment of DNA that is involved in producing a polypeptide chain [factor, gene]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste biljaka koje se nalaze u području Unije, za koje se primjenjuje točka (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje točka (b) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje točka (c) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje točka (d) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje točka (e) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje tačka (e) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje tačka (e) ovog članka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small to medium-sized evergreen shrubs of southern Europe and North Africa [genus Cistus]</p><p><b>kompaktni bijeli pubescentni grm iz