očiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short note recognizing a source of information or of a quoted passage [acknowledgment, citation, credit, mention, quotation, reference]</p><p><i>v.</i> make reference to [advert, bring up, mention, name, refer]</p><p><i>v.</i> commend [mention]</p><p><i>v.</i> refer to [reference]</p><p><i>v.</i> repeat a passage from [quote]</p><p><i>v.</i> refer to for illustration or proof [quote]</p><p><i>v.</i> advance evidence for [abduce, adduce]</p><p><i>v.</i> call in an official matter, such as to attend court [summon, summons]</p><p><b>tipične vjeverice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> typical ground squirrels [Spermophilus, genus Citellus, genus Spermophilus]</p><p><b>prilično velika središnja evroazijska vjeveric (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rather large central Eurasian ground squirrel [souslik, suslik]</p><p><b>Četvrto-crno-plamenača crvenkasto-smeđa vjeveric iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common black-striped reddish-brown ground squirrel of western North America [mantled ground squirrel]</p><p><b>mala vjevericka sa zapada Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small ground squirrel of western United States [antelope chipmunk, antelope squirrel, whitetail antelope squirrel]</p><p><b>Velika zemljana vjeverica sjevernoameričkog krajnjeg sjevera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large ground squirrel of the North American far north [Arctic ground squirrel, parka squirrel]</p><p><b>od žitarica i travnjaka zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Kanade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of sagebrush and grassland areas of western United States and Canada [Richardson ground squirrel, flickertail]</p><p><b>Velika siva vjevericina sa stijenatog područja jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large grey ground squirrel of rocky areas of the southwestern United States [rock squirrel]</p><p><b>rod Bothidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Bothidae [genus Citharichthys]</p><p><b>Vukač koji se nalazi u vodama od Bahama i sjevernog Meksičkog zaljeva do Brazila. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a whiff found in waters from the Bahamas and northern Gulf of Mexico to Brazil [horned whiff]</p><p><b>glazbeni žičani instrument s žica koja su rastegnuta preko ravne zvučne ploče, glazbeni instrument iz 16. stoljeća sličan gitari s zvučnom kutijom u obliku kruške i žičanim žičama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musical stringed instrument with strings stretched over a flat sounding board [zither, zithern]</p><p><i>n.</i> a 16th century musical instrument resembling a guitar with a pear-shaped soundbox and wire strings [cithern, citole, cittern, gittern]</p><p><b>glazbeni instrument iz 16. stoljeća sličan gitari s zvučnom kutijom u obliku kruške i žičanim žičama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a 16th century musical instrument resembling a guitar with a pear-shaped soundbox and wire strings [cither, citole, cittern, gittern]</p><p><b>biti ili imati običaje ili manire ili odjeću gradskog čovjeka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being or having the customs or manners or dress of a city person [city-born, city-bred, cityfied]</p><p><b>Navikli smo na gradske načine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> accustom to urban ways</p><p><b>državljan, državljanin, građanin, podanik, varošanin, žitelj, stanovnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or naturalized member of a state or other political community</p><p><b>Francuski diplomata koji je 1793. pokušao uvući Sjedinjene Države u rat između Francuske i Engleske (1763-1834.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French diplomat who in 1793 tried to draw the United States into the war between France and England (1763-1834) [Edmund Charles Edouard Genet, Genet]</p><p><b>građanstvo, puk, pučanstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of citizens of a state or country [people]</p><p><b>građanski odbor, odbor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a self-constituted organization to promote something [committee]</p><p><b>državljanin, državljanstvo, građanstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the status of a citizen with rights and duties</p><p><i>n.</i> conduct as a citizen</p>