f the state</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or befitting citizens as individuals [civic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of divisions of time) legally recognized in ordinary affairs of life</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or in a condition of social order</p><p><b>tužba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> legal action to protect a private civil right or to compel a civil remedy (as distinguished from criminal prosecution)</p><p><b>civilna vlast, građanska vlast</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who exercises authority over civilian affairs [civil officer]</p><p><b>Vojna cenzura civilne komunikacije (korespondencije ili štampani materijal filmova) koja ulazi ili izlazi iz teritorija pod kontrolom oružanih snaga ili cirkuliše unutar njih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> military censorship of civilian communications (correspondence or printed matter of films) entering or leaving of circulating within territories controlled by armed forces</p><p><b>Nepoštovanje sudskog naloga koji koristi nekom drugom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a failure to follow a court order that benefits someone else</p><p><b>civilni dan, kalendarski dan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a day reckoned from midnight to midnight [calendar day]</p><p><b>pravni status osobe koja je živa, ali koja je lišena prava i privilegija građanina ili člana društva, ukidanje građanskih prava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the legal status of a person who is alive but who has been deprived of the rights and privileges of a citizen or a member of society</p><p><i>n.</i> cancellation of civil rights [attainder]</p><p><b>civilna zaštita</b></p><p><i>n.</i> activities organized by civilians for their own protection in time of war or disaster</p><p><b>građanski neposluh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group's refusal to obey a law because they believe the law is immoral (as in protest against discrimination)</p><p><b>građevinar, građevni inženjer, inženjer graditeljstva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an engineer trained to design and construct and maintain public works (roads or bridges or harbors etc.)</p><p