čne (od &quot;classical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in the manner of Greek and Roman culture</p><p><b>podražavati klasični stil</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make classic or classical [classicize]</p><p><b>kalsicizam, klasicizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a movement in literature and art during the 17th and 18th centuries in Europe that favored rationality and restraint and strict forms [classicalism]</p><p><b>klasicistički, klasicističkog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artistic person who adheres to classicism</p><p><i>n.</i> a student of ancient Greek and Latin [classical scholar]</p><p><b>klasicistički, klasicističkog (od &quot;classicist&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to classicism</p><p><b>napraviti klasični ili klasični (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make classic or classical [classicise]</p><p><b>klasična književnost, klasične nauke, klasika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> study of the literary works of ancient Greece and Rome</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being classified [distinctive]</p><p><b>klasificiranje, klasificirati, klasifikacija, klasifikaciju, poredak, razredba, razvrstavanje, dijeljenje, kategorizacija, sortiranje, kategoriziracija, kategoriziranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of distributing things into classes or categories of the same type [assortment, categorisation, categorization, compartmentalisation, compartmentalization]</p><p><i>n.</i> a group of people or things arranged by class or category [categorisation, categorization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the basic cognitive process of arranging into classes or categories [categorisation, categorization, sorting]</p><p><i>n.</i> restriction imposed by the government on documents or weapons that are available only to certain authorized people</p><p><b>sustav za klasifikaciju stvari. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system for classifying things</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili uključuju klasifikaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or involving classifica