a od 1769. do 1774. koji je izgubio bilo kakvu podršku katoličke Europe, što je dovelo do toga da je crkva pala u ruke svjetovnih knezova (1705-1774) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1769 to 1774 who lost whatever support remained of Catholic Europe, causing the church to fall into the hands of secular princes (1705-1774) [Lorenzo Ganganelli]</p><p><b>klementina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of mandarin orange that is grown around the Mediterranean and in South Africa [clementine tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mandarin orange of a deep reddish orange color and few seeds</p><p><b>vrsta mandarina koja se uzgaja oko Mediterana i u Južnoj Africi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of mandarin orange that is grown around the Mediterranean and in South Africa [clementine]</p><p><b>grčiti, stezanje zuba, stisnuti, zahvat, zakivanje, stisak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small slip noose made with seizing [clinch]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of grasping [clasp, clutch, clutches, grasp, grip, hold]</p><p><i>v.</i> hold in a tight grasp [clinch]</p><p><i>v.</i> squeeze together tightly</p><p><b>grčiti, stezanje zuba, stisnuti, zahvat, zakivanje (od &quot;clench&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> closed or squeezed together tightly [clinched]</p><p><b>stisnuta šaka, pesnica, šaka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hand with the fingers clenched in the palm (as for hitting) [fist]</p><p><b>bilo koja od različitih često snažno mirisajućih biljaka rodova Cleome s navidnim cvjetovima u obliku pauka, tropske i subtropske jednogodišnje ili višegodišnje biljke ili niskoga grmlja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various often strong-smelling plants of the genus Cleome having showy spider-shaped flowers [spiderflower]</p><p><i>n.</i> tropical and subtropical annual or perennial herbs or low shrubs [genus Cleome]</p><p><b>izvorno iz Južne Amerike, ali naturalizirano u toplim dijelovima Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> native to South America but naturalized in warm parts of United States [spider flower, s