something [mount]</p><p><i>v.</i> go upward with gradual or continuous progress [climb up, go up, mount]</p><p><i>v.</i> move with difficulty, by grasping</p><p><i>v.</i> go up or advance [mount, rise, wax]</p><p><i>v.</i> slope upward</p><p><i>v.</i> improve one's social status</p><p><i>v.</i> increase in value or to a higher point [go up, rise]</p><p><b>popuštanje, sići, silaziti, spustiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come down [alight]</p><p><b>uzjahati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> get up on the back of [bestride, get on, hop on, jump on, mount, mount up]</p><p><b>uspeti se, uspinjati se, penjati se, penjati se/popeti se, pentrati se, popeti se, uspentrati se, uzdizati se, uzdići se, uzverati se, verati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> go upward with gradual or continuous progress [climb, go up, mount]</p><p><i>v.</i> appear to be moving upward, as by means of tendrils [ascend]</p><p><i>v.</i> rise in rank or status [jump, rise]</p><p><b>popuštanje, sići, silaziti, spustiti se, odstupanje, povlačenje, uzmak, uzmicanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a retraction of a previously held position [backdown, withdrawal]</p><p><b>koji je sposoban za uzdizanje., S druge strane, za vozila od 8703 do 8704 (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being ascended [ascendable, ascendible]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being surmounted [surmountable]</p><p><b>penjač, planinar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vine or climbing plant that readily grows up a support or over other plants</p><p><i>n.</i> someone seeking social prominence by obsequious behavior [social climber]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who ascends on foot [mounter]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who climbs as a sport</p><p><i>n.</i> an iron spike attached to the shoe to prevent slipping on ice when walking or climbing [climbing iron, crampon, crampoon]</p><p><b>penjanje, uspinjanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that involves rising to a higher point (as in altitude or temperature or intensity etc.) [climb, mounting]</p><p><b>tropska Afrika do Australazije i Polinezije (MT)</b><