, around, just about, more or less, or so, roughly, some]</p><p><b>Skoro suprotno smjeru iz kojeg vjetar dolazi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> nearly opposite to the direction from which wind is coming</p><p><b>udaljeni od sebe (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> located close together [approximate]</p><p><b>gro-plan, snimak iz blizine, isključiti se, zatvoriti, blokirati, prepriječiti, zakrčiti, zatvarati, začepiti, začepljivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cease to operate or cause to cease operating [close, close down, fold, shut down]</p><p><i>v.</i> block passage through [block, impede, jam, obstruct, obturate, occlude]</p><p><i>v.</i> unite or bring into contact or bring together the edges of [close]</p><p><i>v.</i> refuse to talk or stop talking [be quiet, belt up, button up, clam up, dummy up, keep mum, shut up]</p><p><i>adv.</i> very close [at close range]</p><p><b>Prilično je ugodno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> fitting closely but comfortably [close, snug]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 85%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> dense or compact in structure or texture, as a wood composed of small-diameter cells [fine-grained]</p><p><b>Sjedala su pripremljena za plovidbu što bliže vjetru. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the sails trimmed for sailing as close to the wind as possible</p><p><b>Drže se zajedno kao društvene ili kulturne veze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> held together as by social or cultural ties [closely knit]</p><p><b>Ne spremni prihvatiti nove ideje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not ready to receive to new ideas [closed-minded]</p><p><b>(vojna) vojna vježba trupa u standardnom marširanju (rame uz rame) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (military) military drill of troops in standard marching (shoulder-to-shoulder)</p><p><b>posebno čvrsto pakirana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> packed especially tightly</p><p><b>borbe od ruke do ruke u bliskom okruženju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hand-to-hand fighting at close quarters</p><p><b>Spojite se. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> set close together [close set]</p><p><b>prestaje s radom, približen, približio, zaključen, zatvoren, zatvoreni, zatvoreno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not open or affording passage or access</p><p><i>adj.</i> (set theory) of an interval that contains both its endpoints</p><p><i>adj.</i> not open [shut, unopen]</p><p><i>adj.</i> used especially of mouth or eyes [shut]</p><p><i>adj.</i> requiring union membership</p><p><i>adj.</i> with shutters closed</p><p><i>adj.</i> not open to the general public</p><p><i>adj.</i> not having an open mind [unsympathetic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> blocked against entry [closed in]</p><p><b>misterij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that baffles understanding and cannot be explained [enigma, mystery, secret]</p><p><b>prsten</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) a chain of atoms in a molecule that forms a closed loop [ring]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom energije od 1,15 kVA ili većim od 2,15 kVA, ali ne većim od 2,15 kVA (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a complete electrical circuit around which current flows or a signal circulates [loop]</p><p><b>korporacija u vlasništvu nekoliko ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a corporation owned by a few people [close corporation, private corporation, privately held corporation]</p><p><b>Rifički par koji čini kompletnu sintaktičku jedinicu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rhymed couplet that forms a complete syntactic unit</p><p><b>zatvorena krivulja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a curve (such as a circle) having no endpoints</p><p><b>nepopletena fraktura u kojoj slomljene kosti ne probijaju kožu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an uncomplicated fracture in which the broken bones to not pierce the skin [simple fracture]</p><p><b>sličan Gentiani andrewsii, ali s većim cvjetovima, Gencijan iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s cijevičastom plavom ili bijelom cvjetom koji se malo otvara ili uopće ne otvara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to Gentiana andrewsii but with larger flowers [Gentiana clausa, blind gentian]</p><p><i>n.</i> gentian of eastern North America