offeecake with fruits or nuts and often iced</p><p><b>Slatki kolačići od kvasca bez grožđa, orašastih plodova ili začina ili glazure (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous yeast-raised sweet rolls with our without raisins or nuts or spices or a glaze [sweet roll]</p><p><b>tropski grm s blistavim lišćem i mirisnim noćnim cvijećem s krumpiranim ili valovitim korollama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical shrub having glossy foliage and fragrant nocturnal flowers with crimped or wavy corollas [Adam's apple, East Indian rosebay, Nero's crown, Tabernaemontana divaricate, crape jasmine, crepe gardenia, crepe jasmine, pinwheel flower]</p><p><b>crna kava s konjakom i limunom i šećerom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> black coffee with Cognac and lemon peel and sugar [cafe royale]</p><p><b>vrlo listovit loš smrad tropski korovnjak čija se sjemena koriste kao dodatak kavi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very leafy malodorous tropical weedy shrub whose seeds have been used as an adulterant for coffee [Cassia occidentalis, Senna occidentalis, mogdad coffee, stinking weed, styptic weed]</p><p><b>kafić, kavana, zalogajnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small restaurant where drinks and snacks are sold [cafe, coffee bar, coffeehouse]</p><p><b>stoj (obično pokretan) koji prodaje vruću kavu i hranu (posebno noću) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stand (usually movable) selling hot coffee and food (especially at night)</p><p><b>piće slično kavi koje se ponekad zamjenjuje kavom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drink resembling coffee that is sometimes substituted for it</p><p><b>nizak stol na kojem se mogu staviti časopisi i služe kafa ili kokteli. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low table where magazines can be placed and coffee or cocktails are served [cocktail table]</p><p><b>kava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several small trees and shrubs native to the tropical Old World yielding coffee beans [coffee]</p><p><b>urna u kojoj se kafa pravi i održava vrućinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an urn in which coffee is made and kept hot</p><p><b>razrađena knjiga velike veličine koja se može postaviti na sto za kavu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elaborate oversize book suitable for displaying on a coffee table</p><p><b>zelena biljka koja nosi crvene ili crne plodove. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen shrub of western United States bearing small red or black fruits [California buckthorn, California coffee, Rhamnus californicus]</p><p><b>kolač ili slatki kruh koji se obično služi s kavom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cake or sweet bread usually served with coffee [coffee cake]</p><p><b>kafić, kavana, zalogajnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small restaurant where drinks and snacks are sold [cafe, coffee bar, coffee shop]</p><p><b>džezva, ibrik, lončić za kavu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall pot in which coffee is brewed</p><p><b>kofer, sanduk, škrinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ornamental sunken panel in a ceiling or dome [caisson, lacunar]</p><p><i>n.</i> a chest especially for storing valuables</p><p><b>koferdam, prazni prostor između dvije brodske pregrade</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large watertight chamber used for construction under water [caisson, pneumatic caisson]</p><p><b>a još uvijek sastoji se od aparata za frakcijsku destilaciju etanola iz fermentacije u industrijskom obimu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a still consisting of an apparatus for the fractional distillation of ethanol from fermentation on an industrial scale</p><p><b>lijes, mrtvački sanduk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> box in which a corpse is buried or cremated [casket]</p><p><i>v.</i> place into a coffin</p><p><b>za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> finely ground tobacco wrapped in paper [butt, cigaret, cigarette, fag]</p><p><b>član grupe osnivača (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of a group of founders</p><p><b>izbočina, vršak, zubac, zupčanik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a subordinate who performs an important but routine function</p><p><i>n.</i> tooth on the rim of gear wheel [sprocket]</p><p><i>v.</i> roll steel ingots</p><p><i>v.</i> join pieces of wood with cogs</p><p><b>željeznička pruga za strme planine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> railway for steep mountains [rack railway]</p><p><b>neospornost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> persuasive relevance</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being valid and rigorous [rigor, rigour, validity]</p><p><b>neodoljiv, uvjerljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> powerfully persuasive [telling, weighty]</p><p><b>dokaz, opipljiv dokaz</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any factual evidence that helps to establish the truth of something [proof]</p><p><b>zupčast</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having cogs</p><p><b>gegati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> walk unsteadily [dodder, paddle, toddle, totter, waddle]</p><p><i>v.</i> move unsteadily [wobble]</p><p><b>Sposoban da se misli o njemu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being thought about [ponderable]</p><p><b>premišljati, razmišljati, misliti, mozgati, premišljati se, promisliti, promišljati, promozgati, prosuditi, prosuđivati, rasuditi, rasuđivati, razmisliti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> consider carefully and deeply</p><p><i>v.</i> use or exercise the mind or one's power of reason in order to make inferences, decisions, or arrive at a solution or judgments [cerebrate, think]</p><p><b>razmišljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a carefully considered thought about something</p><p><i>n.</i> attentive consideration and meditation [study]</p><p><b>sklon razmišljanju</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to having capacities for cogitation</p><p><i>adj.</i> given to cogitation</p><p><b>konjak, vinjak, cognac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> high quality grape brandy distilled in the Cognac district of France</p><p><b>poznanik, rođak, srodne riječi, srodni jezici</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one related by blood or origin [blood relation, blood relative, sib]</p><p><i>n.</i> a word is cognate with another if both derive from the same word in an ancestral language [cognate word]</p><p><i>adj.</i> related in nature [connate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the same ancestral language</p><p><i>adj.</i> related by blood [akin, blood-related, consanguine, consanguineal, consanguineous, kin]</p><p><b>riječ je srodna drugoj ako su obje izvedene iz iste riječi u izvornom jeziku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a word is cognate with another if both derive from the same word in an ancestral language [cognate]</p><p><b>linija porijekla koja se prati kroz majčinu stranu obitelji, (antropologija) povezani krvnom vezom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> line of descent traced through the maternal side of the family [enation, matrilineage]</p><p><i>n.</i> (anthropology) related by blood [blood kinship, consanguinity]</p><p><b>koji je sposoban biti poznat (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being known [cognizable, cognoscible, knowable]</p><p><b>saznanje, spoznaja, svijest, svjesnost, znanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having knowledge of [awareness, cognizance, consciousness, knowingness]</p><p><b>svjestan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (sometimes followed by `of') having or showing knowledge or understanding or realization or perception [aware, cognizant]</p><p><b>spoznati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be cognizant or aware of a fact or a specific piece of information [cognize, know]</p><p><b>kognicija, poznavanje, saznanje, spoznaja, noeza, znanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the psychological result of perception and learning and reasoning [knowledge, noesis]</p><p><b>kognitivni, spoznajni, spoznajnog</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or being or relating to or involving cognition</p><p><b>mentalni sadržaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sum or range of what has been perceived, discovered, or learned [content, mental object]</p><p><b>kognitivni čimbenik, čimbenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something immaterial (as a circumstance or influence) that contributes to producing a result</p><p><b>kognitivna neuroznanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of neuroscience that studies the biological foundations of mental phenomena</p><p><b>kognitivni znanstvenik koji proučava neurofiziološke temelje mentalnih pojava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cognitive scientist who studies the neurophysiological foundations of mental phenomena</p><p><b>(psikološka) izvedba neke složene kognitivne aktivnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) the performance of some composite cognitive activity [cognitive process, mental process, operation, process]</p><p><b>(psikološka) izvedba neke složene kognitivne aktivnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) the performance of some composite cognitive activity [cognitive operation, mental process, operation, process]</p><p><b>kognitivna psihologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an approach to psychology that emphasizes internal mental processes</p><p><b>kognitivne znanosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the field of science concerned with cognition</p><p><b>znanstvenik koji proučava kognitivne procese (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scientist who studies cognitive processes</p><p><b>grana semantike koja proučava kognitivne aspekte značenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of semantics that studies the cognitive aspects of meaning [conceptual semantics, semasiology]</p><p><b>kognitivno stanje, stanje uma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of a person's cognitive processes [state of mind]</p><p><b>kognitivni, spoznajni, spoznajnog (od &quot;cognitive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with regard to cognition</p><p><b>prepoznatljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being known [cognisable, cognoscible, knowable]</p><p><b>saznanje, spoznaja, svijest, svjesnost, znanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having knowledge of [awareness, cognisance, consciousness, knowingness]</p><p><i>n.</i> range of what one can know or understand [ken]</p><p><i>n.</i> range or scope of what is perceived</p><p><b>koji spoznaje, koji zna ili poznaje, nadležan, svjestan, upoznat</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (sometimes followed by `of') having or showing knowledge or understanding or realization or perception [aware, cognisant]</p><p><b>razumjeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be cognizant or aware of a fact or a specific piece of information [cognise, know]</p><p><b>cognomen, nadimak, obiteljsko ime, prezime</b></p><p><