ng the island of Puerto Rico [PR, Porto Rico, Puerto Rico]</p><p><b>Zajednica Bahama</b></p><p><i>n.</i> island country in the Atlantic to the east of Florida and Cuba [Bahama Islands, Bahamas]</p><p><b>komešanje, metež, uzbuđenje, bura, graja, izgred, remećenje, urnebes, gungula, gužva, strka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disorderly outburst or tumult [disruption, disturbance, flutter, hoo-ha, hoo-hah, hurly burly, kerfuffle, to-do]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making a noisy disturbance [din, ruckus, ruction, rumpus, tumult]</p><p><i>n.</i> confused movement [whirl]</p><p><b>uzrokovati uzbuđenje ili uzbuđenje, promjeniti raspored ili položaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be agitated, excited, or roused [agitate, charge, charge up, excite, rouse, turn on]</p><p><i>v.</i> change the arrangement or position of [agitate, disturb, raise up, shake up, stir up, vex]</p><p><b>društven, kolektivan, komunalni, komunalnom, općinski, zadružni, zajednički, općedruštveni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> for or by a group rather than individuals</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a small administrative district or community</p><p><b>učiniti nešto imovinom općine ili zajednice (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make something the property of the commune or community [communalize]</p><p><b>praksa zajedničkog života i zajedničkog vlasništva, lojalnost i posvećenost interesima vlastite manjine ili etničke skupine umjesto društvu u cjelini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of communal living and common ownership</p><p><i>n.</i> loyalty and commitment to the interests of your own minority or ethnic group rather than to society as a whole</p><p><b>učiniti nešto imovinom općine ili zajednice (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make something the property of the commune or community [communalise]</p><p><b>društven, kolektivan, komunalni, komunalnom, općinski, zadružni, zajednički, općedruštveni (od &quot;communal&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by a group of people rather than an individual</p><p><b>komuna, komune, općina, općinu, komun, zajednica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the smallest administrative district of several European countries</p><p><i>n.</i> a body of people or families living together and sharing everything</p><p><i>v.</i> communicate intimately with</p><p><i>v.</i> receive Communion, in the Catholic church [communicate]</p><p><b>koji se može priopćiti, povjerljiv, prenosiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of disease) capable of being transmitted by infection [catching, contagious, contractable, transmissible, transmittable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> readily communicated</p><p><b>bolest koja se može prenijeti s jedne osobe na drugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease that can be communicated from one person to another</p><p><b>osoba koja ima pravo primati pričest (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person entitled to receive Communion</p><p><b>biti u vezi, dojaviti, dostaviti, dostavljati, informirati, komunicirati, obavijestiti nekoga o nečemu, općiti, poslati, poslati informacije, prenijeti, prenositi podatke, prijenos podatke, priopćavati, priopćiti, saopćavati, slati, javiti, javljati, obavijestiti, obavještavati, priopćivati, saopćiti, saopćivati, dati, davati, predati, predavati, prenositi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> transmit information [pass, pass along, pass on, put across]</p><p><i>v.</i> transmit thoughts or feelings [intercommunicate]</p><p><i>v.</i> transfer to another [convey, transmit]</p><p><i>v.</i> join or connect</p><p><i>v.</i> be in verbal contact</p><p><i>v.</i> administer Communion</p><p><i>v.</i> receive Communion, in the Catholic church [commune]</p><p><b>podnošenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of communicating [communication]</p><p><b>bilo koja od tri arterije u mozgu koje čine krug Willisa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of three arteries in the brain that make up the circle of Willis [arteria communicans]</p><p><b>komuniciranje, komunikacija, komunikaciji, komunikacijske, komunikacijski, pismeno, prijenos podataka, priopćenje, veza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of communicating [communicating]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that is communicated by or to or between people or groups</p><p><i>n.</i> a connection allowing access between persons or places</p><p><b>komunikacijski kanal, priopćajni kanal, kanal, put</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (often plural) a means of communication or access [channel, line]</p><p><b>komunikacijska oprema, komunikacijski sustav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> facility consisting of the physical plants and equipment for disseminating information [communication system]</p><p><b>komunikacijski sustav, priopćajni sustav, komunikacijski sistem, komunikacijska oprema</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system for communicating</p><p><i>n.</i> facility consisting of the physical plants and equipment for disseminating information [communication equipment]</p><p><b>Nauka koja proučava načela prijenosa informacija i metode kojima se one prenose (kao što su štampa, radio ili televizija itd.). (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the discipline that studies the principles of transmiting information and the methods by which it is delivered (as print or radio or television etc.) [communications]</p><p><b>rov koji pruža zaštićen prolaz između stražnje i prednje linije obrambenog položaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trench that provides protected passage between the rear and front lines of a defensive position [approach trench]</p><p><b>korišten u komunikaciji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> used in communication</p><p><b>komuniciranja, komunikacije, komunikacijski, razmjena informacija, veze</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the discipline that studies the principles of transmiting information and the methods by which it is delivered (as print or radio or television etc.) [communication theory]</p><p><b>tehničke i obavještajne informacije koje su dobivene iz komunikacija u inozemstvu od strane drugih odredišta osim onih za koje su namijenjene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> technical and intelligence information derived from foreign communications by other than the intended recipients [COMINT]</p><p><b>komunikacijski protokol, protokol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) rules determining the format and transmission of data [protocol]</p><p><b>komunikacijski satelit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial satellite that relays signals back to earth</p><p><b>Kanadska agencija koja prikuplja obavještajne podatke o komunikacijama i pomaže agencijama za provedbu zakona i sigurnost. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Canadian agency that gathers communications intelligence and assist law enforcement and security agencies [CSE]</p><p><b>Službeni sustav za komunikacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of designing and constructing and maintaining communication systems</p><p><b>komunikacijski, komunikacijsku, komunikativan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to communication</p><p><i>adj.</i> able or tending to communicate [communicatory]</p><p><b>komunikativnost, otvorenost, pričljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being communicative</p><p><b>dojavljivač, komunikator, subesjednik, sugovoritelj, sugovornik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who communicates with others</p><p><b>sposobni ili skloni komunicirati (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able or tending to communicate [communicative]</p><p><b>drugarstvo, komunizam, općenje, pričest, zajedništvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of participating in the celebration of the Eucharist [Holy Communion, manduction, sacramental manduction]</p><p><i>n.</i> sharing thoughts and feelings [sharing]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Christianity) a group of Christians with a common religious faith who practice the same rites</p><p><b>oltar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the table in Christian churches where communion is given [Lord's table, altar]</p><p><b>službeno priopćenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an official report (usually sent in haste) [despatch, dispatch]</p><p><b>nacionalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a change from private property to public property owned by the community [communization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the organization of a nation of the basis of communism [communization]</p><p><i>n.</i> changing something from private to state ownership or control [communization, nationalisation, nationalization]</p><p><b>učiniti komunističkim ili dovesti u skladu s komunističkim načelima, pretvoriti u imovinu države (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make Communist or bring in accord with Communist principles [bolshevise, bolshevize, communize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make into property owned by the state [communize]</p><p><b>komunizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of socialism that abolishes private ownership</p><p><i>n.</i> a political theory favoring collectivism in a classless society</p><p><b>Najviši planinski vrh u Pamirskim planinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the highest mountain peak in the Pamir Mountains [Mount Communism, Mount Garmo, Stalin Peak]</p><p><b>komunist, komunistički, komunističkoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the communist party</p><p><i>n.</i> a socialist who advocates communism [commie]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or marked by communism [communistic]</p><p><b>Komunistička država koja pokriva veliko područje u istočnoj Aziji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a communist nation that covers a vast territory in eastern Asia [Cathay, China, PRC, People's Republic of China, Red China, mainland China]</p><p><b>upravljano gospodarstvo komunističke države (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the managed economy of a communist state</p><p><b>socijalistički manifest napisan od strane Marksa i Engelsa (1842) opisujući povijest radničkog pokreta prema njihovim pogledima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a socialist manifesto written by Marx and Engels (1842) describing the history of the working-class movement according to their views</p><p><b>komunistička stranka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political party that actively advocates a communist form of government</p><p><b>komunistička organizacija osnovana u Kambodži 1970. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a communist organization formed in Cambodia in 1970 [KR, Khmer Rouge, Party of Democratic Kampuchea]</p><p><b>komunistički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> r