lexible face that can plane concave or convex surfaces [circular plane]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička godišnja s crvenim ili ružičastim cvijećima, bilo koja od nekoliko biljaka s listovima raspoređenim na osi kako bi se pokazale kardinalne točke kompasa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American annual with red or rose-colored flowers [Lotus americanus, prairie bird's-foot trefoil, prairie lotus, prairie trefoil]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several plants having leaves so arranged on the axis as to indicate the cardinal points of the compass [compass flower]</p><p><b>točka, točka kompasa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of 32 horizontal directions indicated on the card of a compass [point]</p><p><b>ručna pila sa uskom trouglom oštricom za rezanje krivina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a handsaw with a narrow triangular blade for cutting curves</p><p><b>samilost, saučešće, sažaljenje, sućut, suosjećanje, saosećanje, saosjećanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deep awareness of and sympathy for another's suffering [compassionateness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the humane quality of understanding the suffering of others and wanting to do something about it [pity]</p><p><b>milosrdan, sažalijevati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> share the suffering of [condole with, feel for, pity, sympathize with]</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing or having compassion</p><p><b>(vojni) dopust koji se daje u hitnim slučajevima kao što su obiteljska bolest ili smrt (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (military) leave granted in an emergency such as family sickness or death</p><p><b>milosrdan (od &quot;compassionate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a compassionate manner [pityingly]</p><p><b>samilost, suosjećanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deep awareness of and sympathy for another's suffering [compassion]</p><p><b>funkcionalna istovjetnost, kompatibilnost, mješljivost, spojivost, sukladnost, uskladivost, usklađenost, usuglašenost, podudarnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of sympathetic understanding</p><p><i>n.</i> capability of existing or performing in harmonious or congenial combination</p><p><b>koji odgovara, kompatibilan, kompatibilni, podnošljiv, spojiv, sukladan, u skladu s, usklađen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to exist and perform in harmonious or agreeable combination</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being used with or connected to other devices or components without modification</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of forming a homogeneous mixture that neither separates nor is altered by chemical interaction</p><p><b>aplikacijski softver koji dijeli zajedničke konvencije kako bi se mogli koristiti zajedno, softver koji može raditi na različitim kompjuterima bez izmjena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> application software programs that share common conventions so they can be utilized together</p><p><i>n.</i> software that can run on different computers without modification</p><p><b>kompatibilnost, mogućnost zajedničkog djelovanja, podudarnost, spojivost, uskladivost</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with compatibility</p><p><b>rodoljub, zemljak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person from your own country</p><p><b>jednak, ravan, ravnopravan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is of equal standing with another in a group [equal, match, peer]</p><p><b>natjerati, primorati, prinuditi, prisiliti, natjeravati, obavezati, obvezati, obvezivati, primoravati, prisiljavati, siliti, tjerati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> force somebody to do something [obligate, oblige]</p><p><i>v.</i> necessitate or exact</p><p><b>neodoljiv, nesavladiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> driving or forcing</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to persuade by forcefulness of argument</p><p><b>sažet, skraćen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> briefly giving the gist of something [compact, succinct, summary]</p><p><b>pregled, kolekcija, kompendij, skup, zbirka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a publication containing a variety of works [collection]</p><p><i>n.</i> a concise but comprehensive summary of a larger work</p><p><b>za koje se plaća novac (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> for which money is paid [paying, remunerative, salaried, stipendiary]</p><p><b>kompenzirati, nadoknada, naknaditi, obeštetiti, nadoknaditi, iskupiti se, iskupljivati se, ispraviti, ispravljati, nadoknađivati, popraviti, platiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> adjust for [correct, counterbalance, even off, even out, even up, make up]</p><p><i>v.</i> make amends for [indemnify, recompense, repair]</p><p><i>v.</i> make up for shortcomings or a feeling of inferiority by exaggerating good qualities [cover, overcompensate]</p><p><i>v.</i> make reparations or amends for [correct, redress, right]</p><p><i>v.</i> do or give something to somebody in return [make up, pay, pay off]</p><p><i>v.</i> make payment to [recompense, remunerate]</p><p><b>kompenzirana</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> receiving or eligible for compensation [remunerated, salaried, stipendiary]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, kreditna sredstva mogu se koristiti za određivanje kreditne vrijednosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a minimum credit balance that a bank may require a borrower to keep on deposit as a condition for granting a loan [offsetting balance]</p><p><b>kalibriranje magnetskog kompasa, kompenzacija, nadoknada, nagrada, naknada, odstupnina, odšteta, plata, ravnoteža, nadoknađivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something (such as money) given or received as payment or reparation (as for a service or loss or injury)</p><p><i>n.</i> (psychiatry) a defense mechanism that conceals your undesirable shortcomings by exaggerating desirable behaviors</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of compensating for service or loss or injury [recompense]</p><p><b>(zakonom) naknada za štetu za koju se može lako dokazati da se dogodila i za koju je povrijeđena strana ima pravo na naknadu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) compensation for losses that can readily be proven to have occurred and for which the injured party has the right to be compensated [actual damages, general damages]</p><p><b>trošenje novca prikupljenog pozajmljivanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spending money raised by borrowing [deficit spending, pump priming]</p><p><b>Službeni radni sat (službeni radni sat) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> time off that is granted to a worker as compensation for working overtime</p><p><b>Britanski izraz za nekoga tko uvodi televizijske glume ili kabarete itd., -Predstavlja se kao ceremonijalni učitelj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British term for someone who introduces television acts or cabarets etc</p><p><i>v.</i> act as a master of ceremonies [emcee]</p><p><b>konkurirati, nadmetati se, natjecati se, takmiči, takmičiti, takmičiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> compete for something [contend, vie]</p><p><b>kompetencija, kompetenciju, nadležnost, ovlast, poznavanja, poznavanje, sposobnost, sposobnosti, spremnost, stručnost, nadležnosti, kompetentnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being adequately or well qualified physically and intellectually [competency]</p><p><b>saslušanje za utvrđivanje pravne sposobnosti (za utvrđivanje može li tuženik razumjeti optužbe i surađivati s odvjetnikom pri pripremi obrane) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hearing to determine legal capacity (to determine whether the defendant can understand the charges and cooperate with a lawyer in preparing a defense)</p><p><b>sposobnosti, kompetentnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being adequately or well qualified physically and intellectually [competence]</p><p><b>kompetentan, mjerodavan, mjerodavno, nadležan, nadležna, sposoban, stručan, stručni, nadležnih</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> properly or sufficiently qualified or capable or efficient</p><p><i>adj.</i> adequate, but not outstanding or exceptional</p><p><i>adj.</i> legally qualified or sufficient</p><p><b>kompetentno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with competence [ably, aptly, capably]</p><p><b>konkurencija, konkurentnost, nadmetanje, natjecanje, natječaj, takmičenje, tržišno natjecanje, konkurencije, konkurenciju, natjecanja, natjecanjem, natjecanju, kompeticija, konkuriranje, rivalstvo, suparništvo, konkurent, protivnik, rival, suparnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a business relation in which two parties compete to gain customers</p><p><i>n.</i> an occasion on which a winner is selected from among two or more contestants [contest]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of competing as for profit or a prize [contention, rivalry]</p><p><i>n.</i> the contestant you hope to defeat [challenger, competitor, contender, rival]</p><p><b>kompetitivan, kompetitivni, konkurentan, natjecateljski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving competition or competitiveness [competitory]</p><p><i>adj.</i> subscribing to capitalistic competition [free-enterprise, private-enterprise]</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing a fighting disposition [militant]</p><p><b>kompetitivan, kompetitivni, konkurentan, natjecateljski (od &quot;competitive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in competition</p><p><b>konkurentnost, konkuretnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an aggressive willingness to compete [fight]</p><p><b>konkurent, natjecatelj, suparnik, takmac, konkurencija, protivnik, rival</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the contestant you hope to defeat [challenger, competition, contender, rival]</p><p><b>kompetitivan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving competition or competitiveness [competitive]</p><p><b>kompilacija, prikupljanje, sakupljanje, sastavljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that is compiled (as into a single book or file) [digest]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of compiling (as into a single book or file or list) [compiling]</p><p><b>kompajliranje, kompilirati, prevesti, sabrati, sakupiti, sastaviti, akumulirati, gomilati, kupiti, nagomilati, nakupiti, nakupljati, naslagati, pribirati se, sabirati, sakupljati, skupiti, skupljati, slagati, zgrnuti, zgrnuti se, zgrtati, sastavljati, složiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> get or gather together [accumulate, amass, collect, hoard, pile up, roll up]</p><p><i>v.</i> put together out of existing material [compose]</p><p><i>v.</i> use a computer program to translate source code written in a particular programming language into computer-readable machine code that can be executed</p><p><b>kompajler, kompilator, prevodilac, program prevoditelj, program-prevodilac (u strojni jezik), programski prevoditelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who compiles information (as for reference purposes)</p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a program that decodes instructions written in a higher order language and produces an assembly language program [compiling program]</p><p><b>kompiliranje, sastavljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of compiling (as into a single book or file or list) [compilation]</p><p><b>program prevodilac, program za prevođenje (u strojni jezik)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a program that decodes instructions written in a higher order language and produces an assembly language program [compiler]</p><p><b>ugodnost, samozadovoljstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling you have when you are satisfied with yourself [complacency, self-complacency, self-satisfaction]</p><p><b>samozadovoljstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling you have when you are satisfied with yourself [complacence, self-complacency, self-satisfaction]</p><p><b>spokojan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> contented to a fault with oneself or one's actions [self-complacent, self-satisfied]</p><p><b>spokojan (od &quot;complacent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a self-satisfied manner</p><p><b>jadikovati, naricati, potužiti se, tužiti se, žaliti se, buniti se, cendrati, cmizdriti, jadati se, prigovarati, čangrizati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> express complaints, discontent, displeasure, or unhappiness [kick, kvetch, plain, quetch, sound off]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a formal accusation</p><p><b>podnositelj, tužitelj, žalilac, žalitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who brings an action in a court of law [plaintiff]</p><p><b>jadikovati, naricati, potužiti se, tužiti se, žaliti se (od &quot;complain&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person given to excessive complaints and crying and whining [bellyacher, crybaby, grumbler, moaner, sniveller, squawker, whiner]</p><p><b>jadikovanje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing pain or dissatisfaction of resentment [complaintive]</p><p><b>jadikovanje (od &quot;complaining&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with complaints</p><p><b>naricanje, prigovor, reklamacija, reklamacije, tužba, žalba, jadikovanje, jadikovka, pritužba, optužba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an often persistent bodily disorder or disease [ailment, ill]</p><p><i>n.</i> (formerly) a loud cry (or repeated cries) of pain or rage or sorrow</p><p><i>n.</i> an expression of grievance or resentment</p><p><i>n.</i> (civil law) the first pleading of the plaintiff setting out the facts on which the claim for relief is based</p><p><i>n.</i> (criminal law) a pleading describing some wrong or offense [charge]</p><p><b>izražavanje boli ili nezadovoljstva zbog zamjerke (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing pain or dissatisfaction of resentment [complaining]</p><p><b>popustljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition or tendency to yield to the will of others [compliance, compliancy, deference, obligingness]</p><p><b>ljubazan, popustljiv, učtiv, uslužan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing a cheerful willingness to do favors for others [obliging]</p><p><b>biti međusobno isprepleteni ili međusobno povezani (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be interwoven or interconnected [interconnect, interlink]</p><p><b>dopuna, dovoljan broj časnika i posade za sigurno poslovan, komplement, komplementaran, komplet, potpun, zbirka, nadopuna, upotpunjenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a word or phrase used to complete a grammatical construction</p><p><i>n.</i> a complete number or quantity</p><p><i>n.</i> number needed to make up a whole force [full complement]</p><p><i>n.</i> something added to complete or embellish or make perfect [accompaniment]</p><p><i>n.</i> one of a series of enzymes in the blood serum that are part of the immune response</p><p><i>n.</i> either of two parts that mutually complete each other</p><p><i>v.</i> make complete or perfect</p><p><b>imunološki odgovor u kojem kombinacija antigena-antitela inaktivira komplement (što znači da nije dostupna za sudjelovanje u drugoj kombinaciji antigena-antitela) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an immune response in which an antigen-antibody combination inactivates a complement (so it is unavailable to participate in a second antigen-antibody combination)</p><p><b>krvni test u kojem se uzorak seruma izloži određenom antigenu i komplementu kako bi se utvrdilo jesu li prisutna antitijela na taj određeni antigen ili ne (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blood test in which a sample of serum is exposed to a particular antigen and complement in order to determine whether or not antibodies to that particular antigen are present</p><p><b>djeluju kao ili pružaju dopunu (nešto što dovršava cjelinu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> acting as or providing a complement (something that completes the whole) [complementary, completing]</p><p><b>komplementarnost, komplementiaranost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relation between two opposite states or principles that together exhaust the possibilities</p><p><i>n.</i> the interrelation of reciprocity whereby one thing supplements or depends on the other</p><p><b>dopunski, komplementaran, prateći, pratećim, komplementarna boja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either one of two chromatic colors that when mixed together give white (in the case of lights) or grey (in the case of pigments) [complementary color]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of words or propositions so related that each is the negation of the other</p><p><i>adj.</i> acting as or providing a complement (something that completes the whole) [complemental, completing]</p><p><b>dva ugla čija je suma pravougaoni ugao (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> two angles whose sum is a right angle</p><p><b>komplementarna boja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either one of two chromatic colors that when mixed together give white (in the case of lights) or grey (in the case of pigments) [complementary]</p><p><b>(lingvistički) raspodjela srodnih govornih zvukova ili oblika na takav način da se pojavljuju samo u različitim kontekstima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (linguistics) a distribution of related speech sounds or forms in such a way that they only appear in different contexts [complementation]</p><p><b>Jednostrana DNK koja je komplementarna s RNA-om glasnika ili DNK koja je sintetizirana iz RNA-a glasnika obrnutom transkriptazom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> single-stranded DNA that is complementary to messenger RNA or DNA that has been synthesized from messenger RNA by reverse transcriptase [cDNA]</p><p><b>medicinska praksa koja kombinira tradicionalnu medicinu s alternativnom medicinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of medicine that combines traditional medicine with alternative medicine</p><p><b>gramatikalni odnos riječi ili fraze prema predikatu, (lingvistički) raspodjela srodnih govornih zvukova ili oblika na takav način da se pojavljuju samo u različitim kontekstima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the grammatical relation of a word or phrase to a predicate</p><p><i>n.</i> (linguistics) a distribution of related speech sounds or forms in such a way that they only appear in different contexts [complementary distribution]</p><p><b>boriti se, cjelokupan, cjelovit, čitav, dopuniti, dovršen, dovršenje, dovršiti, dovrštiti, gotov, ispuniti, ispunjavati, izvršiti, kompletan, kompletiran, kompletirati, obaviti, okončati, popuniti, popunjavati, potpun, potpuniti, potpuno, provesti, svršiti, takmičiti se, upotpuniti, upotpunjavati, završiti, cjelokupni, kompletnog, kompletnu, upotpunjuje, dokrajčiti, dokrajčiti se, dokrajčivati, dokrajčivati se, dovršavati, dovršavati se, dovršiti se, okončati se, okončavati, okončavati se, svršavati, svršavati se, svršiti se, završavati, završavati se, završiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come or bring to a finish or an end [finish]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring to a whole, with all the necessary parts or elements</p><p><i>v.</i> complete or carry out [discharge, dispatch]</p><p><i>v.</i> complete a pass [nail]</p><p><i>v.</i> write all the required information onto a form [fill in, fill out, make out]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having every necessary or normal part or component or step</p><p><i>adj.</i> perfect and complete in every respect [consummate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> highly skilled [accomplished]</p><p><i>adj.</i> without qualification [arrant, consummate, double-dyed, everlasting, gross, perfect, pure, sodding, staring, stark, thorough, thoroughgoing, unadulterated, utter]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having come or been brought to a conclusion [all over, concluded, ended, over, terminated]</p><p><b>broja bijelih i crvenih krvnih stanica i broja trombocita u 1 kubnom milimetru krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> counting the number of white and red blood cells and the number of platelets in 1 cubic millimeter of blood [CBC, blood profile]</p><p><b>lom koji uključuje cijelu širinu kostiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> break involving the entire width of the bone</p><p><b>dovršen, dovršeno, kompletiran, upotpunjen, završen, završena, završiti</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> successfully completed or brought to an end [accomplished, realised, realized]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a marriage) completed by the first act of sexual intercourse after the ceremony</p><p><i>adj.</i> caught</p><p><b>definitivno, dovršen, kompletno, potpuna, potpuno, sasvim, u potpunosti</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a complete degree or to the full or entire extent (`whole' is often used informally for `wholly') [all, altogether, entirely, right, totally, whole, wholly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> so as to be complete</p><p><b>cijelost, cjelina, cjeline, cjelovitost, potpunost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being complete and entire</p><p><i>n.</i> (logic) an attribute of a logical system that is so constituted that a contradiction arises if any proposition is introduced that cannot be derived from the axioms of the system</p><p><b>dovršavanje, kompletiranje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> acting as or providing a complement (something that completes the whole) [complemental, complementary]</p><p><b>dopuna, dovršenje, ispun, izvršenje, komplet, kraj, okončanje, prestanak, upotpu