eta potvrda, dokaz, potkrepa, ratifikacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> additional proof that something that was believed (some fact or hypothesis or theory) is correct [check, substantiation, verification]</p><p><i>n.</i> information that confirms or verifies</p><p><i>n.</i> making something valid by formally ratifying or confirming it [ratification]</p><p><i>n.</i> a ceremony held in the synagogue (usually at Pentecost) to admit as adult members of the Jewish community young men and women who have successfully completed a course of study in Judaism</p><p><i>n.</i> a sacrament admitting a baptized person to full participation in the church</p><p><b>saslušanje koje je održao Senat SAD-a kako bi prikupio informacije o tome hoće li odobriti ili odbiti kandidate za visoke savezne dužnosti koje je nominirao predsjednik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hearing held by the US Senate to gather information on whether to approve or reject candidates for high federal office who are nominated by the president</p><p><b>služe za potporu ili potvrdu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to support or corroborate [collateral, confirmatory, confirming, corroborative, corroboratory, substantiating, substantiative, validating, validatory, verificatory, verifying]</p><p><b>služe za potporu ili potvrdu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to support or corroborate [collateral, confirmative, confirming, corroborative, corroboratory, substantiating, substantiative, validating, validatory, verificatory, verifying]</p><p><b>dokazao, potvrdio, potvrđen, potvrđena, potvrđuju</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of persons</p><p><i>adj.</i> having been established or made firm or received the rite of confirmation</p><p><b>krizmanje, pozitivan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> indicating existence or presence of a suspected condition or pathogen [positive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to support or corroborate [collateral, confirmative, confirmatory, corroborative, corroboratory, substantiating, substantiative, validating, validatory, verificatory, verifying]</p><p><b>konfiscirati, zaplijeniti, plijeniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> take temporary possession of as a security, by legal authority [attach, impound, seize, sequester]</p><p><i>adj.</i> surrendered as a penalty [forfeit, forfeited]</p><p><b>konfiskacija, zapljena, pljenidba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> seizure by the government [arrogation]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je proizvod namijenjen za proizvodnju hrane, u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, može se upotrebljavati samo za proizvodnju hrane. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of meat (especially a duck) cooked slowly in its own fat</p><p><b>konzervirano ili kandirano voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> preserved or candied fruit</p><p><b>buknuti, paliti se, planuti, raspaliti se, raspaljivati se, zapaliti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to start burning [enkindle, inflame, kindle]</p><p><i>v.</i> start to burn or burst into flames [catch fire, combust, erupt, ignite, take fire]</p><p><b>požar, vatra</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a very intense and uncontrolled fire [inferno]</p><p><b>izmiješati, izmiksati, kombinirati, miješati, miksati, pomiješati, sjediniti, sjedinjavati, smiješati, smiksati, spajati, spojiti, stapati, stopiti, umiješati, umiksati, združiti, združivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> mix together different elements [blend, coalesce, combine, commingle, flux, fuse, immix, meld, merge, mix]</p><p><b>borba, konflikt, neprijateljstvo, spor, sukob, sukoba, sukobiti se, svađa, bitka, boj, nesuglasica, prepirka, razmirica, oduprijeti se, prekršiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an open clash between two opposing groups (or individuals) [battle, struggle]</p><p><i>n.</i> opposition between two simultaneous but incompatible feelings</p><p><i>n.</i> a hostile meeting of opposing military forces in the course of a war [battle, engagement, fight]</p><p><i>n.</i> a state of opposition between persons or ideas or interests</p><p><i>n.</i> an incompatibility of dates or events</p><p><i>n.</i> opposition in a work of drama or fiction between characters or forces (especially an opposition that motivates the development of the plot)</p><p><i>n.</i> a disagreement or argument about something important [difference, difference of opinion, dispute]</p><p><i>v.</i> be in conflict</p><p><i>v.</i> go against, as of rules and laws [contravene, infringe, run afoul]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je riječ o javnom službeniku, to znači da je njegov osobni interes utjecao na njegove odluke. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a situation in which a public official's decisions are influenced by the official's personal interests</p><p><b>proturječan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in disagreement [at odds, contradictory, self-contradictory]</p><p><i>adj.</i> on bad terms</p><p><b>presijecanje puta, presijecati put, sliv rijeke, stjecište, učću, ušće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a place where things merge or flow together (especially rivers) [meeting]</p><p><i>n.</i> a flowing together [conflux, merging]</p><p><i>n.</i> a coming together of people [concourse]</p><p><b>koji se sliva, pritoka rijeke, pritok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a branch that flows into the main stream [affluent, feeder, tributary]</p><p><i>adj.</i> flowing together [merging]</p><p><b>-Putovanje zajedno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flowing together [confluence, merging]</p><p><b>odgovarati, podesiti, podudarati se, povinovati se, prilagoditi, prilagoditi se, adaptirati se, prilagođavati se, prilagođivati se, ravnati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be similar, be in line with</p><p><i>v.</i> adapt or conform oneself to new or different conditions [adapt, adjust]</p><p><b>slijediti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> observe</p><p><i>v.</i> behave in accordance or in agreement with [follow]</p><p><i>v.</i> fill, satisfy or meet a want or need or condtion ro restriction [fill, fit, fulfil, fulfill, meet, satisfy]</p><p><b>pokoran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> quick to comply</p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed or willing to conform [amenable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> in keeping [accordant, agreeable, concordant, consonant]</p><p><b>na odgovarajući način (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a conformable manner</p><p><b>Projekcija karte u kojoj je mala površina prikazana u svom pravom obliku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a map projection in which a small area is rendered in its true shape [orthomorphic projection]</p><p><b>dogovor, slaganje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> correspondence in form or appearance [conformity]</p><p><b>građa «tijela», uobličenje, forma, izgled, oblik, obličje, pridržavanje, prilagođavanje, prilagođenost, udovoljavanje, usklađenost, usklađivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a symmetrical arrangement of the parts of a thing</p><p><i>n.</i> any spatial attributes (especially as defined by outline) [configuration, contour, form, shape]</p><p><i>n.</i> acting according to certain accepted standards [abidance, compliance, conformity]</p><p><b>entropija izračunana iz vjerojatnosti da se stanje može postići samo slučajno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> entropy calculated from the probability that a state could be reached by chance alone</p><p><b>u skladu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> adhering to established customs or doctrines (especially in religion) [conformist]</p><p><b>ustaljeni običaji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orthodoxy in thoughts and belief [conformity]</p><p><b>konformist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who conforms to established standards of conduct (especially in religious matters)</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by convention and conformity to customs or rules or styles</p><p><i>adj.</i> adhering to established customs or doctrines (especially in religion) [conforming]</p><p><b>sklad, skladu, suglasnost, sukladnost, u skladu sa vladajućim pravilima i standardima, usklađenost, usklađenosti, pridržavanje, prilagođavanje, prilagođenost, udovoljavanje, usklađivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> correspondence in form or appearance [conformance]</p><p><i>n.</i> acting according to certain accepted standards [abidance, compliance, conformation]</p><p><i>n.</i> orthodoxy in thoughts and belief [conformism]</p><p><i>n.</i> concurrence of opinion [accord, accordance]</p><p><i>n.</i> hardened conventionality [ossification]</p><p><b>pobrkati, zaplesti, zbuniti, miješati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be confusing or perplexing to [bedevil, befuddle, confuse, discombobulate, fox, fuddle, throw]</p><p><i>v.</i> mistake one thing for another [confuse]</p><p><b>zbunjen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> perplexed by many conflicting situations or statements [at sea, baffled, befuddled, bemused, bewildered, confused, lost, mazed, mixed-up]</p><p><b>zbunjen (od &quot;confounded&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a perplexed manner [perplexedly]</p><p><b>pobrkati, zaplesti, zbuniti (od &quot;confound&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> that confounds or contradicts or confuses [contradictory]</p><p><b>osoba koja je član svoje klase ili zanimanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is member of one's class or profession [colleague, fellow]</p><p><b>licem u lice, sukobiti, sukobiti se, suočiti, suprotstaviti, oduprijeti se, suočavati se, suočiti se, suprotstaviti se, suprotstavljati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> oppose, as in hostility or a competition [face]</p><p><i>v.</i> deal with (something unpleasant) head on [face, face up]</p><p><i>v.</i> present somebody with something, usually to accuse or criticize [face, present]</p><p><i>v.</i> be face to face with</p><p><b>konfrontacija, obračun, sukob, konfrontiranje, sukobljavanje, suprotstavljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bold challenge</p><p><i>n.</i> discord resulting from a clash of ideas or opinions</p><p><i>n.</i> a hostile disagreement face-to-face [encounter, face-off, showdown]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of hostile groups opposing each other [opposition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a focussed comparison</p><p><b>usporediv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to confrontation</p><p><b>Vjerovao u učenja Konfucija., koji se odnosi na ili karakterističan za konfucijanizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a believer in the teachings of Confucius [Confucianist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of Confucianism</p><p><b>Učenja Konfucija koja naglašavaju ljubav prema čovječanstvu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the teachings of Confucius emphasizing love for humanity</p><p><b>Vjerovao u učenja Konfucija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a believer in the teachings of Confucius [Confucian]</p><p><b>Konfucije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chinese philosopher whose ideas and sayings were collected after his death and became the basis of a philosophical doctrine known a Confucianism (circa 551-478 BC) [K'ung Futzu, Kong the Master, Kongfuze]</p><p><b>Tako sličan da se lako može prepoznati za nešto drugo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> so similar as to be easily identified for another thing [mistakable]</p><p><b>brkati, pomrsiti, postidjeti, praviti nered, smutiti, zabuniti (se), zbrkati, zbuniti, miješati, dezorijentirati, smućivati, uznemiravati, uznemiriti, uzrujati, uzrujavati, zbunjivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> mistake one thing for another [confound]</p><p><i>v.</i> be confusing or perplexing to [bedevil, befuddle, confound, discombobulate, fox, fuddle, throw]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to feel embarrassment [disconcert, flurry, put off]</p><p><i>v.</i> assemble without order or sense [jumble, mix up]</p><p><i>v.</i> make unclear, indistinct, or blurred [blur, obnubilate, obscure]</p><p><b>bezglav, zbunjen, zbunjeni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> perplexed by many conflicting situations or statements [at sea, baffled, befuddled, bemused, bewildered, confounded, lost, mazed, mixed-up]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking orderly continuity [disconnected, disjointed, disordered, garbled, illogical, scattered, unconnected]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having lost your bearings [disoriented, lost]</p><p><i>adj.</i> thrown into a state of disarray or confusion [broken, disordered, upset]</p><p><i>adj.</i> mentally confused</p><p><b>bezglav, zbunjen, zbunjeni (od &quot;confused&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a confused manner</p><p><b>bezglav, zbunjen, zbunjeni (od &quot;confused&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mental state characterized by a lack of clear and orderly thought and behavior [confusion, disarray, mental confusion, muddiness]</p><p><b>zbunjivanje, zbunjujući</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing confusion or disorientation</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking clarity of meaning [perplexing, puzzling]</p><p><b>zbunjivanje, zbunjujući (od &quot;confusing&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a bewildering and confusing manner [bewilderingly]</p><p><b>bezglavost, komešanje, konfuzija, smetenost, zabuna, zbunjenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> disorder resulting from a failure to behave predictably</p><p><i>n.</i> a mental state characterized by a lack of clear and orderly thought and behavior [confusedness, disarray, mental confusion, muddiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of embarrassment that leaves you confused [discombobulation]</p><p><i>n.</i> an act causing a disorderly combination of elements with identities lost and distinctions blended</p><p><i>n.</i> a mistake that results from taking one thing to be another [mix-up]</p><p><b>može se opovrgnuti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to be refuted [confutative, questionable, refutable]</p><p><b>pobijanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the speech act of refuting conclusively</p><p><i>n.</i> evidence that refutes conclusively</p><p><b>može se opovrgnuti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to be refuted [confutable, questionable, refutable]</p><p><b>demantirati, opovrgnuti, poricati, opovrgavati, pobijati, pobiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> prove to be false [disprove]</p><p><b>demantirati, opovrgnuti, poricati (od &quot;confute&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a debater who refutes or disproves by offering contrary evidence or argument [disprover, rebutter, refuter]</p><p><b>glazba sastavljena za ples konge, Latinoamerički ples od tri koraka i udaranja od strane ljudi u jednom redu., Plesati kongu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> music composed for dancing the conga</p><p><i>n.</i> a Latin American dance of 3 steps and a kick by people in single file</p><p><i>v.</i> dance the conga</p><p><b>red ljudi u jednom redu koji izvode ples konga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a line of people in single file performing the conga dance</p><p><b>(arhitektura) konkavno oblikovanje, formalna dozvola za polazak, iznenada i bez ceremonija otpuštanje., obaviti ceremonijalni poklon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (architecture) a concave molding [congee]</p><p><i>n.</i> formal permission to depart [congee]</p><p><i>n.</i> an abrupt and unceremonious dismissal [congee]</p><p><i>v.</i> perform a ceremonious bow [congee]</p><p><b>stegnuti se, zalediti, zamrznuti se, zgusnuti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become gelatinous [jell, set]</p><p><b>stegnuti se, zalediti, zamrznuti se, zgusnuti se (od &quot;congeal&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> congealed into jelly [jelled, jellied]</p><p><b>proces zgrušavanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of congealing [congelation]</p><p><b>kineski pirinčasti krumpir za doručak, (arhitektura) konkavno oblikovanje, formalna dozvola za polazak, iznenada i bez ceremonija otpuštanje., odlazi nakon što dobije službeno dopuštenje, obaviti ceremonijalni poklon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Chinese rice gruel eaten for breakfast [jook]</p><p><i>n.</i> (architecture) a concave molding [conge]</p><p><i>n.</i> formal permission to depart [conge]</p><p><i>n.</i> an abrupt and unceremonious dismissal [conge]</p><p><i>v.</i> depart after obtaining formal permission</p><p><i>v.</i> perform a ceremonious bow [conge]</p><p><b>proces zgrušavanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of congealing [congealment]</p><p><b>životinja ili biljka koja je povezana s drugom (kao što je povezana zajedničkim porijeklom ili članstvom u istom rodu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an animal or plant that bears a relationship to another (as related by common descent or by membership in the same genus) [congener, congeneric, relative]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka ne primjenjuje drugačije pravilo, to znači da se ne primjenjuje drugačije pravilo., životinja ili biljka koja je povezana s drugom (kao što je povezana zajedničkim porijeklom ili članstvom u istom rodu), cjelina (stvara ili osoba) iste vrste ili kategorije kao i druga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a minor chemical constituent that gives a wine or liquor its distinctive character</p><p><i>n.</i> an animal or plant that bears a relationship to another (as related by common descent or by membership in the same genus) [congenator, congeneric, relative]</p><p><i>n.</i> a whole (a thing or person) of the same kind or category as another</p><p><b>istovrstan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an animal or plant that bears a relationship to another (as related by common descent or by membership in the same genus) [congenator, congener, relative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to the same genus [congenerical, congenerous]</p><p><b>od čelika ili čelika od čelika ili čelika (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to the same genus [congeneric, congenerous]</p><p><b>od čelika ili čelika od čelika ili čelika (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to the same genus [congeneric, congenerical]</p><p><b>blizak, istovrstan, odgovarajući, podesan, sličan, srodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suitable to your needs</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of plants) capable of cross-fertilization or of being grafted</p><p><b>primjerenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> compatibility between persons [congenialness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a congenial disposition</p><p><b>blizak, istovrstan, odgovarajući, podesan, sličan, srodan (od &quot;congenial&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a congenial manner</p><p><b>blizak, istovrstan, odgovarajući, podesan, sličan, srodan (od &quot;congenial&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> compatibility between persons [congeniality]</p><p><b>kongenitalan, kongenitalna, od rođenja, prirođen, urođen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> present at birth but not necessarily hereditary [inborn, innate]</p><p><b>defekt koji je prisutan pri rođenju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a defect that is present at birth [birth defect, congenital anomaly, congenital defect, congenital diso