nds [conjugate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> joined together especially in a pair or pairs [conjugate, coupled]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of an organic compound [conjugate]</p><p><b>proteid, složena bjelančevina, složeni protein</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a protein complex combining amino acids with other substances [compound protein]</p><p><b>konjugacija, povezivanje, sprezanje, parenje, sjedinjavanje, spajanje, ujedinjavanje, ujedinjenje, unificiranje, unifikacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being joined together [colligation, conjunction, junction]</p><p><i>n.</i> the inflection of verbs</p><p><i>n.</i> the complete set of inflected forms of a verb</p><p><i>n.</i> a class of verbs having the same inflectional forms</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of pairing a male and female for reproductive purposes [coupling, mating, pairing, sexual union, union]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making or becoming a single unit [jointure, unification, union, uniting]</p><p><b>melodično napreduje u intervalima od sekunde., Vezan u bliskom društvu, U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> progressing melodically by intervals of a second</p><p><i>adj.</i> bound in close association</p><p><i>adj.</i> involving the joint activity of two or more [concerted, conjunctive, cooperative]</p><p><b>spajanje, spoj, spoju, spona, stjecaj prilika, veza, veza (gram ), veznik, zajedno, konjunkcija, spojište, čvor, čvorište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the temporal property of two things happening at the same time [co-occurrence, coincidence, concurrence]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being joined together [colligation, conjugation, junction]</p><p><i>n.</i> an uninflected function word that serves to conjoin words or phrases or clauses or sentences [conjunctive, connective, continuative]</p><p><i>n.</i> the grammatical relation between linguistic units (words or phrases or clauses) that are connected by a conjunction</p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) apparent meeting or passing of two or more celestial bodies in the same degre