ije iste godine (1953.) (1934-1969.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States tennis player who was the first woman to win the United States, British, French, and Australian championships in the same year (1953) (1934-1969) [Little Mo Connolly, Maureen Catherine Connolly]</p><p><b>izvanredni teniser Sjedinjenih Država (rođen 1952) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> outstanding United States tennis player (born in 1952) [James Scott Connors, Jimmy Conors]</p><p><b>sporedno značenje, konotacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> what you must know in order to determine the reference of an expression [intension]</p><p><i>n.</i> an idea that is implied or suggested</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s konotacijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a connotation [connotative of]</p><p><b>imati moć da implicira ili sugeriše nešto osim onoga što je izričito (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the power of implying or suggesting something in addition to what is explicit</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s konotacijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a connotation [connotational]</p><p><b>podrazumijevati, pretpostaviti, uključivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> express or state indirectly [imply]</p><p><i>v.</i> involve as a necessary condition of consequence [predicate]</p><p><b>bračni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to marriage or to the relationship between a wife and husband [conjugal]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a conjugal manner [conjugally]</p><p><b>monotipni rod tropskih američkih stabala: gumbovlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monotypic genus of tropical American trees: button tree [genus Conocarpus]</p><p><b>Sastazelenog drveta ili grma s plodovima sličnim gumbovima i koji daju teško tvrdo kompaktno drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen tree or shrub with fruit resembling buttons and yielding heavy hard compact wood [button mangrove, button tree]</p><p><b>cvetovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mistflower [genus Conoclinium]</p><p><b>biljka s rizomatom u središnjoj i jugoistočnoj Americi i u Zapadnoj Indiji s velikim, navidnim glavama čistih plavih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhizomatous plant of central and southeastern United States and West Indies having large showy heads of clear blue flowers [Eupatorium coelestinum, ageratum, mist-flower, mistflower]</p><p><b>mali fosilni zub u obliku kuža primitivnog kičmenjaka iz reda Conodonta, Ribe s krilcima i notohordom, male (2 inča) izumrle ribe nalik jegulji koje imaju zobe u obliku čunjeva koje sadrže staničnu kost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tiny fossil cone-shaped tooth of a primitive vertebrate of order Conodonta</p><p><i>n.</i> small (2 inches long) extinct eellike fish with a finned tail and a notochord and having cone-shaped teeth containing cellular bone</p><p><b>izumrli red primitivnih kralježnjaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct order of primitive vertebrates [Conodontophorida, order Conodonta, order Conodontophorida]</p><p><b>izumrli red primitivnih kralježnjaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct order of primitive vertebrates [Conodonta, order Conodonta, order Conodontophorida]</p><p><b>pačunj, stožac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shape whose base is a circle and whose sides taper up to a point [cone, cone shape]</p><p><b>rod dvostrukožnih biljaka iz obitelji Umbelliferae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of dicotyledonous plants of the family Umbelliferae [genus Conopodium]</p><p><b>biljka koja se koristi za proizvodnju hrane za životinje, a koja se koristi za proizvodnju hrane za životinje, a koja se koristi za proizvodnju hrane za životinje, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common European plant having edible tubers with the flavor of roasted chestnuts [earthnut]</p><p><b>Australski grmovi (neki drveći) s cvjetovima u guštim šiljcima: dimni grm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian shrubs (some trees) with flowers in dense spikes: smoke bush [genus Conospermum]</p><p><b>član Algonkijskog naroda koji je nekada živio u Marylandu između Chesapeake Baya i rijeke Potomac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of an Algonquian people formerly living in Maryland between Chesapeake Bay and the Potomac river</p><p><b>izvojevati, osvajati, osvojiti, pobijediti, pokoriti, svladati, plijeniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bring under control by force or authority [stamp down, subdue, suppress]</p><p><i>v.</i> take possession of by force, as after an invasion [appropriate, capture, seize]</p><p><i>v.</i> overcome by conquest</p><p><b>pobjediv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> subject to being conquered or overcome</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being surmounted or excelled [superable]</p><p><b>osvajanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of conquering [conquest, subjection, subjugation]</p><p><b>osvajač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is victorious by force of arms [vanquisher]</p><p><b>osvajanja, osvajanje, pobjeda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of conquering [conquering, subjection, subjugation]</p><p><i>n.</i> success in mastering something difficult</p><p><i>n.</i> an act of winning the love or sexual favor of someone [seduction]</p><p><b>osvajač, konkvistador</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an adventurer (especially one who led the Spanish conquest of Mexico and Peru in the 16th century)</p><p><b>Engleski romanopisac (rođen u Poljskoj) poznat po morskim pričama i svojoj narativnoj tehnici (1857-1924) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English novelist (born in Poland) noted for sea stories and for his narrative technique (1857-1924) [Joseph Conrad, Teodor Josef Konrad Korzeniowski]</p><p><b>Američki pisac (1889-1973) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer (1889-1973) [Aiken, Conrad Potter Aiken]</p><p><b>Američki pisac (1889-1973) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer (1889-1973) [Aiken, Conrad Aiken]</p><p><b>mali rod nisko aromatičnih grmova iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of low aromatic shrubs of southeastern United States [genus Conradina]</p><p><b>mali grm iz područja rijeke Apalachicola na jugoistoku Sjedinjenih Država s vrlo aromatičnim ružičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrub of Apalachicola River area in southeastern United States having highly aromatic pinkish flowers [Apalachicola rosemary]</p><p><b>srodni po krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> related by blood [akin, blood-related, cognate, consanguineal, consanguineous, kin]</p><p><b>srodni po krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> related by blood [akin, blood-related, cognate, consanguine, consanguineous, kin]</p><p><b>srodni po krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> related by blood [akin, blood-related, cognate, consanguine, consanguineal, kin]</p><p><b>krvno srodstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (anthropology) related by blood [blood kinship, cognation]</p><p><b>savjest, savjesti, svijest, sviješću, savest</b></p><p><i>n.</i> motivation deriving logically from ethical or moral principles that govern a person's thoughts and actions [moral sense, scruples, sense of right and wrong]</p><p><i>n.</i> conformity to one's own sense of right conduct</p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of shame when you do something immoral</p><p><b>Plaćanje dobrovoljno učinjeno kako bi se smanjila krivnja zbog nepoštenog postupanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> payment made voluntarily to reduce guilt over dishonest dealings</p><p><b>utječe na savjest (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affected by conscience</p><p><b>bez savjesti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking a conscience [unconscionable]</p><p><b>osjetljiv, pošten, savjestan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by extreme care and great effort [painstaking, scrupulous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> guided by or in accordance with conscience or sense of right and wrong</p><p><b>osoba koja odbija služiti u oružanim snagama zbog savjesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who refuses to serve in the armed forces on grounds of conscience [CO]</p><p><b>savjesno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with extreme conscientiousness [religiously, scrupulously]</p><p><b>osjetljiv, pošten, savjestan (od &quot;conscientious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being in accord with the dictates of conscience</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being painstaking and careful [painstakingness]</p><p><b>prihvatljivo za vašu savjest (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> acceptable to your conscience</p><p><b>pri svjesti, svjestan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> intentionally conceived [witting]</p><p><i>adj.</i> knowing and perceiving</p><p><i>adj.</i> (followed by `of') showing realization or recognition of something</p><p><b>pri svijesti, samosvjesno, svjesno, uvjereno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with awareness</p><p><b>savjest, savjesti, svijest, svijesti, svest, saznanje, spoznaja, svjesnost, znanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alert cognitive state in which you are aware of yourself and your situation</p><p><i>n.</i> having knowledge of [awareness, cognisance, cognizance, knowingness]</p><p><b>lijek koji može izazvati promjene raspoloženja i iskrivljene percepcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that can produce mood changes and distorted perceptions [mind-altering drug, psychoactive drug, psychoactive substance]</p><p><b>regrut, novak, mobilizirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is drafted into military service [draftee, inductee]</p><p><i>v.</i> enroll into service compulsorily</p><p><b>novačenje, oporezivanje, regrutacija, regrutiranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> compulsory military service [draft, muster, selective service]</p><p><b>posvetiti, zarediti, darivati, darovati, dati, davati, posvetiti se, posvećivati, posvećivati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> appoint to a clerical posts [ordain, order, ordinate]</p><p><i>v.</i> give entirely to a specific person, activity, or cause [commit, dedicate, devote, give]</p><p><i>v.</i> dedicate to a deity by a vow [vow]</p><p><i>v.</i> render holy by means of religious rites [bless, hallow, sanctify]</p><p><i>adj.</i> solemnly dedicated to or set apart for a high or sacred purpose [consecrated, dedicated]</p><p><b>posvećen, posvećenom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> solemnly dedicated to or set apart for a high or sacred purpose [consecrate, dedicated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> made or declared or believed to be holy [sacred, sanctified]</p><p><b>ceremonija predaje odnosno posvete vojne zastave, posvećivanje, konsakracija, konsekracija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solemn commitment of your life or your time to some cherished purpose (to a service or a goal)</p><p><i>n.</i> (religion) sanctification of something by setting it apart (usually with religious rites) as dedicated to God</p><p><b>dosljedan, redom, sljedeći, susljedan, uzastopan, uzastopni, ravan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> one after the other [back-to-back]</p><p><i>adj.</i> in regular succession without gaps [sequent, sequential, serial, successive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> successive (without a break) [straight]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a consecutive manner [sequentially]</p><p><b>Slijedeće operacije: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sequential execution of operations one after another [sequential operation, serial operation]</p><p><b>sukcesivno, uzastopno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a consecutive manner</p><p><b>postojeće na temelju suglasnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing by consent</p><p><b>koncenzus, konsensus, konsenzus, konsenzusom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> agreement in the judgment or opinion reached by a group as a whole</p><p><b>dozvola, nagodba, odobrenje, odobriti, pristanak, pristati, suglasiti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> permission to do something</p><p><i>v.</i> give an affirmative reply to [accept, go for]</p><p><b>Sporazum između dvije stranke koji je odobren od strane suda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agreement between two parties that is sanctioned by the court</p><p><b>jednoglasan, suglasan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in complete agreement [consentient, unanimous]</p><p><b>jednoglasan, suglasan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in complete agreement [consentaneous, unanimous]</p><p><b>dozvola, nagodba, odobrenje, odobriti, pristanak, pristati, suglasiti se (od &quot;consent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having given consent</p><p><b>posljedica, posljedice, rezultat, važnost, značenje, efekt, ishod, konzekvencija, učinak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a phenomenon that follows and is caused by some previous phenomenon [effect, event, issue, outcome, result, upshot]</p><p><i>n.</i> the outcome of an event especially as relative to an individual [aftermath]</p><p><i>n.</i> having important effects or influence [import, moment]</p><p><b>dosljedan, idući, koji slijedi, onaj koji slijedi, posljedica, rezultat, slijedeći</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring with or following as a consequence [accompanying, attendant, collateral, concomitant, ensuant, incidental, resultant, sequent]</p><p><b>dosljedan, koji proizlazi, važan, značajan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having important issues or results [eventful]</p><p><b>dosljedan, koji proizlazi, važan, značajan (od &quot;consequential&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> having consequence</p><p><b>otuda, prema tome, stoga, zbog toga</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (sentence connectors) because of the reason given [accordingly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> as a consequence [therefore]</p><p><b>Komisija nadležna za ribolov i plovidbu u luci ili rijeci, U skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, poduzeća koja su poduzeta u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 1. ovog članka mogu biti podložna postupcima za utvrđivanje i utvrđivanje odgovarajućih zahtjeva za poduzimanje tih mjera. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a commission with jurisdiction over fisheries and navigation in a port or river</p><p><i>n.</i> the official conservation of trees and soil and rivers etc.</p><p><b>čuvanje, konzervacija, očuvanje, održavanje, uzdržavanje, zaštita</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an occurrence of improvement by virtue of preventing loss or injury or other change [preservation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the preservation and careful management of the environment and of natural resources</p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the maintenance of a certain quantities unchanged during chemical reactions or physical transformations</p><p><b>princip da ukupni električni naboj sustava ostaje konstantan unatoč promjenama unutar sustava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principle that the total electric charge of a system remains constant despite changes inside the system [conservation of electricity]</p><p><b>princip da ukupni električni naboj sustava ostaje konstantan unatoč promjenama unutar sustava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principle that the total electric charge of a system remains constant despite changes inside the system [conservation of charge]</p><p><b>Osnovni princip fizike da je ukupna energija izolovanog sustava nepromenljiva unatoč unutarnjim promjenama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fundamental principle of physics that the total energy of an isolated system is constant despite internal changes [first law of thermodynamics, law of conservation of energy]</p><p><b>Osnovni princip klasične fizike da materija ne može biti stvorena ili uništena u izoliranom sustavu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fundamental principle of classical physics that matter cannot be created or destroyed in an isolated system [conservation of matter, law of conservation of mass, law of conservation of matter]</p><p><b>Osnovni princip klasične fizike da materija ne može biti stvorena ili uništena u izoliranom sustavu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fundamental principle of classical physics that matter cannot be created or destroyed in an isolated system [conservation of mass, law of conservation of mass, law of conservation of matter]</p><p><b>princip da je ukupni linearni moment u zatvorenom sustavu konstantan i da na njega ne utječu procesi koji se događaju unutar sustava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principle that the total linear momentum in a closed system is constant and is not affected by processes occurring inside the system</p><p><b>(fizički) paritet je očuvan u svemiru u kojem su zakoni fizike isti u desnom sustavu koordinata kao i u lijevom sustavu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) parity is conserved in a universe in which the laws of physics are the same in a right-handed system of coordinates as in a left-handed system [mirror symmetry, parity, space-reflection symmetry]</p><p><b>osoba koja radi na zaštiti okoliša od uništenja ili onečišćenja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who works to protect the environment from destruction or pollution [environmentalist]</p><p><b>konzervativizam, otpor promjenama</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political or theological orientation advocating the preservation of the best in society and opposing radical changes [conservativism]</p><p><b>konzervativac, konzervativan, konzervativne</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is reluctant to accept changes and new ideas [conservativist]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a Conservative Party</p><p><i>adj.</i> resistant to change, particularly in relation to politics or religion</p><p><i>adj.</i> having social or political views favoring conservatism</p><p><i>adj.</i> avoiding excess [cautious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unimaginatively conventional [button-down, buttoned-down]</p><p><i>adj.</i> conforming to the standards and conventions of the middle class [bourgeois, materialistic]</p><p><b>Židov koji drži neke zahtjeve Mojsijevog zakona, ali prilagođava druge da se prilagode današnjim okolnostima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Jew who keeps some requirements of Mosaic law but adapts others to suit modern circumstances</p><p><b>Židovi koji se pridržavaju nekih zahtjeva Mojsijevog zakona, ali dopuštaju prilagodbu drugih zahtjeva (kao što su neki od zakona o prehrani) kako bi se prilagodili današnjim okolnostima, vjerovanja i prakse konzervativnih Židova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Jews who keep some of the requirements of the Mosaic law but allow for adaptation of other requirements (as some of the dietary laws) to fit modern circumstances</p><p><i>n.</i> beliefs and practices of Conservative Jews</p><p><b>konzervativna stranka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political party (especially in Great Britain or Australia) that believes in the importance of a capitalist economy with private ownership rather than state control</p><p><b>konzervativac, konzervativan, konzervativne (od &quot;conservative&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a conservative manner [cautiously, guardedly]</p><p><b>konzervativizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political or theological orientation advocating the preservation of the best in society and opposing radical changes [conservatism]</p><p><b>osoba koja ne želi prihvatiti promjene i nove ideje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is reluctant to accept changes and new ideas [conservative]</p><p><b>konzervatorij, konzervatoriju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a schoolhouse with special facilities for fine arts [conservatory]</p><p><b>konzervator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the custodian of a collection (as a museum or library) [curator]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone appointed by a court to assume responsibility for the interests of a minor or incompetent person</p><p><b>odgovornost skrbnika da djeluje u najboljem interesu odjeljenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the responsibility of a conservator to act in the best interests of the ward</p><p><b>konzervatorij, stakleni vrt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the faculty and students of a school specializing in one of the fine arts</p><p><i>n.</i> a schoolhouse with special facilities for fine arts [conservatoire]</p><p><i>n.</i> a greenhouse in which plants are arranged in a pleasing manner [hothouse, indoor garden]</p><p><b>čuvati, konzervirati, očuvati, održavati, sačuvati, ekonomizirati, organizirati, rasporediti, raspoređivati, uštedjeti, uščuvati, štedjeti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fruit preserved by cooking with sugar [conserves, preserve, preserves]</p><p><i>v.</i> keep constant through physical or chemical reactions or evolutionary change</p><p><i>v.</i> keep in safety and protect from harm, decay, loss, or destruction [keep up, maintain, preserve]</p><p><i>v.</i> use cautiously and frugally [economise, economize, husband]</p><p><i>v.</i> preserve with sugar</p><p><b>konzervirano, očuvan, očuvano, sačuvan, sačuvano</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> protected from harm or loss</p><p><b>očuvati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fruit preserved by cooking with sugar [conserve, preserve, preserves]</p><p><b>obazirati se, obazrijeti se, računati, razmatrati, razmisliti, razmišljati, razmotriti, smatrati, uzeti u obzir, razmotrit, smatrate, doživjeti, doživljavati, gledati, misliti, vidjeti, mozgati, promisliti, promišljati, promozgati, prostudirati, proučavati, proučiti, studirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> deem to be [reckon, regard, see, view]</p><p><i>v.</i> give careful consideration to [study]</p><p><i>v.</i> take into consideration for exemplifying purposes [deal, look at, take]</p><p><i>v.</i> show consideration for [count, weigh]</p><p><i>v.</i> think about carefully [debate, deliberate, moot, turn over]</p><p><i>v.</i> judge or regard [believe, conceive, think]</p><p><i>v.</i> look at attentively [regard]</p><p><i>v.</i> look at carefully [look at, view]</p><p><i>v.</i> regard or treat with consideration, respect, and esteem</p><p><b>dosta, podosta, priličan, važan, značajan, znatan, znatno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> large or relatively large in number or amount or extent or degree</p><p><b>značajno, znatno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a great extent or degree [substantially, well]</p><p><b>obazriv, obziran, pažljiv, uviđan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing concern for the rights and feelings of others</p><p><b>obazriv, obziran, pažljiv, uviđan (od &quot;considerate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a considerate manner</p><p><b>briga, brižnost, obazrivost, obzir, obzirnost, pažljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> kind and considerate regard for others [consideration, thoughtfulness]</p><p><b>obzir, okolnosti, razmatranje, razmatrati, razmišljanje, sagledavanje, ugled, uzimanje u obzir, okolnost, podatak, stvar, uvjet, činjenica, briga, brižnost, obazrivost, obzirnost, pažljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of giving careful thought to something</p><p><i>n.</i> information that should be kept in mind when making a decision [circumstance, condition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a discussion of a topic (as in a meeting)</p><p><i>n.</i> kind and considerate regard for others [considerateness, thoughtfulness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a fee charged in advance to retain the services of someone [retainer]</p><p><i>n.</i> a considerate and thoughtful act [thoughtfulness]</p><p><b>imati na umu, razmotren, smatrati, uzet u obzir, uzeto u obzir</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> carefully weighed</p><p><b>izručiti, poslati, povjeriti, predati, prenijeti, pristajati, uručiti, ustupiti, pohraniti, pohranjivati, povjeravati, predavati, uručivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> commit forever</p><p><i>v.</i> give over to another for care or safekeeping [charge]</p><p><i>v.</i> send to an address</p><p><b>primatelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the person to whom merchandise is delivered over</p><p><b>izručiti, poslati, povjeriti, predati, prenijeti, pristajati, uručiti, ustupiti (od &quot;consign&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the person who delivers over or commits merchandise [consignor]</p><p><b>pošiljka, teret, tovar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> goods carried by a large vehicle [cargo, freight, lading, load, loading, payload, shipment]</p><p><i>n.</i> the official act of consigning a person to confinement (as in a prison or mental hospital) [commitment, committal]</p><p><i>n.</i> the delivery of goods for sale or disposal</p><p><b>pošiljatelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the person who delivers over or commits merchandise [consigner]</p><p><b>činiti, obuhvaćati, sadržavati, sastojati se, slagati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> originate (in) [dwell, lie, lie in]</p><p><i>v.</i> have its essential character</p><p><i>v.</i> be consistent in form, tenor, or character</p><p><i>v.</i> be composed of [comprise]</p><p><b>čvrstoća, dosljednost, gustoča, postojeći, usklađenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a harmonious uniformity or agreement among things or parts [consistency]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of holding together and retaining its shape [body, consistency, substance]</p><p><b>dosljednost, dosljednosti, konzistencija, konzistentnost, konzistentnosti, nepromjenljivost, postmodernizam, postojanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of holding together and retaining its shape [body, consistence, substance]</p><p><i>n.</i> a harmonious uniformity or agreement among things or parts [consistence]</p><p><i>n.</i> logical coherence and accordance with the facts</p><p><i>n.</i> (logic) an attribute of a logical system that is so constituted that none of the propositions deducible from the axioms contradict one another</p><p><b>dosljedan, dosljedne, konzistentan, nepromjenljiv, u skladu s, u skladu sa</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (sometimes followed by `with') in agreement or consistent or reliable</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being reproduced [reproducible]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by an orderly, logical, and aesthetically consistent relation of parts [coherent, logical, ordered]</p><p><i>adj.</i> the same throughout in structure or composition [uniform]</p><p><b>dosljedno, konzistentno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a systematic or consistent manner [systematically]</p><p><b>crkveni sud ili upravno tijelo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a church tribunal or governing body</p><p><b>asocirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bring or come into association or action [associate]</p><p><b>Moguće je da se uteši. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to be consoled</p><p><b>utjeha</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the comfort you feel when consoled in times of disappointment [solace, solacement]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of consoling [comfort, solace]</p><p><b>pruža utjehu ili utjehu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affording comfort or solace [comforting, consoling]</p><p><b>hrabriti, kontrolna ploča, konzola, obveznice koje u serijama izdaje V.B., tješiti, upravljačka ploča, utješiti, bodriti, obodriti, ohrabriti, ohrabrivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small table fixed to a wall or designed to stand against a wall [console table]</p><p><i>n.</i> a scientific instrument consisting of displays and an input device that an operator can use to monitor and control a system (especially a computer system)</p><p><i>n.</i> an ornamental scroll-shaped bracket (especially one used to support a wall fixture)</p><p><i>n.</i> housing for electronic instruments, as radio or television [cabinet]</p><p><i>v.</i> give moral or emotional strength to [comfort, solace, soothe]</p><p><b>mali stol pričvršćen na zid ili dizajniran da stoji uz zid (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small table fixed to a wall or designed to stand against a wall [console]</p><p><b>biljke s cvjetovima sličnim cvjetovima cvjetnica, ali različitim po rasporedu latica od cvjetnica cvjetnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plants having flowers resembling the larkspur's but differing from larkspur's in the arrangement of petals [genus Consolida]</p><p><b>uobičajena biljka u južnoj Europi s neogranatim šiljakim cvjetovima plavih ili ponekad ljubičastih ili ružičastih cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commonly cultivated larkspur of southern Europe having unbranched spikelike racemes of blue or sometimes purplish or pinkish flowers [Delphinium ajacis, rocket larkspur]</p><p><b>integrirati, konsolidacija, konsolidacije, konsolidirati, objediniti, robu više pošiljalaca složiti u istom kontejneru, skrutiti, učvrstiti, učvršćivati, združiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> unite into one</p><p><i>v.</i> make firm or secure</p><p><i>v.</i> bring together into a single whole or system</p><p><i>v.</i> form into a solid mass or whole</p><p><i>v.</i> make or form into a solid or hardened mass</p><p><b>pročišćen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> joined together into a whole [amalgamate, amalgamated, coalesced, fused]</p><p><i>adj.</i> forming a solid mass</p><p><b>jačanje, konsolidacija, konsolidiranje, sjedinjenje, integracija, integriranje, združivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> combining into a solid mass</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of combining into an integral whole [integration]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that has consolidated into a compact mass</p><p><b>Sastavljanje u jednu jedinicu, koji imaju tendenciju konsolidacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> combining into a single unit [unifying]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to consolidate [integrative]</p><p><b>hrabriti, kontrolna ploča, konzola, obveznice koje u serijama izdaje V.B., tješiti, upravljačka ploča, utješiti (od &quot;console&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affording comfort or solace [comforting, consolatory]</p><p><b>na utješan ili utješan način (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a comforting or consoling manner [comfortingly]</p><p><b>čista juha obično od govedine ili telečje ili pileće meso (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> clear soup usually of beef or veal or chicken</p><p><b>harmonija, sklad</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the repetition of consonants (or consonant patterns) especially at the ends of words [consonant rhyme]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of sounding harmonious [harmoniousness]</p><p><b>konsonant, suglasnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a speech sound that is not a vowel</p><p><i>n.</i> a letter of the alphabet standing for a spoken consonant</p><p><i>adj.</i> involving or characterized by harmony [harmonic, harmonical, harmonised, harmonized]</p><p><i>adj.</i> in keeping [accordant, agreeable, concordant, conformable]</p><p><b>ponavljanje konsonanata (ili uzoraka konsonanata), posebno na kraju riječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the repetition of consonants (or consonant patterns) especially at the ends of words [consonance]</p><p><b>sustav konsonanata koji se koriste u određenom jeziku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of consonants used in a particular language [consonantal system]</p><p><b>biti ili označen ili sadržavati ili funkcionirati kao konsonant, koji se odnosi na ili ima prirodu konsonanta (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being or marked by or containing or functioning as a consonant</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or having the nature of a consonant</p><p><b>sustav konsonanata koji se koriste u određenom jeziku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of consonants used in a particular language [consonant system]</p><p><b>Zvuči u suosjećanju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> sound in sympathy</p><p><b>društvo, ortak, suprug, združiti, pristajati, slagati se, složiti se, uklapati se, uklopiti se, uskladiti se, usklađivati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the husband or wife of a reigning monarch</p><p><i>n.</i> a family of similar musical instrument playing together [choir]</p><p><i>v.</i> keep company with [affiliate, associate, assort]</p><p><i>v.</i> go together [accord, agree, concord, fit in, harmonise, harmonize]</p><p><i>v.</i> keep company [run]</p><p><b>konzorcij, sindikat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an association of companies for some definite purpose [pool, syndicate]</p><p><b>iste vrste, istovrstan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organism belonging to the same species as another organism</p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to the same species</p><p><b>opći sažetak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an overall summary</p><p><b>glasovit, istaknut, isturen, koji pada u oči, napadan, očit, primjetan, upadljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> obvious to the eye or mind</p><p><i>adj.</i> without any attempt at concealment [blatant, blazing]</p><p><b>Kupivanje skupih usluga i proizvoda kako bi se pokazao svojim bogatstvom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> buying expensive services and products in order to flaunt your wealth</p><p><b>glasovit, istaknut, isturen, koji pada u oči, napadan, očit, primjetan, upadljiv (od &quot;conspicuous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a manner tending to attract attention</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a prominent way [prominently]</p><p><b>glasovit, istaknut, isturen, koji pada u oči, napadan, očit, primjetan, upadljiv (od &quot;conspicuous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being conspicuous</p><p><i>n.</i> high visibility</p><p><b>urota, zavjera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a secret agreement between two or more people to perform an unlawful act [confederacy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a plot to carry out some harmful or illegal act (especially a political plot) [cabal]</p><p><i>n.</i> a group of conspirators banded together to achieve some harmful or illegal purpose [confederacy]</p><p><b>zavjera da se ne govori o nekoj situaciji ili događaju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conspiracy not to talk about some situation or event</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili karakteristike urote ili urotnici (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of conspiracy or conspirators [conspiratorial]</p><p><b>konspirator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a conspiracy [coconspirator, machinator, plotter]</p><p><b>konspirativan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of conspiracy or conspirators [conspirative]</p><p><b>kovati zavjeru</b></p><p><i>v.</i> engage in plotting or enter into a conspiracy, swear together [cabal, complot, conjure, machinate]</p><p><i>v.</i> act in unison or agreement and in secret towards a deceitful or illegal purpose [collude]</p><p><b>policajac, stražar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lawman with less authority and jurisdiction than a sheriff</p><p><i>n.</i> English landscape painter (1776-1837) [John Constable]</p><p><i>n.</i> a police officer of the lowest rank [police constable]</p><p><b>policijski, policija, policijske snage</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the force of policemen and officers [law, police, police force]</p><p><b>Konstanz, Sabor u Konstanci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lake in southeastern Germany on the northern side of the Swiss Alps [Bodensee, Lake Constance]</p><p><i>n.</i> the council in 1414-1418 that succeeded in ending the Great Schism in the Roman Catholic Church [Council of Constance]</p><p><b>konstantnost, postojanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being enduring and free from change or variation [stability]</p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) the tendency for perceived objects to give rise to very similar perceptual experiences in spite of wide variations in the conditions of observation [perceptual constancy]</p><p><i>n.</i> faithfulness and dependability in personal attachments (especially sexual fidelity)</p><p><b>konstanta, konstantan, konstantna vrijednost, konstantno, neprekidan, nepromjenljiv, postojan, postojanost, stalan, stalno, trajan, vjeran, nepromjenljivica, stalnica, čvrst, neprestan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a quantity that does not vary [constant quantity, invariable]</p><p><i>n.</i> a number representing a quantity assumed to have a fixed value in a specified mathematical context</p><p><i>adj.</i> unvarying in nature [changeless, invariant, unvarying]</p><p><i>adj.</i> steadfast in purpose or devotion or affection</p><p><i>adj.</i> uninterrupted in time and indefinitely long continuing [ceaseless, incessant, never-ending, perpetual, unceasing, unremitting]</p><p><b>Engleski skladatelj i dirigent (1905-1951) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English composer and conductor (1905-1951) [Lambert, Leonard Constant Lambert]</p><p><b>G, Newtonova konstanta, gravitacijska konstanta, univerzalna gravitacijska konstanta, veliki G</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the universal constant relating force to mass and distance in Newton's law of gravitation [G, gravitational constant, universal gravitational constant]</p><p><b>konstanta vrijednosti omjera dvije proporcionalne veličine x i y (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the constant value of the ratio of two proportional quantities x and y [factor of proportionality]</p><p><b>količina koja se ne mijenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a quantity that does not vary [constant, invariable]</p><p><b>tipografija je tipografija u kojoj je svakom znaku dodijeljena ista širina (kao kod pisaće mašine) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a typeface is which each character is given the same width (as by a typewriter) [fixed-width font, monospaced font, typewriter font]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od 0,01 do 0,01 mm i (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alloy of copper and nickel with high electrical resistance and a low temperature coefficient [Eureka]</p><p><b>Rumunski skulptor poznat po apstrakcijama životinjskih oblika (1876-1957) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Romanian sculptor noted for abstractions of animal forms (1876-1957) [Brancusi]</p><p><b>rumunski odmaralište na Crnom moru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Romanian resort city on the Black Sea</p><p><b>Rimski car koji je zaustavio progon kršćana i 324. godine kršćanstvo proglasio službenom religijom Rimskog carstva, Grad sa zidinama u sjeveroistočnom Alžiru na istoku od Alžira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Emperor of Rome who stopped the persecution of Christians and in 324 made Christianity the official religion of the Roman Empire [Constantine I, Constantine the Great, Flavius Valerius Constantinus]</p><p><i>n.</i> a walled city in northeastern Algeria to the east of Algiers</p><p><b>Rimski car koji je zaustavio progon kršćana i 324. godine kršćanstvo proglasio službenom religijom Rimskog carstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Emperor of Rome who stopped the persecution of Christians and in 324 made Christianity the official religion of the Roman Empire [Constantine, Constantine the Great, Flavius Valerius Constantinus]</p><p><b>Rimski car koji je zaustavio progon kršćana i 324. godine kršćanstvo proglasio službenom religijom Rimskog carstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Emperor of Rome who stopped the persecution of Christians and in 324 made Christianity the official religion of the Roman Empire [Constantine, Constantine I, Flavius Valerius Constantinus]</p><p><b>Treći carigradski sabor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the largest city and former capital of Turkey [Istanbul, Stamboul, Stambul]</p><p><i>n.</i> the council in 869 that condemned Photius who had become the patriarch of Constantinople without approval from the Vatican, thereby precipitating the schism between the eastern and western churches [Fourth Council of Constantinople]</p><p><i>n.</i> the sixth ecumenical council in 680-681 which condemned Monothelitism by defining two wills in Christ, divine and human [Third Council of Constantinople]</p><p><i>n.</i> the fifth ecumenical council in 553 which held Origen's writings to be heretic [Second Council of Constantinople]</p><p><i>n.</i> the second ecumenical council in 381 which added wording about the Holy Spirit to the Nicene Creed [First Council of Constantinople]</p><p><b>konstantno, kontinuirano, neprekidno, neprestano, stalno, uvijek</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without variation or change, in every case [always, invariably]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without interruption [always, forever, incessantly, perpetually]</p><p><b>Pretpostavka koja je osnovna za argument. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an assumption that is basic to an argument [basic assumption, self-evident truth]</p><p><b>istočkati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> scatter or intersperse like dots or studs [dot, stud]</p><p><i>v.</i> come together as in a cluster or flock [clump, cluster, flock]</p><p><i>v.</i> form a constellation or cluster</p><p><b>plejada, sazviježđe, konstelacija, sazvežđe, zviježđe, konfiguracija, poredak, raspored, smještaj, uređenje, plejeda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arrangement of parts or elements [configuration]</p><p><i>n.</i> a configuration of stars as seen from the earth</p><p><b>ispuniti se zabrinutošću, strahom, zbunjenjem ili zbunjenjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> fill with anxiety, dread, dismay, or confusion</p><p><b>potištenost, strah, zaprepaštenje, alarm, preneraženost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fear resulting from the awareness of danger [alarm, dismay]</p><p><b>konstipirati, opstipirati, zatvarati, zatvoriti, začepiti, začepljivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> impede with a clog or as if with a clog [clog]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be constipated [bind]</p><p><b>ako imate teško ili nepotpuno ili rijetko ispražnjenje crijeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> have difficult or incomplete or infrequent evacuation of the bowels</p><p><b>konstipacija, zatvor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> irregular and infrequent or difficult evacuation of the bowels [irregularity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making something futile and useless (as by routine) [deadening, impairment, stultification]</p><p><b>birači, birački okrug, izborna jedinica, klijentela, kupci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of voters who elect a representative for their area</p><p><b>birač, sastavni, sastavni dio, sastavnica, sastavnom dijelu, dio, komad, komponenta, element, faktor, konstituent, sastojak, konstitutivan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artifact that is one of the individual parts of which a composite entity is made up [component, element]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a constituency</p><p><i>n.</i> something determined in relation to something that includes it [component, component part, part, portion]</p><p><i>n.</i> (grammar) a word or phrase or clause forming part of a larger grammatical construction [grammatical constituent]</p><p><i>n.</i> an abstract part of something [component, element, factor, ingredient]</p><p><i>adj.</i> constitutional in the structure of something (especially your physical makeup) [constitutional, constitutive, organic]</p><p><b>biti, čine, čini, činiti, dobivati, osnovati, postaviti nekoga na položaj, predstavljati, sačinjavati, tvoriti, ustrojiti, imenovati, naimenovati, formirati, obrazovati, sačiniti, konstituirati, osnivati, uspostaviti, uspostavljati, ustanoviti, ustanovljavati, ustrojavati, utemeljiti, utemeljivati, zasnivati, zasnovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> form or compose [be, comprise, make up, represent]</p><p><i>v.</i> create and charge with a task or function [appoint, name, nominate]</p><p><i>v.</i> to compose or represent [form, make]</p><p><i>v.</i> set up or lay the groundwork for [establish, found, institute, plant]</p><p><b>konstituiran, sastavljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> brought about or set up or accepted [established]</p><p><b>konstitucija, sastav, sklop, uređenje, ustav, ustava, ustrojstvo, ustavni zakon, ustavni zakonik, formiranje, organizacija, osnivanje, osnutak, uspostava, uspostavljanje, ustanovljavanje, ustanovljenje, kompozicija, ustroj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> law determining the fundamental political principles of a government [fundamental law, organic law]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of forming or establishing something [establishment, formation, organisation, organization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the constitution written at the Constitutional Convention in Philadelphia in 1787 and subsequently ratified by the original thirteen states [Constitution of the United States, U.S. Constitution, US Constitution, United States Constitution]</p><p><i>n.</i> the way in which someone or something is composed [composition, make-up, makeup, physical composition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a United States 44-gun frigate that was one of the first three naval ships built by the United States [Old Ironsides]</p><p><b>Ustav napisan na Ustavnoj konvenciji u Philadelphiji 1787. godine i kasnije ratifikovan od strane originalnih trinaest država. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the constitution written at the Constitutional Convention in Philadelphia in 1787 and subsequently ratified by the original thirteen states [Constitution, U.S. Constitution, US Constitution, United States Constitution]</p><p><b>država u Novoj Engleskoj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New England state [CT, Connecticut, Ct., Nutmeg State]</p><p><b>konstitucioni, ustavni, koristan, zdrav, konstitutivan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a regular walk taken as a form of exercise</p><p><i>adj.</i> of benefit to or intended to benefit your physical makeup</p><p><i>adj.</i> sanctioned by or consistent with or operating under the law determining the fundamental political principles of a government</p><p><i>adj.</i> existing as an essential constituent or characteristic [built-in, inbuilt, inherent, integral]</p><p><i>adj.</i> constitutional in the structure of something (especially your physical makeup) [constituent, constitutive, organic]</p><p><b>Konvencija američkih državnika koji su izradili nacrt Ustava Sjedinjenih Država 1787. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the convention of United States statesmen who drafted the United States Constitution in 1787</p><p><b>bivša politička stranka u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former political party in the United States</p><p><b>Ustavni zakon. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> incorporate into a constitution, make constitutional [constitutionalize]</p><p><b>ustavni sustav vlasti (obično s pisanim ustavom), zastupanje sustava vlasti prema ustavnim načelima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a constitutional system of government (usually with a written constitution)</p><p><i>n.</i> advocacy of a system of government according to constitutional principles</p><p><b>zagovornik ustavne vlade. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of constitutional government</p><p><b>Ustav, kao i država., prošetati zbog zdravlja ili za probavu, na primjer nakon obroka., Ustavni zakon. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> provide with a constitution, as of a country</p><p><i>v.</i> take a walk for one's health or to aid digestion, as after a meal</p><p><i>v.</i> incorporate into a constitution, make constitutional [constitutionalise]</p><p><b>konstitucioni, ustavni (od &quot;constitutional&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> according to the constitution</p><p><b>bitan, sastavni, temeljan, tvorbeni, zakonodavan, konstitutivan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constitutional in the structure of something (especially your physical makeup) [constituent, constitutional, organic]</p><p><b>nagnati, ograničavati, ograničiti, primorati, prinuditi, prisiliti, stegnuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> compel to behave in a certain way [enforce, impose]</p><p><i>v.</i> to close within bounds, or otherwise limit or deprive of free movement [confine, hold, restrain]</p><p><i>v.</i> severely restrict in scope or extent [stiffen, tighten, tighten up]</p><p><b>neprirodan, ograničen, prinuđen, prisiljen, smeten, usiljen, zbunjen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking spontaneity [forced, strained]</p><p><b>neprirodan, ograničen, prinuđen, prisiljen, smeten, usiljen, zbunjen (od &quot;constrained&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a constrained manner</p><p><b>nagnati, ograničavati, ograničiti, primorati, prinuditi, prisiliti, stegnuti (od &quot;constrain&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> restricting the scope or freedom of action [confining, constrictive, limiting, restricting]</p><p><b>naprezanje, ograničenje, prinuda, blokada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being physically constrained [restraint]</p><p><i>n.</i> a device that retards something's motion [restraint]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of constraining</p><p><b>stegnuti, stisnuti, suziti, gnječiti, komprimirati, prešati, sabiti, skupiti, skupljati, stezati, stiskati, zbiti, zgnječiti, sužavati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> squeeze or press together [compact, compress, contract, press, squeeze]</p><p><i>v.</i> become tight or as if tight [constringe, narrow]</p><p><b>stegnuti, stisnuti, suziti (od &quot;constrict&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> especially tense</p><p><i>adj.</i> drawn together or squeezed physically or by extension psychologically</p><p><b>stegnuti, stisnuti, suziti (od &quot;constrict&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of circumstances) tending to constrict freedom [constrictive, narrowing]</p><p><b>stezanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a narrowing that reduces the flow through a channel [bottleneck, chokepoint]</p><p><i>n.</i> tight or narrow compression [coarctation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tight feeling in some part of the body [tightness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the action or process of compressing</p><p><b>(od okolnosti) koji imaju tendenciju ograničavanja slobode, ograničavanje područja ili slobode djelovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of circumstances) tending to constrict freedom [constricting, narrowing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> restricting the scope or freedom of action [confining, constraining, limiting, restricting]</p><p><b>konstriktor, udav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various large nonvenomous snakes that kill their prey by crushing it in its coils</p><p><b>vrlo velika boa tropske Amerike i Zapadne Indije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very large boa of tropical America and West Indies [boa constrictor]</p><p><b>sužavati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become tight or as if tight [constrict, narrow]</p><p><b>ustrojstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an interpretation of the meaning of something</p><p><b>graditi, izgraditi, konstruirati, konstrukt, sagraditi, sazidati, sinteza, ideja, koncept, pojam, izgrađivati, izraditi, izrađivati, napraviti, načiniti, praviti, proizvesti, proizvoditi, raditi, stvarati, stvoriti, učiniti, činiti, rekonstruirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abstract or general idea inferred or derived from specific instances [concept, conception]</p><p><i>v.</i> make by combining materials and parts [build, make]</p><p><i>v.</i> put together out of artificial or natural components or parts [fabricate, manufacture]</p><p><i>v.</i> draw with suitable instruments and under specified conditions</p><p><i>v.</i> create by linking linguistic units</p><p><i>v.</i> create by organizing and linking ideas, arguments, or concepts</p><p><i>v.</i> reassemble mentally [reconstruct, retrace]</p><p><b>graditeljstva, graditeljstvo, gradnja, gradnju, građenja, građenje, građevinski, građevinsko, izgradnja, izrada, izradu, izvedba, izvođenja, izvođenje, konstruiranje, konstrukcija, ustrojstvo, gradnje, gradnji, izgradnje, izgradnji, izgrađivanje, izrađivanje, građevinarstvo, građevinska industrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of constructing something [building]</p><p><i>n.</i> a group of words that form a constituent of a sentence and are considered as a single unit [expression, grammatical construction]</p><p><i>n.</i> the creation of a construct [mental synthesis]</p><p><i>n.</i> a thing constructed [structure]</p><p><i>n.</i> drawing a figure satisfying certain conditions as part of solving a problem or proving a theorem</p><p><i>n.</i> an interpretation of a text or action [twist]</p><p><i>n.</i> the commercial activity involved in repairing old structures or constructing new ones [building]</p><p><b>građevinarstvo, industrija građevnih materijala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industry that builds housing [housing industry]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> paper suitable for drawing and making cutouts</p><p><b>građevinar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a worker skilled in building offices or dwellings etc. [hard hat]</p><p><b>građevni, konstruktivan, koristan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constructing or tending to construct or improve or promote development</p><p><i>adj.</i> emphasizing what is laudable or hopeful or to the good</p><p><b>U slučaju da je ugovorno povlačenje učinjeno prije izvršenja zahtjeva za izvršavanje, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a breach of contract committed prior to the time of required performance [anticipatory breach]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u slučaju iznajmljivanja ne primjenjuje primjena članka 4. stavka 1. točke (a) ili (b) ovog članka, podnositelj zahtjeva može se odbiti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> action by a landlord that compels a tenant to leave the premises (as by rendering the premises unfit for occupancy) [eviction]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, "službenici" su osoblje koje je podređeno nadležnom tijelu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comprises all acts or omissions or concealments involving breach of equitable or legal duty or trust or confidence [legal fraud]</p><p><b>anabolizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the synthesis in living organisms of more complex substances (e.g., living tissue) from simpler ones together with the storage of energy [anabolism]</p><p><b>(zakon) ima moć i namjeru posjedovati i kontrolirati imovinu, ali bez izravne kontrole ili stvarnog prisustva na njoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) having the power and intention to have and control property but without direct control or actual presence upon it</p><p><b>U slučaju da je osoba koja je uložila zahtjev za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izdavanje odobrenja za izda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trust created by a court (regardless of the intent of the parties) to benefit a party that has been wrongfully deprived of its rights [involuntary trust]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s anabolizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to anabolism [energy-storing]</p><p><b>konstruktivni, konstruktivnim, konstruktivno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a constructive manner</p><p><b>građevni, konstruktivan, koristan (od &quot;constructive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of serving to build or improve</p><p><b>konstruktivizama</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abstractionist artistic movement in Russia after World War I</p><p><b>umjetnik škole konstruktivizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artist of the school of constructivism</p><p><b>graditelj, konstruktor, građevinac, građevinar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who contracts for and supervises construction (as of a building) [builder]</p><p><b>protumačiti, tumačiti, upravljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make sense of [interpret, see]</p><p><b>izjasniti se, izjašnjavati se, priklanjati se, prikloniti se, svrstati se, svrstavati se, zauzeti stranu, zauzimati stranu</b></p><p><i>v.</i> go or occur together [co-occur with, collocate with, cooccur with, go with]</p><p><b>smatraju se istim u suštini ili suštini (kao i tri osobe Trojice) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> regarded as the same in substance or essence (as of the three persons of the Trinity)</p><p><b>Ujediniti se u suštini., Ujediniti u jednu zajedničku tvar (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become united in substance</p><p><i>v.</i> unite in one common substance</p><p><b>Doktrina Visoke anglikanske crkve da nakon posvećenja, supstanca Kristovog tijela i krvi koegzistira s supstancom posvećenog kruha i vina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine of the High Anglican Church that after the consecration of the Eucharist the substance of the body and blood of Christ coexists with the substance of the consecrated bread and wine</p><p><b>običaj ili običaj koji je stekao snagu zakona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a custom or usage that has acquired the force of law</p><p><b>Priručnik koji opisuje običaje određene skupine (posebno ceremonijalne običaje redova monaha) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a manual describing the customs of a particular group (especially the ceremonial practices of a monastic order) [consuetudinary]</p><p><b>Priručnik koji opisuje običaje određene skupine (posebno ceremonijalne običaje redova monaha) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a manual describing the customs of a particular group (especially the ceremonial practices of a monastic order) [consuetudinal]</p><p><b>konzul</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a diplomat appointed by a government to protect its commercial interests and help its citizens in a foreign country</p><p><b>konzularan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having to do with a consul or his office or duties</p><p><b>konzulat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> diplomatic building that serves as the residence or workplace of a consul</p><p><b>Postu konzula. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the post of consul</p><p><b>konzultirati, pitati za savjet, posavjetovati se, savjetovati, savjetovati se, diskutirati, konzultirati se, porazgovarati, prodiskutirati, razgovarati, konferirati, raspraviti, raspravljati, razmatrati, razmotriti, vijećati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> get or ask advice from [confer with]</p><p><i>v.</i> seek information from [look up, refer]</p><p><i>v.</i> have a conference in order to talk something over [confab, confabulate, confer]</p><p><i>v.</i> advise professionally</p><p><b>konzultantske usluge, savjetništvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of giving expert advice within a particular field</p><p><b>konzultant, konzultantski, savjetnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert who gives advice [adviser, advisor]</p><p><b>konzilij, konzultacija, konzultacije, savjetništvo, savjetovanje, konzultiranje, provjeravanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conference (usually with someone important) [audience, interview]</p><p><i>n.</i> a conference between two or more people to consider a particular question</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of referring or consulting [reference]</p><p><b>savjetodavan, savjetodavni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> giving advice [advisory, consultatory, consultive]</p><p><b>davanje savjeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> giving advice [advisory, consultative, consultive]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, "odjel" znači "odjel" u smislu članka 4. stavka 1. točke (b) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a firm of experts providing professional advice to an organization for a fee [consulting firm]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, "odjel" znači "odjel" u smislu članka 4. stavka 1. točke (b) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a firm of experts providing professional advice to an organization for a fee [consulting company]</p><p><b>Služba koju pruža stručnjak (npr. odvjetnik ili liječnik ili CPA itd.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> service provided by a professional advisor (e.g., a lawyer or doctor or CPA etc.)</p><p><b>davanje savjeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> giving advice [advisory, consultative, consultatory]</p><p><b>potrošan, potrošiv, prolazan, razoriv, užitačan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> may be used up</p><p><b>iscrpsti, obuzeti, pojesti, potrošiti, trošiti, uništiti, upotrebljavati, utrošiti, konzumirati, potratiti, protepsti, protratiti, protraćiti, proćerdati, rasipati, rastepsti, rasuti, spiskati, spiskavati, stratiti, straćiti, tratiti, traćiti, ćerdati, crpiti, crpsti, iscrpiti, iscrpljivati, isprazniti, prazniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> eat up completely, as with great appetite [demolish, devour, down, go through]</p><p><i>v.</i> serve oneself to, or consume regularly [have, ingest, take, take in]</p><p><i>v.</i> spend extravagantly [squander, ware, waste]</p><p><i>v.</i> destroy completely</p><p><i>v.</i> use up (resources or materials) [deplete, eat, eat up, exhaust, run through, use up, wipe out]</p><p><i>v.</i> engage fully</p><p><b>korisnik, potrošač, konzument</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who uses goods or services</p><p><b>potrošački kredit, kredit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a line of credit extended for personal or household use</p><p><b>trajna roba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> consumer goods that are not destroyed by use [durable goods, durables]</p><p><b>financijska tvrtka koja daje kredite ljudima koji imaju problema s dobivanjem bankovnog kredita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a finance company that makes loans to people who have trouble getting a bank loan [small loan company]</p><p><b>potrošačka roba, roba široke potrošnje, potrošna roba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> goods (as food or clothing) intended for direct use or consumption</p><p><b>kredit koji uspostavlja potrošački kredit koji se daje za osobnu upotrebu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loan that establishes consumer credit that is granted for personal use [personal loan]</p><p><b>potrošačka košarica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an index of the cost of all goods and services to a typical consumer [CPI, cost-of-living index]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, poduzeća koja se bave proizvodnjom proizvoda mogu se smatrati subjektima koji se bave proizvodnjom proizvoda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marketing research that yields information about the motives and needs of different classes of consumers</p><p><b>potrošačka teorija, potrošački pokret</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the theory that an increasing consumption of goods is economically beneficial</p><p><i>n.</i> a movement advocating greater protection of the interests of consumers</p><p><b>potrošnja, uništavanje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very strong [overwhelming]</p><p><b>besprijekoran, potpun, savršen, usavršiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> fulfill sexually</p><p><i>v.</i> make perfect</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or revealing supreme mastery or skill [masterful, masterly, virtuoso]</p><p><i>adj.</i> perfect and complete in every respect [complete]</p><p><i>adj.</i> without qualification [arrant, complete, double-dyed, everlasting, gross, perfect, pure, sodding, staring, s