ords to be played [basso continuo, figured bass, thorough bass]</p><p><b>dug, kontinuiran, kontinuirano, neprekidan, trajan, trajnom, u nastavku</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> continuing in time or space without interruption [uninterrupted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a function or curve</p><p><b>(kosmologija) teorija da svemir održava stalnu prosječnu gustoću s materijom stvorenom da popuni prazninu koju ostave galaksije koje se udaljavaju jedna od druge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (cosmology) the theory that the universe maintains a constant average density with matter created to fill the void left by galaxies that are receding from each other [steady state theory]</p><p><b>Sredstva za upravljanje sustavima za upravljanje vodom i sustavima za upravljanje vodom i sustavima za upravljanje vodom i vodom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a watch established for the reception of traffic of interest to the unit maintaining the watch [listening watch]</p><p><b>imperfekt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tense of verbs used in describing action that is on-going [imperfect, imperfect tense, progressive, progressive tense]</p><p><b>neprekidno, neprekinuto, neprestano, stalno, trajno, kontinuirano</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at every point</p><p><i>adv.</i> with unflagging resolve [ceaselessly, endlessly, incessantly, unceasingly, unendingly]</p><p><b>dug, kontinuiran, kontinuirano, neprekidan, trajan, trajnom, u nastavku (od &quot;continuous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of something that continues without end or interruption [ceaselessness, incessancy, incessantness]</p><p><b>kontinuum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a continuous nonspatial whole or extent or succession in which no part or portion is distinct or distinguishable from adjacent parts</p><p><b>konto</b></p><p><i>n.</i> 1 conto equals 1,000 escudos in Portugal</p><p><b>pjevice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pewees [genus Contopus]</p><p><b>mala muhač iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small flycatcher of western North America [western wood pewee]<