> the act of changing from one use or function or purpose to another</p><p><b>mentalni poremećaj koji se karakterizira pretvaranjem mentalnog sukoba u somatske oblike (u paralizu ili anesteziju bez očiglednog uzroka) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mental disorder characterized by the conversion of mental conflict into somatic forms (into paralysis or anesthesia having no apparent cause) [conversion hysteria, conversion reaction]</p><p><b>faktorom kojim se količina izražena u jednom skupu jedinica mora pomnožiti kako bi se pretvorila u drugi skup jedinica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> factor by which a quantity that is expressed in one set of units must be multiplied in order to convert it into another set of units</p><p><b>mentalni poremećaj koji se karakterizira pretvaranjem mentalnog sukoba u somatske oblike (u paralizu ili anesteziju bez očiglednog uzroka) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mental disorder characterized by the conversion of mental conflict into somatic forms (into paralysis or anesthesia having no apparent cause) [conversion disorder, conversion reaction]</p><p><b>mentalni poremećaj koji se karakterizira pretvaranjem mentalnog sukoba u somatske oblike (u paralizu ili anesteziju bez očiglednog uzroka) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mental disorder characterized by the conversion of mental conflict into somatic forms (into paralysis or anesthesia having no apparent cause) [conversion disorder, conversion hysteria]</p><p><b>(srednjovjekovna Španjolska i Portugal) Židov ili Maur koji je priznao da se preobratio na kršćanstvo kako bi izbjegao progon ili protjeranje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (medieval Spain and Portugal) a Jew or Moor who professed to convert to Christianity in order to avoid persecution or expulsion</p><p><b>konvertirati, obratiti se, preobratiti, pretvarati, pretvori, pretvoriti, prisvojiti, prometni, promjeniti novac, preobratiti se, preobraćivati se, mijenjati, preinačavati, preinačiti, preinačivati, preobraziti, preobražavati, promijeniti, zamijeniti, zamjenjivati, obratiti, obrlatiti, preobraćati, pridobiti, pridobivati, uvjeravati, uvjeriti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who has been converted to another religious or political belief</p><p><i>v.</i> change from one system to another or to a new plan or policy [change over]</p><p><i>v.</i> change the nature, purpose, or function of something</p><p><i>v.</i> change religious beliefs, or adopt a religious belief</p><p><i>v.</i> exchange or replace with another, usually of the same kind or category [change, commute, exchange]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to adopt a new or different faith</p><p><i>v.</i> score an extra point or points after touchdown by kicking the ball through the uprights or advancing the ball into the end zone</p><p><i>v.</i> complete successfully</p><p><i>v.</i> score (a spare)</p><p><i>v.</i> make (someone) agree, understand, or realize the truth or validity of something [convince, win over]</p><p><i>v.</i> exchange a penalty for a less severe one [commute, exchange]</p><p><i>v.</i> change in nature, purpose, or function</p><p><b>konverter, konvertor, pretvarač, pretvornik, usmjerivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device for changing one substance or form or state into another [convertor]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, države članice mogu odrediti da se za određene instrumente primjenjuje sljedeće: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being exchangeable (especially the ability to convert a currency into gold or other currencies without restriction)</p><p><b>kabriolet, pretvoriv, pripisuje se, promjenljiv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a car that has top that can be folded or removed</p><p><i>n.</i> a corporate security (usually bonds or preferred stock) that can be exchanged for another form of security (usually common stock) [convertible security]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sofa that can be converted into a bed [sofa bed]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being exchanged for or replaced by something of equal value [exchangeable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> designed to be changed from one use or form to another</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being changed in substance as if by alchemy [transformable, translatable, transmutable]</p><p><b>Obveznica koja se može pretvoriti u druge vrijednosne papire pod određenim uvjetima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bond that can be converted to other securities under certain conditions</p><p><b>U slučaju da je vrijednost društva u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) Uredbe (EU) br. 575/2013, vrijednost društva u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ili (b) Uredbe (EU) br. 575/2013 može se smatrati vrijednošću društva u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ili (b) Uredbe (EU) br. 575/2013. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a corporate security (usually bonds or preferred stock) that can be exchanged for another form of security (usually common stock) [convertible]</p><p><b>uređaj za promjenu jedne tvari ili oblika ili stanja u drugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device for changing one substance or form or state into another [converter]</p><p><b>ispupčen, izbočen, konveksan, konveksni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> curving or bulging outward [bulging]</p><p><b>sočivo tako da se zraka svjetlosti koja prolazi kroz njega dovodi u točku ili fokus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lens such that a beam of light passing through it is brought to a point or focus [converging lens]</p><p><b>Poligon tako da nijedna strana ne presječava drugu stranu ili vrh. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a polygon such that no side extended cuts any other side or vertex</p><p><b>poliedrom, svaki ravnina čiji je dio konveksni poligon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a polyhedron any plane section of which is a convex polygon</p><p><b>izbočen oblik, izbočenost, konveksan oblik, konveksnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shape that curves or bulges outward [convexity]</p><p><b>ispupčenje, izbočenost, izbočina, izbočini, izbočen oblik, konveksan oblik, konveksnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property possessed by a conv