f Paul Revere and John Hancock before fleeing to England to avoid the American Revolution (1738-1815) [John Copley, John Singleton Copley]</p><p><b>kopolimer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a polymer consisting of two or more different monomers</p><p><b>zajedno polimeriziraju (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> polymerize together [copolymerize]</p><p><b>zajedno polimeriziraju (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> polymerize together [copolymerise]</p><p><b>Neposlušanost suočavanja s nekim problemom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a failure to face some difficulty squarely</p><p><b>bakar, bakar (metal), bakarni novčić, bakren, kotao, pobakriti, cajkan, murjak, pandur</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ductile malleable reddish-brown corrosion-resistant diamagnetic metallic element [Cu, atomic number 29]</p><p><i>n.</i> a copper penny</p><p><i>n.</i> uncomplimentary terms for a policeman [bull, cop, fuzz, pig]</p><p><i>n.</i> a reddish-brown color resembling the color of polished copper [copper color]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various small butterflies of the family Lycaenidae having coppery wings</p><p><i>v.</i> coat with a layer of copper</p><p><b>vrsta europske bukove s blistavim ljubičastim ili bakarnim lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> variety of European beech with shining purple or copper-colored leaves [Fagus purpurea, Fagus sylvatica atropunicea, Fagus sylvatica purpurea, purple beech]</p><p><b>crvenkasto-smeđa boja slična boji poliranog bakra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reddish-brown color resembling the color of polished copper [copper]</p><p><b>od nečeg kojemu je boja bakra (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of something having the color of copper [coppery]</p><p><b>bakreni sjajnik, halkocit, halkozin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heavy grey mineral that is an ore of copper [chalcocite]</p><p><b>rudnik gdje se iz zemlje kopa bakar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mine where copper is dug from the ground</p><p><b>povećanje nosa s dilatacijom folikula i crvenilo i istaknuta vaskularnost kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enlargement of the nose with dilation of follicles and redness and prominent vascularity of the skin [brandy nose, hammer nose, hypertrophic rosacea, potato nose, rhinophyma, rum-blossom, rum nose, toper's nose]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oxide of copper</p><p><b>bakrena pakovina, bakreni pirit, halkopirit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a yellow copper ore (CuFeS2) made up of copper and iron sulfide [chalcopyrite]</p><p><b>Ribica-kamenaca iz pacifičkih obalnih voda Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rockfish of the Pacific coastal waters of North America [Sebastodes caurinus]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena (CAS RN 1344-26-8) u prosjeku od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a copper salt made by the action of sulfuric acid on copper oxide [copper sulphate, cupric sulfate, cupric sulphate]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena (CAS RN 1344-26-8) u prosjeku od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a copper salt made by the action of sulfuric acid on copper oxide [copper sulfate, cupric sulfate, cupric sulphate]</p><p><b>zviždač ili špijun koji radi za policiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an informer or spy working for the police [nark]</p><p><b>bakrena legura, bakrena slitina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any alloy whose principal component is copper</p><p><b>Složeni su s bakrenim dnom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> provide with a copper bottom</p><p><b>s površinom od 8 mm ili više, ali ne više od 8 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a bottom of copper or sheathed with copper</p><p><b>bjelouška</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common coppery brown pit viper of upland eastern United States [Agkistrodon contortrix]</p><p><i>n.</i> venomous but sluggish reddish-brown snake of Australia [Denisonia superba]</p><p><b>graciozan stil rukopisa zasnovan na pisanju koje se koristi na graviranim bakrenim pločama, odtis napravljen od gravirane bakrene ploče, s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graceful style