ed or orange flowers [Lonicera sempervirens, trumpet flower, trumpet honeysuckle, trumpet vine]</p><p><b>Glabrous godišnji sa tankim vrhovnim korijenom i grmovima bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> glabrous annual with slender taproot and clusters of white flowers [Illecebrum verticullatum]</p><p><b>bilo koja od različitih australskih planina klizača iz roda Kennedia s crvenokrasnim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various Australian climbing plants of the genus Kennedia having scarlet flowers</p><p><b>koraljni greben</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reef consisting of coral consolidated into limestone</p><p><b>divlji cvijet roda Corallorhiza koji raste iz tvrde mase rizoma povezanih s gljivom koja pomaže u apsorpciji hranljivih tvari iz šumskoga tla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wildflower of the genus Corallorhiza growing from a hard mass of rhizomes associated with a fungus that aids in absorbing nutrients from the forest floor</p><p><b>Koraljno more</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arm of the South Pacific to the northeast of Australia</p><p><i>n.</i> a Japanese defeat in World War II (May 1942) [battle of the Coral Sea]</p><p><b>bilo koji od raznih otrovnih elapidnih zmija iz Azije i Afrike i Australije, bilo koja od nekoliko otrovnih zmija Novog svijeta briljantno obložene crvenom i crnom i žutom ili bijelom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various venomous elapid snakes of Asia and Africa and Australia [Old World coral snake]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several venomous New World snakes brilliantly banded in red and black and either yellow or white [New World coral snake, harlequin-snake]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih grmova ili grmljava iz roda Erythrina s trostrukim listovima i rasemi od crvenokrasnih do koralnih crvenih cvijeća i crnim sjemenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various shrubs or shrubby trees of the genus Erythrina having trifoliate leaves and racemes of scarlet to coral red flowers and black seeds [erythrina]</p><p><b>s krupnim ili s krupnim stabljik