><p><i>n.</i> a long cigar with blunt ends</p><p><b>Malo sazvežđe na sjevernoj hemisferi između Bootes i Hercules. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small constellation in the northern hemisphere between Bootes and Hercules</p><p><b>električni pražnjenje uz ionizaciju okolne atmosfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electrical discharge accompanied by ionization of surrounding atmosphere [Saint Elmo's fire, Saint Elmo's light, Saint Ulmo's fire, Saint Ulmo's light, St. Elmo's fire, corona, corposant, electric glow]</p><p><b>rekvijem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a song or hymn of mourning composed or performed as a memorial to a dead person [dirge, lament, requiem, threnody]</p><p><b>koronina, kruna, vijenac, girlanda, rukovet, vjenčić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flower arrangement consisting of a circular band of foliage or flowers for ornamental purposes [chaplet, garland, lei, wreath]</p><p><b>Šav između parijetalnih i frontalnih kostiju lubanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the suture between the parietal and frontal bones of the skull [sutura coronalis]</p><p><b>koronarni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> obstruction of blood flow in a coronary artery by a blood clot (thrombus) [coronary thrombosis]</p><p><i>adj.</i> surrounding like a crown (especially of the blood vessels surrounding the heart)</p><p><b>koronarna arterija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the artery that branches from the aorta to supply blood to the heart [arteria coronaria]</p><p><b>operacija otvorenog srca u kojoj se otvara rebra i uklanja dio krvne žile iz aorte u koronarnu arteriju kako bi se zaobišao blokirani dio koronarne arterije i poboljšao dotok krvi u srce (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> open-heart surgery in which the rib cage is opened and a section of a blood vessel is grafted from the aorta to the coronary artery to bypass the blocked section of the coronary artery and improve the blood supply to the heart [CABG, coronary bypass, coronary bypass surgery]</p><p><b>ateroskleroza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stage of arteriosclerosis involving fatty deposits (atheromas) inside the arterial walls, thus narrowing the arteries [atherosclerosis]</p><p><b>operacija otvorenog srca u kojoj se otvara rebra i uklanja dio krvne žile iz aorte u koronarnu arteriju kako bi se zaobišao blokirani dio koronarne arterije i poboljšao dotok krvi u srce (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> open-heart surgery in which the rib cage is opened and a section of a blood vessel is grafted from the aorta to the coronary artery to bypass the blocked section of the coronary artery and improve the blood supply to the heart [CABG, coronary artery bypass graft, coronary bypass surgery]</p><p><b>operacija otvorenog srca u kojoj se otvara rebra i uklanja dio krvne žile iz aorte u koronarnu arteriju kako bi se zaobišao blokirani dio koronarne arterije i poboljšao dotok krvi u srce (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> open-heart surgery in which the rib cage is opened and a section of a blood vessel is grafted from the aorta to the coronary artery to bypass the blocked section of the coronary artery and improve the blood supply to the heart [CABG, coronary artery bypass graft, coronary bypass]</p><p><b>bolnički odjel posebno opremljen i opremljen za liječenje pacijenata s ozbiljnim srčanim problemima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hospital unit specially staffed and equipped to treat patients with serious cardiac problems</p><p><b>nemogućnost srca da pumpa dovoljno krvi za održavanje normalnih tjelesnih funkcija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inability of the heart to pump enough blood to sustain normal bodily functions [heart failure]</p><p><b>srčana bolest uzrokovana abnormalnošću arterija koje isporučuju krv i kisik srcu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heart disease due to an abnormality of the arteries that supply blood and oxygen to the heart</p><p><b>nedostatak protoka krvi u srčane mišiće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inadequate blood flow to the heart muscles [cardiac insufficiency]</p><p><b>obstrukcija koronarne arterije uzrokovana progresivnom aterosklerozom ili krvnim ugruškom (MT)</