dno ponašanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> correct or appropriate behavior [properness, propriety]</p><p><b>koji poboljšava, koji popravlja, koji ublažuje, korektiv, popravni, protusredstvo, ublažujuće sredstvo, okrepljujuće sredstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device for treating injury or disease [restorative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> designed to promote discipline [disciplinal, disciplinary]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending or intended to correct or counteract or restore to a normal condition</p><p><b>ispravno, korektno, pravilno, pravo, točno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an accurate manner [aright, right]</p><p><b>ispravnost, korektnost, točnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> conformity to fact or truth [rightness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of conformity to social expectations</p><p><b>Talijanski slikar poznat po upotrebi jasnoputlja i perspektive (1494-1534) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian painter noted for his use of chiaroscuro and perspective (1494-1534) [Antonio Allegri da Correggio]</p><p><b>poluostrvo i otok na Filipinima gdje su japanske snage opkoljivale američke snage u Drugom svjetskom ratu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the peninsula and island in the Philippines where Japanese forces besieged American forces in World War II [Bataan]</p><p><b>uzajamna veza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two or more related or complementary variables [correlative]</p><p><i>v.</i> to bear a reciprocal or mutual relation</p><p><i>v.</i> bring into a mutual, complementary, or reciprocal relation</p><p><i>adj.</i> mutually related [correlated, correlative]</p><p><b>korelirani, povezan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> mutually related [correlate, correlative]</p><p><b>korelacija, korelat, međusobna povezanost, međusobni odnosi, ovisnost, povezanost, suodnos, uzajamna zavisnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reciprocal relation between two or more things [correlativity]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statistic representing how closely two variables co-vary [coefficient of correlation, correlation coefficient]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statistical relation between two or more variables such that systematic changes in the value of one variable are accompanied by systematic changes in the other [correlational statistics]</p><p><b>statistička vrijednost koja prikazuje koliko se dvije varijable razlikuju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statistic representing how closely two variables co-vary [coefficient of correlation, correlation]</p><p><b>matricu koja daje korelacije između svih parova skupova podataka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a matrix giving the correlations between all pairs of data sets</p><p><b>korelacijska tablica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a two-way tabulation of the relations between correlates</p><p><b>U vezi s ili korištenjem korelacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or employing correlation</p><p><b>Upotreba statističke korelacije za procjenu snaga odnosa između varijabli (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of statistical correlation to evaluate the strength of the relations between variables</p><p><b>korelacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statistical relation between two or more variables such that systematic changes in the value of one variable are accompanied by systematic changes in the other [correlation]</p><p><b>korelativan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two or more related or complementary variables [correlate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> mutually related [correlate, correlated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing a reciprocal or complementary relation</p><p><b>korelacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reciprocal relation between two or more things [correlation]</p><p><b>dopisivati se, odgovarati, odnositi se, podudarati se, predstavljati, pristajati, suglasan, suglasni</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be compatible, similar or consistent [agree, check, fit, gibe, jibe, match, tally]</p><p><i>v.</i> be equivalent or parallel, in mathematics [equate]</p><p><i>v.</i> exchange messages</p><p><i>v.</i> take the place of or be parallel or equivalent to [represent, stand for]</p><p><b>dopisivanje, korespodencija, korespondencija, odgovaranje, podudaranje, p