ati, zamisliti, zamišljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> create mentally and abstractly rather than with one's hands [create by mental act]</p><p><b>iskazati riječima, iskazati verbalno, iskazivati riječima, iskazivati verbalno, orječiti, stvarati riječima, stvarati verbalno, stvoriti riječima, stvoriti verbalno, verbalizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> create with or from words</p><p><b>Amino kiselina koja se ne nalazi u proteinima, ali se nalazi u mišićnom tkivu kralježnjaka u slobodnom obliku i kao fosfokreatin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an amino acid that does not occur in proteins but is found in the muscle tissue of vertebrates both in the free form and as phosphocreatine [creatine]</p><p><b>Amino kiselina koja se ne nalazi u proteinima, ali se nalazi u mišićnom tkivu kralježnjaka u slobodnom obliku i kao fosfokreatin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an amino acid that does not occur in proteins but is found in the muscle tissue of vertebrates both in the free form and as phosphocreatine [creatin]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom proteina od 0,5% do 0,5% i (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organic compound of creatine and phosphoric acid [creatine phosphoric acid, phosphocreatine]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom proteina od 0,5% do 0,5% i (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organic compound of creatine and phosphoric acid [creatine phosphate, phosphocreatine]</p><p><b>umno stvaralaštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of creating something by thinking</p><p><b>stvaranje uklanjanjem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of creating by removing something</p><p><b>stvaranje iz sirovina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of creating something that is different from the materials that went into it</p><p><b>djelo, formacija, kreacija, osnivanje, ostvarenje, stvaralaštvo, stvaranja, stvaranje, stvaranjem, tvorevina, nastanak, postanak, početak, začetak, bitak, bivstvo, kozmos, makrokozmos, svemir, svijet, univerzum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the human act of creating [creative activity]</p><p><i>n.</i> an artifact that has been brought into existence by someone</p><p><i>n.</i> the event that occurred at the beginning of something [conception]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of starting something for the first time [foundation, founding, initiation, innovation, instauration, institution, introduction, origination]</p><p><i>n.</i> (theology) God's act of bringing the universe into existence</p><p><i>n.</i> everything that exists anywhere [cosmos, existence, macrocosm, universe, world]</p><p><b>pokušaj da se znanstveno podupre istina izvještaja o stvaranju iz Knjige Postanka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an effort to give scientific support for the truth of the account of Creation given in the Book of Genesis</p><p><b>kreacionizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the literal belief in the account of Creation given in the Book of Genesis</p><p><b>kreativan, stvaralački, maštovit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the ability or power to create [originative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> promoting construction or creation</p><p><b>kreacija, stvaralaštvo, stvaranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the human act of creating [creation]</p><p><b>kreativac, umjetnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person whose creative work shows sensitivity and imagination [artist]</p><p><b>kreativni mislilac, mislilac, um</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an important intellectual [mind, thinker]</p><p><b>kreativnost, stvaralaštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to create [creativeness, creativity]</p><p><b>kreativno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a creative manner</p><p><b>kreativnost, stvaralaštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to create [creative thinking, creativity]</p><p><b>kreativnost, kreativnosti, stvaralaštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to create [creative thinking, creativeness]</p><p><b>kreator, stvaralac, tvorac, izumitelj, stvaratelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> terms referring to the Judeo-Christian God [Almighty, Divine, God Almighty, Godhead, Jehovah, Lord, Maker]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who grows or makes or invents things</p><p><b>biće, kreatura, stvorenje, životinja, individua, osoba, pojedinac, čovjek</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a living organism characterized by voluntary movement [animal, animate being, beast, brute, fauna]</p><p><i>n.</i> a human being [wight]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is controlled by others and is used to perform unpleasant or dishonest tasks for someone else [puppet, tool]</p><p><b>stvari koje vas čine udobnim i u miru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> things that make you comfortable and at ease [amenities, comforts, conveniences]</p><p><b>dječje jaslice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hospital where foundlings (infant children of unknown parents) are taken in and cared for [foundling hospital]</p><p><i>n.</i> a representation of Christ's nativity in the stable at Bethlehem</p><p><b>Prva odlučujuća bitka Stogodišnjeg rata. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first decisive battle of the Hundred Years' War [battle of Crecy]</p><p><b>Povjerljivost među mladim modnim urbanim pojedincima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> credibility among young fashionable urban individuals [street cred, street credibility]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s vjerskim vjerovanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a creed [creedal]</p><p><b>pouzdanje, povjerenje, vjera, prihvaćanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mental attitude that something is believable and should be accepted as true [acceptance]</p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of sideboard or buffet [credenza]</p><p><b>(Kršćanstvo) bilo koji od odjeljaka u koje je vjerovanje ili drugo izricanje nauke podijeljeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Christianity) any of the sections into which a creed or other statement of doctrine is divided [article of faith]</p><p><b>dokument, uvjerenje, vjerodajni, vjerodajnica, certifikat, potvrda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a document attesting to the truth of certain stated facts [certificate, certification, credentials]</p><p><b>Službenici koji su u službenom stanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> certified as professional by evidence or testimonials</p><p><b>akreditiv, vjerodajnica, vjerodajnice, certifikat, potvrda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a document attesting to the truth of certain stated facts [certificate, certification, credential]</p><p><b>vrsta ormarića ili šolja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of sideboard or buffet [credence]</p><p><b>vjerodostojnost, uvjerljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being believable or trustworthy [believability, credibleness]</p><p><b>vjerojatan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being believed [believable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (a common but incorrect usage where `credulous' would be appropriate) credulous</p><p><i>adj.</i> appearing to merit belief or acceptance</p><p><b>uvjerljivost, vjerodostojnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being believable or trustworthy [believability, credibility]</p><p><b>vjerojatno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> easy to believe on the basis of available evidence [believably, plausibly, probably]</p><p><b>dug, konto, kredit, kreditirati, kreditni, odobriti, povjerenje, priznanje, ugled, vjera, vjerovati, zasluga, kreditnih, kreditnim, odobravanje, priznavanje, citat, referenca, odobravati, pozajmiti, pozajmljivati, upisati, upisivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> approval [recognition]</p><p><i>n.</i> money available for a client to borrow</p><p><i>n.</i> an accounting entry acknowledging income or capital items [credit entry]</p><p><i>n.</i> used in the phrase `to your credit' in order to indicate an achievement deserving praise</p><p><i>n.</i> arrangement for deferred payment for goods and services [deferred payment]</p><p><i>n.</i> recognition by a college or university that a course of studies has been successfully completed [course credit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a short note recognizing a source of information or of a quoted passage [acknowledgment, citation, cite, mention, quotation, reference]</p><p><i>n.</i> an entry on a list of persons who contributed to a film or written work</p><p><i>n.</i> an estimate, based on previous dealings, of a person's or an organization's ability to fulfill their financial commitments [credit rating]</p><p><i>v.</i> give someone credit for something</p><p><i>v.</i> ascribe an achievement to [accredit]</p><p><i>v.</i> accounting: enter as credit</p><p><i>v.</i> have trust in</p><p><b>kredit koji poduzeće daje kupcu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> credit extended by a business to a customer [charge account, open account]</p><p><b>financijski izvještaj i financijska povijest podnositelja zahtjeva za kredit kako bi se procijenila njihova kreditna sposobnost. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an analyst who studies the financial statements and financial history of applicants for credit in order to evaluate their creditworthiness</p><p><b>zahtjevi za kreditnu liniju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an application for a line of credit</p><p><b>privatno poduzeće koje vodi podatke o potrošačkom kreditu i pruža informacije o kreditu ovlaštenim korisnicima uz naknadu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a private firm that maintains consumer credit data files and provides credit information to authorized users for a fee</p><p><b>kreditna kartica, kartica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a card (usually plastic) that assures a seller that the person using it has a satisfactory credit rating and that the issuer will see to it that the seller receives payment for the merchandise delivered [charge card, charge plate, plastic]</p><p><b>Država u kojoj postoji nedostatak gotovine za pozajmljivanje poduzećima i potrošačima i kamatne stope su visoke. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in which there is a short supply of cash to lend to businesses and consumers and interest rates are high [liquidity crisis, squeeze]</p><p><b>kredit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an accounting entry acknowledging income or capital items [credit]</p><p><b>jedinica akademskog kredita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of academic credit [semester hour]</p><p><b>kreditna linija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the maximum credit that a customer is allowed [bank line, line, line of credit, personal credit line, personal line of credit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a line giving the name of the writer of a story or article [by-line]</p><p><b>Naručivanje koje se prima bez plaćanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an order that is received without payment [bill-me order]</p><p><b>kreditni rejting</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an estimate, based on previous dealings, of a person's or an organization's ability to fulfill their financial commitments [credit]</p><p><b>Račun o primljenim plaćanjima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> account of payments received</p><p><b>sustav za omogućavanje ljudima da kupuju stvari na kredit (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system for allowing people to purchase things on credit</p><p><b>kreditna unija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cooperative depository financial institution whose members can obtain loans from their combined savings</p><p><b>zaslužuje često ograničen pohvale (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of often limited commendation</p><p><b>u izuzetno dostojanom stupnju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a tolerably worthy extent [respectably]</p><p><b>pripisan, pripisano</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually followed by `to') given credit for</p><p><b>kreditor, povjeritelj, vjerovnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person to whom money is owed by a debtor</p><p><b>dug, konto, kredit, kreditirati, kreditni, odobriti, povjerenje, priznanje, ugled, vjera, vjerovati, zasluga, kreditnih, kreditnim (od &quot;credit&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a list of acknowledgements of those who contributed to the creation of a film (usually run at the end of the film)</p><p><b>bonitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trustworthiness with money as based on a person's credit history</p><p><b>kredibilan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an acceptable credit rating [responsible]</p><p><b>vjera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any system of principles or beliefs [creed]</p><p><b>lakovjernost, naivnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tendency to believe readily</p><p><b>lakovjeran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed to believe on little evidence</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing a lack of judgment or experience</p><p><b>lakovjeran (od &quot;credulous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a