vine whose fruit has a netted rind and edible flesh and a musky smell [muskmelon, sweet melon, sweet melon vine]</p><p><b>vrsta muskmelonove loze s plodovima s tanom ljuskom i narandžastom mesom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of muskmelon vine having fruit with a tan rind and orange flesh [cantaloup, cantaloup vine, cantaloupe, cantaloupe vine]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta vinove loze od lubenice koja ima plodove glatke bele kore i bijelo ili zelenkasto meso koje nema miris muške (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a variety of muskmelon vines having fruit with a smooth white rind and white or greenish flesh that does not have a musky smell [Persian melon, honeydew melon, winter melon, winter melon vine]</p><p><b>Vina muskmelon s plodovima koji imaju tanku mrežasti ljusku i slatko zeleno meso (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a muskmelon vine with fruit that has a thin reticulated rind and sweet green flesh [net melon, netted melon, nutmeg melon]</p><p><b>u obliku mliječne trske (Cucumis) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a melon vine of the genus Cucumis [cucumber, cucumber vine]</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka iz obitelji Cucurbitaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the family Cucurbitaceae</p><p><b>bundeve, buče</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Cucurbitaceae [genus Cucurbita]</p><p><b>biljka koja nosi bundeve s globusnim do jajnovitim plodovima s različito prugavima sivom i zelenom i bijelom bradavičnom kore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant bearing squash having globose to ovoid fruit with variously striped grey and green and white warty rinds [Cucurbita mixta, cushaw]</p><p><b>višegodišnje loze suhih dijelova središnje i jugozapadne Sjedinjenih Američkih Država i Meksika s malim tvrdim mrljevim zelenim nejedljivim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial vine of dry parts of central and southwestern United States and Mexico having small hard mottled green inedible fruit [Missouri gourd, buffalo gourd, calabazilla, prairie gourd, prairie gourd vine, wild pumpkin]</p><p><b>biljka s