anjem i uzgojem usjeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> arable land that is worked by plowing and sowing and raising crops [farmland, ploughland, plowland, tillage, tilled land, tilth]</p><p><b>Europska dvostruka s dugim fusiformnim korijenom koji je uzgojem postao ukusan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European biennial having a long fusiform root that has been made palatable through cultivation</p><p><b>kultivirana biljka, uzgojena biljka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plants that are grown for their produce</p><p><b>Oryza sativa, kultivirana riža, riža</b></p><p><i>n.</i> yields the staple food of 50 percent of world's population [Oryza sativa]</p><p><b>široko uzgajana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated [Fragaria ananassa, garden strawberry]</p><p><b>gajenje, kultivacija, kultiviranje, kultiviziranje, njegovanje, obrada, obrađivanje, uzgoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> socialization through training and education to develop one's mind or manners</p><p><i>n.</i> (agriculture) production of food by preparing the land to grow crops (especially on a large scale)</p><p><i>n.</i> a highly developed state of perfection [culture, finish, polish, refinement]</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of fostering the growth of something</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of raising or growing plants (especially on a large scale)</p><p><b>kultivator, obrađivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone concerned with the science or art or business of cultivating the soil [agriculturalist, agriculturist, grower, raiser]</p><p><i>n.</i> a farm implement used to break up the surface of the soil (for aeration and weed control and conservation of moisture) [tiller]</p><p><b>kultura, kulturalno, kulturan, kulture, kulturni, prosvijećen, kulturna, kulturne, kulturnih, kulturnim, kulturno, kulturnog</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the arts and manners that a group favors</p><p><i>adj.</i> denoting or deriving from or distinctive of the ways of living built up by a group of people [ethnic, ethnical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the shared knowledge and values of a society</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the raising of plants or animals</p><p><b>antropolog koji proučava kulturne fenomene kao što su sustavi srodstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anthropologist who studies such cultural phenomena as kinship systems [social anthropologist]</p><p><b>grana antropologije koja se bavi ljudskom kulturom i društvom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of anthropology that deals with human culture and society [social anthropology]</p><p><b>osoblje koje je stručnjak za kulturna pitanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an attache who is a specialist in cultural matters</p><p><b>kulturni pokret</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of people working together to advance certain cultural goals</p><p><b>radikalna reforma u Kini koju je započeo Mao Zedong 1965. godine i koju je u velikoj mjeri provela Crvena garda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radical reform in China initiated by Mao Zedong in 1965 and carried out largely by the Red Guard [Great Proletarian Cultural Revolution]</p><p><b>kultura, kulturalno, kulturan, kulture, kulturni, prosvijećen, kulturna, kulturne, kulturnih, kulturnim, kulturno, kulturnog (od &quot;cultural&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with regard to a culture</p><p><b>osobe koje se zanimaju za kulturu i kulturne aktivnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people interested in culture and cultural activities</p><p><b>gajenje, kultura, kulturan, uljudba, uzgoj, klultura, kulture, kulturi, kulturu, obrazovanje, trgovina, civilizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a particular society at a particular time and place [civilisation, civilization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the tastes in art and manners that are favored by a social group</p><p><i>n.</i> all the knowledge and values shared by a society [acculturation]</p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) the growing of microorganisms in a nutrient medium (such as gelatin or agar)</p><p><i>n.</i> a highly developed state of perfection [cultivation, finish, polish, refinement]</p><p><i>n.</i> the attitudes and behav