rike od tropske kišne šume do umjerenih šumarskih područja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Cyatheaceae: tree ferns of the tropical rain forest to temperate woodlands [genus Cyathea]</p><p><b>najozbiljniji paprikav iz Novog Zelanda i Australije s krunom od spuštenog lista s bijelom donjom stranom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a showy tree fern of New Zealand and Australia having a crown of pinnated fronds with whitish undersides [black tree fern, sago fern, silver tree fern]</p><p><b>tropske drveće paprike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical tree ferns [family Cyatheaceae]</p><p><b>velika boginja prirode drevne Frigije u Mala Aziji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> great nature goddess of ancient Phrygia in Asia Minor [Dindymene, Great Mother, Magna Mater, Mater Turrita]</p><p><b>napad na elektroničke komunikacijske mreže (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an assault on electronic communication networks [cyberwar]</p><p><b>programer koji provali u računalne sustave kako bi ukrao, promijenio ili uništio informacije kao oblik kiber-terorizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a programmer who breaks into computer systems in order to steal or change or destroy information as a form of cyber-terrorism [cyberpunk]</p><p><b>kibernetska umjetnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> art that is produced with the help of computer hardware and software</p><p><b>kafić čiji klijenti sjede na računarskim terminalima i prijavljuju se na internet dok jedu i piju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cafe whose customers sit at computer terminals and log on to the internet while they eat and drink</p><p><b>kiberkrim</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crime committed using a computer and the internet to steal a person's identity or sell contraband or stalk victims or disrupt operations with malevolent programs</p><p><b>kultura koja nastaje korištenjem računala za komunikaciju i zabavu i poslovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the culture that emerges from the use of computers for communication and entertainment and business</p><p><b>kontrolirati funkciju, proces ili stvaranje pomoću računala (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> control a function, process, or creation by a computer [computerise, computerize]</p><p><b>Upravljanje procesima pomoću računala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the control of processes by computer [computerization]</p><p><b>Korisnik računala koji koristi internet. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a computer user who uses the internet</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s načelima kibernetike (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating the principles of cybernetics</p><p><b>kibernetika, kibernetski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) the field of science concerned with processes of communication and control (especially the comparison of these processes in biological and artificial systems)</p><p><b>iracionalni strah od računala ili tehnologije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> irrational fear of computers or technology</p><p><b>kiberpank, cyberpunk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a programmer who breaks into computer systems in order to steal or change or destroy information as a form of cyber-terrorism [cyber-terrorist]</p><p><i>n.</i> a writer of science fiction set in a lawless subculture of an oppressive society dominated by computer technology</p><p><i>n.</i> a genre of fast-paced science fiction involving oppressive futuristic computerized societies</p><p><b>cybersex, kibernetički seks</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sexual arousal involving communication on the internet</p><p><b>cyber-prostor, kibernetski prostor, kiberprostor, prostor u kojem postoje ljudi i računala, umjetni prostor, internet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a computer network consisting of a worldwide network of computer networks that use the TCP/IP network protocols to facilitate data transmission and exchange [internet, net]</p><p><b>napad na elektroničke komunikacijske mreže (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an assault on electronic communication networks [cyber-terrorism]</p><p><b>kiborg</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a human being whose body has been taken over in whole or in part by electromechanical devices [bionic man