hat studies the cellular aspects of heredity (especially the chromosomes)</p><p><b>izvor i razvoj i varijacija stanica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the origin and development and variation of cells [cytogenesis]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih proteinskih molekula koje luče stanice imunološkog sustava koje služe za regulaciju imunološkog sustava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various protein molecules secreted by cells of the immune system that serve to regulate the immune system</p><p><b>organski proces koji se sastoji od podjele citoplazme stanice nakon kariokineze koja dovodi do odvajanja na dvije kćeri stanice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> organic process consisting of the division of the cytoplasm of a cell following karyokinesis bringing about the separation into two daughter cells</p><p><b>od ili povezane s podjelom citoplazme stanice nakon podjele jezgre (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the division of the cytoplasm of a cell following the division of the nucleus</p><p><b>bilo koji od razreda biljnih hormona koji potiču ćelijsku podjelu i odgađaju senescence lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a class of plant hormones that promote cell division and delay the senescence of leaves [kinin]</p><p><b>protoplazma stanice osim jezgre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the protoplasm of a cell excluding the nucleus [cytoplasm]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s znanosti o citologiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the science of cytology [cytological]</p><p><b>uzorak tankog tkiva ili krvi na staklenom posudu i obojen za citološki pregled i dijagnozu pod mikroskopom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin tissue or blood sample spread on a glass slide and stained for cytologic examination and diagnosis under a microscope [cytosmear, smear]</p><p><b>uzorak koji se koristi za citološko ispitivanje i dijagnozu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specimen used for cytologic examination and diagnosis</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s znanosti o citologiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating