eurish manner [play around, smatter]</p><p><i>v.</i> bob forward and under so as to feed off the bottom of a body of water</p><p><b>zaštićena svijetlim mrljama (često se koriste u kombinaciji) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with bright patches (often used in combination) [spattered, splashed, splattered]</p><p><b>diletant</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an amateur who engages in an activity without serious intentions and who pretends to have knowledge [dilettante, sciolist]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous shallow-water ducks that feed by upending and dabbling [dabbling duck]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih plitkovodnih pataka koje se hrane uzdizanjem i škrcanjem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous shallow-water ducks that feed by upending and dabbling [dabbler]</p><p><b>mala evropska greska (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small European grebe [Podiceps ruficollis, little grebe]</p><p><b>u obliku poluploda (C. albicans) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dicotyledonous genus of the family Ericaceae [genus Daboecia]</p><p><b>nizak zelena stalak iz zapadne Europe, predstavljen nekoliko vrsta s cvjetovima od bijelog do ružičasto-fijazlovitog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low straggling evergreen shrub of western Europe represented by several varieties with flowers from white to rose-purple [Connemara heath, St. Dabeoc's heath]</p><p><b>Dhaka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Bangladesh [Dhaka, capital of Bangladesh]</p><p><b>klenić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small European freshwater fish with a slender bluish-green body [Leuciscus leuciscus]</p><p><b>Australoazijski ribolovni kralj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australasian kingfishers [genus Dacelo]</p><p><b>Australski ribolovni pas koji glasno kuka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian kingfisher having a loud cackling cry [kookaburra, laughing jackass]</p><p><b>dača</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Russian country house</p><p><b>Dachau</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a concentration camp for Jews created by the Nazis near Munich in southern Germany</p><p><b>ja