ases in the mixture [Dalton's law of partial pressures, law of partial pressures]</p><p><b>(hemija i fizika) zakon koji navodi da je pritisak koji vrši mješavina plinova jednak sjem partijalnih pritisaka plinova u mješavini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry and physics) law stating that the pressure exerted by a mixture of gases equals the sum of the partial pressures of the gases in the mixture [Dalton's law, law of partial pressures]</p><p><b>Dihromacija karakterizirana smanjenom osjetljivošću na zelenu svjetlost koja rezultira nemogućnošću razlikovanja zelene i ljubičasto-crvene svjetlosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dichromacy characterized by a lowered sensitivity to green light resulting in an inability to distinguish green and purplish-red [deuteranopia, green-blindness]</p><p><b>brana, nasip, pregrada, prepreka, prepriječiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a barrier constructed to contain the flow of water or to keep out the sea [dike, dyke]</p><p><i>n.</i> a metric unit of length equal to ten meters [decameter, decametre, dekameter, dekametre, dkm]</p><p><i>n.</i> female parent of an animal especially domestic livestock</p><p><i>v.</i> obstruct with, or as if with, a dam [dam up]</p><p><b>prepriječiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> obstruct with, or as if with, a dam [dam]</p><p><b>Ptica u pticama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fallow deer [genus Dama]</p><p><b>jelen lopatar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Eurasian deer [fallow deer]</p><p><b>havarija, kvar, oštećenost, oštećenje, oštetiti, pokvariti, povreda, šteta, štetiti, ugruvati, oštećenja, povrede, štete, štetu, ozljeda, zlo, cijena, naštetiti, oštećivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the occurrence of a change for the worse [harm, impairment]</p><p><i>n.</i> loss of military equipment [equipment casualty]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of damaging something or someone [harm, hurt, scathe]</p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of money needed to purchase something [price, terms]</p><p><i>n.</i> any harm or injury resulting from a violation of a legal right [legal injury, wrong]</p><p><i>v.</i> inflict damage upon</p><p><i>v.</i> suffer or be susceptible to damage</p><p><b>popravak štete</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an effort to minimize or curtail damage or loss</p><p><b>oštećen, oštećenja, oštećenje, pokvaren, razoren, razorenih</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> harmed or injured or spoiled</p><p><i>adj.</i> being unjustly brought into disrepute [discredited]</p><p><b>naknada štete, odšteta, oštećenja, popravljanje štete, šteta, štete</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sum of money paid in compensation for loss or injury [amends, indemnification, indemnity, redress, restitution]</p><p><b>oštećivanje, škodljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (sometimes followed by `to') causing harm or injury [detrimental, prejudicial, prejudicious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> designed or tending to discredit, especially without positive or helpful suggestions [negative]</p><p><b>Afričke antilope: sassabies (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> African antelopes: sassabies [genus Damaliscus]</p><p><b>velika južnoafrička antilopa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large South African antelope [sassaby, topi]</p><p><b>Svaka od različitih tvrdih smola iz stabala iz obitelji Dipterocarpaceae i rodova Agathis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various hard resins from trees of the family Dipterocarpaceae and of the genus Agathis [dammar, dammar resin, gum dammar]</p><p><b>kolonijalni krtica-molu iz zapadne Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> colonial mole rat of western Africa</p><p><b>rođen ili stanovnik Damaska, S druge strane, u slučaju da se upotrebljava u proizvodnji čelika, to znači da se ne upotrebljava za proizvodnju čelika., metalni inkrustor sa zlatom i srebrom, od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Damask ili njegov narod, (od metala) ukrašena ili inkrustirana valovitim uzorkom različitih (posebno plemenitih) metala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Damascus</p><p><i>n.</i> a design produced by inlaying gold or silver into steel</p><p><i>v.</i> inlay metal with gold and silver</p><p><i>adj.</i> 