nd) (1892-1983) [Cicily Isabel Fairfield, Rebecca West, West]</p><p><b>Engleska glumica (1882-1976) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English actress (1882-1976) [Thorndike]</p><p><b>duge biljke s cvijećem čiji je miris izraženiji navečer (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> long cultivated herb having flowers whose scent is more pronounced in the evening [Hesperis matronalis, damask violet, sweet rocket]</p><p><b>(Babilonska) boginja zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Babylonian) earth goddess [Damkina]</p><p><b>daminozid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chemical sprayed on fruit trees to regulate their growth so the entire crop can be harvested at one time [Alar]</p><p><b>(Babilonska) boginja zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Babylonian) earth goddess [Damgalnunna]</p><p><b>Svaka od različitih tvrdih smola iz stabala iz obitelji Dipterocarpaceae i rodova Agathis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various hard resins from trees of the family Dipterocarpaceae and of the genus Agathis [damar, dammar resin, gum dammar]</p><p><b>bilo koje od različitih stabala rodova Agathis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various trees of the genus Agathis [kauri pine]</p><p><b>Svaka od različitih tvrdih smola iz stabala iz obitelji Dipterocarpaceae i rodova Agathis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various hard resins from trees of the family Dipterocarpaceae and of the genus Agathis [damar, dammar, gum dammar]</p><p><b>kletva, prokletstvo, proklinjati, psovati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something of little value [darn, hoot, red cent, shit, shucks, tinker's dam, tinker's damn]</p><p><i>v.</i> wish harm upon [anathemise, anathemize, bedamn, beshrew, curse, imprecate, maledict]</p><p><i>adj.</i> used as expletives [goddamn]</p><p><i>adj.</i> expletives used informally as intensifiers [blame, blamed, blasted, blessed, damned, darned, deuced, goddam, goddamn, goddamned, infernal]</p><p><i>adv.</i> extremely [all-fired, all-firedly, bloody]</p><p><b>Zaslužuje prokletstvo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deserving a curse [execrable]</p><p><b>Na prokleti način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a damnable manner [cursedly, damned]</p><p><b>Čin osude, stanje osuđivanja na vječnu kaznu u paklu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of damning</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being condemned to eternal punishment in Hell [eternal damnation]</p><p><b>prijeti prokletstvom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> threatening with damnation [damning]</p><p><b>proklet, prokleti, uklet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people who are condemned to eternal punishment</p><p><i>adj.</i> expletives used informally as intensifiers [blame, blamed, blasted, blessed, damn, darned, deuced, goddam, goddamn, goddamned, infernal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> in danger of the eternal punishment of Hell [cursed, doomed, unredeemed, unsaved]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a damnable manner [cursedly, damnably]</p><p><b>kletva, prokletstvo, proklinjati, psovati (od &quot;damn&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> threatening with damnation [damnatory]</p><p><b>Grčki sudar Dioniziju Starijem koji je (prema legendi) osuđen da sjedi ispod golega mača koji je obješen kosom kako bi mu pokazao da biti kralj nije sretno stanje koje je Damocles rekao da je (4-vi stoljeće prije Krista) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Greek courtier to Dionysius the Elder who (according to legend) was condemned to sit under a naked sword that was suspended by a hair in order to demonstrate to him that being a king was not the happy state Damocles had said it was (4th century BC)</p><p><b>Mlada neudana žena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a young unmarried woman [damosel, damozel, damsel, demoiselle]</p><p><b>Prijatelj Phintiasa koji je zakleo svoj život da će se Phintias vratiti (4. stoljeće prije Krista) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the friend of Phintias who pledged his life that Phintias would return (4th century BC)</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) prema grčkoj legendi: kada je Pitja osuđen na smrt Damon je zauzeo njegovo mjesto da bi Pitiju omogućio da svoje poslove postavi u red (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) according to a Greek legend: when Pythias was sentenced to be executed Damon took his place to allow Pythias to get his affairs in order</p><p><b>Američki pisac humorističkih stiliziranih priča o Broadwayu i podzemlju u New Yorku (1884-1946) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer of humorous stylized stories about Broadway and the New York underground (1884-1946) [Alfred Damon Runyon, Runyon]</p><p><b>Mlada neudana žena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a young unmarried woman [damoiselle, damozel, damsel, demoiselle]</p><p><b>od vrste moskovita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of muscovite</p><p><b>Mlada neudana žena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a young unmarried woman [damoiselle, damosel, damsel, demoiselle]</p><p><b>magla, maglovit, mokar, navlažiti, ohladiti, ovlažiti, prigušiti, smanjiti, ublažiti, učiniti nečitljivim, ugušiti, vlaga, vlažan, zamagliti, zatomiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slight wetness [dampness, moistness]</p><p><i>v.</i> deaden (a sound or noise), especially by wrapping [dampen, dull, muffle, mute, tone down]</p><p><i>v.</i> restrain or discourage</p><p><i>v.</i> make vague or obscure or make (an image) less visible [dampen, deaden]</p><p><i>v.</i> lessen in force or effect [break, dampen, soften, weaken]</p><p><i>adj.</i> slightly wet [dampish, moist]</p><p><b>Proces nekih nepropusnih materijala postavljen u temeljne zidove zgrade blizu zemlje kako bi se spriječilo da vlažnost raste u zgradu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a course of some impermeable material laid in the foundation walls of building near the ground to prevent dampness from rising into the building [damp-proof course]</p><p><b>Proces nekih nepropusnih materijala postavljen u temeljne zidove zgrade blizu zemlje kako bi se spriječilo da vlažnost raste u zgradu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a course of some impermeable material laid in the foundation walls of building near the ground to prevent dampness from rising into the building [damp course]</p><p><b>nakvasiti se, ovlažiti, prigušiti, navlažiti, nav