 to isolate elements sodium and potassium and barium and boron and calcium and magnesium and chlorine (1778-1829) [Humphrey Davy, Sir Humphrey Davy]</p><p><b>Američki graničar i političar iz Tennesseeja koji je umro u opsadi Alamoa (1786-1836) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States frontiersman and Tennessee politician who died at the siege of the Alamo (1786-1836) [Crockett, David Crockett]</p><p><b>duh mora, đavo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bottom of a sea or ocean [Davy Jones's locker, ocean bottom, ocean floor, sea bottom, sea floor, seabed]</p><p><b>dno mora ili oceana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bottom of a sea or ocean [Davy Jones, ocean bottom, ocean floor, sea bottom, sea floor, seabed]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom goriva od 0,15 mas.% ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mas.% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oil lamp that will not ignite flammable gases (methane) [safety lamp]</p><p><b>blago ljubičasta ili plavo-plavo tamno siva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slightly purplish or bluish dark grey [Davy's grey, iron blue, steel gray, steel grey]</p><p><b>blago ljubičasta ili plavo-plavo tamno siva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slightly purplish or bluish dark grey [Davy's gray, iron blue, steel gray, steel grey]</p><p><b>Humphry Davy (od &quot;davy&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English navigator who explored the Arctic while searching for the Northwest Passage (1550-1605) [Davis, John Davis, John Davys]</p><p><b>čavka, Corvus monedula</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common black-and-grey Eurasian bird noted for thievery [Corvus monedula, jackdaw]</p><p><b>misionarski rad za islam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> missionary work for Islam [da'wah]</p><p><b>besposličar, besposličariti, dangubiti, sporost, zaostajati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> take one's time [linger]</p><p><i>v.</i> waste time [dally]</p><p><i>v.</i> hang (back) or fall (behind) in movement, progress, development, etc. [fall back, fall behind, lag]</p><p><b>danguba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who takes more time than necessary [drone, laggard, lagger, poke, trailer]</p><p><b>besposličar, besposličariti, dangubiti, sporost (od &quot;dawdle&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the deliberate act of delaying and playing instead of working [dalliance, trifling]</p><p><b>čavka (od &quot;daw&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American patriot who rode with Paul Revere to warn that the British were advancing on Lexington and Concord (1745-1799) [William Dawes]</p><p><b>osvit, praskozorje, svanuti, svanjivati, svitanje, svitati, zora, daniti se, razdaniti se, razdanjivati se, zazoriti, zoriti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first light of day [aurora, break of day, break of the day, cockcrow, dawning, daybreak, dayspring, first light, morning, sunrise, sunup]</p><p><i>n.</i> the earliest period [morning]</p><p><i>n.</i> an opening time period</p><p><i>v.</i> become clear or enter one's consciousness or emotions [click, come home, fall into place, get across, get through, penetrate, sink in]</p><p><i>v.</i> appear or develop</p><p><i>v.</i> become light</p><p><b>najraniji konj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> earliest horse [eohippus]</p><p><b>veliko brzo rastuće kinesko jednojedno stablo s ravnim svijetlo zelenim listnim listovima i malim kugličnim čunjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large fast-growing Chinese monoecious tree having flat bright-green deciduous leaves and small globular cones [Metasequoia glyptostrodoides, metasequoia]</p><p><b>prvi počeci, svitanje, zora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first light of day [aurora, break of day, break of the day, cockcrow, dawn, daybreak, dayspring, first light, morning, sunrise, sunup]</p><p><b>grad na sjeverozapadu Kanade u Yukonu na rijeci Yukon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in northwestern Canada in the Yukon on the Yukon River</p><p><b>vrsta velikih riba koja se nalazi u australskim rijekama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a species of large fish found in Australian rivers [Australian arowana, Scleropages leichardti, saratoga, spotted barramundi, spotted bonytongue]</p><p><b>rijetka hronična progresivna encefalitis uzrokovana virusom ospica i uglavnom se javlja kod djece i mladih odraslih osoba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rare chronic progressive encephalitis caused by the measles virus and occurring primarily in children and young adults [Bosin's disease, SSPE, Van Bogaert encephalitis, inclusion body encephalitis, sclerosing leukoencephalitis, subacute inclusion body encephalitis, subacute sclerosing leukoencephalitis, subacute sclerosing panencephalitis]</p><p><b>dan, danji, dana, solarni dan, srednji sunčani dan, danje svjetlo, doba, era, sideralni dan, siderički dan, siderični dan, prilika, šansa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> time for Earth to make a complete rotation on its axis [24-hour interval, mean solar day, solar day, twenty-four hour period, twenty-four hours]</p><p><i>n.</i> some point or period in time</p><p><i>n.</i> a day assigned to a particular purpose or observance</p><p><i>n.</i> the time after sunrise and before sunset while it is light outside [daylight, daytime]</p><p><i>n.</i> the recurring hours when you are not sleeping (especially those when you are working)</p><p><i>n.</i> an era of existence or influence</p><p><i>n.</i> the period of time taken by a particular planet (e.g. Mars) to make a complete rotation on its axis</p><p><i>n.</i> the time for one complete rotation of the earth relative to a particular star, about 4 minutes shorter than a mean solar day [sidereal day]</p><p><i>n.</i> a period of opportunity</p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer best known for his autobiographical works (1874-1935) [Clarence Day, Clarence Shepard Day Jr.]</p><p><b>za neodređen broj uzastopnih dana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> for an indefinite number of successive days [day in day out]</p><p><b>nemogućnost jasnog gledanja u jakom svjetlu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inability to see clearly in bright light [hemeralopia]</p><p><b>učenik u internatu koji jede u školi, ali spava kod kuće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a schoolchild at a boarding school who has meals at school but sleeps at home</p><p><b>dnevni pisani zapis događaja (kao što su hapšenja) u policijskoj postaji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the daily written record of events (as arrests) in a police station [blotter, charge sheet, police blotter, rap sheet]</p><p><b>Postepeno i progresivno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> gradually and progressively [daily]</p><p><b>kamp koji pruža brigu i aktivnosti za djecu tijekom dana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a camp providing care and activities for children during the daytime</p><p><b>brigu o djeci tijekom dana dok roditelji rade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> childcare during the day while parents work [daycare]</p><p><b>dječji vrt za nadgledanje djece u predškolskoj dobi dok roditelji rade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nursery for the supervision of preschool children while the parents work [day nursery]</p><p><b>igra igra u danu svjetlu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a game played in daylight</p><p><b>bez odmora. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without respite [all the time]</p><p><b>za neodređen broj uzastopnih dana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> for an indefinite number of successive days [day after day]</p><p><b>Zapadni indijski zimzelena stabla s grmovima bijelih cvjetova u obliku lovora koji su mirisani po danu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> West Indian evergreen shrub having clusters of funnel-shaped white flowers that are fragrant by day [Cestrum diurnum]</p><p><b>nadničar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a laborer who works by the day [day labourer]</p><p><b>nadničar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a laborer who works by the day [day laborer]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih višegodišnjih biljaka s gomilom raskošnih širokih rebrastih listova i grmovima bijelih, plavih ili ljubičastih cvijeća, bilo koja od brojnih višegodišnjih biljaka s gomoljastim korijenima i dugim uskim lištima nalik listovima i obično žutim cvjetovima nalik lilijama koji cvjetaju samo jedan dan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous perennials having mounds of sumptuous broad ribbed leaves and clusters of white, blue, or lilac