s heart surgeon who in 1966 implanted the first artificial heart in a human patient (born in 1908) [Michael Ellis De Bakey]</p><p><b>Francuski nuklearni fizičar koji je generalizirao dualnost val-čestica predloženjem da čestice materije pokazuju valovita svojstva (1892-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French nuclear physicist who generalized the wave-particle duality by proposing that particles of matter exhibit wavelike properties (1892-1987) [Broglie, Louis Victor de Broglie]</p><p><b>de facto, doista, stvaran, zaista, zapravo</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing in fact whether with lawful authority or not</p><p><i>adv.</i> in reality or fact</p><p><b>segregacija (posebno u školama) koja se zapravo događa iako nije propisana zakonom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> segregation (especially in schools) that happens in fact although not required by law</p><p><b>Američki elektroinženjer koji je 1907. patentirao prvu triodnu vakuumsku cijev koja je omogućila otkrivanje i pojačavanje radio valova (1873-1961) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States electrical engineer who in 1907 patented the first triode vacuum tube, which made it possible to detect and amplify radio waves (1873-1961) [Father of Radio, Lee De Forest]</p><p><b>Charles de Gaulle</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French general and statesman who became very popular during World War II as the leader of the Free French forces in exile (1890-1970) [Charles Andre Joseph Marie de Gaulle, Charles de Gaulle, General Charles de Gaulle, General de Gaulle]</p><p><b>pravni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> by right</p><p><i>adv.</i> by law [lawfully, legally]</p><p><b>odvojenost koja je nametnuta zakonom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> segregation that is imposed by law</p><p><b>Američki slikar (rođen u Nizozemskoj) koji je bio vodeći američki predstavnik apstraktnog ekspresionizma (1904-1997) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States painter (born in the Netherlands) who was a leading American exponent of abstract expressionism (1904-1997) [Willem de Kooning]</p><p><