lo to those who sought advice [Oracle of Apollo, Temple of Apollo, oracle of Delphi]</p><p><b>beluga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white whale [genus Delphinapterus]</p><p><b>beluga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small northern whale that is white when adult [beluga, white whale]</p><p><b>oceanski dupini, porodica Delphinidae, porodica oceanskih dupina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dolphins [family Delphinidae]</p><p><b>biljka iz roda Delphinium s palmatno podijeljenim lišcima i navidnim šiljakama različitih boja izbojenih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Delphinium having palmately divided leaves and showy spikes of variously colored spurred flowers</p><p><b>uobičajena biljka u južnoj Europi s neogranatim šiljakim cvjetovima plavih ili ponekad ljubičastih ili ružičastih cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commonly cultivated larkspur of southern Europe having unbranched spikelike racemes of blue or sometimes purplish or pinkish flowers [Consolida ambigua, rocket larkspur]</p><p><b>Dupin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a constellation in the northern hemisphere near Pegasus and Aquila</p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Delphinidae [genus Delphinus]</p><p><b>crno-bijeli delfin koji skače visoko iz vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> black-and-white dolphin that leaps high out of the water [common dolphin]</p><p><b>delta, delta (grčki), ušće, ušće (rijeke)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a low triangular area of alluvial deposits where a river divides before entering a larger body of water</p><p><i>n.</i> an object shaped like an equilateral triangle</p><p><i>n.</i> the 4th letter of the Greek alphabet</p><p><b>ozbiljan oblik hepatitisa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a severe form of hepatitis [hepatitis delta]</p><p><b>alotropi željeza koji su stabilni između 1403 stupnjeva Celzijusa i točke topljenja (= 1532 stupnjeva) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an allotrope of iron that is stable between 1403 degrees centigrade and the melting point (= 1532 degrees)</p><p><b>elektroni izbacivani iz materije ionizirajućim zračenjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electron ejected from matter by ionizing radiation</p><p><b>normalni moždani valovi u encefalogramu osobe u dubokom snu bez snova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the normal brainwave in the encephalogram of a person in deep dreamless sleep [delta wave]</p><p><b>normalni moždani valovi u encefalogramu osobe u dubokom snu bez snova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the normal brainwave in the encephalogram of a person in deep dreamless sleep [delta rhythm]</p><p><b>zrakoplov s krilima koji mu daju izgled jednakokosa trokut (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an airplane with wings that give it the appearance of an isosceles triangle</p><p><b>dehidrogenizirani analog kortizola (trgovinski nazivi Orasone ili Deltasone ili Liquid Pred ili Meticorten) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dehydrogenated analogue of cortisol (trade names Orasone or Deltasone or Liquid Pred or Meticorten) [Liquid Pred, Meticorten, Orasone, prednisone]</p><p><b>deltoidni mišić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large triangular muscle covering the shoulder joint and serving to abduct and flex and extend and rotate the arm [deltoid muscle, musculus deltoideus]</p><p><i>adj.</i> triangular or suggesting a capital delta, with a point at the apex</p><p><b>udarac na vanjskoj strani ramena gdje se deltoidni mišić veže (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bump on the outside of the humerus where the deltoid muscle attaches [deltoid tuberosity]</p><p><b>Jednostavan list u obliku glavne delte. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a simple leaf shaped like a capital delta</p><p><b>veliki trokutasti mišić koji pokriva zglob ramena i služi za otvaranje i savijanje i proširenje i okretanje ruke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large triangular muscle covering the shoulder joint and serving to abduct and flex and extend and rotate the arm [deltoid, musculus deltoideus]</p><p><b>udarac na vanjskoj strani ramena gdje se deltoidni mišić veže (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bump on the outside of the humerus where the deltoid muscle attaches [deltoid eminence]</p><p><b>obmanuti, varati, zavesti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be false to [cozen, deceive, lead on]</p><p><b>potop, potopiti, pljusak, poplava, zatrpati, navodnjavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an overwhelming number or amount [flood, inundation, torrent]</p><p><i>n.</i> a heavy rain [cloudburst, downpour, pelter, soaker, torrent, waterspout]</p><p><i>n.</i> the rising of a body of water and its overflowing onto normally dry land [alluvion, flood, inundation]</p><p><i>v.</i> fill quickly beyond capacity [flood, inundate, swamp]</p><p><i>v.</i> charge someone with too many tasks [flood out, overwhelm]</p><p><i>v.</i> fill or cover completely, usually with water [inundate, submerge]</p><p><b>iluzija, obmana, prijevara, zabluda, zablude</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) an erroneous belief that is held in the face of evidence to the contrary [psychotic belief]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mistaken or unfounded opinion or idea [hallucination]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of deluding [head game, illusion]</p><p><b>koji pate od ili su karakterizirani zabludavanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suffering from or characterized by delusions</p><p><b>bilo koji mentalni poremećaj u kojem halucinacije igraju značajnu ulogu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any mental disorder in which delusions play a significant role</p><p><b>iluzija (česta u paranoji) da ste mnogo veći i moćniji i utjecajniji nego što ste zapravo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a delusion (common in paranoia) that you are much greater and more powerful and influential than you really are</p><p><b>iluzija (česta u paranoji) da vas drugi žele dobiti i frustrirati i osramotiti ili vam naneti patnju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a delusion (common in paranoia) that others are out to get you and frustrate and embarrass you or inflict suffering on you</p><p><b>ne odgovara stvarnosti ili činjenicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inappropriate to reality or facts [false]</p><p><b>na lažan i nerealan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a deceptive and unrealistic manner</p><