kom (a) ovog članka, država članica može odrediti da se u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> act of changing from a war basis to a peace basis including disbanding or discharging troops [demobilization]</p><p><b>demobilizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> release from military service or remove from the active list of military service [demobilize, inactivate]</p><p><i>v.</i> retire from military service [demob, demobilize]</p><p><b>demobilizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> act of changing from a war basis to a peace basis including disbanding or discharging troops [demobilisation]</p><p><b>demobilizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> release from military service or remove from the active list of military service [demobilise, inactivate]</p><p><i>v.</i> retire from military service [demob, demobilise]</p><p><b>demokracija, demokracija., demokracije, demokraciju, demokratsko načelo, demokratija, republika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the political orientation of those who favor government by the people or by their elected representatives</p><p><i>n.</i> a political system in which the supreme power lies in a body of citizens who can elect people to represent them [commonwealth, republic]</p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine that the numerical majority of an organized group can make decisions binding on the whole group [majority rule]</p><p><b>demokrat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Democratic Party</p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of democratic principles</p><p><b>demokratski, demokratskim, demokratsku, demokratska, demokratske</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by or advocating or based upon the principles of democracy or social equality</p><p><i>adj.</i> belong to or relating to the Democratic Party</p><p><i>adj.</i> representing or appealing to or adapted for the benefit of the people at large [popular]</p><p><b>Republika u sjeverozapadnoj Africi na Sredozemnom moru s stanovništvom koji je pretežno sunitski muslimani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic in northwestern Africa on the Mediterranean Sea with a population that is predominantly Sunni Muslim [Algeria, Algerie]</p><p><b>Marxisticko-leninistička grupa koja vjeruje da palestinski ciljevi mogu biti postignuti samo revolucionarnim promjenama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Marxist-Leninist group that believes Palestinian goals can only be achieved by revolutionary change [DFLP, PDFLP, Popular Democratic Front for the Liberation of Palestine]</p><p><b>demokratska stranka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the older of two major political parties in the United States</p><p><b>Demokratska Narodna Republika Koreja, Demokratska NarodnaRepublika Koreja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a communist country in the northern half of the Korean Peninsula [D.P.R.K., DPRK, North Korea]</p><p><b>Demokratska Republika Sveti Toma i Prinsipe</b></p><p><i>n.</i> island nation in the South Atlantic off the west coast of Africa [Sao Thome e Principe, Sao Tome and Principe, Sao Tome e Principe, St. Thomas and Principe]</p><p><b>Demokratska Republika Kongo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic in central Africa [Belgian Congo, Congo, Zaire]</p><p><b>Demokratska Socijalistička Republika Šri Lanka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic on the island of Ceylon [Ceylon, Sri Lanka]</p><p><b>bivša velika politička stranka u Sjedinjenim Državama početkom 19. stoljeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former major political party in the United States in the early 19th century</p><p><b>na demokratski način (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a democratic manner</p><p><b>demokratizacija, demokratizaciji, demokratizacijom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the action of making something democratic [democratization]</p><p><b>postati (više) demokratski, uvesti demokratske reforme (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become (more) democratic [democratize]</p><p><i>v.</i> introduce democratic reforms [democratize]</p><p><b>demokratizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the action of making something democratic [democratisation]</p><p><b>demokratizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become (more) democratic [democratise]</p><p><i>v.</i> introduce democratic reforms [democratise]</p><p><b>Demokrit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek philosopher who developed an atomistic theory of matter (460-370 BC)</p><p><b>antički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> out of fashion [antique, ex, old-fashioned, old-hat, outmoded, passe, passee]</p><p><b>izvaditi informacije iz moduliranog nosioca valova (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> extract information from a modulated carrier wave</p><p><b>demodulacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (electronics) the reception of a signal by extracting it from the carrier wave</p><p><b>demodulator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rectifier that extracts modulation from a radio carrier wave [detector]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) misteriozno i zastrašujuće božanstvo podzemlja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) a mysterious and terrifying deity of the underworld</p><p><b>demograf</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scientist who studies the growth and density of populations and their vital statistics [demographist, population scientist]</p><p><b>demografski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statistic characterizing human populations (or segments of human populations broken down by age or sex or income etc.)</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to demography</p><p><b>znanstvenik koji proučava rast i gustoću populacije i njihove vitalne statistike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scientist who studies the growth and density of populations and their vital statistics [demographer, population scientist]</p><p><b>demografija, demografski podaci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of sociology that studies the characteristics of human populations [human ecology]</p><p><b>Mlada neudana žena., male svijetle boje tropske morske ribe koralnih grebena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a young unmarried woman [damoiselle, damosel, damozel, damsel]</p><p><i>n.</i> small brilliantly colored tropical marine fishes of coral reefs [damselfish]</p><p><b>demolirati, porušiti, razoriti, razrušiti, rušiti, slupati, sravniti, uništiti, razarati, uništavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> destroy completely [pulverise, pulverize]</p><p><i>v.</i> ruin or destroy</p><p><i>v.</i> eat up completely, as with great appetite [consume, devour, down, go through]</p><p><i>v.</i> defeat soundly and humiliatingly [destroy]</p><p><b>srušen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> torn down and broken up [dismantled, razed]</p><p><b>demolirati, porušiti, razoriti, razrušiti, rušiti, slupati, sravniti, uništiti (od &quot;demolish&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> complete destruction of a building [leveling, razing, tearing down]</p><p><b>rušenje, demolicija, destrukcija, propast, razaranje, uništenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event (or the result of an event) that completely destroys something [destruction, wipeout]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of demolishing</p><p><b>demon, đavo, zloduh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an evil supernatural being [daemon, daimon, devil, fiend]</p><p><i>n.</i> a cruel wicked and inhuman person [devil, fiend, monster, ogre]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone extremely diligent or skillful</p><p><b>Kao da su ga opsednuli demoni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> as if possessed by demons</p><p><b>završava nešto (npr. zlato ili srebro) kao više nije zakonsko sredstvo plaćanja zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ending something (e.g. gold or silver) as no longer the legal tender of a country [demonetization]</p><p><b>oduzima vrijednost za plaćanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> deprive of value for payment [demonetize]</p><p><b>demonetizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ending something (e.g. gold or silver) as no longer the legal tender of a country [demonetisation]</p><p><b>oduzima vrijednost za plaćanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> deprive of value for payment [demonetise]</p><p><b>netko tko se ponaša kao da ga posjeduje demon., od, koji se odnosi na, ili kao demon ili posjedovanje od strane demona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who acts as if possessed by a demon</p><p><i>adj.</i> of, pertaining to, or like a demon or possession by a demon [demoniacal, possessed]</p><p><b>od, koji se odnosi na, ili kao demon ili posjedovanje od strane demona (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of, pertaining to, or like a demon or possession by a demon [demoniac, possessed]</p><p><b>Na vrlo uznemiren način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a very agitated manner [frenetically]</p><p><b>demon, đavo, zloduh (od &quot;demon&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> extremely evil or cruel [diabolic, diabolical, fiendish, hellish, infernal, satanic, unholy]</p><p><b>da predstavlja kao đavolski zlo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> to represent as diabolically evil [demonization]</p><p><b>demonizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make into a demon [demonize]</p><p><b>demonizam, sotonizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a belief in and reverence for devils (especially Satan) [Satanism, diabolism]</p><p><b>da predstavlja kao đavolski zlo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> to represent as diabolically evil [demonisation]</p><p><b>demonizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make into a demon [demonise]</p><p><b>Činjenice ili obrede obožavanja đavola (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the acts or rites of worshiping devils [devil-worship, diabolatry]</p><p><b>sposobnost da se dokaže ili logički dokaže (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capability of being demonstrated or logically proved [provability]</p><p><b>dokaziv, koji se može dokazati</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> necessarily or demonstrably true [incontrovertible]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being demonstrated or proved [provable]</p><p><b>dokazivo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an obvious and provable manner [incontrovertibly, provably]</p><p><b>demonstrirati, dokazati, dokazivati, ilustrirati, iskazivati, podnijeti dokaze, pokazati, pokazivati, predočiti, prikazati, pružiti dokaze, izlagati, izložiti, predočavati, predstaviti, predstavljati, prezentirati, prikazivati, utvrditi, utvrđivati, posvjedočiti, svjedočiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give an exhibition of to an interested audience [demo, exhibit, present, show]</p><p><i>v.</i> establish the validity of something, as by an example, explanation or experiment [establish, prove, shew, show]</p><p><i>v.</i> provide evidence for [attest, certify, evidence, manifest]</p><p><i>v.</i> march in protest [march]</p><p><b>predočen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having been demonstrated or verified beyond doubt</p><p><b>demonstracija, izlaganje, javno prikazivanje, pokazivanje, prikaz, prikazivanje, proba, prosvjed, predstavljanje, prezentacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a show or display [presentation, presentment]</p><p><i>n.</i> a show of military force or preparedness</p><p><i>n.</i> a public display of group feelings (usually of a political nature) [manifestation]</p><p><i>n.</i> proof by a process of argument or a series of proposition proving an asserted conclusion [monstrance]</p><p><i>n.</i> a visual presentation showing how something works [demo]</p><p><b>demonstrativan, dokazni, pokazni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pronoun that points out an intended referent [demonstrative pronoun]</p><p><i>adj.</i> given to or marked by the open expression of emotion</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to demonstrate [illustrative]</p><p><b>služi za dokazivanje ili demonstraciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to prove or demonstrate</p><p><b>zamjenik koji ukazuje na namjenski referent (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pronoun that points out an intended referent [demonstrative]</p><p><b>demonstrativan, dokazni, pokazni (od &quot;demonstrative&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a demonstrative manner</p><p><b>demonstrativan, dokazni, pokazni (od &quot;demonstrative&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tending to express your feelings freely</p><p><b>demonstrant, tumač, prosvjednik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a teacher or teacher's assistant who demonstrates the principles that are being taught</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who demonstrates an article to a prospective buyer [sales demonstrator]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who participates in a public display of group feeling [protester]</p><p><b>demoralizacija, demoraliziranost, malodušnost, obeshrabrenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of disorder and confusion [demoralization]</p><p><i>n.</i> depressio