culate, count, look, reckon, rely, swear]</p><p><b>ovisiti o, ovisiti o nečemu</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be contingent on [depend upon, devolve on, hinge on, hinge upon, ride, turn on]</p><p><i>v.</i> put trust in with confidence [depend upon, rely on, rely upon]</p><p><i>v.</i> be dependent on, as for support or maintenance [rely on]</p><p><b>biti ovisno o, Dajte povjerenje u povjerenje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be contingent on [depend on, devolve on, hinge on, hinge upon, ride, turn on]</p><p><i>v.</i> put trust in with confidence [depend on, rely on, rely upon]</p><p><b>pouzdanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being dependable or reliable [dependableness, reliability, reliableness]</p><p><b>pouzdan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of reliance or trust [reliable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of being depended on [honest, reliable, true]</p><p><i>adj.</i> consistent in performance or behavior [rock-steady, steady-going]</p><p><i>adj.</i> financially safe [good, safe, secure]</p><p><b>pouzdanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being dependable or reliable [dependability, reliability, reliableness]</p><p><b>Na vjeran način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a faithful manner [faithfully, reliably]</p><p><b>ovisnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> being abnormally tolerant to and dependent on something that is psychologically or physically habit-forming (especially alcohol or narcotic drugs) [addiction, dependence, dependency, habituation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of relying on or being controlled by someone or something else [dependence, dependency]</p><p><b>član obitelji, ovisi, ovisiti, uzdržavana osoba, uzdržavani član obitelji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who relies on another person for support (especially financial support) [dependent]</p><p><i>adj.</i> contingent on something else [dependent, qualified]</p><p><i>adj.</i> addicted to a drug [dependent, drug-addicted, hooked, strung-out]</p><p><b>određene uvjetima ili okolnostima koje slijede: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being deter