of an asset due to obsolescence or use [wear and tear]</p><p><i>n.</i> a communication that belittles somebody or something [derogation, disparagement]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u slučaju da se primjenjuje članak 3. točka (b) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an allowance for loss due to depreciation</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ili (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 4. točkom (c) ovog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an amount periodically charged to expense or against revenue in compensation for depreciation of property</p><p><b>stopa smanjenja vrijednosti nekretnine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the rate at which the value of property is reduced [rate of depreciation]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje ovaj članak, u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje ovaj članak, to znači da se ne primjenjuje ovaj članak., koji imaju tendenciju smanjivanja ili ponižavanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to decrease or cause a decrease in value [depreciating, depreciatory]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to diminish or disparage [belittling, deprecating, deprecative, deprecatory, depreciatory, slighting]</p><p><b>onaj koji ponižava ili umanjuje vrijednost nečega. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who disparages or belittles the worth of something [detractor, disparager, knocker]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje ovaj članak, u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje ovaj članak, to znači da se ne primjenjuje ovaj članak., koji imaju tendenciju smanjivanja ili ponižavanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to decrease or cause a decrease in value [depreciating, depreciative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to diminish or disparage [belittling, deprecating, deprecative, deprecatory, depreciative, slighting]</p><p><b>pljačka, pustošenje, razaranje, zulum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an act of plundering and pillaging and marauding [predation]</p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) a destructive action [ravage]</p><p><b>deprimirati, pritisnuti, sniziti, tlačiti, ugnjetavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> lower someone's spirits [cast down, deject, demoralise, demoralize, dismay, dispirit, get down]</p><p><i>v.</i> lower (prices or markets)</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to drop or sink [lower]</p><p><i>v.</i> press down [press down]</p><p><i>v.</i> lessen the activity or force of</p><p><b>sedativan, stišavajući, ublažujući, umanjujući, umirujući, sedativ, sredstvo za smirenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that reduces excitability and calms a person [downer, sedative, sedative drug]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of depressing physiological or psychological activity or response by a chemical agent</p><p><b>depresivan, depresivno, deprimiran, neraspoložen, utučen, potišten, snužden</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lower than previously [down]</p><p><i>adj.</i> flattened downward as if pressed from above or flattened along the dorsal and ventral surfaces</p><p><i>adj.</i> filled with melancholy and despondency [blue, dispirited, down, down in the mouth, downcast, downhearted, gloomy, grim, low, low-spirited]</p><p><b>fraktura lubanje gdje je kost gurnuta unutra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fracture of the skull where the bone is pushed in</p><p><b>deprimantan, koji deprimira, koji tišti, spuštajući</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing sad feelings of gloom and inadequacy [cheerless, uncheerful]</p><p><b>deprimantan, koji deprimira, koji tišti, spuštajući (od &quot;depressing&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a depressing manner or to a depressing degree</p><p><b>deperesija, depresija, depresivnost, podtlak, gospodarska kriza, kriza, recesija, potonina, prirodna depresija, udolina, uleknina, uleknuće, potištenost, utučenost, klinička depresija, otisak, udubina, udubljenje, ulegnuće, utisak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mental state characterized by a pessimistic sense of inadequacy and a despondent lack of activity</p><p><i>n.</i> a long-term economic state characterized by unemployment and low prices and low levels of trade and investment [economic crisis, slump]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sunken or depressed geological formation [natural depression]</p><p><i>n.</i> sad feelings of gloom and inadequacy</p><p><i>n.</i> a period during the 1930s when there was a worldwide economic depression and mass unemployment [Great Depression]</p><p><i>n.</i> an air mass of lower pressure [low]</p><p><i>n.</i> a state of depression and anhedonia so severe as to require clinical intervention [clinical depression, depressive disorder]</p><p><i>n.</i> a concavity in a surface produced by pressing [impression, imprint]</p><p><i>n.</i> angular distance below the horizon (especially of a celestial object)</p><p><i>n.</i> pushing down</p><p><b>depresivan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone suffering psychological depression</p><p><b>depresija, klinička depresija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of depression and anhedonia so severe as to require clinical intervention [clinical depression, depression]</p><p><b>bilo koji skeletni mišić koji vuče dio tijela prema dolje, svaki živc čija aktivnost ima tendenciju da smanji aktivnost ili tonus tijela kojem služi., uređaj koji liječnik koristi za pritisak dijela dolje ili na stranu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any skeletal muscle that draws a body part down [depressor muscle]</p><p><i>n.</i> any nerve whose activity tends to reduce the activity or tone of the body part it serves [depressor nerve]</p><p><i>n.</i> a device used by physician to press a part down or aside</p><p><b>bilo koji skeletni mišić koji vuče dio tijela prema dolje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any skeletal muscle that draws a body part down [depressor]</p><p><b>svaki živc čija aktivnost ima tendenciju da smanji aktivnost ili tonus tijela kojem služi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any nerve whose activity tends to reduce the activity or tone of the body part it serves [depressor]</p><p><b>otpustiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> decrease the pressure of [decompress, depressurize]</p><p><b>otpustiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> decrease the pressure of [decompress, depressurise]</p><p><b>gubitak, lišavanje, lišenje, otpuštanje, bijeda, neimaština, oskudica, siromaština, siromaštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of extreme poverty [neediness, privation, want]</p><p><i>n.</i> the disadvantage that results from losing something [loss]</p><p><i>n.</i> act of depriving someone of food or money or rights [privation]</p><p><b>lišiti, oduzeti, uskratiti, lišavati, oduzimati, opljačkati, pljačkati, uskraćivati, ustegnuti, ustezati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> take away possessions from someone [divest, strip]</p><p><i>v.</i> keep from having, keeping, or obtaining</p><p><i>v.</i> take away [impoverish]</p><p><b>lišen, oduzet, oduzete</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by deprivation especially of the necessities of life or healthful environmental influences [disadvantaged]</p><p><b>bezdan, dubina, dubina glasa, dubine, širina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the extent downward or backward or inward [deepness]</p><p><i>n.</i> degree of psychological or intellectual profundity</p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) a low moral state</p><p><i>n.</i> the intellectual ability to penetrate deeply into ideas [astuteness, deepness, profoundness, profundity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the attribute or quality of being deep, strong, or intense</p><p><b>bomba koja eksplodira na unaprijed postavljenoj dubini ispod vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb that explodes at a preset depth under water [depth charge]</p><p><b>bomba koja eksplodira na unaprijed postavljenoj dubini ispod vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb that explodes at a preset depth under water [depth bomb]</p><p><b>navigacijski instrument koji se koristi za mjerenje dubine vodnog tijela (kao što je ultrazvuk ili radar) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> navigational instrument used to measure the depth of a body of water (as by ultrasound or radar)</p><p><b>skup tehnika za istraživanje osnovnih motiva i metoda liječenja različitih mentalnih poremećaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a set of techniques for exploring underlying motives and a method of treating various mental disorders [analysis, psychoanalysis]</p><p><b>dubine, bezdana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (plural) the deepest and most remote part</p><p><b>delegacija, izaslanstvo, poslanstvo, delegiranje, dodjela dužnosti, dodjela ovlasti, ovlaštenje, ovlašćivanje, prenošenje ovlasti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of representatives or delegates [commission, delegacy, delegation, mission]</p><p><i>n.</i> authorizing subordinates to make certain decisions [delegating, delegation, relegating, relegation]</p><p><b>dati punomoćje, delegirati, izaslati, imenovati, izabirati, izabrati, naimenovati, odaslati, odašiljati, odrediti, određivati, opunomoćiti, opunomoćivati, ovlastiti, ovlašćivati, postaviti, postavljati, slati, zadužiti, zaduživati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> transfer power to someone [delegate]</p><p><i>v.</i> appoint as a substitute [deputise, deputize]</p><p><i>v.</i> give an assignment to (a person) to a post, or assign a task to (a person) [assign, delegate, designate]</p><p><b>djelovati kao zamjena, imenovati zamjenika (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> act as a substitute [deputize, step in, substitute]</p><p><i>v.</i> appoint as a substitute [depute, deputize]</p><p><b>delegirati, zamjenjivati, zastupati nekog</b></p><p><i>v.</i> act as a substitute [deputise, step in, substitute]</p><p><i>v.</i> appoint as a substitute [depute, deputise]</p><p><b>član izaslanstva, izaslanik, namjesnik, pomoćnik, predstavnik, zamjenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone authorized to exercise the powers of sheriff in emergencies [deputy sheriff]</p><p><i>n.</i> an assistant with power to act when his superior is absent [lieutenant]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the lower chamber of a legislative assembly (such as in France)</p><p><i>n.</i> a person appointed to represent or act on behalf of others [surrogate]</p><p><b>netko ovlašten za ostvarivanje ovlasti šerifa u hitnim slučajevima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone authorized to exercise the powers of sheriff in emergencies [deputy]</p><p><b>Führer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German Nazi dictator during World War II (1889-1945) [Adolf Hitler, Hitler]</p><p><b>iskorijeniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> move (people) forcibly from their homeland into a new and foreign environment [uproot]</p><p><i>v.</i> pull up by or as if by the roots [extirpate, root out, uproot]</p><p><b>da se nešto pomakne iz prirodnog okruženja., Čin povlačenja ili izlaženja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> to move something from its natural environment [displacement]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of pulling up or out [excision, extirpation]</p><p><b>iskočiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to run off the tracks</p><p><i>v.</i> run off or leave the rails [jump]</p><p><b>Nesreća u kojoj vlak izlazi s pruge. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an accident in which a train runs off its track</p><p><b>Francuski slikar i predstavnik fauvizma (1880-1954) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French painter and exponent of fauvism (1880-1954) [Andre Derain]</p><p><b>pobrkati, poremetiti, praviti nered, remetiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> derange mentally, throw out of mental balance [unbalance]</p><p><i>v.</i> throw into great confusion or disorder [perturb, throw out of kilter]</p><p><b>lud, pomaknut</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> driven insane [crazed, half-crazed]</p><p><b>poremećenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of mental disturbance and disorientation [mental unsoundness, unbalance]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of disturbing the mind or body [overthrow, upset]</p><p><b>transformirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> lower the rated electrical capability of electrical apparatus</p><p><b>derbi, konjske trk, konjske trke, halbcilindar, polucilindar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a felt hat that is round and hard with 