><i>v.</i> treat or speak of with contempt</p><p><b>ismijavanje, ruganje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> contemptuous laughter</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of deriding or treating with contempt [ridicule]</p><p><b>podrugljiv, podsmješljiv, posredan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> abusing vocally [gibelike, jeering, mocking, taunting]</p><p><b>podrugljiv, podsmješljiv, posredan (od &quot;derisive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a disrespectful and mocking manner [derisorily, mockingly, scoffingly]</p><p><b>na nepoštovan i ismijavajući način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a disrespectful and mocking manner [derisively, mockingly, scoffingly]</p><p><b>Tako nerazumno da pozove na ismijavanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> so unreasonable as to invite derision [absurd, cockeyed, idiotic, laughable, ludicrous, nonsensical, preposterous, ridiculous]</p><p><b>koji se može dobiti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being derived</p><p><b>derivacija, izvođenje, izvor, otkrivanje, početak, porijeklo, podrijetlo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the source or origin from which something derives (i.e. comes or issues)</p><p><i>n.</i> (historical linguistics) an explanation of the historical origins of a word or phrase [deriving, etymologizing]</p><p><i>n.</i> a line of reasoning that shows how a conclusion follows logically from accepted propositions</p><p><i>n.</i> (descriptive linguistics) the process whereby new words are formed from existing words or bases by affixation</p><p><i>n.</i> inherited properties shared with others of your bloodline [ancestry, filiation, lineage]</p><p><i>n.</i> drawing of fluid or inflammation away from a diseased part of the body</p><p><i>n.</i> drawing off water from its main channel as for irrigation</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of deriving something or obtaining something from a source or origin</p><p><b>karakteriziraju ga uplicaji koji ukazuju na semantički odnos između riječi i njene baze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by inflections indicating a semantic relation between a word and its base</p><p><b>derivacija, derivacijska morfologija, tvorba riječi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of grammar that deals with the derivations of words</p><p><b>derivacija, derivat, derivativ, deriviran, izveden, izvedena riječ, izvedenica, izvedenice, prerađevina, tvorenica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the result of mathematical differentiation [derived function, differential, differential coefficient, first derivative]</p><p><i>n.</i> a compound obtained from, or regarded as derived from, another compound</p><p><i>n.</i> a financial instrument whose value is based on another security [derivative instrument]</p><p><i>n.</i> (linguistics) a word that is derived from another word</p><p><i>adj.</i> resulting from or employing derivation</p><p><b>Financijski instrument čija je vrijednost temeljena na drugom vrijednosnom papiru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a financial instrument whose value is based on another security [derivative]</p><p><b>derivirati, izvesti, izvlačiti, izvoditi, izvući, potjecati, proistjecati, proizlaze, proizlaziti, dobiti, dobivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> reason by deduction [deduce, deduct, infer]</p><p><i>v.</i> obtain [gain]</p><p><i>v.</i> come from</p><p><i>v.</i> develop or evolve from a latent or potential state [educe]</p><p><i>v.</i> come from [come, descend]</p><p><b>izveden, izvedeno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> formed or developed from something else</p><p><b>rezultat matematičke diferencijacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the result of mathematical differentiation [derivative, differential, differential coefficient, first derivative]</p><p><b>izvođenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (historical linguistics) an explanation of the historical origins of a word or phrase [derivation, etymologizing]</p><p><b>duboki unutarnji sloj kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the deep vascular inner layer of the skin [corium, dermis]</p><p><b>uklanjanje ožiljaka ili tetovaža anestezijom površine kože te zatim brusenje ili skidanje neke od vanjskog sloja kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> removal of scars or tattoos by anesthetizing the skin surface and then sanding or scraping off some of the outer skin layer</p><p><b>Prenositelji važnih bolesti ljudi i životinja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vectors of important diseases of man and animals [genus Dermacentor]</p><p><b>uobičajena krpelja koja može preneti Rocky Mountain spotted fever i tularemiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common tick that can transmit Rocky Mountain spotted fever and tularemia [American dog tick, wood tick]</p><p><b>dermalan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a cuticle or cuticula [cuticular, epidermal, epidermic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or located in the dermis [dermic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or existing on or affecting the skin [cutaneal, cutaneous]</p><p><b>red Dermaptera, red uholaža, uholaže</b></p><p><i>n.</i> earwigs and a few related forms [order Dermaptera]</p><p><b>dermatitis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the skin</p><p><b>larve žive ispod kože domaćih sisavaca i ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> larvae live under the skin of domestic mammals and humans [genus Dermatobia]</p><p><b>velika tropska američka muha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large tropical American fly [human botfly]</p><p><b>linije koje formiraju uzorke na koži (posebno na vrhovima prstiju i dlanova ruku i podnožja stopala) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lines that form patterns on the skin (especially on the fingertips and the palms of the hands and the soles of the feet)</p><p><b>proučavanje spirala i petlja i lukova na vrhovima prstiju i na dlanovima i podnožju stopala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of the whorls and loops and arches in the fingertips and on the palms of the hand and the soles of the feet</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili praktikuju dermatologiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or practicing dermatology [dermatological]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili praktikuju dermatologiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or practicing dermatology [dermatologic]</p><p><b>