etanje, spuštanje, podrijetlo, spust, kosina, krivina, nagib, nizbrdica, loza, obitelj, porod, rod, soj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a movement downward</p><p><i>n.</i> properties attributable to your ancestry [extraction, origin]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of changing your location in a downward direction</p><p><i>n.</i> the kinship relation between an individual and the individual's progenitors [filiation, line of descent, lineage]</p><p><i>n.</i> a downward slope or bend [declension, declination, decline, declivity, downslope, fall]</p><p><i>n.</i> the descendants of one individual [ancestry, blood, blood line, bloodline, line, line of descent, lineage, origin, parentage, pedigree, stemma, stock]</p><p><b>koji se može opisati (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being described</p><p><b>opisati, opisivanje, opisivati, označiti, spomenuti, ocrtati, ocrtavati, prikazati, prikazivati, izvijestiti, izvještavati, crtati, iscrtati, išarati, označavati, determinirati, identificirati, imenovati, odrediti, određivati, otkriti, otkrivati, raspoznavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give a description of [depict, draw]</p><p><i>v.</i> to give an account or representation of in words [account, report]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a mark or lines on a surface [delineate, draw, line, trace]</p><p><i>v.</i> identify as in botany or biology, for example [discover, distinguish, identify, key, key out, name]</p><p><b>iskazan, opisan, opisanim, opisuju, opisana, opisani, opisuje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> represented in words especially with sharpness and detail</p><p><b>opis, opis 35, opis programskog elementa, opisivanje, opisom, prikaz, verbalni opis, deskripcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statement that represents something in words [verbal description]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of describing something</p><p><i>n.</i> sort or variety</p><p><b>deskriptivna, očigledan, opisan, pregledan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to describe or inform or characterized by description</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an approach to linguistic analysis that aims at the description of a language's forms, structures and usage</p><p><b>opisni pridjev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an adjective that ascribes to its noun the value of an attribute of that noun (e.g., `a nervous person' or `a musical speaking voice') [qualifying adjective]</p><p><b>etnografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of anthropology that provides scientific description of individual human societies [ethnography]</p><p><b>podređeni stav koji ne ograničava ili ograničava značenje samostalne fraze koju mijenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a subordinate clause that does not limit or restrict the meaning of the noun phrase it modifies [nonrestrictive clause]</p><p><b>Geometrija svojstava koja ostaju nepromenljiva pod projekcijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the geometry of properties that remain invariant under projection [projective geometry]</p><p><b>gramatika koja je proizvedena opisnom lingvistikom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a grammar that is produced by descriptive linguistics</p><p><b>deskriptivna lingvistika, sinkronijska lingvistika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a description (at a given point in time) of a language with respect to its phonology and morphology and syntax and semantics without value judgments</p><p><b>deskriptivna, očigledan, opisan, pregledan (od &quot;descriptive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by giving a description</p><p><b>(etička) doktrina koja smatra da moralne izjave imaju vrijednost istine, (lingvistički) doktrina koja podupire ili promoviše opisujuću lingvističku znanost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (ethics) a doctrine holding that moral statements have a truth value</p><p><i>n.</i> (linguistics) a doctrine supporting or promoting descriptive linguistics</p><p><b>deskriptor, opis, opisivač, izraz, oblik, označitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the phonological or orthographic sound or appearance of a word that can be used to describe or identify something [form, signifier, word form]</p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of stored information that is used to 