eful manner [spitefully]</p><p><b>opljačkati, orobiti, pljačkati, harati, oplijeniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> steal goods [foray, loot, pillage, plunder, ransack, reave, rifle, strip]</p><p><i>v.</i> destroy and strip of its possession [plunder, rape, spoil, violate]</p><p><b>čin svlačenja i uzimanja silom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of stripping and taking by force [despoilment, despoliation, spoil, spoilation, spoliation]</p><p><b>opljačkati, orobiti, pljačkati (od &quot;despoil&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having been robbed and destroyed by force and violence [pillaged, raped, ravaged, sacked]</p><p><b>opljačkati, orobiti, pljačkati (od &quot;despoil&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who takes spoils or plunder (as in war) [freebooter, looter, pillager, plunderer, raider, spoiler]</p><p><b>pljačka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of stripping and taking by force [despoilation, despoliation, spoil, spoilation, spoliation]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) kći Zeusa i Demeter (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) daughter of Zeus and Demeter [Cora, Kore, Persephone]</p><p><b>čin svlačenja i uzimanja silom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of stripping and taking by force [despoilation, despoilment, spoil, spoilation, spoliation]</p><p><b>gubiti nadu, malodušnost, obeshrabriti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> lose confidence or hope</p><p><b>osjećati se potlačeno i obeshrabreno i bez nade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feeling downcast and disheartened and hopeless [despondency, disconsolateness, heartsickness]</p><p><b>potištenost, utučenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feeling downcast and disheartened and hopeless [despondence, disconsolateness, heartsickness]</p><p><b>malodušan, očajan, snužden, utučen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> without or almost without hope [heartsick]</p><p><b>malodušan, očajan, snužden, utučen (od &quot;despondent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with desperation [despairingly]</p><p><b>despot, silnik, autokrat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cruel and oppressive dictator [autocrat, tyrant