icies and removing monuments dedicated to him and renaming places named in his honor [de-Stalinisation, de-Stalinization, destalinisation]</p><p><b>suprotstaviti se učincima i politikama stalinizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> counteract the effects and policies of Stalinism [destalinise]</p><p><b>cilj, destinacija, mjesto, namjena, odredišni, odredište, opredjeljenje, sudbina, svrha</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the place designated as the end (as of a race or journey) [finish, goal]</p><p><i>n.</i> the ultimate goal for which something is done [terminus]</p><p><i>n.</i> written directions for finding some location [address, name and address]</p><p><b>namijeniti, odrediti, opredijeliti, namjenjivati, namjeravati, određivati, predodrediti, predodređivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> decree or designate beforehand [designate, doom, fate]</p><p><i>v.</i> design or destine [designate, intend, specify]</p><p><b>nužan, određen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> headed or intending to head in a certain direction [bound]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually followed by `to') governed by fate [bound]</p><p><b>sudbina, sudbinu, usud, fatum, kob, sudba, okolnosti, sreća</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event (or a course of events) that will inevitably happen in the future [fate]</p><p><i>n.</i> the ultimate agency regarded as predetermining the course of events (often personified as a woman) [fate]</p><p><i>n.</i> your overall circumstances or condition in life (including everything that happens to you) [circumstances, fate, fortune, lot, luck, portion]</p><p><b>lišen, lišen (čega), oskudan, siromašan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> poor enough to need help from others [impoverished, indigent, necessitous, needy, poverty-stricken]</p><p><i>adj.</i> completely wanting or lacking [barren, devoid, free, innocent]</p><p><b>oskudica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state without friends or money or prospects</p><p><b>Smanji naglasak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> reduce the emphasis [de-emphasise, de-emphasize]</p><p><b>dokinuti, iskorijeniti, istrijebiti, izg