ology) the process of an individual organism growing organically [growing, growth, maturation, ontogenesis, ontogeny]</p><p><i>n.</i> a recent event that has some relevance for the present situation</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making some area of land or water more profitable or productive or useful [exploitation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a district that has been developed to serve some purpose</p><p><i>n.</i> a state in which things are improving</p><p><i>n.</i> processing a photosensitive material in order to make an image visible [developing]</p><p><i>n.</i> (music) the section of a composition or movement (especially in sonata form) where the major musical themes are developed and elaborated</p><p><b>razvojni, razvojnih, razvojan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or constituting development</p><p><b>Mjere razvoja djeteta (u tjelesnoj veličini ili motoričkim vještinama ili psihološkoj funkciji) izražene u smislu starosnih normi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measure of a child's development (in body size or motor skill or psychological function) expressed in terms of age norms</p><p><b>grana anatomije koja proučava strukturalne promjene pojedinca od oplodnje do zrelosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of anatomy that studies structural changes of an individual from fertilization to maturity</p><p><b>Učenje koje se odvija kao normalan dio kognitivnog razvoja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> learning that takes place as a normal part of cognitive development</p><p><b>dječja psihologija, razvojna psihologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of psychology that studies the social and mental development of children [child psychology, genetic psychology]</p><p><b>razvojni, razvojnih (od &quot;developmental&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to development</p><p><b>Ljudi koji su mentalno retardirani. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people collectively who are mentally retarded [mentally retarded, retarded]</p><p><b>glagolska imenica, odglagolska imenica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a noun that is derived from a verb [verbal noun]</p><p><b>Hindu majčinska boginja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Hindu mother goddess</p><p><b>antikonformizam, nastranost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state or condition markedly different from the norm [aberrance, aberrancy, aberration]</p><p><i>n.</i> deviate behavior [deviation]</p><p><b>devijantan, koji zastranjuje, nastran</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person whose behavior deviates from what is acceptable especially in sexual behavior [degenerate, deviate, pervert]</p><p><i>adj.</i> markedly different from an accepted norm [aberrant, deviate]</p><p><b>odstupati, odstupiti, skrenuti, skretati, zastraniti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person whose behavior deviates from what is acceptable especially in sexual behavior [degenerate, deviant, pervert]</p><p><i>v.</i> turn aside [divert]</p><p><i>v.</i> be at variance with [depart, diverge, vary]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to turn away from a previous or expected course</p><p><i>adj.</i> markedly different from an accepted norm [aberrant, deviant]</p><p><b>abnormalno pomicanje lokacije nosnog pregrada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal shift in location of the nasal septum</p><p><b>abnormalno pomicanje zidova koji razdvajaju dvije komore (obično u nosnoj šupljini) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal displacement of any wall that separates two chambers (usually in the nasal cavity)</p><p><b>devijacija, odstupanje, otklon, divergencija, razlika, digresija, odmak, odmicanje, odvraćanje, otklanjanje, skretanje, udaljivanje, zastranjenje, zastranjivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variation that deviates from the standard or norm [departure, difference, divergence]</p><p><i>n.</i> the difference between an observed value and the expected value of a variable or function</p><p><i>n.</i> the error of a compass due to local magnetic disturbances</p><p><i>n.</i> deviate behavior [deviance]</p><p><i>n.</i> a turning aside (of your course or attention or concern) [deflection, deflexion, digression, divagation, diversion]</p><p><b>i