uits and a forked root formerly thought to have magical powers [Mandragora officinarum, mandrake]</p><p><b>naziv za vrstu Sarcosomataceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common name for a variety of Sarcosomataceae</p><p><b>godišnji od južne Sjedinjenih Američkih Država do Meksika s velikim bijeljastim ili žutočastim cvijećima obilježenim ljubičastim i dugim zakrivljenim kljunom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual of southern United States to Mexico having large whitish or yellowish flowers mottled with purple and a long curving beak [Proboscidea louisianica, common devil's claw, common unicorn plant, elephant-tusk, proboscis flower, ram's horn]</p><p><b>Obična planinara istočne Sjeverne Amerike koja se širi preko drugih biljaka i nosi brojne panike malih kremastih bijelih cvijeća, U slučaju da je u pitanju krastavac, to znači da je krastavac u stanju da se odredi na određenu vrstu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common climber of eastern North America that sprawls over other plants and bears numerous panicles of small creamy white flowers [Clematis virginiana, old man's beard, virgin's bower]</p><p><i>n.</i> slender-bodied non-stinging insect having iridescent wings that are outspread at rest [darning needle, dragonfly, mosquito hawk, sewing needle, skeeter hawk, snake doctor, snake feeder]</p><p><b>biljka iz roda Argemone s velikim bijelim ili žutim cvijećem i trnastima lišcima, stabljikama i strudama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Argemone having large white or yellow flowers and prickly leaves and stems and pods [argemone, prickly poppy, white thistle]</p><p><b>Europska višegodišnja biljka s žutim i narandžastim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common European perennial having showy yellow and orange flowers [Linaria vulgaris, butter-and-eggs, toadflax, wild snapdragon]</p><p><b>vrlo tamna čokoladna torta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very dark chocolate cake [devil's food cake]</p><p><b>vrlo tamna čokoladna torta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very dark chocolate cake [devil's food]</p><p><b>Stari svijet izbijanje uvedeno kao korov u istočnim Sjedinjenim Državama, Ne neatraktivni europski korov čiji cvijeće okreće prema suncu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Old World spurge introduced as a weed in the eastern United States [Euphorbia peplus, petty spurge]</p><p><i>n.</i> not unattractive European weed whose flowers turn toward the sun [Euphorbia helioscopia, sun spurge, wartweed, wartwort]</p><p><b>smrdljiva pomalo mesna tropska biljka iz jugoistočne Azije uzgajana zbog svojih jestivih kormova ili u stakleniku zbog svojih velikih listova i najozbiljnijih tamno crvenih špatova koji okružuju veliki špat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> foul-smelling somewhat fleshy tropical plant of southeastern Asia cultivated for its edible corms or in the greenhouse for its large leaves and showy dark red spathe surrounding a large spadix [Amorphophallus rivieri, snake palm, umbrella arum]</p><p><b>Vina s bijelim cvjetovima s debelim korijenima i malim crnim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white-flowered vine having thick roots and bearing small black berries [Bryonia alba, white bryony]</p><p><b>naziv za vrstu Sarcosomataceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common name for a variety of Sarcosomataceae</p><p><b>malo listno drvo ili grm iz istočne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small deciduous clump-forming tree or shrub of eastern United States [American angelica tree, Aralia spinosa, Hercules'-club]</p><p><b>tropski godišnji žbunljivi otrovni potgrm s plodovima koji se dijele na pet trnastih orašastih plodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical annual procumbent poisonous subshrub having fruit that splits into five spiny nutlets [Tribulus terestris, caltrop]</p><p><b>bezbrižan, nemaran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> cheerfully irresponsible [carefree, freewheeling, happy-go-lucky, harum-scarum, slaphappy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by a carefree unconventionality or disreputableness [raffish, rakish]</p><p><b>Činjenice ili obrede obožavanja đavola (MT)</b></