cohol, glycol]</p><p><b>vrlo veliki albatros (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very large albatross [wandering albatross]</p><p><b>različita vrsta albatrosa s crnim nogama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of albatross with black feet [black-footed albatross, gooney, gooney bird, goonie, goony]</p><p><b>albatrosi, porodica Diomedeidae, porodica albatrosa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> albatrosses [family Diomedeidae]</p><p><b>rod iz obitelji Droseraceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of the family Droseraceae [genus Dionaea]</p><p><b>biljka mesojedna u obalnim ravnicama Karolina koja ima osjetljive škriljaste marginalno čvrste listove koji zatvaraju i hvataju insekte (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> carnivorous plant of coastal plains of the Carolinas having sensitive hinged marginally bristled leaf blades that close and entrap insects [Venus's flytrap, Venus's flytraps]</p><p><b>Orgijski festival u drevnoj Grčkoj u čast Dioniza (= Bakha) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an orgiastic festival in ancient Greece in honor of Dionysus (= Bacchus) [Bacchanalia]</p><p><b>Dioniza ili ga obožavao. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or worshipping Dionysus</p><p><b>tiranin iz Sirakuze koji se borio protiv Kartaginaca (430-367 pr. n. e.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tyrant of Syracuse who fought the Carthaginians (430-367 BC) [Dionysius the Elder]</p><p><b>tiranin iz Sirakuze koji se borio protiv Kartaginaca (430-367 pr. n. e.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tyrant of Syracuse who fought the Carthaginians (430-367 BC) [Dionysius]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) bog vina i plodnosti i drame (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) god of wine and fertility and drama</p><p><b>bilo koji cikad iz roda Dioon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any cycad of the genus Dioon</p><p><b>Grčki matematičar koji je prvi pokušao razviti algebarsku notaciju (3. stoljeće) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek mathematician who was the first to try to develop an algebraic notation (3rd century)</p><p><b>diopter</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of measurement of the refractive power of a lens which is equal to the reciprocal of the focal length measured in meters [dioptre]</p><p><b>Jedinica za mjerenje snage lomljenja sočiva koja je jednaka reciproci žarišne udaljenosti izmerene u metarima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of measurement of the refractive power of a lens which is equal to the reciprocal of the focal length measured in meters [diopter]</p><p><b>Francuski modni dizajner čija je prva kolekcija iz 1947. godine stvorila stil koji je postao poznat kao New Look (1905-1957) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French couturier whose first collection in 1947 created a style that became known as the New Look (1905-1957) [Christian Dior]</p><p><b>diorama</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a picture (or series of pictures) representing a continuous scene [cyclorama, panorama]</p><p><b>diorit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a granular crystalline intrusive rock</p><p><b>slijepa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> yams [genus Dioscorea]</p><p><b>uzgajan u Australiji i Polineziji zbog velikog korijena s finim jestivim bijelim mesom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grown in Australasia and Polynesia for its large root with fine edible white flesh [water yam, white yam]</p><p><b>Čvrsta kineska loza naturalizirana u Sjedinjenim Državama i uzgajana kao ukrasna planinara zbog svojih blistavih lišća u obliku srca i aromatičnih listova cimeta i u tropima zbog svojih jestivih gomoljica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hardy Chinese vine naturalized in United States and cultivated as an ornamental climber for its glossy heart-shaped cinnamon-scented leaves and in the tropics for its edible tubers [Chinese yam, cinnamon vine]</p><p><b>Izglavlje od tropisne Afrike i Azije za koje se uzgajaju velike gomoljice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> yam of tropical Africa and Asia cultivated for it large tubers [air potato]</p><p><b>Južnoafrička loza s masivnim korijenom prekrivenim duboko puklom kore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African vine having a massive rootstock covered with deeply fissured bark [Hottentot's bread vine, Hottentot bread vine, elephant's-foot, tortoise plant]</p><p><b>s rizomom koja je prethodno sušena i koja se koristi za liječenje reuma ili bolesti jetre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having a rhizome formerly dried and used to treat rheumatism or liver disorders [wild yam]</p><p><b>tropski američki jam s malim žutim jestivim gomoljicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American yam with small yellow edible tubers [cush-cush]</p><p><b>slijepa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> yams [family Dioscoreaceae, yam family]</p><p><b>rod drveća ili grmova koji imaju lijepo i vrijedno drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of trees or shrubs that have beautiful and valuable wood [genus Diospyros]</p><p><b>tropsko stablo iz južne Azije koje ima tvrdo tamno boje srčane drveće koje se koristi u kabinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical tree of southern Asia having hard dark-colored heartwood used in cabinetwork [ebony, ebony tree]</p><p><b>kaki</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small deciduous Asiatic tree bearing large red or orange edible astringent fruit [Japanese persimmon, kaki]</p><p><b>veliki azijski drvo s tvrdim mermernim zebrawoodom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large Asiatic tree having hard marbled zebrawood [Andaman marble, marble-wood, marblewood]</p><p><b>Azijsko drvo peršuna koje se uzgaja zbog malog žutog ili ljubičasto-crnog voća koje su vrlo cijenili afganistanska plemena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Asiatic persimmon tree cultivated for its small yellow or purplish-black edible fruit much valued by Afghan tribes [date plum]</p><p><b>Srednje veličine drvo suvih šuma u južnim i istočnim Sjedinjenim Državama koje nosi žuto ili narandžasto vrlo adstringentno voće koje je jestivo kada je potpuno zreo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized tree of dry woodlands in the southern and eastern United States bearing yellow or orange very astringent fruit that is edible when fully ripe [American persimmon, possumwood]</p><p><b>inhibitor angiotenzina II koji se koristi za l