osomes or twice the haploid number</p><p><b>stanje biti diploidni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of being diploid</p><p><b>diploma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a document certifying the successful completion of a course of study [sheepskin]</p><p><b>diplomacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> negotiation between nations [diplomatic negotiations]</p><p><i>n.</i> subtly skillful handling of a situation [delicacy, discreetness, finesse]</p><p><i>n.</i> wisdom in the management of public affairs [statecraft, statesmanship]</p><p><b>diplomat, diplomata</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an official engaged in international negotiations [diplomatist]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who deals tactfully with others</p><p><b>medicinski stručnjak čija je stručnost potvrđena diplomom koju je dodijelila odgovarajuća stručna skupina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medical specialist whose competence has been certified by a diploma granted by an appropriate professional group</p><p><b>diplomatski, diplomatskim, diplomatical</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of diplomacy</p><p><i>adj.</i> using or marked by tact in dealing with sensitive matters or people [diplomatical]</p><p><b>vladina zgrada u kojoj diplomati žive ili rade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> government building in which diplomats live or work</p><p><b>diplomatski kor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of diplomatic personnel [corps diplomatique, diplomatic service]</p><p><b>diplomatski imunitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> exemption from taxation or normal processes of law that is offered to diplomatic personnel in a foreign country</p><p><b>diplomata koji predstavlja jednu vladu drugoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a diplomat representing one government to another [minister]</p><p><b>misija koja služi diplomatskim ciljevima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mission serving diplomatic ends</p><p><b>diplomacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> negotiation between nations [diplomacy]</p><p><b>diplomatska pošta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mail pouch that is sealed shut and that is used to carry