</i> soiled or likely to soil with dirt or grime [soiled, unclean]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of behavior or especially language) characterized by obscenity or indecency</p><p><i>adj.</i> vile [filthy, lousy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> spreading pollution or contamination [contaminating]</p><p><i>adj.</i> contaminated with infecting organisms [pestiferous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of color) discolored by impurities [dingy, muddied, muddy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a manuscript) defaced with changes [foul, marked-up]</p><p><i>adj.</i> obtained illegally or by improper means [ill-gotten]</p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing or revealing hostility or dislike</p><p><i>adj.</i> violating accepted standards or rules [cheating, foul, unsporting, unsportsmanlike]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unethical or dishonest [shoddy, sordid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unpleasantly stormy</p><p><b>atomska bomba koja ostavlja značajnu radioaktivnu kontaminaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an atom bomb that leaves considerable radioactive contamination</p><p><b>osoba koja se smatra prezirnom ili prezirnom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is deemed to be despicable or contemptible [bum, crumb, git, lowlife, puke, rat, rotter, scum bag, skunk, so-and-so, stinker, stinkpot]</p><p><b>Neprijatna šala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an indelicate joke [blue joke, blue story, dirty story]</p><p><b>osobne stvari koje bi mogle biti neugodne ako se objave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> personal matters that could be embarrassing if made public [dirty linen]</p><p><b>osobne stvari koje bi mogle biti neugodne ako se objave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> personal matters that could be embarrassing if made public [dirty laundry]</p><p><b>nepošten dobitak, nepoštena dobit, plijen, prljavi novac, ukradena roba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> goods or money obtained illegally [booty, loot, pillage, plunder, prize, swag]</p><p><b>sredovječni čovjek sa požudnim sklonostima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a middle-aged man with lecherous inclinations</p><p><b>ponašanje koje je nepravedno ili neetično ili nesportsko (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> conduct that is unfair or unethical or unsportsmanlike</p><p><b>Neprijatna šala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an indelicate joke [blue joke, blue story, dirty joke]</p><p><b>lopovluk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unkind or aggressive trick</p><p><b>podmuklo komercijalno ili političko ponašanje namijenjeno diskreditiranju protivnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> underhand commercial or political behavior designed to discredit an opponent</p><p><b>ofanziva koju izvodi tajna policija ili vojska režima protiv revolucionarnih i terorističkih pobunjenika i obilježena je korištenjem otmica, mučenja i ubojstava, a žrtve su često civili. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an offensive conducted by secret police or the military of a regime against revolutionary and terrorist insurgents and marked by the use of kidnapping and torture and murder with civilians often being the victims</p><p><b>uvredljiva ili nepristojna riječ ili fraza, riječ koja se smatra neizvjesnom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an offensive or indecent word or phrase [filth, obscenity, smut, vulgarism]</p><p><i>n.</i> a word that is considered to be unmentionable</p><p><b>Ima prljavo lice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a dirty face</p><p><b>imajući razvratne misli (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having lewd thoughts</p><p><b>kaljanje, mazanje, prljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of soiling something [soiling, soilure]</p><p><b>DSP</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman mythology) god of the underworld [Dis Pater, Orcus, Pluto]</p><p><b>(Rimska mitologija) bog podzemlja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman mythology) god of the underworld [Dis, Orcus, Pluto]</p><p><b>bilo koji orhidej iz roda Disa, Agencija za borbenu podršku u Ministarstvu obrane odgovorna za razvoj i rad i podršku informacijskih sustava kako bi služila potrebama predsjednika i ministra obrane i zajedničkih načelnika osoblja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any orchid of the genus Disa</p><p><i>n.</i> a combat support agency in the Department of Defense responsible for developing and operating and supporting information systems to serve the needs of the President and the Secretary of Defense and the Joint Chiefs of Staff [Defense Information Systems Agency]</p><p><b>invaliditet, nedostatak, nemoć, nesposobnost, nesposobnosti, onesposobljenost, invalidnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of being unable to perform as a consequence of physical or mental unfitness [disablement, handicap, impairment]</p><p><b>Službenici za invaliditet (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> insurance benefits paid in case of disability</p><p><b>mjesečno plaćanje osobama koje su invalide i koje ne mogu raditi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monthly payment made to someone who has become disabled and is unable to work [disability payment]</p><p><b>invalidsko osiguranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> social insurance for the disabled</p><p><b>invaliditet koji ometa ili sprečava hodanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disability that interferes with or prevents walking</p><p><b>mjesečno plaćanje osobama koje su invalide i koje ne mogu raditi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monthly payment made to someone who has become disabled and is unable to work [disability check]</p><p><b>onemogućiti, onesposobiti, deaktivirati, isključiti, isključivati, onemogućavati, onesposobljavati, hendikepirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make unable to perform a certain action [disenable, incapacitate]</p><p><i>v.</i> injure permanently [handicap, incapacitate, invalid]</p><p><b>bespomoćan, nesposoban za rad, nesposobnost za rad, onemogućen, onesposobljen, osakaćen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people collectively who are crippled or otherwise physically handicapped [handicapped]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having restricted mental or physical functioning as a consequence of injury or illness [handicapped]</p><p><b>invaliditet, invalidnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of being unable to perform as a consequence of physical or mental unfitness [disability, handicap, impairment]</p><p><b>onemogućavanje</b></p><p><i>adj