>n.</i> something that is discovered</p><p><i>n.</i> a productive insight [breakthrough, find]</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) compulsory pretrial disclosure of documents relevant to a case</p><p><b>Slavlje u čast otkrića Amerike od strane Christophera Kolumba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a legal holiday commemorating the discovery of America by Christopher Columbus [Columbus Day, October 12]</p><p><b>diskreditirati, gubitak ugleda, izgubiti povjerenje, nevjerica, ozloglasiti, obrukati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being held in low esteem [disrepute]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be distrusted or disbelieved</p><p><i>v.</i> damage the reputation of [disgrace]</p><p><i>v.</i> reject as false [disbelieve]</p><p><b>koji imaju tendenciju da dovedu u diskredit ili ružno ime (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to bring discredit or disrepute</p><p><b>na nečasan način ili u nečasnom stupnju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a dishonorable manner or to a dishonorable degree [disgracefully, dishonorably, dishonourably, ignominiously, ingloriously, shamefully]</p><p><b>diskreditirati, gubitak ugleda, izgubiti povjerenje, nevjerica (od &quot;discredit&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being unjustly brought into disrepute [damaged]</p><p><i>adj.</i> suffering shame [disgraced, dishonored, shamed]</p><p><b>diskretan, oprezan, pametan, uzdržljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by prudence or modesty and wise self-restraint</p><p><i>adj.</i> unobtrusively perceptive and sympathetic [discerning]</p><p><i>adj.</i> heedful of potential consequences [circumspect]</p><p><b>diskretan, oprezan, pametan, uzdržljiv (od &quot;discreet&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with discretion</p><p><b>diskretan, oprezan, pametan, uzdržljiv (od &quot;discreet&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> knowing how to avoid embarrassment or distress [circumspection, discretion, prudence]</p><p><i>n.</i> subtly skillful handling of a situation [delicacy, diplomacy, finesse]</p><p><b>nedosljednost, nepodudarnost, nesklad, neslaganje, nesuglasje, neus