about what to do [cue]</p><p><b>demodulator FM signala, diskriminator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who (or that which) differentiates [differentiator]</p><p><b>diskriminirajući, koji diskriminira</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being biased or having a belief or attitude formed beforehand [prejudiced]</p><p><i>adj.</i> containing or implying a slight or showing prejudice [invidious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of making fine distinctions [discriminative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> manifesting partiality [preferential]</p><p><b>koji luta, koji pretresa, koji raspravlja, koji se udaljuje od predmeta, koji sudi, koji tumara, koji zaključuje, nestalan, nesuvisao</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> proceeding to a conclusion by reason or argument rather than intuition [dianoetic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of e.g. speech and writing) tending to depart from the main point or cover a wide range of subjects [digressive, excursive, rambling]</p><p><b>lutajući, nestalno, nesuvislo, pretresajući, raspravljajući, sudeći, tumarajući, udaljujući se od predmeta, zaključujući</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a rambling manner [ramblingly]</p><p><b>koji luta, koji pretresa, koji raspravlja, koji se udaljuje od predmeta, koji sudi, koji tumara, koji zaključuje, nestalan, nesuvisao (od &quot;discursive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being discursive</p><p><b>disk, disko</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an athletic competition in which a disk-shaped object is thrown as far as possible</p><p><i>n.</i> a disk used in throwing competitions [saucer]</p><p><b>diskutirati, rasprava, raspraviti, raspravljati, raspravljati o nečemu, razmotriti, rasprave</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to consider or examine in speech or writing [discourse, talk about]</p><p><i>v.</i> speak with others about (something) [hash out, talk over]</p><p><b>sudionik u formalnoj raspravi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a participant in a formal discussion</p><p><b>diskusija, pregovaranje, rasprava, raspravljanje, razgovor, razmatranje, vijećanje, debata</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extended communication (often interactive) dealing with some particular topic [discourse, treatment]</p><p><i>n.</i> an exchange of views on some topic [give-and-take, word]</p><p><b>mali razred učenika koji su dio većeg kursa, ali se uče odvojeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small class of students who are part of a larger course but are taught separately [section]</p><p><b>nadmenost, omalovažavati, prezir, prezirati, nipodaštavati, ismijati, ismijavati, odbaciti, odbacivati, odbijati, odbiti, prezreti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lack of respect accompanied by a feeling of intense dislike [contempt, despite, scorn]</p><p><i>n.</i> a communication that indicates lack of respect by patronizing the recipient [condescension, patronage]</p><p><i>v.</i> look down on with disdain [contemn, despise, scorn]</p><p><i>v.</i> reject with contempt [freeze off, pooh-pooh, reject, scorn, spurn, turn down]</p><p><b>uvredljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing extreme contempt [contemptuous, insulting, scornful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing arrogant superiority to and disdain of those one views as unworthy [haughty, imperious, lordly, overbearing, prideful, sniffy, supercilious, swaggering]</p><p><b>oholo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a proud and domineering manner [cavalierly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without respect [contemptuously, contumeliously, scornfully]</p><p><b>uvredljiv (od &quot;disdainful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of displaying arrogance by patronizing those considered inferior [condescension, superciliousness]</p><p><b>bolest, oboljenje, bolesti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an impairment of health or a condition of abnormal functioning</p><p><b>bolest koju karakterizira oštećenje neuromuskularnih spojeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease characterized by impairment of neuromuscular junctions</p><p><b>bolest kože, kožna bolest, kožni poremećaj, poremećaj kože</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease affecting the skin [skin disease, skin disorder]</p><p><b>bolestan, obolio</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> caused by o