asing manner</p><p><b>nezadovoljstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling of being displeased or annoyed or dissatisfied with someone or something</p><p><b>perušati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> strip of honors, possessions, or attributes [deplume]</p><p><i>v.</i> strip of feathers [deplumate, deplume, pluck, pull, tear]</p><p><b>iskrcajna luka, zabavljati se, razonoditi, ugađati, ugoditi, zabaviti, zabavljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> occupy in an agreeable, entertaining or pleasant fashion [amuse, divert]</p><p><i>v.</i> play boisterously [cavort, frisk, frolic, gambol, lark, lark about, rollick, romp, run around, skylark, sport]</p><p><b>raspoloživ, slobodan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an item that can be disposed of after it has been used</p><p><i>adj.</i> free or available for use or disposition</p><p><i>adj.</i> designed to be disposed of after use</p><p><b>prihoda (naknade) koja vam je dostupna za štednju ili potrošnju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> income (after taxes) that is available to you for saving or spending</p><p><b>disponiranje, dispozicija, na raspolaganju, odlaganja, odlaganje, odlaganje opasnog otpada, preraspodjela, raspolaganje, raspoloženje, administracija, uprava, odstranjivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the power to use something or someone</p><p><i>n.</i> a method of tending to or managing the affairs of a some group of people (especially the group's business affairs) [administration]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act or means of getting rid of something [disposition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a kitchen appliance for disposing of garbage [electric pig, garbage disposal]</p><p><b>Sredstva za proizvodnju električnih goriva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant for disposing of sewage [sewage disposal plant]</p><p><b>disponirati, raspolagati, rasporediti, raspoređivati, uređivati, bacati, baciti, hitati, hititi, hitnuti, izbaciti, izbacivati, maknuti, micati, napustiti, napuštati, odbaciti, odbacivati, odlagati, odložiti, ostaviti, ostavljati, pobacati, premetati, riješiti se, rješavati se, sklanjati, skloniti, uklanjati, ukloniti, škartirati, naginjati, kvalificirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give, sell, or transfer to another</p><p><i>v.</i> throw or cast away [cast aside, cast away, cast out, chuck out, discard, fling, put away, throw away, throw out, toss, toss away, toss out]</p><p><i>v.</i> make receptive or willing towards an action or attitude or belief [incline]</p><p><i>v.</i> place or put in a particular order</p><p><i>v.</i> make fit or prepared [qualify]</p><p><b>raspolagati, riješiti se, ustupiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> deal with or settle</p><p><b>disponiran, impulzivan, nagao, rad, rad čemu, raspoložen, raspoloživ, raspoređen, sklon, voljan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having made preparations [fain, inclined, prepared]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually followed by `to') naturally disposed toward [apt, given, minded, tending]</p><p><b>dispozicija, određenje, raspolaganje, raspored, razmještaj, raspoloženje, temperament, ćud, odlaganje, odstranjivanje, sklonost, tendencija, težnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> your usual mood [temperament]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act or means of getting rid of something [disposal]</p><p><i>n.</i> an attitude of mind especially one that favors one alternative over others [inclination, tendency]</p><p><i>n.</i> a natural or acquired habit or characteristic tendency in a person or thing</p><p><b>iseliti, istjerati s posjeda, izbaciti, izvlastiti, lišiti imovine</b></p><p><i>v.</i> deprive of the possession of real estate</p><p><b>iseliti, istjerati s posjeda, izbaciti, izvlastiti, lišiti imovine (od &quot;dispossess&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> physically or spiritually homeless or deprived of security [homeless, roofless]</p><p><b>istjerivanje iz posjeda, izvlaštenje, otimanje, egzorcizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the expulsion of someone (such as a tenant) from the possession of land by process of law [eviction, legal ouster]</p><p><i>n.</i> freeing from evil spirits [exorcism]</p><p><b>ocrnjivanje, omalovažavanje, potcjenjivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of speaking contemptuously of [disparagement]</p><p><b>širenje u inozemstvo ili izvan njega (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> spread abroad or out</p><p><b>opovrgavanje, pobijanje, opovrgnuće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any evidence that helps to establish the falsity of something [falsification, refutation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of determining that something is false [falsification, falsifying, refutal, refutation]</p><p><b>disproporcija, nesklad, nesrazmjer, nesrazmjera, nesrazmjernost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lack of proportion</p><p><b>nesrazmjeran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> out of proportion [disproportionate]</p><p><b>neproporcionalan, nesrazmjeran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> out of proportion [disproportional]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not proportionate</p><p><b>neproporcionalno, nesrazmjerno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> out of proportion</p><p><i>adv.</i> to a disproportionate degree</p><p><b>dokazati neispravnost, dokazati neistinu, pobijati, opovrgavati, opovrgnuti, pobiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> prove to be false [confute]</p><p><b>dokazati neispravnost, dokazati neistinu, pobijati (od &quot;disprove&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a debater who refutes or disproves by offering contrary evidence or argument [confuter, rebutter, refuter]</p><p><b>sporan, sporno, sumnjiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being disproved [debatable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> open to argument or debate [arguable, debatable, moot]</p><p><b>diskutant</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who disputes [controversialist, eristic]</p><p><b>rasprava, debata</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the formal presentation of a stated proposition and the opposition to it (usually followed by a vote) [debate, public debate]</p><p><i>n.</i> a contentious speech act [arguing, argument, contention, contestation, controversy, disceptation, tilt]</p><p><b>S druge strane, ako je osoba u stanju da se bori protiv drugih osoba ili osoba koje su u stanju da se bore protiv njih, ona može biti u stanju da se bori protiv njih ili da se ne slaže s njima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined or showing an inclination to dispute or disagree, even to engage in law suits [combative, contentious, disputative, litigious]</p><p><b>Na sporni način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a disputatious manner [argumentatively]</p><p><b>S druge strane, ako je osoba u stanju da se bori protiv drugih osoba ili osoba koje su u stanju da se bore protiv njih, ona može biti u stanju da se bori protiv njih ili da se ne slaže s njima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined or showing an inclination to dispute or disagree, even to engage in law suits [combative, contentious, disputatious, litigious]</p><p><b>osporavati, osporiti, parnica, pobiti, prepirka, rasprava, raspravljati, razlika u mišljenju, spor, sporiti, sporovati, svađa, svađalo, nesuglasica, razmirica, pobijati, proturječiti, protusloviti, porječkati se, posvaditi se, posvađati se, prepirati se, prepucavati se, rječkati se, sporiti se, svađati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disagreement or argument about something important [conflict, difference, difference of opinion]</p><p><i>n.</i> coming into conflict with [contravention]</p><p><i>v.</i> take exception to [challenge, gainsay]</p><p><i>v.</i> have a disagreement over something [altercate, argufy, quarrel, scrap]</p><p><b>osporavan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> subject to disagreement and debate</p><p><b>diskvalifikacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unfitness that bars you from participation</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of preventing someone from participating by finding them unqualified</p><p><b>diskvalificirati, onemogućiti (od &quot;disqualify&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> disqualified by law or rule or provision</p><p><i>adj.</i> barred from competition for violation of rules</p><p><b>diskvalificirati, onemogućiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make unfit or unsuitable [indispose, unfit]</p><p><i>v.</i> declare unfit</p><p><b>diskvalificirati, onemogućiti (od &quot;disqualify&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> depriving of legal right [disabling]</p><p><b>briga, uznemiravati, uznemirivati, zabrinjavati, uznemiriti, uzrujati, uzrujavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of mild anxiety about possible developments [anxiousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of seeming ill at ease [unease, uneasiness]</p><p><i>v.</i> disturb in mind or make uneasy or cause to be worried or alarmed [cark, disorder, distract, perturb, trouble, unhinge]</p><p><b>briga, uznemiravati, uznemirivati, zabrinjavati (od &quot;disquiet&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> afflicted with or marked by anxious uneasiness or trouble or grief [distressed, disturbed, upset, worried]</p><p><b>neprijatan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing mental discomfort</p><p><b>neprijatan (od &quot;disquieting&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a disquieting manner</p><p><b>nelagoda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feelings of anxiety that make you tense and irritable [edginess, inquietude, uneasiness]</p><p><b>ispitivanje, istraživanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elaborate analytical or explanatory essay or discussion</p><p><b>Britanski državnik koji je kao premijer kupio većinski udio u Suezskom kanalu i učinio kraljicu Viktoriju caricom Indije (1804-1881) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British statesman who as Prime Minister bought controlling interest in the Suez Canal and made Queen Victoria the empress of India (1804-1881) [Benjamin Disraeli, First Earl of Beaconsfield]</p><p><b>ignoriranje, izostaviti, ne obazirati se, ne obazirati se na, nepažnja, nepoštovanje, neuvažavanje, nebriga, ignorirati, odbaciti, odbacivati, odbijati, odbiti, zanemariti, zanemarivati, isključiti, isključivati, zapustiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lack of attention and due care [neglect]</p><p><i>n.</i> willful lack of care and attention [neglect]</p><p><i>v.</i> refuse to acknowledge [cut, ignore, snub]</p><p><i>v.</i> bar from attention or consideration [brush aside, brush off, discount, dismiss, ignore, push aside]</p><p><i>v.</i> give little or no attention to [ignore, neglect]</p><p><b>izostavljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not noticed inadvertently [forgotten]</p><p><b>izostavljanje, izostavljene</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in spite of everything [disregardless, irrespective, no matter, regardless]</p><p><b>Unatoč svemu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in spite of everything [disregarding, irrespective, no matter, regardless]</p><p><b>ruševnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in need of repairs</p><p><b>nepoštovanje zbog nedostatka poštovanja ili dobrog ugleda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dishonorableness by virtue of lacking respectability or a good reputation [disreputableness, unrespectability]</p><p><b>na lošem glasu, nepristojan, zloglasan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking respectability in character or behavior or appearance</p><p><b>netko kome nedostaje javna poštovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone lacking public esteem</p><p><b>na lošem glasu, nepristojan (od &quot;disreputable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dishonorableness by virtue of lacking respectability or a good reputation [disreputability, unrespectability]</p><p><b>Na neugodan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a disreputable manner</p><p><b>loš ugled</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being held in low esteem [discredit]</p><p><b>nepoštovanje, neučtivost, nepoštivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expression of lack of respect [discourtesy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a disrespectful mental attitude</p><p><i>n.</i> a manner that is generally disrespectful and contemptuous [contempt]</p><p><i>v.</i> show a lack of respect for</p><p><i>v.</i> have little or no respect for [disesteem]</p><p><b>bez poštovanja</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> exhibiting lack of respect</p><p><i>adj.</i> neither feeling nor showing respect [aweless, awless]</p><p><b>bez poštovanja (od &quot;disrespectful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a disrespectful manner</p><p><b>razodijevati se, razodjenuti se, skidati se, skinuti se, svlačiti se, svući se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> get undressed [discase, peel, strip, strip down, uncase, unclothe, undress]</p><p><b>iščupati, poremetiti, prekinuti, raskinuti, razbiti, srušiti, prekidati, upadati, upasti, remetiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a break in [break up, cut off, interrupt]</p><p><i>v.</i> throw into disorder</p><p><i>v.</i> interfere in someone else's activity [interrupt]</p><p><b>poremećen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by breaks or gaps</p><p><b>eksploziv koji se koristi za oštećenje mete koja je pod napadom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a high explosive that is used to damage the target that is under attack [bursting explosive]</p><p><b>lom, poremećaj, prekid, prijelom, rascjep, raskid, raskol, razdor, ometanje, prekidanje, bura, graja, izgred, remećenje, urnebes</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an act of delaying or interrupting the continuity [break, gap, interruption]</p><p><i>n.</i> a disorderly outburst or tumult [commotion, disturbance, flutter, hoo-ha, hoo-hah, hurly burly, kerfuffle, to-do]</p><p><i>n.</i> an event that results in a displacement or discontinuity [dislocation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of causing disorder [perturbation]</p><p><b>koji remeti, razoran, remetilački</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by unrest or disorder or insubordination [riotous, troubled, tumultuous, turbulent]</p><p><b>koji remeti, razoran (od &quot;disruptive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a disruptive manner</p><p><b>poniziti, uvrijediti, vrijeđati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> treat, mention, or speak to rudely [affront, insult]</p><p><b>nelagodnost, nezadovoljenost, nezadovoljnost, nezadovoljstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling of being displeased and discontent</p><p><b>Ne ispunjava očekivanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not up to expectations [disappointing, unsatisfying]</p><p><b>nezadovoljan, razočaran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in a state of sulky dissatisfaction [disgruntled]</p><p><b>nezadovoljiti, ne zadovoljavati, ne zadovoljiti, razočarati, razočaravati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> fail to satisfy</p><p><b>rasijecati, secirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cut open or cut apart</p><p><i>v.</i> make a mathematical, chemical, or grammatical analysis of [analyse, analyze, break down, take apart]</p><p><b>rasijecati, secirati (od &quot;dissect&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having one or more indentations reaching nearly to the midrib [cleft]</p><p><b>seciranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cutting so as to separate into pieces</p><p><i>n.</i> a minute and critical analysis</p><p><i>n.</i> detailed critical analysis or examination one part at a time (as of a literary work)</p><p><b>kriti, pretvarati se, prikriti, praviti se, hiniti, kriti se, maskirati se, prerušiti se, prerušivati se, prikriti se, prikrivati se, zabašuriti se, zakrabuljiti se, afektirati, glumatati, glumiti, izigravati, prenavljati se, prenemagati se, producirati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make believe with the intent to deceive [affect, feign, pretend, sham]</p><p><i>v.</i> hide under a false appearance [cloak, mask]</p><p><i>v.</i> behave unnaturally or affectedly [act, pretend]</p><p><b>kriti, pretvarati se, prikriti (od &quot;dissemble&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who professes beliefs and opinions that he or she does not hold in order to conceal his or her real feelings or motives [dissimulator, hypocrite, phoney, phony, pretender]</p><p><b>obmana, obmanjivanje, opsjena, prijevara, varanje, varka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pretending with intention to deceive [feigning, pretence, pretense]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of deceiving [deceit, deception, dissimulation]</p><p><b>rasturati, razbacivati, sijati, prenijeti, prenositi, priopćavati, priopćiti, pronijeti, pronositi, propagirati, proširiti, proširivati, razglasiti, razglašavati, raširiti, raširivati, širiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become widely known [broadcast, circularise, circularize, circulate, diffuse, disperse, distribute, pass around, propagate, spread]</p><p><b>upale vezivnog tkiva s različitim obilježjima uključujući groznicu, slabost i umornost te bolove u zglobovima i oštećenja kože na licu, vratu ili rukama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inflammatory disease of connective tissue with variable features including fever and weakness and fatigability and joint pains and skin lesions on the face or neck or arms [SLE, systemic lupus erythematosus]</p><p><b>hronično progresivno živčano poremećaj koje uključuje gubitak mijelinske omotače oko određenih živčanih vlakana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chronic progressive nervous disorder involving loss of myelin sheath around certain nerve fibers [MS, disseminated sclerosis, multiple sclerosis]</p><p><b>hronično progresivno živčano poremećaj koje uključuje gubitak mijelinske omotače oko određenih živčanih vlakana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chronic progressive nervous disorder involving loss of myelin sheath around certain nerve fibers [MS, disseminated multiple sclerosis, multiple sclerosis]</p><p><b>diseminacija podataka, razumijevanja, razumijevanje, širenje, diseminacija, disperzija, rasap, rasijavanje, rasipanje, raspršenje, raspršivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the opening of a subject to widespread discussion and debate [airing, public exposure, spreading]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being diffused or dispersed [diffusion]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of dispersing or diffusing something [diffusion, dispersal, dispersion]</p><p><b>Difuzijom se širi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> spreading by diffusion [diffusing, diffusive, dispersive]</p><p><b>Nekoga tko širi vijesti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who spreads the news [propagator]</p><p><b>nesklad, nesloga, neslaganje, nesložnost, nesuglasica, nesuglasje, razilaženje u mišljenju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> disagreement among those expected to cooperate [discord]</p><p><i>n.</i> a conflict of people's opinions or actions or characters [disagreement, dissonance]</p><p><b>disidencija, misliti drugačije, ne slagati se, buniti se, oponirati, pobuniti se, prosvjedovati, protestirati, protiviti se, usprotiviti se, ne složiti se, razilaziti se, razići se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) the difference of one judge's opinion from that of the majority</p><p><i>n.</i> a difference of opinion</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of protesting [objection, protest]</p><p><i>v.</i> withhold assent</p><p><i>v.</i> express opposition through action or words [protest, resist]</p><p><i>v.</i> be of different opinions [differ, disagree, take issue]</p><p><b>disident</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who dissents from some established policy [contestant, dissident, objector, protester]</p><p><b>(katoličana) odbijaju prisustvovati službama Anglikanske crkve, Ne slažem se, posebno s većinom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of Catholics) refusing to attend services of the Church of England [recusant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> disagreeing, especially with a majority [dissenting, dissident]</p><p><b>drugog mišljenja, odvojen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> disagreeing, especially with a majority [dissentient, dissident]</p><p><b>mišljenje koje se ne slaže s sudskim odlukom o slučaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an opinion that disagrees with the court's disposition of the case</p><p><b>neslaganje (posebno neslaganje s mišljenjem većine) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> dissenting (especially dissenting with the majority opinion) [divisive, factious]</p><p><b>dugo i formalno razgovarati o temi (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> talk at length and formally about a topic [discourse, hold forth]</p><p><b>disertacija, rasprava, teza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a treatise advancing a new point of view resulting from research [thesis]</p><p><b>loša usluga, šteta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an act intended to help that turns out badly [ill service, ill turn]</p><p><b>cijepati, cjepkati, dijeliti, podijeliti, podjeljivati, podvojiti, rascijepati, rascijepiti, rascjepkati, rascjepkavati, rascjepljivati, raskoliti, raspoloviti, rastaviti, rastavljati, razdijeliti, razdjeljivati, razdvajati, razdvojiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> separate into parts or portions [carve up, divide, separate, split, split up]</p><p><b>disidentstvo, neslaganje, nesuglasice, rascjep</b></p><p><i>n.</i> disagreement</p><p><b>disident, raskolnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who dissents from some established policy [contestant, dissenter, objector, protester]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by departure from accepted beliefs or standards [heretical, heterodox]</p><p><i>adj.</i> disagreeing, especially with a majority [dissentient, dissenting]</p><p><b>Radikalna teroristička grupa koja se odvojila 1997. godine kada je glavna struja Privremene IRA predložila prekid vatre. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radical terrorist group that broke away in 1997 when the mainstream Provisional IRA proposed a cease-fire [RIRA, Real IRA, Real Irish Republican Army]</p><p><b>Proizvodnja i proizvodnja sirovina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the emergence of seeds as seed pods burst open when they are ripe</p><p><b>rasplakaju se silom, kao i neke zrele posude za sjeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> bursting open with force, as do some ripe seed vessels</p><p><b>različit, raznolik, raznovrstan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not similar</p><p><i>adj.</i> not alike or similar [unalike]</p><p><b>nejednakost, nesličnost, razlika, različitost, raznovrsnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being dissimilar [unsimilarity]</p><p><b>Postaju različiti mijenjanjem kvaliteta zvuka., napraviti neponovljiv, Postaju različiti ili manje slični. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become dissimilar by changing the sound qualities</p><p><i>v.</i> make dissimilar</p><p><i>v.</i> become dissimilar or less similar</p><p><b>katabolizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a linguistic process by which one of two similar sounds in a word becomes less like the other</p><p><i>n.</i> breakdown in living organisms of more complex substances into simpler ones together with release of energy [catabolism, destructive metabolism, katabolism]</p><p><b>Nepodjednakoća dokazana odsustvom sličnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dissimilarity evidenced by an absence of likeness [unlikeness]</p><p><b>kriti, pretvarati se, prikriti, simulirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> hide (feelings) from other people</p><p><b>obmana, obmanjivanje, opsjena, prijevara, varanje, varka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of deceiving [deceit, deception, dissembling]</p><p><b>skrivanje pod lažnim izgledom s namjerom zavaravanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> concealing under a false appearance with the intent to deceive</p><p><b>osoba koja tvrdi da ima uvjerenja i mišljenja koja ne drži kako bi sakrila svoja prava osjećanja ili motive. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who professes beliefs and opinions that he or she does not hold in order to conceal his or her real feelings or motives [dissembler, hypocrite, phoney, phony, pretender]</p><p><b>potratiti, proćerdati, rasipati, rasplinuti se, raspršiti, raspršiti se, rasturati, rasturiti, trošiti, rastjerivati, razagnati, rasijati se, rasipati se, raspršivati se, rastepsti se, rasuti se, razdijeliti se, razdjeljivati se, razdvajati se, razdvojiti se, raštrkati se, raštrkavati se, raštrkivati se, piskati, protepsti, protratiti, protraćiti, rasprčkati, rasprčkavati, rastepsti, rasuti, razbacivati se, spiskati, spiskavati, stratiti, straćiti, tratiti, traćiti, ćerdati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to cause to separate and go in different directions [break up, dispel, disperse, scatter]</p><p><i>v.</i> move away from each other [disperse, scatter, spread out]</p><p><i>v.</i> spend frivolously and unwisely [fool, fool away, fritter, fritter away, frivol away, shoot]</p><p><i>v.</i> live a life of pleasure, especially with respect to alcoholic consumption</p><p><b>lakouman, narušena zdravlja, neumjeren, raskalašen, raspršen, raspušten, rastjeran, razuzdan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> unrestrained by convention or morality [debauched, degenerate, degraded, dissolute, fast, libertine, profligate, riotous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> preoccupied with the pursuit of pleasure and especially games of chance [betting, card-playing, sporting]</p><p><b>disipacija, gubitak (energije), rasipanje, raspršenost, rasturanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> breaking up and scattering by dispersion</p><p><i>n.</i> dissolute indulgence in sensual pleasure [dissolution, licentiousness, looseness, profligacy]</p><p><i>n.</i> useless or profitless activity [waste,