. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> resembles a thimble on a finger [Verpa bohemica]</p><p><b>rano</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> during an early stage [early]</p><p><b>Evroazijska orhideja s navidnim ružičastim ili ljubičastim cvijećem u losom šiljku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian orchid with showy pink or purple flowers in a loose spike [Orchis mascula, male orchis]</p><p><b>proljetna orhideja s cvijetom žute, zelene ili ružičaste sepalnosti i širokim smeđim baršunastom usnama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spring-blooming spider orchid having a flower with yellow or green or pink sepals and a broad brown velvety lip [Ophrys sphegodes]</p><p><b>nizak višegodišnji trillium s bijelim cvetovima pronađen u jugoistočnim Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a low perennial white-flowered trillium found in the southeastern United States [dwarf-white trillium, snow trillium]</p><p><b>radar koji je dio sustava ranog upozorenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radar that is part of an early warning system</p><p><b>mreža radarskih instalacija namijenjenih otkrivanju neprijateljskih raketa ili zrakoplova dok još ima vremena za njihovo presretanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a network of radar installations designed to detect enemy missiles or aircraft while there is still time to intercept them</p><p><b>od jugozapadne Europe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of southwestern Europe [American cress, American watercress, Barbarea praecox, Barbarea verna, Belle Isle cress, land cress]</p><p><b>biljaka koje cvjetaju u proljeće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of plants that bloom during the spring [early-flowering, late-spring-blooming, spring-blooming, spring-flowering]</p><p><b>biljaka koje cvjetaju u proljeće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of plants that bloom during the spring [early-blooming, late-spring-blooming, spring-blooming, spring-flowering]</p><p><b>sat vremena rano ujutro. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an hour early in the morning</p><p><b>-Bio sam malo rano. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being somewhat early</