.</i> of the eastern part of a city e.g. Manhattan</p><p><b>k istoku, ka istoku, E, istok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cardinal compass point that is at 90 degrees [E, due east, east]</p><p><i>adj.</i> moving toward the east [eastbound]</p><p><i>adv.</i> toward the east [eastwards]</p><p><b>k istoku, ka istoku (od &quot;eastward&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> toward the east [eastward]</p><p><b>blago nagnut, jednostavan, kratka stanka pri veslanju, lagan, lagodan, lak, lako, miran, nesmetan, olako, olakšavajući, polako, udoban, ugodan, jednostavno, lagano, olakšavajućeg, prost</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> posing no difficulty</p><p><i>adj.</i> not hurried or forced [easygoing, leisurely]</p><p><i>adj.</i> free from worry or anxiety</p><p><i>adj.</i> affording pleasure</p><p><i>adj.</i> having little impact [gentle, soft]</p><p><i>adj.</i> readily exploited or tricked</p><p><i>adj.</i> in fortunate circumstances financially [comfortable, prosperous, well-fixed, well-heeled, well-off, well-situated, well-to-do]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by moderate steepness [gentle]</p><p><i>adj.</i> affording comfort</p><p><i>adj.</i> casual and unrestrained in sexual behavior [light, loose, promiscuous, sluttish, wanton]</p><p><i>adj.</i> less in demand and therefore readily obtainable</p><p><i>adj.</i> obtained with little effort or sacrifice, often obtained illegally</p><p><i>adv.</i> with ease (`easy' is sometimes used informally for `easily') [easily]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without speed (`slow' is sometimes used informally for `slowly') [slow, slowly, tardily]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a relaxed manner [soft]</p><p><b>naslonjač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a comfortable upholstered armchair [lounge chair, overstuffed chair]</p><p><b>lagodan, laka hoda, lakonog, lakouman, uviđavan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> easy unobstructed progress [clear sailing, plain sailing]</p><p><b>max</b></p><p><i>n.</i> street names for gamma hydroxybutyrate [Georgia home boy, goop, grievous bodily harm, liquid ecstasy, max, scoop, soap]</p>