p><p><i>n.</i> the repetition of a sound resulting from reflection of the sound waves [replication, reverberation, sound reflection]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) a nymph who was spurned by Narcissus and pined away until only her voice remained</p><p><i>n.</i> a reply that repeats what has just been said</p><p><i>n.</i> a reflected television or radio or radar beam</p><p><i>n.</i> a close parallel of a feeling, idea, style, etc.</p><p><i>n.</i> an imitation or repetition</p><p><i>v.</i> to say again or imitate [repeat]</p><p><i>v.</i> ring or echo with sound [resound, reverberate, ring]</p><p><i>v.</i> call to mind [recall]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an enclosed space for producing reverberation of a sound</p><p><b>dubinomjer, dubinomer, sonar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument that sends out an acoustic pulse in water and measures distances in terms of the time for the echo of the pulse to return [asdic, sonar]</p><p><b>određivanje lokacije nečega mjerenjem vremena potrebno za povratak odjeka iz nje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> determining the location of something by measuring the time it takes for an echo to return from it [echolocation]</p><p><b>EKG, ekokardiogram</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graphical image of the heart produced by an echocardiograph</p><p><b>ultrazvuk koji stvara sliku srca i njegovih abnormalnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sonograph that creates an image of the heart and its abnormalities</p><p><b>ehokardiografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a noninvasive diagnostic procedure that uses ultrasound to study to structure and motions of the heart</p><p><b>ekoencefalogram</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graphical image of the brain produced by an echoencephalograph</p><p><b>ultrazvuk koji stvara sliku mozga i njegovih abnormalnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sonograph that creates an image of the brain and its abnormalities</p><p><b>neinvazivni dijagnostički postupak koji koristi ultrazvuk za proučavanje anatomije mozga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a noninvasive diagnostic procedure that uses ultrasound to study the anatomy of the brain</p><p><b>Slika strukture koja se proizvodi ultrazvukom (odrazovi visokončanih zvučnih valova) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an image of a structure that is produced by ultrasonography (reflections of high-frequency sound waves) [sonogram]</p><p><b>ehografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> using the reflections of high-frequency sound waves to construct an image of a body organ (a sonogram) [sonography, ultrasonography, ultrasound]</p><p><b>jeka, lažni cilj, odjek, odjekivati, odziv, eho, krat. Humanitarian Aid Office, ECHO (od &quot;echo&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of words) formed in imitation of a natural sound [imitative, onomatopoeic, onomatopoeical, onomatopoetic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> like or characteristic of an echo [echolike]</p><p><b>jeka, lažni cilj, odjek, odjekivati, odziv, eho, krat. Humanitarian Aid Office, ECHO (od &quot;echo&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of sounds) repeating by reflection [reechoing]</p><p><b>ponavljanje zvukova koje su izgovorili drugi, (psihijatrija) mehaničko i besmisleno ponavljanje riječi druge osobe (kao u shizofreniji) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infant's repetition of sounds uttered by others</p><p><i>n.</i> (psychiatry) mechanical and meaningless repetition of the words of another person (as in schizophrenia)</p><p><b>koji nema ili ne stvara odjek (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or producing no echo</p><p><b>sličnost ili karakteristika odjeka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> like or characteristic of an echo [echoic]</p><p><b>određivanje lokacije nečega mjerenjem vremena potrebno za povratak odjeka iz nje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> determining the location of something by measuring the time it takes for an echo to return from it [echo sounding]</p><p><b>bilo koji od grupa virusa povezanih s različitim bolestima uključujući virusni meningitis i blage respiratorne bolesti i proljev kod novorođenčadi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a group of viruses associated with various diseases including viral meningitis and mild respiratory disorders and diarrhea in newborn infants</p><p><b>prav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not fake or counterfeit [genuine]</p><p><b>njemački katolički teolog koji se neumorno suprotstavljao Martin Lutheru (1486-1543) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a German Roman Catholic theologian who was an indefatigable opponent of Martin Luther (1486-1543) [Johann Eck, Johann Maier, Johann Maier Eck]</p><p><b>Njemački rimokatolički teolog i mističar (1260-1327) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German Roman Catholic theologian and mystic (1260-1327) [Johannes Eckhart, Meister Eckhart]</p><p><b>duge kreme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> oblong cream puff</p><p><b>eklampsija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic condition characterized by convulsions and possibly coma during or immediately after pregnancy</p><p><b>izvjesnost, uspjeh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enthusiastic approval [acclaim, acclamation, plaudit, plaudits]</p><p><i>n.</i> ceremonial elegance and splendor [pomp]</p><p><i>n.</i> brilliant or conspicuous success or effect</p><p><b>eklektičan, eklektik, ekletički</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who selects according to the eclectic method [eclecticist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> selecting what seems best of various styles or ideas</p><p><b>eklekticizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> making decisions on the basis of what seems best instead of following some single doctrine or style [eclecticism]</p><p><b>eklekticizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> making decisions on the basis of what seems best instead of following some single doctrine or style [eclectic method]</p><p><b>netko tko bira prema eklektičnoj metodi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who selects according to the eclectic method [eclectic]</p><p><b>eklipsa, pomračenje, pomrčina, zasjeniti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one celestial body obscures another [occultation]</p><p><i>v.</i> be greater in significance than [dominate, overshadow]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause an eclipse of (a celestial body) by intervention [occult]</p><p><b>elipsa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> omission or suppression of parts of words or sentences [ellipsis]</p><p><b>ekliptičan, ekliptika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the great circle representing the apparent annual path of the sun</p><p><b>ekloga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short poem descriptive of rural or pastoral life [bucolic, idyl, idyll]</p><p><b>"elektronsko ratovanje" je elektronsko ratovanje koje se vodi radi sprečavanja ili smanjenja učinkovite upotrebe elektromagnetnog spektra od strane neprijatelja; (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electronic warfare undertaken to prevent or reduce an enemy's effective use of the electromagnetic spectrum [electronic countermeasures]</p><p><b>nasilje koje se provodi radi ostvarivanja političkih ili društvenih ciljeva zaštitnika okoliša (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> violence carried out to further the political or social objectives of the environmentalists [ecological terrorism, ecological warfare, ecoterrorism]</p><p><b>korištenje tehničkog jezika ekologije kako bi korisnik izgledao ekološki svjesno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> using the technical language of ecology to make the user seem ecologically aware</p><p><b>ekološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by the interdependence of living organisms in an environment [ecological]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the science of ecology [bionomic, bionomical, ecological]</p><p><b>ekološki, ekoloških, prirodan, prirodnih, ekološka, ekološke</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by the interdependence of living organisms in an environment [ecologic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the science of ecology [bionomic, bionomical, ecologic]</p><p><b>(ekologija) status organizma u njegovoj okoliši i zajednici (koji utječe na njegov opstanak kao vrste) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (ecology) the status of an organism within its environment and community (affecting its survival as a species) [niche]</p><p><b>ekološka sukcesija, sukcesija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (ecology) the gradual and orderly process of change in an ecosystem brought about by the progressive replacement of one community by another until a stable climax is established [succession]</p><p><b>nasilje koje se provodi radi ostvarivanja političkih ili društvenih ciljeva zaštitnika okoliša (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> violence carried out to further the political or social objectives of the environmentalists [eco-warfare, ecological warfare, ecoterrorism]</p><p><b>nasilje koje se provodi radi ostvarivanja političkih ili društvenih ciljeva zaštitnika okoliša (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> violence carried out to further the political or social objectives of the environmentalists [eco-warfare, ecological terrorism, ecoterrorism]</p><p><b>u ekološkom smislu</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to ecology</p><p><b>ekolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a biologist who studies the relation between organisms and their environment</p><p><b>ekologija, okoliš, zaštita okoliša</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the environment as it relates to living organisms</p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of biology concerned with the relations between organisms and their environment [bionomics, environmental science]</p><p><b>ekonometrijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to econometrics</p><p><b>ekonomista koji koristi statističke i matematičke metode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economist who uses statistical and mathematical methods [econometrist]</p><p><b>ekonometrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the application of mathematics and statistics to the study of economic and financial data</p><p><b>ekonomista koji koristi statističke i matematičke metode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economist who uses statistical and mathematical methods [econometrician]</p><p><b>ekonomski, gospodarski, privredni, štedljiv, ekonomska, ekonomske, ekonomskih, ekonomsko, gospodarska, gospodarske, gospodarski sustav, gospodarskih, gospodarskog, gospodarskoj, gospodarskom, privredno, čuvaran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an economy, the system of production and management of material wealth [economical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the science of economics</p><p><i>adj.</i> using the minimum of time or resources necessary for effectiveness [economical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with worldly necessities of life (especially money)</p><p><i>adj.</i> financially rewarding</p><p><b>ekonomska pomoć</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gift of money or other material help to support a person or cause [aid, assistance, economic assistance, financial aid, financial assistance]</p><p><b>Stalno vijeće Ujedinjenih naroda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a permanent council of the United Nations [ECOSOC]</p><p><b>Komisija Gospodarskog i socijalnog vijeća Ujedinjenih naroda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a commission of the Economic and Social Council of the United Nations [ECOSOC commission]</p><p><b>gospodarska pomoć</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gift of money or other material help to support a person or cause [aid, assistance, economic aid, financial aid, financial assistance]</p><p><b>Komisija Ekonomskog i socijalnog vijeća Ujedinjenih naroda koja se bavi ekonomskim razvojem afričkih naroda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the commission of the Economic and Social Council of the United Nations that is concerned with economic development of African nations</p><p><b>Komisija Ekonomskog i socijalnog vijeća Ujedinjenih naroda koja se bavi ekonomskim razvojem zemalja Azije i Dalekog istoka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the commission of the Economic and Social Council of the United Nations that is concerned with economic development of countries in Asia and the Far East</p><p><b>Komisija Ekonomskog i socijalnog vijeća Ujedinjenih naroda koja se bavi ekonomskim razvojem u Europi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the commission of the Economic and Social Council of the United Nations that is concerned with economic development in Europe</p><p><b>Komisija Ekonomskog i socijalnog vijeća Ujedinjenih naroda koja se bavi ekonomskim razvojem u Latinskoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the commission of the Economic and Social Council of the United Nations that is concerned with economic development in Latin America</p><p><b>stanje gospodarstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of the economy</p><p><b>konzumacija, korištenje, potrošnja, trošenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (economics) the utilization of economic goods to satisfy needs or in manufacturing [consumption, usance, use, use of goods and services]</p><p><b>ekonomska kriza, gospodarska kriza, kriza, recesija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long-term economic state characterized by unemployment and low prices and low levels of trade and investment [depression, slump]</p><p><b>ekonomist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert in the science of economics [economist]</p><p><b>ekonomska geografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of geography concerned with the production and distribution of commodities</p><p><b>grana geologije koja se bavi ekonomski vrijednim geološkim materijalima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of geology that deals with economically valuable geological materials</p><p><b>ekonomski rast, gospodarski rast</b></p><p><i>n.</i> steady growth in the productive capacity of the economy (and so a growth of national income)</p><p><b>slobodnička osoba koja se zalaže za maksimiziranje individualnih prava i minimiziranje uloge države (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a libertarian who advocates maximizing individual rights and minimizing the role of the state</p><p><b>mobilizacija gospodarstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mobilization of the economy [economic mobilization]</p><p><b>mobilizacija gospodarstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mobilization of the economy [economic mobilisation]</p><p><b>ekonomska politika, gospodarska politika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government policy for maintaining economic growth and tax revenues</p><p><b>ekonomski proces</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any process affecting the production and development and management of material wealth</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve proizvode koji se proizvode u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje odredba o proizvodnji za proizvodnju za koje se primjenjuje odredba o proizvodnji za koje se primjenjuje odredba o proizvodnji za koje se primjenjuje odredba o proizvodnji za koje se primjenjuje odredba o proizvodnji za koje se primjenjuje odredba o proizvodnji za koje se primjenjuje odredba o proizvodnji za koje se primjenjuje odredba o proizvod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the return derived from cultivated land in excess of that derived from the poorest land cultivated under similar conditions [rent]</p><p><b>ekonomija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of social science that deals with the production and distribution and consumption of goods and services and their management [economics, political economy]</p><p><b>kazna grupe prekidom poslovnih odnosa s njom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> punishment of a group by cutting off commercial dealings with them</p><p><b>ekonomski sustav, gospodarski sustav, ekonomija, ekonomski sistem, gospodarstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of production and distribution and consumption [economy]</p><p><b>ekonomska teorija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (economics) a theory of commercial activities (such as the production and consumption of goods)</p><p><b>ekonomska vrijednost, vrijednost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount (of money or goods or services) that is considered to be a fair equivalent for something else [value]</p><p><b>čuvaran, ekonomičan, ekonomičniji, ekonomski, ekonomsko, gospodarski, rentabilan, štedljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> using the minimum of time or resources necessary for effectiveness [economic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an economy, the system of production and management of material wealth [economic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> avoiding waste [frugal, scotch, sparing, stinting]</p><p><b>ekonomski</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to economic science</p><p><i>adv.</i> in an economical manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to the economic system</p><p><b>ekonomičnost, ekonomija, e