i se medicinski koristi za kelatiranje metalnih iona u slučajevima trovanja olovom ili teškim metalima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a complex molecule used medically to chelate metal ions in cases of lead or heavy metal poisoning [ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid]</p><p><b>Njemački organski kemičar koji je proučavao alkoholnu fermentaciju i otkrio zimase (1860-1917) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German organic chemist who studied alcoholic fermentation and discovered zymase (1860-1917) [Buchner]</p><p><b>izučiti, naobraziti se, obrazovati, odgajati, odgojiti, školovati, učiti, educirati, izobraziti, izobražavati, naobraziti, naobražavati, podučavati, podučiti, poučavati, poučiti, pripremati, razvijati, trenirati, civilizirati, kultivirati, prosvijetiti, rafinirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give an education to</p><p><i>v.</i> create by training and teaching [develop, prepare, train]</p><p><i>v.</i> teach or refine to be discriminative in taste or judgment [civilise, civilize, cultivate, school, train]</p><p><b>naobražen, obrazovan, obrazovani, obrazovanog, odgojen, školovan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> possessing an education (especially having more than average knowledge)</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by full comprehension of the problem involved [enlightened]</p><p><b>student, učenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a learner who is enrolled in an educational institution [pupil, student]</p><p><b>edukacija, izobrazba, naobrazba, nastava, obrazovanje, odgajanje, odgoj, odgoj i obrazovanje, pedagogija, prosvjeta, školovanje, školstvo, edukacijom, naobrazbi, obrazovanja, odgojem, prosvjete, školstva, obrazovanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activities of educating or instructing [didactics, educational activity, instruction, pedagogy, teaching]</p><p><i>n.</i> knowledge acquired by learning and instruction</p><p><i>n.</i> the gradual process of acquiring knowledge</p><p><i>n.</i> the profession of teaching (especially at a school or college or university)</p><p><i>n.</i> the result of good upbringing (especially knowledge of correct social behavior) [breeding, training]</p><p><i>n.</i> the United States federal department that administers all federal programs dealing with education (including federal aid to educational institutions and students) [Department of Education, Education Department]</p><p><b>savezni odjel Sjedinjenih Država koji upravlja svim saveznim programima koji se bave obrazovanjem (uključujući savezne pomoći obrazovnim ustanovama i studentima) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the United States federal department that administers all federal programs dealing with education (including federal aid to educational institutions and students) [Department of Education, Education]</p><p><b>osoba koja je sekretar Ministarstva obrazovanja, poziciju šefa Odjela za obrazovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the person who holds the secretaryship of the Department of Education [Secretary of Education]</p><p><i>n.</i> the position of the head of the Education Department [Secretary of Education]</p><p><b>nastavni, obrazovan, obrazovni, obrazovnim, obrazovnog, odgojni, prosvjetne, prosvjetni, školstvo, obrazovna, prosvjeta, prosvjete, prosvjetu, edukacijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the process of education</p><p><i>adj.</i> providing knowledge</p><p><b>aktivnosti edukacije ili poučavanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activities of educating or instructing [didactics, education, instruction, pedagogy, teaching]</p><p><b>odgojno-obrazovna ustanova, obrazovna institucija, obrazovna ustanova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an institution dedicated to education</p><p><b>Program za pružanje obrazovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a program for providing education</p><p><b>stručnjak za teoriju obrazovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in the theory of education [educationist]</p><p><b>nastavni, obrazovan, obrazovni, obrazovnim, obrazovnog, odgojni, prosvjetne, prosvjetni, školstvo, obrazovna, prosvjeta, prosvjete, prosvjetu (od &quot;educational&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an educational manner</p><p><b>stručnjak za teoriju obrazovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in the theory of education [educationalist]</p><p><b>nastavni, obrazovni, odgojni, prosvjetni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resulting in education</p><p><b>nastavnik, odgajatelj, odgojitelj, pedagog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who educates young people [pedagog, pedagogue]</p><p><b>razvijati, proizlaziti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> deduce (a principle) or construe (a meaning) [draw out, elicit, evoke, extract]</p><p><i>v.</i> develop or evolve from a latent or potential state [derive]</p><p><b>zasladiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make sweeter in taste [dulcify, dulcorate, sweeten]</p><p><b>obrazovanje i zabava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> entertainment that is intended to be educational</p><p><b>Edvard Grieg</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Norwegian composer whose work was often inspired by Norwegian folk music (1843-1907) [Edvard Hagerup Grieg, Grieg]</p><p><b>Edvard Grieg</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Norwegian composer whose work was often inspired by Norwegian folk music (1843-1907) [Edvard Grieg, Grieg]</p><p><b>Norveški slikar (1863-1944) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Norwegian painter (1863-1944) [Munch]</p><p><b>Kralj Engleske i Irske 1936., Kralj Engleske od 1901. do 1910., Kralj Engleske i Irske od 1547. do 1553., Kralj Engleske koji je krunisan u dobi od 13 godina nakon smrti svog oca Edwarda IV. ali je odmah bio zatvoren u Londonskom tornju gdje su on i njegov mlađi brat ubijeni (1470-1483), Kralj Engleske od 1461. do 1470. i od 1471. do 1483., sin Edwarda II i kralj Engleske od 1327-1377, Kralj Engleske od 1307. do 1327. i sin Edwarda I., Kralj Engleske od 1272. do 1307., treći sin Elizabete II. (rođen 1964.), sin Edwarda III. koji je porazio Francuze u Crecyju i Poitiersu u Stogodišnjem ratu (1330-1376) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> King of England and Ireland in 1936 [Duke of Windsor, Edward VIII]</p><p><i>n.</i> King of England from 1901 to 1910 [Albert Edward, Edward VII]</p><p><i>n.</i> King of England and Ireland fro