>Gornji dio je od gromastih biljaka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coarse annual grass having fingerlike spikes of flowers [goose grass, wire grass, yard grass, yardgrass]</p><p><b>aromatska kora od cascarille (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic bark of cascarilla [cascarilla bark, sweetwood bark]</p><p><b>potpuno kopnene žabe pljačkaše (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> completely terrestrial robber frogs [genus Eleutherodactylus]</p><p><b>dići, dignuti, oplemeniti, podići, podignuti, podizati, unaprijediti, uzdići, promaknuti, promicati, promovirati, unapređivati, ustoličiti, uzdignuti, uzdizati, dizati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give a promotion to or assign to a higher position [advance, kick upstairs, promote, raise, upgrade]</p><p><i>v.</i> raise from a lower to a higher position [bring up, get up, lift, raise]</p><p><i>v.</i> raise in rank or condition [lift, raise]</p><p><b>povišen, povišenog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a railway that is powered by electricity and that runs on a track that is raised above the street level [el, elevated railroad, elevated railway, overhead railway]</p><p><i>adj.</i> raised above the ground</p><p><i>adj.</i> of high moral or intellectual value [exalted, grand, high-flown, high-minded, idealistic, lofty, noble-minded, rarefied, rarified, sublime]</p><p><i>adj.</i> increased in amount or degree [raised]</p><p><b>željeznička pruga koja se napaja električnom energijom i koja ide po traci koja je podignuta iznad razine ulice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a railway that is powered by electricity and that runs on a track that is raised above the street level [el, elevated, elevated railway, overhead railway]</p><p><b>željeznička pruga koja se napaja električnom energijom i koja ide po traci koja je podignuta iznad razine ulice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a railway that is powered by electricity and that runs on a track that is raised above the street level [el, elevated, elevated railroad, overhead railway]</p><p><b>dizanje, elevacija, nagib, podignuće, povišenje, uzdignuće, uzdizanje, uzvišenje, visina, ALT, EL, altituda, uzvisina, ustoličenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the event of something being raised upward [lift, raising]</p><p><i>n.</i> the highest level or degree attainable [acme, height, meridian, peak, pinnacle, summit, superlative, tiptop, top]</p><p><i>n.</i> angular distance above the horizon (especially of a celestial object) [ALT, EL, altitude]</p><p><i>n.</i> a raised or elevated geological formation [natural elevation]</p><p><i>n.</i> distance of something above a reference point (such as sea level)</p><p><i>n.</i> (ballet) the height of a dancer's leap or jump</p><p><i>n.</i> drawing of an exterior of a structure</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of increasing the wealth or prestige or power or scope of something [aggrandisement, aggrandizement]</p><p><b>dizalica, dizalo, elevator, lift, osobno dizalo, podizač, silos, visinsko kormilo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lifting device consisting of a platform or cage that is raised and lowered mechanically in a vertical shaft in order to move people from one floor to another in a building [lift]</p><p><i>n.</i> the airfoil on the tailplane of an aircraft that makes it ascend or descend</p><p><b>čovjek zaposlen za rad na liftu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man employed to operate an elevator [elevator man, liftman]</p><p><b>gdje putnici jašu gore i dolje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> where passengers ride up and down [car]</p><p><b>Djevojka koja radi na liftu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a girl employed to operate an elevator</p><p><b>čovjek zaposlen za rad na liftu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man employed to operate an elevator [elevator boy, liftman]</p><p><b>Operator dizala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an operator of an elevator</p><p><b>vertikalni otvor u zgradi koji omogućuje prolaz dizala s sprata na sprat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vertical shaft in a building to permit the passage of an elevator from floor to floor</p><p><b>jedanaest</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cardinal number that is the sum of ten and one [11, XI]</p><p><i>n.</i> a team that plays football [football team]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being one more than ten [11, xi]</p><p><b>(bivši u Britaniji) ispit koji su 11 i 12 godina stari učenici uzimali za odabir odgovarajućih kandidata za osnovnu školu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (formerly in Britain) an examination taken by 11 and 12 year old students to select suitable candidates for grammar school [11-plus]</p><p><b>s jedanaest strana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having eleven sides</p><p><b>jedanaesti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> position 11 in a countable series of things</p><p><i>adj.</i> coming next after the tenth and just before the twelfth in position [11th]</p><p><b>nastaje iz dva skupa korijena (kranijalnog i kičmenog) koji se ujedine u nervu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> arises from two sets of roots (cranial and spinal) that unite to form the nerve [accessory nerve, nervus accessorius, spinal accessory]</p><p><b>Najkasniji mogući trenutak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the latest possible moment [last minute]</p><p><b>patuljak, vilenjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (folklore) fairies that are somewhat mischievous [brownie, gremlin, hob, imp, pixie, pixy]</p><p><i>n.</i> below 3 kilohertz [extremely low frequency]</p><p><b>Apotekijum gljivice iz obitelji Pezizaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> apothecium of a fungus of the family Pezizaceae</p><p><b>dijete, đavolak, đavolast, patuljak, patuljast, vilinski, zloban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suggestive of an elf in strangeness and otherworldliness [fey]</p><p><i>adj.</i> small and delicate [elflike]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or made or done by or as if by an elf</p><p><i>adj.</i> usually good-naturedly mischievous [elfish, elvish]</p><p><b>pakostan, poput đavolka, poput patuljka, vragolast, vraški, zloban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> usually good-naturedly mischievous [elfin, elvish]</p><p><b>Mali i osjetljivi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> small and delicate [elfin]</p><p><b>Britanski skladatelj zbornih i orkestarskih djela uključujući dvije simfonije, kao