u Engleskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> born in England [Endicott, John Endecott, John Endicott]</p><p><b>okončan, završen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having come or been brought to a conclusion [all over, complete, concluded, over, terminated]</p><p><b>endemičan, endemične, endemski, ograničen na neko područje, endemske, endemsku, endem, autohton, domaći, urođen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease that is constantly present to a greater or lesser degree in people of a certain class or in people living in a particular location [endemic disease]</p><p><i>n.</i> a plant that is native to a certain limited area</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a disease (or anything resembling a disease) constantly present to greater or lesser extent in a particular locality [endemical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> native to or confined to a certain region</p><p><i>adj.</i> originating where it is found [autochthonal, autochthonic, autochthonous, indigenous]</p><p><b>endemijska bolest</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease that is constantly present to a greater or lesser degree in people of a certain class or in people living in a particular location [endemic]</p><p><b>akutna infekcija uzrokovana riketsijom i prenosi se ugrizem zaražene buhe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acute infection caused by rickettsia and transmitted by the bite of an infected flea [murine typhus, rat typhus, urban typhus]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s bolešću (ili bilo čim slično bolesti) koja je stalno prisutna u većoj ili manjoj mjeri na određenom mjestu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a disease (or anything resembling a disease) constantly present to greater or lesser extent in a particular locality [endemic]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, država članica može odrediti da se u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka primjenjuje sljedeće: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nativeness by virtue of originating or occurring naturally (as in a particular place) [autochthony, indigenousness]</p><p><b>područje Antarktika između zemlje Queen Maud i zemlje Wilkes (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a region of Antarctica between Queen Maud Land and Wilkes Land</p><p><b>(biohemija) procesa koji prati ili zahtijeva apsorpciju energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (biochemistry) of a process accompanied by or requiring the absorption of energy</p><p><b>djelovanje kroz kožu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> acting by absorption through the skin [endermic]</p><p><b>djelovanje kroz kožu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> acting by absorption through the skin [endermatic]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2., posljednje faze partije šaha nakon što je većina komada uklonjena sa ploče (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the final stages of an extended process of negotiation [end game]</p><p><i>n.</i> the final stages of a chess game after most of the pieces have been removed from the board [end game]</p><p><b>Rođen u Engleskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> born in England [Endecott, John Endecott, John Endicott]</p><p><b>ekstremitet, kraj, nastavak, okončanja, okončanje, okončavanje, svršetak, završavanje, završetak, dočetak, završetak riječi, prekid, prestanak, zaključivanje, istek, konac, zaključak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the end of a word (a suffix or inflectional ending or final morpheme) [termination]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of ending something [conclusion, termination]</p><p><i>n.</i> the point in time at which something ends [end]</p><p><i>n.</i> event whose occurrence ends something [conclusion, finish]</p><p><i>n.</i> the last section of a communication [close, closing, conclusion, end]</p><p><b>salata cikorija, salata-cikorija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated herb with leaves valued as salad green [Cichorium endivia, witloof]</p><p><i>n.</i> variety of endive having leaves with irregular frilled edges [chicory escarole, escarole]</p><p><b>beskonačan, beskrajan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tiresomely long [eternal, interminable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> infinitely great in number</p><p><i>adj.</i> having no known beginning and presumably no end [dateless, sempiternal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the ends united so as to form a continuous whole</p><p><b>beskrajno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> continuing forever without end [infinitely]</p><p><i>adv.</i> with unflagging resolve [ceaselessly, continuously, incessantly, unceasingly, unendingly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> (spatial sense) seeming to have no bounds</p><p><i>adv.</i> all the time [interminably]</p><p><b>beskonačan, beskrajan (od &quot;endless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being (or seeming to be) without end</p><p><b>unutarnji sloj klice koji se razvija u sluznicu probavnog i respiratornog sustava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inner germ layer that develops into the lining of the digestive and respiratory systems [endoderm, entoblast, entoderm, hypoblast]</p><p><b>endokarditis, upala srčane opne</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the endocardium and heart valves</p><p><b>membrana koja obložava šupljine srca i čini dio srčanih zalisaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the membrane that lines the cavities of the heart and forms part of the heart valves</p><p><b>unutrašnji sloj usplođa, košpica, koštica, špica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the hard inner (usually woody) layer of the pericarp of some fruits (as peaches or plums or cherries or olives) that contains the seed [pit, stone]</p><p><b>ispunjava gramatiku jedne od njegovih sastavnih dijelova (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> fulfilling the grammatical role of one of its constituents</p><p><b>upale sluznice materničnog vrata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the mucous lining of the uterine cervix</p><p><b>membrana koja obložava unutrašnjost lubanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> membrane lining the inside of the skull</p><p><b>od ili pripadaju endokrinim žlijezdama ili njihovim izlučcima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or belonging to endocrine glands or their secretions [endocrine]</p><p><b>hormon, hormoni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the secretion of an endocrine gland that is transmitted by the blood to the tissue on which it has a specific effect [hormone, internal secretion]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of the glands of the endocrine system that secrete hormones directly into the bloodstream [ductless gland, endocrine gland]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or belonging to endocrine glands or their secretions [endocrinal]</p><p><b>bilo koja žlijezda endokrinog sustava koja izlučuje hormone izravno u krvotok (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the glands of the endocrine system that secrete hormones directly into the bloodstream [ductless gland, endocrine]</p><p><b>endokrini sustav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of glands that produce endocrine secretions that help to control bodily metabolic activity</p><p><b>liječnik koji se specijalizira za dijagnozu i liječenje stanja koja utječu na endokrini sustav (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> physician who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of conditions affecting the endocrine system</p><p><b>endokrinologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of medicine dealing with the endocrine glands and their secretions</p><p><b>unutarnji sloj klice koji se razvija u sluznicu probavnog i respiratornog sustava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inner germ layer that develops into the lining of the digestive and respiratory systems [endoblast, entoblast, entoderm, hypoblast]</p><p><b>endodoncija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of dentistry dealing with diseases of the dental pulp [endodontics]</p><p><b>za ili u vezi s endodoncijom ili s njome ili s njome povezanim ili s njome obavljanim radom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or involving or practicing endodontics</p><p><b>endodoncija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of dentistry dealing with diseases of the dental pulp [endodontia]</p><p><b>zubar specijaliziran za bolesti zubne pulpe i živca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dentist specializing in diseases of the dental pulp and nerve</p><p><b>(nuklearne reakcije) koja se događa s apsorpcijom energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a nuclear reaction) occurring with absorpti