zling]</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling an oracle in obscurity of thought [oracular]</p><p><b>kanon u kojem su ulazi u uzastopne dijelove označeni kriptičnim simbolima i uređajima (popularno u 15. i 16. stoljeću) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a canon in which the entrances of successive parts were indicated by cryptic symbols and devices (popular in the 15th and 16th centuries) [enigma canon, enigmatical canon, riddle canon]</p><p><b>Ne razumijem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not clear to the understanding [enigmatic, puzzling]</p><p><b>kanon u kojem su ulazi u uzastopne dijelove označeni kriptičnim simbolima i uređajima (popularno u 15. i 16. stoljeću) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a canon in which the entrances of successive parts were indicated by cryptic symbols and devices (popular in the 15th and 16th centuries) [enigma canon, enigmatic canon, riddle canon]</p><p><b>Na tajni način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a cryptic manner [cryptically, mysteriously]</p><p><b>Atol na Marshallskim otocima., Drugi svjetski rat (februar 1944) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an atoll in the Marshall Islands</p><p><i>n.</i> World War II (February 1944)</p><p><b>nastavak sintaksne jedinice iz jednog stiha u sljedeći bez pauze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the continuation of a syntactic unit from one line of verse into the next line without a pause [enjambment]</p><p><b>nastavak sintaksne jedinice iz jednog stiha u sljedeći bez pauze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the continuation of a syntactic unit from one line of verse into the next line without a pause [enjambement]</p><p><b>naložiti, narediti, propisati, zabraniti, zapovijedati, nalagati, naređivati, reći, zapovjediti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> issue an injunction</p><p><i>v.</i> give instructions to or direct somebody to do something with authority [order, say, tell]</p><p><b>naložiti, narediti, propisati, zabraniti, zapovijedati (od &quot;enjoin&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a judicial remedy issued in order to prohibit a party from doing or continuing to do a certain activity [cease and desist order, enjoinment, injunction]</p><p><b>(zakon) pravni lijek koji se izdaje kako bi se stranci zabranila obavljanje ili nastavak obavljanja određene djelatnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a judicial remedy issued in order to prohibit a party from doing or continuing to do a certain activity [cease and desist order, enjoining, injunction]</p><p><b>doživjeti, gustirati, imati, naslađivati se, radovati se, uživati, zabavljati se, uživajte, uživaju, voljeti, doživljavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> derive or receive pleasure from [bask, relish, savor, savour]</p><p><i>v.</i> have benefit from</p><p><i>v.</i> get pleasure from [love]</p><p><i>v.</i> have for one's benefit</p><p><i>v.</i> take delight in [delight, revel]</p><p><b>prijatan, ugodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affording satisfaction or pleasure [gratifying, pleasurable]</p><p><b>prijatan (od &quot;enjoyable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pleasantness resulting from something that can be enjoyed</p><p><b>ugodan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an enjoyable manner [agreeably, pleasantly]</p><p><b>doživjeti, gustirati, imati, naslađivati se, radovati se, uživati, zabavljati se, uživajte, uživaju (od &quot;enjoy&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who delights in having or using or experiencing something</p><p><b>naslada, užitak, uživanje, zadovoljstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the pleasure felt when having a good time</p><p><i>n.</i> act of receiving pleasure from something [delectation]</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) the exercise of the legal right to enjoy the benefits of owning property [use]</p><p><b>antiaritmički lijek (trgovinski naziv Enkaid) koji se koristi za liječenje životno opasnih aritmija, ali povećava rizik od iznenadne smrti kod pacijenata s srčanim udarom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antiarrhythmic drug (trade name Enkaid) used to treat life-threatening arrhythmias but increases the risk of sudden death in heart attack patients [encainide]</p><p><b>enkefalin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an endorphin having opiate qualities that occurs in the brain and spinal cord and elsewhere</p><p><b>Bog vode i bog mudrosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> water god and god of wisdom</p><p><b>Legendarni prijatelj Gilgamiša. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> legendary friend of Gilgamish</p><p><b>potpaliti, raspaliti, uzbuditi, zapaliti, buditi, izazivati, izazvati, pobuditi, pobuđivati, podjariti, potaknuti, potaći, poticati, probuditi, raspaljivati, raspiriti, rasplamsati, rasplamsavati, razbuktati, razbuktavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to start burning [conflagrate, inflame, kindle]</p><p><i>v.</i> call forth (emotions, feelings, and responses) [arouse, elicit, evoke, fire, kindle, provoke, raise]</p><p><b>zapalio (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> set afire [ignited, kindled]</p><p><b>upalna komplikacija guba koja rezultira bolnim kožnim oštećenjima na rukama, nogama i licu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inflammatory complication of leprosy that results in painful skin lesions on the arms and legs and face [erythema nodosum leprosum]</p><p><b>preplitati se, oplesti, plesti, preplesti, viti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> spin, wind, or twist together [entwine, interlace, intertwine, lace, twine]</p><p><b>povećati, povećati se, proširiti, uvećati, povećavati, uvećavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make larger</p><p><i>v.</i> make large [blow up, magnify]</p><p><i>v.</i> become larger or bigger</p><p><i>v.</i> add details, as to an account or idea [dilate, elaborate, expand, expatiate, exposit, expound, flesh out, lucubrate]</p><p><b>povećan, uvećan, uvećanom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of an organ or body part) excessively enlarged as a result of increased size in the constituent cells [hypertrophied]</p><p><i>adj.</i> as of a photograph [blown-up]</p><p><i>adj.</i> larger than normal</p><p><i>adj.</i> enlarged to an abnormal degree [exaggerated, magnified]</p><p><b>abnormalno proširenje srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal enlargement of the heart [cardiomegaly, megacardia, megalocardia]</p><p><b>povećana slika, povećanje, povećavanje, proširenje, uvećanje, ekspanzija, proširivanje, širenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of increasing (something) in size or volume or quantity or scope [expansion]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being enlarged</p><p><i>n.</i> a discussion that provides additional information [elaboration, expansion]</p><p><i>n.</i> a photographic print that has been enlarged [blowup, magnification]</p><p><b>povećati, povećati se, proširiti, uvećati (od &quot;enlarge&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> photographic equipment consisting of an optical projector used to enlarge a photograph</p><p><b>osvijetliti, prosvijetiti, prosvijetliti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make understand [edify]</p><p><i>v.</i> give spiritual insight to [irradiate]</p><p><i>v.</i> make free from confusion or ambiguity [clear, clear up, crystalise, crystalize, crystallise, crystallize, elucidate, illuminate, shed light on, sort out, straighten out]</p><p><b>prosvijetljen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people who have been introduced to the mysteries of some field or activity [initiate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having knowledge and spiritual insight</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by full comprehension of the problem involved [educated]</p><p><b>osvijetliti, prosvijetiti, prosvijetliti (od &quot;enlighten&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to increase knowledge or dissipate ignorance [illuminating, informative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> enlightening or uplifting so as to encourage intellectual or moral improvement [edifying]</p><p><b>prosvjetiteljstvo, prosvjetiteljstva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> education that results in understanding and the spread of knowledge</p><p><i>n.</i> (Hinduism and Buddhism) the beatitude that transcends the cycle of reincarnation [nirvana]</p><p><i>n.</i> a movement in Europe from about 1650 until 1800 that advocated the use of reason and individualism instead of tradition and established doctrine [Age of Reason]</p><p><b>Bog zraka i kralj sumerskih bogova. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> god of the air and king of the Sumer