f southern Australia and Tasmania having white to rose or purple-red flowers [common heath]</p><p><b>mala uspravna grmljavina iz Australije i Tasmanije s mirisnim cvijećem slonovače (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small erect shrub of Australia and Tasmania with fragrant ivory flowers [blunt-leaf heath, common heath]</p><p><b>mala grmlja južne i zapadne Australije s ružičastim do ružičastog ljubičastog cijevastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrub of southern and western Australia having pinkish to rosy purple tubular flowers [Port Jackson heath]</p><p><b>ponavljanje nakon riječi koje su u međuvremenu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> repetition after intervening words</p><p><b>ponavljanje riječi ili fraze na početku uzastopnih rečenica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> repetition of a word or phrase at the beginning of successive clauses [anaphora]</p><p><b>recapitulacija glavnih ideja govora (posebno u obrnutom redu), ponavljanje grupe riječi u obrnutom redoslijedu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> recapitulation of the main ideas of a speech (especially in reverse order)</p><p><i>n.</i> repetition of a group of words in reverse order</p><p><b>Odmah se preformulira radi pojačanja ili opravdanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> immediate rephrasing for intensification or justification</p><p><b>biskup ili metropolita zadužen za eparhiju u Istočnoj Crkvi, guverner ili prefekt eparhije u drevnoj Grčkoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bishop or metropolitan in charge of an eparchy in the Eastern Church</p><p><i>n.</i> the governor or prefect of an eparchy in ancient Greece</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s eparhijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an eparchy</p><p><b>provincija u drevnoj Grčkoj, biskupija Istočne pravoslavne crkve (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a province in ancient Greece</p><p><i>n.</i> a diocese of the Eastern Orthodox Church [exarchate]</p><p><b>epoleta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> adornment consisting of an ornamental cloth pad worn on the shoulder [epaulet]</p><p><b>Oklop koji štiti rame (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> armor plate that protects the shoulder</p><p><b>mačevi mač sličan foliji ali s težim oštricom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fencing sword similar to a foil but with a heavier blade</p><p><b>tanka epitelna membrana koja obložava komore mozga i kanala kičmene moždine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thin epithelial membrane lining the ventricles of the brain and the spinal cord canal</p><p><b>Ustavljanje samoglasnika ili konsonanta u riječ kako bi se lakše izgovorio (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the insertion of a vowel or consonant into a word to make its pronunciation easier</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s epentezom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to epenthesis [parasitic]</p><p><b>veliki stolni središte s granatnim nositeljima za voće ili slatkiše ili cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large table centerpiece with branching holders for fruit or sweets or flowers</p><p><b>Stara hebrejska mjera suha jednaka oko bušelu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Hebrew unit of dry measure equal to about a bushel [ephah]</p><p><b>Stara hebrejska mjera suha jednaka oko bušelu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Hebrew unit of dry measure equal to about a bushel [epha]</p><p><b>čvoroviti i gotovo bez listova pustinjski grm s smanjenim listovima poput ljuske i crvenkastim mesnim sjemenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> jointed and nearly leafless desert shrub having reduced scalelike leaves and reddish fleshy seeds [joint fir]</p><p><b>Kineska efedra koja daje efedrin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chinese ephedra yielding ephedrine [mahuang]</p><p><b>Efedra: u nekim klasifikacijama uključenim u Gnetaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ephedras: in some classifications included in the Gnetaceae [family Ephedraceae]</p><p><b>Bijeli bez mirisa prah ili kristalni alkaloid iz biljaka rodova Ephedra (posebno Ephedra sinica) ili sintetički proizveden (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white odorless powdered or crystalline alkaloid from plants of the genus Ephedra (especially Ephedra sinica) or made synthetically</p><p><b>jednodnevna mušica, prolazna stvar, stvar kratka vijeka, vodeni cvijet, vrsta kukaca kratka vijeka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something transitory</p><p><b>kratkotrajan, prolazan, trenutan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anything short-lived, as an insect that lives only for a day in its winged form [ephemeron]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lasting a very short time [fugacious, passing, short-lived, transient, transitory]</p><p><b>svojstvo trajanja za vrlo kratko vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of lasting for a very short time [ephemeralness, fleetingness]</p><p><b>kratkotrajan, prolazan, trenutan (od &quot;ephemeral&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of lasting for a very short time [ephemerality, fleetingness]</p><p><b>kratkoživotni insekt (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> short-lived insect [ephemeropteran]</p><p><b>ptice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mayflies [Ephemeroptera, order Ephemerida, order Ephemeroptera]</p><p><b>ptice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mayflies [family Ephemeridae]</p><p><b>astronomski kalendar, efemeride</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an annual publication containing astronomical tables that give the positions of the celestial bodies throughout the year</p><p><b>(astronomija) mjerilo vremena definirano Zemljinim orbitalnim kretanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) a measure of time defined by Earth's orbital motion [TDT, TT, terrestrial dynamical time, terrestrial time]</p><p><b>Sve je kratkoživotno, kao što je insekt koji živi samo jedan dan u svom krilatom obliku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anything short-lived, as an insect that lives only for a day in its winged form [ephemeral]</p><p><b>ptice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mayflies [Ephemerida, order Ephemerida, order Ephemeroptera]</p><p><b>kratkoživotni insekt (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> short-lived insect [ephemerid]</p><p><b>stanovnik drevnog grčkog grada Efeza., o ili povezan s drevnim Efesom ili njegovim ljudima ili jezikom ili kulturom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a resident of the ancient Greek city of Ephesus</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to ancient Ephesus or its people or language or culture</p><p><b>Novi zavjet knjiga koja sadrži pismo Svetog Pavla Efežanima koje objašnjava božanski plan za svijet i njegovo ispunjenje u Kristu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book containing the epistle from Saint Paul to the Ephesians which explains the divine plan for the world and the consummation of this in Christ [Epistle of Paul the Apostle to the Ephesians, Epistle to the Ephesians]</p><p><b>mali moljci čije ličinke prave svilene tunele i hrane se pohranjenim hranljivim proizvodima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small moths whose larvae spin silken tunnels and feed on stored food products [genus Ephestia]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve proizvode koji sadrže: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small moth whose larvae feed on tobacco and other dried plant products [cacao moth, tobacco moth]</p><p><b>Stari grčki grad na zapadnoj obali Male Azije u današnjem Turskoj., Treći sveopšti koncil 431. godine koji je proglasio Mariju majkom Božjom i osudio Pelagija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Greek city on the western shore of Asia Minor in what is now Turkey</p><p><i>n.</i> the third ecumenical council in 431 which declared Mary as mother of God and condemned Pelagius [Council of Ephesus]</p><p><b>mala obitelj koja obuhvaća ribljake (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small family comprising the spadefishes [family Ephippidae]</p><p><b>Sjedljarke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> saddlebills [genus Ephippiorhynchus]</p><p><b>veliki crno-bijeli čvor iz tropske Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large black-and-white stork of tropical Africa [jabiru, saddlebill]</p><p><b>Inventar osobnosti o samoproglašenju temeljen na Hans Eysenckovoj faktorskoj analizi osobnosti koja pretpostavlja tri osnovna faktora (dva najvažnija su ekstroverzija u introverziju i neurotizam) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a self-report personality inventory based on Hans Eysenck's factor analysis of personality which assumes three basic factors (the two most important being extraversion to introversion and neuroticism) [Eysenck Personality Inventory]</p><p><b>ep, epski, epsko djelo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long narrative poem telling of a hero's deeds [epic poem, epos, heroic poem]</p><p><i>adj.</i> very imposing or impressive [heroic, larger-than-life]</p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting or having to do with or suggestive of a literary epic [epical]</p><p><b>ep</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long narrative poem telling of a hero's deeds [epic, epos, heroic poem]</p><p><b>pjesma proslavlja djela nekog junaka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> poetry celebrating the deeds of some hero [heroic poetry]</p><p><b>koji predstavlja ili ima veze s ili sugeriše književni ep. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting or having to do with or suggestive of a literary epic [epic]</p><p><b>skupina bracta koja simulira čašu kao u karanfili ili hibisku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of bracts simulating a calyx as in a carnation or hibiscus [calycle, calyculus, false calyx]</p><p><b>u vezi s epikantusom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the epicanthus</p><p><b>vertikalno preokret kože preko nosnog kantusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vertical fold of skin over the nasal canthus [epicanthus]</p><p><b>vertikalno preokret kože preko nosnog kantusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vertical fold of skin over the nasal canthus [epicanthic fold]</p><p><b>kratki dio jednjaka koji se proteže prema dolje od dijafragme do želuca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the short part of the esophagus extending downward from the diaphragm to the stomach</p><p><b>Najunažniji od dva sloja perikarda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the innermost of the two layers of the pericardium [visceral pericardium]</p><p><b>najudaljeniji sloj periharpa voća kao koža breskve ili grožđa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> outermost layer of the pericarp of fruits as the skin of a peach or grape [exocarp]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s epikarpom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the epicarp</p><p><b>koji imaju i muške i ženske spolne osobine i organe, imaju dvosmislen spolni identitet, koji imaju neprikladne ženske osobine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one having both male and female sexual characteristics and organs [androgyne, epicene person, gynandromorph, hermaphrodite, intersex]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having an ambiguous sexual identity [bisexual]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having unsuitable feminine qualities [cissy, effeminate, emasculate, sissified, sissy, sissyish]</p><p><b>koji imaju i muške i ženske spolne osobine i organe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one having both male and female sexual characteristics and organs [androgyne, epicene, gynandromorph, hermaphrodite, intersex]</p><p><b>epicentar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the point on the Earth's surface directly above the focus of an earthquake [epicentre]</p><p><b>epicentar, epicentru</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the point on the Earth's surface directly above the focus of an earthquake [epicenter]</p><p><b>Projekcija na kosti iznad kondila koja služi za vezivanje mišića i ligamenata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a projection on a bone above a condyle serving for the attachment of muscles and ligaments</p><p><b>bolno upale mišića i mekih tkiva oko epikondila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> painful inflammation of the muscles and soft tissues around an epicondyle</p><p><b>mišić i aponeuroza i koža koja pokriva lubanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the muscle and aponeurosis and skin covering the cranium</p><p><b>Epiktet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek philosopher who was a Stoic (circa 50-130)</p><p><b>epikurejac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person devoted to refined sensuous enjoyment (especially good food and drink) [bon vivant, epicurean, foodie, gastronome, gourmet]</p><p><b>čovjek koji uživa u profinjenim čulnim nasladama, epikurejac, epikurejski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person devoted to refined sensuous enjoyment (especially good food and drink) [bon vivant, epicure, foodie, gastronome, gourmet]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of Epicurus or epicureanism</p><p><i>adj.</i> devoted to pleasure [hedonic, hedonistic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> displaying luxury and furnishing gratification to the senses [luxuriant, luxurious, sybaritic, voluptuary, voluptuous]</p><p><b>doktrinu hedonizma koju su branili neki drevni grčki filozofi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a doctrine of hedonism that was defended by several ancient Greek philosophers</p><p><b>raspoloženje i navike epikura (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the disposition and habits of an epicure</p><p><b>Epikur</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek philosopher who believed that the world is a random combination of atoms and that pleasure is the highest good (341-270 BC)</p><p><b>krug koji se okreće oko drugog kruga (unutra ili izvan njega) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a circle that rolls around (inside or outside) another circle</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s epiciklom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an epicycle [epicyclical]</p><p><b>vanjski zupčanik koji se okreće oko središnjeg sunčevog zupčanika epicikličnog vlaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an outer gear that revolves about a central sun gear of an epicyclic train [planet gear, planet wheel, planetary gear]</p><p><b>Sistemi epicikličnih zupčanika u kojima se barem jedna os kotača okreće oko druge fiksne osi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of epicyclic gears in which at least one wheel axis itself revolves about another fixed axis [epicyclic train]</p><p><b>Sistemi epicikličnih zupčanika u kojima se barem jedna os kotača okreće oko druge fiksne osi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of epicyclic gears in which at least one wheel axis itself revolves about another fixed axis [epicyclic gear train]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s epiciklom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an epicycle [epicyclic]</p><p><b>crta koju stvara točka na krugu koja se okreće oko drugog kruga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a line generated by a point on a circle rolling around another circle</p><p><b>S odjeljkom za obradu ili za obradu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> designed primarily for rhetorical display [epideictical]</p><p><b>vrsta govornog govora koji se koristi za pohvalu ili osudu osobe ili skupine ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a type of oratory used to eulogize or condemn a person or group of people</p><p><b>S odjeljkom za obradu ili za obradu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> designed primarily for rhetorical display [epideictic]</p><p><b>epidemički, epidemija, pomor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a widespread outbreak of an infectious disease</p><p><i>adj.</i> (especially of medicine) of disease or anything resembling a disease</p><p><b>kolera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute intestinal infection caused by ingestion of contaminated water or food [Asiatic cholera, Indian cholera, cholera]</p><p><b>bilo koja zarazna bolest koja se razvija i brzo se širi na mnoge ljude (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any infectious disease that develops and spreads rapidly to many people</p><p><b>encefalitis koji je bio epidemija između 1915 i 1926 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an encephalitis that was epidemic between 1915 and 1926 [encephalitis lethargica, lethargic encephalitis, sleeping sickness, sleepy sickness]</p><p><b>stanje u kojem velika grupa ljudi pokazuje isto stanje nasilne mentalne agitacije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a condition in which a large group of people exhibit the same state of violent mental agitation [mass hysteria]</p><p><b>meningitis uzrokovan bakterijama i često smrtonosan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> meningitis caused by bacteria and often fatal [brain fever, cerebrospinal fever, cerebrospinal meningitis]</p><p><b>akutna zarazna bolest koja se javlja u epidemijskom obliku i sa paroksizmom boli (obično u prsima) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute infectious disease occurring in epidemic form and featuring paroxysms of pain (usually in the chest) [Bornholm disease, diaphragmatic pleurisy, epidemic pleurodynia, myosis]</p><p><b>akutna zarazna virusna bolest obilježena groznicom i oticanjem parotidnih žlijezda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute contagious viral disease characterized by fever and by swelling of the parotid glands [mumps]</p><p><b>akutna zarazna bolest koja se javlja u epidemijskom obliku i sa paroksizmom boli (obično u prsima) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute infectious disease occurring in epidemic form and featuring paroxysms of pain (usually in the chest) [Bornholm disease, diaphragmatic pleurisy, epidemic myalgia, myosis]</p><p><b>zarazna virusna bolest koja je blaži oblik ospica koji traje tri ili četiri dana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a contagious viral disease that is a milder form of measles lasting three or four days [German measles, rubella, three-day measles]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s epidemiologijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to epidemiology [epidemiological]</p><p><b>epidemiološki, epidemiološka, epidemiološkoj, epidemiološke</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to epidemiology [epidemiologic]</p><p><b>medicinski znanstvenik koji proučava prijenos i kontrolu epidemijskih bolesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a medical scientist who studies the transmission and control of epidemic diseases</p><p><b>epedmiologija, epidemiologia, epidemiologija, epidemiološki</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of medical science dealing with the transmission and control of disease</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta orhideje iz roda Epidendrum (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various orchids of the genus Epidendrum</p><p><b>veliki i promjenjivi rod kopnenih ili epifitnih ili litofitnih orhideja iz tropskih i subtropskih Amerika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large and variable genus of terrestrial or epiphytic or lithophytic orchids of tropical and subtropical Americas [genus Epidendrum]</p><p><b>Orhideja iz Floride i Bahama s prikazivim cvjetovima svijetle boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orchid of Florida and the Bahamas having showy brightly colored flowers [Encyclia tampensis, butterfly orchid]</p><p><b>Meksička epifitna orhideja s blijedozeleno-zeleno-zeleno cvijeće s bijelom ljubičasto-viničastom usnom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mexican epiphytic orchid having pale green or yellow-green flowers with white purple-veined lip [Encyclia venosa, butterfly orchid, butterfly orchis]</p><p><b>epidermički, koji se tiče gornjeg sloja kože</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a cuticle or cuticula [cuticular, dermal, epidermic]</p><p><b>bilo koja stanica koja čini epidermis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the cells making up the epidermis</p><p><b>epidermički, koji se tiče gornjeg sloja kože</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a cuticle or cuticula [cuticular, dermal, epidermal]</p><p><b>epiderma, pokožica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the outer layer of the skin covering the exterior body surface of vertebrates [cuticle]</p><p><b>optički projektor koji daje slike transparentnih i nepromenljivih predmeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an optical projector that gives images of both transparent and opaque objects</p><p><b>pasjemenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a convoluted tubule in each testis</p><p><b>bolna upala epididima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> painful inflammation of the epididymis</p><p><b>regionalna anestezija koja je rezultat ubrizgavanja anestetika u epiduralni prostor kičmene moždine, na ili izvan dure mater (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> regional anesthesia resulting from injection of an anesthetic into the epidural space of the spinal cord [epidural anaesthesia, epidural anesthesia]</p><p><i>adj.</i> on or outside the dura mater [extradural]</p><p><b>regionalna anestezija koja je rezultat ubrizgavanja anestetika u epiduralni prostor kičmene moždine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> regional anesthesia resulting from injection of an anesthetic into the epidural space of the spinal cord [epidural, epidural anesthesia]</p><p><b>epiduralna anestezija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> regional anesthesia resulting from injection of an anesthetic into the epidural space of the spinal cord [epidural, epidural anaesthesia]</p><p><b>injekcija anestetičke tvari u epiduralni prostor kičmene moždine kako bi se proizvela epiduralna anestezija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> injection of an anesthetic substance into the epidural space of the spinal cord in order to produce epidural anesthesia</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, za sve vrste biljaka koje se mogu uzimati za proizvodnju biljaka iz područja Unije, primjenjuje se sljedeći tarifni broj: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small creeping evergreen shrubs: trailing arbutus [genus Epigaea]</p><p><b>nizak rastovi vječnozelena grmlja istočne Sjeverne Amerike s kožnim lištima i grmovima mirisnih ružičastih ili bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing evergreen shrub of eastern North America with leathery leaves and clusters of fragrant pink or white flowers [mayflower, trailing arbutus]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s prednjim zidovima trbuha, ležanje na ili preko trbuha (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the anterior walls of the abdomen</p><p><i>adj.</i> lying on or over the stomach</p><p><b>jedna od tri arterije koje opskrbljuju prednje zidove trbuha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of three arteries supplying the anterior walls of the abdomen [arteria epigastrica]</p><p><b>blagi udarac u sredini ispod prsne kosti (gdje udar može utjecati na solarni pleksus) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slight depression in the midline just below the sternum (where a blow can affect the solar plexus) [pit of the stomach]</p><p><b>vene koje služe prednjim zidovima trbuha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> veins serving the anterior walls of the abdomen</p><p><b>područje koje leži na ili iznad želuca (samo ispod prsne kosti) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the region lying on or over the stomach (just below the sternum)</p><p><b>Geološka promjena u mineralnom sadržaju stijena nakon što se stijena formirala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a geological change in the mineral content of rock after the rock has formed</p><p><b>jezičac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flap of cartilage that covers the windpipe while swallowing</p><p><b>upale epiglotise (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the epiglottis</p><p><b>ponižavajući oponašač nekog uglednog pisca, umjetnika ili glazbenika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inferior imitator of some distinguished writer, artist, or musician [epigone]</p><p><b>ponižavajući oponašač nekog uglednog pisca, umjetnika ili glazbenika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inferior imitator of some distinguished writer, artist, or musician [epigon]</p><p><b>epigram</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a witty saying [quip]</p><p><b>Kratko i duhovno i kao poezija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> terse and witty and like a maxim [aphoristic, apothegmatic]</p><p><b>epigraf</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a quotation at the beginning of some piece of writing</p><p><i>n.</i> an engraved inscription</p><p><b>epigrafija, epigrafika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of ancient inscriptions</p><p><b>korištenje komada doniranog rožnjačnog tkiva za popravak oka osobe kojoj je uklonjen katarakta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> using a piece of donated corneal tissue to repair the eye of someone who has had a cataract removed</p><p><b>rod bubrege porijeklom iz Meksika i Srednje Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of ladybugs native to Mexico and Central America [genus Epilachna]</p><p><b>Uvođen u Sjedinjene Države iz Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> introduced into the United States from Mexico [Mexican bean beetle, bean beetle]</p><p><b>uklanjanje dlaka na tijelu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> remove body hair [depilate]</p><p><b>Sastav smola i vosaka za uklanjanje kozmetički neželjenih dlaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mixture of resins and waxes to remove cosmetically undesirable hair</p><p><b>depilacija, depiliranje, epilacija, epiliranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> loss of hair</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of removing hair (as from an animal skin) [depilation]</p><p><b>Kozmetik za privremeno uklanjanje neželjene dlakave kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cosmetic for temporary removal of undesired hair [depilator, depilatory]</p><p><b>epilepsija u kojoj napadi uključuju gubitak svijesti i tonicne grčeve mišića praćeni općim trzanjem, napad u kojem pacijent izgubi svijest i ima grčeve po cijelom tijelu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> epilepsy in which the attacks involve loss of consciousness and tonic spasms of the musculature followed by generalized jerking [generalized epilepsy, grand mal, grand mal epilepsy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a seizure during which the patient becomes unconscious and has convulsions over the entire body [generalized seizure, grand mal]</p><p><b>epilepsija koja se karakterizira paroksizmalnim napadima kratkog zamagljenosti svijesti (i možda i drugim abnormalnostima), kratak napad karakteriziran trenutačnom nesvjesnošću i lokalnim mišićnim grčevima ili grčevima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> epilepsy characterized by paroxysmal attacks of brief clouding of consciousness (and possibly other abnormalities) [petit mal, petit mal epilepsy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a seizure of short duration characterized by momentary unconsciousness and local muscle spasms or twitching [petit mal]</p><p><b>epilepsija, padavica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disorder of the central nervous system characterized by loss of consciousness and convulsions</p><p><b>epileptički</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who has epilepsy</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of epilepsy</p><p><b>krčenja s smanjenom sviješću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> convulsions accompanied by impaired consciousness</p><p><b>uzgajaju na kamenu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> growing on stone</p><p><b>veliki široko rasprostranjeni rod biljaka i potgoriva posebno zapadne Sjeverne Amerike i arktičkih područja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large widely distributed genus of herbs and subshrubs of especially western North America and Arctic areas [genus Epilobium]</p><p><b>Visoka sjevernoamerička višegodišnja biljka s puzećim korijenima i uskim listovima i šiljakama ružičastavičasta ljubičasta cvjetova koja se u velikoj količini nalazi u spaljenim područjima ili nedavnim čistinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall North American perennial with creeping rootstocks and narrow leaves and spikes of pinkish-purple flowers occurring in great abundance in burned-over areas or recent clearings [fireweed, giant willowherb, rosebay willowherb, wickup]</p><p><b>grm sa jugozapada SAD-a do Meksika s sjajnim crvenim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrublet of southwestern United States to Mexico having brilliant scarlet flowers [California fuchsia, Zauschneria californica, humming bird's trumpet]</p><p><b>biljka iz Europe i Azije s ljubičastokrvenim cvijećem i dlakavim stabljikama i lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant of Europe and Asia having purplish-red flowers and hairy stems and leaves [codlins-and-cream, hairy willowherb]</p><p><b>kratak govor (često u stihu) koji glumac upućuje direktno publici na kraju predstave, kratak odlomak dodan na kraju književnog djela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short speech (often in verse) addressed directly to the audience by an actor at the end of a play [epilogue]</p><p><i>n.</i> a short passage added at the end of a literary work [epilogue]</p><p><b>epilog, ishod, zaključak, pogovor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short speech (often in verse) addressed directly to the audience by an actor at the end of a play [epilog]</p><p><i>n.</i> a short passage added at the end of a literary work [epilog]</p><p><b>biljke koje su izrasle u sredozemnom području do Indije i istočne Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herbaceous perennials of Mediterranean to India and eastern Asia [genus Epimedium]</p><p><b>polako rastuća puzava biljka s polusvetim lišćama na uspravnim žičastim stabljikama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slow-growing creeping plant with semi-evergreen leaves on erect wiry stems [barrenwort, bishop's hat]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) brat Prometeja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) brother of Prometheus</p><p><b>karakterizira se nepotpunom metamorfozom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by incomplete metamorphosis</p><p><b>Nalazi se oko stjenovitih obala ili na grebenim