ice, kapital, pravednost, pravičnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the difference between the market value of a property and the claims held against it</p><p><i>n.</i> the ownership interest of shareholders in a corporation</p><p><i>n.</i> conformity with rules or standards [fairness]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je kreditni subjekt u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, u slučaju da je kreditni subjekt u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s član (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loan secured by equity value in the borrower's home [home equity credit, home equity loan, home loan]</p><p><b>ekvivalencija, isto vrijednost, jednakost, jednakost po vrijedosti, jednakovrijednost, ravnopravnost, usklađenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of being essentially equal or equivalent [equality, equation, par]</p><p><i>n.</i> essential equality and interchangeability</p><p><i>n.</i> qualities that are comparable [comparability, compare, comparison]</p><p><b>ekvivalent, ekvivalentan, iste vrijednosti, isti, istovjetan, istovrijedan, istovrstan, jednak, jednako vrijedan, odgovarajući, odgovrajući, protuvrijednost, ravnopravan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person or thing equal to another in value or measure or force or effect or significance etc</p><p><i>n.</i> the atomic weight of an element that has the same combining capacity as a given weight of another element [combining weight, eq, equivalent weight]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being essentially equal to something [tantamount]</p><p><b>atomska masa elementa koji ima istu kombiniranu sposobnost kao i datom težinom drugog elementa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the atomic weight of an element that has the same combining capacity as a given weight of another element [combining weight, eq, equivalent]</p><p><b