advertent incorrectness [erroneousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a misconception resulting from incorrect information [erroneous belief]</p><p><i>n.</i> (baseball) a failure of a defensive player to make an out when normal play would have sufficed [misplay]</p><p><i>n.</i> departure from what is ethically acceptable [wrongdoing]</p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) the occurrence of an incorrect result produced by a computer [computer error]</p><p><i>n.</i> part of a statement that is not correct [mistake]</p><p><b>(telekomunikacije) sustav kodiranja koji uključuje dodatne bitove pariteta kako bi se otkrile pogreške (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (telecommunication) a coding system that incorporates extra parity bits in order to detect errors [ECC]</p><p><b>Sposoban za pogrešku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of making an error [erring]</p><p><b>bez pogreške (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> free from error</p><p><b>imitacija, nadomjestak, surogat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial or inferior substitute or imitation</p><p><i>adj.</i> artificial and inferior [substitute]</p><p><b>galski jezik škotskih brđana, galskoškotski, irski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several related languages of the Celts in Ireland and Scotland [Gaelic, Goidelic]</p><p><b>Američki pisac poznat po romanima o siromaštvu i degeneraciji (1903-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States author remembered for novels about poverty and degeneration (1903-1987) [Caldwell, Erskine Preston Caldwell]</p><p><b>Američki pisac poznat po romanima o siromaštvu i degeneraciji (1903-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States author remembered for novels about poverty and degeneration (1903-1987) [Caldwell, Erskine Caldwell]</p><p><b>nekada</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at a previous time [at one time, erstwhile, formerly, once]</p><p><b>bivši, nekada</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to some prior time [former, old, one-time, onetime, quondam, sometime]</p><p><i>adv.</i> at a previous time [at one time, erst, formerly, once]</p><p><b>koordinirano univerzalno vrijeme kada se događaj primi na Zemlji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the coordinated universal time when an event is received on Earth [Earth-received time]</p><p><b>biljke iz područja Mediterana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual to perennial herbs of the Mediterranean region [genus Eruca]</p><p><b>Europski godišnji stalak često uzgajan kao biljka za salate koja se žanje kada je mlada i krhka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect European annual often grown as a salad crop to be harvested when young and tender [Eruca vesicaria sativa, arugula, garden rocket, rocket, rocket salad, roquette]</p><p><b>Europski godišnji stalak često uzgajan kao biljka za salate koja se žanje kada je mlada i krhka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect European annual often grown as a salad crop to be harvested when young and tender [Eruca sativa, arugula, garden rocket, rocket, rocket salad, roquette]</p><p><b>podrignuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> eject or send out in large quantities, also metaphorical [spew, spew out]</p><p><i>v.</i> expel gas from the stomach [belch, bubble, burp]</p><p><b>podrigivanje, riganje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (of volcanos) pouring out fumes or lava (or a deposit so formed) [eruption, extravasation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a reflex that expels gas noisily from the stomach through the mouth [belch, belching, burp, burping]</p><p><b>obrazovan, učen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing profound knowledge [learned]</p><p><b>obrazovan, učen (od &quot;erudite&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with erudition [learnedly]</p><p><b>obrazovan, učen (od &quot;erudite&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> profound scholarly knowledge [encyclopaedism, encyclopedism, erudition, learnedness, learning, scholarship]</p><p><b>erudicija, erudicije, obrazovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> profound scholarly knowledge [encyclopaedism, encyclopedism, eruditeness, learnedness, learning, scholarship]</p><p><b>izbacivati, izbiti, buknuti, paliti se, planuti, raspaliti se, raspaljivati se, zapaliti se, eksplodirati, eruptirati, rigati, briznuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> start abruptly [break out]</p><p><i>v.</i> erupt or intensify suddenly [break open, burst out, flare, flare up, irrupt]</p><p><i>v.</i> start to burn or burst into flames [catch fire, combust, conflagrate, ignite, take fire]</p><p><i>v.</i> break out [break through, come out, push through]</p><p><i>v.</i> become active and spew forth lava and rocks [belch, extravasate]</p><p><i>v.</i> force out or release suddenly and often violently something pent up [break, burst]</p><p><i>v.</i> appear on the skin</p><p><i>v.</i> become raw or open [break out, recrudesce]</p><p><b>erupcija, izbacivanje, izljev, nicanje, probijanje, vulkanska erupcija, izbijanje, izboj, navala, provala, prasak, tresak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sudden occurrence of a violent discharge of steam and volcanic material [volcanic eruption]</p><p><i>n.</i> symptom consisting of a breaking out and becoming visible</p><p><i>n.</i> (of volcanos) pouring out fumes or lava (or a deposit so formed) [eructation, extravasation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden violent spontaneous occurrence (usually of some undesirable condition) [irruption, outbreak]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden very loud noise [bam, bang, blast, clap]</p><p><i>n.</i> the emergence of a tooth as it breaks through the gum</p><p><b>eruptivan, izbačen, vulkanski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> producing or characterized by eruptions</p><p><i>adj.</i> produced by the action of fire or intense heat [igneous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> actively spewing out lava</p><p><b>Američki košarkaški naprijed (rođen 1950.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States basketball forward (born in 1950) [Dr. J, Julius Erving, Julius Winfield Erving]</p><p><b>povijesnik umjetnosti (1892-1968) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> art historian (1892-1968) [Panofsky]</p><p><b>Njemački feldmaršal poznat po sjajnom generalstvu u Sjevernoj Africi tijekom Drugog svjetskog rata (1891-1944) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German field marshal noted for brilliant generalship in North Africa during World War II (1891-1944) [Desert Fox, Rommel]</p><p><b>Austrijski fizičar koji je otkrio valnu jednadžbu (1887-1961) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Austrian physicist who discovered the wave equation (1887-1961) [Schrodinger]</p><p><b>bakterije u obliku šipke koje napadaju biljke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rod-shaped motile bacteria that attack plants</p><p><b>veliki rod ukrasnih biljaka s čirnim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large genus of decorative plants with thistlelike flower heads [genus Eryngium]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 3. ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 3. ovog Pravilnika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coarse prickly perennial eryngo with aromatic roots [button snakeroot]</p><p><b>Europski vječnozeleni eringo s iskrivljenim trnastima lištima naturaliziran na istočnoj obali Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European evergreen eryngo with twisted spiny leaves naturalized on United States east coast [sea eryngium, sea holly, sea holm]</p><p><b>Eryngium yuccifolium, kotrljan, sikavac, zmijska trava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coarse prickly perennial eryngo of United States thought to cure rattlesnake bite [button snakeroot, rattlesnake's master, rattlesnake master]</p><p><b>biljke iz roda Eryngium (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Eryngium [eringo]</p><p><b>veliki rod jednogodišnjih ili višegodišnjih biljaka neki uzgajani zbog svojih cvijeća a neki zbog svojih atraktivnih zimzelenih listova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large genus of annual or perennial herbs some grown for their flowers and some for their attractive evergreen leaves [genus Erysimum]</p><p><b>u obliku od šarene, čvrste, dvostruke ili kratkotrajne višegodišnje biljke uzgojene zbog svojih krajnjih cvjetova narandžasto-žutih cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> showy erect biennial or short-lived perennial cultivated for its terminal racemes of orange-yellow flowers [Cheiranthus allionii, Siberian wall flower]</p><p><b>dvostruko ili kratkotrajno višegodišnje prairie rocket s narandžasto-žutim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> biennial or short-lived perennial prairie rocket having orange-yellow flowers [Cheiranthus asperus, Erysimum asperum, western wall flower]</p><p><b>dvostruko ili kratkotrajno višegodišnje prairie rocket s narandžasto-žutim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> biennial or short-lived perennial prairie rocket having orange-yellow flowers [Cheiranthus asperus, Erysimum arkansanum, western wall flower]</p><p><b>tanka žuta-cvjetna evropska senfa često uznemirujuća kao korov (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender yellow-flowered European mustard often troublesome as a weed [wormseed mustard]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka iz južne Europe s grmovima mirisnih cvijeća svih boja, posebno žute i narandžaste boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of southern Europe having clusters of fragrant flowers of all colors especially yellow and orange [Cheiranthus cheiri, wallflower]</p><p><b>crveni vjetar, erizipel</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute streptococcal infection characterized by deep-red inflammation of the skin and mucous membranes</p><p><b>obitelj gljiva parazitskih uglavnom na lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of fungi parasitic mostly on leaves [family Erysiphaceae]</p><p><b>za sve vrste biljaka; (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> saprophytic and parasitic fungi that live on plants [order Erysiphales]</p><p><b>rod prašnoga plesna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of powdery mildews [genus Erysiphe]</p><p><b>neuobičajeno crvenilo kože uzrokovano širenjem krvnih žila (kao što su opekline od sunca ili upaljenje) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal redness of the skin resulting from dilation of blood vessels (as in sunburn or inflammation)</p><p><b>crveni osip uzrokovan preosjetljivošću na lijek ili bolest ili drugi alergen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a red rash caused by hypersensitivity to a drug or disease or other allergen</p><p><b>stanje kože koje se karakterizira osjetljivim crvenim čvorovima na špinama i nogama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> skin condition characterized by tender red nodules on the shins and legs</p><p><b>upalna komplikacija guba koja rezultira bolnim kožnim oštećenjima na rukama, nogama i licu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inflammatory complication of leprosy that results in painful skin lesions on the arms and legs and face [ENL]</p><p><b>crvenilo kože uzrokovano izlaganjem sunčevim zrake (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> redness of the skin caused by exposure to the rays of the sun [sunburn]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili karakteriziraju eritemom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characterized by erythema</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih grmova ili grmljava iz roda Erythrina s trostrukim listovima i rasemi od crvenokrasnih do koralnih crvenih cvijeća i crnim sjemenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various shrubs or shrubby trees of the genus Erythrina having trifoliate leaves and racemes of scarlet to coral red flowers and black seeds [coral tree]</p><p><b>malo polusvetlo široko rasprostranjeno stablo iz istočne Južne Afrike s narandžastokrvenim cvijećem i malim koralnim crvenim sjemenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small semi-evergreen broad-spreading tree of eastern South Africa with orange-scarlet flowers and small coral-red seeds [Cape kafferboom, kaffir boom]</p><p><b>mala južnoamerička trnasta stabla s tamnocrvenom i crvenom crvenom cvjetom samostalna ili u skupovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small South American spiny tree with dark crimson and scarlet flowers solitary or clustered [ceibo, common coral tree, cry-baby tree, crybaby tree]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s članko