n, estimation, idea]</p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment of the qualities of something or somebody [estimation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a document appraising the value of something (as for insurance or taxation) [appraisal, estimation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement indicating the likely cost of some job</p><p><i>n.</i> the respect with which a person is held [estimation]</p><p><i>v.</i> judge tentatively or form an estimate of (quantities or time) [approximate, gauge, guess, judge]</p><p><i>v.</i> judge to be probable [calculate, count on, figure, forecast, reckon]</p><p><b>porez na dohodak koji se periodično plaća na dohodak koji nije podliježan porezu na izvor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> income tax paid periodically on income that is not subject to withholding taxes</p><p><b>Izjava koja se zahtijeva od poreznog obveznika čiji porez oduziman od prihoda ne pokriva poreznu obvezu za godinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> return required of a taxpayer whose tax withheld from income does not meet the tax liability for the year [declaration of estimated tax]</p><p><b>estimacija, ocjena, određivanje, poštovanje, procjena, procjena stanja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a document appraising the value of something (as for insurance or taxation) [appraisal, estimate]</p><p><i>n.</i> the respect with which a person is held [estimate]</p><p><i>n.</i> an approximate calculation of quantity or degree or worth [approximation, estimate, idea]</p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment of the qualities of something or somebody [estimate]</p><p><b>estimator, procjenitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert at calculation (or at operating calculating machines) [calculator, computer, figurer, reckoner]</p><p><b>(rijetko) ili se javljaju ljeti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (rare) of or occurring in summer [aestival]</p><p><b>spavanje tijekom ljeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> sleep during summer [aestivate]</p><p><b>(zoologija) prestanak ili usporavanje aktivnosti tijekom ljeta, (botanica) raspored sepal i latica u cvjetnom pupoljku prije nego se otvori (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (zoology) cessation or slowing of activity during the summer [aestivation]</p><p><i>n.</i> (botany) the arrangement of sepals and petals in a flower bud before it opens [aestivation]</p><p><b>Estonija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic in northeastern Europe on the Baltic Sea [Esthonia, Republic of Estonia]</p><p><b>Estonac, Estonka, estonski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the official language of Estonia [Esthonian]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to Estonia or the people or culture of Estonia</p><p><b>monetarna jedinica u Estoniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Estonia</p><p><b>sprečavanje da protivnik dokaže tvrdnju koja je u</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rule of evidence whereby a person is barred from denying the truth of a fact that has already been settled</p><p><b>Najmoćniji ženski hormon koji se prirodno javlja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the most powerful female hormone that occurs naturally [oestradiol]</p><p><b>transdermalni flaster koji omogućuje apsorpciju estradiola u krvotok (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a transdermal patch that allows estradiol to be absorbed into the blood stream</p><p><b>estragon, tarkanj, taragon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic perennial of southeastern Russia [Artemisia dracunculus, tarragon]</p><p><i>n.</i> fresh leaves (or leaves preserved in vinegar) used as seasoning [tarragon]</p><p><b>odstraniti, otuđiti, udaljiti, udaljiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> remove from customary environment or associations</p><p><i>v.</i> arouse hostility or indifference in where there had formerly been love, affection, or friendliness [alienate, disaffect]</p><p><b>uzrokovan da se ne voli (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> caused to be unloved [alienated]</p><p><b>otuđivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> separation resulting from hostility [alienation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling of being alienated from other people [alienation, disaffection]</p><p><b>odstraniti, otuđiti, udaljiti (od &quot;estrange&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> making one feel out of place or alienated</p><p><b>nebeski objekt, nebesko tijelo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a natural object existing outside the earth and outside the earth's atmosphere [extraterrestrial object]</p><p><b>prirodni estrogeni hormon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a naturally occurring estrogenic hormone [oestriol]</p><p><b>estrogen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a general term for female steroid sex hormones that are secreted by the ovary and responsible for typical female sexual characteristics [oestrogen]</p><p><b>antagonist za estrogen koji se koristi u liječenju raka dojke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antagonist for estrogen that is used in the treatment of breast cancer [tamoxifen]</p><p><b>estrogen (od &quot;estrogen&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or caused by estrogen</p><p><b>prirodno prisutan slab estrogeni hormon koji izlučuje majčinski jajnik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a naturally occurring weak estrogenic hormone secreted by the mammalian ovary [Estronol, oestrone, theelin]</p><p><b>prirodno prisutan slab estrogeni hormon koji izlučuje majčinski jajnik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a naturally occurring weak estrogenic hormone secreted by the mammalian ovary [estrone, oestrone, theelin]</p><p><b>estrus</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of lower mammals) showing or in a state of estrus</p><p><b>primjenjuje se na sisare koji nisu ljudi: stanje ili razdoblje pojačane seksualne uzbuđenja i aktivnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> applies to nonhuman mammals: a state or period of heightened sexual arousal and activity [heat, oestrus, rut]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili pronađen u estuarijima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or found in estuaries [estuarine]</p><p><b>estuarijski, koji pripada ušću</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or found in estuaries [estuarial]</p><p><b>estuarij, ušće, ušće rijeke, ušću</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the wide part of a river where it nears the sea</p><p><b>pretjerana želja za hranom, ekstremna proždrljivost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> excessive desire to eat [edacity, ravenousness, voraciousness, voracity]</p><p><i>n.</i> extreme gluttony [edacity, rapaciousness, rapacity, voraciousness, voracity]</p><p><b>proždrljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> extremely hungry [famished, ravenous, sharp-set, starved]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (often followed by `for') ardently or excessively desirous [avid, devouring, greedy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> devouring or craving food in great quantities [edacious, rapacious, ravening, ravenous, voracious, wolfish]</p><p><b>i drugi ("et al". se koristi kao skraćenica od `et alii' (muško množina) ili `et aliae' (žensko množina) ili `et alia' (neutralno množina) kada se odnosi na nekoliko osoba), i drugdje (koristi se kada se odnosi na druge pojave u tekstu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> and others ('et al.' is used as an abbreviation of `et alii' (masculine plural) or `et aliae' (feminine plural) or `et alia' (neuter plural) when referring to a number of people) [et al., et alia, et aliae, et alii]</p><p><i>adv.</i> and elsewhere (used when referring to other occurrences in a text) [et al., et alibi]</p><p><b>i drugi ("et al". se koristi kao skraćenica od `et alii' (muško množina) ili `et aliae' (žensko množina) ili `et alia' (neutralno množina) kada se odnosi na nekoliko osoba), i drugdje (koristi se kada se odnosi na druge pojave u tekstu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> and others ('et al.' is used as an abbreviation of `et alii' (masculine plural) or `et aliae' (feminine plural) or `et alia' (neuter plural) when referring to a number of people) [et al, et alia, et aliae, et alii]</p><p><i>adv.</i> and elsewhere (used when referring to other occurrences in a text) [et al, et alibi]</p><p><b>i drugi ("et al". se koristi kao skraćenica od `et alii' (muško množina) ili `et aliae' (žensko množina) ili `et alia' (neutralno množina) kada se odnosi na nekoliko osoba) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> and others ('et al.' is used as an abbreviation of `et alii' (masculine plural) or `et aliae' (feminine plural) or `et alia' (neuter plural) when refer