</i> anesthetize with ether [etherize]</p><p><b>Anestezija s eterom (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> anesthetize with ether [etherise]</p><p><b>ethernet, lokalna mreža tipa sabirnice s asinkronim pristupo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a type of network technology for local area networks</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom električne energije od 1,15 kVA ili većim od 2,15 kVA, ali ne većim od 2,15 kVA, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several types of coaxial cable used in ethernets</p><p><b>etički, etika, moralan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principles of right and wrong that are accepted by an individual or a social group [moral principle, value-system, value orientation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a system of principles governing morality and acceptable conduct [ethical code]</p><p><b>etičan, etički, moralan, etička</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the philosophical study of ethics</p><p><i>adj.</i> conforming to accepted standards of social or professional behavior</p><p><i>adj.</i> adhering to ethical and moral principles [honorable, honourable]</p><p><b>sustav načela kojima se upravlja moralno i prihvatljivo ponašanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of principles governing morality and acceptable conduct [ethic]</p><p><b>lijek na recept</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that is available only with written instructions from a doctor or dentist to a pharmacist [prescription, prescription drug, prescription medicine]</p><p><b>etika, etički motiv, moral, moralnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> motivation based on ideas of right and wrong [ethics, morality, morals]</p><p><b>etički</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an ethical manner</p><p><b>filozof koji se specijalizirao za etiku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a philosopher who specializes in ethics [ethicist]</p><p><b>doktrina da su etika i etički ideje valjani i važni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a doctrine that ethics and ethical ideas are valid and important</p><p><b>filozof koji se specijalizirao za etiku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a philosopher who specializes in ethics [ethician]</p><p><b>ćudoređe, etika, etički motiv, moral, moralnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> motivation based on ideas of right and wrong [ethical motive, morality, morals]</p><p><i>n.</i> the philosophical study of moral values and rules [moral philosophy]</p><p><b>etički odbor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a committee appointed to consider ethical issues [ethics panel]</p><p><b>Odbor imenovan za razmatranje etičkih pitanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a committee appointed to consider ethical issues [ethics committee]</p><p><b>Etiopija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Ethiopia is a republic in northeastern Africa on the Red Sea [Abyssinia, Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia, Yaltopya]</p><p><b>Etiopljanin, Etiopljanka, etiopski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Ethiopia</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Ethiopia or its people or languages</p><p><b>Velika zelena biljka s velikim lišcima u obliku vesla i plodovima koji se ne mogu jesti, ali imaju jestive mladoplodne izdanke. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large evergreen arborescent herb having huge paddle-shaped leaves and bearing inedible fruit that resemble bananas but edible young flower shoots [Abyssinian banana, Ensete ventricosum, Musa ensete]</p><p><b>dominantni i službeni jezik Etiopije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the dominant and official language of Ethiopia [Amharic]</p><p><b>novčana jedinica u Etiopiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Ethiopia</p><p><b>jedna od osam kostiju lubanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the eight bones of the cranium [ethmoid bone]</p><p><b>jedna od osam kostiju lubanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the eight bones of the cranium [ethmoid]</p><p><b>sinusni sinus nosne šupljine (za mostom nosa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sinus of the meatuses of the nasal cavity (behind the bridge of the nose) [ethmoidal sinus, sinus ethmoidales]</p><p><b>ogranak oftalmološke arterije koji opskrbljuje strukture u i oko nosne kapsule (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a branch of the ophthalmic artery supplying structures in and around the nasal capsule [arteria ethmoidalis]</p><p><b>sinusni sinus nosne šupljine (za mostom nosa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sinus of the meatuses of the nasal cavity (behind the bridge of the nose) [ethmoid sinus, sinus ethmoidales]</p><p><b>vene koje ispuštaju etmoidalne sinuse i prazne u gornju oftalmološku venu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> veins that drain the ethmoidal sinuses and empty into the superior ophthalmic vein [vena ethmoidalis]</p><p><b>vladar provincije (kao u Rimskom carstvu i Bizantinskom carstvu) ili neki vjerski vladari s svjetovnim autoritetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ruler of a province (as in the Roman Empire and Byzantine Empire) or certain religious rulers with secular authority</p><p><b>etnički, etničkog, nacionalan, etnička, etničke</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is a member of an ethnic group</p><p><i>adj.</i> denoting or deriving from or distinctive of the ways of living built up by a group of people [cultural, ethnical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not acknowledging the God of Christianity and Judaism and Islam [heathen, heathenish, pagan]</p><p><b>etničko čišćenje, etničkog čišćenja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mass expulsion and killing of one ethnic or religious group in an area by another ethnic or religious group in that area</p><p><b>etnička skupina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people of the same race or nationality who share a distinctive culture [ethnos]</p><p><b>Šala na račun neke etničke skupine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a joke at the expense of some ethnic group</p><p><b>grupa koja ima različite nacionalne ili kulturne tradicije od većine stanovništva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group that has different national or cultural traditions from the majority of the population</p><p><b>narodna glazba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the traditional and typically anonymous music that is an expression of the life of people in a community [folk, folk music]</p><p><b>uvreda nečijoj rasi ili jeziku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slur on someone's race or language</p><p><b>etničan, etnički, jezični</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> denoting or deriving from or distinctive of the ways of living built up by a group of people [cultural, ethnic]</p><p><b>etničan, etnički, jezični (od &quot;ethnical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to ethnicity</p><p><b>etnicitet, etničnost, etnološko porijeklo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ethnic quality or affiliation resulting from racial or cultural ties</p><p><b>Osredotočen na određenu etničku grupu, obično na vlastitu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> centered on a specific ethnic group, usually one's own</p><p><b>etnocentrizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> belief in the superiority of one's own ethnic group</p><p><b>antropolog koji radi etnografiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anthropologist who does ethnography</p><p><b>etnografski, etnografskog, etnografska, etnografske, etnografsku</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to ethnography [ethnographical]</p><p><b>etnografski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to ethnography [ethnographic]</p><p><b>etnografija, etnologija, etnologije, etnologiju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of anthropology that provides scientific description of individual human societies [descriptive anthropology]</p><p><b>o ili povezan s etnologijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to ethnology [ethnological]</p><p><b>o ili povezan s etnologijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to ethnology [ethnologic]</p><p><b>etnolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anthropologist who studies ethnology</p><p><b>etimologija, etnologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of anthropology that deals with the division of humankind into races and with their origins and distribution and distinctive characteristics</p><p><b>ethos, etnos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people of the same race or nationality who share a distinctive culture [ethnic group]</p><p><b>bijeli kristalni prah (trgovinski naziv Ethocaine) koji se primjenjuje u blizini živaca kao lokalni anestetik u stomatologiji i medicini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white crystalline powder (trade name Ethocaine) administered near nerves as a local anesthetic in dentistry and medicine [procaine]</p><p><b>zoolog koji proučava ponašanje životinja u njihovom prirodnom staništu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a zoologist who studies the behavior of animals in their natural habitats</p><p><b>etnologija, etologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of zoology that studies the behavior of animals in their natural habitats</p><p><b>(antropologija) karakteristični duh kulture ili doba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (anthropology) the distinctive spirit of a culture or an era</p><p><b>bezbojna, nestabilna i vrlo zapaljiva tekućina koja se nekada koristila kao anestetik za inhalaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless volatile highly flammable liquid formerly used as an inhalation anesthetic [diethyl ether, divinyl ether, ether, ethyl ether, vinyl ether]</p><p><b>Nezapaljiva tekućina (trgovinski naziv Ethrane) koja se koristi kao inhalacijski anestetik za opću anesteziju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nonflammable liquid (trade name Ethrane) used as an inhalation general anesthetic [enflurane]</p><p><b>u slučaju da je proizvod iz članka 1. stavka 1. točke (a) ili (b) ovog članka upotrebljen u proizvodima iz članka 1. stavka 2. točke (a) ili (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (b) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antibiotic (trade name Erythrocin or E-Mycin or Ethril or Ilosone or Pediamycin) obtained from the actinomycete Streptomyces erythreus [E-Mycin, Erythrocin, Ilosone, Pediamycin, erythromycin]</p><p><b>etil</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the univalent hydrocarbon radical C2H5 derived from ethane by the removal of one hydrogen atom [ethyl group, ethyl radical]</p><p><b>aromatični bezbojni zapaljivi tekući ester od etanola i sirćetne kiseline (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fragrant colorless flammable volatile liquid ester made from ethanol and acetic acid</p><p><b>u fermentiranim i destiliranim pićima, alkohol bez okusa od 95 posto ili 190 posto, koji se koristi za mešanje s viskijem i za proizvodnju gina i likera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the intoxicating agent in fermented and distilled liquors [ethanol, fermentation alcohol, grain alcohol]</p><p><i>n.</i> nonflavored alcohol of 95 percent or 190 proof used for blending with straight whiskies and in making gin and liqueurs [neutral spirits]</p><p><b>Bijeli kristalni ester koji se koristi kao lokalni anestetik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white crystalline ester used as a local anesthetic [benzocaine]</p><p><b>bezbojni zapaljivi plin koji se koristi kao lokalni površinski anestetik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless flammable gas used as a local surface anesthetic</p><p><b>bezbojna, nestabilna i vrlo zapaljiva tekućina koja se nekada koristila kao anestetik za inhalaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless volatile highly flammable liquid formerly used as an inhalation anesthetic [diethyl ether, divinyl ether, ether, ethoxyethane, vinyl ether]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom ugljikovodika od 1,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the univalent hydrocarbon radical C2H5 derived from ethane by the removal of one hydrogen atom [ethyl, ethyl radical]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom ugljikovodika od 1,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the univalent hydrocarbon radical C2H5 derived from ethane by the removal of one hydrogen atom [ethyl, ethyl group]</p><p><b>etilen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flammable colorless gaseous alkene [ethene]</p><p><b>etilen-glikol, glikol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sweet but poisonous syrupy liquid used as an antifreeze and solvent [ethanediol, glycol]</p><p><b>perkloretilen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anthelmintic agent used against hookworm and other nematodes [carbon dichloride, tetrachlorethylene, tetrachloroethylene]</p><p><b>kompleksni molekul koji se medicinski koristi za kelatiranje metalnih iona u slučajevima trovanja olovom ili teškim metalima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a complex molecule used medically to chelate metal ions in cases of lead or heavy metal poisoning [EDTA]</p><p><b>alkini, etin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless flammable gas used chiefly in welding and in organic synthesis [acetylene, alkyne]</p><p><b>Francuski liječnik koji je opisao srčane anomalije uključujući Fallotovu tetralogiju (1850-1911) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French physician who described cardiac anomalies including Fallot's tetralogy (1850-1911) [Fallot]</p><p><b>Smanjivanje rasta ili razvoja, (zelenog biljka) isključivanjem sunčeve svjetlosti., biti blijeda ili bolesna, (posebno biljaka) razvijen bez hlorofila time što je lišen svjetlosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make weak by stunting the growth or development of</p><p><i>v.</i> bleach and alter the natural development of (a green plant) by excluding sunlight</p><p><i>v.</i> make pale or sickly</p><p><i>adj.</i> (especially of plants) developed without chlorophyll by being deprived of light [blanched, etiolated]</p><p><b>(posebno biljaka) razvijen bez hlorofila time što je lišen svjetlosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (especially of plants) developed without chlorophyll by being deprived of light [blanched, etiolate]</p><p><b>bled i bolesno izgleda., čin slabljenja usporavanjem rasta ili razvoja nečega., (botanica) čin stvaranja biljke bez klorofila uzgajanjem bez izlaganja sunčevoj svjetlosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pale and sickly appearance</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of weakening by stunting the growth or development of something</p><p><i>n.</i> (botany) the act of causing a plant to develop without chlorophyll by growing it without exposure to sunlight</p><p><b>etiološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the philosophical study of causation [aetiologic, aetiological, etiological]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the etiology of a disease [aetiologic, aetiological, etiological]</p><p><b>filozofskog proučavanja uzro