 plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> broad and bushy Asiatic twining shrub with pinkish fruit [Euonymus radicans vegetus, evergreen bittersweet]</p><p><b>široka i grmljava azijska grmljava stabla s ružičastim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> broad and bushy Asiatic twining shrub with pinkish fruit [Euonymus fortunei radicans, evergreen bittersweet]</p><p><b>pupavac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pinkish-brown hoopoe with black-and-white wings [Upupa epops]</p><p><b>veliki rod uglavnom tropskih biljaka s glavama bijele ili ljubičaste boje cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large genus of chiefly tropical herbs having heads of white or purplish flowers [genus Eupatorium]</p><p><b>niskorazrastujući tropski američki grm s dugim tankim lišćama koji se koristi za pravljenje blago stimulativnog pića nalik čaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low spreading tropical American shrub with long slender leaves used to make a mildly stimulating drink resembling tea [Ayapana triplinervis, ayapana]</p><p><b>Europska biljka s lištima i grmovima crvenkasto-fioleta cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coarse European herb with palmately divided leaves and clusters of small reddish-purple flower heads [hemp agrimony]</p><p><b>biljka od korovlja iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s podijeljenim lišcima i dugim grmovima zelenkastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> weedy plant of southeastern United States having divided leaves and long clusters of greenish flowers [dog fennel]</p><p><b>biljka s rizomatom u središnjoj i jugoistočnoj Americi i u Zapadnoj Indiji s velikim, navidnim glavama čistih plavih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhizomatous plant of central and southeastern United States and West Indies having large showy heads of clear blue flowers [Conoclinium coelestinum, ageratum, mist-flower, mistflower]</p><p><b>Srednja i srednja visina (osim za uske i škrgačke biljke) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American herb having whorled leaves and terminal clusters of small pinkish or purple flower heads [Joe-