/i> of or relating to or characterized by euphony [euphonic]</p><p><b>koji ima ugodan zvuk, koji je ugodan u govoru, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a pleasant sound [euphonous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of speech or dialect) pleasing in sound</p><p><b>basov rog (medenjeni vjetrovni instrument) koji je tenor obitelji tuba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bass horn (brass wind instrument) that is the tenor of the tuba family</p><p><b>koji ima ugodan zvuk (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a pleasant sound [euphonious]</p><p><b>blagozvučje, blagozvučnost, eufonija, blagoglasje, glazba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any agreeable (pleasing and harmonious) sounds [music]</p><p><b>tip rod Euphorbiaceae: vrlo veliki rod raznih biljaka koje sve imaju mliječni sok (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Euphorbiaceae: very large genus of diverse plants all having milky juice [genus Euphorbia]</p><p><b>Europska višegodišnja biljka s zelenkasto žutom vrhunskom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European perennial herb with greenish yellow terminal flower clusters [wood spurge]</p><p><b>Voskasti grm sjevernog Meksika i jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wax-coated shrub of northern Mexico and southwestern United States [candelilla]</p><p><b>Afrički patuljak, sokulentan višegodišnji grm s brojnim tankim spuštenih grana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> African dwarf succulent perennial shrub with numerous slender drooping branches [Euphorbia medusae, medusa's head]</p><p><b>Česta višegodišnja biljka s bledobijom bijelom ljetnicom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common perennial United States spurge having showy white petallike bracts [flowering spurge, tramp's spurge, wild spurge]</p><p><b>Poinsettia iz Sjedinjenih Država i istočnog Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> poinsettia of United States and eastern Mexico [Mexican fire plant, fire-on-the-mountain, painted leaf]</p><p><b>Vječna biljka iz Starog svijeta s lišćem nalik cipresu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World perennial having foliage rese