 and Asia [Eurasian]</p><p><b>Eureka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alloy of copper and nickel with high electrical resistance and a low temperature coefficient [constantan]</p><p><i>n.</i> a town in northwest California on an arm of the Pacific Ocean</p><p><b>tumačenje ritma glazbenih kompozicija u harmoničnim pokretima tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the interpretation in harmonious bodily movements of the rhythm of musical compositions [eurhythmy, eurythmics, eurythmy]</p><p><b>tumačenje ritma glazbenih kompozicija u harmoničnim pokretima tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the interpretation in harmonious bodily movements of the rhythm of musical compositions [eurhythmics, eurythmics, eurythmy]</p><p><b>Euripid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the greatest tragic dramatists of ancient Greece (480-406 BC)</p><p><b>euro, eura</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic monetary unit of most members of the European Union (introduced in 1999)</p><p><b>Žargona dokumenata i propisa Europske zajednice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the jargon of European community documents and regulations</p><p><b>Europska zajednica i Europljani (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> focussed on Europe and the Europeans [Europocentric]</p><p><b>Vjerovanje u prevlast Europe i Europljana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> belief in the preeminence of Europe and the Europeans</p><p><b>eurovaluta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> currency of the major financial and industrial countries held in those countries for the purpose of lending and borrowing</p><p><b>eurodolar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a United States dollar deposited in a European bank and used as an international currency to finance trade</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjena skupina uključujući dinosaure s patkom i njihove rane rođake (hadrosaure, trachodon i iguanodon) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widespread group including duck-billed dinosaurs and their early relatives (hadrosaurs, trachodon and iguanodon) [Euronithopoda, Ornithopoda, suborder Euronithopoda, suborder Ornithopoda]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjena s