between Europe and Asia [Black Sea]</p><p><b>elektronvolt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of energy equal to the work done by an electron accelerated through a potential difference of 1 volt [electron volt]</p><p><b>Njemačka ljubavnica Adolfa Hitlera (1910-1945) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the German mistress of Adolf Hitler (1910-1945) [Braun]</p><p><b>Američka glumica (rođena u Engleskoj) (1899-1991) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States actress (born in England) (1899-1991) [Le Gallienne]</p><p><b>snažno laksativno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> strongly laxative [cathartic, purgative]</p><p><b>evakuirati, isprazniti, napustiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> move out of an unsafe location into safety</p><p><i>v.</i> empty completely</p><p><i>v.</i> move people from their homes or country</p><p><i>v.</i> create a vacuum in (a bulb, flask, reaction vessel)</p><p><i>v.</i> excrete or discharge from the body [empty, void]</p><p><b>evakuacija, napuštanje, povlačenje, ispražnjavanje, pražnjenje, izlučivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of removing the contents of something [emptying, voidance]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of evacuating</p><p><i>n.</i> the bodily process of discharging waste matter [elimination, excreting, excretion, voiding]</p><p><b>evakuirana osoba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who has been evacuated from a dangerous place</p><p><b>izbjeći, izbjegavati, izvrdati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> avoid or try to avoid fulfilling, answering, or performing (duties, questions, or issues) [circumvent, dodge, duck, elude, fudge, hedge, parry, put off, sidestep, skirt]</p><p><i>v.</i> escape, either physically or mentally [bilk, elude]</p><p><i>v.</i> practice evasion</p><p><i>v.</i> use cunning or deceit to escape or avoid</p><p><b>bodovati, ocijeniti, procijeniti, vrednovati, cijeniti, procjenjivati, valorizirati, ocjenjivati, prosuditi, prosuđivati, suditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> evaluate or estimate the nature, quality, ability, extent, or significance of [appraise, assess, measure, valuate, value]</p><p><i>v.</i> form a critical opinion of [judge, pass judgment]</p><p><b>evaluacija, evaluacijski, ocjena, ocjenjivanja, ocjenjivanje, procjena, valorizacija, vrednovanje, evaluacijskih, valorizacije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> act of ascertaining or fixing the value or worth of [rating]</p><p><i>n.</i> an appraisal of the value of something [rating, valuation]</p><p><b>koji provode ili uključuju pažljivu procjenu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> exercising or involving careful evaluations [appraising]</p><p><b>procjenitelj, ocjenitelj, ocjenjivač, poznavalac, procjenjivač, sudac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an authority who is able to estimate worth or quality [judge]</p><p><b>izgubiti se, nestati, blijedjeti, gubiti se, izblijedjeti, iščezavati, iščeznuti, nestajati, rasplinjavati se, rasplinuti se, zamirati, zamrijeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> disappear gradually [blow over, fade, fleet, pass, pass off]</p><p><b>gubljenje, iščezavanje, nestajanje, prolažanje, prolaženje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the event of fading and gradually vanishing from sight</p><p><b>koji nestaje, kratkotrajan, letimičan, prolazan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to vanish like vapor</p><p><b>evanđelje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the four books in the New Testament (Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John) that tell the story of Christ's life and teachings [Gospel, Gospels]</p><p><b>evanđeoski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or being a Christian church believing in personal conversion and the inerrancy of the Bible especially the 4 Gospels</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or in keeping with the Christian gospel especially as in the first 4 books of the New Testament</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by ardent or zealous enthusiasm for a cause [evangelistic]</p><p><b>protestantska denominacija kalvinističke vjere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Protestant denomination of Calvinist faith</p><p><b>metodistička denominacija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Methodist denomination</p><p><b>naglašava važnost osobnog obraćenja i vjere kao sredstva za spasenje. (