, priredba, slučaj, slučajnost, sportska disciplina, zgoda, događajem, slučaju, slueaj, efekt, ishod, konzekvencija, posljedica, rezultat, učinak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that happens at a given place and time</p><p><i>n.</i> a special set of circumstances [case]</p><p><i>n.</i> a phenomenon located at a single point in space-time</p><p><i>n.</i> a phenomenon that follows and is caused by some previous phenomenon [consequence, effect, issue, outcome, result, upshot]</p><p><b>osoba koja kao profesija planira društvene događaje (obično za vladine ili korporativne službenike) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who plans social events as a profession (usually for government or corporate officials)</p><p><b>sadržajan, sadržajnom, važan, značajan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of events or incidents</p><p><i>adj.</i> having important issues or results [consequential]</p><p><b>sumrak, večer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the latter part of the day (the period of decreasing daylight from late afternoon until nightfall) [eve, even, evening]</p><p><b>izbočina crijeva kroz trbušni zid (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> protrusion of the intestine through the abdominal wall</p><p><b>eventualan, eventualnih, krajnji, moguć</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> expected to follow in the indefinite future from causes already operating</p><p><b>eventualnost, mogućnost, slučajnost, kontingencija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a possible event or occurrence or result [contingence, contingency]</p><p><b>eventualno, krajnje, krajnji, na kraju, posljedično, konačno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> after an unspecified period of time or an especially long delay [finally]</p><p><b>desiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come out in the end</p><p><b>bilo kada, ikad, ikada, svagda, uopće, uvijek</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at any time [of all time]</p><p><i>adv.</i> at all times [always, e'er]</p><p><i>adv.</i> (intensifier for adjectives) very [ever so]</p><p><b>(intenzifikator za pridjevove) vrlo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (intensifier for adjectives) very [ever]</p><p><b>Označen stalnim promjenama ili djelotvornim djelovanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by continuous change or effective action [changing]</p><p><b>Uvijek biti prisutan. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being always present</p><p><b>bilo kada, ikad, ikada, svagda, uopće, uvijek (od &quot;ever&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain in the central Himalayas on the border of Tibet and Nepal [Mount Everest, Mt. Everest]</p><p><b>država u jugoistočnim Sjedinjenim Državama između Atlantika i Meksičkog zaljeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in southeastern United States between the Atlantic and the Gulf of Mexico [FL, Fla., Florida, Sunshine State]</p><p><b>veliko subtropsko močvare u južnoj Floridi koja je poznata po svojoj divljini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large subtropical swamp in southern Florida that is noted for its wildlife</p><p><b>Nacionalni park Everglades</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a national park in Florida containing an immense subtropical wilderness with mangrove swamps and rare birds and wild animals</p><p><b>zimzelen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant having foliage that persists and remains green throughout the year [evergreen plant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of plants and shrubs) bearing foliage throughout the year</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih bukova južne hemisfere koji imaju male obično zimzelene lišće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various beeches of the southern hemisphere having small usually evergreen leaves [southern beech]</p><p><b>široka i grmljava azijska grmljava stabla s ružičastim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> broad and bushy Asiatic twining shrub with pinkish fruit [Euonymus fortunei radicans, Euonymus radicans vegetus]</p><p><b>grm iz istočne Sjedinjenih Država s blistavim zimzeljenim lišćama i plavo-crnim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub of the eastern United States having shining evergreen leaves and bluish-black fruit [Vaccinium myrsinites]</p><p><b>Kalifornijska zimzelena divlja šljiva s trnastima kožnim listovima i bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> California evergreen wild plum with spiny leathery leaves and white flowers [Prunus ilicifolia, holly-leaf cherry, holly-leaved cherry, islay]</p><p><b>hrupna višegodišnja evroazijska trava slična ovsima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coarse perennial Eurasian grass resembling oat [Arrhenatherum elatius, French rye, false oat, tall meadow grass, tall oat grass]</p><p><b>tvrdo grmljevo zimzeleno grmlje iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike koje ima kisle crne bobice i sjajno zeleno lišće koje se koristi u cvjetnim aranžmanima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stiff bushy evergreen shrub of western North America having sour black berries and glossy green foliage used in floral arrangements [Vaccinium ovatum]</p><p><b>uvijekzeleno stablo iz južnih Sjedinjenih Država s velikim čvrstim blistavim lišćama i velikim bijelim slatko mirisnim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen tree of southern United States having large stiff glossy leaves and huge white sweet-smelling flowers [Magnolia grandiflora, bull bay, large-flowering magnolia, southern magnolia]</p><p><b>visoka višegodišnja trava koja se širi puzećim rizomima i uzgaja se za krmnu uporabu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall perennial grass that spreads by creeping rhizomes and is grown for fodder [Aleppo grass, Johnson grass, Sorghum halepense, means grass]</p><p><b>zelena hrast iz južne Europe s lištima sličnim lištima šumovca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen oak of southern Europe having leaves somewhat resembling those of holly [Quercus ilex, holly-leaved oak, holm oak, holm tree]</p><p><b>biljka koja ima lišće koje ostaje zeleno tijekom cijele godine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant having foliage that persists and remains green throughout the year [evergreen]</p><p><b>Washington</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in northwestern United States on the Pacific [WA, Wash., Washington]</p><p><b>zelena borovnica iz jugoistočne Europe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen hawthorn of southeastern Europe [Crataegus oxyacantha]</p><p><b>Stalnozelena šarena od istočne Sjeverne Amerike s dugoličnim kožnim listovima i malim crnim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen holly of eastern North America with oblong leathery leaves and small black berries [Ilex glabra, gall-berry, gallberry, inkberry]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički zimzeleni paprikac s pramenjenim lišćama i gustim grmovima lančastih listova, Sjevernoamerički paprika sa večnozelenim lišćama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American evergreen fern having pinnate leaves and dense clusters of lance-shaped fronds [Christmas fern, Polystichum acrostichoides, canker brake, dagger fern]</p><p><i>n.</i> North American fern with evergreen fronds [Dryopteris marginalis, leatherleaf wood fern, marginal wood fern]</p><p><b>dugotrajan, neven, trajan, vječan, vječit, večan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of various genera of the family Compositae having flowers that can be dried without loss of form or color [everlasting flower]</p><p><i>adj.</i> continuing forever or indefinitely [aeonian, ageless, eonian, eternal, perpetual, unceasing, unending]</p><p><i>adj.</i> without qualification [arrant, complete, consummate, double-dyed, gross, perfect, pure, sodding, staring, stark, thorough, thoroughgoing, unadulterated, utter]</p><p><b>Svaka biljka iz različitih rodova iz obitelji Compositae s cvijećem koje se može sušiti bez gubitka oblika ili boje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of various genera of the family Compositae having flowers that can be dried without loss of form or color [everlasting]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko višegodišnjih vinograda rod Lathyrus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several perennial vines of the genus Lathyrus</p><p><b>dugotrajan, neven, trajan, vječan, vječit, večan (od &quot;everlasting&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> for a limitless time [eternally, evermore, forever]</p><p><b>dugotrajan, neven, trajan, vječan, vječit, večan (od &quot;everlasting&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of lasting forever</p><p><b>uvijek, zauvijek</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at any future time [forevermore]</p><p><i>adv.</i> for a limitless time [eternally, everlastingly, forever]</p><p><b>lišajevi iz obitelji Usneaceae s višenjakovitim ili grmljivim talusom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lichens of the family Usneaceae having a pendulous or shrubby thallus [genus Evernia]</p><p><b>bilo kada, ikad, ikada, svagda, uopće, uvijek (od &quot;ever&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States civil rights worker in Mississippi [Medgar Evers, Medgar Wiley Evers]</p><p><b>položaj okrenut prema van, Čin prevrtanja naopako. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the position of being turned outward</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of turning inside out [everting, inversion]</p><p><b>Chris Evert</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States tennis player who won women's singles titles in the United States and at Wimbledon (born in 1954) [Chris Evert, Chrissie Evert, Christine Marie Evert]</p><p><i>v.</i> turn inside out</p><p><b>Chris Evert (od &quot;evert&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of turning inside out [eversion, inversion]</p><p><b>o, sav, svaki, sve, sva, svaka, svake, svakih, svako, svakog</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of count nouns) each and all of the members of a group considered singly and without exception</p><p><i>adj.</i> each and all of a series of entities or intervals as specified</p><p><b>jednako</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to the same degree (often followed by `as') [as, equally]</p><p><b>U svakom pogledu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in every way</p><p><b>(koristi se kao intenzivna) svakih (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used as intensive) every</p><p><b>na kraju svakog dana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at the end of each day [nightly]</p><p><b>povremeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> occasionally [every so often]</p><p><b>u intervalima od tri mjeseca (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in three month intervals [quarterly]</p><p><b>povremeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> occasionally [every now and then]</p><p><b>bez propusta tjedan dana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without missing a week [each week, hebdomadally, weekly]</p><p><b>slučajno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a random manner [arbitrarily, at random, haphazardly, indiscriminately, randomly, willy-nilly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> haphazardly [helter-skelter]</p><p><b>godišnje</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without missing a year [annually, each year, yearly]</p><p><b>svakidašnji, svakidašnjica, svakodnevan, svakodnevne, svakodnevnica, svakodnevnice, svakodnevnom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> found in the ordinary course of events [mundane, quotidian, routine, unremarkable, workaday]</p><p><i>adj.</i> appropriate for ordinary or routine occasions [casual, daily]</p><p><i>adj.</i> commonplace and ordinary</p><p><b>svakidašnji, svakidašnjica, svakodnevan, svakodnevne, svakodnevnica, svakodnevnice, svakodnevnom (od &quot;everyday&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ordinariness as a consequence of being frequent and commonplace [commonness, commonplaceness]</p><p><b>obična osoba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ordinary person</p><p><b>na bilo koje ili na sva mjesta (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to or in any or all places [all over, everywhere]</p><p><b>svagdje, svuda, svugdje</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to or in any or all places [all over, everyplace]</p><p><b>iseliti, istjerati, istjerati s posjeda</b></p><p><i>v.</i> expel or eject without recourse to legal process</p><p><i>v.</i> expel from one's property or force to move out by a legal process [force out]</p><p><b>deložacija, evikcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> action by a landlord that compels a tenant to leave the premises (as by rendering the premises unfit for occupancy) [constructive eviction]</p><p><i>n.</i> the expulsion of someone (such as a tenant) from the possession of land by process of law [dispossession, legal ouster]</p><p><b>argument, dokaz, dokazati, dokazivanje, evidencija, očiglednost, očitost, pokazati, razjasniti, svjedočenje, svjedočiti, trag, dokazi, dokazivati, pokazivati, posvjedočiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> your basis for belief or disbelief [grounds]</p><p><i>n.</i> an indication that makes something evident</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) all the means by which any alleged matter of fact whose truth is investigated at judicial trial is established or disproved</p><p><i>v.</i> provide evidence for [attest, certify, demonstrate, manifest]</p><p><i>v.</i> provide evidence for [bear witness, prove, show, testify]</p><p><i>v.</i> give evidence [tell]</p><p><b>svjedoći</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> supported by evidence</p><p><b>evidentan, evidentno, jasan, očevidan, očit, otvoren, vidljiv, vidljivi</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> clearly revealed to the mind or the senses or judgment [apparent, manifest, palpable, patent, plain, unmistakable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being seen or noticed [discernible, observable]</p><p><b>koji služe kao dokazi ili se temelje na njima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving as or based on evidence [evidentiary]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na dokaze ili predstavljaju dokaze, koji služe kao dokazi ili se temelje na njima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to or constituting evidence</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving as or based on evidence [evidential]</p><p><b>očito</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> unmistakably (`plain' is often used informally for `plainly') [apparently, manifestly, obviously, patently, plain, plainly]</p><p><b>grješan, grozna, loš, nevolja, opak, zala, zao, zla, zlo, hudoba, iskvarenost, nemoral, nemoralnost, pokvarenost, zloća, zločestoća, zloba, pokvaren, zločest</b></p><p><i>n.</i> morally objectionable behavior [immorality, iniquity, wickedness]</p><p><i>n.</i> that which causes harm or destruction or misfortune</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being morally wrong in principle or practice [evilness]</p><p><i>adj.</i> morally bad or wrong</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the nature of vice [vicious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or exerting a malignant influence [malefic, malevolent, malign]</p><p><b>pogled za koji se vjeruje da ima moć nanosa štete. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a look that is believed to have the power of inflicting harm</p><p><b>duh koji ima sklonost da uzrokuje štetu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spirit tending to cause harm</p><p><b>koji ima loš izgled. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an evil appearance</p><p><b>ima loše misli ili namjere (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having evil thoughts or intentions</p><p><b>grešnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who sins (without repenting) [sinner]</p><p><b>čin prekršaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of transgressing [transgression]</p><p><b>grješan, grozna, loš, nevolja, opak, zala, zao, zla, zlo (od &quot;evil&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a wicked evil manner [wickedly]</p><p><b>zlo, zloba, zloća</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being morally wrong in principle or practice [evil]</p><p><b>dokazati, izložiti, pobijediti, pokazati, iskazati, iskazivati, manifestirati, očitovati, pokazivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give expression to [express, show]</p><p><b>izvaditi drob, izvaditi utrobu, vaditi drob, vaditi utrobu</b></p><p><i>v.</i> surgically remove a part of a structure or an organ [resect]</p><p><i>v.</i> remove the contents of</p><p><i>v.</i> remove the entrails of [disembowel, draw]</p><p><i>v.</i> take away a vital or essential part of</p><p><i>adj.</i> having been disembowelled</p><p><b>evisceracija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical removal of an organ (or the contents of an organ) from a patient</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of removing the bowels or viscera [disembowelment]</p><p><i>n.</i> altering something (as a legislative act or a statement) in such a manner as to reduce its value</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to primjena na proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 98. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being avoided or warded off [avertable, avertible, avoidable]</p><p><b>evokacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> imaginative re-creation</p><p><i>n.</i> calling up supposed supernatural forces by spells and incantations [summoning]</p><p><i>n.</i> stimulation that calls up (draws forth) a particular class of behaviors [elicitation, induction]</p><p><b>izazivački</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to bring to mind [redolent, remindful, reminiscent, resonant]</p><p><b>buditi (uspomene), dozivati, evocirati, prizivati, probuditi, buditi, izazivati, izazvati, pobuditi, pobuđivati, podjariti, potaknuti, potaći, poticati, raspaliti, raspaljivati, raspiriti, rasplamsati, rasplamsavati, razbuktati, razbuktavati, zametnuti, dočarati, naslikati sliku, predložiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> call forth (emotions, feelings, and responses) [arouse, elicit, enkindle, fire, kindle, provoke, raise]</p><p><i>v.</i> evoke or provoke to appear or occur [call forth, kick up, provoke]</p><p><i>v.</i> deduce (a principle) or construe (a meaning) [draw out, educe, elicit, extract]</p><p><i>v.</i> summon into action or bring into existence, often as if by magic [arouse, bring up, call down, call forth, conjure, conjure up, invoke, put forward, raise, stir]</p><p><i>v.</i> call to mind [paint a picture, suggest]</p><p><b>evocirani, pobuđeni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> called forth from a latent or potential state by stimulation [elicited]</p><p><b>električni odgovor središnjeg živčanog sustava koji proizlazi iz vanjskog podražaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the electrical response of the central nervous system produced by an external stimulus</p><p><b>evolucija, evolucije, postanak, postanka, razviće, razvoj, razvitak, filogenija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a process in which something passes by degrees to a different stage (especially a more advanced or mature stage) [development]</p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) the sequence of events involved in the evolutionary development of a species or taxonomic group of organisms [organic evolution, phylogenesis, phylogeny]</p><p><b>evolutivni, evolucijski (od &quot;evolutionary&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an evolutionary way</p><p><b>evolutivni, evolucijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or produced by evolution</p><p><b>Opći smjer evolucijske promjene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a general direction of evolutionary change</p><p><b>evolucionizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) a scientific theory of the origin of species of plants and animals [theory of evolution, theory of organic evolution]</p><p><b>osoba koja vjeruje u organsku evoluciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who believes in organic evolution</p><p><b>evoluirati, nastajali, nastajati, raširiti se, razviti, razviti se, razvijati se, razvijati, steći, sticati, stjecati, usvajati, usvojiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> work out [develop, germinate]</p><p><i>v.</i> undergo development or evolution</p><p><i>v.</i> gain through experience [acquire, develop]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, države članice mogu dopustiti da se radi na korištenju radi radicijskih sustava za upravljanje energijom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> military action involving the use of electromagnetic energy to determine or exploit or reduce or prevent hostile use of the electromagnetic spectrum [electronic warfare]</p><p><b>ovca, Éwé jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a people living in southern Benin and Togo and southeastern Ghana</p><p><i>n.</i> a Kwa language spoken by the Ewe in Ghana and Togo and Benin</p><p><i>n.</i> female sheep</p><p><b>pripadnik naroda koji živi u području sjeverne Mongolije i istočnog Sibira, Tunguski jezik Evenki u istočnom Sibiru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the people inhabiting an area of northern Mongolia and eastern Siberia [Evenki]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Tungusic language of the Evenki in eastern Siberia [Evenki, Tungus, Tunguz]</p><p><b>bokal, ibrik, krčag, vrč</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an open vessel with a handle and a spout for pouring [pitcher]</p><p><b>maligni tumor u koštanoj srži (obično u zdjelici ili dugim kostima) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> malignant tumor in bone marrow (usually in the pelvis or in long bones) [Ewing's tumor, Ewing's tumour, endothelial myeloma]</p><p><b>maligni tumor u koštanoj srži (obično u zdjelici ili dugim kostima) (MT)</b></p><p>