d [dig up, turn up]</p><p><i>v.</i> form by hollowing</p><p><i>v.</i> remove the inner part or the core of [dig, hollow]</p><p><b>iskop, iskopavanje, arheološko nalazište, iskopina, rudarstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of digging [dig, digging]</p><p><i>n.</i> the site of an archeological exploration [archeological site, dig]</p><p><i>n.</i> a hole in the ground made by excavating</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of extracting ores or coal etc from the earth [mining]</p><p><b>bager, bager jaružar, bager za kopanje zemlje, edskavator, ekskavator, iskapač, stroj za iskapanje zemlje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a workman who excavates for foundations of buildings or for quarrying</p><p><i>n.</i> a machine for excavating [digger, power shovel, shovel]</p><p><b>nadvisiti, prekoračiti, prelaziti, premašiti, premašivati, prevladati, prijeći, nadmašivati, nadilaziti, nadići, natkriliti, nadigrati, nadmašiti, prestići, preteći</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be greater in scope or size than some standard [surpass, transcend]</p><p><i>v.</i> be superior or better than some standard [go past, overstep, pass, top, transcend]</p><p><i>v.</i> be or do something to a greater degree [outdo, outgo, outmatch, outperform, outstrip, surmount, surpass]</p><p><b>(geologija) vjerojatnost da će potres uzrokovati razinu kretanja tla koja će tijekom određenog vremena izloženosti premašiti određenu referentnu razinu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (geology) the probability that an earthquake will generate a level of ground motion that exceeds a specified reference level during a given exposure time</p><p><b>prekoračenje, prelazeći, prelazi, prevladavanje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> far beyond what is usual in magnitude or degree [exceptional, olympian, prodigious, surpassing]</p><p><b>neizmjerno, previše</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to an extreme degree [deathly, extremely, super]</p><p><b>isticati se, nadmašiti, nadmašivati, odlikovati se, razriješiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> distinguish oneself [stand out, surpass]</p><p><b>biti dobar u (MT)<