><i>adv.</i> to an exceptional degree</p><p><b>istaknuti, izvadak, izvod, odlomak, odsječak, praviti izvode</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a passage selected from a larger work [excerption, extract, selection]</p><p><i>v.</i> take out of a literary work in order to cite or copy [extract, take out]</p><p><b>izvadak, odlomak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a passage selected from a larger work [excerpt, extract, selection]</p><p><b>eksces, franšiza, odbitna franšiza, ostaci, ostatak, ostatke, prekomjeran, prekoračenje, preobilje, prestup, pretjeranost, višak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a quantity much larger than is needed [nimiety, surplus, surplusage]</p><p><i>n.</i> immoderation as a consequence of going beyond sufficient or permitted limits [excessiveness, inordinateness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being more than full [overabundance, surfeit]</p><p><i>n.</i> excessive indulgence [overindulgence]</p><p><i>adj.</i> more than is needed, desired, or required [extra, redundant, spare, supererogatory, superfluous, supernumerary, surplus]</p><p><b>neumjeren, predimenzioniran, pretjeran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> beyond normal limits [inordinate, undue, unreasonable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unrestrained, especially with regard to feelings [extravagant, exuberant, overweening]</p><p><b>neobičan, neumjeren, prekomjerno, pretjeran, previše</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a degree exceeding normal or proper limits [overly, to a fault, too]</p><p><b>neumjeren, predimenzioniran, pretjeran (od &quot;excessive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> immoderation as a consequence of going beyond sufficient or permitted limits [excess, inordinateness]</p><p><b>burza, izmjena, mijenjati, promet, promijeniti, razmijeniti, razmjena, zamijeniti, zamjena, razmijenili, razmjene, zamjenu, razmjenjivanje, centrala, mijenjanje, izmijeniti, izmjenjivati, razmjenjivati, zamjenjivati, preinačavati, preinačiti, preinačivati, preobraziti, preobražavati, pretvarati, pretvoriti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chemical process in which one atom or ion or group changes