mething that agitates and arouses [excitement]</p><p><b>uzbudljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of drugs e.g.) able to excite or stimulate [excitant, excitatory]</p><p><b>uzbudljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of drugs e.g.) able to excite or stimulate [excitant, excitative]</p><p><b>nadražiti, pobuditi, pobuđivati, pokrenuti, raspaljivati, uzbuditi, uzbuđivati, komešati se, stimulirati, uskomešati se, nadraživati, napaliti, napaljivati, potaknuti, poticati, raspaliti, uspaliti, uspaljivati, komešati, potresati, potresti, uskomešati, uzdrmati, uzrujati, uzrujavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> arouse or elicit a feeling</p><p><i>v.</i> act as a stimulant [stimulate]</p><p><i>v.</i> stir feelings in [stimulate, stir]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be agitated, excited, or roused [agitate, charge, charge up, commove, rouse, turn on]</p><p><i>v.</i> stimulate sexually [arouse, sex, turn on, wind up]</p><p><i>v.</i> stir the feelings, emotions, or peace of [shake, shake up, stimulate, stir]</p><p><i>v.</i> raise to a higher energy level [energise, energize]</p><p><i>v.</i> produce a magnetic field in</p><p><b>napaljen, raspaljen, uzbuđen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of persons) excessively affected by emotion [aroused, emotional, worked up]</p><p><i>adj.</i> in an aroused state</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by uncontrolled excitement or emotion [delirious, frantic, mad, unrestrained]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of e.g. a molecule) made reactive or more reactive [activated]</p><p><b>napaljen, raspaljen, uzbuđen (od &quot;excited&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with excitement</p><p><b>uzbudljivost, uzbuđenje, zanimljivost, galama, metež, uzrujanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling of lively and cheerful joy [exhilaration]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being emotionally aroused and worked up [excitation, fervor, fervour, inflammation]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that agitates and arouses [excitation]</p><p><i>n.</i> disturbance usually in protest [agitation, hullabaloo, turmoil, upheaval]</p><p><b>uzbudljiv, uzbudljive</b></p>