ate act of omission [elision, exception]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of forcing out someone or something [ejection, expulsion, riddance]</p><p><b>Nijedan dva elektron ili proton ili neutron u datom sustavu ne može biti u stanju karakteriziranim istim skupom kvantnih brojeva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> no two electrons or protons or neutrons in a given system can be in states characterized by the same set of quantum numbers [Pauli exclusion principle]</p><p><b>Pravilo koje predviđa da se dokazi koji su inače prihvatljivi ne mogu koristiti u kaznenom suđenju ako su rezultat nezakonitog policijskog ponašanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rule that provides that otherwise admissible evidence cannot be used in a criminal trial if it was the result of illegal police conduct</p><p><b>ekskluzivan, isključiv, isključiva, izuzetan, izuzetnim, neuračunat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a news report that is reported first by one news organization [scoop]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not divided or shared with others [sole]</p><p><i>adj.</i> excluding much or all</p><p><i>adj.</i> not divided among or brought to bear on more than one object or objective [single, undivided]</p><p><b>povlastica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a right reserved exclusively by a particular person or group (especially a hereditary or official right) [perquisite, prerogative, privilege]</p><p><b>ekskluzivno, isključivo, isključno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without any others being included or involved [alone, entirely, only, solely]</p><p><b>isključivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tendency to associate with only a select group [clannishness, cliquishness]</p><p><b>kontemplirati, meditirati, misliti, mozgati, promisliti, promišljati, promozgati, razmatrati, razmisliti, razmišljati, razmotriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come up with (an idea, plan, explanation, theory, or principle) after a mental effort [contrive, devise, forge, formulate, invent]</p><p><i>v.</i> reflect deeply on a subject [chew over, contemplate, meditate, mull, mull over, muse, ponder, reflect,