ika, izgovor, izlika, izvinuti, opravdanje, opravdati, oprostiti, osloboditi, opraštati, objasniti, ispričavati, opravdavati, racionalizirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a defense of some offensive behavior or some failure to keep a promise etc. [alibi, exculpation, self-justification]</p><p><i>n.</i> a note explaining an absence</p><p><i>n.</i> a poor example [apology]</p><p><i>v.</i> accept an excuse for [pardon]</p><p><i>v.</i> grant exemption or release to [exempt, let off, relieve]</p><p><i>v.</i> serve as a reason or cause or justification of [explain]</p><p><i>v.</i> defend, explain, clear away, or make excuses for by reasoning [apologise, apologize, rationalise, rationalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> ask for permission to be released from an engagement [beg off]</p><p><i>v.</i> excuse, overlook, or make allowances for [condone]</p><p><b>odobrena izuzeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> granted exemption</p><p><b>ispričati, isprika, izgovor, izlika, izvinuti, opravdanje, opravdati, oprostiti, osloboditi (od &quot;excuse&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who pardons or forgives or excuses a fault or offense [forgiver, pardoner]</p><p><b>Glavni izvršni odjel vlade Sjedinjenih Država. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the chief executive department of the United States government [White House]</p><p><b>odvratan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of very poor quality or condition [deplorable, miserable, woeful, wretched]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unequivocally detestable [abominable, detestable, odious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> deserving a curse [damnable]</p><p><b>proklinjati, gaditi se, gnušati se, groziti se, užasavati se, zazirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> find repugnant [abhor, abominate, loathe]</p><p><i>v.</i> curse or declare to be evil or anathema or threaten with divine punishment [accurse, anathematise, anathematize, anathemise, anathemize, comminate]</p><p><b>Mržnja u kombinaciji s odvratnošću., prizivanje nekoj natprirodnoj moći da nanese zlo nekome ili nekoj grupi ljudi., predmet prokletstva ili mržnje (MT)</b></