za, zatvarač, poveznica, spojka, spojnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who fastens or makes fast</p><p><i>n.</i> restraint that attaches to something or holds something in place [fastening, fixing, holdfast]</p><p><b>spoj, veza, vezanje, kopča, poveznica, spojka, spojnica, spona, zatvarač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> restraint that attaches to something or holds something in place [fastener, fixing, holdfast]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of fastening things together [attachment]</p><p><b>brže</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> more quickly [quicker]</p><p><b>najbrže, najbrži</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> most quickly [quickest]</p><p><b>gadljiv, izbirljiv, koji probira</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> giving careful attention to detail</p><p><i>adj.</i> having complicated nutritional requirements [exacting]</p><p><b>gadljiv, izbirljiv, koji probira (od &quot;fastidious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a fastidious and painstaking manner [painstakingly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a fastidious manner</p><p><b>gadljiv, izbirljiv, koji probira (od &quot;fastidious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being meticulous about matters of taste or style</p><p><b>s visokom visinom od oko 30 mm ili više, ali ne više od 30 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having clusters of erect branches (often appearing to form a single column)</p><p><b>post, gladovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abstaining from food [fast]</p><p><b>krafne tradicionalno jesti na Shrove utorak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> doughnut traditionally eaten on Shrove Tuesday</p><p><b>čvrstoća, brzina, brzost, hitrina, hitrost, hitroća, žustrina, uporište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rate (usually rapid) at which something happens [speed, swiftness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being fixed in place as by some firm attachment [fixedness, fixity, fixture, secureness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a strongly fortified defensive structure [stronghold]</p><p><b>celulit, debeo, debljina, gojiti se, jak, masnoća, mast, mastan, obilan, salo, ugojen, unosan, debela, masni, masno, masnoće, masti, loj, pretilost, debljati, gojiti, toviti, udebljati, ugojiti, utoviti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soft greasy substance occurring in organic tissue and consisting of a mixture of lipids (mostly triglycerides)</p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of body tissue containing stored fat that serves as a source of energy [adipose tissue, fatty tissue]</p><p><i>n.</i> excess bodily weight [avoirdupois, blubber, fatness]</p><p><i>v.</i> make fat or plump [fatten, fatten out, fatten up, fill out, flesh out, plump, plump out]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having an (over)abundance of flesh</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a relatively large diameter</p><p><i>adj.</i> containing or composed of fat [fatty]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lucrative [juicy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by great fruitfulness [fertile, productive, rich]</p><p><b>Bogata i privilegirana osoba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wealthy and privileged person</p><p><b>masna stanica, adipocit, adipozna stanica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cells composed of fat [adipose cell]</p><p><b>malo ili nikakve šanse za uspjeh (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> little or no chance of success [slim chance]</p><p><b>ozbiljan stan u kojem masnoća blokira arteriju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> serious condition in which fat blocks an artery</p><p><b>zdravilište koje se specijalizira za pomoć ljudima u mršavljenju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a health spa that specializes in helping people lose weight</p><p><b>Europska biljka naturalizirana u Sjevernoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European plant naturalized in North America [Chenopodium bonus-henricus, allgood, good-king-henry, wild spinach]</p><p><b>metabolički proces koji razgrađuje unosene masti u masne kiseline i glicerol, a zatim u jednostavnije spojeve koje mogu koristiti stanice tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a metabolic process that breaks down ingested fats into fatty acids and glycerol and then into simpler compounds that can be used by cells of the body</p><p><b>debeljko</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rotund individual [butterball, fatso, fatty, roly-poly]</p><p><b>Posljednji dan prije Posljednjeg posta., karneval koji se u nekim zemljama održava u Šrov utorak (posljednji dan prije Posjeta), ali posebno u New Orleansu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the last day before Lent [Mardi Gras, Shrove Tuesday, pancake day]</p><p><i>n.</i> a carnival held in some countries on Shrove Tuesday (the last day before Lent) but especially in New Orleans [Mardi Gras]</p><p><b>bez masti ili masnih čvrstih tvari (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> without fat or fat solids [fatless, nonfat]</p><p><b>rastvoran u mastima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> soluble in fats</p><p><b>vitamin topljiv u masti, vitamini topljivi u mastima</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any vitamin that is soluble in fats</p><p><b>miraž u Mesinskom moreuzu (pripisuje se Arthurian čarobnjak Morgan le Fay) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mirage in the Strait of Messina (attributed to the Arthurian sorcerer Morgan le Fay)</p><p><b>Palestinska politička i vojna organizacija koju je osnovao Yasser Arafat 1958. godine kako bi se radila na stvaranju palestinske države. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Palestinian political and military organization founded by Yasser Arafat in 1958 to work toward the creation of a Palestinian state [al-Asifa, al-Fatah]</p><p><b>Palestinska međunarodna teroristička organizacija koja se odvojila od PLO-a 1974. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Palestinian international terrorist organization that split from the PLO in 1974 [ANO, Abu Nidal Organization, Arab Revolutionary Brigades, Black September, Fatah-RC, Revolutionary Organization of Socialist Muslims]</p><p><b>Teroristička grupa koju je 1995. godine organizirao Yasser Arafat kao oružano krilo Al-Fatah-a. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a terrorist group organized by Yasser Arafat in 1995 as the armed wing of al-Fatah [Tanzim]</p><p><b>Palestinska međunarodna teroristička organizacija koja se odvojila od PLO-a 1974. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Palestinian international terrorist organization that split from the PLO in 1974 [ANO, Abu Nidal Organization, Arab Revolutionary Brigades, Black September, Fatah Revolutionary Council, Revolutionary Organization of Socialist Muslims]</p><p><b>fatalan, koban, kobno, poguban, smrtan, smrtonosan, kobne</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> bringing death</p><p><i>adj.</i> having momentous consequences [fateful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of events) having extremely unfortunate or dire consequences [black, calamitous, disastrous, fateful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> controlled or decreed by fate [fateful]</p><p><b>nesreća koja uzrokuje smrt nekoga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an accident that causes someone to die [casualty]</p><p><b>fatalizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a submissive mental attitude resulting from acceptance of the doctrine that everything that happens is predetermined and inevitable</p><p><i>n.</i> a philosophical doctrine holding that all events are predetermined in advance for all time and human beings are powerless to change them</p><p><b>fatalist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anyone who submits to the belief that they are powerless to change their destiny [determinist, predestinarian, predestinationist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to fatalism [fatalistic]</p><p><b>fatalističan, fatalistički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to fatalism [fatalist]</p><p><b>fatalnost, kob</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a death resulting from an accident or a disaster [human death]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being able to cause death or fatal disasters</p><p><b>odnos smrtnosti u području prema stanovništvu tog područja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio of deaths in an area to the population of that area [death rate, deathrate, mortality, mortality rate]</p><p><b>kobno, smrtno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with fatal consequences or implications</p><p><b>slana svinjska mesa iz stražnje strane svinjske lešine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> salt pork from the back of a hog carcass</p><p><b>kob, sudbina, udes, usud, fatum, sudba, okolnosti, sreća</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event (or a course of events) that will inevitably happen in the future [destiny]</p><p><i>n.</i> the ultimate agency regarded as predetermining the course of events (often personified as a woman) [destiny]</p><p><i>n.</i> your overall circumstances or condition in life (including everything that happens to you) [circumstances, destiny, fortune, lot, luck, portion]</p><p><i>v.</i> decree or designate beforehand [designate, destine, doom]</p><p><b>koban, od sudbine unaprijed određen, osuđen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually followed by `to') determined by tragic fate [doomed]</p><p><b>koban, odlučan, proročki, sudbonosan, upravljan od sudbine, zlokoban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having momentous consequences [fatal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> ominously prophetic [foreboding, portentous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of events) having extremely unfortunate or dire consequences [black, calamitous, disastrous, fatal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> controlled or decreed by fate [fatal]</p><p><b>kobno, odlučno, zlokobno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a prophetically fateful manner</p><p><b>Čovjek koji je glup, nesposoban budala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who is a stupid incompetent fool [bozo, cuckoo, goof, goofball, goose, jackass, twat, zany]</p><p><b>(koristi se neformalno) glup (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used informally) stupid [blockheaded, boneheaded, duncical, duncish, loggerheaded, thick, thick-skulled, thickheaded, wooden-headed]</p><p><b>otac, redovnik, tata, osnivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a male parent (also used as a term of address to your father) [begetter, male parent]</p><p><i>n.</i> the founder of a family [forefather, sire]</p><p><i>n.</i> `Father' is a term of address for priests in some churches (especially the Roman Catholic Church or the Orthodox Catholic Church) [Padre]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Christianity) any of about 70 theologians in the period from the 2nd to the 7th century whose writing established and confirmed official church doctrine [Church Father, Father of the Church]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who holds an important or distinguished position in some organization</p><p><i>n.</i> God when considered as the first person in the Trinity [Father-God, Fatherhood]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who founds or establishes some institution [beginner, founder, founding father]</p><p><i>n.</i> the head of an organized crime family [don]</p><p><i>v.</i> make (offspring) by reproduction [beget, bring forth, engender, generate, get, mother, sire]</p><p><b>katolički svećenik koji je bio junak detektivskih priča G. K. Chestertona. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Catholic priest who was the hero of detective stories by G. K. Chesterton</p><p><b>Legendarni zaštitnik djece. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the legendary patron saint of children [Kriss Kringle, Saint Nicholas, Saint Nick, Santa, Santa Claus, St. Nick]</p><p><b>Čovjek koji preuzima sve funkcije pravog oca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who takes over all the functions of the real father [father surrogate]</p><p><b>Američki elektroinženjer koji je 1907. patentirao prvu triodnu vakuumsku cijev koja je omogućila otkrivanje i pojačavanje radio valova (1873-1961) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States electrical engineer who in 1907 patented the first triode vacuum tube, which made it possible to detect and amplify radio waves (1873-1961) [De Forest, Lee De Forest]</p><p><b>(Kršćanstvo) bilo koji od oko 70 teologa u razdoblju od 2. do 7. stoljeća čiji su pisani dokazi utvrdili i potvrdili službeni crkveni nauk (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Christianity) any of about 70 theologians in the period from the 2nd to the 7th century whose writing established and confirmed official church doctrine [Church Father, Father]</p><p><b>Američki izumitelj koji je 1775. godine dizajnirao potopnicu koja je bila neučinkovita, ali mu je kasnije zaslužila priznanje kao pionir podmornice (1742-1824) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American inventor who in 1775 designed a man-propelled submarine that was ineffectual but subsequently earned him recognition as a submarine pioneer (1742-1824) [Bushnell, David Bushnell]</p><p><b>Čovjek koji preuzima sve funkcije pravog oca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who takes over all the functions of the real father [father figure]</p><p><b>SAD: treća nedjelja u lipnju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> US: third Sunday in June</p><p><b>Čovjek (često moćan ili utjecajni čovjek) koji izaziva osjećaje obično osjećate za svog pravog oca i s kojim se identificirate psihološki (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man (often a powerful or influential man) who arouses emotions usually felt for your real father and with whom you identify psychologically</p><p><b>Bog kao prva osoba u Trojstvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> God when considered as the first person in the Trinity [Father, Fatherhood]</p><p><b>svekar, tast</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the father of your spouse</p><p><b>očinstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the kinship relation between an offspring and the father [paternity]</p><p><i>n.</i> God when considered as the first person in the Trinity [Father, Father-God]</p><p><i>n.</i> the status of a religious leader</p><p><i>n.</i> the status of a father</p><p><b>domovinski, otadžbina, domovina, zavičaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the country where you were born [country of origin, homeland, mother country, motherland, native land]</p><p><b>bez oca koji živi., bez poznatog ili pravno odgovornog oca (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having no living father</p><p><i>adj.</i> not having a known or legally responsible father</p><p><b>Kao otac ili očevsko pravo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> like or befitting a father or fatherhood [fatherly]</p><p><b>dobrohotnost i zaštitljivost ili prikladnost oca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the benignity and protectiveness of or befitting a father [paternal quality]</p><p><b>očinski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> like or befitting a father or fatherhood [fatherlike]</p><p><b>dokučiti, duljinska mjera 6 stopa, hvat, mjeriti dubinu, nastojati proniknuti, ft, paš, sežanj, šest stopa, prodrijeti, sondirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a linear unit of measurement (equal to 6 feet) for water depth [fthm]</p><p><i>n.</i> (mining) a unit of volume (equal to 6 cubic feet) used in measuring bodies of ore [fthm]</p><p><i>v.</i> come to understand [bottom, penetrate]</p><p><i>v.</i> measure the depth of (a body of water) with a sounding line [sound]</p><p><b>(od dubine) može se sondirati ili mjeriti za dubinu, (od značenja) sposobna prodrijeti ili shvatiti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of depth) capable of being sounded or measured for depth [plumbable, soundable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of meaning) capable of being penetrated or comprehended</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> depth finder for determining depth of water or a submerged object by means of ultrasound waves [sonic depth finder]</p><p><b>osjetljivost na umor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> susceptibility to fatigue</p><p><b>trud, umor, umoriti se, zamarati, zamor, zamor materijala, zamoriti, umarati se, zamarati se, zamoriti se, zasititi se, zasićivati se, habati se, iscrpiti, iscrpljivati, iscrpsti, iskrzati se, istrošiti, izmarati, izmoriti, izmožditi, izmožđivati, izmučiti se, iznuriti, pohabati se, potrošiti, premarati, premoriti, trošiti, umarati, umoriti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> temporary loss of strength and energy resulting from hard physical or mental work [tiredness, weariness]</p><p><i>n.</i> used of materials (especially metals) in a weakened state caused by long stress</p><p><i>n.</i> (always used with a modifier) boredom resulting from overexposure to something</p><p><i>n.</i> labor of a nonmilitary kind done by soldiers (cleaning or digging or draining or so on) [fatigue duty]</p><p><i>v.</i> lose interest or become bored with something or somebody [jade, pall, tire, weary]</p><p><i>v.</i> exhaust or get tired through overuse or great strain or stress [fag, fag out, jade, outwear, tire, tire out, wear, wear down, wear out, wear upon, weary]</p><p><b>razbijanje u metalu zbog metalnog umorstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crack in metal resulting from metal fatigue</p><p><b>težak rad</b></p><p