ederalizma. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a former political party in the United States that favored a strong centralized federal government</p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of federalism</p><p><b>Velika politička stranka u SAD-u početkom 19. stoljeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a major political party in the United States in the early 19th century [American Federalist Party, Federal Party]</p><p><b>stanje pod saveznom kontrolom, Čin stavljanja pod savezni nadzor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being under federal control [federalisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of being put under federal control [federalisation]</p><p><b>Ujediniti se na saveznom nivou ili se udružiti u ligu., staviti pod kontrolu i autoritet savezne vlade, Ući u savez za zajednički cilj (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> unite on a federal basis or band together as a league [federalise, federate]</p><p><i>v.</i> put under the control and authority of a federal government [federalise]</p><p><i>v.</i> enter into a league for a common purpose [federalise, federate]</p><p><b>federalno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by federal government</p><p><b>organizirati na federalnoj osnovi, savezni, sjediniti u savez, udružen u federalnom savezu</b></p><p><i>v.</i> enter into a league for a common purpose [federalise, federalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> unite on a federal basis or band together as a league [federalise, federalize]</p><p><i>adj.</i> united under a central government [federated]</p><p><b>Ujedinjeni pod centralnom vladom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> united under a central government [federate]</p><p><b>Savezne Države Mikronezije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a country scattered over Micronesia with a constitutional government in free association with the United States [Micronesia, TT]</p><p><b>federacija, federacije, savez, savezna država, konfederacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organization formed by merging several groups or parties</p><p><i>n.</i> a union of political organizations [confederacy, confederation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the a