><p><i>n.</i> creation by the physical union of male and female gametes [fecundation, fertilisation, impregnation]</p><p><i>n.</i> making fertile as by applying fertilizer or manure [dressing, fecundation, fertilisation]</p><p><b>Stari embrion od trenutka oplodnje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the age of an embryo counting from the time of fertilization [fetal age, gestational age]</p><p><b>membrana koja se formira oko oplođene jajne ćelije i sprečava prodiranje dodatnih spermija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the membrane that forms around a fertilized ovum and prevents penetration by additional spermatozoon</p><p><b>oploditi, oplođivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> provide with fertilizers or add nutrients to [feed, fertilise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make fertile or productive [fecundate, fertilise]</p><p><i>v.</i> introduce semen into (a female) [fecundate, fertilise, inseminate]</p><p><b>embrio, zametak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an animal organism in the early stages of growth and differentiation that in higher forms merge into fetal stages but in lower forms terminate in commencement of larval life [conceptus, embryo]</p><p><b>zigota</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) the diploid cell resulting from the union of a haploid spermatozoon and ovum (including the organism that develops from that cell) [zygote]</p><p><b>gnojivo, umjetno gnojivo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any substance such as manure or a mixture of nitrates used to make soil more fertile [fertiliser, plant food]</p><p><b>šiba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a switch (a stick or cane or flat paddle) used to punish children</p><p><b>žar, žestina, vatra, vatrenost, zanos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feelings of great warmth and intensity [ardor, ardour, fervidness, fervor, fervour, fire]</p><p><b>vatren, vreo</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by intense emotion [ardent, fervid, fiery, impassioned, perfervid, torrid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (archaic) extremely hot, burning, or glowing [fervid]</p><p><b>vatren, vreo (od &quot;fervent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with passio