ssal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to the relation of a feudal vassal to his lord</p><p><i>adj.</i> owing feudal allegiance to or being subject to a sovereign</p><p><b>febra, groznica, visoka temperatura, vručica, vrućica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rise in the temperature of the body [febricity, febrility, feverishness, pyrexia]</p><p><i>n.</i> intense nervous anticipation</p><p><b>uzrokovan herpesom simplex virusa tipa 1 (HSV-1) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> caused by herpes simplex virus type 1 (HSV-1) [cold sore, herpes labialis, oral herpes]</p><p><b>stanje ekstremnog uzbuđenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of extreme excitement</p><p><b>bilo koje od nekoliko stabala s lišćama ili kore koja se koristi za ublažavanje groznice ili za koje se smatra da označavaju regije bez groznice., dekoratni grm ili malo stablo močvarnih područja u jugozapadnoj Sjedinjenim Državama s velikim ružičastim ili bijelim sepalom i kožom iz Georgia za liječenje groznice, visoka brzo rastuća drvena stabla s lišćama koje sadrže ljekovito ulje, Afričko drvo koje bi trebalo označiti zdrave regije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several trees having leaves or bark used to allay fever or thought to indicate regions free of fever</p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental shrub or small tree of swampy areas in southwestern United States having large pink or white sepals and yielding Georgia bark for treating fever [Georgia bark, Pinckneya pubens, bitter-bark]</p><p><i>n.</i> tall fast-growing timber tree with leaves containing a medicinal oil [Eucalyptus globulus, blue gum]</p><p><i>n.</i> African tree supposed to mark healthful regions [Acacia xanthophloea]</p><p><b>febra, groznica, visoka temperatura, vručica, vrućica (od &quot;fever&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> highly or nervously excited</p><p><b>divlja kamilica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bushy aromatic European perennial herb having clusters of buttonlike white-rayed flower heads [Chrysanthemum parthenium, Tanacetum parthenium]</p><p><b>grozničav, uzbuđen</b></p