stitutions) and invests them in financial assets [financial organisation, financial organization]</p><p><b>financijski gubitak, novčani gubitak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> loss of money or decrease in financial value</p><p><b>Federalna agencija u Ministarstvu financija koja upravlja vladinim sustavima isplate i prikupljanja i pruža središnje računovodstvo i financijsko izvještavanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the federal agency in the Treasury Department that manages the government's disbursement and collection systems and provides central accounting and financial reporting</p><p><b>pasiva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an obligation to pay money to another party [indebtedness, liability]</p><p><b>blagajnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an officer charged with receiving and disbursing funds [treasurer]</p><p><b>financijska institucija, financijska ustanova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an institution (public or private) that collects funds (from the public or other institutions) and invests them in financial assets [financial institution, financial organization]</p><p><b>financijska institucija, financijska ustanova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an institution (public or private) that collects funds (from the public or other institutions) and invests them in financial assets [financial institution, financial organisation]</p><p><b>financijsko izvješće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a document showing credits and debits [statement]</p><p><b>financijska potpora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> financial resources provided to make some project possible [backing, financial backing, funding, support]</p><p><b>financijska godina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any accounting period of 12 months [fiscal year]</p><p><b>financijski</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> from a financial point of view</p><p><b>financijer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person skilled in large scale financial transactions [moneyman]</p><p><i>v.</i> conduct financial operations</p><p><b>financiranja, financiranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of financing [funding]</p><p><b>veliki platno-glavni kit s duboki