ly a race)</p><p><i>n.</i> the downfall of someone (as of persons on one side of a conflict)</p><p><i>n.</i> event whose occurrence ends something [conclusion, ending]</p><p><i>n.</i> (wine tasting) the taste of a wine on the back of the tongue (as it is swallowed)</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of finishing [finishing]</p><p><i>v.</i> come or bring to a finish or an end [complete]</p><p><i>v.</i> finally be or do something [end up, fetch up, finish up, land up, wind up]</p><p><i>v.</i> have an end, in a temporal, spatial, or quantitative sense [cease, end, stop, terminate]</p><p><i>v.</i> provide with a finish</p><p><i>v.</i> finish eating all the food on one's plate or on the table [eat up, polish off]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to finish a relationship with somebody</p><p><b>za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 4. točaka (a) i (b) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the final coating of (eg., paint, plaster, varnish, etc.) [finishing coat]</p><p><b>linija koja označava mjesto cilja utrke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a line indicating the location of the finish of a race [finishing line]</p><p><b>dokončati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> finish a task completely [clear up, finish up, get through, mop up, polish off, wrap up]</p><p><b>Ispuni (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> fill out [round out]</p><p><b>završiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> finish a task completely [clear up, finish off, get through, mop up, polish off, wrap up]</p><p><i>v.</i> finally be or do something [end up, fetch up, finish, land up, wind up]</p><p><b>dovršen, finiširan, gotov, svršen, završen, završene, završetka, završimo, uništen, upropašten</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of materials or goods) brought to the desired final state</p><p><i>adj.</i> ended or brought to an end</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of skills or the products of skills) brought to or having the greatest excellence</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a surface coating or finish applied</p><p><i>adj.</i> brought to ruin [ruined]</p><p><b>ličilac, radnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (baseball) a relief 