knuti, odapeti, odapinjati, zapucati, buditi, izazivati, izazvati, pobuditi, pobuđivati, potaknuti, potaći, poticati, probuditi, raspaliti, raspaljivati, raspiriti, rasplamsati, rasplamsavati, razbuktati, razbuktavati, sažeći, sažgati, sažigati, spaliti, spaljivati, žeći, žgati, ložiti, tankirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the event of something burning (often destructive)</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of firing weapons or artillery at an enemy [firing]</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of combustion of inflammable materials producing heat and light and (often) smoke [flame, flaming]</p><p><i>n.</i> a fireplace in which a relatively small fire is burning</p><p><i>n.</i> once thought to be one of four elements composing the universe (Empedocles)</p><p><i>n.</i> feelings of great warmth and intensity [ardor, ardour, fervency, fervidness, fervor, fervour]</p><p><i>n.</i> fuel that is burning and is used as a means for cooking</p><p><i>n.</i> a severe trial</p><p><i>n.</i> intense adverse criticism [attack, blast, flack, flak]</p><p><i>v.</i> start firing a weapon [open fire]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to go off [discharge]</p><p><i>v.</i> bake in a kiln so as to harden</p><p><i>v.</i> terminate the employment of [can, dismiss, displace, force out, give notice, give the axe, give the sack, sack, send away, terminate]</p><p><i>v.</i> go off or discharge [discharge, go off]</p><p><i>v.</i> drive out or away by or as if by fire</p><p><i>v.</i> call forth (emotions, feelings, and responses) [arouse, elicit, enkindle, evoke, kindle, provoke, raise]</p><p><i>v.</i> destroy by fire [burn, burn down]</p><p><i>v.</i> provide with fuel [fuel]</p><p><i>v.</i> generate an electrical impulse</p><p><i>v.</i> become ignited [flame up]</p><p><i>v.</i> start or maintain a fire in [ignite, light]</p><p><b>javljač požara, požarna uzbuna, vatrodojavni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shout or bell to warn that fire has broken out</p><p><i>n.</i> an alarm that is tripped off by fire or smoke [smoke alarm]</p><p><b>(Stari zavjet) Božji način uništavanja grešnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Old Testament) God's means of destroying sinners</p><p><b>svejedni mrav iz tropske i subtropske Amerike koji može naneti bolno ubod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> omnivorous ant of tropical and subtropical America that can inflict a painful sting</p><p><b>tropski američki klik bube s svijetlim svjetlosnim mrljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American click beetle having bright luminous spots [Pyrophorus noctiluca, firefly]</p><p><b>zvono zvono da se daje požarni alarm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bell rung to give a fire alarm</p><p><b>bakterijska palež</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease blackening the leaves of pear and apple trees [pear blight]</p><p><b>požarna brigada, vatrogasna brigada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a private or temporary organization of individuals equipped to fight fires [fire company]</p><p><i>n.</i> British name for a fire department</p><p><b>zelena južnoamerička grmlja koja ima sjajne trubljevito narandžaste cvijeće, guste grane evroazijske biljke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen South American shrub having showy trumpet-shaped orange flowers [Streptosolen jamesonii, fire-bush, marmalade bush]</p><p><i>n.</i> densely branched Eurasian plant [Bassia scoparia, Kochia scoparia, belvedere, burning bush, fire-bush, summer cypress]</p><p><b>šef vatrogasnog odjela. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the head of a fire department [fire marshal]</p><p><b>skup standarda koje je vlada uspostavila i provela za sprječavanje požara i sigurnost u slučaju požara kao što su požarni izlazi itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> set of standards established and enforced by government for fire prevention and safety in case of fire as in fire escapes etc</p><p><b>privatna ili privremena organizacija pojedinaca opremljena za gašenje požara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a private or temporary organization of individuals equipped to fight fires [fire brigade]</p><p><b>Priprema za ispaljivanje granata na metu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> preparation for the delivery of shellfire on a target</p><p><b>ratni radar koji kontrolira isporuku vatre na vojnu metu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> naval radar that controls the delivery of fire on a military target</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to samo jedan od glavnih elemenata u ovom poglavlju, to znači da se ne primjenjuje niti jedan od sljedećih elemenata: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> naval weaponry consisting of a system for controlling the delivery of fire on a military target</p><p><b>vatrogasci, vatrogasna služba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the department of local government responsible for preventing and extinguishing fires</p><p><b>Vrata otporna na vatru koja se mogu zatvoriti kako bi se spriječilo širenje požara. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fire-resistant door that can be closed to stop the spread of a fire</p><p><b>vježba namijenjena obuci ljudi u dužnostima i postupcima za bijeg koji se trebaju slijediti u slučaju požara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an exercise intended to train people in duties and escape procedures to be followed in case of fire</p><p><b>vatrogasna kola, vatrogasna štrcaljka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various large trucks that carry firemen and equipment to the site of a fire [fire truck]</p><p><b>stubište (često na vanjskoj strani zgrade) koje omogućuje izlazak u slučaju požara ili druge hitne situacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stairway (often on the outside of a building) that permits exit in the case of fire or other emergency [emergency exit]</p><p><b>aparat za gašenje požara, protupožarni aparat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a manually operated device for extinguishing small fires [asphyxiator, extinguisher]</p><p><b>vatrogasac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a fire department who tries to extinguish fires [fire-eater, firefighter, fireman]</p><p><b>od željeza ili čelika, s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 85%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fire iron consisting of a metal rod with a handle [poker, salamander, stove poker]</p><p><b>protupožarno crijevo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large hose that carries water from a fire hydrant to the site of the fire</p><p><b>vodovod za uzimanje vode za gašenje požara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an upright hydrant for drawing water to use in fighting a fire [fireplug, plug]</p><p><b>osiguranje od gubitka zbog požara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> insurance against loss due to fire</p><p><b>Metalni alat za peć (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> metal fireside implements</p><p><b>vatrogasac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the head of a fire department [fire chief]</p><p><b>službenik koji je odgovoran za sprječavanje i istragu požara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an official who is responsible for the prevention and investigation of fires</p><p><b>vatreni opal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an opal with flaming orange and yellow and red colors [girasol]</p><p><b>višegodišnje biljke iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike, s crvenim cvijećem s uskim nečenim laticama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial herb of eastern North America, having red flowers with narrow notched petals [Silene virginica]</p><p><b>jama čiji pod je sijajuća lava. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pit whose floor is incandescent lava</p><p><b>Europski salamander tamne kože s obično žutim mrljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European salamander having dark skin with usually yellow spots [Salamandra maculosa, spotted salamander]</p><p><b>Prodaja imovine po vrlo niskim cijenama obično kada se prodavatelj suočava s stečajem, prodaja robe koja je navodno oštećena požarom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sale of assets at very low prices typically when the seller faces bankruptcy</p><p><i>n.</i> a sale of merchandise supposedly damaged by fire</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju električnih vozila od električne energije od više od 50 kW (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a metal screen before an open fire for protection (especially against flying sparks) [fireguard]</p><p><b>oružje koje se sastoji od broda koji nosi eksploziv koji je postavljen na odlazak kako bi uništio neprijateljske brodove. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a weapon consisting of a ship carrying explosives that is set adrift to destroy enemy ships</p><p><b>požarna stanica, vatrogasna stanica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a station housing fire apparatus and firemen [firehouse]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih trnastih grmova roda Pyracantha s malim bijelim cvijećem s tvrdo crvenim ili narandžastom bojom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various thorny shrubs of the genus Pyracantha bearing small white flowers followed by hard red or orange-red berries [Pyracantha, firethorn, pyracanth]</p><p><b>za proizvodnju električnih vozila od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tongs for taking hold of burning coals [coal tongs]</p><p><b>stražarski toranj gdje je postavljen stražar da gleda na vatru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a watchtower where a lookout is posted to watch for fires</p><p><b>Zemaljski zimzeleni grm ili malo stablo iz zapadne Australije s sjajnim žuto-narandžastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a terrestrial evergreen shrub or small tree of western Australia having brilliant yellow-orange flowers [Christmas tree, Nuytsia floribunda, flame tree]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju električnih goriva za motorne motore, neovisno o tome jesu li to motori ili motori koji se koriste za proizvodnju električnih goriva za motorne motore. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trench especially constructed for the delivery of small-arms fire</p><p><b>Svaka od različitih velikih kamiona koji prevoze vatrogasce i opremu na mjesto požara. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various large trucks that carry firemen and equipment to the site of a fire [fire engine]</p><p><b>rasplamsati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> arouse or excite feelings and passions [heat, ignite, inflame, stir up, wake]</p><p><i>v.</i> begin to smoke [light, light up]</p><p><b>netko tko hoda bos na gorljivim ugljenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who walks barefoot on burning coals</p><p><b>ceremonija hoda bosonog preko vrućih kamenja ili postelje od ugljena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ceremony of walking barefoot over hot stones or a bed of embers</p><p><b>službenik koji je odgovoran za upravljanje i zaštitu šumske površine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an official who is responsible for managing and protecting an area of forest [forest fire fighter, ranger]</p><p><b>(tokom Drugog svjetskog rata u Britaniji) netko čija je dužnost bila da gleda na požare uzrokovane bombama bačenim iz zraka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (during World War II in Britain) someone whose duty was to watch for fires caused by bombs dropped from the air</p><p><b>(tokom Drugog svjetskog rata u Britaniji) gledajući za požare započete bombama koje su pale s neba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (during World War II in Britain) watching for fires started by bombs that dropped from the sky</p><p><b>Gaillardia pulchella, gailardija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual of central United States having showy long-stalked yellow flower heads marked with scarlet or purple in the center [Gaillardia pulchella, Indian blanket, blanket flower, fire-wheel]</p><p><b>žaba iz srednje i istočne Europe s crvenim ili narandžastim mrljama pomiješanim sa crnom na donjoj strani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> toad of central and eastern Europe having red or orange patches mixed with black on its underside [Bombina bombina]</p><p><b>zelena južnoamerička grmlja koja ima sjajne trubljevito narandžaste cvijeće, guste grane evroazijske biljke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen South American shrub having showy trumpet-shaped orange flowers [Streptosolen jamesonii, fire bush, marmalade bush]</p><p><i>n.</i> densely branched Eurasian plant [Bassia scoparia, Kochia scoparia, belvedere, burning bush, fire bush, summer cypress]</p><p><b>vatrogasac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a fire department who tries to extinguish fires [fire fighter, firefighter, fireman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a belligerent grouch [hothead]</p><p><i>n.</i> a performer who pretends to swallow fire [fire-swallower]</p><p><b>Poinsettia iz Sjedinjenih Država i istočnog Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> poinsettia of United States and eastern Mexico [Euphorbia cyathophora, Mexican fire plant, painted leaf]</p><p><b>palež</b></p><p><i>n.</i> malicious burning to destroy property [arson, incendiarism]</p><p><b>protupožarni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> difficult to burn [fire-resisting, fire-resistive, fire-retardant]</p><p><b>teško se spali (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> difficult to burn [fire-resistant, fire-resistive, fire-retardant]</p><p><b>teško se spali (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> difficult to burn [fire-resistant, fire-resisting, fire-retardant]</p><p><b>teško se spali (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> difficult to burn [fire-resistant, fire-resisting, fire-resistive]</p><p><b>izvođač koji se pretvara da proguta vatru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a performer who pretends to swallow fire [fire-eater]</p><p><b>Gaillardia pulchella, gailardija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual of central United States having showy long-stalked yellow flower heads marked with scarlet or purple in the center [Gaillardia pulchella, Indian blanket, blanket flower, fire wheel]</p><p><b>obožavanje vatre. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the worship of fire [pyrolatry]</p><p><b>vatreno oružje, kratko vatreno oružje, pištolj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a portable gun [piece, small-arm]</p><p><b>vatrena kugla, vatrena lopta, vatrenu loptu, bolid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an especially luminous meteor (sometimes exploding) [bolide]</p><p><i>n.</i> a highly energetic and indefatigable person [ball of fire, human dynamo, powerhouse]</p><p><i>n.</i> a ball of fire (such as the sun or a ball-shaped discharge of lightning)</p><p><i>n.</i> the luminous center of a nuclear explosion</p><p><b>topničku bazu za podršku naprednim vojnicima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artillery base to support advancing troops</p><p><b>Muškarac je svijetlo crven s crnim krilima i repom., Istočna podvrsta sjevernog oriela, tropski američki muhač koji se nalazi na sjeveru do južnog Teksasa i Arizone (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the male is bright red with black wings and tail [Piranga olivacea, redbird, scarlet tanager]</p><p><i>n.</i> eastern subspecies of northern oriole [Baltimore bird, Baltimore oriole, Icterus galbula galbula, hangbird]</p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American flycatcher found as far north as southern Texas and Arizona [Pyrocephalus rubinus mexicanus, vermillion flycatcher]</p><p><b>brod opremljen za gašenje požara na brodovima ili duž obale (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a boat equipped to fight fires on ships or along a waterfront</p><p><b>bomba koja je dizajnirana da pokrene požare, Napad zapaljivim bombama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb that is designed to start fires [incendiary, incendiary bomb]</p><p><i>v.</i> attack with incendiary bombs</p><p><b>peć (kao na parnoj lokomotivi) u kojoj se gorivo sagorijeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a furnace (as on a steam locomotive) in which fuel is burned</p><p><b>komad drveta koji je spaljen ili gori, netko tko namjerno podstiče nevolje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of wood that has been burned or is burning [brand]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who deliberately foments trouble [inciter, instigant, instigator, provoker]</p><p><b>Živi u toplim vlažnim područjima, npr. oko peći. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lives in warm moist areas e.g. around furnaces [Thermobia domestica]</p><p><b>Uzak polje koje je očistiti za kontrolu širenja prerijske požara ili šumski požar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a narrow field that has been cleared to check the spread of a prairie fire or forest fire [fireguard]</p><p><b>vatrostalna cigla</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brick made of fire clay</p><p><b>potpaljivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a criminal who illegally sets fire to property [arsonist, incendiary]</p><p><i>n.</i> a true bug: brightly colored bug that can exude a stain</p><p><b>od čvrste gline (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heat-resistant clay</p><p><b>praskalica, petarda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> firework consisting of a small explosive charge and fuse in a heavy paper casing [banger, cracker]</p><p><b>otpušten, zapaljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having lost your job [discharged, dismissed, laid-off, pink-slipped]</p><p><b>Sastav plinova (uglavnom metana) koji se formira u rudnicima ugljena i postaje eksplozivan kada se pomiješa s zrakom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mixture of gases (mostly methane) that form in coal mines and become explosive when mixed with air</p><p><b>S druge konstrukcije od metala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> metal supports for logs in a fireplace [andiron, dog, dog-iron]</p><p><b>Stvorenje iz germanske mitologije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a creature of Teutonic mythology [dragon]</p><p><b>vatrogasac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a fire department who tries to extinguish fires [fire-eater, fire fighter, fireman]</p><p><b>krijesnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American click beetle having bright luminous spots [Pyrophorus noctiluca, fire beetle]</p><p><i>n.</i> nocturnal beetle common in warm regions having luminescent abdominal organs [lightning bug]</p><p><b>Uzak polje koje je očistiti za kontrolu širenja prerijske požara ili šumski požar, S druge strane, za proizvodnju električnih vozila od električne energije od više od 50 kW (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a narrow field that has been cleared to check the spread of a prairie fire or forest fire [firebreak]</p><p><i>n.</i> a metal screen before an open fire for protection (especially against flying sparks) [fire screen]</p><p><b>stanica s vatrogasnim aparatima i vatrogascima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a station housing fire apparatus and firemen [fire station]</p><p><b>svjetlo vatre (posebno u kaminu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the light of a fire (especially in a fireplace)</p><p><b>(dijel) tvari koja se lako gori i može se koristiti za pokretanje vatre uglja ili koksa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (a piece of) a substance that burns easily and can be used to start a coal or coke fire</p><p><b>Uređaj za punjenje dušama koji je imao tip pištolja s kamenom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a muzzle loader that had a flintlock type of gunlock [flintlock]</p><p><b>vatrogasac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> play in which children pretend to put out a fire</p><p><i>n.</i> a laborer who tends fires (as on a coal-fired train or steamship) [stoker]</p><p><i>n.</i> a pitcher who does not start the game [relief pitcher, reliever]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a fire department who tries to extinguish fires [fire-eater, fire fighter, firefighter]</p><p><b>sjekira koja ima dug ručnik i glavu s jednom oštricom i vrh na drugoj strani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ax that has a long handle and a head with one cutting edge and a point on the other side [fireman's axe]</p><p><b>sjekira koja ima dug ručnik i glavu s jednom oštricom i vrh na drugoj strani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ax that has a long handle and a head with one cutting edge and a point on the other side [fireman's ax]</p><p><b>čin nošenja osobe preko ramena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of carrying a person over your shoulder</p><p><b>Firenca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in central Italy on the Arno [Florence]</p><p><b>kamin, ognjišće, ognjište, peć na drva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an open recess in a wall at the base of a chimney where a fire can be built [hearth, open fireplace]</p><p><b>vodovod za uzimanje vode za gašenje požara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an upright hydrant for drawing water to use in fighting a fire [fire hydrant, plug]</p><p><b>(vojni) relativni kapacitet za pucanje na metu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (military) the relative capacity for delivering fire on a target</p><p><b>nesagoriv, nezapaljiv, vatrostalan</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make resistant to fire</p><p><i>adj.</i> impervious to damage by fire</p><p><b>(nautički) komora ili odjeljak u kojem se peći broda goriju ili peče (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (nautical) chamber or compartment in which the furnaces of a ship are stoked or fired [stokehold, stokehole]</p><p><b>područje u blizini kamina (obično asfaltirano i prošireno u prostoriju), Dom simboliziran kao dio kamina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an area near a fireplace (usually paved and extending out into a room) [hearth]</p><p><i>n.</i> home symbolized as a part of the fireplace [hearth]</p><p><b>komad kremen koji je udaren da se zapali vatru, peščani kamen koji izdržava veliku vrućinu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of flint that is struck to light a fire</p><p><i>n.</i> a sandstone that withstands intense heat</p><p><b>oluja u kojoj se jak vjetar uvuče u stup vrućeg zraka koji se diže iznad teško bombardiranog područja, Izbijanje kontroverze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a storm in which violent winds are drawn into the column of hot air rising over a severely bombed area</p><p><i>n.</i> an outburst of controversy</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih trnastih grmova roda Pyracantha s malim bijelim cvijećem s tvrdo crvenim ili narandžastom bojom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various thorny shrubs of the genus Pyracantha bearing small white flowers followed by hard red or orange-red berries [Pyracantha, fire thorn, pyracanth]</p><p><b>zgrada iz koje bi bilo teško pobjeći ako bi zapalila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a building that would be hard to escape from if it were to catch fire</p><p><b>firewall, vatrozid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (colloquial) the application of maximum thrust</p><p><i>n.</i> (computing) a security system consisting of a combination of hardware and software that limits the exposure of a computer or computer network to attack from crackers</p><p><i>n.</i> a fireproof (or fire-resistant) wall designed to prevent the spread of fire through a building or a vehicle</p><p><b>Svaka snažna alkoholna pića (kao što su snažni viski ili rum) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any strong spirits (such as strong whisky or rum)</p><p><b>Visoka sjevernoamerička višegodišnja biljka s puzećim korijenima i uskim listovima i šiljakama ružičastavičasta ljubičasta cvjetova koja se u velikoj količini nalazi u spaljenim područjima ili nedavnim čistinama, američka korovnica s malim bijelim ili zelenkastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall North American perennial with creeping rootstocks and narrow leaves and spikes of pinkish-purple flowers occurring in great abundance in burned-over areas or recent clearings [Epilobium angustifolium, giant willowherb, rosebay willowherb, wickup]</p><p><i>n.</i> an American weedy plant with small white or greenish flowers [Erechtites hieracifolia]</p><p><b>Istočnoaustralijsko stablo koje se široko uzgaja kao stablo za sjenu i zbog svojih sjajnih lišća i kružnih grama najozbiljnije crvene do narandžaste crvene boje cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> eastern Australian tree widely cultivated as a shade tree and for its glossy leaves and circular clusters of showy red to orange-scarlet flowers [Stenocarpus sinuatus, wheel tree]</p><p><b>drvo za ogrjev, cjepanica, drvo za potpalu, glavnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wood used for fuel</p><p><b>duhovitost, oštroumlje, vatromet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) a device with an explosive that burns at a low rate and with colored flames [pyrotechnic]</p><p><b>gađanje, paljba, paljenje, žarenja, žarenje, pucnjava, vatra, loženje, potpala, potpaljivanje, otkaz, otpuštanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of firing weapons or artillery at an enemy [fire]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of discharging a gun [discharge, firing off]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of setting something on fire [ignition, inflammation, kindling, lighting]</p><p><i>n.</i> the termination of someone's employment (leaving them free to depart) [discharge, dismissal, dismission, liberation, release, sack, sacking]</p><p><b>Komora koja je dio pištolja koji prima naboj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chamber that is the part of a gun that receives the charge [gun chamber]</p><p><b>linija iz koje vojnici isporučuju vatru, Najnaprednija i odgovornija grupa u aktivnostima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the line from which soldiers deliver fire</p><p><i>n.</i> the most advanced and responsible group in an activity</p><p><b>akcija koja pali naboj u vatrenom oružju (MT)</