uštva (1859-1947) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English sociologist and economist and a central member of the Fabian Society (1859-1947) [Sidney James Webb, Sidney Webb, Webb]</p><p><b>Britanski fizičar (rođen na Novom Zelandu) koji je otkrio atomsko jezgro i predložio nuklearni model atoma (1871-1937) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British physicist (born in New Zealand) who discovered the atomic nucleus and proposed a nuclear model of the atom (1871-1937) [Ernest Rutherford, First Baron Rutherford of Nelson, Rutherford]</p><p><b>Britanski fizičar (rođen na Novom Zelandu) koji je otkrio atomsko jezgro i predložio nuklearni model atoma (1871-1937) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British physicist (born in New Zealand) who discovered the atomic nucleus and proposed a nuclear model of the atom (1871-1937) [Ernest Rutherford, First Baron Rutherford, Rutherford]</p><p><b>Engleski pjesnik i viktorijanski pjesnik (1809-1892) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Englishman and Victorian poet (1809-1892) [Alfred Lord Tennyson, Alfred Tennyson, Tennyson]</p><p><b>Baza koju mora prvi dodirnuti igrač u bejzbolu., položaj igrača u bejzbol timu koji je stacioniran na prvom mjestu baza na infield (brojajući u suprotnom smjeru kazaljke na kući), početni stadij u postizanju nečega. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the base that must be touched first by a base runner in baseball</p><p><i>n.</i> the fielding position of the player on a baseball team who is stationed at first of the bases in the infield (counting counterclockwise from home plate) [first]</p><p><i>n.</i> the initial stage in accomplishing something</p><p><b>(baseball) osoba koja igra prvu bazu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (baseball) the person who plays first base [first sacker]</p><p><b>bitka u Prvom svjetskom ratu (1914) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> battle in World War I (1914) [Ypres, battle of Ypres]</p><p><b>Na prvi pogled ili dojam. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> at the first glimpse or impression</p><p><b>Agent koji je uzrok svih stvari ali nema uzrok. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agent that is the cause of all things but does not itself have a cause [prime mover, primum mobile]</p><p><b>najviši čin u klasifikaciji, Pošta koja uključuje pisma i razglednice te pakete zapečaćene protiv inspekcije, najdraže smještaj na brodu, vlaku ili zrakoplovu, Pritom se ne može koristiti za prijevoz. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the highest rank in a classification</p><p><i>n.</i> mail that includes letters and postcards and packages sealed against inspection [1st-class mail, 1st class, first-class mail]</p><p><i>n.</i> the most expensive accommodations on a ship or train or plane</p><p><i>adv.</i> by first class conveyance</p><p><b>Drugi sveopšti koncil iz 381. godine koji je dodao riječi o Svetom Duhu u Nicejanski vjerovjesni znak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the second ecumenical council in 381 which added wording about the Holy Spirit to the Nicene Creed [Constantinople]</p><p><b>Savjet Zapadne Crkve 1245. godine koji je ekskomunicirao car Svetoga Rimskog Carstva Frederika II i planirao novi križarski rat protiv Svete Zemlje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the council of the Western Church in 1245 that excommunicated Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II and planned a new crusade against the Holy Land [Lyons]</p><p><b>Prvi sveopšti koncil 325. godine koji je sastavio Nicejanski vjerovjesni zakon i osudio jeresiju arijanstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first ecumenical council in 325 which produced the wording of the Nicene Creed and condemned the heresy of Arianism [Nicaea]</p><p><b>bratić, rođak, sestrična</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the child of your aunt or uncle [cousin, cousin-german, full cousin]</p><p><b>kolektivni naziv za brojne mirisne vlakne u nosnoj sluznici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collective term for numerous olfactory filaments in the nasal mucosa [nervii olfactorii, olfactory nerve]</p><p><b>Krstaški rat od 1096. do 1099. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Crusade from 1096 to 1099</p><p><b>stepen od jednog. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a degree of one</p><p><b>rezultat matematičke diferencijacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the result of mathematical differentiation [derivative, derived function, differential, differential coefficient]</p><p><b>Engleski general koji se smatra jednim od najvećih generala u povijesti (1650-1722) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English general considered one of the greatest generals in history (1650-1722) [Churchill, Duke of Marlborough, John Churchill]</p><p><b>Britanski general i državnik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British general and statesman [Arthur Wellesley, Duke of Wellington, Iron Duke, Wellington]</p><p><b>Britanski feldmaršal (1850-1916) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British field marshal (1850-1916) [Herbert Kitchener, Horatio Herbert Kitchener, Kitchener]</p><p><b>Britanski državnik koji je kao premijer kupio većinski udio u Suezskom kanalu i učinio kraljicu Viktoriju caricom Indije (1804-1881) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British statesman who as Prime Minister bought controlling interest in the Suez Canal and made Queen Victoria the empress of India (1804-1881) [Benjamin Disraeli, Disraeli]</p><p><b>Engleski državnik koji je okončao Sedmogodišnji rat (1708. - 1778.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English statesman who brought the Seven Years' War to an end (1708-1778) [Pitt, Pitt the Elder, William Pitt]</p><p><b>Englez i whigovski državnik koji je (pod Georgeom I.) bio prvi britanski premijer (1676.-1745.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Englishman and Whig statesman who (under George I) was effectively the first British prime minister (1676-1745) [Robert Walpole, Sir Robert Walpole, Walpole]</p><p><b>Britanski feldmaršal u Sjevernoj Africi u Drugom svjetskom ratu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British field marshal in North Africa in World War II [Archibald Percival Wavell, Wavell]</p><p><b>Prvo Novozavjetno pismo koje se tradicionalno pripisuje Svetom Ivanu Apostolu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first New Testament epistle traditionally attributed to Saint John the Apostle [I John]</p><p><b>knjiga Novog zavjeta koja sadrži prvo pismo svetog Pavla crkvi u Korintu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book containing the first epistle from Saint Paul to the church at Corinth [First Epistle to the Corinthians, I Corinthians]</p><p><b>Novozavjetna knjiga koja sadrži prvo pismo Svetog Pavla Solunjanima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book containing Saint Paul's first epistle to the Thessalonians [First Epistle to the Thessalonians, I Thessalonians]</p><p><b>knjiga Novog zavjeta koja sadrži prvo pismo Svetog Pavla Timoteju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book containing Saint Paul's first epistle to Timothy [First Epistle to Timothy, I Timothy]</p><p><b>prva knjiga Novog zavjeta koja se tradicionalno pripisuje Svetom Petru Apostolu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first New Testament book traditionally attributed to Saint Peter the Apostle [I Peter]</p><p><b>knjiga Novog zavjeta koja sadrži prvo pismo svetog Pavla crkvi u Korintu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book containing the first epistle from Saint Paul to the church at Corinth [First Epistle of Paul the Apostle to the Corinthians, I Corinthians]</p><p><b>Novozavjetna knjiga koja sadrži prvo pismo Svetog Pavla Solunjanima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book containing Saint Paul's first epistle to the Thessalonians [First Epistle of Paul the Apostle to the Thessalonians, I Thessalonians]</p><p><b>knjiga Novog zavjeta koja sadrži prvo pismo Svetog Pavla Timoteju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book containing Saint Paul's first epistle to Timothy [First Epistle of Paul the Apostle to Timothy, I Timothy]</p><p><b>svećenstvo u Francuskoj i vođe crkve u Britaniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the clergy in France and the heads of the church in Britain [Lords Spiritual]</p><p><b>prizemlje, razizemlje, suteren</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the floor of a building that is at or nearest to the level of the ground around the building [ground floor, ground level]</p><p><b>Najniži omjer prijenosa u prijenosnom sandučiću motornog vozila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lowest forward gear ratio in the gear box of a motor vehicle [first, low, low gear]</p><p><b>prvo poluvrijeme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first of two halves of play</p><p><b>najniži ton u harmonijskom nizu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lowest tone of a harmonic series [fundamental, fundamental frequency]</p><p><b>prvi uđe- prvi van</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inventory accounting in which the oldest items (those first acquired) are assumed to be the first sold [FIFO]</p><p><b>vodeća žena u umjetnosti ili poslu, supruga izvršnog direktora. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the leading woman in an art or profession</p><p><i>n.</i> the wife of a chief executive</p><p><b>maternji jezik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one's native language [maternal language, mother tongue]</p><p><b>Prvi savet Zapadne crkve održan u Lateranskom dvoru 1123. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first council of the Western Church held in the Lateran Palace in 1123</p><p><b>tijelo ostaje u mirovanju ili u pokretu sa stalnom brzinom osim ako na njega ne djeluje vanjska sila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a body remains at rest or in motion with a constant velocity unless acted upon by an external force [Newton's first law, Newton's first law of motion]</p><p><b>Osnovni princip fizike da je ukupna energija izolovanog sustava nepromenljiva unatoč unutarnjim promjenama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fundamental principle of physics that the total energy of an isolated system is constant despite internal changes [conservation of energy, law of conservation of energy]</p><p><b>časnik u vojsci ili zrakoplovstvu ili u mornarici koji je iznad 2. poručnika i ispod kapetana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a commissioned officer in the Army or Air Force or Marines ranking above a 2nd lieutenant and below a captain [1st lieutenant]</p><p><b>zora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first light of day [aurora, break of day, break of the day, cockcrow, dawn, dawning, daybreak, dayspring, morning, sunrise, sunup]</p><p><b>Britanski ministar za ekonomsku strategiju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the British cabinet minister responsible for economic strategy [Treasury]</p><p><b>Zapovjednik britanskih snaga u Američkom ratu za neovisnost. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commander of the British forces in the American War of Independence [Charles Cornwallis, Cornwallis]</p><p><b>časnik ispod kapetana na komercijalnom brodu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the officer below the master on a commercial ship [mate]</p><p><b>aritmetička sredina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sum of the values of a random variable divided by the number of values [arithmetic mean, expectation, expected value]</p><p><b>U slučaju hipoteke koja ima prednost nad svim hipotekama i zastavnim obvezama osim onih koje su propisane zakonom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mortgage that has priority over all mortgages and liens except those imposed by law</p><p><b>ime</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the name that precedes the surname [forename, given name]</p><p><b>najprije, prije svega, prvo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> before anything else [first, first off, firstly, foremost]</p><p><b>proslavlja se u mnogim zemljama kako bi se proslavio dolazak proljeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> observed in many countries to celebrate the coming of spring [May 1, May Day]</p><p><b>naoružano krilo (ilegalne) Komunističke stranke Španjolske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an armed wing of the (illegal) Communist Party of Spain [GRAPO]</p><p><b>prvo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> before anything else [first, first of all, firstly, foremost]</p><p><b>netko osuđen po prvi put (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone convicted for the first time</p><p><b>prva divizija u koju je igra igre podijeljena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first division into which the play of a game is divided</p><p><b>zamjene i glagola koja se koriste za govornika ili pisca jezika u kojem se pojavljuju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pronouns and verbs used to refer to the speaker or writer of the language in which they