ine kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> burn causing redness of the skin surface</p><p><b>Netko koji je obicno gledao na otvaranju pozorišnih predstava. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone habitually a spectator at the openings of theatrical productions</p><p><b>(u slučaju da je to primjenjivo na određenu vrstu proizvoda) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a partial correlation in which the effects of only one variable are removed (held constant)</p><p><b>završetak na prvom mjestu (kao u utrci) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a finish in first place (as in a race)</p><p><b>prvorazredan, prvorazredno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of the highest quality [A-one, ace, crack, super, tiptop, top-notch, topnotch, tops]</p><p><i>adv.</i> quite well [very well]</p><p><b>Onaj koji je prvoklasni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who is first-rate</p><p><b>članova tima, biti redoviti član tima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of members of a team</p><p><i>adj.</i> being a regular member of a team</p><p><b>U slučaju da je osoba u prvom godini iskustva (posebno u srednjoj školi ili koledžu u Sjedinjenim Državama) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> used of a person in the first year of an experience (especially in United States high school or college) [freshman]</p><p><b>potomstvo koje je prvo u redu rođenja., Prvo po redu rođenja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the offspring who came first in the order of birth [eldest]</p><p><i>adj.</i> first in order of birth [eldest]</p><p><b>iz prve ruke</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> received directly from a source</p><p><i>adv.</i> from the original source [at first hand]</p><p><b>najprije, prvo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> before anything else [first, first of all, first off, foremost]</p><p><b>morski zaljev, uski zaljev, ušće rijeke, zaton</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English linguist who contributed to linguistic semantics and to prosodic phonology and who was noted for his insistence on studying both sound and meaning in context (1890-1960) [J. R. Firth, John Rupert Firth]</p><p><i>n.</i> a long narrow estuary (especially in Scotland)</p><p><b>Prirod na jugozapadnoj obali Škotske koji se uliva u Sjeverni kanal (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a firth on the southwestern coast of Scotland emptying into the North Channel</p><p><b>veliki proljak na istočnoj obali Škotske i ušću rijeke Forth (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large firth on the east coast of Scotland and the estuary of the Forth River</p><p><b>Zakon usvojen od strane Kongresa 1978. godine kojim se uspostavljaju postupci za traženje sudskog odobrenja za nadzor inostrane obavještajne službe i stvaranje Suda za nadzor inostrane obavještajne službe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an act passed by Congress in 1978 to establish procedures for requesting judicial authorization for foreign intelligence surveillance and to create the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court [Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act]</p><p><b>državna blagajna ili kraljevska blagajna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state treasury or exchequer or a royal treasury</p><p><b>financijski, fiskalni, poslovan, poslovnoj</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving financial matters [financial]</p><p><b>fiskalna politika, porezna politika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government policy for dealing with the budget (especially with taxation and borrowing)</p><p><b>fiskalna godina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any accounting period of 12 months [financial year]</p><p><b>financijski, fiskalni, poslovan, poslovnoj (od &quot;fiscal&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in financial matters [in fiscal matters]</p><p><b>Njemački kemičar poznat po sintezi hemina (1881-1945), Njemački kemičar poznat po radu na sintetičkim šećerima i purinama (1852-1919), Šahovski majstor Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German chemist noted for his synthesis of hemin (1881-1945) [Hans Fischer]</p><p><i>n.</i> German chemist noted for work on synthetic sugars and the purines (1852-1919) [Emil Hermann Fischer]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States chess master [Bobby Fischer, Robert James Fischer]</p><p><b>vrsta sluzne gljive (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.