iko malih grmova ili vinove loze s čistim ili lobnim lišćama i žutim do narandžasto-crvenim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several small shrubs or twining vines having entire or lobed leaves and racemes of yellow to orange-red flowers</p><p><b>šavovi od igle koji stvaraju zigzag linije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> needlepoint embroidery stitch that produces zigzag lines [bargello]</p><p><b>Crveno-fioleta stolno grožđe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> purplish-red table grape</p><p><b>Zemaljski zimzeleni grm ili malo stablo iz zapadne Australije s sjajnim žuto-narandžastim cvijećem, izvod: od:, Sjevernoaustralijsko stablo s bijelim cvijećem i širokim lišćama, Južnoaustralijsko drvo koje ima panike sjajne crvene boje cvijeća, tropski američki trnasti grm ili drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a terrestrial evergreen shrub or small tree of western Australia having brilliant yellow-orange flowers [Christmas tree, Nuytsia floribunda, fire tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> showy tropical tree or shrub native to Madagascar [Delonix regia, Poinciana regia, flamboyant, peacock flower, royal poinciana]</p><p><i>n.</i> north Australian tree having white flowers and broad leaves [Brachychiton australis, broad-leaved bottletree]</p><p><i>n.</i> south Australian tree having panicles of brilliant scarlet flowers [Brachychiton acerifolius, Sterculia acerifolia, flame durrajong]</p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American thorny shrub or small tree [Acacia farnesiana, cassie, huisache, mimosa bush, scented wattle, sweet acacia, sweet wattle]</p><p><b>gori svijetlo., zapaliti se (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> burn brightly [blaze up, burn up, flare]</p><p><i>v.</i> become ignited [fire]</p><p><b>s blistavom narandžastom crvenom bojom plamena (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the brilliant orange-red color of flames [flame-coloured]</p><p><b>s blistavom narandžastom crvenom bojom plamena (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the brilliant orange-red color of flames [flame-colored]</p><p><b>biljka iz roda Kniphofia s dugi