skih regija čija se sjemena otkucaju i postaju želatinska kada su vlažna i koriste se kao blagi laksativ (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plantain of Mediterranean regions whose seeds swell and become gelatinous when moist and are used as a mild laxative [Plantago psyllium, Spanish psyllium, psyllium]</p><p><b>oralni antiaritmički lijek (trgovinski naziv Tambocor) koji se koristi kao posljednje sredstvo za liječenje aritmija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> oral antiarrhythmic medication (trade name Tambocor) used as a last resort in treating arrhythmias [Tambocor]</p><p><b>mala mrlja, mrlja, pjega, točkica, krhotina, mrljica, pruga, točka, šara, zabrljati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small fragment of something broken off from the whole [bit, chip, flake, scrap]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small contrasting part of something [dapple, maculation, patch, speckle, spot]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a spot or mark onto [blob, blot, spot]</p><p><b>mala mrlja, mrlja, pjega, točkica (od &quot;fleck&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a pattern of dots [dotted, specked, speckled, stippled]</p><p><b>fleksija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being flexed (as of a joint) [flexion, flexure]</p><p><i>n.</i> deviation from a straight or normal course [flexion, inflection]</p><p><b>opernatiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> feed, care for, and rear young birds for flight</p><p><i>v.</i> decorate with feathers [flight]</p><p><i>v.</i> grow feathers [feather]</p><p><b>(ptica) s razvijenim perjem ili perjem, koje su s perjem, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of birds) having developed feathers or plumage [mature]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of an arrow) equipped with feathers [vaned]</p><p><b>bez krila</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of an arrow) not equipped with feathers [unfledged, unvaned]</p><p><b>goluždravac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any new participant in some activity [entrant, fledgling, freshman, neophyte, newbie, newcomer, starter]</p><p><i>n.</i> young bird that has just fledged or become capable of flying [fledgling]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a young bir