fer the least resistant to fluid flow [aerodynamic, sleek, streamlined]</p><p><b>lijek protiv tumora koji se koristi za liječenje nekih vrsta raka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antineoplastic drug used to treat some cancers</p><p><b>Američki avijator koji je (s Richardom E. Byrdom) pilotirao prvi let iznad Sjevernog pola (1890-1928) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States aviator who (with Richard E. Byrd) piloted the first flight over the North Pole (1890-1928) [Bennett]</p><p><b>gripa, gripe, influenca, prehlada, virusna prehlada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute febrile highly contagious viral disease [grippe, influenza]</p><p><b>kiks, brljati, buniti se, fušati, griješiti, kiksati, kvariti, packati, petljati, pogriješiti, pokvariti, preturati, prtljati, prčkati, sfušati, spackati, spetljati, sprtljati, sprčkati, uništavati, uništiti, upropastiti, upropaštavati, uprskati, uprskavati, zabuniti se, zafrknuti, zbrljati, zbunjivati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an embarrassing mistake [bloomer, blooper, blunder, boner, boo-boo, botch, bungle, foul-up, fuckup, pratfall]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a mess of, destroy or ruin [ball up, blow, bobble, bodge, bollix, bollix up, bollocks, bollocks up, botch, botch up, bumble, bungle, fluff, foul up, fuck up, fumble, louse up, mess up, mishandle, muck up, muff, screw up, spoil]</p><p><b>fluktuirati, kolebati se, mijenjati se, njihati se, varirati, kolebati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to fluctuate or move in a wavelike pattern</p><p><i>v.</i> move or sway in a rising and falling or wavelike pattern [vacillate, waver]</p><p><i>v.</i> be unstable</p><p><b>fluktuirati, kolebati se, mijenjati se, njihati se, varirati (od &quot;fluctuate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having unpredictable ups and downs</p><p><b>fluktuacija, kolebanje, nestalnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wave motion</p><p><i>n.</i> an instance of change [variation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being unsteady and subject to changes [wavering]</p><p><b>dimnjak, gripa, malje, pahuljica, pahuljice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flat bladelike projection on the arm of an anchor [fluke]</p><p><i>n.</i> organ pipe whose tone is produced by air passing across the sharp edge of a fissure or lip [flue pipe, labial pipe]</p><p><i>n.</i> a conduit to carry off smoke</p><p><b>svirala, svirala orgulja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> organ pipe whose tone is produced by air passing across the sharp edge of a fissure or lip [flue, labial pipe]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organ stop with the tone of a flue pipe</p><p><b>za glazbu od metala ili čelika, s masenim udubljenjem od 300 mm ili većim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brass instrument resembling a cornet but with a wider bore [flugelhorn]</p><p><b>fluentnost, fluentnosti, glatkoća, lakoća, tečnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> powerful and effective language [eloquence, smoothness]</p><p><i>n.</i> skillfulness in speaking or writing</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being facile in speech and writing [articulateness, volubility]</p><p><b>bez poteškoća, gladak, okretan, tečan, tekući, živahan, elokventan, rječit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> smooth and unconstrained in movement [fluid, liquid, smooth]</p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing yourself readily, clearly, effectively [eloquent, facile, silver, silver-tongued, smooth-spoken]</p><p><b>Afazija karakterizirana tečnim, ali beznačajnim govorom i ozbiljnim oštećenjem sposobnosti razumijevanja govorenih ili pisanih riječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aphasia characterized by fluent but meaningless speech and severe impairment of the ability understand spoken or written words [Wernicke's aphasia, impressive aphasia, receptive aphasia, sensory aphasia]</p><p><b>bez poteškoća, bez zapinjanja, glatko, tekuće</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a fluent manner</p><p><b>dlačica, dlake, malje, pahulja, pahuljica, pahuljice, paperje, brljati, buniti se, fušati, griješiti, kiksati, kvariti, packati, petljati, pogriješiti, pokvariti, preturati, prtljati, prčkati, 