al small tropical Asian lizards capable of gliding by spreading winglike membranes on each side of the body [dragon, flying dragon]</p><p><b>borbeni manevar. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wrestling maneuver</p><p><b>Ptica u istočnoindijskom području (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian flying squirrel [Petaurista petaurista, flying cat, taguan]</p><p><b>mali leteći falanger (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tiny flying phalanger</p><p><b>Noćni falangeri koji se kreću skokovima koristeći sklopove kože poput padobrana duž strana tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nocturnal phalangers that move with gliding leaps using parachute-like folds of skin along the sides of the body [flying phalanger, flying squirrel]</p><p><b>Noćni falangeri koji se kreću skokovima koristeći sklopove kože poput padobrana duž strana tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nocturnal phalangers that move with gliding leaps using parachute-like folds of skin along the sides of the body [flying opossum, flying squirrel]</p><p><b>izumrli gmizavac iz Jure i Krede s ptičjim kljunom i membranskim krilima podržanim vrlo dugim četvrtim prstom svakog prednjeg udova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extinct reptile of the Jurassic and Cretaceous having a bird-like beak and membranous wings supported by the very long fourth digit of each forelimb [pterosaur]</p><p><b>tropske ribe s velikim prsnim perajima poput ventilatora za podmorsko klizanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical fish with huge fanlike pectoral fins for underwater gliding [butterflyfish, flying gurnard]</p><p><b>leteći tanjur</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an (apparently) flying object whose nature is unknown [UFO, unidentified flying object]</p><p><b>škola letenja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school for teaching students to fly airplanes</p><p><b>mobilna skupina obučenih osoba (policije ili rukovodstva ili službenika) sposobnih za brzo kretanje u slučaju vanrednih situacija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mobile group of trained people (police or executives or officials) able to move quickly