 into focus [focalize, focus]</p><p><i>v.</i> put (an image) into focus [focalize, focus, sharpen]</p><p><b>fokalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the confinement of an infection to a limited area [focalisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of bringing into focus [focalisation, focusing]</p><p><b>fokusirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> concentrate on a particular place or spot [focalise, localise, localize]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring into focus or alignment [concenter, concentre, focalise, focus]</p><p><i>v.</i> become focussed or come into focus [focalise, focus]</p><p><i>v.</i> put (an image) into focus [focalise, focus, sharpen]</p><p><b>fokusni, žarišni (od &quot;focal&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a focal manner</p><p><b>fokus, fokusirati, namjestiti, pažnja, pažnjom, upraviti, usredotočiti, usredotočiti se, žarište, žiža, fokusiranje, koncentriranje, usredeotočavanje, fokalna točka, žarišna točka, fokusirati se, koncentrirati se, usredotočivati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the concentration of attention or energy on something [centering, direction, focal point, focusing, focussing]</p><p><i>n.</i> maximum clarity or distinctness of an image rendered by an optical system</p><p><i>n.</i> maximum clarity or distinctness of an idea</p><p><i>n.</i> a central point or locus of an infection in an organism [focal point, nidus]</p><p><i>n.</i> special emphasis attached to something [stress]</p><p><i>n.</i> a point of convergence of light (or other radiation) or a point from which it diverges [focal point]</p><p><i>n.</i> a fixed reference point on the concave side of a conic section</p><p><i>v.</i> direct one's attention on something [center, centre, concentrate, pore, rivet]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to converge on or toward a central point</p><p><i>v.</i> bring into focus or alignment [concenter, concentre, focalise, focalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> become focussed or come into focus [focalise, focalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> put (an image) into focus [focalise, focalize, sharpen]</p><p><b>centrirati</b></p><p><