atic European herbs with pinnately compound leaves and yellow flowers [genus Foeniculum]</p><p><b>uzgajan posebno zbog svoje jestive aromatične bubulne baze stabljike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grown especially for its edible aromatic bulbous stem base [Florence fennel, Foeniculum vulgare dulce]</p><p><b>od kojih: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> strongly aromatic with a smell of aniseed [common fennel]</p><p><b>uzgajan posebno zbog svoje jestive aromatične bubulne baze stabljike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grown especially for its edible aromatic bulbous stem base [Florence fennel, Foeniculum dulce]</p><p><b>fetalni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a fetus [fetal]</p><p><b>sustav krvnih žila i struktura kroz koje se krv kreće u fetusu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of blood vessels and structures through which blood moves in a fetus [fetal circulation]</p><p><b>abnormalno stanje fetusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal condition of a fetus [fetal distress]</p><p><b>elektronički monitor koji prati otkucaje srca fetusa i kontrakcije maternice tijekom porođaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electronic monitor that monitors fetal heartbeat and the mother's uterine contractions during childbirth [electronic fetal monitor, electronic foetal monitor, fetal monitor]</p><p><b>kretanje fetusa unutar maternice (obično otkriveno do 16. tjedna trudnoće) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> motion of a fetus within the uterus (usually detected by the 16th week of pregnancy) [fetal movement]</p><p><b>Oponosno loše smrdljivo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> offensively malodorous [fetid, foul, foul-smelling, funky, ill-scented, noisome, smelly, stinking]</p><p><b>Blagane iz Sibira i istočne Azije s lošim mirisom zelenobjelog cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bugbane of Siberia and eastern Asia having ill-smelling green-white flowers [Cimicifuga foetida, fetid bugbane]</p><p><b>višegodišnja listovita nisko rastuća smrdljiva močvarna biljka iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s malenim cvijećem zatvorenim u mrljano zeleno ili ljubičasto spathe u obliku kapulja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous perennial low-growing fetid swamp plant of eastern North America having minute flowers enclosed in a mottled greenish or purple cowl-shaped spathe [Symplocarpus foetidus, polecat weed, skunk cabbage]</p><p><b>medicinska grana koja se bavi fetusom u maternici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of medicine concerned with the fetus in the uterus [fetology]</p><p><b>mjerenje fetusa (posebno prečnika glave) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> measurement of a fetus (especially the diameter of the head) [fetometry]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko antigena koji se prirodno pojavljuju u fetusu i ponekad u odraslih s rakom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several antigens that occur naturally in the fetus and sometimes in adults with cancer [fetoprotein]</p><p><b>vonj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a distinctive odor that is offensively unpleasant [fetor, malodor, malodour, mephitis, reek, stench, stink]</p><p><b>stetoskop postavljen na trbušnicu trudnice kako bi slušao otkucaje srca fetusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stethoscope placed on the pregnant woman's abdomen to listen for the fetal heartbeat [fetoscope]</p><p><b>dijagnoza prije porođaja koja omogućuje izravno promatranje fetusa u maternici i uzimanje fetalne krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prenatal diagnosis that allows direct observation of a fetus in the uterus and the withdrawal of fetal blood [fetoscopy]</p><p><b>fetus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unborn or unhatched vertebrate in the later stages of development showing the main recognizable features of the mature animal [fetus]</p><p><b>magla, zamagliti, zbuniti, maglovitost, nejasnost, neodređenost, zamagljenost, pomračiti, pomračivati, pomutiti, pomućivati, zamagljivati, zamračiti, zamračivati, zamutiti, zamućivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> droplets of water vapor suspended in the air near the ground</p><p><i>n.</i> an atmosphere in which visibility is reduced because of a cloud of some substance [fogginess, murk, murkiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> confusion characterized by lack of clarity [daze, haze]</p><p><i>v.</i> make less visible or unclear [becloud, befog, cloud, haze over, mist, obnubilate, obscure]</p><p><b>-Moglo je. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> get foggy</p><p><b>Velika masa magle na moru (kao što se vidi iz daljine) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large mass of fog on the sea (as seen from a distance)</p><p><b>zadržan maglom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> enveloped in fog</p><p><b>Nekoga čiji stil je van mode. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone whose style is out of fashion [dodo, fogy, fossil]</p><p><b>zaklonjena maglom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> obscured by fog [foggy]</p><p><b>izmaglica, maglovitost, magla</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an atmosphere in which visibility is reduced because of a cloud of some substance [fog, murk, murkiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being indistinct and without sharp outlines [blurriness, fuzziness, indistinctness, softness]</p><p><b>maglovit, maglovito</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> stunned or confused and slow to react (as from blows or drunkenness or exhaustion) [dazed, groggy, logy, stuporous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> indistinct or hazy in outline [bleary, blurred, blurry, fuzzy, hazy, muzzy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> filled or abounding with fog or mist [brumous, hazy, misty]</p><p><i>adj.</i> obscured by fog [fogged]</p><p><b>State Department Sjedinjenih Država, koji se nalazi u zgradi u niskozemnom području Washingtona u blizini rijeke Potomac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States Department of State, which is housed in a building in a low-lying area of Washington near the Potomac River</p><p><b>glasno nizak upozorenje koje mogu čuti brodovi na maglovini, S druge strane, za uređaje za proizvodnju električnih vozila: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loud low warning signal that can be heard by fogbound ships [fogsignal]</p><p><i>n.</i> a warning device consisting of a horn that generates a loud low tone</p><p><b>svjetiljke koje pružaju snažnu svjetlost za upotrebu u maglovitom 