r or back with foil</p><p><b>folija, staniol, trag životinje (od &quot;foil&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> disappointingly unsuccessful [defeated, disappointed, discomfited, frustrated, thwarted]</p><p><b>folija, staniol, trag životinje (od &quot;foil&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an act of hindering someone's plans or efforts [frustration, thwarting]</p><p><b>tovariti, utrapiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to force onto another</p><p><i>v.</i> insert surreptitiously or without warrant</p><p><b>Prodaju kao istinske, prodaju s namjerom zavaravanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> sell as genuine, sell with the intention to deceive [fob off, palm off]</p><p><b>vitamin B koji je bitan za rast i reprodukciju stanica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is essential for cell growth and reproduction [folate, folic acid, pteroylglutamic acid, pteroylmonoglutamic acid, vitamin Bc, vitamin M]</p><p><b>folna kiselina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is essential for cell growth and reproduction [folacin, folic acid, pteroylglutamic acid, pteroylmonoglutamic acid, vitamin Bc, vitamin M]</p><p><b>bora, nabor, obor, omot, preklopiti, presaviti, prijevoj, saviti, složiti, zamotati, zaviti, kovrea, pregib, zavoj, zajednica, stado, preklapati, presavijati, presavinuti, zavrnuti, zavrtati, isključiti se, zatvoriti, smotati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an angular or rounded shape made by folding [bend, crease, crimp, flexure, plication]</p><p><i>n.</i> a group of people who adhere to a common faith and habitually attend a given church [congregation, faithful]</p><p><i>n.</i> a geological process that causes a bend in a stratum of rock [folding]</p><p><i>n.</i> a group of sheep or goats [flock]</p><p><i>n.</i> a folded part (as in skin or muscle) [plica]</p><p><i>n.</i> a pen for sheep [sheep pen, sheepcote, sheepfold]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of folding [folding]</p><p><i>v.</i> bend or lay so that one part covers the other [fold up, turn up]</p><p><i>v.</i> incorporate a food ingredient into a mixture