ections (rather than by swinging on hinges) [accordion door]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (b) ovog Pravilnika, države članice mogu odrediti da se za određene instrumente primjenjuje sljedeće odredbe: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> currency issued by a government or central bank and consisting of printed paper that can circulate as a substitute for specie [paper currency, paper money]</p><p><b>pilom s zubnim oštricom koja se savije u ručicu (kao džepni nož) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a saw with a toothed blade that folds into a handle (the way a pocketknife folds)</p><p><b>stranica koja se prekrši u knjigu ili časopis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oversize page that is folded in to a book or magazine [gatefold]</p><p><b>od ili koje pripadaju biljnom listu ili na njega liče, s brojnim listovima, (posebno metamorfnih stijena) s tankim slojevima ili slojevima nalik lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or resembling the leaf of a plant</p><p><i>adj.</i> bearing numerous leaves [foliaged, foliose]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (especially of metamorphic rock) having thin leaflike layers or strata [foliate, foliated]</p><p><b>listoliki ukras, lišće, list, listić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the main organ of photosynthesis and transpiration in higher plants [leaf, leafage]</p><p><i>n.</i> (architecture) leaf-like architectural ornament [foliation]</p><p><b>s brojnim listovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> bearing numerous leaves [foliaceous, foliose]</p><p><b>paginirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> hammer into thin flat foils</p><p><i>v.</i> decorate with leaves</p><p><i>v.</i> coat or back with metal foil</p><p><i>v.</i> number the pages of a book or manuscript [page, paginate]</p><p><i>v.</i> grow leaves</p><p><i>adj.</i> ornamented with foliage or foils [foliated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (often used as a combining form) having or resembling a leaf or having a specified kind or number of leaves</p><p><i>adj.</i> (especially of metamorphic rock) having thin leaflike layers or strata [foliaceous, foliated]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50%, (posebno metamorfnih stijena) s tankim slojevima ili slojevima nalik lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> ornamented with foliage or foils [foliate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (especially of metamorphic rock) having thin leaflike layers or strata [foliaceous, foliate]</p><p><b>Folijacija, listić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (botany) the process of forming leaves [leafing]</p><p><i>n.</i> (geology) the arrangement of leaflike layers in a rock</p><p><i>n.</i> (architecture) leaf-like architectural ornament [foliage]</p><p><i>n.</i> the production of foil by cutting or beating metal into thin leaves</p><p><i>n.</i> the work of coating glass with metal foil</p><p><b>folna kiselina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is essential for cell growth and reproduction [folacin, folate, pteroylglutamic acid, pteroylmonoglutamic acid, vitamin Bc, vitamin M]</p><p><b>(psihijatrija) psihološki poremećaj misli ili osjećaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychiatry) a psychological disorder of thought or emotion [disturbance, mental disorder, mental disturbance, psychological disorder]</p><p><b>istodobno pojavljivanje simptoma mentalnog poremećaja (kao zablude) u dvije osobe koje su blisko povezane (kao braća i sestre ili muž i žena) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the simultaneous occurrence of symptoms of a mental disorder (as delusions) in two persons who are closely related (as siblings or man and wife)</p><p><b>list, broj stranice, paginacija, arak, list papira</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of numbering pages [page number, pagination, paging]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sheet of any written or printed material (especially in a manuscript or book) [leaf]</p><p><i>n.</i> a book (or manuscript) consisting of large sheets of paper folded in the middle to make two leaves or four pages</p><p><b>(često se koristi kao kombinirani oblik) s letcima (sastavljeni listovi) ili određenim vrstama ili brojem letaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (often used as a combining form) having leaflets (compound leaves) or a specified kind or number of leaflets</p><p><b>listovit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> bearing numerous leaves [foliaceous, foliaged]</p><p><b>Složeni sjemenici, sjemenice i sjemenice, s masenim udjelom ili ne većim od 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin layer or stratum of (especially metamorphic) rock</p><p><b>folk-glazba, narod, narodna glazba, narodne, narodni, narodnih, pučki, avet, puk, pleme, obitelj, obiteljska loza, porodica, rod, rodbina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people in general (often used in the plural) [common people, folks]</p><p><i>n.</i> a social division of (usually preliterate) people [tribe]</p><p><i>n.</i> people descended from a common ancestor [family, family line, kinfolk, kinsfolk, phratry, sept]</p><p><i>n.</i> the traditional and typically anonymous music that is an expression of the life of people in a community [ethnic music, folk music]</p><p><b>folklorni likovni izraz, narodna umjetnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genre of art of unknown origin that reflects traditional values of a society</p><p><b>pjesma koju tradicionalno pjevaju obični ljudi u nekom regionu i koja je dio njihove kulture (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a song that is traditionally sung by the common people of a region and forms part of their culture [folk song, folksong]</p><p><b>folklorni ples, narodni ples</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a style of dancing that originated among ordinary people (not in the royal courts) [folk dancing]</p><p><i>v.</i> perform a folk-dance</p><p><b>Neko tko radi narodne plesove. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who does folk dances</p><p><b>ples koji je nastao među običnim ljudima (ne na kraljevskom dvoru) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a style of dancing that originated among ordinary people (not in the royal courts) [folk dance]</p><p><b>popularna ali pogrešna etimologija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a popular but erroneous etymology</p><p><b>folklorna glazba, narodna glazba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the traditional and typically anonymous music that is an expression of the life of people in a community [ethnic music, folk]</p><p><b>narodni pisac koji komponira u stilu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a folk writer who composes in verse</p><p><b>pjevač narodnih pjesama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a singer of folk songs [jongleur, minstrel, poet-singer, troubadour]</p><p><b>narodna pjesma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a song that is traditionally sung by the common people of a region and forms part of their culture [folk ballad, folksong]</p><p><b>Priča koja se širi usmenom komunikacijom među običnim ljudima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tale circulated by word of mouth among the common folk [folktale]</p><p><b>pisac narodnih priča. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a writer of folktales</p><p><b>floklorne, folklor, folklora, folkloristika, folkloristiku, folklorna, folklorni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the unwritten lore (stories and proverbs and riddles and songs) of a culture</p><p><b>porodica, ukućani, narod, puk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> your parents</p><p><i>n.</i> people in general (often used in the plural) [common people, folk]</p><p><b>pjesma koju tradicionalno pjevaju obični ljudi u nekom regionu i koja je dio njihove kulture (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a song that is traditionally sung by the common people of a region and forms part of their culture [folk ballad, folk song]</p><p><b>-Postoji i drugačije mišljenje., vrlo neformalan i poznat. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to the common people, especially in regard to speech patterns, attitudes, etc.</p><p><i>adj.</i> very informal and familiar</p><p><b>bajka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tale circulated by word of mouth among the common folk [folk tale]</p><p><b>čahura, folikula, mahuna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any small spherical group of cells containing a cavity</p><p><b>gonadotropni hormon koji se luči iz prednje hipofize i stimulira rast grafijskih folikula kod samcica sisavaca i aktivira stanice kod mužjaka sisavaca koje formiraju spermu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gonadotropic hormone that is secreted by the anterior pituitary and stimulates growth of Graafian follicles in female mammals, and activates the cells in male mammals that form sperm [FSH]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili koje čine folikule (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or constituting a follicle</p><p><b>upaljenost folikula dlake (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of a hair follicle</p><p><b>bezumlje, budalaština, glupost, ludorija, ludost (od &quot;folly&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a revue with elaborate costuming</p><p><b>držati se, goniti, postupiti prema, pratiti, razumjeti, slediti, slijediti, slušati, ugledati se na, slijede, slijedite, ići, pokoravati se, pokoriti se, poslušati, povinovati se, pridržavati se, udovoljavati, udovoljiti, udovoljivati, gledati, paziti, pripaziti, promatrati, naslijediti, informirati se, interesirati se, zanimati se, nadgledati, nadzirati, ganjati, hvatati, juriti, loviti, naganjati, natjeravati, proganjati, progoniti, ustrajati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to travel behind, go after, come after</p><p><i>v.</i> be later in time [postdate]</p><p><i>v.</i> come as a logical consequence [fall out]</p><p><i>v.</i> travel along a certain course [travel along]</p><p><i>v.</i> act in accordance with someone's rules, commands, or wishes [abide by, comply]</p><p><i>v.</i> come after in time, as a result [come after]</p><p><i>v.</i> behave in accordance or in agreement with [conform to]</p><p><i>v.</i> be next</p><p><i>v.</i> choose and follow [adopt, espouse]</p><p><i>v.</i> to bring something about at a later time than</p><p><i>v.</i> imitate in behavior [take after]</p><p><i>v.</i> follow, discover, or ascertain the course of development of something [trace]</p><p><i>v.</i> follow with the eyes or the mind [keep an eye on, observe, watch, watch over]</p><p><i>v.</i> be the successor (of) [come after, succeed]</p><p><i>v.</i> perform an accompaniment to [accompany, play along]</p><p><i>v.</i> keep informed [keep abreast, keep up]</p><p><i>v.</i> to be the product or result [come]</p><p><i>v.</i> accept and follow the leadership or command or guidance of</p><p><i>v.</i> adhere to or practice</p><p><i>v.</i> work in a specific place, with a specific subject, or in a specific function [be]</p><p><i>v.</i> keep under surveillance [surveil, survey]</p><p><i>v.</i> follow in or as if in pursuit [pursue]</p><p><i>v.</i> grasp the meaning</p><p><i>v.</i> keep to [stick to, stick with]</p><p><b>implementirati, izvesti, izvoditi, izvršavati, izvršiti, ostvariti, ostvarivati, provesti, provoditi, realizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> pursue to a conclusion or bring to a successful issue [carry out, follow through, follow up, go through with, implement, put through]</p><p><b>Učini ono što drugi rade. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> do what someone else is doing</p><p><b>izmahnuti, tijelom pratiti pokret, implementirati, izvesti, izvoditi, izvršavati, izvršiti, ostvariti, ostvarivati, provesti, provoditi, realizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> carry a stroke to natural completion after hitting or releasing a ball</p><p><i>v.</i> pursue to a conclusion or bring to a successful issue [carry out, follow out, follow up, go through with, implement, put through]</p><p><b>kontrola, nastaviti, pismo u kome se pozivamo na prethodno pismo, pratnja, praćenje bolesnika, implementirati, izvesti, izvoditi, izvršavati, izvršiti, ostvariti, ostvarivati, provesti, provoditi, realizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> pursue to a conclusion or bring to a successful issue [carry out, follow out, follow through, go through with, implement, put through]</p><p><i>v.</i> increase the effectiveness or success of by further action</p><p><b>nastaviti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> carry further or advance [act on, pursue]</p><p><b>odmah drugi inning prisiljen na kriket tim postiže propisan broj utrka manje od svojih protivnika u prvom inningu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an immediate second innings forced on a cricket team scoring a prescribed number of runs fewer than its opponents in the first innings</p><p><b>izmahnuti, tijelom pratiti pokret</b></p><p><i>n.</i> carrying some project or intention to full completion</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of carrying a stroke to its natural completion</p><p><b>kontrola, nastaviti, pismo u kome se pozivamo na prethodno pismo, pratnja, praćenje bolesnika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of work that exploits or builds on earlier work [followup]</p><p><i>n.</i> an activity that continues something that has already begun or that repeats something that has already been done [followup]</p><p><i>n.</i> a subsequent examination of a patient for the purpose of monitoring earlier treatment [followup, reexamination, review]</p><p><b>pristaša, sljedbenik, udvarač, pristalica, sljednik, štovatelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who accepts the leadership of another</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who travels behind or pursues another</p><p><b>pristaša, sljedbenik, udvarač (od &quot;follower&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of followers or enthusiasts [following]</p><p><b>Oživljavajuća islamska fundamentalistička organizacija sa sjedištem u Nigeriji za koju se vjeruje da planira terorističke napade. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a resurgent Islamic fundamentalist organization based in Nigeria that is thought to be planning terrorist attacks [al Sunna Wal Jamma]</p><p><b>idući, nakon, niz, nizom, ovaj, praćenje, pratnja, slijede, slijedeće, slijedeći, sljedeće, sljedeći, sljedećim, sljedeću, gonjenje, lov, potjera, naredni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of followers or enthusiasts [followers]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of pursuing in an effort to overtake or capture [chase, pursual, pursuit]</p><p><i>adj.</i> about to be mentioned or specified [undermentioned]</p><p><i>adj.</i> immediately following in time or order [next]</p><p><i>adj.</i> going or proceeding or coming after in the same direction</p><p><i>adj.</i> in the desired direction</p><p><b>kontrola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of work th