s or claims or privileges</p><p><b>blag, milostiv, obziran, popustljiv, strpljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing patient and unruffled self-control and restraint under adversity [longanimous]</p><p><b>nedopuštati, zabraniti, zabranjivati, braniti, priječiti, prohibirati, proskribirati, zapriječiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> command against [disallow, interdict, nix, prohibit, proscribe, veto]</p><p><i>v.</i> keep from happening or arising [foreclose, forestall, preclude, prevent]</p><p><b>službena zabrana ili uredba protiv nečega, U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, "službenici" su: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an official prohibition or edict against something [ban, banning, forbidding]</p><p><i>n.</i> the action of prohibiting or inhibiting or forbidding (or an instance thereof) [inhibition, prohibition]</p><p><b>zabranjen, zabranjena</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> excluded from use or mention [out, prohibited, proscribed, taboo, tabu, verboten]</p><p><b>Sveti grad Lamaizma., zidani dio Pekinga koji okružuje palaču koja je nekada bila rezidencija kineskog cara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sacred city of Lamaism [Lassa, Lhasa, capital of Tibet]</p><p><i>n.</i> a walled section of Beijing that encloses the palace that was formerly the residence of the emperor of China</p><p><b>izvorno jabuka s drveta znanja dobra i zla u Edenu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> originally an apple from the tree of knowledge of good and evil in the Garden of Eden</p><p><b>zabranjujući</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an official prohibition or edict against something [ban, banning, forbiddance]</p><p><i>adj.</i> harshly uninviting or formidable in manner or appearance [dour, grim]</p><p><i>adj.</i> threatening or foreshadowing evil or tragic developments [baleful, menacing, minacious, minatory, ominous, sinister, threatening]</p><p><b>zabranjujući (od &quot;forbidding&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an unpleasant or menacing manner</p><p><b>natjerati, oskvrnuti, prinuda, prisiliti, probiti, prodrijeti, sila, snaga, sile, jakost, jačina, silina, silovitost, žestina, ljudstvo, osoblje, ratna jedinica, vojna jedinica, vojne snage, vojska, nasilje, forsirati, iznuditi, iznuđivati, nametati, nametnuti, natjeravati, primorati, primoravati, prinuditi, prisiljavati, pritiskati, pritisnuti, siliti, tjerati, gurati, gurnuti, odgurivati, odgurnuti, utisnuti, upraviti, upravljati, usmjeravati, usmjeriti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a powerful effect or influence</p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the influence that produces a change in a physical quantity</p><p><i>n.</i> physical energy or intensity [forcefulness, strength]</p><p><i>n.</i> group of people willing to obey orders [personnel]</p><p><i>n.</i> a unit that is part of some military service [military force, military group, military unit]</p><p><i>n.</i> an act of aggression (as one against a person who resists) [violence]</p><p><i>n.</i> one possessing or exercising power or influence or authority [power]</p><p><i>n.</i> a group of people having the power of effective action</p><p><i>n.</i> (of a law) having legal validity [effect]</p><p><i>n.</i> a putout of a base runner who is required to run [force-out, force out, force play]</p><p><i>v.</i> to cause to do through pressure or necessity, by physical, moral or intellectual means [coerce, hale, pressure, squeeze]</p><p><i>v.</i> urge or force (a person) to an action [impel]</p><p><i>v.</i> move with force [push]</p><p><i>v.</i> impose urgently, importunately, or inexorably [thrust]</p><p><i>v.</i> squeeze like a wedge into a tight space [squeeze, wedge]</p><p><i>v.</i> force into or from an action or state, either physically or metaphorically [drive, ram]</p><p><i>v.</i> do forcibly</p><p><i>v.</i> take by force [storm]</p><p><b>Osnovana 1972. godine kao osobna sigurnosna snaga Arafata i drugih vođa PLO-a. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> formed in 1972 as a personal security force for Arafat and other PLO leaders</p><p><b>odbijati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to move back by force or influence [beat back, drive, push back, repel, repulse]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju motora s unutarnjim sagorevanjem, u skladu s člankom 86. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, upotrebljavaju se: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mechanical system of lubricating internal combustion engines in which a pump forces oil into the engine bearings [force-feed lubricating system, lubricating system, pressure-feed lubricating system, pressure feed]</p><p><b>zaštitno polje, polje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the space around a radiating body within which its electromagnetic oscillations can exert force on another similar body not in contact with it [field, field of force]</p><p><b>viša sila, Božja volja, prst Božji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a natural and unavoidable catastrophe that interrupts the expected course of events [act of God, inevitable accident, unavoidable casualty, vis major]</p><p><b>istjerati, izvlačiti, izvući, potjerati, tjerati, ištrcati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a putout of a base runner who is required to run [force, force-out, force play]</p><p><i>v.</i> force to leave (an office) [depose]</p><p><i>v.</i> terminate the employment of [can, dismiss, displace, fire, give notice, give the axe, give the sack, sack, send away, terminate]</p><p><i>v.</i> force or drive out [drive out, rouse, rout out]</p><p><i>v.</i> press, force, or thrust out of a small space [crowd out]</p><p><i>v.</i> expel from one's property or force to move out by a legal process [evict]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to come out in a squirt [eject, squeeze out, squirt]</p><p><i>v.</i> force with the thumb [gouge]</p><p><i>v.</i> emit or cause to move with force of effort</p><p><b>Snaga primijenjena na jedinicu površine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the force applied to a unit area of surface [pressure, pressure level]</p><p><b>Putuut baznog trkača koji mora trčati (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a putout of a base runner who is required to run [force, force-out, force out]</p><p><b>pumpa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pump used to force a liquid up and expel it under pressure</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju električnih vozila od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of measurement of physical force</p><p><b>Hraniti nekoga tko ne želi ili ne može jesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> feed someone who will not or cannot eat</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju motora s unutarnjim sagorevanjem, u skladu s člankom 86. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, upotrebljavaju se: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mechanical system of lubricating internal combustion engines in which a pump forces oil into the engine bearings [force feed, lubricating system, pressure-feed lubricating system, pressure feed]</p><p><b>Napraviti prisilno slijetanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a forced landing</p><p><b>Putuut baznog trkača koji mora trčati (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a putout of a base runner who is required to run [force, force out, force play]</p><p><b>forsiran, iznuđen, nenaravan, primoran, prinudan, prinukan, prisilan, prisiljen, usiljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> produced by or subjected to forcing</p><p><i>adj.</i> forced or compelled</p><p><i>adj.</i> made necessary by an unexpected situation or emergency</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking spontaneity [constrained, strained]</p><p><b>hranjenje koje se sastoji od isporuke hranjivog rastvora (kao što je kroz nosnu cijev) nekome tko ne može ili ne želi jesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feeding that consists of the delivery of a nutrient solution (as through a nasal tube) to someone who cannot or will not eat [gavage]</p><p><b>Neplanirano slijetanje zrakoplova koje se izvodi u okolnostima (neuspjeh motora ili nepovoljno vrijeme) koje nisu pod kontrolom pilota (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unscheduled airplane landing that is made under circumstances (engine failure or adverse weather) not under the pilot's control [emergency landing]</p><p><b>prodaja imovine od strane šerifa na temelju sudskog naloga o izvršenju kako bi se zadovoljila neplaćena obveza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sale of property by the sheriff under authority of a court's writ of execution in order satisfy an unpaid obligation [execution sale, judicial sale, sheriff's sale]</p><p><b>snažan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by or full of force or strength (often but not necessarily physical)</p><p><i>adj.</i> forceful and definite in expression or action [emphatic]</p><p><b>snažno, nasilno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with full force</p><p><b>jakost, jačina, sila, silina, silovitost, snaga, žestina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> physical energy or intensity [force, strength]</p><p><b>nedostatak snage (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking force [unforceful]</p><p><b>Mješavina mletog sirovog piletine i gljiva s pistacijima i tartufima i lukom i petrisolja i puno maslaca i vezano s jajima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mixture of ground raw chicken and mushrooms with pistachios and truffles and onions and parsley and lots of butter and bound with eggs [farce]</p><p><b>pinceta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extractor consisting of a pair of pincers used in medical treatment (especially for the delivery of babies)</p><p><b>Rođenje u kojem se forceps stavlja kroz vaginu i koristi za hvatanje glave fetusa i povlačenje kroz porođajni kanal (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> delivery in which forceps are inserted through the vagina and used to grasp the head of the fetus and pull it through the birth canal</p><p><b>Malo poznata palestinska grupa odgovorna za bombardovanja i ubijanje Izraelaca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a little known Palestinian group responsible for bombings and for killing Israelis [Umar al-Mukhtar Forces]</p><p><b>nasilan, prisilan, silovit, uvjerljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> impelled by physical force especially against resistance [physical, strong-arm]</p><p><b>snažno, prisilno, silom</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a forcible manner</p><p><b>istjerivanje, izbacivanje, izgon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of expelling or projecting or ejecting [ejection, expulsion, projection]</p><p><b>u obliku forcepa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> shaped like a forceps</p><p>