, forgo, relinquish, waive]</p><p><i>v.</i> turn away from [quit, relinquish, renounce]</p><p><b>pokazatelj, predokus, predosjećaj, predznak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an early limited awareness of something yet to occur</p><p><b>najaviti događaj, predskazati, predvidjeti, prognozirati, proreći, nagovijestiti, nagovješćivati, najaviti, najavljivati, navijestiti, naviještati, navješćivati, naznačiti, naznačivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> foreshadow or presage [announce, annunciate, harbinger, herald]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a prediction about [anticipate, call, forebode, predict, prognosticate, promise]</p><p><i>v.</i> indicate, as with a sign or an omen [augur, auspicate, betoken, bode, forecast, foreshadow, omen, portend, predict, prefigure, presage, prognosticate]</p><p><b>predviđanje, gatanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statement made about the future [forecasting, prediction, prognostication]</p><p><i>n.</i> the art or gift of prophecy (or the pretense of prophecy) by supernatural means [divination, fortune telling, soothsaying]</p><p><b>predumišljaj, oprez, opreznost, predostrožnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> planning or plotting in advance of acting [premeditation]</p><p><i>n.</i> judiciousness in avoiding harm or danger [care, caution, precaution]</p><p><b>Razmišljajući o budućnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> thoughtful of the future</p><p><b>predznak, nagovještaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that is experienced as indicating important things to come [augury, preindication, sign]</p><p><b>platforma na čelu prednjeg stuba, čvor konjske grijehe koji raste naprijed između ušiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a platform at the head of a foremast</p><p><i>n.</i> a lock of a horse's mane that grows forward between the ears [forelock]</p><p><b>uvijek, vječito, vječno, za sva vremena, zauvijek, zauvjek</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> for a limitless time [eternally, everlastingly, evermore]</p><p><i>adv.</i> for a very long or seemingly endless time [forever and a day]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without interruption [always, constantly, incessantly, perpetually]</p><p><b>za vrlo dugo ili naizgled beskrajno vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> for a very long or seemingly endless time [forever]</p><p><b>u bilo kojem budućem trenutku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at any future time [evermore]</p><p><b>opomenuti, upozoriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> warn in advance or beforehand [previse]</p><p><b>opomenuti, upozoriti (od &quot;forewarn&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an early warning about a future event [premonition]</p><p><b>bilo koji od prednjih par krila na insektu koji ima četiri krila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of the anterior pair of wings on an insect that has four wings [fore-wing, fore wing]</p><p><b>Žena koja je predsjedavajući porote, Žena koja vodi grupu radnika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman who is foreperson of a jury [forelady]</p><p><i>n.</i> a woman in charge of a group of workers</p><p><b>predgovor, uvodna riječ</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short introductory essay preceding the text of a book [preface, prolusion]</p><p><b>globa, gubitak, kazna, pokora, žrtva, gubiti, izgubiti, odreći se, odricati se, uskratiti si, uskraćivati si</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that is lost or surrendered as a penalty [forfeiture]</p><p><i>n.</i> a penalty for a fault or mistake that involves losing or giving up something [forfeiture]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of losing or surrendering something as a penalty for a mistake or fault or failure to perform etc. [forfeiture, sacrifice]</p><p><i>v.</i> lose (s.th.) or lose the right to (s.th.) by some error, offense, or crime [forego, forgo, give up, throw overboard, waive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> surrendered as a penalty [confiscate, forfeited]</p><p><b>globa, gubitak, kazna, pokora (od &quot;forfeit&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> surrendered as a penalty [confiscate, forfeit]</p><p><b>gubitak, gubljenje, konfiskacija, oduzimanje prava, žrtva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that is lost or surrendered as a penalty [forfeit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a penalty for a fault or mistake that involves losing or giving up something [forfeit]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of losing or surrendering something as a penalty for a mistake or fault or failure to perform etc. [forfeit, sacrifice]</p><p><b>spriječiti pojavu: (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> prevent the occurrence of [avert, avoid, debar, deflect, fend off, forefend, head off, obviate, stave off, ward off]</p><p><b>nalik vilici. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a fork [bifurcate, biramous, branched, fork-like, forked, pronged, prongy]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Forficulidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of Forficulidae [genus Forficula]</p><p><b>ponekad uništavajuće za uzgojene lupine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sometimes destructive to cultivated bulbs [common European earwig]</p><p><b>tipične ušičice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> typical earwigs [family Forficulidae]</p><p><b>naći se, sastati se, nalaziti se, okupiti se, okupljati se, pribirati, sakupiti se, sakupljati se, sastajati se, skupiti se, skupljati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> collect in one place [assemble, foregather, gather, meet]</p><p><b>falsificirati, kovačko ognjište, kovačnica, kovati, krivotvoriti, patvoriti, iskovati, ukucati, lažirati, formirati, modelirati, oblikovati, uobličavati, uobličiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> furnace consisting of a special hearth where metal is heated before shaping</p><p><i>n.</i> a workplace where metal is worked by heating and hammering [smithy]</p><p><i>v.</i> create by hammering [hammer]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a copy of with the intent to deceive [counterfeit, fake]</p><p><i>v.</i> come up with (an idea, plan, explanation, theory, or principle) after a mental effort [contrive, devise, excogitate, formulate, invent]</p><p><i>v.</i> move ahead steadily</p><p><i>v.</i> move or act with a sudden increase in speed or energy [spirt, spurt]</p><p><i>v.</i> make something, usually for a specific function [form, mold, mould, shape, work]</p><p><i>v.</i> make out of components (often in an improvising manner) [fashion]</p><p><b>kovani, krivotvoren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> reproduced fraudulently [bad]</p><p><b>falsifikator, kovač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who operates a forge</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who makes copies illegally [counterfeiter]</p><p><b>falsifikat, krivotvorenje, krivotvorina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a copy that is represented as the original [counterfeit]</p><p><i>n.</i> criminal falsification by making or altering an instrument with intent to defraud</p><p><b>zaboraviti, zaboravljati, propustiti, propuštati, ostaviti, ostavljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> dismiss from the mind [bury]</p><p><i>v.</i> be unable to remember [blank out, block, draw a blank]</p><p><i>v.</i> forget to do something</p><p><i>v.</i> leave behind unintentionally [leave]</p><p><b>Ulica imena za flunitrazepan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> street names for flunitrazepan [Mexican valium, R-2, circle, roach, roofy, rope, rophy]</p><p><b>nezaboravak, potočnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small perennial herb having bright blue or white flowers [Myosotis scorpiodes, mouse ear]</p><p><b>zaboravan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of memory) deficient in retentiveness or range [short, unretentive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not mindful or attentive [mindless, unmindful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> failing to keep in mind [oblivious]</p><p><b>Neorganizirana osoba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flighty and disorganized person [scatterbrain]</p><p><b>zaboravan (od &quot;forgetful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a forgetful manner</p><p><b>zaboravljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tendency to forget</p><p><i>n.</i> unawareness caused by neglectful or heedless failure to remember</p><p><b>lako zaboravljen. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> easily forgotten</p><p><b>kovani materijal, kovanje, otkivak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shaping metal by heating and hammering</p><p><b>lako se opravdavaju ili opraštaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> easily excused or forgiven [excusable, venial]</p><p><b>na opravdan način ili na opravdan stepen (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an excusable manner or to an excusable degree [excusably, pardonably]</p><p><b>opraštati, oprostiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> stop blaming or grant forgiveness</p><p><i>v.</i> absolve from payment</p><p><b>opraštanje, oproštaj, praštanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> compassionate feelings that support a willingness to forgive</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of excusing a mistake or offense [pardon]</p><p><b>opraštati, oprostiti (od &quot;forgive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who pardons or forgives or excuses a fault or offense [excuser, pardoner]</p><p><b>blag, koji oprašta, milostiv, pomirljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined or able to forgive and show mercy</p><p><i>adj.</i> providing absolution [absolvitory, exonerative]</p><p><b>blago, milostivo, pomirljivo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with forgiveness</p><p><b>blag, koji oprašta, milostiv, pomirljiv (od &quot;forgiving&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tendency to be kind and forgiving [kindness]</p><p><b>prethoditi, gubiti, izgubiti, odreći se, odricati se, uskratiti si, uskraćivati si</b></p><p><i>v.</i> do without or cease to hold or adhere to [dispense with, forego, foreswear, relinquish, waive]</p><p><i>v.</i> be earlier in time [antecede, antedate, forego, precede, predate]</p><p><i>v.</i> lose (s.th.) or lose the right to (s.th.) by some error, offense, or crime [forego, forfeit, give up, throw overboard, waive]</p><p><b>prethoditi (od &quot;forgo&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of renouncing [forswearing, renunciation]</p><p><b>zaboravio, zaboravljen, zaboravljena, zaboravljene</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not noticed inadvertently [disregarded]</p><p><b>forinta, mađarska forinta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Hungary</p><p><b>račvati, račvati se, rašlje, vile, vilica, viljuška, grananje, račvanje, rašljanje, granati se, razgranati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cutlery used for serving and eating food</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of branching out or dividing into branches [branching, forking, ramification]</p><p><i>n.</i> the region of the angle formed by the junction of two branches [crotch]</p><p><i>n.</i> an agricultural tool used for lifting or digging</p><p><i>n.</i> the angle formed by the inner sides of the legs where they join the human trunk [crotch]</p><p><i>v.</i> lift with a pitchfork [pitchfork]</p><p><i>v.</i> place under attack with one's own pieces, of two enemy pieces</p><p><i>v.</i> divide into two or more branches so as to form a fork [branch, furcate, ramify, separate]</p><p><i>v.</i> shape like a fork</p><p><b>isporučiti, isporučivati, izručiti, izručivati, predati, predavati, prepustiti, prepuštati, uručiti, uručivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to surrender someone or something to another [deliver, fork over, fork up, hand over, render, turn in]</p><p><b>isporučiti, isporučivati, izručiti, izručivati, predati, predavati, prepustiti, prepuštati, uručiti, uručivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to surrender someone or something to another [deliver, fork out, fork up, hand over, render, turn in]</p><p><b>isporučiti, isporučivati, izručiti, izručivati, predati, predavati, prepustiti, prepuštati, uručiti, uručivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to surrender someone or something to another [deliver, fork out, fork over, hand over, render, turn in]</p><p><b>nalik vilici. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a fork [bifurcate, biramous, branched, forficate, forked, pronged, prongy]</p><p><b>račvast, rascijepan, raskoljen, rašljast, razdvojen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a fork [bifurcate, biramous, branched, forficate, fork-like, pronged, prongy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having two meanings with intent to deceive [double]</p><p><b>oblik munje koja se brzo kreće u cik-cak putanju s jednim krajem podijeljenim (kao vilica) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of lightning that moves rapidly in a zigzag path with one end divided (fork-like) [chain lightning]</p><p><b>grananje, račvanje, rašljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the place where something divides into branches [furcation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of branching out or dividing into branches [branching, fork, ramification]</p><p><b>viljuškar, viličar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small industrial vehicle with a power operated forked platform in front that can be inserted under loads to lift and move them</p><p><b>beznadan, bijedan, napušten, odbačen, usamljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by or showing hopelessness</p><p><b>nesigurni ili očajni poduhvat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hopeless or desperate enterprise</p><p><b>beznadan, bijedan, napušten, odbačen, usamljen (od &quot;forlorn&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a forlorn manner</p><p><b>beznadan, bijedan, napušten, odbačen, usamljen (od &quot;forlorn&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sadness resulting from being forsaken or abandoned [desolation, loneliness]</p><p><b>bon, činiti, forma, formirati, formular, izraditi, model, načiniti, oblik, oblikovanje, oblikovati, obrazac, obrazovati, potvrda, razred, red, sačiniti, tiskanica, tvoriti, ustanoviti, ustrojiti, vrsta, forme, oblika, obliku, izraz, označitelj, klasa, uzorak, izgled, obličje, figura, građa, ljudsko tijelo, stas, tijelo, tjelesna građa, trup, lik, varijanta, predstavljati, sačinjavati, uobličiti, modelirati, uobličavati, utisnuti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the phonological or orthographic sound or appearance of a word that can be used to describe or identify something [descriptor, signifier, word form]</p><p><i>n.</i> a category of things distinguished by some common characteristic or quality [kind, sort, variety]</p><p><i>n.</i> a perceptual structure [pattern, shape]</p><p><i>n.</i> any spatial attributes (especially as defined by outline) [configuration, conformation, contour, shape]</p><p><i>n.</i> alternative names for the body of a human being [anatomy, bod, build, chassis, figure, flesh, frame, human body, material body, physical body, physique, shape, soma]</p><p><i>n.</i> the spatial arrangement of something as distinct from its substance [shape]</p><p><i>n.</i> the visual appearance of something or someone [cast, shape]</p><p><i>n.</i> a printed document with spaces in which to write</p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) a group of organisms within a species that differ in trivial ways from similar groups [strain, var., variant]</p><p><i>n.</i> an arrangement of the elements in a composition or discourse</p><p><i>n.</i> a particular mode in which something is manifested</p><p><i>n.</i> (physical chemistry) a distinct state of matter in a system [phase]</p><p><i>n.</i> a body of students who are taught together [class, course, grade]</p><p><i>n.</i> an ability to perform well</p><p><i>n.</i> a life-size dummy used to display clothes [manakin, manikin, mannequin, mannikin]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mold for setting concrete</p><p><i>v.</i> create (as an entity) [organise, organize]</p><p><i>v.</i> to compose or represent [constitute, make]</p><p><i>v.</i> develop into a distinctive entity [spring, take form, take shape]</p><p><i>v.</i> give shape or form to [shape]</p><p><i>v.</i> make something, usually for a specific function [forge, mold, mould, shape, work]</p><p><i>v.</i> establish or impress firmly in the mind [imprint]</p><p><i>v.</i> assume a form or shape</p><p><b>postanu mjehurićasti ili pjenasti ili pjenast (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become bubbly or frothy or foaming [effervesce, fizz, foam, froth, sparkle]</p><p><b>vrsta riječi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the traditional categories of words intended to reflect their functions in a grammatical context [part of speech, word class]</p><p><b>umjetna taksonomska kategorija za organizme čiji su pravi odnosi nejasni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial taxonomic category for organisms of which the true relationships are obscure</p><p><b>(biologija) umjetna taksonomska kategorija za organizme čiji su pravi odnosi nejasni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) an artificial taxonomic category for organisms of which the true relationships are obscure</p><p><b>(biologija) umjetna taksonomska kategorija za organizme čiji su pravi odnosi nejasni, umjetna taksonomska kategorija utvrđena na temelju morfološke sličnosti za organizme s nejasnim istinskim vezama, posebno fosilne oblike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) an artificial taxonomic category for organisms of which the true relationships are obscure</p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial taxonomic category established on the basis of morphological resemblance for organisms of obscure true relationships especially fossil forms</p><p><b>form rodove nesavršenih gljiva od kojih su neke vrste sada smještene u rodove Pellicularia i Corticium jer su pronađene njihove savršene faze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> form genus of imperfect fungi some species of which are now placed in genera Pellicularia and Corticium because their perfect stages have been found [genus Rhizoctinia]</p><p><b>pismo obrazac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a letter that is printed in multiple copies and mailed to a list of recipients</p><p><b>naslov, titula</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an identifying appellation signifying status or function: e.g. `Mr.' or `General' [title, title of respect]</p><p><b>politički sistem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the members of a social organization who are in power [political system]</p><p><b>To je samo stvar forme. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being a matter of form only</p><p><b>ceremonijalan, formalan, formalni, propisan, službeni, svečan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lavish dance requiring formal attire [ball]</p><p><i>n.</i> a gown for evening wear [dinner dress, dinner gown, evening gown]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being in accord with established forms and conventions and requirements (as e.g. of formal dress)</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of or befitting a person in authority</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of spoken and written language) adhering to traditional standards of correctness and without casual, contracted, and colloquial forms</p><p><i>adj.</i> represented in simplified or symbolic form [conventional, schematic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> logically deductive</p><p><i>adj.</i> refined or imposing in manner or appearance [courtly, stately]</p><p><b>vrt postavljen na redovitim linijama s biljkama raspoređenim na simetričnim mjestima ili u geometrijskim uzorcima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a garden laid out on regular lines with plants arranged in symmetrical locations or in geometrical designs</p><p><b>Svaki logički sustav koji abstrahira oblik izjava od njihovog sadržaja kako bi se utvrdili apstraktni kriteriji dosljednosti i valjanosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any logical system that abstracts the form of statements away from their content in order to establish abstract criteria of consistency and validity [mathematical logic, symbolic logic]</p><p><b>grana semantike koja proučava logičke aspekte značenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of semantics that studies the logical aspects of meaning</p><p><b>formaldehid, formaldehis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless poisonous gas [methanal]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a 10% solution of formaldehyde in water [formol]</p><p><b>Čin formalizacije (kao što je utvrđivanje formalnih pravila koja uređuju klase izraza) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making formal (as by stating formal rules governing classes of expressions) [formalization]</p><p><b>službeno ili službeno, Izjaviti ili učiniti pravno valjanim (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make formal or official [formalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> declare or make legally valid [formalize, validate]</p><p><b>koji se bave ili karakteriziraju strogim pridržavanjem priznatih oblika (posebno u religiji ili umjetnosti), davanje formalnog statusa ili odobrenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with or characterized by rigorous adherence to recognized forms (especially in religion or art) [formalistic, formalized]</p><p><i>adj.</i> given formal standing or endorsement [formalized]</p><p><b>formalizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine that formal structure rather than content is what should be represented</p><p><i>n.</i> (philosophy) the philosophical theory that formal (logical or mathematical) statements have no meaning but that its symbols (regarded as physical entities) exhibit a form that has useful applications</p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of scrupulous adherence to prescribed or external forms</p><p><b>koji se bave ili karakteriziraju strogim pridržavanjem priznatih oblika (posebno u religiji ili umjetnosti) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with or characterized by rigorous adherence to recognized forms (especially in religion or art) [formalised, formalized]</p><p><b>formalnosti, formalnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a requirement of etiquette or custom [formality]</p><p><b>formalnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a requirement of etiquette or custom [formalities]</p><p><i>n.</i> a manner that strictly observes all forms and ceremonies [formalness]</p><p><i>n.</i> compliance with formal rules</p><p><b>Čin formalizacije (kao što je utvrđivanje formalnih pravila koja uređuju klase izraza) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making formal (as by stating formal rules governing classes of expressions) [formalisation]</p><p><b>službeno ili službeno, Izjaviti ili učiniti pravno valjanim (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make formal or official [formalise]</p><p><i>v.</i> declare or make legally valid [formalise, validate]</p><p><b>koji se bave ili karakteriziraju strogim pridržavanjem priznatih oblika (posebno u religiji ili umjetnosti), davanje formalnog statusa ili odobrenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with or characterized by rigorous adherence to recognized forms (especially in religion or art) [formalised, formalistic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> given formal standing or endorsement [formalised]</p><p><b>ispravno, primjereno, propisno, službeno, formalno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with official authorization [officially]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a formal manner</p><p><b>ceremonijalan, formalan, formalni, propisan, službeni, svečan (od &quot;formal&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a manner that strictly observes all forms and ceremonies [formality]</p><p><b>odjeća za izlazak, večernja haljina, večernje odijelo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> attire to wear on formal occasions in the evening [evening clothes, evening dress, eveningwear]</p><p><b>format, format naredbe, format podatka, formatiranje, formatu, oblik, oblikovanje, aranžirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the organization of information according to preset specifications (usually for computer processing) [data format, data formatting, formatting]</p><p><i>n.</i> the general appearance of a publication</p><p><i>v.</i> set (printed matter) into a specific format [arrange]</p><p><i>v.</i> determine the arrangement of (data) for storage and display (in computer science)</p><p><i>v.</i> divide (a disk) into marked sectors so that it may store data [initialise, initialize]</p><p><b>oblikovanje, osnivanje, postrojba, raspored, stvaranje, tvorba, formiranje, formacija, formaciju, organizacija, osnutak, uspostava, uspostavljanje, ustanovljavanje, ustanovljenje, geološka formacija, geološka tvorevina, sastav, uređenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arrangement of people or things acting as a unit</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of fabricating something in a particular shape [shaping]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of forming or establishing something [constitution, establishment, organisation, organization]</p><p><i>n.</i> (geology) the geological features of the earth [geological formation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a particular spatial arrangement</p><p><i>n.</i> natural process that causes something to form</p><p><i>n.</i> creation by mental activity</p><p><b>formant, formativan, koji daje oblik, plastičan, tvoran, tvorben</b></p><p><i>n.</i> minimal language unit that has a syntactic (or morphological) function</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of forming new cells and tissues</p><p><i>adj.</i> forming or capable of forming or molding or fashioning [plastic, shaping]</p><p><b>ćelija embriona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cell of an embryo [embryonic cell]</p><p><b>(računarski znanost) upotrebljivi kapacitet diska (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) t