.</i> an asset of special worth or utility [long suit, metier, speciality, specialty, strength, strong point, strong suit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a musical composition or musical passage to be performed loudly</p><p><i>n.</i> the stronger part of a sword blade between the hilt and the foible</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used chiefly as a direction or description in music) loud [loud]</p><p><i>adv.</i> used as a direction in music [loudly]</p><p><b>forte-piano, glasovir, klavir, pianoforte, pijanino, pijano</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a keyboard instrument that is played by depressing keys that cause hammers to strike tuned strings and produce sounds [piano, pianoforte]</p><p><b>(uglavnom smjer ili opis u glazbi) glasno i snažno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (chiefly a direction or description in music) loud and strong</p><p><b>dalje, naprijed, unaprijed, daleko</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in southern Scotland that flows eastward to the Firth of Forth [Forth River]</p><p><i>adv.</i> from a particular thing or place or position (`forth' is obsolete) [away, off]</p><p><i>adv.</i> forward in time or order or degree [forward, onward]</p><p><i>adv.</i> out into view</p><p><b>rijeka u južnoj Škotskoj koja teče prema istoku do Firth of Forth (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in southern Scotland that flows eastward to the Firth of Forth [Forth]</p><p><b>predstojeći</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> at ease in talking to others [extroverted, outgoing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of the relatively near future [approaching, coming, upcoming]</p><p><i>adj.</i> available when required or as promised</p><p><b>predstojeći (od &quot;forthcoming&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being imminent and liable to happen soon [imminence, imminency, imminentness, impendence, impendency]</p><p><b>iskren, izravan, otvoren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by directness in manner or speech [blunt, candid, frank, free-spoken, outspoken, plainspoken, point-blank, straight-from-the-shoulder]</p><p><i>adv.</i> directly and without evasion 