> add nutrients to</p><p><i>v.</i> add alcohol to (beverages) [lace, spike]</p><p><b>glazbeno djelo ili glazbeni odlomak koji se izvodi vrlo glasno, (uglavnom smjer ili opis u glazbi) vrlo glasno i snažno, Uputstvo u glazbi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musical composition or musical passage to be performed very loudly</p><p><i>adj.</i> (chiefly a direction or description in music) very loud and strong</p><p><i>adv.</i> a direction in music [very loudly]</p><p><b>duhovna moć, hrabrost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> strength of mind that enables one to endure adversity with courage</p><p><b>četrnaest dana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a period of fourteen consecutive days [two weeks]</p><p><b>dvaput mjesečno, polumjesečni, polumjesečno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring every two weeks [biweekly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> every two weeks [biweekly]</p><p><b>programski jezik FORTRAN, programski jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a high-level programing language for mathematical and scientific purposes</p><p><b>Kompajler za programe napisane u FORTRAN-u (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compiler for programs written in FORTRAN</p><p><b>Program napisan u FORTRAN-u (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a program written in FORTRAN</p><p><b>grad, tvrđava, utvrda, utvrdu, tvrđa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fortified defensive structure [fort]</p><p><b>slučajan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having no cause or apparent cause [causeless, uncaused]</p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring by happy chance</p><p><b>slučajan (od &quot;fortuitous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by good fortune [as luck would have it, fortunately, luckily]</p><p><b>slučajnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of happening accidentally and by lucky chance</p><p><b>slučajnost, koincidencija, nesreća</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anything that happens suddenly or by chance without an apparent cause [accident, chance event, stroke]</p><p><b>(Rimska mitologija) boginja sreće i sreće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman mythology) the goddess of fortune and good luck</p><p><b>sretan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having unexpected good fortune</p><p><i>adj.</i> supremely favored [golden]</p><p><i>adj.</i> presaging good fortune [rosy]</p><p><b>na radost, na sreću</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by good fortune [as luck would have it, fortuitously, luckily]</p><p><b>bogatstvo, sreća, sudbine, slućajnost, vjerojatnost, zgoda, fortuna, kob, okolnosti, sudba, sudbina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unknown and unpredictable phenomenon that causes an event to result one way rather than another [chance, hazard, luck]</p><p><i>n.</i> a large amount of wealth or prosperity</p><p><i>n.</i> an unknown and unpredictable phenomenon that leads to a favorable outcome [luck]</p><p><i>n.</i> your overall circumstances or condition in life (including everything that happens to you) [circumstances, destiny, fate, lot, luck, portion]</p><p><b>kolač sreće, kolačić sudbine</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thin folded wafer containing a maxim on a slip of paper</p><p><b>Osoba koja traži bogatstvo kroz brak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who seeks wealth through marriage</p><p><b>gatara, vračara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who foretells your personal future [fortuneteller]</p><p><b>gatanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the art or gift of prophecy (or the pretense of prophecy) by supernatural means [divination, foretelling, soothsaying]</p><p><b>maleni rod grmova porijeklom iz južne Kine koji proizvodi mala jajnovitna voća slična narančama: uključuje kumquate (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of shrubs native to south China producing small ovoid fruits resembling oranges: includes kumquats [genus Fortunella]</p><p><b>Krsta s okruglim plodovima kumquata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub bearing round-fruited kumquats [marumi, marumi kumquat, round kumquat]</p><p><b>Šumovi s ovalnim plodovima kumquata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub bearing oval-fruited kumquats [nagami, nagami kumquat, oval kumquat]</p><p><b>vračara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who foretells your personal future [fortune teller]</p><p><b>praksa predviđanja budućnosti ljudi (obično za plaćanje) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of predicting people's futures (usually for payment)</p><p><b>četrdeset, četrdesetak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cardinal number that is the product of ten and four [40, XL]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being ten more than thirty [40, twoscore, xl]</p><p><b>dremuckanje, drijemanje, drijemež, kratko spavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sleeping for a short period of time (usually not in bed) [catnap, light sleep, nap, short sleep, snooze]</p><p><b>-Biti osam više od četrdeset. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being eight more than forty [48, xlviii]</p><p><b>redovni broj četrdeset osam u redoslijedu brojanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> the ordinal number of forty-eight in counting order [48th]</p><p><b>redovni broj četrdeset pet u redoslijedu brojanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> the ordinal number of forty-five in counting order [45th]</p><p><b>redovni broj od četrdeset jedan u redoslijedu brojanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> the ordinal number of forty-one in counting order [41st]</p><p><b>.45-kalibarski pištolj., biti pet više od četrdeset (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a .45-caliber pistol</p><p><i>adj.</i> being five more than forty [45, xlv]</p><p><b>Četiri više od četrdeset. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being four more than forty [44, xliv]</p><p><b>redovni broj četrdeset i četiri u redoslijedu brojanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> the ordinal number of forty-four in counting order [44th]</p><p><b>Da je devet više od četrdeset. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being nine more than forty [49, il]</p><p><b>kopač zlata u doba zlatne groznice, kopač zlata u Kaliforniji 1849.</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a miner who took part in the California gold rush in 1849</p><p><b>redovni broj četrdeset devet u redoslijedu brojanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> the ordinal number of forty-nine in counting order [49th]</p><p><b>-Biti jedan više od četrdeset. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being one more than forty [41, xli]</p><p><b>redovni broj od četrdeset i dva u redu brojanja (MT)</