ary]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in the fourth place [fourthly]</p><p><b>Savjet 869. godine koji je osudio Photiusa koji je postao patrijarh Konstantinopola bez odobrenja Vatikana, čime je ubrzano raskol između istočne i zapadne crkve (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the council in 869 that condemned Photius who had become the patriarch of Constantinople without approval from the Vatican, thereby precipitating the schism between the eastern and western churches [Constantinople]</p><p><b>jedan od dva lubanjna živca na obje strane koji kontroliraju gornje nagibne mišiće očiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of the two cranial nerves on either side that control the superior oblique muscles of the eyes [trochlear, trochlear nerve, trochlearis]</p><p><b>Četvrti križarski rat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Crusade from 1202 to 1204 that was diverted into a battle for Constantinople and failed to recapture Jerusalem</p><p><b>Četvrta ili najniža paluba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fourth or lowest deck [orlop, orlop deck]</p><p><b>vrijeme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fourth coordinate that is required (along with three spatial dimensions) to specify a physical event [time]</p><p><b>Pisanje pisama svom sinu (1694-1773) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> suave and witty English statesman remembered mostly for letters to his son (1694-1773) [Chesterfield, Philip Dormer Stanhope]</p><p><b>Engleski pisac i povjesničar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English writer and historian [Horace Walpole, Horatio Walpole, Walpole]</p><p><b>sedma sila</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the press, including journalists, newspaper writers, photographers</p><p><b>Lateranski vijeće 1215. godine je bio najvažniji vijeće srednjeg vijeka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Lateran Council in 1215 was the most important council of the Middle Ages</p><p><b>pravni praznik u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a legal holiday in the United States [Independence Day, July 4]</p><p><b>dvadeset pet posto, jedna četvrtina, četvrti dio, četvrtina</b></p><p><i>n.</i