na europska malina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the common European raspberry [European raspberry, Rubus idaeus, wild raspberry]</p><p><b>građa, kadar, konzola, lažirati, nosač, okosnica, okvir, podesiti, rebro, sačiniti, skelet, sklop, slaba građevna kategorija, uokviriti, uramiti, zamisliti, blok, brodsko rebro, filmska slika, figura, ljudsko tijelo, stas, tijelo, tjelesna građa, trup, inning, izmjena, kostur, systema skeletale, uokvirenje, uhvatiti u klopku, uhvatiti u zamku</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the framework for a pair of eyeglasses</p><p><i>n.</i> a single one of a series of still transparent pictures forming a cinema, television or video film</p><p><i>n.</i> alternative names for the body of a human being [anatomy, bod, build, chassis, figure, flesh, form, human body, material body, physical body, physique, shape, soma]</p><p><i>n.</i> (baseball) one of nine divisions of play during which each team has a turn at bat [inning]</p><p><i>n.</i> a single drawing in a comic strip</p><p><i>n.</i> an application that divides the user's display into two or more windows that can be scrolled independently</p><p><i>n.</i> a system of assumptions and standards that sanction behavior and give it meaning [frame of reference]</p><p><i>n.</i> the hard structure (bones and cartilages) that provides a frame for the body of an animal [skeletal system, skeleton, systema skeletale]</p><p><i>n.</i> the internal supporting structure that gives an artifact its shape [skeletal frame, skeleton, underframe]</p><p><i>n.</i> a structure supporting or containing something [framework]</p><p><i>n.</i> a framework that supports and protects a picture or a mirror [framing]</p><p><i>n.</i> one of the ten divisions into which bowling is divided</p><p><i>v.</i> enclose in or as if in a frame [border, frame in]</p><p><i>v.</i> enclose in a frame, as of a picture</p><p><i>v.</i> take or catch as if in a snare or trap [ensnare, entrap, set up]</p><p><i>v.</i> formulate in a particular style or language [c