<p><i>adv.</i> in a brotherly manner</p><p><b>druženja s drugima na bratski ili prijateljski način (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> associating with others in a brotherly or friendly way [fraternization]</p><p><b>biti u prijateljskoj vezi s nekim, kao s bratom, pogotovo s neprijateljem (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be on friendly terms with someone, as if with a brother, especially with an enemy [fraternize]</p><p><b>bratinstvo, bratstvo, studentsko udruženje određenoga koledža, udruženje studenata nekog koledža ili škole, udruga, udruženje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a social club for male undergraduates [frat]</p><p><i>n.</i> people engaged in a particular occupation [brotherhood, sodality]</p><p><b>kuća koja se koristi kao boravište poglavlja bratstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a house used as a residence by a chapter of a fraternity [chapterhouse, frat house]</p><p><b>druženja s drugima na bratski ili prijateljski način (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> associating with others in a brotherly or friendly way [fraternisation]</p><p><b>pobratimiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be on friendly terms with someone, as if with a brother, especially with an enemy [fraternise]</p><p><b>Osoba koja ubija svog brata ili sestru., Vatra koja povrijedi ili ubije saveznika, Ubojstvo tvog brata. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who murders their brother or sister</p><p><i>n.</i> fire that injures or kills an ally [friendly fire]</p><p><i>n.</i> the murder of your sibling</p><p><b>njemački naslov ili oblik adrese za odraslu ženu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a German courtesy title or form of address for an adult woman</p><p><b>obmana, prijevara, zloporaba, hohštapler, varalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intentional deception resulting in injury to another person</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who makes deceitful pretenses [fake, faker, imposter, impostor, pretender, pseud, pseudo, role player, sham, shammer]</p><p><i>n.</i> something intended to deceive [dupery, fraudulence, hoax, humbug, put-on]</p><p><b>stvarna prevara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> actual deceit [positive fraud]</p><p><b>prevara koja se pretpostavlja iz okolnosti iako onaj koji je počinio ne mora imati nikakvu zlu namjeru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fraud that is presumed from the circumstances although the one who commits it need not have had any evil intent</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u slučaju poduzetnika ne provodi izvršenje, u slučaju poduzetnika se može provesti izvršenje u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fraud that arises from a disparity between the instrument intended to be executed and the instrument actually executed</p><p><b>U slučaju prijevare koja je predmetom presude ili presude, osoba može se smatrati krivim ili krivim u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) Uredbe (EU) br. 1095/2012. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fraud which intentionally causes a person to execute an instrument or make an agreement or render a judgment</p><p><b>Izjava o podmuklom ili dvoličnom predstavljanju, kvaliteta da je prevarant, nešto namjerno za prevarenje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fraudulent or duplicitous representation [duplicity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being fraudulent [deceit]</p><p><i>n.</i> something intended to deceive [dupery, fraud, hoax, humbug, put-on]</p><p><b>neovlašten, nepošten, prijevarno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> intended to deceive [deceitful, fallacious]</p><p><b>Nezakonito poduzimanje (kao što su iznuđivanje ili prijevara ili trgovina drogom ili prostitucija) obavljeno u svrhu ostvarivanja profita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an illegal enterprise (such as extortion or fraud or drug peddling or prostitution) carried on for profit [illegitimate enterprise, racket]</p><p><b>neovlašten, nepošten, prijevarno (od &quot;fraudulent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a dishonest and fraudulent manner</p><p><b>bremenit, ispunjen, nakrcan, pun</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by distress</p><p><i>adj.</i> filled with or attended with [pregnant]</p><p><b>Njemački naslov ili naslov za neudatu ženu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a German courtesy title or form of address for an unmarried woman</p><p><b>Dvostruko travlje s bijelim cvijećem koje u vrućem vremenu emitira zapaljivu paru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian perennial herb with white flowers that emit flammable vapor in hot weather [Dictamnus alba, burning bush, dittany, gas plant]</p><p><b>Jasen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ash [genus Fraxinus]</p><p><b>s lištima svjetlozelene ili srebrne boje ispod i tvrdim smeđom drvenom bojom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spreading American ash with leaves pale green or silvery beneath and having hard brownish wood [white ash]</p><p><b>mali pepeo močvarnih područja jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small ash of swampy areas of southeastern United States [swamp ash]</p><p><b>Bjelokosica, s čestima i slijepom, s visokom visinom od oko 5 mm do 8 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby ash of southwestern United States having fragrant white flowers [flowering ash]</p><p><b>grmljav Kalifornijanski pepeo s blesavim bijelim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby California ash with showy off-white flowers [flowering ash]</p><p><b>Visoki pepeo Europe do Kavkaza s lištima blistavo tamno-zeleno iznad i blijedo dolino ispod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall ash of Europe to the Caucasus having leaves shiny dark-green above and pale downy beneath [European ash, common European ash]</p><p><b>drvo iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike koje daje tvrdo lagano drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> timber tree of western North America yielding hard light wood [Fraxinus oregona, Oregon ash]</p><p><b>intenzivno širenje sjevernoameričkog drveta s tamno smeđim teškim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vigorous spreading North American tree having dark brown heavy wood [basket ash, black ash, brown ash, hoop ash]</p><p><b>drvo iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike koje daje tvrdo lagano drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> timber tree of western North America yielding hard light wood [Fraxinus latifolia, Oregon ash]</p><p><b>crni jasen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> southern Mediterranean ash having fragrant white flowers in dense panicles and yielding manna [flowering ash, manna ash]</p><p><b>malo američko stablo s baršunastom grančicom i donjim površinama lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> smallish American tree with velvety branchlets and lower leaf surfaces [downy ash, red ash]</p><p><b>od vrste crvene pepela s blistavim granama i donjim površinama lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of red ash having glossy branchlets and lower leaf surfaces [green ash]</p><p><b>pepel centralnih i južnih Sjedinjenih Država s plavozeleno-zelenim lišće i tvrdim smeđim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ash of central and southern United States with bluish-green foliage and hard brown wood [blue ash]</p><p><b>nisko rastući pepeo Teksasa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing ash of Texas [mountain ash]</p><p><b>drvo iz središnje i jugoistočne Sjedinjene Države s dlakavim granama i natečenom podlogom debla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> timber tree of central and southeastern United States having hairy branchlets and a swollen trunk base [pumpkin ash]</p><p><b>mali grmovi u jugozapadnim Sjedinjenim Državama i sjeverozapadnom Meksiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrubby ash of southwestern United States and northwestern Mexico [Arizona ash]</p><p><b>bučna svađa, izlizati, kavga, pohabati se, grebati, grepsti, iskrzati, trljati, trti, žuljati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a noisy fight [affray, disturbance, ruffle]</p><p><i>v.</i> wear away by rubbing [frazzle]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause friction [chafe, fret, rub, scratch]</p><p><b>pohaban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> worn away or tattered along the edges</p><p><b>Engleski socijalni antropolog poznat po studijama primitivne religije i magije (1854-1941) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English social anthropologist noted for studies of primitive religion and magic (1854-1941) [James George Frazer, Sir James George Frazer]</p><p><b>dotrajalost, istrošenost, izlizati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of extreme exhaustion</p><p><i>v.</i> wear away by rubbing [fray]</p><p><i>v.</i> exhaust physically or emotionally</p><p><b>ćud, ćudljiv, fanatik, frik, frikač, hir, nakaza, prohtjev, freak, kreatura, monstrum, čudovište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person or animal that is markedly unusual or deformed [lusus naturae, monster, monstrosity]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is so ardently devoted to something that it resembles an addiction [addict, junkie, junky, nut]</p><p><i>v.</i> lose one's nerve [freak out, gross out]</p><p><b>preplašen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wild delusion (especially one induced by a hallucinogenic drug) [disorientation]</p><p><i>v.</i> lose one's nerve [freak, gross out]</p><p><b>otkačen, bizaran, ekscentričan, nekonvencionalan, čudan, šašav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> changeable [capricious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of a freak</p><p><i>adj.</i> conspicuously or grossly unconventional or unusual [bizarre, eccentric, flakey, flaky, freaky, gonzo, off-the-wall, outlandish, outre]</p><p><b>otkačen (od &quot;freakish&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> unpredictably [capriciously]</p><p><b>otkačen (od &quot;freakish&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marked strangeness as a consequence of being abnormal [abnormality]</p><p><b>bizaran, ekscentričan, nekonvencionalan, otkačen, čudan, šašav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> strange and somewhat frightening</p><p><i>adj.</i> conspicuously or grossly unconventional or unusual [bizarre, eccentric, flakey, flaky, freakish, gonzo, off-the-wall, outlandish, outre]</p><p><b>pjega, sunčana pjega, sunčane pjege</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small brownish spot (of the pigment melanin) on the skin [lentigo]</p><p><i>v.</i> become freckled</p><p><i>v.</i> mark with freckles</p><p><b>pjegav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or covered with or resembling freckles [lentiginose, lentiginous]</p><p><b>Američki plesač i filmski glumac poznat po svom originalnom i gracioznom stepu (1899-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States dancer and cinema actor noted for his original and graceful tap dancing (1899-1987) [Astaire]</p><p><b>Engleski astrofizičar i zagovornik teorije stabilnog stanja kosmologije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an English astrophysicist and advocate of the steady state theory of cosmology [Hoyle, Sir Fred Hoyle]</p><p><b>Frederick Sanger</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English biochemist who determined the sequence of amino acids in insulin and who invented a technique to determine the genetic sequence of an organism (born in 1918) [Frederick Sanger, Sanger]</p><p><b>Američki psiholog i vodeći zagovornik behaviorizma (1904-1990) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States psychologist and a leading proponent of behaviorism (1904-1990) [B. F. Skinner, Burrhus Frederic Skinner, Skinner]</p><p><b>Američki filmski redatelj (rođen u Austriji) (1907-1997) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States filmmaker (born in Austria) (1907-1997) [Zinnemann]</p><p><b>Korporacija ovlaštena Kongresom za pružanje sekundarnog tržišta za stambene hipoteke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a corporation authorized by Congress to provide a secondary market for residential mortgages [FHLMC, Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corporation]</p><p><b>Francuski skulptor poznat po stvaranju Kip slobode koji se nalazi u luci New Yorka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French sculptor best known for creating the Statue of Liberty now in New York harbor [Bartholdi]</p><p><b>Francuski skladatelj (rođen u Poljskoj) i pijanist romantične škole (1810-1849) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French composer (born in Poland) and pianist of the romantic school (1810-1849) [Chopin]</p><p><b>Američki štampač poznat po dizajniranju pisaca (1865-1947) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States printer noted for designing typefaces (1865-1947) [Frederic William Goudy, Goudy]</p><p><b>Američki štampač poznat po dizajniranju pisaca (1865-1947) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States printer noted for designing typefaces (1865-1947) [Frederic Goudy, Goudy]</p><p><b>Engleski povjesničar poznat po svojim radovima o povijesti engleskog prava (1850-1906) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English historian noted for his works on the history of English law (1850-1906) [Maitland]</p><p><b>Grad u sjevernom Marylandu zapadno od Baltimorea. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in northern Maryland to the west of Baltimore</p><p><b>Sveti rimski car od 1152. do 1190. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Holy Roman Emperor from 1152 to 1190 [Barbarossa, Frederick I]</p><p><b>Carl Lewis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States athlete who won gold medals at the Olympics for his skill in sprinting and jumping (born in 1961) [Carl Lewis, Lewis]</p><p><b>Američki slikar poznat po sjajnim bojama i odvažnom četkičkom radu (1859-1935) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States painter noted for brilliant colors and bold brushwork (1859-1935) [Childe Hassam, Hassam]</p><p><b>Engleski skladatelj orkestarskih djela (1862-1934) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English composer of orchestral works (1862-1934) [Delius]</p><p><b>Američki abolicionist koji je pobjegao iz ropstva i postao utjecajni pisac i predavač na Sjeveru (1817-1895) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States abolitionist who escaped from slavery and became an influential writer and lecturer in the North (1817-1895) [Douglass]</p><p><b>sin Fredericka Williama koji je 1701. postao prvi kralj Pruske (1657-1713.), Sveti rimski car od 1152. do 1190. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> son of Frederick William who in 1701 became the first king of Prussia (1657-1713)</p><p><i>n.</i> Holy Roman Emperor from 1152 to 1190 [Barbarossa, Frederick Barbarossa]</p><p><b>kralj Pruske od 1740. do 1786., Sveti rimski car koji je vodio Šesti križarski rat i krunisao se kraljem Jeruzalema (1194-1250) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of Prussia from 1740 to 1786 [Frederick the Great]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Holy Roman Emperor who led the Sixth Crusade and crowned himself king of Jerusalem (1194-1250) [Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II]</p><p><b>Američki povjesničar koji je naglasio ulogu zapadne granice u američkoj povijesti (1861-1951) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States historian who stressed the role of the western frontier in American history (1861-1951) [Turner]</p><p><b>Engleski filolog koji je prvi predložio Oxford English Dictionary (1825-1910) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English philologist who first proposed the Oxford English Dictionary (1825-1910) [Furnivall]</p><p><b>Američki pejzažni arhitekta, odgovoran za dizajn Central Parka u New Yorku (1822-1903) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States landscape architect primarily responsible for the design of Central Park in New York City (1822-1903) [Olmsted]</p><p><b>Američki skladatelj (rođen u Austriji) koji je surađivao s Lernerom na nekoliko mjuzikla (1901-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States composer (born in Austria) who collaborated with Lerner on several musicals (1901-1987) [Loewe]</p><p><b>Pravnik Sjedinjenih Država koji je bio glavni sudac Vrhovnog suda (1890-1953) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States jurist who served as chief justice of the Supreme Court (1890-1953) [Vinson]</p><p><b>Britanski državnik pod Georgeom III čije je politike dovele do pobune u američkim kolonijama (1732-1792) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British statesman under George III whose policies led to rebellion in the American colonies (1732-1792) [North, Second Earl of Guilford]</p><p><b>Frederick Sanger</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English biochemist who determined the sequence of amino acids in insulin and who invented a technique to determine the genetic sequence of an organism (born in 1918) [Fred Sanger, Sanger]</p><p><b>Frederick Soddy</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English chemist whose work on radioactive disintegration led to the discovery of isotopes (1877-1956) [Soddy]</p><p><b>kralj Pruske od 1740. do 1786. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of Prussia from 1740 to 1786 [Frederick II]</p><p><b>Kurčev Brandenburg koji je obnovio svoje područje nakon uništenja tijekom Tridesetogodišnjeg rata (1620-1688) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Elector of Brandenburg who rebuilt his domain after its destruction during the Thirty Years' War (1620-1688) [Great Elector]</p><p><b>sin Frederika I. koji je postao kralj Pruske 1713. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> son of Frederick I who became king of Prussia in 1713</p><p><b>Kralj Pruske koji se upleo u skup rat s Francuskom (1744-1797) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of Prussia who became involved in a costly war with France (1744-1797)</p><p><b>kralj Pruske koji se uplio u Napoleonove ratove (1770-1840) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of Prussia who became involved in the Napoleonic Wars (1770-1840)</p><p><b>Kralj Pruske koji je nasilno potisnuo demokratske pokrete (1795-1865) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of Prussia who violently suppressed democratic movements (1795-1865)</p><p><b>grad u sjeveroistočnoj Virginiji na rijeci Rappahannock, važna bitka u Američkom građanskom ratu (1862) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in northeastern Virginia on the Rappahannock River</p><p><i>n.</i> an important battle in the American Civil War (1862) [Battle of Fredericksburg]</p><p><b>Španjolski pjesnik i dramaturg kojeg su Francoovi vojnici ubili ubrzo nakon početka Španjolskog građanskog rata (1898-1936) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Spanish poet and dramatist who was shot dead by Franco's soldiers soon after the start of the Spanish Civil War (1898-1936) [Garcia Lorca, Lorca]</p><p><b>Glavni grad provincije New Brunswick (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the provincial capital of New Brunswick</p><p><b>besplatan, besplatno, drzak, gratis, nevezan, osloboditi, protočan, riješiti se, slobodan, nevezani, slobodna, slobodne, slobodni, slobodno, slobodnog, slobodnom, slobodom, povoljno, voljno, neograničen, izbaviti, izbaciti, izbacivati, maknuti, micati, oslobađati, sklanjati, skloniti, uklanjati, ukloniti, izuzeti, izuzimati, poštedjeti, pošteđivati, razdužiti, iskrčiti, krčiti, prokrčiti, raskrčiti, raščistiti, raščišćavati, napustiti, napuštati, odbaciti, odbacivati, odreći se, odricati se, odstupati, odstupiti, ostaviti, ostavljati, povlačiti se, povući se, prepustiti, prepuštati, ustupati, ustupiti, otpustiti, odmrzavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people who are free [free people]</p><p><i>v.</i> grant freedom to [liberate, loose, release, unloose, unloosen]</p><p><i>v.</i> relieve from [disembarrass, rid]</p><p><i>v.</i> remove or force out from a position [dislodge]</p><p><i>v.</i> grant relief or an exemption from a rule or requirement to [exempt, relieve]</p><p><i>v.</i> make (information) available for publication [release]</p><p><i>v.</i> free from obligations or duties [discharge]</p><p><i>v.</i> free or remove obstruction from [disengage]</p><p><i>v.</i> let off the hook [absolve]</p><p><i>v.</i> part with a possession or right [give up, release, relinquish, resign]</p><p><i>v.</i> release (gas or energy) as a result of a chemical reaction or physical decomposition [liberate, release]</p><p><i>v.</i> make (assets) available [release, unblock, unfreeze]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not limited or hampered</p><p><i>adj.</i> unconstrained or not chemically bound in a molecule or not fixed and capable of relatively unrestricted motion</p><p><i>adj.</i> costing nothing [complimentary, costless, gratis, gratuitous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not occupied or in use</p><p><i>adj.</i> not fixed in position [detached]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not held in servitude</p><p><i>adj.</i> not taken up by scheduled activities [spare]</p><p><i>adj.</i> completely wanting or lacking [barren, destitute, devoid, innocent]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not literal [liberal, loose]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without restraint [loose]</p><p><b>(sport) stanje profesionalnog sportaša koji slobodno pregovara o ugovoru za igranje za bilo koji tim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (sports) the state of a professional athlete who is free to negotiate a contract to play for any team</p><p><b>(sportski) profesionalni sportaš koji može potpisati ugovor za igranje u bilo kojem timu, netko koji djeluje slobodno ili čak neodgovorno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (sports) a professional athlete who is free to sign a contract to play for any team</p><p><i>n.</i> someone acting freely or even irresponsibly [free spirit, freewheeler]</p><p><b>proces razmišljanja u kojem ideje (riječi ili slike) sugeriraju druge ideje u nizu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thought process in which ideas (words or images) suggest other ideas in a sequence</p><p><b>(elektrskog luka) neprekidno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of an electric arc) continuous [sustained]</p><p><b>u kojima se jajne ćelije razvijaju na središnjem stupcu u složenom jajniku bez septe ili samo s septom na osnovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> where ovules develop on a central column in a compound ovary lacking septa or with septa at base only</p><p><b>Elektron koji nije vezan za atom ili ion ili molekul, ali se slobodno kreće pod utjecajem električnog polja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electron that is not attached to an atom or ion or molecule but is free to move under the influence of an electric field</p><p><b>(fizička) termodinamička veličina ekvivalentna sposobnosti fizičkog sustava za obavljanje posla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a thermodynamic quantity equivalent to the capacity of a physical system to do work [energy]</p><p><b>ekonomija koja se uglavnom oslanja na tržišne sile za raspodjelu dobara i resursa i određivanje cijena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economy that relies chiefly on market forces to allocate goods and resources and to determine prices [laissez-faire economy, market economy, private enterprise]</p><p><b>Idealni pokret pada nečega podložno samo gravitacijskom polju, iznenada naglo smanjenje neke količine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ideal falling motion of something subject only to a gravitational field</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden sharp decrease in some quantity [dip, drop, fall]</p><p><b>slobodni morfem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a morpheme that can occur alone [free morpheme]</p><p><b>Francuski pokret tijekom Drugog svjetskog rata koji je u Londonu organizirao Charles de Gaulle kako bi se borio za oslobođenje Francuske od njemačke kontrole i za obnovu republike. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a French movement during World War II that was organized in London by Charles de Gaulle to fight for the liberation of France from German control and for the restoration of the republic [Fighting French]</p><p><b>milost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Christian theology) the free and unmerited favor or beneficence of God [grace, grace of God]</p><p><b>ručni (rad)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> freedom to do as you see fit [blank check]</p><p><b>Pub koji nije pod kontrolom pivovarije i tako slobodno prodaje različite marke piva i piva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a public house that is not controlled by a brewery and so is free to sell different brands of beer and ale</p><p><b>slobodan udarac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (soccer) a place kick that is allowed for a foul or infringement by the other team</p><p><b>dobrovoljac, najamnik, nezavisan novinar, nezavisan pisac, plaćenik, slobodne profesije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a writer or artist who sells services to different employers without a long-term contract with any of them [free-lance, freelance, freelancer, independent, self-employed person]</p><p><b>popis robe koja nisu predmet tarifa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a list of commodities that are not subject to tariffs</p><p><b>slobodno živući</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lifestyle given to easy indulgence of the appetites</p><p><b>spolni odnos između osoba koje nisu u braku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sexual intercourse between individuals who are not married to one another [extramarital sex]</p><p><b>nešto što je stečeno bez napora ili plaćanja ili obveze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something acquired without effort or payment or obligation</p><p><b>slobodni morfem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a morpheme that can occur alone [free form]</p><p><b>mikroskopski osjetilni živčani završetci u koži koji nisu povezani s bilo kojim specifičnim osjetilnim receptorom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> microscopic sensory nerve endings in the skin that are not connected to any specific sensory receptor</p><p><b>besplatan, besplatno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without payment [for free, gratis]</p><p><b>amnestija, oprost, pomilovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the formal act of liberating someone [amnesty, pardon]</p><p><b>Ljudi koji su slobodni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> people who are free [free]</p><p><b>fagocit koji cirkuliše u krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a phagocyte that circulates in the blood</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, "priključkom" znači područje koje se nalazi u blizini luke u kojoj se roba namijenjena ponovnom otpremu može primiti i skladištiti bez plaćanja carina., U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (c) ovog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an area adjoining a port where goods that are intended for reshipment can be received and stored without payment of duties [free zone]</p><p><i>n.</i> a port open on equal terms to all commercial vessels</p><p><b>mediji koje nisu ograničene ili kontrolirane vladinom cenzurom u vezi s politikom ili ideologijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a press not restricted or controlled by government censorship regarding politics or ideology</p><p><b>slobodni radikal, slobodni radikali</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an atom or group of atoms with at least one unpaired electron [radical]</p><p><b>odriješene ruke, potpuna sloboda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the removal of constraints [play]</p><p><b>bivša politička stranka u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former political party in the United States</p><p><b>netko koji djeluje slobodno ili čak neodgovorno (MT)</b></p>