avilnika, proizvodnja se može provoditi na temelju postupaka utvrđenih u članku 6. stavku 1. točaka 1. točaka 2. točaka 2. točaka 3. i 3. točaka 3. i 3. točaka 3. i 3. točaka 3. i 4. točaka 3. i 4. točaka 3. i 4. točaka 3. i 4. toč (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any one or more chlorofluorocarbons (or related compounds) that are used as an aerosol propellant, organic solvent, or refrigerant</p><p><b>frekvencija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the number of occurrences within a given time period [frequency, oftenness]</p><p><b>frekvencija, frekvencijski, frekvencijsko, frekventan, učestalost, apsolutna frekvencija, čestotnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the number of occurrences within a given time period [frequence, oftenness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio of the number of observations in a statistical category to the total number of observations [relative frequency]</p><p><i>n.</i> the number of observations in a given statistical category [absolute frequency]</p><p><b>frekvencijski pojas, frekvencija, valna duljina, valna dužina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a band of adjacent radio frequencies (e.g., assigned for transmitting radio or television signals) [waveband]</p><p><b>distribucija frekvencija, frekvencijska raspodjela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a distribution of observed frequencies of occurrence of the values of a variable</p><p><b>frekvencijska modulacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> modulation of the frequency of the (radio) carrier wave [FM]</p><p><b>amplitudno frekvencijski odziv, frekvencijska karakteristika, frekvencijska svojstva, frekvencijski odziv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (electronics) a curve representing the output-to-input ratio of a transducer as a function of frequency</p><p><b>(elektronika) grafikon frekvencijskog odgovora s amplitudom signala ili dobitkom prikazanim u odnosu na frekvenciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (electronics) a graph of frequency response with signal amplitude or gain plotted against frequency [frequency-response curve]</p><p><b>(elektronika) grafikon frekvencijskog odgovora s amplitudom signala ili dobitkom prikazanim u odnosu na frekvenciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (electronics) a graph of frequency response with signal amplitude or gain plotted against frequency [frequency-response characteristic]</p><p><b>čest, frekventan, pohađati, učestalo, učestao, čestih, posjećivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> do one's shopping at [buy at, patronise, patronize, shop, shop at, sponsor]</p><p><i>v.</i> be a regular or frequent visitor to a certain place [haunt]</p><p><i>adj.</i> coming at short intervals or habitually</p><p><i>adj.</i> frequently encountered</p><p><b>Riječ je oblik glagola koji služi za izražavanje učestale ponavljanja neke radnje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a verb form that serves to express frequent repetition of an action</p><p><b>čest, frekventan, pohađati, učestalo, učestao, čestih (od &quot;frequent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a regular customer [patron]</p><p><b>česti, često, frekventno, učestalo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> many times at short intervals [oft, often, oftentimes, ofttimes]</p><p><b>freska</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mural done with watercolors on wet plaster</p><p><i>n.</i> a durable method of painting on a wall by using watercolors on wet plaster</p><p><i>v.</i> paint onto wet plaster on a wall</p><p><b>čist, neiskusan, neuvježban, nov, osvježiti, svjež, svježa, svježe, svježina, bezobrazan, drzak, nedavno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> recently made, produced, or harvested</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a cycle) beginning or occurring again</p><p><i>adj.</i> imparting vitality and energy [bracing, brisk, refreshful, refreshing, tonic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> original and of a kind not seen before [new, novel]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not canned or otherwise preserved</p><p><i>adj.</i> not containing or composed of salt water [sweet]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having recently calved and therefore able to give milk</p><p><i>adj.</i> with restored energy [invigorated, refreshed, reinvigorated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not soured or preserved [sweet, unfermented]</p><p><i>adj.</i> free from impurities [clean]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not yet used or soiled [unused]</p><p><i>adj.</i> improperly forward or bold [impertinent, impudent, overbold, sassy, saucy, smart, wise]</p><p><i>adv.</i> very recently [freshly, new, newly]</p><p><b>mahuna, svježa mahuna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> beans eaten before they are ripe as opposed to dried</p><p><b>vjetar s brzinom od 19 do 24 čvorova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wind moving 19-24 knots</p><p><b>svježa riba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soldiers who are regarded as expendable in the face of artillery fire [cannon fodder, fodder]</p><p><b>Hrana koja nije konzervirana konzerviranjem ili dehidracijom ili zamrzavanjem ili pušenjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> food that is not preserved by canning or dehydration or freezing or smoking [fresh foods]</p><p><b>Hrana koja nije konzervirana konzerviranjem ili dehidracijom ili zamrzavanjem ili pušenjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> food that is not preserved by canning or dehydration or freezing or smoking [fresh food]</p><p><b>vjetar 39-46 čvorova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wind moving 39-46 knots</p><p><b>Prilika za novi početak bez predrasuda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an opportunity to start over without prejudice [clean slate, tabula rasa]</p><p><b>slatka voda, svježa voda, slatkovodan, slatkovodne</b></p><p><i>n.</i> water that is not salty [freshwater]</p><p><b>nedavno se uklanjao (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> cut recently</p><p><b>osvježiti, osvježiti se, okrepljivati, okrijepiti, osvježavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make (to feel) fresh [refresh]</p><p><i>v.</i> become or make oneself fresh again [freshen up, refresh, refreshen]</p><p><i>v.</i> make fresh again [refresh, refreshen]</p><p><b>učiniti svjetlije i ljepše, postati ili se ponovno osvežiti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make brighter and prettier [refurbish, renovate]</p><p><i>v.</i> become or make oneself fresh again [freshen, refresh, refreshen]</p><p><b>osvježiti, osvježiti se (od &quot;freshen&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anything that freshens<