ctricity by oxidation of fuel (hydrogen and oxygen or zinc and air)</p><p><b>odnos broja pređenih kilometara prema broju spaljenih galona benzina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio of the number of miles traveled to the number of gallons of gasoline burned [gas mileage, gasoline mileage, mileage]</p><p><b>filtar u vodovodu goriva koji odvaja prašinu i čestice hrđe iz goriva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a filter in the fuel line that screens out dirt and rust particles from the fuel</p><p><b>U slučaju vozila s brzinom od 300 km/h, to znači da je brzina goriva u vozilu veća od 300 km/h. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an indicator of the amount of fuel remaining in a vehicle [fuel indicator]</p><p><b>U slučaju vozila s brzinom od 300 km/h, to znači da je brzina goriva u vozilu veća od 300 km/h. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an indicator of the amount of fuel remaining in a vehicle [fuel gauge]</p><p><b>mehanički sustav za ubrizgavanje atomiziranog goriva izravno u cilindre motora s unutarnjim sagorevanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mechanical system to inject atomized fuel directly into the cylinders of an internal-combustion engine [fuel injection system]</p><p><b>mehanički sustav za ubrizgavanje atomiziranog goriva izravno u cilindre motora s unutarnjim sagorevanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mechanical system to inject atomized fuel directly into the cylinders of an internal-combustion engine [fuel injection]</p><p><b>količina preostalih goriva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of fuel remaining</p><p><b>cijev koja prevozi benzin iz spremnika u benzinski motor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pipe that carries gasoline from a tank to a gasoline engine [gas line, petrol line]</p><p><b>loživo ulje, ložno ulje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a petroleum product used for fuel [heating oil]</p><p><b>odvojena spremnica goriva u zrakoplovu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a detachable container of fuel on an airplane [pod]</p><p><b>napajanje gorivom, dovod goriva, sistem za dovod goriva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> equipment in a motor vehicle or aircraft that delivers fuel to the engine</p><p><b>bomba koja koristi eksploziv gorivo-vazduh (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb that uses a fuel-air explosive [aerosol bomb, thermobaric bomb, vacuum bomb, volume-detonation bomb]</p><p><b>aerosol bomba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device consisting of a container of fuel and two explosive charges [FAE]</p><p><b>goriva, gorivo, ogrjev, trošak (od &quot;fuel&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> heated, driven, or produced by burning fuel</p><p><b>goriva, gorivo, ogrjev, trošak (od &quot;fuel&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of supplying or taking on fuel [refueling]</p><p><b>Meksički romanopisac (rođen 1928.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mexican novelist (born in 1928) [Carlos Fuentes]</p><p><b>moćna i bogata teroristička organizacija osnovana 1957. kao gerilska ruka kolumbijske komunističke stranke. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a powerful and wealthy terrorist organization formed in 1957 as the guerilla arm of the Colombian communist party [FARC, Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia]</p><p><b>nečistoća, pljesniv zadah, prašina, prljavština, zagušljiv zrak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (British informal) an airless smoky smelly atmosphere</p><p><b>kratkovječan, prolazan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lasting a very short time [ephemeral, passing, short-lived, transient, transitory]</p><p><b>kratkovječan, prolazan (od &quot;fugacious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lack of enduring qualities (used chiefly of plant parts) [fugacity]</p><p><b>tendencija plina da se širi ili izlazi iz zraka, nedostatku trajnog kvaliteta (uglavnom se koristi za dijelove biljaka) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tendency of a gas to expand or escape</p><p><i>n.</i> the lack of enduring qualities (used chiefly of plant parts) [fugaciousness]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili u stilu glazbene fuge (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or in the style of a musical fugue</p><p><b>u fugalnom stilu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a fugal style</p><p><b>Južnoafrički dramaturg čije su drame sadržavale rasne napetosti u Južnoj Africi tijekom apartheida (rođen 1932.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African playwright whose plays feature the racial tensions in South Africa during apartheid (born in 1932) [Athol Fugard]</p><p><b>(Britanski neformalni) slabo ventilirano (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (British informal) poorly ventilated</p><p><b>bjegunac, časovit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who flees from an uncongenial situation [fleer, runaway]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is sought by law officers [fugitive from justice]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lasting for a markedly brief time [fleeting, momentaneous, momentary]</p><p><b>netko koga traže policajci. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is sought by law officers [fugitive]</p><p><b>kolovođa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a leader and organizer and spokesman (especially a political leader)</p><p><b>nečistoća, pljesniv zadah, prašina, prljavština, zagušljiv zrak (od &quot;fug&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (slang) extremely ugly</p><p><b>bomba koja se nosi balonom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb carried by a balloon [balloon bomb]</p><p><b>Ribe su vrlo cenjene kao delikates u Japanu, ali vrlo opasne jer su koža i organi otrovni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blowfish highly prized as a delicacy in Japan but highly dangerous because the skin and organs are poisonous</p><p><b>fuga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dissociative disorder in which a person forgets who they are and leaves home to create a new life [psychogenic fugue]</p><p><i>n.</i> a dreamlike state of altered consciousness that may last for hours or days</p><p><i>n.</i> a musical form consisting of a theme repeated a fifth above or a fourth below its first statement</p><p><b>grmljavo japansko trešnje s blijedo ružičastim cvjetovima, ugasli vulkan u južnom središtu Honšua koji je najviši vrh u Japanu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby Japanese cherry tree having pale pink blossoms [Prunus incisa, fuji cherry]</p><p><i>n.</i> an extinct volcano in south central