omarima čije se ličinke hrane gljivicama ili raspadajućom vegetacijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> minute blackish gregarious flies destructive to mushrooms and seedlings [sciara, sciarid]</p><p><i>n.</i> mosquito-like insect whose larvae feed on fungi or decaying vegetation</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste goveđih žitarica, koje se upotrebljavaju u proizvodnji goveđih žitarica, primjenjuje se sljedeći popis: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the taxonomic kingdom including yeast, molds, smuts, mushrooms, and toadstools [Fungi, kingdom Fungi]</p><p><b>red gljiva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the order of fungi</p><p><b>koji liče na gljivice (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling fungi [fungoid]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog članka, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the stalk of a plant ovule or seed [funiculus]</p><p><b>uspinjača, žičan, žičana željeznica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a railway up the side of a mountain pulled by a moving cable and having counterbalancing ascending and descending cars [cable railway, funicular railway]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or operated by a cable</p><p><b>uspinjača, žičana željeznica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a railway up the side of a mountain pulled by a moving cable and having counterbalancing ascending and descending cars [cable railway, funicular]</p><p><b>upalu funikula (posebno upalu spermatične vrpce) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of a funiculus (especially an inflammation of the spermatic cord)</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog članka,, Svaka od nekoliko struktura tijela nalik na žicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the stalk of a plant ovule or seed [funicle]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several body structure resembling a cord</p><p><b>bojazan, kukavica, kukavičluk, strah, ustuknuti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of nervous depression [blue funk]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States biochemist (born in Poland) who showed that several diseases were caused by dietary deficiencies and who coined the term `vitamin' for the chemicals involved (1884-1967) [Casimir Funk]</p><p><i>n.</i> an earthy type of jazz combining it with blues and soul</p><p><i>v.</i> draw back, as with fear or pain [cringe, flinch, quail, recoil, shrink, squinch, wince]</p><p><b>dugout kao mjesto sigurnog povlačenja (kada je u funk) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dugout as a place of safe retreat (when in a funk)</p><p><b>robustni istočnoazijski višegodišnji biljni biljci s racemoznim cvijećem: lilije banane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> robust east Asian clump-forming perennial herbs having racemose flowers: plantain lilies [Hosta, genus Funka, genus Hosta]</p><p><b>jedna od mnogih obitelji ili podobitelji u koje neki sustavi klasifikacije podjeljuju Liliaceae, ali nisu široko prihvaćeni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of many families or subfamilies into which some classification systems subdivide the Liliaceae but not widely accepted [Hostaceae, family Funkaceae, family Hostaceae]</p><p><b>bojažljiv, kukavički, otkvačen, plašljiv, smrdljiv, strašljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> offensively malodorous [fetid, foetid, foul, foul-smelling, ill-scented, noisome, smelly, stinking]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of jazz) having the soulful feeling of early blues [low-down]</p><p><i>adj.</i> stylish and modern in an unconventional way</p><p><i>adj.</i> in a state of cowardly fright</p><p><b>brodski dimnjak, dimnjak, lijevak, ljevak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conical shape with a wider and a narrower opening at the two ends [funnel shape]</p><p><i>n.</i> a conically shaped utensil having a narrow tube at the small end</p><p><i>n.</i> (nautical) smokestack consisting of a shaft for ventilation or the passage of smoke (especially the smokestack of a ship)</p><p><i>v.</i> move or pour through a funnel</p><p><b>s masenim udubljenjem od oko 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conical shape with a wider and a narrower opening at the two ends [funnel]</p><p><b>mreža paukova u obliku lovora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a funnel-