ke flies that produce galls on plants [gall gnat, gallfly]</p><p><b>Obična višegodišnja biljka široko rasprostranjena u južnim i istočnim Sjedinjenim Državama s spušteni grumci ružičastih cvijeća i debelih bazalnih listova koji sugeriraju oblik lavlje noge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common perennial herb widely distributed in the southern and eastern United States having drooping clusters of pinkish flowers and thick basal leaves suggesting a lion's foot in shape [Nabalus serpentarius, Prenanthes serpentaria, lion's foot]</p><p><b>mala samohrana osa koja proizvodi žuč na hrastovima i drugim biljkama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small solitary wasp that produces galls on oaks and other plants [cynipid gall wasp, cynipid wasp, gallfly]</p><p><b>Stalnozelena šarena od istočne Sjeverne Amerike s dugoličnim kožnim listovima i malim crnim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen holly of eastern North America with oblong leathery leaves and small black berries [Ilex glabra, evergreen winterberry, gallberry, inkberry]</p><p><b>Neuromuskularni blokator (trgovinski naziv Flaxedil) koji se koristi kao mišićni relaksant pri primjeni anestezije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> neuromuscular blocking agent (trade name Flaxedil) used as a muscle relaxant in the administration of anesthesia [Flaxedil]</p><p><b>galantan, hrabar, otmjen, otmjen čovjek, udvarač, kicoš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who is much concerned with his dress and appearance [beau, clotheshorse, dandy, dude, fashion plate, fop, sheik, swell]</p><p><i>n.</i> a man who attends or escorts a woman [squire]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unflinching in battle or action</p><p><i>adj.</i> lively and spirited [dashing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or displaying great dignity or nobility [lofty, majestic, proud]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being attentive to women like an ideal knight [chivalrous, knightly]</p><p><b>Čisti pas koji je osvojio trostruku krunu 1930. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thoroughbred that won the triple crown in 1930</p><p><b>galantan, hrabar, o