alnost kao muškarac ili žena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> your identity as it is experienced with regard to your individuality as male or female</p><p><b>otvoreno izražavanje stavova koji drugima ukazuju na stepen vaše muškoće ili ženstvenosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the overt expression of attitudes that indicate to others the degree of your maleness or femaleness</p><p><b>gen, transdukcija gena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) a segment of DNA that is involved in producing a polypeptide chain [cistron, factor]</p><p><b>mikročip koji drži DNK sonde koje čine pola dvostruke spirale DNK i može prepoznati DNK iz uzoraka koji se testiraju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a microchip that holds DNA probes that form half of the DNA double helix and can recognize DNA from samples being tested [DNA chip]</p><p><b>vektor za isporuku gena u stanice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vector for delivering genes into cells [transducing vector]</p><p><b>ekspresija gena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> conversion of the information encoded in a gene first into messenger RNA and then to a protein</p><p><b>Plesarka iz Sjedinjenih Država koja je nastupila u mnogim glazbenim filmovima (1912-1996) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States dancer who performed in many musical films (1912-1996) [Eugene Curran Kelly, Kelly]</p><p><b>(genetika) osobine koje se nasljeđuju zajedno kao posljedica povezanosti njihovih gena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) traits that tend to be inherited together as a consequence of an association between their genes [linkage]</p><p><b>(genetika) mutacija uzrokovana intramolekularnom reorganizacijom gena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) a mutation due to an intramolecular reorganization of a gene [point mutation]</p><p><b>Američki golfista koji je prvi osvojio sva četiri glavna golf turnira (1902-1999) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States golfer who was first to win all four major golf tournaments (1902-1999) [Sarazen]</p><p><b>Američki boksač koji je osvojio svjetsko prvenstvo u teškoj kategoriji poraženjem Jacka Dempseya dva puta (1898-1978) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States prizefighter who won the world heavyweight championship by defeating Jack Dempsey twice (1898-1978) [James Joseph Tunney, Tunney]</p><p><b>genetičko inženjerstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the technology of preparing recombinant DNA in vitro by cutting up DNA molecules and splicing together fragments from more than one organism [genetic engineering, recombinant DNA technology]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s rodoslovom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to genealogy [genealogical]</p><p><b>rodoslovni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to genealogy [genealogic]</p><p><b>rodoslovni (od &quot;genealogical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a genealogical manner</p><p><b>stručnjak za genealogiju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert in genealogy</p><p><b>genalogija, genealogija, genealogiji, genologija, genealoško stablo, obiteljsko stablo, rodoslov, rodoslovlje, rodoslovno stablo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> successive generations of kin [family tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> the study or investigation of ancestry and family history</p><p><b>general, generalan, generalni, glavni, okvirni, općenit, općenito, opći, sveopći, njemački, opća, opće, općeg, prosječan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a general officer of the highest rank [full general]</p><p><i>n.</i> the head of a religious order or congregation [superior general]</p><p><i>n.</i> a fact about the whole (as opposed to particular)</p><p><i>v.</i> command as a general</p><p><i>adj.</i> applying to all or most members of a category or group</p><p><i>adj.</i> not specialized or limited to one class of things</p><p><i>adj.</i> prevailing among and common to the general public</p><p><i>adj.</i> affecting the entire body</p><p><i>adj.</i> somewhat indefinite</p><p><i>adj.</i> of worldwide scope or applicability [cosmopolitan, ecumenical, oecumenical, universal, world-wide, worldwide]</p><p><b>osoba ovlaštena za obavljanje svih vrsta poslovanja za glavnog rukovo