 idea or conclusion having general application [generalisation, generality]</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of formulating general concepts by abstracting common properties of instances [abstraction, generalisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) transfer of a response learned to one stimulus to a similar stimulus [generalisation, stimulus generalisation, stimulus generalization]</p><p><b>generalizirati, uopćiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> draw from specific cases for more general cases [extrapolate, generalise, infer]</p><p><i>v.</i> speak or write in generalities [generalise]</p><p><i>v.</i> cater to popular taste to make popular and present to the general public [generalise, popularise, popularize, vulgarise, vulgarize]</p><p><i>v.</i> become systemic and spread throughout the body [generalise]</p><p><b>generaliziran, generalizirani, opći, poopćeni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not biologically differentiated or adapted to a specific function or environment [generalised]</p><p><b>anksioznost koja se odlikuje hroničnom anksioznošću i simptomima kao što su napetost, znojenje, drhtanje, vrtoglavica ili razdražljivost itd. koja traje više od šest mjeseci. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anxiety disorder characterized by chronic free-floating anxiety and such symptoms as tension or sweating or trembling or lightheadedness or irritability etc that has lasted for more than six months [GAD, anxiety reaction]</p><p><b>generalizirana epilepsija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> epilepsy in which the attacks involve loss of consciousness and tonic spasms of the musculature followed by generalized jerking [epilepsia major, grand mal, grand mal epilepsy]</p><p><b>napad u kojem pacijent izgubi svijest i ima grčeve po cijelom tijelu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a seizure during which the patient becomes unconscious and has convulsions over the entire body [epilepsia major, grand mal]</p><p><b>najčešće, obični, obično, općenito, uglavnom, uobičajeno, uopće</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> usually [by and large, more often than not, 