p><i>n.</i> (mineralogy) a hollow rock or nodule with the cavity usually lined with crystals</p><p><b>geodetski, geodetska</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (mathematics) the shortest line between two points on a mathematically defined surface (as a straight line on a plane or an arc of a great circle on a sphere) [geodesic line]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or determined by geodesy [geodesical, geodetic]</p><p><b>geodetska kupola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lightweight dome constructed of interlocking polygons</p><p><b>(matematika) najkraća linija između dvije točke na matematički definiranoj površini (kao ravna linija na ravnini ili luk velikog kruga na kugli) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (mathematics) the shortest line between two points on a mathematically defined surface (as a straight line on a plane or an arc of a great circle on a sphere) [geodesic]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili određene geodezijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or determined by geodesy [geodesic, geodetic]</p><p><b>geodezija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of geology that studies the shape of the earth and the determination of the exact position of geographical points</p><p><b>geodetski, mjernički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or determined by geodesy [geodesic, geodesical]</p><p><b>Veliki jestivi školjka pronađen kopanje duboko u pješčano blato duž pacifičke obale Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large edible clam found burrowing deeply in sandy mud along the Pacific coast of North America</p><p><b>Engleski pjesnik, poznat kao autor Canterbury Tales (1340-1400) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English poet remembered as author of the Canterbury Tales (1340-1400) [Chaucer]</p><p><b>Velški kronikar koji je napisao izvještaj o kraljevima Britanije za koji se sada vjeruje da sadrži malo povijesnih činjenica, ali je izvor legende o Arturu (oko 1100-1154) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Welsh chronicler who wrote an account of the kings of Britain which is now believed to contain little historical fact but it is a source of the Arthurian legend (circa 1100-1154)</p><p><b>Uro od 10 g. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of shrubs or small trees of tropical and subtropical America [genus Geoffroea]</p><p><b>trnasti grm ili malo stablo uobičajeno u središnjoj Argentini s malim narandžastim ili žutim cvijećem s jestivim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thorny shrub or small tree common in central Argentina having small orange or yellow flowers followed by edible berries [chanal, chanar]</p><p><b>šuma od šuma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a holly shrub</p><p><b>obitelj gljiva iz reda Helotiales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of fungi belonging to the order Helotiales [family Geoglossaceae]</p><p><b>tip rod Geoglossaceae koji obuhvaća zemaljske jezike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Geoglossaceae comprising the earthtongues [genus Geoglossum]</p><p><b>geograf</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert on geography</p><p><b>geografske, geografski, zemljopisni, zemljopisnog</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the science of geography [geographical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> determined by geography [geographical]</p><p><b>geografsko područje, geografska regija, zemljopisna područje, zemljopisna regija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a demarcated area of the Earth [geographic region, geographical area, geographical region]</p><p><b>istraživanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> to travel for the purpose of discovery [exploration]</p><p><b>geografska točka, zemljopisna točka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a point on the surface of the Earth [geographical point]</p><p><b>geografska regija, geografsko područje, zemljopisna područje, zemljopisna regija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a demarcated area of the Earth [geographic area, geographical area, geographical region]</p><p><b>geografski, geografskom, zemljopisni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the science of geography [geographic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> determined by geography [geographic]</p><p><b>geografska regija, geografsko područje, zemljopisna područje, zemljopisna regija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a demarcated area of the Earth [geographic area, geographic region, geographical region]</p><p><b>zemljopisna oznaka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a name or sign used on certain products which corresponds to a specific geographical location or origin [GI]</p><p><b>bivša britanska jedinica za dužinu koja je jednaka 1.853.184 metara. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former British unit of length equivalent to 6,080 feet (1,853.184 meters) [Admiralty mile, mi, mile, naut mi, nautical mile]</p><p><b>geografska točka, zemljopisna točka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a point on the surface of the Earth [geographic point]</p><p><b>geografska regija, geografsko područje, zemljopisna područje, zemljopisna regija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a demarcated area of the Earth [geographic area, geographic region, geographical area]</p><p><b>geografska zona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the regions of the surface of the Earth loosely divided according to latitude or longitude [zone]</p><p><b>zemljopisno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to geography</p><p><b>geografske, geografski, zemljopisni, zemljopisnog (od &quot;geographic&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> study of the earth's surface [geography]</p><p><b>geografija, zemljopis, zemljopisa, zemljopisu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> study of the earth's surface [geographics]</p><p><b>geološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or based on geology [geological]</p><p><b>geološki proces</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (geology) a natural process whereby geological features are modified [geological process]</p><p><b>Geološka doba, geološko vrijeme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time of the physical formation and development of the earth (especially prior to human history) [geological time]</p><p><b>geološki, geološkom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or based on geology [geologic]</p><p><b>Upotreba kemijske analize za procjenu starosti geoloških uzoraka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> use of chemical analysis to estimate the age of geological specimens [dating]</