ly influenced the surrealists (1888-1978) [Chirico]</p><p><b>Talijanski slikar i povjesničar umjetnosti (1511-1574) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian painter and art historian (1511-1574) [Vasari]</p><p><b>Talijanski pjesnik koji se smatra nacionalnim pjesnikom moderne Italije (1835-1907) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian poet considered the national poet of modern Italy (1835-1907) [Carducci]</p><p><b>Florentinski slikar koji je napustio strog vizantijski stil i razvio više naturalistički stil (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Florentine painter who gave up the stiff Byzantine style and developed a more naturalistic style [Giotto di Bondone]</p><p><b>Florentinski slikar koji je napustio strog vizantijski stil i razvio više naturalistički stil (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Florentine painter who gave up the stiff Byzantine style and developed a more naturalistic style [Giotto]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1775. do 1799. koji je služio tijekom Francuske revolucije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1775 to 1799 who served during the French Revolution [Giannangelo Braschi, Pius VI]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1484. do 1492. poznat kao nepotist i napadnut od strane Savonarole zbog svoje svjetovnosti (1432-1492.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1484 to 1492 who was known as a nepotist and was attacked by Savonarola for his worldliness (1432-1492) [Innocent VIII]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1963. do 1978. koji je ublažio ograničenja na post i na međureligijske brakove (1897-1978) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1963 to 1978 who eased restrictions on fasting and on interfaith marriages (1897-1978) [Paul VI]</p><p><b>Talijanski slikar (1696-1770) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian painter (1696-1770) [Tiepolo]</p><p><b>Talijanski pjesnik (rođen u Francuskoj) (1313-1375) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian poet (born in France) (1313-1375) [Boccaccio]</p><p><b>John Cabot</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian explorer who led the English expedition in 1497 that discovered the mainland of North America and explored the coast from Nova Scotia to Newfoundland (ca. 1450-1498) [Cabot, John Cabot]</p><p><b>slikar iz florentinske škole (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> painter of the Florentine school [Cimabue]</p><p><b>Florentinski pomornik koji je istraživao istočnu obalu Sjeverne Amerike (oko 1485-1528) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Florentine navigator who explored the eastern coast of North America (circa 1485-1528) [Giovanni da Verrazzano, Verrazano, Verrazzano]</p><p><b>Florentinski pomornik koji je istraživao istočnu obalu Sjeverne Amerike (oko 1485-1528) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Florentine navigator who explored the eastern coast of North America (circa 1485-1528) [Giovanni da Verrazano, Verrazano, Verrazzano]</p><p><b>sin Lorenza de'Medicija i papa od 1513 do 1521. koji je ekskomunicirao Martina Luthera i koji je 1521. Henryju VIII. dodijelio titulu branioca vjere (1475-1521) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> son of Lorenzo de'Medici and pope from 1513 to 1521 who excommunicated Martin Luther and who in 1521 bestowed on Henry VIII the title of Defender of the Faith (1475-1521) [Leo X]</p><p><b>(Rimska katolička crkva) talijanski i rimokatolički redovnik koji je osnovao red franjevaca (1181-1226) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) an Italian and the Roman Catholic monk who founded the Franciscan order of friars (1181-1226) [Francis of Assisi, Saint Francis, Saint Francis of Assisi, St. Francis, St. Francis of Assisi]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1700. do 1721. koji je osudio jansenske ideje o papinskoj nepogrešivosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1700 to 1721 who condemned Jansenist ideas on papal infallibility [Clement XI]</p><p><b>talijanski avanturist koji je napisao živopisne izvještaje o svojim seksualnim susretima (1725-1798) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Italian adventurer who wrote vivid accounts of his sexual encounters (1725-1798) [Casanova, Casanova de Seingalt, Giovanni Jacopo Casanova de Seingalt]</p><p><b>talijanski avanturist koji je napisao živopisne izvještaje o svojim seksualnim susretima (1725-1798) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Italian adventurer who wrote vivid accounts of his sexual encounters (1725-1798) [Casanova, Casanova de Seingalt, Giovanni Jacopo Casanova]</p><p><b>Italijanski skulptor i arhitekt baroknog razdoblja u Italiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian sculptor and architect of the baroque period in Italy [Bernini]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1846. do 1878. koji je 1854. proglasio dogmu o Bezgrešnom začeću Djevice Marije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1846 to 1878 who in 1854 declared the dogma of the Immaculate Conception of the Virgin Mary [Giovanni Mastai-Ferretti, Pius IX]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1846. do 1878. koji je 1854. proglasio dogmu o Bezgrešnom začeću Djevice Marije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1846 to 1878 who in 1854 declared the dogma of the Immaculate Conception of the Virgin Mary [Giovanni Maria Mastai-Ferretti, Pius IX]</p><p><b>Talijanski skladatelj (1526-1594) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian composer (1526-1594) [Palestrina]</p><p><b>Italijanski papa od 1878. do 1903. koji je bio zainteresiran za napredak učenja i koji je otvorio tajne arhive Vatikana svim učenicima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1878 to 1903 who was interested in the advancement of learning and who opened the Vatican secret archives to all scholars [Gioacchino Pecci, Leo XIII]</p><p><b>Talijanski astronom koji je prvi primijetio linije (koje je nazvao kanalima) na površini Marsa (1835-1910) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian astronomer who first noted lines (which he called canals) on the surface of Mars (1835-1910) [Schiaparelli]</p><p><b>(ponekad uvredljivo) čin prevari ili prevare, (ponekad uvredljivo) prevariti ili prevariti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (sometimes offensive) an act of swindling or cheating [gyp]</p><p><i>v.</i> (sometimes offensive) to cheat or swindle [gyp]</p><p><b>Ciganin, Ciganka, ciganski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a laborer who moves from place to place as demanded by employment [gypsy, itinerant]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a people with dark skin and hair who speak Romany and who traditionally live by seasonal work and fortunetelling [Bohemian, Gypsy, Roma, Romani, Romany, Rommany]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who resembles a Gypsy in leading an unconventional, nomadic way of life [gypsy]</p><p><b>Europski molj u Sjevernoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European moth introduced into North America [Lymantria dispar, gypsy moth]</p><p><b>dlakava evroazijska biljka s bijelim cvjetovima s dvije usne (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hairy Eurasian herb with two-lipped white flowers [Lycopus europaeus, gypsywort]</p><p><b>rod Giraffa, rod žirafa, žirafe</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Giraffidae [genus Giraffa]</p><p><b>najviši živi četvorokrvac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tallest living quadruped [camelopard, giraffe]</p><p><b>žirafa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tallest living quadruped [Giraffa camelopardalis, camelopard]</p><p><b>Giraffidae, porodica Giraffidae, porodica žirafa, žirafe</b></p><p><i>n.</i> giraffes [family Giraffidae]</p><p><b>ukrasan nosilac svijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ornate candle holder [girandole]</p><p><b>svijećnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ornate candle holder [girandola]</p><p><b>Finansijer Sjedinjenih Država (rođen u Francuskoj) koji je pomogao u financiranju rata 1812. (1750-1831) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States financier (born in France) who helped finance the War of 1812 (1750-1831) [Stephen Girard]</p><p><b>vatreni opal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an opal with flaming orange and yellow and red colors [fire opal]</p><p><i>n.</i> tall perennial with hairy stems and leaves [Helianthus tuberosus, Jerusalem artichoke, Jerusalem artichoke sunflower]</p><p><b>Francuski romanopisac i dramski pisac čije su drame bile reinterpretacije grčkih mitova (1882-1944) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French novelist and dramatist whose plays were reinterpretations of Greek myths (1882-1944) [Hippolyte Jean Giraudoux, Jean Giraudoux]</p><p><b>bockati, opasati, opasivati, podsmijeh, podsmijevati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> prepare oneself for a military confrontation [arm, build up, fortify]</p><p><i>v.</i> put a girdle on or around [girdle]</p><p><i>v.</i> bind with something round or circular [encircle]</p><p><b>greda, gredni, grednih, nosač, poduljni nosač, podvlaka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a beam made usually of steel</p><p><b>kaiš, opasač, pojas, korzet, steznik, opasati, opasivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an encircling or ringlike structure</p><p><i>n.</i> a band of material around the waist that strengthens a skirt or trousers [cincture, sash, waistband, waistcloth]</p><p><i>n.</i> a woman's close-fitting foundation garment [corset, stays]</p><p><i>v.</i> cut a girdle around so as to kill by interrupting the circulation of water and nutrients [deaden]</p><p><i>v.</i> put a girdle on or around [gird]</p><p><b>Bantu jezik koji se govori u obalnim područjima istočne Kenije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Bantu language spoken in the coastal regions of eastern Kenya</p><p><b>cura, djevojčica, djevojka, djevojci, djevojke, djevojku, curica, kćer, kćerka, kći</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a young female [fille, miss, missy, young lady, young woman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a youthful female person [female child, little girl]</p><p><i>n.</i> a female human offspring [daughter]</p><p><i>n.</i> a girl or young woman with whom a man is romantically involved [girlfriend, lady friend]</p><p><i>n.</i> a friendly informal reference to a grown woman</p><p><b>pomoćnica koja ima niz dužnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a female assistant who has a range of duties</p><p><b>Djevojka koja je član izviđačke grupe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a girl who is a member of the Girl Scouts</p><p><b>organizacija mladih žena i djevojaka osnovana 1912. godine za razvoj karaktera i osposobljavanje za građanstvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organization of young women and girls founded in 1912 for character development and citizenship training</p><p><b>Izuzetno talentirana mlada žena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extremely talented young female person</p><p><b>djevojka, prijateljica, prijteljica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any female friend</p><p><i>n.</i> a girl or young woman with whom a man is romantically involved [girl, lady friend]</p><p><b>djetinjstvo djevojčice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the childhood of a girl [maidenhood, maidhood]</p><p><b>djevojački</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> befitting or characteristic of a young girl [schoolgirlish]</p><p><b>djevojački (od &quot;girlish&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> like a girl</p><p><b>djevojački (od &quot;girlish&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> being characteristic of a girl</p><p><b>ček koji britanska vlada daje nekome tko je nezaposlen, Britanski financijski sustav u kojem banka ili pošta prenose novac s jednog računa na drugi kada dobiju odobrenje za to. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a check given by the British government to someone who is unemployed [giro cheque]</p><p><i>n.</i> a British financial system in which a bank or a post office transfers money from one account to another when they receive authorization to do so</p><p><b>Račun u pošti koji se može koristiti na sličan način kao i račun u banci. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an account at a post office that can be used in similar ways to an account at a bank</p><p><b>ček koji britanska vlada daje nekome tko je nezaposlen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a check given by the British government to someone who is unemployed [giro]</p><p><b>Talijanski religiozni i politički reformator (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian religious and political reformer [Savonarola]</p><p><b>Francuska umjerena politička stranka koja je bila na vlasti (1791-1793) tijekom Francuske revolucije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the French moderate political party that was in power (1791-1793) during the French Revolution</p><p><b>Član umjerene republikanske stranke koja je bila na vlasti tijekom Francuske revolucije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the moderate republican party that was in power during the French Revolution [Girondist]</p><p><b>doktrinu Girondista. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine of the Girondists</p><p><b>Član umjerene republikanske stranke koja je bila na vlasti tijekom Francuske revolucije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the moderate republican party that was in power during the French Revolution [Girondin]</p><p><b>babilonski bog vatre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Babylonian god of fire</p><p><b>kolan, obim, opasati (konja) kolanom, opseg</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the distance around a person's body</p><p><i>n.</i> stable gear consisting of a band around a horse's belly that holds the saddle in place [cinch]</p><p><i>v.</i> tie a cinch around [cinch]</p><p><b>Američka filmska glumica koja se pojavila u filmovima D. W. Griffitha (1896-1993) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film actress who appeared in films by D. W. Griffith (1896-1993) [Lillian Gish]</p><p><b>stvarčica, aparat, izum, naprava, sprava, spraveica, spravica, sredstvo, uređaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something unspecified whose name is either forgotten or not known [doodad, doohickey, doojigger, gimmick, gizmo, gubbins, thingamabob, thingamajig, thingmabob, thingmajig, thingumabob, thingumajig, thingummy, whatchamacallit, whatchamacallum, whatsis, widget]</p><p><i>n.</i> a device or control that is very useful for a particular job [appliance, contraption, contrivance, convenience, gadget, gizmo, widget]</p><p><b>bit, suština, centar, esencija, jezgra, središte, srž</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the central meaning or theme of a speech or literary work [burden, core, effect, essence]</p><p><i>n.</i> the choicest or most essential or most vital part of some idea or experience [center, centre, core, essence, heart, heart and soul, inwardness, kernel, marrow, meat, nitty-gritty, nub, pith, substance, sum]</p><p><b>osoba koja se smatra prezirnom ili prezirnom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is deemed to be despicable or co