f news or promises etc.</p><p><i>n.</i> disposing of property by voluntary transfer without receiving value in return</p><p><i>adj.</i> given or giving freely [big, bighearted, bounteous, bountiful, freehanded, handsome, liberal, openhanded]</p><p><b>porađanje, porođaj, porod, rađanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of giving birth [birth, birthing, parturition]</p><p><b>Upravljanje lijekovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of administering medication [administration]</p><p><b>verbalni čin priznavanja poraza, čin odricanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a verbal act of admitting defeat [surrender, yielding]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of forsaking [forsaking]</p><p><b>drevni egipatski grad na zapadnoj obali Nila nasuprot Kaira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Egyptian city on the west bank of the Nile opposite Cairo [El Giza, Gizeh]</p><p><b>drevni egipatski grad na zapadnoj obali Nila nasuprot Kaira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Egyptian city on the west bank of the Nile opposite Cairo [El Giza, Giza]</p><p><b>stvarčica, aparat, izum, naprava, sprava, spraveica, spravica, sredstvo, uređaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something unspecified whose name is either forgotten or not known [doodad, doohickey, doojigger, gimmick, gismo, gubbins, thingamabob, thingamajig, thingmabob, thingmajig, thingumabob, thingumajig, thingummy, whatchamacallit, whatchamacallum, whatsis, widget]</p><p><i>n.</i> a device or control that is very useful for a particular job [appliance, contraption, contrivance, convenience, gadget, gismo, widget]</p><p><b>želudac, želudac (ptice)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thick-walled muscular pouch below the crop in many birds and reptiles for grinding food [gastric mill, ventriculus]</p><p><b>Danski romanopisac (1857-1919) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Danish novelist (1857-1919) [Karl Gjellerup]</p><p><b>glatko izbočenje čelne kosti između i iznad obrva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a smooth prominence of the frontal bone between and above the eyebrows [mesophyron]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s glabelom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the glabella</p><p><b>bez dlaka ili sličan rast ili sklonost do bezdlaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking hair or a similar growth or tending to become hairless</p><p><b>s masom od 0,15 g/m2 ili većom od 0,15 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having no hair or similar growth</p><p><b>(uglavnom za voće) konzervirano premazanjem šećerom ili omogućavanjem apsorpcije šećera (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used especially of fruits) preserved by coating with or allowing to absorb sugar [candied, crystalised, crystalized]</p><p><b>glečerski, ledenjakov</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or derived from a glacier</p><p><i>adj.</i> devoid of warmth and cordiality [frigid, frosty, frozen, icy, wintry]</p><p><i>adj.</i> extremely cold [arctic, frigid, gelid, icy, polar]</p><p><b>kamen koji je odnesen glečera na mjesto daleko od svog porijekla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a boulder that has been carried by a glacier to a place far distant from its place of origin</p><p><b>bilo koji vremenski period u kojem su glečeri prekrivali veliki dio površine Zemlje, od prije dva milijuna do prije 11 tisuća godina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any period of time during which glaciers covered a large part of the earth's surface [glacial period, ice age]</p><p><i>n.</i> from two million to 11 thousand years ago [Pleistocene, Pleistocene epoch]</p><p><b>bilo koji vremenski period u kojem su glečeri prekrivali veliki dio površine Zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any period of time during which glaciers covered a large part of the earth's surface [glacial epoch, ice age]</p><p><b>glečerski, ledenjakov (od &quot;glacial&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by a glacier</p><p><b>pokriven ledom ili snijegom ili glečera, Postaju zamrznute i prekrivene glečerima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cover with ice or snow or a glacier</p><p><i>v.</i> become frozen and covered with glaciers</p><p><b>pokrivena ledom (kao glečer) ili pod utjecajem glečera (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with ice (as by a glacier) or affected by glacial action</p><p><b>glacijacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of being covered with glaciers or masses of ice</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of covering the earth with glaciers or masses of ice</p><p><b>glečer, ledenjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slowly moving mass of ice</p><p><b>crvena violeta s žutim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dogtooth violet of western North America having bright yellow flowers [Erythronium grandiflorum, snow lily]</p><p><b>prolaz kroz koji voda iz superglacija ulazi u glečer, izbušavajući ili do temelja stijene ili do dubine zajedničke šljune (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chute through which supraglacial water enters a glacier, boring either to the bedrock or to the depth of common crevasse formation [moulin]</p><p><b>biti veseo, obradovati, radostan, razdragan, sretan, veseo, zadovoljan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous plants of the genus Gladiolus native chiefly to tropical and South Africa having sword-shaped leaves and one-sided spikes of brightly colored funnel-shaped flowers [gladiola, gladiolus, sword lily]</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing or causing joy and pleasure</p><p><i>adj.</i> eagerly disposed to act or to be of service [happy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> feeling happy appreciation</p><p><i>adj.</i> cheerful and bright [beaming]</p><p><b>Toplo dobrodošlicu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a warm welcome</p><p><b>razveseliti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make glad or happy [joy]</p><p><i>v.</i> become glad or happy</p><p><b>razveseliti (od &quot;gladden&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made joyful [exhilarated]</p><p><b>Iris s ljubičastim cvijećem i smrdljivim lišćama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> iris with purple flowers and foul-smelling leaves [Iris foetidissima, gladdon iris, roast beef plant, stinking gladwyn, stinking iris]</p><p><b>Iris s ljubičastim cvijećem i smrdljivim lišćama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> iris with purple flowers and foul-smelling leaves [Iris foetidissima, gladdon, roast beef plant, stinking gladwyn, stinking iris]</p><p><b>proplanak, čistina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tract of land with few or no trees in the middle of a wooded area [clearing]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički paprikac sa uskim listovima na žutožutožutih stabljika lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American fern with narrow fronds on yellowish leafstalks [Athyrium pycnocarpon, Diplazium pycnocarpon, narrow-leaved spleenwort, silvery spleenwort]</p><p><b>Visoka gruba američka biljka s palmatnim lišćama i brojnim malim bijelim dvostrukocnim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall coarse American herb having palmate leaves and numerous small white dioecious flowers [Napaea dioica]</p><p><b>doživljavanje radosti i zadovoljstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> experiencing joy and pleasure [gladness, gladsomeness]</p><p><b>gladijator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (ancient Rome) a professional combatant or a captive who entertained the public by engaging in mortal combat</p><p><i>n.</i> a professional boxer [prizefighter]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili nalik gladijatorima ili njihovom borbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or resembling gladiators or their combat</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih biljaka iz roda Gladiolus, izvorno iz tropske i južnoafričke regije, s lištima u obliku mača i jednostranim šiljcima s svijetle boje cvjetova u obliku lovora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous plants of the genus Gladiolus native chiefly to tropical and South Africa having sword-shaped leaves and one-sided spikes of brightly colored funnel-shaped flowers [glad, gladiolus, sword lily]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih biljaka iz roda Gladiolus, izvorno iz tropske i južnoafričke regije, s lištima u obliku mača i jednostranim šiljcima s svijetle boje cvjetova u obliku lovora, Veliki središnji dio prsne kosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous plants of the genus Gladiolus native chiefly to tropical and South Africa having sword-shaped leaves and one-sided spikes of brightly colored funnel-shaped flowers