t accomplished little or nothing (1883-1970) [Reuben Lucius Goldberg, Rube Goldberg]</p><p><b>zgubidan, varati, zabušavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soldier who performs his duties without proper care or effort</p><p><i>n.</i> an idle worthless person [good-for-naught, good-for-nothing, goof-off, ne'er-do-well, no-account]</p><p><i>n.</i> a brick-shaped block that looks like gold but is not</p><p><i>n.</i> anything that is supposed to be valuable but turns out to be worthless</p><p><i>v.</i> deprive of by deceit [bunco, con, defraud, diddle, hornswoggle, mulct, nobble, rook, scam, short-change, swindle, victimize]</p><p><i>v.</i> avoid (one's assigned duties) [fiddle, shirk, shrink from]</p><p><b>zgubidan (od &quot;goldbrick&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the evasion of work or duty [goofing off, shirking, slacking, soldiering]</p><p><b>običan kraljić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European kinglet with a black-bordered yellow crown patch [Regulus regulus, golden-crested kinglet]</p><p><b>bilo koje od različitih biljaka rodova Ranunculus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Ranunculus [butter-flower, buttercup, butterflower, crowfoot, kingcup]</p><p><b>zlatan, zlatna sredina, zlatna svadba, zlatni, zlatne, zlatno, zlatnu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the deep slightly brownish color of gold [aureate, gilded, gilt, gold]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by peace and prosperity [halcyon, prosperous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> made from or covered with gold [gilded, gold]</p><p><i>adj.</i> supremely favored [fortunate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> suggestive of gold</p><p><i>adj.</i> presaging or likely to bring good luck or a good outcome [favorable, favourable, lucky, prosperous]</p><p><b>razdoblje kada je neka aktivnost ili vještina bila na vrhuncu, bilo koji period (ponekad zamišljen) velikog mira i blagostanja i sreće, (klasična mitologija) prvo i najbolje doba svijeta, vrijeme idealne sreće, prosperiteta i nevinosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a time period when some activity or skill was a