ual [gentleness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being gradual or of coming about by gradual stages [graduality]</p><p><b>apsolvent, apsolvirati, diplomiran, diplomirani student, diplomirati, obilježiti, završiti, alumnus, diplomac, baždariti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who has received a degree from a school (high school or college or university) [alum, alumna, alumnus, grad]</p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument for measuring fluid volume</p><p><i>v.</i> receive an academic degree upon completion of one's studies</p><p><i>v.</i> confer an academic degree upon</p><p><i>v.</i> make fine adjustments or divide into marked intervals for optimal measuring [calibrate, fine-tune]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to studies beyond a bachelor's degree [postgraduate]</p><p><b>osoba koja je završila studij (uključujući bolničku praksu) u školi za obuku medicinskih sestara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who has completed the course of study (including hospital practice) at a nurses training school [trained nurse]</p><p><b>škola na sveučilištu koja nudi studije koje vode do stupnjeva izvan diplome. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school in a university offering study leading to degrees beyond the bachelor's degree [grad school]</p><p><b>student koji nastavlja studije nakon diplomiranja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a student who continues studies after graduation [grad student, postgraduate]</p><p><b>diplomiran, razvrstano</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked with or divided into degrees [calibrated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> taking place by degrees [gradational, gradatory]</p><p><b>cilindrični diplomirani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cylindrical graduate</p><p><b>ljestvica, mjerna ljestvica, mjerna skala, skala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ordered reference standard [ordered series, scale, scale of measurement]</p><p><b>Svaka porezna obveza koja se primjenjuje na određene vrste proizvoda ili usluga. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any tax in which the rate increases as the amount subject to taxation increases [progressive tax]</p><p><b>Tijelo studenata koji su diplomirali zajedno ove godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of students who graduate together this year</p><p><b>diplomiranje, graduacija, izglađivanje, diplomski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the successful completion of a program of study</p><p><i>n.</i> an academic exercise in which diplomas are conferred [commencement, commencement ceremony, commencement exercise, graduation exercise]</p><p><i>n.</i> a line (as on a vessel or ruler) that marks a measurement</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of arranging in grades [gradation]</p><p><b>akademski rad u kojem se dodjeljuju diplome (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an academic exercise in which diplomas are conferred [commencement, commencement ceremony, commencement exercise, graduation]</p><p><b>od ili koje se odnose na ili karakteristične za drevne Grke i Rimljane, posebno njihovu umjetnost, književnost ili kulturu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or characteristic of the ancient Greeks and Romans, especially their art, literature, or culture [Greco-Roman, classical]</p><p><b>Bogotvo iz klasične mitologije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deity of classical mythology [Greco-Roman deity]</p><p><b>Obožavatelj Grčke i svega što je grčko., karakterizira ljubav prema Grčkoj i grčkim stvarima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an admirer of Greece and everything Greek [philhellene, philhellenist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by a love of Greece and Grecian things [Graecophilic, philhellene, philhellenic]</p><p><b>karakterizira ljubav prema Grčkoj i grčkim stvarima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by a love of Greece and Grecian things [Graecophile, philhellene, philhellenic]</p><p><b>Njemačka tenisačica koja je osvojila sedam ženskih singlova na Wimbledonu (rođena 1969.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German tennis player who won seven women's singles titles at Wimbledon (born in 1969) [Steffi Graf, Stephanie Graf]</p><p><b>cepelin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large rigid dirigible designed to carry passengers or bombs [zeppelin]</p><p><b>grafiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rude decoration inscribed on rocks or walls [graffito]</p><p><b>Neprijatno ukrasno ukrasno grafičko delo na stijeni ili zidu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rude decoration inscribed on rocks or walls [graffiti]</p><p><b>cijepika, izdanak, kalem, kalemljenje, mladica, presadak, presaditi, ucjena, ucjenjivati, podmićivanje, cijepiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (surgery) tissue or organ transplanted from a donor to a recipient [transplant]</p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of offering something (usually money) in order to gain an illicit advantage [bribery]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of grafting something onto something else [grafting]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to grow together parts from different plants [engraft, ingraft]</p><p><i>v.</i> place the organ of a donor into the body of a recipient [transplant]</p><p><b>cijepika, izdanak, kalem, kalemljenje, mladica, presadak, presaditi, ucjena, ucjenjivati (od &quot;graft&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of grafting something onto something else [graft]</p><p><b>Američki evanđeo-propovjednik poznat kao masovni evanđelista (rođen 1918.), Američki plesač i koreograf čiji je rad bio poznat po svojoj strogosti i tehničkoj strogosti (1893-1991), U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvod se može upotrebljavati za proizvodnju sirovina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States evangelical preacher famous as a mass evangelist (born in 1918) [Billy Graham, William Franklin Graham]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States dancer and choreographer whose work was noted for its austerity and technical rigor (1893-1991) [Martha Graham]</p><p><i>n.</i> flour made by grinding the entire wheat berry including the bran [graham flour, whole meal flour, whole wheat flour]</p><p><b>Hleb od brašna od pšenice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bread made of graham (whole wheat) flour</p><p><b>poluslatki kreker od cjelovite pšenice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> semisweet whole-wheat cracker</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvod se može upotrebljavati za proizvodnju sirovina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flour made by grinding the entire wheat berry including the bran [graham, whole meal flour, whole wheat flour]</p><p><b>Engleski romanopisac i katoličar (1904-1991) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English novelist and Catholic (1904-1991) [Greene, Henry Graham Greene]</p><p><b>Engleski pisac (rođen u Škotskoj) dječjih priča (1859-1932) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English writer (born in Scotland) of children's stories (1859-1932) [Kenneth Grahame]</p><p><b>gral, sveti gral</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the object of any prolonged endeavor</p><p><i>n.</i> (legend) chalice used by Christ at the Last Supper [Holy Grail, Sangraal]</p><p><b>zrnatost, zrno, žitni, žito, zrna, žitnih, zrnce, žitarica, žitarice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relatively small granular particle of a substance</p><p><i>n.</i> foodstuff prepared from the starchy grains of cereal grasses [cereal, food grain]</p><p><i>n.</i> the side of leather from which the hair has been removed</p><p><i>n.</i> a weight unit used for pearls or diamonds: 50 mg or 1/4 carat [metric grain]</p><p><i>n.</i> 1/60 dram</p><p><i>n.</i> 1/7000 pound</p><p><i>n.</i> dry seed-like fruit produced by the cereal grasses: e.g. wheat, barley, Indian corn [caryopsis]</p><p><i>n.</i> a cereal grass</p><p><i>n.</i> the smallest possible unit of anything</p><p><i>n.</i> the direction, texture, or pattern of fibers found in wood or leather or stone or in a woven fabric</p><p><i>n.</i> the physical composition of something (especially with respect to the size and shape of the small constituents of a substance) [texture]</p><p><i>v.</i> thoroughly work in [ingrain]</p><p><i>v.</i> paint (a surface) to make it look like stone or wood</p><p><i>v.</i> form into grains [granulate]</p><p><i>v.</i> become granular [granulate]</p><p><b>u fer