e night (as midnight to 8 a.m.) [night shift]</p><p><b>Noćna straža (od ponoći do 8 ujutro) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a watch during the night (as from midnight to 8 a.m.) [middle watch, midwatch, night watch]</p><p><b>trudna</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in an advanced stage of pregnancy [big, enceinte, expectant, great, heavy, large, with child]</p><p><b>broj trudnoća koje je žena u, trudnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the number of the pregnancy that a woman is in</p><p><i>n.</i> a pregnant woman</p><p><b>(obstetrika) žena koja je trudna po prvi put (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (obstetrics) a woman who is pregnant for the first time [primigravida]</p><p><b>žena koja je po drugi put trudna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman who is pregnant for the second time [secundigravida]</p><p><b>žena koja je trudna treći put (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman who is pregnant for the third time [tertigravida]</p><p><b>tehnički termini za trudnoću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> technical terms for pregnancy [gravidity, gravidness]</p><p><b>tehnički termini za trudnoću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> technical terms for pregnancy [gravidation, gravidness]</p><p><b>trudna (od &quot;gravid&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> technical terms for pregnancy [gravidation, gravidity]</p><p><b>gravimetar, areometar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument for determining the specific gravity of a liquid or solid [hydrometer]</p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument for measuring variations in the gravitational field of the earth [gravity meter]</p><p><b>gravimetrijske</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to hydrometry [hydrometric]</p><p><b>kvantitativna analiza po masi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> quantitative analysis by weight</p><p><b>gravimetrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the measurement of specific gravity [hydrometry]</p><p><b>remontno brodogradilište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large dock from which water can be pumped out [dry dock, drydock]</p><p><b>alat koji koristi gravir (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tool used by an engraver [graver, pointel, pointrel]</p><p><b>dostojanstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> formality in bearing and appearance [dignity, lordliness]</p><p><b>težiti ka</b></p><p><i>v.</i> move toward</p><p><i>v.</i> be attracted to</p><p><i>v.</i> move due to the pull of gravitation</p><p><b>gravitacija, gravitiranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the force of attraction between all masses in the universe [gravitational attraction, gravitational force, gravity]</p><p><i>n.</i> movement downward resulting from gravitational attraction</p><p><i>n.</i> a figurative movement toward some attraction</p><p><b>(fizički) talas koji se pretpostavlja da se širi gravitacijom i putuje brzinom svjetlosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a wave that is hypothesized to propagate gravity and to travel at the speed of light [gravity wave]</p><p><b>gravitacijski, gravitacioni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or caused by gravitation [gravitative]</p><p><b>(fizici) sila privlačenja između svih masa u svemiru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the force of attraction between all masses in the universe [gravitation, gravitational force, gravity]</p><p><b>implozija zvijezde koja je rezultat njene vlastite gravitacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the implosion of a star resulting from its own gravity</p><p><b>G, Newtonova konstanta, gravitacijska konstanta, univerzalna gravitacijska konstanta, veliki G</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the universal constant relating force to mass and distance in Newton's law of gravitation [G, constant of gravitation, universal gravitational constant]</p><p><b>polje sile oko tijela konačne mase (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a field of force surrounding a body of finite mass</p><p><b>(fizici) sila privlačenja između svih masa u svemiru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the force of attraction between all masses in the universe [gravitation, gravitational attraction, gravity]</p><p><b>Slab interakcija između čestica koja proizlazi iz njihove mase. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a weak interaction between particles that results from their mass</p><p><b>(fizička) masa tijela mjerena gravitacijskom privlačnošću za druga tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the mass of a body as measured by its gravitational attraction for other bodies</p><p><b>(fizička) teorija da se bilo koje dvije čestice materije međusobno privlače silom koja je direktno proporcionalna sa proizvodom njihovih masa i obrnuto proporcionalna kvadratu udaljenosti između njih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the theory that any two particles of matter attract one another with a force directly proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them [Newton's theory of gravitation, theory of gravitation, theory of gravity]</p><p><b>gravitacijski, gravitacioni (od &quot;gravitational&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to gravitation</p><p><b>gravitacijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or caused by gravitation [gravitational]</p><p><b>graviton</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gauge boson that mediates the (extremely weak) gravitational interactions between particles</p><p><b>gravitacija, gravitacije, ozbiljnost, sila teža, teža, važnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the force of attraction between all masses in the universe [gravitation, gravitational attraction, gravitational force]</p><p><i>n.</i> a manner that is serious and solemn [graveness, soberness, sobriety, somberness, sombreness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a solemn and dignified feeling [solemnity]</p><p><b>bomba koja pada zbog gravitacije i nije usmjerena na metu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb that falls because of gravity and is not guided to a target [dumb bomb]</p><p><b>Sklonite se na sklonost u kojoj visivi zid izgleda da je kliznuo prema dolje u odnosu na podnožje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inclined fault in which the hanging wall appears to have slipped downward relative to the footwall [common fault, normal fault]</p><p><b>gradijent gravitacijskih sila koje djeluju na različite dijelove nesfernog objekta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gradient in the gravitational forces acting on different parts of a nonspherical object</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to samo jedan od glavnih uređaja za mjerenje, to znači da je to samo jedan od glavnih uređaja za mjerenje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument for measuring variations in the gravitational field of the earth [gravimeter]</p><p><b>(fizički) talas koji se pretpostavlja da se širi gravitacijom i putuje brzinom svjetlosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a wave that is hypothesized to propagate gravity and to travel at the speed of light [gravitation wave]</p><p><b>(svemirski let) putanj koji prolazi blizu planetarnog tijela kako bi dobio energiju iz njegovog gravitacijskog polja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (spaceflight) a trajectory that passes close to a planetary body in order to gain energy from its gravitational field</p><p><b>gravura</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a printing process that uses an etched or engraved plate [intaglio, intaglio printing]</p><p><i>n.</i> a printing plate used in the process of gravure</p><p><i>n.</i> an intaglio print produced by gravure [heliogravure, photogravure]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of intaglio printing</p><p><b>sos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sauce made by adding stock, flour, or other ingredients to the juice and fat that drips from cooking meats</p><p><i>n.</i> the seasoned but not thickened juices that drip from cooking meats [pan gravy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden happening that brings good fortune (as a sudden opportunity to make money) [bonanza, boom, bunce, godsend, gold rush, manna from heaven, windfall]</p><p><b>jelo (često u obliku čamca) za serviranje umaka ili umaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dish (often boat-shaped) for serving gravy or sauce [boat, gravy holder, sauceboat]</p><p><b>jelo (često u obliku čamca) za serviranje umaka ili umaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dish (often boat-shaped) for serving gravy or sauce [boat, gravy boat, saucebo