ette and green flowers often striped purple or brown or red with the dorsal sepal incurved to form a hood [helmet orchid]</p><p><b>novajlija, početnik, žutokljunac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an awkward and inexperienced youth [cub, rookie]</p><p><b>plastenik, stakleni vrt, staklenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a building with glass walls and roof [glasshouse]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or caused by the greenhouse effect</p><p><b>učinak staklenika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> warming that results when solar radiation is trapped by the atmosphere [greenhouse warming]</p><p><b>plin koji doprinosi staklenikom tako što apsorbira infracrveno zračenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gas that contributes to the greenhouse effect by absorbing infrared radiation [greenhouse gas]</p><p><b>staklenički plin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gas that contributes to the greenhouse effect by absorbing infrared radiation [greenhouse emission]</p><p><b>zagrijavanje koje nastaje kada je sunčevo zračenje zarobljeno u atmosferi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> warming that results when solar radiation is trapped by the atmosphere [greenhouse effect]</p><p><b>bijela muha koja živi u staklenicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> whitefly that inhabits greenhouses [Trialeurodes vaporariorum]</p><p><b>mlad, svjež, tratina, zelen, zeleniti se, zelena, zelene, zelenih, zeleno, zelenom (od &quot;green&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the phenomenon of vitality and freshness being restored [rejuvenation]</p><p><b>zelenkast</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of the color between blue and yellow in the color spectrum [dark-green, green, light-green]</p><p><b>plava boja, odbojena zelenom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shade of blue tinged with green [aqua, aquamarine, cobalt blue, peacock blue, turquoise]</p><p><b>Zlatna boja, odbojena zelenom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shade of yellow tinged with green</p><p><b>od smeđe boje, obojena zelenom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of brown tinged with green</p><p><b>od sive boje, odbojene zelenom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of