on meeting) [salutation]</p><p><b>čestitka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a card sent to express personal greetings</p><p><b>Australijski golfer (rođen 1955) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian golfer (born in 1955) [Gregory John Norman, Norman]</p><p><b>primitivni protozoji paraziti u insektima i drugim beskičmenjacima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vermiform protozoans parasitic in insects and other invertebrates</p><p><b>red u podklasi Telosporidia (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an order in the subclass Telosporidia [order Gregarinida]</p><p><b>društven</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of animals) tending to form a group with others of the same species</p><p><i>adj.</i> instinctively or temperamentally seeking and enjoying the company of others</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of plants) growing in groups that are close together</p><p><b>društven (od &quot;gregarious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a gregarious manner [sociably]</p><p><b>društven (od &quot;gregarious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being gregarious--having a dislike of being alone</p><p><b>Augustinski redovnik i botaničar čiji su eksperimenti u uzgoju vrtnog graška doveli do njegovog konačnog priznanja kao osnivača znanosti genetičke (1822-1884) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Augustinian monk and botanist whose experiments in breeding garden peas led to his eventual recognition as founder of the science of genetics (1822-1884) [Johann Mendel, Mendel]</p><p><b>gregorijanski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Pope Gregory I or to the plainsong chants of the Roman Catholic Church</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Pope Gregory XIII or the calendar he introduced in 1582</p><p><b>Sunčev kalendar koji je danas u općoj upotrebi, koji je uvodio Gregorije XIII 1582. kako bi ispravio pogrešku u julijanskom kalendaru uklanjanjem 10 dana, tako da se 5. oktobar zove 15. oktobar i da samo stogodišnje godine koje se dijele sa 400 trebaju biti prestupne godine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the solar calendar now in general use, introduced by Gregory XIII in 1582 to correct an error in the Julian calendar by suppressing 10 days, making Oct 5 be called Oct 15, and providing that only centenary years divisible by 400 should be leap years [New Style calendar]</p><p><b>mjesec, mjesec gregorijanskoga kalendara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a month in the Gregorian calendar</p><p><b>različita pjevačka pjesma po pape Grgriju I. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of plainsong named after Pope Gregory I</p><p><b>bilo koji od sustava načina koji se koristi u gregorijanskim pjesmama do 1600. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a system of modes used in Gregorian chants up until 1600 [church mode, ecclesiastical mode, medieval mode]</p><p><b>S druge strane, radi se o teleskopima za slikanje zraka, koji imaju paraboloidno primarno ogledalo i hiperboloidno sekundarno ogledalo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reflecting telescope that has a paraboloidal primary mirror and a hyperboloidal secondary mirror [Cassegrainian telescope]</p><p><b>(Rimska katolička crkva) crkveni otac poznat po svojoj stalnoj borbi protiv navodnih krivovjerja, Talijanski papa od 1831. do 1846., papa koji je sponzorirao uvođenje modernog kalendara (1572-1585), talijanski papa od 1406. do 1415. koji je radio na okončanju Velike raskoši i koji se povukao da bi to omogućio (1327-1417), talijanski papa koji se borio za uspostavljanje nadmoći pape nad rimskokatoličkom crkvom i nadmoći crkve nad državom (1020-1085), (Rimska katolička crkva) talijanski papa poznat po svom duhovnom i svjetovnom vodstvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) a church father known for his constant fight against perceived heresies [Gregory Nazianzen, Gregory of Nazianzen, St. Gregory of Nazianzen]</p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1831 to 1846 [Bartolomeo Alberto Capillari, Gregory XVI]</p><p><i>n.</i> the pope who sponsored the introduction of the modern calendar (1572-1585) [Gregory XIII, Ugo Buoncompagni]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Italian pope from 1406 to 1415 who worked to end the Great Schism and who retired to make it possible (1327-1417) [Angelo Correr, Gregory XII]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Italian pope who fought to establish the supremacy of the pope over the Roman Catholic Church and the supremacy of the church over the state (1020-1085) [Gregory VII, Hildebrand]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) an Italian pope distinguished for his spiritual and temporal leadership [Gregory I, Gregory the Great, Saint Gregory I, St. Gregory I]</p><p><b>Američki seksualni fiziolog čiji je predosjećaj da progesteron može blokirati ovulaciju doveo do razvoja oralne kontracepcijske pilule (1903-1967) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States sexual physiologist whose hunch that progesterone could block ovulation led to the development of the oral contraceptive pill (1903-1967) [Gregory Pincus, Pincus]</p><p><b>(Rimska katolička crkva) talijanski papa poznat po svom duhovnom i svjetovnom vodstvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) an Italian pope distinguished for his spiritual and temporal leadership [Gregory, Gregory the Great, Saint Gregory I, St. Gregory I]</p><p><b>Australijski golfer (rođen 1955) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian golfer (born in 1955) [Greg Norman, Norman]</p><p><b>(Rimska katolička crkva) crkveni otac poznat po svojoj stalnoj borbi protiv navodnih krivovjerja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) a church father known for his constant fight against perceived heresies [Gregory, Gregory of Nazianzen, St. Gregory of Nazianzen]</p><p><b>(Rimska katolička crkva) crkveni otac poznat po svojoj stalnoj borbi protiv navodnih krivovjerja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) a church father known for his constant fight against perceived heresies [Gregory, Gregory Nazianzen, St. Gregory of Nazianzen]</p><p><b>Američki seksualni fiziolog čiji je predosjećaj da progesteron može blokirati ovulaciju doveo do razvoja oralne kontracepcijske pilule (1903-1967) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States sexual physiologist w