 her reclusiveness (1905-1990) [Garbo, Greta Garbo]</p><p><b>Kanadski hokejaš s visokim rezultatima (rođen 1961.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> high-scoring Canadian ice-hockey player (born in 1961) [Wayne Gretzky]</p><p><b>Svaka biljka ili biljka iz roda Grevillea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any shrub or tree of the genus Grevillea</p><p><b>visoka grmlja sa cilindričnim cvetovima crvenih cvjetova i pinnatifičnim lištima svižnjastim i sivim ispod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall shrub with cylindrical racemes of red flowers and pinnatifid leaves silky and grey beneath [red-flowered silky oak]</p><p><b>srednji do visok brzo rastuće stablo s narančastim cvijećima i pernate bipinate lišća svilovit-dlakavi ispod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium to tall fast-growing tree with orange flowers and feathery bipinnate leaves silky-hairy beneath [silky oak]</p><p><b>drvo koje daje tvrdo teško crvenkasto drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree yielding hard heavy reddish wood [beefwood]</p><p><b>malo tanko stablo s obično čitavim sivo-zelenim višenim lišćama i bijelim ili kremastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small slender tree with usually entire grey-green pendulous leaves and white or cream-colored flowers [silver oak]</p><p><b>Zebra s manje neprekidnim prugama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> zebra with less continuous stripes [Equus grevyi]</p><p><b>rod tropskih i subtropskih planinara ili grmova ili stabala Starog svijeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of tropical and subtropical Old World climbers or shrubs or trees [genus Grewia]</p><p><b>otporan na sušu Azijski drveći grm koji daje ugodno kiselu malu crvenu voću koja se obično koristi u šerpetama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> drought-resistant Asiatic treelike shrub bearing pleasantly acid small red edible fruits commonly used in sherbets [phalsa]</p><p><b>osijedjeti, sijed, siv, siva, siva boja, sivo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer of western adventure novels (1875-1939) [Zane Grey]</p><p><i>n.</i> Queen of England for nine days in 1553 [Lady Jane Grey]</p><p><i>n.</i> Englishman who as Prime Minister implemented social reforms including the abolition of slavery throughout the British Empire (1764-1845) [Charles Grey, Second Earl Grey]</p><p><i>n.</i> any organization or party whose uniforms or badges are grey [gray]</p><p><i>n.</i> a neutral achromatic color midway between white and black [gray, grayness, greyness]</p><p><i>n.</i> clothing that is a grey color [gray]</p><p><i>n.</i> horse of a light gray or whitish color [gray]</p><p><i>v.</i> make grey [gray]</p><p><i>v.</i> turn grey [gray]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of an achromatic color of any lightness intermediate between the extremes of white and black [gray, grayish, greyish]</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing characteristics of age, especially having grey or white hair [gray, gray-haired, gray-headed, grey-haired, grey-headed, grizzly, hoar, hoary, white-haired]</p><p><i>adj.</i> used to signify the Confederate forces in the American Civil War (who wore grey uniforms) [gray]</p><p><i>adj.</i> intermediate in character or position [gray]</p><p><b>izvorno iz Europe, ali je uvedeno u Ameriku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> native to Europe but introduced in America [Alnus incana, gray alder]</p><p><b>srednja površina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an intermediate area [gray area]</p><p><b>srednjovelika breza iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s bijelom ili blijedo sivom kore i bezvrijednim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized birch of eastern North America having white or pale grey bark and valueless wood [American gray birch, American grey birch, Betula populifolia, gray birch]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička ptica pjevačica čiji se glas podsjeća na mačiće meving (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American songbird whose call resembles a cat's mewing [Dumetella carolinensis, catbird, gray catbird]</p><p><b>Plodač koji se nalazi od Sjeverne Karoline do Floride i istočnog Meksičkog zaljeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flounder found from North Carolina to Florida and the eastern Gulf of Mexico [Etropus rimosus, gray flounder]</p><p><b>tamno siva američka lisica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dark grey American fox [Urocyon cinereoargenteus, gray fox]</p><p><b>rimokatolički redovnik u sivom odelu franjevačkog reda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Roman Catholic friar wearing the grey habit of the Franciscan order [Franciscan]</p><p><b>je crvena trava iz Kanade i istočnih Sjedinjenih Država koja ima žute cvijeće koje se ponekad koristi za bojenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dyer's weed of Canada and the eastern United States having yellow flowers sometimes used in dyeing [Solidago nemoralis, gray goldenrod]</p><p><b>Ženka crna žablja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> female black grouse [gray hen, grayhen, greyhen, heath hen]</p><p><b>žabri žabri s crnom glavom i bez grebena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a jay of northern North America with black-capped head and no crest [Canada jay, Perisoreus canadensis, camp robber, gray jay, whisker jack]</p><p><b>ptica koja se razmnožava na jugoistoku SAD-a i zimi u tropskoj Americi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kingbird that breeds in the southeastern United States and winters in tropical America [Tyrannus domenicensis domenicensis, gray kingbird, petchary]</p><p><b>Stari svijet leming (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World lemming [gray lemming, red-backed lemming]</p><p><b>siva ekonomija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unofficial market in which goods are bought and sold at prices lower than the official price set by a regulatory agency [gray market]</p><p><b>grivo-živo živčano tkivo koje sadrži stanična tijela i vlakna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> greyish nervous tissue containing cell bodies as well as fibers [gray matter, gray substance, grey substance, substantia grisea]</p><p><b>cipal, cipli, skakavica, skočac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> highly valued lean flesh of marine or freshwater mullet [gray mullet, mullet]</p><p><i>n.</i> freshwater or coastal food fishes a spindle-shaped body [gray mullet, mullet]</p><p><b>jarebica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common European partridge [Hungarian partridge, Perdix perdix, gray partridge]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste biljaka koje se mogu upotrebljavati za proizvodnju biljaka u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje članak 3. točka (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje članak 3. točka (a) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fern growing on rocks or tree trunks and having fronds greyish and scurfy below [Polypodium polypodioides, gray polypody, resurrection fern]</p><p><b>veliki brzo rastući poplar s slabijim lobnim listovima sivim na donjoj površini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large rapidly growing poplar with faintly lobed dentate leaves grey on the lower surface [Populus canescens, gray poplar]</p><p><b>nizak višegodišnji biljci s mnogo grana u zapadnim Sjedinjenim Državama s srebrnim lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low much-branched perennial of western United States having silvery leaves [Artemisia cana, Seriphidium canum, gray sage, silver sage, silver sagebrush]</p><p><b>velikog sivo-smeđeg orla s kratkim bijelom kužom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bulky greyish-brown eagle with a short wedge-shaped white tail [European sea eagle, Haliatus albicilla, ern, erne, gray sea eagle, white-tailed sea eagle]</p><p><b>Uobičajena evropska klizanja koja se koriste kao hrana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common European skate used as food [Raja batis, gray skate]</p><p><b>Nalazi se u plitkim vodama uz obalu Floride. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found in shallow waters off the coast of Florida [Lutjanus griseus, gray snapper, mangrove snapper]</p><p><b>grivo-bijela masa ravne ribe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> greyish-white flesh of a flatfish [gray sole]</p><p><b>grivo-živo živčano tkivo koje sadrži stanična tijela i vlakna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> greyish nervous tissue containing cell bodies as well as fibers [gray matter, gray substance, grey matter, substantia grisea]</p><p><b>srednji