thrae but with flower heads having fewer rays and disk flowers [little-head snakeweed]</p><p><b>niskorazrastajući ljepljivi potgrm jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s uskim linearnim lištima na mnogim tankim granama i stotinama sitnih žutih cvjetnih glavaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing sticky subshrub of southwestern United States having narrow linear leaves on many slender branches and hundreds of tiny yellow flower heads [broom snakeroot, broom snakeweed, rabbit-weed, rabbitweed, snakeweed, turpentine weed]</p><p><b>godišnji iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s čvrstim drvenim granama s ljepljivim lišće i žutim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual of southwestern United States having rigid woody branches with sticky foliage and yellow flowers [broom-weed, broomweed]</p><p><b>Nemaju hrabrosti ili vitalnosti., slaba volja, hrabrost ili vitalnost (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking courage or vitality</p><p><i>adj.</i> weak in willpower, courage or vitality [namby-pamby, spineless, wishy-washy]</p><p><b>karakteristika nedostatka hrabrosti i odlučnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of lacking courage and determination</p><p><b>odlučnost, petlja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fortitude and determination [backbone, grit, gumption, moxie, sand]</p><p><b>osobina koja pokazuje hrabrost i odlučnost unatoč mogućem gubitku ili povredi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of showing courage and determination in spite of possible loss or injury [pluck, pluckiness]</p><p><b>Oznaka hrabrosti i odlučnosti u suočavanju s teškoćama ili opasnostima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by courage and determination in the face of difficulties or danger [plucky]</p><p><b>kada suši daje tvrdu tvar koja se koristi npr. u lopticama za golf. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> when dried yields a hard substance used e.g. in golf balls [balata]</p><p><b>gutaperča, gutaperka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a whitish rubber derived from the coagulated milky latex of gutta-percha trees</p><p><b>jedno od nekoliko istočnoindijskih stabala koja daju gutta-percha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of several East Indian trees yielding gutta-percha</p><p><i>n.</i> one of several East Indian trees yielding gutta-percha [Palaquium gutta]</p><p><b>dno, izdubiti, izolučiti, krovni žlijeb, odvodni kanal, oluk, prostor za uvezivanje, slivnik, uvezna margina, žlijeb</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a channel along the eaves or on the roof [trough]</p><p><i>n.</i> misfortune resulting in lost effort or money [sewer, toilet]</p><p><i>n.</i> a worker who guts things (fish or buildings or cars etc.)</p><p><i>n.</i> a tool for gutting fish</p><p><i>v.</i> burn unsteadily, feebly, or low</p><p><i>v.</i> flow in small streams</p><p><i>v.</i> wear or cut gutters into</p><p><i>v.</i> provide with gutters</p><p><b>mediji koji se bave senzacionalnim novinarstvom (posebno u vezi privatnog života javnih ličnosti) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> press that engages in sensational journalism (especially concerning the private lives of public figures)</p><p><b>dijete koje provodi većinu svog vremena na ulici, posebno u slumskim područjima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a child who spends most of his time in the streets especially in slum areas [street urchin]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjena obitelj uglavnom tropskih stabala i grmova i vinove loze koja proizvodi ulja i smole i neki korisni drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed family of chiefly tropical trees and shrubs and vines that produce oils and resins and some usable timber [Clusiaceae, St John's wort family, family Clusiaceae, family Guttiferae]</p><p><b>korišten u nekim klasifikacijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used in some classifications [order Guttiferales]</p><p><b>žderati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> eat greedily [devour, pig, raven]</p><p><b>grlen, grleni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a consonant articulated in the back of the mouth or throat [guttural consonant, pharyngeal, pharyngeal consonant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> like the sounds of frogs and crows [croaky]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or articulated in the throat</p><p><b>suzbijekle izražene u stražnjem dijelu usta ili grla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a consonant articulated in the back of the mouth or throat [guttural, pharyngeal, pharyngeal consonant]</p><p><b>guturalan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a guttural manner</p><p><b>(Britanski žarg) šef (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (British slang) boss</p><p><b>brk samarice, čovjek, dečko, konop za učvrščivanje, mladić, momak, uzda teretnog uređaja, ismijati, ismijavati, izrugati se, izrugivati se, podrugivati se, rugati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an informal term for a youth or man [bozo, cat, hombre, sod]</p><p><i>n.</i> an effigy of Guy Fawkes that is burned on a bonfire on Guy Fawkes Day</p><p><i>n.</i> a cable, wire, or rope that is used to brace something (especially a tent) [guy cable, guy rope, guy wire]</p><p><i>v.</i> subject to laughter or ridicule [blackguard, jest at, laugh at, make fun, poke fun, rib, ridicule, roast]</p><p><i>v.</i> steady or support with a guy wire or cable</p><p><b>kabl, žica ili užad koja se koristi za vezanje nečeg (posebno šatora) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cable, wire, or rope that is used to brace something (especially a tent) [guy, guy rope, guy wire]</p><p><b>Francuski pisac poznat posebno po svojim kratkim pričama (1850-1893) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French writer noted especially for his short stories (1850-1893) [Henri Rene Albert Guy de Maupassant, Maupassant]</p><p><b>Engleski zavjeritelj koji je pogubljen zbog uloge u zavjeri da se raznijeti James I i kuće parlamenta (1570-1606) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English conspirator who was executed for his role in a plot to blow up James I and the Houses of Parliament (1570-1606) [Fawkes]</p><p><b>Dan za proslavu otkrića zavere za barut. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> day for the celebration of the discovery of the Gunpowder Plot</p><p><b>Ovakve noći se spaljuju slike Guy Fawkesa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> effigies of Guy Fawkes are burned on this night [Bonfire Night]</p><p><b>papa koji je 1122. natjerao cara Henryja V. da potpiše konkordat koji priznaje pravo crkve da izabere vlastito vodstvo (umro 1124.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pope who in 1122 forced the Holy Roman Emperor Henry V to sign a concordat that recognized the right of the church to choose its own leadership (died in 1124) [Calixtus II]</p><p><b>kabl, žica ili užad koja se koristi za vezanje nečeg (posebno šatora) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cable, wire, or rope that is used to brace something (especially a tent) [guy, guy cable, guy wire]</p><p><b>kabl, žica ili užad koja se koristi za vezanje nečeg (posebno šatora) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cable, wire, or rope that is used to brace something (especially a tent) [guy, guy cable, guy rope]</p><p><b>Gvajana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic in northeastern South America [British Guiana, Co-operative Republic of Guyana]</p><p><b>osnovna jedinica novca u Gvajani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Guyana</p><p><b>u Gujanama ili u njima živi., od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Gujanu ili njezine stanovnike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Guyana</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Guyana or its inhabitants</p><p><b>vodena planina vulkanskog podnožja (posebno u Tihom oceanu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a seamount of volcanic origin (especially in the Pacific Ocean)</p><p><b>bančenje, lokanje, lokati, tamaniti, žderanje, polokati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> drink greedily or as if with great thirst</p><p><b>žderonja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who drinks heavily (especially alcoholic beverages)</p><p><i>n.</i> a drinker who swallows large amounts greedily [gulper]</p><p><b>bančenje, lokanje, lokati, tamaniti, žderanje (od &quot;guzzle&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the drinking of large mouthfuls rapidly [gulping, swilling]</p><p><b>Keltski bog neba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Celtic sky god</p><p><b>Keltski bog podzemlja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Celtic underworld god</p><p><b>Engleska komedija i ljubavnica Karla II (1650-1687) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English comedienne and mistress of Charles II (1650-1687) [Eleanor Gwyn, Eleanor Gwynn, Eleanor Gwynne, Gynne, Gywn, Nell Gwynn, Nell Gwynne, Nell Gywn]</p><p><b>jedinica SI za energiju apsorbiranu iz ionizirajućeg zračenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the SI unit of energy absorbed from ionizing radiation [gray]</p><p><b>prebacivanje s jedne strane broda na drugu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> shift from one side of the ship to the other [change course, jib, jibe]</p><p><b>dvorana za vježbanje s utezima, gimnastika, teretana, trim-kabinet, trim-kabinetom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> athletic facility equipped for sports or physical training [gymnasium]</p><p><b>za upotrebu u proizvodnji električnih goriva ili električne energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sports equipment consisting of a piece of thick padding on the floor for gymnastic sports [mat]</p><p><b>osoba koja provodi svo slobodno vrijeme u sportu ili vježbanju u teretani ili zdravilištu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who spends all leisure time playing sports or working out in a gymnasium or health spa</p><p><b>tenisica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a canvas shoe with a pliable rubber sole [sneaker, tennis shoe]</p><p><b>odjeća za nošenje tijekom sudjelovanja u gimnastičkim vježbama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> clothes prescribed for wear while participating in gymnastic exercise</p><p><b>Sastanak na kojem jahači i konji pokazuju niz vještina i sposobnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a meet at which riders and horses display a range of skills and aptitudes</p><p><b>mali rod kopnenih orhideja iz Sjeverne Amerike i umjerene Evroazije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of terrestrial orchids of North America and temperate Eurasia [genus Gymnadenia]</p><p><b>Europska orhideja s gustim šiljcima mirisnih ružičastih ili ljubičastih ili crvenih cvijeća s vidljivim šporama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European orchid having dense spikes of fragrant pink or lilac or red flowers with conspicuous spurs [fragrant orchid]</p><p><b>sličan Gymnadenia conopsea ali s manjim cvijećima na kraćim stabljikama i puno kraćim šporama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to Gymnadenia conopsea but with smaller flowers on shorter stems and having much shorter spurs [short-spurred fragrant orchid]</p><p><b>rod sjevernoameričkih kopnenih orhideja koji se obično uključuju u rod Habenaria (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of North American terrestrial orchids usually included in genus Habenaria [genus Gymnadeniopsis]</p><p><b>dvorana za vježbanje s utezima, gimnastička dvorana, gimnazija, teretana, vježbaonica, gimnastička sala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school for students intermediate between elementary school and college [lycee, lyceum, middle school, secondary school]</p><p><i>n.</i> athletic facility equipped for sports or physical training [gym]</p><p><b>gimnastičar, vježbač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an athlete who is skilled in gymnastics</p><p><b>gimnastičar, vježbač (od &quot;gymnast&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> vigorously active [acrobatic, athletic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or used in exercises intended to develop strength and agility</p><p><b>gimnastička sprava, sprava za vježbanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sports equipment used in gymnastic exercises [exerciser]</p><p><b>gimnastika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (gymnastics) an exercise designed to develop and display strength and agility and balance (usually performed with or on some gymnastic apparatus)</p><p><i>n.</i> a sport that involves exercises intended to display strength and balance and agility [gymnastics]</p><p><b>konj, kozlić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a padded gymnastic apparatus on legs [horse]</p><p><b>fiskultura, gimnasticirati, gimnastika, tjelovježba, gimnastička</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sport that involves exercises intended to display strength and balance and agility [gymnastic exercise]</p><p><b>rod Zoarcidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Zoarcidae [genus Gymnelis]</p><p><b>Arktički jegulj bez ljuske, svijetle boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brightly colored scaleless Arctic eelpout [fish doctor]</p><p><b>veliki rod nisko rastućih kugličastih južnoameričkih kaktusa s trnastima rebrima prekrivenim mnogim gomoljicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large genus of low-growing globular South American cacti with spiny ribs covered with many tubercles [genus Gymnocalycium]</p><p><b>hrastovi paprike: u nekim sustavima klasifikacije uključeni u rod Thelypteris (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> oak ferns: in some classification systems included in genus Thelypteris [genus Gymnocarpium]</p><p><b>Gymnocarpium dryopteris, Thelypteris dryopteris:, kisela lastreja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bright blue-green fern widely distributed especially in damp acid woodlands of temperate northern hemisphere [Thelypteris dryopteris, oak fern]</p><p><b>Gymnocarpium robertianum, vapnenačka lastreja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> yellow-green fern of rocky areas of northern hemisphere [limestone fern, northern oak fern]</p><p><b>malo rodno listno drveće iz Kine i Sjedinjenih Država s panikularnim cvijećem i debelom pulpnom strudom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of deciduous trees of China and United States having paniculate flowers and thick pulpy pods [genus Gymnocladus]</p><p><b>lijepo stablo iz središnje i istočne Sjeverne Amerike s velikim bipinatnim lišćama i zelenobranim cvijećem s velikim drvenim smeđim čunjama čija se sjemena koriste kao zamjena za kavu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> handsome tree of central and eastern North America having large bipinnate leaves and green-white flowers followed by large woody brown pods whose seeds are used as a coffee substitute [Kentucky coffee tree, bonduc, chicot]</p><p><b>koji sadrže samo kalifornijski kondor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> containing solely the California condor [genus Gymnogyps]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički kondor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American condor [California condor]</p><p><b>čirevi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slime molds [Myxomycota, division Gymnomycota, division Myxomycota]</p><p><b>red vodozemljana uključujući cecilije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an order of amphibians including caecilians [order Gymnophiona]</p><p><b>rod gljiva koji se karakterizira narandžastom bojom spornog naslaga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of fungus characterized by the orange color of the spore deposit [genus Gymnopilus]</p><p><b>gljiva s smeđom narandžastom plodnim tijelom i prstenjem blizu vrha stabljike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus with a brownish orange fruiting body and a ring near the top of the stalk</p><p><b>otrovna gljiva sa suhom kapa i koridora koji ne ostavlja puno prstena na robusnom stabljku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a poisonous fungus with a dry cap and a cortina that does not leave much of a ring on the robust stalk</p><p><b>divovska gljiva na sjeverozapadu Pacifika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a giant fungus of the Pacific Northwest</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama uvrštene u obitelj Laniidae: australske vrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications placed in the family Laniidae: Australian piping crows [genus Gymnorhina]</p><p><b>crno-bijela ptica veličine vrana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crow-sized black-and-white bird [piping crow, piping crow-shrike]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s gimnosofijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to gymnosophy</p><p><b>član hinduističke sekte koja prakticira gimnosofiju (posebno nudizam) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> member of a Hindu sect practicing gymnosophy (especially nudism)</p><p><b>Nauka sekte hinduističkih filozofa koji su se bavili golotinjom i asketizmom i meditacijom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine of a sect of Hindu philosophers who practiced nudity and asceticism and meditation</p><p><b>golosjemenjače</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plants of the class Gymnospermae having seeds not enclosed in an ovary</p><p><b>porodica gimnospermi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of gymnosperms</p><p><b>rodom gimnospermije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of gymnosperms</p><p><b>biljke s golim sjemenom 