56-1928) [First Viscount Haldane of Cloan, Richard Burdon Haldane, Richard Haldane]</p><p><b>Zemljane zmije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ground snakes [genus Haldea]</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama stavljene u rod Haldea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications placed in genus Haldea [Potamophis striatula, eastern ground snake]</p><p><b>Haldol) koji se koristi za liječenje nekih psihotičnih poremećaja i Touretteovog sindroma. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tranquilizer (trade name Haldol) used to treat some psychotic disorders and Tourette's syndrome [haloperidol]</p><p><b>čio, dovući, snažan, zdrav, forsirati, iznuditi, iznuđivati, nametati, nametnuti, natjerati, natjeravati, primorati, primoravati, prinuditi, prisiliti, prisiljavati, pritiskati, pritisnuti, siliti, tjerati, tegliti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soldier of the American Revolution who was hanged as a spy by the British [Nathan Hale]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States astronomer who discovered that sunspots are associated with strong magnetic fields (1868-1938) [George Ellery Hale]</p><p><i>n.</i> prolific United States writer (1822-1909) [Edward Everett Hale]</p><p><i>v.</i> to cause to do through pressure or necessity, by physical, moral or intellectual means [coerce, force, pressure, squeeze]</p><p><i>v.</i> draw slowly or heavily [cart, drag, haul]</p><p><i>adj.</i> exhibiting or restored to vigorous good health [whole]</p><p><b>nacionalni park na Havajima uključujući i uspavan vulkan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a national park in Hawaii including a dormant volcano</p><p><b>čio, dovući, snažan, zdrav (od &quot;hale&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of robust good health [wholeness]</p><p><b>rod biljaka iz Euroazije i Amerike: spurgled gentians (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of herbs of Eurasia and the Americas: spurred gentians [genus Halenia]</p><p><b>čio, dovući, snažan, zdrav (od &quot;hale&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> 100 halers equal 1 koruna Slovakia [heller]</p><p><i>n.</i> 100 halers equal 1 koruna in Czec