i> medium-sized live-bearing shark with eyes at either end of a flattened hammer-shaped head [hammerhead shark]</p><p><b>srednjorodna živa morska pasa s očima na oba kraja ravne glave u obliku čekića (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized live-bearing shark with eyes at either end of a flattened hammer-shaped head [hammerhead]</p><p><b>bat, čekić, kladivo, kovati, pribiti, prikucati, promjenjivi uložak, udarati, udarati čekićem, zabiti, zakucati, zakucavati (od &quot;hammer&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of pounding (delivering repeated heavy blows) [hammer, pound, pounding]</p><p><b>hrvanje u kojem je ruka protivnika okrenuta iza leđa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wrestling hold in which the opponent's arm is twisted up behind his back</p><p><b>Američki tekstopisac koji je surađivao na mnogim glazbenim komedijama (najuspješnije s Richardom Rodgersom) (1895-1960) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States lyricist who collaborated on many musical comedies (most successfully with Richard Rodgers) (1895-1960) [Oscar Hammerstein, Oscar Hammerstein II]</p><p><b>deformirani prst koji je savijen u luk poput kandže (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deformed toe which is bent in a clawlike arch</p><p><b>Američki pisac tvrdog detektivske fantastike (1894-1961) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer of hard-boiled detective fiction (1894-1961) [Dashiell Hammett, Samuel Dashiell Hammett]</p><p><b>Loša glumaca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> poor acting by a ham actor [overacting]</p><p><b>mreža za ležanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small natural hill [hillock, hummock, knoll, mound]</p><p><i>n.</i> a hanging bed of canvas or rope netting (usually suspended between two trees) [sack]</p><p><b>(glazba) elektronička simulacija cijevnog organa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (music) an electronic simulation of a pipe organ [electric organ, electronic organ, organ]</p><p><b>Hamurabi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Babylonian king who codified the laws of Sumer and Mesopotamia (died 1750 BC) [Hammurapi]</p><p><b>Ham