 place]</p><p><b>hapaks, hapakseriemenon, hapakslegomenon, hapax legomenon, nekrotizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a word with a special meaning used for a special occasion [nonce word]</p><p><b>slučajan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> dependent upon or characterized by chance [hit-or-miss]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by great carelessness [slapdash, slipshod, sloppy]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without care [haphazardly]</p><p><b>slučajno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a random manner [arbitrarily, at random, every which way, indiscriminately, randomly, willy-nilly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without care [haphazard]</p><p><b>nepredvidivost, slučajnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of lacking any predictable order or plan [noise, randomness, stochasticity]</p><p><b>kratak dio iz Proroka koji se čita svake subate u judovskoj sinagogi nakon čitanja Tore. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short selection from the Prophets read on every Sabbath in a Jewish synagogue following a reading from the Torah [Haftarah, Haftorah, Haphtorah]</p><p><b>kratak dio iz Proroka koji se čita svake subate u judovskoj sinagogi nakon čitanja Tore. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short selection from the Prophets read on every Sabbath in a Jewish synagogue following a reading from the Torah [Haftarah, Haftorah, Haphtarah]</p><p><b>loše sreće, nesretan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deserving or inciting pity [miserable, misfortunate, pathetic, piteous, pitiable, pitiful, poor, wretched]</p><p><b>haploid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) an organism or cell having only one complete set of chromosomes</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a cell or organism having a single set of chromosomes [haploidic, monoploid]</p><p><b>haploid (od &quot;haploid&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a cell or organism having a single set of chromosomes [haploid, monoploid]</p><p><b>stanje haploidnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of being haploid</p><p><b>rod višegodišnjih biljaka ili grmova s žutim cvijećem iz Sjeverne i Južne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of North and South American perennial herbs or shrubs with yellow flowers [genus Haplopappus]</p><p><b>tamnozelena uspravna biljka sjeverozapadne Sjedinjenih Država i jugozapadne Kanade s čvrstima lišcima u gustim tuftovima i žutim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dark green erect herb of northwestern United States and southwestern Canada having stiff leaves in dense tufts and yellow flower heads [Stenotus acaulis, stemless golden weed]</p><p><b>godišnji iz južnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika s českom lišće i blijedo žuti cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual of southern United States and Mexico having bristly leaves and pale yellow flowers [camphor daisy]</p><p><b>trogodišnja biljka iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s slabim česnom lišćama i žutim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender perennial of western North America having weakly bristly leaves and yellow flower heads [yellow spiny daisy]</p><p><b>red u podklasi Acnidosporidia (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an order in the subclass Acnidosporidia [order Haplosporidia]</p><p><b>parazit kod beskičmenjaka i donjih kičmenjaka koji nemaju poznati gospodarski značaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> parasite in invertebrates and lower vertebrates of no known economic importance</p><p><b>haplotip</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) a combination of alleles (for different genes) that are located closely together on the same chromosome and that tend to be inherited together</p><p><b>slučajan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by accident [by chance, by luck]</p><p><b>bivati, desiti se, dešavati se, događati, dogoditi se, zbivati se, događati se, odigrati se, odigravati se, održati se, održavati se, odvijati se, odviti se, zbiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come to pass [come about, fall out, go on, hap, occur, pass, pass off, take place]</p><p><i>v.</i> happen, occur, or be the case in the course of events or by chance [bechance, befall]</p><p><i>v.</i> chance to be or do something, without intention or causation</p><p><i>v.</i> come into being [materialise, materialize]</p><p><i>v.</i> come upon, as if by accident [bump, chance, encounter, find]</p><p><b>nabasati, naići, naletjeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> find unexpectedly [attain, chance on, chance upon, come across, come upon, discover, fall upon, light upon, strike]</p><p><b>događaj, događanje, zbivanje, happening, pojava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that happens [natural event, occurrence, occurrent]</p><p><b>koincidencija, slučajnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that might have been arranged although it was really accidental [coincidence]</p><p><b>korisno, pripito, radosno, sretno, umjesno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a joyous manner [blithely, gayly, jubilantly, merrily, mirthfully]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in an unexpectedly lucky way</p><p><b>osobna sreća, radost, sreća, veselost, zadovoljstvo, veselje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> state of well-being characterized by emotions ranging from contentment to intense joy [felicity]</p><p><i>n.</i> emotions experienced when in a state of well-being</p><p><b>dobre volje, koji donosi sreću, koji odražava sreću, koristan, plodan, prikladan, pripit, radostan, razdragan, sretan, ugodan, umjestan, veseo, zadovoljan, zgodan, razdragana, srećan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> enjoying or showing or marked by joy or pleasure</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by good fortune [felicitous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> eagerly disposed to act or to be of service [glad]</p><p><i>adj.</i> well expressed and to the point [well-chosen]</p><p><b>neočekivano sreće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unexpected piece of good luck [break, good luck]</p><p><b>Rođenje djeteta živoga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the live birth of a child [blessed event]</p><p><b>vrijeme dana kada bar prodaje alkoholna pića po sniženoj cijeni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time of day when a bar sells alcoholic drinks at a reduced price</p><p><b>Veseli i neodgovorno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> cheerfully irresponsible [carefree, devil-may-care, freewheeling, harum-scarum, slaphappy]</p><p><b>Habsburg</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a roya