lex sound</p><p><i>n.</i> any of a series of musical tones whose frequencies are integral multiples of the frequency of a fundamental</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to harmony as distinct from melody and rhythm</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to harmonics</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the branch of acoustics that studies the composition of musical sounds</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to vibrations that occur as a result of vibrations in a nearby body [sympathetic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> involving or characterized by harmony [consonant, harmonical, harmonised, harmonized]</p><p><b>harmonička analiza, harmonijska analiza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> analysis of a periodic function into a sum of simple sinusoidal components [Fourier analysis]</p><p><b>zakon koji navodi da je odnos kvadrata revolucionarnog perioda (u godinama) prema kočici orbitalne osi (u astronomskim jedinicama) isti za sve planete (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a law stating that the ratio of the square of the revolutionary period (in years) to the cube of the orbital axis (in astronomical units) is the same for all planets [Kepler's third law]</p><p><b>srednja vrijednost n brojeva izražena kao recipročna vrijednost aritmetičke sredine recipročnih vrijednosti brojeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mean of n numbers expressed as the reciprocal of the arithmetic mean of the reciprocals of the numbers</p><p><b>periodični pokret u kojem je pomak ili simetričan oko točke ili je zbir takvih pokreta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a periodic motion in which the displacement is either symmetrical about a point or is the sum of such motions</p><p><b>(matematika) napredak brojeva čije reciproci čine aritmetičku progresiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (mathematics) a progression of terms whose reciprocals form an arithmetic progression</p><p><b>harmonika, usna harmonika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small rectangular free-reed instrument having a row of free reeds set back in air holes and played by blowing into the desired hole [harp, mouth har