tve koje se trebaju izvoditi kao solo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the official of a synagogue who conducts the liturgical part of the service and sings or chants the prayers intended to be performed as solos [cantor]</p><p><b>opasnost, riskirati, rizik, sreća, slućajnost, vjerojatnost, zgoda, nagađati, naslutiti, naslućivati, hazardirati, kockati se, reskirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a source of danger [endangerment, jeopardy, peril, risk]</p><p><i>n.</i> an unknown and unpredictable phenomenon that causes an event to result one way rather than another [chance, fortune, luck]</p><p><i>n.</i> an obstacle on a golf course</p><p><i>v.</i> put forward, of a guess, in spite of possible refutation [guess, pretend, venture]</p><p><i>v.</i> put at risk [adventure, jeopardize, stake, venture]</p><p><i>v.</i> take a risk in the hope of a favorable outcome [adventure, chance, gamble, risk, run a risk, take a chance, take chances]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u slučaju osiguranja od opasnosti od požara ili oluje, osiguranje koje se primjenjuje na osiguranje od opasnosti od požara ili oluje može se smatrati osiguranjem od opasnosti od požara ili oluje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> insurance that provides protection against certain risks such as storms or fires</p><p><b>mali rod grmova i potgrmova zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s cvijećem koje mijenja boju dok sazrevaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of shrubs and subshrubs of western United States having flowers that change color as they mature [genus Hazardia]</p><p><b>Zapadni američki grmovi s bijelim filtim lišćem i žutim cvijećem koji postaju crveno-fijazloviti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> western American shrubs having white felted foliage and yellow flowers that become red-purple [hoary golden bush]</p><p><b>hazardan, opasan, riskantan, rizičan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving risk or danger [risky, wild]</p><p><b>opasno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a dangerous manner [dangerously, perilously]</p><p><b