hout pain [ill health, unhealthiness]</p><p><b>zdravstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of individuals whose work helps to maintain the health of their clients</p><p><b>medicinski radnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who helps in identifying or preventing or treating illness or disability [PCP, caregiver, health care provider, primary care provider]</p><p><b>teretana, toplice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a place of business with equipment and facilities for exercising and improving physical fitness [health club, spa]</p><p><b>zdravstvena skrb, zdravstvena zaštita</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the preservation of mental and physical health by preventing or treating illness through services offered by the health profession [health care]</p><p><b>pružanje zdravstvene skrbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the provision of health care [care delivery, health care delivery]</p><p><b>bolnica, zdravstvena institucija, zdravstvena ustanova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> building where medicine is practiced [health facility, medical building]</p><p><b>zdrav, zdrava, sanitarni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> conducive to good health of body or mind</p><p><i>adj.</i> free from filth and pathogens [sanitary]</p><p><b>zdrav, zdrava (od &quot;healthful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of promoting good health</p><p><b>zdraviji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> improved in health or physical condition [fitter]</p><p><b>na zdrav nacin</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a levelheaded manner</p><p><b>dobro zdravlje, zdravlje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being vigorous and free from bodily or mental disease [good health]</p><p><b>ljekovit, zdrav, zdravim, zdravog</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or indicating good health in body or mind</p><p><i>adj.</i> financially secure and functioning well</p><p><i>adj.</i> promoting health [good for you, salubrious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> exercising or showing good judgment [intelligent, level-headed, levelheaded, sound]</p><p><i>adj.</i> large in amount or extent or degree [goodish, goodly, hefty, respectable, sizable, sizeable, tidy]</p><p><b>gomila, gruda, hrpa, mnoštvo, nagomilati, naslagati, natovariti, brdo, naslaga, hrpetina, masa, krntija, starudija, kupiti, nagomilavati, nakupiti, nakupljati, skupiti, skupljati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collection of objects laid on top of each other [agglomerate, cumulation, cumulus, mound, pile]</p><p><i>n.</i> (often followed by `of') a large number or amount or extent [batch, deal, flock, good deal, great deal, hatful, lot, mass, mess, mickle, mint, mountain, muckle, passel, peck, pile, plenty, pot, quite a little, raft, sight, slew, spate, stack, tidy sum, wad]</p><p><i>n.</i> a car that is old and unreliable [bus, jalopy]</p><p><i>v.</i> bestow in large quantities</p><p><i>v.</i> arrange in stacks [pile, stack]</p><p><i>v.</i> fill to overflow</p><p><b>gomilati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> arrange into piles or stacks [pile up, stack up]</p><p><b>gomila, gruda, hrpa, mnoštvo, nagomilati, naslagati, natovariti (od &quot;heap&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large number or amount [dozens, gobs, lashings, loads, lots, oodles, piles, rafts, scads, scores, slews, stacks, tons, wads]</p><p><i>adv.</i> very much</p><p><b>čuti, ispitivati, saslušati, saslušavati, saznati, slušati, čujemo, čuo, načuti, saznavati, preslušati, preslušavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> perceive (sound) via the auditory sense</p><p><i>v.</i> get to know or become aware of, usually accidentally [discover, find out, get a line, get wind, get word, learn, pick up, see]</p><p><i>v.</i> examine or hear (evidence or a case) by judicial process [try]</p><p><i>v.</i> receive a communication from someone</p><p><i>v.</i> listen and pay attention [listen, take heed]</p><p><b>Slušaj svaki detalj i daj puno slušanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> listen to every detail and give a full hearing to</p><p><b>zvučan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> heard or perceptible by the ear [audible]</p><p><b>raspravljen, čuo</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> detected or perceived by the sense of hearing</p><p><b>slušač, slušalac, slušatelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who listens attentively [attender, auditor, listener]</p><p><b>rasprava, raspravljanje, ročište, saslušanje, sluh, slušanje, slušanja, audijencija, sudska rasprava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a proceeding (usually by a court) where evidence is taken for the purpose of determining an issue of fact and reaching a decision based on that evidence</p><p><i>n.</i> an opportunity to state your case and be heard [audience]</p><p><i>n.</i> the range within which a voice can be heard [earreach, earshot]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of hearing attentively [listening]</p><p><i>n.</i> a session (of a committee or grand jury) in which witnesses are called and testimony is taken</p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to hear [audition, auditory modality, auditory sense, sense of hearing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> able to perceive sound</p><p><b>elektronički uređaj koji pojačava zvuk i nosi se kako bi se nadoknadio slab sluh, Konusni akustični uređaj koji se nekada koristio za usmjeravanje zvuka u uho osobe s oštećenim sluhom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electronic device that amplifies sound and is worn to compensate for poor hearing [deaf-aid]</p><p><i>n.</i> a conical acoustic device formerly used to direct sound to the ear of a hearing-impaired person [ear trumpet]</p><p><b>oštećenje sluha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> impairment of the sense of hearing [hearing impairment]</p><p><b>pas obučen da pomaže gluhim signalizirajući pojavu određenih zvukova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dog trained to assist the deaf by signaling the occurrence of certain sounds</p><p><b>Službenik koji je imenovan od strane državne agencije za provođenje istrage ili administrativnog saslušanja kako bi agencija mogla ostvariti svoja zakonska ovlasti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an official appointed by a government agency to conduct an investigation or administrative hearing so that the agency can exercise its statutory powers [hearing officer]</p><p><b>oštećenje sluha</b></p><p><i>n.</i> impairment of the sense of hearing [hearing disorder]</p><p><b>gluhoća</b></p><p><i>n.</i> partial or complete loss of hearing [deafness]</p><p><b>Službenik koji je imenovan od strane državne agencije za provođenje istrage ili administrativnog saslušanja kako bi agencija mogla ostvariti svoja zakonska ovlasti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an official appointed by a government agency to conduct an investigation or administrative hearing so that the agency can exercise its statutory powers [hearing examiner]</p><p><b>ima gubitak sluha (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a hearing loss [hard-of-hearing]</p><p><b>Slušaj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> listen [hark, harken]</p><p><b>glas, govorkanje, prepričavanje, rekla-kazala, glasina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gossip (usually a mixture of truth and untruth) passed around by word of mouth [rumor, rumour]</p><p><i>adj.</i> heard through another rather than directly</p><p><b>dokazi zasnovani na onome što je netko rekao svjedoku a ne na izravnom znanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evidence based on what someone has told the witness and not of direct knowledge</p><p><b>Pravilo koje ne prihvaća kao dokaz bilo kakvu izjavu osim izjave svjedoka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rule that declares not admissible as evidence any statement other than that by a witness</p><p><b>mrtvačka kola, odar, košuta dvogodišnjakinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vehicle for carrying a coffin to a church or a cemetery</p><p><b>Izdavač američkih novina čiji je uvođenje velikih naslovnica i senzacionalnog izvještavanja promijenilo američko novinarstvo (1863-1951) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States newspaper publisher whose introduction of large headlines and sensational reporting changed American journalism (1863-1951) [William Randolph Hearst]</p><p><b>jezgra, ljubav, pamćenje, srce, srčani, srčanost, središte, suština, jezgri, srcu, središtu, centar, sredina, bit, esencija, srž, duh, duša, blagost, dragost, naklonost, nježnost, privrženost, sklonost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the locus of feelings and intuitions [bosom]</p><p><i>n.</i> the hollow muscular organ located behind the sternum and between the lungs [pump, ticker]</p><p><i>n.</i> the courage to carry on [mettle, nerve, spunk]</p><p><i>n.</i> an area that is approximately central within some larger region [center, centre, eye, middle]</p><p><i>n.</i> the choicest or most essential or most vital part of some idea or experience [center, centre, core, essence, gist, heart and soul, inwardness, kernel, marrow, meat, nitty-gritty, nub, pith, substance, sum]</p><p><i>n.</i> an inclination or tendency of a certain kind [spirit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a plane figure with rounded sides curving inward at the top and intersecting at the bottom</p><p><i>n.</i> a firm rather dry variety meat (usually beef or veal)</p><p><i>n.</i> a positive feeling of liking [affection, affectionateness, fondness, philia, tenderness, warmheartedness, warmness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a playing card in the major suit that has one or more red hearts on it</p><p><b>bit, centar, esencija, jezgra, središte, srž, suština</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the choicest or most essential or most vital part of some idea or experience [center, centre, core, essence, gist, heart, inwardness, kernel, marrow, meat, nitty-gritty, nub, pith, substance, sum]</p><p><i>adv.</i> with complete faith [body and soul]</p><p><b>srčani infarkt, infarkt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden severe instance of abnormal heart function</p><p><b>ponavljajući se nagli napadi nesvjesnosti uzrokovani poremećenom provodivosti impulsa koji reguliše otkucaje srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> recurrent sudden attacks of unconsciousness caused by impaired conduction of the impulse that regulates the heartbeat [Adams-Stokes syndrome, Stokes-Adams syndrome, atrioventricular block]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko uzgojenih slatkih trešanja s slatkim sokovitim plodovima u obliku srca, veliki srčani slatki trešnje sa mekom mesom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several cultivated sweet cherries having sweet juicy heart-shaped fruits [oxheart, oxheart cherry]</p><p><i>n.</i> large heart-shaped sweet cherry with soft flesh [oxheart, oxheart cherry]</p><p><b>bolest srca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of the heart [cardiopathy]</p><p><b>nemogućnost srca da pumpa dovoljno krvi za održavanje normalnih tjelesnih funkcija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inability of the heart to pump enough blood to sustain normal bodily functions [coronary failure]</p><p><b>Zmajev na dlanu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crease on the palm [line of heart, love line, mensal line]</p><p><b>hitna procedura koja koristi ritmičku kompresiju srca (ili kroz prsni zid ili, tijekom operacije, izravno na srce) u pokušaju održavanja cirkulacije tijekom srčanog zastoja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an emergency procedure that employs rhythmic compression of the heart (either through the chest wall or, during surgery, directly to the heart) in an attempt to maintain circulation during cardiac arrest [cardiac massage]</p><p><b>monitor srčane aktivnosti, srčani monitor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of electronic equipment for continual observation of the function of the heart [cardiac monitor]</p><p><b>abnormalni zvuk srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal sound of the heart [cardiac murmur, murmur]</p><p><b>mišićno tkivo srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the muscle tissue of the heart [cardiac muscle]</p><p><b>država u jugoistočnim Sjedinjenim Državama na Meksičkom zaljevu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in the southeastern United States on the Gulf of Mexico [AL, Ala., Alabama, Camellia State]</p><p><b>drvena višegodišnja planina s velikim ukrasnim sjemenama koje liče na balone (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> woody perennial climbing plant with large ornamental seed pods that resemble balloons [Cardiospermum halicacabum, balloon vine]</p><p><b>frekvencija srca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the rate at which the heart beats [pulse, pulse rate]</p><p><b>ritam kucajućeg srca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the rhythm of a beating heart [cardiac rhythm]</p><p><b>specijalista za kardiologiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in cardiology [cardiologist, heart surgeon]</p><p><b>specijalista za kardiologiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in cardiology [cardiologist, heart specialist]</p><p><b>bilo koji kirurški zahvat koji uključuje srce (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any surgical procedure involving the heart</p><p><b>morski jezerac s tijelom u obliku srca u čvrstoj trnjastoj ljusci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sea urchin having a heart-shaped body in a rigid spiny shell</p><p><b>ventil za kontrolu jednokrevetnog protoka krvi, implantat koji zamjenjuje prirodni srčani ventil (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a valve to control one-way flow of blood [cardiac valve]</p><p><i>n.</i> an implant that replaces a natural cardiac valve</p><p><b>komora srca koja prima krv iz atrija i pumpa je u arterije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chamber of the heart that receives blood from an atrium and pumps it to the arteries [ventricle]</p><p><b>Hrana s malim sadržajem masti i natrija i drugih sastojaka koji mogu potaknuti bolesti srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of foods that are low in fats and sodium and other ingredients that may foster heart disease</p><p><b>Divlji đumbir s trajnim žarkim listovima u obliku srca, zelena, nisko rastuća višegodišnja biljka s mrljano-zelenim i srebrno-sivim, srčano-okretnim oštrim listovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wild ginger having persistent heart-shaped pungent leaves [Asarum shuttleworthii, heartleaf]</p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen low-growing perennial having mottled green and silvery-grey heart-shaped pungent leaves [Asarum virginicum, heartleaf]</p><p><b>višegodišnji drveni aster iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial wood aster of eastern North America [Aster cordifolius]</p><p><b>pumpa za održavanje cirkulacije tijekom operacije srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pump to maintain circulation during heart surgery</p><p><b>srcolik</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a leaf) shaped like a heart [cordate, cordiform]</p><p><b>Priča u privatnosti., otvoreno i direktno bez rezerve ili tajnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an intimate talk in private</p><p><i>adj.</i> openly straightforward and direct without reserve or secretiveness [candid, open]</p><p><b>bezuslovnom i oduševljenom predanosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> with unconditional and enthusiastic devotion [whole-souled, wholehearted]</p><p><b>jad, ožalošćenost, tuga, žalost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intense sorrow caused by loss of a loved one (especially by death) [brokenheartedness, grief, heartbreak]</p><p><b>kucanje srca, otkucaji srca, puls, djelić sekunde, otkucaj srca, tren, tren oka, trenutak, treptaj oka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the rhythmic contraction and expansion of the arteries with each beat of the heart [beat, pulsation, pulse]</p><p><i>n.</i> a very short time (as the time it takes the eye to blink or the heart to beat) [New York minute, blink of an eye, flash, instant, jiffy, split second, trice, twinkling, wink]</p><p><i>n.</i> an animating or vital unifying force</p><p><b>jad, ožalošćenost, tuga, žalost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intense sorrow caused by loss of a loved one (especially by death) [brokenheartedness, grief, heartache]</p><p><b>jad, ožalošćenost, tuga, žalost (od &quot;heartbreak&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a charming person who is irresponsible in emotional relationships</p><p><i>n.</i> a narrow defeat or a defeat at the last minute</p><p><b>jad, ožalošćenost, tuga, žalost (od &quot;heartbreak&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing or marked by grief or anguish [grievous, heartrending]</p><p><b>pun tuge. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of sorrow [brokenhearted, heartsick]</p><p><b>žgaravica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a painful burning sensation in the chest caused by gastroesophageal reflux (backflow from the stomach irritating the esophagus) [pyrosis]</p><p><b>žgaravica (od &quot;heartburn&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intense resentment</p><p><b>odobriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give encouragement to [cheer, embolden