ds [Arnica cordifolia]</p><p><b>Ustanovljeni kalifornijski grm s lišćama s srčano-oblikovanim režnjevima na dnu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect California shrub having leaves with heart-shaped lobes at the base [Arctostaphylos andersonii]</p><p><b>bez srca, bezdušan, neosjetljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking in feeling or pity or warmth [hardhearted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> devoid of courage or enthusiasm</p><p><b>bezdušno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a heartless manner</p><p><b>bezdušnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an absence of concern for the welfare of others [coldheartedness, hardheartedness]</p><p><b>uzrokovanje ili označavanje tugom ili tjeskobom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing or marked by grief or anguish [grievous, heartbreaking]</p><p><b>bilo koja bolest biljaka u kojoj središnji dio biljke trune (posebno u drveću) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant disease in which the central part of a plant rots (especially in trees)</p><p><b>srca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of whist in which players avoid winning tricks containing hearts or the queen of spades [Black Maria]</p><p><b>maćuhica, mir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common and long cultivated European herb from which most common garden pansies are derived [Johnny-jump-up, Viola tricolor, love-in-idleness, pink of my John, wild pansy]</p><p><i>n.</i> violet of Pacific coast of North America having white petals tinged with yellow and deep violet [Viola ocellata, two-eyed violet]</p><p><i>n.</i> common Old World viola with creamy often violet-tinged flowers [Viola arvensis, field pansy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the absence of mental stress or anxiety [ataraxis, peace, peace of mind, peacefulness, repose, serenity]</p><p><b>biljni vinogradi iz tropske Amerike i Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herbaceous vine of tropical America and Africa [Cardiospermum grandiflorum]</p><p><b>pun tuge., bez ili gotovo bez nade. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of sorrow [brokenhearted, heartbroken]</p><p><i>adj.</i> without or almost without hope [despondent]</p