e property of someone who dies intestate</p><p><b>nasljednici</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a female heir [inheritress, inheritrix]</p><p><b>(zakon) bilo koje imanje koje se po zakonu ili običaju smatra nerazdvojnim od nasljedstva nasljeđuje se s tim nasljedstvom, Nešto što je u obitelji generacijama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) any property that is considered by law or custom as inseparable from an inheritance is inherited with that inheritance</p><p><i>n.</i> something that has been in a family for generations</p><p><b>Njemački matematički fizičar poznat po utvrđivanju načela neizvjesnosti (1901-1976) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German mathematical physicist noted for stating the uncertainty principle (1901-1976) [Werner Karl Heisenberg]</p><p><b>kradnja, pljačka naoružano, počiniti provalu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of stealing [rip-off]</p><p><i>n.</i> robbery at gunpoint [armed robbery, holdup, stickup]</p><p><i>v.</i> commit a burglary [burglarise, burglarize, burgle]</p><p><b>Heitor Villa Lobos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Brazilian composer (1887-1959) [Villa-Lobos]</p><p><b>obalni region zapadnog Arapskog poluotoka koji se graniči s Crvenim morem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coastal region of the western Arabian Peninsula bordering on the Red Sea [Hedjaz, Hijaz]</p><p><b>Muhammadov let iz Meke u Medinu 622. godine koji je označio početak muslimanske ere., putovanje velike grupe kako bi pobjegli iz neprijateljskog okruženja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the flight of Muhammad from Mecca to Medina in 622 which marked the beginning of the Muslim era [Hegira]</p><p><i>n.</i> a journey by a large group to escape from a hostile environment [exodus, hegira]</p><p><b>Hel</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Norse mythology) goddess of the dead and queen of the underworld [Hela]</p><p><b>Hel</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Norse mythology) goddess of the dead and queen of the underworld [Hel]</p><p><b>držan, zadrži, polje, slika, drži, držite, održava, održavaju, održavala, održavanja</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occupied or in the control of</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) lijepa kći Zeusa i Lede koja je oteta od strane Pariza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the beautiful daughter of Zeus and Leda who was abducted by Paris [Helen of Troy]</p><p><b>Američki predavač i pisac koji je bio slijep i gluh od svoje 19. godine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States lecturer and writer who was blind and deaf from the age of 19 months [Helen Keller, Keller]</p><p><b>poznata glumica pozornice i ekrana (1900-1993) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acclaimed actress of stage and screen (1900-1993) [Hayes]</p><p><b>Američki pisac romantičnih romana o nepravednom postupanju s američkim domorocima (1830-1885) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer of romantic novels about the unjust treatment of Native Americans (1830-1885) [Helen Maria Fiske Hunt Jackson, Jackson]</p><p><b>Američki predavač i pisac koji je bio slijep i gluh od svoje 19. godine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States lecturer and writer who was blind and deaf from the age of 19 months [Helen Adams Keller, Keller]</p><p><b>Američki socijalni ekonomist (1876-1933) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States social economist (1876-1933) [Woodbury]</p><p><b>Američki pisac romantičnih romana o nepravednom postupanju s američkim domorocima (1830-1885) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer of romantic novels about the unjust treatment of Native Americans (1830-1885) [Helen Hunt Jackson, Jackson]</p><p><b>Tenisačica iz Sjedinjenih Država koja je dominirala ženskim tenisom u 1920-ima i 1930-ima (1905-1998) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States tennis player who dominated women's tennis in the 1920s and 1930s (1905-1998) [Helen Wills, Helen Wills Moody, Moody]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) lijepa kći Zeusa i Lede koja je oteta od strane Pariza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the beautiful daughter of Zeus and Leda who was abducted by Paris [Helen]</p><p><b>Australski operski sopran (1861-1931) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian operatic soprano (1861-1931) [Dame Nellie Melba, Melba]</p><p><b>Američki operni sopran (1903-1972) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States operatic soprano (1903-1972) [Traubel]</p><p><b>Tenisačica iz Sjedinjenih Država koja je dominirala ženskim tenisom u 1920-ima i 1930-ima (1905-1998) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States tennis player who dominated women's tennis in the 1920s and 1930s (1905-1998) [Helen Newington Wills, Helen Wills Moody, Moody]</p><p><b>Tenisačica iz Sjedinjenih Država koja je dominirala ženskim tenisom u 1920-ima i 1930-ima (1905-1998) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States tennis player who dominated women's tennis in the 1920s and 1930s (1905-1998) [Helen Newington Wills, Helen Wills, Moody]</p><p><b>Glavni grad države Montana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capital of the state of Montana [capital of Montana]</p><p><b>rod američkih biljaka s cvijećem žute boje: škrgač (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of American herbs with flowers having yellow rays: sneezeweeds [genus Helenium]</p><p><b>Severnoamerička višegodišnja biljka s žutim cvijećem u kasno ljeto (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American perennial with bright yellow late summer flowers [autumn sneezeweed]</p><p><b>čvrsta višegodišnja biljka zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s cvjetnim glavama s spuštenicama narandžastih žutih zraka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stout perennial herb of western United States having flower heads with drooping orange-yellow rays [orange sneezeweed, owlclaws]</p><p><b>u južnoj Kaliforniji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sneezeweed of southwestern United States especially southern California [rosilla]</p><p><b>Alternativne klasifikacije za kaktus wrens (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> alternative classifications for the cactus wrens [Campylorhynchus, genus Campylorhynchus, genus Heleodytes]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na Sunce ili u blizini Sunca (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to or near the sun [heliacal]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na Sunce ili u blizini Sunca (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to or near the sun [heliac]</p><p><b>rod kornjače iz visoravni Guyane u Južnoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of pitcher plants of the Guiana Highlands in South America [genus Heliamphora]</p><p><b>Svaka biljka iz roda Helianthemum (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Helianthemum [sun rose, sunrose]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka iz istočne Sjedinjenih Država s ranim usamljenim žutim cvijećem, nakon čega slijede kasni bezcvetni cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of the eastern United States having early solitary yellow flowers followed by late petalless flowers [Crocanthemum canadense, frost-weed, frostweed, frostwort]</p><p><b>drvena višegodišnja biljka s žutim cvjetovima iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> woody yellow-flowered perennial of southeastern United States [rush rose]</p><p><b>suncokret</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Helianthus having large flower heads with dark disk florets and showy yellow rays [sunflower]</p><p><b>suncokret iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s uskim listovima i pronađen u močvarama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sunflower of eastern North America having narrow leaves and found in bogs [swamp sunflower]</p><p><b>Godišnji suncokreta uzgojen za silažu i za njegova sjemena koja su izvor ulja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual sunflower grown for silage and for its seeds which are a source of oil [common sunflower, mirasol]</p><p><b>vrlo visoka američka višegodišnja biljka iz središnje i istočne Sjedinjenih Država u Kanadi koja ima jestive korenje gomoljaste vrste (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very tall American perennial of central and the eastern United States to Canada having edible tuberous roots [Indian potato, giant sunflower, tall sunflower]</p><p><b>visoka višegodišnja biljka s nekoliko velikih cvjetnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall rough-leaved perennial with a few large flower heads [showy sunflower]</p><p><b>visoka višegodišnja biljka iz središnje Sjedinjenih Država do Kanade s zlatno žutim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall perennial of central United States to Canada having golden-yellow flowers [Maximilian's sunflower]</p><p><b>sličan običnom suncokrvu sa tankim obično razgranatim stabljikama uobičajenim u središnjim Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to the common sunflower with slender usually branching stems common in central United States [prairie sunflower]</p><p><b>visoka višegodišnja biljka s dlakavim stabljikama i lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall perennial with hairy stems and leaves [Jerusalem artichoke, Jerusalem artichoke sunflower, girasol]</p><p><b>pužasta oblika, spiralan, vijčani</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in the shape of a coil [coiling, spiral, spiraling, turbinate, volute, voluted, whorled]</p><p><b>veliki rod uglavnom afričkih i australijskih biljaka i grmova: vječni cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large genus of mostly African and Australian herbs and shrubs: everlasting flowers [genus Helichrysum]</p><p><b>Australska biljka naturalizirana u Španjolskoj s cvijećem od limune do tamno zlatnog boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian plant naturalized in Spain having flowers of lemon yellow to deep gold [golden everlasting, strawflower, yellow paper daisy]</p><p><b>grm s bijelim vletenim granama i vletenim listovima s mirisnim cvijećem koji formira dugačke spreje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub with white woolly branches and woolly leaves having fragrant flowers forming long sprays [Ozothamnus secundiflorus, cascade everlasting]</p><p><b>kopneni puževi uključujući obični jestivi pužev i neke štetočine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> land snails including the common edible snail and some pests [family Helicidae]</p><p><b>tuba koja se uvlači preko ramena glazbenika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tuba that coils over the shoulder of the musician [bombardon]</p><p><b>helikopter, vrtložnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an aircraft without wings that obtains its lift from the rotation of overhead blades [chopper, eggbeater, whirlybird]</p><p><b>rod grmova i malih stabala iz tropske Amerike i Azije s cilindričnim plodovima spiralno okrenutim jedan oko drugog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of shrubs and small trees of tropical America and Asia having cylindrical fruits spirally twisted around one another [genus Helicteres]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijski grm koji se često uzgaja zbog svojih dlakavih lišća i narandžastih cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian shrub often cultivated for its hairy leaves and orange-red flowers [nut-leaved screw tree]</p><p><b>rod spiralnih ili zakrivljenih ili ravnih aerobnih bakterija s zaobljenim krajevima i višestrukim flagelama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of helical or curved or straight aerobic bacteria with rounded ends and multiple flagella [genus Heliobacter]</p><p><b>vrsta vrste Heliobacter (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the type species of genus Heliobacter [H. pylori]</p><p><b>Sunce u središtu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the sun as the center</p><p><b>paralaks nebeskog tijela koristeći dvije točke u Zemljinoj orbiti oko Sunca kao osnovnu liniju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the parallax of a celestial body using two points in the earth's orbit around the sun as the baseline [annual parallax]</p><p><b>heliogram</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a message transmitted by means of the sun's rays</p><p><b>heliograf</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an apparatus for sending telegraphic messages by using a mirror to turn the sun's rays off and on</p><p><i>v.</i> signal by means of a mirror and the using the sun's rays</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an intaglio print produced by gravure [gravure, photogravure]</p><p><b>heliolatrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the worship of the sun [sun-worship]</p><p><b>heliometar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instrument used to measure the angular separation of two stars that are too far apart to be included in the field of view of an ordinary telescope</p><p><b>granicu koja označava rub sunčevog utjecaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the boundary marking the edge of the sun's influence</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih južnoafričkih biljaka i potgreblja uzgojenih za dugačke najozbiljnije stabljike svijetlo plavih cvijeća s bijelim očima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various South African herbs and subshrubs cultivated for long showy racemes of bright blue flowers with white eyes</p><p><b>bilo koji sjevernoamerički višegodišnji grm iz roda Heliopsis s velikim žutim cvjetovima nalik na margarine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any North American shrubby perennial herb of the genus Heliopsis having large yellow daisylike flowers [oxeye]</p><p><b>Stari bog sunca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) ancient god of the sun</p><p><b>heliosfera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the region inside the heliopause containing the sun and solar system</p><p><b>Terapeutsko izlaganje sunčevoj svjetlosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> therapeutic exposure to sunlight [insolation]</p><p><b>rod Noctuidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Noctuidae [genus Heliothis]</p><p><b>srednjo veličine, čije su ličinke kukuruzni ušni crvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized moth whose larvae are corn earworms [Heliothis zia]</p><p><b>larva noctitudnog molja, srednjo veličine, čije su ličinke kukuruzni ušni crvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> larva of a noctuid moth [corn earworm, cotton bollworm, tobacco budworm, tomato fruitworm, vetchworm]</p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized moth whose larvae are corn earworms [heliothis moth]</p><p><b>bradavka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> green chalcedony with red spots that resemble blood [bloodstone]</p><p><b>Odgovor na sunce. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an orienting response to the sun</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom masne mase ne većim od 10 kg, ali ne većim od 10 kg, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> duplicator consisting of a gelatin plate from which ink can be taken to make a copy [hectograph]</p><p><b>uglavnom slatkovodni protozoi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mostly freshwater protozoa [