aničena na određeno geografsko područje) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of illnesses caused by a viral infection (usually restricted to a specific geographic area) [VHF, haemorrhagic fever, viral haemorrhagic fever, viral hemorrhagic fever]</p><p><b>akutna zarazna bolest obilježena upalom pluća i infekcijom krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute infectious disease characterized by pneumonia and blood infection [pasteurellosis]</p><p><b>moždani udar uzrokovan puknutošću krvne žile u mozgu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stroke caused by the rupture of a blood vessel in the brain [haemorrhagic stroke]</p><p><b>Venozna oticanja vanjskog ili unutarnjeg analnog sphinctera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> venous swelling external or internal to the anal sphincter [haemorrhoid, piles]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko vena koje odlijevaju zidove analnog kanala i rektuma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several veins draining the walls of the anal canal and rectum [rectal vein, vena rectalis]</p><p><b>kirurški postupak za vezanje i uklanjanje hemoroida (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical procedure for tying hemorrhoids and excising them [haemorrhoidectomy]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena (CAS RN 1344-26-8) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a granular brown substance composed of ferric oxide [haemosiderin]</p><p><b>abnormalno odlaganje hemosiderina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal deposit of hemosiderin [haemosiderosis]</p><p><b>hemostaza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical procedure of stopping the flow of blood (as with a hemostat) [haemostasia, haemostasis, hemostasis]</p><p><b>hemostaza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical procedure of stopping the flow of blood (as with a hemostat) [haemostasia, haemostasis, hemostasia]</p><p><b>kirurški instrument koji zaustavlja krvarenje pritiskom na krvni žilac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a surgical instrument that stops bleeding by clamping the blood vessel [haemostat]</p><p><b>koji imaju tendenciju kontrolirati krvarenje kontrakcijom tkiva ili krvnih žila (MT)</b></