racters (1936-1990) [Jim Henson]</p><p><b>koji je u skladu s naprednim tokovima, koji vodi računa o naprednim strujanjima, koji vodi računa o naprednim strujanju</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> informed about the latest trends [hip, hip to]</p><p><b>grupa životinjskih DNK virusa uključujući viruse pataka i štakora i vjeveric i druge, kao i virus koji uzrokuje hepatitis B kod ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of animal DNA viruses including viruses of ducks and woodchucks and squirrels and others as well as the virus causing hepatitis B in humans</p><p><b>polisaharid proizveden u bazofilima (posebno u plućima i jetri) i koji inhibira aktivnost trombina u koagulaciji krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a polysaccharide produced in basophils (especially in the lung and liver) and that inhibits the activity of thrombin in coagulation of the blood [Lipo-Hepin, Liquaemin]</p><p><b>jetreni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous small green nonvascular plants of the class Hepaticopsida growing in wet places and resembling green seaweeds or leafy mosses [liverwort]</p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to or affecting the liver</p><p><b>arterije koje opskrbljuju jetru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> arteries that supply the liver [arteria hepatica]</p><p><b>koma koja se može pojaviti u teškim slučajevima bolesti jetre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coma that can occur in severe cases of liver disease</p><p><b>kanal koji ispušta žuč iz jetre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the duct that drains bile from the liver</p><p><b>bilo koji od pet režnja koji čine jetru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the five lobes forming the liver</p><p><b>kratka vena koja nosi krv u jetru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short vein that carries blood into the liver [portal, portal vein, vena portae]</p><p><b>obična tanjera iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common tanager of southwestern United States and Mexico [Piranga flava hepatica]</p><p><b>vena koja isuši jetru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vein that drains the liver [vena hepatica]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko biljaka roda Hepatica s tri-lobednim lišćama i bijelim ili ružičastim cvijećima u ranom proljeću, obična jetrena biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several plants of the genus Hepatica having three-lobed leaves and white or pinkish flowers in early spring [liverleaf]</p><p><i>n.</i> a common liverwort [Marchantia polymorpha]</p><p><b>Hepatovorti: obuhvaća red Anthocerotales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> liverworts: comprises orders Anthocerotales [Hepaticopsida, class Hepaticae, class Hepaticopsida]</p><p><b>Hepatovorti: obuhvaća red Anthocerotales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> liverworts: comprises orders Anthocerotales [Hepaticae, class Hepaticae, class Hepaticopsida]</p><p><b>hepatitis, upala jetre, žutica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the liver caused by a virus or a toxin</p><p><b>hepatitis A</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute but benign form of viral hepatitis caused by an RNA virus that does not persist in the blood serum and is usually transmitted by ingesting food or drink that is contaminated with fecal matter [infectious hepatitis]</p><p><b>virus koji uzrokuje hepatitis A (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the virus causing hepatitis A</p><p><b>hepatitis B</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute (sometimes fatal) form of viral hepatitis caused by a DNA virus that tends to persist in the blood serum and is transmitted by sexual contact or by transfusion or by ingestion of contaminated blood or other bodily fluids [serum hepatitis]</p><p><b>virusni hepatitis koji se klinički ne razlikuje od hepatitisa B, ali je uzrokovan jednostranim RNA virusom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a viral hepatitis clinically indistinguishable from hepatitis B but caused by a single-stranded RNA virus</p><p><b>ozbiljan oblik hepatitisa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a severe form of hepatitis [delta hepatitis]</p><p><b>hepatokarcinom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> carcinoma of the liver [hepatocellular carcinoma, hepatoma, malignant hepatoma]</p><p><b>Hepatocelularni karcinom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> carcinoma of the liver [hepatocarcinoma, hepatoma, malignant hepatoma]</p><p><b>vitamin b2</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that prevents skin lesions and weight loss [lactoflavin, ovoflavin, riboflavin, vitamin B2, vitamin G]</p><p><b>venski refluks koji se javlja kod kongestivnog zatajenja srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a venous reflux occurring in congestive heart failure</p><p><b>hepatolentikularna degeneracija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rare inherited disorder of copper metabolism [Wilson's disease]</p><p><b>hepatom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> carcinoma of the liver [hepatocarcinoma, hepatocellular carcinoma, malignant hepatoma]</p><p><b>nepravilno povećanje jetre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal enlargement of the liver [megalohepatia]</p><p><b>otrovno za jetru (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> toxic to the liver</p><p><b>bilo koji toksin koji utječe na jetru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any toxin that affects the liver</p><p><b>Američka filmska glumica koja se pojavila u mnogim filmovima s Spencer Tracy (1907-2003) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film actress who appeared in many films with Spencer Tracy (1907-2003) [Katharine Hepburn, Katharine Houghton Hepburn]</p><p><b>Hefest</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the lame god of fire and metalworking in ancient mythology [Hephaistos]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) bog vatre i metalurške obrade u drevnoj mitologiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the lame god of fire and metalworking in ancient mythology [Hephaestus]</p><p><b>sedam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cardinal number that is the sum of six and one [7, VII, septenary, septet, seven, sevener]</p><p><b>bezbojna kristalna sintetička masna kiselina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless crystalline synthetic fatty acid [margaric acid]</p><p><b>polugon sa sedam strana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a seven-sided polygon</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% masenog udjela, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless volatile highly 