ili osobna ili mješovita) koja se može naslijediti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any property (real or personal or mixed) that can be inherited</p><p><b>filozofsko učenje da je nasljednost važnija od okoliša u određivanju intelektualnog rasta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the philosophical doctrine that heredity is more important than environment in determining intellectual growth</p><p><b>naslijedan, naslijeđen, nasljedan, nasljedni, obiteljska povezanost</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring among members of a family usually by heredity [familial, genetic, inherited, transmissible, transmitted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> inherited or inheritable by established rules (usually legal rules) of descent [ancestral, patrimonial, transmissible]</p><p><b>nervni poremećaj u kasnom djetinjstvu i ranom odraslom dobu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nervous disorder of late childhood and early adulthood</p><p><b>bolest ili poremećaj koji se nasljeđuje genetski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease or disorder that is inherited genetically [congenital disease, genetic abnormality, genetic defect, genetic disease, genetic disorder, hereditary disease, inherited disease, inherited disorder]</p><p><b>bolest ili poremećaj koji se nasljeđuje genetski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease or disorder that is inherited genetically [congenital disease, genetic abnormality, genetic defect, genetic disease, genetic disorder, hereditary condition, inherited disease, inherited disorder]</p><p><b>oblik neuropatije koji može početi između djetinjstva i mlađe odrasle dobi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of neuropathy that can begin between childhood and young adulthood [Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease]</p><p><b>(genetika) osobine stečene biološkim nasljedstvom od roditelja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) attributes acquired via biological heredity from the parents [inheritance]</p><p><b>nasljednost, nasljedstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the biological process whereby genetic factors are transmitted from one generation to the next</p><p