ed to throw the image to the side where it can be viewed [off-axis reflector]</p><p><b>Sladnjak i filantrop iz Sjedinjenih Država koji je stvorio industrijski model grada Hershey, Pennsylvania, industrijski grad istočno od Harrisburga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States confectioner and philanthropist who created the model industrial town of Hershey, Pennsylvania [Milton Snavely Hershey]</p><p><i>n.</i> an industrial town to the east of Harrisburg</p><p><b>čokolada od mlijeka koju je napravila tvrtka Hershey. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bar of milk chocolate made by the Hershey company</p><p><b>okrug u južnoj Engleskoj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a county in southern England</p><p><b>Teutonska boginja plodnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Teutonic goddess of fertility [Nerthus]</p><p><b>herc, herc (hertz), jedinica za frekvenciju (Hz)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the unit of frequency [Hz, cps, cycle, cycle per second, cycles/second]</p><p><i>n.</i> German physicist who was the first to produce electromagnetic waves artificially (1857-1894) [Heinrich Hertz, Heinrich Rudolph Hertz]</p><p><i>n.</i> German physicist who with James Franck proved the existence of the stationary energy states postulated by Bohr (1887-1975) [Gustav Hertz, Gustav Ludwig Hertz]</p><p><b>fizičara Heinricha Hertza ili njegovog rada ili s njim povezanog. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the physicist Heinrich Hertz or his work</p><p><b>bivše ime za radio valove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former name for a radio wave</p><p><b>Kanadski fizičar (rođen u Njemačkoj) poznat po doprinosu razumijevanju strukture molekula (rođen 1904.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Canadian physicist (born in Germany) noted for contributions to understanding the structure of molecules (born in 1904) [Gerhard Herzberg]</p><p><b>drugi mjesec civilne godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the second month of the civil year</p><p><b>Heziod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek poet whose existing works describe rural life and the genealogies 