rests in eastern spiritual values (1877-1962) [Hermann Hesse]</p><p><b>hesenski, gumene Wellington čizme, gumene čizme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (19th century) a man's high tasseled boot [Hessian boot, Wellington, Wellington boot, jackboot]</p><p><b>gumene Wellington čizme, gumene čizme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (19th century) a man's high tasseled boot [Wellington, Wellington boot, hessian, jackboot]</p><p><b>mala muha čije ličinke oštećuju pšenicu i druga zrna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small fly whose larvae damage wheat and other grains [Mayetiola destructor]</p><p><b>granat u boji od žute do smeđe boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a garnet ranging in color from yellow to brown [cinnamon stone, essonite]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) boginja vatre i njenog vatre u drevnoj mitologiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the goddess of the hearth and its fire in ancient mythology</p><p><b>"Hit" je dialektalna varijanta riječi "heated" (to je varijanta riječi "hot") (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made warm or hot (`het' is a dialectal variant of `heated') [heated, heated up, het up]</p><p><b>uzbuđen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made warm or hot (`het' is a dialectal variant of `heated') [heated, heated up, het]</p><p><i>adj.</i> worked up emotionally by anger or excitement</p><p><b>Blatni plantazi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mud plantains [genus Heteranthera]</p><p><b>vodena biljka s žutim cvijećem u obliku zvijezde (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grassy-leaved North American aquatic plant with yellow star-shaped blossoms [mud plantain, water star grass]</p><p><b>Kategorija koja se koristi u nekim sustavima klasifikacije za razne bazidomicetne gljivice uključujući hrđave i smute (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> category used in some classification systems for various basidiomycetous fungi including rusts and smuts [subclass Heterobasidiomycetes]</p><p><b>peščani štakori (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sand rats [genus Heterocephalus]</p><p><b>s vrhom od 30 mm do 30 mm, ali ne više od 30 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> possessing a tail with the upper lobe larger than the lower and with the vertebral column prolonged into the upper lobe</p><p><b>repno pljuvače s nejednakim režnjevima u kojem se kralježnica okreće prema gore u veći režanj kao kod morskih pasa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tail fin with unequal lobes in which the vertebral column turns upward into the larger lobe as in sharks</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od 99,99% ili više, ali ne više od 99,99%, Prsten od više vrsta atoma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound containing a heterocyclic ring [heterocyclic, heterocyclic compound]</p><p><i>n.</i> a ring of atoms of more than one kind [heterocyclic ring]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od 99,99% ili više, ali ne više od 99,99%, s masenim udjelom ugljika od 0,01 do 0,01 mas.% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound containing a heterocyclic ring [heterocycle, heterocyclic compound]</p><p><i>adj.</i> containing a closed ring of atoms of which at least one is not a carbon atom</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od 99,99% ili više, ali ne više od 99,99% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound containing a heterocyclic ring [heterocycle, heterocyclic]</p><p><b>Prsten od više vrsta atoma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ring of atoms of more than one kind [heterocycle]</p><p><b>(ptičjih stopala) s prvim i drugim prstima okrenutim unazad, trećim i četvrtim naprijed (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of bird feet) having the first and second toes directed backward the third and fourth forward</p><p><b>ptičji stopala s prvim i drugim prstima svake noge usmjerene unazad, a treći i četvrti naprijed (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bird's foot having the first and second toes of each foot directed backward and the third and fourth forward</p><p><b>rod malih kolubridnih zmija koji sadrže sjevernoameričke zmije s kopitnim nosom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of small colubrid snakes containing the North American hognose snakes [genus Heterodon]</p><p><b>heterodoksan, inovjeran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by departure from accepted beliefs or standards [dissident, heretical]</p><p><b>krivovjerje, heterodoksija, neortodoksnost, nesvakidašnjost, neuobičajenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any opinions or doctrines at variance with the official or orthodox position [heresy, unorthodoxy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being unorthodox [unorthodoxy]</p><p><b>heterodinski</b></p><p><i>v.</i> combine (a radio frequency wave) with a locally generated wave of a different frequency so as to produce a new frequency equal to the sum or the difference between the two</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the beat produced by heterodyning two oscillations</p><p><b>oscilator čiji izlaz heterodineza s ulaznim radio signalima kako bi proizveo sumu i razliku tonova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oscillator whose output heterodynes with the incoming radio signal to produce sum and difference tones [local oscillator]</p><p><b>radio prijemnik koji kombinira lokalno generiranu frekvenciju s nosiocem frekvencije kako bi proizveo superzvučni signal koji se demodulira i pojačava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radio receiver that combines a locally generated frequency with the carrier frequency to produce a supersonic signal that is demodulated and amplified [superhet, superheterodyne receiver]</p><p><b>od parazita (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of parasites</p><p><b>heterogenitet, heterogenost, nejednakost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being diverse and not comparable in kind [heterogeneousness]</p><p><b>heterogen, mješovit, nespojiv, raznolik, raznorodni, raznovrstan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> consisting of elements that are not of the same kind or nature [heterogenous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> originating outside the body [heterogenous]</p><p><b>heterogen, mješovit, nespojiv, raznolik, raznorodni, raznovrstan (od &quot;heterogeneous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being diverse and not comparable in kind [heterogeneity]</p><p><b>heterogeneza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the alternation of two or more different forms in the life cycle of a plant or animal [alternation of generations, xenogenesis]</p><p><b>heterogen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> consisting of elements that are not of the same kind or nature [heterogeneous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> originating outside the body [heterogeneous]</p><p><b>Tkivo iz životinje jedne vrste koje se koristi kao privremeni presadak (kao u slučajevima teških opekotina) na pojedinca druge vrste (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tissue from an animal of one species used as a temporary graft (as in cases of severe burns) on an individual of another species [xenograft]</p><p><b>koji imaju više oblika gametoecija na istoj biljci (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having several forms of gametoecia on the same plant [polygamous, polyoicous]</p><p><b>sve žutozelenije alge s nejednakim trajanjem žlijezda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> all the yellow-green algae having flagella of unequal length [Chrysophyceae, class Chrysophyceae, class Heterokontae]</p><p><b>alge koje sadrže hlorofil a i obično c i žlijezde nejednakog dužine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> algae having chlorophyll a and usually c, and flagella of unequal lengths [division Heterokontophyta]</p><p><b>ne odgovarajući po strukturi ili evolucijskom podrijetlu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not corresponding in structure or evolutionary origin [heterological, heterologous]</p><p><b>ne odgovarajući po strukturi ili evolucijskom podrijetlu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not corresponding in structure or evolutionary origin [heterologic, heterologous]</p><p><b>ne odgovarajući po strukturi ili evolucijskom podrijetlu, koji su dobiveni od organizama različite ali srodne vrste (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not corresponding in structure or evolutionary origin [heterologic, heterological]</p><p><i>adj.</i> derived from organisms of a different but related species</p><p><b>(biologija) nedostatak usklađenosti naizgled sličnih dijelova tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) the lack of correspondence of apparently similar body parts</p><p><b>jedna vrsta: toyon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one species: toyon [genus Heteromeles]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije "Korišćenje" u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvođač proizvodi proizvode iz kategorije "Korišćenje" u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental evergreen treelike shrub of the Pacific coast of the United States having large white flowers and red berrylike fruits [Christmas berry, Christmasberry, Photinia arbutifolia, tollon, toyon]</p><p><b>(od insekta) koji prolazi nepune metamorfoze u kojima je nimfa u biti slična odrasloj i nema faze pupalnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of an insect) undergoing incomplete metamorphosis in which the nymph is essentially like the adult and there is no pupal stage [heterometabolous]</p><p><b>razvoj insekata s nepotpunom metamorfozom u kojoj nijedna pupalna faza ne prethodi zrelosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> development of insects with incomplete metamorphosis in which no pupal stage precedes maturity [heterometaboly]</p><p><b>(od insekta) koji prolazi nepune metamorfoze u kojima je nimfa u biti slična odrasloj i nema faze pupalnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of an insect) undergoing incomplete metamorphosis in which the nymph is essentially like the adult and there is no pupal stage [heterometabolic]</p><p><b>razvoj insekata s nepotpunom metamorfozom u kojoj nijedna pupalna faza ne prethodi zrelosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> development of insects with incomplete metamorphosis in which no pupal stage precedes maturity [heterometabolism]</p><p><b>mali glodari iz Novog svijeta koji se kopali poput miševa s pelenačima na obrazima i stražnjim udovima i repom prilagođenim skakanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small New World burrowing mouselike rodents with fur-lined cheek pouches and hind limbs and tail adapted to leaping [family Heteromyidae]</p><p><b>Dvije riječi su heteronimi ako se pišu na isti način, ali se razlikuju u izgovoru. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> two words are heteronyms if they are spelled the same way but differ in pronunciation</p><p><b>protutijelo pronađeno u krvi osobe koja pati od zarazne mononukleoze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antibody found in the blood of someone suffering from infectious mononucleosis [Forssman antibody, heterophile antibody]</p><p><b>krvni test za otkrivanje heterofilnih antitijela koja aglutiniraju ovčje crvene krvne stanice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blood test to detect heterophil antibodies that agglutinate sheep red blood cells</p><p><b>protutijelo pronađeno u krvi osobe koja pati od zarazne mononukleoze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antibody found in the blood of someone suffering from infectious mononucleosis [Forssman antibody, heterophil antibody]</p><p><b>(genetika) organizam ili stanica s brojem hromozoma koji nije parni višestruki broja haploidnih hromozoma za tu vrstu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) an organism or cell having a chromosome number that is not an even multiple of the haploid chromosome number for that species</p><p><b>stanje da je heteroploidna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of being heteroploid</p><p><b>prave bube (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> true bugs [suborder Heteroptera]</p><p><b>pravi insekti: insekti čija su prednja krila membranska, ali imaju kožne vrhove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> true bugs: insects whose forewings are membranous but have leathery tips</p><p><b>škrtovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tattlers [genus Heteroscelus]</p><p><b>Udaljenost od regije Pacifika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tattler of Pacific coastal regions [Polynesian tattler]</p><p><b>heteroseksizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> discrimination in favor of heterosexual and against homosexual people</p><p><b>heteroseksualac, heteroseksualan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person having a sexual orientation to persons of the opposite sex [heterosexual person, straight, straight person]</p><p><i>adj.</i> sexually attracted to members of the opposite sex</p><p><b>osoba koja ima seksualnu orijentaciju prema osobama suprotnog spola (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person having a sexual orientation to persons of the opposite sex [heterosexual, straight, straight person]</p><p><b>heteroseksualnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sexual attraction to (or sexual relations with) persons of the opposite sex [heterosexuality, straightness]</p><p><b>heteroseksualnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sexual attraction to (or sexual relations with) persons of the opposite sex [heterosexualism, straightness]</p><p><b>(genetika) sklonost ukrštenog organizma da ima kvalitete koje su superiornije od onih bilo kojeg roditelja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) the tendency of a crossbred organism to have qualities superior to those of either parent [hybrid vigor]</p><p><b>Uređaji za proizvodnju: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flatfishes: halibut [order Heterosomata, order Pleuronectiformes]</p><p><b>karakterizira heterospornost (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by heterospory</p><p><b>razvoj mikro i megaspora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the development of both microspores and megaspores</p><p><b>Ribe bez čeljusti s prednjim dijelom tijela prekrivenim kostnim pločama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct jawless fish with the anterior part of the body covered with bony plates</p><p><b>izumrla skupina rib bez čeljusti ili riboljubnih kičmenjaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct group of armored jawless fishes or fish-like vertebrate [suborder Heterostraci]</p><p><b>bilo kakvo abnormalno položaje organa tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any abnormal position of the organs of the body [transposition]</p><p><b>rod sjevernoameričkih biljaka s žutim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of yellow-flowered North American herbs [genus Heterotheca]</p><p><b>dlakava višegodišnja biljka s žutim cvjetnim glavama u granatiranim grmovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hairy perennial with yellow flower heads in branched clusters [Chrysopsis villos