ts long mucilaginous green pods used as basis for soups and stews [Abelmoschus esculentus, gumbo, lady's-finger, okra, okra plant]</p><p><b>Šumovi iz južne i zapadne Australije s bez- ili plitko-zubljenim listovima i ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> southern and western Australian shrub with unlobed or shallowly lobed toothed leaves and purple flowers [Radyera farragei, bush hibiscus]</p><p><b>Australsko stablo s kiselim lišće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree with acid foliage [sorrel tree]</p><p><b>grmljava biljka iz tropske Azije koja raste zbog žutih ili ružičastih do crvenokrasnih cvjetova koji liče na hibiskus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bushy herb of tropical Asia grown for its yellow or pink to scarlet blooms that resemble the hibiscus [Abelmoschus moschatus, abelmosk, musk mallow]</p><p><b>sjajan grm iz solenih močvara istočne Sjedinjenih Država s velikim ružičastom bojom cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> showy shrub of salt marshes of the eastern United States having large rose-colored flowers [common rose mallow, rose mallow, swamp mallow, swamp rose mallow]</p><p><b>Kineski grm ili malo stablo s bijelim ili ružičastim cvijećima koje se noću pretvaraju u tamno crveno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chinese shrub or small tree having white or pink flowers becoming deep red at night [Confederate rose, Confederate rose mallow, cotton rose]</p><p><b>Veliki naivni azijski grm ili malo stablo s velikim jednostrukom ili dvostrukom crvenom do duboko crvenom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large showy Asiatic shrub or small tree having large single or double red to deep-red flowers [China rose, Chinese hibiscus, Rose of China, shoe black, shoeblack plant]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijska rijetko trnasta godišnja biljka ili višegodišnji potgrm koji se široko uzgaja zbog svojih mesnih čaša koje se koriste u pite i žele i zbog svog vlakna bast (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian sparsely prickly annual herb or perennial subshrub widely cultivated for its fleshy calyxes used in tarts and jelly and for its bast fiber [Jamaica sorrel, red sorrel, roselle, rozelle, sorrel]</p><p><b>Azijski grm ili malo grmlje s najozbiljnije ruže ili ljubičaste ili bijele cvijeće u obliku zvona i obično s tri lobne lišće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic shrub or small shrubby tree having showy bell-shaped rose or purple or white flowers and usually three-lobed leaves [rose of Sharon]</p><p><b>grmlje koje se široko rasprostranjuje duž tropskih obala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby tree widely distributed along tropical shores [balibago, mahagua, mahoe, majagua, purau]</p><p><b>Jednogodišnje korovlje s prolaznim žutim ljubičastim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual weedy herb with ephemeral yellow purple-eyed flowers [black-eyed Susan, bladder ketmia, flower-of-an-hour, flowers-of-an-hour]</p><p><b>štucanje, štucati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) the state of having reflex spasms of the diaphragm accompanied by a rapid closure of the glottis producing an audible sound [hiccup, singultus]</p><p><i>v.</i> breathe spasmodically, and make a sound [hiccup]</p><p><b>dekorativne afričke grmlje ili planinarice s crvenim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental African shrub or climber with red flowers [Combretum bracteosum, hiccup nut]</p><p><b>štucati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) the state of having reflex spasms of the diaphragm accompanied by a rapid closure of the glottis producing an audible sound [hiccough, singultus]</p><p><i>v.</i> breathe spasmodically, and make a sound [hiccough]</p><p><b>dekorativne afričke grmlje ili planinarice s crvenim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental African shrub or climber with red flowers [Combretum bracteosum, hiccough nut]</p><p><b>seljačina, seljak, seljo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is not very intelligent or interested in culture [bumpkin, chawbacon, hayseed, rube, yahoo, yokel]</p><p><i>adj.</i> awkwardly simple and provincial [bumpkinly, rustic, unsophisticated]</p><