ate) [Eusebius Hieronymus, Eusebius Sophronius Hieronymus, Jerome, Saint Jerome, St. Jerome]</p><p><b>Nizozemski slikar (1450-1516) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch painter (1450-1516) [Bosch, Jerom Bos]</p><p><b>-Smiješno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affectedly genteel [grandiose, highfalutin, highfaluting, hoity-toity, la-di-da]</p><p><b>Američki pisac i vojnik koji je vodio prvi crni puk u vojsci Unije (1823-1911) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer and soldier who led the first Black regiment in the Union Army (1823-1911) [Thomas Higginson, Thomas Wentworth Storrow Higginson]</p><p><b>trgovati, cjenjkati se, cjenkati se, natezati se, pogađati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> wrangle (over a price, terms of an agreement, etc.) [chaffer, haggle, huckster]</p><p><b>u potpunom neredu., Na neuredan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in utter disorder [disorderly, hugger-mugger, jumbled, topsy-turvy]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a disordered manner [topsy-turvy]</p><p><b>jak, uzvišen, velik, visok, Visoki, jakom, velikim, visine, visinu, visoke, visokim, visoko, visokog, visoku</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lofty level or position or degree</p><p><i>n.</i> an air mass of higher than normal pressure</p><p><i>n.</i> a state of sustained elation</p><p><i>n.</i> a state of altered consciousness induced by alcohol or narcotics</p><p><i>n.</i> a high place [heights]</p><p><i>n.</i> a public secondary school usually including grades 9 through 12 [high school, highschool, senior high, senior high school]</p><p><i>n.</i> a forward gear with a gear ratio that gives the greatest vehicle velocity for a given engine speed [high gear]</p><p><i>adj.</i> greater than normal in degree or intensity or amount</p><p><i>adj.</i> (literal meaning) being at or having a relatively great or specific elevation or upward extension (sometimes used in combinations like `knee-high')</p><p><i>adj.</i> standing above others in quality or position [eminent]</p><p><i>adj.</i> used of sounds and voices [high-pitched]</p><