inal leech]</p><p><b>Hirundinidae</b></p><p><i>n.</i> swallows and martins [family Hirundinidae]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Hirundinidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Hirundinidae [genus Hirundo]</p><p><b>od Australije i Polinezije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of Australia and Polynesia [tree martin, tree swallow]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička lasica koja živi u kolonijama i gradi blatasti gnijezdo na liticama i zidovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American swallow that lives in colonies and builds bottle-shaped mud nests on cliffs and walls [cliff swallow]</p><p><b>Obična lasica iz Sjeverne Amerike i Europe koja gnijezda u stajama itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common swallow of North America and Europe that nests in barns etc. [barn swallow, chimney swallow]</p><p><b>hispanički, Hispanik, Hispanoamerikanac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an American whose first language is Spanish [Hispanic American, Spanish American]</p><p><i>adj.</i> related to a Spanish-speaking people or culture [Latino]</p><p><b>Amerikanci čiji je prvi jezik španjolski. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an American whose first language is Spanish [Hispanic, Spanish American]</p><p><b>Hispaniola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an island in the West Indies [Haiti, Hayti]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s otokom Hispaniola u Zapadnoj Indiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the West Indian island of Hispaniola</p><p><b>(od životinja ili biljaka) s tvrdim grubošću dlake ili četkica (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of animals or plants) having stiff coarse hairs or bristles</p><p><b>veliki hroničari sa tvrdom kosom iz prerija s kratkom travom u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large stiff-haired rodent of shortgrass prairies of United States [Perognathus hispidus]</p><p><b>bijesno protisnuti, izviždati, piskavi šum, pištati, psikanje, psikati, siktanje, siktati, zviždati, šištati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fricative sound (especially as an expression of disapproval) [fizzle, hissing, hushing, sibilation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a cry