on of monocytes and monoblasts in the blood [histiocytic leukemia, monoblastic leukaemia, monoblastic leukemia, monocytic leukaemia, monocytic leukemia]</p><p><b>leukemija koju karakteriše proliferacija monocita i monoblasta u krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leukemia characterized by the proliferation of monocytes and monoblasts in the blood [histiocytic leukaemia, monoblastic leukaemia, monoblastic leukemia, monocytic leukaemia, monocytic leukemia]</p><p><b>bolest krvi koju karakterizira abnormalno razmnožavanje makrofagova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blood disease characterized by an abnormal multiplication of macrophages</p><p><b>stanje u kojem stanice jednog tkiva mogu preživjeti u prisutnosti stanica drugog tkiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> condition in which the cells of one tissue can survive in the presence of cells of another tissue</p><p><b>obitelj od pedeset ili više gena na šestom ljudskom hromozomu koji kodiraju proteine na površini stanica i koji igraju ulogu u imunološkom odgovoru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of fifty or more genes on the sixth human chromosome that code for proteins on the surfaces of cells and that play a role in the immune response</p><p><b>histogram</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bar chart representing a frequency distribution</p><p><b>Neusklađenost u kojoj tkivo jedne osobe ne može biti preseljeno na drugu osobu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> incompatibility in which one person's tissue cannot be transplanted to another person</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s histologijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to histology [histological]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s histologijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to histology [histologic]</p><p><b>koji uključuju upotrebu histoloških ili histoloških tehnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> involving the use of histology or histological techniques</p><p><b>histolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anatomist who specializes in the microscopic study of animal tissues</p><p><b>histologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of biology that studies the microscopic structure of animal or plant tissues</p><p><b>Jednostavan protein koji sadrži uglavnom osnovne aminokiseline (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a simple protein containing mainly basic amino acids</p><p><b>povjesnik, historičar, povjesničar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is an authority on history and who studies it and writes about it [historiographer]</p><p><b>historijski, povijesne, povijesni, povijestan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to the past [historical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> important in history</p><p><b>godine, povijesno razdoblje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an era of history having some distinctive feature [age]</p><p><b>historijski, historijsko, povijesni, povijestan, povijesna, povijesne, povijesnog, povijesnoj, povijesnom, povesni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the study of history</p><p><i>adj.</i> having once lived or existed or taken place in the real world as distinct from being legendary</p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to the past [historic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> used of the study of a phenomenon (especially language) as it changes through time [diachronic]</p><p><b>Pisanje koje ima povijesnu vrijednost (za razliku od fikcije ili mita itd.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> writing having historical value (as opposed to fiction or myth etc.) [historical paper, historical record]</p><p><b>historijska lingvistika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of linguistic change [diachronic linguistics, diachrony]</p><p><b>Pisanje koje ima povijesnu vrijednost (za razliku od fikcije ili mita itd.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> writing having historical value (as opposed to fiction or myth etc.) [historical document, historical record]</p><p><b>Upotreba sadašnjeg vremena za opisivanje prošlih djela ili stanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of the present tense to describe past actions or states</p><p><b>Pisanje koje ima povijesnu vrijednost (za razliku od fikcije ili mita itd.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> writing having historical value (as opposed to fiction or myth etc.) [historical document, historical paper]</p><p><b>škola njemačkih ekonomista i pravnih filozofa iz 19. stoljeća koji su pokušali objasniti moderne ekonomske sustave u evolucijskim ili povijesnim terminima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school of 19th century German economists and legal philosophers who tried to explain modern economic systems in evolutionary or historical terms</p><p><b>povijesno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> throughout history</p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to history</p><p><b>historijski, historijsko, povijesni, povijestan, povijesna, povijesne, povijesnog, povijesnoj, povijesnom, povesni (od &quot;historical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of having in fact existed in the past</p><p><i>n.</i> significance owing to its history</p><p><b>historicizam, neostilovi, historizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a theory that social and cultural events are determined by history</p><p><b>historija, povijest, prošlost, anamneza, povijesno, povijesti, priča, prošlosti (od &quot;history&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an illustrious past [celebrated, storied]</p><p><b>historiograf, povjesničar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is an authority on history and who studies it and writes about it [historian]</p><p><b>historiografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a body of historical literature</p><p><i>n.</i> the writing of history</p><p><b>historija, povijest, prošlost, anamneza, povijesno, povijesti, priča, prošlosti, kronika, povijesna kronika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the aggregate of past events</p><p><i>n.</i> a record or narrative description of past events [account, chronicle, story]</p><p><i>n.</i> the discipline that records and interprets past events involving human beings</p><p><i>n.</i> the continuum of events occurring in succession leading from the past to the present and even into the future</p><p><i>n.</i> all that is remembered of the past as preserved in writing</p><p><b>akademski odjel odgovoran za podučavanje povijesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the academic depa