ator during World War II (1889-1945) [Adolf Hitler, Der Fuhrer]</p><p><b>o ili u vezi s ili sugeriše Adolf Hitler ili njegov nacistički režim u Njemačkoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or suggestive of Adolf Hitler or his Nazi regime in Germany</p><p><b>(od batera) bez udarca, bez bodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a batter) without a hit</p><p><i>adj.</i> having no points scores [goalless, pointless, scoreless]</p><p><b>plaćeni ubojica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a professional killer who uses a gun [gun, gun for hire, gunman, gunslinger, hired gun, hit man, shooter, torpedo, triggerman]</p><p><b>napadač, smečer, udarač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (baseball) a ballplayer who is batting [batsman, batter, slugger]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who hits [striker]</p><p><b>nailaženje, pogađanje, udaranje, udarac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of contacting one thing with another [hit, striking]</p><p><b>(bezbol) mjera udarača performanse (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (baseball) a measure of a batter's performance [batting average]</p><p><b>član drevnog naroda koji je naseljavao Anadoliju i sjevernu Siriju oko 2000 do 1200 pne., jezik Hetita i glavni jezik Anatolijanske skupine jezika, od ili u vezi s Hetitskim narodom ili njihovim jezikom ili kulturom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of an ancient people who inhabited Anatolia and northern Syria about 2000 to 1200 BC</p><p><i>n.</i> the language of the Hittites and the principal language of the Anatolian group of languages</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Hittite people or their language or culture</p><p><b>virus koji uzrokuje AIDS</b></p><p><i>n.</i> infection by the human immunodeficiency virus</p><p><i>n.</i> the virus that causes acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS) [human immunodeficiency virus]</p><p><b>košnica, prihvatiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a teeming multitude</p><p><i>n.</i> a man-made receptacle that houses a swarm of bees [beehive]</p><p><i>n.</i> a structure that provides a natural habitation for bees [bee