g a white deposit (especially on objects outside) [frost, hoar, rime]</p><p><b>srebrno-bijele boje, Velika starost (posebno siva ili bijela s godinama) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a silvery-white color [frostiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> great age (especially grey or white with age)</p><p><b>hrapav, promukao</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deep and harsh sounding as if from shouting or illness or emotion [gruff, husky]</p><p><b>hrapav, promukao (od &quot;hoarse&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a hoarse or husky voice [huskily]</p><p><b>promuklost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a throaty harshness [gruffness, huskiness]</p><p><b>sijed, star</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing characteristics of age, especially having grey or white hair [gray, gray-haired, gray-headed, grey, grey-haired, grey-headed, grizzly, hoar, white-haired]</p><p><i>adj.</i> ancient [rusty]</p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with fine whitish hairs or down [canescent]</p><p><b>Visoka europska godišnja s sivo-zelenim listovima i gustima glavama malih bijelih cvijeća s dlakavim čunjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall European annual with downy grey-green foliage and dense heads of small white flowers followed by hairy pods [Berteroa incana, hoary alyssum]</p><p><b>Visoka europska godišnja s sivo-zelenim listovima i gustima glavama malih bijelih cvijeća s dlakavim čunjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall European annual with downy grey-green foliage and dense heads of small white flowers followed by hairy pods [Berteroa incana, hoary alison]</p><p><b>Zapadni američki grmovi s bijelim filtim lišćem i žutim cvijećem koji postaju crveno-fijazloviti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> western American shrubs having white felted foliage and yellow flowers that become red-purple [Hazardia cana]</p><p><b>veliki sjevernoamerički planinski svizac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large North American mountain marmot [Marmota caligata, whistler, whistling marmot]</p><p><b>biljka iz roda Tephrosia s pinatnim listovima i bijelim ili ljubičastim cvijećem i ravnim dlakavim čunjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant of the genus Tephrosia having pinnate leaves and white or purplish flowers and flat hairy pods</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička godišnja ili dvogodišnja biljka s dugim mekanim dlakama na lišću, široko rasprostranjena višegodišnja biljka iz Starog svijeta, naturalizirana u Sjevernoj Americi, s fino dlakavim lištima i neosjetljivim bijelim mirisnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American annual or biennial with long soft hairs on the leaves [Plantago virginica]</p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed Old World perennial naturalized in North America having finely hairy leaves and inconspicuous white fragrant flowers [Plantago media]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka iz Sjeverne Amerike s sivo-dlakavim listovima koja daje crveni ili žuti pigment (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial North American plant with greyish hairy foliage yielding a red or yellow pigment [Indian paint, Lithospermum canescens]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički grm s bijeljastim lišćama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American shrub with whitish canescent leaves [Salix candida, sage willow]</p><p><b>Crested smrdljiva južnoamerička ptica čiji mladići imaju kandže na prvom i drugom prstima krila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crested ill-smelling South American bird whose young have claws on the first and second digits of the wings [Opisthocomus hoazin, hoactzin, stinkbird]</p><p><b>lukavstvo, obmana, prijevara, šala, nasamariti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something intended to deceive [dupery, fraud, fraudulence, humbug, put-on]</p><p><i>v.</i> subject to a playful hoax or joke [play a joke on, pull someone's leg]</p><p><b>lukavstvo, obmana, prijevara, šala (od &quot;hoax&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who plays practical jokes on others [cut-up, practical joker, prankster, tricker, trickster]</p><p><b>beskrajni vijak, ploča na kamin, polica, vilenjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (folklore) a small grotesque supernatural creature that makes trouble for human beings [goblin, hobgoblin]</p><p><i>n.</i> (folklore) fairies that are somewhat mischievous [brownie, elf, gremlin, imp, pixie, pixy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a hard steel edge tool used to cut gears</p><p><i>n.</i> a shelf beside an open fire where something can be kept warm</p><p><i>v.</i> cut with a hob</p><p><b>Hobart</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port and state capital of Tasmania</p><p><b>Engleski materijalista i politički filozof koji je zagovarao apsolutnu suverenost kao jedinu vrstu vlade koja bi mogla riješiti probleme uzrokovane sebičnošću ljudskih bića (1588. - 1679.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English materialist and political philosopher who advocated absolute sovereignty as the only kind of government that could resolve problems caused by the selfishness of human beings (1588-1679) [Thomas Hobbes]</p><p><b>hobit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary being similar to a person but smaller and with hairy feet</p><p><b>hramanje, šepati, šepanje, hramati, šepesati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shackle for the ankles or feet [fetter]</p><p><i>n.</i> the uneven manner of walking that results from an injured leg [hitch, limp]</p><p><i>v.</i> walk impeded by some physical limitation or injury [gimp, hitch, limp]</p><p><i>v.</i> hamper the action or progress of</p><p><i>v.</i> strap the foreleg and hind leg together on each side (of a horse) in order to keep the legs on the same side moving in unison [hopple]</p><p><b>dugačka suknja vrlo uska ispod koljena, nosena između 1910. i 1914. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long skirt very narrow below the knees, worn between 1910 and 1914</p><p><b>Neugodan, loše ponašan tinejdžer. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an awkward bad-mannered adolescent boy</p><p><b>hramanje, šepati (od &quot;hobble&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who has a limp and walks with a hobbling gait [limper]</p><p><b>poznati engleski kriketer (1882-1963) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> notable English cricketer (1882-1963) [John Berry Hobbs, Sir Jack Hobbs]</p><p><b>hobi, najmilija zabava, omiljena zabava, razonoda, sokol lastavičar, žurica</