ine]</p><p><i>n.</i> tarsal joint of the hind leg of hoofed mammals [hock-joint]</p><p><i>v.</i> leave as a guarantee in return for money [pawn, soak]</p><p><i>v.</i> disable by cutting the hock</p><p><b>Tarzalni zglob stražnje noge kopitavih sisavaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tarsal joint of the hind leg of hoofed mammals [hock]</p><p><b>hokej, igra hokeja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a game resembling ice hockey that is played on an open field [field hockey]</p><p><i>n.</i> a game played on an ice rink by two opposing teams of six skaters each who try to knock a flat round puck into the opponents' goal with angled hockey sticks [hockey game, ice hockey]</p><p><b>sastanak na kojem hokejci primaju posebnu procjenu i upute (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a meeting at which hockey players receive special evaluation and instruction</p><p><b>trener hokejaša. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coach of hockey players</p><p><b>igra koju igraju na klizalištu dvije protivničke ekipe od šest klizara koje pokušavaju udarati ravnu okruglu puk u protivnički gol sa uglovljenim hokejskim štapovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a game played on an ice rink by two opposing teams of six skaters each who try to knock a flat round puck into the opponents' goal with angled hockey sticks [hockey, ice hockey]</p><p><b>liga hokejaških timova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a league of hockey teams</p><p><b>sportista koji igra hokej. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an athlete who plays hockey [ice-hockey player]</p><p><b>vulkanizirani gumeni disk prečnika 3 inča koji se koristi umjesto lopte u hokeju na ledu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vulcanized rubber disk 3 inches in diameter that is used instead of a ball in ice hockey [puck]</p><p><b>sezona kada se igra hokej (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the season when hockey is played</p><p><b>klizanje na ledu za igranje hokeja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ice skate worn for playing hockey</p><p><b>sportski alat koji se sastoji od zakrivljenog ili uglog štapova koje hokejci koriste za pomicanje kru