on, toot]</p><p><i>v.</i> use the horn of a car [claxon]</p><p><i>v.</i> cry like a goose [cronk]</p><p><i>v.</i> eject the contents of the stomach through the mouth [barf, be sick, cast, cat, chuck, disgorge, puke, purge, regorge, regurgitate, retch, sick, spew, spue, throw up, upchuck, vomit, vomit up]</p><p><b>gakati, trubiti (od &quot;honk&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a driver who causes his car's horn to make a loud honking sound</p><p><i>n.</i> informal terms for the nose [beak, hooter, nozzle, schnoz, schnozzle, snoot, snout]</p><p><i>n.</i> common greyish-brown wild goose of North America with a loud, trumpeting call [Branta canadensis, Canada goose, Canadian goose]</p><p><b>(Slang) uvredljiva imena za bijelca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (slang) offensive names for a White man [honkie, honky, whitey]</p><p><b>(Slang) uvredljiva imena za bijelca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (slang) offensive names for a White man [honkey, honky, whitey]</p><p><b>(Slang) uvredljiva imena za bijelca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (slang) offensive names for a White man [honkey, honkie, whitey]</p><p><b>jeftini klub za piće i ples. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cheap drinking and dancing establishment [barrelhouse]</p><p><b>jeftini loš glasni noćni klub ili plesna dvorana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cheap disreputable nightclub or dance hall [dive]</p><p><b>Glavni i najveći grad Havaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Hawaii [Hawaiian capital, capital of Hawaii]</p><p><b>čast, obraz, počast, poštovanje, prihvatiti, slava, akolada, lovorike, nagrada, priznanje, east, poeast, uvažavanje, štovanje, honorirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tangible symbol signifying approval or distinction [accolade, award, honour, laurels]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being honored [honour, laurels]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being honorable and having a good name [honour]</p><p><i>n.</i> a woman's virtue or chastity [honour, pureness, purity]</p><p><i>v.</i> bestow honor or rewards upon [honour, reward]</p><p><i>v.</i> show respect towards [abide by, honour, observe, respect]</p><p><i>v.</i> accept as pay [honour]</p><p><b>pratnja za uglednog gosta ili za lijes na vojnom sprovodu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an escort for a distinguished guest or for the casket at a military funeral [guard of honor]</p><p><b>Stara tradicija koja se još uvijek ponekad održava. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient tradition still sometimes observed</p><p><b>sustav ponašanja u kojem se vjeruje da sudionici neće nepristojno iskoristiti druge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of conduct in which participants are trusted not to take unfair advantage of others</p><p><b>cijenjen, čestit, dostojan, uvažen, dobar</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not disposed to cheat or defraud [honest]</p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of being honored [honourable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> adhering to ethical and moral principles [ethical, honourable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> deserving of esteem and respect [estimable, good, respectable]</p><p><b>otpušten iz oružanih snaga s pohvalnim dosjeom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a discharge from the armed forces with a commendable record</p><p><b>službeno priznanje zasluga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an official recognition of merit [mention]</p><p><b>cijenjen, čestit, dostojan, uvažen (od &quot;honorable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of deserving honor or respect [honourableness]</p><p><b>časno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an honorable manner [uprightly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> with honor [honourably]</p><p><b>honorar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fee paid for a nominally free service</p><p><b>naslovni, počasan, počasni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> given as an honor without the normal duties</p><p><b>stepen koji se dodjeljuje u čast primatelja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a degree conferred to honor the recipient [honoris causa]</p><p><b>institucija za unapređenje umjetnosti ili znanosti ili književnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an institution for the advancement of art or science or literature [academy]</p><p><b>Franc