re patients receive treatment [infirmary]</p><p><i>n.</i> a medical institution where sick or injured people are given medical or surgical care</p><p><b>muškarac koji radi u bolnici i koji ima opće dužnosti koje ne uključuju liječenje pacijenata. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a male hospital attendant who has general duties that do not involve the medical treatment of patients [orderly]</p><p><b>Jednostavan krevet s okvirom u tri dijela tako da se glava ili sredina ili stopala mogu podići prema potrebi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a single bed with a frame in three sections so the head or middle or foot can be raised as required</p><p><b>stavljanje u bolničku bolnicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> placing in medical care in a hospital [hospitalisation, hospitalization]</p><p><b>kapelan u bolnici. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chaplain in a hospital</p><p><b>stopa zaposlenosti bolnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> occupancy rate for hospitals</p><p><b>soba u bolnici za brigu o pacijentima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a room in a hospital for the care of patients</p><p><b>bolnički brod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ship built to serve as a hospital</p><p><b>vojni vlak izgrađen za prevoz ranjenih vojnika u bolnicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a military train built to transport wounded troops to a hospital</p><p><b>bolnički odjel</b></p><p><i>n.</i> block forming a division of a hospital (or a suite of rooms) shared by patients who need a similar kind of care [ward]</p><p><b>bolničko liječenje, hospitalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> placing in medical care in a hospital [hospital care, hospitalization]</p><p><b>primati u bolnicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> admit into a hospital [hospitalize]</p><p><b>gostoljubivost, gostoljubivosti, gostoljublje, gostoprimstvo, gostoprimstvom, hotelijerstvo, gostoljubivošću, srdačan prijem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> kindness in welcoming guests or strangers [cordial reception]</p><p><b>bolničko liječenje, hospitalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a period of time when you are confined to a h