ic in central Europe [Magyarorszag, Republic of Hungary]</p><p><b>glad, gladi, gladovati, glađu, čeznuti, željeti, žuditi, žudjeti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a physiological need for food [hungriness]</p><p><i>n.</i> strong desire for something (not food or drink) [hungriness, thirst, thirstiness]</p><p><i>v.</i> feel the need to eat</p><p><i>v.</i> have a craving, appetite, or great desire for [crave, lust, starve, thirst]</p><p><i>v.</i> be hungry [famish, starve]</p><p><b>prosvjed ili demonstracija nezaposlenih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a march of protest or demonstration by the unemployed</p><p><b>nezaposlena osoba koja učestvuje u maršu gladi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unemployed person who participates in a hunger march</p><p><b>štrajk glađu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a voluntary fast undertaken as a means of protest</p><p><b>gladan, gladan (biti), natašte (od &quot;hungry&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in the manner of someone who is very hungry [ravenously]</p><p><b>nostalgija, čežnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a physiological need for food [hunger]</p><p><i>n.</i> prolonged unfulfilled desire or need [longing, yearning]</p><p><i>n.</i> strong desire for something (not food or drink) [hunger, thirst, thirstiness]</p><p><b>gladan, gladan (biti), natašte</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> feeling hunger</p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually followed by `for') extremely desirous [athirst, thirsty]</p><p><b>velika kriška, veliki koma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a well-built sexually attractive man</p><p><i>n.</i> a large piece of something without definite shape [lump]</p><p><b>čučati, čučnuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> sit on one's heels [crouch, hunker down, scrunch, scrunch up, squat]</p><p><b>čučati, čučnuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> sit on one's heels [crouch, hunker, scrunch, scrunch up, squat]</p><p><i>v.</i> take shelter</p><p><i>v.</i> hold stubbornly to a position</p><p><b>član Siouan naroda koji je sastavio podjelu Teton Sioux i koji je ranije živio u zapadnoj Dakotas, Siouanski jezik kojim govore Hunkpapa. (MT)</b></