ljaka i malih grmova s bijelim ili ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of herbs and small shrubs with white or purple flowers [genus Hybanthus]</p><p><b>hibrid, hibridan, hibridni, križan, melez, rašljasti sklop</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a word that is composed of parts from different languages (e.g., `monolingual' has a Greek prefix and a Latin root) [loan-blend, loanblend]</p><p><i>n.</i> a composite of mixed origin</p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) an organism that is the offspring of genetically dissimilar parents or stock [cross, crossbreed]</p><p><i>adj.</i> produced by crossbreeding [intercrossed]</p><p><b>hibridi Petunia axillaris i Petunia integrifolia: složena skupina petunija s jednim ili dvostrukim cvijećem u boji od bijelo do ljubičasto (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hybrids of Petunia axillaris and Petunia integrifolia: a complex group of petunias having single or double flowers in colors from white to purple [Petunia hybrida]</p><p><b>bilo koji od brojnih hibridnih begonija s gomoljastim korijenima i cvjetovima različitih boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous hybrid begonias having tuberous roots and variously colored flowers [Begonia tuberhybrida]</p><p><b>(genetika) sklonost ukrštenog organizma da ima kvalitete koje su superiornije od onih bilo kojeg roditelja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) the tendency of a crossbred organism to have qualities superior to those of either parent [heterosis]</p><p><b>križanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) the act of mixing different species or varieties of animals or plants and thus to produce hybrids [cross, crossbreeding, crossing, hybridization, hybridizing, interbreeding]</p><p><b>hibridizirati, križati, miješati, ukrštati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> breed animals or plants using parents of different races and varieties [cross, crossbreed, hybridize, interbreed]</p><p><b>hibridizacija, križanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) the act of mixing different species or varieties of animals or plants and thus to produce hybrids [cross, crossbreeding, crossing, hybridisation, hybridizing, interbreeding]</p><p><b>hibridizirati, križati, miješati, ukrštati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> breed animals or plants using parents of different races and varieties [cross, crossbreed, hybridise, interbreed]</p><p><b>križanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) the act of mixing different species or varieties of animals or plants and thus to produce hybrids [cross, crossbreeding, crossing, hybridisation, hybridization, interbreeding]</p><p><b>hibridna stanica nastala fuzijom limfocita i tumorske stanice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hybrid cell resulting from the fusion of a lymphocyte and a tumor cell</p><p><b>bilo koji od lijekova za liječenje epilepsije koji se koriste u grupi protiv- konvulzivnih lijekova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a group of anticonvulsant drugs used in treating epilepsy</p><p><b>pore koji izlijevaju vodu na površinu ili rubom lišća viših biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pore that exudes water on the surface or margin of a leaf of higher plants [water pore, water stoma]</p><p><b>cista ispunjena tekućinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cyst filled with liquid</p><p><b>U slučaju da se ne provodi ispitivanje, ispitivanje se može provesti u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 2. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> infestation with larval echinococci (tapeworms) [echinococcosis, hydatidosis]</p><p><b>abnormalnost tijekom trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormality during pregnancy [hydatidiform mole, molar pregnancy]</p><p><b>abnormalnost tijekom trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormality during pregnancy [hydatid mole, molar pregnancy]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se ne provodi ispitivanje, ispitivanje se može provesti u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 2. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> infestation with larval echinococci (tapeworms) [echinococcosis, hydatid disease]</p><p><b>grad u južnom Pakistanu na rijeci Indusu, grad u južnom središnjem Indiji u Andhra Pradešu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in southern Pakis