apija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the internal and external use of water in the treatment of disease [hydropathy]</p><p><b>akumuliranje tekućine u pleuralnoj šupljini (prostor između pluća i zidova prsa) često uzrokovano bolešću srca ili bubrega. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> accumulation of fluid in the pleural cavity (the space between the lungs and the walls of the chest) often resulting from disease of the heart or kidneys</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,25% ili više, ali ne više od 0,25%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing combined water (especially water of crystallization as in a hydrate) [hydrated]</p><p><b>hidroksid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound of an oxide with water [hydrated oxide]</p><p><i>n.</i> a chemical compound containing the hydroxyl group</p><p><b>anion OH koji ima jedan kisik i jedan vodik atom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the anion OH having one oxygen and one hydrogen atom [hydroxyl ion]</p><p><b>hidroksi</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being or containing a hydroxyl group</p><p><b>bilo koja kiselina koja ima hidroksilne grupe osim hidroksilne skupine u samoj kiselini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any acid that has hydroxyl groups in addition to the hydroxyl group in the acid itself</p><p><b>translucentno kristalno jedinjenje koje se nalazi u šećernjoj trsci i šećernjoj repe te nezrelim grožđama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a translucent crystalline compound found in sugar cane and sugar beets and unripe grapes [glycolic acid, glycollic acid]</p><p><b>od kiseline, u obliku bijeli-toxicnog kristalnog derivata benzena, rastvorljivog u bijeloj boji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic white soluble crystalline acidic derivative of benzene [carbolic acid, oxybenzene, phenol, phenylic acid]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% masenog udjela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crystalline derivative of benzoic acid</p><p><b>hidroxidirektiv masne kiseline (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hydroxy derivative of butyric acid [oxybutyric acid]</p><p><b>antiinflamatorni lijek (t