n ovipositor specialized for stinging or piercing [hymenopter, hymenopteran, hymenopteron]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka s tuftovanim bazalnim lištima i kratkim stabljikama bez lišća s jednom žutom cvjetnom glavom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial having tufted basal leaves and short leafless stalks each bearing a solitary yellow flower head [Tetraneuris acaulis, stemless hymenoxys]</p><p><b>bijela kosa sa perjavim lišcima i nekoliko čvrstih stabljika s posebno lijepim jednim velikim žutim cvjetnim glavom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> whitish hairy plant with featherlike leaves and a few stout stems each bearing an especially handsome solitary large yellow flower head [Tetraneuris grandiflora, alpine sunflower, old man of the mountain]</p><p><b>(etnički slur) uvredljiv izraz za Židove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (ethnic slur) offensive term for a Jew [kike, sheeny, yid]</p><p><b>crkvena pjesma, himna, himan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a song of praise (to God or to a saint or to a nation) [anthem]</p><p><i>v.</i> sing a hymn</p><p><i>v.</i> praise by singing a hymn</p><p><b>pjesmopisac koji sadrži zbirku himni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a songbook containing a collection of hymns [hymnary, hymnbook]</p><p><b>pjesmopisac koji sadrži zbirku himni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a songbook containing a collection of hymns [hymnal, hymnbook]</p><p><b>pjesmopisac koji sadrži zbirku himni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a songbook containing a collection of hymns [hymnal, hymnary]</p><p><b>Pjevanje psalma ili himne. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of singing psalms or hymns [psalmody]</p><p><b>najraniji fosilnih vodozemljana ikada pronađen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> earliest fossil amphibian ever found [genus Hynerpeton]</p><p><b>fosilni amfibiji devonskog doba s dobro razvijenim prednjim udovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fossil amphibian of the Devonian having well-developed forelimbs</p><p><b>U-oblikna kost na dnu jezika koja podržava mišiće jezika, od ili u vezi s hyoidnom kosom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i