ivač Društva Isusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Spaniard and Roman Catholic theologian and founder of the Society of Jesus [Loyola, Saint Ignatius of Loyola, St. Ignatius of Loyola]</p><p><b>ognjen, vatren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> produced under conditions involving intense heat [pyrogenic, pyrogenous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> produced by the action of fire or intense heat [eruptive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> like or suggestive of fire [fiery]</p><p><b>Skamena stijena formirana tvrdom topljenom magmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rock formed by the solidification of molten magma</p><p><b>može emitirati iskre ili izgorjeti u plamen (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> can emit sparks or burst into flame</p><p><b>divlji oganj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pale light sometimes seen at night over marshy ground [friar's lantern, jack-o'-lantern, will-o'-the-wisp]</p><p><i>n.</i> an illusion that misleads [will-o'-the-wisp]</p><p><b>upaljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of burning [burnable, ignitible]</p><p><b>paliti, sijati se, upaliti, upaliti se, zapaliti, zažariti, buknuti, paliti se, planuti, raspaliti se, raspaljivati se, zapaliti se, rasplamsati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to start burning [light]</p><p><i>v.</i> start to burn or burst into flames [catch fire, combust, conflagrate, erupt, take fire]</p><p><i>v.</i> arouse or excite feelings and passions [fire up, heat, inflame, stir up, wake]</p><p><i>v.</i> start or maintain a fire in [fire, light]</p><p><b>zapalio (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> set afire [enkindled, kindled]</p><p><b>upaljač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance used to ignite or kindle a fire [ignitor, lighter]</p><p><i>n.</i> a device for lighting or igniting fuel or charges or fires [ignitor, light, lighter]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of burning [burnable, ignitable]</p><p><b>paljenje, zapaljenje, zažarivanje, loženje, potpala, potpaljivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of initiating combustion or catching fire</p><p><i>n.</i> the mechanism that ignites