g born to parents who were not married [bar sinister, bastardy]</p><p><i>n.</i> unlawfulness by virtue of not being authorized by or in accordance with law</p><p><b>bespravan, nelegitiman, nelegitimni, nevaljan, nezakonit, protupravan, vanbračan, vanbračni, ilegalan, nedopušten</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the illegitimate offspring of unmarried parents [bastard, by-blow, illegitimate child, love child, whoreson]</p><p><i>adj.</i> contrary to or forbidden by law [illicit, outlaw, outlawed, unlawful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of marriages and offspring</p><p><b>kopile</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the illegitimate offspring of unmarried parents [bastard, by-blow, illegitimate, love child, whoreson]</p><p><b>Nezakonito poduzimanje (kao što su iznuđivanje ili prijevara ili trgovina drogom ili prostitucija) obavljeno u svrhu ostvarivanja profita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an illegal enterprise (such as extortion or fraud or drug peddling or prostitution) carried on for profit [fraudulent scheme, racket]</p><p><b>bespravan, nelegitiman, nelegitimni, nevaljan, nezakonit, protupravan, vanbračan, vanbračni (od &quot;illegitimate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a manner disapproved or not allowed by custom [illicitly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> of biological parents not married to each other [out of wedlock]</p><p><b>neliberalan, neotesan, neprosvijećen, ograničen, škrt, uskogrudan, zaostao</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> narrow-minded about cherished opinions [intolerant]</p><p><b>neotesanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition not to be liberal (generous) with money</p><p><b>neliberalan, neotesan, neprosvijećen, ograničen, škrt, uskogrudan, zaostao (od &quot;illiberal&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a narrow-minded manner [intolerantly]</p><p><b>nedopušten, nedopuštena, nedozvoljen, nezakonit, protuzakonit, zabranjen, ilegalan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> contrary to accepted morality (especially sexual morality) or convention</p><p><i>adj.</i> contrary to or forbidden by law [illegitimate, outlaw, outlawed, unlawful]</p><p><b>i