združivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> mix together different elements [blend, coalesce, combine, commingle, conflate, flux, fuse, meld, merge, mix]</p><p><b>nepokretan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not capable of movement or of being moved</p><p><i>adj.</i> securely fixed in place [fast, firm]</p><p><b>fiksiranje (kao što je odlitak od gips) dijela tijela kako bi se potaknulo pravilno iscjeljivanje, Čin ograničavanja kretanja ili nemogućnosti kretanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fixation (as by a plaster cast) of a body part in order to promote proper healing [immobilization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of limiting movement or making incapable of movement [immobilization, immobilizing]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka,, da se drži ili spriječi kretanje, učiniti bespomoćnim., (aktiva) pretvoriti u osnovni kapital, (i) zabraniti pretvaranje ili korištenje (imovine), uzrok da se ne može kretati (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> hold as reserve or withdraw from circulation [immobilize]</p><p><i>v.</i> to hold fast or prevent from moving [immobilize, pin, trap]</p><p><i>v.</i> make defenseless [immobilize]</p><p><i>v.</i> convert (assets) into fixed capital [immobilize]</p><p><i>v.</i> prohibit the conversion or use of (assets) [block, freeze, immobilize]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be unable to move [immobilize]</p><p><b>nepokretnost, nepomičnost, ukipljenost, ukočenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> remaining in place [fixedness, stationariness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of not moving</p><p><b>imobilizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fixation (as by a plaster cast) of a body part in order to promote proper healing [immobilisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of limiting movement or making incapable of movement [immobilisation, immobilizing]</p><p><b>povlačiti novac iz opticaja, učiniti nepokretnim, učvrstiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> hold as reserve or withdraw from circulation [immobilise]</p><p><i>v.</i> to hold fast or prevent from moving [immobilise, pin, trap]</p><p><i>v.</i> make defenseless [immobilise]</p><p><i>v.</i> convert (assets) into fixed capital [immobilise]</p><p><i>v.</i> prohibit the conversion or use of (assets) [block, freeze, immobilise]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be unable to move [immobilise]</p><p><b>povlačiti novac iz opticaja, učiniti nepokretnim, učvrstiti (od &quot;immobilize&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of limiting movement or making incapable of movement [immobilisation, immobilization]</p><p><b>neumjeren, pretjeran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> beyond reasonable limits</p><p><b>neumjeren, pretjeran (od &quot;immoderate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without moderation</p><p><i>adv.</i> to a degree that exceeds the bounds or reason or moderation [unreasonably]</p><p><b>neumjerenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being excessive and lacking in moderation [immoderation]</p><p><b>pretjerivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being excessive and lacking in moderation [immoderateness]</p><p><b>nepristojan, neskroman</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing an exaggerated opinion of your importance, ability, etc</p><p><i>adj.</i> offending against sexual mores in conduct or appearance</p><p><b>nepristojan, neskroman (od &quot;immodest&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without modesty</p><p><b>nepristojnost, neskromnost, egzibicionizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being vain and conceited</p><p><i>n.</i> the perverse act of exposing and attracting attention to your own genitals [exhibitionism]</p><p><b>žrtvovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> offer as a sacrifice by killing or by giving up to destruction</p><p><b>žrtva, žrtvovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> killing or offering as a sacrifice</p><p><b>nećudoredan, nemoralan, amoralan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deliberately violating accepted principles of right and wrong</p><p><i>adj.</i> not adhering to ethical or moral principles [base]</p><p><b>nećudorednost, nemoral, nemoralnost, nećudoređe, razvratnost, hudoba, iskvarenost, pokvarenost, zlo, zloća, zločestoća</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of not being in accord with standards of right or good conduct</p><p><i>n.</i> morally objectionable behavior [evil, iniquity, wickedness]</p><p><b>nemoralno, razvratno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without regard for morality [amorally]</p><p><b>besmrtan, besmrtnik, bog, božanstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person (such as an author) of enduring fame</p><p><i>n.</i> any supernatural being worshipped as controlling some part of the world or some aspect of life or who is the personification of a force [deity, divinity, god]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not subject to death</p><p><b>komemorirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be or provide a memorial to a person or an event [commemorate, immortalize, memorialise, memorialize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make famous forever [eternalise, eternalize, eternise, eternize, immortalize]</p><p><b>besmrtnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality or state of being immortal</p><p><i>n.</i> perpetual life after death</p><p><b>učiniti besmrtnim, komemorirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be or provide a memorial to a person or an event [commemorate, immortalise, memorialise, memorialize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make famous forever [eternalise, eternalize, eternise, eternize, immortalise]</p><p><b>smilje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mostly widely cultivated species of everlasting flowers having usually purple flowers [Xeranthemum annuum]</p><p><b>(sporama ili mikroorganizmima) koji se ne mogu kretati (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of spores or microorganisms) not capable of movement [nonmotile]</p><p><b>ne može se kretati (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lacking an ability to move</p><p><b>nepokretnost, nepomičnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> not capable of being moved or rearranged [immovableness]</p><p><b>nepokolebljiv, nepokretan, nekretnina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> property consisting of houses and land [real estate, real property, realty]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not able or intended to be moved [immoveable, stabile, unmovable]</p><p><b>od tkanine prepunene supstancom (npr. gipsom Pariza) koja se ubrzo nakon nanošenja tvrdi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bandage of cloth impregnated with a substance (e.g., plaster of Paris) that hardens soon after it is applied</p><p><b>nepokretnost, nepomičnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> not capable of being moved or rearranged [immovability]</p><p><b>Tako da ne mogu da se pomaknem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> so as to be incapable of moving</p><p><b>ne može se premjestiti ili nije namijenjen za premještanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not able or intended to be moved [immovable, stabile, unmovable]</p><p><b>imun, nepovrediv, otporan, slobodan, zaštićen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is immune to a particular infection</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the condition of immunity</p><p><i>adj.</i> secure against</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or conferring immunity (to disease or infection) [resistant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually followed by `to') not affected by a given influence</p><p><b>(medicinski) osoba (ili životinja) koja ima neki patogen na koji je imuna, ali koji ga može prenijeti na druge. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) a person (or animal) who has some pathogen to which he is immune but who can pass it on to others [carrier]</p><p><b>imunoglobulina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a class of proteins produced in lymph tissue in vertebrates and that function as antibodies in the immune response [Ig, immune globulin, immune serum globulin, immunoglobulin]</p><p><b>imunoglobulina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a class of proteins produced in lymph tissue in vertebrates and that function as antibodies in the immune response [Ig, immune gamma globulin, immune serum globulin, immunoglobulin]</p><p><b>imunosna reakcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bodily defense reaction that recognizes an invading substance (an antigen: such as a virus or fungus or bacteria or transplanted organ) and produces antibodies specific against that antigen [immune response, immunologic response]</p><p><b>imuni odgovor, imuni odziv, imunološki odgovor, imunosni odgovor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bodily defense reaction that recognizes an invading substance (an antigen: such as a virus or fungus or bacteria or transplanted organ) and produces antibodies specific against that antigen [immune reaction, immunologic response]</p><p><b>imunoglobulina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a class of proteins produced in lymph tissue in vertebrates and that function as antibodies in the immune response [Ig, immune gamma globulin, immune globulin, immunoglobulin]</p><p><b>lijek koji smanjuje normalni imunološki odgovor tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that lowers the body's normal immune response [immunosuppressant, immunosuppressive, immunosuppressive drug, immunosuppressor]</p><p><b>imuni sustav, imunološki sustav, obrambeni sustav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system (including the thymus and bone marrow and lymphoid tissues) that protects the body from foreign substances and pathogenic organisms by producing the immune response</p><p><b>Čin stvaranja imuniteta (posebno vakciniranjem) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making immune (especially by inoculation) [immunization]</p><p><b>cijepiti, imunizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> law: grant immunity from prosecution [immunize]</p><p><i>v.</i> perform vaccinations or produce immunity in by inoculation [immunize, inoculate, vaccinate]</p><p><b>ako su postali nesposobni za bolest (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having been rendered unsusceptible to a disease [immunized, vaccinated]</p><p><b>imunitet, imunost, oslobođenje, oslobođenje (od poreza itd.), otpornost, povlastica, nepodložnost, nepovredivost, zaštiaenost, izuzetak, izuzeće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of not being susceptible [unsusceptibility]</p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) the condition in which an organism can resist disease [resistance]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being unaffected by something</p><p><i>n.</i> an act exempting someone [exemption, granting immunity]</p><p><b>imunizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making immune (especially by inoculation) [immunisation]</p><p><b>imunizirati, cijepiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> law: grant immunity from prosecution [immunise]</p><p><i>v.</i> perform vaccinations or produce immunity in by inoculation [immunise, inoculate, vaccinate]</p><p><b>ako su postali nesposobni za bolest (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having been rendered unsusceptible to a disease [immunised, vaccinated]</p><p><b>Svaka tvar ili organizam koji izaziva imunološki odgovor (proizvodi imunitet) kada se unese u tijelo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any substance or organism that provokes an immune response (produces immunity) when introduced into the body [immunogen]</p><p><b>imunološko određivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> identification of a substance (especially a protein) by its action as an antigen [immunochemical assay]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s imunohemijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to immunochemistry</p><p><b>Identifikacija tvari (posebno proteina) djelovanjem kao antigena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> identification of a substance (especially a protein) by its action as an antigen [immunoassay]</p><p><b>područje kemije koje se bavi kemijskim procesima u imunologiji (kao što su kemijske studije antigena i antitela) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the field of chemistry concerned with chemical processes in immunology (such as chemical studies of antigens and antibodies) [chemoimmunology]</p><p><b>imunokompetencija, imunološki status</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to develop an immune response following exposure to an antigen</p><p><b>koji je sposoban za razvoj imunološkog odgovora nakon izlaganja antigenu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of developing an immune response following exposure to an antigen</p><p><b>imunokompromitirani</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> unable to develop a normal immune response usually because of malnutrition or immunodeficiency or immunosuppressive therapy</p><p><b>imunodeficijencija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> immunological disorder in which some part of the body's immune system is inadequate and resistance to infectious diseases is reduced</p><p><b>Ne može se razviti 