 expressly stated but can be inferred [import, significance]</p><p><i>n.</i> an accusation that brings into intimate and usually incriminating connection</p><p><i>n.</i> a logical relation between propositions p and q of the form `if p then q' [conditional relation, logical implication]</p><p><i>n.</i> a relation implicated by virtue of involvement or close connection (especially an incriminating involvement)</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili se odnose na logičke implikacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or concerned with logical implication</p><p><b>koji imaju tendenciju sugerišemo ili impliciramo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to suggest or imply [suggestive]</p><p><b>bezuvjetan, implicitan, koji proizlazi sam po sebi, koji se podrazumijeva, slijep, uvijen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> implied though not directly expressed [inexplicit]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being without doubt or reserve [unquestioning]</p><p><b>implicitan, inherentan, temeljan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in the nature of something though not readily apparent [inherent, underlying]</p><p><b>implicitno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without doubting or questioning</p><p><i>adv.</i> without ever expressing so clearly</p><p><b>bezuvjetan, implicitan, koji proizlazi sam po sebi, koji se podrazumijeva, slijep, uvijen (od &quot;implicit&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inexplicitness as a consequence of being implied or indirect</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trust inferred by operation of law</p><p><b>Neprijatno ili dosadno zabavno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> naughtily or annoyingly playful [arch, impish, mischievous, pixilated, prankish, puckish, wicked]</p><p><b>integrirati, integrirati se, skvrčiti, skvrčiti se, uvući se u se, zbiti, zbiti se, zgusnuti, zgusnuti se, implodirati, praskati, prasnuti, prskati, prsnuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> burst inward [go off]</p><p><b>moliti, preklinjati, zaklinjati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> call upon in supplication [beg, pray]</p><p><b