ively as obligatory</p><p><b>impozantan, koji imponira, markantan, znatan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> impressive in appearance [baronial, noble, stately]</p><p><i>adj.</i> used of a person's appearance or behavior [distinguished, grand, magisterial]</p><p><b>impozantan, koji imponira, markantan, znatan (od &quot;imposing&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an impressive manner [impressively]</p><p><b>davanje, kaznena zadaća, namet, nametanje, polaganje, porez, teret, varanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of imposing something (as a tax or an embargo) [infliction]</p><p><i>n.</i> an uncalled-for burden</p><p><b>nemogućnost, nemoguanost, nevjerojatnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> incapability of existing or occurring [impossibleness]</p><p><i>n.</i> an alternative that is not available [impossible action]</p><p><b>nemoguče, nemoguć, nemoguće, nemogućim, neostvarljivo, smiješan, nevjerojatan, nezamisliv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that cannot be done</p><p><i>adj.</i> not capable of occurring or being accomplished or dealt with</p><p><i>adj.</i> totally unlikely [inconceivable, out of the question, unimaginable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of persons or their behavior) not acceptable or reasonable [unacceptable]</p><p><b>Alternativa koja nije dostupna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alternative that is not available [impossibility]</p><p><b>nemoguanost, nevjerojatnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> incapability of existing or occurring [impossibility]</p><p><b>Do nivoa nemogućeg postizanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a degree impossible of achievement</p><p><b>davanje, porez</b></p><p><i>n.</i> money collected under a tariff [custom, customs, customs duty]</p><p><i>n.</i> the lowest stone in an arch -- from which it springs [springer]</p><p><b>hohštapler, varalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who makes deceitful pretenses [fake, faker, fraud, impostor, pretender, pseud, pseudo, role player, sham, shammer]</p><p><b>samozvanac, varalica, hohštapler</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who makes deceitful pretens