ecision [imprecision]</p><p><b>kvaliteta nedostatka preciznosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of lacking precision [impreciseness]</p><p><b>nedodirljivost, nesavladivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having the strength to withstand attack [invulnerability]</p><p><b>neosvojiv, nepokolebljiv, nesavladiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> immune to attack [inviolable, secure, strong, unassailable, unattackable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of conceiving [conceptive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> incapable of being overcome, challenged or refuted [inexpugnable]</p><p><b>Neposvojivo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an impregnable manner</p><p><b>bremenita, impregnirati, natopiti, natopljen, obremeniti, oploditi, oplođen, trudna, zasaditi, natapati, prožeti, prožimati, fertilizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> fill, as with a certain quality [infuse, instill, tincture]</p><p><i>v.</i> infuse or fill completely [saturate]</p><p><i>v.</i> fertilize and cause to grow</p><p><i>v.</i> make pregnant [bang up, knock up, prang up]</p><p><b>impregnacija, oplođenje, zasićivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> material with which something is impregnated</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of totally saturating something with a substance [saturation]</p><p><i>n.</i> creation by the physical union of male and female gametes [fecundation, fertilisation, fertilization]</p><p><b>impresario, posrednik, organizator, promotor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sponsor who books and stages public entertainments [promoter, showman]</p><p><b>dojmiti se, imponirati, imponirati kome, impresionirati, ispuniti, načiniti utisak, nametnuti, napraviti utisak, ostaviti trag, otisak, pečat, prenijeti, prenjeti, silom novačiti mornare, učiniti utisak na koga, utisak, utiskivanje, utisnuti, žig, izazivati divljenje, dirnuti, dojmiti, ganuti, pogoditi, taknuti, naštampati, otisnuti, printati, tiskati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of coercing someone into government service [impressment]</p><p><i>v.</i> have an emotional or cognitive impact upon [affect, move, strike]</p><p><i>v.</i> impress positively</p><p><i>v.</i> produce or try to produce a vivid impression of [ingrain, instill]</p><p><i>v.</i> mark or stamp with or as if with pressure [imprint]</p><p><i>v.</i> reproduce by printing [print]</p><p><i>v.</i> take (someone) against his will for compulsory service, especially on board a ship [shanghai]</p><p><i>v.</i> dye (fabric) before it is spun [yarn-dye]</p><p><b>impresioniran, začuđen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deeply or markedly affected or influenced</p><p><b>dojmljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> easily impressed or influenced [impressionable, waxy]</p><p><b>dojam, impresija, izdanje, kopija, otisak, utisak, učinak, slika, udubina, udubljenje, ulegnuće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vague idea in which some confidence is placed [belief, feeling, notion, opinion]</p><p><i>n.</i> an outward appearance [effect]</p><p><i>n.</i> a clear and telling mental image [mental picture, picture]</p><p><i>n.</i> a concavity in a surface produced by pressing [depression, imprint]</p><p><i>n.</i> a symbol that is the result of printing or engraving [stamp]</p><p><i>n.</i> all the copies of a work printed at one time [printing]</p><p><i>n.</i> (dentistry) an imprint of the teeth and gums in wax or plaster</p><p><i>n.</i> an impressionistic portrayal of a person</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of pressing one thing on or into the surface of another</p><p><b>koji lako prima dojmove, osjetljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> easily impressed or influenced [impressible, waxy]</p><p><b>impresionizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school of late 19th century French painters who pictured appearances by strokes of unmixed colors to give the impression of reflected light</p><p><b>slikar koji slijedi teorije impresionizma., koji se odnosi na ili karakterističan za impresionizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a painter who follows the theories of Impressionism</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of Impressionism [impressionistic]</p><p><b>o ili povezan s ili na temelju dojmova umjesto na činjenicama ili obrazloženju, koji se odnosi na ili karakterističan za impresionizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or based on an impression rather than on facts or reasoning</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of Impressionism [impressionist]</p><p><b>dojmljiv, impozantan, impozantni, impresivan, impresivni, impresivno, izrazit, koji ostavlja dojam, koji ostavlja jak dojam, uzbudljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> making a strong or vivid impression</p><p><i>adj.</i> producing a strong effect [telling]</p><p><b>Afazija karakterizirana tečnim, ali beznačajnim govorom i ozbiljnim oštećenjem sposobnosti razumijevanja govorenih ili pisanih riječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aphasia characterized by fluent but meaningless speech and severe impairment of the ability understand spoken or written words [Wernicke's aphasia, fluent aphasia, receptive aphasia, sensory aphasia]</p><p><b>dojmljiv, impozantan, impozantni, impresivan, impresivni, impresivno, izrazit, koji ostavlja dojam, koji ostavlja jak dojam, uzbudljiv (od &quot;impressive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an impressive manner [imposingly]</p><p><b>impresivnost, veličanstvenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> splendid or imposing in size or appearance [grandness, magnificence, richness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of making a strong or vivid impression on the mind</p><p><b>novačenje silom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of coercing someone into government service [impress]</p><p><b>imprimatur</b></p><p><i>n.</i> formal and explicit approval [countenance, endorsement, indorsement, sanction, warrant]</p><p><b>naznaka štampara, obilježiti, otisnuti, oznaka, štampati, urezati, utisak, utisnut, utisnuti, žig, otisak, udubina, udubljenje, ulegnuće, formirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a distinctive influence</p><p><i>n.</i> a concavity in a surface produced by pressing [depression, impression]</p><p><i>n.</i> an identification of a publisher</p><p><i>n.</i> an impression produced by pressure or printing [embossment]</p><p><i>n.</i> a device produced by pressure on a surface</p><p><i>v.</i> establish or impress firmly in the mind [form]</p><p><i>v.</i> mark or stamp with or as if with pressure [impress]</p><p><b>naznaka štampara, obilježiti, otisnuti, oznaka, štampati, urezati, utisak, utisnut, utisnuti, žig (od &quot;imprint&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a learning process in early life whereby species specific patterns of behavior are established</p><p><b>sputavati, uhapsiti, utamničiti, zatvoriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> lock up or confine, in or as in a jail [gaol, immure, incarcerate, jail, jug, lag, put away, put behind bars, remand]</p><p><i>v.</i> confine as if in a prison</p><p><b>uhićen, zarobljen, zatvoren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being in captivity [captive, confined, jailed]</p><p><b>kazna zatvora, kazna zatvorom, utamničenje, zatvor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> putting someone in prison or in jail as lawful punishment</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being imprisoned [captivity, immurement, incarceration]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of confining someone in a prison (or as if in a prison) [internment]</p><p><b>nevjerojatnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being improbable [improbableness]</p><p><b>nevjerojatan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not likely to be true or to occur or to have occurred [unlikely]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a probability too low to inspire belief [unbelievable, unconvincing, unlikely]</p><p><i>adj.</i> too improbable to admit of belief [marvellous, marvelous, tall]</p><p><b>nevjerojatan (od &quot;improbable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being improbable [improbability]</p><p><b>Nije lako vjerovati. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> not easy to believe [implausibly, incredibly, unbelievably]</p><p><b>bez pripreme, improvizacija, na brzinu, nepripreman</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extemporaneous speech or remark</p><p><i>n.</i> a short musical passage that seems to have been made spontaneously without advance preparation</p><p><i>adj.</i> with little or no preparation or forethought [ad-lib, extemporaneous, extemporary, extempore, off-the-cuff, offhand, offhanded, unrehearsed]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without advance preparation [ad lib, ad libitum, spontaneously]</p><p><b>koji ne odgovara, kriv, neodgovarajući, nepodesan, nepravilan, neprikladan, nepriličan, nepristojan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not suitable or right or appropriate</p><p><i>adj.</i> not conforming to legality, moral law, or social convention [unconventional, unlawful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not appropriate for a purpose or occasion [wrong]</p><p><b>nepravi razlomak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fraction whose numerator is larger than the denominator</p><p><b>nepravilno, nepropisno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an improper way</p><p><b>koji ne odgovara, kriv, neodgovarajući, nepodesan, nepravilan, neprikladan, nepriličan, nepristojan (od &quot;improper&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an improper demeanor [impropriety]</p><p><b>neprikladnost, nepriličnost, netočnost, sloboda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an improper demeanor [improperness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of being improper</p><p><i>n.</i> an indecent or improper act [indecency]</p><p><i>n.</i> an act of undue intimacy [familiarity, indecorum, liberty]</p><p><b>koji se može popraviti, sposoban za sjetvu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> susceptible of improvement</p><p><b>iskoristiti, napredovati, ojačati, oplemeniti, poboljšanje, poboljšati, poboljšati se, poboljšavanje, popraviti, unapređenje, unaprijediti, usavršiti, poboljšala, poboljšanju, unapređenja, unaprijedilo, poboljšavati, popravljati, unapređivati, usavršavati, poboljšavati se, popraviti se, popravljati se, usavršavati se, usavršiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to make better [ameliorate, amend, better, meliorate]</p><p><i>v.</i> get better [ameliorate, better, meliorate]</p><p><b>oplemenjen, oplemenjene, oplemenjeno, poboljšan, poboljšano, poboljšanom, unapređivali, unapređivati, usavršen, usavršene, usavršeno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made more desirable or valuable or profitable</p><p><i>adj.</i> become or made better in quality</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of land) made ready for development or agriculture by clearing of trees and brush</p><p><b>napredak, poboljšanje, porast, porastom, sanacija, unapređenje, unapređenju, usavršavanja, usavršavanje, poboljšanja, poboljšanju, poboljšavanje, popravak, popravljanje, unapređivanje, melioracija, razvitak, razvoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a change for the better [advance, betterment]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of improving something</p><p><i>n.</i> a condition superior to an earlier condition [melioration]</p><p><b>dodatak, poboljšavatelj, poboljšivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone devoted to the promotion of human welfare and to social reforms [do-gooder, humanitarian]</p><p><i>n.</i> a component that is added to something to improve it [add-on, addition]</p><p><b>bezbrižnost, nehajnost, nesmotrenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lack of prudence and care by someone in the management of resources [shortsightedness]</p><p><b>bezbrižan, nesmotren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not provident</p><p><i>adj.</i> not given careful consideration [ill-considered, ill-judged, shortsighted]</p><p><b>bezbrižan, nesmotren (od &quot;improvident&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an improvident manner</p><p><b>poboljšanja, poboljšanje, poboljšavajući, poboljšavanje, unapređenja, unapređenje, unapređivanje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> getting higher or more vigorous [up]</p><p><b>improvizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a creation spoken or written or composed extemporaneously (without prior preparation)</p><p><i>n.</i> an unplanned expedient [temporary expedient]</p><p><i>n.</i> a performance given extempore without planning or preparation [extemporisation, extemporization]</p><p><b>improvizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> perform without preparation [ad-lib, extemporise, extemporize, improvize]</p><p><i>v.</i> manage in a makeshift way [extemporize]</p><p><b>improviziran, pomoćni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> done or made using whatever is available [jury-rigged, makeshift]</p><p><b>eksplozivna naprava koja je improvizirana (MT)</