/i> a neutral or uncommitted person (especially in politics) [fencesitter, mugwump]</p><p><i>n.</i> a writer or artist who sells services to different employers without a long-term contract with any of them [free-lance, free lance, freelance, freelancer, self-employed person]</p><p><i>adj.</i> free from external control and constraint</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of political bodies) not controlled by outside forces [autonomous, self-governing, sovereign]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a clause) capable of standing syntactically alone as a complete sentence [main]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not controlled by a party or interest group</p><p><b>Agencija vlade Sjedinjenih Država koja je stvorena Kongresom i nezavisna je od izvršnih odjela. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agency of the United States government that is created by an act of Congress and is independent of the executive departments</p><p><b>Reč u složenoj rečenici koja može biti sama kao cjelovita rečenica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a clause in a complex sentence that can stand alone as a complete sentence [main clause]</p><p><b>parlamentarna demokracija na istočnoj polovici otoka Nove Gvineje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a parliamentary democracy on the eastern half of the island of New Guinea [Papua New Guinea]</p><p><b>Nezavisna Država Samoa, Samoa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a constitutional monarchy on the western part of the islands of Samoa in the South Pacific [Samoa, Samoa i Sisifo, Western Samoa]</p><p><b>(statistika) promjenljiva čije su vrijednosti neovisne o promjenama vrijednosti drugih promjenljivih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (statistics) a variable whose values are independent of changes in the values of other variables [experimental variable]</p><p><b>neovisno, nezavisno, samostalne, samostalno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> on your own</p><p><i>adv.</i> apart from others [severally]</p><p><b>propranolol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first beta blocker (trade name Inderal) used in treating hypertension and angina pectoris and essential tremor [propanolol]</p><p><b>neopisiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> defying expression or description [indefinable, ineffable, unspeakable, untellable, unutterable]</p><p><b>U neizrecivom stepenu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to an inexpressible degree [ineffably, inexpressibly, unspeakably, unutterably]</p><p><b>Snaga da se oduprem uništenju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the strength to resist destruction</p><p><b>nerazoriv, neuništiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not easily destroyed</p><p><i>adj.</i> very long lasting [durable, perdurable, undestroyable]</p><p><b>Ne može se konačno odlučiti ili utvrditi, S druge strane, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 98.: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not capable of being definitely decided or ascertained [undeterminable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> incapable of being definitely ascertained or calculated</p><p><b>na neodređen način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an indeterminable manner</p><p><b>kvaliteta nejasnoće i loše definirane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being vague and poorly defined [indefiniteness, indefinity, indeterminateness, indetermination]</p><p><b>heisenbergov princip neodređenosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (quantum theory) the theory that it is impossible to measure both energy and time (or position and momentum) completely accurately at the same time [uncertainty principle]</p><p><b>neodređeno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not precisely determined or established [undetermined]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a capacity for continuing to grow at the apex</p><p><i>adj.</i> of uncertain or ambiguous nature</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a quantity) having no definite value, as an equation that cannot be solved</p><p><i>adj.</i> not leading to a definite ending or result</p><p><b>neodređeno (od &quot;indeterminate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being vague and poorly defined [indefiniteness, indefinity, indeterminacy, indetermination]</p><p><b>kvaliteta nejasnoće i loše definirane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being vague and poorly defined [indefiniteness, indefinity, indeterminacy, indeterminateness]</p><p><b>indeks, indeksirati, index, kazalo pojmova, kažiprst, pokazatelj, popis, registar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a numerical scale used to compare variables with one another or with some reference number</p><p><i>n.</i> a number or ratio (a value on a scale of measurement) derived from a series of observed facts [index number, indicant, indicator]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mathematical notation indicating the number of times a quantity is multiplied by itself [exponent, power]</p><p><i>n.</i> an alphabetical listing of names and topics along with page numbers where they are discussed</p><p><i>n.</i> the finger next to the thumb [forefinger, index finger]</p><p><i>v.</i> list in an index</p><p><i>v.</i> provide with an index</p><p><i>v.</i> adjust through indexation</p><p><b>najraniji dokumentirani slučaj bolesti koji je uključen u epidemiološko istraživanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the earliest documented case of a disease that is included in an epidemiological study</p><p><b>kažiprst</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the finger next to the thumb [forefinger, index]</p><p><b>fosil za koji se zna da je živio u određenom geološkom dobu koji se može koristiti za datiranje sloja stijene u kojem se nalazi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fossil known to have lived in a particular geologic age that can be used to date the rock layer in which it is found [guide fossil]</p><p><b>fond vezan uz indeks</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mutual fund whose assets are stocks on a given list</p><p><i>n.</i> a mutual fund that invests in the stocks that are the basis of a well-known stock or bond index</p><p><b>indeks vode</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a number or ratio (a value on a scale of measurement) derived from a series of observed facts [index, indicant, indicator]</p><p><b>odnos brzine svjetlosti u vakuumu prema brzini svjetlosti u mediju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio of the velocity of light in a vacuum to that in a medium [refractive index]</p><p><b>(računovodstvo) regi