 current by electrostatic or magnetic processes [induce]</p><p><i>v.</i> introduce or initiate</p><p><b>induktivitet, induktivnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electrical phenomenon whereby an electromotive force (EMF) is generated in a closed circuit by a change in the flow of current [induction]</p><p><i>n.</i> an electrical device (typically a conducting coil) that introduces inductance into a circuit [inductor]</p><p><b>mjera svojstva električnog kola kojim se u njemu inducira elektromotorna sila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measure of the property of an electric circuit by which an electromotive force is induced in it</p><p><b>novak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person inducted into an organization or social group</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is drafted into military service [conscript, draftee]</p><p><b>indukcija, početak, inicijacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a formal entry into an organization or position or office [initiation, installation]</p><p><i>n.</i> an electrical phenomenon whereby an electromotive force (EMF) is generated in a closed circuit by a change in the flow of current [inductance]</p><p><i>n.</i> reasoning from detailed facts to general principles [generalisation, generalization, inductive reasoning]</p><p><i>n.</i> stimulation that calls up (draws forth) a particular class of behaviors [elicitation, evocation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of bringing about something (especially at an early time)</p><p><i>n.</i> an act that sets in motion some course of events [initiation, trigger]</p><p><b>ubrzava kontinuirani zrak elektrona do velikih brzina pomoću električnog polja proizvedenog promjenom magnetnog toka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> accelerates a continuous beam of electrons to high speeds by means of the electric field produced by changing magnetic flux [betatron]</p><p><b>indukcijski svitak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coil for producing a high voltage from a low-voltage source</p><p><b>indukcijsko grijanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the heating of a conducting material caused by an 