als with the creation and management of systems that integrate people and materials and energy in productive ways [industrial management]</p><p><b>industrijsko poduzeće, industrijalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the development of industry on an extensive scale [industrialisation, industrialization]</p><p><b>financijska tvrtka koja daje male kredite industrijskim radnicima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a finance company that makes small loans to industrial workers [industrial bank]</p><p><b>grana inženjerstva koja se bavi stvaranjem i upravljanjem sustavima koji integriraju ljude, materijale i energiju na produktivne načine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of engineering that deals with the creation and management of systems that integrate people and materials and energy in productive ways [industrial engineering]</p><p><b>zemljište udaljeno od centra grada koje je namijenjeno za skupinu preduzeća i tvornica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tract of land at a distance from city center that is designed for a cluster of businesses and factories</p><p><b>industrijska biljka, industrijsko postrojenje, tvornica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> buildings for carrying on industrial labor [plant, works]</p><p><b>industrijski proces</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a systematic series of mechanical or chemical operations that produce or manufacture something</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko grana psihologije koja nastoji primijeniti psihološke principe na praktične probleme obrazovanja ili industrije ili marketinga itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several branches of psychology that seek to apply psychological principles to practical problems of education or industry or marketing etc. [applied psychology]</p><p><b>industrijska revolucija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the transformation from an agricultural to an industrial nation [technological revolution]</p><p><b>sindikat koji prihvaća sve radnike u određenoj industriji bez obzira na zanat. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a labor union that admits all workers in a given industry irrespective of their craft [vertical union]</p><p><b>kanal kojim upravlja jedna ili više industrija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a canal that is operated by one or more industries</p><p><b>bivši međunarodni sindikat i radikalni radnički pokret u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former international labor union and radical labor movement in the United States [I.W.W., IWW]</p><p><b>od 85 g/m2 do 85 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> extremely strong or concentrated or durable [weapons-grade]</p><p><b>industrijalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the development of industry on an extensive scale [industrial enterprise, industrialization]</p><p><b>organizirati (proizvodnju nečega) u industriju, razvoj industrije (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> organize (the production of something) into an industry [industrialize]</p><p><i>v.</i> develop industry [industrialize]</p><p><b>industrijski proizvedeni (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made industrial [industrialized]</p><p><b>ekonomski sustav izgrađen na velikim industrijama umjesto na poljoprivredi ili zanatstvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economic system built on large industries rather than on agriculture or craftsmanship</p><p><b>industrijalac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who manages or has significant financial interest in an industrial enterprise</p><p><b>industijalizacija, industrijalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the development of industry on an extensive scale [industrial enterprise, industrialisation]</p><p><b>organizirati (proizvodnju nečega) u industriju, razvoj industrije (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> organize (the production of something) into an industry [industrialise]</p><p><i>v.</i> develop industry [industrialise]</p><p><b>industrijski proizvedeni (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made industrial [industrialised]</p><p><b>industrijski, industrijskih, industrijskim, industrijskog (od &quot;industrial&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by industrial means</p><p><b>marljiv, radin, radišan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by hard work and perseverance [hardworking, tireless, untiring]</p><p><i>adj.</i> working hard to promote an enterprise [energetic, gumptious, up-and-coming]</p><p><b>marljivo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an industrious manner</p><p><b>marljivost, radinost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> persevering determination to perform a task [diligence, industry]</p><p><b>gospodarska grana, industrija, marljivost, radinost, industrije, industriji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the people or companies engaged in a particular kind of commercial enterprise</p><p><i>n.</i> the organized action of making of goods and services for sale [manufacture]</p><p><i>n.</i> persevering determination to perform a task [diligence, industriousness]</p><p><b>analitičar stanja koja utječu na određenu industriju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an analyst of conditions affecting a particular industry</p><p><b>stanovnik, postojati, prebivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to exist as an inner activating spirit, force, or principle</p><p><b>stanovnik, žitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> activation by an inner spirit or force or principle</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who inhabits a particular place [denizen, dweller, habitant, inhabitant]</p><p><b>stanovnik (od &quot;indwell&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing or residing as an inner activating spirit or force or principle</p><p><b>opojno sredstvo, alkohol, alkoholni napitak, alkoholno piće, opojno piće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a liquor or brew containing alcohol as the active agent [alcohol, alcoholic beverage, alcoholic drink, intoxicant]</p><p><b>napiti se, opiti, pijanica, uznijeti, zgroziti, cugati, nacugati se, napijati se, opijati se, opiti se, pijančevati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chronic drinker [drunk, drunkard, rummy, sot, wino]</p><p><i>v.</i> fill with sublime emotion [beatify, exalt, exhilarate, thrill, tickle pink]</p><p><i>v.</i> make drunk (with alcoholic drinks) [intoxicate, soak]</p><p><i>v.</i> become drunk or drink excessively [hit it up, soak, souse]</p><p><b>opijen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> stupefied or excited by a chemical substance (especially alcohol) [drunk, gone, intoxicated, ripped]</p><p><b>opojenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> habitual intoxication [alcohol addiction, alcoholism, drunkenness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a temporary state resulting from excessive consumption of alcohol [drunkenness, inebriety, insobriety, intoxication, tipsiness]</p><p><b>privremeno stanje koje je posljedica prekomjerne konzumacije alkohola (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a temporary state resulting from excessive consumption of alcohol [drunkenness, inebriation, insobriety, intoxication, tipsiness]</p><p><b>neprikladno za hranu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not suitable for food [uneatable]</p><p><b>neiskazan, neopisiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> defying expression or description [indefinable, indescribable, unspeakable, untellable, unutterable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> too sacred to be uttered [unnameable, unspeakable, unutterable]</p><p><b>U neizrecivom stepenu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to an inexpressible degree [indescribably, inexpressibly, unspeakably, unutterably]</p><p><b>bezuspješan, neefektan, nemoćan, nedjelotvoran, neefektivan, neefikasan, neučinkovit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not producing an intended effect [ineffectual, uneffective]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking in power or forcefulness [ineffectual, unable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking the ability or skill to perform effectively [inefficient]</p><p><b>bezuspješan, neefektan, nemoćan (od &quot;ineffective&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an ineffective manner [inefficaciously]</p><p><b>nedjelotvornost, neefikasnost, neučinkovitost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lacking the power to be effective [ineffectuality, ineffectualness]</p><p><b>bezuspješan, neuspješan, nevažeći, uzaludan, nedjelotvoran, neefektan, neefektivan, neefikasan, neučinkovit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not producing an intended effect [ineffective, uneffective]</p><p><i>adj.</i> producing no result or effect [futile, meaningless, otiose, unavailing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking in power or forcefulness [ineffectiv