<i>adj.</i> having or fostering a warm or friendly and informal atmosphere [cozy, intimate]</p><p><b>Na način koji ne uzima forme i ceremonije ozbiljno., Slobodno od prisiljavanja ili srama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a manner that does not take forms and ceremonies seriously</p><p><i>n.</i> freedom from constraint or embarrassment [ease]</p><p><b>neformalno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without formality</p><p><i>adv.</i> with the use of colloquial expressions [colloquially, conversationally]</p><p><b>dopisnik, dostavljač, informator, doušnik, svjedok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who supplies information [source]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who sees an event and reports what happened [witness, witnesser]</p><p><b>informatički, informatičko, informatika, informatologija, obavjesništvo, informacijska znanost, informacijske znanosti, obrada informacija, računarska znanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sciences concerned with gathering, manipulating, storing, retrieving, and classifying recorded information [IP, information processing, information science]</p><p><b>informacija, informacije, informacijski, informiranje, navod, obavijest, obavijesti, obavještavanje, obavještenje, podaci, podatak, priopćenje, vijest, obavijestan, Informacijska, informacijske, informacijskih, informativne, informativnim, podatke, vijesti, poruka, činjenica, podatci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a message received and understood [info]</p><p><i>n.</i> knowledge acquired through study or experience or instruction</p><p><i>n.</i> formal accusation of a crime</p><p><i>n.</i> a collection of facts from which conclusions may be drawn [data]</p><p><i>n.</i> (communication theory) a numerical measure of the uncertainty of an outcome [entropy, selective information]</p><p><b>razdoblje koje počinje u posljednjoj četvrtini 20. stoljeća kada su informacije postale lako dostupne putem publikacija i manipulacije informacijama pomoću računala i računalnih mreža. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a period beginning in the last quarter of the 20th century when information became easily accessible through publications and through the manipulation of information by computers and computer networks</p><p><b>bilten s najnovijim informacijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bulletin containing the latest information</p><p><b>prikupljanje informacija, prikupljanje podataka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of collecting information</p><p><b>sustav mjerenja informacija na temelju vjerojatnosti događaja koji prenose informacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of measurement of information based on the probabilities of the events that convey information</p><p><b>obrada informacija, obradba informacija, obradba obavijesti, informacijska znanost, informacijske znanosti, računarska znanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sciences concerned with gathering, manipulating, storing, retrieving, and classifying recorded information [IP, informatics, information science]</p><p><b>kompjuter, kompjutor, računalo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a machine for performing calculations automatically [computer, computing device, computing machine, data processor, electronic computer]</p><p><b>Povratak koji daje informacije poreznom obvezniku, ali ne izračunava poreznu obvezu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a return that provides information to the tax collector but does not compute the tax liability</p><p><b>informacijska znanost, informacijske znanosti, informatika, obavijesna znanost, obrada informacija, računarska znanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sciences concerned with gathering, manipulating, storing, retrieving, and classifying recorded information [IP, informatics, information processing]</p><p><b>informacijska veleprometnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extensive electronic network (such as the internet) used for the rapid transfer of sound and video and graphics in digital form [superhighway]</p><p><b>informacijski sustav, obavijesni sustav, informativni sustav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> system consisting of the network of all communication channels used within an organization [data system]</p><p><b>informacijska tehnologija, informacijske tehnologije, informatička tehnologija, zajednica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of engineering that deals with the use of computers and telecommunications to retrieve and store and transmit information [IT]</p><p><b>teorija informacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a statistical theory dealing with the limits and efficiency of information processing</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, "službenici" su osoblje koja je odgovorna za obavljanje obavještajnih zadaća u okviru sustava za upravljanje informacijama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of information or information technology during a time of crisis or conflict to achieve or promote specific objectives over a specific adversary or adversaries [IW]</p><p><b>informativan, informativna, informativne</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or having the nature of information</p><p><b>Sastav za proizvodnju proteina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the template for protein synthesis [mRNA, messenger RNA, template RNA]</p><p><b>informativan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to increase knowledge or dissipate ignorance [enlightening, illuminating]</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to instruct or enlighten or inform [instructive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> providing or conveying information [informatory]</p><p><b>informativan (od &quot;informative&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an informative manner [instructively]</p><p><b>pružanje ili prijenos informacija (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> providing or conveying information [informative]</p><p><b>informiran, obaviješten, obaviješteni, obavješten, upoznajemo, upoznalo, upoznat</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having much knowledge or education</p><p><b>informirani pristanak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> consent by a patient to undergo a medical or surgical treatment or to participate in an experiment after the patient understands the risks involved</p><p><b>dostavljač, doušnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who reveals confidential information in return for money [betrayer, blabber, rat, squealer]</p><p><b>pravo vlade da odbije da otkrije identitet doušnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the right of the government to refuse to reveal the identity of an informer</p><p><b>TV reklama prikazana u obliku kratkog dokumentarnog filma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a television commercial presented in the form of a short documentary [infomercial]</p><p><b>informiranje, javljanje, obavještavanje, obznanjivanje, priopćavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> to furnish incriminating evidence to an officer of the law (usually in return for favors) [ratting]</p><p><i>n.</i> a speech act that conveys information [making known]</p><p><b>infotainment, spoj informacije i zabave</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a film or TV program presenting the facts about a person or event [docudrama, documentary, documentary film]</p><p><b>dalje, dolje, ispod</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (in writing) at a later place [below]</p><p><b>ispod vašeg dostojanstva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> beneath your dignity</p><p><b>kršiti, prekršiti, prestupiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> act in disregard of laws, rules, contracts, or promises [breach, break, go against, offend, transgress, violate]</p><p><b>kršenje, prekršaj, prelom, prijestup</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crime less serious than a felony [infringement, misdemeanor, misdemeanour, violation]</p><p><b>pripadnost grupi ispod ljudi u evolucijskom razvoju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to a group below humans in evolutionary development</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na donju vilicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the lower jaw [mandibular]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 88.:, Ne može se prekršiti ili narušiti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> difficult or impossible to break or separate into parts</p><p><i>adj.</i> not capable of being violated or infringed [absolute, inviolable]</p><p><b>arterija koja potječe iz maksilarne arterije i opskrbljuje strukture ispod orbite (od donjeg kapka do gornje usne) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery that originates from the maxillary artery and supplies structures below the orbit (from lower eyelid to upper lip) [arteria infraorbitalis]</p><p><b>infracrveni, infracrveno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the infrared region of the electromagnetic spectrum [infrared frequency]</p><p><i>n.</i> electromagnetic radiation with wavelengths longer than visible light but shorter than radio waves [infrared emission, infrared light, infrared radiation]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or employing wavelengths longer than light but shorter than radio waves</p><p><b>Elektromagnetsko zračenje s valnim duljinama dužim od vidljive svjetlosti, ali kraćim od radio valova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electromagnetic radiation with wavelengths longer than visible light but shorter than radio waves [infrared, infrared light, infrared radiation]</p><p><b>Infracrvena regija elektromagnetnog spektra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the infrared region of the electromagnetic spectrum [infrared]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom energije od 1,15 kVA ili većim od 2,15 kVA, ali ne većim od 1,15 kVA, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electric heater consisting of a high-power incandescent lamp that emits infrared radiation [heat lamp]</p><p><b>Elektromagnetsko zračenje s valnim duljinama dužim od vidljive svjetlosti, ali kraćim od radio valova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electromagnetic radiation with wavelengths longer than visible light but shorter than radio waves [infrared, infrared emission, infrared radiation]</p><p><b>infracrveno zračenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electromagnetic radiation with wavelengths longer than visible light but shorter than radio waves [infrared, infrared emission, infrared light]</p><p><b>infracrveno zračenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ray of infrared radiation</p><p><b>spektar infracrvenog zračenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the spectrum of infrared radiation</p><p><b>Upotreba infracrvenog zračenja (kao što su infracrvene lampe ili grijačke podloge ili boce za toplu vodu) za ublažavanj