i član potklase Infusoria (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any member of the subclass Infusoria</p><p><b>bilo koje drvo ili grm iz roda Inga s obilnim listovima i blesterima obično bijelim. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any tree or shrub of the genus Inga having pinnate leaves and showy usually white flowers</p><p><b>dekoratno zimzeleno stablo s masom bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental evergreen tree with masses of white flowers [ice-cream bean]</p><p><b>tropsko stablo iz Srednje Amerike i Zapadne Indije i Portorika s šiljakama bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical tree of Central America and West Indies and Puerto Rico having spikes of white flowers [guama]</p><p><b>pobiranje, žetva, prikupljanje, zahtjev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> request for a sum of money [appeal, collection, solicitation]</p><p><b>Engleski svećenik poznat po pesimističkim propovijedama i člancima (1860-1954), Američki dramaturg (1913-1973) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English prelate noted for his pessimistic sermons and articles (1860-1954) [Gloomy Dean, William Ralph Inge]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States playwright (1913-1973) [William Inge]</p><p><b>ponavljati, ponoviti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to say, state, or perform again [iterate, reiterate, repeat, restate, retell]</p><p><b>domišljat, dovitljiv, genijalan, okretan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing inventiveness and skill [clever, cunning]</p><p><b>domišljat, dovitljiv, genijalan, okretan (od &quot;ingenious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an ingenious manner</p><p><b>inventivnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the power of creative imagination [cleverness, ingenuity, inventiveness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being ingenious [cleverness, ingenuity]</p><p><b>glumica koja se specijalizirala za ulogu nevine djevojke bez vještine., nevina mlada djevojka bez umjetnosti (posebno kao što je prikazana na pozornici), ulogu nevine mlade žene bez umjetnosti u predstavi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an actress who specializes in playing the role of an artless innocent young girl</p><p><i>n.</i> an artless innocent young girl (especially as portrayed on the stage)</p><p><i>n.</i> the role of an innocent artless young woman in a play</p><p><b>domišljatost, dosjetljivost, dovitljivost, genijalnost, inventivnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the power of creative imagination [cleverness, ingeniousness, inventiveness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being ingenious [cleverness, ingeniousness]</p><p><b>bezazlen, domišljat</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by an inability to mask your feelings [artless]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking in sophistication or worldliness [innocent]</p><p><b>bezazlen, domišljat (od &quot;ingenuous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an ingenuous manner [artlessly]</p><p><b>bezazlen, domišljat (od &quot;ingenuous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of innocent naivete [artlessness, innocence, naturalness]</p><p><i>n.</i> openly straightforward or frank</p><p><b>pripadnik zapadnog finskog naroda koji je nekada živio u baltičkoj pokrajini gdje je sagrađen Sankt Peterburg (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of western Finnish people formerly living in the Baltic province where Saint Petersburg was built [Ingerman, Ingrian]</p><p><b>pripadnik zapadnog finskog naroda koji je nekada živio u baltičkoj pokrajini gdje je sagrađen Sankt Peterburg (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of western Finnish people formerly living in the Baltic province where Saint Petersburg was built [Inger, Ingrian]</p><p><b>konzumirati, asimilirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> serve oneself to, or consume regularly [consume, have, take, take in]</p><p><i>v.</i> take up mentally [absorb, assimilate, take in]</p><p><b>čvrsta i tekuća hrana koja se uzima u tijelo kroz usta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> solid and liquid nourishment taken into the body through the mouth</p><p><b>gutanje, gutanjem, proguta, progutati, hranidba, hranjenje, jedenje, konzumacija, konzumiranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of taking food into the body through the mouth (as by eating) [consum