stven, implicitan, temeljan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing as an essential constituent or characteristic [built-in, constitutional, inbuilt, integral]</p><p><i>adj.</i> in the nature of something though not readily apparent [implicit in, underlying]</p><p><b>instinkt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inborn pattern of behavior often responsive to specific stimuli [instinct]</p><p><b>inherentno, po sebi, prirođeno, svojstveno, u sebi</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an inherent manner</p><p><b>naslijediti, nasljeđivati, ne davati, pojesti, ukočiti, zabraniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> obtain from someone after their death</p><p><i>v.</i> receive from a predecessor</p><p><i>v.</i> receive by genetic transmission</p><p><b>Sposoban za nasljeđivanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being inherited [heritable]</p><p><b>baština, naslijeđe, nasljedstvo, nasljeđe, nasljeđivanje, ostavina, ostavština, tekovina, nasljedovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hereditary succession to a title or an office or property [heritage]</p><p><i>n.</i> that which is inherited [heritage]</p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) attributes acquired via biological heredity from the parents [hereditary pattern]</p><p><i>n.</i> any attribute or immaterial possession that is inherited from ancestors [heritage]</p><p><b>porez na naslijeđe, porez na nasljedstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tax on the estate of the deceased person [death duty, death tax, estate tax]</p><p><b>naslijeđen, naslijeđene</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring among members of a family usually by heredity [familial, genetic, hereditary, transmissible, transmitted]</p><p><b>bolest ili poremećaj koji se nasljeđuje genetski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease or disorder that is inherited genetically [congenital disease, genetic abnormality, genetic defect, genetic disease, genetic disorder, hereditary condition, hereditary disease, inherited disorder]</p><p><b>bolest ili poremećaj koji se nasljeđuje genetski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease or disorder that is inherited genetically [c