gram [initialize]</p><p><i>v.</i> divide (a disk) into marked sectors so that it may store data [format, initialize]</p><p><b>riječ formirana od početnih slova nekoliko riječi u imenu i izgovara se kao jedna riječ, skraćenica formirana od početnih slova nekoliko riječi u imenu i izgovara se odvojeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a word formed from the initial letters of the several words in the name and pronounced as one word [acronym]</p><p><i>n.</i> an abbreviation formed from the initial letters of the several words in the name and pronounced separately</p><p><b>inicijalizacija, pokretanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) the format of sectors on the surface of a hard disk drive so that the operating system can access them and setting a starting position [initialisation, low-level formatting]</p><p><b>inicijalizirati, inicirati, početi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> assign an initial value to a computer program [initialise]</p><p><i>v.</i> divide (a disk) into marked sectors so that it may store data [format, initialise]</p><p><b>inicijalno, početno, polazno, u početku</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at the beginning [ab initio]</p><p><b>otpočeti, početak, pokrenuti, potaknuti, upoznati, započeti, početnik, oživotvoriti, zametnuti, inicirati, načeti, načinjati, otvarati, otvoriti, započinjati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone new to a field or activity [beginner, novice, tiro, tyro]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who has been admitted to membership in a scholarly field [learned person, pundit, savant]</p><p><i>n.</i> people who have been introduced to the mysteries of some field or activity [enlightened]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring into being [originate, start]</p><p><i>v.</i> take the lead or initiative in [pioneer]</p><p><i>v.</i> accept people into an exclusive society or group, usually with some rite [induct]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring up a topic for discussion [broach]</p><p><i>v.</i> set in motion, start an event or prepare the way for [lead up]</p><p><b>inicijacija, inicijalizacija, iniciranje, poči