>nedužnost, nevinost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of innocent naivete [artlessness, ingenuousness, naturalness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being unsullied by sin or moral wrong [pureness, purity, sinlessness, whiteness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a state or condition of being innocent of a specific crime or offense</p><p><b>Nevin kvalitet ili stvar ili čin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an innocent quality or thing or act</p><p><b>Bijeli i lavandasti do blijedo-plavi cvijeće rastu u savršenih prstenova široko raspoređenih traka oko stabljika formirajući neku vrstu pagode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white and lavender to pale-blue flowers grow in perfect rings of widely spaced bands around the stems forming a kind of pagoda [Collinsia bicolor, Collinsia heterophylla, purple chinese houses]</p><p><b>bezazlen, bezazleni, bezgrešan, nedužan, nevin, nevinim</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who lacks knowledge of evil [inexperienced person]</p><p><i>adj.</i> free from evil or guilt [clean-handed, guiltless]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking intent or capacity to injure [innocuous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> free from sin [impeccant, sinless]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking in sophistication or worldliness [ingenuous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not knowledgeable about something specified [unacquainted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> completely wanting or lacking [barren, destitute, devoid, free]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of things) lacking sense or awareness</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1198. do 1216. godine, koji je pokrenuo Četvrti križarski rat i pod kojim je intervencija pape u europsku politiku dosegla vrhunac (1161-1216) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1198 to 1216 who instituted the Fourth Crusade and under whom papal intervention in European politics reached its height (1161-1216) [Lotario di Segni]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1484. do 1492. poznat kao nepotist i napadnut od strane Savonarole zbog svoje svjetovnosti (1432-1492.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1484 to 1492 who was known as a nepotist and was attacked by Savonarola for his worldliness (1432-1492) [Giovanni Battista Cibo]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1676. do 1689. godine čije je papstvo bilo obilježeno borbom s Francuskim kraljem Lujijem XIV. oko papine vlasti nad francuskim katolicima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1676 to 1689 whose papacy was marked by the struggle with Louis XIV of France over papal authority over French Catholics [Benedetto Odescalchi]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1691. do 1700. koji je ukinuo nepotizam unutar crkvene hijerarhije i bio je svetski voljen zbog svoje dobročinstva i pobožnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1691 to 1700 who abolished nepotism within the church hierarchy and was universally loved for his charity and piety [Antonio Pignatelli]</p><p><b>bezazlen, bezazleni, bezgrešan, nedužan, nevin, nevinim (od &quot;innocent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a not unlawful manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a naively innocent manner</p><p><b>Dan nevine dječice, Nevina dječica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> December 28, commemorating Herod's slaughter of the children of Bethlehem [Holy Innocents' Day]</p><p><b>bezopasan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not injurious to physical or mental health</p><p><i>adj.</i> not causing disapproval [unobjectionable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking intent or capacity to injure [innocent]</p><p><b>Velika arterija koja nastaje iz luk aorte i dijeli se u desnu subklavijalnu arteriju i desnu zajedničku karotidnu arteriju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large artery arising from the arch of the aorta and divides into the right subclavian artery and the right common carotid artery</p><p><b>Velika zapaljena kost koja čini polovinu zdjelice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large flaring bone forming one half of the pelvis [hipbone]</p><p><b>vena formirana spajanjem unutarnje jugularske i podklavijalne vene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> veins formed by the union of the internal jugular and subclavian veins [brachiocephalic vein, vena brachiocephalica]</p><p><b>dati nešto novo, inovirati, uvesti novinu, uvesti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bring something new to an environment [introduce]</p><p><b>inovacija, inovacije, inovativnost, inoviranje, izum, pronalazak, invencija, ideja, umotvorina, zamisao</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a creation (a new device or process) resulting from study and experimentation [invention]</p><p><i>n.</i> the creation of something in the mind [conception, design, excogitation, invention]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of starting something for the first time [creation, foundation, founding, initiation, instauration, institution, introduction, origination]</p><p><b>biti ili proizvesti nešto kao ništa učinjeno ili iskusio ili stvoren prije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being or producing something like nothing done or experienced or created before [groundbreaking, innovative]</p><p><b>inovacijski, inovativan, koji donosi promjene, novatorski, novotarski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> ahead of the times [advanced, forward-looking, modern]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being or producing something like nothing done or experienced or created before [groundbreaking, innovational]</p><p><b>inovacijski, inovativan, koji donosi promjene, novatorski, novotarski (od &quot;innovative&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> originality by virtue of introducing new ideas</p><p><b>pionir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who helps to open up a new line of research or technology or art [groundbreaker, pioneer, trailblazer]</p><p><b>bez štetnog učinka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having no adverse effect</p><p><b>grad u jugozapadnoj Austriji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> city in southwestern Austria</p><p><b>aluzija, insinuacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an indirect (and usually malicious) implication [insinuation]</p><p><b>bezbrojan, neizbrojiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> too numerous to be counted [countless, infinite, innumerous, multitudinous, myriad, numberless, uncounted, unnumberable, unnumbered, unnumerable]</p><p><b>bezbrojan, neizbrojiv (od &quot;innumerable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a number beyond counting [countlessness]</p><p><b>nedostatak znanja i razumijevanja matematičkih pojmova i metoda (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking knowledge and understanding of mathematical concepts and methods</p><p><b>bezbrojan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> too numerous to be counted [countless, infinite, innumerable, multitudinous, myriad, numberless, uncounted, unnumberable, unnumbered, unnumerable]</p><p><b>lijek (trgovinski naziv Inocor) koji se intravenski koristi u srčanoj insuficijenciji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug (trade name Inocor) used intravenously in heart failure [amrinone]</p><p><b>cjepivo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance (a virus or toxin or immune serum) that is introduced into the body to produce or increase immunity to a particular disease [inoculum]</p><p><b>cijepiti, dati injekciju, dati vakcinu, kalemiti, ucjepak, imunizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> introduce an idea or attitude into the mind of</p><p><i>v.</i> introduce a microorganism into</p><p><i>v.</i> perform vaccinations or produce immunity in by inoculation [immunise, immunize, vaccinate]</p><p><i>v.</i> insert a bud for propagation</p><p><i>v.</i> impregnate with the virus or germ of a disease in order to render immune</p><p><b>cijepiti, dati injekciju, dati vakcinu, kalemiti, ucjepak (od &quot;inoculate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of protecting against disease by introducing a vaccine into the body to induce immunity [vaccinating]</p><p><b>kalemljenje, usađivanje, cijepljenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> taking a vaccine as a precaution against contracting a disease [vaccination]</p><p><b>liječnik koji cijepi ljude protiv bolesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a medical practitioner who inoculates people against diseases [vaccinator]</p><p><b>supstanca (virus ili toksin ili imunološki serum) koja se unositi u tijelo kako bi se proizveo ili povećao imunitet na određenu bolest (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance (a virus or toxin or immune serum) that is introduced into the body to produce or increase immunity to a particular disease [inoculant]</p><p><b>bez mirisa, bezmirisan, nemirisav, nemirišljav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having no odor [odorless, odourless]</p><p><b>bezazlen, bezopasan, dobroćudan, neškodljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not causing anger or annoyance [unoffending]</p><p><i>adj.</i> giving no offense</p><p><b>bezopasno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a not unpleasantly offensive manner</p><p><b>ne može obavljati svoju normalnu funkciju, Ne prikladno za operaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not able to perform its normal function</p><p><i>adj.</i> not suitable for surgery</p><p><b>bez učinka</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not working or taking effect</p><p><b>neblagovremen, nepogodan, neprimjeren, neumjesan, nezgodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not opportune</p><p><b>neblagovremen, nepogodan, neprimjeren, neumjesan, nezgodan (od &quot;inopportune&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at an inconvenient time [malapropos]</p><p><b>neblagovremen, nepogodan, neprimjeren, neumjesan, nezgodan (od &quot;inopportune&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of occurring at an inconvenient time [untimeliness]</p><p><b>neumjeren, pretjeran, razuzdan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> beyond normal limits [excessive, undue, unreasonable]</p><p><b>neumjeren, pretjeran, razuzdan (od &quot;inordinate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> extremely [extraordinarily]</p><p><b>neumjeren, pretjeran, razuzdan (od &quot;inordinate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> immoderation as a consequence of going beyond sufficient or permitted limits [excess, excessiveness]</p><p><b>anorganski, neorganski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating or belonging to the class of compounds not having a carbon basis</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking the properties characteristic of living organisms</p><p><b>anorganska kemija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the chemistry of compounds that do not contain hydrocarbon radicals</p><p><b>bilo koje spojeno jedinjenje koje ne sadrži ugljik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any compound that does not contain carbon</p><p><b>fosfati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt of phosphoric acid [orthophosphate, phosphate]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom ugljika ne većim od 0,9 g/cm3 (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> not involving carbon compounds</p><p><b>spajati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come together or open into each other [anastomose]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to join or open into each other by anastomosis [anastomose]</p><p><b>anastomoza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a natural or surgical joining of parts or branches of tubular structures so as to make or become continuous [anastomosis]</p><p><b>nukleozid koji se formira od deaminacije adenozina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nucleoside that is formed by the deamination of adenosine</p><p><b>inositol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an optically inactive alcohol that is a component of the vitamin B complex</p><p><b>pacijent koji boravi u bolnici u kojoj se liječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a patient who is residing in the hospital where he is being treated [inmate]</p><p><b>ulaska (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inflow [inpouring, inrush]</p><p><b>ulaska, -Sto se uliva unutra. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inflow [inpour, inrush]</p><p><i>adj.</i> pouring inward</p><p><b>dovođenje, staviti, transmisija, ulaz, ulazni, ulaznih, unos, upis, ulazne, ulazno, komentar, napomena, opaska, primjedba, pripomena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> signal going into an electronic system [input signal]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement that expresses a personal opinion or belief or adds information [comment, remark]</p><p><i>n.</i> any stimulating information or event [stimulant, stimulation, stimulus]</p><p><i>n.</i> a component of production</p><p><i>v.</i> enter (data or a program) into a computer</p><p><b>ulazni podaci, ulazni podatak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a computer file that contains data that serve as input to a device or program [input file]</p><p><b>ulazna naprava, ulazni sklop</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device that can be used to insert data into a computer or other computational device [data input device]</p><p><b>(računovodstvo) računalna datoteka koja sadrži podatke koji služe kao ulaz u uređaj ili program (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a computer file that contains data that serve as input to a device or program [input data]</p><p><b>Program koji organizira ulaz u računalo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a utility program that organizes the input to a computer</p><p><b>Routine koja piše iz vanjskog izvora u unutarnju skladište. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a routine that writes from an external source to an internal store</p><p><b>signal koji ulazi u elektronički sustav (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> signal going into an electronic system [input]</p><p><b>istraga, očevid, pretres, straga, sudska istraga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inquiry into the cause of an unexpected death</p><p><b>nemir, nelagoda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feelings of anxiety that make you tense and irritable [disquietude, edginess, uneasiness]</p><p><b>informirati se, ispitati, ispitivati, istraživati, pitati, raspitivati se, tražiti, iskati, priupitati, upitati, zapitati, pitati se, raspitati se, upitati se, zapitati se, ispipati, ispipavati, istražiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> address a question to and expect an answer from [ask, enquire]</p><p><i>v.</i> have a wish or desire to know something [enquire, wonder]</p><p><i>v.</i> conduct an inquiry or investigation of [enquire, investigate]</p><p><b>anketar, ispitivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who asks a question [asker, enquirer, querier, questioner]</p><p><b>ispitivački, radoznao, raspitivanje, ispitivanje, propitivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a request for information [questioning]</p><p><i>adj.</i> given to inquiry</p><p><b>ispitivački, radoznao, raspitivanje (od &quot;inquiring&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an inquiring manner [enquiringly]</p><p><b>ispitivanje, istraga, istraživanje, očevid, raspitivanje, upit, uvid, zahtjev, pitanje, javna istraga, javna provjera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a search for knowledge [enquiry, research]</p><p><i>n.</i> an instance of questioning [enquiry, interrogation, query, question]</p><p><i>n.</i> a systematic investigation of a matter of public interest [enquiry]</p><p><b>privatni detektiv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a private detective</p><p><b>inkvizicija, istraga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former tribunal of the Roman Catholic Church (1232-1820) created to discover and suppress heresy</p><p><i>n.</i> a severe interrogation (often violating the rights or privacy of individuals)</p><p><b>koji rado ispituje, radoznao, znatiželjan, znatiželjnik, znatiželjnika</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing curiosity [questioning, speculative, wondering]</p><p><i>adj.</i> inquiring or appearing to inquire</p><p><b>koji rado ispituje, radoznao, znatiželjan, znatiželjnik, znatiželjnika (od &quot;inquisitive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with curiosity [curiously, interrogatively]</p><p><b>koji rado ispituje, radoznao, znatiželjan, znatiželjnik, znatiželjnika (od &quot;inquisitive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of active curiosity [curiousness]</p><p><b>inkvizitor, istraživač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a questioner who is excessively harsh [interrogator]</p><p><i>n.</i> an official of the ecclesiastical court of the Inquisition</p><p><b>inkvizitorski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> especially indicating a form of prosecution in which proceedings are secret and the accused is questioned by a prosecutor who acts also as the judge</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by inquisitive interest</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the authority to conduct official investigations</p><p><b>marljiv i temeljan u istraživanju ili istrazi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> diligent and thorough in inquiry or investigation [probing, searching]</p><p><b>Agencija koja je glavni izvor u State Departmentu za tumačenje analiza globalnih događaja i središnja točka za pitanja politike i aktivnosti obavještajne zajednice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agency that is the primary source in the State Department for interpretive analyses of global developments and focal point for policy issues and activities of the Intelligence Community [Bureau of Intelligence and Research]</p><p><b>prepad, provala, upad</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an encroachment or intrusion</p><p><i>n.</i> an invasion or hostile attack</p><p><b>navala, odronjavanje, pritisak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inflow [inpour, inpouring]</p><p><b>Agencija u Ministarstvu pravosuđa koja provodi zakone i propise za ulazak osoba rođenih u inozemstvu u Sjedinjene Države. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agency in the Department of Justice that enforces laws and regulations for the admission of foreign-born persons to the United States [Immigration and Naturalization Service]</p><p><b>nezdrav (klima)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> detrimental to health [unhealthful, unhealthy]</p><p><b>nezdrav (klima) (od &quot;insalubrious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being insalubrious and debilitating [insalubrity]</p><p><b>kvaliteta nesretnog i oslabljujućeg (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being insalubrious and debilitating [insalubriousness]</p><p><b>bezuman, lud, umobolan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> afflicted with or characteristic of mental derangement</p><p><i>adj.</i> very foolish [harebrained, mad]</p><p><b>mentalna bolnica, mentalna ustanova, psihijatrijska bolnica, psihijatrijska ustanova, sanatorij, žuta kuća</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hospital for mentally incompetent or unbalanced person [asylum, institution, mental home, mental hospital, mental institution, psychiatric hospital]</p><p><b>bezumno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an insane manner [crazily, dementedly, madly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> (used as intensives) extremely [deadly, deucedly, devilishly, madly]</p><p><b>bezuman, lud, umobolan (od &quot;insane&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> obsolete terms for legal insanity [lunacy, madness]</p><p><b>nehigijenski, nezdrav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not sanitary or healthful [unhealthful, unsanitary]</p><p><b>bezumlje, ludilo, bolest uma, mentalna bolest, umobolnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> relatively permanent disorder of the mind</p><p><b>(kriminalno pravo) razlog u kojem optuženi tvrdi ne