ion [imaginative]</p><p><b>dosjetljivo, iznalazački</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an inventive manner</p><p><b>inventivnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the power of creative imagination [cleverness, ingeniousness, ingenuity]</p><p><b>izumitelj, pronalazač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is the first to think of or make something [artificer, discoverer]</p><p><b>inventar, inventarizacija, inventarni, inventura, lista vrsta, popis, zalihe, zaliha, provjera inventara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a detailed list of all the items in stock [stock list]</p><p><i>n.</i> the merchandise that a shop has on hand [stock]</p><p><i>n.</i> (accounting) the value of a firm's current assets including raw materials and work in progress and finished goods</p><p><i>n.</i> a collection of resources [armory, armoury]</p><p><i>n.</i> making an itemized list of merchandise or supplies on hand [inventorying, stock-taking, stocktaking]</p><p><i>v.</i> make or include in an itemized record or report [stock-take, take stock]</p><p><b>računovodstvo koje kontrolira i procjenjuje inventar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> accounting that controls and evaluates inventory</p><p><b>nadzor inventara, nadzor roba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> supervision of the supply and storage and accessibility of items in order to insure an adequate supply without excessive oversupply</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an item listed in an inventory</p><p><b>rasprodaja, rasprodaja zaliha</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sale to reduce inventory [clearance sale]</p><p><b>inventura, provjera inventara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> making an itemized list of merchandise or supplies on hand [inventory, stock-taking, stocktaking]</p><p><b>inverzan, inverzni, obrat, obratan, obrnut, obrnuti, preokrenut, suprotnost, suprotan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something inverted in sequence or character or effect [opposite]</p><p><i>adj.</i> reversed (turned backward) in order or nature or effect [reverse]</p><p><i>adj.</i> opposite in nature or effect or relation to another quantity</p><p><b>kut koji ima kosekant jednako određenom broju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the angle that has a cosecant equal to a given number [arc cosecant, arccosecant]</p><p><b>obrnuta funkcija kosina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inverse function of the cosine [arc cosine, arccos, arccosine]</p><p><b>obrnuta funkcija cotangenta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inverse function of the cotangent [arc cotangent, arccotangent]</p><p><b>inverzna funkcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a function obtained by expressing the dependent variable of one function as the independent variable of another</p><p><b>obrnuta funkcija sekanta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inverse function of the secant [arc secant, arcsec, arcsecant]</p><p><b>obrnuta funkcija sinus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inverse function of the sine [arc sine, arcsin, arcsine]</p><p><b>obrnuta funkcija tangente (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inverse function of the tangent [arc tangent, arctan, arctangent]</p><p><b>obratno, obrnuto</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an inverse or contrary manner [reciprocally]</p><p><b>invertiranje, inverzija, obrat, preokretanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the layer of air near the earth is cooler than an overlying layer</p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal condition in which an organ is turned inward or inside out (as when the upper part of the uterus is pulled into the cervical canal after childbirth)</p><p><i>n.</i> a chemical process in which the direction of optical rotation of a substance is reversed from dextrorotatory to levorotary or vice versa</p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) a kind of mutation in which the order of the genes in a section of a chromosome is reversed</p><p><i>n.</i> the reversal of the normal order of words [anastrophe]</p><p><i>n.</i> (counterpoint) a variation of a melody or part in which ascending intervals are replaced by descending intervals and vice versa</p><p><i>n.</i> a term formerly used to mean taking on the gender role of the opposite sex [sexual inversion]