ber of one of four linguistic divisions of the prehistoric Greeks</p><p><i>n.</i> the ancient Greek inhabitants of Attica and related regions in Ionia</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to the ancient Ionians who lived in Attica and related territories, to their Ionic dialect of Greek, or to their culture</p><p><b>Drugi grčki red. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the second Greek order [Ionic order]</p><p><b>Jonsko more</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arm of the Mediterranean Sea between western Greece and southern Italy</p><p><b>ionski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the dialect of Ancient Greek spoken and written in Attica and Athens and Ionia [Attic, Classical Greek, Ionic dialect]</p><p><i>adj.</i> containing or involving or occurring in the form of ions</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to the Ionic order of classical Greek architecture</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Ionia or its inhabitants or its language</p><p><b>zraku iona koji se kreće u istom smjeru na istoj brzini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a beam of ions moving in the same direction at the same speed [ion beam]</p><p><b>kemijska veza u kojoj jedan atom gubi elektron da bi formirao pozitivan ion a drugi atom dobiva elektron da bi formirao negativan ion (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chemical bond in which one atom loses an electron to form a positive ion and the other atom gains an electron to form a negative ion [electrostatic bond, electrovalent bond]</p><p><b>naboj na jonu je jednak konstantnom naboju e pomnoženom sa čitavim brojem od 1 do 15 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the charge on an ion is equal to a constant charge e multiplied by an integer from 1 to 15</p><p><b>Dialekt starog grčkog koji se govori i piše u Atici, Atini i Jonji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the dialect of Ancient Greek spoken and written in Attica and Athens and Ionia [Attic, Classical Greek, Ionic]</p><p><b>Terapija koja koristi lokalnu električnu struju za unos iona lijeka u tkiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> therapy that uses a local electric current to introduce t