nizak kupolični oblik, srednji visoki čvor iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> handsome East Indian evergreen tree often planted as an ornamental for its fragrant white flowers that yield a perfume [Mesua ferrea, ironwood tree, rose chestnut]</p><p><i>n.</i> exceptionally tough or hard wood of any of a number of ironwood trees</p><p><i>n.</i> a small slow-growing deciduous tree of northern Iran having a low domed shape [iron-tree, iron tree, ironwood tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized hop hornbeam of eastern North America [Eastern hop hornbeam, Ostrya virginiana, ironwood tree]</p><p><b>lijep istočnoindijski vječnozeleni drvo koje se često sadilo kao ukras zbog svojih mirisnih bijelih cvijeća koje daju miris, malo, sporo rastuće listno stablo iz sjevernog Irana koje ima nizak kupolični oblik, srednji visoki čvor iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> handsome East Indian evergreen tree often planted as an ornamental for its fragrant white flowers that yield a perfume [Mesua ferrea, ironwood, rose chestnut]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small slow-growing deciduous tree of northern Iran having a low domed shape [iron-tree, iron tree, ironwood]</p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized hop hornbeam of eastern North America [Eastern hop hornbeam, Ostrya virginiana, ironwood]</p><p><b>S druge željezne konstrukcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> work made of iron (gratings or rails or railings etc)</p><p><b>radnik u čeličani</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who makes articles of iron</p><p><b>ljevaonice željeza, topionica, željezara, topionice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the workplace where iron is smelted or where iron goods are made</p><p><b>ironija, podsmijeh, željezan, gvozden</b></p><p><i>n.</i> witty language used to convey insults or scorn [caustic remark, sarcasm, satire]</p><p><i>n.</i> incongruity between what might be expected and what actually occurs</p><p><i>n.</i> a trope that involves incongruity between what is expected and what occurs</p><p><b>obitelj sjevernoamerič