r</p><p><b>neizmjenjiv, neopoziv, neporeciv, neopoziva, neopozive, neporecivo</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> incapable of being retracted or revoked [irrevokable]</p><p><b>definitivno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an irrevocable manner</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 94. točka (a) ovog poglavlja ne vrijede: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> incapable of being retracted or revoked [irrevocable]</p><p><b>regija koja je etnički ili povijesno povezana s jednom zemljom, ali je politički kontrolirana od strane druge zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a region that is related ethnically or historically to one country but is controlled politically by another [irredenta]</p><p><b>iredentizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine that irredenta should be controlled by the country to which they are ethnically or historically related [irredentism]</p><p><b>zagovornik iredentizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of irredentism [irredentist]</p><p><b>ispirati, natapati, navodnjavati, orositi, navodniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> supply with water, as with channels or ditches or streams [water]</p><p><i>v.</i> supply with a constant flow or sprinkling of some liquid, for the purpose of cooling, cleansing, or disinfecting</p><p><b>natapanje, navodnjavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> supplying dry land with water by means of ditches etc</p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) cleaning a wound or body organ by flushing or washing out with water or a medicated solution</p><p><b>vodovod za proizvodnju vode na suvom zemljištu na umjetan način (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ditch to supply dry land with water artificially</p><p><b>razdražljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an irritable petulant feeling [choler, crossness, fretfulness, fussiness, peevishness, petulance]</p><p><i>n.</i> excessive sensitivity of an organ or body part [excitability]</p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to exhibit uncontrolled anger [biliousness, peevishness, pettishness, snappishness, surliness, temper]</p><p><b>razdražljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> easily irritated or annoyed [cranky, fractious, nettlesome, peckish, peevish, pettish, petulant, scratchy, techy, testy, tetchy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> abnormally sensitive to a stimulus</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of responding to stimuli [excitable]</p><p><b>ponavljajući se bolovi u trbuhu i proljev (često se izmjenjuju s razdobljima zatvoru) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> recurrent abdominal pain and diarrhea (often alternating with periods of constipation) [mucous colitis, spastic colon]</p><p><b>Na petulantni način., na iritabilni način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a petulant manner [pettishly, petulantly, testily]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in an irritable manner</p><p><b>iritans</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that causes irritation and annoyance [thorn]</p><p><b>ići na živce, izazvati, nadražiti, razdražiti, razljutiti, dražiti, iritirati, nadraživati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause annoyance in [annoy, bother, chafe, devil, get at, get to, gravel, nark, nettle, rag, rile, vex]</p><p><i>v.</i> excite to an abnormal condition, or chafe or inflame</p><p><i>v.</i> excite to some characteristic action or condition, such as motion, contraction, or nervous impulse, by the application of a stimulus</p><p><b>uzbuđen do nestrpljenja ili besa (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> aroused to impatience or anger [annoyed, miffed, nettled, peeved, pissed, pissed off, riled, roiled, steamed, stung]</p><p><b>ići na živce, izazvati, nadražiti, razdražiti, razljutiti (od &quot;irritate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing irritation or annoyance [annoying, bothersome, galling, nettlesome, pesky, pestering, pestiferous, plaguey, plaguy, teasing, vexatious, vexing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of physical stimuli) serving to stimulate or excite [irritative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> causing physical discomfort [painful]</p><p><b>na iritirajući način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an irritating manner</p><p><b>draženje, iritacija, iritiranje, ljutnja, nadražaj, nadraživanje, razdraženost, razdraživanje, nelagoda, iritantnost, izazivanje, provokacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the psychological state of being irritated or annoyed [annoyance, botheration, vexation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden outburst of anger [pique, temper]</p><p><i>n.</i> (pathology) abnormal sensitivity to stimulation</p><p><i>n.</i> the neural or electrical arousal of an organ or muscle or gland [excitation, innervation]</p><p><i>n.</i> an uncomfortable feeling of mental painfulness or distress [discomfort, soreness]</p><p><i>n.</i> unfriendly behavior that causes anger or resentment [aggravation, provocation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of troubling or annoying someone [annoyance, annoying, vexation]</p><p><b>(koristi se za fizičke podražaje) koji služe za stimulaciju ili uzbuđenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of physical stimuli) serving to stimulate or excite [irritating]</p><p><b>ugurati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> enter uninvited [intrude]</p><p><i>v.</i> erupt or intensify suddenly [break open, burst out, erupt, flare, flare up]</p><p><i>v.</i> increase rapidly and in an uncontrolled manner [explode]</p><p><b>izbijanje, izboj, navala, provala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden violent entrance</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden sharp increase in the relative numbers of a population</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden violent spontaneous occurrence (usually of some undesirable condition) [eruption, outbreak]</p><p><b>Iz magmatske stijene koja je zagorjela ispod površine zemlje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of igneous rock that has solidified beneath the earth's surface [plutonic]</p><p><b>Ured Ministarstva financija odgovoran za naplate poreza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bureau of the Treasury Department responsible for tax collections [Internal Revenue Service]</p><p><b>Irtiš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Asian river that rises in the Altai Mountains in northern China and flows generally northwest to become a tributary of the Ob River [Irtish River, Irtysh, Irtysh River]</p><p><b>Irtiš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Asian river that rises in the Altai Mountains in northern