ually plural) loose-fitting nightclothes worn for sleeping or lounging [pajama, pj's, pyjama]</p><p><b>blokiranje, elektroničko ometanje, miješanje postaja, ometanje, zaglušivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deliberate radiation or reflection of electromagnetic energy for the purpose of disrupting enemy use of electronic devices or systems [electronic jamming, jam]</p><p><b>Kašmir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an area in southwestern Asia whose sovereignty is disputed between Pakistan and India [Cashmere, Kashmir]</p><p><b>prepuniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> crowd or pack to capacity [chock up, cram, jam, ram, wad]</p><p><b>vrsta sedana koja se koristi u Indiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of sedan chair used in India</p><p><b>Prvi mjesec godine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first month of the year [January]</p><p><b>Češki obrazovni reformator (1592-1670) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Czech educational reformer (1592-1670) [Comenius, John Amos Comenius]</p><p><b>Južnoafrički državnik i vojnik (1870-1950) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African statesman and soldier (1870-1950) [Smuts]</p><p><b>Boemski fiziolog poznat po otkriću Purkinjevih stanica i Purkinjeove mreže (1787-1869) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Bohemian physiologist remembered for his discovery of Purkinje cells and the Purkinje network (1787-1869) [Johannes Evangelista Purkinje, Purkinje]</p><p><b>Nizozemski astronom koji je dokazao da se galaksija okreće i predložio postojanje Oortovog oblaka (1900-1992) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch astronomer who proved that the galaxy is rotating and proposed the existence of the Oort cloud (1900-1992) [Oort]</p><p><b>Čehoslovački vjerski reformator koji je predvidio reformaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Czechoslovakian religious reformer who anticipated the Reformation [Hus, Huss, John Huss]</p><p><b>Nizozemski žanrovski slikar (1626-1679) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch genre painter (1626-1679) [Steen]</p><p><b>Nizozemski prirodnjak i mikroskopist koji je predložio klasifikaciju insekata i koji je među prvim prepoznao stanice u životinjama i prvi je vidio crvene krvne stanice (1637-1680) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch naturalist and microscopist who proposed a classification of insects and who was among the first to recognize cells in animals and was the first to see red blood cells (1637-1680) [Swammerdam]</p><p><b>Holandski ekonomist poznat po radu u ekonometriji (1903-1994) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch economist noted for his work in econometrics (1903-1994) [Tinbergen]</p><p><b>Nizozemski slikar poznat po upotrebi svjetlosti (1632-1675) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch painter renowned for his use of light (1632-1675) [Jan Vermeer, Vermeer]</p><p><b>Jan van Eyck</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Flemish painter who was a founder of the Flemish school of painting and who pioneered modern techniques of oil painting (1390-1441) [Eyck, van Eyck]</p><p><b>Nizozemski slikar poznat po upotrebi svjetlosti (1632-1675) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch painter renowned for his use of light (1632-1675) [Jan van der Meer, Vermeer]</p><p><b>Engleska romanopisac poznat po svojim pronicljivim portretima obitelji srednje klase (1775-1817) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English novelist noted for her insightful portrayals of middle-class families (1775-1817) [Austen]</p><p><b>nepoznata ili izmišljena žena koja je stranka u sudskom postupku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unknown or fictitious woman who is a party to legal proceedings</p><p><b>Američka filmska glumica i kćerka Henry Fonda (rođena 1937) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film actress and daughter of Henry Fonda (born in 1937) [Fonda]</p><p><b>Engleska zoologinja poznata po studijama šimpanza u divljini (rođena 1934.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English zoologist noted for her studies of chimpanzees in the wild (born in 1934) [Goodall]</p><p><b>Američki pisac i kritičar urbanističkog planiranja (rođen 1916.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer and critic of urban planning (born in 1916) [Jacobs]</p><p><b>Kraljica Engleske kao treća žena Henrija VIII. i majka Edwarda VI. (1509-1537) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Queen of England as the third wife of Henry VIII and mother of Edward VI (1509-1537) [Seymour]</p><p><b>buka, larma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a metallic sound [jingle]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a sound typical of metallic objects [jingle, jingle-jangle]</p><p><b>buka, larma (od &quot;jangle&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> like the discordant ringing of nonmusical metallic objects striking together [jangly]</p><p><b>Kao nesloženi zvon nemuzikalnih metalnih predmeta koji se udaraju zajedno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> like the discordant ringing of nonmusical metallic objects striking together [jangling]</p><p><b>Pjevačica iz SAD-a koja je umrla od predoziranja drogom na vrhuncu svoje popularnosti (1943-1970) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States singer who died of a drug overdose at the height of her popularity (1943-1970) [Joplin]</p><p><b>Odani potpornik., Turski vojnik. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loyal supporter</p><p><i>n.</i> a Turkish soldier</p><p><b>domar, vratar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed to clean and maintain a building</p><p><b>nizozemski katolički teolog (1585-1638) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Dutch Roman Catholic theologian (1585-1638) [Cornelis Jansen, Cornelius Jansenius]</p><p><b>Rimokatolički nauk Kornelija Jansena i njegovih učenika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Roman Catholic doctrine of Cornelis Jansen and his disciples</p><p><b>zagovornik jansenizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of Jansenism</p><p><b>siječanj, januar, siječnja, siječnju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first month of the year [Jan]</p><p><b>1. siječnja, Dan sv. Marije Bogorodice, Nova godina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church and Anglican Church) feast day celebrating the circumcision of Jesus [Circumcision, Feast of the Circumcision]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) a holy day of obligation [Solemnity of Mary]</p><p><i>n.</i> the first day of the year [New Year's, New Year's Day]</p><p><b>19. siječnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> celebrated in southern United States [Lee's Birthday, Robert E Lee's Birthday, Robert E Lee Day]</p><p><b>kršćanski sveti dan., Dan imenovan za inauguraciju predsjednika Sjedinjenih Država. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Christian holy day [Saint Agnes's Eve]</p><p><i>n.</i> the day designated for inauguration of the United States President [Inauguration Day]</p><p><b>Dvanaest dana nakon Božića. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> twelve days after Christmas [Epiphany, Epiphany of Our Lord, Three Kings' Day, Twelfth day]</p><p><b>(Rimska mitologija) rimski bog vrata i prolaza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman mythology) the Roman god of doorways and passages</p><p><b>koji imaju ili se bave polaritetima ili kontrastima, Označen namjernim varanjem, posebno pretvaranjem jednog seta osjećaja i djelovanjem pod utjecajem drugog., Ima dva lica - jedno gleda u budućnost i jedno u prošlost (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or concerned with polarities or contrasts</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by deliberate deceptiveness especially by pretending one set of feelings and acting under the influence of another [ambidextrous, deceitful, double-dealing, double-faced, double-tongued, duplicitous, two-faced]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having two faces--one looking to the future and one to the past [two-faced]</p><p><b>(Ofenzivni slang) uvredljiv izraz za osobu japanskog porijekla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (offensive slang) offensive term for a person of Japanese descent [Nip]</p><p><b>godišnji iz tropske Azije naturaliziran u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an annual of tropical Asia naturalized in United States [Lespedeza striata, japan clover, japanese clover]</p><p><b>Japan, crni lak, Japana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a string of more than 3,000 islands to the east of Asia extending 1,300 miles between the Sea of Japan and the western Pacific Ocean [Japanese Archipelago, Japanese Islands]</p><p><i>n.</i> a constitutional monarchy occupying the Japanese Archipelago [Nihon, Nippon]</p><p><i>n.</i> lacquerware decorated and varnished in the Japanese manner with a glossy durable black lacquer</p><p><i>n.</i> lacquer with a durable glossy black finish, originally from the orient</p><p><i>v.</i> coat with a lacquer, as done in Japan</p><p><b>Japanski listovići koji se uzgajaju zbog svojih mirisnih žutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous Japanese shrub cultivated for its fragrant yellow flowers [Chimonanthus praecox, Japanese allspice, winter sweet]</p><p><b>ukrasna azijska loza s najozbiljnije narandžasto-žuto voće s crvenom arilom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental Asiatic vine with showy orange-yellow fruit with a scarlet aril [Celastric articulatus, Celastrus orbiculatus, Japanese bittersweet, oriental bittersweet]</p><p><b>Visoka zimzelena stabla iz Japana i Kine koja daju vrijedno mekano drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall evergreen of Japan and China yielding valuable soft wood [Cryptomeria japonica, Japanese cedar, sugi]</p><p><b>godišnji iz tropske Azije naturaliziran u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an annual of tropical Asia naturalized in United States [Lespedeza striata, jap clover, japanese clover]</p><p><b>topla oceanska struja koja teče sjeveroistočno od obale Japana u sjeverni Pacifik. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a warm ocean current that flows northeastwardly off the coast of Japan into the northern Pacific ocean [Kuroshio, Kuroshio current]</p><p><b>žuti vosak dobiven od bobica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a yellow wax obtained from sumac berries [Japan wax]</p><p><b>Depresija u dnu Tihog oceana na sjeveroistoku Japana koja doseže dubine od 30.000 stopa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a depression in the floor of the Pacific Ocean to the northeast of Japan that reaches depths of 30,000 feet</p><p><b>žuti vosak dobiven od bobica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a yellow wax obtained from sumac berries [Japan tallow]</p><p><b>Japanac, Japanka, japanski, Japanskog, japansko, japanskoj, japanski jezik</b></p><p><i>n