n in Hungary) who established the Pulitzer prizes (1847-1911) [Pulitzer]</p><p><b>Američki političar koji je beskrupulozno optužio mnoge građane da su komunisti (1908-1957) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States politician who unscrupulously accused many citizens of being Communists (1908-1957) [Joseph McCarthy, McCarthy]</p><p><b>Engleski pisac romana i poezije rođen u Indiji (1865-1936) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English author of novels and poetry who was born in India (1865-1936) [Kipling, Rudyard Kipling]</p><p><b>Joseph Alois Schumpeter</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States economist (born in Czechoslovakia) (1883-1950) [Joseph Alois Schumpeter, Schumpeter]</p><p><b>vjerski vođa koji je 1830 (1805-1844) osnovao Mormonsku crkvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> religious leader who founded the Mormon Church in 1830 (1805-1844) [Smith]</p><p><b>Staljin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Russian leader who succeeded Lenin as head of the Communist Party and created a totalitarian state by purging all opposition (1879-1953) [Iosif Vissarionovich Dzhugashvili, Stalin]</p><p><b>General Sjedinjenih Država koji je zapovijedao savezničkim snagama u Kini, Burmi i Indiji tijekom Drugog svjetskog rata (1883-1946) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States general who commanded the Allied forces in China and Burma and India during World War II (1883-1946) [Stilwell, Uncle Joe, Vinegar Joe Stilwell]</p><p><b>višegodišnje aromatično bilje iz jugoistočne Azije s velikim lištima obično svijetle ili plitke boje i šiljakama plavo-fioletskih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial aromatic herb of southeastern Asia having large usually bright-colored or blotched leaves and spikes of blue-violet flowers [Coleus blumei, Solenostemon blumei, Solenostemon scutellarioides, painted nettle]</p><p><b>Židovski general koji je vodio pobunu Židova protiv Rimljana i zatim napisao povijest tih događaja (37-100) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Jewish general who led the revolt of the Jews against the Romans and then wrote a history of those events (37-100) [Flavius Josephus, Joseph ben Matthias]</p><p><b>zadirkivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be silly or tease one another [banter, chaff, jolly, kid]</p><p><b>Američki humorist koji je pisao o ruralnom životu (1818-1885) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States humorist who wrote about rural life (1818-1885) [Henry Wheeler Shaw, Shaw]</p><p><b>(Stari zavjet) Mojsijev nasljednik koji je vodio Izraelce u Obećanu zemlju, Knjiga iz Starog zavjeta koja opisuje kako je Jozue vodio Izraelce u Kanaan (Obećanu zemlju) nakon smrti Mojsija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Old Testament) Moses' successor who led the Israelites into the Promised Land</p><p><i>n.</i> a book in the Old Testament describing how Joshua led the Israelites into Canaan (the Promised Land) after the death of Moses [Book of Joshua, Josue]</p><p><b>veliki granatasti drveni yucca sa jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država koji ima kratke lišće i zelenilave bijele cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large branched arborescent yucca of southwestern United States having short leaves and clustered greenish white flowers [Yucca brevifolia]</p><p><b>Američki patriota koji je britanskom kralju predstavio žalbe kolonista (1744-1775) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American patriot who presented the colonists' grievances to the English king (1744-1775) [Quincy]</p><p><b>Engleski lončar koji je osnovao lončarenje poznato po svom kineskome kosti (1754-1827) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English potter who started a pottery famous for its bone china (1754-1827) [Spode]</p><p><b>Engleski lončar (1730-1795) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English potter (1730-1795) [Wedgwood]</p><p><b>Američki kemičar (1839-1903) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States chemist (1839-1903) [Gibbs]</p><p><b>Tito</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Yugoslav statesman who led the resistance to German occupation during World War II and established a communist state after the war (1892-1980) [Marshal Tito, Tito]</p><p><b>Kineski bog obožavan u obliku idola. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Chinese god worshipped in the form of an idol</p><p><b>kineski hram ili svetište za obožavanje idola (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Chinese temple or shrine for idol worship</p><p><b>tanka štap od tamjana spaljen prije joss od strane Kineza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slender stick of incense burned before a joss by the Chinese</p><p><b>gurati, izgurati, naletjeti na, tiskati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of jostling (forcing your way by pushing) [jostling]</p><p><i>v.</i> make one's way by jostling, pushing, or shoving</p><p><i>v.</i> come into rough contact with while moving [shove]</p><p><b>gurati, izgurati, naletjeti na, tiskati se (od &quot;jostle&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of jostling (forcing your way by pushing) [jostle]</p><p><b>Knjiga iz Starog zavjeta koja opisuje kako je Jozue vodio Izraelce u Kanaan (Obećanu zemlju) nakon smrti Mojsija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a book in the Old Testament describing how Joshua led the Israelites into Canaan (the Promised Land) after the death of Moses [Book of Joshua, Joshua]</p><p><b>jota, pribilježiti, točkica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brief (and hurriedly handwritten) note [jotting]</p><p><i>n.</i> a slight but appreciable amount [hint, mite, pinch, soupcon, speck, tinge, touch]</p><p><i>v.</i> write briefly or hurriedly [jot down]</p><p><b>napišite kratko ili žurno (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> write briefly or hurriedly [jot]</p><p><b>mali bilježnik za grube bilješke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small notebook for rough notes</p><p><b>kratka (i žurno rukom napisana) bilješka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brief (and hurriedly handwritten) note [jot]</p><p><b>(Nordijska mitologija) jedan od grupe divova često u sukobu s Aesir (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Norse mythology) one of a group of giants often in conflict with the Aesir [Jotunn]</p><p><b>(Nordijska mitologija) jedan od grupe divova često u sukobu s Aesir (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Norse mythology) one of a group of giants often in conflict with the Aesir [Jotun]</p><p><b>džul, James Prescott Joule</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of electrical energy equal to the work done when a current of one ampere passes through a resistance of one ohm for one second [J, watt second]</p><p><i>n.</i> English physicist who established the mechanical theory of heat and discovered the first law of thermodynamics (1818-1889) [James Prescott Joule]</p><p><b>drmati, drmusati, odskakivati, poskakivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden jarring impact [jar, jolt, shock]</p><p><i>v.</i> move up and down repeatedly [bounce]</p><p><b>kronika, novine, žurnal, časopis, dnevne novine, Dnevnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a daily written record of (usually personal) experiences and observations [diary]</p><p><i>n.</i> a periodical dedicated to a particular subject</p><p><i>n.</i> a ledger in which transactions have been recorded as they occurred [daybook]</p><p><i>n.</i> a record book as a physical object</p><p><i>n.</i> the part of the axle contained by a bearing</p><p><b>Sljedeći članak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bearing of a journal</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> metal housing for a journal bearing</p><p><b>stil u kojem su novine napisane. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the style in which newspapers are written</p><p><b>novinarstvo, publicistika, žurnalistika, Novinstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> newspapers and magazines collectively [news media]</p><p><i>n.</i> the profession of reporting or photographing or editing news stories for one of the media</p><p><b>novinar, novinarka, pisac dnevnika, žurnalist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a writer for newspapers and magazines</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who keeps a diary or journal [diarist, diary keeper]</p><p><b>pravo novinara da odbije da otkrije izvore povjerljivih informacija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the right of a journalist to refuse to divulge sources of confidential information</p><p><b>novinarski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or having the characteristics of journalism</