y [exuberate, exult, rejoice, triumph]</p><p><b>likovanje, proslava, slavlje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of extreme joy [exultation, jubilance, jubilancy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a joyful occasion for special festivities to mark some happy event [celebration]</p><p><i>n.</i> the utterance of sounds expressing great joy [exultation, rejoicing]</p><p><b>jubilej, obljetnica, svetkovina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a special anniversary (or the celebration of it)</p><p><b>drevno kraljevstvo južne Palestine s Jeruzalemom kao središtem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient kingdom of southern Palestine with Jerusalem as its center [Judah]</p><p><b>Južni dio drevne Palestine naslijedio je kraljevstvo Juda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the southern part of ancient Palestine succeeding the kingdom of Judah [Judea]</p><p><b>Juda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Old Testament) the fourth son of Jacob who was forebear of one of the tribes of Israel</p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient kingdom of southern Palestine with Jerusalem as its center [Juda]</p><p><b>židovski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of the Jews or their culture or religion [Judaical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Jews or their culture or religion [Jewish]</p><p><b>materijali koji se odnose na judaizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> materials relating to Judaism</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Židove ili njihovu kulturu ili religiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of the Jews or their culture or religion [Judaic]</p><p><b>judaizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Jews collectively who practice a religion based on the Torah and the Talmud [Hebraism, Jewish religion]</p><p><i>n.</i> the monotheistic religion of the Jews having its spiritual and ethical principles embodied chiefly in the Torah and in the Talmud</p><p><b>okno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (New Testament) supposed brother of St. James [Jude, Saint Jude, St. Jude, Thaddaeus]</p><p><i>n.</i> (New Testament) the Apostle who betrayed Jesus to his e