tor]</p><p><i>v.</i> determine the result of (a competition)</p><p><i>v.</i> form a critical opinion of [evaluate, pass judgment]</p><p><i>v.</i> judge tentatively or form an estimate of (quantities or time) [approximate, estimate, gauge, guess]</p><p><i>v.</i> pronounce judgment on [label, pronounce]</p><p><i>v.</i> put on trial or hear a case and sit as the judge at the trial of [adjudicate, try]</p><p><b>službenik dodijeljen suca generalnom odvjetniku, službenik koji služi kao pravni savjetnik vojnog zapovjednika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an officer assigned to the judge advocate general</p><p><i>n.</i> a staff officer serving as legal adviser to a military commander</p><p><b>Viši pravni savjetnik jedne od vojnih grana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the senior legal advisor to a branch of the military</p><p><b>odjeća koju nose akademicari ili suci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gown worn by academics or judges [academic gown, academic robe]</p><p><b>mišljenje, ocjena, osuda, presuda, procjena, prosudba, prosuđivanje, rasuđivanje, sposobnost prosuđivanja, sposobnost rasuđivanja, sud, pravno mišljenje, bistrost, moć prosuđivanja, moć rasuđivanja, oštroumnost, promišljenost, pronicljivost, razboritost, razložitost, razložnost, razumnost, sudska odluka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the legal document stating the reasons for a judicial decision [judgment, legal opinion, opinion]</p><p><i>n.</i> an opinion formed by judging something [judgment, mind]</p><p><i>n.</i> the cognitive process of reaching a decision or drawing conclusions [judging, judgment]</p><p><i>n.</i> the mental ability to understand and discriminate between relations [discernment, judgment, sagaciousness, sagacity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the capacity to assess situations or circumstances shrewdly and to draw sound conclusions [judgment, perspicacity, sound judgement, sound judgment]</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) the determination by a court of competent jurisdiction on matters submitted to it [judgment, judicial decision]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of judging or assessing a person or situation or event [assessment, judgment]</p><p><b>sudska presuda donesena u korist tužitelja kada tuženik ne dođe na sud (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment entered in favor of the plaintiff when the defendant defaults (fails to appear in court) [default judgement, default judgment, judgment by default]</p><p><b>(Novi zavjet) dan na kraju vremena nakon Harmagedona kada će Bog odrediti sudbine svih pojedinačnih ljudi u skladu s dobrim i zlim njihovim zemaljskim životima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (New Testament) day at the end of time following Armageddon when God will decree the fates of all individual humans according to the good and evil of their earthly lives [Day of Judgement, Day of Judgment, Doomsday, Judgment Day, Last Day, Last Judgement, Last Judgment, crack of doom, day of reckoning, doomsday, end of the world, eschaton]</p><p><b>Odluka o plaćanju novčane štete pojedincu (ili društvu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment rendered against an individual (or corporation) for the payment of money damages [judgment in personam, personal judgement, personal judgment]</p><p><b>presuda izrečena o statusu nekog određenog subjekta ili imovine ili stvari (za razliku od one izrečene o osobama) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment pronounced on the status of some particular subject or property or thing (as opposed to one pronounced on persons) [judgment in rem]</p><p><b>sudski sud koji odlučuje o pitanju bez suđenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment disposing of the matter without a trial [dismissal, judgment of dismissal]</p><p><b>sudski sud koji je donesen na temelju analize i odlučivanja o predloženih činjeničnih pitanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> judgment rendered through analysis and adjudication of the factual issues presented [judgment on the merits]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je sud odlučio da se ne primjenjuje pravna odredba, tužitelj se može odlučiti na temelju pravne odredbe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment rendered