<p><i>n.</i> (Swahili) a long garment (usually white) with long sleeves</p><p><b>kalijevom solom (KCl) (trgovinski nazivi K-Dur 20, Kaochlor i K-lor i Klorvess i K-lit) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> salt of potassium (KCl) (trade names K-Dur 20, Kaochlor and K-lor and Klorvess and K-lyte) [K-Dur 20, K-lor, K-lyte, Klorvess, potash muriate, potassium chloride, potassium muriate]</p><p><b>Činskog i Mandžurskog sorga s malim bijelim ili smeđim zrnama (koristima za hranu) i suhim čipnim stabljikama (koristima za krmnu hranu, gorivo i slamenicu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sorghums of China and Manchuria having small white or brown grains (used for food) and dry pithy stalks (used for fodder, fuel and thatching)</p><p><b>kaolin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fine usually white clay formed by the weathering of aluminous minerals (as feldspar) [china clay, china stone, kaoline, porcelain clay, terra alba]</p><p><b>kaolin, kaolinit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fine usually white clay formed by the weathering of aluminous minerals (as feldspar) [china clay, china stone, kaolin, porcelain clay, terra alba]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,25% ili više, ali ne više od 0,25%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mineral consisting of aluminum silicate</p><p><b>Neustavan mezon proizveden kao rezultat sudara čestica visoke energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unstable meson produced as the result of a high-energy particle collision [K particle, k-meson, kappa-meson]</p><p><b>trgovačko ime za lijek protiv dijareje u fiksnoj kombinaciji koji koristi kaolin kao adsorbent i pektin kao omekšivač (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trade name for a fixed-combination antidiarrheal drug that use kaolin as the adsorbent and pectin as the emollient</p><p><b>100 kapeika jednako je 1 rublje u Bjelorusiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> 100 kapeikas equal 1 rubel in Belarus</p><p><b>11. slovo hebrejskog alfabeta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the 11th letter of the Hebrew alphabet</p><p><b>Turska teroristička grupa fundamentalističkih muslimana s vezama s Al Kaidom koja djeluje u Njemačkoj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Turkish terrorist group of fundamentalist Muslims with ties to al-Qaeda that operates in Germany [Association of Islamic Groups and Communities, Caliphate State]</p><p><b>kapok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant fiber from the kapok tree [silk cotton, vegetable silk]</p><p><i>n.</i> massive tropical tree with deep ridges on its massive trunk and bearing large pods of seeds covered with silky floss [Bombay ceiba, Ceiba pentandra, God tree, ceiba tree, silk-cotton tree, white silk-cotton tree]</p><p><b>sarkom koji počinje purpurnatim mrljama na stopama i nogama i širi se od kože do limfnih čvorova i unutarnjih organa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sarcoma that starts with purplish spots on the feet and legs and spreads from the skin to lymph nodes and internal organs</p><p><b>sada rijetka komplikacija vakcinacije koja se nadovezuje na atopijski dermatitis s visokom groznicom i generaliziranim mjehurićima i papulovesicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a now rare complication of vaccinia superimposed on atopic dermatitis with high fever and generalized vesicles and papulovesicles [eczema vaccinatum]</p><p><b>kapa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the 10th letter of the Greek alphabet</p><p><b>Neustavan mezon proizveden kao rezultat sudara čestica visoke energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unstable meson produced as the result of a high-energy particle collision [K particle, k-meson, kaon]</p><p><b>jezikom Čada koji se govori južno od jezera Čad (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Chadic language spoken south of Lake Chad [Higi]</p><p><b>malo novozelandsko rašireno zeleno stablo koje se često uzgaja u toplim područjima kao ukrasno stablo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small New Zealand broadleaf evergreen tree often cultivated in warm regions as an ornamental [Griselinia littoralis]</p><p><b>uništeni ili ubijeni (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> destroyed or killed [done for, gone]</p><p><b>pustinja u Turkmenistanu južno od Aralskog mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a desert in Turkmenistan to the south of the Aral Sea [Qara Qum, Turkestan Desert]</p><p><b>dio Arktičkog oceana sjeverno od Sibira i istočno od Barentsovog mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> part of the Arctic Ocean to the north of Siberia and to the east of the Barents Sea</p><p><b>karabiner</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oblong metal ring with a spring clip [carabiner, snap ring]</p><p><b>Najveći grad u Pakistanu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the largest city in Pakistan</p><p><b>Židovska sekta koja priznaje samo Hebrejska pisma kao izvor božansko nadahnute zakonodavstva i poriče autoritet postbiblijske tradicije Talmuda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Jewish sect that recognizes only the Hebrew Scriptures as the source of divinely inspired legislation and denies the authority of the postbiblical tradition of the Talmud</p><p><b>pripadnik turskog naroda koji živi u blizini Aralskog jezera u središnjoj Aziji, Turkijski jezik koji govore Karakalpakovi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a Turkic people living near Lake Aral in central Asia</p><p><i>n.</i> the Turkic language spoken by the Karakalpak</p><p><b>planinski lanac u sjevernom Kašmiru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain range in northern Kashmir [Karakoram Range, Karakorum Range, Mustagh, Mustagh Range]</p><p><b>planinski lanac u sjevernom Kašmiru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain range in northern Kashmir [Karakoram, Karakorum Range, Mustagh, Mustagh Range]</p><p><b>planinski lanac u sjevernom Kašmiru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain range in northern Kashmir [Karakoram, Karakoram Range, Mustagh, Mustagh Range]</p><p><b>čvrste grubo dlakođe iz srednje Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hardy coarse-haired sheep of central Asia [broadtail, caracul]</p><p><b>pjevanje popularnih pjesama uz glazbu orkestra (obično u barovima ili noćnim klubovima) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> singing popular songs accompanied by a recording of an orchestra (usually in bars or nightclubs)</p><p><b>karat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the unit of measurement for the proportion of gold in an alloy [carat, kt]</p><p><b>karate</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a traditional Japanese system of unarmed combat</p><p><b>izlučivanje azijskog stabla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> exudate of an Asian tree [sterculia gum]</p><p><b>Grad u središnjem Iraku južno od Bagdada. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city of central Iraq to the south of Baghdad [Kerbala, Kerbela]</p><p><b>Češki pisac koji je u Engleski uvodio riječ `robot' (1890-1938) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Czech writer who introduced the word `robot' into the English language (1890-1938) [Capek]</p><p><b>regija u Finskoj i Rusiji između Finske zaljebe i Bijelog mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a region in Finland and Russia between the Gulf of Finland and the White Sea</p><p><b>pripadnik finskog naroda koji živi u Kareliji u sjeverozapadnoj Europi Rusije, Finski jezik kojim govore stanovnici Karelije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Finnish people living in Karelia in northwestern European Russia [Carelian]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Finnic language spoken by the people of Karelia [Carelian]</p><p><b>Istmus između Finske zaljeve i jezera Ladoga koji povezuje Finsku i Rusiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the isthmus between the Gulf of Finland and Lake Ladoga that connects Finland and Russia</p><p><b>Tibeto-birmanski jezik koji se govori na granici Tajlanda i Burme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Tibeto-Burman language spoken in the Thailand and Burmese borderlands [Karenic]</p><p><b>Danska pisateljica koja je živela u Keniji 19 godina i poznata je po svojim spisima o Africi (1885-1962) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Danish writer who lived in Kenya for 19 years and is remembered for her writings about Africa (1885-1962) [Baroness Karen Blixen, Blixen, Dinesen, Isak Dinesen]</p><p><b>Američki psihijatar (1885-1952) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States psychiatrist (1885-1952) [Horney, Karen Horney]</p><p><b>Američki psihijatar (1885-1952) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States psychiatrist (1885-1952) [Horney, Karen Danielsen Horney]</p><p><b>Tibeto-birmanski jezik koji se govori na granici Tajlanda i Burme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Tibeto-Burman language spoken in the Thailand and Burmese borderlands [Karen]</p><p><b>Austrijac koji je postao nacistički dužnosnik koji je upravljao koncentracijskim logorima gdje su u Drugom svjetskom ratu ubijeni milijuni Židova (1906-1962) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Austrian who became the Nazi official who administered the concentration camps where millions of Jews were murdered during World War II (1906-1962) [Adolf Eichmann, Eichmann]</p><p><b>Danski filolog (1846-1896) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Danish philologist (1846-1896) [Verner]</p><p><b>Švicarski fizičar koji je proučavao superprovodljivost (rođen 1927.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Swiss physicist who studied superconductivity (born in 1927) [Muller]</p><p><b>Američki psihijatar i sin Charlesa Meningera (1893-1990) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States psychiatrist and son of Charles Menninger (1893-1990) [Karl Menninger, Menninger]</p><p><b>Njemački izdavač niza putničkih vodiča (1801.-1859.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German publisher of a series of travel guidebooks (1801-1859) [Baedeker]</p><p><b>Švicarski protestantski teolog (1886-1968) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Swiss Protestant theologian (1886-1968) [Barth]</p><p><b>Austrijski virtuoz pijanista i skladatelj mnogih djela za klavir (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Austrian virtuoso pianist and composer of many works for the piano [Czerny]</p><p><b>Njemački matematičar koji je razvio teoriju brojeva i koji je primijenio matematiku na struju i magnetizam te astronomiju i geodeziju (1777-1855) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German mathematician who developed the theory of numbers and who applied mathematics to electricity and magnetism and astronomy and geodesy (1777-1855) [Gauss, Karl Gauss]</p><p><b>Njemački pripovjedač koji je pričao apsurdne priče o svojim avanturama kao vojnik i lovac. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German raconteur who told