d cap, service cap, yachting cap]</p><p><b>Njemački astronom koji je prvi iznio zakone planetarnog kretanja (1571-1630) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German astronomer who first stated laws of planetary motion (1571-1630) [Johan Kepler, Johannes Kepler]</p><p><b>zakon koji navodi da je orbita svake planete elipsa s suncem na jednom fokusu elipse (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a law stating that the orbit of each planet is an ellipse with the sun at one focus of the ellipse</p><p><b>(astronomija) jedan od tri empirijska zakona planetarnog kretanja koje je objavio Johannes Kepler (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) one of three empirical laws of planetary motion stated by Johannes Kepler [Kepler's law of planetary motion]</p><p><b>(astronomija) jedan od tri empirijska zakona planetarnog kretanja koje je objavio Johannes Kepler (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) one of three empirical laws of planetary motion stated by Johannes Kepler [Kepler's law]</p><p><b>Zakon koji se odnosi na brzinu kojom se planete kreću. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a law concerning the speed at which planets travel [law of areas, law of equal areas]</p><p><b>zakon koji navodi da je odnos kvadrata revolucionarnog perioda (u godinama) prema kočici orbitalne osi (u astronomskim jedinicama) isti za sve planete (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a law stating that the ratio of the square of the revolutionary period (in years) to the cube of the orbital axis (in astronomical units) is the same for all planets [harmonic law]</p><p><b>čuvati, održan, pohranjenih, sačuvan, sačuvao, zadržao je</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (especially of promises or contracts) not violated or disregarded [unbroken]</p><p><b>održavanje u dobrom stanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> kept in good condition [maintained, well-kept]</p><p><b>preljubna žena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an adulterous woman [fancy woman, mistress]</p><p><b>jezik Čad koji se govori u Čadu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Chadic language spoken in Chad</p><p><b>bol u rožnjači (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pain in the cornea</p><p><b>neuobičajeno izbočenje rožnice oka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal bulging of the cornea of the eye</p><p><b>roživo, keratin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fibrous scleroprotein that occurs in the outer layer of the skin and in horny tissues such as hair, feathers, nails, and hooves [ceratin]</p><p><b>organski proces kojim se keratin depozituje u stanicama i stanice postaju rogaste (kao u noktima i kosi) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> organic process by which keratin is deposited in cells and the cells become horny (as in nails and hair) [keratinization]</p><p><b>pretvoriti u keratin, Postaju napaljeni i impregnirani keratinom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> convert into keratin [keratinize]</p><p><i>v.</i> become horny and impregnated with keratin [keratinize]</p><p><b>organski proces kojim se keratin depozituje u stanicama i stanice postaju rogaste (kao u noktima i kosi) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> organic process by which keratin is deposited in cells and the cells become horny (as in nails and hair) [keratinisation]</p><p><b>pretvoriti u keratin, Postaju napaljeni i impregnirani keratinom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> convert into keratin [keratinise]</p><p><i>v.</i> become horny and impregnated with keratin [keratinise]</p><p><b>keratitis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the cornea causing watery painful eyes and blurred vision</p><p><b>tumor kože koji brzo raste (posebno kod starijih osoba) i nalik je karcinomu, ali se ne širi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> skin tumor that grows rapidly (especially in older people) and resembles a carcinoma but does not spread</p><p><b>hernija rožnjače (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hernia of the cornea</p><p><b>upale rožnice i spojne kosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the cornea and conjunctiva</p><p><b>abnormalna konska izbočina rožnice oka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal cone-shaped protrusion of the cornea of the eye</p><p><b>bilo koji poremećaj kože koji se sastoji od tumora koji izgleda kao rogovit. (MT