om polipropilena (CAS RN 1344-26-8) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mineral consisting of potassium magnesium double sulphate</p><p><b>Dorothea Lange</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States photographer remembered for her portraits of rural workers during the Depression (1895-1965) [Dorothea Lange]</p><p><b>skijaš na skijanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cross-country skier</p><p><b>jedinica sunčevog zračenja, Američki astronom i pionir u zrakoplovstvu koji je izumio bolometar i pridonio dizajnu ranih zrakoplova (1834-1906) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unit of solar radiation</p><p><i>n.</i> United States astronomer and aviation pioneer who invented the bolometer and contributed to the design of early aircraft (1834-1906) [Samuel Pierpoint Langley]</p><p><b>Američki kemičar koji je proučavao kemiju površina i razvio lampu sa volframom punu plina i radio na visokotemperaturnim električnim pražnjavama (1881-1957) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States chemist who studied surface chemistry and developed the gas-filled tungsten lamp and worked on high temperature electrical discharges (1881-1957) [Irving Langmuir]</p><p><b>Langobardi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a Germanic people who invaded northern Italy in the 6th century [Lombard]</p><p><b>Uroci za uzgoj i uzgoj za uzgoj, veliki jedljivi morski rakovi koji imaju trnasti ljusak ali nemaju velike klesnice pravih jastoga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> warm-water lobsters without claws [crayfish, rock lobster, spiny lobster]</p><p><i>n.</i> large edible marine crustacean having a spiny carapace but lacking the large pincers of true lobsters [crawfish, crayfish, rock lobster, sea crawfish, spiny lobster]</p><p><b>U lovu u europskim vodama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> caught in European waters [Norwegian lobster, scampo]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijsko stablo koje nosi jestivu žutu bobicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian tree bearing an edible yellow berry [Lansium domesticum, langset, lanseh tree]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijsko stablo koje nosi jestivu 