ova i stupnjeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a square matrix of n rows and columns</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s zemljama Latinske Amerike ili njihovim narodima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the countries of Latin America or their people</p><p><b>podobitelj obitelji Centropomidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a subfamily of the family Centropomidae</p><p><b>Iz latinskog ili imitatorskog jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> derived from or imitative of Latin</p><p><b>Umjetni jezik zasnovan na latinskom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial language based on Latin</p><p><b>grupa jezika izvedenih iz latinskog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the group of languages derived from Latin [Romance, Romance language]</p><p><b>Pišite latinski alfabet., razlog za usvajanje katolicizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> write in the Latin alphabet [Latinize, Romanise, Romanize]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to adopt Catholicism [catholicise, catholicize, latinize]</p><p><b>riječ ili fraza pozajmljena iz latinskog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a word or phrase borrowed from Latin</p><p><b>latinist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in the Latin language</p><p><b>Pišite latinski alfabet., Prevoditi na latinski., razlog za usvajanje katolicizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> write in the Latin alphabet [Latinise, Romanise, Romanize]</p><p><i>v.</i> translate into Latin</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to adopt Catholicism [catholicise, catholicize, latinise]</p><p><b>latino</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native of Latin America [Latin American]</p><p><i>adj.</i> related to a Spanish-speaking people or culture [Hispanic]</p><p><b>Malo kasno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> somewhat late</p><p><b>veliki leđni mišić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a broad flat muscle on either side of the back [lat]</p><p><b>geografska širina, opseg, paralela, širina, zemljopisna širina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the angular distance between an imaginary line around a heavenly body parallel to its equator and the equator itself</p><p><i>n.</i> freedom from normal restraints in condu