/p><p><i>n.</i> a pale purple color</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a pale purple color [lilac, lilac-colored]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 1. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste biljaka u kategoriji "svetljane" u skladu s člankom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste biljaka u kategoriji "svetljane" u skladu s člankom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> branching aromatic Mediterranean shrub with woolly stems and leaves and yellow flowers [Santolina chamaecyparissus]</p><p><b>od ružičaste boje s lavendalom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of pink tinged with lavender [lilac-pink, violet-pink]</p><p><b>Od nečega obojanog lavandom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of something tinged with lavender</p><p><b>nužnik (od &quot;lav&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tennis player who in 1962 was the second man to win the Australian and French and English and United States singles titles in the same year [Rod Laver, Rodney George Laver]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Old Testament) large basin used by a priest in an ancient Jewish temple to perform ritual ablutions</p><p><i>n.</i> edible red seaweeds [red laver]</p><p><i>n.</i> seaweed with edible translucent crinkly green fronds [sea lettuce]</p><p><b>izdašan, obasipati, obilat, rasipan, rasipati, velikodušan</b></p><p><i>v.</i> expend profusely [shower]</p><p><i>adj.</i> very generous [munificent, overgenerous, too-generous, unsparing, unstinted, unstinting]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by extravagance and profusion [lucullan, plush, plushy]</p><p><b>izdašan, obasipati, obilat, rasipan, rasipati, velikodušan (od &quot;lavish&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a wasteful manner [extravagantly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a rich and lavish manner [extravagantly, richly]</p><p><b>izdašan, obasipati, obilat, rasipan, rasipati, velikodušan (od &quot;lavish&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality possessed by something that is excessively expensive [luxury, sumptuosity, sumptuousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> excessive spending [extravagance, high life, highlife, prodigality]</p><p><b>Francuski kemičar poznat kao otac moderne kemije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French chemist known as the father of modern chemistry [Antoine Laurent Lavoisier, Antoine Lavoisier]</p><p><b>Sovjetski šef tajne policije pod Josifom Stalinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Soviet chief of secret police under Joseph Stalin [Beria]</p><p><b>pravilo, pravni, pravo, zakon, zakonodavstvo, zakona, zakonom, jurisprudencija, prirodni zakon, policija, policijske snage</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the collection of rules imposed by authority [jurisprudence]</p><p><i>n.</i> legal document setting forth rules governing a particular kind of activity</p><p><i>n.</i> a rule or body of rules of conduct inherent in human nature and essential to or binding upon human society [natural law]</p><p><i>n.</i> a generalization that describes recurring facts or events in nature [law of nature]</p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of philosophy concerned with the law and the principles that lead courts to make the decisions they do [jurisprudence, legal philosophy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the learned profession that is mastered by graduate study in a law school and that is responsible for the judicial system [practice of law]</p><p><i>n.</i> the force of policemen and officers [constabulary, police, police force]</p><p><b>odvjetnik u Škotskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solicitor in Scotland</p><p><b>sud, sudnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tribunal that is presided over by a magistrate or by one or more judges who administer justice according to the laws [court, court of justice, court of law, lawcourt]</p><p><b>diplomu koja se dodjeljuje nekome tko je uspješno završio pravni fakultet (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> degree conferred on someone who successfully completes law school</p><p><b>provedba prava, provedba zakona, provedbom zakona, provođenje prava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ensuring obedience to the laws</p><p><b>služba za javni red i sigurnost, služba za očuvanje javnog reda i sigurnosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agency responsible for insuring obedience to the laws</p><p><b>odvjetnički ured</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a firm of lawyers</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of rules applied to commercial transactions [commercial law, mercantile law]</p><p><b>Akcija i reakcija su jednake i suprotne. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> action and reaction are equal and opposite [Newton's third law, Newton's third law of motion, third law of motion]</p><p><b>(hidrostatički) očiti gubitak težine tijela uronjenog u tekućinu jednak je težini premještene tekućine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (hydrostatics) the apparent loss in weight of a body immersed in a fluid is equal to the weight of the displaced fluid [Archimedes' principle]</p><p><b>Zakon koji se odnosi na brzinu kojom se planete kreću. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a law concerning the speed at which planets travel [Kepler's second law, law of equal areas]</p><p><b>Zakon koji potvrđuje da će dugoročno vjerojatnost odrediti performanse. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a law affirming that in the long run probabilities will determine performance</p><p><b>(hemija) princip da je (u kemijskoj ravnoteži) u reverzibilnoj reakciji odnos brzine napredne reakcije prema brzini reverzne reakcije konstantna za tu reakciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) the principle that (at chemical equilibrium) in a reversible reaction the ratio of the rate of the forward reaction to the rate of the reverse reaction is a constant for that reaction [equilibrium law]</p><p><b>Gestaltov princip organizacije koji tvrdi da postoji urođena tendencija za percepcijom nepotpunih objekata kao kompletnih i za zatvaranje ili popunjavanje praznina i za percepciju asimetričnih podražaja kao simetričnih. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Gestalt principle of organization holding that there is an innate tendency to perceive incomplete objects as complete and to close or fill gaps and to perceive asymmetric stimuli as symmetric [closure]</p><p><b>Gestaltov princip organizacije koji drži da će se aspekti perceptivnog polja koji se kreću ili funkcionišu na sličan način doživljavati kao jedinica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Gestalt principle of organization holding that aspects of perceptual field that move or function in a similar manner will be perceived as a unit [common fate]</p><p><b>Osnovni princip fizike da je ukupna energija izolovanog sustava nepromenljiva unatoč unutarnjim promjenama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fundamental principle of physics that the total energy of an isolated system is constant despite internal changes [conservation of energy, first law of thermodynamics]</p><p><b>Osnovni princip klasične fizike da materija ne može biti stvorena ili uništena u izoliranom sustavu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fundamental principle of classical physics that matter cannot be created or destroyed in an isolated system [conservation of mass, conservation of matter, law of conservation of matter]</p><p><b>Osnovni princip klasične fizike da materija ne može biti stvorena ili uništena u izoliranom sustavu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fundamental principle of classical physics that matter cannot be created or destroyed in an isolated system [conservation of mass, conservation of matter, law of conservation of mass]</p><p><b>(kemija) zakon koji navodi da svaka čista tvar uvijek sadrži iste elemente kombinirane u istim masnim proporcijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) law stating that every pure substance always contains the same elements combined in the same proportions by weight [law of definite proportions]</p><p><b>Gestaltov princip organizacije koji tvrdi da postoji urođena tendencija da se linija smatra nastavkom svog uspostavljenog smjera. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Gestalt principle of organization holding that there is an innate tendency to perceive a line as continuing its established direction [continuation, good continuation]</p><p><b>(kemija) zakon koji navodi da svaka čista tvar uvijek sadrži iste elemente kombinirane u istim masnim proporcijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) law stating that every pure substance always contains the same elements combined in the same proportions by weight [law of constant proportion]</p><p><b>zakon padajućih prinosa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a law affirming that to continue after a certain level of performance has been reached will result in a decline in effectiveness</p><p><b>(psihologija) princip da se ponašanje bira po njihovim posljedicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) the principle that behaviors are selected by their consequences</p><p><b>Zakon koji se odnosi na brzinu kojom se planete kreću. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a law concerning the speed at which planets travel [Kepler's second law, law of areas]</p><p><b>(kemijski) zakon koji navodi da su proporcije u kojima se dva elementa odvojeno kombinuju s trećim elementom također proporcije u kojima se kombinuju zajedno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) law stating that the proportions in which two elements separately combine with a third element are also the proportions in which they combine together [law of reciprocal proportions]</p><p><b>(fizički) zakon koji kaže da bilo koja dva tijela privlače jedni druge s silom koja je direktno proporcionalna sa proizvodom njihovih masa i obrnuto proporcionalna kvadratu udaljenosti između njih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the law that states any two bodies attract each other with a force that is directly proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them [Newton's law of gravitation]</p><p><b>Svaki član homolognog para hromozoma se odvaja neovisno o članovima drugih parova tako da su rezultati nasumični. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> each member of a pair of homologous chromosomes separates independently of the members of other pairs so the results are random</p><p><b>zakon velikih brojeva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (statistics) law stating that a large number of items taken at random from a population will (on the average) have the population statistics [Bernoulli's law]</p><p><b>(kemija) zakon koji navodi sljedeći princip: brzina kemijske reakcije je izravno proporcionalna molekulskim koncentracijama reagirajućih tvari. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) the law that states the following principle: the rate of a chemical reaction is directly proportional to the molecular concentrations of the reacting substances</p><p><b>Zakoni (počevši od Deset zapovijedi) koje je Bog dao Izraelcima preko Mojsija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the laws (beginning with the Ten Commandments) that God gave to the Israelites through Moses [Mosaic law]</p><p><b>jedan od tri osnovna zakona klasične mehanike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of three basic laws of classical mechanics [Newton's law, Newton's law of motion]</p><p><b>(hemija) zakon koji navodi da kada se dva elementa mogu kombinirati kako bi formirali više od jedne spoje količine jednog od njih koji se kombiniraju s fiksnom količinom drugog će pokazati jednostavnu višestruku vezu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) law stating that when two elements can combine to form more than one compound the amounts of one of them that combines with a fixed amount of the other will exhibit a simple multiple relation [Dalton's law]</p><p><b>pravo država, internacionalno pravo, međunarodno pravo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of laws governing relations between nations [international law]</p><p><b>prirodni zakon, zakon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a generalization that describes recurring facts or events in nature [law]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, poduzeća mogu imati: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principle that entities should not be multiplied needlessly [Occam's Razor, Ockham's Razor, principle of parsimony]</p><p><b>(hemija i fizika) zakon koji navodi da je pritisak koji vrši mješavina plinova jednak sjem partijalnih pritisaka plinova u mješavini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry and physics) law stating that the pressure exerted by a mixture of gases equals the sum of the partial pressures of the gases in the mixture [Dalton's law, Dalton's law of partial pressures]</p><p><b>Gestaltov princip organizacije koji smatra da se (s druge stvari jednake) predmeti ili događaji koji su jedni drugima blizu (u prostoru ili vremenu) doživljavaju kao da pripadaju zajedno kao jedinica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Gestalt principle of organization holding that (other things being equal) objects or events that are near to one another (in space or time) are perceived as belonging together as a unit [proximity]</p><p><b>(kemijski) zakon koji navodi da su proporcije u kojima se dva elementa odvojeno kombinuju s trećim elementom također proporcije u kojima se kombinuju zajedno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) law stating that the proportions in which two elements separately combine with a third element are also the proportions in which they combine together [law of equivalent proportions]</p><p><b>članovi para homolognih hromozoma odvajaju se tijekom formiranja gameta i raspoređuju se na različite gamete tako da svaki gamet prima samo jednog člana para (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> members of a pair of homologous chromosomes separate during the formation of gametes and are distributed to different gametes so that every gamete receives only one member of the pair</p><p><b>Gestaltov princip organizacije koji smatra da (sve ostalo jednako) dijelovi polja podražaja koji su slični jedni drugima imaju tendenciju da se doživljavaju kao pripadajući zajedno kao jedinica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Gestalt principle of organization holding that (other things being equal) parts of a stimulus field that are similar to each other tend to be perceived as belonging together as a unit [similarity]</p><p><b>izraz koji se koristi u Magna Carta da se odnosi na tada uspostavljen zakon kraljevstva (za razliku od rimskog ili civilnog prava) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a phrase used in the Magna Carta to refer to the then established law of the kingdom (as distinct from Roman or civil law)</p><p><b>(fizička) zakon koji uređuje odnose između stanja energije u zatvorenom sustavu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a law governing the relations between states of energy in a closed system</p><p><b>(fizički) gustoća idealnog plina na konstantnom pritisku varira obrnuto s temperaturom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the density of an ideal gas at constant pressure varies inversely with the temperature [Charles's law, Gay-Lussac's law]</p><p><b>netko tko krši zakon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who violates the law [lawbreaker, violator]</p><p><b>policijski dužnosnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an officer of the law [lawman, peace officer]</p><p><b>pravni rad (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of law</p><p><b>fakultet koji nudi studije koje vode do diplome pravnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graduate school offering study leading to a law degree [school of law]</p><p><b>student pravnog fakulteta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a student in law school</p><p><b>miroljubiv, pokoran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of individuals) adhering strictly to laws and rules and customs [observant]</p><p><b>(kriminalno pravo) djelo koje je kažnjivo zakonom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (criminal law) an act punishable by law [crime, criminal offence, criminal offense]</p><p><b>legislatura, zakonodavno tijelo, zakonodavstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> persons who make or amend or repeal laws [general assembly, legislative assembly, legislative body, legislature]</p><p><b>netko tko krši zakon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who violates the law [law offender, violator]</p><p><b>sud</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tribunal that is presided over by a magistrate or by one or more judges who administer justice according to the laws [court, court of justice, court of law, law court]</p><p><b>pravedan, zakonit, zakoniti, zakonski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> conformable to or allowed by law</p><p><i>adj.</i> according to custom or rule or natural law [rule-governed]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a legally established claim [rightful, true]</p><p><i>adj.</i> authorized, sanctioned by, or in accordance with law [legitimate, licit]</p><p><b>zakonito, zakonski</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a manner acceptable to common custom [legitimately, licitly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> by law [de jure, legally]</p><p><b>Rođeni u braku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> born in wedlock</p><p><b>pravičnost, u skladu sa zakonom, zakonitost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of conforming to law</p><p><b>-Pravitelj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a maker of laws [lawmaker]</p><p><b>bezakonit, protuzakonit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> without law or control [anarchic, anarchical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lax in enforcing laws [wide-open]</p><p><i>adj.</i> disobedient to or defiant of law [outlaw]</p><p><b>ilegalno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an illegal manner [illegally, illicitly]</p><p><b>bezakonje, anarhija, bezvlašće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of lawlessness and disorder (usually resulting from a failure of government) [anarchy]</p><p><i>n.</i> illegality as a consequence of unlawful acts [outlawry]</p><p><b>-Pravitelj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a maker of laws [lawgiver]</p><p><b>legislacija, legislativa, zakonodavstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making or enacting laws [legislating, legislation]</p><p><b>policijski dužnosnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an officer of the law [law officer, peace officer]</p><p><b>batist, ledina, livada, proplanak, tanko platno, tratina, travnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a field of cultivated and mowed grass</p><p><b>kuglačka igra igra na ravnom travnjaku s pristranim drvenim lopticama koje se valjaju na džeku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bowling game played on a level lawn with biased wooden balls that are rolled at a jack [bowls]</p><p><b>kolica za nošenje malih tereta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cart for carrying small loads [barrow, garden cart, wheelbarrow]</p><p><b>stolica ostavljena vani za korištenje na travnjaku ili u vrtu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chair left outside for use on a lawn or in a garden [garden chair]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za uređaje za uređivanje i uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređivanje uređaja za uređ (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> furniture intended for use on a lawn or in a garden</p><p><b>stroj za košnju tratine, kosilica, kosilica za travu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> garden tool for mowing grass on lawns [mower]</p><p><b>grupa ljudi okupljenih za društvenu interakciju izvan vrata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a party of people assembled for social interaction out of doors [fete champetre, garden party]</p><p><b>tenis na travi, tenis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a game played with rackets by two or four players who hit a ball back and forth over a net that divides the court [tennis]</p><p><b>vrtna alatka, vrtni alat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used for working in gardens or yards [garden tool]</p><p><b>Rimski mučenik, Velški vojnik koji je od 1916. do 1918. godine organizirao arapsku pobunu protiv Turaka., Engleski slikar portretnih slika poznat po seriji portretnih slika vođa saveza protiv Napoleona (1769-1830), Engleska glumica (1898-1952), Američki fizičar koji je razvio ciklotron (1901-1958), Engleski romanopisac, pjesnik i esejista čiji rad osuđuje industrijsko društvo i istražuje seksualne odnose (1885-1930), grad u sjeveroistočnom Kansasu na rijeci Kansas (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Roman martyr [Laurentius, Saint Lawrence, St. Lawrence]</p><p><i>n.</i> Welsh soldier who from 1916 to 1918 organized the Arab revolt against the Turks [Lawrence of Arabia, T. E. Lawrence, Thomas Edward Lawrence]</p><p><i>n.</i> English portrait painter remembered for the series of portraits of the leaders of the alliance against Napoleon (1769-1830) [Sir Thomas Lawrence]</p><p><i>n.</i> English actress (1898-1952) [Gertrude Lawrence]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States physicist who developed the cyclotron (1901-1958) [E. O. Lawrence, Ernest Orlando Lawrence]</p><p><i>n.</i> English novelist and poet and essayist whose work condemned industrial society and explored sexual relationships (1885-1930) [D. H. Lawrence, David Herbert Lawrence]</p><p><i>n.</i> a town in northeastern Kansas on the Kansas River</p><p><b>Engleski pisac irskog podrijetla koji je veći dio života proveo u mediteranskim područjima (1912-1990) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English writer of Irish descent who spent much of his life in Mediterranean regions (1912-1990) [Durrell, Lawrence George Durrell]</p><p><b>Engleski pisac irskog podrijetla koji je veći dio života proveo u mediteranskim područjima (1912-1990) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English writer of Irish descent who spent much of his life in Mediterranean regions (1912-1990) [Durrell, Lawrence Durrell]</p><p><b>Velški vojnik koji je od 1916. do 1918. godine organizirao arapsku pobunu protiv Turaka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Welsh soldier who from 1916 to 1918 organized the Arab revolt against the Turks [Lawrence, T. E. Lawrence, Thomas Edward Lawrence]</p><p><b>Američki bejzbolista (rođen 1925) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States baseball player (born 1925) [Berra, Yogi, Yogi Berra]</p><p><b>lawrencij, Lw, atomski broj 103, lorensij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radioactive transuranic element synthesized from californium [Lr, atomic number 103]</p><p><b>zakona, zakoni, zakonima</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first of three divisions of the Hebrew Scriptures comprising the first five books of the Hebrew Bible considered as a unit [Pentateuch, Torah]</p><p><b>veliko drvo iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s promjerom debla do 12 stopa i visinom do 200 stopa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large timber 