na slatkog krumpira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungus causing soft watery rot in fruits and vegetables and rings of dry rot around roots of sweet potatoes [Rhizopus stolonifer, ring rot fungus]</p><p><b>biti ispuštena (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be leaked [leak]</p><p><b>curenje, istjecanje, lekaža</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the discharge of a fluid from some container [escape, leak, outflow]</p><p><b>curiti, gubitak, gubljenje, gubljenje (npr. memorije), istjecanje, otvor, prodor vode, propuštati, pukotina (od &quot;leak&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a surreptitious informant</p><p><b>Engleski paleontolog (sin Louisa Leakeya i Mary Leakey) koji je nastavio rad svojih roditelja, Engleski paleontolog (žena Louisa Leakeyja) koji je otkrio lubanju Zinjanthropusa koja je bila stara 1.750.000 godina (1913-1996), Engleski paleontolog čiji je izvještaj o fosilnim otkrićima u Tanzaniji promijenio teorije ljudske evolucije (1903-1972) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English paleontologist (son of Louis Leakey and Mary Leakey) who continued the work of his parents [Richard Erskine Leakey, Richard Leakey]</p><p><i>n.</i> English paleontologist (the wife of Louis Leakey) who discovered the Zinjanthropus skull that was 1,750,000 years old (1913-1996) [Mary Douglas Leakey, Mary Leakey]</p><p><i>n.</i> English paleontologist whose account of fossil discoveries in Tanzania changed theories of human evolution (1903-1972) [Louis Leakey, Louis Seymour Bazett Leakey]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se ne primjenjuje ovaj standard, za svaki proizvod koji se upotrebljava za proizvodnju električne energije, potrebno je utvrditi: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of permitting leaks or leakage</p><p><b>koji ne propušta, ne curi, plin)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not subject to leaks</p><p><b>brbljav, koji prokapljuje, propustan, propustljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> permitting the unwanted passage of fluids or gases</p><p><i>adj.</i> used informally</p><p><i>adj.</i> prone to communicate confidential information [blabbermouthed, talebearing, tattling]</p><p><b>vjerni i istiniti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> faithful and true</p><p><b>mršav, naginjanje, naginjati se, nagnuti se, naslanjanje, oslanjanje, osloniti, postan, slab, suh, tanak, nagnutost, nakrivljenost, neravnost, iskriviti, iskrivljavati, izvijati, izviti, kriviti, nagibati, naginjati, nagnuti, naheriti, nakositi, nakriviti, pregibati, presavijati, presavinuti, savijati, savinuti, svijati, svinuti, ukositi, zakositi, zakriviti, zakrivljivati, osloniti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property possessed by a line or surface that departs from the vertical [inclination, leaning, list, tilt]</p><p><i>v.</i> to incline or bend from a vertical position [angle, slant, tilt, tip]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to lean or incline</p><p><i>v.</i> have a tendency or disposition to do or be something [be given, incline, run, tend]</p><p><i>v.</i> rely on for support</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to lean to the side [list]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking excess flesh [thin]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking in mineral content or combustible material</p><p><i>adj.</i> containing little excess [skimpy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not profitable or prosperous</p><p><b>Odmor za podršku (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> rest on for support [lean on, rest on]</p><p><b>pomaknite gornji dio tijela unazad i dolje (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> move the upper body backwards and down [recline]</p><p><b>Odmor za podršku (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> rest on for support [lean against, rest on]</p><p><b>krhotina s krovom koja ima samo jednu nagibnu stranu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rough shelter whose roof has only one slope</p><p><b>šator koji je pričvršćen na stranu zgrade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tent that is attached to the side of a building</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) mlada voljena Heroja koji se utopio u oluji u Hellespont na jednom od svojih noćnih posjeta da je vidi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) a youth beloved of Hero who drowned in a storm in the Hellespont on one of his nightly visits to see her</p><p><b>mršav, naginjanje, naginjati se, nagnuti se, naslanjanje, oslanjanje, osloniti, postan, slab, suh, tanak (od &quot;lean&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (horseshoes) the throw of a horseshoe so as to lean against (but not encircle) the stake</p><p><b>kosi, nagnut, tendencija, nagnutost, nakrivljenost, neravnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inclination to do something [propensity, tendency]</p><p><i>n.</i> a natural inclination [proclivity, propensity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property possessed by a line or surface that departs from the vertical [inclination, lean, list, tilt]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of deviating from a vertical position</p><p><i>adj.</i> departing or being caused to depart from the true vertical or horizontal [atilt, canted, tilted, tipped]</p><p><b>visoka okrugla mramorna zvonika u Pisi koja nije pravougačna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tall round marble campanile in Pisa that is not perpendicular [Leaning Tower of Pisa]</p><p><b>visoka okrugla mramorna zvonika u Pisi koja nije pravougačna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tall round marble campanile in Pisa that is not perpendicular [Leaning Tower]</p><p><b>mršavost, slabost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being meager [exiguity, meagerness, meagreness, poorness, scantiness, scantness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of having little body fat [spareness, thinness]</p><p><b>cupkati, divokoza, odskočiti, preskakivati, skakanje, skakati, skakutati, skočiti, skok, porast, odskakutati, preskakati, preskočiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light, self-propelled movement upwards or forwards [bounce, bound, leaping, saltation, spring]</p><p><i>n.</i> an abrupt transition [jump, saltation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden and decisive increase [jump]</p><p><i>n.</i> the distance leaped (or to be leaped)</p><p><i>v.</i> move forward by leaps and bounds [bound, jump, spring]</p><p><i>v.</i> pass abruptly from one state or topic to another [jump]</p><p><i>v.</i> jump down from an elevated point [jump, jump off]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to jump or leap [jump]</p><p><b>ime dana koji se dodaje tijekom prestupne godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the name of the day that is added during a leap year [February 29, bissextile day]</p><p><b>isticati se, istaknuti se, istaći se, izdvajati se, izdvojiti se, odskakati, odskočiti, odudarati, razlikovati se, stršati, stršiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be highly noticeable [jump, jump out, stand out, stick out]</p><p><i>v.</i> jump out from a hiding place and surprise (someone) [burst forth, rush out, sally out]</p><p><b>sekunda (mjerena atomskim satom) dodana ili oduzeta od Greenwichskog vremena kako bi se nadoknadila usporavanje rotacije Zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a second (as measured by an atomic clock) added to or subtracted from Greenwich Mean Time in order to compensate for slowing in the Earth's rotation</p><p><b>prestupna god, prijestupna godina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a calendar year with an extra day added in February [366 days, bissextile year, intercalary year]</p><p><b>cupkati, divokoza, odskočiti, preskakivati, skakanje, skakati, skakutati, skočiti, skok (od &quot;leap&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who bounds or leaps (as in competition) [bounder]</p><p><b>napredovanje kao u dječijoj igri, preskačući prepreke ili natjecatelje, igra u kojoj se jedno dijete savije a drugo skače., skoči preko., napredak velikim skokovima umjesto malim porastom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> advancing as if in the child's game, by leaping over obstacles or competitors</p><p><i>n.</i> a game in which one child bends down and another leaps over</p><p><i>v.</i> jump across</p><p><i>v.</i> progress by large jumps instead of small increments</p><p><b>nestašan, živahan, skok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light, self-propelled movement upwards or forwards [bounce, bound, leap, saltation, spring]</p><p><b>Britanski umjetnik i pisac bezumnih stihova (1812-1888), Heroj tragedije Williama Shakespearea koji je izdan i zlostavljan od strane dvije njegove kćeri. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British artist and writer of nonsense verse (1812-1888) [Edward Lear]</p><p><i>n.</i> the hero of William Shakespeare's tragedy who was betrayed and mistreated by two of his scheming daughters [King Lear]</p><p><b>izučiti, naučiti, saznati, učenje, učiti, uče, sticati, usvajati, usvojiti, načuti, saznavati, čuti, pohađati, studirati, školovati se, instruirati, podučavati, podučiti, poučavati, poučiti, provjeravati, provjeriti, ustanoviti, ustanovljavati, utvrditi, utvrđivati, uvjeravati se, uvjeriti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> gain knowledge or skills [acquire, larn]</p><p><i>v.</i> get to know or become aware of, usually accidentally [discover, find out, get a line, get wind, get word, hear, pick up, see]</p><p><i>v.</i> commit to memory [con, memorise, memorize]</p><p><i>v.</i> be a student of a certain subject [read, study, take]</p><p><i>v.</i> impart skills or knowledge to [instruct, teach]</p><p><i>v.</i> find out, learn, or determine with certainty, usually by making an inquiry or other effort [ascertain, check, determine, find out, see, watch]</p><p><b>načitan, naučen, naučile, naučili, naučio, učen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing profound knowledge [erudite]</p><p><i>adj.</i> highly educated [knowing, knowledgeable, lettered, well-educated, well-read]</p><p><i>adj.</i> established by conditioning or learning [conditioned]</p><p><b>osoba koja je primljena u članstvo u znanstvenom području (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who has been admitted to membership in a scholarly field [initiate, pundit, savant]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, poduzeća koja se bave stručnim radom mogu imati: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the three professions traditionally believed to require advanced learning and high principles</p><p><b>Reakcija koja je stečena učenjem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reaction that has been acquired by learning [learned response]</p><p><b>Reakcija koja je stečena učenjem. (