 za Jupiter (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an epithet for Jupiter [Jupiter Fulgur, Jupiter Fulminator]</p><p><b>gromobran</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is a frequent target of negative reactions and serves to distract attention from another</p><p><i>n.</i> a metallic conductor that is attached to a high point and leads to the ground [lightning conductor]</p><p><b>neprolazno svjetlom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not penetrable by light [light-tight]</p><p><b>i određeno vrijeme spavanja., (vojni) signal da ugasite svjetla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a prescribed bedtime</p><p><i>n.</i> (military) signal to turn the lights out [taps]</p><p><b>brod svjetionik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ship equipped like a lighthouse and anchored where a permanent lighthouse would be impracticable</p><p><b>graciozan, lak, ljubak</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> moving easily and quickly [light, tripping]</p><p><i>adj.</i> carefree and happy and lighthearted [blithe, blithesome, light-hearted, lighthearted]</p><p><b>graciozan, lak, ljubak (od &quot;lightsome&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> moving with quick light steps [trippingly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a light-hearted manner [light-heartedly]</p><p><b>graciozan, lak, ljubak (od &quot;lightsome&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cheerful feeling you have when nothing is troubling you [carefreeness, insouciance, lightheartedness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the gracefulness of a person or animal that is quick and nimble [agility, legerity, lightness, nimbleness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being lighthearted and frivolous [lightness]</p><p><b>lagani</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a professional boxer who weighs between 131 and 135 pounds</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is unimportant but cheeky and presumptuous [jackanapes, whippersnapper]</p><p><i>n.</i> an amateur boxer who weighs no more than 132 pounds</p><p><i>n.</i> a wrestler who weighs 139-154 pounds</p><p><i>adj.</i> weighing relatively little compared with another item or object of similar use</p><p><i>adj.</i> having no importance or i