inty [belike, in all likelihood, in all probability, probably]</p><p><b>izjednačavati, izjednačiti, sravniti, sravnjivati, usporediti, uspoređivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> consider or describe as similar, equal, or analogous [compare, equate]</p><p><b>sličnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similarity in appearance or character or nature between persons or things [alikeness, similitude]</p><p><i>n.</i> picture consisting of a graphic image of a person or thing [semblance]</p><p><b>izjednačavati, izjednačiti, sravniti, sravnjivati, usporediti, uspoređivati (od &quot;liken&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of comparing similarities</p><p><b>isto tako, na isti način, slično, također</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in like or similar manner [similarly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in addition [also, as well, besides, too]</p><p><i>adv.</i> equally [alike]</p><p><b>dopadanje, naklonost, sviđanje, sviđati, voljenje, preferencija, sklonost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of pleasure and enjoyment</p><p><b>100 makuta jednako je 1 zaire u Zairu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> 100 makuta equal 1 zaire in Zaire</p><p><b>jorgovan, ljubičast</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Syringa having large panicles of usually fragrant flowers</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a pale purple color [lavender, lilac-colored]</p><p><b>od plave boje sa lavendalom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of blue tinged with lavender [violet-blue]</p><p><b>od svjetlo ljubičaste boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a pale purple color [lavender, lilac]</p><p><b>od ružičaste boje s lavendalom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of pink tinged with lavender [lavender-pink, violet-pink]</p><p><b>od purpura obojenog lilakom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of purple tinged with lilac</p><p><b>osnovna jedinica novca u Swazilandu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Swaziland</p><p><b>obuhvaća vrste koje se ponekad dijele u sljedeće obitelji: Alliaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> includes species sometimes divided among the following families: Alliaceae [family Liliaceae, lily family]</p><p><b>za biljke iz obitelji Liliaceae ili koje pripadaju biljkama ili su karakteristične za biljke iz obitelji Liliaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or characteristic of plants of the family Liliaceae</p><p><b>biljka koja raste iz bulbe ili korme ili rizoma ili gomolja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant growing from a bulb or corm or rhizome or tuber</p><p><b>red jednokotilnih biljaka uključujući Amaryllidaceae i Liliaceae i Iridaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an order of monocotyledonous plants including Amaryllidaceae and Liliaceae and Iridaceae [order Liliales]</p><p><b>Engleski baletni plesač (rođen 1910.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English ballet dancer (born in 1910) [Dame Alicia Markova, Markova]</p><p><b>obitelj jednokotilnih biljaka potklase Liliidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of monocotyledonous plants of the subclass Liliidae</p><p><b>rod biljaka s jednim koštom, uglavnom biljke s uglavnom petaloidnim sepalom i laticama i složenim pistilima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of monocotyledonous plants comprising mostly herbs having usually petaloid sepals and petals and compound pistils</p><p><b>jedan od četiri podklase ili superredova monocotyledona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of four subclasses or superorders of Monocotyledones [subclass Liliidae]</p><p><b>biljka s jednokotilnom biljkom s cvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monocotyledonous flowering plant [endogen, monocot, monocotyledon]</p><p><b>porodica jednosupnica, porodica liliopsida, porodica monokotiledona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of flowering plants having a single cotyledon (embryonic leaf) in the seed [monocot family]</p><p><b>rod jednosupnica, rod liliopsida, rod monokotiledona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of flowering plants having a single cotyledon (embryonic leaf) in the seed [monocot genus]</p><p><b>s sadržajem sjemena koje proizvode embrion s jednim kotiledom i lištima s paralelnim žilama: uključuje travnjake i lilije te palme i orhideje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comprising seed plants that produce an embryo with a single cotyledon and parallel-veined leaves: includes grasses and lilies and palms and orchids [Monocotyledonae, Monocotyledones, class Liliopsida, class Monocotyledonae, class Monocotyledones]</p><p><b>Lilit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in ancient Semitic folklore: a female demon who attacks children</p><p><b>ljiljan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of Liliaceae [genus Lilium]</p><p><b>Japanski lilij sa zlatnim zrake (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Japanese lily with golden rays [mountain lily]</p><p><b>obična lilija istočne Sjedinjenih Država s žutim ili crvenkastim cvjetovima s smeđim mrljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common lily of the eastern United States having nodding yellow or reddish flowers spotted with brown [Canada lily, meadow lily, wild meadow lily, wild yellow lily]</p><p><b>lilij na istočnom Mediteranu i na Balkanu s širokim bijelim cvjetovima u obliku lovora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lily of eastern Mediterranean and the Balkans with broad funnel-shaped white flowers [Annunciation lily, Lent lily, Madonna lily, white lily]</p><p><b>lilij južnoistočnih Sjedinjenih Država s čašnim cvjetovima sa duboko žutim do crvenokrasnim rekurzivnim laticama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lily of southeastern United States having cup-shaped flowers with deep yellow to scarlet recurved petals [leopard lily, pine lily, tiger lily]</p><p><b>lilij zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s najozbiljnijim narandžast-crvenom ljubičasto-pomičkanim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lily of western North America with showy orange-red purple-spotted flowers [Columbia tiger lily, Oregon lily]</p><p><b>Istočnoazijska višegodišnja biljka s velikim crvenkasto-narandžastim crnim pločama s reflektiranim laticama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> east Asian perennial having large reddish-orange black-spotted flowers with reflexed petals [devil lily, kentan, tiger lily]</p><p><b>Visoki lilij imaju velike bijele trube u obliku cvijeća koji cvjetaju u proljeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall lily have large white trumpet-shaped flowers that bloom in the spring [Bermuda lily, Easter lily, white trumpet lily]</p><p><b>lilij na pacifičkoj obali Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orange-flowered lily of Pacific coast of United States [coast lily]</p><p><b>lilij s malim tupim ljubičastim cvijećima iz sjeverozapadne Europe i sjeverozapadne Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lily with small dull purple flowers of northwestern Europe and northwestern Asia [Turk's-cap, martagon]</p><p><b>lilij srednje Sjeverne Amerike s povratnim narandžastoprozirnim cvjetovima s dubokim crvenim mrljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lily of central North America having recurved orange-red flowers with deep crimson spots [Michigan lily]</p><p><b>lilij zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s narandžastokrvenim do crvenokrasno-maroon-makičastom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lily of western United States having orange-red to crimson maroon-spotted flowers [leopard lily, panther lily]</p><p><b>lilij istočne Sjeverne Amerike s narandžastom do narandžasto-crveno-fioletskim ptičastim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lily of eastern North America having orange to orange-red purple-spotted flowers [wood lily]</p><p><b>lilij istočnih Sjedinjenih Država s narandžastom do crvenom crvenom ptičastom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lily of the eastern United States with orange to red maroon-spotted flowers [Turk's-cap, Turk's cap-lily]</p><p><b>kraljica havajskih otoka (1838-1917) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> queen of the Hawaiian islands (1838-1917) [Lydia Kamekeha Paki Liliuokalani]</p><p><b>industrijski grad u sjevernoj Francuskoj blizu belgijske granice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industrial city in northern France near the Belgian border</p><p><b>Američka filmska glumica koja se pojavila u filmovima D. W. Griffitha (1896-1993) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film actress who appeared in films by D. W. Griffith (1896-1993) [Gish]</p><p><b>Američki dramaturg (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States playwright [Hellman]</p><p><b>Američka zabavljačica poznata po ulogama u komičnim operaama (1861-1922) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States entertainer remembered for her roles in comic operas (1861-1922) [Russell]</p><p><b>Britanska glumica (rođena u Kanadi) (1898-1989) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British actress (born in Canada) (1898-1989) [Beatrice Lillie, Lady Peel]</p><p><b>Britanska glumica i ljubavnica princa koji je kasnije postao Edward VII. (1853-1929) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British actress and mistress of the prince who later became Edward VII (1853-1929) [Emilie Charlotte le Breton, Jersey Lillie, Langtry]</p><p><b>Zemlju koju je zamišljao Jonathan Swift, gdje su živjeli mali ljudi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a land imagined by Jonathan Swift that was inhabited by tiny people</p><p><b>vrlo mala osoba (slična Liliputijanu), Visoki stanovnik Lilliputa u romanu Jonathana Swifta., mali., vrlo mali, (neformalno) malo i od male važnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a very small person (resembling a Lilliputian)</p><p><i>n.</i> a 6-inch tall inhabitant of Lilliput in a novel by Jonathan Swift</p><p><i>adj.</i> tiny</p><p><i>adj.</i> very small [bantam, diminutive, flyspeck, midget, petite, tiny]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (informal) small and of little importance [fiddling, footling, little, niggling, petty, picayune, piddling, piffling, trivial]</p><p><b>Glavni grad Malavija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital of Malawi [capital of Malawi]</p><p><b>vesel ritam u glazbi., artikuliraju na vrlo pažljiv i ritmičan način (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a jaunty rhythm in music [swing]</p><p><i>v.</i> articulate in a very careful and rhythmic way</p><p><b>karakteriziran je plutajućim ritmom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by a buoyant rhythm [swinging, swingy, tripping]</p><p><b>đurđica, ljiljan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any liliaceous plant of the genus Lilium having showy pendulous flowers</p><p><b>obuhvaća vrste koje se ponekad dijele u sljedeće obitelji: Alliaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> includes species sometimes divided among the following families: Alliaceae [Liliaceae, family Liliaceae]</p><p><b>Andska biljka s grlom od blesavih ružičasta ljubičastih cvjetova nalik lilijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Andean herb having umbels of showy pinkish-purple lily-like flowers [Alstroemeria pelegrina, Peruvian lily]</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka iz roda Agapanthus s čvorom od bledo-fioleta cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Agapanthus having umbels of showy blue to purple flowers [agapanthus]</p><p><b>đurđica, đurđevak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing perennial plant having usually two large oblong lanceolate leaves and a raceme of small fragrant nodding bell-shaped flowers followed by scarlet berries [Convallaria majalis, May lily]</p><p><b>plutajuće lišće vodene ljiljanke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> floating leaves of a water lily</p><p><b>Sjedinjene Države koloratura sopran (rođen u Francuskoj) (1904-1976) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States coloratura soprano (born in France) (1904-1976) [Alice-Josephine Pons, Pons]</p><p><b>Azijska višegodišnja biljka s zelenim listovima poput trave i grmovima tamno-mavičastih cvjetova poput grožđa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic perennial tufted herb with grasslike evergreen foliage and clusters of dark mauve grapelike flowers [Liriope muscari, lilyturf]</p><p><b>lako se uplaši. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> easily frightened [chicken, chickenhearted, white-livered, yellow, yellow-bellied]</p><p><b>Azijski stalež sa blistavim lišćama i spuštenim grmovima bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> broad-leaved evergreen Asiatic shrub with glossy leaves and drooping clusters of white flowers [Japanese andromeda, Pieris japonica, andromeda]</p><p><b>nevin</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> restricted to whites only [white]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a pure white color</p><p><b>Azijska višegodišnja biljka s zelenim listovima poput trave i grmovima tamno-mavičastih cvjetova poput grožđa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic perennial tufted herb with grasslike evergreen foliage and clusters of dark mauve grapelike flowers [Liriope muscari, lily turf]</p><p><b>Glavni i najveći grad i gospodarski centar Perua (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capital and largest city and economic center of Peru [capital of Peru]</p><p><b>biljka graha od busha koja se uzgaja uglavnom u južnim Sjedinjenim Državama s malim ravnim jestivim sjemenima, biljka od grma ili visokokvalitetne biljke graha s velikim ravnim jestivim sjemenima, Širi ravni grah nježno kuhan. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bush bean plant cultivated especially in southern United States having small flat edible seeds [Phaseolus lunatus, butter-bean plant, butter bean, sieva bean]</p><p><i>n.</i> bush or tall-growing bean plant having large flat edible seeds [Phaseolus limensis, lima bean plant]</p><p><i>n.</i> broad flat beans simmered gently</p><p><b>biljka od grma ili visokokvalitetne biljke graha s velikim ravnim jestivim sjemenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bush or tall-growing bean plant having large flat edible seeds [Phaseolus limensis, lima bean]</p><p><b>šljunčari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slugs [family Limacidae]</p><p><b>od ili nalik pužku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or resembling a slug [limacoid]</p><p><b>od ili nalik pužku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or resembling a slug [limacine]</p><p><b>dugačka uska laguna blizu ušća rijeke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long narrow lagoon near the mouth of a river</p><p><b>rod Pleuronectidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Pleuronectidae [genus Limanda]</p><p><b>rod Limacidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Limacidae [genus Limax]</p><p><b>bodk, član, ekstremitet, osakatiti, raskomadati, raščlaniti, ud, drška, grana, krak, krilo, odvojak, ogranak, rukav, rukavac, ručica, ručka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the jointed appendages of an animal used for locomotion or grasping: arm</p><p><i>n.</i> any of the main branches arising from the trunk 