aničavanje, ograničavati, ograničenje, ograničiti, ograničiti se, prepreka, mjera, delimitacija, demarkacija, razgraničenje, opredijeliti se, precizirati, specificirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the greatest possible degree of something [bound, boundary]</p><p><i>n.</i> final or latest limiting point [terminal point, terminus ad quem]</p><p><i>n.</i> as far as something can go</p><p><i>n.</i> the boundary of a specific area [demarcation, demarcation line]</p><p><i>n.</i> the mathematical value toward which a function goes as the independent variable approaches infinity [limit point, point of accumulation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the greatest amount of something that is possible or allowed [limitation]</p><p><i>v.</i> place limits on (extent or amount or access) [bound, confine, restrict, throttle, trammel]</p><p><i>v.</i> restrict or confine within limits [circumscribe, confine to]</p><p><i>v.</i> decide upon or fix definitely [define, determine, fix, set, specify]</p><p><b>granica, limes</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mathematical value toward which a function goes as the independent variable approaches infinity [limit, point of accumulation]</p><p><b>granica, limitacija, nedostatak, ograničenja, ograničenje, ograničenjima, uvjet, ograničavanje, restrikcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a principle that limits the extent of something [restriction]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being limited or restricted</p><p><i>n.</i> the greatest amount of something that is possible or allowed [limit]</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a time period after which suits cannot be brought</p><p><i>n.</i> an act of limiting or restricting (as by regulation) [restriction]</p><p><b>ograničen, ograničena, ograničenom, poseban</b></p><p><i>n.</i> public transport consisting of a fast train or bus that makes only a few scheduled stops [express]</p><p><i>adj.</i> small in range or scope</p><p><i>adj.</i> subject to limits or subjected to limits [circumscribed]</p><p><i>adj.</i> including only a part</p><p><i>adj.</i> mediocre [modified]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not excessive</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a specific function or scope [special]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not unlimited</p><p><b>Ako je to potrebno, Komisija može odlučiti o tome. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an audit of limited scope (limited in time span or confined to particular accounts etc.)</p><p><b>društvo s ograničenom odgovornosti, društvo s ograničenom odgovornošću, trgovačko društvo s određenim jamstvom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a company that is organized to give its owners limited liability [Ld., Ltd.]</p><p><b>izdanje ograničeno na određeni broj primjeraka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edition that is restricted to a specific number of copies</p><p><b>ograničena odgovornost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the liability of a firm's owners for no more than the capital they have invested in the firm</p><p><b>(računovodstvo) usluga (manje iscrpna od revizije) koja zainteresiranim stranama pruža određeno jamstvo u pogledu pouzdanosti financijskih podataka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (accounting) a service (less exhaustive than an audit) that provides some assurance to interested parties as to the reliability of financial data [review]</p><p><b>rat čiji je cilj manji od bezuslovnog poraza neprijatelja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a war whose objective is less than the unconditional defeat of the enemy</p><p><b>ograničen, ograničena, ograničenom (od &quot;limited&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a limited manner</p><p><b>granica, limes, limit, ograničanje, ograničavanje, ograničavati, ograničenje, ograničiti, ograničiti se, prepreka (od &quot;limit&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (electronics) a nonlinear electronic circuit whose output is limited in amplitude [clipper]</p><p><b>granični, ograničavanja, ograničavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the grammatical relation that exists when a word qualifies the meaning of the phrase [modification, qualifying]</p><p><i>adj.</i> restricting the scope or freedom of action [confining, constraining, constrictive, restricting]</p><p><i>adj.</i> stri