 jezični mišić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mobile mass of muscular tissue covered with mucous membrane and located in the oral cavity [clapper, glossa, tongue]</p><p><b>zajednički jezik koji govore govornici različitih jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common language used by speakers of different languages [interlanguage, koine]</p><p><b>knjiški, jezičan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a consonant that is produced with the tongue and other speech organs</p><p><i>adj.</i> consisting of or related to language [linguistic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to or resembling or lying near the tongue</p><p><b>arterija koja potječe iz vanjske karotide i opskrbljuje donju stranu jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery originating from the external carotid artery and supplying the under side of the tongue [arteria lingualis]</p><p><b>vena koja prima krv iz jezika i usta i isprazni u unutarnju jugularu ili facu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vein that receives blood from the tongue and the floor of the mouth and empties into the internal jugular or the facial vein [vena lingualis]</p><p><b>knjiški (od &quot;lingual&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to language [linguistically]</p><p><b>umjetni jezik. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial language</p><p><b>vrlo začinjeni portugalski svinjski kobasić ukusan češnjakom i lukom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a highly seasoned Portuguese pork sausage flavored with garlic and onions</p><p><b>pasta u dugim tankim ravnim trakama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pasta in long slender flat strips [linguini]</p><p><b>pasta u dugim tankim ravnim trakama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pasta in long slender flat strips [linguine]</p><p><b>jezikoslovac, lingvist, lingvista, poliglot</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in linguistics [linguistic scientist]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who speaks more than one language [polyglot]</p><p><b>jezični, lingvistički, lingvistika, jezične, jezičnih, jezičnim, jezičnoj, jezičnom, jezičnu, jezičan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> consisting of or related to language [lingual]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the scientific study of language</p><p><b>atlas koji prikazuje raspodjelu karakterističnih jezičkih značajki (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an atlas showing the distribution of distinctive linguistic features [dialect atlas]</p><p><b>jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a systematic means of communicating by the use of sounds or conventional symbols [language]</p><p><b>(lingvistički) govornikovo implicitno, internalizirano poznavanje pravila svog jezika (u suprotnosti s jezičnim performansama) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (linguistics) a speaker's implicit, internalized knowledge of the rules of their language (contrasted with linguistic performance)</p><p><b>kontekst</b></p><p><i>n.</i> discourse that surrounds a language unit and helps to determine its interpretation [context, context of use]</p><p><b>lingvistička geografija, dijalektologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of the geographical distribution of linguistic features [dialect geography]</p><p><b>(lingvistički) govornik je stvarni korištenje jezika u stvarnim situacijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (linguistics) a speaker's actual use of language in real situations</p><p><b>jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a process involved in human language</p><p><i>n.</i> the cognitive processes involved in producing and understanding linguistic communication [language]</p><p><b>korištenje govornih karakteristika ili dijalekta za identifikaciju govornika rase ili religije ili društvene klase (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> using speech characteristics or dialect to identify a speaker's race or religion or social class</p><p><b>jezična relacija, jezični odnos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relation between linguistic forms or constituents</p><p><b>(lingvistički) pravilo koje opisuje (ili propisuje) jezikovnu praksu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (linguistics) a rule describing (or prescribing) a linguistic practice [rule]</p><p><b>lingvist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in linguistics [linguist]</p><p><b>govorni 