><p><b>Francuski pjesnik i pisac (1810-1857) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French poet and writer (1810-1857) [Alfred de Musset, Musset]</p><p><b>Američki umjetnik koji je razvio staklo Tiffany (1848-1933) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States artist who developed Tiffany glass (1848-1933) [Tiffany]</p><p><b>bivši francuski zlatni novčić (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former French gold coin</p><p><b>kralj Francuske (921-954) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France (921-954) [Louis IV]</p><p><b>Francuski fizičar poznat po istraživanju magnetizma (rođen 1904.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French physicist noted for research on magnetism (born in 1904) [Neel]</p><p><b>Engleski radiobiolog u čiju čast je nazvana siva (SI jedinica energije za apsorbiranu dozu zračenja) (1905-1965) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English radiobiologist in whose honor the gray (the SI unit of energy for the absorbed dose of radiation) was named (1905-1965) [Gray]</p><p><b>Američki arhitekt poznat po svojim neboderacima s čeličnim okvirima i zbog izmišljanja fraze "form slijedi funkciju" (1856-1924) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States architect known for his steel framed skyscrapers and for coining the phrase `form follows function' (1856-1924) [Louis Henry Sullivan, Louis Sullivan, Sullivan]</p><p><b>Američki arhitekt poznat po svojim neboderacima s čeličnim okvirima i zbog izmišljanja fraze "form slijedi funkciju" (1856-1924) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States architect known for his steel framed skyscrapers and for coining the phrase `form follows function' (1856-1924) [Louis Henri Sullivan, Louis Sullivan, Sullivan]</p><p><b>Ludovik I.</b></p><p><i>n.</i> third son of Charlemagne and king of France and Germany and Holy Roman Emperor (778-840) [Louis the Pious]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske i Njemačke (846-879) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France and Germany (846-879) [Louis le Begue, Louis the German, Louis the Stammerer]</p><p><b>Ludovik III. Slijepi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> son of Louis II and king of the France and Germany (863-882)</p><p><b>Američki arhitekt (rođen u Estoniji) (1901-1974) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States architect (born in Estonia) (1901-1974) [Kahn]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske (921-954) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France (921-954) [Louis d'Outremer]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske i sin Ludvika VIII. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France and son of Louis VIII [Saint Louis, St. Louis]</p><p><b>Francuski izumitelj prvog praktičnog fotografskih postupaka, dagerotipa (1789-1851) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French inventor of the first practical photographic process, the daguerreotype (1789-1851) [Daguerre]</p><p><b>Francuski istraživač (s Jacquesom Marquetteom) u dolini rijeke Mississippi (1645-1700) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French explorer (with Jacques Marquette) of the upper Mississippi River valley (1645-1700) [Joliet, Jolliet, Louis Jolliet]</p><p><b>Francuski istraživač (s Jacquesom Marquetteom) u dolini rijeke Mississippi (1645-1700) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French explorer (with Jacques Marquette) of the upper Mississippi River valley (1645-1700) [Joliet, Jolliet, Louis Joliet]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske i Njemačke (846-879) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France and Germany (846-879) [Louis II, Louis the German, Louis the Stammerer]</p><p><b>posljednji karolingijski kralj Francuske (967-987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the last Carolingian king of France (967-987) [Louis V]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske (1289-1316) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France (1289-1316) [Louis X, Louis the Quarreller]</p><p><b>Engleski paleontolog čiji je izvještaj o fosilnim otkrićima u Tanzaniji promijenio teorije ljudske evolucije (1903-1972) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English paleontologist whose account of fossil discoveries in Tanzania changed theories of human evolution (1903-1972) [Leakey, Louis Seymour Bazett Leakey]</p><p><b>Francuski kemičar i biolog čije je otkriće da fermentiranje uzrokuju mikroorganizmi rezultiralo procesom pasterizacije (1822-1895) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French chemist and biologist whose discovery that fermentation is caused by microorganisms resulted in the process of pasteurization (1822-1895) [Pasteur]</p><p><b>Engleski paleontolog čiji je izvještaj o fosilnim otkrićima u Tanzaniji promijenio teorije ljudske evolucije (1903-1972) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English paleontologist whose account of fossil discoveries in Tanzania changed theories of human evolution (1903-1972) [Leakey, Louis Leakey]</p><p><b>Američki pisac (rođen 1917.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer (born in 1917) [Auchincloss, Louis Auchincloss]</p><p><b>Američki arhitekt poznat po svojim neboderacima s čeličnim okvirima i zbog izmišljanja fraze "form slijedi funkciju" (1856-1924) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States architect known for his steel framed skyscrapers and for coining the phrase `form follows function' (1856-1924) [Louis Henri Sullivan, Louis Henry Sullivan, Sullivan]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske čije su vojne pobjede učvrstile njegovo vladavino (1081-1137) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France whose military victories consolidated his reign (1081-1137) [Louis VI, Louis the Far, Louis the Wideawake]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske čije su vojne pobjede učvrstile njegovo vladavino (1081-1137) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France whose military victories consolidated his reign (1081-1137) [Louis VI, Louis the Bruiser, Louis the Wideawake]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske i Njemačke (846-879) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France and Germany (846-879) [Louis II, Louis le Begue, Louis the Stammerer]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske od 1643. do 1715. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France from 1643 to 1715 [Louis XIV, Sun King]</p><p><b>Ludovik I.</b></p><p><i>n.</i> third son of Charlemagne and king of France and Germany and Holy Roman Emperor (778-840) [Louis I]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske (1289-1316) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France (1289-1316) [Louis X, Louis le Hutin]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske i Njemačke (846-879) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France and Germany (846-879) [Louis II, Louis le Begue, Louis the German]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske čije su vojne pobjede učvrstile njegovo vladavino (1081-1137) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France whose military victories consolidated his reign (1081-1137) [Louis VI, Louis the Bruiser, Louis the Far]</p><p><b>Američki pisac (1885-1977) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer (1885-1977) [Untermeyer]</p><p><b>posljednji karolingijski kralj Francuske (967-987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the last Carolingian king of France (967-987) [Louis le Faineant]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske čije su vojne pobjede učvrstile njegovo vladavino (1081-1137) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France whose military victories consolidated his reign (1081-1137) [Louis the Bruiser, Louis the Far, Louis the Wideawake]</p><p><b>Francuski nuklearni fizičar koji je generalizirao dualnost val-čestica predloženjem da čestice materije pokazuju valovita svojstva (1892-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French nuclear physicist who generalized the wave-particle duality by proposing that particles of matter exhibit wavelike properties (1892-1987) [Broglie, de Broglie]</p><p><b>kralj Francuske koji je vodio neuspješan Drugi križarski rat i često se borio s Engleskim Henrikom II (1120-1180) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France who led the unsuccessful Second Crusade and fought frequent wars with Henry II of England (1120-1180)</p><p><b>kralj Francuske koji je povećao moć krune nad feudalnim gospodarima (1187-1226) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France who increased the power of the Crown over the feudal lords (1187-1226)</p><p><b>kralj Francuske (1289-1316) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France (1289-1316) [Louis le Hutin, Louis the Quarreller]</p><p><b>Kralj Francuske koji je srušio savez nepovratnih plemića i ujedinio Francusku osim Bretanije (1423-1483) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France who put down an alliance of unruly nobles and unified France except for Brittany (1423-1483)</p><p><b>kralj Francuske koji je bio popularan među svojim podanicima (1462.-1515.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France who was popular with his subjects (1462-1515)</p><p><b>kralj Francuske od 1610. do 1643. koji se u velikoj mjeri oslanjao na savjete kardinala Richelieua (1601-1643) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France from 1610 to 1643 who relied heavily on the advice of Cardinal Richelieu (1601-1643)</p><p><b>kralj Francuske od 1643. do 1715. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France from 1643 to 1715 [Louis the Great, Sun King]</p><p><b>unuk Ludvika XIV i kralj Francuske od 1715. do 1774. koji je vodio Francusku u rat za austrusko nasljeđe i Sedmogodišnji rat (1710-1774) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grandson of Louis XIV and king of France from 1715 to 1774 who led France into the War of the Austrian Succession and the Seven Years' War (1710-1774)</p><p><b>kralj Francuske od 1774. do 1792. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> king of France from 1774 to 1792</p><p><b>Hector Berlioz</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French composer of romantic works (1803-1869) [Berlioz, Hector Berlioz]</p><p><b>Američki romanopisac poznat po dječjim knjigama (1832-1888) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States novelist noted for children's books (1832-1888) [Alcott]</p><p><b>Sculptor iz Sjedinjenih Država (rođen u Rusiji) poznat po masivnim oblicima obojenog drveta (1899-1988) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States sculptor (born in Russia) known for massive shapes of painted wood (1899-1988) [Nevelson]</p><p><b>Luiziana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in southern United States on the Gulf of Mexico [LA, La., Pelican State]</p><p><b>teritorija u zapadnim Sjedinjenim Državama kupljena od Francuske 1803. za 15 milijuna dolara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> territory in the western United States purchased from France in 1803 for $15 million</p><p><b>rodom ili prebivalištem Louisiane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or resident of Louisiana [Louisianian]</p><p><b>rodom ili prebivalištem Louisiane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or resident of Louisiana [Louisianan]</p><p><b>Najveći grad u Kentuckyju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the largest city in Kentucky</p><p><b>ljenčariti, lješkariti, predvorje, salon, soba za odmor, zahod, kauč, ležaj, sofa, čekaonica, bazati, dangubiti, džabalebariti, tumarati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an upholstered seat for more than one person [couch, sofa]</p><p><i>n.</i> a room (as in a hotel or airport) with seating where people can wait [waiting area, waiting room]</p><p><i>v.</i> sit or recline comfortably</p><p><i>v.</i> be about [footle, hang around, lallygag, linger, loaf, loiter, lollygag, lurk, mess about, mill about, mill around, tarry]</p><p><b>zavaliti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be lazy or idle [arse about, arse around, bum, bum about, bum around, frig around, fuck off, loaf, loll, loll around, lounge around, waste one's time]</p><p><b>zavaliti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be lazy or idle [arse about, arse around, bum, bum about, bum around, frig around, fuck off, loaf, loll, loll around, lounge about, waste one's time]</p><p><b>željeznički vagon s barom i stolovima i foteljima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> railroad car having a bar and tables and lounge chairs [club car]</p><p><b>udoban čepirani fotelju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a comfortable upholstered armchair [easy chair, overstuffed chair]</p><p><b>Čovjek koji se šeta po salonu hotela i barova u potrazi za ženama koje će ga podržati. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who idles about in the lounges of hotels and bars in search of women who would support him [lizard]</p><p><b>dvodijelno odijelo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a business suit consisting of a matching jacket and skirt or trousers [two-piece, two-piece suit]</p><p><b>ljenčariti, lješkariti, predvorje, salon, soba za odmor, zahod (od &quot;lounge&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who wastes time [dallier, dilly-dallier, dillydallier, mope]</p><p><i>n.</i> an armchair whose back can be lowered and foot can be raised to allow the sitter to recline in it [recliner, reclining chair]</p><p><i>n.</i> an article of clothing designed for comfort and leisure wear</p><p><b>odjeća pogodna za opuštanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> clothing suitable for relaxation</p><p><b>muški mekani jakna obično sa remen kravata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man's soft jacket usually with a tie belt [smoking jacket]</p><p><b>Pižame koje se nose dok se odmaraju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pajamas worn while lounging [lounging pyjama]</p><p><b>Pižame koje se nose dok se odmaraju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pajamas worn while lounging [lounging pajama]</p><p><b>odjeća koja se nosi prije nošenja ili dok se odmara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a robe worn before dressing or while lounging [dressing gown, robe-de-chambre]</p><p><b>vukodlak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monster able to change appearance from human to wolf and back again [lycanthrope, werewolf, wolfman]</p><p><b>lupa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small magnifying glass (usually set in an eyepiece) used by jewelers and horologists [jeweler's loupe]</p><p><b>mrgođenje, mrštiti se, namrštiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> set lower [lower]</p><p><i>v.</i> make lower or quieter [lower, turn down]</p><p><i>v.</i> look angry or sullen, wrinkle one's forehead, as if to signal disapproval [frown, glower, lower]</p><p><b>uš, vaš, uši</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wingless usually flattened bloodsucking insect parasitic on warm-blooded animals [sucking louse]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who has a nasty or unethical character undeserving of respect [dirt ball, insect, worm]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several small insects especially aphids that feed by sucking the juices from plants [plant louse]</p><p><i>n.</i> wingless insect with mouth parts adapted for biting [bird louse, biting louse]</p><p><b>Krvotopiva dipterozna muha parazitska na ptice i sisare (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bloodsucking dipterous fly parasitic on birds and mammals [hippoboscid]</p><p><b>brljati, buniti se, fušati, griješiti, kiksati, kvariti, packati, petljati, po