uel]</p><p><b>Španjolski pjesnik čije je djelo karakteriziralo elegantno stilo (1561-1627) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Spanish poet whose work was characterized by an affected elegance of style (1561-1627) [Gongora]</p><p><b>označavanje bez zagrada za stvaranje matematičkih izraza u kojima svaki operator prethodi svojim operandima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a parenthesis-free notation for forming mathematical expressions in which each operator precedes its operands [Polish notation, prefix notation]</p><p><b>Luke, Luka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (New Testament) the Apostle closely associated with St. Paul and traditionally assumed to be the author of the third Gospel [Saint Luke, St. Luke]</p><p><i>n.</i> one of the four Gospels in the New Testament [Gospel According to Luke, Gospel of Luke]</p><p><b>mlak, ravnodušan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> moderately warm [tepid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> feeling or showing little interest or enthusiasm [half-hearted, halfhearted, tepid]</p><p><b>mlak, ravnodušan (od &quot;lukewarm&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an unenthusiastically lukewarm manner [tepidly]</p><p><b>mlak, ravnodušan (od &quot;lukewarm&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a warmness resembling the temperature of the skin [tepidity, tepidness]</p><p><i>n.</i> lack of passion, force or animation [tepidness]</p><p><b>Glavna bitka balkanskih ratova (1912) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principal battle of the Balkan Wars (1912) [battle of Lule Burgas]</p><p><b>mir, tišina, uspavati se, utihnuti, smiriti, smirivati, stišati, utišati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pause during which things are calm or activities are diminished [letup]</p><p><i>n.</i> a period of calm weather [quiet]</p><p><i>v.</i> calm by deception</p><p><i>v.</i> become quiet or less intensive [calm down]</p><p><i>v.</i> make calm or still [calm, calm down, quiet, quieten, still, tranquilize, tranquillise, tranquillize]</p><p><b>uspavanka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a quiet song intended to lull a child to sleep [berceuse, cradlesong]</p><p><i>n.</