ustre, lusterless]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking luster or shine [lackluster, lacklustre, lusterless]</p><p><b>svojstvo da ima mali kontrast ili ga nema (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of having little or no contrast [flatness, lusterlessness, mat, matt, matte]</p><p><b>blistav, koji se lašti, sjajan, svjetlucav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made smooth and bright by or as if by rubbing [bright, burnished, shining, shiny]</p><p><i>adj.</i> brilliant</p><p><i>adj.</i> reflecting light [glistening, glossy, sheeny, shining, shiny]</p><p><b>razdoblje od pet godina, ceremonijalno čišćenje rimskog stanovništva svakih pet godina nakon popisa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a period of five years</p><p><i>n.</i> a ceremonial purification of the Roman population every five years following the census</p><p><b>energičan, jedar, krepak, pohotljiv, zdrav, živahan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> vigorously passionate [concupiscent, lustful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> endowed with or exhibiting great bodily or mental health [full-blooded, hearty, red-blooded]</p><p><b>freak, kreatura, monstrum, nakaza, čudovište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person or animal that is markedly unusual or deformed [freak, monster, monstrosity]</p><p><b>Dašt-e Lut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a desert in eastern Iran [Dasht-e-Lut]</p><p><b>industrijska konurbacija na sjeveroistoku Kine na južnom kraju poluotoka Liaodong (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industrial conurbation in northeastern China on the southern end of the Liaodong Peninsula [Luda]</p><p><b>lutnjist, svirač lutnje, svirač na lutnji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musician who plays the lute [lutenist, lutist]</p><p><b>brtvilo, kit, lijepiti, lutnja, leut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance for packing a joint or coating a porous surface to make it impervious to gas or liquid [luting]</p><p><i>n.</i> chordophone consisting of a plucked instrument having a pear-shaped body, a usually bent neck, and a fretted fingerboard</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s corpus luteumom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating t