aordinary ability to attract [charismatic]</p><p><b>privlačnost željeza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> attraction for iron [magnetic force, magnetism]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom materijala od 0,25% ili više, ali ne više od 0,25%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> container consisting of any configuration of magnetic fields used to contain a plasma during controlled thermonuclear reactions</p><p><b>memorija s magnetnim mjehurićima</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nonvolatile storage device that holds information in the form of bubbles on a thin film of magnetic silicate</p><p><b>Kompas zasnovan na pokazatelju (kao magnetnoj igli) koji ukazuje na magnetni sjever (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> compass based on an indicator (as a magnetic needle) that points to the magnetic north</p><p><b>(računovodstvo) mali ferit toroid ranije korišten u slučajnom pristupu memorije za pohranu jedan bit podataka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a tiny ferrite toroid formerly used in a random access memory to store one bit of data [core]</p><p><b>(računovodstvo) računalna memorija koja se sastoji od niza magnetnih jezgara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a computer memory consisting of an array of magnetic cores [core memory]</p><p><b>magnetna deklinacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the angle (at a particular location) between magnetic north and true north [magnetic variation, variation]</p><p><b>(fizički) kut koji magnetna igla čini s ravninom horizonta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the angle that a magnetic needle makes with the plane of the horizon [angle of dip, dip, inclination, magnetic inclination]</p><p><b>Dipol s suprotnim magnetnim polovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dipole with opposing magnetic poles</p><p><b>(fizički) struja u petlji stvara magnetno polje karakteristično za magnetni dipol (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a current loop gives rise to a magnetic field characteristic of a magnetic dipole</p><p><b>disk, disketa, magnetski disk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a memory device consisting of a flat disk covered with a magnetic coating on which information is stored [disc, disk, magnetic disk]</p><p><b>disk, disketa, magnetski disk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a memory device consisting of a flat disk covered with a magnetic coating on which information is stored [disc, disk, magnetic disc]</p><p><b>imaginarna crta paralelna ekvatoru gdje magnetna igla nema dubinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary line paralleling the equator where a magnetic needle has no dip [aclinic line]</p><p><b>magnetsko polje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lines of force surrounding a permanent magnet or a moving charged particle [flux, magnetic flux]</p><p><b>količina magnetnog toka u jedinici površine pravougaono na smjer magnetnog toka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of magnetic flux in a unit area perpendicular to the direction of magnetic flow [magnetic flux density, magnetic induction, magnetic intensity]</p><p><b>magnetski tok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measure of the strength of a magnetic field over a given area</p><p><i>n.</i> the lines of force surrounding a permanent magnet or a moving charged particle [flux, magnetic field]</p><p><b>količina magnetnog toka u jedinici površine pravougaono na smjer magnetnog toka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of magnetic flux in a unit area perpendicular to the direction of magnetic flow [magnetic field strength, magnetic induction, magnetic intensity]</p><p><b>mjerenje jačine magnetnog polja po jedinici površine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measure of the strength of a magnetic field per unit area [flux unit]</p><p><b>magnetska sila</b></p><p><i>n.</i> attraction for iron [magnetic attraction, magnetism]</p><p><b>Elektromagnet (kao na magnetofonu) koji pretvara električne varijacije u magnetne varijacije koje se mogu pohraniti na površini i kasnije preuzeti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electromagnet (as on a tape recorder) that converts electrical variations into magnetic variations that can be stored on a surface and later retrieved</p><p><b>(fizički) kut koji magnetna igla čini s ravninom horizonta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the angle that a magnetic needle makes with the plane of the horizon [angle of dip, dip, inclination, magnetic dip]</p><p><b>magnetska indukcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process that makes a substance magnetic (temporarily or permanently) [magnetisation, magnetization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of magnetic flux in a unit area perpendicular to the direction of magnetic flow [magnetic field strength, magnetic flux density, magnetic intensity]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom masne mase ne većim od 10 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ink that contains particles of a magnetic substance whose presence can be detected by magnetic sensors</p><p><b>količina magnetnog toka u jedinici površine pravougaono na smjer magnetnog toka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of magnetic flux in a unit area perpendicular to the direction of magnetic flow [magnetic field strength, magnetic flux density, magnetic induction]</p><p><b>magnetit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oxide of iron that is strongly attracted by magnets [magnetite]</p><p><b>tehnologija brze željeznice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> high-speed rail technology [maglev]</p><p><b>linija sile u magnetnom polju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a line of force in a magnetic field</p><p><b>magnetni medij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any storage medium in which different patterns of magnetization are used to represent stored bits or bytes of information [magnetic storage, magnetic storage medium]</p><p><b>zamišljena linija koja prolazi kroz oba magnetna pola Zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary line passing through both magnetic poles of the Earth</p><p><b>(nautički) morski rudnik koji se detonira mehanizmom koji reagira na magnetni materijal (kao što je čelični trup broda) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (nautical) a marine mine that is detonated by a mechanism that responds to magnetic material (as the steel hull of a ship)</p><p><b>obrtni moment koji se vrši na magnet ili dipol kada se nalazi u magnetnom polju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the torque exerted on a magnet or dipole when it is placed in a magnetic field [moment of a magnet]</p><p><b>hipotetički čestica s jednim magnetnim polom umjesto uobičajenih dva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hypothetical particle with a single magnetic pole instead of the usual two</p><p><b>tanak magnet obješen u magnetnom kompasu na montiranju s malo trenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slender magnet suspended in a magnetic compass on a mounting with little friction</p><p><b>magnetski sjever, sjever</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the direction in which a compass needle points [compass north, north]</p><p><b>magnetski pol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two points where the lines of force of the Earth's magnetic field are vertical</p><p><i>n.</i> one of the two ends of a magnet where the magnetism seems to be concentrated [pole]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% masenog udjela, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brownish iron sulfide mineral (FeS) having weak magnetic properties [pyrrhotine, pyrrhotite]</p><p><b>magnetofon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> recorder consisting of equipment for making records on magnetic media</p><p><b>magnetska rezonanca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> resonance of electrons or atoms or molecules or nuclei to radiation frequencies as a result of space quantization in a magnetic field</p><p><b>magnetna rezonancija, Magnetska rezonancija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of nuclear magnetic resonance of protons to produce proton density images [MRI]</p><p><b>magnetna memorija, magnetno pohranjivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any storage medium in which different patterns of magnetization are used to represent stored bits or bytes of information [magnetic medium, magnetic storage medium]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta uređaja za uređivanje podataka ili uređaja za uređivanje podataka ili uređaja za uređivanje podataka ili uređaja za uređivanje podataka ili uređaja za uređi