that registers magnetic variations (especially variations of the earth's magnetic field)</p><p><b>magnetohidrodinamika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of the interaction of magnetic fields and electrically conducting fluids (as plasma or molten metal)</p><p><b>magnetometar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a meter to compare strengths of magnetic fields [gaussmeter]</p><p><b>sila koja stvara magnetni tok (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the force that produces magnetic flux</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of measurement of magnetomotive force</p><p><b>jedinica magnetnog momenta molekularnog ili atomskog ili subatomskog čestica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of magnetic moment of a molecular or atomic or subatomic particle</p><p><b>magnetno polje planete (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the magnetic field of a planet</p><p><b>magnetnim (mikrovalna cijev)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a diode vacuum tube in which the flow of electrons from a central cathode to a cylindrical anode is controlled by crossed magnetic and electric fields</p><p><b>Magnificat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Luke) the canticle of the Virgin Mary (from Luke 1:46 beginning `Magnificat anima mea Dominum')</p><p><b>povećanja, povećanje, uvećanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of expanding something in apparent size</p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio of the size of an image to the size of the object</p><p><i>n.</i> making to seem more important than it really is [exaggeration, overstatement]</p><p><i>n.</i> a photographic print that has been enlarged [blowup, enlargement]</p><p><b>veličanstvenost, impresivnost, blistavost, briljantnost, grandioznost, izuzetnost, izvanrednost, izvrsnost, raskošnost, uzvišenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> splendid or imposing in size or appearance [grandness, impressiveness, richness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being magnificent or splendid or grand [brilliance, grandeur, grandness, splendor, splendour]</p><p><b>čarobno, divan, izvanredan, krasan, monumentalnim, prekrasan, sjajan, veličanstven</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by grandeur [brilliant, glorious, splendid]</p><p><b>divno, krasno, veličanstveno, izvrstan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> extremely well [excellently, famously, splendidly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in an impressively beautiful manner [gorgeously, resplendently, splendidly]</p><p><b>osoba odlikovanog ranga ili izgleda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person of distinguished rank or appearance</p><p><b>povećan, uvećan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> enlarged to an abnormal degree [enlarged, exaggerated]</p><p><b>lupa, povećalo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scientific instrument that magnifies an image</p><p><b>povećati, povećati se, pretjerivati, preuveličavati, uvećati, uvećavati, uveličati, hiperbolizirati, napuhati, napuhavati, napuhivati, napuhnuti, pretjerati, pretjeravati, preuveličati, uveličavati, povećavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> increase in size, volume or significance [amplify]</p><p><i>v.</i> to enlarge beyond bounds or the truth [amplify, exaggerate, hyperbolise, hyperbolize, overdraw, overstate]</p><p><i>v.</i> make large [blow up, enlarge]</p><p><b>lupa, povećalo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> light microscope consisting of a single convex lens that is used to produce an enlarged image [hand glass, simple microscope]</p><p><b>Vrlo uzbuđen stil. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> high-flown style [grandiloquence, grandiosity, ornateness, rhetoric]</p><p><b>hvalisav, visokoparan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lofty in style [grandiloquent, tall]</p><p><b>hvalisav, visokoparan (od &quot;magniloquent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a rhetorically grandiloquent manner [grandiloquently]</p><p><b>magnituda, veličina, značaj, jakost, jačina, snaga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of relative size or extent (whether large or small)</p><p><i>n.</i> a number assigned to the ratio of two quantities [order of magnitude]</p><p><i>n.</i> relative importance</p><p><b>kvantitavna relacija, odnos magnituda, odnos veličina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relation between magnitudes [quantitative relation]</p><p><b>magnolija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dried bark of various magnolias</p><p><i>n.</i> any shrub or tree of the genus Magnolia</p><p><b>Američka listnatog lišća magnolija s velikim lišćama i plodovima poput malog krastavca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American deciduous magnolia having large leaves and fruit like a small cucumber [cucumber tree]</p><p><b>podklasa Magnoliidae: rodovi Liriodendron, Magnolia i Manglietia (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> subclass Magnoliidae: genera Liriodendron, Magnolia, and Manglietia [Magnoliaceae, family Magnoliaceae]</p><p><b>malo uspravno listno stablo s velikim lištima u višenim formacijama na vrhovima grana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small erect deciduous tree with large leaves in coiled formations at branch tips [earleaved umbrella tree]</p><p><b>uvijekzeleno stablo iz južnih Sjedinjenih Država s velikim čvrstim blistavim lišćama i velikim bijelim slatko mirisnim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen tree of southern United States having large stiff glossy leaves and huge white sweet-smelling flowers [bull bay, evergreen magnolia, large-flowering magnolia, southern magnolia]</p><p><b>veliki listovit grm ili drvo iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s ogromnim lišćama u gustim lažnim vrtljama i velikim kremastim cvijećima obojenim u ljubičast prema dnu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large deciduous shrub or tree of southeastern United States having huge leaves in dense false whorls and large creamy flowers tinged purple toward the base [great-leaved macrophylla, large-leaved cucumber tree, large-leaved magnolia]</p><p><b>Veliki listovit grm ili malo stablo s velikim otvorenim ružičastim do ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large deciduous shrub or small tree having large open rosy to purplish flowers [Chinese magnolia, saucer magnolia]</p><p><b>država na dubokom jugu na Meksičkom zaljevu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in the Deep South on the gulf of Mexico [MS, Miss., Mississippi]</p><p><b>ljeplovita magnolija iz Japana koja ima mirisne bijele zvijezdane cvijeće koje cvjetaju prije nego se listovi razotknu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrubby magnolia from Japan having fragrant white starlike flowers blooming before leaves unfold [star magnolia]</p><p><b>malo listno stablo iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s kremastima bijelim cvijećima i velikim lištima u formacijama poput kišobrana na krajevima grana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small deciduous tree of eastern North America having creamy white flowers and large leaves in formations like umbrellas at the ends of branches [elk-wood, elkwood, umbrella magnolia, umbrella tree]</p><p><b>grm ili drvo s prilično malim mirisnim bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub or small tree having rather small fragrant white flowers [swamp bay, swamp laurel, sweet bay]</p><p><b>podklasa Magnoliidae: rodovi Liriodendron, Magnolia i Manglietia (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> subclass Magnoliidae: genera Liriodendron, Magnolia, and Manglietia [family Magnoliaceae, magnolia family]</p><p><b>obitelj cvjetnica s dva koštana, koja se smatra najprimitivnijom od postojećih angiospermi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of dicotyledonous flowering plants regarded as among the most primitive of extant angiosperms</p><p><b>rod dvostrukocnih cvjetnica koji se smatraju najprimitivnijim od postojećih angiosperma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of dicotyledonous flowering plants regarded as among the most primitive of extant angiosperms</p><p><b>skupina obitelji stabala i grmova i biljaka s dobro razvijenim periantama i apokarpnim jajnika i općenito se smatraju najprimitivnijim postojećim cvjetnim biljkama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of families of trees and shrubs and herbs having well-developed perianths and apocarpous ovaries and generally regarded as the most primitive extant flowering plants [ranalian complex, subclass Magnoliidae]</p><p><b>od biljaka s cvjetnim stablama koja proizvode sjemena zatvorena u jajniku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comprising flowering plants that produce seeds enclosed in an ovary [Angiospermae, Anthophyta, class Angiospermae, division Anthophyta, division Magnoliophyta]</p><p><b>cvjetnica s dva kotilena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flowering plant with two cotyledons [dicot, dicotyledon, exogen]</p><p><b>porodice dikotiledona, porodice dvosupnica, porodice magnoliopsida</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of flowering plants having two cotyledons (embryonic leaves) in the seed which usually appear at germination [dicot family]</p><p><b>rod dikotiledona, rod dvosupnica, rod magnoliopsida</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of flowering plants having two cotyledons (embryonic leaves) in the seed which usually appear at germination [dicot genus]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% do 85%, ali ne više od 85% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comprising seed plants that produce an embryo with paired cotyledons and net-veined leaves [Dicotyledonae, Dicotyledones, class Dicotyledonae, class Dicotyledones, class Magnoliopsida]</p><p><b>velika bočica vina za piće ili vino (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large wine bottle for liquor or wine</p><p><b>veliko umjetničko ili književno djelo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a great work of art or literature</p><p><b>s masenim udubljenjem od oko 10 mm ili više, ali ne više od 10 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rolling hitch similar to a clove hitch</p><p><b>brbljavica, svraka, svrha</b></p><p><i>n.</i> long-tailed black-and-white crow that utters a raucous chattering call</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who collects things that have been discarded by others [pack rat, scavenger]</p><p><i>n.</i> an obnoxious and foolish and loquacious talker [babbler, chatterbox, chatterer, prater, spouter]</p><p><b>Belgijski slikar (1898-1967) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Belgian surrealist painter (1898-1967) [Rene Magritte]</p><p><b>Meksikanska biljka koja se koristi za proizvodnju pulquea, izvor bezbojnog meksičkog pića, mescala., Filipinska biljka koja proizvodi tvrdo vlakno za proizvodnju grube niti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mexic