ated the forces of Antony and Cleopatra at Actium (63-12 BC) [Agrippa]</p><p><b>Američki misionar koji je osnovao postaju u Oregonu gdje su kršćanstvo, obrazovanje i medicina bili dostupni domorocima (1802-1847) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States frontier missionary who established a post in Oregon where Christianity and schooling and medicine were available to Native Americans (1802-1847) [Whitman]</p><p><b>Herbert Marcuse</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States political philosopher (born in Germany) concerned about the dehumanizing effects of capitalism and modern technology (1898-1979) [Herbert Marcuse]</p><p><b>pokladni utorak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the last day before Lent [Fat Tuesday, Shrove Tuesday, pancake day]</p><p><i>n.</i> a carnival held in some countries on Shrove Tuesday (the last day before Lent) but especially in New Orleans [Fat Tuesday]</p><p><b>glavni babilonski bog. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the chief Babylonian god [Baal Merodach, Bel-Merodach, Merodach]</p><p><b>bedevija, kobila</b></p><p><i>n.</i> female equine animal [female horse]</p><p><i>n.</i> a dark region of considerable extent on the surface of the moon [maria]</p><p><b>(zatvoreno more) plovno vodeno tijelo pod jurisdikcijom jedne države (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (closed sea) a navigable body of water under the jurisdiction of a single nation</p><p><b>(slobodno more) plovno vodeno tijelo na koje sve nacije imaju jednak pristup (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (free sea) a navigable body of water to which all nations have equal access</p><p><b>(naše more) Mediteran do drevnih Rimljana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (our sea) the Mediterranean to the ancient Romans</p><p><b>zbunjeno mnoštvo stvari. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a confused multitude of things [clutter, fuddle, jumble, muddle, smother, welter]</p><p><b>dug i uski cirruski oblak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long narrow flowing cirrus cloud</p><p><b>Bitka 1800. godine u kojoj su Francuzi pod Napoleonom Bonaparteom dobili veliku pobjedu nad Austrija