he area immediately inside the boundary [border, perimeter]</p><p><i>n.</i> an amount beyond the minimum necessary</p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of collateral a customer deposits with a broker when borrowing from the broker to buy securities [security deposit]</p><p><i>n.</i> (finance) the net sales minus the cost of goods and services sold [gross profit, gross profit margin]</p><p><i>n.</i> the blank space that surrounds the text on a page</p><p><i>n.</i> a permissible difference [allowance, leeway, tolerance]</p><p><b>depozitni račun kod trgovanja futuresima</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an account with a securities brokerage in which the broker extends credit</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, u slučaju kada je u pitanju trgovački ugovor, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ovog Pravilnika, trgovački ugovor se može smatrati ugovorom koji se ne odnosi na trgovački ugovor. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a demand by a broker that a customer deposit enough to bring his margin up to the minimum requirement [call]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je to potrebno za osiguranje sigurnosti, u slučaju da je to potrebno za osiguranje sigurnosti, u slučaju da je to potrebno za osiguranje sigurnosti, u slučaju da je to potrebno za osiguranje sigurnosti, u slučaju da je to potrebno za osiguranje sigurnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the margin required in order to insure safety [margin of safety, safety margin]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) Uredbe (EU) br. 1303/2013 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio gross profits divided by net sales [gross margin, profit margin]</p><p><b>granica sigurnosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the margin required in order to insure safety [margin of error, safety margin]</p><p><b>rubni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> at or constituting a border or edge [fringy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of questionable or minimal quality [borderline]</p><p><i>adj.</i> just barely adequate or within a lower limit [bare]</p><p><i>adj.</i> producing at a rate that barely covers production costs</p><p><b>granični trošak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the increase or decrease in costs as a result of one more or one less unit of output [differential cost, incremental cost]</p><p><b>s jajnikom na zidu duž ventralne šavure jednostavnog jajnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> with ovules borne on the wall along the ventral suture of a simple ovary [ventral placentation]</p><p><b>(ekonomika) iznos koji se povećava s povećanjem jedne jedinice ekonomske robe ili usluge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (economics) the amount that utility increases with an increase of one unit of an economic good or service</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički paprika sa večnozelenim lišćama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American fern with evergreen fronds [Dryopteris marginalis, evergreen wood fern, leatherleaf wood fern]</p><p><b>napisane napomene u rubnici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> notes written in the margin</p><p><b>marginalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the social process of becoming or being made marginal (especially as a group within the larger society) [marginalization]</p><p><b>U nekim slučajevima, to znači da se određeni ljudi mogu smatrati "nižim ili vanjskim rubom" u odnosu na određene skupine ljudi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> relegate to a lower or outer edge, as of specific groups of people [marginalize]</p><p><b>svojstvo da je marginalan ili na rubovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being marginal or on the fringes</p><p><b>marginalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the social process of becoming or being made marginal (especially as a group within the larger society) [marginalisation]</p><p><b>U nekim slučajevima, to znači da se određeni ljudi mogu smatrati "nižim ili vanjskim rubom" u odnosu na određene skupine ljudi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> relegate to a lower or outer edge, as of specific groups of people [marginalise]</p><p><b>rubni (od &quot;marginal&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a marginal manner</p><p><b>uključuje dinosaure s kostim glavama (pachycephalosaurs) i rogovima (ceratopsian) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> includes boneheaded (pachycephalosaurs) and horned (ceratopsian) dinosaurs [marginocephalian, suborder Marginocephalia]</p><p><b>uključuje dinosaure s kostim glavama (pachycephalosaurs) i rogovima (ceratopsian) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> includes boneheaded (pachycephalosaurs) and horned (ceratopsian) dinosaurs [Marginocephalia, suborder Marginocephalia]</p><p><b>veliko poluvjeklo zeleno stablo iz Istočne Indije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large semi-evergreen tree of the East Indies [Azadirachta indica, Melia Azadirachta, arishth, neem, neem tree, nim tree]</p><p><b>markgrof</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the military governor of a frontier province in medieval Germany</p><p><i>n.</i> a German nobleman ranking above a count (corresponding in rank to a British marquess)</p><p><b>Visoka ljeplovita višegodišnja biljka s bijelim cvjetovima, višegodišnji potgrm na Kanarskim otocima s obično blijedožutim cvjetovima nalik margariti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall leafy-stemmed Eurasian perennial with white flowers [Chrysanthemum leucanthemum, Leucanthemum vulgare, moon daisy, ox-eyed daisy, oxeye daisy, white daisy]</p><p><i>n.</i> perennial subshrub of the Canary Islands having usually pale yellow daisylike flowers [Argyranthemum frutescens, Chrysanthemum frutescens, Paris daisy, marguerite daisy]</p><p><b>višegodišnji potgrm na Kanarskim otocima s obično blijedožutim cvjetovima nalik margariti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial subshrub of the Canary Islands having usually pale yellow daisylike flowers [Argyranthemum frutescens, Chrysanthemum frutescens, Paris daisy, marguerite]</p><p><b>Engleska spisateljica čiji je roman o lezbijskom odnosu bio zabranjen u Britaniji dugi niz godina (1883-1943) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English writer whose novel about a lesbian relationship was banned in Britain for many years (1883-1943) [Hall, Radclyffe Hall]</p><p><b>Lapor, marijski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a rural Finnish people living in eastern Russia [