uciji (1757-1834) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French soldier who served under George Washington in the American Revolution (1757-1834) [La Fayette, Lafayette, Marquis de Lafayette]</p><p><b>Francuska slikarka poznata po svojim portretima (1755-1842) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French painter noted for her portraits (1755-1842) [Elisabeth Vigee-Lebrun, Vigee-Lebrun]</p><p><b>aktivist za kontrolu rađanja koji je 1921. godine otvorio prvu kontrolu rađanja kliniku u Londonu (1880-1958) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> birth-control campaigner who in 1921 opened the first birth control clinic in London (1880-1958) [Marie Charlotte Carmichael Stopes, Stopes]</p><p><b>Francuska modelkinja (sjedi u Engleskoj nakon 1802.) koja je napravila vosakove smrtne maske istaknutih žrtava Francuske revolucije i obišla Britaniju sa svojim vosakovim modelima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French modeler (resident in England after 1802) who made wax death masks of prominent victims of the French Revolution and toured Britain with her wax models [Madame Tussaud, Marie Grosholtz, Tussaud]</p><p><b>hronični oblik spondilitisa uglavnom kod muškaraca i obilježen poremećenom pokretljivošću kralježnice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chronic form of spondylitis primarily in males and marked by impaired mobility of the spine [ankylosing spondylitis, rheumatoid spondylitis]</p><p><b>Grad koji je glavna luka Alandskog otoka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town that is the chief port of the Aland islands [Maarianhamina]</p><p><b>bileć, kaljužnica, kadifica, neven</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various tropical American plants of the genus Tagetes widely cultivated for their showy yellow or orange flowers</p><p><b>hašiš, marihuana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strong-smelling plant whose dried leaves can be smoked for a pleasant effect or pain reduction [Cannabis sativa, ganja, marijuana]</p><p><i>n.</i> the most commonly used illicit drug [cannabis, ganja, marijuana]</p><p><b>hašiš, marihuana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strong-smelling plant wh