<i>adj.</i> (of a manuscript) defaced with changes [dirty, foul]</p><p><b>izrazito</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a clearly noticeable manner</p><p><b>biljeg, marker, označitelj, oznaka, obilježje, simbol, znak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> some conspicuous object used to distinguish or mark something</p><p><i>n.</i> a distinguishing symbol [mark, marking]</p><p><i>n.</i> a writing implement for making a mark</p><p><b>cijena, kupovati, kurs, market, plasirati, prodavati, promet, sajam, tražnja, trg, trgovati, trgovina, trgovište, tržišni, tržište, tržiti, tržni, tržnica, pijaca, tržišne, tržišno, tržišnu, tržišta, tržištu, dućan, prehrambena trgovina, supermarket, trgovina živežnim namirnicama, tržište vrijednosnica, tržište vrijednosnih papira, bazar, buvljak, komercijalizirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the world of commercial activity where goods and services are bought and sold [market place, marketplace]</p><p><i>n.</i> the customers for a particular product or service</p><p><i>n.</i> a marketplace where groceries are sold [food market, grocery, grocery store]</p><p><i>n.</i> the securities markets in the aggregate [securities industry]</p><p><i>n.</i> an area in a town where a public mercantile establishment is set up [market place, marketplace, mart]</p><p><i>v.</i> engage in the commercial promotion, sale, or distribution of</p><p><i>v.</i> buy household supplies</p><p><i>v.</i> deal in a market</p><p><i>v.</i> make commercial [commercialise, commercialize]</p><p><b>analiza tržišta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marketing research that yields information about the marketplace</p><p><b>analitičar uvjeta koji utječu na tržište (posebno na berzu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an analyst of conditions affecting a market (especially the stock market)</p><p><b>stopa povrata od ulaganja, tržišna kapitalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an estimation of the value of a business that is obtained by multiplying the number of shares outstanding by the current price of a share [market capitalization]</p><p><b>stopa povrata od ulaganja, tržišna kapitalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an estimation of the value of a business that is obtained by multiplying the number of shares outstanding by the current price of a share [market capitalisation]</p><p><b>spomenik u obliku križa postavljen na tržnici grada gdje se često vrši javni posao (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cross-shaped monument set up in the marketplace of a town where public business is often conducted</p><p><b>određeni dan za održavanje javnog tržišta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fixed day for holding a public market</p><p><b>tržišna ekonomija, tržišno gospodarstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economy that relies chiefly on market forces to allocate goods and resources and to determine prices [free enterprise, laissez-faire economy, private enterprise]</p><p><b>Interakcija ponude i potražnje koja oblikuje tržišnu ekonomiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the interaction of supply and demand that shapes a market economy</p><p><b>vrt u kojem se uzgajaju voće i povrće za prodaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a garden where fruit and vegetables are grown for marketing</p><p><b>tržno povrćarstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the growing of vegetables or flowers for market</p><p><b>trgovac koji posjeduje ili upravlja trgovinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a merchant who owns or manages a shop [shopkeeper, storekeeper, tradesman]</p><p><b>newsletter koji je napisao analitičar dioničara i prodao pretplatnicima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a newsletter written by an analyst of the stock market and sold to subscribers</p><p><b>U slučaju da je trgovački subjekt u stanju da izvrši određenu transakciju, trgovački subjekt može da izvrši određenu transakciju na temelju članka 4. stavka 2. točke (a) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (b) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (c) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (d) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (e) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (c) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (e) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (c) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (e) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (e) ili članka 4. stavka 2. točke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an order to a broker to sell or buy stocks or commodities at the prevailing market price</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) Uredbe (EU) br. 952/2013 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the extent to which a product is recognized and bought by customers in a particular market</p><p><b>tržnica, bazar, buvljak, tržište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an area in a town where a public mercantile establishment is set up [market, marketplace, mart]</p><p><i>n.</i> the world of commercial activity where goods and services are bought and sold [market, marketplace]</p><p><b>tržišna cijena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the price at which buyers and sellers trade the item in an open marketplace [market value]</p><p><b>istraživanje tržišta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> research that gathers and analyzes information about the moving of good or services from producer to consumer [marketing research]</p><p><b>javni trg gdje se prodaju hrana i robna roba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a public marketplace where food and merchandise is sold [open-air market, open-air marketplace]</p><p><b>osoba vješt u planiranju marketinških kampanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone skilled in planning marketing campaigns</p><p><b>trgovište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a (usually small) town where a public market is held at stated times</p><p><b>tržišna vrijednost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the price at which buyers and sellers trade the item in an open marketplace [market price]</p><p><b>dobra prođa, utrživ</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being in demand by especially employers</p><p><i>adj.</i> fit to be offered for sale [merchantable, sellable, vendable, vendible]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being marketed</p><p><b>trgovac, trgovački djelatnik, prodavač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who promotes or exchanges goods or services for money [seller, trafficker, vender, vendor]</p><p><b>istraživanje tržišta, marketing, marketinška, marketnig, prodavanje, tržništvo, kupoprodaja, trgova