a pointed iron hand tool that is used to separate strands of a rope or cable (as in splicing) [marlingspike, marlinspike]</p><p><b>ručni alat od šiljatog željeza koji se koristi za odvajanje lanca ili kabla (kao u splicingu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pointed iron hand tool that is used to separate strands of a rope or cable (as in splicing) [marlinespike, marlinspike]</p><p><b>ručni alat od šiljatog željeza koji se koristi za odvajanje lanca ili kabla (kao u splicingu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pointed iron hand tool that is used to separate strands of a rope or cable (as in splicing) [marlinespike, marlingspike]</p><p><b>Metamorfna stijena s približno istim sastavom kao i merulja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> metamorphic rock with approximately the same composition as marl [marlstone]</p><p><b>Engleski pjesnik i dramaturg koji je uveo prazan stih kao oblik dramatičnog izražavanja, tvrdog ciničnog detektiva (jednog od ranih detektivskih heroja u američkoj fikciji) kojeg je stvorio Raymond Chandler (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English poet and playwright who introduced blank verse as a form of dramatic expression [Christopher Marlowe]</p><p><i>n.</i> tough cynical detective (one of the early detective heroes in American fiction) created by Raymond Chandler [Philip Marlowe]</p><p><b>Metamorfna stijena s približno istim sastavom kao i merulja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> metamorphic rock with approximately the same composition as marl [marlite]</p><p><b>kvariti, nagrditi, pokvariti, uprljati, upropastiti (od &quot;mar&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or resembling or abounding in marl</p><p><b>marmelada, pekmez</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a preserve made of the pulp and rind of citrus fruits</p><p><b>drvo iz Zapadne Indije i sjeverne Južne Amerike koje daje sočno jestivo voće veličine naranče (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree of the West Indies and northern South America bearing succulent edible orange-sized fruit [Genipa Americana, genipap fruit, jagua]</p><p><b>zelena južnoamerička grmlja koja ima sjajne trubljevito narandžaste cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen South American shrub having showy trumpet-shaped orange flowers [Streptosolen jamesonii, fire-bush, fire bush]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta običnih narančastih stabala koja daju kiselo ili gorko voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various common orange trees yielding sour or bitter fruit [Citrus aurantium, Seville orange, bigarade, bitter orange, bitter orange tree, sour orange]</p><p><b>smeđe, ovalno meso voća čini odličan sirup. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brown oval fruit flesh makes excellent sherbet [mammee, sapote]</p><p><b>tropsko američko stablo koje ima drvo poput mahagonija i slatko jestivo voće u obliku jaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American tree having wood like mahogany and sweet edible egg-shaped fruit [Calocarpum zapota, Pouteria zapota, mammee, sapote]</p><p><b>unutrašnje more u sjeverozapadnoj Turskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inland sea in northwestern Turkey [Marmara Denizi, Marmora, Sea of Marmara, Sea of Marmora]</p><p><b>unutrašnje more u sjeverozapadnoj Turskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inland sea in northwestern Turkey [Marmara, Marmora, Sea of Marmara, Sea of Marmora]</p><p><b>juha skuhana u velikom loncu, veliki lonac, posebno onaj s nogama koji se koristi npr. za kuhanje juhe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soup cooked in a large pot</p><p><i>n.</i> a large pot especially one with legs used e.g. for cooking soup</p><p><b>unutrašnje more u sjeverozapadnoj Turskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inland sea in northwestern Turkey [Marmara, Marmara Denizi, Sea of Marmara, Sea of Marmora]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili karakteristične za mermer (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of marble [marmorean]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili karakteristične za mermer (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of marble [marmoreal]</p><p><b>mali južnoamerički i srednjoamerički majmun s mekanim krznom s kandžama umjesto no