quipped faction active in the West Bank [Aksa Martyrs Brigades, al-Aksa Martyrs Brigades]</p><p><b>Sredozemski germander s malim dlakavim listovima i crvenkasto ljubičastim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mediterranean germander having small hairy leaves and reddish purple flowers [Teucrium marum, cat thyme]</p><p><b>Krsta s okruglim plodovima kumquata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub bearing round-fruited kumquats [Fortunella japonica, marumi kumquat, round kumquat]</p><p><b>Krsta s okruglim plodovima kumquata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub bearing round-fruited kumquats [Fortunella japonica, marumi, round kumquat]</p><p><b>stablo iz doline Amazona koje daje lagano krhko drvo koje se na lokalnom nivou smatra otpornim na napad insekata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree of the Amazon valley yielding a light brittle timber locally regarded as resistant to insect attack [Simarouba amara]</p><p><b>bilo koji od grupe hinduističkih bogova oluje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a group of Hindu storm gods</p><p><b>čaroban, čudesan, čuditi se, čudo, divan, diviti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that causes feelings of wonder [wonder]</p><p><i>v.</i> be amazed at [wonder]</p><p><i>v.</i> express astonishment or surprise about something</p><p><b>obična vrtna biljka Sjeverne Amerike koja ima mirisne crvene ili ljubičaste ili žute ili bijele cvijeće koje se otvaraju kasno popodne (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common garden plant of North America having fragrant red or purple or yellow or white flowers that open in late afternoon [Mirabilis jalapa, Mirabilis uniflora, common four-o'clock]</p><p><b>Engleski pjesnik (1621-1678) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English poet (1621-1678) [Andrew Marvell]</p><p><b>Neko ispunjen divljenjem i strahom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone filled with admiration and awe [wonderer]</p><p><b>čudan, čudesan, divan, izvanredan, predivnog, prekrasan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> extraordinarily good or great [fantastic, grand, howling, marvelous, rattling, terrific, tremendous, wonderful, wondrous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being or having the character of a miracle [marvelous, miraculous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> too improbable to admit of belief [improbable, marvelous, tall]</p><p><b>čudan, čudesan, divan, izvanredan, predivnog, prekrasan (od &quot;marvellous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (used as an intensifier) extremely well [marvelously, superbly, terrifically, toppingly, wonderfully, wondrous, wondrously]</p><p><b>čaroban, čarobni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> extraordinarily good or great [fantastic, grand, howling, marvellous, rattling, terrific, tremendous, wonderful, wondrous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> too improbable to admit of belief [improbable, marvellous, tall]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being or having the character of a miracle [marvellous, miraculous]</p><p><b>čaroban, čarobni (od &quot;marvelous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (used as an intensifier) extremely well [marvellously, superbly, terrifically, toppingly, wonderfully, wondrous, wondrously]</p><p><b>Američki dramaturg poznat po lagi komediji (rođen 1927) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States playwright noted for light comedies (born in 1927) [Neil Simon, Simon]</p><p><b>Marx</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States comedian [Herbert Marx, Zeppo]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States comedian [Arthur Marx, Harpo]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States comedian [Chico, Leonard Marx]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States comedian [Groucho, Julius Marx]</p><p><i>n.</i> founder of modern communism [Karl Marx]</p><p><b>obitelj američkih komičara koja se sastoji od četiri brata s anarhičnim smjesom za humor. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of United States comedians consisting of four brothers with an anarchic sense of humor</p><p><b>marksizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the economic and political theories of Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels that hold that human actions and institutions are economically determined and that class struggle is needed to create historical change and that capitalism will ultimately be superseded by communism</p><