u (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> iron with a lofted face for hitting high shots to the green [seven iron]</p><p><b>Arapsko ime za Bliski istok (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Arabic name for the Middle East</p><p><b>(Islam) muslimansko mjesto molitve (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Islam) a Muslim place of worship [musjid]</p><p><b>krinka, kriti, maska, maska za podvodni ribolov, maske, maskirati, maskirati se, pretvarati se, zakrabuljiti, zaštitna maska, krabulja, obrazina, hiniti, kriti se, praviti se, prerušiti se, prerušivati se, prikriti se, prikrivati se, zabašuriti se, zakrabuljiti se, prerušiti, prerušivati, prikriti, prikrivati, sakriti, skrivati, zabašuriti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a covering to disguise or conceal the face</p><p><i>n.</i> activity that tries to conceal something</p><p><i>n.</i> a party of guests wearing costumes and masks [masque, masquerade, masquerade party]</p><p><i>n.</i> a protective covering worn over the face</p><p><i>v.</i> hide under a false appearance [cloak, dissemble]</p><p><i>v.</i> put a mask on or cover with a mask</p><p><i>v.</i> make unrecognizable [disguise]</p><p><i>v.</i> cover with a sauce</p><p><i>v.</i> shield from light [block out]</p><p><b>maskirajući, maskiranom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having its true character concealed with the intent of misleading [cloaked, disguised]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having markings suggestive of a mask</p><p><b>ples na kojem gosti nose kostime i maske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ball at which guests wear costumes and masks [fancy-dress ball, masquerade ball]</p><p><b>najčešća škrga u vlažnim staništima u Sjevernoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commonest shrew of moist habitats in North America [Sorex cinereus]</p><p><b>krinka, kriti, maska, maska za podvodni ribolov, maske, maskirati, maskirati se, pretvarati se, zakrabuljiti, zaštitna maska (od &quot;mask&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a participant in a masquerade [masquer, masquerader]</p><p><b>pokrivanje, zaklanjanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of concealing the existence of something by obstructing the view of it [cover, covering, screening]</p><p><i>n.</i> the blocking of one sensation resulting from the presence of another sensation</p><p><i>n.</i> scenery used to block the audience's view of parts of the stage that should not be seen [masking piece]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> adhesive tape used to cover the part of a surface that should not be painted [masking tape]</p><p><b>scenery koji se koristi za blokiranje pogleda publike na dijelove pozornice koji ne bi trebali biti viđeni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> scenery used to block the audience's view of parts of the stage that should not be seen [masking]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> adhesive tape used to cover the part of a surface that should not be painted [masking paper]</p><p><b>mazohizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sexual pleasure obtained from receiving punishment (physical or psychological)</p><p><b>Nekoga tko uživa u kažnjavanju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who obtains pleasure from receiving punishment</p><p><b>koji dobivaju zadovoljstvo ili seksualno zadovoljstvo od zlostavljanja ili dominacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deriving pleasure or sexual gratification from being abused or dominated</p><p><b>na masohistički način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a masochistic manner</p><p><b>mason, zidar, kamenorezac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American Revolutionary leader from Virginia whose objections led to the drafting of the Bill of Rights (1725-1792) [George Mason]</p><p><i>n.</i> English film actor (1909-1984) [James Mason, James Neville Mason]</p><p><i>n.</i> English writer (1865-1948) [A. E. W. Mason, Alfred Edward Woodley Mason]</p><p><i>n.</i> a craftsman who works with stone or brick [stonemason]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a widespread secret fraternal order pledged to mutual assistance and brotherly love [Freemason]</p><p><b>granicu izm