rialization]</p><p><i>n.</i> an appearance in bodily form (as of a disembodied spirit) [manifestation, materialization]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that comes into existence as a result [materialization, offspring]</p><p><b>Doći u postojanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come into being [happen, materialize]</p><p><b>materijalizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a desire for wealth and material possessions with little interest in ethical or spiritual matters [philistinism]</p><p><i>n.</i> (philosophy) the philosophical theory that matter is the only reality [physicalism]</p><p><b>Osoba koja ima veliko poštovanje prema materijalnom imovinu., netko tko misli da ništa ne postoji osim fizičke materije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone with great regard for material possessions</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who thinks that nothing exists but physical matter</p><p><b>materijalist, materijalistički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by materialism [mercenary, worldly-minded]</p><p><i>adj.</i> conforming to the standards and conventions of the middle class [bourgeois, conservative]</p><p><b>materijalistički. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a materialistic manner</p><p><b>materijalnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> relevance requiring careful consideration</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being physical [corporality, corporeality, physicalness]</p><p><b>proces stvaranja, pojavljivanje u tjelesnom obliku (kao da je beztjelni duh), nešto što dolazi u postojanje kao rezultat toga. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of coming into being [materialisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> an appearance in bodily form (as of a disembodied spirit) [manifestation, materialisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that comes into existence as a result [materialisation, offspring]</p><p><b>materijalizirati, ostvariti, otjeloviti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come into being [happen, materialise]</p><p><b>materijalno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to material aspects</p><p><i>adv.</i> to a significant degree</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (