fitting a mother [maternal quality, maternity, motherliness]</p><p><i>n.</i> motherly care</p><p><b>Pokazuju majčinski instinkt. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing maternal instincts</p><p><b>materinji</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a maternal manner [motherly]</p><p><b>materinstvo, rodilište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being pregnant [gestation, pregnancy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the kinship relation between an offspring and the mother [motherhood]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of having or showing the tenderness and warmth and affection of or befitting a mother [maternal quality, maternalism, motherliness]</p><p><b>rodilište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hospital that provides care for women during pregnancy and childbirth and for newborn infants</p><p><b>rodilište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hospital ward that provides care for women during pregnancy and childbirth and for newborn infants</p><p><b>prijatelji, par</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pair of people who live together [couple, match]</p><p><b>(koristi se u govornom jeziku) imaju odnos prijatelja ili prijatelja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used colloquially) having the relationship of friends or pals [chummy, pally, palsy-walsy]</p><p><b>matematika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a science (or group of related sciences) dealing with the logic of quantity and shape and arrangement [mathematics, maths]</p><p><b>netko tko predaje matematiku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who teaches mathematics [mathematics teacher]</p><p><b>matematički, matematičko, matematičkog, matematski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or of the nature of mathematics</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or having ability to think in or work with numbers [numerical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> beyond question</p><p><i>adj.</i> statistically possible though highly improbable</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by the exactness or precision of mathematics</p><p><b>funkcija, matematička funkcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (mathematics) a mathematical relation such that each element of a given set (the d