er and sculptor [Henri Emile Benoit Matisse, Henri Matisse]</p><p><b>hrvač, rvač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> combatant who tries to throw opponent to the ground [grappler, wrestler]</p><p><b>Pocahontas</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Powhatan woman (the daughter of Powhatan) who befriended the English at Jamestown and is said to have saved Captain John Smith's life (1595-1617) [Pocahontas, Rebecca Rolfe]</p><p><b>matrijarh, žena kao glava plemena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a female head of a family or tribe [materfamilias]</p><p><i>n.</i> a feisty older woman with a big bosom (as drawn in cartoons)</p><p><b>karakteristika matrijarhat (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of a matriarchy</p><p><b>matrijarhat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of social organization in which a female is the family head and title is traced through the female line [matriarchy]</p><p><b>matrijarh, žena kao glava plemena (od &quot;matriarch&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of societies or families) having a female as the family head or having descent traced through the female line</p><p><b>matrijarhat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of social organization in which a female is the family head and title is traced through the female line [matriarchate]</p><p><b>prijem u grupu (posebno na koledžu ili sveučilištu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> admission to a group (especially a college or university) [matriculation]</p><p><b>uglavnom oljčane biljke iz Starog svijeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chiefly Old World strong-smelling weedy herbs [genus Matricaria]</p><p><b>kamilica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual Eurasian herb similar in fragrance and medicinal uses to chamomile though taste is more bitter and effect is considered inferior [German chamomile, Matricaria recutita, sweet false chamomile, wild chamomile]</p><p><b>Europski godišnji korov s bijelim cvijećem i fino podijeljenim lišćama, prirodan i ponekad uzgajan u istočnoj Sjevernoj Americi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ubiquitous European annual weed with white flowers and finely divided lea