an]</p><p><b>Medina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in western Saudi Arabia [Al Madinah]</p><p><i>n.</i> the ancient quarter of many cities in northern Africa</p><p><b>tropski Stari svijet ukrasni zimzeleni grmovi s mesnim lištima i velikim panicama bijele ružičaste cveće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical Old World ornamental evergreen shrubs having fleshy leaves and large panicles of white pink flowers [genus Medinilla]</p><p><b>lijep tropski zimzelena epifitni grm uzgojen zbog svog bujnog lišća i ogromnih panika ružičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a beautiful tropical evergreen epiphytic shrub grown for its lush foliage and huge panicles of pink flowers</p><p><b>osrednji, prosječan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> moderate to inferior in quality [second-rate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking exceptional quality or ability [average, fair, middling]</p><p><i>adj.</i> poor to middling in quality</p><p><b>prosječni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ordinariness as a consequence of being average and not outstanding [averageness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person of second-rate ability or value [second-rater]</p><p><b>kaniti, namjeravati, premišljati, razmišljati, snovati, kontemplirati, meditirati, misliti, mozgati, promisliti, promišljati, promozgati, razmatrati, razmisliti, razmotriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> reflect deeply on a subject [chew over, contemplate, excogitate, mull, mull over, muse, ponder, reflect, ruminate, speculate, think over]</p><p><i>v.</i> think intently and at length, as for spiritual purposes [contemplate, study]</p><p><b>meditacija, razmišljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> continuous and profound contemplation or musing on a subject or series of subjects of a deep or abstruse nature [speculation]</p><p><i>n.</i> (religion) contemplation of spiritual matters (usually on religious or philosophical subjects)</p><p><b>kontemplativan, meditativan, sklon razmišljanju, zamišljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deeply or seriously thoughtful [brooding, broody, contemplative, musing, pensive, pondering, reflecti