31) [Dewey, Melvil Dewey]</p><p><b>Pravnik i glavni sudac Vrhovnog suda Sjedinjenih Država (1833-1910) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States jurist and chief justice of the United States Supreme Court (1833-1910) [Fuller, Melville Weston Fuller]</p><p><b>Pravnik i glavni sudac Vrhovnog suda Sjedinjenih Država (1833-1910) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States jurist and chief justice of the United States Supreme Court (1833-1910) [Fuller, Melville W. Fuller]</p><p><b>Američki kemičar poznat po otkriću niza kemijskih reakcija u fotosintezi (1911-) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States chemist noted for discovering the series of chemical reactions in photosynthesis (1911-) [Calvin]</p><p><b>mem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the 13th letter of the Hebrew alphabet</p><p><b>član, članica, pripadnik, ud, zastupnik, člana, članice, ekstremitet, okrajina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the persons who compose a social group (especially individuals who have joined and participate in a group organization) [fellow member]</p><p><i>n.</i> anything that belongs to a set or class</p><p><i>n.</i> an external body part that projects from the body [appendage, extremity]</p><p><i>n.</i> an organization that is a member of another organization (especially a state that belongs to a group of nations)</p><p><i>n.</i> the male sex organ (`member' is a euphemism) [penis, phallus]</p><p><b>Banka koja je članica Federalnog rezervnog sustava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bank that is a member of the Federal Reserve System</p><p><b>zastupnik, poslanik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elected member of the British Parliament: a member of the House of Commons [Parliamentarian]</p><p><b>član, članica, pripadnik, ud, zastupnik, člana, članice (od &quot;member&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having members</p><p><b>od grupe ili grupe bez članova (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a group or set having no members</p><p><b>broj članova, članski, članstvo, članstva, članstvom, grupa, kategorija, skupina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of