</p><p><i>n.</i> a place of business for retailing goods [outlet, retail store, sales outlet]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of rules applied to commercial transactions [commercial law, law merchant]</p><p><b>merkantilizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economic system (Europe in 18th century) to increase a nation's wealth by government regulation of all of the nation's commercial interests [mercantilism]</p><p><b>merkantilizam, komercijalizam, trgovanje, trgovina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economic system (Europe in 18th century) to increase a nation's wealth by government regulation of all of the nation's commercial interests [mercantile system]</p><p><i>n.</i> transactions (sales and purchases) having the objective of supplying commodities (goods and services) [commerce, commercialism]</p><p><b>lijek (trgovinski naziv Purinethol) koji ometa metabolizam purina i koji se koristi za liječenje akutne limfocitne leukemije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug (trade name Purinethol) that interferes with the metabolism of purine and is used to treat acute lymphocytic leukemia [Purinethol]</p><p><b>Flamanski geograf koji je živio u Njemačkoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Flemish geographer who lived in Germany [Gerardus Mercator, Gerhard Kremer]</p><p><b>Projekcija Zemlje na cilindru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a map projection of the earth onto a cylinder [Mercator's projection]</p><p><b>Projekcija Zemlje na cilindru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a map projection of the earth onto a cylinder [Mercator projection]</p><p><b>Američki plesač i koreograf (rođen 1922.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States dancer and choreographer (born in 1922) [Cunningham]</p><p><b>planina u Andima u Argentini (visina 22 210 stopa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain in the Andes in Argentina (22,210 feet high)</p><p><b>rod Veneridae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Veneridae [genus Mercenaria]</p><p><b>jedljiva američka školjka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edible American clam [Venus mercenaria, hard-shell clam, hard clam, quahaug, quahog, round clam]</p><p><b>ćiftinski, koristoljubiv, najamnički, plaćenički, plaćenik, plaćenik (vojnik)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person hired to fight for another country than their own [soldier of fortune]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by materialism [materialistic, worldly-minded]</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving for wages in a foreign army [free-lance, freelance]</p><p><i>adj.</i> profit oriented [mercantile, moneymaking]</p><p><b>Prodavač tekstilnih proizvoda (posebno svile), Britanski proizvođač štampanih tkanina koji je izumio mercerizing (1791-1866) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dealer in textiles (especially silks)</p><p><i>n.</i> British maker of printed calico cloth who invented mercerizing (1791-1866) [John Mercer]</p><p><b>tretirati za jačanje i poboljšanje sjaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> treat to strengthen and improve the luster [mercerize]</p><p><b>od pamukovog niti koja je tretirana natrijum hidroksidom kako bi se smanjila i povećala njen sjaj i afinitet za boju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of cotton thread that has been treated with sodium hydroxide to shrink it and increase its luster and affinity for dye [mercerized]</p><p><b>tretirati za jačanje i poboljšanje sjaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> treat to strengthen and improve the luster [mercerise]</p><p><b>od pamukovog niti koja je tretirana natrijum hidroksidom kako bi se smanjila i povećala njen sjaj i afinitet za boju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of cotton thread that has been treated with sodium hydroxide to shrink it and increase its luster and affinity for dye [mercerised]</p><p><b>roba, roba (teret), trgovati, proizvod, proizvodi, trgovačka roba, poslovati, tržiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commodities offered for sale [product, ware]</p><p><i>v.</i> engage in the trade of [trade]</p><p><b>trgovac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a businessperson engaged in retail trade [merchant]</p><p><b>marketing na prodajnom mjestu, trgovina robom, kupoprodaja, trgovanje, trgovina, t