/p><p><i>adv.</i> without pity [pitilessly, remorselessly, unmercifully]</p><p><b>nemilosrdnost, okrutnost, nemilost, nemilostivost, nesmiljenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feelings of extreme heartlessness [cruelty, pitilessness, ruthlessness]</p><p><i>n.</i> inhumaneness evidenced by an unwillingness to be kind or forgiving [unmercifulness]</p><p><b>Belgijski biciklista koji je pet puta osvojio Tour de France (rođen 1945.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Belgian racing cyclist who won the Tour de France five times (born in 1945) [Eddy Merckx]</p><p><b>Grčka filmska glumica (1925-1994) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek film actress (1925-1994) [Anna Amalia Mercouri, Melina Mercouri]</p><p><b>podložna iznenadnim nepredvidivim promjenama, koji se odnose na planet Merkur ili su pod njegovim (astrološkim) utjecajem, koji se odnosi na ili ima karakteristike (rekovite, lukav, brz, lopovski) pripisane bogu Merkurju, koji se odnose na živu ili sadrže živu ili su uzrokovani njom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> liable to sudden unpredictable change [erratic, fickle, quicksilver]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or under the (astrological) influence of the planet Mercury</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or having characteristics (eloquence, shrewdness, swiftness, thievishness) attributed to the god Mercury</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or containing or caused by mercury</p><p><b>maslava koja sadrži živu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ointment containing mercury</p><p><b>rod tankih biljaka iz obitelji Euphorbiaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of slender herbs belonging to the family Euphorbiaceae [genus Mercurialis]</p><p><b>Eurafrička godišnja biljka naturalizirana u Americi kao korov. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurafrican annual naturalized in America as a weed [boys-and-girls, herb mercury, herbs mercury]</p><p><b>Europska višegodišnja korovnica sa zelenkastim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European perennial weedy plant with greenish flowers [dog's mercury, dog mercury]</p><p><b>od ili sadržavaju živu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or containing mercury [mercurous]</p><p><b>bijeli otrovni rastvorljivi kristalni sublimat žive (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white poisonous soluble crystalline sublimate of mercury [bichloride of mercury, corrosive sublimate, mercury chloride]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom srebra od 1 do 10 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mercurial compound applied topically as an antiseptic [merbromine]</p><p><b>od ili sadržavaju živu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or containing mercury [mercuric]</p><p><b>bez ukusnog bezbojnog praha koji se koristi u medicini kao katartičar. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tasteless colorless powder used medicinally as a cathartic [calomel]</p><p><b>planeta Merkur, živa, živin preparat, Merkur</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heavy silvery toxic univalent and bivalent metallic element [Hg, atomic number 80, hydrargyrum, quicksilver]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman mythology) messenger of Jupiter and god of commerce</p><p><i>n.</i> the smallest planet and the nearest to the sun</p><p><i>n.</i> temperature measured by a mercury thermometer</p><p><b>Barometar koji pokazuje pritisak prema visini stuba žive (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> barometer that shows pressure by the height of a column of mercury</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena (POP) od 0,9 mas.% ili više, ali ne više od 0,9 mas.% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a primary cell consisting of a zinc anode and a cathode of mercury oxide and an electrolyte of potassium hydroxide</p><p><b>bijeli otrovni rastvorljivi kristalni sublimat žive (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white poisonous soluble crystalline sublimate of mercury [bichloride of mercury, corrosive sublimate, mercuric chloride]</p><p><b>Bjeloviti koji se kada suhi nasilno eksplodira ako se udari ili zagrije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fulminate that when dry explodes violently if struck or heated [fulminate of mercury, fulminating mercury]</p><p><b>To je stanje uzrokovano unesenjem ili udisanjem žive. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic condition caused by ingesting or inhaling mercury</p><p><b>Program letova na rakete koji su poduzele SAD između 1961. i 1963. s ciljem stavljanja čovjeka u orbitu oko Zemlje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a program of rocket-powered flights undertaken by US between 1961 and 1963 with the goal of putting a man in orbit around the earth</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom ugljika od 0,01 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thermometer consisting of mercury contained in a bulb at the bottom of a graduated sealed glass capillary tube marked in degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit [mercury-in-glass thermometer]</p><p><b>zagađeni žive (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> contaminated by mercury</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom ugljika od 10%, ali ne više od 50% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mercury thermometer designed to measure the temperature of the human body [clinical thermometer]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom ugljika od 0,01 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thermometer consisting of mercury contained in a bulb at the bottom of a graduated sealed glass capillary tube marked in degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit [mercury thermometer]</p><p><b>UV svjetlo koje emitira jak plavičasto svjetlo (bogato ultraljubičastim zračenjem) dok električna struja prolazi kroz par žive (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ultraviolet lamp that emits a strong bluish light (rich in ultraviolet radiation) as electric current passes through mercury vapor</p><p><b>milosrđe, milost, oproštaj, sažaljenje, uspjeh, milosrdnost, milostivost, samilost, sućut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leniency and compassion shown toward offenders by a person or agency charged with administering justice [clemency, mercifulness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to be kind and forgiving [mercifulness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling that motivates compassion [mercifulness]</p><p><i>n.</i> something for which to be thankful</p><p><i>n.</i> alleviation of distress</p><p><b>eutanazija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of killing someone painlessly (especially someone suffering from an incurable illness) [euthanasia]</p><p><b>Božji prijestolje., zlatno pokriće kovčeg saveza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the throne of God</p><p><i>n.</i> the golden covering of the ark of the covenant</p><p><b>čist, jedini, jezero, potpun, pravi, puki, puni, ribnjak, sam, sav, upravo takav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small pond of standing water</p><p><i>adj.</i> being nothing more than specified</p><p><i>adj.</i> apart from anything else [bare, simple]</p><p><b>Vođa američkih građanskih prava čija je registracija na koledžu uzrokovala nered u tradicionalno segregiranom Mississippiju (rođen 1933), Engleski romanopisac i pjesnik (1828-1909) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States civil rights leader whose college registration caused riots in traditionally segregated Mississippi (born in 1933) [James Howard Meredith, James Meredith]</p><p><i>n.</i> English novelist and poet (1828-1909) [George Meredith]</p><p><b>jedino, prosto, samo toliko, samo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> and nothing more [but, just, only, simply]</p><p><b>stari izraz za spomenik koji se sastojao od gomile kamenja na kojoj je bila postavljena ploča (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an old term for a landmark that consisted of a pile of stones surmounted by an upright slab [mearstone, meerestone]</p><p><b>kao ili u vezi s prostitutkom, bez ukusnog i naivnog., na temelju pretpostavke (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> like or relating to a prostitute</p><p><i>adj.</i> tastelessly showy [brassy, cheap, flash, flashy, garish, gaudy, gimcrack, loud, tacky, tatty, tawdry, trashy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> based on pretense [gilded, glossy, specious]</p><p><b>Na način koji je neispravno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a meretricious manner [flashily]</p><p><b>izgled istine koji je lažan ili obmanjujuć., bez ukusne ostvarenja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an appearance of truth that is false or deceptive [speciousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> tasteless showiness [brashness, flashiness, garishness, gaudiness, glitz, loudness, taw