uto-zapuštenim cvjetovima u obliku zvona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Uvularia having yellowish drooping bell-shaped flowers [bellwort, wild oats]</p><p><b>vrteška, vrtuljak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a never-ending cycle of activities and events (especially when they seem to have little purpose)</p><p><i>n.</i> a large, rotating machine with seats for children to ride or amusement [carousel, carrousel, roundabout, whirligig]</p><p><b>slavljenik koji učestvuje u bučnoj zabavi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a celebrant who shares in a noisy party [reveler, reveller]</p><p><b>zabava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a boisterous celebration [conviviality, jollification]</p><p><b>rod biljaka iz obitelji Boraginaceae koji rastu u umjereno temperiranim područjima i imaju plave ili ljubičaste cvijeće u obliku lovora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of herbs belonging to the family Boraginaceae that grow in temperate regions and have blue or purple flowers shaped like funnels [genus Mertensia]</p><p><b>glatka uspravna biljka sa istočnog sjevernog dijela Sjeverne Amerike koja ima čitave lišće i blesave cvijeće koje je u pupoljku ružičaste boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> smooth erect herb of eastern North America having entire leaves and showy blue flowers that are pink in bud [Virginia bluebell, Virginia cowslip]</p><p><b>svjetlo-crstalni prah (trgovinski naziv Merthiolate) koji se koristi kao kirurški antiseptik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light-colored crystalline powder (trade name Merthiolate) used as a surgical antiseptic [sodium ethylmercurithiosalicylate, thimerosal]</p><p><b>Religiozni i pisac iz Sjedinjenih Država (1915-1968), Sociolog iz Sjedinjenih Država (1910-2003) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States religious and writer (1915-1968) [Thomas Merton]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States sociologist (1910-2003) [Robert King Merton, Robert Merton]</p><p><b>Američka filmska glumica (rođena 1949) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film actress (born in 1949) [Streep]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika, podrijetlo za proizvodnju i prodaju: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small to medium evergreen dioecious trees of oceanic climates: puka [genus Meryta]</p><p><b>maleno okruglo stablo s glavom na Novom Zelandu s velikim smočastim listovima i panicama zeleno-bijelog cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small roundheaded New Zealand tree having large resinous leaves and panicles of green-white flowers [puka]</p><p><b>mesa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flat tableland with steep edges [table]</p><p><i>n.</i> a city in Arizona just to the east of Phoenix</p><p><b>nacionalni park u Coloradu koji sadrži prapovijesna stena na liticama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a national park in Colorado containing prehistoric cliff dwellings</p><p><b>niz brda u sjeveroistočnoj Minnesoti gdje su otkrivene bogate rudne nalazišta željeza 1887. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a range of hills in northeastern Minnesota where rich iron ore deposits were discovered in 1887</p><p><b>brak s osobom nižeg društvenog statusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a marriage with a person of inferior social status</p><p><b>toksični antikonvulzivni lijek (trgovinski naziv Mesantoin) koji se koristi u liječenju epilepsije kada manje toksični antikonvulzivni lijekovi nisu djelotvorni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic anticonvulsant drug (trade name Mesantoin) used in the treatment of epilepsy when less toxic anticonvulsants have been ineffective [mephenytoin]</p><p><b>Hinduistički sunčev praznik na početku nove astrološke godine kada Sunce uđe u sazvežđe Ovana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Hindu solar holiday at the beginning of the new astrological year when the sun enters the constellation Aries</p><p><b>mali bezkičmenog kaktusa u obliku kugle, bezbojan meksički alkohol destilirani od fermentiranih sokova određenih pustinjskih biljaka iz roda Agavaceae (posebno biljke stoljeća) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small spineless globe-shaped cactus [Lophophora williamsii, mezcal, peyote]</p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless Mexican liquor distilled from fermented juices of certain desert plants of the genus Agavaceae (especially the century plant)</p><p><b>grm ili malo stablo s pimetnim lišćama otrovnim za stoku i guste raseme intenzivno mirisnih plavih cvijeća i crvenih graha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub or small tree having pinnate leaves poisonous to livestock and dense racemes of intensely fragrant blue flowers and red beans [Sophora secundiflora, coral bean, frijolillo, frijolito]</p><p><b>Vrh kaktusa mescal u obliku gumbova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the button-shaped top of the mescal cactus [magic mushroom, sacred mushroom]</p><p><b>meskalin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the hallucinatory alkaloid that is the active agent in mescal buttons [peyote]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 1. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka ne primjenjuje druga pravila, to znači da se ne primjenjuje druga pravila. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African annual or biennial plants having flowers that open only in bright sunlight [genus Mesembryanthemum]</p><p><b>Stari svijet godišnji široko prirodni u toplim područjima s bijelim cvijećem i mesnim lišće prekriveno dlakama koje liče na led (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World annual widely naturalized in warm regions having white flowers and fleshy foliage covered with hairs that resemble ice [ice plant, icicle plant]</p><p><b>u slučaju da je proizvodnja proizvoda u skladu s člankom 1. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe ograničena na proizvodnju proizvoda koji sadrže: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing South African succulent plant having a capsular fruit containing edible pulp [Carpobrotus edulis, Hottentot's fig, Hottentot fig, sour fig]</p><p><b>srednji dio mozga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the middle portion of the brain [midbrain]</p><p><b>mesodermalno tkivo koje formira vezivno tkivo i krv i glatke mišiće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mesodermal tissue that forms connective tissue and blood and smooth muscles</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili smješten u mezenteriju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or located in a mesentery</p><p><b>jedna od dvije grane aorte koja prolazi između dva sloja mezenterija do crijeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of two branches of the aorta that pass between the two layers of the mesentery to the intestines [arteria mesenterica]</p><p><b>Plex autonomnih živaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plexus of autonomic nerves [plexus mesentericus]</p><p><b>potokan portalne vene koji prolazi iz crijeva između dva sloja mezenterija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the portal vein passing from the intestine between the two layers of mesentery [vena mesenterica]</p><p><b>dvostruki sloj peritoneuma koji se veže za stražnji zid trbušne šupljine i podržava tanko crijevo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a double layer of peritoneum that attaches to the back wall of the abdominal cavity and supports the small intestines</p><p><b>isprepletenost, mreža, mreža (elemenata), oko, oko mreže, otvor, stupica, uhvatiti u mrežu, zamka, ispreplitanje, povezanost, povezivanje, preplitanje, obavezati, pokrenuti, pokretati, uključiti, uključivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the number of openings per linear inch of a screen</p><p><i>n.</i> contact by fitting together [engagement, interlocking, meshing]</p><p><i>n.</i> the topology of a network whose components are all connected directly to every other component [mesh topology]</p><p><i>n.</i> an open fabric of string or rope or wire woven together at regular intervals [meshing, meshwork, net, network]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of interlocking or meshing [interlock, interlocking, meshing]</p><p><i>v.</i> keep engaged [engage, lock, operate]</p><p><i>v.</i> coordinate in such a way that all parts work together effectively [interlock]</p><p><i>v.</i> work together in harmony</p><p><i>v.</i> entangle or catch in (or as if in) a mesh [enmesh, ensnarl]</p><p><b>topologija mreže čije su sve komponente povezane izravno s svakom drugom komponentom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the topology of a network whose components are all connected directly to every other component [mesh]</p><p><b>isprepletenost, mreža, mreža (elemenata), oko, oko mreže, otvor, stupica, uhvatiti u mrežu, zamka (od &quot;mesh&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the holy city of Shiite Muslims [Mashhad]</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a network</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of toothed parts or gears) interlocked and interacting [engaged, intermeshed]</p><p><b>mreža, ispreplitanje, povezanost, povezivanje, preplitanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> contact by fitting together [engagement, interlocking, mesh]</p><p><i>n.</i> an open fabric of string or rope or wire woven together at regular intervals [mesh, meshwork, net, network]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of interlocking or meshing [interlock, interlocking, mesh]</p><p><b>beznačajno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> senseless [meshugga, meshugge, meshuggeneh, meshuggener]</p><p><b>(Jidiš) ludilo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) craziness [mishegaas, mishegoss]</p><p><b>beznačajno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> senseless [meshuga, meshugge, meshuggeneh, meshuggener]</p><p><b>beznačajno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> senseless [meshuga, meshugga, meshuggeneh, meshuggener]</p><p><b>(Jidiš) ludi budala, beznačajno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a crazy fool [meshuggener]</p><p><i>adj.</i> senseless [meshuga, meshugga, meshugge, meshuggener]</p><p><b>(Jidiš) ludi budala, beznačajno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a crazy fool [meshuggeneh]</p><p><i>adj.</i> senseless [meshuga, meshugga, meshugge, meshuggeneh]</p><p><b>mreža</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an open fabric of string or rope or wire woven together at regular intervals [mesh, meshing, net, network]</p><p><b>da je u ili usmjeren prema srednjoj liniji ili mesijalnoj ravni tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being in or directed toward the midline or mesial plane of the body</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s mezonom, s masenim udjelom vlage od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to a meson [mesonic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or characterized by moderate or a well-balanced supply of moisture</p><p><b>Austrijski liječnik koji je pokušao liječiti bolesti hipnozom (1734-1815) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Austrian physician who tried to treat diseases with a form of hypnotism (1734-1815) [Franz Anton Mesmer, Friedrich Anton Mesmer]</p><p><b>privlači i zadržava zanimanje kao da je čarolija (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> attracting and holding interest as if by a spell [hypnotic, mesmerizing, spellbinding]</p><p><b>hipnotizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> attract strongly, as if with a magnet [bewitch, magnetise, magnetize, mesmerize, spellbind]</p><p><i>v.</i> induce hypnosis in [hypnotise, hypnotize, mesmerize]</p><p><b>da ti se pažnja fiksira kao da si začaran. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having your attention fixated as though by a spell [fascinated, hypnotised, hypnotized, mesmerized, spell-bound, spellbound, transfixed]</p><p><b>Hipnoza je čin indukcije hipnoze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of inducing hypnosis [hypnotism, suggestion]</p><p><b>hipnotizer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who induces hypnosis [hypnotiser, hypnotist, hypnotizer, mesmerizer]</p><p><b>hipnotizirati, očarati, opčiniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> attract strongly, as if with a magnet [bewitch, magnetise, magnetize, mesmerise, spellbind]</p><p><i>v.</i> induce hypnosis in [hypnotise, hypnotize, mesmerise]</p><p><b>da ti se pažnja fiksira kao da si začaran. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having your attention fixated as though by a spell [fascinated, hypnotised, hypnotized, mesmerised, spell-bound, spellbound, transfixed]</p><p><b>hipnotizer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who induces hypnosis [hypnotiser, hypnotist, hypnotizer, mesmerist]</p><p><b>hipnotizirati, očarati, opčiniti (od &quot;mesmerize&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> attracting and holding interest as if by a spell [hypnotic, mesmeric, spellbinding]</p><p><b>feudalni gospodar koji je bio gospodar vlastitim stanarima na zemljištu koje je držan od superiornog gospodara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feudal lord who was lord to his own tenants on land held from a superior lord</p><p><b>Meksiko i Srednja Amerika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mexico and Central America</p><p><b>član jednog od različitih naroda koji žive u Mezoamerici, o ili koji se odnose na ljude Mezoamerice ili njihove jezike ili kulture (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of one of the various peoples inhabiting Mesoamerica</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the people of Mesoamerica or their languages or cultures</p><p><b>srednji sloj klice koji se razvija u mišiće i kosti i hrskavicu i krv i vezivno tkivo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the middle germ layer that develops into muscle and bone and cartilage and blood and connective tissue [mesoderm]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na mezoderm ili se izvode iz njega (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or derived from the mesoderm [mesodermal]</p><p><b>srednji sloj perikarpusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the middle layer of a pericarp</p><p><b>mezenteriju koja drži donji debeljak na dorsalnom trbušnom zidu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mesentery that holds the lower colon to the dorsal abdominal wall</p><p><b>zlatni hrčeri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> golden hamsters [genus Mesocricetus]</p><p><b>mali svijetlo obojeni hrčak koji se često drži kao kućni ljubimac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small light-colored hamster often kept as a pet [Syrian hamster, golden hamster]</p><p><b>srednji sloj klice koji se razvija u mišiće i kosti i hrskavicu i krv i vezivno tkivo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the middle germ layer that develops into muscle and bone and cartilage and blood and connective tissue [mesoblast]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na mezoderm ili se izvode iz njega (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or derived from the mesoderm [mesoblastic]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička triprsta Oligocen životinja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American three-toed Oligocene animal</p><p><b>srednji dio kamenog doba počinje prije oko 15.000 godina, od ili u vezi s srednjim razdobljem kamenog doba (nakon paleolita) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> middle part of the Stone Age beginning about 15,000 years ago [Epipaleolithic, Mesolithic Age]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a middle period of the Stone Age (following the paleolithic)</p><p><b>srednji dio kamenog doba počinje prije oko 15.000 godina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> middle part of the Stone Age beginning about 15,000 years ago [Epipaleolithic, Mesolithic]</p><p><b>Osoba s dobro razvijenim mišićnim tijelom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person with a well-developed muscular body</p><p><b>s robusnom mišićnom tjelesnom građenom osobinom koju karakteriše prevladavanje struktura (koštane i mišićne i vezivno tkivo) razvijenih iz embrionalnog mezodermalnog sloja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a robust muscular body-build characterized by predominance of structures (bone and muscle and connective tissue) developed from the embryonic mesodermal layer [muscular]</p><p><b>mišićno i veliko kostije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> muscular and big-boned [athletic type]</p><p><b>mezon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elementary particle responsible for the forces in the atomic nucleus [mesotron]</p><p><b>mezon (od &quot;meson&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to a meson [mesic]</p><p><b>glatko izbočenje čelne kosti između i iznad obrva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a smooth prominence of the frontal bone between and above the eyebrows [glabella]</p><p><b>biljka koja raste u okolini s prosječnim zalihom vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> land plant growing in surroundings having an average supply of water [mesophytic plant]</p><p><b>u srednji vlažnom okruženju ili se prilagođava tome (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being or growing in or adapted to a moderately moist environment</p><p><b>biljka koja raste u okolini s prosječnim zalihom vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> land plant growing in surroundings having an average supply of water [mesophyte]</p><p><b>Zemlja između rijeke Tigris i Eufrat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the land between the Tigris and Euphrates</p><p><b>atmosferski sloj između stratosfere i termosfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the atmospheric layer between the stratosphere and the thermosphere</p><p><b>mezoteliom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of carcinoma of the mesothelium lining lungs or abdomen or heart</p><p><b>obdjev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> epithelium originating in the embryonic mesoderm</p><p><b>elementarna čestica odgovorna za sile u atomskom jezgru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elementary particle responsible for the forces in the atomic nucleus [meson]</p><p><b>mezozoik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> from 230 million to 63 million years ago [Age of Reptiles, Mesozoic era]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or denoting the Mesozoic era</p><p><b>od 230 do 63 milijuna godina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> from 230 million to 63 million years ago [Age of Reptiles, Mesozoic]</p><p><b>Slatkici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medlars [genus Mespilus]</p><p><b>mušmula</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small deciduous Eurasian tree cultivated for its fruit that resemble crab apples [medlar, medlar tree]</p><p><b>bilo koje od nekoliko malih trnastih stabala ili grmova roda Prosopis s malim cvijećem u osjetnim cilindričnim šiljcima nakon kojih slijede velike struke bogate šećerom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several small spiny trees or shrubs of the genus Prosopis having small flowers in axillary cylindrical spikes followed by large pods rich in sugar [mesquite]</p><p><b>bilo koje od nekoliko malih trnastih stabala ili grmova roda Prosopis s malim cvijećem u osjetnim cilindričnim šiljcima nakon kojih slijede velike struke bogate šećerom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several small spiny trees or shrubs of the genus Prosopis having small flowers in axillary cylindrical spikes followed by large pods rich in sugar [mesquit]</p><p><b>gume dobivene od struka mesquite (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gum obtained from mesquite pods</p><p><b>čorbasta hrana, hraniti se, isprljati, izm