frared but shorter than radio waves)</p><p><i>n.</i> kitchen appliance that cooks food by passing an electromagnetic wave through it [microwave oven]</p><p><i>v.</i> cook or heat in a microwave oven [micro-cook, nuke, zap]</p><p><b>bomba koja eksplodira u zraku i oslobađa masivan izboj elektromagnetne energije dovoljan da onesposobiti računare i telekomunikacije bez ubijanja ljudi ili oštećenja zgrada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb that explodes in midair and releases a massive burst of electromagnetic energy sufficient to disable computers and telecommunications without killing people or damaging buildings [E-bomb]</p><p><b>Diatermijska naprava koja koristi mikrovalno zračenje kao izvor toplote (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> diathermy machine that uses microwave radiation as the source of heat</p><p><b>linearni ubrzač koji koristi mikrovalove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> linear accelerator that uses microwaves</p><p><b>kuhinjski aparat koji kuha hranu prolaženjem elektromagnetnog talasa kroz njega (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> kitchen appliance that cooks food by passing an electromagnetic wave through it [microwave]</p><p><b>radar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> measuring instrument in which the echo of a pulse of microwave radiation is used to detect and locate distant objects [radar, radio detection and ranging, radiolocation]</p><p><b>korištenje spektroskopije za proučavanje atomske ili molekularne rezonanse u mikrovalnom spektru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of spectroscopy to study atomic or molecular resonances in the microwave spectrum</p><p><b>dio elektromagnetskog spektra koji odgovara mikrovalnim valovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of the electromagnetic spectrum corresponding to microwaves</p><p><b>hidroklorotiazid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a diuretic drug (trade name Microzide, Esidrix, and HydroDIURIL) used in the treatment of hypertension [Esidrix, HydroDIURIL, hydrochlorothiazide]</p><p><b>koralne zmije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coral snakes [genus Micruroides]</p><p><b>r