and for his opposition to government intervention in the economy (born in 1912) [Friedman]</p><p><b>Sladnjak i filantrop iz Sjedinjenih Država koji je stvorio industrijski model grada Hershey, Pennsylvania (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States confectioner and philanthropist who created the model industrial town of Hershey, Pennsylvania [Hershey]</p><p><b>rod tropskih američkih orhideja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of tropical American orchids [genus Miltonia]</p><p><b>sedativ i sedativ (trgovinski naziv Miltown i Equanil i Meprin) koji se koristi za liječenje mišićne napetosti i anksioznosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sedative and tranquilizer (trade name Miltown and Equanil and Meprin) used to treat muscle tension and anxiety [Equanil, Meprin, meprobamate]</p><p><b>U kategoriji "Specialties" se podrazumijevaju: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus including the common European kits [genus-Milvus]</p><p><b>tamni staromorski zmajev koji se uglavnom hrani mrvom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dark Old World kite feeding chiefly on carrion [black kite]</p><p><b>Najveći grad u Wisconsinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> largest city of Wisconsin</p><p><b>(od sanskritske riječi za "refleksiju" ili "interpretiranje") jedan od šest ortodoksnih filozofskih sustava ili gledišta na ritualne tradicije ukorijenjene u Veda i Brahmana za razliku od Vedante koja se uglavnom oslanja na Upanishade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (from the Sanskrit word for `reflection' or `interpretation') one of six orthodox philosophical systems or viewpoints on ritual traditions rooted in the Vedas and the Brahmanas as opposed to Vedanta which relies mostly on the Upanishads</p><p><b>mimika, pantomima, oponašati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an actor who communicates entirely by gesture and facial expression [mimer, mummer, pantomimer, pantomimist]</p><p><i>n.</i> a performance using gestures and body movements without words [dumb show, pantomime]</p><p><i>v.</i> imitate (a person or manner), especially for satirical effect [mimic]</p><p><i>v.</i> act out without words but with gestures and bodily movements only [pantomime]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 98. točka (a) ovog članka primjenjuje se sljedeći tarifni broj: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rotary duplicator that uses a stencil through which ink is pressed (trade mark Roneo) [Roneo, Roneograph, mimeograph, mimeograph machine]</p><p><i>v.</i> print copies from (a prepared stencil) using a mimeograph [mimeograph]</p><p><b>umnožavanje dokumenta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rotary duplicator that uses a stencil through which ink is pressed (trade mark Roneo) [Roneo, Roneograph, mimeo, mimeograph machine]</p><p><i>v.</i> print copies from (a prepared stencil) using a mimeograph [mimeo]</p><p><b>mimika (od &quot;mime&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an actor who communicates entirely by gesture and facial expression [mime, mummer, pantomimer, pantomimist]</p><p><b>mimezis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the imitative representation of nature and human behavior in art and literature</p><p><i>n.</i> any disease that shows symptoms characteristic of another disease</p><p><i>n.</i> the representation of another person's words in a speech</p><p><b>karakterizira ili je prirodne prirode ili korištenje mimesis, koji pokazuju mimikriju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by or of the nature of or using mimesis</p><p><i>adj.</i> exhibiting mimicry</p><p><b>falsificiran, glumac, imitirati, koji oponaša, krivotvoren, ličiti na, mimičar, oponašati, podražavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who mimics (especially an actor or actress) [mimicker]</p><p><i>v.</i> imitate (a person or manner), especially for satirical effect [mime]</p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting an imitation</p><p><b>netko tko oponaša (posebno glumac ili glumica) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who mimics (especially an actor or actress) [mimic]</p><p><b>ponašanje oponašanja., U slučaju da se primjenjuje jedna od navedenih metoda, primjenjuje se sljedeća metoda: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of mimicking [apery]</p><p><i>n.</i> the resemblance of an animal species to another species or to natural objects</p><p><b>ponekad se smatra podobitelj Troglodytidae: ptice-mačkice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sometimes considered a subfamily of Troglodytidae: mockingbirds [family Mimidae]</p><p><b>Mimir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Norse mythology) giant who lives in the roots of Yggdrasil and guards the well of wisdom</p><p><b>mimoza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen Australasian tree having white or silvery bark and young leaves and yellow flowers [Acacia dealbata, silver wattle]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various tropical shrubs or trees of the genus Mimosa having usually yellow flowers and compound leaves</p><p><i>n.</i> a mixed drink containing champagne and orange juice [buck's fizz]</p><p><b>tropski američki trnasti grm ili drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American thorny shrub or small tree [Acacia farnesiana, cassie, flame tree, huisache, scented wattle, sweet acacia, sweet wattle]</p><p><b>podstruka iz tropske Amerike i Australije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prostrate or semi-erect subshrub of tropical America, and Australia [action plant, humble plant, live-and-die, sensitive plant, shame plant, touch-me-not]</p><p><b>poluplješti trnasti zimzeleni grm tropske Amerike s složenim lišćama osjetljivim na svjetlost i dodir (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> semi-climbing prickly evergreen shrub of tropical America having compound leaves sensitive to light and touch [sensitive plant]</p><p><b>obitelj trnastih drvenih biljaka (obično grmova ili malih stabala) čiji lišće oponaša životinje u osjetljivosti na dodir (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of spiny woody plants (usually shrubs or small trees) whose leaves mimic animals in sensitivity to touch [family Mimosaceae]</p><p><b>Alternativno ime koje se koristi u nekim sustavima klasifikacije za obitelj Mimosaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> alternative name used in some classification systems for the family Mimosaceae [subfamily