/b></p><p><i>n.</i> a troupe of performers in blackface typically giving a comic program of negro songs and jokes</p><p><i>n.</i> a variety show in which the performers are made up in blackface</p><p><b>grupa minstrelova., balade koje pjevaju minstrelci, umjetnost minstrel (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a troupe of minstrels</p><p><i>n.</i> ballads sung by minstrels</p><p><i>n.</i> the art of a minstrel</p><p><b>izmisliti, izumiti, izvor, kovati novac, kovnica, metvica, porijeklo, menta, gomila, hrpa, hrpetina, masa, mnoštvo, iskovati, kovati, skovati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (often followed by `of') a large number or amount or extent [batch, deal, flock, good deal, great deal, hatful, heap, lot, mass, mess, mickle, mountain, muckle, passel, peck, pile, plenty, pot, quite a little, raft, sight, slew, spate, stack, tidy sum, wad]</p><p><i>n.</i> any north temperate plant of the genus Mentha with aromatic leaves and small mauve flowers</p><p><i>n.</i> any member of the mint family of plants</p><p><i>n.</i> the leaves of a mint plant used fresh or candied</p><p><i>n.</i> a candy that is flavored with a mint oil [mint candy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a plant where money is coined by authority of the government</p><p><i>v.</i> form by stamping, punching, or printing [coin, strike]</p><p><i>adj.</i> as if new</p><p><b>slatkiše koje je okusan s uljem od mentone (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a candy that is flavored with a mint oil [mint]</p><p><b>velika obitelj aromatičnih biljaka i grmova s cvijećem nalik usnama usta i s četvoroklopnim jajnika s četiri jednosemena oraha i uključujući mentinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large family of aromatic herbs and shrubs having flowers resembling the lips of a mouth and four-lobed ovaries yielding four one-seeded nutlets and including mint [Labiatae, Lamiaceae, family Labiatae, family Lamiaceae]</p><p><b>dvostruko travlje s žutim cvjetovima poput gumbova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tansy-scented Eurasian perennial herb with buttonlike yellow flowers [Chrysanthemum balsamita, Tanacetum balsamita, alecost, balsam herb, bible leaf, costmary]</p><p><b>Bourbon i šećer i muda na slomljenom ledu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bourbon and sugar and mint over crushed ice [julep]</p><p><b>Slatki razrjeđeni sirup s posječenim lišćama mentine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sweetened diluted vinegar with chopped mint leaves</p><p><b>miris na mentolu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> smelling of mint</p><p><b>kovanje, kovani novac, kovanice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coins collectively [coinage, metal money, specie]</p><p><i>n.</i> fee paid to a mint by the government for minting a coin</p><p><i>n.</i> act or process of minting coins</p><p><b>izmisliti, izumiti, izvor, kovati novac, kovnica, metvica, porijeklo, menta (od &quot;mint&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skilled worker who coins or stamps money [coiner, moneyer]</p><p><b>oznaka na novčiću koja označava kovanicu u kojoj je proizvedena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mark on a coin that identifies the mint where it was produced</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili ukazuju na mentolu, od aromatske mentine, posebno mentine piparne (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or suggestive of mint</p><p><i>adj.</i> of the flavor of mint, particularly peppermint</p><p><b>uglavnom višegodišnje biljke sjeverne hemisfere često s navikom stvaranja podmeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mostly perennial herbs of northern hemisphere often with mat-forming habit [genus Minuartia]</p><p><b>minuend, umanjenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the number from which the subtrahend is subtracted</p><p><b>menuet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stately court dance in the 17th century</p><p><i>n.</i> a stately piece of music composed for dancing the minuet</p><p><b>Nizozemski kolonizator koji je od domorodaca kupio Manhattan za 24 dolara (1580-1638) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch colonist who bought Manhattan from the Native Americans for the equivalent of $24 (1580-1638) [Minnewit, Peter Minnewit, Peter Minuit]</p><p><b>bez, lišen, manje, minus, negativan, oduzimanje, umanjen za, umanjena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arithmetic operation in which the difference between two numbers is calculated [subtraction]</p><p><i>adj.</i> on the negative side or lower end of a scale</p><p><i>adj.</i> involving disadvantage or harm [negative]</p><p><b>znak koji označava operaciju oduzimanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sign indicating the operation of subtraction</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s malom kurzivnom pismom razvijenom iz uncial (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a small cursive script developed from uncial [minuscule]</p><p><b>nevažan, verzal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the characters that were once kept in bottom half of a compositor's type case [lower-case letter, lowercase, small letter]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small cursive script developed from uncial between the 7th and 9th centuries and used in medieval manuscripts</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a small cursive script developed from uncial [minuscular]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lowercase [little, small]</p><p><i>adj.</i> extremely small [miniscule]</p><p><b>beznačajan, iscrpan, malen, minuta, neznatan, podroban, pribilješka, primjedba, sićušan, sitan, točan, tren, zabilješka, zabilješke sa sastanaka, zabilježiti, zapisnik, izračun vrijeme, minut, minuti, minutne, minutnim, silan, min., trenutak, mah, sekunda, čas, časak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of time equal to 60 seconds or 1/60th of an hour [min]</p><p><i>n.</i> an indefinitely short time [bit, mo, moment, second]</p><p><i>n.</i> a particular point in time [instant, moment, second]</p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of angular distance equal to a 60th of a degree [arcminute, minute of arc]</p><p><i>n.</i> a short note</p><p><i>n.</i> distance measured by the time taken to cover it [hour]</p><p><i>adj.</i> infinitely or immeasurably small [infinitesimal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by painstaking care and detailed examination [narrow]</p><p><b>Knjiga u kojoj su zapisnici zapisani. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a book in which minutes have been written</p><p><b