t for public worship (at least ten males over thirteen years of age)</p><p><b>Miocen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> from 25 million to 13 million years ago [Miocene epoch]</p><p><b>od 25 do 13 milijuna godina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> from 25 million to 13 million years ago [Miocene]</p><p><b>(genetika) ćelijska podjela koja proizvodi reprodukcijske stanice u spolno razmnožavajućim organizmama, refleksna kontrakcija mišića sfinktera iris-a kao odgovor na svijetlo svjetlo (ili određene lijekove) zbog čega se zjenica smanjuje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) cell division that produces reproductive cells in sexually reproducing organisms [meiosis, reduction division]</p><p><i>n.</i> reflex contraction of the sphincter muscle of the iris in response to a bright light (or certain drugs) causing the pupil to become smaller [light reflex, myosis, pupillary reflex]</p><p><b>lijek koji uzrokuje mioz (sušenje zjenice oka), koji uzrokuju suženje zjenice oka ili su povezani s njom ili uzrokuju suženje zjenice oka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that causes miosis (constriction of the pupil of the eye) [miotic drug, myotic, myotic drug]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or causing constriction of the pupil of the eye [myotic]</p><p><b>lijek koji uzrokuje mioz (sušenje zjenice oka) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that causes miosis (constriction of the pupil of the eye) [miotic, myotic, myotic drug]</p><p><b>liječenje glaukoma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a treatment for glaucoma</p><p><b>(računalnička znanost) jedinica za mjerenje brzine izvršavanja CPU-a računala (ali ne cijelog sustava) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a unit for measuring the execution speed of a computer's CPU (but not the whole system) [million instructions per second]</p><p><b>Francuski revolucionar koji je bio istaknut u ranim danima Francuske revolucije (1749-1791) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French revolutionary who was prominent in the early days of the French Revolution (1749-1791) [Comte de Mirabeau, Honore-Gabriel Victor Riqueti]</p><p><b>Četiri sata. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> four o'clocks [genus Mirabilis]</p><p><b>Kalifornija u četiri sata sa ljubičastim crvenim cvijećem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> California four o'clock with purple-red flowers [California four o'clock, Mirabilis laevis]</p><p><b>obična vrtna biljka Sjeverne Amerike koja ima mirisne crvene ili ljubičaste ili žute ili bijele cvijeće koje se otvaraju kasno popodne (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common garden plant of North America having fragrant red or purple or yellow or white flowers that open in late afternoon [Mirabilis uniflora, common four-o'clock, marvel-of-Peru]</p><p><b>Kalifornija u četiri sata sa ljubičastim crvenim cvijećem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> California four o'clock with purple-red flowers [California four o'clock, Mirabilis californica]</p><p><b>ljeploviti divlji cvijet s mirisnim vitkim ili blijedo ružičastim cvijećem u obliku trube (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leafy wildflower having fragrant slender white or pale pink trumpet-shaped flowers [maravilla, sweet four o'clock]</p><p><b>divlji cvijet s živopisnim tamno ružičastim cijevičnim večernim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wildflower having vibrant deep pink tubular evening-blooming flowers [Colorado four o'clock, desert four o'clock, maravilla]</p><p><b>lišćavi divlji cvijet s lavandrovom-ružičastim cvijećem koji se otvara uvečer i ostaje kroz hladni dio sljedećeg dana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leafy wildflower with lavender-pink flowers that open in the evening and remain through cool part of the next day [mountain four o'clock]</p><p><b>obična vrtna biljka Sjeverne Amerike koja ima mirisne crvene ili ljubičaste ili žute ili bijele cvijeće koje se otvaraju kasno popodne (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common garden plant of North America having fragrant red or purple or yellow or white flowers that open in late afternoon [Mirabilis jalapa, common four-o'clock, marvel-of-Peru]</p><p><b>čudo, srednjovjekovna drama, začudni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any amazing or wonderful occurrence</p><p><i>n.</i> a marvellous event manifesting a supernatural act of a divine agent</p><p><b>osoba koja tvrdi ili se navodi da čini čuda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who claims or is alleged to perform miracles [miracle worker]</p><p><b>srednjovjekovna predstava koja predstavlja epizode iz života svetog ili mučenika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a medieval play representing episodes from the life of a saint or martyr</p><p><b>osoba koja tvrdi ili se navodi da čini čuda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who claims or is alleged to perform miracles [miracle man]</p><p><b>obožavanje čuda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the worship of miracles [thaumatolatry]</p><p><b>čudan, čudesan, čudotvoran, izvanredan, natprirodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being or having the character of a miracle [marvellous, marvelous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> peculiarly fortunate or appropriate [heaven-sent, providential]</p><p><b>mana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Old Testament) food that God gave the Israelites during the Exodus [manna, manna from heaven]</p><p><b>čudan, čudesan, čudotvoran, izvanredan, natprirodan (od &quot;miraculous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a miraculous manner</p><p><b>fatamorgana, iluzija, opsjena, optička varka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an optical illusion in which atmospheric refraction by a layer of hot air distorts or inverts reflections of distant objects</p><p><i>n.</i> something illusory and unattainable</p><p><b>Pravilo da vas policija (kada vas ispiti nakon uhićenja) mora upozoriti da sve što kažete može biti korišteno kao dokaz i pročitati vam vaša ustavna prava (pravo na odvjetnika i pravo na šutnju dok ne savjetuje odvjetnik) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the rule that police (when interrogating you after an arrest) are obliged to warn you that anything you say may be used as evidence and to read you your constitutional rights (the right to a lawyer and the right to remain silent until advised by a lawyer)</p><p><b>Godišnji suncokreta uzgojen za silažu i za njegova sjemena koja su izvor ulja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual sunflower grown for silage and for its seeds which are a source of oil [Helianthus annuus, common sunflower]</p><p><b>blato, glib, kal, močvara, okaljati, ukaljati, uprskati blatom, zaglibiti se, zaglibiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soft wet area of low-lying land that sinks underfoot [morass, quag, quagmire, slack]</p><p><i>n.</i> deep soft mud in water or slush [slop]</p><p><i>n.</i> a difficulty or embarrassment that is hard to extricate yourself from</p><p><i>v.</i> entrap [entangle]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to get stuck as if in a mire [bog down]</p><p><i>v.</i> be unable to move further [bog down, get stuck, grind to a halt]</p><p><i>v.</i> soil with mud, muck, or mire [muck, muck up, mud]</p><p><b>u zamci ili pod uslovom da je na primjer u blatu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> entangled or hindered as if e.g. in mire [involved]</p><p><b>malo poznatiji kamarupanski jezici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> little known Kamarupan languages [Abor, Dafla, Mirish]</p><p><b>različita biljka lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of leaf bug [capsid, mirid bug]</p><p><b>različita biljka lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of leaf bug [capsid, mirid]</p><p><b>čvorovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leaf bugs [Capsidae, family Capsidae, family Miridae]</p><p><b>malo poznatiji kamarupanski jezici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> little known Kamarupan languages [Abor, Dafla, Miri]</p><p><b>mračan, taman</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of liquids) clouded as with sediment [cloudy, muddy, murky, turbid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> dark or gloomy [murky]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1., Španjolski slikar (1893-1983) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> New Zealand conifer used for lumber [Podocarpus ferruginea, Prumnopitys ferruginea, black pine]</p><p><i>n.</i> Spanish surrealist painter (1893-1983) [Joan Miro]</p><p><b>slonovi morski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> elephant seals [genus Mirounga]</p><p><b>obrazac, odbijati, odražavati, ogledalo, ogledati, retrovizor, staklo, uglačana površina, zrcaliti, zrcalne, zrcalo, špigl</b></p><p><i>n.</i> polished surface that forms images by reflecting light</p><p><i>n.</i> a faithful depiction or reflection</p><p><i>v.</i> reflect as if in a mirror</p><p><i>v.</i> reflect or resemble</p><p><b>domaći karp s nekim velikim sjajnim ljuskama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> domestic carp with some large shining scales</p><p><b>zrcalna slika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a likeness in which left and right are reversed [reflection, reflexion]</p><p><b>(fizički) paritet je očuvan u svemiru u kojem su zakoni fizike isti u desnom sustavu koordinata kao i u lijevom sustavu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) parity is conserved in a universe in which the laws of physics are the same in a right-handed system of coordinates as in a left-handed system [conservation of parity, parity, space-reflection symmetry]</p><p><b>odnos opozicije između kristala ili molekula koji su odraz jedni drugih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation of opposition between crystals or molecules that are reflections of one another [enantiomorphism]</p><p><b>kao odraženo u zrcalu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> like or characteristic of a mirror image</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of reflecting light like a mirror [specular]</p><p><b>radost, veselost, veselje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> great merriment [glee, gleefulness, hilarity, mirthfulness]</p><p><b>veseo, smiješan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of or showing high-spirited merriment [gay, jocund, jolly, jovial, merry]</p><p><i>adj.</i> arousing or provoking laughter [amusing, comic, comical, funny, laughable, risible]</p><p><b>sretno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a joyous manner [blithely, gayly, happily, jubilantly, merrily]</p><p><b>veseo (od &quot;mirthful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> great merriment [glee, gleefulness, hilarity, mirth]</p><p><b>Nedostatak veselja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking mirth</p><p><b>muljevit, močvaran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of soil) soft and watery [boggy, marshy, mucky, muddy, quaggy, sloppy, sloughy, soggy, squashy, swampy, waterlogged]</p><p><b>Stavio si pogrešnu adresu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> put a wrong address on [misdirect]</p><p><b>nesreća, nesretan slučaj, nezgoda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instance of misfortune [mischance, mishap]</p><p><b>dati loš savjet (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give bad advice to [misguide]</p><p><b>neispravno ili loše poravnanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> align imperfectly or badly</p><p><b>ekscentričnost, iskrivljenost, neporavnatost, odstupanje, otklon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the spatial property of things that are not properly aligned</p><p><b>neprikladno savezništvo (posebno u vezi braka) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unsuitable alliance (especially with regard to marriage)</p><p><b>Napravi loš savez. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a bad alliance</p><p><b>netko tko ne voli ljude uopšte. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who dislikes people in general [misanthropist]</p><p><b>mizantropski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> believing the worst of human nature and motives [cynical, misanthropical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> hating mankind in general [misanthropical]</p><p><b>Vjerovanje u najgore ljudske prirode i motiva., mrziti čovječanstvo u cjelini. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> believing the worst of human nature and motives [cynical, misanthropic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> hating mankind in general [misanthropic]</p><p><b>mizantrop</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who dislikes people in general [misanthrope]</p><p><b>mržnja prema čovječanstvu., sklonost da ne voli i ne vjeruje drugim ljudima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hatred of mankind</p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to dislike and mistrust other people</p><p><b>zlouporaba, pronevjera, pronevjerenje, zloporaba, zloupotreba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wrong use or application</p><p><i>n.</i> the fraudulent appropriation of funds or property entrusted to your care but actually owned by someone else [defalcation, 