oneous manner [erroneously]</p><p><b>greška, pobrkati, pogreška, pogriješiti, prevariti se, propust, zabluda, zabuna, zabuniti (se), zabuniti se, zamijeniti (od &quot;mistake&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> putting the wrong interpretation on [misinterpretation, misunderstanding]</p><p><b>gospodin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of address for a man [Mr, Mr.]</p><p><b>biljka s rizomatom u središnjoj i jugoistočnoj Americi i u Zapadnoj Indiji s velikim, navidnim glavama čistih plavih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhizomatous plant of central and southeastern United States and West Indies having large showy heads of clear blue flowers [Conoclinium coelestinum, Eupatorium coelestinum, ageratum, mist-flower]</p><p><b>nejasno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a misty manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a vague way [vaguely]</p><p><b>vrijeme pogrešno (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> time incorrectly</p><p><b>nešto što se nalazi u vrijeme kada ne bi moglo postojati ili se dogoditi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something located at a time when it could not have existed or occurred [anachronism, misdating]</p><p><b>maglovitost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cloudiness resulting from haze or mist or vapor [haziness, steaminess, vaporousness, vapourousness]</p><p><b>drozd imelaš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large European thrush that feeds on mistletoe berries [Turdus viscivorus, missel thrush, mistletoe thrush]</p><p><b>bijela imela, imela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American plants closely resembling Old World mistletoe [false mistletoe]</p><p><i>n.</i> Old World parasitic shrub having branching greenish stems with leathery leaves and waxy white glutinous berries [Old World mistletoe, Viscum album]</p><p><i>n.</i> shrub of central and southeastern Europe [Loranthus europaeus]</p><p><b>biljka iz roda Rhipsalis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant of the genus Rhipsalis</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama smatra se podobiteljjom Loranthaceae, u nekim klasifikacijama uključuje Viscaceae: parazitski ili hemiparazitski grmovi ili grmovi ili mala stabla tropskih i umjerenih regija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications considered a subfamily of Loranthaceae [Viscaceae, family Viscaceae]</p><p><i>n.</i> in some classification includes Viscaceae: parasitic or hemiparasitic shrublets or shrubs or small trees of tropical and temperate regions [Loranthaceae, family Loranthaceae]</p><p><b>grm ili malo stablo koje se često uzgaja kao kućna biljka s lišćem poput jastog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub or small tree often grown as a houseplant having foliage like mistletoe [Ficus deltoidea, Ficus diversifolia, mistletoe rubber plant]</p><p><b>grm ili malo stablo koje se često uzgaja kao kućna biljka s lišćem poput jastog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub or small tree often grown as a houseplant having foliage like mistletoe [Ficus deltoidea, Ficus diversifolia, mistletoe fig]</p><p><b>veliki europski bršljan koji se hrani bobicama jastogova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large European thrush that feeds on mistletoe berries [Turdus viscivorus, missel thrush, mistle thrush]</p><p><b>maestral</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strong north wind that blows in France during the winter</p><p><b>Neispravno prevoditi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> translate incorrectly</p><p><b>pogrešan prijevod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an incorrect translation</p><p><b>maltretirati, zlorabiti, zlostavljati, zloupotrijebiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> treat badly [abuse, ill-treat, ill-use, maltreat, step]</p><p><b>maltretirati, zlorabiti, zlostavljati, zloupotrijebiti (od &quot;mistreat&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> subjected to cruel treatment [abused, ill-treated, maltreated]</p><p><b>loše ophođenje, maltretiranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of treating (someone or something) badly</p><p><b>domaćica, gazdarica, gospodar, gospodarica, gospođa, ljubavnica, majstorica, učiteljica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an adulterous woman [fancy woman, kept woman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a woman schoolteacher (especially one regarded as strict) [schoolma'am, schoolmarm, schoolmistress]</p><p><i>n.<