rpose</p><p><b>Sveučilište inženjerstva u Cambridgeu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an engineering university in Cambridge [Massachusetts Institute of Technology]</p><p><b>Engleski inženjer zrakoplovstva (1895-1937), Američki avijator i general koji je bio rani zagovornik vojne zračne moći (1879-1936), Američki astronom koji je proučavao sunčeve mrlje i maglice (1818-1889), Američka spisateljica poznata po romanu o jugu tijekom američkog građanskog rata (1900-1949), Američki radnički vođa, Plesarka iz Sjedinjenih Država koja je osnovala prvu crnu klasičnu baletnu kompaniju (rođena 1934.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English aeronautical engineer (1895-1937) [R. J. Mitchell, Reginald Joseph Mitchell]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States aviator and general who was an early advocate of military air power (1879-1936) [Billy Mitchell, William Mitchell]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States astronomer who studied sunspots and nebulae (1818-1889) [Maria Mitchell]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer noted for her novel about the South during the American Civil War (1900-1949) [Margaret Mitchell, Margaret Munnerlyn Mitchell]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States labor leader [John Mitchell]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States dancer who formed the first Black classical ballet company (born in 1934) [Arthur Mitchell]</p><p><b>puzeće zimzelene biljke Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creeping evergreen herbs of North America [genus Mitchella]</p><p><b>puzava drvena biljka sa istoka Sjeverne Amerike s sjajnim večnozelenim lišcima i crvenim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creeping woody plant of eastern North America with shiny evergreen leaves and scarlet berries [boxberry, partridgeberry, twinberry]</p><p><b>Robert Mitchum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film actor (1917-1997) [Robert Mitchum]</p><p><b>crv, dijete, doprinos, filir, grinja, novčić, obol, pola groša, sitan stvor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slight but appreciable amount [hint, jot, pinch, soupcon, speck, tinge, touch]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous very small to minute arachnids often infesting animals or plants or stored foods</p><p><b>kutija za sakupljanje milostinje, posebno jedna u crkvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> box for collecting alms, especially one in a church [alms box, poor box]</p><p><b>rodni nizki tanki biljni biljci iz Sjeverne Amerike i sjeveroistočne Azije s cvijećem s trostrukim ili pinnatifičnim laticama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of low slender herbs of North America and northeastern Asia having flowers with trifid or pinnatifid petals [genus Mitella]</p><p><b>miterwort sjeveroistočne Sjeverne Amerike obično s dva suprotna lista na uspravnim cvjetnim stabljikama koji se završavaju u uspravnim rascima bijelih cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> miterwort of northeastern North America usually with two opposite leaves on erect flowering stems that terminate in erect racemes of white flowers [fairy cup]</p><p><b>mala biljka s lišćama u bazalnom skupu i sitnim zelenkastim cvijećima u tankim rascima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small plant with leaves in a basal cluster and tiny greenish flowers in slender racemes [five-point bishop's cap]</p><p><b>biskupska čast, biskupska kapa, klin, mitra, pol pravog kuta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> joint that forms a corner [miter joint, mitre, mitre joint]</p><p><i>n.</i> the surface of a beveled end of a piece where a miter joint is made [mitre]</p><p><i>n.</i> a liturgical headdress worn by bishops on formal occasions [mitre]</p><p><i>v.</i> bevel the edges of, to make a miter joint</p><p><i>v.</i> confer a miter on (a bishop)</p><p><i>v.</i> fit together in a miter joint</p><p><b>za proizvodnju električnih vozila s motorom za vožnju ili motorom za vožnju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hand tool for guiding handsaws in making crosscuts or miter joints [mitre box]</p><p><b>spoj koji čini ugao (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> joint that forms a corner [miter, mitre, mitre joint]</p><p><b>Helvella s sadljastim plodnim dijelom i kremastoj boji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a helvella w