e]</p><p><i>v.</i> mix together different elements [blend, coalesce, combine, commingle, conflate, flux, fuse, immix, meld, merge]</p><p><i>v.</i> open (a place) to members of all races and ethnic groups [desegregate, integrate]</p><p><i>v.</i> combine (electronic signals)</p><p><i>v.</i> add as an additional element or part [mix in]</p><p><i>v.</i> to bring or combine together or with something else [amalgamate, commix, mingle, unify]</p><p><i>v.</i> mix so as to make a random order or arrangement [ruffle, shuffle]</p><p><b>umiješati, miješati, pomiješati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause (something) to be mixed with (something else) [blend in]</p><p><i>v.</i> add as an additional element or part [mix]</p><p><b>brkati, gužva, nered, pomiješati, tuča, zbrka</b></p><p><i>v.</i> assemble without order or sense [confuse, jumble]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be perplexed or confounded [stump]</p><p><b>brkati, gužva, nered, pomiješati, tuča, zbrka, zabuna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mistake that results from taking one thing to be another [confusion]</p><p><b>(hemija, fizika) koji se mogu miješati (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (chemistry, physics) capable of being mixed [miscible]</p><p><b>izmiješan, izmješan, miješan, miješani, mješovit, opijen, ošamućen, pomiješan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> consisting of a haphazard assortment of different kinds [assorted, miscellaneous, motley, sundry]</p><p><i>adj.</i> involving or composed of different races [interracial]</p><p><b>asortiman, izbor, mnoštvo, plejada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collection containing a variety of sorts of things [assortment, miscellanea, miscellany, mixture, motley, potpourri, salmagundi, smorgasbord, variety]</p><p><b>pupolj koji daje i lišće i cvijeće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bud yielding both leaves and flowers</p><p><b>miješano piće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> made of two or more ingredients</p><p><b>mješovita ekonomija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economic system that combines private and state enterprises</p><p><b>mješoviti uzgoj</b></p><