 intensity of [check, contain, control, curb, hold, hold in]</p><p><i>v.</i> make less severe or harsh [mince, soften]</p><p><i>v.</i> make less strong or intense [tame, tone down]</p><p><i>v.</i> make more temperate, acceptable, or suitable by adding something else [mollify, season, temper]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being within reasonable or average limits</p><p><i>adj.</i> not extreme [temperate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by avoidance of extravagance or extremes [restrained]</p><p><b>vjetar 13-18 čvorova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wind moving 13-18 knots</p><p><b>vjetar 32-38 čvorova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wind moving 32-38 knots [near gale]</p><p><b>srednji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> intermediate in size [medium-size, medium-sized, moderate-sized]</p><p><b>srednji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> intermediate in size [medium-size, medium-sized, moderate-size]</p><p><b>umjereno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to certain extent or degree [fairly, jolly, middling, passably, pretty, reasonably, somewhat]</p><p><i>adv.</i> with moderation</p><p><b>obuzdati, ograničiti se, oportunista, smekšati, smiriti, suzdržljiv, ublažiti, umjeren, umjerenjak, umjeriti (od &quot;moderate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being moderate in price or expenditures [modestness, reasonableness]</p><p><i>n.</i> quality of being moderate and avoiding extremes [moderation]</p><p><b>smirujući, ublažavajući</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lessening in intensity or strength</p><p><b>dosljednost, suzbijanje, suzdržavanje, suzdržljivost, umjerenost, uzdržavanje, zadržavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> quality of being moderate and avoiding extremes [moderateness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a change for the better [easing, relief]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of avoiding excesses [temperance]</p><p><i>n.</i> the action of lessening in severity or intensity [mitigation]</p><p><b>politika umjerenja ili djelovanja s umjerenošću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the policy of being moderate or acting with moderation</p><p><b>umjeren pijac (za razliku od potpunog uzdržanika), Osoba koja zauzima položaj u političkom središtu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a moderate drinker (as opposed to a total abstainer)</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who takes a position in the political center [centrist, middle of the roader, moderate]</p><p><b>politička filozofija izbjegavanja krajnosti ljevice i desnice uzimajući umjereni stav ili način djelovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political philosophy of avoiding the extremes of left and right by taking a moderate position or course of action [centrism]</p><p><b>(od tempoa) umjereno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of tempo) moderate</p><p><b>arbitar, ispitivač, moderator, moderatorski, posrednik, regulator, usklađivač, voditelj višekorisničke komunikacije elektroničkom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any substance used to slow down neutrons in nuclear reactors</p><p><i>n.</i> in the Presbyterian church, the officer who presides over a synod or general assembly</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who presides over a forum or debate</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who mediates disputes and attempts to avoid violence</p><p><b>poziciju moderatora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the position of moderator</p><p><b>moderan, nov, suvremen, moderna, moderne, moderno, rezidencijalno, suvremena, suvremene, suvremenih, suvremenom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a contemporary person</p><p><i>n.</i> a typeface (based on an 18th century design by Gianbattista Bodoni) distinguished by regular shape and hairline serifs and heavy downstrokes [Bodoni, Bodoni font, modern font]</p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to the modern era</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a recently developed fashion or style [mod, modernistic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of present-day art and music and literature and architecture</p><p><i>adj.</i> ahead of the times [advanced, forward-looking, innovative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> used of a living language [New]</p><p><b>stil baleta koji dopušta širu raznolikost pokreta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a style of ballet that admits a wider variety of movements</p><p><b>sti