><b>otok sjeverozapadno od Walesa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an island to the northwest of Wales [Anglesea, Anglesea Island, Anglesey, Anglesey Island]</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je država članica članica članica, država članica članica koja je podnositelj zahtjeva za odobrenje mora biti država članica u kojoj se nalazi., od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Monako ili njegov narod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Monaco [Monegasque]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Monaco or its people [Monegasque]</p><p><b>Monako</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a constitutional monarchy in a tiny enclave on the French Riviera [Principality of Monaco]</p><p><b>Glavni grad Monaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital of Monaco</p><p><b>(hemija) atom koji ima valenciju od jedan, Jedinstveni metafizički entitet od kojeg se navodi da materijalna svojstva proizlaze., (biologija) jednokćelijski mikroorganizam (posebno prvostojni protuzoani) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) an atom having a valence of one</p><p><i>n.</i> a singular metaphysical entity from which material properties are said to derive [monas]</p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) a single-celled microorganism (especially a flagellate protozoan)</p><p><b>operacija s točno jednim operandom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an operation with exactly one operand [unary operation]</p><p><b>Bliski bacan iz južne Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brilliantly colored pheasant of southern Asia [monaul]</p><p><b>imati samo jednog muža u isto vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having only one husband at a time</p><p><b>stanje imati samo jednog muža u isto vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of having only one husband at a time</p><p><b>monarh, vladar, car</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nation's ruler or head of state usually by hereditary right [crowned head, sovereign]</p><p><i>n.</i> large migratory American butterfly having deep orange wings with black and white markings [Danaus plexippus, milkweed butterfly, monarch butterfly]</p><p><b>veliki selidbeni američki leptir s duboko narandžastim krilima s crno-bijelim oznakama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large migratory American butterfly having deep orange wings with black and white markings [Danaus plexippus, milkweed butterfly, monarch]</p><p><b>koji imaju karakteristike ili odgovaraju ili su dostojni monarha, vladaju ili imaju vrhovnu moć koja leži kod monarha (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the characteristics of or befitting or worthy of a monarch [monarchical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> ruled by or having the supreme power resting with a monarch [monarchic, monarchical]</p><p><b>monarh, vladar, car (od &quot;monarch&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> ruled by or having the supreme power resting with a monarch [monarchal, monarchical]</p><p><b>koji imaju karakteristike ili odgovaraju ili su dostojni monarha, vladaju ili imaju vrhovnu moć koja leži kod monarha (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the characteristics of or befitting or worthy of a monarch [monarchal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> ruled by or having the supreme power resting with a monarch [monarchal, monarchic]</p><p><b>monarhizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a belief in and advocacy of monarchy as a political system</p><p><b>zagovornik principa monarhije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of the principles of monarchy [royalist]</p><p><b>kraljevina, monarhija, monarhije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an autocracy governed by a monarch who usually inherits the authority</p><p><b>za proizvodnju biljaka od biljaka iz stabla od poluproizvodnog izvora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various aromatic herbs of the genus Monarda [wild bergamot]</p><p><b>godišnji konjski konj iz središnjih i zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i sjevernog Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an annual horsemint of central and western United States and northern Mexico [horsemint, lemon mint]</p><p><b>višegodišnje biljke iz Sjeverne Amerike (od New Yorka do Illinoisa i planina Aljaske) s aromatičnim listovima i grmovima žuto-ružičastih kuglica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial herb of North America (New York to Illinois and mountains of Alaska) having aromatic leaves and clusters of yellowish-pink balls [basil balm]</p><p><b>višegodišnje aromatično bilje iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s različito obojenim cijevičnim cvijećem u gustim najozbiljnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial aromatic herb of eastern North America having variously colored tubular flowers in dense showy heads [bee balm, beebalm, bergamot mint, oswego tea]</p><p><b>višegodišnje biljke iz Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial herb of North America [bee balm, beebalm]</p><p><b>godišnji iz južnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual of southern United States [plains lemon monarda]</p><p><b>Visoka, uspravna višegodišnja ili jednogodišnja biljka s lanceolatičnim listovima i glavama ljubičasto-pomičastih kremasto-cvrkica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall erect perennial or annual having lanceolate leaves and heads of purple-spotted creamy flowers [horsemint]</p><p><b>rod mirisnih biljaka iz obitelji Labiatae u zapadnim Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of fragrant herbs of the family Labiatae in the western United States [genus Monardella]</p><p><b>aromatična californijska godišnja biljka s lanceolatičnim listovima i grmovima ruževičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fragrant California annual herb having lanceolate leaves and clusters of rose-purple flowers [mustang mint]</p><p><b>umjetni jezik. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial language</p><p><b>Jedinstveni metafizički entitet od kojeg se navodi da materijalna svojstva proizlaze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a singular metaphysical entity from which material properties are said to derive [monad]</p><p><b>manastir, samostan, samostanom, samostanu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the residence of a religious community</p><p><b>kaluđerski, manastirski, monaški, redovnički, samostanski, redovnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a male religious living in a cloister and devoting himself to contemplation and prayer and work [monk]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of communal life sequestered from the world under religious vows [cloistered, cloistral, conventual, monastical]</p><p><b>habit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long loose habit worn by monks in a monastery</p><p><b>crkveni red</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of person living under a religious rule [order]</p><p><b>Odvojeni od svijeta pod vjerskim zavjetima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of communal life sequestered from the world under religious vows [cloistered, cloistral, conventual, monastic]</p><p><b>Askeza kao oblik vjerskoga života (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> asceticism as a form of religious life</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mas.% ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mas.% (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an element consisting of a single atom [monoatomic]</p><p><b>Bliski bacan iz južne Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brilliantly colored pheasant of southern Asia [monal]</p><p><b>monotički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or having or hearing with only one ear</p><p><b>monotički (od &quot;monaural&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a monaural manner [in one ear, to one ear]</p><p><b>mineral crvenkasto-smeđe boje koji sadrži rijetke zemaljske metale (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reddish-brown mineral containing rare earth metals</p><p><b>ponedjeljak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the second day of the week [Mon]</p><p><b>Nizozemski slikar čiji rad (srezanje linija pod pravim uglom i ravnica u primarnim bojama) utjecao je na razvoj apstraktne umjetnosti (1872-1944) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch painter whose work (intersecting lines at right angles and planes in primary colors) influenced the development of abstract art (1872-1944) [Piet Mondrian]</p><p><b>koji imaju muške i ženske reproduktivne organe u istoj biljci ili životinji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having male and female reproductive organs in the same plant or animal [monoecious, monoicous]</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je država članica članica članica, država članica članica koja je podnositelj zahtjeva za odobrenje mora biti država članica u kojoj se nalazi., od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Monako ili njegov narod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Monaco [Monacan]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Monaco or its people [Monacan]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mas.% ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mas.% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alloy of nickel and copper and other metals (such as iron and/or manganese and/or aluminum) [Monell metal]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mas.% ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mas.% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alloy of nickel and copper and other metals (such as iron and/or manganese and/or aluminum) [Monel metal]</p><p><b>Pro-karotne bakterije i plavo-zelene alge i razni primitivni patogeni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prokaryotic bacteria and blue-green algae and various primitive pathogens [Prokayotae, kingdom Monera, kingdom Prokaryotae]</p><p><b>monera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> organisms that typically reproduce by asexual budding or fission and whose nutritional mode is absorption or photosynthesis or chemosynthesis [moneron]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Monera</p><p><b>monera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> organisms that typically reproduce by asexual budding or fission and whose nutritional mode is absorption or photosynthesis or chemosynthesis [moneran]</p><p><b>jedna vrsta: jednoklatna zimska zelena biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one species: one-flowered wintergreen [genus Moneses]</p><p><b>čvrsta zimzelena patuljasta biljka sjevernog umjerenog područja s jednim bijelom završnom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> delicate evergreen dwarf herb of north temperate regions having a solitary white terminal flower [Pyrola uniflora, one-flowered pyrola, one-flowered wintergreen]</p><p><b>koji imaju jedan estrozni ciklus godišnje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having one estrous cycle per year [monoestrous]</p><p><b>Francuski slikar impresionista (1840-1926) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French impressionist painter (1840-1926) [Claude Monet]</p><p><b>ekonomska teorija koja tvrdi da su promjene u nezaposlenosti i stopi inflacije obično uzrokovane promjenama u ponudi novca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economic theory holding that variations in unemployment and the rate of inflation are usually caused by changes in the supply of money</p><p><b>zagovornik teorije da su ekonomske fluktuacije uzrokovane povećanjem ili smanjenjem količine novca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of the theory that economic fluctuations are caused by increases or decreases in the supply of money</p><p><b>monetaran, monetarni, novčani</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or involving money [pecuniary]</p><p><b>fond, monetarni fond, novčani fond</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reserve of money set aside for some purpose [fund]</p><p><b>financije, financijska sredstva, novčana sredstva, novčani resursi, sredstva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> assets in the form of money [cash in hand, finances, funds, pecuniary resource]</p><p><b>vrijednost iza novca u monetarnom sustavu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the value behind the money in a monetary system [standard]</p><p><b>monetarni sustav, novčani sustav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anything that is generally accepted as a standard of value and a measure of wealth in a particular country or region [medium of exchange]</p><p><b>moneta, novčana jedinica, valuta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of money</p><p><b>cijena, novčana vrijednost, vrijednost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of having material worth (often indicated by the amount of money something would bring if sold) [cost, price]</p><p><b>utvrđivanje nečega (npr. zlata ili srebra) kao zakonitog sredstva plaćanja zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> establishing something (e.g. gold or silver) as the legal tender of a country [monetization]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, države članice mogu: (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give legal value to or establish as the legal tender of a country [monetize]</p><p><b>utvrđivanje nečega (npr. zlata ili srebra) kao zakonitog sredstva plaćanja zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> establishing something (e.g. gold or silver) as the legal tender of a country [monetisation]</p><p><b>unovčiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give legal value to or establish as the legal tender of a country [monetise]</p><p><b>financijski, novac, novčani, novca, novčana oskudica, pare</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the most common medium of exchange</p><p><i>n.</i> wealth reckoned in terms of money</p><p><i>n.</i> the official currency issued by a government or national bank</p><p><b>pojas s skrivenim dijelom za držanje novca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> belt with a concealed section for holding money</p><p><b>kasica, mala blagajna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a container (usually with a slot in the top) for keeping money at home [bank, coin bank, savings bank]</p><p><i>n.</i> a strongbox for holding cash [cashbox, till]</p><p><b>onaj čiji je posao razmjena novca jedne zemlje za novac druge zemlje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one whose business is to exchange the money of one country for that of another country [exchanger]</p><p><b>kovrie čija se školjka koristi za novac u dijelovima južnog Tihog oceana i u dijelovima Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cowrie whose shell is used for money in parts of the southern Pacific and in parts of Africa [Cypraea moneta]</p><p><b>novčar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who receives or invests or pays out money [money handler]</p><p><b>osoba koja prima ili ulaže ili isplaćuje novac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who receives or invests or pays out money [money dealer]</p><p><b>pranje novca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> concealing the source of illegally gotten money</p><p><b>novčano tržište, tržište novca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a market for short-term debt instruments</p><p><b>novčana uputnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a written order for the payment of a sum to a named individual [postal order]</p><p><b>biljka iz jugoistočne Europe koja se uzgaja zbog mirisnih ljubičastih cvijeća i okruglih ravnih papirnatih srebrno-bijelog sjemena koja se koriste za unutarnju dekoraciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> southeastern European plant cultivated for its fragrant purplish flowers and round flat papery silver-white seedpods that are used for indoor decoration [Lunaria annua, honesty, satin flower, satinpod, silver dollar]</p><p><b>ponuda novca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the total stock of money in the economy</p><p><b>projekt koji generiše kontinuirani protok novca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a project that generates a continuous flow of money [cash cow, moneymaker]</p><p><b>vreća za novac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drawstring bag for holding money</p><p><b>imućan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> based on or arising from the possession of money or wealth [monied]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having an abundant supply of money or possessions of value [affluent, flush, loaded, substantial, wealthy]</p><p><b>financijski, novac, novčani, novca, novčana oskudica, pare (od &quot;money&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skilled worker who coins or stamps money [coiner, minter]</p><p><b>netko čiji je glavni interes u životu zarađivanje novca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone whose main interest in life is moneymaking</p><p><b>lihvar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who lends money at excessive rates of interest [loan shark, shylock, usurer]</p><p><b>ne zasniva se na posjedovanju novca, bez novca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not based on the possession of money</p><p><i>adj.</i> having no money</p><p><b>netko tko je uspješan u gomilanju bogatstva, projekt koji generiše kontinuirani protok novca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is successful in accumulating wealth</p><p><i>n.</i> a project that generates a continuous flow of money [cash cow, money-spinner]</p><p><b>čin zarađivanja novca (i nakupljanja bogatstva), ostvaruje značajan profit, profitno orijentirana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making money (and accumulating wealth)</p><p><i>adj.</i> producing a sizeable profit [lucrative, remunerative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> profit oriented [mercantile, mercenary]</p><p><b>financijer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person skilled in large scale financial transactions [financier]</p><p><b>Vina s lozom trakama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loosestrife vine [Lysimachia nummularia, creeping Charlie, creeping Jenny]</p><p><b>prodavač, trgovac, piljariti, preprodavati, torbariti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who purchases and maintains an inventory of goods to be sold [bargainer, dealer, trader]</p><p><i>v.</i> sell or offer for sale from place to place [hawk, huckster, peddle, pitch, vend]</p><p><b>Sjeme biljke mung grah, Sjeme biljke mung grah korišteno za hranu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> seed of the mung bean plant [golden gram, green bean, green gram, green soy, mash bean, moong, mung, mung bean, munggo]</p><p><i>n.</i> seed of the mung bean plant used for food [golden gram, green bean, green gram, green soy, mash bean, moong, mung, mung bean, munggo]</p><p><b>100 mongova jednako je 1 tugriku u Mongoliji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> 100 mongo equal 1 tugrik in Mongolia</p><p><b>Mongol, Mongolka, mongolski jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the nomadic peoples of Mongolia [Mongolian]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the region of Mongolia or its people or their languages or cultures [Mongolian]</p><p><b>carska dinastija Kine od 1279. do 1368. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the imperial dynasty of China from 1279 to 1368 [Yuan, Yuan dynasty]</p><p><b>Tatari</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Mongolian people of central Asia who invaded Russia in the 13th century [Tartar, Tatar]</p><p><b>Mongolija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked socialist republic in central Asia [Mongolian People's Republic, Outer Mongolia]</p><p><i>n.</i> a vast region in Asia including the Mongolian People's Republic and China's Inner Mongolia</p><p><b>član nomadskog naroda Mongolije, jezik iz Altajskog jezika koji se govori u Mongoliji, od ili u vezi s današnjom Mongolijskom Narodnom Republikom, o regiji Mongolije ili njenu narodu ili njihovim jezicima ili kulturama ili o njima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the nomadic peoples of Mongolia [Mongol]</p><p><i>n.</i> a family of Altaic language spoken in Mongolia [Mongolic, Mongolic language]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the modern Mongolian People's Republic</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the region of Mongolia or its people or their languages or cultures [Mongol]</p><p><b>monetarna jedinica u Mongoliji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Mongolia</p><p><b>Mongolija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked socialist republic in central Asia [Mongolia, Outer Mongolia]</p><p><b>urođeni poremećaj uzrokovan dodatnim 21. hromozomom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a congenital disorder caused by having an extra 21st chromosome [Down's syndrome, Down syndrome, mongolism, trisomy 21]</p><p><b>Mongol, Mongolka, mongolski jezik (od &quot;mongol&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of Altaic language spoken in Mongolia [Mongolian, Mongolic language]</p><p><b>jezik iz Altajskog jezika koji se govori u Mongoliji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of Altaic language spoken in Mongolia [Mongolian, Mongolic]</p><p><b>urođeni poremećaj uzrokovan dodatnim 21. hromozomom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a congenital disorder caused by having an extra 21st chromosome [Down's syndrome, Down syndrome, mongolianism, trisomy 21]</p><p><b>član obitelji Mongoloid, osoba koja pati od Downovog sindroma (više se tehnički ne koristi u tom smislu, sada se smatra uvredljivom), karakterističan za ili sličan mongolskom, od ili koje se odnose na ili karakteristične za jednu od tradicionalnih rasnih podjela čovječanstva uključujući posebno narode srednje i istočne Azije, (oštar) ili povezan s ili pati od Downovog sindroma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Mongoloid family</p><p><i>n.</i> a person suffering from Down syndrome (no longer used technically in this sense, now considered offensive)</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of or resembling a Mongol</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or characteristic of one of the traditional racial division of humankind including especially peoples of central and eastern Asia</p><p><i>adj.</i> (offensive) of or relating to or suffering from Down syndrome</p><p><b>mješanac, melez, pas, pas mješanac, đukac, đukela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> derogatory term for a variation that is not genuine [bastard]</p><p><i>n.</i> an inferior dog or one of mixed breed [cur, mutt]</p><p><b>Zbog toga sam postao mesarica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become a mongrel [mongrelize]</p><p><b>Zbog toga sam postao mesarica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become a mongrel [mongrelise]</p><p><b>polinom u jednoj varijabli (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a polynomial in one variable</p><p><b>Teniserka iz Sjedinjenih Država (rođena u Jugoslaviji 1973.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States tennis player (born in Yugoslavia in 1973) [Seles]</p><p><b>na temelju ili proizlaze iz posjedovanja novca ili bogatstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> based on or arising from the possession of money or wealth [moneyed]</p><p><b>nadimak, cognomen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a familiar name for a person (often a shortened version of a person's given name) [byname, cognomen, nickname, sobriquet, soubriquet]</p><p><b>bilo koja od gljiva iz roda Monilia s sličnim kvascima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the yeastlike imperfect fungi of the genus Monilia</p><p><b>parazitska gljiva koja može zaraziti usta ili kožu ili crijeva ili vaginu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a parasitic fungus that can infect the mouth or the skin or the intestines or the vagina [Candida albicans]</p><p><b>infekcija uzrokovana gljivicama iz roda Monilia ili Candida (posebno Candida albicans) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infection caused by fungi of the genus Monilia or Candida (especially Candida albicans) [candidiasis, moniliasis]</p><p><b>obitelj nesavršenih gljiva s bijelim ili svijetlom bojama hifa i spore koje se proizvode i