dogen, liliopsid, monocotyledon]</p><p><b>porodica jednosupnica, porodica liliopsida, porodica monokotiledona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of flowering plants having a single cotyledon (embryonic leaf) in the seed [liliopsid family]</p><p><b>rod jednosupnica, rod liliopsida, rod monokotiledona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of flowering plants having a single cotyledon (embryonic leaf) in the seed [liliopsid genus]</p><p><b>biljka s jednokotilnom biljkom s cvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monocotyledonous flowering plant [endogen, liliopsid, monocot]</p><p><b>s sadržajem sjemena koje proizvode embrion s jednim kotiledom i lištima s paralelnim žilama: uključuje travnjake i lilije te palme i orhideje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comprising seed plants that produce an embryo with a single cotyledon and parallel-veined leaves: includes grasses and lilies and palms and orchids [Liliopsida, Monocotyledones, class Liliopsida, class Monocotyledonae, class Monocotyledones]</p><p><b>s sadržajem sjemena koje proizvode embrion s jednim kotiledom i lištima s paralelnim žilama: uključuje travnjake i lilije te palme i orhideje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comprising seed plants that produce an embryo with a single cotyledon and parallel-veined leaves: includes grasses and lilies and palms and orchids [Liliopsida, Monocotyledonae, class Liliopsida, class Monocotyledonae, class Monocotyledones]</p><p><b>U zrnu je samo jedno zrno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a flowering plant) having a single cotyledon in the seed as in grasses and lilies</p><p><b>monokracija, autoritarizam, despotizam, diktatura, staljinizam, totalitarizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of government in which the ruler is an absolute dictator (not restricted by a constitution or laws or opposition etc.) [Caesarism, Stalinism, absolutism, authoritarianism, despotism, dictatorship, one-man rule, shogunate, totalitarianism, tyranny]</p><p><b>vid samo jednim okom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vision with only one eye</p><p><b>monokultura</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cultivation of a single crop (on a farm or area or country)</p><p><b>S jednim kotačem koji se pokreće pedalima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vehicle with a single wheel that is driven by pedals [unicycle]</p><p><b>vrsta granularnih leukocita koji djeluju u gutanju bakterija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a type of granular leukocyte that functions in the ingestion of bacteria</p><p><b>leukemija koju karakteriše proliferacija monocita i monoblasta u krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leukemia characterized by the proliferation of monocytes and monoblasts in the blood [histiocytic leukaemia, histiocytic leukemia, monoblastic leukaemia, monoblastic leukemia, monocytic leukemia]</p><p><b>leukemija koju karakteriše proliferacija monocita i monoblasta u krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leukemia characterized by the proliferation of monocytes and monoblasts in the blood [histiocytic leukaemia, histiocytic leukemia, monoblastic leukaemia, monoblastic leukemia, monocytic leukaemia]</p><p><b>povećanje broja monocita u krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> increase in the number of monocytes in the blood</p><p><b>Francuski biohemičar koji je (s Francois Jacobom) objasnio kako se geni aktiviraju i sugerirao postojanje RNA-a glasnika (1910-1976) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French biochemist who (with Francois Jacob) explained how genes are activated and suggested the existence of messenger RNA (1910-1976) [Jacques Lucien Monod, Jacques Monod]</p><p><b>s jednim glasnim dijelom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a single vocal part [monodical]</p><p><b>s jednim glasnim dijelom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a single vocal part [monodic]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Monodontidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Monodontidae [genus Monodon]</p><p><b>Mali arktički kit mužjak s dugim spiralnim slonovačkim kljupom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Arctic whale the male having a long spiral ivory tusk [narwal, narwhal, narwhale]</p><p><b>Narvali (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> narwhals [family Monodontidae]</p><p><b>glazba koja se sastoji od jednog vokalnog dijela (obično s pratnjom) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> music consisting of a single vocal part (usually with accompaniment) [monophonic music, monophony]</p><p><b>koji imaju muške i ženske reproduktivne organe u istoj biljci ili životinji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having male and female reproductive organs in the same plant or animal [monecious, monoicous]</p><p><b>koji imaju jedan estrozni ciklus godišnje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having one estrous cycle per year [monestrous]</p><p><b>sočivo s jednim fokusom koje se koristi nakon operacije katarakte kako bi se osigurao jasan vid na daljinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lens with a single focus that is used after cataract surgery to provide clear distance vision [monofocal lens implant]</p><p><b>sočivo s jednim fokusom koje se koristi nakon operacije katarakte kako bi se osigurao jasan vid na daljinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lens with a single focus that is used after cataract surgery to provide clear distance vision [monofocal IOL]</p><p><b>monogamist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who practices monogamy (one spouse at a time) [monogynist]</p><p><b>monogaman</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of relationships and of individuals) having one mate</p><p><b>monogaman (od &quot;monogamous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice or state of having only one spouse at a time [monogamy]</p><p><b>praksa ili stanje imati samo jednog bračnog druga u isto vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the practice or state of having only one spouse at a time [monogamousness]</p><p><b>spolno razmnožavanje proizvodnjom i oslobađanjem spora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> asexual reproduction by the production and release of spores [sporulation]</p><p><b>za ili u vezi s nasljednim obiljem kojim upravlja jedan par gena (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an inheritable character that is controlled by a single pair of genes</p><p><b>nasljedna bolest koju kontrolira samo jedan par gena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inherited disease controlled by a single pair of genes [monogenic disorder]</p><p><b>nasljedna bolest koju kontrolira samo jedan par gena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inherited disease controlled by a single pair of genes [monogenic disease]</p><p><b>monogamija, monogram</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graphic symbol consisting of 2 or more letters combined (usually your initials)</p><p><b>monografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a detailed and documented treatise on a particular subject</p><p><b>imati jednu glavu ili glavnu ženu u isto vrijeme (zajedno s konkubinama) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having one head or chief wife at a time (along with concubines) [monogynous]</p><p><b>monogamist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who practices monogamy (one spouse at a time) [monogamist]</p><p><b>imati jednu glavu ili glavnu ženu u isto vrijeme (zajedno s konkubinama) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having one head or chief wife at a time (along with concubines) [monogynic]</p><p><b>imati samo jednu ženu u isto vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having only one wife at a time</p><p><b>hibrid proizveden ukrcavanjem roditelja koji su homozigotni osim jednog gena koji ima dva alela (kao u Mendelovim eksperimentima s vrtnim grašakima) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hybrid produced by crossing parents that are homozygous except for a single gene locus that has two alleles (as in Mendel's experiments with garden peas)</p><p><b>hibridizacija koristeći jednu osobinu s dva alela (kao u Mendelovim eksperimentima s vrtnim grašakima) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hybridization using a single trait with two alleles (as in Mendel's experiments with garden peas)</p><p><b>Hidrat koji sadrži jedan molekul vode po molekuli spoja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hydrate that contains one molecule of water per molecule of the compound</p><p><b>koji imaju muške i ženske reproduktivne organe u istoj biljci ili životinji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having male and female reproductive organs in the same plant or animal [monecious, monoecious]</p><p><b>obožavanje jednog boga, ali bez tvrdnje da je jedini bog. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the worship of a single god but without claiming that it is the only god</p><p><b>Osoba koja zna samo jedan jezik., koristeći ili poznajući samo jedan jezik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who knows only one language</p><p><i>adj.</i> using or knowing only one language</p><p><b>na jednorječnom jeziku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a monolingual manner</p><p><b>monolit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a single great stone (often in the form of a column or obelisk)</p><p><b>monolitan, monolitski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> imposing in size or bulk or solidity [massive, monumental]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by massiveness and rigidity and total uniformity</p><p><b>zabavljač koji nastupa sam. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an entertainer who performs alone</p><p><b>monolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> speech you make to yourself [soliloquy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a long utterance by one person (especially one that prevents others from participating in the conversation)</p><p><i>n.</i> a (usually long) dramatic speech by a single actor</p><p><b>Pričaj sa sobom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> talk to oneself [monologuize, soliloquise, soliloquize]</p><p><b>Pričaj sa sobom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> talk to oneself [monologuise, soliloquise, soliloquize]</p><p><b>manija ograničena na jednu stvar ili ideju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mania restricted to one thing or idea [possession]</p><p><b>osoba koja pati od monomanije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person suffering from monomania</p><p><b>Opsednut jednim predmetom ili idejom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> obsessed with a single subject or idea</p><p><b>monomer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a simple compound whose molecules can join together to form polymers</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing one atom of metal in the molecule</p><p><b>rod Formicidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Formicidae [genus Monomorium]</p><p><b>mali sjajan crni mrav (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tiny glossy black ant [little black ant]</p><p><b>mali crveni mrav toplih područja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small red ant of warm regions [pharaoh's ant, pharaoh ant]</p><p><b>od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> consisting of only one morpheme</p><p><b>bilo kakva neuropatija jednog živčanog debla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any neuropathy of a single nerve trunk</p><p><b>rijeka koja izlazi u sjevernoj Zapadnoj Virginiji i teče sjeverno u Pennsylvaniji gdje se spoji s rijecom Allegheny u Pittsburghu kako bi formirala rijeku Ohio (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river that rises in northern West Virginia and flows north into Pennsylvania where it joins the Allegheny River at Pittsburgh to form the Ohio River [Monongahela River]</p><p><b>rijeka koja izlazi u sjevernoj Zapadnoj Virginiji i teče sjeverno u Pennsylvaniji gdje se spoji s rijecom Allegheny u Pittsburghu kako bi formirala rijeku Ohio (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river that rises in northern West Virginia and flows north into Pennsylvania where it joins the Allegheny River at Pittsburgh to form the Ohio River [Monongahela]</p><p><b>s jednim jedrom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having only one nucleus [mononucleate]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjen sustav slobodnih i fiksnih makrofagova dobivenih iz koštane srži (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a widely distributed system of free and fixed macrophages derived from bone marrow [MPS, system of macrophages]</p><p><b>s jednim jedrom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having only one nucleus [mononuclear]</p><p><b>mononukleoza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute disease characterized by fever and swollen lymph nodes and an abnormal increase of mononuclear leucocytes or monocytes in the bloodstream [glandular fever, infectious mononucleosis, kissing disease, mono]</p><p><b>fosili dugonogi veličine puretine pronađeni prije 75 milijuna godina u pustinji Gobi imaju ptičje slične spojene kosti zgloba i kijele grudi i dug rep koji liči na dinosaur. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.