inhabiting mountainous regions</p><p><b>igra na karte španjolskog podrijetla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gambling card game of Spanish origin [four-card monte, three-card monte]</p><p><b>Najviši planinski vrh u Alpama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the highest mountain peak in the Alps [Mont Blanc]</p><p><b>grad i popularno odmaralište u Kneževini Monako (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town and popular resort in the principality of Monaco</p><p><b>Montego Bay</b></p><p><i>n.</i> port and resort city in northwestern Jamaica</p><p><b>Crna Gora, Crne Gore, Crnu Goru</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former country bordering on the Adriatic Sea [Crna Gora]</p><p><b>grad u zapadnoj Kaliforniji južno od San Francisca na poluotoku na južnom kraju zaljeva Monterey (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in western California to the south of San Francisco on a peninsula at the southern end of Monterey Bay</p><p><b>Uliv u Pacifiku u zapadnoj Kaliforniji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inlet of the Pacific Ocean in western California</p><p><b>visoki kalifornijski cipres endemičan u zaljevu Monterey (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall California cypress endemic on Monterey Bay [Cupressus macrocarpa]</p><p><b>visoki kalifornijski bor s dugim iglama u grmovima od tri, gusto krunčanik i tamno smeđa duboko rascjepkana kora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall California pine with long needles in bunches of 3, a dense crown, and dark brown deeply fissured bark [Pinus radiata]</p><p><b>Monterrey</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industrial city in northeastern Mexico</p><p><b>Francuska plemićkinja koja je bila ljubavnica Luja XIV. dok ga nije privukla Madame de Maintenon (1641-1707) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French noblewoman who was mistress to Louis XIV until he became attracted to Madame de Maintenon (1641-1707) [Francoise-Athenais de Rochechouart, Marquise de Montespan]</p><p><b>Francuski politički filozof koji je zagovarao odvajanje izvršne i zakonodavne i sudske vlasti (1689-1755) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French political philosopher w