t Greece near the Aegean coast [Mt. Olympus, Olimbos, Olympus]</p><p><b>ugasli vulkan u južnom Meksiku između Mexico Cityja i Veracruza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extinct volcano in southern Mexico between Mexico City and Veracruz [Citlaltepetl, Mt Orizaba, Pico de Orizaba]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) planina u središnjoj Grčkoj gdje su (prema grčkoj mitologiji) živjele Muze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) a mountain in central Greece where (according to Greek mythology) the Muses lived [Liakoura, Parnassus]</p><p><b>vulkan na Luzonu sjeverozapadno od Manile (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a volcano on Luzon to the northwest of Manila [Pinatubo]</p><p><b>planinski vrh u središnjem Washingtonu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain peak in central Washington [Mount Tacoma, Mt. Rainier, Rainier]</p><p><b>Nacionalni park Mount Rainier</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a national park in Washington having mountain terrain featuring glaciers and alpine lakes and streams and swamps</p><p><b>planina u Black Hills u Južnoj Dakoti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain in the Black Hills of South Dakota [Mt. Rushmore, Rushmore]</p><p><b>država u sjeverno-srednjem dijelu Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in north central United States [Coyote State, S.D., SD, South Dakota]</p><p><b>aktivni vulkan u Cascade Rangeu u jugozapadnom Washingtonu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an active volcano in the Cascade Range in southwestern Washington [Mount St. Helens, Mt. St. Helens]</p><p><b>vulkanski planinski vrh u Cascade Rangeu u sjevernoj Kaliforniji (visina 14.162 stopa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a volcanic mountain peak in the Cascade Range in northern California (14,162 feet high) [Shasta]</p><p><b>vrh u Skaljastim planinama u središnjem Koloradu (14.036 stopa visine) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a peak in the Rocky Mountains in central Colorado (14,036 feet high) [Sherman]</p><p><b>planinski vrh na južnom Sinajskom poluostrvu (visina 7.500 stopa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain peak in the southern Sinai Peninsula (7,500 feet high) [Sinai]</p><p><b>aktivni vulkan u Cascade Rangeu u jugozapadnom Washingtonu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an active volcano in the Cascade Range in southwestern Washington [Mount Saint Helens, Mt. St. Helens]</p><p><b>planinski vrh u središnjem Washingtonu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain peak in central Washington [Mount Rainier, Mt. Rainier, Rainier]</p><p><b>uzjahati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> get up on the back of [bestride, climb on, get on, hop on, jump on, mount]</p><p><b>Bivša rezidencija Georgea Washingtona u sjeveroistočnoj Virginiji s pogledom na rijeku Potomac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the former residence of George Washington in northeastern Virginia overlooking the Potomac river</p><p><b>vulkan u jugozapadnoj Italiji na obali Mediterana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a volcano in southwestern Italy on the Mediterranean coast [Mt. Vesuvius, Vesuvius]</p><p><b>Najviši vrh u Sierra Nevada niz u Kaliforniji (14,494 stopa visine) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the highest peak in the Sierra Nevada range in California (14,494 feet high) [Whitney]</p><p><b>vrh u planinama San Juan u Coloradu (visina 14.246 stopa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a peak in the San Juan mountains of Colorado (14,246 feet high) [Wilson]</p><p><b>brdo, brdski, gora, gorski, planina, planinski, brdske, gori, gorske, goru, gomila, hrpa, hrpetina, masa, mnoštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a land mass that projects well above its surroundings [mount]</p><p><i>n.</i> (often followed by `of') a large number or amount or extent [batch, deal, flock, good deal, great deal, hatful, heap, lot, mass, mess, mickle, mint, muckle, passel, peck, pile, plenty, pot, quite a little, raft, sight, slew, spate, stack, tidy sum, wad]</p><p><b>mala grmljava klovna iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike, stablo zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrubby maple of eastern North America [Acer spicatum, mountain maple]</p><p><i>n.</i> tree of western United States [Alnus rhombifolia, white alder]</p><p><b>dekoratni zimzeleni grm iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s malim bijelim cvjetovima u obliku zvona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental evergreen shrub of southeastern United States having small white bell-shaped flowers [Pieris floribunda, fetterbush, mountain fetterbush]</p><p><b>biljka s svilovitim lišćama iz Skalnih planina s plavo-bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> silky-foliaged herb of the Rocky Mountains with bluish-white flowers [Alpine anemone, Anemone tetonensis]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta drveća iz roda Sorbus, drvo koje ima drvo slično alpskom pepelju, nisko rastući pepeo Teksasa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various trees of the genus Sorbus</p><p><i>n.</i> tree having wood similar to the alpine ash [Eucalyptus regnans]</p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing ash of Texas [Fraxinus texensis]</p><p><b>puževi sa velikim bijelim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creeping evergreen shrub with large white flowers [Dryas octopetala]</p><p><b>špilja koja se kreće i stvara podloge, uvijekzelena grmlja u visokim planinskim područjima sjeverne hemisfere, uzgajana zbog svojih ružičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creeping mat-forming evergreen shrub of high mountain regions of northern hemisphere grown for its rose-pink flowers [Loiseleuria procumbens, alpine azalea]</p><p><b>Noćni glodari na pacifičkoj obali Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bulky nocturnal burrowing rodent of uplands of the Pacific coast of North America [Aplodontia rufa, sewellel]</p><p><b>brdski bicikl</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bicycle with a sturdy frame and fat tires [all-terrain bike, off-roader]</p><p><b>brda zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država slična papirnati brdi ali s smeđom kore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> birch of western United States resembling the paper birch but having brownish bark [Betula fontinalis, Western birch, Western paper birch, swamp birch, water birch]</p><p><b>velika bezopasna sjajna crna sjevernoamerička zmija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large harmless shiny black North American snake [Elaphe obsoleta, black rat snake, blacksnake, pilot blacksnake]</p><p><b>Cystopteris montana, brdska papratka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fern of rocky mountainous areas of hemisphere [Cystopteris montana]</p><p><b>Bliznica iz zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s pojedinačnim cvijećem i pomalo kislim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect blueberry of western United States having solitary flowers and somewhat sour berries [Viccinium membranaceum, bilberry, thin-leaved bilberry]</p><p><b>zelena biljka s malim bijelim cvijećem i crvenim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen mat-forming shrub of North America and northern Eurasia having small white flowers and red berries [Arctostaphylos uva-ursi, bear's grape, common bearberry, creashak, hog cranberry, mealberry, red bearberry, sand berry, sandberry, wild cranberry]</p><p><b>gorje, planinski lanac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a series of hills or mountains [chain, chain of mountains, mountain range, range, range of mountains]</p><p><b>glodari porijeklom iz planina Čilea i Perua, a sada uzgajani u zatočeništvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rodent native to the mountains of Chile and Peru and now bred in captivity [mountain viscacha]</p><p><b>planinari sjeveroistočne Sjeverne Amerike koji imaju voskani ljubičasto-plavi cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> climber of northeastern North America having waxy purplish-blue flowers [Clematis verticillaris, purple clematis, purple virgin's bower]</p><p><b>planinar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who climbs mountains [mountaineer]</p><p><b>alpinizam, planinarenja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of climbing a mountain [mountaineering]</p><p><b>Sjeverne Europe i Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of northern Europe and America [Lycopodium selago, fir clubmoss, little clubmoss]</p><p><b>nizak zimzelena stabla u visokim sjevernim umjerenim područjima Europe i Azije i Amerike koja nose crvene jestive bobice, Crvene bobice slične američkim brusnicama, ali manje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low evergreen shrub of high north temperate regions of Europe and Asia and America bearing red edible berries [Vaccinium vitis-idaea, cowberry, foxberry, lingberry, lingenberry, lingonberry]</p><p><i>n.</i> tart red berries similar to American cranberries but smaller [cowberry, lingonberry, lowbush cranberry]</p><p><b>Borealna ili alpska pijesna biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> boreal or alpine sandwort [Arenaria groenlandica, mountain sandwort, mountain starwort]</p><p><b>U istočnoj Australiji postoji čvrsta grmljavina s krajnjim grmljavinama crvenih cvijeća koji daju mnogo nektara., pustinjski gušter koji se hrani mravima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect bushy shrub of eastern Australia having terminal clusters of red flowers yielding much nectar [Lambertia formosa, honey-flower, honeyflower]</p><p><i>n.</i> desert lizard that feeds on ants [Moloch horridus, spiny lizard]</p><p><b>malo istočnoindijsko stablo s cvjetovima nalik orhideji i tvrdim tamnim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small East Indian tree having orchid-like flowers and hard dark wood [Bauhinia variegata, orchid tree]</p><p><b>različita vrsta mačje noge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of cat's foot</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve proizvode koji sadrže: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common European mountain fern having fragrant lemon or balsam scented fronds [Dryopteris oreopteris, Oreopteris limbosperma]</p><p><b>dekoratni zimzeleni grm iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s malim bijelim cvjetovima u obliku zvona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental evergreen shrub of southeastern United States having small white bell-shaped flowers [Pieris floribunda, fetterbush, mountain andromeda]</p><p><b>uzrokovane reketsijalnim bakterijama i prenose se drvenim krpeljima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> caused by rickettsial bacteria and transmitted by wood ticks [Rocky Mountain spotted fever, tick fever]</p><p><b>lišćavi divlji cvijet s lavandrovom-ružičastim cvijećem koji se otvara uvečer i ostaje kroz hladni dio sljedećeg dana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leafy wildflower with lavender-pink flowers that open in the evening and remain through cool part of the next day [Mirabilis oblongifolia]</p><p><b>Smatra se da je to životinja koja živi u planinskom dijelu sjeverozapadne Sjeverne Amerike. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sure-footed mammal of mountainous northwestern North America [Oreamnos americanus, Rocky Mountain goat]</p><p><b>planinski gorila</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gorilla of Kivu highlands [Gorilla gorilla beringei]</p><p><b>dekoratni zimzeleni grm s pacifičke obale Sjeverne Amerike s tamno zelenim pinnatnim listovima i žutim cvjetovima s plavo-crnim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental evergreen shrub of Pacific coast of North America having dark green pinnate leaves and racemes of yellow flowers followed by blue-black berries [Mahonia aquifolium, Oregon grape, Oregon holly grape, holly-leaves barberry, hollygrape]</p><p><b>mali grm s sitnim večnozelenim lišćama i ružičastim ili ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrub with tiny evergreen leaves and pink or purple flowers [Bryanthus taxifolius, Phyllodoce caerulea]</p><p><b>velika zimzelena stabla zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large evergreen of western United States [Tsuga mertensiana, black hemlock]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka iz sjeverozapadne Sjedinjenih Država i zapadne Kanade koja liči na štap i ima bijele ili ružičaste cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of northwestern United States and western Canada resembling a hollyhock and having white or pink flowers [Iliamna acerifolia, Iliamna ruvularis]</p><p><b>listovita biljka s nekoliko stabljika u gomili s 1 bijelom i tupom ljubičastim cvijetom u svakoj gornjoj oslozi lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leafy plant having a few stems in a clump with 1 white and dull purple flower in each upper leaf axil [Cypripedium montanum]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički zimzeleni grm s sjajnim lišćama i bijelim ili ružičastim cvijećem, Drvo na pacifičkoj obali koje ima aromatično lišće i male cvjetove u obliku umbellata, a zatim plodove nalik maslinima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a North American evergreen shrub having glossy leaves and white or rose-colored flowers [American laurel, Kalmia latifolia, calico bush, wood laurel]</p><p><i>n.</i> Pacific coast tree having aromatic foliage and small umbellate flowers followed by olivelike fruit [California bay tree, California laurel, California olive, Oregon myrtle, Umbellularia californica, pepperwood, sassafras laurel, spice tree]</p><p><b>Japanski lilij sa zlatnim zrake, Bjelokvetna višegodišnja biljka iz Novog Zelanda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Japanese lily with golden rays [Lilium auratum]</p><p><i>n.</i> showy white-flowered perennial of New Zealand [Mount Cook lily, Ranunculus lyalii]</p><p><b>Felis concolor, kuguar, puma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large American feline resembling a lion [Felis concolor, catamount, cougar, painter, panther, puma]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fern of the genus Dryopteris [Dryopteris oreades]</p><p><b>Čovjek koji živi na granici. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who lives on the frontier [backwoodsman, frontiersman]</p><p><b>mala grmljava klovna iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrubby maple of eastern North America [Acer spicatum, mountain alder]</p><p><b>Svaka od višegodišnjih biljaka iz roda Pycnanthemum (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a number of perennial herbs of the genus Pycnanthemum</p><p><b>Antilope iz Etiopije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shaggy antelope of mountains of Ethiopia [Tragelaphus buxtoni]</p><p><b>Visoko drvo s tvrdim, teškim, ružičastim ili svjetlo smeđim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall timber tree with hard heavy pinkish or light brown wood [Eucalyptus delegatensis, alpine ash]</p><p><b>Grozljivci planinskih područja zapadne Južne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rodent of mountains of western South America</p><p><b>Europski i Mala azijski paprikac s kratkim tankim korenom i gusto tuftiranim svijetlo zelenim lišćama nalik petrašlju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fern of Europe and Asia Minor having short slender rhizome and densely tufted bright green fronds resembling parsley [Cryptogramma crispa, European parsley fern]</p><p><b>Kaliforniačka perutica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> California partridge [Oreortyx picta palmeri, mountain quail]</p><p><b>klanac, planinski prijevoj, prevoj, prijevoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the location in a range of mountains of a geological formation that is lower than the surrounding peaks [notch, pass]</p><p><b>Vrh planine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the summit of a mountain</p><p><b>Brojni biljci (Pinus spp.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low tufted perennial phlox with needlelike evergreen leaves and pink or white flowers [Phlox subulata, dwarf phlox, moss phlox, moss pink]</p><p><b>zeleno stablo iz Novog Zelanda slično kawaka, visoki bor zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s čvrstima plavo-zelenim iglama, nizak grmasti bor srednje Europe s kratkim svijetlo zelenim iglama u grmovima po dvije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen tree of New Zealand resembling the kawaka [Libocedrus bidwillii, pahautea]</p><p><i>n.</i> tall pine of western North America with stout blue-green needles [Pinus monticola, silver pine, western white pine]</p><p><i>n.</i> low shrubby pine of central Europe with short bright green needles in bunches of two [Pinus mugo, Swiss mountain pine, dwarf mountain pine, mugho pine, mugo pine]</p><p><b>biljka koja stvara podloge s tamno ružičastim cvijećima na kratkim uspravnim listnim stabljikama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mat-forming plant with deep pink flowers on short erect leafy stems [Penstemon newberryi]</p><p><b>Kaliforniačka perutica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> California partridge [Oreortyx picta palmeri, mountain partridge]</p><p><b>gorje, planinski lanac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a series of hills or mountains [chain, chain of mountains, mountain chain, range, range of mountains]</p><p><b>vrijedna pasmina za krmljenje suhih planinskih područja i ravnica zapadne Sjeverne Amerike do sjevernog Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> valuable forage grass of dry upland areas and plains of western North America to northern Mexico [Indian millet, Oryzopsis hymenoides, silk grass, silkgrass]</p><p><b>Šumovi od niskog do prostranog rasta s tankim granama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing to prostrate shrub with slender trailing branches [Dacridium laxifolius, Lepidothamnus laxifolius]</p><p><b>Europska alpska ruža s crvenokrasnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European alpine rose with crimson flowers [Rosa pendulina]</p><p><b>Borealna ili alpska pijesna biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> boreal or alpine sandwort [Arenaria groenlandica, mountain daisy, mountain starwort]</p><p><b>sve divlje ovce koje žive u planinskim područjima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any wild sheep inhabiting mountainous regions</p><p><b>mučnina i problema s disanjem kod planinara iznad 10.000 stopa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nausea and shortness of breath experienced by mountain climbers above ten thousand feet</p><p><b>Često živi u hrastovitim i borovim staništima u stjenovitim planinskim područjima jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> frequents oak and pine habitats in rocky mountainous areas of United States southwest and Mexico [Eumeces callicephalus]</p><p><b>Azijska biljka slična špinatu koja se često koristi kao biljka za liječenje bolesti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic plant resembling spinach often used as a potherb [Atriplex hortensis, garden orache]</p><p><b>slijepoce iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spleenwort of eastern North America [Asplenium montanum]</p><p><b>standardno vrijeme u 7. vremenskoj zoni zapadno od Greenwicha, izračunato na 105. meridijanu zapadno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> standard time in the 7th time zone west of Greenwich, reckoned at the 105th meridian west [MST, Mountain Time]</p><p><b>