.</i> mat-forming perennial found in cold springs of the eastern United States [American watercress, Cardamine rotundifolia]</p><p><b>usko-pristapljena skoro izumrla zebra južne Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> narrow-striped nearly extinct zebra of southern Africa [Equus zebra zebra]</p><p><b>alpinist, alpinista, brđanin, gorštak, planinac, planinar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who climbs mountains [mountain climber]</p><p><i>v.</i> climb mountains for pleasure as a sport</p><p><b>planinarenje, planinarstvo, planiranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of climbing a mountain [mountain climbing]</p><p><b>brdovit, gorovit, planinski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having hills and crags [cragged, craggy, hilly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> like a mountain in size and impressiveness</p><p><i>adj.</i> containing many mountains</p><p><b>stranica ili pad planine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the side or slope of a mountain [versant]</p><p><b>šarlatan, varalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flamboyant deceiver [charlatan]</p><p><b>montirana, na konju, namješten, pripremljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> assembled for use</p><p><i>adj.</i> decorated with applied ornamentation</p><p><b>brdo, brežuljak, dizati se, gora, gore, jahaći konj, mijenjati se, montiranje, montirati, namještenje, okov, okvir, organizirati, planina, popeti, popeti se, postaviti, postolje, povisivati se, udesiti, uzdići se, uzjahati, uzvišenje (od &quot;mount&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skilled worker who mounts pictures or jewels etc.</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who ascends on foot [climber]</p><p><b>kolokvijalni izraz za člana Kraljevske kanadske konjske policije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> colloquial term for a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police</p><p><b>savezna policija Kanade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the federal police force of Canada [RCMP, Royal Canadian Mounted Police]</p><p><b>montaža, montiranje, namještenje, ugradnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that involves rising to a higher point (as in altitude or temperature or intensity etc.)