iti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> water soaked soil [clay]</p><p><i>n.</i> slanderous remarks or charges</p><p><i>v.</i> soil with mud, muck, or mire [mire, muck, muck up]</p><p><i>v.</i> plaster with mud</p><p><b>kupanje u toplom blatu (kao kod reuma) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bath in warm mud (as for treating rheumatism)</p><p><b>cigla napravljena od pečene blatine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brick made from baked mud</p><p><b>ospe koja gradi blate stanice na čvrstom podnožju u koje ženke polažu jaja položena u paralizirane ličinke insekata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wasp that constructs mud cells on a solid base in which females place eggs laid in paralyzed insect larvae</p><p><b>radnik koji kopa jarke. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a laborer who digs ditches [ditch digger]</p><p><b>područje nisko blatnjaste zemlje u blizini estuara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tract of low muddy land near an estuary</p><p><b>ptica koja se nalazi u Sjevernoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coot found in North America [American coot, Fulica americana, marsh hen, water hen]</p><p><b>s uskim ravnim, srpnim, potopljenim lišćama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having narrow flat sickle-shaped submerged fronds [Wolffiella gladiata, bogmat]</p><p><b>mase blata koju je dijete oblikovalo u oblik pite (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mass of mud that a child has molded into the shape of pie</p><p><b>vodena biljka s žutim cvijećem u obliku zvijezde (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grassy-leaved North American aquatic plant with yellow star-shaped blossoms [Heteranthera dubia, water star grass]</p><p><b>-Bodina blato. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a puddle of mud</p><p><b>vodeni sjevernoamerički salamander s crvenim perjenim vanjskim žlijezdelima, Veliki salamander sjevernoameričkih rijeka i potoka, larva salamandra iz planinskih jezera Meksika koja obično živi bez metamorfoze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aquatic North American salamander with red feathery external gills [Necturus maculosus]</p><p><i>n.</i> large salamander of North American rivers and streams [Cryptobranchus alleganiensis, hellbender]</p><p><i>n.</i> larval salamander of mountain lakes of Mexico that usually lives without metamorphosing [Ambystoma mexicanum, axolotl]</p><p><b>mrlja koju stvara blat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stain produced by mud</p><p><b>slatkovodna kornjača koja živi na dnu blatnih rijeka Sjeverne i Srednje Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bottom-dwelling freshwater turtle inhabiting muddy rivers of North America and Central America</p><p><b>prekrivena blatom ili kao da je blatna (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with or as if with mud</p><p><b>od ili sa udioom blatnih cigla (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or incorporating mud bricks</p><p><b>Borba u blatu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> wrestle in mud [mudwrestle]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za proizvode iz kategorije II., veliki sumak iz središnje Sjedinjene Države s ravnom glavom i izbočenom vilicom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flesh of scaleless food fish of the southern United States [catfish]</p><p><i>n.</i> large catfish of central United States having a flattened head and projecting jaw [Pylodictus olivaris, flathead catfish, goujon, shovelnose catfish, spoonbill catfish]</p><p><b>trkački konj koji dobro trči na blatnom trkačkom stazi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a racehorse that runs well on a muddy racetrack</p><p><b>blatan, blatno, blatnjav, mutan, pomućen, prljav, promukao, zablatiti, zamrljan, zamućen (od &quot;muddy&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of color) discolored by impurities [dingy, dirty, muddy]</p><p><b>Vlažnost tla prekrivenog ili natopljenog vodom, mentalno stanje koje se karakterizira nedostatkom jasnih i uređenih misli i ponašanja, kvaliteta toga što je maglovito. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the wetness of ground that is covered or soaked with water [sloppiness, wateriness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mental state characterized by a lack of clear and orderly thought and behavior [confusedness, confusion, disarray, mental confusion]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being cloudy [cloudiness, murkiness]</p><p><b>nered, pobrkati, smutiti, zbrka, zbrkati, stiska, škripac, brčkati, zabuniti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a confused multitude of things [clutter, fuddle, jumble, mare's nest, smother, welter]</p><p><i>n.</i> informal terms for a difficult situation [fix, hole, jam, kettle of fish, mess, pickle]</p><p><i>v.</i> make into a puddle [puddle]</p><p><i>v.</i> mix up or confuse [addle, puddle]</p><p><b>zbunjen i nejasan. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> confused and vague [addled, befuddled, muzzy, woolly, woolly-headed, wooly, wooly-minded]</p><p><b>Glupi i zbunjeni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> stupid and confused [addlebrained, addlepated, puddingheaded]</p><p><b>blatan, blatno, blatnjav, mutan, pomućen, prljav, promukao, zablatiti, zamrljan, zamućen, močvaran</b></p><p><i>v.</i> dirty with mud [muddy up]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become muddy</p><p><i>v.</i> make turbid</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of soil) soft and watery [boggy, marshy, miry, mucky, quaggy, sloppy, sloughy, soggy, squashy, swampy, waterlogged]</p><p><i>adj.</i> dirty and messy [mucky]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of color) discolored by impurities [dingy, dirty, muddied]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of liquids) clouded as with sediment [cloudy, mirky, murky, turbid]</p><p><b>Prljavo od blata. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> dirty with mud [muddy]</p><p><b>blatobran</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a curved piece above the wheel of a bicycle or motorcycle to protect the rider from water or mud thrown up by the wheels [splash-guard, splash guard]</p><p><b>Špilja od trske u močvarnim područjima Iraka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reed hut in the marshlands of Iraq</p><p><b>rituala pokret ruke u hinduističkom religijskom plesu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ritual hand movement in Hindu religious dancing</p><p><b>nalazi se u tropskim obalnim područjima Afrike i Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found in tropical coastal regions of Africa and Asia [mudspringer]</p><p><b>klizište blato (MT)</b></p><