<b>mračan, mrak, tama, magla</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an atmosphere in which visibility is reduced because of a cloud of some substance [fog, fogginess, murkiness]</p><p><i>v.</i> make dark, dim, or gloomy</p><p><b>mračan, sumoran, taman (od &quot;murky&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> unclearly</p><p><i>adv.</i> with a dim light [dimly]</p><p><b>magla</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an atmosphere in which visibility is reduced because of a cloud of some substance [fog, fogginess, murk]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being cloudy [cloudiness, muddiness]</p><p><b>mračan, sumoran, taman</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of liquids) clouded as with sediment [cloudy, mirky, muddy, turbid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> dark or gloomy [mirky]</p><p><b>lučki grad na sjeverozapadu Rusije na poluotoku Kola. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port city in northwestern Russia on the Kola Peninsula</p><p><b>buniti se, gunđati, prigušeni glasovi, romorenje, šapat, šum, šuštati, zujanje, žamoriti, žuborenje, žuboriti, gunđanje, mrgođenje, mrmljati, mrmoriti, promrmljati, šaptati, kreketati, prigovarati, progunđati, zanovijetati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a low continuous indistinct sound [murmuration, murmuring, mussitation, mutter, muttering]</p><p><i>n.</i> a schwa that is incidental to the pronunciation of a consonant [murmur vowel]</p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal sound of the heart [cardiac murmur, heart murmur]</p><p><i>n.</i> a complaint uttered in a low and indistinct tone [grumble, grumbling, murmuring, mutter, muttering]</p><p><i>v.</i> speak softly or indistinctly</p><p><i>v.</i> make complaining remarks or noises under one's breath [croak, gnarl, grumble, mutter]</p><p><b>šva koja je sporedna izgovoru konsonanta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a schwa that is incidental to the pronunciation of a consonant [murmur]</p><p><b>Niska neprekidna nejasna zvuk (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a low continuous indistinct sound [murmur, murmuring, mussitation, mutter, muttering]</p><p><b>buniti se, gunđati, prigušeni glasovi, romorenje, šapat, šum, šuštati, zujanje, žamoriti, žuborenje, žuboriti (od &quot;murmur&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who speaks softly and indistinctly [mumbler, mutterer]</p><p><b>gunđanje, mrgođenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a low continuous indistinct sound [murmur, murmuration, mussitation, mutter, muttering]</p><p><i>n.</i> a complaint uttered in a low and indistinct tone [grumble, grumbling, murmur, mutter, muttering]</p><p><i>adj.</i> making a low continuous indistinct sound [susurrant, whispering]</p><p><b>karakterizira se blažim zvukovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by soft sounds [rustling, soughing, susurrous]</p><p><b>superplemena glodavca u biti jednaka podredu Myomorpha ali isključuje Dipodidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a superfamily of rodents essentially equal to the suborder Myomorpha but with the Dipodidae excluded [superfamily Muroidea]</p><p><b>Urođenica Južne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edible tuber native to South America [Irish potato, potato, spud, tater, white potato]</p><p><b>krevet koji se može savijati ili zamahnuti u ormarić kada se ne koristi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bed that can be folded or swung into a cabinet when not being used</p><p><b>Humoristički aksiom koji kaže da sve što može poći po zlu poći će po zlu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> humorous axiom stating that anything that can go wrong will go wrong [Sod's Law]</p><p><b>bilo koja bolest kućnih životinja koja liči na kugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any disease of domestic animals that resembles a plague</p><p><b>Britanski klasičar (rođen u Australiji) koji je zagovarao Društvo naroda i Ujedinjene nacije (1866-1957), Škotski filolog i leksikograf koji je oblikovao Oxford English Dictionary (1837-1915), južnoistočna rijeka Australije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British classical scholar (born in Australia) who advocated the League of Nations and the United Nations (1866-1957) [George Gilbert Aime Murphy, Gilbert Murray]</p><p><i>n.</i> Scottish philologist and the lexicographer who shaped the 