ering from mysophobia</p><p><b>grad u južnoj Indiji jugozapadno od Bangalorea, država u južnoj Indiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in southern India to the southwest of Bangalore</p><p><i>n.</i> state in southern India [Karnataka]</p><p><b>Širi se trnasti grm tropske Azije s velikim uspravnim cvjetovima žutih cvjetova s crvenim znakovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spreading thorny shrub of tropical Asia bearing large erect racemes of red-marked yellow flowers [Caesalpinia decapetala, Caesalpinia sepiaria]</p><p><b>misteriozan, tajanstven, zagonetan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of an obscure nature [cryptic, cryptical, deep, inscrutable, mystifying]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having an import not apparent to the senses nor obvious to the intelligence [mystic, mystical, occult, orphic, secret]</p><p><b>misteriozan, tajanstven, zagonetan (od &quot;mysterious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a cryptic manner [cryptically, enigmatically]</p><p><b>misterij, tajanstvenost, tajna, zagonetka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that baffles understanding and cannot be explained [closed book, enigma, secret]</p><p><i>n.</i> a story about a crime (usually murder) presented as a novel or play or movie [mystery story, whodunit]</p><p><b>roman u kojem je čitatelj izazvan da riješi zagonetku prije nego što ga detektiv objasni na kraju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> novel in which the reader is challenged to solve a puzzle before the detective explains it at the end [detective novel]</p><p><b>srednjovjekovna predstava koja prikazuje epizode iz života Krista. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a medieval play representing episodes from the life of Christ</p><p><b>priča o zločinu (obično ubojstvo) predstavljena kao roman ili predstava ili film (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a story about a crime (usually murder) presented as a novel or play or movie [mystery, whodunit]</p><p><b>mističan, mistik, tajanstven, zagonetan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who believes in the existence of realities beyond human comprehension [religious mystic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having an import not apparent to the senses nor obvious to the intelligence [mysterious, mystical, occult, orphic, secret]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or resembling mysticism [mystical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of mysticism [mystical]</p><p><b>član taoističke Trojstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Taoist Trinity [Ling-pao]</p><p><b>tajnovit, mističan, okultan, tajnovitu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of mysticism [mystic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or resembling mysticism [mystic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having an import not apparent to the senses nor obvious to the intelligence [mysterious, mystic, occult, orphic, secret]</p><p><b>tajnovit, mističan, okultan, tajnovitu (od &quot;mystical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a mystical manner</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> baleen whales: right whales [suborder Mysticeti]</p><p><b>misticizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a religion based on mystical communion with an ultimate reality [religious mysticism]</p><p><i>n.</i> obscure or irrational thought</p><p><b>zbunjivanje, zbunjenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> confusion resulting from failure to understand [bafflement, befuddlement, bemusement, bewilderment, obfuscation, puzzlement]</p><p><i>n.</i> something designed to mystify or bewilder</p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of obscuring people's understanding, leaving them baffled or bewildered [obfuscation]</p><p><b>u zabludi, varati, zaluđivati, zbunjivati (od &quot;mystify&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> totally perplexed and mixed up [metagrabolised, metagrabolized, metagrobolised, metagrobolized]</p><p><b>posebno zbunjujući problem za koji se kaže da ima ispravno rješenje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a particularly baffling problem that is said to have a correct solution [puzzle, puzzler, teaser]</p><p><b>u zabludi, varati, zaluđivati, zbunjivati, frapirati, preneraziti, preneražavati, smesti, smetati, zabezeknuti, zadiviti, zapanjiti, zapanjivati, zaprepastiti, zaprepašćivati, začuditi, zbuniti, zgranjivati, zgranuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be a mystery or bewildering to [amaze, baffle, beat, bewilder, dumbfound, flummox, get, gravel, nonplus, perplex, pose, puzzle, stick, stupefy, vex]</p><p><i>v.</i> make mysterious</p><p><b>u zabludi, varati, zaluđivati, zbunjivati (od &quot;mystify&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of an obscure nature [cryptic, cryptical, deep, inscrutable, mysterious]</p><p><b>aura povišene vrijednosti ili interesa ili značenja koja okružuje osobu ili stvar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an aura of heightened value or interest or meaning surrounding a person or thing</p><p><b>mit, mitska osoba, mitski, priče o bogovima, ritual</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a traditional story accepted as history</p><p><b>mit, mitska osoba, mitski, priče o bogovima, ritual (od &quot;myth&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or having the nature of myth</p><p><i>adj.</i> based on or told of in traditional stories [fabulous, mythical, mythologic, mythological]</p><p><b>izmišljen, mitska, mitski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> based on or told of in traditional stories [fabulous, mythic, mythologic, mythological]</p><p><b>zamišljeno biće iz mitologije ili baike. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary being of myth or fable</p><p><b>čudovište poznato u folkloru i mitovima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monster renowned in folklore and myth [mythical monster]</p><p><b>čudovište poznato u folkloru i mitovima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monster renowned in folklore and myth [mythical creature]</p><p><b>Mjesto koje postoji samo u mašti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a place that exists only in imagination [fictitious place, imaginary place]</p><p><b>interpretirati kao mit ili u smislu mitologije, pretvoriti u mit. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> interpret as a myth or in terms of mythology [mythicize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make into a myth [mythicize, mythologise, mythologize]</p><p><b>interpretirati kao mit ili u smislu mitologije, pretvoriti u mit. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> interpret as a myth or in terms of mythology [mythicise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make into a myth [mythicise, mythologise, mythologize]</p><p><b>zasnovan na ili ispričan u tradicionalnim pričama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> based on or told of in traditional stories [fabulous, mythic, mythical, mythological]</p><p><b>mitske, mitski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> based on or told of in traditional stories [fabulous, mythic, mythical, mythologic]</p><p><b>preispitivanje poruke kao mit. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the restatement of a message as a myth [mythologization]</p><p><b>Izgraditi mit., pretvoriti u mit. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> construct a myth [mythologize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make into a myth [mythicise, mythicize, mythologize]</p><p><b>stručnjak za mitologiju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert on mythology</p><p><b>preispitivanje poruke kao mit. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the restatement of a message as a myth [mythologisation]</p><p><b>Izgraditi mit., pretvoriti u mit. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> construct a myth [mythologise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make into a myth [mythicise, mythicize, mythologise]</p><p><b>mitologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> myths collectively</p><p><i>n.</i> the study of myths</p><p><b>otok u istočnoj Grčkoj u istočnom Egejskom moru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an island of eastern Greece in the eastern Aegean Sea [Lesbos, Lesvos]</p><p><b>morski školjke s tamnom izduženom ljuskom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marine bivalve mollusk having a dark elongated shell [marine mussel]</p><p><b>morske školjke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marine mussels [family Mytilidae]</p><p><b>vrsta rodovi iz obitelji Mytilidae: morske školjke glatke lupine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the family Mytilidae: smooth-shelled marine mussels [genus Mytilus]</p><p><b>školjka sa tamnom ljuskom koja živi vezana za stijene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mussel with a dark shell that lives attached to rocks [edible mussel]</p><p><b>hipotiroidizam obilježen sušom kože i oteklinom oko usan