.</i> either of two phenols derived from naphthalene</p><p><b>vitamin rastvorljiv u mastima koji pomaže u zgrušavanju krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fat-soluble vitamin that helps in the clotting of blood [antihemorrhagic factor, vitamin K]</p><p><b>Škotski matematičar koji je izumio logaritme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Scottish mathematician who invented logarithms [John Napier]</p><p><b>skup razreda šipki koje su ranije koristili za množenje i dijeljenje metodom koju je izumio John Napier (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a set of graduated rods formerly used to do multiplication and division by a method invented by John Napier [Napier's rods]</p><p><b>skup razreda šipki koje su ranije koristili za množenje i dijeljenje metodom koju je izumio John Napier (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a set of graduated rods formerly used to do multiplication and division by a method invented by John Napier [Napier's bones]</p><p><b>logaritam na bazi e (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a logarithm to the base e [natural logarithm]</p><p><b>pelena, pelene, salveta, ubrus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small piece of table linen that is used to wipe the mouth and to cover the lap in order to protect clothing [serviette, table napkin]</p><p><i>n.</i> garment consisting of a folded cloth drawn up between the legs and fastened at the waist [diaper, nappy]</p><p><b>krugli trak koji se koristi za držanje natrpe određene osobe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a circular band used to hold a particular person's napkin</p><p><b>Napulj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port and tourist center in southwestern Italy [Napoli]</p><p><b>Europski luk s bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European onion with white flowers [Allium neopolitanum, daffodil garlic, flowering onion]</p><p><b>napoleonske, Bonaparte, Napoleon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French general who became emperor of the French (1769-1821) [Bonaparte, Little Corporal, Napoleon Bonaparte, Napoleon I]</p><p><i>n.</i> a rectangular piece of pastry with thin flaky layers and filled with custar