b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of neglecting responsibilities and lacking concern [neglect, negligence]</p><p><b>ženski haljinac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loose dressing gown for women [housecoat, negligee, peignoir, wrapper]</p><p><b>ženski haljinac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loose dressing gown for women [housecoat, neglige, peignoir, wrapper]</p><p><b>aljkavost, bezobzirnost, nebriga, nehat, nemar, nemaran, nemarnost, nerad, propust, nehaj, nehajnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> failure to act with the prudence that a reasonable person would exercise under the same circumstances [carelessness, neglect, nonperformance]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of neglecting responsibilities and lacking concern [neglect, neglectfulness]</p><p><b>aljkav, bezbrižan, bezobrazan, nemaran, nepažljiv, neradan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by neglect and undue lack of concern</p><p><b>bezobrazno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a negligent manner</p><p><b>beznačajan, neznatan, zanemariv, beznačajno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> so small as to be meaningless</p><p><i>adj.</i> not worth considering [paltry, trifling]</p><p><b>dogovarati, dogovoriti, pregovarati, sporazumijevati se, sporazumjeti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be successful [bring off, carry off, manage, pull off]</p><p><i>v.</i> sell or discount</p><p><i>v.</i> transfer by endorsement to another in return for value received</p><p><i>v.</i> succeed in passing through, around, or over [negotiate]</p><p><i>v.</i> confer with another in order to come to terms or reach an agreement</p><p><i>v.</i> discuss the terms of an arrangement [negotiate, talk terms]</p><p><b>o kojem se može pregovarati, prenosiv, prodajan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being passed or negotiated</p><p><i>adj.</i> able to be negotiated or arranged by compromise [on the table]</p><p><i>adj.</i> legally transferable to the ownership of another [assignable, conveyable, transferable, transferrable]</p><p><b>prenosivi instrument, prenosivi vrijednosni papir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unconditional order or promise to pay an amount of money</p><p><b>pregovarač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who negotiates (confers with others in order to reach a settlement) [negotiator, treater]</p><p><b>dogovarati, pogađati se, posredovati, pregovarati, pregovora, prenijeti, savlađivati, ugovarati, voditi posao, zaključiti, dogovoriti, sporazumijevati se, sporazumjeti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> discuss the terms of an arrangement [negociate, talk terms]</p><p><i>v.</i> succeed in passing through, around, or over [negociate]</p><p><b>dogovaranje, pregovaranje, pregovaranje (o parametrima veze), pregovori, pretresanje, savlađivan, dijalog, razgovor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a discussion intended to produce an agreement [dialogue, talks]</p><p><i>n.</i> the activity or business of negotiating an agreement</p><p><b>posrednik, pregovarač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who negotiates (confers with others in order to reach a settlement) [negotiant, treater]</p><p><b>Žena pregovarač. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman negotiator [negotiatrix]</p><p><b>Žena pregovarač. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman negotiator [negotiatress]</p><p><b>ideološki stav koji smatra crnu kulturu nezavisnom i valjanu po svojim uvjetima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ideological position that holds Black culture to be independent and valid on its own terms</p><p><b>crn, crnac, crnački</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person with African ancestry, "Negro" and "Negroid" are archaic and pejorative today [African-American, Black, Negroid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having skin rich in melanin pigments [colored, coloured]</p><p><b>tropski grm s okruglim smeđkasto-crvenim bradavičnim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stout spreading or semi-climbing tropical shrub with round brownish-red warty fruit [Sarcocephalus esculentus, Sarcocephalus latifolius]</p><p><b>tropsko zapadnoafričko zimzeleno stablo s žestokim aromatičnim sjemenima koje se koristi kao začin i u narodnoj medicini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical west African evergreen tree bearing pungent aromatic seeds used as a condiment and in folk medicine [Guinea pepper, Xylopia aethiopica]</p><p><b>spiritual</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of religious song originated by Blacks in the southern United States [spiritual]</p><p><b>u obliku vina s dlakavim lišće i tamno ljubičastom crnom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> twining vine with hairy foliage and dark purplish-brown flowers [Vincetoxicum hirsutum, Vincetoxicum negrum]</p><p><b>negroidan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person with African ancestry, "Negro" and "Negroid" are archaic and pejorative today [African-American, Black, Negro]</p><p><b>kuhano vino</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wine and hot water with sugar and lemon juice and nutmeg</p><p><b>Nehemija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Old Testament book telling how a Jewish official at the court of Artaxerxes I in 444 BC became a leader in rebuilding Jerusalem after the Babylonian Captivity [Book of Nehemiah]</p><p><b>Indijski državnik i vođa s Gandhijem u borbi za vlast (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Indian statesman and leader with Gandhi in the struggle for home rule [Jawaharlal Nehru]</p><p><b>autonomna regija sjeveroistočne Kine koju su anektirali vladari Mančura 1635. godine i postala sastavni dio Kine 1911. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an autonomous region of northeastern China that was annexed by the Manchu rulers in 1635 and became an integral part of China in 1911 [Inner Mongolia]</p><p><b>njištanje, njištati, rzanje, rzati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the characteristic sounds made by a horse [nicker, whicker, whinny]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a characteristic sound, of a horse [nicker, whicker, whinny]</p><p><b>komšija, komšinica, susjed, susjeda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who lives (or is located) near another [neighbour]</p><p><i>n.</i> a nearby object of the same kind [neighbour]</p><p><i>v.</i> live or be located as a neighbor [neighbour]</p><p><i>v.</i> be located near or adjacent to [neighbour]</p><p><b>kvart, stambeno susjedstvo, susjedske, susjedstvo, blizina, okolica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a surrounding or nearby region [locality, neck of the woods, neighbourhood, vicinity]</p><p><i>n.</i> people living near one another [neighbourhood]</p><p><i>n.</i> the approximate amount of something (usually used prepositionally as in `in the region of') [region]</p><p><i>n.</i> an area within a city or town that has some distinctive features (especially one forming a community)</p><p><b>obližnjem, susjedne, susjedni, susjednim</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a common boundary or edge [adjacent, conterminous, contiguous]</p><p><b>sklonost biti prijateljski i korisno susjedima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to be friendly and helpful to neighbors [good-neighborliness, good-neighbourliness, neighbourliness]</p><p><b>komšija, komšinica, susjed, susjeda (od &quot;neighbor&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> exhibiting the qualities expected in a friendly neighbor [neighbourly]</p><p><b>biti susjedan, dopirati, graničiti, graničiti se, predmet, susjed, susjeda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who lives (or is located) near another [neighbor]</p><p><i>n.</i> a nearby object of the same kind [neighbor]</p><p><i>v.</i> live or be located as a neighbor [neighbor]</p><p><i>v.</i> be located near or adjacent to [neighbor]</p><p><b>blizina, granični, okolice, okolina, susjedi, susjedni, susjedstvo, okolica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a surrounding or nearby region [locality, neck of the woods, neighborhood, vicinity]</p><p><i>n.</i> people living near one another [neighborhood]</p><p><b>sklonost biti prijateljski i korisno susjedima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to be friendly and helpful to neighbors [good-neighborliness, good-neighbourliness, neighborliness]</p><p><b>susjedski, susjedskih</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> exhibiting the qualities expected in a friendly neighbor [neighborly]</p><p><b>Američki astronaut (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States astronaut [Armstrong]</p><p><b>Američki dramaturg poznat po lagi komediji (rođen 1927) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States playwright noted for light comedies (born in 1927) [Marvin Neil Simon, Simon]</p><p><b>bakterija koja proizvodi gnoj i koja uzrokuje gonoreju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the pus-producing bacterium that causes gonorrhea [gonococcus]</p><p><b>isto tako ne, ni, nijedan, nijedan od dva, nikakav, niti</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not either</p><p><b>središnje plato područje Arapskog poluotoka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a central plateau region of the Arabian Peninsula [Najd]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, za sve vrste životinja koje žive u vodama u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, za sve vrste životinja koje žive u vodama u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, za sve vrste životinja u vodama u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ovog Pravilnika, za sve vrste životinja u vodama u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, za sve vrste životinja u vodama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the aggregate of actively swimming animals in a body of water ranging from microscopic organisms to whales</p><p><b>inhibitor proteaze (trgovinski naziv Viracept) koji se koristi u liječenju HIV- a obično u kombinaciji s drugim lijekovima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a protease inhibitor (trade name Viracept) used in treating HIV usually in combination with other drugs [Viracept]</p><p><b>Engleska komedija i ljubavnica Karla II (1650-1687) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English comedienne and mistress of Charles II (1650-1687) [Eleanor Gwyn, Eleanor Gwynn, Eleanor Gwynne, Gwynn, Gynne, Gywn, Nell Gwynne, Nell Gywn]</p><p><b>Engleska komedija i ljubavnica Karla II (1650-1687) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English comedienne and mistress of Charles II (1650-1687) [Eleanor Gwyn, Eleanor Gwynn, Eleanor Gwynne, Gwynn, Gynne, Gywn, Nell Gwynn, Nell Gywn]</p><p><b>Engleska komedija i ljubavnica Karla II (1650-1687) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English comedienne and mistress of Charles II (1650-1687) [Eleanor Gwyn, Eleanor Gwynn, Eleanor Gwynne, Gwynn, Gynne, Gywn, Nell Gwynn, Nell Gwynne]</p><p><b>Američki novinar koji je razotkrivao loše uvjete u mentalnim ustanovama (1867-1922) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> muckraking United States journalist who exposed bad conditions in mental institutions (1867-1922) [Elizabeth Cochrane Seaman, Elizabeth Seaman, Seaman]</p><p><b>političarka iz Wyominga koja je bila prva žena guverner u Sjedinjenim Državama (1876-1977) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a politician in Wyoming who was the first woman governor in the United States (1876-1977) [Nellie Tayloe Ross, Ross]</p><p><b>političarka iz Wyominga koja je bila prva žena guverner u Sjedinjenim Državama (1876-1977) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a politician in Wyoming who was the first woman governor in the United States (1876-1977) [Nellie Ross, Ross]</p><p><b>Engleski admiral koji je porazio francusku flotu Napoleona ali je smrtno ranjen u Trafalgaru (1758-1805), bilo koji od nekoliko borbenih držanja u kojima se ruka prolazi ispod protivnikovog ramena s leđa i ruka vrši pritisak na stražnji dio vrata. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English admiral who defeated the French fleets of Napoleon but was mortally wounded at Trafalgar (1758-1805) [Admiral Nelson, Horatio Nelson, Lord Nelson, Viscount Nelson]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several wrestling holds in which an arm is passed under the opponent's arm from behind and the hand exerts pressure on the back of the neck</p><p><b>Američki pisac (1909-1981) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer (1909-1981) [Algren]</p><p><b>Južnoafrički državnik koji je pušten iz zatvora da postane prvi demokratski izabrani predsjednik države 1994. (rođen 1918.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African statesman who was released from prison to become the nation's first democratically elected president in 1994 (born in 1918) [Mandela, Nelson Rolihlahla Mandela]</p><p><b>Južnoafrički državnik koji je pušten iz zatvora da postane prvi demokratski izabrani predsjednik države 1994. (rođen 1918.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African statesman who was released from prison to become the nation's first democratically elected president in 1994 (born in 1918) [Mandela, Nelson Mandela]</p><p><b>ponekad stavljen u obitelj Nymphaeaceae: lotosi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sometimes placed in the family Nymphaeaceae: lotuses [genus Nelumbo]</p><p><b>vodeni lilij istočne Sjeverne Amerike s blijedožutim cvijećem i jestivim kugličnim sjemenama nalik orašastima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> water lily of eastern North America having pale yellow blossoms and edible globular nutlike seeds [American lotus, water chinquapin, yanquapin]</p><p><b>izvorno iz istočne Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> native to eastern Asia [Indian lotus, lotus, sacred lotus]</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama smatraju se neovisnom obitelji vodenih lilija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications considered an independent family of water lilies [subfamily Nelumbonaceae]</p><p><b>Jednog uma. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> of one mind [nemine contradicente, unanimously]</p><p><b>komarci, porodica Culicidae, porodica komaraca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mosquitoes [suborder Nematocera]</p><p><b>Nesegmentirani crvi: okrugli crvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unsegmented worms: roundworms [Aschelminthes, phylum Aschelminthes, phylum Nematoda]</p><p><b>Nesegmentirani crvi s izduženim zaobljenim tijelom s obje strane na vrhu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unsegmented worms with elongated rounded body pointed at both ends [nematode worm, roundworm]</p><p><b>Nesegmentirani crvi s izduženim zaobljenim tijelom s obje strane na vrhu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unsegmented worms with elongated rounded body pointed at both ends [nematode, roundworm]</p><p><b>Barbiturat (trgovinski naziv Nembutal) koji se koristi kao sedativ i hipnotik i antispasmodik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a barbiturate (trade name Nembutal) used as a sedative and hypnotic and antispasmodic [pentobarbital, pentobarbital sodium, yellow jacket]</p><p><b>dolina u jugoistočnoj Grčkoj gdje su se održavale Nemejske igre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a valley in southeastern Greece where the Nemean Games were held</p><p><b>Stare panhelenske igre koje su se održavale svake dvije godine u Nemeji u drugoj i četvrtoj godini svake Olimpijade. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ancient Panhellenic games held biennially at Nemea in the second and fourth years of each Olympiad</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) ogroman lav ugušen od strane Herkula kao prvi od svojih 12 radova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) an enormous lion strangled by Hercules as the first of his 12 labors</p><p><b>Sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> proboscis worms [Nemertina, phylum Nemertea, phylum Nemertina]</p><p><b>Meki nesegmentirani morski crvi koji imaju proboscis nalik niti i sposobnost istezanja i kontrakcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soft unsegmented marine worms that have a threadlike proboscis and the ability to stretch and contract [nemertine, proboscis worm, ribbon worm]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> proboscis worms [Nemertea, phylum Nemertea, phylum Nemertina]</p><p><b>Meki nesegmentirani morski crvi koji imaju proboscis nalik niti i sposobnost istezanja i kontrakcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soft unsegmented marine worms that have a threadlike proboscis and the ability to stretch and contract [nemertean, proboscis worm, ribbon worm]</p><p><b>propast, suparnik, zaslužena patnja, zaslužena pažnja, zla kob, Nemesis, Nemeza, Nemezis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the goddess of divine retribution and vengeance</p><p><i>n.</i> something causing misery or death [bane, curse, scourge]</p><p><b>Jednog uma. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> of one mind [nem con, unanimously]</p><p><b>biljke iz roda Nemophila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Nemophila</p><p><b>Ustanovljena cjelogodišnja biljka s tamno ljubičastom ili ljubičastom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> straggling California annual herb with deep purple or violet flowers [Pholistoma auritum, fiesta flower]</p><p><b>Kalifornijska godišnja koja ima bijele cvijeće s tamno ljubičastim mrljom na svakom laticju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> California annual having white flowers with a deep purple blotch on each petal [five-spot]</p><p><b>delikatna kalifornijska godišnja s plavim cvijećem označenim tamnim mrljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> delicate California annual having blue flowers marked with dark spots [baby blue-eyes]</p><p><b>Uralički jezik kojim govori samojed sjevernog Sibira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Uralic language spoken by a Samoyed of northern Siberia [Nentsi, Nentsy, Yurak-Samoyed]</p><p><b>Uralički jezik kojim govori samojed sjevernog Sibira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Uralic language spoken by a Samoyed of northern Siberia [Nenets, Nentsy, Yurak-Samoyed]</p><p><b>Uralički jezik kojim govori samojed sjevernog Sibira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Uralic language spoken by a Samoyed of northern Siberia [Nenets, Nentsi, Yurak-Samoyed]</p><p><b>(koristi se kao kombinirana forma) nedavna ili nova (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used as a combining form) recent or new</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih stilova džeza koji su se pojavili nakon 1940. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various styles of jazz that appeared after 1940 [modern jazz, new jazz]</p><p><b>Darvinove teorije ili teorije koje se odnose na njih, kako su one izmijenjene modernim genetskim otkrićima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Darwin's theories as modified by modern genetic findings</p><p><b>moderna darvinistička teorija koja objašnjava nove vrste u smislu genetskih mutacija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a modern Darwinian theory that explains new species in terms of genetic mutations</p><p><b>od ili u vezi sa modernom verzijom Lamarckizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a modern version of Lamarckism</p><p><b>moderna Lamarckijeva teorija koja naglašava važnost čimbenika okoliša u genetskim promjenama i zadržava pojam nasljeđivanja stečenih znakova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a modern Lamarckian theory emphasizing the importance of environmental factors in genetic changes and retaining the notion of the inheritance of acquired characters</p><p><b>Latinski od renesanse (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Latin since the Renaissance [New Latin]</p><p><b>antibiotika dobiven od aktinomiceta i korišten (kao sulfat pod trgovačkim imenom Neobiotic) kao crijevni antiseptik u operaciji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antibiotic obtained from an actinomycete and used (as a sulphate under the trade name Neobiotic) as an intestinal antiseptic in surgery [fradicin, neomycin]</p><p><b>Australski plućni ribe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extant Australian lungfishes [genus Neoceratodus]</p><p><b>ugrožena vrsta plućne ribe koja se nalazi u rijekama u Queenslandu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an endangered species of lungfish found in rivers in Queensland [Australian lungfish, Queensland lungfish]</p><p><b>karakteristika oživljavanja ranijeg klasičnog stila (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of a revival of an earlier classical style [neoclassical]</p><p><b>karakteristika oživljavanja ranijeg klasičnog stila (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of a revival of an earlier classical style [neoclassic]</p><p><b>neoklasicizam, neoklasicizma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> revival of a classical style (in art or literature or architecture or music) but from a new perspective or with a new motivation</p><p><b>zagovornik neoklasicizma, koji se odnose na ili zagovaraju neoklasicizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of neoclassicism</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or advocating neoclassicism [neoclassicistic]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili zagovaraju neoklasicizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or advocating neoclassicism [neoclassicist]</p><p><b>neokolonijalizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> control by a powerful country of its former colonies (or other less developed countries) by economic pressures</p><p><b>konzervativca koji se potpisuje na neokonservatizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conservative who subscribes to neoconservatism [neoconservative]</p><p><b>pristup politici ili teologiji koji predstavlja povratak na tradicionalnu gledište (za razliku od više liberalne ili radikalne škole misli 1960-ih) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an approach to politics or theology that represents a return to a traditional point of view (in contrast to more liberal or radical schools of thought of the 1960s)</p><p><b>konzervativca koji se potpisuje na neokonservatizam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conservative who subscribes to neoconservatism [neocon]</p><p><b>Kortikalni dio neencefalona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cortical part of the neencephalon [neopallium]</p><p><b>Neokortex mozga ili povezan s njim (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the neocortex of the cerebrum</p><p><b>neodimij, neodijum, neodij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a yellow trivalent metallic element of the rare earth group [Nd, atomic number 60]</p><p><b>dio mozga koji ima najnovije filogenetsko podrijetlo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of the brain having the most recent phylogenetic origin [neencephalon]</p><p><b>umjetnički pokret zasnovan na ekspresionizmu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an art movement based on expressionism</p><p><b>Šarenici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> round-tailed muskrat [genus Neofiber]</p><p><b>od mokrišta na Floridi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of Florida wetlands [Florida water rat, round-tailed muskrat]</p><p><b>rod gljiva iz obitelji Hygrophoraceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of fungi belonging to the family Hygrophoraceae [genus Neohygrophorus]</p><p><b>gljiva s malim smeđim konveksnim kapom s potisnutim diskom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus with a small brown convex cap with a depressed disc</p><p><b>rod gljiva iz obitelji Polyporaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of fungi belonging to the family Polyporaceae [genus Neolentinus]</p><p><b>Polypore s velikim čepom (do 15 inča u promjeru) i širokim stabljkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gilled polypore with a large cap (up to 15 i