rine and usually increased blood cholesterol [nephrosis]</p><p><b>rez u bubreg (obično za uklanjanje kamena) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> incision into a kidney (usually to remove a kidney stone)</p><p><b>otrovno za bubrege (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> toxic to the kidney</p><p><b>bilo koji toksin koji utječe na bubrege (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any toxin that affects the kidneys</p><p><b>Egipatska boginja povezana s obredima mrtvih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Egyptian goddess associated with ritual of the dead</p><p><b>Svaka biljka iz roda Nephthytis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Nephthytis</p><p><b>tropska rizomatna biljka uzgajana kao ukrasna biljka zbog svojih velikih sagitiranih listova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical rhizomatous plant cultivated as an ornamental for its large sagittate leaves</p><p><b>vodeni škorpioni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> water scorpions [family Nepidae]</p><p><b>nepotizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> favoritism shown to relatives or close friends by those in power (as by giving them jobs)</p><p><b>osoba koja ima moć i koja favorizira rodbinu ili bliske prijatelje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a powerful person who shows favoritism to relatives or close friends</p><p><b>(Rimska mitologija) bog mora, džinovski planet s prstenom ledenih čestica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman mythology) god of the sea</p><p><i>n.</i> a giant planet with a ring of ice particles</p><p><b>neptunij, neptunijum</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radioactive transuranic metallic element [Np, atomic number 93]</p><p><b>šmokljan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an insignificant student who is ridiculed as being affected or boringly studious [dweeb, grind, swot, wonk]</p><p><i>n.</i> an intelligent but single-minded expert in a particular technical field or profession</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) bilo koja od 50 morskih nimfa koje su bile kćeri boga mora Nerea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) any of the 50 sea nymphs who were daughters of the sea god Nereus</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) bog mora sin Pontusa i Gae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) a sea god son of Pontus and Gaea</p><p><b>Nergal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Akkadian) god ruling with his consort Ereshkigal the world of the dead</p><p><b>neritidni gastropod s kratkom glatkom ili spiralno oštricanom školjkom s debelim, obično zubnim vanjskim usnom i zubnim operculumom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a neritid gastropod having a short smooth or spirally ridged shell with thick usually toothed outer lip and toothed operculum</p><p><b>gastropod s crvenkastim zubnim izbočima oko otvora školjke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gastropod having reddish toothlike projections around the shell opening [bleeding tooth]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s područjem mora iznad kontinentalnog pojasa koji je dublje od 200 m, o području plitke vode koja se susreće s obalom mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the region of the sea over the continental shelf which is less than 200 meters deep</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the region of shallow water adjoining the seacoast</p><p><b>oceanske vode od plimo do dubine oko 100 brahmi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ocean waters from the low tide mark to a depth of about 100 fathoms</p><p><b>Operkulirani morski pužovi obalnih voda s kratkom spiralnom ljuskom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> operculate seasnail of coastal waters with a short spiral shell [neritid gastropod]</p><p><b>Operkulirani morski pužovi obalnih voda s kratkom spiralnom ljuskom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> operculate seasnail of coastal waters with a short spiral shell [neritid]</p><p><b>neritidi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> neritids [family Neritidae]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornately marked and brightly colored snails of brackish waters</p><p><b>jedna vrsta: olandrija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one species: oleander [genus Nerium]</p><p><b>Nerium oleander, oleandar, oleander</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ornamental but poisonous flowering shrub having narrow evergreen leaves and clusters of fragrant white to pink or red flowers: native to East Indies but widely cultivated in warm regions [oleander, rose bay]</p><p><b>Njemački fizičar i kemičar koji je formulirao treći zakon termodinamike (1864-1941) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German physicist and chemist who formulated the third law of thermodynamics (1864-1941) [Walther Hermann Nernst]</p><p><b>Neron</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Roman Emperor notorious for his monstrous vice and fantastic luxury (was said to have started a fire that destroyed much of Rome in 64) but the Roman Empire remained prosperous during his rule (37-68) [Lucius Domitius Ahenobarbus, Nero Claudius Caesar Drusus Germanicus]</p><p><b>Neron</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Roman Emperor notorious for his monstrous vice and fantastic luxury (was said to have started a fire that destroyed much of Rome in 64) but the Roman Empire remained prosperous during his rule (37-68) [Lucius Domitius Ahenobarbus, Nero]</p><p><b>tropski grm s blistavim lišćem i mirisnim noćnim cvijećem s krumpiranim ili valovitim korollama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical shrub having glossy foliage and fragrant nocturnal flowers with crimped or wavy corollas [Adam's apple, East Indian rosebay, Tabernaemontana divaricate, coffee rose, crape jasmine, crepe gardenia, crepe jasmine, pinwheel flower]</p><p><b>Sjevernoameričke vodene zmije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American water snakes [genus Nerodia]</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama stavljen u rod Nerodia (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications placed in the genus Nerodia [Natrix sipedon, banded water snake, common water snake]</p><p><b>ulje od žute boje koje se nalazi u cvjetovima naranče i koristi se u parfemiji i kao aromatizator (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an odoriferous yellow oil found in orange flowers and used in perfumery and as a flavoring</p><p><b>Teutonska boginja plodnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Teutonic goddess of fertility [Hertha]</p><p><b>Čileanski pjesnik (1904-1973) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chilean poet (1904-19