nents or circuits [electronic network]</p><p><i>v.</i> communicate with and within a group</p><p><b>arhitektura mreže, mrežna arhitektura</b></p><p><i>n.</i> specification of design principles (including data formats and procedures) for creating a network configuration of data processors</p><p><b>Grupa sličnih ljudi ujedinjenih putem interneta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of like-minded people united by the internet</p><p><b>raspored programa koji će se emitirati na mreži (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the schedule of programs to be broadcast on a network</p><p><b>topologija mreže, topologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the configuration of a communication network [topology]</p><p><b>s mrežom vena ili rebra (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a network of veins or ribs</p><p><b>Američki matematičar koji je pridonio razvoju atomske bombe i digitalnih računala s pohranjenim programom (1903-1957) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States mathematician who contributed to the development of atom bombs and of stored-program digital computers (1903-1957) [John von Neumann, von Neumann]</p><p><b>živčani, živčanih, živčanim, živčanog</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the nervous system [nervous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to neurons [neuronal, neuronic]</p><p><b>struktura koja se dorsalno izlazi iz kičmenog centra i okružuje kičmenu moždinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a structure arising dorsally from a vertebral centrum and enclosing the spinal cord [vertebral arch]</p><p><b>nervni impuls, živčani impuls</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the electrical discharge that travels along a nerve fiber [impulse, nerve impulse, nervous impulse]</p><p><b>neuronska mreža</b></p><p><i>n.</i> computer architecture in which processors are connected in a manner suggestive of connections between neurons [neural network]</p><p><i>n.</i> any network of neurons or nuclei that function together to perform some function in the body [neural network]</p><p><b>mreža sastavljena od vrlo jednostavnih procesora, neural