ean and variance [Gaussian distribution]</p><p><b>Achondroplastični patuljak čija je mala veličina rezultat genetske mane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an achondroplastic dwarf whose small size is the result of a genetic defect [hypoplastic dwarf, primordial dwarf, true dwarf]</p><p><b>Normalni rasjed</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inclined fault in which the hanging wall appears to have slipped downward relative to the footwall [common fault, gravity fault]</p><p><b>Dvogodišnja škola za obuku nastavnika osnovnih škola (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a two-year school for training elementary teachers [teachers college]</p><p><b>glaukom koji je posljedica oštećenja optičkog živca iako je intraokularni pritisak normalan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> glaucoma that results from damage to the optic nerve although the intraocular pressure is normal</p><p><b>normalnost, prirodnost, uobičajnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> being within certain limits that define the range of normal functioning [normality]</p><p><i>n.</i> expectedness as a consequence of being usual or regular or common [normality]</p><p><b>Uvođenje standarda ili propisa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the imposition of standards or regulations [normalization, standardisation, standardization]</p><p><b>normalizirati se, normalizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become normal or return to its normal state [normalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make normal or cause to conform to a norm or standard [normalize, renormalise, renormalize]</p><p><b>normalizirati se (od &quot;normalise&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who normalizes [normalizer]</p><p><b>uobičajenost, normalnost, prirodnost, uobičajnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> being within certain limits that define the range of normal functioning [normalcy]</p><p><i>n.</i> (of a solution) concentration expressed in gram equivalents of solute per liter [N]</p><p><i>n.</i> expectedness as a consequence of being usual or regular or common [normalcy]</p><p><i>n.</i> conformity with the norm</p><p><b>normalizacija, normalizarinje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the imposition of standards or regulations [normalisation, standardisation, standardization]</p><p><b>normalizirati, normalizirati se, temperirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become normal or return to its normal state [normalise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make normal or cause to conform to a norm or standard [normalise, renormalise, renormalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring to a desired consistency, texture, or hardness by a process of gradually heating and cooling [anneal, temper]</p><p><b>normalizirati (od &quot;normalize&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who normalizes [normaliser]</p><p><b>inače, normalno, obično</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> under normal conditions [commonly, ordinarily, unremarkably, usually]</p><p><b>Američki operni sopran (rođen 1945), Australijski golfer (rođen 1955), stanovnik Normandije, od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Normandiju, od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Normane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States operatic soprano (born in 1945) [Jessye Norman]</p><p><i>n.</i> Australian golfer (born in 1955) [Greg Norman, Gregory John Norman]</p><p><i>n.</i> an inhabitant of Normandy</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Normandy</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of the Normans</p><p><b>romanški stil koji se prvi put pojavio u Normandiji oko 950 n.e. i korišten u Britaniji od Normanovskog osvajanja do 12. stoljeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Romanesque style first appearing in Normandy around 950 AD and used in Britain from the Norman Conquest until the 12th century</p><p><b>invazija i naseljavanje Engleske od strane Normana nakon bitke kod Hastingsa (1066) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the invasion and settlement of England by the Normans following the battle of Hastings (1066)</p><p><b>srednjovjekovni normanski dijalekt starog francuskog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the medieval Norman dialect of Old French [Norman-French, Old North French]</p><p><b>Kanadski filmski redatelj (rođen 1926.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Canadian filmmaker (born in 1926) [Jewison]</p><p><b>Američki pisac (rođen 1923.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer (born in 1923) [Mailer]</p><p><b>Američki socijalista koji je bio šest puta kandidat za predsjednika (1884-1968) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States socialist who was a candidate for president six times (1884-1968) [Norman Thomas, Thomas]</p><p><b>Američki ilustrator čiji radovi predstavljaju sentimentalan idealizirani pogled na svakodnevni život (1894-1978) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States illustrator whose works present a sentimental idealized view of everyday life (1894-1978) [Rockwell]</p><p><b>Američki socijalista koji je bio šest puta kandidat za predsjednika (1884-1968) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States socialist who was a candidate for president six times (1884-1968) [Norman Mattoon Thomas, Thomas]</p><p><b>srednjovjekovni normanski dijalekt starog francuskog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the medieval Norman dialect of Old French [Norman French, Old North French]</p><p><b>bivša pokrajina sjeverozapadne Francuske na Engleskom kanalu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former province of northwestern France on the English channel [Normandy]</p><p><b>bivša pokrajina sjeverozapadne Francuske na Engleskom kanalu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former province of northwestern France on the English channel [Normandie]</p><p><b>normativni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or dealing with norms</p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to giving directives or rules [prescriptive]</p><p><b>antihipertenzivni lijekovi (trgovinski nazivi Trandate i Normodyne) koji blokiraju alfa i beta- adrenergičke receptore simpatičkog živčanog sustava (što dovodi do smanjenja krvnog tlaka) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antihypertensive drug (trade names Trandate and Normodyne) that blocks alpha and beta-adrenergic receptors of the sympathetic nervous system (leading to a decrease in blood pressure) [Trandate, labetalol, labetalol hydrochloride]</p><p><b>ako imate normalan krvni tlak (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having normal blood pressure</p><p><b>normalna tjelesna temperatura (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> normal body temperature</p><p><b>(Nordijska mitologija) bilo koja od tri boginje sudbine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Norse mythology) any of the three goddesses of destiny [weird sister]</p><p><b>Američki pisac (1870-1902) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer (1870-1902) [Benjamin Franklin Norris Jr., Frank Norris]</p><p><b>Engleski kemičar (1897-1978) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English chemist (1897-1978) [Ronald George Wreyford Norrish]</p><p><b>norveški</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inhabitant of Scandinavia [Northman, Scandinavian]</p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Norway [Norseman, Norwegian]</p><p><i>n.</i> the northern family of Germanic languages that are spoken in Scandinavia and Iceland [Nordic, North Germanic, North Germanic language, Scandinavian, Scandinavian language]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Scandinavia or its peoples or cultures [Scandinavian]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Norway or its people or culture or language [Norwegian]</p><p><b>Bogobojaznost koju su obožavali drevni Normani. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deity worshipped by the ancient Norsemen</p><p><b>mitologija Skandinavije (odjelno podeljena između Britanije i Njemačke) sve do uspostave kršćanstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mythology of Scandinavia (shared in part by Britain and Germany) until the establishment of Christianity</p><p><b>u Norveškoj ili u toj zemlji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Norway [Norse, Norwegian]</p><p><b>sjever, sjeverni, sjeverni vjetar, okrenut sjever, sjevera, sjevernih, sjeverno, sjevernog, sjeveru, sever, magnetski sjever</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the region of the United States lying to the north of the Mason-Dixon line</p><p><i>n.</i> the United States (especially the northern states during the American Civil War) [Union]</p><p><i>n.</i> the cardinal compass point that is at 0 or 360 degrees [N,