drobates pelagicus, stormy petrel]</p><p><b>teritorij u sjeverno-srednjoj Australiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a territory in north central Australia</p><p><b>mala zimzelena biljka sa istočne Sjeverne Amerike koja ima sitna lišća na ravnim granama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small evergreen of eastern North America having tiny scalelike leaves on flattened branchlets [American arborvitae, Thuja occidentalis, white cedar]</p><p><b>Plovlja na istočnoj obali Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> whiting of the east coast of United States [Menticirrhus saxatilis]</p><p><b>Srednja i srednja granica (srednja i srednja granica) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender fern of northern North America with shining chestnut-colored stipes and bipinnate fronds with usually distinct marginal sori [Alpine woodsia, Woodsia alpina, flower-cup fern]</p><p><b>stanovnike sjevera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inhabitant of the North</p><p><i>n.</i> an American who lives in the North (especially during the American Civil War) [Yank, Yankee]</p><p><b>najsjeverniji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated farthest north [northmost]</p><p><b>sjeverni, sjeverno, sjevernog, sjevernom, sjevernjak, snažni sjeverni vjetar, stanovnik sjevera (od &quot;northern&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being to the north</p><p><b>bilo koje područje koje se nalazi na sjeveru ili prema sjeveru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any region lying in or toward the north</p><p><b>stanovnik Skandinavije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inhabitant of Scandinavia [Norse, Scandinavian]</p><p><b>Najviše sjeverno smještena (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated farthest north [northernmost]</p><p><b>Američki biohemičar (1891-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States biochemist (1891-1987) [John Howard Northrop]</p><p><b>Kanadski književni kritičar zainteresiran za upotrebu mita i simbolike (1912-1991) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Canadian literary critic interested in the use of myth and symbolism (1912-1991) [Frye, Herman Northrop Frye]</p><p><b>najseverniji okrug Engleske. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the northernmost county of England</p><p><b>Anglo-saksijsko kraljevstvo u sjevernoj Engleskoj do 876. godine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Anglo-Saxon kingdom in northern England until 876</p><p><b>ka sjeveru, na sjever, sjeverni, sjeverni pravac, sjever, sjeverno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cardinal compass point that is at 0 or 360 degrees [N, due north, north]</p><p><i>adj.</i> moving toward the north [northbound]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a northern direction [north, northerly, northwards]</p><p><b>sjeverno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a northern direction [north, northerly, northward]</p><p><b>sjeverozapad, sjeverozapadan, sjeverozapadno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the northwestern region of the United States [northwestern United States]</p><p><i>n.</i> the direction corresponding to the northwestward compass point</p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point midway between north and west [NW, nor'-west, northwestward]</p><p><i>n.</i> a location in the northwestern part of a country, region, or city</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the northwest [northwesterly, northwestern]</p><p><i>adj.</i> coming from the northwest [northwesterly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> to, toward, or in the northwest [nor'-west, north-west]</p><p><b>Kompasna točka koja je jedna točka sjeverno od sjeverozapada. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point that is one point north of northwest [NWbN]</p><p><b>Kompasna točka koja je jedna točka zapadno od sjeverozapada. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point that is one point west of northwest [NWbW]</p><p><b>vodeni put između Atlantskog i Tihog oceana duž sjeverne obale Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a water route between the Atlantic Ocean and the Pacific Ocean along the northern coast of North America</p><p><b>Velika teritorija u sjeverozapadnom Kanadi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large territory in northwestern Canada</p><p><b>vjetar sa sjeverozapada. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wind from the northwest [northwester]</p><p><b>sjeverozapadni vjetar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wind from the northwest [northwest wind]</p><p><b>sjeverozapadan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> coming from the northwest [northwest]</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the northwest [northwest, northwestern]</p><p><b>sjeverozapadna, sjeverozapadan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the northwest [northwest, northwesterly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a region of the United States generally including Washington</p><p><b>Sjeverozapadni region Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the northwestern region of the United States [Northwest]</p><p><b>kompasna točka na pola puta između sjevera i zapada, prema sjeverozapadu., u sjeverozapadnom smjeru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point midway between north and west [NW, nor'-west, northwest]</p><p><i>adj.</i> toward the northwest</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a northwestward direction [northwestwardly]</p><p><b>u sjeverozapadnom smjeru (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a northwestward direction [northwestward]</p><p><b>tritsiklični antidepresiv (trgovinski naziv Pamelor) koji se koristi zajedno s psihoterapijom za liječenje distimne depresije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tricyclic antidepressant drug (trade name Pamelor) used along with psychotherapy to treat dysthymic depression [Pamelor]</p><p><b>(Perzijski) praznik Nove godine u Iranu i Azerbejdžanu i Afganistanu i Pakistanu i dijelovima Indije i među Kurdim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Persian) the new year holiday in Iran and Azerbaijan and Afghanistan and Pakistan and parts of India and among the Kurds [Nowrooz, Nowruz]</p><p><b>vasodilatator (trgovinski naziv Norvasc) u obliku tableta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vasodilator (trade name Norvasc) taken in tablet form [amlodipine besylate]</p><p><b>inhibitor proteaze (trgovinski naziv Norvir) koji se koristi u liječenju HIV-a (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a protease inhibitor (trade name Norvir) used in treating HIV [ritonavir]</p><p><b>Norveška</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a constitutional monarchy in northern Europe on the western side of the Scandinavian Peninsula [Kingdom of Norway, Noreg, Norge]</p><p><b>škamp</b></p><p><i>n.</i> edible European lobster resembling the American lobster but slenderer [Nephrops norvegicus]</p><p><b>Veliki evroazijski klovn prirodni u Sjevernoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large Eurasian maple tree naturalized in North America [Acer platanoides]</p><p><b>obični domaći štakor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common domestic rat [Rattus norvegicus, brown rat]</p><p><b>smreka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall pyramidal spruce native to northern Europe having dark green foliage on spreading branches with pendulous branchlets and long pendulous cones [Picea abies]</p><p><b>norveški, norveški jezik, Norvežanka, Norvežankin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Norway [Norse, Norseman]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Scandinavian language that is spoken in Norway</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Norway or its people or culture or language [Norse]</p><p><b>pas kompakte srednje veličine s teškim sivim krznom razvijen u Norveškoj za lov na losove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> breed of compact medium-sized dog with a heavy grey coat developed in Norway for hunting elk [elkhound]</p><p><b>norveška kruna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Norway [krone]</p><p><b>U lovu u europskim vodama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> caught in European waters [langoustine, scampo]</p><p><b>norveška novčana jedinica, norveška valuta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Norway</p><p><b>Norveško more</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of the Atlantic that lies off the Norwegian coast to the north of the North Sea</p><p><b>Engleska pasmina malog kratkoponog terjera s ravnim žičastom crvenom ili sivom ili crno-sumanom dlačinom i ustima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English breed of small short-legged terrier with a straight wiry red or grey or black-and-tan coat and erect ears</p><p><b>ispust, nanjušiti, nos, njuh, njuška, ući u trag, udisati, uvlačiti nosom, pedalj, mlaznica, čeprkati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the organ of smell and entrance to the respiratory tract [olfactory organ]</p><p><i>n.</i> a front that resembles a human nose (especially the front of an aircraft)</p><p><i>n.</i> the front or forward projection of a tool or weapon</p><p><i>n.</i> a small distance</p><p><i>n.</i> a symbol of inquisitiveness</p><p><i>n.</i> the sense of smell (especially in animals)</p><p><i>n.</i> a natural skill</p><p><i>n.</i> a projecting spout from which a fluid is discharged [nozzle]</p><p><i>v.</i> search or inquire in a meddlesome way [horn in, intrude, poke, pry]</p><p><i>v.</i> advance the forward part of with caution</p><p><i>v.</i> catch the scent of [scent, wind]</p><p><i>v.</i> push or move with the nose</p><p><i>v.</i> rub noses [nuzzle]</p><p><i>v.</i> defeat by a narrow margin</p><p><b>Ulice imena za kokain (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> street names for cocaine [C, blow, coke, snow]</p><p><b>prednji dio koji se sastoji od konjske glave rakete ili rakete koja štiti korisni teret od toplote tijekom prolaska kroz atmosferu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> front consisting of the conical head of a missile or rocket that protects the payload from heat during its passage through the atmosphere [ogive]</p><p><b>cenzus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a periodic count of the population [census, nosecount]</p><p><b>iznenadan napad, pikiranje, pikirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a steep nose-down descent by an aircraft [dive, nosedive]</p><p><b>Ulice imena za heroin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> street names for heroin [big H, hell dust, scag, skag, smack, thunder]</p><p><b>flauta koja se svira puhanjem kroz nosnice (koristi se u nekim azijskim zemljama) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flute that is played by blowing through the nostrils (used in some Asian countries)</p><p><b>kozmetička operacija za poboljšanje izgleda nosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cosmetic surgery to improve the appearance of your nose [rhinoplasty]</p><p><b>prepoznavanje ili otkriva