><i>n.</i> Old World nutcracker [common nutcracker]</p><p><b>razbijač oraha zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nutcracker of the western United States [Clark's nutcracker]</p><p><b>atomski, jezgrovit, nuklearan, nuklearni, nuklearne</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (weapons) deriving destructive energy from the release of atomic energy [atomic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or constituting the nucleus of an atom</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or constituting the nucleus of a cell</p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting or like a nucleus</p><p><b>katarakta koja pogađa jezgru leće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cataract that affects the nucleus of the lens</p><p><b>kemičar koji se specijalizirao za nuklearnu kemiju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chemist who specializes in nuclear chemistry [radiochemist]</p><p><b>nuklearna kemija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the chemistry of radioactive substances [radiochemistry]</p><p><b>nacije koje posjeduju nuklearno oružje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the nations possessing nuclear weapons</p><p><b>Vojna doktrina da će neprijatelj biti odvraćen od korištenja nuklearnog oružja sve dok može biti uništen kao posljedica toga. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the military doctrine that an enemy will be deterred from using nuclear weapons as long as he can be destroyed as a consequence</p><p><b>atomska energija, nuklearna energija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the energy released by a nuclear reaction [atomic energy]</p><p><b>Inženjerstvo koje se bavi projektovanjem, izgradnjom i radom nuklearnog reaktora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of engineering concerned with the design and construction and operation of nuclear reactors</p><p><b>Eksplozija atomske bombe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the explosion of an atomic bomb [atomic explosion]</p><p><b>obitelj koja se sastoji od roditelja i njihovih djece i baka i djedova bračnog partnera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family consisting of parents and their children and grandparents of a marital partner [conjugal family]</p><p><b>nuklearna fisija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear reaction in which a massive nucleus splits into smaller nuclei with the simultaneous release of energy [fission]</p><p><b>nuklearno gorivo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fuel (such as uranium) that can be used in nuclear reactors as a source of electricity</p><p><b>nuklearna fuzija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear reaction in which nuclei combine to form more massive nuclei with the simultaneous release of energy [fusion, nuclear fusion reaction]</p><p><b>nuklearna reakcija u kojoj se jezgre spajaju kako bi formirale masivnije jezgre s istovremenim oslobađanjem energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear reaction in which nuclei combine to form more massive nuclei with the simultaneous release of energy [fusion, nuclear fusion]</p><p><b>nuklearna magnetna rezonancija, nuklearna magnetska rezonancija, nuklearnomagnetska rezonanca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> resonance of protons to radiation in a magnetic field [NMR, proton magnetic resonance]</p><p><b>nuklearna medicina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of medicine that uses radioactive materials either to image a patient's body or to destroy diseased cells</p><p><b>U slučaju da se radi o nuklearnom reaktoru, radi se o reakciji na jedru. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> severe overheating of the core of a nuclear reactor resulting in the core melting and radiation escaping [meltdown]</p><p><b>fizičar koji se specijalizirao za nuklearnu fiziku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a physicist who specializes in nuclear physics</p><p><b>nuklearna fizika, atomska fizika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of physics that studies the internal structure of atomic nuclei [atomic physics, nucleonics]</p><p><b>nuklearna energija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nuclear energy regarded as a source of electricity for the power grid (for civilian use) [atomic power]</p><p><b>korištenje nuklearnog reaktora ili za proizvodnju električne energije za pogon motora (kao u nuklearnoj podmornici) ili za izravno zagrijavanje goriva (kao u nuklearnim raketama) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of a nuclear reactor either to produce electricity to power an engine (as in a nuclear submarine) or to directly heat a propellant (as in nuclear rockets)</p><p><b>nuklearna reakcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a process that alters the energy or structure or composition of atomic nuclei</p><p><b>nuklearni reaktor, reaktor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) any of several kinds of apparatus that maintain and control a nuclear reaction for the production of energy or artificial elements [reactor]</p><p><b>Neovisna federalna agencija osnovana 1974. godine za licenciranje i regulaciju nuklearnih elektrana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an independent federal agency created in 1974 to license and regulate nuclear power plants [NRC]</p><p><b>rezonančna apsorpcija gama zraka od strane jezgre koja je identična jezgri koja je emitirala gama zrake (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the resonance absorption of a gamma ray by a nucleus identical to the nucleus that emitted the gamma ray</p><p><b>ribonukleinska kiselina pronađena u nukleolu stanice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ribonucleic acid found in the nucleolus of the cell [nRNA]</p><p><b>motor za rakete u kojem se nuklearni reaktor koristi za zagrijavanje goriva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rocket engine in which a nuclear reactor is used to heat a propellant</p><p><b>nautilus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a submarine that is propelled by nuclear power [nautilus, nuclear-powered submarine]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, države članice mogu zabraniti da se u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka upotrebljavaju nuklearne naprave za provođenje terorističkih aktivnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of a nuclear device by a terrorist organization to cause massive devastation or the use (or threat of use) of fissionable radioactive materials</p><p><b>premještanje ćelijske jezgre i njenog genetičkog materijala iz jedne stanice u drugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> moving a cell nucleus and its genetic material from one cell to another [SCNT, somatic cell nuclear transfer, somatic cell nuclear transplantation]</p><p><b>borbena glava rakete dizajnirana za isporuku atomske bombe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the warhead of a missile designed to deliver an atom bomb [atomic warhead, nuke, thermonuclear warhead]</p><p><b>nuklearno oružje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a weapon of mass destruction whose explosive power derives from a nuclear reaction [atomic weapon]</p><p><b>Dugo vrijeme tame i ekstremne hladnoće koje bi, prema znanstvenicima, slijedilo nuklearni rat. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long period of darkness and extreme cold that scientists predict would follow a full-scale nuclear war</p><p><b>brod čija pokretačka snaga dolazi iz energije nuklearnog reaktora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ship whose motive power comes from the energy of a nuclear reactor</p><p><b>nautilus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a submarine that is propelled by nuclear power [nautilus, nuclear submarine]</p><p><b>nukleaza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> general term for enzymes that catalyze the hydrolysis of nucleic acid by cleaving chains of nucleotides into smaller units</p><p><b>formirati u jezgru, s jedrom ili koji se javljaju u jedru (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> form into a nucleus</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a nucleus or occurring in the nucleus [nucleated]</p><p><b>s jedrom ili koji se javljaju u jedru (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a nucleus or occurring in the nucleus [nucleate]</p><p><b>(biohemija) bilo koji od različitih makromolekula sastavljenih od nukleotidnih lanca koji su vitalni sastavni dijelovi svih živih stanica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biochemistry) any of various macromolecules composed of nucleotide chains that are vital constituents of all living cells</p><p><b>određeni dio hromozoma koji je povezan s nukleolusom nakon nuklearne podjele (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the particular part of a chromosome that is associated with a nucleolus after nuclear division [nucleolar organizer, nucl