mb with atomic weapons [atom-bomb]</p><p><i>v.</i> cook or heat in a microwave oven [micro-cook, microwave, zap]</p><p><b>bezizražajan, beznačajan, bezvrijedan, nevažeći, nevaženje, ništavan, ništavilo, ništica, nula, bezizrazan, ništavila, ništavnim, figa, friška figa, ništa, pišljivi bob, šipak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a quantity of no importance [aught, cipher, cypher, goose egg, nada, naught, nil, nix, nothing, zero, zilch, zip, zippo]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking any legal or binding force [void]</p><p><b>prazan skup, prazni skup</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a set that is empty</p><p><b>prostor koji ne sadrži točke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a space that contains no points</p><p><b>dolina ili dolina u južnoj Aziji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ravine or gully in southern Asia</p><p><b>prostrana suha ravnica južne Australije koja se proteže u unutrašnjosti od Velike australske zaljeve (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vast arid plain of southern Australia stretching inland from the Great Australian Bight</p><p><b>Doktrina prava država da država može odbiti priznati ili provesti savezni zakon usvojen od strane Kongresa Sjedinjenih Država, čin poništavanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the states'-rights doctrine that a state can refuse to recognize or to enforce a federal law passed by the United States Congress</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of nullifying [override]</p><p><b>obeskrijepiti, osujetiti, poništavati, poništiti, ukinuti, uništiti (od &quot;nullify&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deprived of legal force [invalidated]</p><p><b>Zaustavljač poništavanja., službenik koji može poništiti ili poništiti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of nullification</p><p><i>n.</i> an official who can invalidate or nullify [invalidator, voider]</p><p><b>obeskrijepiti, osujetiti, poništavati, poništiti, ukinuti, uništiti, dokinuti, neutralizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> declare invalid [annul, avoid, invalidate, quash, void]</p><p><i>v.</i> show to be invalid [invalidate]</p><p><i>v.</i> make ineffective by counterbalancing the effect of [negate, neutralise, neutralize]</p><p><b>(obstetrika) žena koja nikada nije rodila dijete (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (obstetrics) a woman who has never give birth to a child</p><p><b>nevaljanost, nevaženje, nevrijednost, ništa, ništavilo, nitko, nula, poništenje, ništavnost, praznina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of nonexistence [nihility, nothingness, void]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that is null (especially an enactment that has no legal validity)</p><p><b>obamro, ukočen, zanijemio, zaprepastiti, otupiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make numb or insensitive [benumb, blunt, dull]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking sensation [asleep, benumbed]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (followed by `to') not showing human feeling or sensitivity [dead]</p><p><i>adj.</i> so frightened as to be unable to move</p><p><b>mala australska marsipalija s dugim čunjem i snažnim kandžama za hranjenje termitima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Australian marsupial having long snout and strong claws for feeding on termites [Myrmecobius fasciatus, anteater, banded anteater]</p><p><b>broj, brojka, cifra, izbrojiti, izdanje, iznos, iznositi, koeficijent, količina, mnogo, mnoštvo, niz, numerirati, sadržavati, suma, velik broj, broja, brojem, broju, niza, znamenka, broj telefona, telefonski broj, vrijediti, listati, nabrajati, brojati, brojiti, izbrojati, nabrojati, nabrojiti, pobrajati, pobrojati, pobrojavati, pobrojiti, prebrojati, prebrojavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property possessed by a sum or total or indefinite quantity of units or individuals [figure]</p><p><i>n.</i> a concept of quantity involving zero and units</p><p><i>n.</i> a short performance that is part of a longer program [act, bit, routine, turn]</p><p><i>n.</i> the number is used in calling a particular telephone [phone number, telephone number]</p><p><i>n.</i> a symbol used to represent a number [numeral]</p><p><i>n.</i> one of a series published periodically [issue]</p><p><i>n.</i> a select company of people</p><p><i>n.</i> a numeral or