MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a notice of someone's death [necrology, obituary]</p><p><b>Slučajno primjedba., U slučaju u kojem je sudski sud odlučio da se odredi da se sudski sud odluči na temelju članka 107. stavka 1. točke (a) ili (b) ovog članka, sudski sud može odlučiti na temelju članka 107. stavka 1. točke (c) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an incidental remark [passing comment]</p><p><i>n.</i> an opinion voiced by a judge on a point of law not directly bearing on the case in question and therefore not binding [dictum]</p><p><b>kratak životopis, nekrolog, nekrološki, osmrtnica, posmrtni, umrlica, parta, partecetl</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a notice of someone's death [necrology, obit]</p><p><b>buniti se, cilj, cjelovit skup instrukcija i podataka, namjera, objekt, predmet, prigovarati, prigovoriti, stvar, svrha, usprotiviti se, zamjerati, objekat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tangible and visible entity [physical object]</p><p><i>n.</i> the goal intended to be attained (and which is believed to be attainable) [aim, objective, target]</p><p><i>n.</i> (grammar) a constituent that is acted upon</p><p><i>n.</i> the focus of cognitions or feelings</p><p><i>n.</i> (computing) a discrete item that provides a description of virtually anything known to a computer</p><p><i>v.</i> express or raise an objection or protest or criticism or express dissent</p><p><i>v.</i> be averse to or express disapproval of</p><p><b>biljarska lopta koja je prva lopta koju je udario kugla. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the billiard ball that is intended to be the first ball struck by the cue ball</p><p><b>objektni kod, odredišni kod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the machine-language output of a compiler that is ready for execution on a particular computer</p><p><b>objektiv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lens or system of lenses in a telescope or microscope that is nearest the object being viewed [object lens, objective, objective lens]</p><p><b>Računarski jezik na koji se treba prevesti nešto napisano na drugom računalnom jeziku., jezik na koji se treba prevesti tekst napisan na drugom jeziku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a computer language into which something written in another computer language is to be translated [target language]</p><p><i>n.</i> the language into which a text written in another language is to be translated [target language]</p><p><b>objektiv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lens or system of lenses in a telescope or microscope that is nearest the object being viewed [object glass, objective, objective lens]</p><p><b>Kazna namijenjena kao upozorenje drugima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> punishment intended as a warning to others [deterrent example, example, lesson]</p><p><b>predmet kojim se upravlja prijevjer. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the object governed by a preposition [prepositional object]</p><p><b>predmet koji prima direktno djelovanje glagola (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the object that receives the direct action of the verb [direct object]</p><p><b>objektni program</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fully compiled or assembled program ready to be loaded into the computer [target program]</p><p><b>vizualno shvaćanje poznatih predmeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the visual perception of familiar objects</p><p><b>objektno usmjerena baza podataka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a database in which the operations carried out on information items (data objects) are considered part of their definition</p><p><b>sustav upravljanja bazom podataka namijenjen upravljanju objektno orijentiranom bazom podataka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a database management system designed to manage an object-oriented database</p><p><b>stvaranje programa koji može koristiti i podržavati objekte (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creating a program that can use and support objects [object-oriented programming]</p><p><b>(računarski znanost) programski jezik koji omogućuje programeru da poveže skup postupaka s svakom vrstom strukture podataka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a programming language that enables the programmer to associate a set of procedures with each type of data structure [object-oriented programming language]</p><p><b>objektno orjentirano programiranje, objektno usmjereno programiranje, objektno orijentirano programiranje, objektno programiranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creating a program that can use and support objects [object-oriented programing]</p><p><b>objektni jezik, objektno usmjeren programski jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a programming language that enables the programmer to associate a set of procedures with each type of data structure [object-oriented programing language]</p><p><b>objektifikacija, utjelovljenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of representing an abstraction as a physical thing</p><p><i>n.</i> a concrete representation of an abstract idea or principle</p><p><b>ostvariti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make external or objective, or give reality to [exteriorise, exteriorize, externalise, externalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make impersonal or present as an object [depersonalise, depersonalize]</p><p><b>negodovanje, neodobravanje, prigovor, primjedba, protest, zamjerka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of expressing earnest opposition or protest [expostulation, remonstrance, remonstration]</p><p><i>n.</i> the speech act of objecting</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of protesting [dissent, protest]</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a procedure whereby a party to a suit says that a particular line of questioning or a particular witness or a piece of evidence or other matter is improper and should not be continued and asks the court to rule on its impropriety or illegality</p><p><b>nepoželjan, neprijatan, neugodan, odvratan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing disapproval or protest [obnoxious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> liable to objection or debate [exceptionable]</p><p><b>nepoželjan, neprijatan, neugodan (od &quot;objectionable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being hateful [hatefulness, obnoxiousness]</p><p><b>Na neprijatan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an obnoxious manner [obnoxiously, offensively]</p><p><b>bez predrasuda, cilj, cilju, nepristran, objektiv, objektivan, padež objekta, pravičan, realan, smjer, stvaran, svrha</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the goal intended to be attained (and which is believed to be attainable) [aim, object, target]</p><p><i>n.</i> the lens or system of lenses in a telescope or microscope that is nearest the object being viewed [object glass, object lens, objective lens]</p><p><i>adj.</i> undistorted by emotion or personal bias [nonsubjective]</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving as or indicating the object of a verb or of certain prepositions and used for certain other purposes [accusative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> emphasizing or expressing things as perceived without distortion of personal feelings or interpretation</p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to immediate experience of actual things or events</p><p><b>akuzativ</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the case of nouns serving as the direct object of a verb [accusative, accusative case]</p><p><b>objektiv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lens or system of lenses in a telescope or microscope that is nearest the object being viewed [object glass, object lens, objective]</p><p><b>objektivno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with objectivity</p><p><b>bez predrasuda, cilj, cilju, nepristran, objektiv, objektivan, padež objekta, pravičan, realan, smjer, stvaran, svrha (od &quot;objective&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> judgment based on observable phenomena and uninfluenced by emotions or personal prejudices [objectivity]</p><p><b>objektivnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> judgment based on observable phenomena and uninfluenced by emotions or personal prejudices [objectiveness]</p><p><b>disident</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who dissents from some established policy [contestant, dissenter, dissident, protester]</p><p><b>umjetničko djelo neke umjetničke vrijednosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a work of art of some artistic value [art object, piece]</p><p><b>kuditi, prigovarati, osuditi, ozloglasiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> express strong disapproval of [condemn, decry, excoriate, reprobate]</p><p><i>v.</i> censure severely [castigate, chasten, chastise, correct]</p><p><b>karanje, prekorijevanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rebuking a person harshly [chiding, scolding, tongue-lashing]</p><p><b>list s okruglim vrhom i konicnom podlozom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a leaf having a rounded apex and tapering base</p><p><b>laika posvećenom vjerskoj djelatnosti ili vjerskoj životu, s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lay person dedicated to religious work or the religious life</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the equatorial diameter greater than the polar diameter [pumpkin-shaped]</p><p><b>svojstvo okruglog oblika koji je ravnan na polovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property possessed by a round shape that is flattened at the poles [ellipticity]</p><p><b>dar, prinošenje žrtve, žrtva, žrtvovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of contributing to the funds of a church or charity [offering]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of offering the bread and wine of the Eucharist [religious offering]</p><p><b>obavezan, obavezati, prisiliti, natjerati, natjeravati, obvezati, obvezivati, primorati, primoravati, prinuditi, prisiljavati, siliti, tjerati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> force somebody to do something [compel, oblige]</p><p><i>v.</i> commit in order to fulfill an obligation</p><p><i>v.</i> bind by an obligation [bind, hold, oblige]</p><p><i>adj.</i> restricted to a particular condition of life</p><p><b>organizam koji ne može rasti u prisutnosti kisika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organism that cannot grow in the presence of oxygen</p><p><b>obavezan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> caused by law or conscience to follow a certain course</p><p><b>činidba, dužnost, obaveza, obećanje, obligacija, obveza, obvezom, obvezu, prinuda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the social force that binds you to the courses of action demanded by that force [duty, responsibility]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being obligated to do or pay something</p><p><i>n.</i> a personal relation in which one is indebted for a service or favor [indebtedness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a written promise to repay a debt [certificate of indebtedness, debt instrument]</p><p><i>n.</i> a legal agreement specifying a payment or action and the penalty for failure to comply</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, države članice mogu odrediti da se u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom (b) ovog članka: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating or constituting or qualified to create a legal or financial obligation</p><p><b>trajni ali podređeni motiv, dio glazbene partiture koji se mora izvoditi bez promjena ili izostavljanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a persistent but subordinate motif [obbligato]</p><p><i>n.</i> a part of the score that must be performed without change or omission [obbligato]</p><p><b>koji primorava, obavezan, obvezatan, obvezatnu, obvezno (od &quot;obligatory&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an obligatory manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a manner that cannot be evaded [compulsorily, mandatorily]</p><p><b>koji primorava, obavezan, obvezatan, obvezatnu, obvezno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> morally or legally constraining or binding</p><p><i>adj.</i> required by obligation or compulsion or convention</p><p><b>obavezati, obvezati, primorati, prinuditi, učiniti uslugu, zadužiti, natjerati, natjeravati, obvezivati, primoravati, prisiliti, prisiljavati, siliti, tjerati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> force somebody to do something [compel, obligate]</p><p><i>v.</i> bind by an obligation [bind, hold, obligate]</p><p><i>v.</i> provide a service or favor for someone [accommodate]</p><p><b>dužan, obvezan, obvezna, vezan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> under a moral obligation to do something [duty-bound]</p><p><b>obavezati, obvezati, primorati, prinuditi, učiniti uslugu, zadužiti (od &quot;oblige&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who performs a service or does a favor [accommodator]</p><p><b>ljubazan, učtiv, uslužan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing a cheerful willingness to do favors for others [complaisant]</p><p><b>ljubazan, učtiv, uslužan (od &quot;obliging&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in accommodation [accommodatingly]</p><p><b>ljubazan, učtiv, uslužan (od &quot;obliging&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition or tendency to yield to the will of others [complaisance, compliance, compliancy, deference]</p><p><b>kos, kosa linija, kosi, nakrivljen, neiskren, neupravan, posredan, prikriven, skretati u stranu, zaobilazan, zavisan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any grammatical case other than the nominative [oblique case]</p><p><i>n.</i> a diagonally arranged abdominal muscle on either side of the torso [abdominal external oblique muscle, external oblique muscle, musculus obliquus externus abdominis]</p><p><i>adj.</i> slanting or inclined in direction or course or position--neither parallel nor perpendicular nor right-angled</p><p><i>adj.</i> indirect in departing from the accepted or proper way [devious]</p><p><b>kut koji nije pravougaoni kut ili višestruki pravougaoni kut (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an angle that is not a right angle or a multiple of a right angle</p><p><b>zavoj u kojem se uzastopni okretovi provode naklonno gore ili dolje po udovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bandage in which successive turns proceed obliquely up or down a limb</p><p><b>bilo koji gramatčki slučaj osim nominativnog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any grammatical case other than the nominative [oblique]</p><p><b>trougao koji ne sadrži pravougaoni ugao (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a triangle that contains no right angle</p><p><b>prijemnik koronarnog sinususa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the coronary sinus [vena obliqua atrii sinistri]</p><p><b>s visokom visinom od 0,01 mm ili većom od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having oblique angles</p><p><b>u nepravocrtnoj liniji</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to, toward or at one side [sidelong, sideways]</p><p><i>adv.</i> at an oblique angle [aslant, athwart]</p><p><b>kos, kosa linija, kosi, nakrivljen, neiskren, neupravan, posredan, prikriven, skretati u stranu, zaobilazan, zavisan (od &quot;oblique&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being neither parallel nor perpendicular, but at a slanting angle</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being oblique and rambling indirectly [deviousness]</p><p><b>zabluda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the presentation during labor of the head of the fetus at an abnormal angle [asynclitism]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being deceptive [deceptiveness]</p><p><b>Moguće je potpuno uništiti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to be obliterated completely [removable]</p><p><b>odstraniti, precrtavati, uništiti, zataškati, zbrisati, brisati, izbrisati, likvidirati, maknuti, micati, odstranjivati, uklanjati, ukloniti, tajiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> mark for deletion, rub off, or erase [kill, wipe out]</p><p><i>v.</i> make undecipherable or imperceptible by obscuring or concealing [blot out, hide, obscure, veil]</p><p><i>v.</i> remove completely from recognition or memory [efface]</p><p><i>v.</i> do away with completely, without leaving a trace</p><p><i>adj.</i> reduced to nothingness [blotted out, obliterated]</p><p><b>Smanjen na ništa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> reduced to nothingness [blotted out, obliterate]</p><p><b>uništenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> destruction by annihilating something [annihilation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the complete destruction of every trace of something [eradication]</p><p><b>Eliminator koji uklanja sve tragove. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an eliminator that does away with all traces</p><p><b>oproštaj, zaborav, zaboravnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being disregarded or forgotten [limbo]</p><p><i>n.</i> total forgetfulness [obliviousness]</p><p><b>koji slabo pamti, zaboravan, zaboravljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (followed by `to' or `of') lacking conscious awareness of [unmindful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> failing to keep in mind [forgetful]</p><p><b>zaboravnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> total forgetfulness [oblivion]</p><p><b>dugoljast, duguljast, izduženog oblik, pravokutnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plane figure that deviates from a square or circle due to elongation</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a leaf shape) having a somewhat elongated form with approximately parallel sides</p><p><i>adj.</i> deviating from a square or circle or sphere by being elongated in one direction</p><p><b>Jednostavan list koji je okrugljen na svakom kraju s paralelnim stranama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a simple leaf that is rounded at each end with parallel sides</p><p><b>Woodsia ilvensis, crvenkasta vudsija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common rock-inhabiting fern of northern temperate regions having rusty-brown stipes and lanceolate pinnate fronds [Woodsia ilvensis, fragrant woodsia, rusty woodsia]</p><p><b>dugoljast, duguljast, izduženog oblik (od &quot;oblong&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being shaped like a rectangle [rectangularity]</p><p><b>kleveta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> state of disgrace resulting from public abuse [opprobrium]</p><p><i>n.</i> a false accusation of an offense or a malicious misrepresentation of someone's words or actions [calumniation, calumny, defamation, hatchet job, traducement]</p><p><b>antipatičan, mrzak, nepodnošljiv, odvratan, omražen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing disapproval or protest [objectionable]</p><p><b>antipatičan, mrzak, nepodnošljiv, odvratan, omražen (od &quot;obnoxious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an obnoxious manner [objectionably, offensively]</p><p><b>antipatičan, mrzak, nepodnošljiv, odvratan, omražen (od &quot;obnoxious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being hateful [hatefulness, objectionableness]</p><p><b>pomračiti, pomračivati, pomutiti, pomućivati, zamagliti, zamagljivati, zamračiti, zamračivati, zamutiti, zamućivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make less visible or unclear [becloud, befog, cloud, fog, haze over, mist, obscure]</p><p><i>v.</i> make unclear, indistinct, or blurred [blur, confuse, obscure]</p><p><b>oboa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slender double-reed instrument [hautbois, hautboy]</p><p><b>oboe je bio na nižoj visini od običnog oboea. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oboe pitched a minor third lower than the ordinary oboe</p><p><b>alt oboe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alto oboe</p><p><b>glazbenik koji svira oboe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musician who plays the oboe</p><p><b>grčka jedinica težine jednaka jednoj desetini grama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Greek unit of weight equal to one tenth of a gram</p><p><b>(oblik lišća) u obliku jaja s uskim krajem na dnu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a leaf shape) egg-shaped with the narrower end at the base</p><p><b>list u obliku jaja s uskim krajem na dnu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an egg-shaped leaf with the narrower end at the base</p><p><b>bestidan, nepristojan, odvratan, opscen, razvratan, sramotan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> designed to incite to indecency or lust</p><p><i>adj.</i> offensive to the mind [abhorrent, detestable, repugnant, repulsive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> suggestive of or tending to moral looseness [lewd, raunchy, salacious]</p><p><b>bestidan, nepristojan, odvratan, opscen, razvratan, sramotan (od &quot;obscene&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to an obscene degree</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a lewd and obscene manner [lewdly]</p><p><b>bludnost, nepristojnost, opscenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of behaving in an obscene manner [bawdiness, lewdness, salaciousness, salacity]</p><p><i>n.</i> an offensive or indecent word or phrase [dirty word, filth, smut, vulgarism]</p><p><i>n.</i> an obscene act</p><p><b>politika protivljenja prosvjetljenju ili širenju znanja, namjerno djelo namijenjeno da nešto nejasno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a policy of opposition to enlightenment or the spread of knowledge</p><p><i>n.</i> a deliberate act intended to make something obscure</p><p><b>Osoba koja je namjerno nejasna. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is deliberately vague</p><p><b>mračan, mrak, mutan, nejasan, neopažen, nepoznat, neprimjetan, neshvatljiv, taman, zamračiti, pomračiti, pomračivati, pomutiti, pomućivati, zamagliti, zamagljivati, zamračivati, zamutiti, zamućivati, tajiti, zataškati, nepriznat</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make less visible or unclear [becloud, befog, cloud, fog, haze over, mist, obnubilate]</p><p><i>v.</i> make unclear, indistinct, or blurred [blur, confuse, obnubilate]</p><p><i>v.</i> make obscure or unclear [bedim, overcloud]</p><p><i>v.</i> reduce a vowel to a neutral one, such as a schwa</p><p><i>v.</i> make undecipherable or imperceptible by obscuring or concealing [blot out, hide, obliterate, veil]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not clearly expressed or understood [vague]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by difficulty of style or expression [dark]</p><p><i>adj.</i> difficult to find [hidden]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not famous or acclaimed [unknown, unsung]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not drawing attention [unnoticeable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> remote and separate physically or socially [apart, isolated]</p><p><b>mračan, mrak, mutan, nejasan, neopažen, nepoznat, neprimjetan, neshvatljiv, taman, zamračiti (od &quot;obscure&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an obscure manner</p><p><b>mračan, mrak, mutan, nejasan, neopažen, nepoznat, neprimjetan, neshvatljiv, taman, zamračiti (od &quot;obscure&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being humble and unimportant [humbleness, lowliness, unimportance]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being indistinct or indefinite for lack of adequate illumination [obscurity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being unclear or abstruse and hard to understand [abstruseness, obscurity, reconditeness]</p><p><b>mrak, nejasnoća, nepoznatost, nerazgovjetnost, tama, zabitnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being unclear or abstruse and hard to understand [abstruseness, obscureness, reconditeness]</p><p><i>n.</i> an obscure and unimportant standing</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being indistinct or indefinite for lack of adequate illumination [obscureness]</p><p><b>ponizan, pretjerano uslužan, ulagivački</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> attempting to win favor from influential people by flattery [bootlicking, fawning, sycophantic, toadyish]</p><p><i>adj.</i> attentive in an ingratiating or servile manner</p><p><b>ponizan, pretjerano uslužan, ulagivački (od &quot;obsequious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an obsequious manner [servilely, subserviently]</p><p><b>ponizan, pretjerano uslužan, ulagivački (od &quot;obsequious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abject or cringing submissiveness [servility, subservience]</p><p><b>pogreb, sprovod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ceremony at which a dead person is buried or cremated [funeral]</p><p><b>vidljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being seen or noticed [discernible, evident]</p><p><b>na primjetan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a noticeable manner [noticeably, perceptibly]</p><p><b>čuvanje, običaj, obred, održavanje, pridržavanje, propis, ceremonija, svečanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of observing [observation, watching]</p><p><i>n.</i> a formal event performed on a special occasion [ceremonial, ceremonial occasion, ceremony]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of noticing or paying attention [notice, observation]</p><p><i>n.</i> conformity with law or custom or practice etc. [honoring]</p><p><b>pažljiv, promatrački, pronicljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> paying close attention especially to details</p><p><i>adj.</i> quick to notice [observing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of individuals) adhering strictly to laws and rules and customs [law-abiding]</p><p><b>pažljiv, promatrački, pronicljiv (od &quot;observant&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an observant manner [observingly]</p><p><b>moć opažaja, moć promatranja, motrenje, opažanje, opažanje nebeskih tijela, prigovor, primjedba, promatranje, pronicljivost, opservacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making and recording a measurement</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of observing [observance, watching]</p><p><i>n.</i> a remark expressing careful consideration [reflection, reflexion]</p><p><i>n.</i> facts learned by observing</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of noticing or paying attention [notice, observance]</p><p><b>promatrač koji se sastoji od opservatorije u obliku kupole (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lookout consisting of a dome-shaped observatory</p><p><b>osmatračnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elevated post affording a wide view [lookout]</p><p><b>Stanica postavljena za praćenje nečega. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a station set up for making observations of something</p><p><b>objekat koji ima širok pogled na okolinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a structure commanding a wide view of its surroundings [lookout, lookout station, observatory]</p><p><b>opažački, pronicljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relying on observation or experiment [data-based, experimental]</p><p><b>opservatorij, opservatorija, osmatračnica, zvjezdarnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a building designed and equipped to observe astronomical phenomena</p><p><i>n.</i> a structure commanding a wide view of its surroundings [lookout, lookout station, observation tower]</p><p><b>čuvati, motriti, napominjati, opažati, paziti, pažljivo promatrati, poštuju, pratiti nešto, pridržavati se, promatrati, proslavljati, proučavati, razgledati, stavljati primjedbe, zapaziti, slediti, slijediti, opservirati, detektirati, konstatirati, nalaziti, naći, opaziti, otkriti, otkrivati, primijetiti, primjećivati, pronalaziti, pronaći, utvrditi, utvrđivati, zamijetiti, zamjećivati, zapažati, komentirati, napomenuti, navesti, navoditi, pripomenuti, pripominjati, spomenuti, spominjati, praznovati, slaviti, gledati, pratiti, pripaziti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> discover or determine the existence, presence, or fact of [detect, discover, find, notice]</p><p><i>v.</i> make mention of [mention, note, remark]</p><p><i>v.</i> observe with care or pay close attention to [note, take note]</p><p><i>v.</i> watch attentively</p><p><i>v.</i> show respect towards [abide by, honor, honour, respect]</p><p><i>v.</i> behave as expected during of holidays or rites [celebrate, keep]</p><p><i>v.</i> follow with the eyes or the mind [follow, keep an eye on, watch, watch over]</p><p><i>v.</i> stick to correctly or closely [keep, maintain]</p><p><i>v.</i> conform one's action or practice to [keep]</p><p><b>uočen, vidljivo</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> discovered or determined by scientific observation [ascertained, discovered]</p><p><b>U slučaju požara u kojem je mjesto udarca (izbijanje) vidljivo promatraču. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fire for which the point of impact (the burst) can be seen by an observer</p><p><b>gledatelj, koji pridržava, opažač, osmatrač, pisac pregleda, promatrač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who becomes aware (of things or events) through the senses [beholder, perceiver, percipient]</p><p><i>n.</i> an expert who observes and comments on something [commentator]</p><p><b>Meridijan koji prolazi kroz zenit promatrača. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a meridian that passes through the observer's zenith</p><p><b>koji opaža, koji se drži nečega, pažljiv, pomnjiv, promatrački</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> quick to notice [observant]</p><p><b>promatrački</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an observant manner [observantly]</p><p><b>obuzimati, proganjati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> haunt like a ghost [ghost, haunt]</p><p><i>v.</i> be preoccupied with something</p><p><b>opsjednut</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing excessive or compulsive concern with something [haunted, preoccupied, taken up]</p><p><i>adj.</i> influenced or controlled by a powerful force such as a strong emotion [possessed]</p><p><b>dodijavanje, dosada, fiksna ideja, napast, opsesija, opsjednutost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an irrational motive for performing trivial or repetitive actions, even against your will [compulsion]</p><p><i>n.</i> an unhealthy and compulsive preoccupation with something or someone [fixation]</p><p><b>karakterizira ili predstavlja opsesiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by or constituting an obsession [obsessive]</p><p><b>na kompulzivan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a compulsive manner [compulsively, obsessively]</p><p><b>opsesivan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who has obsessions</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by or constituting an obsession [obsessional]</p><p><b>osoba s opsesivno-kompulzivnim karakteristikama, karakterizira opsesije i kompulzije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person with obsessive-compulsive characteristics</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by obsessions and compulsions</p><p><b>anksiozni poremećaj karakteriziran ponavljajućim i upornim mislima i osjećajima i ponavljajućim, ritualiziranim ponašanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anxiety disorder characterized by recurrent and persistent thoughts and feelings and repetitive, ritualized behaviors</p><p><b>osobnost koju karakterizira snažna potreba za ponavljanjem određenih djela ili rituala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> personality characterized by a strong need to repeat certain acts or rituals</p><p><b>opsesivan (od &quot;obsessive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a compulsive manner [compulsively, obsessionally]</p><p><b>opsesivan (od &quot;obsessive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extreme compulsiveness [obsessivity]</p><p><b>ekstremna kompulzivnost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extreme compulsiveness [obsessiveness]</p><p><b>opsidijan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acid or granitic glass formed by the rapid cooling of lava without crystallization</p><p><b>postanu zastarjele, nestaju u upotrebi (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become obsolete, fall into disuse</p><p><b>starenje, staromodnost, zastarijevanje, zastarjelost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of becoming obsolete</p><p><b>izlazi iz upotrebe, koji zastarijeva</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> becoming obsolete</p><p><b>antikan, istrošen, rudimentaran, staromodan, zastario</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> no longer in use [disused]</p><p><b>antikan, istrošen, rudimentaran, staromodan, zastario (od &quot;obsolete&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being out of date and not current [superannuation]</p><p><b>poteškoća, prepreka, smetnja, zapreka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something immaterial that stands in the way and must be circumvented or surmounted [obstruction]</p><p><i>n.</i> an obstruction that stands in the way (and must be removed or