, dim, dull, dumb, slow]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an angle between 90 and 180 degrees</p><p><b>Jednostavan list s okruglim ili tupim vrhom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a simple leaf having a rounded or blunt tip</p><p><b>trougao koji sadrži tup unutarnji kut (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a triangle that contains an obtuse interior angle [obtuse-angled triangle]</p><p><b>trougao koji sadrži tup unutarnji kut (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a triangle that contains an obtuse interior angle [obtuse triangle]</p><p><b>glup, nenaoštren, ograničen, potmuo, tup (od &quot;obtuse&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a stupid manner [densely, dumbly]</p><p><b>glup, nenaoštren, ograničen, potmuo, tup (od &quot;obtuse&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being slow to understand [dullness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of lacking a sharp edge or point</p><p><b>avers, lice, naličje, pandan, prednja strana kovanice, prednja strana zastave, prednjica, suprotnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the more conspicuous of two alternatives or cases or sides</p><p><i>n.</i> the side of a coin or medal bearing the principal stamp or design</p><p><b>izbjegavati, kloniti se, odstraniti, predusresti, ukloniti, eliminirati, odstranjivati, otklanjati, otkloniti, riješiti se, rješavati se, uklanjati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> do away with [eliminate, rid of]</p><p><i>v.</i> prevent the occurrence of [avert, avoid, debar, deflect, fend off, forefend, forfend, head off, stave off, ward off]</p><p><b>izbjegavati, kloniti se, odstraniti, predusresti, ukloniti (od &quot;obviate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made impossible [preclusive]</p><p><b>Čin sprečavanja nečeg predviđanjem i učinkovito uklanjanjem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of preventing something by anticipating and disposing of it effectively [forestalling, preclusion]</p><p><b>jasan, očevidan, očigledan, očit, razumljiv, vidan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> easily perceived by the senses or grasped by the mind</p><p><b>jasno, očigledno, očito</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> unmistakably (`plain' is often used informally for `plainly') [apparently, evidently, manifestly, patently, plain, plainly]</p><p><b>jasan, očevidan, očigledan, očit, razumljiv, vidan (od &quot;obvious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being easy to see and understand [noticeability, noticeableness, patency]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South American wood sorrel cultivated for its edible tubers [Oxalis crenata, Oxalis tuberosa, oka]</p><p><b>okarina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> egg-shaped terra cotta wind instrument with a mouthpiece and finger holes [sweet potato]</p><p><b>Engleski skolastički filozof i navodni autor Occamove brijele (1285.-1349.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English scholastic philosopher and assumed author of Occam's Razor (1285-1349) [Ockham, William of Occam, William of Ockham]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, poduzeća mogu imati: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principle that entities should not be multiplied needlessly [Ockham's Razor, law of parsimony, principle of parsimony]</p><p><b>događaj, mogućnost, navrat, okolnost, povod, prigoda, prigodni, prigodu, prilika, prouzrokovati, razlog, slučaj, zgoda, odlućujući trenutak, posebna prilika, događanje, zbivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that occurs at a critical time [juncture]</p><p><i>n.</i> a vaguely specified social event [affair, function, social function, social occasion]</p><p><i>n.</i> reason</p><p><i>n.</i> the time of a particular event</p><p><i>n.</i> an opportunity to do something</p><p><i>v.</i> give occasion to</p><p><b>okazionalan, povremen, povremene, povremene naravi, prigodan, prilagođen, rijedak, slučajan, zgodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring from time to time</p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring or appearing at usually irregular intervals [episodic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring on a temporary or irregular basis [casual]</p><p><i>adj.</i> recurring or reappearing from time to time [periodic]</p><p><b>neredovno, povremeno, slučajno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> sporadically and infrequently [at times, from time to time, now and again, now and then, on occasion, once in a while]</p><p><b>navrata, prigode</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something you have to do</p><p><b>zapad, zapadne države</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the countries of (originally) Europe and (now including) North America and South America [West]</p><p><i>n.</i> the hemisphere that includes North America and South America [New World, western hemisphere]</p><p><b>zapadni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native inhabitant of the Occident</p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial language</p><p><i>adj.</i> denoting or characteristic of countries of Europe and the western hemisphere [Hesperian]</p><p><b>Napravi ga zapadnim. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make western in character [occidentalize, westernise, westernize]</p><p><b>znanstveno znanje zapadnih kultura i jezika i ljudi, kvalitete ili običaja ili ponašanja karakteristična za zapadne civilizacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the scholarly knowledge of western cultures and languages and people</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality or customs or mannerisms characteristic of Western civilizations</p><p><b>Napravi ga zapadnim. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make western in character [occidentalise, westernise, westernize]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s osovinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the occiput</p><p><b>membranska kost u obliku tanjira koja čini stražnji dio lubanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a saucer-shaped membrane bone that forms the back of the skull</p><p><b>dio moždane kore u obje hemisfere mozga koji leži na stražnjem dijelu glave. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> that part of the cerebral cortex in either hemisphere of the brain lying in the back of the head [occipital lobe]</p><p><b>bilo koje od konvolucija vanjske površine okcipitalnog režnja mozga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the convolutions of the outer surface of the occipital lob