za održavanje sigurnog i zdravog radnog okruženja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government agency in the Department of Labor to maintain a safe and healthy work environment [OSHA]</p><p><b>Terapija koja se temelji na uključivanju u smislene aktivnosti svakodnevnog života, posebno kako bi se omogućilo ili poticalo sudjelovanje u takvim aktivnostima unatoč oštećenjima ili ograničenjima u fizičkim ili mentalnim funkcijama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> therapy based on engagement in meaningful activities of daily life, especially to enable or encourage participation in such activities in spite of impairments or limitations in physical or mental functions</p><p><b>okupiran, zauzeše, zauzet</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> held or filled or in use</p><p><i>adj.</i> seized and controlled as by military invasion</p><p><i>adj.</i> resided in [tenanted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having ones attention or mind or energy engaged [engaged]</p><p><b>okupator, stanovnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who lives at a particular place for a prolonged period or who was born there [occupant, resident]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a military force who is residing in a conquered foreign country</p><p><b>baviti se, ispunjavati, okupirati, posjedovati, zakupiti, zaokupljati, zaposjesti, zaposliti, zauzeti, zauzimati, okupirati se, zanimati se, zaposliti se, čeprkati, biti okupiran, brinuti se, nadirati, napadati, napasti, osvajati, osvojiti, zaposjedati, trebati, uzeti, uzimati, obuzeti, obuzimati, zaokupiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> keep busy with [busy]</p><p><i>v.</i> live (in a certain place) [lodge in, reside]</p><p><i>v.</i> occupy the whole of [fill]</p><p><i>v.</i> be on the mind of [concern, interest, worry]</p><p><i>v.</i> march aggressively into another's territory by military force for the purposes of conquest and occupation [invade]</p><p><i>v.</i> require (time or space) [take, use up]</p><p><i>v.</i> consume all of one's attention or time [absorb, engage, engross]</p><p><i>v.</i> assume, as of positions or role