 weight equal to about 2.75 pounds</p><p><i>n.</i> a Turkish liquid unit equal to 1.3 pints</p><p><i>n.</i> South American wood sorrel cultivated for its edible tubers [Oxalis crenata, Oxalis tuberosa, oca]</p><p><b>okapi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to the giraffe but smaller with much shorter neck and stripe on the legs [Okapia johnstoni]</p><p><b>okapi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> okapis [genus Okapia]</p><p><b>okapi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to the giraffe but smaller with much shorter neck and stripe on the legs [okapi]</p><p><b>u redu, ok, odobravati, odobriti, potvrditi, potvrđivati, pristajati, pristati, sankcionirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an endorsement [O.K., OK, okeh, okey]</p><p><i>v.</i> give sanction to [O.K., approve, sanction]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being satisfactory or in satisfactory condition [all right, cool, fine, hunky-dory, o.k., ok]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a satisfactory or adequate manner [O.K., all right, alright]</p><p><b>jezero u jugoistočnoj Floridi na sjeveru Everglades (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lake in southeast Florida to the north of the Everglades [Lake Okeechobee]</p><p><b>vodeni put kojim se male brodove prelaze između Atlantskog oceana i Meksičkog zaljeva kroz jezero Okeechobee i kanal Caloosahatchee i rijeku Caloosahatchee (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a waterway used by small boats to travel between the Atlantic Ocean and the Gulf of Mexico through Lake Okeechobee and the Caloosahatchee Canal and the Caloosahatchee River [Cross-Florida Waterway]</p><p><b>Veliki močvarni područje sjeveroistočne Floride i jugoistočne Gruzije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large swampy area of northeast Florida and southeast Georgia</p><p><b>ok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an endorsement [O.K., OK, okay, okey]</p><p><b>Njemački prirodnjak čije su nagađanja da su biljke i životinje sastavljene od sitnih živih `infusoria' dovele do teorije stanice (1779-1851) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German naturalist whose speculations that plants and animals are made up of tiny living `infusoria' led to the cell theory (1779-1851) [Lorenz Oken, Lorenz Okenfuss, Okenfuss]</p><p><b>Njemački prirodnjak čije su nagađanja da su biljke i životinje sastavljene od sitnih živih `infusoria' dovele do teorije stanice (1779-1851) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German naturalist whose speculations that plants and animals are made up of tiny living `infusoria' led to the cell theory (1779-1851) [Lorenz Oken, Lorenz Okenfuss, Oken]</p><p><b>ok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an endorsement [O.K., OK, okay, okeh]</p><p><b>Najveće otoke središnjih Ryukyu otoka, kampanja u posljednjim danima Drugog svjetskog rata u Tihom oceanu (april do lipnja 1945) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the largest island of the central Ryukyu Islands</p><p><i>n.</i> a campaign in the closing days of World War II in the Pacific (April to June 1945) [Okinawa campaign]</p><p><b>kampanja u posljednjim danima Drugog svjetskog rata u Tihom oceanu (april do lipnja 1945) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a campaign in the closing days of World War II in the Pacific (April to June 1945) [Okinawa]</p><p><b>Oklahoma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in south central United States [OK, Oklahoma, Sooner State]</p><p><b>Oklahoma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in south central United States [OK, Okla., Sooner State]</p><p><b>Glavni i najveći grad Oklahome (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capital and largest city of Oklahoma [capital of Oklahoma]</p><p><b>rodom ili prebivalištem Oklahome (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or resident of Oklahoma [Sooner]</p><p><b>bamija, okra</b></p><p><i>n.</i> long green edible beaked pods of the okra plant</p><p><i>n.</i> tall coarse annual of Old World tropics widely cultivated in southern United States and West Indies for its long mucilaginous green pods used as basis for soups and stews [Abelmoschus esculentus, Hibiscus esculentus, gumbo, lady's-finger, okra plant]</p><p><i>n.</i> long mucilaginous green pods [gumbo]</p><p><b>Visoka gruba godišnja biljka iz tropskih područja Starog svijeta, široko uzgajana u južnim Sjedinjenim Državama i Zapadnoj Indiji zbog svojih dugih mucilaginoznih zelenih čunjeva koji se koriste kao osnova za juhe i gulaš. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall coarse annual of Old World tropics widely cultivated in southern United States and West Indies for its long mucilaginous green pods used as basis for soups and stews [Abelmoschus esculentus, Hibiscus esculentus, gumbo, lady's-finger, okra]</p><p><b>jak lager napravljen u Njemačkoj za slavlje Oktoberfesta., jesen festival koji uključuje veselje i piće piva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strong lager made originally in Germany for the Oktoberfest celebration [Octoberfest]</p><p><i>n.</i> an autumn festival that involves merrymaking and drinking beer</p><p><b>list ili traka od lista palme talipot koji se u Indiji koristi za pisanje papira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leaf or strip from a leaf of the talipot palm used in India for writing paper [olla]</p><p><b>Kralj i zaštitnik Norveške (995-1030) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> King and patron saint of Norway (995-1030) [Olav II, Saint Olaf, Saint Olav, St. Olaf, St. Olav]</p><p><b>Kralj i zaštitnik Norveške (995-1030) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> King and patron saint of Norway (995-1030) [Olaf II, Saint Olaf, Saint Olav, St. Olaf, St. Olav]</p><p><b>antikan, bivši, davno prošao, drevan, nekadašnji, star, starački, starinski, vremešan, godine, pređašnji, stare, stari, starih, starim, starinskih, staro, starog, staroga, starom, velik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> past times (especially in the phrase `in days of old')</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used especially of persons) having lived for a relatively long time or attained a specific age</p><p><i>adj.</i> of long duration</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used for emphasis) very familiar</p><p><i>adj.</i> skilled through long experience [older]</p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to some prior time [erstwhile, former, one-time, onetime, quondam, sometime]</p><p><i>adj.</i> very good [bang-up, bully, corking, cracking, dandy, great, groovy, keen, neat, nifty, not bad, peachy, slap-up, smashing, swell]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a very early stage in development</p><p><i>adj.</i> just preceding something else in time or order [previous]</p><p><b>starija dob, starost, starosti, kasne godine života, staračka dob, starije godine, treća dob</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a late time of life [age, eld, geezerhood, years]</p><p><b>ružna ili razdražljiva žena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ugly or ill-tempered woman [bag]</p><p><b>Centralni kazneno sud u Londonu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the central criminal court in London</p><p><b>poznati izraz za čovjeka., Živopisni stariji čovjek., bivši muški učenik škole (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a familiar term of address for a man [old man]</p><p><i>n.</i> a vivacious elderly man</p><p><i>n.</i> a former male pupil of a school</p><p><b>ekskluzivna neformalna mreža koja povezuje članove društvene klase ili profesije ili organizacije kako bi se osigurale veze i informacije i usluge (posebno u poslovanju ili politici) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an exclusive informal network linking members of a social class or profession or organization in order to provide connections and information and favors (especially in business or politics)</p><p><b>slovenački jezik na koji je Biblija prevedena u 9. stoljeću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Slavic language into which the Bible was translated in the 9th century [Church Slavic, Old Church Slavic, Old Church Slavonic]</p><p><b>Zakonotvornik Sjedinjenih Država koji se protivio korištenju papirnate valute (1782-1858) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States legislator who opposed the use of paper currency (1782-1858) [Benton, Thomas Hart Benton]</p><p><b>član crkve koju su u 19. stoljeću osnovali njemački katolici koji su odbili prihvatiti nepogrešivost pape. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the church formed in the 19th century by German Catholics who refused to accept the infallibility of the Pope</p><p><b>Katoličke crkve koje su se odvojile od rimokatoličke crkve u 18. stoljeću (MT)</b></p><p><i>