<p><i>n.</i> the oldest recorded Latin (dating back at early as the 6th century B.C.)</p><p><b>država u srednjem Atlantiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Mid-Atlantic state [Free State, MD, Maryland, Md.]</p><p><b>Stara neudana žena., bilo koja biljka iz roda Zinnia uzgajana zbog svojih različitih i svijetle obojenih cvjetnica, obično uzgajana drvena biljka iz Starog svijeta s velikim ružičastim do crvenim cvijećem, gubitnik u igri stare djevojke., igra karata s pakom karata iz kojeg je uklonjena jedna kraljica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elderly unmarried woman [spinster]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Zinnia cultivated for their variously and brightly colored flower heads [old maid flower, zinnia]</p><p><i>n.</i> commonly cultivated Old World woody herb having large pinkish to red flowers [Cape periwinkle, Catharanthus roseus, Madagascar periwinkle, Vinca rosea, cayenne jasmine, periwinkle, red periwinkle, rose periwinkle]</p><p><i>n.</i> the loser in a game of old maid</p><p><i>n.</i> a card game using a pack of cards from which one queen has been removed</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka iz roda Zinnia uzgajana zbog svojih različitih i svijetle obojenih cvjetnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Zinnia cultivated for their variously and brightly colored flower heads [old maid, zinnia]</p><p><b>otac, starac, starček, stari, suprug, pelin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who is very old [Methuselah, graybeard, greybeard]</p><p><i>n.</i> a familiar term of address for a man [old boy]</p><p><i>n.</i> an informal term for your father</p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic herb of temperate Eurasia and North Africa having a bitter taste used in making the liqueur absinthe [Artemisia absinthium, absinthe, common wormwood, lad's love]</p><p><i>n.</i> (slang) boss</p><p><b>bijela kosa sa perjavim lišcima i nekoliko čvrstih stabljika s posebno lijepim jednim velikim žutim cvjetnim glavom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> whitish hairy plant with featherlike leaves and a few stout stems each bearing an especially handsome solitary large yellow flower head [Hymenoxys grandiflora, Tetraneuris grandiflora, alpine sunflower]</p><p><b>pavitina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dense festoons of greenish-grey hairlike flexuous strands anchored to tree trunks and branches by sparse wiry roots [Spanish moss, Tillandsia usneoides, black moss, long moss]</p><p><i>n.</i> vigorous deciduous climber of Europe to Afghanistan and Lebanon having panicles of fragrant green-white flowers in summer and autumn [Clematis vitalba, traveler's joy, traveller's joy]</p><p><i>n.</i> common climber of eastern North America that sprawls over other plants and bears numerous panicles of small creamy white flowers [Clematis virginiana, devil's darning needle, virgin's bower]</p><p><b>Veliki europski slikar prije 19. stoljeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a great European painter prior to 19th century</p><p><b>nasljedno bogatstvo uspostavljenih obitelji gornje klase. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inherited wealth of established upper-class families [silver spoon]</p><p><b>(Judao-kršćanske i islamske religije) glavni duh zla i protivnik Boga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judeo-Christian and Islamic religions) chief spirit of evil and adversary of God [Beelzebub, Devil, Lucifer, Prince of Darkness, Satan, the Tempter]</p><p><b>izumrli germanski jezik srednjovjekovne Skandinavije i Islanda od oko 700 do 1350 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the extinct Germanic language of medieval Scandinavia and Iceland from about to 700 to 1350</p><p><b>srednjovjekovni normanski dijalekt starog francuskog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the medieval Norman dialect of Old French [Norman-French, Norman French]</p><p><b>država u jugoistočnim Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in southeastern United States [N.C., NC, North Carolina, Tar Heel State]</p><p><b>stara osoba, starac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elderly person [golden ager, oldster, senior citizen]</p><p><b>mrtvi jezik (ne-njemačkog) Prusaca (iz