iji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Dravidian language spoken in south central India</p><p><b>čovječja ribica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European aquatic salamander with permanent external gills that lives in caves [Proteus anguinus]</p><p><b>član rane mezoameričke civilizacije koja se usredotočila oko Veracruza koja je procvjetala između 1300. i 400. godine prije Krista. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of an early Mesoamerican civilization centered around Veracruz that flourished between 1300 and 400 BC</p><p><b>Američki pejzažni arhitekta, odgovoran za dizajn Central Parka u New Yorku (1822-1903) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States landscape architect primarily responsible for the design of Central Park in New York City (1822-1903) [Frederick Law Olmsted]</p><p><b>neformalna riječ (abstrakt od riječi s ovim završetkom) za neku neidentificiranu granicu znanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an informal word (abstracted from words with this ending) for some unidentified branch of knowledge</p><p><b>Glavni grad države Washington, ravnica u Grčkoj u sjeverozapadnom Peloponezu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capital of the state of Washington [capital of Washington]</p><p><i>n.</i> a plain in Greece in the northwestern Peloponnese</p><p><b>olimpijada, Olimpijske igre</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the four-year intervals between Olympic Games</p><p><i>n.</i> the modern revival of the ancient games held once every 4 years in a selected country [Olympic Games, Olympics]</p><p><b>olimpijski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an athlete who participates in the Olympic games</p><p><i>n.</i> a classical Greek god after the overthrow of the Titans [Olympic god]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of the region of Olympia in Greece or its inhabitants [Olympic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to the greater gods of ancient Greece whose abode was Mount Olympus</p><p><i>adj.</i> majestic in manner or bearing [majestic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> far beyond what is usual in magnitude or degree [exceeding, exceptional, prodigious, surpassing]</