iki raznolik red vodenih ptica koji se nalaze uz obalu mora i unutarnjih voda: ptice na obali i ptice na obali koje se rone (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large diverse order of aquatic birds found along seacoasts and inland waters: shorebirds and coastal diving birds [Charadriiformes]</p><p><b>mali red makroskopskih slatkovodnih i slanih vodenih algi s razlikom osovine: kamenčari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small order of macroscopic fresh and brackish water algae with a distinct axis: stoneworts [Charales]</p><p><b>lažni škorpioni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> false scorpions [Chelonethida, Pseudoscorpiones, Pseudoscorpionida, order Pseudoscorpiones, order Pseudoscorpionida]</p><p><b>Urezi za uzgoj i uzgoj hrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tortoises and turtles [Chelonia, Testudinata, Testudines, order Testudinata, order Testudines]</p><p><b>stari red koji datira iz ranog eocena: šišmiši: podred Megachiroptera (voćni šišmiši) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an old order dating to early Eocene: bats: suborder Megachiroptera (fruit bats) [Chiroptera]</p><p><b>Jednobunčane zelene alge koje se razmnožavaju sporama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unicellular green algae that reproduce by spores [Chlorococcales]</p><p><b>jednostavne vodene gljive uglavnom saprofitne, ali neke parazitne na višim biljkama ili životinjama ili slatkovodnim gljivima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> simple aquatic fungi mostly saprophytic but some parasitic on higher plants or animals or fresh water fungi [Chytridiales]</p><p><b>red uglavnom tropskih močvarnih riboljudnih vodenjaka s dugim nogama i kljunom i (osim flaminga) bez mrežastih nogu: čvrstice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> order of chiefly tropical marsh-dwelling fish-eating wading birds with long legs and bills and (except for flamingos) unwebbed feet: herons [Ciconiiformes]</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama smatra se filom kraljevstva Protista (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications considered a phylum of the kingdom Protista [Cilioflagellata, Dinoflagellata, order D