ima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chronic breakdown of cartilage in the joints [degenerative arthritis, degenerative joint disease]</p><p><b>stanica iz koje se razvije kost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cell from which bone develops [bone-forming cell]</p><p><b>benigni tumor kostiju i vlaknastog tkiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> benign tumor of bone and fibrous tissue</p><p><b>benigni tumor koji sadrži i kost i hrskavicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> benign tumor containing both bone and cartilage</p><p><b>liječenje skeletne deformacije namjernim lomom kostiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> treatment of a skeletal deformity by intentionally fracturing a bone</p><p><b>osteoklast</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cell that functions in the breakdown and resorption of bone tissue</p><p><b>zrele stanice kostiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mature bone cell</p><p><b>nepravilan razvoj kostiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> defective bone development</p><p><b>autosomno dominantno poremećaj vezivnog tkiva karakteriziran krhkim kostima koje se lako lomljaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> autosomal dominant disorder of connective tissue characterized by brittle bones that fracture easily</p><p><b>maligni tumor kostiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> malignant bone tumor [osteosarcoma]</p><p><b>obitelj velikih riba koje žive u slatkoj vodi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of large fishes that live in freshwater [family Osteoglossidae]</p><p><b>Teleost riba s kostim jezikom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> teleost fish with bony tongues [Order Osteoglossiformes]</p><p><b>anatom koji je stručan u osteologiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anatomist who is skilled is osteology [osteologist]</p><p><b>anatom koji je stručan u osteologiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anatomist who is skilled is osteology [osteologer]</p><p><b>osteologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of anatomy that studies the bones of the vertebrate skeleton</p><p><b>liza kostiju uzrokovana bolestima ili infekcijama ili nedostatkom krvnog opskrbe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lysis of b