ive containing mestranol and a progestin compound</p><p><b>jaje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the female reproductive cell [egg cell]</p><p><b>biti dužan, biti obavezan, dugovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be obliged to pay or repay</p><p><i>v.</i> be indebted to, in an abstract or intellectual sense</p><p><i>v.</i> be in debt</p><p><b>Owen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Welsh industrialist and social reformer who founded cooperative communities (1771-1858) [Robert Owen]</p><p><i>n.</i> English comparative anatomist and paleontologist who was an opponent of Darwinism (1804-1892) [Sir Richard Owen]</p><p><b>Velški poglavica koji je predvodio pobunu protiv vladavine Henrija IV. u Walesu (1359-1416) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Welsh chieftain who led a revolt against Henry IV's rule in Wales (1359-1416) [Glendower]</p><p><b>Američki pisac (1860-1938) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer (1860-1938) [Wister]</p><p><b>Jesse Owens</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States athlete and Black American whose success in the 1936 Olympic Games in Berlin outraged Hitler (1913-1980) [James Cleveland Owens, Jesse Owens]</p><p><b>grad u sjeverozapadnom Kentuckyju na rijeci Ohio (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in northwestern Kentucky on the Ohio River</p><p><b>dužan, uslijed, zadužen, zahvaljujući, zbog</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> owed as a debt [outstanding, undischarged]</p><p><b>buljina, sova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nocturnal bird of prey with hawk-like beak and claws and large head with front-facing eyes [bird of Minerva, bird of night, hooter]</p><p><b>čvrsta višegodišnja biljka zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s cvjetnim glavama s spuštenicama narandžastih žutih zraka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stout perennial herb of western United States having flower heads with drooping orange-yellow rays [Helenium hoopesii, orange sneezeweed]</p><p><b>mlada sova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> young owl</p><p><b>Obično tamno obojeni noćni molj srednje veličine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> usually dull-colored medium-sized nocturnal moth [noctuid, noc