 meridian west [PST, Pacific Time]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za životinje iz područja iz članka 1. stavka 1. točke (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje članak 2. točka (a) ovog članka, za životinje iz područja iz članka 1. stavka 2. točke (b) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje članak 2. točka (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> food and game fish of marine and fresh waters of northwestern coast of North America [Acipenser transmontanus, Sacramento sturgeon, white sturgeon]</p><p><b>standardno vrijeme u 8. vremenskoj zoni zapadno od Greenwicha, izračunato na 120-om meridijanu zapadno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> standard time in the 8th time zone west of Greenwich, reckoned at the 120th meridian west [PST, Pacific Standard Time]</p><p><b>najčešće čuvana žaba na pacifičkoj obali Amerike. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the most commonly heard frog on the Pacific coast of America [Hyla regilla]</p><p><b>Tripletail pronađen u Pacifiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tripletail found in the Pacific [Lobotes pacificus]</p><p><b>morsa iz Beringovog mora i sjevernog Tihog oceana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a walrus of the Bering Sea and northern Pacific [Odobenus divergens]</p><p><b>mala ili srednja nepravilno razgranata stabla na pacifičkoj obali Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small or medium irregularly branched tree of the Pacific coast of North America [California yew, Taxus brevifolia, western yew]</p><p><b>na miran način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a peaceable manner [peaceably]</p><p><b>pacifikacija, smirivanje, umirenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of appeasing someone or causing someone to be more favorably inclined [mollification]</p><p><i>n.</i> a treaty to cease hostilities [peace, peace treaty]</p><p><i>n.</i> actions taken by a government to defeat insurgency [counterinsurgency]</p><p><b>Nauka da je sva nasilje neopravdano, vjerovanje da se svi međunarodni sporovi mogu riješiti arbitražom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine that all violence is unjustifiable [pacifism, passivism]</p><p><i>n.</i> the belief that all international disputes can be settled by arbitration [pacifism]</p><p><b>mirotvorac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone opposed to violence as a means of settling disputes [disarmer, pacifist]</p><p><b>duda, duda varalica, varalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who tries to bring peace [conciliator, make-peace, peacemaker, reconciler]</p><p><i>n.</i> anything that serves to pacify</p><p><i>n.</i> device used for an infant to suck or bite on [baby's dummy, comforter, teething ring]</p><p><b>pacifizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine that all violence is unjustifiable [pacificism, passivism]</p><p><i>n.</i> the belief that all international disputes can be settled by arbitration [pacificism]</p><p><b>pacifist, pacifista, mirotvorac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone opposed to violence as a means of settling disputes [disarmer, pacificist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> opposed to war [dovish, pacifistic]</p><p><b>pacifist, pacifista (od &quot;pacifist&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> opposed to war [dovish, pacifist]</p><p><b>na miroljubiv način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a pacifistic manner</p><p><b>smiriti, stišati, umiriti, uspostaviti mir, pacificirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be more favorably inclined [appease, assuage, conciliate, gentle, gruntle, lenify, mollify, placate]</p><p><i>v.</i> fight violence and try to establish peace in (a location)</p><p><b>tempo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (music) the speed at which a composition is to be played [tempo]</p><p><i>n.</i> walking with slow regular strides</p><p><b>specijalni žaruljasti živčani završetak koji se nalazi u podkožnom tkivu kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialized bulblike nerve ending located in the subcutaneous tissue of the skin</p><p><b>bala, brtva, brtviti, čopor, denjak, družina, gomila, krdo, mnoštvo, nositi, omot, paket, pakirati, spakira