passes close to an atomic nucleus [pair creation, pair production]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hand tool for holding consisting of a compound lever for grasping [pair of tweezers, pincer, tweezer]</p><p><b>kliješta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gripping hand tool with two hinged arms and (usually) serrated jaws [pliers, plyers]</p><p><b>škare, škarice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edge tool having two crossed pivoting blades [scissors]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various devices for taking hold of objects [tongs]</p><p><b>hlače</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (usually in the plural) a garment extending from the waist to the knee or ankle, covering each leg separately [pant, trousers]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hand tool for holding consisting of a compound lever for grasping [pair of pincers, pincer, tweezer]</p><p><b>bez nogu pravougaoni klavijatur (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a legless rectangular harpsichord [virginal]</p><p><b>formiraju par ili parovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> form a pair or pairs [couple, pair, partner off]</p><p><b>transformacija gamma-zraka fotona u elektron i pozitron kada foton prolazi blizu atomskog jezgra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the transformation of a gamma-ray photon into an electron and a positron when the photon passes close to an atomic nucleus [pair creation, pair formation]</p><p><b>bračni par, dvoje, oženiti se, par, parica, razdijeliti na parove, spariti, spariti se, udati se (od &quot;pair&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring in pairs or as a pair [mated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of leaves etc [opposite]</p><p><i>adj.</i> mated sexually</p><p><b>parenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of pairing a male and female for reproductive purposes [conjugation, coupling, mating, sexual union, union]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of grouping things or people in pairs</p><p><b>frakcijska novčana jedinica u Bangladešu i Indiji i Nepalu i Pakistanu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fractional monetary unit in Bangladesh and India and Nepal and Pakistan</p><p><b>od tkanine od mekane vune s obojenim vrtoglavim uzorkom zakrivljenih oblika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soft wool fabric with a colorful swirled pattern of curved shapes</p><p><b>član jednog od dva šosonska naroda (sjeverni Paiute i južni Paiute) koji su povezani s Aztekima i žive u jugozapadnim Sjedinjenim Državama, Šosonejski jezik koji govore Paiute. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of either of two Shoshonean peoples (northern Paiute and southern Paiute) related to the Aztecs and living in the southwestern United States [Piute]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Shoshonean language spoken by the Paiute</p><p><b>Formosanski jezik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Formosan language</p><p><b>par labavih hlača vezanih za strun oko struka, (obično u množini) ručne odjeće za spavanje ili za odmaranje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pair of loose trousers tied by a drawstring around the waist [pyjama]</p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) loose-fitting nightclothes worn for sleeping or lounging [jammies, pj's, pyjama]</p><p><b>Azijska biljka koja se uzgaja zbog svog skupa jestivih bijeli stabljike s tamnozelenih lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic plant grown for its cluster of edible white stalks with dark green leaves [Brassica rapa chinensis, Chinese white cabbage, bok choi, bok choy, pakchoi]</p><p><b>Azijska biljka koja se uzgaja zbog svog skupa jestivih bijeli stabljike s tamnozelenih lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic plant grown for its cluster of edible white stalks with dark green leaves [Brassica rapa chinensis, Chinese white cabbage, bok choi, bok choy, pak choi]</p><p><b>Pakistan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Muslim republic that occupies the heartland of ancient south Asian civilization in the Indus River valley [Islamic Republic of Pakistan, West Pakistan]</p><p><b>Pakistanac, pakistanski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Pakistan</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Pakistan or its people or language</p><p><b>novčana jedinica u Pakistanu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Pakistan</p><p><b>osnovna jedinica novca u Pakistanu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Pakistan [rupee]</p><p><b>drugar, pajdaš, prijatelj, buraz, drug, frend, kompa, kompanjon, kompić, rista, sudrug</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a close friend who accompanies his buddies in their activities [brother, buddy, chum, crony, sidekick]</p><p><i>v.</i> become friends [chum up, pal up]</p><p><b>Postaju prijatelji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become friends [chum up, pal]</p><p><b>dvorac, dvorcem, palača, palačom, dvorca, dvorom, palaca, palače, palači, palaču, dvor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large and stately mansion [castle]</p><p><i>n.</i> the governing group of a kingdom</p><p><i>n.</i> a large ornate exhibition hall</p><p><i>n.</i> official residence of an exalted person (as a sovereign)</p><p><b>S druge strane, za vozila s brzinom iznad 50 km/h (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a passenger car for day travel [chair car, drawing-room car, parlor car, parlour car]</p><p><b>palača izgrađena u 17. stoljeću za Luja XIV. jugozapadno od Pariza u blizini grada Versailles (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a palace built in the 17th century for Louis XIV southwest of Paris near the city of Versailles [Versailles]</p><p><b>hrabar čovjek, paladin, vitez</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who fights for a cause [champion, fighter, hero]</p><p><b>primitivnijih dijelova mozga filogenetski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the more primitive parts of the brain phylogenetically [paleencephalon, paleoencephalon]</p><p><b>tip rod iz obitelji Palaemonidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the family Palaemonidae [genus Palaemon]</p><p><b>veliki (od 30 cm ili više) jestivi slatkovodni škampi koji su uobičajeni u australskim rijekama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large (a foot or more) edible freshwater prawn common in Australian rivers [long-clawed prawn, river prawn]</p><p><b>škampi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prawns [family Palaemonidae]</p><p><b>paleoantropologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the scientific study of human fossils [human palaeontology, human paleontology, paleoanthropology]</p><p><b>grana paleontologije koja se bavi porijeklom i rastom i strukturom fosilnih životinja i biljaka kao živih organizama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a branch of paleontology that deals with the origin and growth and structure of fossil animals and plants as living organisms [paleobiology]</p><p><b>proučavanje fosilnih biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of fossil plants [paleobotany]</p><p><b>proučavanje klime prošlih doba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of the climate of past ages [paleoclimatology]</p><p><b>grana paleobotanije koja proučava fosilna stabla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of paleobotany that studies fossil trees [paleodendrology]</p><p><b>grana ekologije koja proučava drevnu ekologiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of ecology that studies ancient ecology [paleoecology]</p><p><b>etnografija paleolitskih ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ethnography of paleolithic humans [paleoethnography]</p><p><b>proučavanje geografije drevnih vremena ili drevnih epoha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of the geography of ancient times or ancient epochs [paleogeography]</p><p><b>proučavanje geoloških obilježja koji su nekada bili na površini Zemlje, ali su sada zakopani ispod stijena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of geologic features once at the surface of the earth but now buried beneath rocks [paleogeology]</p><p><b>Drugi dio kamenog doba počinje oko 750.000 do 500.000 godina prije Krista i traje do kraja posljednjeg ledenog doba oko 8.500 godina prije Krista., od ili u vezi s drugim razdobljem kamenog doba (nakon eolita) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> second part of the Stone Age beginning about 750,000 to 500,000 years BC and lasting until the end of the last ice age about 8,500 years BC [Paleolithic, Paleolithic Age]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the second period of the Stone Age (following the eolithic) [paleolithic]</p><p><b>proučavanje (posebno praistorijskih) antikviteta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of (especially prehistoric) antiquities [paleology]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s paleontologijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to paleontology [paleontological]</p><p><b>paleontolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in paleontology [fossilist, paleontologist]</p><p><b>paleontologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the earth science that studies fossil organisms and related remains [fossilology, paleontology]</p><p><b>proučavanje bolesti iz prošlosti (kao što je zaključeno iz fosilnih dokaza) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of disease of former times (as inferred from fossil evidence) [paleopathology]</p><p><b>paleobiologija ptica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the paleobiology of birds [paleornithology]</p><p><b>proučavanje fosilnih životinja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of fossil animals [paleozoology]</p><p><b>borilište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a public place in ancient Greece or Rome devoted to the training of wrestlers and other athletes [palestra]</p><p><b>objašnjenje prošlih događaja u smislu znanstvenih uzroka (kao geološki uzroci) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the explanation of past events in terms of scientific causes (as geological causes) [paletiology]</p><p><b>Anatolijanski jezik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Anatolian language</p><p><b>nosiljka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a closed litter carried on the shoulders of four bearers [palanquin]</p><p><b>nosiljka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a closed litter carried on the shoulders of four bearers [palankeen]</p><p><b>veliki rod malezijskih stabala s mliječnim sokom i kožnim lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large genus of Malaysian trees with milky juice and leathery leaves [genus Palaquium]</p><p><b>jedno od nekoliko istočnoindijskih stabala koja daju gutta-percha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of several East Indian trees