 (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> pronounce a consonant with the tongue against the palate [palatalise]</p><p><b>proizvodi se s prednjim dijelom jezika u blizini ili dodirujući se tvrdom nepcu (kao `y') ili s čepicom jezika u blizini tvrdog nepca (kao `ch' u `chin' ili `j' u `gin') (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> produced with the front of the tongue near or touching the hard palate (as `y') or with the blade of the tongue near the hard palate (as `ch' in `chin' or `j' in `gin') [palatal, palatalised]</p><p><b>naklonost, nepce, tek, ukus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the upper surface of the mouth that separates the oral and nasal cavities [roof of the mouth]</p><p><b>carski, kao dvorac, kao zamak, raskošan, sjajan, veličanstven</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or being a palace</p><p><i>adj.</i> suitable for or like a palace</p><p><b>teritorij u jugozapadnoj Njemačkoj kojim su prije vladali grofovi palatini, teritorij pod nadležnošću grofa palatina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a territory in southwestern Germany formerly ruled by the counts palatine [Pfalz]</p><p><i>n.</i> a territory under the jurisdiction of a count palatine</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih važnih dužnosnika u starom Rimu., (Srednji vijek) gospodar palatinate koji je izvršio suverene ovlasti nad svojim zemljama, Najvažnije od Sedam brda u Rimu., ili od dvije nepravilno oblikovane kosti koje čine stražnji dio tvrdog nepca i pomažu u stvaranju nosne šupljine i podu orbita, koji se odnosi na ili leži u blizini nepca, od ili u vezi s grofa palatine i njegove kraljevske prerogative, od ili u vezi s palačom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various important officials in ancient Rome</p><p><i>n.</i> (Middle Ages) the lord of a palatinate who exercised sovereign powers over his lands [palsgrave]</p><p><i>n.</i> the most important of the Seven Hills of Rome</p><p><i>n.</i> either of two irregularly shaped bones that form the back of the hard palate and helps to form the nasal cavity and the floor of the orbits [os palatinum, palatine bone]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or lying near the palate [palatal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a count palatine and his royal prerogatives</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a palace</p><p><b>jedna od nekoliko arterija koje opskrbljuju lice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of several arteries supplying the face [arteria palatina]</p><p><b>ili od dvije nepravilno oblikovane kosti koje čine stražnji dio tvrdog nepca i pomažu u stvaranju nosne šupljine i podu orbita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two irregularly shaped bones that form the back of the hard palate and helps to form the nasal cavity and the floor of the orbits [os palatinum, palatine]</p><p><b>Šav u sredini tvrdog nepca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the seam at the middle of the hard palate</p><p><b>nepčana tonzila, tonzile</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two masses of lymphatic tissue one on each side of the oral pharynx [faucial tonsil, tonsil, tonsilla]</p><p><b>vena koja odvodjuje područje nepca i isprazni u facialnu venu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vein that drains the region of the palate and empties into the facial vein [vena palatina]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na nepce i jezik. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the palate and tongue</p><p><b>kirurško rezekcija nepotrebnog tkiva u ustima i ustima kako bi se otvorili dišni putevi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical resection of unnecessary palatal and oropharyngeal tissue to open the airway [PPP, UPPP, uvulopalatopharyngoplasty]</p><p><b>Palau</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic in the western central Pacific Ocean in association with the United States [Republic of Palau, TT]</p><p><i>n.</i> a chain of more than 200 islands about 400 miles long in the western central Pacific Ocean [Belau, Palau Islands, Pelew]</p><p><b>lzvor je niz od više od 200 otoka dug oko 400 milja u zapadnom središnjem Pacifiku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chain of more than 200 islands about 400 miles long in the western central Pacific Ocean [Belau, Palau, Pelew]</p><p><