and vines usually having a tall columnar trunk bearing a crown of very large leaves [Arecaceae, Palmaceae, family Arecaceae, family Palmaceae, family Palmae, palm family]</p><p><b>red Palmales</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coextensive with the family Palmae: palms [order Palmales]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na dlan ili podnožju stopala (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the palm of the hand or the sole of the foot [volar]</p><p><b>(od nogu vodenih ptica) sa tri prsta spojena tankim slojem kože, od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of the feet of water birds) having three toes connected by a thin fold of skin</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a leaf shape [palm-shaped]</p><p><b>list nalik otvorenoj ruci. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a leaf resembling an open hand</p><p><b>Na način koji je lak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a palmate manner</p><p><b>s masenim udubljenjem od oko 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having lobes radiating from a central point</p><p><b>od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a leaf shape</p><p><b>abnormalnost u kojoj su prsti objedinjeni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormality in which the fingers are webbed</p><p><b>dlan, lopatica, palma, palmama, palme, šaka (od &quot;palm&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States golfer (born in 1929) [Arnold Daniel Palmer, Arnold Palmer]</p><p><b>Veliki poluotok Antarktika koji se proteže oko 1200 milja sjeverno prema Južnoj Americi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large peninsula of Antarctica that extends some 1200 miles north toward South America [Antarctic Peninsula]</p><p><b>vrsta male palme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several low-growing palms with fan-shaped leaves</p><p><b>Država na dubokom jugu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in the Deep South [S.C., SC, South Carolina]</p><p><b>Predskazivač koji predviđa tvoju budućnost po linijama na tvojim dlanovima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fortuneteller who predicts your future by the lines on your palms [chiromancer, palmister]</p><p><b>Predskazivač koji predviđa tvoju bud