ijelovima Sjedinjenih Država s najozbiljnijim žutim cvijećem i plavo-zelenom koreom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> densely branched spiny tree of southwestern United States having showy yellow flowers and blue-green bark [Cercidium floridum, Parkinsonia florida]</p><p><b>manje od Florida pompano (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> smaller than Florida pompano [California pompano, Palometa simillima]</p><p><b>manje od Florida pompano (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> smaller than Florida pompano [California pompano, palometa]</p><p><b>konj svjetlo smeđe ili zlatne boje s kremasto ili bijelom grivom i repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a horse of light tan or golden color with cream-colored or white mane and tail</p><p><b>Drugi razred nagradni borac. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a second-rate prize fighter [stumblebum]</p><p><b>trnasti grm rodova Cercidium koji raste u suvim dijelovima jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i susjednog Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thorny shrub of the genus Cercidium that grows in dry parts of the southwestern United States and adjacent Mexico</p><p><b>kvaliteta osjetljivosti dodirom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being perceivable by touch [tangibility, tangibleness]</p><p><b>jasan, očevidan, opipljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being perceived [tangible]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (medicine) can be felt by palpation</p><p><i>adj.</i> clearly revealed to the mind or the senses or judgment [apparent, evident, manifest, patent, plain, unmistakable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> so intense as to be almost touched or felt</p><p><b>da bi se osjetila. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> so as to be palpable</p><p><b>opipati, opipavati, pipati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> examine (a body part) by palpation [feel]</p><p><b>palpaciji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a method of examination in which the examiner feels the size or shape or firmness or location of something (of body parts when the examiner is a health professional) [tactual exploration]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili uključuju palpaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or involving palpation</p><p><b>kapak, vjeđa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two folds of skin that can be moved to cover or open the eye [eyelid, lid]</p><p><b>dio spojeve koji obloži stražnju površinu kapaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of the conjunctiva lining the posterior surface of the eyelids [conjunctival layer of eyelids, tunica conjunctiva palpebrarum]</p><p><b>trepnuti ili trepnuti, posebno više puta, s kapcima (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> wink or blink, especially repeatedly</p><p><i>adj.</i> having eyelids</p><p><b>ponavljajuće treptanje ili treptanje (posebno ako je nekontrolisano i uporno) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> repeated blinking or winking (especially if uncontrolled and persistent)</p><p><b>s blagim i brzim drhtanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a slight and rapid trembling motion [palpitating]</p><p><b>drhtati, kucati, lupati, pulsirati, treperiti, udarati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to throb or beat rapidly</p><p><i>v.</i> shake with fast, tremulous movements [quake, quiver]</p><p><i>v.</i> beat rapidly [flutter]</p><p><b>drhtati, kucati, lupati, pulsirati, treperiti, udarati (od &quot;palpitate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a slight and rapid trembling motion [palpitant]</p><p><b>drhtanje, kucanje, lupanje srca, palpatorni, treperenje, udaranje, palpitacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rapid and irregular heart beat</p><p><i>n.</i> a shaky motion [quiver, quivering, shakiness, shaking, trembling, vibration]</p><p><b>(Srednji vijek) gospodar palatinate koji je izvršio suverene ovlasti nad svojim zemljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Middle Ages) the lord of a palatinate who exercised sovereign powers over his lands [palatine]</p><p><b>paraliziran, ukočen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affected with palsy or uncontrollable tremor</p><p><b>oduzeti, oduzetost, paraliza, paralizirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> loss of the ability to move a body part [paralysis]</p><p><i>n.</i> a condition marked by uncontrollable tremor</p><p><i>v.</i> affect with palsy</p><p><b>(koristi se u govornom jeziku) imaju odnos prijatelja ili prijatelja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used colloquially) having the relationship of friends or pals [chummy, matey, pally]</p><p><b>okolišati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be deliberately ambiguous or unclear in order to mislead or withhold information [beat around the bush, equivocate, prevaricate, tergiversate]</p><p><b>okolišati (od &quot;palter&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trivial act of lying or being deliberately unclear [fibbing]</p><p><b>bezvrijednost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> worthlessness due to insignificance [sorriness]</p><p><b>beznačajan, bezvrijedan, bijedan, jadan, podao, sitan, tričav, za preziranje, mizeran, bedan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not worth considering [negligible, trifling]</p><p><i>adj.</i> contemptibly small in amount [measly, miserable]</p><p><b>tritsiklični antidepresiv (trgovinski naziv Pamelor) koji se koristi zajedno s psihoterapijom za liječenje distimne depresije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tricyclic antidepressant drug (trade name Pamelor) used along with psychotherapy to treat dysthymic depression [nortriptyline]</p><p><b>Pamir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountain range in central Asia that is centered in Tajikistan but extends into Kyrgyzstan and Afghanistan and Pakistan and western China [the Pamirs]</p><p><b>Pamlico</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Algonquian people formerly of the Pamlico river valley in North Carolina</p><p><i>n.</i> the Algonquian language of the Pamlico</p><p><b>pampasi, stepe u Južnoj Americi, pampa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the vast grassy plains of northern Argentina</p><p><b>Visoka višegodišnja trava iz pampe Južne Amerike koja ima srebrne perje i raste u velikim gustim gomilama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall perennial grass of pampas of South America having silvery plumes and growing in large dense clumps [Cortaderia selloana]</p><p><b>maziti, ugađati, popustiti, popuštati, razmaziti, tetošiti, udovoljavati, udovoljiti, ugoditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> tr