.</i> wash dirt in a pan to separate out the precious minerals [pan, pan out]</p><p><b>uspeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be a success</p><p><i>v.</i> wash dirt in a pan to separate out the precious minerals [pan, pan off]</p><p><b>mali šimpanza močvarnih šuma u Zairu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small chimpanzee of swamp forests in Zaire [bonobo, pygmy chimpanzee]</p><p><b>pečen u loncu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> roast in a pan</p><p><b>čimpanza, čimpanze</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intelligent somewhat arboreal ape of equatorial African forests [chimp, chimpanzee]</p><p><b>duge dlakave šimpanze iz istočno-srednje Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> long-haired chimpanzees of east-central Africa [eastern chimpanzee]</p><p><b>crno-lice čimpanze iz središnje Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> black-faced chimpanzees of central Africa [central chimpanzee]</p><p><b>čimpanze sa maskom ili bledim licem iz zapadne Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> masked or pale-faced chimpanzees of western Africa [western chimpanzee]</p><p><b>pržen u tegli. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> broil in a pan</p><p><b>pržiti u loncu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> fry in a pan</p><p><b>od ili u vezi sa svim Grcima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to all the Greeks [Panhellenic]</p><p><b>lijek za sve</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the goddess of healing</p><p><i>n.</i> hypothetical remedy for all ills or diseases [catholicon, cure-all, nostrum]</p><p><b>bezbrižnost, efektnost, elan, perjanica, poletnost, raskoš, samouvjerenost, sjaj, ukras od perja, "Elana"</b></p><p><i>n.</i> distinctive and stylish elegance [dash, elan, flair, style]</p><p><i>n.</i> a feathered plume on a helmet</p><p><b>analgetik za blagi bol, ali ne i za upalu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an analgesic for mild pain but not for inflammation [Anacin III, Datril, Phenaphen, Tempra, Tylenol, acetaminophen]</p><p><b>Panama, panamski šešir, slamnati šešir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic on the Isthmus of Panama [Republic of Panama]</p><p><i>n.</i> a stiff hat made of straw with a flat crown [Panama hat, boater, leghorn, sailor, skimmer, straw hat]</p><p><b>Panamski kanal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ship canal 40 miles long across the Isthmus of Panama built by the United States (1904-1914)</p><p><b>zona koja se sastoji od pojasa zemlje preko Panamskog preliva koji sadrži Panamski kanal (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a zone consisting of a strip of land across the Isthmus of Panama that contains the Panama Canal [Canal Zone]</p><p><b>Panamá</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a resort and fishing town on the Gulf of Mexico in northwest Florida</p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Panama [Panamanian capital, capital of Panama]</p><p><b>panamski šešir, slamnati šešir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stiff hat made of straw with a flat crown [Panama, boater, leghorn, sailor, skimmer, straw hat]</p><p><b>tvrdo teško crveno drvo drveta quira, veliki uspravni grm iz Kolumbije s velikim lišćama s velikim listovima i osnim rascima mirisnih žutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hard heavy red wood of a quira tree [quira]</p><p><i>n.</i> large erect shrub of Colombia having large odd-pinnate leaves with large leaflets and axillary racemes of fragrant yellow flowers [Panama redwood tree, Platymiscium pinnatum]</p><p><b>veliki uspravni grm iz Kolumbije s velikim lišćama s velikim listovima i osnim rascima mirisnih žutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large erect shrub of Colombia having large odd-pinnate leaves with large leaflets and axillary racemes of fragrant yellow flowers [Panama redwood, Platymiscium pinnatum]</p><p><b>Velika listovita stabla porijeklom iz Paname i od kojih zemlja uzima ime (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large deciduous tree native to Panama and from which the country takes its name [Sterculia apetala]</p><p><b>u Panami ili u toj zemlji, o ili povezan s ili karakterističan za Panamu ili njezine stanovnike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Panama</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Panama or its people</p>