no, podudaranje, poklapanje, usporedan, usporedna crta, usporednica, usporednik, analogija, paralelna, paralelni, analogan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something having the property of being analogous to something else [analog, analogue]</p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary line around the Earth parallel to the equator [latitude, line of latitude, parallel of latitude]</p><p><i>n.</i> (mathematics) one of a set of parallel geometric figures (parallel lines or planes)</p><p><i>v.</i> be parallel to</p><p><i>v.</i> make or place parallel to something [collimate]</p><p><i>v.</i> duplicate or match [duplicate, twin]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being everywhere equidistant and not intersecting</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the simultaneous performance of multiple operations</p><p><b>Samo jedna crta može biti crta kroz točku paralelnu drugoj crti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> only one line can be drawn through a point parallel to another line [Euclid's fifth axiom]</p><p><b>preča, prečka, vratilo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gymnastic apparatus consisting of two parallel wooden rods supported on uprights [bars]</p><p><b>Zatvoreni krug u kojem se struja dijeli na dvije ili više staza prije nego se ponovno kombinuje kako bi se završio krug (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a closed circuit in which the current divides into two or more paths before recombining to complete the circuit [shunt circuit]</p><p><b>usporedno sučeljeparallel interface</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an interface between a computer and a printer where the computer sends multiple bits of information to the printer simultaneously [parallel port]</p><p><b>zbirka biografija poznatih parova Grka i Rimljana napisao Plutarha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collection of biographies of famous pairs of Greeks and Romans written by Plutarch</p><p><b>paralela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary line around the Earth parallel to the equator [latitude, line of latitude, parallel]</p><p><b>paralelni rad</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the simultaneous execution of two or more operations 