e crown of the head [parietal cortex]</p><p><b>tvrdi vanjski sloj perikarda koji je povezan s dijafragmom i grudnom kostom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tough outermost layer of the pericardium that is attached to the diaphragm and the sternum</p><p><b>u kojima se jajne ćelije razvijaju na zidu ili se na zidu male izrasline koje formiraju razbijene pregrade unutar složenog jajnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> where ovules develop on the wall or slight outgrowths of the wall forming broken partitions within a compound ovary</p><p><b>pleura koja obiluje unutrašnje zidove prsnog koša i pokriva dijafragmu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pleura that lines the inner chest walls and covers the diaphragm</p><p><b>red Hypericales, red Parietales</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large order of dicotyledonous plants of subclass Dilleniidae [Hypericales, order Hypericales, order Parietales]</p><p><b>mala vrsta bezštiklih biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of stingless herbs [genus Parietaria]</p><p><b>biljka koja raste u pukotinama s dugim uskim lišcima i malim ružičastim apetalnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herb that grows in crevices having long narrow leaves and small pink apetalous flowers [pellitory, pellitory-of-the-wall, wall pellitory]</p><p><b>čvor u blizini stražnjeg kraja svake hemisfere koji odvaja parijetalne režnjeve i okcipitalne režnjeve u obje hemisfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sulcus near the posterior end of each hemisphere that separates the parietal lobes and the occipital lobes in both hemispheres [parieto-occipital sulcus]</p><p><b>čvor u blizini stražnjeg kraja svake hemisfere koji odvaja parijetalne režnjeve i okcipitalne režnjeve u obje hemisfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sulcus near the posterior end of each hemisphere that separates the parietal lobes and the occipital lobes in both hemispheres [parieto-occipital fissure]</p><p><b>Šav između parijetalne i temporalne kosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the suture between the parietal and the temporal bones</p><p><b>klađenje u kojem pobjednici dijele ukupni uložen iznos (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> betting where winners share the total amount wagered</p><p><b>lupina, obrezivanje, oljuštena ljuska, podrezivanje, strugotine</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin fragment or slice (especially of wood) that has been shaved from something [shaving, sliver]</p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) a part of a fruit or vegetable that is pared or cut off</p><p><b>mali oštar nož za obaranje voća ili povrća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small sharp knife used in paring fruits or vegetables [parer]</p><p><b>(oblike lišća) pinat s parom letaka na vrhu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a leaf shape) pinnate with a pair of leaflets at the apex [abruptly-pinnate, even-pinnate]</p><p><b>pariški, pariških, Pariškoj, Pariz, Pariza, Paris</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of France [City of Light, French capital, capital of France]</p><p><i>n.</i> sometimes placed in subfamily Trilliaceae [genus Paris]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the prince of Troy who abducted Helen from her husband Menelaus and provoked the Trojan War</p><p><i>n.</i> a town in northeastern Texas</p><p><b>višegodišnji potgrm na Kanarskim otocima s obično blijedožutim cvjetovima nalik margariti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial subshrub of the Canary Islands having usually pale yellow daisylike flowers [Argyranthemum frutescens, Chrysanthemum frutescens, marguerite, marguerite daisy]</p><p><b>otrovna dvostruka so bakar arsenata i bakar acetata, Zeleni, žuti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic double salt of copper arsenate and copper acetate</p><p><i>n.</i> a shade of green tinged with yellow [chartreuse, pea green, yellow green, yellowish green]</p><p><b>Europska biljka s žuto-zelenim cvijećem sličnim i blisko povezanim s trilliumima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European herb with yellow-green flowers resembling and closely related to the trilliums [herb Paris]</p><p><b>Sveučilište u Parizu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a university in Paris [Sorbonne, University of Paris]</p><p><b>okrug, parohija, župa, župljani, župna knjiga, župne, župni, župnoj, župu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a local church community</p><p><i>n.</i> the local subdivision of a diocese committed to one pastor</p><p><b>župljanin, župljanka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a parish</p><p><b>Parižanin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or resident of Paris</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Paris or its inhabitants</p><p><b>Žena rođena ili rezident Pariza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a female native or resident of Paris</p><p><b>upotreba dvosmislenih riječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of ambiguous words</p><p><b>analogija, istovrijednost, jednakost, način provjere točnosti poruke, obračunski kurs, paritet, parnost, sličnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (obstetrics) the number of liveborn children a woman has delivered [para]</p><p><i>n.</i> (mathematics) a relation between a pair of integers: if both integers are odd or both are even they have the same parity</p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a bit that is used in an error detection procedure in which a 0 or 1 is added to each group of bits so that it will have either an odd number of 1's or an even number of 1's [check bit, parity bit]</p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) parity is conserved in a universe in which the laws of physics are the same in a right-handed system of coordinates as in a left-handed system [conservation of parity, mirror symmetry, space-reflection symmetry]</p><p><i>n.</i> functional equality</p><p><b>bit pariteta, bit parnosti, ispitni bit, kontrolni bit, paritetni bit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a bit that is used in an error detection procedure in which a 0 or 1 is added to each group of bits so that it will have either an odd number of 1's or an even number of 1's [check bit, parity]</p><p><b>ispit parnosti, kontrola pariteta, provjera paritete</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of checking for errors in computer functioning [odd-even check, redundancy check]</