ves a part or a share [sharer]</p><p><b>razdijeljen, razdvojen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a margin incised almost to the base so as to create distinct divisions or lobes</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a leaf having margins incised almost to the base so as to create distinct divisions or lobes</p><p><b>prizemlje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ornamental flower garden</p><p><i>n.</i> seating at the rear of the main floor (beneath the balconies) [parquet circle]</p><p><b>malen rod sjevernoameričkih biljaka i grmova s krajnjim panicama malih cvjetova zraka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of North American herbs and shrubs with terminal panicles of small ray flowers [genus Parthenium]</p><p><b>mnogo-ogranat podgrm s srebrnim lišćama i malim bijelim cvijećima iz Teksasa i sjevernog Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> much-branched subshrub with silvery leaves and small white flowers of Texas and northern Mexico [guayule]</p><p><b>tropska američka godišnja trava s malim bljesnim glavama bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American annual weed with small radiate heads of white flowers [bastard feverfew]</p><p><b>čvrsta višegodišnja biljka sa bijelocvrstih cvijeća iz istočnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stout perennial herb of the eastern United States with whitish flowers [American feverfew, prairie dock, wild quinine]</p><p><b>(botanica) razvoj voća bez oplodnje ili sjemena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (botany) the development of a fruit without fertilization or seeds</p><p><b>drvene loze s vrhovima poput diska na vrhovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> woody vines having disklike tips on the tendrils [genus Parthenocissus]</p><p><b>obična sjevernoamerička loza s složenim lišćama i plavo-crnim bojama poput bobica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common North American vine with compound leaves and bluish-black berrylike fruit [American ivy, Virginia creeper, woodbine]</p><p><b>Azijska loza s tri-lobed