let) solo ples ili plesna figura (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (ballet) a solo dance or dance figure [variation]</p><p><b>Pasadena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in southwestern California to the east of Los Angeles</p><p><b>velika afrička antilopa s dugim ravnim gotovo uspravnim rogovima, divlje koze Irana i susjednih regija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large African antelope with long straight nearly upright horns [oryx]</p><p><i>n.</i> wild goat of Iran and adjacent regions [Capra aegagrus, bezoar goat]</p><p><b>paskal, Pascal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of pressure equal to one newton per square meter [Pa]</p><p><i>n.</i> French mathematician and philosopher and Jansenist [Blaise Pascal]</p><p><i>n.</i> a programing language designed to teach programming through a top-down modular approach</p><p><b>Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several types of commercially grown celery having green stalks [Paschal celery]</p><p><b>Kompajler za programe napisane u Pascal-u (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compiler for programs written in Pascal</p><p><b>pritisak primjenjen bilo gdje na tijelo tekućine uzrokuje da se sila jednako prenosi u svim smjerovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pressure applied anywhere to a body of fluid causes a force to be transmitted equally in all directions [Pascal's law of fluid pressures]</p><p><b>pritisak primjenjen bilo gdje na tijelo tekućine uzrokuje da se sila jednako prenosi u svim smjerovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pressure applied anywhere to a body of fluid causes a force to be transmitted equally in all directions [Pascal's law]</p><p><b>Židovski praznik Pashe., kršćanski praznik Uskrs. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Jewish feast of the Passover [Pascha]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Christian festival of Easter [Pascha]</p><p><b>Židovski praznik Pashe., kršćanski praznik Uskrs. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Jewish feast of the Passover [Pasch]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Christian festival of Easter [Pasch]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s Pasha ili Uskrsom (MT)</b></p><