aits]</p><p><i>n.</i> a difficult juncture [head, straits]</p><p><i>n.</i> one complete cycle of operations (as by a computer)</p><p><i>n.</i> an automatic advance to the next round in a tournament without playing an opponent [bye]</p><p><i>n.</i> a permit to enter or leave a military installation [liberty chit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a complimentary ticket</p><p><i>n.</i> a usually brief attempt [crack, fling, go, offer, whirl]</p><p><i>n.</i> (sports) the act of throwing the ball to another member of your team [flip, toss]</p><p><i>n.</i> success in satisfying a test or requirement [passing, qualifying]</p><p><i>v.</i> go across or through</p><p><i>v.</i> move past [go by, go past, pass by, surpass, travel by]</p><p><i>v.</i> make laws, bills, etc. or bring into effect by legislation [legislate]</p><p><i>v.</i> pass by [elapse, glide by, go along, go by, lapse, slide by, slip away, slip by]</p><p><i>v.</i> place into the hands or custody of [give, hand, pass on, reach, turn over]</p><p><i>v.</i> stretch out over a distance, space, time, or scope [extend, go, lead, run]</p><p><i>v.</i> travel past [overhaul, overtake]</p><p><i>v.</i> come to pass [come about, fall out, go on, hap, happen, occur, pass off, take place]</p><p><i>v.</i> go unchallenged [clear]</p><p><i>v.</i> use up a period of time in a specific way [spend]</p><p><i>v.</i> pass over, across, or through [draw, guide, run]</p><p><i>v.</i> transmit information [communicate, pass along, pass on, put across]</p><p><i>v.</i> disappear gradually [blow over, evanesce, fade, fleet, pass off]</p><p><i>v.</i> go successfully through a test or a selection process [make it]</p><p><i>v.</i> be superior or better than some standard [exceed, go past, overstep, top, transcend]</p><p><i>v.</i> accept or judge as acceptable</p><p><i>v.</i> allow to go without comment or censure</p><p><i>v.</i> transfer to another</p><p><i>v.</i> pass into a specified state or condition [lapse, sink]</p><p><i>v.</i> throw (a ball) to another player</p><p><i>v.</i> be inherited by [devolve, fall, return]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to pass [make pass]</p><p><i>v.</i> grant authorization or clearance for [authorise, authorize, clear]</p><p><i>v.</i> pass from physical life and lose all bodily attributes and functions necessary to sustain life [buy the farm, cash in one's chips, choke, conk, croak, decease, die, drop dead, exit, expire, give-up the ghost, go, kick the bucket, pass away, perish, pop off, snuff it]</p><p><i>v.</i> eliminate from the body [egest, eliminate, excrete]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of advancing the ball by throwing it [passing]</p><p><b>prelaz ili putovanje s jednog mjesta na drugo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a passage or journey from one place to another [move through, pass over, pass through, transit]</p><p><b>proslijedi (naredba), dojaviti, javiti, javljati, komunicirati, obavijestiti, obavještavati, priopćavati, priopćiti, priopćivati, saopćavati, saopćiti, saopćivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> transmit information [communicate, pass, pass on, put across]</p><p><b>prenijeti, prenositi, priopćavati, priopćiti, pronijeti, pronositi, propagirati, proširiti, proširivati, razglasiti, razglašavati, raširiti, raširivati, širiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be distributed [circulate, distribute, pass on]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become widely known [broadcast, circularise, circularize, circulate, diffuse, disperse, disseminate, distribute, propagate, spread]</p><p><b>iščeznuti, preminuti, prolaziti, umrijeti, crknuti, izdahnuti, krepati, skončati, skončavati, umirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> pass from physical life and lose all bodily attributes and functions necessary to sustain life [buy the farm, cash in one's chips, choke, conk, croak, decease, die, drop dead, exit, expire, give-up the ghost, go, kick the bucket, pass, perish, pop off, snuff it]</p><p><i>v.</i> go out of existence</p><p><b>proći, prolaziti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> move past [go by, go past, pass, surpass, travel by]</p><p><b>nogometaš koji hvata (ili bi trebao hvati) napredni prolaz (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a football player who catches (or is supposed to catch) a forward pass [pass receiver, receiver]</p><p><b>(Američki nogomet) uspješan napredni prolaz u nogometu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (American football) a successful forward pass in football [completion]</p><p><b>ocijeniti, ocjenjivati, procijeniti, procjenjivati, prosuditi, prosuđivati, suditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> form a critical opinion of [evaluate, judge]</p><p><b>predstaviti, blijedjeti, gubiti se, izblijedjeti, izgubiti se, iščezavati, iščeznuti, nestajati, nestati, rasplinjavati se, rasplinuti se, zamirati, zamrijeti, desiti se, dešavati se, događati se, dogoditi se, odigrati se, odigravati se, održati se, održavati se, odvijati se, odviti se, zbiti se, zbivati se, emitirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be accepted as something or somebody in a false character or identity</p><p><i>v.</i> disregard</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be circulated and accepted in a false character or identity</p><p><i>v.</i> disappear gradually [blow over, evanesce, fade, fleet, pass]</p><p><i>v.</i> come to pass [come about, fall out, go on, hap, happen, occur, pass, take place]</p><p><i>v.</i> expel (gases or odors) [breathe, emit]</p><p><b>predati, presuđivati, dati, davati, dodati, dodavati, izručiti, izručivati, predavati, proslijediti, prosljeđivati, uručiti, uručivati, ostaviti, ostavljati, prenijeti, prenositi, priopćavati, priopćiti, hitati, juriti, nadirati, napredovati, odjuriti, odmaknuti, odmaći, odmicati, poodmaknuti, poodmaći, poodmicati, uznapredovati, žuriti, dojaviti, javiti, javljati, komunicirati, obavijestiti, obavještavati, priopćivati, saopćavati, saopćiti, saopćivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> place into the hands or custody of [give, hand, pass, reach, turn over]</p><p><i>v.</i> transmit (knowledge or skills) [give, impart, leave]</p><p><i>v.</i> move forward, also in the metaphorical sense [advance, go on, march on, move on, progress]</p><p><i>v.</i> give to or transfer possession of</p><p><i>v.</i> refer to another person for decision or judgment [relegate, submit]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be distributed [circulate, distribute, pass around]</p><p><i>v.</i> transmit information [communicate, pass, pass along, put across]</p><p><b>razdijeliti, malaksati, onesvijestiti se, distribuirati, podijeliti, raspodijeliti, razdati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> pass out from weakness, physical or emotional distress due to a loss of blood supply to the brain [conk, faint, swoon]</p><p><i>v.</i> give to several people [distribute, give out, hand out]</p><p><i>v.</i> lose consciousness due to a sudden trauma, for example [black out, zonk out]</p><p><b>prijeći, preskočiti, zaobilaziti, zaobići, prelaziti, presijecati, presjeći, prolaziti, proći, nadlijetati, brisati, obrisati, oribati, otrti, ribati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> bypass [jump, skip, skip over]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a passage or journey from one place to another [move through, pass across, pass through, transit]</p><p><i>v.</i> travel across or pass over [cover, cross, cut across, cut through, get across, get over, track, traverse]</p><p><i>v.</i> fly over [overfly]</p><p><i>v.</i> rub with a circular motion [wipe]</p><p><b>nogometaš koji hvata (ili bi trebao hvati) napredni prolaz (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a football player who catches (or is supposed to catch) a forward pass [pass catcher, receiver]</p><p><b>doživjeti, prenošenje kroz, prijeći, prijelaz kroz, proći, propustiti, prolazni</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a passage or journey from one place to another [move through, pass across, pass over, transit]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to move through</p><p><i>v.</i> pass through an enemy line [infiltrate]</p><p><b>odbaciti, odbacivati, odbijati, odbiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> refuse to accept [decline, refuse, reject, turn down]</p><p><i>v.</i> fail to acknowledge</p><p><b>mokriti, pišati, piškiti, pomokriti se, popišati se, popiškiti se, urinirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> eliminate urine [make, make water, micturate, pee, pee-pee, piddle, piss, puddle, relieve oneself, spend a penny, take a leak, urinate, wee, wee-wee]</p><p><b>uspjeti lako. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> succeed at easily [ace, breeze through, nail, sail through, sweep through]</p><p><b>doživjeti, prenošenje kroz, prijeći, prijelaz kroz, proći, propustiti, prolazni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an opening that resembles a window between two rooms (especially a shelved opening between a kitchen and dining room that is used to pass dishes)</p><p><b>osrednji, podnošljiv, prihvatljiv, prohodan, prolazan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to be passed or traversed or crossed</p><p><i>adj.</i> about average [adequate, fair to middling, tolerable]</p><p><b>u određenoj mjeri ili stupnju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to certain extent or degree [fairly, jolly, middling, moderately, pretty, reasonably, somewhat]</p><p><b>(štrom) napadački udarac s jednom nogom naprijed, stražnjom nogom ravno i mačem izloženom naprijed (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (fencing) an attacking thrust made with one foot forward and the back leg straight and with the sword arm outstretched forward [lunge, straight thrust]</p><p><b>dodavanje, doturanje, hodnik, klanac, odlomak, pasaža, prijelaz, prohod, prolaska, prolaz, prolazak, put, putovanje, vozarina, tranzicija, otvor, kanal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of passing from one state or place to the next [transition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a section of text</p><p><i>n.</i> a way through or along which someone or something may pass</p><p><i>n.</i> the passing of a law by a legislative body [enactment]</p><p><i>n.</i> a journey usually by ship [transit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a short section of a musical composition [musical passage]</p><p><i>n.</i> a path or channel or duct through or along which something may pass [passageway]</p><p><i>n.</i> a bodily reaction of changing from one place or stage to another [passing]</p><p><i>n.</i> the motion of one object relative to another [passing]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of passing something to another person [handing over]</p><p><b>hodnik, prolaz, prolazom, kanal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a passage between rooms or between buildings</p><p><i>n.</i> a path or channel or duct through or along which something may pass [passage]</p><p><b>član Algonkijskog naroda povezanog s Maleciteom i koji živi u sjeveroistočnom Maineu i New Brunswicku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Algonquian people related to the Malecite and living in northeastern Maine and New Brunswick</p><p><b>u hodnom položaju s podignutom desnom prednjom nogom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in walking position with right foreleg raised</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ovog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a record of deposits and withdrawals and interest held by depositors at certain banks [bankbook]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je uloženi novac u račun uložitelja u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, uloženi novac u račun uložitelja u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe može se koristiti za plaćanje poreznih obveza. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a savings account in which deposits and withdrawals are recorded in the depositor's passbook</p><p><b>staromodan, antički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> out of fashion [antique, demode, ex, old-fashioned, old-hat, outmoded, passee]</p><p><b>glavni ključ, otpirač, paspartu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> key that secures entrance everywhere [master, master key, passkey]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mounting for a picture using gummed tape</p><p><b>Bacanje koje je hvatač trebao uhvatiti ali nije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pitch that the catcher should have caught but did not</p><p>