ič</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who can find paths through unexplored territory [guide, scout]</p><p><b>besputan, bez staze, neispitan, neprohodan, neutrt</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking pathways [roadless, trackless, untracked, untrod, untrodden]</p><p><b>patogen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any disease-producing agent (especially a virus or bacterium or other microorganism)</p><p><b>patofiziologija, patogeneza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the origination and development of a disease</p><p><b>patogen (od &quot;pathogen&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to cause disease [infective, morbific]</p><p><b>u patogenu način (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a pathogenic manner</p><p><b>patološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> caused by or altered by or manifesting disease or pathology [diseased, morbid, pathological]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the practice of pathology [pathological]</p><p><b>organski proces koji se događa kao posljedica bolesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organic process occurring as a consequence of disease [pathological process]</p><p><b>patološki, patoloških</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the practice of pathology [pathologic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> caused by or evidencing a mentally disturbed condition</p><p><i>adj.</i> caused by or altered by or manifesting disease or pathology [diseased, morbid, pathologic]</p><p><b>organski proces koji se događa kao posljedica bolesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organic process occurring as a consequence of disease [pathologic process]</p><p><b>patološko stanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a physical condition that is caused by disease</p><p><b>patološki, patoloških (od &quot;pathological&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to pathology</p><p><b>patolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a doctor who specializes in medical diagnosis [diagnostician]</p><p><b>patologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of medical science that studies the causes and nature and effects of diseases</p><p><i>n.</i> any deviation from a healthy or normal condition</p><p><b>patos