agana]</p><p><b>larve žive u i hrane se sjemenom graška. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> larvae live in and feed on seeds of the pea plant [Bruchus pisorum]</p><p><b>mladi paun (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a young peafowl [peachick]</p><p><b>od srednje blago žuto-zelene boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a moderate slightly yellowish-green color</p><p><b>Teška debela žuta magla. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heavy thick yellow fog [pea soup]</p><p><b>Edukator koji je osnovao prvi vrtić u Sjedinjenim Državama (1804-1894) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> educator who founded the first kindergarten in the United States (1804-1894) [Elizabeth Palmer Peabody, Elizabeth Peabody]</p><p><b>bezbrižnost, mir, mirovanje, red, tišina, mira, mirovnim, miru</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state prevailing during the absence of war</p><p><i>n.</i> harmonious relations</p><p><i>n.</i> the absence of mental stress or anxiety [ataraxis, heartsease, peace of mind, peacefulness, repose, serenity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the general security of public places [public security]</p><p><i>n.</i> a treaty to cease hostilities [pacification, peace treaty]</p><p><b>Svaka politika koja se zalaže za održavanje mirnih međunarodnih odnosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any policy that advocates maintaining peaceful international relations</p><p><b>civilna organizacija koju sponzorira vlada Sjedinjenih Država. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a civilian organization sponsored by the United States government</p><p><b>država sjeverno-srednje Sjedinjenih Država koja graniči s Kanadom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of north central United States bordering on Canada [N.D., ND, North Dakota]</p><p><b>Otvaranje pregovora o mirovnom sporazumu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> opening move in negotiating a peace treaty</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka iz roda Spathiphyllum s bijelim ili zelenim špatom i čipom mirisnih cvijeća i često uzgajana kao ukrasna biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Spathiphyllum having a white or green spathe and a spike of fragrant flowers and often cultivated as an ornamental [spathe flower, spathiphyllum]</p><p><b>protestni marš protiv (posebnog) rata i u korist mira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a protest march against (a particular) war and in favor of peace</p><p><b>mir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the absence of mental stress or anxiety [ataraxis, heartsease, peace, peacefulness, repose, serenity]</p><p><b>Westfalski mir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the peace treaty that ended the Thirty Years' War in 1648</p><p><b>nešto što je ponuđeno protivniku u nadi da će dobiti mir (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something offered to an adversary in the hope of obtaining peace [olive branch]</p><p><b>policijski dužnosnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an officer of the law [law officer, lawman]</p><p><b>visoko ukrašena ceremonijalna pipa američkih Indijanaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a highly decorated ceremonial pipe of Amerindians [calumet, pipe of peace]</p><p><b>Svaki društveni proces koji poduzimaju vlade koje žele da njihovi građani vjeruju da pokušavaju izbjeći oružane neprijateljstva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any social process undertaken by governments who want their citizens to believe they are trying to avoid armed hostilities</p><p><b>Ugovor o prekidu neprijateljstava. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a treaty to cease hostilities [pacification, peace]</p><p><b>miroljubiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined or disposed to peace [peaceable]</p><p><b>miran, miroljubiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined or disposed to peace [peace-loving]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not disturbed by strife or turmoil or war [peaceful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed to peace or of a peaceful nature [pacific]</p><p><b>miran, miroljubiv (od &quot;peaceable&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state that is calm and tranquil [peacefulness]</p><p><b>na miran način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a peaceable manner [pacifically]</p><p><b>miran, mirnih, mirno, mirnog, smiren, tih, pasivan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not disturbed by strife or turmoil or war [peaceable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> peacefully resistant in response to injustice [passive]</p><p><b>mirno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a peaceful manner</p><p><b>mir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state that is calm and tranquil [peaceableness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the absence of mental stress or anxiety [ataraxis, heartsease, peace, peace of mind, repose, serenity]</p><p><b>pripadnik vojne snage koja je dodijeljena (često s međunarodnom sankcijom) da očuva mir u području sukoba, netko tko održava mir., Pištolj policajca na starom Zapadu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a military force that is assigned (often with international sanction) to preserve peace in a trouble area</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who keeps peace</p><p><i>n.</i> the pistol of a law officer in the old West</p><p><b>održavanje mira</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of keeping the peace by military forces (especially when international military forces enforce a truce between hostile groups or nations) [peacekeeping mission, peacekeeping operation]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the preservation of peace between hostile groups by international military forces</p><p><b>aktivnosti održavanja mira vojnim snagama (posebno kada međunarodne vojne snage provode primirje između neprijateljskih skupina ili država) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of keeping the peace by military forces (especially when international military forces enforce a truce between hostile groups or nations) [peacekeeping, peacekeeping operation]</p><p><b>aktivnosti održavanja mira vojnim snagama (posebno kada međunarodne vojne snage provode primirje između neprijateljskih skupina ili država) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of keeping the peace by military forces (especially when international military forces enforce a truce between hostile groups or nations) [peacekeeping, peacekeeping mission]</p><p><b>mirotvorac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who tries to bring peace [conciliator, make-peace, pacifier, reconciler]</p><p><i>n.</i> a belt-fed machine gun capable of fi