rson [bucolic, provincial]</p><p><i>n.</i> one of a (chiefly European) class of agricultural laborers</p><p><i>n.</i> a crude uncouth ill-bred person lacking culture or refinement [Goth, barbarian, boor, churl, tike, tyke]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjena pobuna 1381. protiv poreza i drugih nepravdi koje su ugnjetavale siromašne ljude u Engleskoj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a widespread rebellion in 1381 against poll taxes and other inequities that oppressed the poorer people of England [Great Revolt]</p><p><b>stanje da si seljak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being a peasant</p><p><b>seljaštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the class of peasants</p><p><b>puding napravljen od prečišćenog škrinka pomiješanog s jajima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pudding made with strained split peas mixed with egg</p><p><b>čokolada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> husk of a pea [pea pod]</p><p><b>treset</b></p><p><i>n.</i> partially carbonized vegetable matter saturated with water</p><p><b>mokra spužvača vegetacije u raspadanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wet spongy ground of decomposing vegetation [bog]</p><p><b>pitmos, tresetina, tresetišna mahovina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various pale or ashy mosses of the genus Sphagnum whose decomposed remains form peat [bog moss, sphagnum, sphagnum moss]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili od prirode šuma (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or of the nature of peat</p><p><b>čvrsta polugura sa oštrim šiljakom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stout lever with a sharp spike [cant dog, dog hook, peavy]</p><p><b>čvrsta polugura sa oštrim šiljakom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stout lever with a sharp spike [cant dog, dog hook, peavey]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,05 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,05 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having nine hinged bands of bony plates [Dasypus novemcinctus, Texas armadillo, nine-banded armadillo]</p><p><b>oblutak, pošljunčiti, šljunak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small smooth rounded rock</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko južnoafričkih biljaka