regarious pig-like wild animals of North America and South America [musk hog]</p><p><b>kljucati, laki poljubac, mnoštvo, množina, prihvatiti se, probiti, gomila, hrpa, hrpetina, masa, cmoknuti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (often followed by `of') a large number or amount or extent [batch, deal, flock, good deal, great deal, hatful, heap, lot, mass, mess, mickle, mint, mountain, muckle, passel, pile, plenty, pot, quite a little, raft, sight, slew, spate, stack, tidy sum, wad]</p><p><i>n.</i> a British imperial capacity measure (liquid or dry) equal to 2 gallons</p><p><i>n.</i> a United States dry measure equal to 8 quarts or 537.605 cubic inches</p><p><i>v.</i> hit lightly with a picking motion [beak, pick]</p><p><i>v.</i> eat by pecking at, like a bird [pick up]</p><p><i>v.</i> kiss lightly [smack]</p><p><i>v.</i> eat like a bird [peck at, pick at]</p><p><i>v.</i> bother persistently with trivial complaints [hen-peck, nag]</p><p><b>kljucati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> eat like a bird [peck, pick at]</p><p><b>kurac, pimpek, dijetao, djetlić, žuna, kljun</b></p><p><i>n.</i> obscene terms for penis [cock, dick, prick, putz, shaft, tool]</p><p><i>n.</i> bird with strong claws and a stiff tail adapted for climbing and a hard chisel-like bill for boring into wood for insects [peckerwood, woodpecker]</p><p><i>n.</i> horny projecting mouth of a bird [beak, bill, neb, nib]</p><p><b>farmer, osoba s američkog Juga, dijetao, djetlić, žuna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bird with strong claws and a stiff tail adapted for climbing and a hard chisel-like bill for boring into wood for insects [pecker, woodpecker]</p><p><b>redoslijed važnosti, hijerarhija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the organization of people at different ranks in an administrative body [hierarchy, power structure]</p><p><b>gladan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> somewhat hungry</p><p><i>adj.</i> easily irritated or annoyed [cranky, fractious, irritable, nettlesome, peevish, pettish, petulant, scratchy, techy, testy, tetchy]</p><p><b>Fosilni paprika iz ugljikovog razdoblja koji se odlikuje redovnim rasporedom letaka nalik češlju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Carboniferous fossil fern characterized by a regular arrangement of the leaflets resembling a comb</p><p><b>Pecos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Rio Grande that flows southeastward from New Mexico through western Texas [Pecos River]</p><p><b>Pecos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Rio Grande that flows southeastward from New Mexico through western Texas [Pecos]</p><p><b>Pečuh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two large muscles of the chest [musculus pectoralis, pectoral, pectoral muscle, pectoralis]</p><p><b>mala školjka koja živi u plitkim vodama i blatnim ravnicama na atlantskoj obali Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small scallop inhabiting shallow waters and mud flats of the Atlantic coast of North America [bay scallop]</p><p><b>veliki školjak koji živi u dubokim vodama atlantske obale Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large scallop inhabiting deep waters of the Atlantic coast of North America [giant scallop, sea scallop]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili dobivene od pektina (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or derived from pectin</p><p><b>složena kiselina koja se nalazi u zrelom voću i nekim povrćem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a complex acid that occurs in ripe fruit and some vegetables</p><p><b>pektin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various water-soluble colloidal carbohydrates that occur in ripe fruit and vegetables</p><p><b>Kao češalj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> like a comb</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s pubisom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the pubis</p><p><b>veliki red gastropoda koji obuhvaćaju jednovalvne mehuriće koje imaju jedan žlijezdo nalik češlju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large order of gastropods comprising univalve mollusks that have a single gill resembling a comb [order Pectinibranchia]</p><p><b>škrilje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> scallops [family Pectinidae]</p><p><b>grudni, prsni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two large muscles of the chest [musculus pectoralis, pecs, pectoral muscle, pectoralis]</p><p><i>n.</i> an adornment worn on the chest or breast [pectoral medallion]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the chest or thorax [thoracic]</p><p><b>kosti oblikovane od ključne kosti i lopatica kod ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bony arch formed by the collarbones and shoulder blades in humans [shoulder girdle]</p><p><b>ili par peraja smještenih odmah iza glave kod ribe koje pomažu u kontroli smjera kretanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of a pair of fins situated just behind the head in fishes that help control the direction of movement</p><p><b>Složena je na kosturnom podršci na kojoj su prednje udove kralježnjaka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skeletal support to which the forelimbs of vertebrates are attached</p><p><b>ukras koji se nosi na grudima ili grudima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an adornment worn on the chest or breast [pectoral]</p><p><b>ili dva velika mišića prsa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two large muscles of the chest [musculus pectoralis, pecs, pectoral, pectoralis]</p><p><b>Američki pijesak koji puha prsa kada se udvara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American sandpiper that inflates its chest when courting [Calidris melanotos, jacksnipe]</p><p><b>vene koje isušuju grudi i prazne u podklavijsku venu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> veins that drain the pectoral muscles and empty into the subclavian vein [vena pectoralis]</p><p><b>prsni mišić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two large muscles of the chest [musculus pectoralis, pecs, pectoral, pectoral muscle]</p><p><b>skeletni mišić koji dovodi i okreće ruku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skeletal muscle that adducts and rotates the arm [greater pectoral muscle, musculus pectoralis major]</p><p><b>mali prsni mišić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skeletal muscle that draws down the scapula or raises the ribs [musculus pectoralis minor, smaller pectoral muscle]</p><p><b>prsa, prsni koš, toraks</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of the human torso between the neck and the diaphragm or the corresponding part in other vertebrates [chest, thorax]</p><p><b>opljačkati, pronevjeriti, utajiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> appropriate (as property entrusted to one's care) fraudulently to one's own use [defalcate, embezzle, malversate, misappropriate]</p><p><b>pronevjera, pronevjerenje, zloporaba, zloupotreba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fraudulent appropriation of funds or property entrusted to your care but actually owned by someone else [defalcation, embezzlement, misapplication, misappropriation]</p><p><b>osoba koja krši povjerenje uzimajući (novce) za vlastitu upotrebu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who violates a trust by taking (money) for his own use [defalcator, embezzler]</p><p><b>čudan, čudnovat, individualan, neobičan, osebujan, osobenost, osobna imovina, osobna osobina, osobni, svojstven, individualni, poseban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> beyond or deviating from the usual or expected [curious, funny, odd, queer, rum, rummy, singular]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unique or specific to a person or thing or category [particular, special]</p><p><i>adj.</i> markedly different from the usual</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of one only</p><p><b>brzina u odnosu na lokalni standard mirovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> velocity with respect to the local standard of rest</p><p><b>karakterna crta, neobičnost, osobenost, osobina, izvanrednost, jedinstvenost, naročitost, osobitost, posebnost, razlikovnost, specifičnost, specijalnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an odd or unusual characteristic [distinctive feature, distinguishing characteristic]</p><p><i>n.</i> a distinguishing trait [distinctiveness, speciality, specialness, specialty]</p><p><i>n.</i> something unusual -- perhaps worthy of collecting [curio, curiosity, oddity, oddment, rarity]</p><p><b>lično, znatiželjno, posebno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> uniquely or characteristically [particularly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a manner differing from the usual or expected [curiously, inexplicably, oddly]</p><p><i>a