nd Quaker who founded the colony of Pennsylvania (1644-1718) [William Penn]</p><p><i>n.</i> a university in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania [Pennsylvania, University of Pennsylvania]</p><p><b>Količina koju možete kupiti za novčić. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount that can be bought for a penny [pennyworth]</p><p><b>plamenac, zastavica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the award given to the champion [crown]</p><p><i>n.</i> a flag longer than it is wide (and often tapering)</p><p><i>n.</i> a long flag [pennon, streamer, waft]</p><p><b>s krilcima s perjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having feathered wings</p><p><b>vrsta rodovi iz obitelji Pennatulidae: morski peraci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the family Pennatulidae: sea pens [genus Pennatula]</p><p><b>morski olovke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sea pens [family Pennatulidae]</p><p><b>maslaca u kratkim cijevima s dijagonalno rezanim krajevima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pasta in short tubes with diagonally cut ends</p><p><b>100 penija je u Finskoj nekada bilo jednako 1 marki. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> 100 pennia formerly equaled 1 markka in Finland</p><p><b>bez novca, bez pet para, siromah, siromašan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not having enough money to pay for necessities [hard up, impecunious, in straitened circumstances, penurious, pinched]</p><p><b>bez novca, bez pet para, siromah, siromašan (od &quot;penniless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of lacking money [impecuniousness, penuriousness]</p><p><b>sistem brda u Britaniji koji se proteže od škotske granice na sjeveru do rijeke Trent na jugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of hills in Britain that extend from the Scottish border in the north to the Trent River in the south [Pennines]</p><p><b>sistem brda u Britaniji koji se proteže od škotske granice na sjeveru do rijeke Trent na jugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of hills in Britain that extend from the Scottish border in the north to the Trent River in the south [Pennine Chain]</p><p><b>autorstvo, pisanje, pisano stvaral