een the anus and the genital organs</p><p><b>omotač vezivnog tkiva koji pokriva snop živčanih vlakana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sheath of connective tissue that covers a bundle of nerve fibers</p><p><b>doba, epoha, era, menstruacija, period, razdoblje, rok, vremenski razmak, vrijeme, razdoblja, razdoblju, stilskim, interval, geološki period, geološko razdoblje, točka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an amount of time [period of time, time period]</p><p><i>n.</i> the interval taken to complete one cycle of a regularly repeating phenomenon</p><p><i>n.</i> (ice hockey) one of three divisions into which play is divided in hockey games</p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of geological time during which a system of rocks formed [geological period]</p><p><i>n.</i> the end or completion of something</p><p><i>n.</i> the monthly discharge of blood from the uterus of nonpregnant women from puberty to menopause [catamenia, flow, menses, menstruation, menstruum]</p><p><i>n.</i> a punctuation mark (.) placed at the end of a declarative sentence to indicate a full stop or after abbreviations [full point, full stop, point, stop]</p><p><b>trajanje, vrijeme igre</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (in games or plays or other performances) the time during which play proceeds [play, playing period]</p><p><b>razdoblje, rok, vremenski period, period</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an amount of time [period, time period]</p><p><b>Svaka umjetnička djela čija je posebna vrijednost u tome što podsjeća na povijesno razdoblje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any work of art whose special value lies in its evocation of a historical period</p><p><b>cikličan, periodičan, periodni, povremen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> happening or recurring at regular intervals [periodical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> recurring or reappearing from time to time [occasional]</p><p><b>bilo koja jodna kiselina koja sadrži kisik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any acid of iodine that contains oxygen</p><p><b>nepravilno disanje novorođenčadi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> irregular breathing of newborns</