y be accepted or conceded</p><p><b>na dozvoljeni način (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a permissible manner [allowably]</p><p><b>dopuštenje, dozvola, odobrenje, pravo, privilegija, suglasnost, licenca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> approval to do something</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving a formal (usually written) authorization [license, permit]</p><p><b>dopustiv, dopušten, dozvoljen, popustljiv, previše tolerantan, slobodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not preventive</p><p><i>adj.</i> granting or inclined or able to grant permission</p><p><b>(zakonom) smanjenje vrijednosti naslijeđa uzrokovano djelovanjem ili zanemarivanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) reduction in the value of an estate caused by act or neglect [waste]</p><p><b>dopustiv, dopušten, dozvoljen, popustljiv, previše tolerantan, slobodan (od &quot;permissive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a permissive manner</p><p><b>popustljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to allow freedom of choice and behavior [tolerance]</p><p><b>davati, dopustiti, dopuštenje, dozvola, dozvoliti, omogućivati, propusnica, propust, pustiti, licenca, licencija, odobrenje, dopuštati, dozovljavati, odobravati, odobriti, puštati, dozvoljavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a legal document giving official permission to do something [licence, license]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving a formal (usually written) authorization [license, permission]</p><p><i>n.</i> large game fish [Trachinotus falcatus]</p><p><i>v.</i> consent to, give permission [allow, countenance, let]</p><p><i>v.</i> make it possible through a specific action or lack of action for something to happen [allow, let]</p><p><i>v.</i> allow the presence of or allow (an activity) without opposing or prohibiting [allow, tolerate]</p><p><b>sposobnost promjene redoslijeda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ability to change sequence [permutableness, transposability]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of changing sequence [transposable]</p><p><b>sposobn