kes charitable donations intended to increase human well-being [altruist]</p><p><b>čovjekoljublje, filantropija, filantropije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> voluntary promotion of human welfare [philanthropic gift]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s filatelijom ili od interesa za filatelice (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to philately or of interest to philatelists [philatelical]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s filatelijom ili od interesa za filatelice (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to philately or of interest to philatelists [philatelic]</p><p><b>na filatelički način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a philatelic manner</p><p><b>sakupljač i student poštanskih maraka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collector and student of postage stamps [stamp collector]</p><p><b>filatelija, skupljanje maraka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the collection and study of postage stamps [stamp collecting, stamp collection]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) običan seljak koji je ponudio gostoljubivost Zeusu i Hermesu kad su došli na Zemlju bez otkrivanja njihovih identiteta kako bi testirao pobožnost ljudi, (Novi zavjet) kršćanin (vjerojatno živi u Kolose) čiji je rob pobjegao i otišao vidjeti Svetog Pavla, knjiga Novog zavjeta koja sadrži pismo svetog Pavla Filemonu u kojem se od njega traži da oprosti robu koji je pobjegao. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) a simple countryman who offered hospitality to Zeus and Hermes when they came to earth without revealing their identities in order to test people's piety</p><p><i>n.</i> (New Testament) a Christian (probably living in Colossae) whose slave escaped and went to see Saint Paul</p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book containing an epistle from Saint Paul to Philemon asking Philemon to forgive the slave for escaping [Epistle of Paul the Apostle to Philemon, Epistle to Philemon]</p><p><b>filharmonije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large orchestra [symphony, symphony orchestra]</p><p><i>adj.</i> composing or characteristic of an orchestral group</p><p><i>adj.</i> devoted to or appreciative of music</p><p><b>visina koja se koristi za podešavanje instrumenata za koncerte (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the pitch used to tune instruments for concert performances [concert pitch, international pitch]</p><p><b>Obožavatelj Grčke i svega što je grčko., karakterizira ljubav prema Grčkoj i grčkim stvarima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an admirer of Greece and everything Greek [Graecophile, philhellenist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by a love of Greece and Grecian things [Graecophile, Graecophilic, philhellenic]</p><p><b>karakterizira ljubav prema Grčkoj i grčkim stvarima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by a love of Greece and Grecian things [Graecophile, Graecophilic, philhellene]</p><p><b>Divljenje Grčkoj i Grcima i grčkim običajima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> admiration for Greece and the Greeks and Greek customs</p><p><b>Obožavatelj Grčke i svega što je grčko. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an admirer of Greece and everything Greek [Graecophile, philhellene]</p><p><b>blagost, dragost, naklonost, nježnost, privrženost, sklonost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a positive feeling of liking [affection, affectionateness, fondness, heart, tenderness, warmheartedness, warmness]</p><p><b>Francuski kraljevski arhitekt koji je izgradio palaču i vrtove Tuileries u Parizu za Katarinu de Medicije (1515-1570) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French royal architect who built the Tuileries Palace and Gardens in Paris for Catherine de Medicis (1515-1570) [Delorme, Philibert Delorme, de l'Orme]</p><p><b>Francuski kraljevski arhitekt koji je izgradio palaču i vrtove Tuileries u Parizu za Katarinu de Medicije (1515-1570) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French royal architect who built the Tuileries Palace and Gardens in Paris for Catherine de Medicis (1515-1570) [Delorme, Philibert de l'Orme, de l'Orme]</p><p><b>Filip</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Englishman and husband of Elizabeth II (born 1921) [Duke of Edinburgh, Prince Philip]</p><p><b>Američki fizičar koji je proučavao elektroničku strukturu