onema prepoznat u jeziku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of phonemes recognized in a language</p><p><b>po fonemiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by phonemics [phonemic]</p><p><b>fonologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of the sound system of a given language and the analysis and classification of its phonemes [phonology]</p><p><b>nazvati, telefon, telefonirati, telefonske, telefonski, tel. (od &quot;phone&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the person initiating a telephone call [caller, caller-up, telephoner]</p><p><b>fonetičan, fonetski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to speech sounds [phonic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the scientific study of speech sounds</p><p><b>alfabet znakova namijenjen predstavljanju određenih glasova govora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alphabet of characters intended to represent specific sounds of speech [sound alphabet]</p><p><b>pisani znak koji se koristi u fonetičkom transkripciji za predstavljanje određenog govornog zvuka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a written character used in phonetic transcription of represent a particular speech sound</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se koristi samo za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije 95.0 ili 95.0 u skladu s člankom 93. točkom (a) ovog pravilnika, točka (b) ovog pravilnika ne smije biti primjenjiva na proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije 95.0 ili 95. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a transcription intended to represent each distinct speech sound with a separate symbol</p><p><b>fonetike (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by phonetics</p><p><b>stručnjak za fonetiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in phonetics</p><p><b>fonetika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of acoustics concerned with speech processes including its production and perception and acoustic analysis</p><p><b>kriv, krivotvoren, lažan, neprav, patvoren, tobožnji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who professes beliefs and opinions that he or she does not hold in order to conceal his or her real feelings or motives [dissembler, dissimulator, hypocrite, phony, pretender]</p><p><i>adj.</i> fraudulent [bastard, bogus, fake, phony]</p><p><b>akustičan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to the phonic method of teaching reading</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to speech</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to speech sounds [phonetic]</p><p><b>fonetika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> teaching reading by training beginners to associate letters with their sound values</p><p><b>fonogram</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any written symbol standing for a sound or syllable or morpheme or word</p><p><b>fonogram (od &quot;phonogram&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a phonogram</p><p><b>fonograf, gramofon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> machine in which rotating records cause a stylus to vibrate and the vibrations are amplified acoustically or electronically [record player]</p><p><b>album, ploča</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an album for holding phonograph records [record album]</p><p><b>Stylus koji je nekada radio zvuk po žlijezdu na gramofonu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stylus that formerly made sound by following a groove in a phonograph record [needle]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom materijala od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sound recording consisting of a disk with a continuous groove [disc, disk, phonograph recording, platter, record]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom materijala od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sound recording consisting of a disk with a continuous groove [disc, disk, phonograph record, platter, record]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 mm i (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disk coated with cellulose acetate [acetate disk]</p><p><b>fonološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to phonology [phonological]</p><p><b>sustav telefona koji se koristi na određenom jeziku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of phones used in a particular language [phonological system]</p><p><b>fonološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to phonology [phonologic]</p><p><b>fonološki sustav, fonološko ustrojstvo, glasovni sustav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of phones used in a particular language [phonologic system]</p><p><b>stručnjak za fonologiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in phonology</p><p><b>fonologija, psaltir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of the sound system of a given language and the analysis and classification of its phonemes [phonemics]</p><p><b>morbidni strah od zvukova uključujući i vlastiti glas (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a morbid fear of sounds including your own voice [acousticophobia]</p><p><b>folirant, folirantski, kriv, krivotvoren, lažan, neprav, nepravi, patvoren, šminker, tobožnji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who professes beliefs and opinions that he or she does not hold in order to conceal his or her real feelings or motives [dissembler, dissimulator, hypocrite, phoney, pretender]</p><p><i>adj.</i> fraudulent [bastard, bogus, fake, phoney]</p><p><b>bilo koja od različitih američkih parazitskih biljaka sličnih jastogom Starog svijeta: lažni jastog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various American parasitic plants similar to Old World mistletoe: false mistletoe [genus Phoradendron]</p><p><b>Tradicionalni božićni mistel u Americi: raste na listnatim drvećem i može ozbiljno oslabiti biljku domaćina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the traditional mistletoe of Christmas in America: grows on deciduous trees and can severely weaken the host plant [American mistletoe, Phoradendron serotinum]</p><p><b>Tradicionalni božićni mistel u Americi: raste na listnatim drvećem i može ozbiljno oslabiti biljku domaćina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the traditional mistletoe of Christmas in America: grows on deciduous trees and can severely weaken the host plant [American mistletoe, Phoradendron flavescens]</p><p><b>potkovnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hermaphrodite wormlike animal living in mud of the sea bottom</p><p><b>potkovnjaci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small phylum of wormlike marine animals [Phoronidea, phylum Phoronida]</p><p><b>potkovnjaci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small phylum of wormlike marine animals [Phoronida, phylum Phoronida]</p><p><b>bezbojni otrovni plin koji miriše na novoosekano sijeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless poisonous gas that smells like new-mown hay</p><p><b>fosfataza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a group of enzymes that act as a catalyst in the hydrolysis of organic phosphates</p><p><b>fosfat, fosfati, fosfatni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt of phosphoric acid [inorganic phosphate, orthophosphate]</p><p><i>n.</i> carbonated drink with fruit syrup and a little phosphoric acid</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solution containing a phosphate buffer [PBS]</p><p><b>bezbojan plin s jakim ribljivim mirisom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless gas with a strong fishy smell</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom proteina od 0,5% do 0,5% i (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organic compound of creatine and phosphoric acid [creatine phosphate, creatine phosphoric acid]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom masnih kiselina od 1 kPa do 1 kPa, ali ne više od 1 kPa, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various compounds composed of fatty acids and phosphoric acid and a nitrogenous base</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,25% ili više, ali ne više od 0,25% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> containing chemically bound phosphoric acid</p><p><b>fosfor, fosforni premaz zaslona, fosforni sloj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a synthetic substance that is fluorescent or phosphorescent</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm i (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a corrosion-resistant bronze containing phosphorus</p><p><b>da pokažu fosforescenciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to exhibit phosphorescence</p><p><b>fosforescencija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fluorescence that persists after the bombarding radiation has ceased</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom fosfora od 0,01 do 0,01 mmol/l, ali ne većim od 0,01 mmol/l, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> emitting light without appreciable heat as by slow oxidation of phosphorous</p><p><b>fosfor, fosforni premaz zaslona, fosforni sloj (od &quot;phosphor&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing or characteristic of phosphorus [phosphorous]</p><p><b>kiselina koja se koristi u đubrivima i sapunima: H3PO4 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acid used in fertilizers and soaps: H3PO4 [orthophosphoric acid]</p><p><b>koji sadrže ili su karakteristični za fosfor (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing or characteristic of phosphorus [phosphoric]</p><p><b>čista ili žuta monobasinska kiselina (H3PO2) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a clear or yellow monobasic acid (H3PO2) [hypophosphorous acid, orthophosphorous acid]</p><p><b>fosfor, zvijezda danica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a multivalent nonmetallic element of the nitrogen family that occurs commonly in inorganic phosphate rocks and as organic phosphates in all living cells [P, atomic number 15]</p><p><i>n.</i> a planet (usually Venus) seen just before sunrise in the eastern sky [Lucifer, daystar, morning star]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom svjetlosti od 1 lumen na kvadratni centimetar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of illumination equal to 1 lumen per square centimeter</p><p><b>bol u oku uzrokovan izlaganjem jakom svjetlu (često povezan s albinizmom) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pain in the eye resulting from exposure to bright light (often associated with albinism) [photophobia]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili uzrokovane svjetlom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or caused by light</p><p><b>rod listnatog i večnozelenog istočnoazijskog stabla i grma koji se široko uzgajaju kao ukrasne biljke zbog svojih bijelih cvijeća i crvenih plodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of deciduous and evergreen east Asian trees and shrubs widely cultivated as ornamentals for their white flowers and red fruits [genus Photinia]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije "Korišćenje" u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvođač proizvodi proizvode iz kategorije "Korišćenje" u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)<