.</i> a variety of leaf-nosed bat</p><p><b>vrsta rod Phylloxeridae: biljne uši (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Phylloxeridae: plant lice [genus Phylloxera]</p><p><b>razorno za različite grožđe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> destructive to various grape plants [grape louse, grape phylloxera]</p><p><b>biljne uši (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant lice [family Phylloxeridae]</p><p><b>evolucija, filogenija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) the sequence of events involved in the evolutionary development of a species or taxonomic group of organisms [evolution, organic evolution, phylogeny]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s evolucijskim razvojem organizama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the evolutionary development of organisms [phyletic]</p><p><b>afinitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) state of relationship between organisms or groups of organisms resulting in resemblance in structure or structural parts [affinity]</p><p><b>u pogledu filogenije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with regard to phylogeny</p><p><b>evolucija, filogenija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) the sequence of events involved in the evolutionary development of a species or taxonomic group of organisms [evolution, organic evolution, phylogenesis]</p><p><b>(lingvistički) velika grupa jezika koji su povijesno povezani, (biologija) glavna taksonomska skupina životinja i biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (linguistics) a large group of languages that are historically related</p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) the major taxonomic group of animals and plants</p><p><b>Kukaši</b></p><p><i>n.</i> phylum or class of elongated wormlike parasites that live in the intestines of vertebrates: spiny-headed worms [Acanthocephala]</p><p><b>Sredstva za proizvodnju: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> segmented worms: earthworms [Annelida]</p><p><b>bezgrebači: arahnidi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> jointed-foot invertebrates: arachnids [Arthropoda]</p><p><b>Nesegmentirani crvi: okrugli crvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unsegmented worms: roundworms [Aschelminthes, Nematoda, phylum Nematoda]</p><p><b>ramenonošci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marine invertebrates that resemble mollusks [Brachiopoda]</p><p><b>mahovnjaci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marine or freshwater animals that form colonies of zooids [Bryozoa, polyzoa]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za životinje koje žive u području Unije, primjenjuje se sljedeći tarifni broj: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> arrowworms: a group of small active transparent marine worms [Chaetognatha]</p><p><b>koljeno Chordata, koljeno svitkovaca, svitkovci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comprises true vertebrates and animals having a notochord [Chordata]</p><p><b>vodene žlijezde (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hydras [Cnidaria, Coelenterata, phylum Coelenterata]</p><p><b>vodene žlijezde (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hydras [Cnidaria, Coelenterata, phylum Cnidaria]</p><p><b>filum u kraljevstvu Protoctista (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a phylum in the kingdom Protoctista [Cryptophyta]</p><p><b>Slijedeći proizvodi: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comb jellies [Ctenophora]</p><p><b>mali morski organizmi veličine tačke koji se nalaze u velikom broju na usnama jastoga. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tiny marine organisms each the size of a period found in great numbers on lobsters' lips [Cycliophora]</p><p><b>bodljikaši, koljeno Echinodermata, koljeno bodljikaša</b></p><p><i>n.</i> radially symmetrical marine invertebrates including e.g. starfish and sea urchins and sea cucumbers [Echinodermata]</p><p><b>Koekstenzivan s ili podfilomom Bryozoa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coextensive with or a subphylum of Bryozoa [Ectoprocta]</p><p><b>ponekad se smatra podfilomom Bryozoa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sometimes considered a subphylum of Bryozoa [Endoprocta, Entoprocta]</p><p><b>Gastropodi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gastropods [Mollusca]</p><p><b>Nesegmentirani crvi: okrugli crvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unsegmented worms: roundworms [Aschelminthes, Nematoda, phylum Aschelminthes]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> proboscis worms [Nemertea, Nemertina, phylum Nemertina]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> proboscis worms [Nemertea, Nemertina, phylum Nemertea]</p><p><b>potkovnjaci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small phylum of wormlike marine animals [Phoronida, Phoronidea]</p><p><b>koljeno Platyhelminthes, koljeno plošnjaka, plošnjaci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flatworms [Platyhelminthes]</p><p><b>čirovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> beard worms [Pogonophora]</p><p><b>koljeno Porifera, koljeno spužvi, spužve</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coextensive with the subkingdom Parazoa: sponges [Porifera]</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama smatraju se superfilom ili podkraljevstvom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications considered a superphylum or a subkingdom [Protozoa]</p><p><b>podjela nižih biljaka koja sadrži jednončelične i biflagelatne alge koje formiraju sjajčana spojeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a division of lower plants comprising unicellular and biflagellate algae that form starchy compounds [Pyrrophyta]</p><p><b>kolnjaci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a phylum including: rotifers [Rotifera]</p><p><b>štrcaljci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> peanut worms [Sipuncula]</p><p><b>bilo koji član roda Physa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any member of the genus Physa</p><p><b>Portugalski ratni čovjek (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Portuguese man-of-war [genus Physalia]</p><p><b>žitarica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ground cherries [genus Physalis]</p><p><b>Starozemska višegodišnja biljka uzgajana zbog svoje ukrasne narandžaste crvene čaše s napunjenim papirom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World perennial cultivated for its ornamental inflated papery orange-red calyx [Chinese lantern plant, bladder cherry, winter cherry]</p><p><b>godišnje od Meksika i južnih Sjedinjenih Država koje imaju jestivo ljubičasto viskozno voće slično malim paradajzom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual of Mexico and southern United States having edible purplish viscid fruit resembling small tomatoes [Mexican husk tomato, jamberry, tomatillo]</p><p><b>godišnji od tropske Južne Amerike s jestivim ljubičastim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual of tropical South America having edible purple fruits [cape gooseberry, purple ground cherry]</p><p><b>Meksikanski godišnji plod naturaliziran u istočnoj Sjevernoj Americi s žutom do ljubičastim jestivim plodovima sličnim malim paradajzom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mexican annual naturalized in eastern North America having yellow to purple edible fruit resembling small tomatoes [jamberry, miltomate, purple ground cherry, tomatillo]</p><p><b>Stari kosmati godišnji iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s slatko žutim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stout hairy annual of eastern North America with sweet yellow fruits [dwarf cape gooseberry, strawberry tomato]</p><p><b>dekorativne američke godišnje s okruglim mesnim žutim bojama zatvorenim u školjku nalik mjehuru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> decorative American annual having round fleshy yellow berries enclosed in a bladderlike husk [downy ground cherry, strawberry tomato]</p><p><b>Nalazi se na morskim plažama od Virginije do Južne Amerike s zelenkasto-žutim cvijećima i narandžastom ili žutom bojom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found on sea beaches from Virginia to South America having greenish-yellow flowers and orange or yellow berries [yellow henbane]</p><p><b>mali rod zapadnih sjevernoameričkih biljaka sličnih Lesquerelli: bladderpods (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of western North American herbs similar to Lesquerella: bladderpods [genus Physaria]</p><p><b>rod Physeter</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Physeteridae [genus Physeter]</p><p><b>Veliki kit s velikom šupljinom u glavi koja sadrži spermaceti i ulje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large whale with a large cavity in the head containing spermaceti and oil [black whale, cachalot, sperm whale]</p><p><b>porodica Physeteridae, porodica ulješura, ulješure</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sperm whales [family Physeteridae]</p><p><b>Terapija koja koristi fizičke sredstvo: vježbe i masaža i drugi načini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> therapy that uses physical agents: exercise and massage and other modalities [physical therapy, physiotherapy]</p><p><b>lijek za čišćenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a purging medicine [aperient, cathartic, purgative]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije 1. i 2. točka (a) ovog članka primjenjuje se sljedeći tarifni broj: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small tropical American tree yielding purple dye and a tanning extract and bearing physic nuts containing a purgative oil that is poisonous in large quantities [Jatropha curcus]</p><p><b>fizički, fizikalan, stvaran, tjelesan, fizikalno, fizikalnog, fizička, fizičke, fizičku, psihički, tjelesna</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving the body as distinguished from the mind or spirit</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the sciences dealing with matter and energy</p><p><i>adj.</i> having substance or material existence</p><p><i>adj.</i> according with material things or natural laws (other than those peculiar to living matter)</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by energetic bodily activity</p><p><i>adj.</i> impelled by physical force especially against resistance [forcible, strong-arm]</p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with material things</p><p><b>sposobnost izvršavanja nekog fizičkog djela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to perform some physical act</p><p><b>grana antropologije koja se bavi nastankom i varijacijom ljudskih bića. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of anthropology dealing with the genesis and variation of human beings</p><p><b>fizička privlačnost, seksualna privlačnost, tjelesna privlačnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a desire for sexual intimacy [concupiscence, eros, sexual desire]</p><p><b>figura, građa, ljudsko tijelo, stas, tijelo, tjelesna građa, trup</b></p><p><i>n.</i> alternative names for the body of a human being [anatomy, bod, build, chassis, figure, flesh, form, frame, human body, material body, physique, shape, soma]</p><p><b>promjena iz jednog stanja (čvrstoga ili tekućeg ili plinovog) u drugo bez promjene kemijskog sastava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a change from one state (solid or liquid or gas) to another without a change in chemical composition [phase change, phase transition, state change]</p><p><b>fizikalna kemija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of chemistry dealing with the physical properties of chemical substances</p><p><b>kompozicija, sastav, uređenje, ustroj, ustrojstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the way in which someone or something is composed [composition, constitution, make-up, makeup]</p><p><b>tjelesna kondicija, fiziološko stanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition or state of the body or bodily functions [physiological condition, physiological state]</p><p><b>kontakt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of touching physically [contact]</p><p><b>tjelesni odgoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> training in the development of and care for the human body</p><p><b>Područje za upravljanje financijskim instrumentima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an entity that has physical existence</p><p><b>fiskultura, gombanje, tjelovježba, vježba, vježbanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of exerting your muscles in various ways to keep fit [exercise, exercising, physical exertion, workout]</p><p><b>fizičko opterećenje, fiskultura, gombanje, tjelovježba, vježba, vježbanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of exerting your muscles in various ways to keep fit [exercise, exercising, physical exercise, workout]</p><p><b>dobro fizičko stanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> good physical condition [fitness]</p><p><b>fizička geografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of physical features of the earth's surface [physiography]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tangible and visible entity [object]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom materijala od 99,99% ili više, ali ne više od 99,99% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pendulum consisting of an actual object allowed to rotate freely around a horizontal axis [compound pendulum]</p><p><b>fizikalna pojava, fizikalni fenomen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a natural phenomenon involving the physical properties of matter and energy</p><p><b>fizikalni proces, proces, tijek, tok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sustained phenomenon or one marked by gradual changes through a series of states [process]</p><p><b>fizikalno svojstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any property used to characterize matter and energy and their interactions</p><p><b>pružanje pomoći osobama s invaliditetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> providing help for disabled persons [physical restoration, therapeutic rehabilitation]</p><p><b>pružanje pomoći osobama s invaliditetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> providing help for disabled persons [physical rehabilitation, therapeutic rehabilitation]</p><p><b>fizička svojstva, pojave i zakoni nečega (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the physical properties, phenomena, and laws of something [physics]</p><p><b>fizioterapeut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> therapist who treats injury or dysfunction with exercises and other physical treatments of the disorder [physiotherapist]</p><p><b>fizikalna medicina, fizikalna terapija, radna terapija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> therapy that uses physical agents: exercise and massage and other modalities [physiatrics, physiotherapy]</p><p><b>fizička topologija, fizički ustroj komunikacijske mreže</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the appearance of the network</p><p><b>troškovi reprodukcije fizičke imovine minus razne naknade (posebno amortizacija) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cost of reproducing physical property minus various allowances (especially depreciation) [reproduction cost]</p><p><b>materijalizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (philosophy) the philosophical theory that matter is the only reality [materialism]</p><p><b>zaokupljenost zadovoljavanjem fizičkih želja i apetita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> preoccupation with satisfaction of physical drives and appetites [animalism]</p><p><b>fizički</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in accord with physical laws</p><p><b>fizički, fizikalan, stvaran, tjelesan, fizikalno, fizikalnog, fizička, fizičke, fizičku, psihički, tjelesna (od &quot;physical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being physical [corporality, corporeality, materiality]</p><p><b>liječnik, ljekar, doktor, dr.med.</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a licensed medical practitioner [Dr., MD, doc, doctor, medico]</p><p><b>pomoć u samoubojstvu ako je pomoćnik liječnik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> assisted suicide where the assistant is a physician</p><p><b>pravo liječnika da odbije da otkrije povjerljive informacije pacijenta bez njegove suglasnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the right of a physician to refuse to divulge confidential information from a patient without the consent of the patient</p><p><b>fizičar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scientist trained in physics</p><p><b>koji se odnose na fizičku kemiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to physical chemistry</p><p><b>fizika, fizici, fizike, fiziku</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the science of matter and energy and their interactions [natural philosophy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the physical properties, phenomena, and laws of something [physical science]</p><p><b>akademski odjel odgovoran za nastavu i istraživanje fizike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the academic department responsible for teaching and research in physics [department of physics]</p><p><b>laboratorij za istraživanje fizike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a laboratory for research in physics [physics laboratory]</p><p><b>laboratorij za istraživanje fizike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a laboratory for research in physics [physics lab]</p><p><b>Slatkovodni puževi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> freshwater snails [family Physidae]</p><p><b>fizionomija, izraz lica, vanjski izgled</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the human face (`kisser' and `smiler' and `mug' are informal terms for `face' and `phiz' is British) [countenance, kisser, mug, phiz, smiler, visage]</p><p><b>fizička geografija, fizički zemljopis, geomorfologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of physical features of the earth's surface [physical geography]</p><