> relating to or involving piezoelectricity</p><p><b>kristal koji se može koristiti kao pretvarač (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crystal that can be used as a transducer</p><p><b>Električna energija proizvedena mehaničkim pritiskom na određene kristale (posebno kvarc ili Rochelleova sol) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electricity produced by mechanical pressure on certain crystals (notably quartz or Rochelle salt) [piezo effect, piezoelectricity]</p><p><b>piezoelektricitet, pojava električnog naboja u nekim kristalima zbog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electricity produced by mechanical pressure on certain crystals (notably quartz or Rochelle salt) [piezo effect, piezoelectric effect]</p><p><b>pijezometar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument for measuring high pressures</p><p><b>besmislica, brbljanje, glupost, brbljati, klafrati, klepetati, laprdati, lupetati, naklapati, torokati, zvocati, ćaskati, ćeretati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trivial nonsense [balderdash, fiddle-faddle]</p><p><i>v.</i> speak (about unimportant matters) rapidly and incessantly [blab, blabber, chatter, clack, gabble, gibber, maunder, palaver, prate, prattle, tattle, tittle-tattle, twaddle]</p><p><i>v.</i> act in a trivial or ineffective way</p><p><b>besmislica, brbljanje, glupost (od &quot;piffle&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (informal) small and of little importance [fiddling, footling, lilliputian, little, niggling, petty, picayune, piddling, trivial]</p><p><b>krmak, oprasiti, oprasiti se, prasac, prase, režnji, svinja, svinjetina, šipka, svinje, krme, Sus scrofa, domaća svinja, gica, pajcek, prostak, sirovina, cajkan, murjak, pandur</b></p><p><i>n.</i> domestic swine [Sus scrofa, grunter, hog, squealer]</p><p><i>n.</i> a coarse obnoxious person [slob, sloven, slovenly person]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person regarded as greedy and pig-like [hog]</p><p><i>n.</i> uncomplimentary terms for a policeman [bull, cop, copper, fuzz]</p><p><i>n.</i> mold consisting of a bed of sand in which pig iron is cast [pig bed]</p><p><i>n.<