irs especially fine soft ones [pilose, pilous]</p><p><b>četvorobridni stup, pilaster, polustup, pilastar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rectangular column that usually projects about a third of its width from the wall to which it is attached</p><p><b>Poncije Pilat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Roman procurator of Judea who ordered that Jesus be crucified (died in AD 36) [Pontius Pilate]</p><p><b>riža kuhana u dobro začinjenoj juhi s lukom ili seljerom i obično peradi ili divljem ili školjkama i ponekad paradajzom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rice cooked in well-seasoned broth with onions or celery and usually poultry or game or shellfish and sometimes tomatoes [pilaf, pilaff, pilaw]</p><p><b>riža kuhana u dobro začinjenoj juhi s lukom ili seljerom i obično peradi ili divljem ili školjkama i ponekad paradajzom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rice cooked in well-seasoned broth with onions or celery and usually poultry or game or shellfish and sometimes tomatoes [pilaf, pilaff, pilau]</p><p><b>sardela, srdela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small fatty fish usually canned [sardine]</p><p><i>n.</i> small fishes found in great schools along coasts of Europe [Sardina pilchardus, sardine]</p><p><b>balvan, brdo, dlaka, gomila, gomilati, hrpa, kalup, nagomilati, naslaga, skup, slagati, složiti, stup, svežanj, zgrnuti, hrpetina, masa, mnoštvo, kupiti, nagomilavati, nakupiti, nakupljati, skupiti, skupljati, sabiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collection of objects laid on top of each other [agglomerate, cumulation, cumulus, heap, mound]</p><p><i>n.</i> (often followed by `of') a large number or amount or extent [batch, deal, flock, good deal, great deal, hatful, heap, lot, mass, mess, mickle, mint, mountain, muckle, passel, peck, plenty, pot, quite a little, raft, sight, slew, spate, stack, tidy sum, wad]</p><p><i>n.</i> a large sum of money (especially as pay or profit) [big bucks, big money, bundle, megabucks]</p><p><i>n.</i> fine soft dense hair (as the fine short hair of cattle or deer or the wool of sheep or the undercoat of certain dogs) [down]</p><p><i>n.</i> battery consisting of voltaic cells arranged in series [galvanic pile, voltaic pile]</p><p><i>n.</i> a column of wood or steel or concrete that is driven into the ground to provide support for a structure [piling, spile, stilt]</p><p><i>n.</i> the yarn (as in a rug or velvet or corduroy) that stands up from the weave [nap]</p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear reactor that uses controlled nuclear fission to generate energy [atomic pile, atomic reactor, chain reactor]</p><p><i>v.</i> arrange in stacks [heap, stack]</p><p><i>v.</i> press tightly together or cram [jam, mob, pack, throng]</p><p><i>v.</i> place or lay as if in a pile</p><p><b>zabijač stupova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a machine that drives piling into the ground</p><p><b>stan izgrađen na stupovima u jezeru ili u blizini jezera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dwelling built on piles in or near a lake [lake dwelling]</p><p><b>gomilanje, akumulirati, gomilati, nagomilati, nagomilavati, nakupiti, nakupljati, okupiti, okupljati, pribirati, prikupiti, prikupljati, sakupiti, sakupljati, skupiti, skupljati, zgrnuti, zgrnuti se, zgrtati, kupiti, naslagati, pribirati se, sabirati, sabrati, slagati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> collect or gather [accumulate, amass, conglomerate, cumulate, gather]</p><p><i>v.</i> arrange into piles or stacks [heap up, stack up]</p><p><i>v.</i> get or gather together [accumulate, amass, collect, compile, hoard, roll up]</p><p><b>za manje rastuće tropske višegodišnje biljke koje se uzgajaju zbog svog blatu bez uboda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing tropical perennials grown for their stingless foliage [genus Pilea]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 1. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste biljaka koje se mogu upotrebljavati u proizvodnji biljaka za uzgoj u skladu s člankom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje točka (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste biljaka za uzgoj u skladu s člankom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći odredbi: (MT)</b></p><p