tes (Rocky Mountains) having dense branches with fissured rust-brown bark and short needles in bunches of 5 and thorn-tipped cone scales [Rocky Mountain bristlecone pine, bristlecone pine]</p><p><b>Srednje veličine trostrukog borova sa pacifičke obale Sjedinjenih Država s istaknutim čvorom na svakoj stupnici čvora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized three-needled pine of the Pacific coast of the United States having a prominent knob on each scale of the cone [knobcone pine]</p><p><b>tanak, srednji, dvostrukožljivi bor iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender medium-sized two-needled pine of eastern North America [jack pine]</p><p><b>vrlo malo stablo slično Rocky Mountain pinonu ali s jednom iglom po fascicleu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very small tree similar to Rocky mountain pinon but having a single needle per fascicle [California single-leaf pinyon]</p><p><b>veliki petiglavni europski bor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large five-needled European pine [Swiss pine, Swiss stone pine, arolla pine, cembra nut tree]</p><p><b>Mali dvostruko- ili trostruko-žiglji pinon iz Meksika i južnog Teksasa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small two-needled or three-needled pinon of Mexico and southern Texas [Mexican nut pine, pinon pine]</p><p><b>šumovi s dvije igle s obalne sjeverozapadne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby two-needled pine of coastal northwestern United States [lodgepole, lodgepole pine, shore pine, spruce pine]</p><p><b>podvrste visokih borova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall subspecies of lodgepole pine [Sierra lodgepole pine]</p><p><b>s velikom površinom od oko 10 m2 do 20 m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pine native to Japan and Korea having a wide-spreading irregular crown when mature [Japanese red pine, Japanese table pine]</p><p><b>Veliki bor južne Sjedinjene Države s kratkim iglama u hrpom od 2-3 i crveno-sjedom kore kada su zrele (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large pine of southern United States having short needles in bunches of 2-3 and red-brown bark when mature [short-leaf pine, shortleaf pine, shortleaf yellow pine]</p><p><b>mali kompaktni dvostruki pinon iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small compact two-needled pinon of southwestern United States [Rocky mountain pinon]</p><p><b>Zapadni sjevernoamerički bor s dugim iglama i vrlo fleksibilnim udovima i tamno sivom bradom sa brdima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> western North American pine with long needles and very flexible limbs and dark-grey furrowed bark [limber pine]</p><p><b>veliki bor s dvije igle iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s svjetlim mekanim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large two-needled pine of southeastern United States with light soft wood [spruce pine]</p><p><b>Visoki simetrični bor zapadne Sjeverne Amerike koji ima duge plavo-zelene igle u grmovima od 3 i izdužene čunje na širenju nešto višenastrih grana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall symmetrical pine of western North America having long blue-green needles in bunches of 3 and elongated cones on spreading somewhat pendulous branches [Jeffrey's pine, Jeffrey pine, black pine]</p><p><b>mali sporo rastući bor zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država sličan boru čipke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small slow-growing pine of western United States similar to the bristlecone pine [ancient pine]</p><p><b>Pinon iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država koji ima samo jednu iglu i često mnogo stabljika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pinon of southwestern United States having solitary needles and often many stems [single-leaf, single-leaf pine, single-leaf pinyon]</p><p><b>visoki bor zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s čvrstima plavo-zelenim iglama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall pine of western North America with stout blue-green needles [mountain pine, silver pine, western white pine]</p><p><b>nizak grmasti bor srednje Europe s kratkim svijetlo zelenim iglama u grmovima po dvije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low shrubby pine of central Europe with short bright green needles in bunches of two [Swiss mountain pine, dwarf mountain pine, mountain pine, mugho pine, mugo pine]</p><p><b>dvostruko ili trostruko iglo (Pinus spp.) uglavnom se nalazi na sjeverozapadnoj obali Kalifornije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> two-needled or three-needled pinon mostly of northwestern California coast [bishop's pine, bishop pine]</p><p><b>veliki dvostruki borovi iz jugoistočne Europe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large two-needled timber pine of southeastern Europe [black pine]</p><p><b>veliki bor s tri igle iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s vrlo dugim iglama i čvrstom izokrenutom udom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large three-needled pine of southeastern United States having very long needles and gnarled twisted limbs [Georgia pine, longleaf pine, pitch pine, southern yellow pine]</p><p><b>petiglavi pinon iz južne Kalifornije i sjeverne Baje Kalifornije koji ima (ponekad tri- ili četveriglavi koji pokazuju hibridizaciju iz Pinus californiarum) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> five-needled pinon of southern California and northern Baja California having (sometimes three-needled or four-needled showing hybridization from Pinus californiarum) [Parry's pinyon, Pinus quadrifolia]</p><p><b>Srednje veličine dvostrukožljivi bor južne Europe s raspršivom krunom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized two-needled pine of southern Europe having a spreading crown [European nut pine, stone pine, umbrella pine]</p><p><b>Česta i široko rasprostranjena visoka drvena borova zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s tamnozelenim iglama u gomilama od 2 do 5 i debelom kore s tamno smeđim pločama kada su zrele (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common and widely distributed tall timber pine of western North America having dark green needles in bunches of 2 to 5 and thick bark with dark brown plates when mature [bull pine, ponderosa, ponderosa pine, western yellow pine]</p><p><b>mali dvonožni gornji bor iz istočnih Sjedinjenih Država (Apalači) s tamno smeđom ljuskom i šiljastim ljuskama s trnjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small two-needled upland pine of the eastern United States (Appalachians) having dark brown flaking bark and thorn-tipped cone scales [hickory pine, prickly pine, table-mountain pine]</p><p><b>petiglavi pinon iz južne Kalifornije i sjeverne Baje Kalifornije koji ima (ponekad tri- ili četveriglavi koji pokazuju hibridizaciju iz Pinus californiarum) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> five-needled pinon of southern California and northern Baja California having (sometimes three-needled or four-needled showing hybridization from Pinus californiarum) [Parry's pinyon, Pinus parryana]</p><p><b>visoki kalifornijski bor s dugim iglama u grmovima od tri, gusto krunčanik i tamno smeđa duboko rascjepkana kora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall California pine with long needles in bunches of 3, a dense crown, and dark brown deeply fissured bark [Monterey pine]</p><p><b>borovi iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s dugim iglama u gomilama od dvije i crvenkasto crno crno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pine of eastern North America having long needles in bunches of two and reddish bark [Canadian red pine, red pine]</p><p><b>veliki bor s tri igle sa istočnog područja Sjedinjenih Država i jugoistočnog Kanade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large three-needled pine of the eastern United States and southeastern Canada [northern pitch pine, pitch pine]</p><p><b>veliki trostruki bor pijesnih močvara jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large three-needled pine of sandy swamps of southeastern United States [pond pine]</p><p><b>srednji bor sjeverozapadnog Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-size pine of northwestern Mexico [southwestern white pine]</p><p><b>visoki bor iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall-growing pine of eastern North America [American white pine, eastern white pine, weymouth pine]</p><p><b>srednji veliki dvostruki bor sjeverne Europe i Azije s crveno-sjedom kora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium large two-needled pine of northern Europe and Asia having flaking red-brown bark [Scotch fir, Scotch pine, Scots pine]</p><p><b>visoka, širenja tri-igle bor iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s crvenkasto-smeđom puklom kore i punom grmljivom gornjom glavom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall spreading three-needled pine of southeastern United States having reddish-brown fissured bark and a full bushy upper head [frankincense pine, loblolly pine]</p><p><b>Veliki japanski ukrasni biljci s dugim iglama u gomilama po 2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large Japanese ornamental having long needles in bunches of 2 [Japanese black pine, black pine]</p><p><b>Srednje veličine petiglavog bora iz jugozapadne Kalifornije s dugim cilindričnim čunjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized five-needled pine of southwestern California having long cylindrical cones [Torrey's pine, Torrey pine, grey-leaf pine, sabine pine, soledad pine]</p><p><b>Obični mali grmasti borovi iz istočnih Sjedinjenih Država koji imaju straggling često okrenuti ili grane i kratke igle u bukama od 2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common small shrubby pine of the eastern United States having straggling often twisted or branches and short needles in bunches of 2 [Jersey pine, Virginia pine, scrub pine]</p><p><b>vrtivjetar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial subshrub of Tenerife having leaves in rosettes resembling pinwheels [Aeonium haworthii]</p><p><i>n.</i> a wheel that has numerous pins that are set at right angles to its rim</p><p><i>n.</i> a toy consisting of vanes of colored paper or plastic that is pinned to a stick and spins when it is pointed into the wind [pinwheel wind collector]</p><p><i>n.</i> a circular firework that spins round and round emitting colored fire [catherine wheel]</p><p><b>tropski grm s blistavim lišćem i mirisnim noćnim cvijećem s krumpiranim ili valovitim korollama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical shrub having glossy foliage and fragrant nocturnal flowers with crimped or wavy corollas [Adam's apple, East Indian rosebay, Nero's crown, Tabernaemontana divaricate, coffee rose, crape jasmine, crepe gardenia, crepe jasmine]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je proizvod proizveden u skladu s člankom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvođač mora imati pravo na odobravanje za proizvodnju proizvoda koji se proizvodi u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pinwheel-shaped rolls spread with cinnamon and sugar and filled with e.g. jam before baking</p><p><b>igračka koja se sastoji od štapova od obojenog papira ili plastike koji je prikovan na štap i okreće se kada je uperi u vjetar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toy consisting of vanes of colored paper or plastic that is pinned to a stick and spins when it is pointed into the wind [pinwheel]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the round shape of a pinwheel</p><p><b>mali crv sličan niti koji zaražava ljudska crijeva i rektum posebno kod djece (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small threadlike worm infesting human intestines and rectum especially in children [Enterobius vermicularis, threadworm]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko nisko rastućih borova zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several low-growing pines of western North America [pinon]</p><p><b>cepin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ax used by mountain climbers for cutting footholds in ice [ice ax, ice axe]</p><p><b>mezon koji drži jezgro zajedno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a meson involved in holding the nucleus together [pi-meson]</p><p><b>biti pionir, krčiti put, nastaniti, pionir, pionirski, prokrčiti put, razviti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who helps to open up a new line of research or technology or art [groundbreaker, innovator, trailblazer]</p><p><i>n.</i> one of the first colonists or settlers in a new territory</p><p><i>v.</i> open up an area or prepare a way [open up]</p><p><i>v.</i> take the lead or initiative in [initiate]</p><p><i>v.</i> open up and explore a new area</p><p><b>pobožan, svetom, nabožan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing or expressing reverence for a deity</p><p><b>lažno govore o religiji ili moralu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> insincere talk about religion or morals [cant]</p><p><b>pobožan, svetom, nabožan (od &quot;pious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a devout and pious manner [devoutly]</p><p><b>pijetet, pobožnost, poniznost, štovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> righteousness by virtue of being pious [piety]</p><p><b>cijukati, koščica, koštica, pijukati, promijeniti, sjeme (voća), točka, zvjezdica, strijeljati, ucmekati, upucati, ustrijeliti, gađati, nastrijeliti, pogađati, pogoditi, pucati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of poultry</p><p><i>n.</i> a minor nonspecific ailment</p><p><i>n.</i> a small hard seed found in some fruits</p><p><i>n.</i> a mark on a die or on a playing card (shape depending on the suit) [spot]</p><p><i>n.</i> a radar echo displayed so as to show the position of a reflecting surface [blip, radar target]</p><p><i>v.</i> kill by firing a missile [shoot]</p><p><i>v.</i> hit with a missile from a weapon [hit, shoot]</p><p><i>v.</i> defeat thoroughly [mop up, rack up, whip, worst]</p><p><b>biti ubijen ili umrijeti (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be killed or die [buy it]</p><p><b>beznačajna osoba, bezveznjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is small and insignificant [small fry, squirt]</p><p><b>tip rod Pipidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Pipidae [genus Pipa]</p><p><b>Južnoamerička žaba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a South American toad [Pipa pipa, Surinam toad]</p><p><b>Južnoamerička žaba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a South American toad [Pipa americana, Surinam toad]</p><p><b>cijev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fee charged for the use of pipes</p><p><i>n.</i> a long tube made of metal or plastic that is used to carry water or oil or gas etc. [pipe, piping]</p><p><b>Indsko smokvo poznato po svojoj velikosti i dugovječnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fig tree of India noted for great size and longevity [Ficus religiosa, bo tree, peepul, pipal tree, pipul, sacred fig]</p><p><b>Indsko smokvo poznato po svojoj velikosti i dugovječnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fig tree of India noted for great size and longevity [Ficus religiosa, bo tree, peepul, pipal, pipul, sacred fig]</p><p><b>bužir, cijev, cjevovod, frula, gajde, lula, pištaljka, svirala, cev, kreštati, kriještati, kričati, pištati, vrištati, zakriještati, zakričati, zapištati, zavrištati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tube with a small bowl at one end [tobacco pipe]</p><p><i>n.</i> a long tube made of metal or plastic that is used to carry water or oil or gas etc. [pipage, piping]</p><p><i>n.</i> a hollow cylindrical shape [tube]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tubular wind instrument</p><p><i>n.</i> the flues and stops on a pipe organ [organ pipe, pipework]</p><p><i>v.</i> utter a shrill cry [pipe up, shriek, shrill]</p><p><i>v.</i> transport by pipeline</p><p><i>v.</i> play on a pipe</p><p><i>v.</i> trim with piping</p><p><b>mala domaća bomba obično smještena u metalnu cijev (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small homemade bomb usually contained in a metal pipe</p><p><b>glava lule</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small round container that is open at the top for holding tobacco [bowl]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a clamp for holding pipe that is to be cut or threaded [pipe vise]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cleaning implement consisting of a flexible tufted wire that is used to clean a pipe stem</p><p><b>podsjekačica cijevi, sjekač cijevi, uređaj za rezanje cijevi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hand tool for cutting pipe</p><p><b>stišati se, utišati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become quiet or quieter [hush, quiesce, quiet, quiet down, quieten]</p><p><b>fantastična ali uzaludna nada (od fantazija izazvanih opijum pipom) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fantastic but vain hope (from fantasies induced by the opium pipe) [dream]</p><p><b>Sredstva za proizvodnju električnih goriva i goriva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a craftsman who installs and repairs pipes and fixtures and appliances [plumber]</p><p><b>armatura cijevi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fitting consisting of threaded pieces of pipe for joining pipes together [pipefitting]</p><p><b>prijevoz do odredišta cijevima, dovesti kroz cijevi (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> transport to a destination through pipes</p><p><i>v.</i> bring in through pipes</p><p><b>Glavni piplista u bendu džepova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the chief piper in a band of bagpipes</p><p><b>visoko ukrašena ceremonijalna pipa američkih Indijanaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a highly decorated ceremonial pipe of Amerindians [calumet, peace pipe]</p><p><b>orgulje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wind instrument whose sound is produced by means of pipes arranged in sets supplied with air from a bellows and controlled from a large complex musical keyboard [organ]</p><p><b>skladište cijevi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rack for holding a smoker's pipes</p><p><b>pušač koji koristi cijev (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a smoker who uses a pipe</p><p><b>kreštati, kriještati, kričati, pištati, vrištati, zakriještati, zakričati, zapištati, zavrištati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> begin to play or sing</p><p><i>v.</i> utter a shrill cry [pipe, shriek, shrill]</p><p><b>čvrsta listnatog vinogreba s velikim lišcima i cvijećem s kalijskom cijevom zakrivljenom poput zdjele cijevi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hardy deciduous vine having large leaves and flowers with the calyx tube curved like the bowl of a pipe [Aristolochia durior, Aristolochia macrophylla, Dutchman's-pipe]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a clamp for holding pipe that is to be cut or threaded [pipe clamp]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> adjustable wrench for gripping and turning a pipe [tube wrench]</p><p><b>bijela glina</b></p><p><i>v.</i> whiten or clean with pipe-clay</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, za proizvodnju proizvo