e se upotrebljavati. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> related to the leafhoppers and spittlebugs but rarely damages cultivated plants [planthopper]</p><p><b>(botanica) biljni proizvod koji djeluje kao hormon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (botany) a plant product that acts like a hormone [growth regulator, phytohormone]</p><p><b>biljke, carstvo Plantae, carstvo biljaka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (botany) the taxonomic kingdom comprising all living or extinct plants [Plantae, kingdom Plantae]</p><p><b>biljni svijet, biljka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (botany) a living organism lacking the power of locomotion [flora, plant]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko malih insekata, posebno lisnatog stabla koji se hrane usisavanjem soka iz biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several small insects especially aphids that feed by sucking the juices from plants [louse]</p><p><b>biljna tvar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> material derived from plants [plant substance]</p><p><b>klasifikacija biljaka, sistematika biljaka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the order of plants</p><p><b>biljni organ</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a functional and structural unit of a plant or fungus</p><p><b>biljna građa, biljni dio</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any part of a plant or fungus [plant structure]</p><p><b>Prirodna izbočina ili rast iz biljnog tijela ili organa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a natural projection or outgrowth from a plant body or organ [enation]</p><p><b>Bilinogojstvo, biljni proizvod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a product made from plant material</p><p><b>botaničar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a biologist specializing in the study of plants [botanist, phytologist]</p><p><b>biljna građa, biljni dio</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any part of a plant or fungus [plant part]</p><p><b>biljna tvar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> material derived from plants [plant material]</p><p><b>biljno tkivo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tissue of a plant</p><p><b>bilo koja tvar koju proizvode biljke koja je po svojim svojstvima slična izvanstaničnom bakterijskom toksinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any substance produced by 