ino dlakavim lištima i neosjetljivim bijelim mirisnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed Old World perennial naturalized in North America having finely hairy leaves and inconspicuous white fragrant flowers [hoary plantain]</p><p><b>Planine iz mediteranskih regija čija se sjemena otkucaju i postaju želatinska kada su vlažna i koriste se kao blagi laksativ (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plantain of Mediterranean regions whose seeds swell and become gelatinous when moist and are used as a mild laxative [Spanish psyllium, fleawort, psyllium]</p><p><b>Srednja Amerika s crvenkastim listovima i širokim listovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American plantain having reddish leafstalks and broad leaves [broad-leaved plantain, rugel's plantain]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička godišnja ili dvogodišnja biljka s dugim mekanim dlakama na lišću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American annual or biennial with long soft hairs on the leaves [hoary plantain]</p><p><b>banana za pečenje, bokvica, trputec</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous plants of the genus Plantago</p><p><i>n.</i> a banana tree bearing hanging clusters of edible angular greenish starchy fruits [Musa paradisiaca, plantain tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> starchy banana-like fruit</p><p><b>kozmopolitska obitelj malih biljaka i nekoliko grmlja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cosmopolitan family of small herbs and a few shrubs [Plantaginaceae, family Plantaginaceae]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih višegodišnjih biljaka s gomilom raskošnih širokih rebrastih listova i grmovima bijelih, plavih ili ljubičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous perennials having mounds of sumptuous broad ribbed leaves and clusters of white, blue, or lilac flowers [day lily]</p><p><b>Bananski drvo s visivim grmovima jestivih uglovitih zelenkasto-škrobnijih plodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a banana tree bearing hanging clusters of edible angular greenish starchy fruits [Musa paradisiaca, plantain]</p><p><b>Različite mačke. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of pussytoes</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s biljkama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to plants</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili se javljaju na donjoj površini stopala (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or occurring on the undersurface of the foot</p><p><b>Sklonite noge i noge na površini noge. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flexion of the toes when the sole of the foot is stroked firmly on the outer side from the heel to the front in persons over the age of 2 years</p><p><b>bradavica na podnožju stopala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wart occurring on the sole of the foot</p><p><b>kolonija, nasad, plantaža, sad, sađenje, zasađivanje, voćnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an estate where cash crops are grown on a large scale (especially in tropical areas)</p><p><i>n.</i> a newly established colony (especially in the colonization of North America)</p><p><i>n.</i> garden consisting of a small cultivated wood without undergrowth [grove, orchard, woodlet]</p><p><b>vlasnik ili upravitelj plantaže (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the owner or manager of a plantation [planter]</p><p><b>Konj obilježen izdržljivost i obučen da se kreće na brzom trčanje šetnje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a horse marked by stamina and trained to move at a fast running walk [Tennessee walker, Tennessee walking horse, Walking horse]</p><p><b>biljka, biljni, oprema, poduzeće, posaditi, posaditi biljku, postaviti, postrojenje, prijevara, saditi, tvornica, uglaviti, uređaj, zasaditi, bilja, flore, pogona, postrojenja, uređaja (od &quot;plant&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used especially of ideas or principles) deeply rooted [deep-rooted, deep-seated, implanted, ingrained]</p><p><i>adj.</i> set in the soil for growth</p><p><b>plantažer, vlasnik plantaže</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the owner or manager of a plantation [plantation owner]</p><p><i>n.</i> a worker who puts or sets seeds or seedlings into the ground</p><p><i>n.</i> a decorative pot for house plants</p><p><b>koktel od ruma i limunskog soka s šećerom i pone