ivating plants (fruit or flowers or vegetables or ornamental plants) [horticulturist]</p><p><b>u obliku pločne cilijane ličinke hidrozoana koelenterata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the flat ciliated free-swimming larva of hydrozoan coelenterates</p><p><b>broš, plaketa, ploča, tanjur, značka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (pathology) a small abnormal patch on or inside the body</p><p><i>n.</i> a memorial made of brass [brass, memorial tablet]</p><p><b>antiinflamatorni lijek (trgovinski naziv Plaquenil) koji se koristi u liječenju reumatoidnog artritisa i malarije i lupusa eritematosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anti-inflammatory drug (trade name Plaquenil) used in the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis and malaria and lupus erythematosus [hydroxychloroquine]</p><p><b>bara, isprepletati, lokva, plesti, pljuskanje, zapljuskivanje, pljuskati, pljusnuti, pokapati, polijevati, politi, poprskati, poprskavati, pošpricati, poštrcati, prskati, zalijevati, zaliti, zapljusnuti, špricati, štrcati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sound like water splashing [splash]</p><p><i>v.</i> interlace the shoots of [pleach]</p><p><i>v.</i> dash a liquid upon or against [spatter, splash, splatter, splosh, swash]</p><p><b>protoplazma rodničnih stanica koja sadrži hromozome i gene, bezbožna vodena tekućina krvi i limfe koja ne sadrži stanice, ali u kojoj su suspendirane krvne stanice (eritrociti, leukociti i trombociti) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the protoplasm of the germ cells that contains chromosomes and genes [germ plasm]</p><p><i>n.</i> the colorless watery fluid of the blood and lymph that contains no cells, but in which the blood cells (erythrocytes, leukocytes, and thrombocytes) are suspended [blood plasma, plasma]</p><p><b>plazma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the colorless watery fluid of the blood and lymph that contains no cells, but in which the blood cells (erythrocytes, leukocytes, and thrombocytes) are suspended [blood plasma, plasm]</p><p><i>n.</i> a green slightly translucent variety of chalcedony used as a gemstone</p><p><i>n.</i> (physical chemistry) a fourth state of matter distinct from solid or liquid or gas and present in stars and fusion reactors</p><p><b>stanica koja se razvija iz B limfocita u reakciji na specifičan antigen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cell that develops from a B lymphocyte in reaction to a specific antigen [plasmacyte]</p><p><b>tanka membrana (dvostruki sloj lipida) koja okružuje citoplazmu stanice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin membrane (a double layer of lipids) enclosing the cytoplasm of a cell [cell membrane, cytomembrane]</p><p><b>fizika plazme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of physics concerned with matter in its plasma phase</p><p><b>bilo koji od proteina u krvnoj plazmi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the proteins in blood plasma</p><p><b>Koagulacijski faktor čiji nedostatak rezultira hemoragijskom tendencijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coagulation factor whose deficiency results in a hemorrhagic tendency [factor XI]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 mas.% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the precursor of a plasma cell</p><p><b>stanica koja se razvija iz B limfocita u reakciji na specifičan antigen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cell that develops from a B lymphocyte in reaction to a specific antigen [plasma cell]</p><p><b>neoplazma plazmatičnih stanica (obično u koštanoj srži) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> neoplasm of plasma cells (usually in bone marrow)</p><p><b>plasma se odvaja od cjelokupne krvi i ostatak se vraća donatoru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plasma is separated from whole blood and the rest is returned to the donor</p><p><b>plazmid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small cellular inclusion consisting of a ring of DNA that is not in a chromosome but is capable of autonomous replication [plasmid DNA]</p><p><b>plazmid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small cellular inclusion consisting of a ring of DNA that is not in a chromosome but is capable of autonomous replication [plasmid]</p><p><b>fibrinolizin, plazmin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an enzyme that dissolves the fibrin of blood clots [fibrinolysin]</p><p><b>plazminogen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inactive form of plasmin that occurs in plasma and is converted to plasmin by organic solvents</p><p><b>aktivator plazminogena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> protease produced in the kidney that converts plasminogen to plasmin and so initiates fibrinolysis [urokinase]</p><p><b>u obliku sluzi iz klase Myxomycetes (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slime mold of the class Myxomycetes [acellular slime mold, myxomycete, true slime mold]</p><p><b>paraziti malarije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> malaria parasites [family Plasmodiidae]</p><p><b>tip rod Plasmodiophoraceae koji obuhvaća sitne biljne parazitske gljivice slične sluznicama i ponekad uključene među njih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of Plasmodiophoraceae comprising minute plant parasitic fungi similar to and sometimes included among the slime molds [genus Plasmodiophora]</p><p><b>gljiva koja je slična sluznici koja uzrokuje otekline ili deformacije korijena kupusa i srodnih biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus resembling slime mold that causes swellings or distortions of the roots of cabbages and related plants [clubroot fungus]</p><p><b>obitelj gljiva koje često uzrokuju hipertrofiju u biljkama sjemenki (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of fungi often causing hypertrophy in seed plants [family Plasmodiophoraceae]</p><p><b>plasmodium</b></p><p><i>n.</i> multinucleate sheet of cytoplasm characteristic of some stages of such organisms as slime molds</p><p><i>n.</i> parasitic protozoan of the genus Plasmodium that causes malaria in humans [Plasmodium vivax, malaria parasite]</p><p><b>plasmodium</b></p><p><i>n.</i> parasitic protozoan of the genus Plasmodium that causes malaria in humans [malaria parasite, plasmodium]</p><p><b>Pobjeda 1757. godine Britanaca pod Cliveom nad Siraj-ud-daula koji je uspostavio britansku nadmoć nad Bengalom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the victory in 1757 by the British under Clive over Siraj-ud-daula that established British supremacy over Bengal [battle of Plassey]</p><p><b>flaster, gips, kreč, krečiti, melem, naljepak, pokriti, žbuka, žbukati, medicinski flaster, ožbukati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mixture of lime or gypsum with sand and water</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several gypsum cements [plaster of Paris]</p><p><i>n.</i> a medical dressing consisting of a soft heated mass of meal or clay that is spread on a cloth and applied to the skin to treat inflamed areas or improve circulation etc. [cataplasm, poultice]</p><p><i>n.</i> a surface of hardened plaster (as on a wall or ceiling) [plasterwork]</p><p><i>n.</i> adhesive tape used in dressing wounds [adhesive plaster, sticking plaster]</p><p><i>v.</i> apply a heavy coat to [plaster over, stick on]</p><p><i>v.</i> cover conspicuously or thickly, as by pasting something on [beplaster]</p><p><i>v.</i> affix conspicuously</p><p><i>v.</i> apply a plaster cast to</p><p><i>v.</i> coat with plaster [daub]</p><p><i>v.</i> dress by covering with a therapeutic substance [poultice]</p><p><b>gips</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bandage consisting of a firm covering (often made of plaster of Paris) that immobilizes broken bones while they heal [cast, plaster cast]</p><p><b>gips</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bandage consisting of a firm covering (often made of plaster of Paris) that immobilizes broken bones while they heal [cast, plaster bandage]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mas.% ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mas.% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several gypsum cements [plaster]</p><p><b>Nanesi tešku obluku na (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> apply a heavy coat to [plaster, stick on]</p><p><b>osoba (smatrana) bez ljudskih nedostataka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person (considered to be) without human failings</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wallboard with a gypsum plaster core bonded to layers of paper or fiberboard [gypsum board]</p><p><b>pijan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of hair) made smooth by applying a sticky or glossy substance [slicked]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of walls) covered with a coat of plaster [sealed]</p><p><i>adj.</i> very drunk [besotted, blind drunk, blotto, cockeyed, crocked, fuddled, loaded, pie-eyed, pissed, pixilated, slopped, sloshed, smashed, soaked, soused, sozzled, squiffy, stiff, tight, wet]</p><p><b>fasader, zidar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a worker skilled in applying plaster</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hand tool with a flat face used for smoothing and finishing the surface of plaster or cement or stucco [float]</p><p><b>flaster, gips, kreč, krečiti, melem, naljepak, pokriti, žbuka, žbukati (od &quot;plaster&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the application of plaster [daubing]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trowel used to spread and smooth plaster</p><p><b>s površinom od tvrdog gips (kao što je zid ili strop) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a surface of hardened plaster (as on a wall or ceiling) [plaster]</p><p><b>gipkost, plastičan, plastična masa, plastične, plastičnost, plastika, plastiku, savitljiv, savitljivost, vitkost, plastične mase, kartica, kreditna kartica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> generic name for certain synthetic or semisynthetic materials that can be molded or extruded into objects or films or filaments or used for making e.g. coatings and adhesives</p><p><i>n.</i> a card (usually plastic) that assures a seller that the person using it has a satisfactory credit rating and that the issuer will see to it that the seller receives payment for the merchandise delivered [charge card, charge plate, credit card]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being molded or modeled (especially of earth or clay or other soft material) [fictile, moldable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being influenced or formed [pliant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> forming or capable of forming or molding or fashioning [formative, shaping]</p><p><b>umjetnost oblikovanja ili modeliranja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the arts of shaping or modeling</p><p><b>plastična vrećica, vrećica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bag made of thin plastic material</p><p><b>bomba napravljena od plastičnog eksploziva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb made of plastic explosive</p><p><b>eksplozivni materijal koji se lako oblikuje oko predmeta kojeg je namijenjen uništiti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an explosive material that is easily molded around the object it is intended to destroy [plastique]</p><p><b>plastična folija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin sheet of (usually plastic and usually transparent) material used to wrap or cover things [film]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena (CAS RN 1344-26-8) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a laminate made by bonding plastic layers</p><p><b>kirurg koji ljepša tijelo (posebno lice) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a surgeon who beautifies the body (especially the face) [cosmetic surgeon]</p><p><b>operacije koje se odnose na terapijsku ili kozmetičku reformu tkiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgery concerned with therapeutic or cosmetic reformation of tissue [anaplasty, reconstructive surgery]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wrapping consisting of a very thin transparent sheet of plastic</p><p><b>u plastičnom obliku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a plastic manner</p><p><b>plastelin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a synthetic material resembling clay but remaining soft</p><p><b>Postaju plastični, kao što je dodavanje plastikanta., proizvoditi plastiku, kao što je dodavanje plastifikatora (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become plastic, as by having a plasticizer added [plasticize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make plastic, as by the addition of a plasticizer [plasticize]</p><p><b>plastifikator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance added to plastics or other materials to make them more pliable [plasticizer]</p><p><b>plasticitet tla, plastičnost, savitljivost, spareni helični filament</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being physically malleable [malleability]</p><p><b>Postaju plastični, kao što je dodavanje plastikanta., proizvoditi plastiku, kao što je dodavanje plastifikatora (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become plastic, as by having a plasticizer added [plasticise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make plastic, as by the addition of a plasticizer [plasticise]</p><p><b>plastifikator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance added to plastics or other materials to make them more pliable [plasticiser]</p><p><b>industrija plastičnih masa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industry that manufactures plastic articles</p><p><b>plastidi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various small particles in the cytoplasm of the cells of plants and some animals containing pigments or starch or oil or protein</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, za potrebe primjene ovog članka, za sve proizvode koji se upotrebljavaju u proizvodnji plastike, za potrebe primjene ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći uvjet: (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> preserve (tissue) with plastics, as for teaching and research purposes</p><p><b>Proces koji uključuje fiksiranje i dehidraciju te prisilno impregnaciju i tvrđivanje bioloških tkiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a process involving fixation and dehydration and forced impregnation and hardening of biological tissues</p><p><b>eksplozivni materijal koji se lako oblikuje oko predmeta kojeg je namijenjen uništiti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an explosive material that is easily molded around the object it is intended to destroy [plastic explosive]</p><p><b>od čelika ili od majice za žene, prednji dio muške košulje, metalni prsački oklop koji se nosio ispod oklopa, veliki podloga nosi od strane mačevalaca za zaštitu grudi, (zoologija) dio kornjače koje formira donji dio školjke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ornamental front of a woman's bodice or shirt</p><p><i>n.</i> the front of man's dress shirt</p><p><i>n.</i> a metal breastplate that was worn under a coat of mail</p><p><i>n.</i> a large pad worn by a fencer to protect the chest</p><p><i>n.</i> (zoology) the part of a turtle's shell forming its underside</p><p><b>jelo, pripremiti kartu, pripremiti mapu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a map showing planned or actual features of an area (streets and building lots etc.)</p><p><i>v.</i> make a plat of [plot]</p><p><b>utor između Argentine i Urugvaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an estuary between Argentina and Uruguay [La Plata, Rio de la Plata]</p><p><b>bivši grad u Boeotiji, poraz perzijske vojske od strane Grka u Platei 479. pne. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former town in Boeotia</p><p><i>n.</i> a defeat of the Persian army by the Greeks at Plataea in 479 BC [battle of Plataea]</p><p><b>tip rod Plataleidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Plataleidae [genus Platalea]</p><p><b>Čisti bijeli žličasti žličar južne Evrasije i sjeveroistočne Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pure white crested spoonbill of southern Eurasia and northeastern Africa [common spoonbill]</p><p><b>čokoladice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spoonbills [family Plataleidae]</p><p><b>bilo koje od nekoliko stabala rodova Platanus s tankom bjelom kore koja se odmjeri u male ploče i lobne lišće i kugličaste glave plodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several trees of the genus Platanus having thin pale bark that scales off in small plates and lobed leaves and ball-shaped heads of fruits [plane tree, sycamore]</p><p><b>Koextenzivna s rodom Platanus: platani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coextensive with the genus Platanus: plane trees [family Platanaceae, plane-tree family]</p><p><b>Rijenski delfini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> river dolphins [family Platanistidae]</p><p><b>biljne biljke iz područja sjeverne i južne hemisfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herbaceous terrestrial orchids of temperate northern and southern hemispheres [genus Platanthera]</p><p><b>Orhideja južnoeuropske vrste s mirisnim zelenkasto-bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> south European orchid having fragrant greenish-white flowers [Habenaria bifolia, lesser butterfly orchid]</p><p><b>južnoeuropska orhideja s tamnozelenim cvijećem koje su v