unus domestica and Prunus armeniaca [plumcot tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> hybrid between plum and apricot</p><p><b>Hibridi proizvedeni ukrcavanjem Prunus domestica i Prunus armeniaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hybrid produced by crossing Prunus domestica and Prunus armeniaca [plumcot]</p><p><b>paperje, perjanica, perje, pero, dotjerati se, dotjerivati se, lickati se, nalickati se, srediti se, sređivati se, urediti se, uređivati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anything that resembles a feather in shape or lightness</p><p><i>n.</i> a feather or cluster of feathers worn as an ornament</p><p><i>n.</i> the light horny waterproof structure forming the external covering of birds [feather, plumage]</p><p><i>v.</i> rip off [fleece, gazump, hook, overcharge, pluck, rob, soak, surcharge]</p><p><i>v.</i> be proud of [congratulate, pride]</p><p><i>v.</i> deck with a plume</p><p><i>v.</i> clean with one's bill [preen]</p><p><i>v.</i> form a plume</p><p><i>v.</i> dress or groom with elaborate care [dress, preen, primp]</p><p><b>Uročnjava u obliku trske iz roda Erianthus s velikim perjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reedlike grass of the genus Erianthus having large plumes</p><p><b>biljka iz Kine i Japana koja se široko uzgaja zbog svojih plemastih panikala kremastih bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herb of China and Japan widely cultivated for its plumelike panicles of creamy white flowers [Macleaya cordata, bocconia]</p><p><b>bilo koji od brojnih dvostruko- ili višegodišnjih biljaka s lijepim ljubičastim ili žutim ili povremeno bijelim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous biennial to perennial herbs with handsome purple or yellow or occasionally white flower heads [plumed thistle]</p><p><b>od biljke s vrhom s perjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a plant tipped with a plume</p><p><b>savršena stvar, suho grožđe, šljiva, tamnoljubičasta (od &quot;plum&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or covered with or abounding in plumes [plumy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having an ornamental plume or feathery tuft [plumate, plumose]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a knight's helmet) having a decorative plume [crested]</p><p><b>vrsta škorpije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of scorpionfish [Scorpaena grandicornis]</p><p><b>bilo koji od brojnih dvostruko- ili višegodišnjih biljaka s lijepim ljubičastim ili žutim ili povremeno bijelim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous biennial to perennial herbs with handsome purple or yellow or occasionally white flower heads [plume thistle]</p><p><b>visoka trava na Novom Zelandu koja raste za plemske cvjetne glave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall grass of New Zealand grown for plumelike flower heads [Arundo richardii, Cortaderia richardii, toe toe, toetoe]</p><p><b>kao sliv. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a plume [plumy]</p><p><b>ljeploviti grmovi i stabla tropske Amerike s granama poput kandelabra i mirisnim bijelim ili ružičastim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrubs and trees of tropical America having branches like candelabra and fragrant white or pink flowers [Plumiera, genus Plumeria]</p><p><b>Indijski frangipani s uspravnom navukom i koničnim oblikom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> frangipani of India having an erect habit and conical form [pagoda tree, temple tree]</p><p><b>visoka, malo razgranata, kužna stabla s velikim mirisnim žutim cvijećem s bijelim središtima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall sparingly branched conical tree having large fragrant yellow flowers with white centers [West Indian jasmine, pagoda tree]</p><p><b>ljeploviti grmovi i stabla tropske Amerike s granama poput kandelabra i mirisnim bijelim ili ružičastim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrubs and trees of tropical America having branches like candelabra and fragrant white or pink flowers [Plumeria, genus Plumeria]</p><p><b>Kao šljiva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a plum fruit</p><p><b>olovni visak, olovnica, visak, sručiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the metal bob of a plumb line [plumb, plumb bob]</p><p><i>v.</i> drop sharply [plump]</p><p><b>vrlo poželjno, (glas) utjecajno blag i bogat (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very desirable</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a voice) affectedly mellow and rich</p><p><b>s masenim udubljenjem od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an ornamental plume or feathery tuft [plumate, plumed]</p><p><b>bez uvijanja, bucmast, debeljkast, debeljuškast, debeo, gojiti se, gomila, jasan, naglo, pothraniti, pumašan, punačak, punašan, splasnuti, sručiti, tresnuti, debljati, gojiti, toviti, udebljati, ugojiti, utoviti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sound of a sudden heavy fall</p><p><i>v.</i> drop sharply [plummet]</p><p><i>v.</i> set (something or oneself) down with or as if with a noise [flump, plank, plonk, plop, plump down, plunk, plunk down]</p><p><i>v.</i> make fat or plump [fat, fatten, fatten out, fatten up, fill out, flesh out, plump out]</p><p><i>v.</i> give support (to) or make a choice (of) one out of a group or number [go]</p><p><i>adj.</i> sufficiently fat so as to have a pleasing fullness of figure [chubby, embonpoint]</p><p><i>adv.</i> straight down especially heavily or abruptly</p><p><b>sručiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> drop heavily [plank down, plonk down]</p><p><i>v.</i> set (something or oneself) down with or as if with a noise [flump, plank, plonk, plop, plump, plunk, plunk down]</p><p><b>Budi iza. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be behind [back, endorse, indorse, plunk for, support]</p><p><b>Doći iznenada i neočekivano. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> arrive suddenly and unannounced</p><p><b>debljati, gojiti, toviti, udebljati, ugojiti, utoviti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> depart suddenly</p><p><i>v.</i> make fat or plump [fat, fatten, fatten out, fatten up, fill out, flesh out, plump]</p><p><b>Napuni se treseći. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make fuller by shaking [fluff up, shake up]</p><p><b>bez uvijanja, bucmast, debeljkast, debeljuškast, debeo, gojiti se, gomila, jasan, naglo, pothraniti, pumašan, punačak, punašan, splasnuti, sručiti, tresnuti (od &quot;plump&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very large</p><p><b>oblina, punašnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bodily property of being well rounded [embonpoint, roundness]</p><p><b>paperje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> down feather of young birds</p><p><b>kao sliv., s masnim udelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, s masnim udubljenjem od više od 50 mm, ali ne više od 500 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a plume [plumelike]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or covered with or abounding in plumes [plumed]</p><p><i>adj.</i> adorned with feathers or plumes [feathered, feathery]</p><p><b>haranje, harati, plijen, pljačka, pljačkati, pljačku, raznositi, nepošten dobitak, nepoštena dobit, prljavi novac, ukradena roba, poharati, oplijeniti, orobiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> goods or money obtained illegally [booty, dirty money, loot, pillage, prize, swag]</p><p><i>v.</i> take illegally [loot]</p><p><i>v.</i> plunder (a town) after capture [sack]</p><p><i>v.</i> steal goods [despoil, foray, loot, pillage, ransack, reave, rifle, strip]</p><p><i>v.</i> destroy and strip of its possession [despoil, rape, spoil, violate]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je riječ o iznosu od 50 EUR, u slučaju da je riječ o iznosu od 100 EUR, u slučaju da je iznos od 100 EUR. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of plundering (especially the embezzlement of goods on shipboard)</p><p><b>pokraden</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> wrongfully emptied or stripped of anything of value [looted, pillaged, ransacked]</p><p><b>haranje, harati, plijen, pljačka, pljačkati, pljačku, raznositi (od &quot;plunder&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who takes spoils or plunder (as in war) [despoiler, freebooter, looter, pillager, raider, spoiler]</p><p><b>pljačka, pljaćku</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of stealing valuable things from a place [pillage, pillaging]</p><p><i>adj.</i> given to taking by force what is desired</p><p><b>gnjuranje, pad, poniranje, potapanje, roniti, ronjenje, uroniti, zagnjuriti, zagnjurivanje, zamočiti, zariti, zaroniti, intrigirati, zainteresirati, zaintrigirati, bacati se, baciti se, posvetiti se, posvećivati se, udubiti se, udubljivati se, unijeti se, unositi se, zadubiti se, zadubljivati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brief swim in water [dip]</p><p><i>n.</i> a steep and rapid fall</p><p><i>v.</i> thrust or throw into [immerse]</p><p><i>v.</i> drop steeply [dive, plunk]</p><p><i>v.</i> dash violently or with great speed or impetuosity</p><p><i>v.</i> begin with vigor [launch]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be immersed [immerse]</p><p><i>v.</i> fall abruptly [dump]</p><p><i>v.</i> immerse briefly into a liquid so as to wet, coat, or saturate [dip, douse, dunk, souse]</p><p><i>v.</i> devote (oneself) fully to [absorb, engross, engulf, immerse, soak up, steep]</p><p><b>klip, lakouman igrač, masivan čep, nerazuman, teški konjanik, teško stapalo, ronilac, stap</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who risks losses for the possibility of considerable gains [speculator]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who dives (into water) [diver]</p><p><i>n.</i> hand tool consisting of a stick with a rubber suction cup at one end [plumber's helper]</p><p><i>n.</i> mechanical device that has a plunging or thrusting motion [piston]</p><p><b>pad, sručiti, zaroniti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hollow twanging sound</p><p><i>n.</i> (baseball) hitting a baseball so that it drops suddenly [plunker]</p><p><i>v.</i> make or move along with a sound as of a horse's hooves striking the ground [clop, clump, clunk]</p><p><i>v.</i> set (something or oneself) down with or as if with a noise [flump, plank, plonk, plop, plump, plump down, plunk down]</p><p><i>v.</i> drop steeply [dive, plunge]</p><p><i>v.</i> pull lightly but sharply with a plucking motion [pick, pluck]</p><p><i>adv.</i> with a short hollow thud [plop]</p><p><b>sručiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> set (something or oneself) down with or as if with a noise [flump, plank, plonk, plop, plump, plump down, plunk]</p><p><b>Budi iza. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be behind [back, endorse, indorse, plump for, support]</p><p><b>pad (od &quot;plunk&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (baseball) hitting a baseball so that it drops suddenly [plunk]</p><p><b>davno prošlo vrijeme, pluskvamperfekt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a perfective tense used to express action completed in the past [past perfect, past perfect tense, pluperfect tense]</p><p><i>adj.</i> more than perfect</p><p><b>pluskvamperfekt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a perfective tense used to express action completed in the past [past perfect, past perfect tense, pluperfect]</p><p><b>množina, plural, u pluralu, višestruk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the form of a word that is used to denote more than one [plural form]</p><p><i>adj.</i> composed of more than one member, set, or kind</p><p><i>adj.</i> grammatical number category referring to two or more items or units</p><p><b>množina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the form of a word that is used to denote more than one [plural]</p><p><b>pluralizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of pluralizing or attributing plurality to [pluralization]</p><p><b>znak s gramatskim morfema koji ukazuje na množina (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> mark with a grammatical morpheme that indicates plural [pluralize]</p><p><b>pluralisam, pluralizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a social organization in which diversity of racial or religious or ethnic or cultural groups is tolerated</p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine that reality consists of several basic substances or elements</p><p><i>n.</i> the practice of one person holding more than one benefice at a time</p><p><b>svećenik koji ima više od jednog blagodatnika u isto vrijeme, filozof koji vjeruje da nijedno objašnjenje ne može objasniti sve prirodne pojave., osoba koja vjeruje da različite etničke, kulturne ili vjerske skupine mogu živjeti zajedno u društvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cleric who holds more than one benefice at a time</p><p><i>n.</i> a philosopher who believes that no single explanation can account for all the phenomena of nature</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who believes that distinct ethnic or cultural or religious groups can exist together in society</p><p><b>pluralistička, pluralistički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the philosophical doctrine of pluralism</p><p><b>množina, plural, većina, većina glasova, mnoštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being plural</p><p><i>n.</i> a large indefinite number [battalion, large number, multitude, pack]</p><p><i>n.</i> (in an election with more than 2 options) the number of votes for the candidate or party receiving the greatest number (but less that half of the votes) [relative majority]</p><p><b>Čin pluralizacije ili pripisivanja pluraliteta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of pluralizing or attributing plurality to [pluralisation]</p><p><b>znak s gramatskim morfema koji ukazuje na množina (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> mark with a grammatical morpheme that indicates plural [pluralise]</p><p><b>i, plus, pozitivan, pozitivna veličina, pribrojiti, više, dobra strana, pozitivna strana, prednost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a useful or valuable quality [asset]</p><p><i>n.</i> the arithmetic operation of summing [addition, summation]</p><p><i>adj.</i> on the positive side or higher end of a scale</p><p><i>adj.</i> involving advantage or good [positive]</p><p><b>pumperice, široke spo gaće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> men's baggy knickers hanging below the knees</p><p><b>znak koji označava operaciju dodavanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sign indicating the operation of addition</p><p><b>pliš, vrsta samta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fabric with a nap that is longer and softer than velvet</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by extravagance and profusion [lavish, lucullan, plushy]</p><p><b>(iz teksture) nalik plušnom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of textures) resembling plush [plushy]</p><p><b>od samta, sličan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of textures) resembling plush [plush-like]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by extravagance and profusion [lavish, lucullan, plush]</p><p><b>Plutarh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek biographer who wrote Parallel Lives (46?-120 AD)</p><p><b>porodica gljiva iz reda Agaricales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of fungi belonging to the order Agaricales [family Pluteaceae]</p><p><b>veliki rod gljiva iz obitelji Pluteaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large genus of fungi belonging to the family Pluteaceae [genus Pluteus, roof mushroom]</p><p><b>Agaric s sjajnim crvenim šeširom i vitkim stabljkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agaric with a brilliant scarlet cap and a slender stalk</p><p><b>mala jestiva agarica sa vitkim stabljkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small edible agaric with a slender stalk [deer mushroom]</p><p><b>jedljiva agarica koja se nalazi u hrpom pilane tvrdog drveta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edible agaric found in piles of hardwood sawdust [sawdust mushroom]</p><p><b>lik iz crtića kojeg je stvorio Walt Disney., (Rimska mitologija) bog podzemlja, Veliki asteroid za koji se nekada mislilo da je najudaljenija planeta poznata od Sunca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cartoon character created by Walt Disney</p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman mythology) god of the underworld [Dis, Dis Pater, Orcus]</p><p><i>n.</i> a large asteroid that was once thought to be the farthest known planet from the sun</p><p><b>novčana aristokracija, plutokracija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political system governed by the wealthy people</p><p><b>plutokrat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who exercises power by virtue of wealth</p><p><b>plutokrat (od &quot;plutocrat&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of a plutocrat [plutocratical]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili karakteristika plutokrat (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of a plutocrat [plutocratic]</p><p><b>Velika masa upadajuće magmanske stijene za koju se vjeruje da se zaglavila duboko u zemlji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large mass of intrusive igneous rock believed to have solidified deep within the earth [batholite, batholith, plutonic rock]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili karakteristika Hades ili Tartarus (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Hades or Tartarus [Hadean, Tartarean]</p><p><b>Iz magmatske stijene koja je zagorjela ispod površine zemlje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of igneous rock that has solidified beneath the earth's surface [irruptive]</p><p><b>Velika masa upadajuće magmanske stijene za koju se vjeruje da se zaglavila duboko u zemlji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large mass of intrusive igneous rock believed to have solidified deep within the earth [batholite, batholith, pluton]</p><p><b>plutonij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solid silvery grey radioactive transuranic element whose atoms can be split when bombarded with neutrons [Pu, atomic number 94]</p><p><b>izotop plutonija koji se vrlo brzo raspodijeli i koji se koristi u atomskom oružju i kao gorivo za reaktore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a highly fissionable isotope of plutonium that is used in atomic weapons and as a reactor fuel</p><p><b>nuklearnog oružja u kojem se ogromna energija oslobađa nuklearnom fisijom (razbijanjem jezgra teškog elementa kao što su uranij 235 ili plutonij 239) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear weapon in which enormous energy is released by nuclear fission (splitting the nuclei of a heavy element like uranium 235 or plutonium 239) [A-bomb, atom bomb, atomic bomb, fission bomb]</p><p><b>s ciljem stvaranja "izračunavanja" u skladu s člankom 97. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a steel or beryllium sphere containing plutonium 239 that triggers nuclear fission when compressed by explosives [plutonium trigger]</p><p><b>s ciljem stvaranja "izračunavanja" u skladu s člankom 97. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a steel or beryllium sphere containing plutonium 239 that triggers nuclear fission when compressed by explosives [plutonium pit]</p><p><b>Zlatni plovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> golden plovers [genus Pluvialis]</p><p><b>Kursevi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coursers [genus Pluvianus]</p><p><b>Afrički korser koji se hrani insektima parazitima na krokodilima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> African courser that feeds on insect parasites on crocodiles [crocodile bird]</p><p><b>kišomjer, ambrograf, ambrometar, pluviograf, pluviometar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gauge consisting of an instrument to measure the quantity of precipitation [rain gage, rain gauge, udometer]</p><p><b>peti mjesec revolucionarnog kalendara (januar i veljača) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fifth month of the Revolutionary calendar (January and February)</p><p><b>častiti, dodati, gostiti, krstariti, marljivo raditi, nabor, ošinuti, pohitjeti, požuriti, prometovati, salijetati, saobraćati, sklonost, sloj, spojiti, struk, vršiti posao, opremati, opremiti, opskrbiti, opskrbljivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the strands twisted together to make yarn or rope or thread</p><p><i>n.</i> (usually in combinations) one of several layers of cloth or paper or wood as in plywood</p><p><i>v.</i> give what is desired or needed, especially support, food or sustenance [cater, provide, supply]</p><p><i>v.</i> apply oneself diligently</p><p><i>v.</i> travel a route regularly [run]</p><p><i>v.</i> join together as by twisting, weaving, or molding</p><p><i>v.</i> wield vigorously</p><p><i>v.</i> use diligently</p><p><b>šperploča</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a laminate made of thin layers of wood [plywood]</p><p><b>častiti, dodati, gostiti, krstariti, marljivo raditi, nabor, ošinuti, pohitjeti, požuriti, prometovati, salijetati, saobraćati, sklonost, sloj, spojiti, struk, vršiti posao (od &quot;ply&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who plies a trade [plier]</p><p><b>kliješta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gripping hand tool with two hinged arms and (usually) serrated jaws [pair of pliers, pliers]</p><p><b>Plymouth</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in Massachusetts founded by Pilgrims in 1620</p><p><b>kolonija koju su osnovali hodočasnici kada su stigli na Plymouth Rock 1620. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> colony formed by the Pilgrims when they arrived at Pl