orm [poetry, verse]</p><p><b>pjesnik, pjesnika, pjesnikinja, poeta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a writer of poems (the term is usually reserved for writers of good poetry)</p><p><b>pjesnik koji je nezvanično smatran za počastnog čovjeka u određenoj grupi ili regiji., pjesnik službeno imenovan za kraljevsko domaćinstvo u Velikoj Britaniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a poet who is unofficially regarded as holding an honorary position in a particular group or region</p><p><i>n.</i> the poet officially appointed to the royal household in Great Britain</p><p><b>pjevač narodnih pjesama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a singer of folk songs [folk singer, jongleur, minstrel, troubadour]</p><p><b>pjesnikinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman poet</p><p><b>pjesnički, poetski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to poetry [poetical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by romantic imagery</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to poets</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of or befitting poetry [poetical]</p><p><b>rezultat (dobar ili loš) koji je zaslužan i odgovarajući (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an outcome (good or bad) that is well deserved and fitting [comeupance, comeuppance, just deserts]</p><p><b>licencu koju je pisac ili umjetnik koristio kako bi povećao učinak svog djela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> license used by a writer or artist to heighten the effect of their work</p><p><b>(prosodija) sustav versikacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (prosody) a system of versification [prosody, rhythmic pattern]</p><p><b>poetičan, pjesnički, poetski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to poetry [poetic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of or befitting poetry [poetic]</p><p><b>poetičan (od &quot;poetical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a poetic manner</p><p><b>poetika, teorija poezije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> study of poetic works</p><p><b>sastavlja stihove ili ih stavlja u stihove (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> compose verses or put into verse [poetize, verse, versify]</p><p><b>pisac koji komponira rime. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a writer 