us Swainsona that are poisonous to sheep [darling pea]</p><p><b>Obična višegodišnja smrtna kamna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common perennial death camas [Zigadenus nuttalli]</p><p><b>glatka američka močvarna grmlja s pinatnim lišćama i zelenkastim cvijećima s zelenkastim bijelim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> smooth American swamp shrub with pinnate leaves and greenish flowers followed by greenish white berries [Rhus vernix, Toxicodendron vernix, poison ash, poison sumac]</p><p><b>plin koji je otrovan za udah ili kontakt (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gas that is poisonous to breath or contact</p><p><b>Velika grana dvostruko biljke porijeklom iz Euroazije i Afrike i neprimjereno u Sjevernoj Americi s velikim listima nalik paprarima i bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large branching biennial herb native to Eurasia and Africa and adventive in North America having large fernlike leaves and white flowers [California fern, Conium maculatum, Nebraska fern, hemlock, poison parsley, winter fern]</p><p><b>dermatitis uzrokovan kontaktom s biljkom otrovnog bršljana, planina koja se širi na istočnoj i središnjoj strani Sjedinjenih Država s trnatim listovima i zelenkastim cvijećem s bijelim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dermatitis resulting from contact with the poison ivy plant</p><p><i>n.</i> climbing plant common in eastern and central United States with ternate leaves and greenish flowers followed by white berries [Rhus radicans, Toxicodendron radicans, markweed, poison mercury, poison oak]</p><p><b>planina koja se širi na istočnoj i središnjoj strani Sjedinjenih Država s trnatim listovima i zelenkastim cvijećem s bijelim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> climbing plant common in eastern and central United States with ternate leaves and greenish flowers followed by white berries [Rhus radicans, Toxicodendron radicans, markweed, poison ivy, poison oak]</p><p><b>mliječni rastvor iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> milkweed of southwester