>n.</i> the target company defends itself by making its stock less attractive to an acquirer</p><p><b>dermatitis uzrokovan kontaktom s otrovnom biljkom sumake, glatka američka močvarna grmlja s pinatnim lišćama i zelenkastim cvijećima s zelenkastim bijelim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dermatitis resulting from contact with a poison sumac plant</p><p><i>n.</i> smooth American swamp shrub with pinnate leaves and greenish flowers followed by greenish white berries [Rhus vernix, Toxicodendron vernix, poison ash, poison dogwood]</p><p><b>Evroazijska biljka prirodna u Americi koja ima bijele cvijeće i otrovne dlakave lišće i nosi crne bobice koje su ponekad otrovne, ali ponekad jestive. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian herb naturalized in America having white flowers and poisonous hairy foliage and bearing black berries that are sometimes poisonous but sometimes edible [Solanum nigrum, black nightshade, common nightshade, poisonberry]</p><p><b>Evroazijska biljka prirodna u Americi koja ima bijele cvijeće i otrovne dlakave lišće i nosi crne bobice koje su ponekad otrovne, ali ponekad jestive. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian herb naturalized in America having white flowers and poisonous hairy foliage and bearing black berries that are sometimes poisonous but sometimes edible [Solanum nigrum, black nightshade, common nightshade, poison-berry]</p><p><b>trovatelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who kills with poison</p><p><b>otrovanje, trovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the physiological state produced by a poison or other toxic substance [intoxication, toxic condition]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving poison to a person or animal with the intent to kill</p><p><b>gadan, odvratan, otrovan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the qualities or effects of a poison [toxicant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not safe to eat</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by deep ill will [venomous, vicious]</p><p><b>otrovna višegodišnja vinograda Starog svijeta s ljubičastim cvijećem i ovalnim koralno crvenim bojama (MT)</b></p><