stributed throughout both hemispheres [family Polygalaceae, milkwort family]</p><p><b>poligamija, poligamist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is married to two or more people at the same time</p><p><b>imati više partnera u isto vrijeme, koji imaju više oblika gametoecija na istoj biljci (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having more than one mate at a time</p><p><i>adj.</i> having several forms of gametoecia on the same plant [heteroicous, polyoicous]</p><p><b>poligamija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition or practice of having more than one spouse at a time</p><p><b>gen koji sam po sebi ima mali utjecaj na fenotip, ali koji može djelovati zajedno s drugima kako bi proizveo promjenjive varijacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gene that by itself has little effect on the phenotype but which can act together with others to produce observable variations</p><p><b>U slučaju da je genetski podrijetlo podrijetlo koje je pod kontrolom više gena istovremeno ili je s njim povezano. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to an inheritable character that is controlled by several genes at once</p><p><b>nasljedna bolest koju kontroliraju nekoliko gena istovremeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inherited disease controlled by several genes at once [polygenic disorder]</p><p><b>nasljedna bolest koju kontroliraju nekoliko gena istovremeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inherited disease controlled by several genes at once [polygenic disease]</p><p><b>mnogoježičan, poliglot, poliglotski, višejezičan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who speaks more than one language [linguist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a command of or composed in many languages</p><p><b>mnogokut, mnogokutnik, poligon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a closed plane figure bounded by straight sides [polygonal shape]</p><p><b>rod biljaka reda Polygonales uglavnom iz sjeverne umjerene zone (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of plants of order Polygonales chiefly of the north temperate zone [buckwheat family, family Polygonaceae]</p><p><b>s više strana ili u