itant of or reside in [dwell, inhabit, live]</p><p><i>v.</i> fill with inhabitants</p><p><b>obiluje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> furnished with inhabitants</p><p><b>gradsko područje, urbano područje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a geographical area constituting a city or town [urban area]</p><p><b>broj stanovnika, naseljavanje, populacija, populacijski, pučanstvo, stanovništvo, populacije, populaciji, populacijska, populaciju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the people who inhabit a territory or state</p><p><i>n.</i> a group of organisms of the same species inhabiting a given area</p><p><i>n.</i> (statistics) the entire aggregation of items from which samples can be drawn [universe]</p><p><i>n.</i> the number of inhabitants (either the total number or the number of a particular race or class) in a given place (country or city etc.)</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of populating (causing to live in a place)</p><p><b>Komisija Ekonomskog i socijalnog vijeća Ujedinjenih naroda koja se bavi kontrolama stanovništva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the commission of the Economic and Social Council of the United Nations that is concerned with population control</p><p><b>Kontrola rasta stanovništva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> control over the growth of population</p><p><b>rast broja stanovnika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> increase in the number of people who inhabit a territory or state</p><p><b>grafikon koji pokazuje broj ljudi u funkciji njihovih godina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chart showing the number of people as a function of their ages</p><p><b>znanstvenik koji proučava rast i gustoću populacije i njihove vitalne statistike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scientist who studies the growth and density of populations and their vital statistics [demographer, demographist]</p><p><b>promjena u relativnom broju različitih skupina pojedinaca koje čine populaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a change in the relative numbers of the different groups of individuals making up a population</p><p><b>populizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the political doctrine that supports the rights and powers of the common people in their struggle with the privileged elite</p><p><b>Neko tko se zalaže za prava običnog naroda nad onima elite. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who advocates the rights of the common people over those of the elite</p><p><b>bivša politička stranka u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former political party in the United States [People's Party]</p><p><b>gusto naseljen, napučen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> densely populated [thickly settled]</p><p><b>rod drveća iz obitelji Salicaceae koji se nalazi na sjevernoj hemisferi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of trees of the family Salicaceae that is found in the northern hemisphere [genus Populus]</p><p><b>popel koji se široko uzgaja u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a poplar that is widely cultivated in the United States [abele, aspen poplar, silver-leaved poplar, white aspen, white poplar]</p><p><b>popel sjeveroistočne Sjeverne Amerike s širokim lišćama u obliku srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> poplar of northeastern North America with broad heart-shaped leaves [balsam poplar, hackmatack, tacamahac]</p><p><b>veliki brzo rastući poplar s slabijim lobnim listovima sivim na donjoj površini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large rapidly growing poplar with faintly lobed dentate leaves grey on the lower surface [gray poplar, grey poplar]</p><p><b>Popel u istočnoj i središnjoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common poplar of eastern and central United States [Eastern cottonwood, necklace poplar]</p><p><b>Aspen s uskom krunom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aspen with a narrow crown [Canadian aspen, big-toothed aspen, bigtooth aspen, bigtoothed aspen, large-toothed aspen, large tooth aspen]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički popel s velikim zaobljenim listovima sa škrobom i drvenim drvetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American poplar with large rounded scalloped leaves and brownish bark and wood [black cottonwood, downy poplar, swamp cottonwood, swamp poplar]</p><p><b