jene u rod Haldea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications placed in genus Haldea [Haldea striatula, eastern ground snake]</p><p><b>kalij karbonat, potaša</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a potassium compound often used in agriculture and industry [caustic potash, potassium hydroxide]</p><p><b>bijeli kristalni dvosulfat aluminija: kalijski dvosulfat aluminija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white crystalline double sulfate of aluminum: the potassium double sulfate of aluminum [alum, potassium alum]</p><p><b>kalijevom solom (KCl) (trgovinski nazivi K-Dur 20, Kaochlor i K-lor i Klorvess i K-lit) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> salt of potassium (KCl) (trade names K-Dur 20, Kaochlor and K-lor and Klorvess and K-lyte) [K-Dur 20, K-lor, K-lyte, Kaochlor, Klorvess, potassium chloride, potassium muriate]</p><p><b>kalij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light soft silver-white metallic element of the alkali metal group [K, atomic number 19]</p><p><b>kristalna so (KHCO3) koja se koristi u prahu za pečenje i kao antacid (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crystalline salt (KHCO3) that is used in baking powder and as an antacid [potassium bicarbonate, potassium hydrogen carbonate]</p><p><b>bijeli kristalni dvosulfat aluminija: kalijski dvosulfat aluminija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white crystalline double sulfate of aluminum: the potassium double sulfate of aluminum [alum, potash alum]</p><p><b>kristalna so (KHCO3) koja se koristi u prahu za pečenje i kao antacid (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crystalline salt (KHCO3) that is used in baking powder and as an antacid [potassium acid carbonate, potassium hydrogen carbonate]</p><p><b>Sol koja se koristi posebno u prahu za pečenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt used especially in baking powder [cream of tartar, potassium hydrogen tartrate, tartar]</p><p><b>Bijela kristalna sol (KBr) koja se koristi kao sedativ i u fotografiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white crystalline salt (KBr) used as a sedative and in photography</p><p><b>Bijela so (K2CO3) koja je osnovna u rastvoru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white salt (K2CO3) that is basic in solution</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,25% ili više, ali ne više od 0,25%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white salt (KClO3) used in matches, fireworks, and explosives</p><p><b>kalijevom solom (KCl) (trgovinski nazivi K-Dur 20, Kaochlor i K-lor i Klorvess i K-lit) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> salt of potassium (KCl) (trade names K-Dur 20, Kaochlor and K-lor and Klorvess and K-lyte) [K-Dur 20, K-lor, K-lyte, Kaochlor, Klorvess, potash muriate, potassium muriate]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,25% ili više, ali ne više od 0,25%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a poisonous salt (KCN) used in electroplating and in photography</p><p><b>Oranžno-crvena sol koja se koristi za proizvodnju boja i fotografije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an orange-red salt used in making dyes and in photography</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena (CAS RN 1344-26-8) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cyanide compound that is prepared by the reaction of potassium cyanide with ferrous salts [yellow prussiate of potash]</p><p><b>kristalna so (KHCO3) koja se koristi u prahu za pečenje i kao antacid (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crystalline salt (KHCO3) that is used in baking powder and as an antacid [potassium acid carbonate, potassium bicarbonate]</p><p><b>Sol koja se koristi posebno u prahu za pečenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt used especially in baking powder [cream of tartar, potassium bitartrate, tartar]</p><p><b>kalijev hidroksid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a potassium compound often used in agriculture and industry [caustic potash, potash]</p><p><b>kristalna sol u organskoj sintezi i pri proizvodnji fotografskih emulzija te u jodiranoj stolnoj soli (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crystalline salt in organic synthesis and in making photographic emulsions and in iodized table salt</p><p><b>kalijevom solom (KCl) (trgovinski nazivi K-Dur 20, Kaochlor i K-lor i Klorvess i K-lit) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> salt of potassium (KCl) (trade names K-Dur 20, Kaochlor and K-lor and Klorvess and K-lyte) [K-Dur 20, K-lor, K-lyte, Kaochlor, Klorvess, potash muriate, potassium chloride]</p><p><b>(KNO3) se koristi uglavnom kao đubrivo i eksploziv (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (KNO3) used especially as a fertilizer and explosive [niter, nitre, saltpeter, saltpetre]</p><p><b>otrovna sol koja stvara tamno ljubičaste kristale i kada se rastvori u vodi, izgleda ljubičasto-crveno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a poisonous salt that forms dark purple crystals and is purple-red when dissolved in water [permanganate of potash]</p><p><b>dvostruka sol koja se koristi u Seidlitz prahu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a double salt used in Seidlitz powder [Rochelle salt, Rochelle salts]</p><p><b>Geološko datiranje koje se temelji na udjelovima radioaktivnog kalijuma u uzorku stijena i njegovom proizvodu raspada, argonu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> geological dating that relies on the proportions of radioactive potassium in a rock sample and its decay product, argon</p><p><b>pijenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a serving of drink (usually alcoholic) drawn from a keg [draft, draught, tipple]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of drinking (especially an alcoholic drink)</p><p><b>krumpir, krumpirov</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edible tuber native to South America [Irish potato, murphy, spud, tater, white potato]</p><p><i>n.</i> annual native to South America having underground stolons bearing edible starchy tubers [Solanum tuberosum, white potato, white potato vine]</p><p><b>biljka s velikim jestivim korijenima iz Amazonske doline, Sjevernoamerička loza s mirisnim cvjetovima i jestivim gomoljicama, u obliku orašastih gomila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> twining plant of Amazon basin having large edible roots [Pachyrhizus tuberosus, yam bean]</p><p><i>n.</i> a North American vine with fragrant blossoms and edible tubers [Apios americana, Apios tuberosa, Indian potato, groundnut, groundnut vine, wild bean]</p><p><i>n.</i> nutlike tuber [groundnut, wild bean]</p><p><b>crno-žuto bubače koje se u odrasloj i larvnoj fazi hrani lišćama krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> black-and-yellow beetle that feeds in adult and larval stages on potato leaves [Colorado beetle, Colorado potato beetle, Leptinotarsa decemlineata, potato bug]</p><p><b>-Pomalo krumpira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blight of potatoes [potato disease, potato mildew, potato mold, potato murrain]</p><p><b>crno-žuto bubače koje se u odrasloj i larvnoj fazi hrani lišćama krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> black-and-yellow beetle that feeds in adult and larval stages on potato leaves [Colorado beetle, Colorado potato beetle, Leptinotarsa decemlineata, potato beetle]</p><p><b>čips</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin crisp slice of potato fried in deep fat [Saratoga chip, chip, crisp]</p><p><b>-Pomalo krumpira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blight of potatoes [potato blight, potato mildew, potato mold, potato murrain]</p><p><b>velika i gospodarski važna obitelj biljaka ili grmova ili stabala često snažno mirisnih i ponekad narkotičnih ili otrovnih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large and economically important family of herbs or shrubs or trees often strongly scented and sometimes narcotic or poisonous [Solanaceae, family Solanaceae]</p><p><b>Veliki australijski zimzelena paprika s jestivom korijenom ponekad se koristi kao povrće od strane autohtonih ljudi, Srednja cijela površina: od oko 5 m2 do 6 m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large Australasian evergreen fern with an edible rhizome sometimes used as a vegetable by indigenous people [Marattia salicina]</p><p><i>n.</i> small epiphytic fern of South America with tuberous swellings along rhizomes [Solanopteris bifrons]</p><p><b>gljivica koja uzrokuje bolest u krumpiru karakteriziranu crnim mrljama na gomoljima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungus causing a disease in potatoes characterized by black scurfy spots on the tubers [Pellicularia filamentosa, Rhizoctinia solani]</p><p><b>-Pomalo krumpira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blight of potatoes [potato blight, potato disease, potato mold, potato murrain]</p><p><b>-Pomalo krumpira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blight of potatoes [potato blight, potato disease, potato mildew, potato murrain]</p><p><b>bolest lišća biljaka krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of the leaves of potato plants</p><p><b>grivo-smeđi molj čija je ličinka crv u bubrezima krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> greyish-brown moth whose larva is the potato tuberworm [Phthorimaea operculella, potato tuber moth, splitworm]</p><p><b>-Pomalo krumpira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blight of potatoes [potato blight, potato disease, potato mildew, potato mold]</p><p><b>povećanje nosa s dilatacijom folikula i crvenilo i istaknuta vaskularnost kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enlargement of the nose with dilation of follicles and redness and prominent vascularity of the skin [brandy nose, copper nose, hammer nose, hypertrophic rosacea, rhinophyma, rum-blossom, rum nose, toper's nose]</p><p><b>napravljen od rezanog krumpira i jaja sa malo brašna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> made of grated potato and egg with a little flour [latke]</p><p><b>krastavci, pečeni krumpir, luščenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crisp fried potato peeling [potato peelings, potato skin]</p><p><b>krastavci, pečeni krumpir, luščenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crisp fried potato peeling [potato peel, potato skin]</p><p><b>trka novosti u kojoj natjecatelji premještaju krumpir s jednog mjesta na drugo jedno u isto vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a novelty race in which competitors move potatoes from one place to another one at a time</p><p><b>salata od krumpira, krumpir salata</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various salads having chopped potatoes as the base</p><p><b>uzrok bolesti krompira karakterizirane smeđakivim korkovitim tkivom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cause of a potato disease characterized by brownish corky tissue [Streptomyces scabies]</p><p><b>krastavci, pečeni krumpir, luščenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crisp fried potato peeling [potato peel, potato peelings]</p><p><b>Južnoamerički grm ili malo drvo koje se široko uzgaja u tropima, čvrsta škrgača iz Čilea koja se uzgaja kao ukras zbog svojih mirisnih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South American shrub or small tree widely cultivated in the tropics [Brazilian potato tree, Solanum macranthum, Solanum wrightii]</p><p><i>n.</i> hardy climbing shrub of Chile grown as an ornamental for its fragrant flowers [Solanum crispum]</p><p><b>grivo-smeđi molj čija je ličinka crv u bubrezima krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> greyish-brown moth whose larva is the potato tuberworm [Phthorimaea operculella, potato moth, splitworm]</p><p><b>larva krumpirskog molja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> larva of potato moth [Phthorimaea operculella]</p><p><b>Vina iz Kostarike rijetko naoružana šiljakim bodljicama i s velikim lilak-plavim cvjetovima, u obliku od šarene ili crvene trske, s lišćama i cvjetovima od plavog boje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vine of Costa Rica sparsely armed with hooklike spines and having large lilac-blue flowers [Solanum wendlandii, giant potato creeper]</p><p><i>n.</i> copiously branched vine of Brazil having deciduous leaves and white flowers tinged with blue [Solanum jasmoides]</p><p><b>gljivična bolest koja uzrokuje tamne bradavice u očima bubrega krumpira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungous disease causing dark warty spongy excrescences in the eyes of potato tubers</p><p><b>gljivica koja uzrokuje bolest bradavica u gomoljima krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungus causing potato wart disease in potato tubers [Synchytrium endobioticum]</p><p><b>Larva velikog zelenog bijelacasta jastogova koji se hrani biljkama paradajza i krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large green white-striped hawkmoth larva that feeds on tomato and potato plants [Manduca quinquemaculata, tomato hornworm]</p><p><b>bolest žute patuljke u biljkama krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the yellow dwarf disease of potato plants [yellow dwarf of potato]</p><p><b>virus koji uzrokuje usporavanje rasta rasta i žutiranje lišća biljaka krumpira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the virus that produces stunting and yellowing of the leaves of potato plants</p><p><b>pripadnik Algonkijskog naroda iz Michigana i Wisconsina., Algonkijski jezik koji govore Potawatomi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Algonquian people originally of Michigan and Wisconsin</p><p><i>n.</i> the Algonquian language spoken by the Potawatomi</p><p><b>s velikim trbuhom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a large belly [abdominous, paunchy]</p><p><b>slang za guzicu, S druge strane, u slučaju da se radi o električnom gorivu, to znači da se radi o električnom gorivu koji se koristi za proizvodnju električne energije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slang for a paunch [bay window, corporation, pot, tummy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a bulbous stove in which wood or coal is burned [potbelly stove]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se radi o električnom gorivu, to znači da se radi o električnom gorivu koji se koristi za proizvodnju električne energije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bulbous stove in which wood or coal is burned [potbelly]</p><p><b>književni sastav lošeg kvaliteta koji je napisan brzo da bi se zaradilo (da bi se vrelo u lonac) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a literary composition of poor quality that was written quickly to make money (to boil the pot)</p><p><b>(od biljke u loncu) koja je prevelika za svoj spremnik što dovodi do čvrstosti ili upletanja korijena (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a potted plant) grown too large for its container resulting in matting or tangling of the roots [rootbound]</p><p><b>radnik u gostionici ili javnom domu koji služi kupcima i radi razne poslove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a worker in an inn or public house who serves customers and does various chores [potman]</p><p><b>nelegalno destilirano irsko viski (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unlawfully distilled Irish whiskey</p><p><b>Ruski časnik i političar koji je bio omiljen Katarini II. i 1762. pomogao joj je da preuzme vlast. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Russian officer and politician who was a favorite of Catherine II and in 1762 helped her to seize power [Grigori Aleksandrovich Potemkin, Grigori Potemkin, Grigori Potyokin, Potyokin]</p><p><b>nešto što izgleda impresivno, ali zapravo nema nikakve suštine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that seems impressive but in fact lacks substance</p><p><b>stanje snažnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being potent [potency]</p><p><b>jakost, moć, moćnost, potentnost, sila, snaga, sposobnost, jačina, učinkovitost, izvedivost, moguanost, potencijal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the power or right to give orders or make decisions [authorisation, authority, authorization, dominance, say-so]</p><p><i>n.</i> capacity to produce strong physiological or chemical effects [effectiveness, strength]</p><p><i>n.</i> the inherent capacity for coming into being [potential, potentiality]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being potent [potence]</p><p><b>djeluje snažno, moćan, potentan, snažan, sposoban, uvjerljiv, jak</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having great influence [powerful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or wielding force or authority [strong]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a strong physiological or chemical effect [stiff, strong]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a male) capable of copulation [virile]</p><p><b>vladar, vlastodržac, diktator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ruler who is unconstrained by law [dictator]</p><p><b>moguć, mogućih, mogućnost, potencijal, potencijala, potencijalan, potencijalnih, potencijalno, izvedivost, moguanost, sposobnost, napon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inherent capacity for coming into being [potency, potentiality]</p><p><i>n.</i> the difference in electrical charge between two points in a circuit expressed in volts [electric potential, potential difference, potential drop, voltage]</p><p><i>adj.</i> existing in possibility [possible]</p><p><i>adj.</i> expected to become or be [likely]</p><p><b>napon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the difference in electrical charge between two points in a circuit expressed in volts [electric potential, potential, potential drop, voltage]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom energije od 1,15 kVA ili većim od 2,15 kVA (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> resistors connected in series across a voltage source [voltage divider]</p><p><b>pad napona, napon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the difference in electrical charge between two points in a circuit expressed in volts [electric potential, potential, potential difference, voltage]</p><p><b>mehanička energija koju tijelo ima zbog svog položaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mechanical energy that a body has by virtue of its position [P.E.]</p><p><b>Mjerenje potencijalne energije jediničnog naboja u određenoj točki u krugu u odnosu na referentnu točku (zemlja) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measure of the potential energy of a unit charge at a given point in a circuit relative to a reference point (ground)</p><p><b>mogućnost, potencijal, potencijalnost, izvedivost, moguanost, sposobnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the inherent capacity for coming into being [potency, potential]</p><p><i>n.</i> an aptitude that may be developed [capability, capableness]</p><p><b>potencijalno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with a possibility of becoming actual</p><p><b>omogućiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> increase the effect of or act synergistically with (a drug or a physiological or biochemical phenomenon)</p><p><b>potencijacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) the synergistic effect of two drugs given simultaneously</p><p><b>uglavnom višegodišnje biljke i grmovi sjeverne hemisfere: petoglavi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chiefly perennial northern hemisphere herbs and shrubs: cinquefoil [genus Potentilla]</p><p><b>nizko rastuća višegodišnja biljka s srebrnim lištima ispod. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing perennial having leaves silvery beneath [goose-tansy, goose grass, silverweed]</p><p><b>potemciometar, potenciometar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument for measuring direct current electromotive forces</p><p><i>n.</i> a resistor with three terminals, the third being an adjustable center terminal [pot]</p><p><b>djeluje snažno, moćan, potentan, snažan, sposoban, uvjerljiv (od &quot;potent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a manner having a powerful influence [powerfully]</p><p><b>biljka od biljaka od vrste S. spp. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of thorny herbs or shrubs of the family Rosaceae [genus Poterium]</p><p><b>Europska vrtna biljka s ljubičastim cvijećem i lištima koja se ponekad koristi za salate (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European garden herb with purple-tinged flowers and leaves that are sometimes used for salads [burnet bloodwort, pimpernel, salad burnet]</p><p><b>puna posuda, puna zdjela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quantity contained in a pot [pot]</p><p><b>osoba koja stalno puši marihuanu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who smokes marijuana habitually</p><p><b>metež, zabrinuti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an excited state of agitation [dither, flap, fuss, tizzy]</p><p><i>v.</i> make upset or troubled</p><p><i>v.</i> make a fuss [dither, flap]</p><p><b>Svaka biljka koja se koristi za proizvodnju hrane ili začina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various herbaceous plants whose leaves or stems or flowers are cooked and used for food or seasoning</p><p><b>jama, rupa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pit or hole produced by wear or weathering (especially in a road surface) [chuckhole]</p><p><b>jama, rupa (od &quot;pothole&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who explores caves [spelaeologist, speleologist, spelunker]</p><p><b>S-obliknu kuku za objesiti lonac preko vatre. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an S-shaped hook to suspend a pot over a fire</p><p><b>bilo koja od različitih tropskih lijana rodova Scindapsus, Zeleni lijana, široko uzgajana zbog svog raznovrsnog lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various tropical lianas of the genus Scindapsus</p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen liana widely cultivated for its variegated foliage [Epipremnum aureum, Scindapsus aureus, golden pothos, ivy arum]</p><p><b>Taverna koja se sastoji od zgrade s barom i javnim sobama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tavern consisting of a building with a bar and public rooms [gin mill, pub, public house, saloon, taphouse]</p><p><b>neprofesionalni arheolog, netko tko sudjeluje u natjecanjima kako bi sakupio trofeje., osoba koja lovi za hranu (ne za sport) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nonprofessional archeologist</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who participates in contests in order to collect trophies</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who hunts for food (not for sport)</p><p><b>napitak, travarica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a medicinal or magical or poisonous beverage</p><p><b>ceremonijalna gozba koju održavaju neki Indijanci sjeverozapadne obale Sjeverne Amerike (kao što je proslava vjenčanja ili novog pristupanja) u kojoj domaćin daje poklone članovima plemena i drugima kako bi pokazao svoje superiorno bogatstvo (ponekad, ranije, do vlastitog osiromašenja) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ceremonial feast held by some Indians of the northwestern coast of North America (as in celebrating a marriage or a new accession) in which the host gives gifts to tribesmen and others to display his superior wealth (sometimes, formerly, to his own impoverishment)</p><p><b>Sve što se dogodi da je dostupno posebno kada se nudi neočekivanom gostu ili kada ga gosti donesu i podijele svi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> whatever happens to be available especially when offered to an unexpected guest or when brought by guests and shared by all</p><p><b>radnik u gostionici ili javnom domu koji služi kupcima i radi razne poslove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a worker in an inn or public house who serves customers and does various chores [potboy]</p><p><b>rijeka u istočnom središnjem dijelu Sjedinjenih Država, Termin se ponekad koristi za Washington, D.C. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in the east central United States [Potomac River]</p><p><i>n.</i> term sometimes used to refer to Washington, D.C.</p><p><b>rijeka u istočnom središnjem dijelu Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in the east central United States [Potomac]</p><p><b>snažna 