r [praetorian, pretorial, pretorian]</p><p><b>pretorijanac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Praetorian Guard [Praetorian Guard]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a Roman praetor [praetorial, pretorial, pretorian]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of or similar to the corruptible soldiers in the Praetorian Guard with respect to corruption or political venality [Pretorian]</p><p><b>član pretorske straže, elitni tjelohranitelj rimskog cara u drevnom Rimu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Praetorian Guard [Praetorian]</p><p><i>n.</i> the elite bodyguard of a Roman Emperor in ancient Rome</p><p><b>dvorana moćnika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tent of an ancient Roman general [pretorium]</p><p><b>Ured pretora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the office of praetor</p><p><b>Glavni i najveći grad Češke u zapadnom dijelu zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of the Czech Republic in the western part of the country [Czech capital, Prague, Praha]</p><p><b>dosadan, koji se odnosi na pragmatizam, koji se u sve miješa, koristan, objektivan, poučan, pragmatičan, sistematičan, pragmatička sankcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imperial decree that becomes part of the fundamental law of the land [pragmatic sanction]</p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with practical matters [matter-of-fact, pragmatical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or concerning the theory of pragmatism [pragmatical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> guided by practical experience and observation rather than theory [hard-nosed, hardheaded, practical]</p><p><b>pragmatička sankcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imperial decree that becomes part of the fundamental law of the land [pragmatic]</p><p><b>teorije pragmatizma ili o njoj, koji se bave praktičnim pitanjima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or concerning the theory of pragmatism [pragmatic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with practical matters [matter-of-fact, pragmatic]</p><p><b>dosadno, korisno, objektivno, poučno, pragmatično, sistematično</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a realistic manner</p><p>