n inedible fruit [Cucurbita foetidissima, Missouri gourd, buffalo gourd, calabazilla, prairie gourd, wild pumpkin]</p><p><b>lijepa čvrsta sjevernoamerička trava s lišćem koje se na jesen pretvara u blijedo broncu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> handsome hardy North American grass with foliage turning pale bronze in autumn [Andropogon scoparius, Schizachyrium scoparium, broom beard grass, wire grass]</p><p><b>Crni čunjak iz sjevernoameričkih prajera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brown mottled North American grouse of western prairies [prairie chicken, prairie fowl]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička godišnja s crvenim ili ružičastim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American annual with red or rose-colored flowers [Lotus americanus, compass plant, prairie bird's-foot trefoil, prairie trefoil]</p><p><b>lažna malova zapadne Sjedinjene Države s crvenim cvjetovima rasemosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> false mallow of western United States having racemose red flowers [Malvastrum coccineum, Sphaeralcea coccinea, red false mallow]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko glodavca sjevernoameričkih prerija koji žive u velikim složenim jamacima koji laju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several rodents of North American prairies living in large complex burrows having a barking cry [prairie dog]</p><p><b>višegodišnje biljke sjevernoameričkih prerija s gustim glavama malih bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial herb of North American prairies having dense heads of small white flowers [Desmanthus ilinoensis, prickle-weed]</p><p><b>Orhideja močvarnih ili vlažnih područja sjeverno-srednje Sjedinjenih Država s rasemi vrlo mirisnih kremasto- ili zelenkasto-bijelocvetnih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orchid of boggy or wet lands of north central United States having racemes of very fragrant creamy or greenish white flowers [Habenaria leucophaea, prairie white-fringed orchis]</p><p><b>široko raspoređen između Mississippija i Rocky Mountains (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed between the Mississippi and the Rockies [Crotalus viridis, Western rattlesnake, prairie rattlesnake]</p><p><b>široko raspoređen između Mississippija i Rocky Mountains (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed between the Mississippi and the Rockies [Crotalus viridis, Western rattlesnake, prairie rattler]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko sjevernoameričkih biljaka roda Erysimum s velikim žutim cvijećem, bilo koja od nekoliko zapadne američke biljke roda Cheiranthus s velikim žutim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several North American plants of the genus Erysimum having large yellow flowers</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several western American plants of the genus Cheiranthus having large yellow flowers</p><p><b>višegodišnja bačvarna bijela biljka iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial cottony-white herb of southwestern United States [Artemisia gnaphalodes, Artemisia ludoviciana, cudweed, western mugwort, white sage]</p><p><b>aromatska višegodišnja biljka s svilovitim listovima iz suhih sjevernih dijelova sjeverne hemisfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> silky-leaved aromatic perennial of dry northern parts of the northern hemisphere [Artemisia frigida, wormwood sage]</p><p><b>veliki voz s širokim kotačima i lukovitim platnom vrhom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large wagon with broad wheels and an arched canvas top [Conestoga, Conestoga wagon, covered wagon, prairie wagon]</p><p><b>Severnoamerička višegodišnja biljka s dlakavim bazalnim pinnatnim listovima i ljubičastim cvijećem i plodovima s vrhom s perjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American perennial with hairy basal pinnate leaves and purple flowers and plume-tipped fruits [Geum triflorum, purple avens]</p><p><b>vrsta tla koja se nalazi pod travnjama u umjerenoj klimi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a type of soil occurring under grasses in temperate climates</p><p><b>biljka s uglavnom bazalnim listovima i tankim otvorenim cvjetovima od bijelih ili blijedo ružičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant with mostly basal leaves and slender open racemes of white or pale pink flowers [Lithophragma parviflorum]</p><p><b>Illinois</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a midwestern state in north-central United States [IL, Ill., Illinois, Land of Lincoln]</p><p><b>sličan običnom suncokrvu sa tankim obično razgranatim stabljikama uobičajenim u središnjim Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to the common sunflower with slender usually branching stems common in central United States [Helianthus petiolaris]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička godišnja s crvenim ili ružičastim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American annual with red or rose-colored flowers [Lotus americanus, compass plant, prairie bird's-foot trefoil, prairie lotus]</p><p><b>Trillium centralne Sjedinjene Države s tamno ljubičastom sesilnom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trillium of central United States having dark purple sessile flowers [Trillium recurvatum, prairie wake-robin]</p><p><b>tipična volja u proširenoj prerijskoj regiji središnje Sjedinjenih Država i južnog Kanade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> typical vole of the extended prairie region of central United States and southern Canada [Microtus ochrogaster]</p><p><b>veliki voz s širokim kotačima i lukovitim platnom vrhom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large wagon with broad wheels and an arched canvas top [Conestoga, Conestoga wagon, covered wagon, prairie schooner]</p><p><b>Trillium centralne Sjedinjene Države s tamno ljubičastom sesilnom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trillium of central United States having dark purple sessile flowers [Trillium recurvatum, prairie trillium]</p><p><b>od središnje Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of central North America [Platanthera leucophea]</p><p><b>Orhideja močvarnih ili vlažnih područja sjeverno-srednje Sjedinjenih Država s rasemi vrlo mirisnih kremasto- ili zelenkasto-bijelocvetnih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orchid of boggy or wet lands of north central United States having racemes of very fragrant creamy or greenish white flowers [Habenaria leucophaea, prairie orchid]</p><p><b>tanka šumovita vrba iz sušnih područja Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender shrubby willow of dry areas of North America [Salix humilis]</p><p><b>Canis latrans, kojot</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small wolf native to western North America [Canis latrans, brush wolf, coyote]</p><p><b>hvaliti, hvaljenje, pohvala, slava, slaviti, veličati, pohvaliti, pohvaljivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expression of approval and commendation [congratulations, extolment, kudos]</p><p><i>n.</i> offering words of homage as an act of worship</p><p><i>v.</i> express approval of</p><p><b>pun hvale</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of or giving praise [laudatory, praising]</p><p><b>hvale vrijedan, pohvalan (od &quot;praiseworthy&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an admirable manner [admirably, commendable, laudably]</p><p><b>kvalitetu koja zaslužuje pohvalu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being worthy of praise [laudability, laudableness]</p><p><b>hvale vrijedan, pohvalan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of high praise [applaudable, commendable, laudable]</p><p><b>hvaliti, hvaljenje, pohvala, slava, slaviti, veličati (od &quot;praise&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of or giving praise [laudatory, praiseful]</p><p><b>svojstvo zaslužene pohvale (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of deserving praise</p><p><b>Hinduistički bog koji personifikuje kreativnu snagu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Hindu god personifying a creative force</p><p><b>bilo koji od modernih indijskih jezika, bilo koji od narodnih indijskih jezika sjeverne i središnje Indije (kao što se razlikuje od sanskrita) zabilježen od 3. stoljeća prije Krista do 4. stoljeća nakon Krista (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the modern Indic languages</p><p><i>n.</i> any of the vernacular Indic languages of north and central India (as distinguished from Sanskrit) recorded from the 3rd century BC to the 4th century AD</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s Prakritom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Prakrit</p><p><b>praline</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cookie-sized candy made of brown sugar and butter and pecans</p><p><b>dječja kolica, kolica za bebe, kolica za šetnju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small vehicle with four wheels in which a baby or child is pushed around [baby buggy, baby carriage, carriage, go-cart, perambulator, pushchair, pusher, stroller]</p><p><b>propinjanje, šepurenje, kočoperiti se, paradirati, producirati se, razmetati se, šepiriti se, šepuriti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a proud stiff pompous gait [strut, swagger]</p><p><i>v.</i> to walk with a lofty proud gait, often in an attempt to impress others [cock, ruffle, sashay, strut, swagger, tittup]</p><p><i>v.</i> spring forward on the hind legs</p><p><i>v.</i> cause (a horse) to bound spring forward</p><p><i>v.</i> ride a horse such that it springs and bounds forward</p><p><b>propinjanje, šepurenje (od &quot;prance&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mettlesome or fiery horse</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s obrokom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a meal</p><p><b>nesreća koja uključuje automobil ili avion, sudara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crash involving a car or plane</p><p><i>v.</i> crash</p><p><b>oploditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make pregnant [bang up, impregnate, knock up]</p><p><b>kititi se, nestašluk, oblačiti, podvala, skok, šaljivi ispad, upadljivo, fora, nepodopština, psina, smicalica, vic, šala, štos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acting like a clown or buffoon [buffoonery, clowning, frivolity, harlequinade, japery]</p><p><i>n.</i> a ludicrous or grotesque act done for fun and amusement [antic, caper, joke, put-on, trick]</p><p><i>v.</i> dress or decorate showily or gaudily</p><p><i>v.</i> dress up showily</p><p><b>Neprijatno ili dosadno zabavno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> naughtily or annoyingly playful [arch, impish, implike, mischievous, pixilated, puckish, wicked]</p><p><b>-Karakteristike davanja se neugodnim šalama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of indulging in disreputable pranks [