cially by Catholics) [rosary]</p><p><b>molitvenik, časlovac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a book containing prayers [prayerbook]</p><p><b>mali tepih koji muslimani koriste za vrijeme svojih molitvi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small rug used by Muslims during their devotions [prayer rug]</p><p><b>službi u kojoj ljudi pjevaju himne i mole se zajedno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a service at which people sing hymns and pray together [prayer service]</p><p><b>Apokrifa koja se sastoji od teksta koji je dodan Danijelovoj knjizi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Apocryphal book consisting of text added to the Book of Daniel</p><p><b>mali tepih koji muslimani koriste za vrijeme svojih molitvi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small rug used by Muslims during their devotions [prayer mat]</p><p><b>službi u kojoj ljudi pjevaju himne i mole se zajedno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a service at which people sing hymns and pray together [prayer meeting]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) šal s ritualno vezanim frengom na svakom uglu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a shawl with a ritually knotted fringe at each corner [tallis, tallith]</p><p><b>cilindar s molitvama napisanim na njemu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cylinder with prayers written on it</p><p><b>molitvenik, časlovac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a book containing prayers [prayer book]</p><p><b>bogougodan, koji se moli Bogu, pobožan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed to pray or appearing to pray</p><p><b>bogomoljka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the common mantis [Mantis religioso, praying mantis]</p><p><b>bogomoljka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the common mantis [Mantis religioso, praying mantid]</p><p><b>prazosin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antihypertensive drug (trade name Minipress) [Minipress]</p><p><b>Komunistička država koja pokriva veliko područje u istočnoj Aziji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a communist nation that covers a vast territory in eastern Asia [Cathay, China, Communist China, People's Republic of China, Red China, mainland China]</p><p><b>pretkršćanski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or being the time before the beginning of the Christian era</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili koje potječu iz Amerike prije dolaska Kolumba (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or originating in the Americas before the arrival of Columbus</p><p><b>abnormalno stanje trudnoće koje se karakterizira hipertenzijom i zadržavanjem tekućine te albuminurijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal state of pregnancy characterized by hypertension and fluid retention and albuminuria [preeclampsia]</p><p><b>nadmoćno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a preeminent degree [preeminently]</p><p><b>Visoka ponuda koja je namijenjena sprečavanju protivničkih igrača da ponude. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a high bid that is intended to prevent the opposing players from bidding [preempt, preemptive bid]</p><p><b>pravo prve kupnje, pravo prvokupa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the judicial principle asserting the supremacy of federal over state legislation on the same subject [preemption]</p><p><i>n.</i> the right of a government to seize or appropriate something (as property) [preemption]</p><p><i>n.</i> the right to purchase something in advance of others [preemption]</p><p><i>n.</i> a prior appropriation of something [preemption]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na pravo kupnje iz prve ruke, koji se odnosi na pretkupnju</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> designed or having the power to deter or prevent an anticipated situation or occurrence [preemptive]</p><p><b>iznenadni napad koji je pokrenut kako bi se spriječio neprijatelj od toga da vam to učini. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a surprise attack that is launched in order to prevent the enemy from doing it to you</p><p><b>osoba koja stječe zemljište na temelju predizbora zemljišta, ponuđač u bridžu koji daje preventivnu ponudu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who acquires land by preemption [preemptor]</p><p><i>n.</i> a bidder in bridge who makes a preemptive bid [preemptor]</p><p><b>postojanje prije ili prije nečega (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing previously or before something [pre-existing, preexistent, preexisting]</p><p><b>postojanje prije ili prije nečega (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing previously or before something [pre-existent, preexistent, preexisting]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili označava vrijeme prije perioda Jura (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or denoting the time before the Jurassic period</p><p><b>slikar ili pisac posvećen obnovi ranih renesansnih ideala., od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Pre-Raphaelites (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a painter or writer dedicated to restoring early Renaissance ideals</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of the Pre-Raphaelites</p><p><b>bilo koji filozof koji je živio prije Sokrata, Prije vremena Sokratesa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any philosopher who lived before Socrates</p><p><i>adj.</i> before the time of Socrates [presocratic]</p><p><b>propovijedati, zagovarati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> deliver a sermon [prophesy]</p><p><i>v.</i> speak, plead, or argue in favor of [advocate]</p><p><b>propovjednik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone whose occupation is preaching the gospel [preacher man, sermoniser, sermonizer]</p><p><b>propovjednik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone whose occupation is preaching the gospel [preacher, sermoniser, sermonizer]</p><p><b>Moralizacija dostavljena dosadno na propovijedan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> moralization delivered tediously in a preachy manner</p><p><b>Govori kao da držiš propovijed. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> speak as if delivering a sermon [moralise, moralize, sermonise, sermonize]</p><p><b>propovijed</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an address of a religious nature (usually delivered during a church service) [discourse, sermon]</p><p><i>n.</i> a moralistic rebuke [sermon]</p><p><b>propovijed o moralnoj ili vjerskoj temi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sermon on a moral or religious topic [homily]</p><p><b>sklon ili obilježen dosadnim moralnošću (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined to or marked by tedious moralization</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili namijenjene djeci u dobi od 9 do 12 godina (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or designed for children between the ages of 9 and 12 [preteen]</p><p><b>godišnja utrka za trogodišnje konje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an annual race for three-year-old horses</p><p><b>niz bitova odaslan na početku prijenosa zbog prila, početni niz, preambula, predgovor, uvod, uvodni dio</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a preliminary introduction to a statute or constitution (usually explaining its purpose)</p><p><i>v.</i> make a preliminary introduction, usually to a formal document</p><p><b>nalazi se ispred anusa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in front of the anus</p><p><b>Dogovorite se unaprijed. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> arrange beforehand</p><p><b>Nešto dogovoreno unaprijed. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something arranged in advance</p><p><b>za proizvodnju dijelova (zgrade), posebno u tvornici, kako bi se mogli lako transportirati i brzo sastavljati na gradilištu zgrada (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to manufacture sections of (a building), especially in a factory, so that they can be easily transported to and rapidly assembled on a building site of buildings [prefabricate]</p><p><b>stipendija koju katedrala dodjeljuje kanoniku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the stipend assigned by a cathedral to a canon</p><p><b>kanon koji prima prebend za služenje crkvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a canon who receives a prebend for serving the church</p><p><b>Pretkambrij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the eon following the Hadean time and preceding the Phanerozoic eon [Precambrian aeon, Precambrian eon, Precambrian period]</p><p><b>Eon nakon Hadeanskog vremena i prije Fanerozoikskog eona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the eon following the Hadean time and preceding the Phanerozoic eon [Precambrian, Precambrian eon, Precambrian period]</p><p><b>Eon nakon Hadeanskog vremena i prije Fanerozoikskog eona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the eon following the Hadean time and preceding the Phanerozoic eon [Precambrian, Precambrian aeon, Precambrian period]</p><p><b>Eon nakon Hadeanskog vremena i prije Fanerozoikskog eona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the eon following the Hadean time and preceding the Phanerozoic eon [Precambrian, Precambrian aeon, Precambrian eon]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s tumorom koji nije maligan, ali će vjerojatno postati maligan ako se ne liječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a growth that is not malignant but is likely to become so if not treated</p><p><b>neizvjestan, neobrazložen, neosnovan, nepouzdan, nesiguran, opasan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affording no ease or reassurance [unstable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> fraught with danger [parlous, perilous, touch-and-go]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not secure [shaky]</p><p><b>neizvjestan, neobrazložen, neosnovan, nepouzdan, nesiguran, opasan (od &quot;precarious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a precarious manner</p><p><b>dvojba, dvojbenost, neizvjesnost, neodređenost, nesigurnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extreme dangerousness</p><p><i>n.</i> being unsettled or in doubt or dependent on chance [uncertainness, uncertainty]</p><p><b>montažni dio</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of structural members especially of concrete</p><p><b>izražavanje molbe ili molbe (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing entreaty or supplication [precatory]</p><p><b>izražavanje molbe ili molbe (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing entreaty or supplication [precative]</p><p><b>mjera opreza, obazrivost, oprez, opreznost, predostrožnost, smotrenost, upozorenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a precautionary measure warding off impending danger or damage or injury etc. [guard, safeguard]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of practicing caution in advance</p><p><i>n.</i> judiciousness in avoiding harm or danger [care, caution, forethought]</p><p><b>za zaštitu od moguće opasnosti ili kvaru (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> taken in advance to protect against possible danger or failure [precautionary]</p><p><b>obazriv, oprezan, smotren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> taken in advance to protect against possible danger or failure [precautional]</p><p><b>prima krv iz glave, ruku i grudi i isprazni u desnu prednje srce. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> receives blood from the head and arms and chest and empties into the right atrium of the heart [superior vena cava]</p><p><b>biti ispred čega, dogoditi se (prije), nalaziti, prednjačiti, prethoditi, stajati ispred, zauzimati, predvoditi, voditi, uvesti, uvoditi, započeti, započinjati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be earlier in time [antecede, antedate, forego, forgo, predate]</p><p><i>v.</i> come before [predate]</p><p><i>v.</i> be the predecessor of [come before]</p><p><i>v.</i> move ahead (of others) in time or space [lead]</p><p><i>v.</i> furnish with a preface or introduction [introduce, preface, premise]</p><p><b>prednost, prednjačenje, prvenstvo, starješinstvo, viši položaj, prioritet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> status established in order of importance or urgency [precedency, priority]</p><p><i>n.</i> preceding in time [antecedence, antecedency, anteriority, precedency, priority]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of preceding in time or order or rank (as in a ceremony) [precedency, precession]</p><p><b>prioritet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> status established in order of importance or urgency [precedence, priority]</p><p><i>n.</i> preceding in time [antecedence, antecedency, anteriority, precedence, priority]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of preceding in time or order or rank (as in a ceremony) [precedence, precession]</p><p><b>presudan, prethodan, prethodni, slučaj, presedan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an example that is used to justify similar occurrences at a later time [case in point]</p><p><i>n.</i> (civil law) a law established by following earlier judicial decisions [case law, common law]</p><p><i>n.</i> a system of jurisprudence based on judicial precedents rather than statutory laws [case law, common law]</p><p><i>n.</i> a subject mentioned earlier (preceding in time)</p><p><i>adj.</i> preceding in time, order, or significance</p><p><b>presudan, prethodan, prethodni, slučaj (od &quot;precedent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or supported or justified by a precedent</p><p><b>s presedanom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with precedent</p><p><b>imaju prednost (posebno zbog dužeg radnog vremena) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having precedence (especially because of longer service)</p><p><b>predkodiranje, prethodan, prethodni, prethođenje, prednji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing or coming before</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a person who has held and relinquished a position or office [past, retiring]</p><p><b>glazbeni direktor zbora. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the musical director of a choir [cantor, choirmaster]</p><p><b>pozicija precentora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the position of precentor</p><p><b>konvulzija frontalnog režnja koji je ograničen na leđima centralnim sulcusom i koji sadrži motorno područje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the convolution of the frontal lobe that is bounded in back by the central sulcus and that contains the motor area</p><p><b>naredba, pravilo, propis, uputa, učenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rule of personal conduct [principle]</p><p><i>n.</i> a doctrine that is taught [commandment, teaching]</p><p><b>nastavnik, učitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> teacher at a university or college (especially at Cambridge or Oxford) [don]</p><p><b>položaj predvodnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the position of preceptor</p><p><b>kretanje u kretanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> move in a gyrating fashion</p><p><b>precesija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the motion of a spinning body (as a top) in which it wobbles so that the axis of rotation sweeps out a cone</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of preceding in time or order or rank (as in a ceremony) [precedence, precedency]</p><p><b>spori pomak na zapad jednodnevica duž ravnine ekliptike uzrokovan precesom Zemljine osi rotacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slow westward shift of the equinoxes along the plane of the ecliptic caused by precession of the Earth's axis of rotation</p><p><b>Kloriranje prije drugog kemijskog postupka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chlorination prior to another chemical process</p><p><b>izborni okrug, okolina, policijska stanica, teren, kotar, okrug</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a district of a city or town marked out for administrative purposes</p><p><b>kvaliteta da je zahtjevna ili pretjerano prefinjena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being fastidious or excessively refined [preciousness]</p><p><b>dragocjen, dragocjen -a, dragocjenom, jako, lijep, mio, neobično, omiljen, plemenitih, skup, skupocjen, voljen, vrijedan, vrlo</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by feeling or showing fond affection for [cherished, treasured, wanted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of high worth or cost</p><p><i>adj.</i> held in great esteem for admirable qualities especially of an intrinsic nature [valued]</p><p><i>adj.</i> obviously contrived to charm [cute]</p><p><i>adv.</i> extremely [preciously]</p><p><b>crveni koralj, koralj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the hard stony skeleton of a Mediterranean coral that has a delicate red or pink color and is used for jewelry [coral, red coral]</p><p><b>plemeniti metal, dragocjeni metal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the less common and valuable metals often used to make coins or jewelry</p><p><b>dragi kamen, dragulj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a precious or semiprecious stone incorporated into a piece of jewelry [gem, jewel]</p><p><b>dragocjen, dragocjen -a, dragocjenom, jako, lijep, mio, neobično, omiljen, plemenitih, skup, skupocjen, voljen, vrijedan, vrlo (od &quot;precious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> extremely [precious]</p><p><b>dragocjen, dragocjen -a, dragocjenom, jako, lijep, mio, neobično, omiljen, plemenitih, skup, skupocjen, voljen, vrijedan, vrlo (od &quot;precious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality possessed by something with a great price or value [costliness, dearness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the positive quality of being precious and beyond value [invaluableness, pricelessness, valuableness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being fastidious or excessively refined [preciosity]</p><p><b>bezdan, litica, ponor, propast, provalija, strmina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a very steep cliff</p><p><b>kvaliteta događaja s naglim žurbom ili bez upozorenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of happening with headlong haste or without warning [abruptness, precipitancy, precipitateness, precipitousness, suddenness]</p><p><b>kvaliteta događaja s naglim žurbom ili bez upozorenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of happening with headlong haste or without warning [abruptness, precipitance, precipitateness, precipitousness, suddenness]</p><p><b>sredstvo koje uzrokuje stvaranje obilježja, Napravljeno je vrlo žurno i bez odgovarajuće rasprave. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agent that causes a precipitate to form</p><p><i>adj.</i> done with very great haste and without due deliberation [hasty, overhasty, precipitate, precipitous]</p><p><b>talog, taložiti, padati, pasti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a precipitated solid substance in suspension or after settling or filtering</p><p><i>v.</i> bring about abruptly</p><p><i>v.</i> separate as a fine suspension of solid particles</p><p><i>v.</i> fall from clouds [come down, fall]</p><p><i>v.</i> fall vertically, sharply, or headlong</p><p><i>v.</i> hurl or throw violently</p><p><i>adj.</i> done with very great haste and without due deliberation [hasty, overhasty, precipitant, precipitous]</p><p><b>talog (od &quot;precipitate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at breakneck speed [headlong]</p><p><b>talog (od &quot;precipitate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of happening with headlong haste or without warning [abruptness, precipitance, precipitancy, precipitousness, suddenness]</p><p><b>talog (od &quot;precipitate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> bringing on suddenly or abruptly</p><p><b>oborina, oborine, pad, padaline, padavine, precipitacija, taloženje, žurba, taložni procesi, padalina, padavina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quantity of water falling to earth at a specific place within a specified period of time</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of forming a chemical precipitate</p><p><i>n.</i> the falling to earth of any form of water (rain or snow or hail or sleet or mist) [downfall]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of casting down or falling headlong from a height</p><p><i>n.</i> an unexpected acceleration or hastening</p><p><i>n.</i> overly eager speed (and possible carelessness) [haste, hastiness, hurriedness, hurry]</p><p><b>S druge strane, radi se na proizvodnji električnih plinova. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> removes dust particles from gases by electrostatic precipitation [Cottrell precipitator, electrostatic precipitator]</p><p><b>antitelo koje uzrokuje obaranje kada se ujedini sa svojim antigenom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antibody that causes precipitation when it unites with its antigen</p><p><b>okomit, strm, vrletan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> done with very great haste and without due deliberation [hasty, overhasty, precipitant, precipitate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> extremely steep [abrupt, sharp]</p><p><b>oštro</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> very suddenly and to a great degree [sharply]</p><p><i>adv.</i> abruptly</p><p><b>okomit, strm, vrletan (od &quot;precipitous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property possessed by a slope that is very steep [abruptness, steepness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of happening with headlong haste or without warning [abruptness, precipitance, precipitancy, precipitateness, suddenness]</p><p><b>kratak izvod, kratak pregled, sažetak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sketchy summary of the main points of an argument or theory [abstract, outline, synopsis]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a summary (of)</p><p><b>brižljiv, određen, pedantan, precizan, precizni, savjestan, točan, uredan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> sharply exact or accurate or delimited</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of ideas, images, representations, expressions) characterized by perfect conformity to fact or truth [accurate, exact]</p><p><b>baš, brižno, pedantno, taman, točnije, točno, uredno, precizno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> indicating exactness or preciseness [exactly, just, properly]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in