al phase, preclinical test]</p><p><b>isključiti, isključivati, odstraniti, odvratiti, onemogućavati, onemogućiti, sprečavati, spriječiti, ukloniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> keep from happening or arising [forbid, foreclose, forestall, prevent]</p><p><i>v.</i> make impossible, especially beforehand [close out, rule out]</p><p><b>prekluzija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of preventing something by anticipating and disposing of it effectively [forestalling, obviation]</p><p><b>-Nemoćno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made impossible [obviating]</p><p><b>koje su okružene slijepom kožom i očiju su im otvorene. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of hatchlings) covered with down and having eyes open</p><p><b>drzak, napredan, prerano sazrio, prijevremen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by or characteristic of exceptionally early development or maturity (especially in mental aptitude)</p><p><i>adj.</i> appearing or developing early</p><p><b>početak zubića u ranijem uzrastu nego što se očekivalo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> teething at an earlier age than expected</p><p><b>drzak, napredan, prerano sazrio, prijevremen (od &quot;precocious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a precocious manner</p><p><b>drzak, napredan, prerano sazrio, prijevremen (od &quot;precocious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intelligence achieved far ahead of normal developmental schedules [precocity]</p><p><b>prijevremeni razvoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intelligence achieved far ahead of normal developmental schedules [precociousness]</p><p><b>predznanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> knowledge of an event before it occurs [foreknowledge]</p><p><b>predviđanje budućnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> foreseeing the future [clairvoyant, second-sighted]</p><p><b>-Zapamtite. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> conceive beforehand</p><p><b>unaprijed stvoren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of an idea or opinion) formed beforehand</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to primjenjivo u slučaju poduzeća, to se može smatrati pravnim postupkom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an opinion formed beforehand without adequate evidence [parti pris, preconceived notion, preconceived opinion, preconception, prepossession]</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to primjenjivo u slučaju poduzeća, to se može smatrati pravnim postupkom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an opinion formed beforehand without adequate evidence [parti pris, preconceived idea, preconceived opinion, preconception, prepossession]</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to primjenjivo u slučaju poduzeća, to se može smatrati pravnim postupkom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an opinion formed beforehand without adequate evidence [parti pris, preconceived idea, preconceived notion, preconception, prepossession]</p><p><b>predrasuda, preduvjerenje, predviđanje, zaključak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an opinion formed beforehand without adequate evidence [parti pris, preconceived idea, preconceived notion, preconceived opinion, prepossession]</p><p><i>n.</i> a partiality that prevents objective consideration of an issue or situation [bias, prejudice]</p><p><b>unaprijed smišljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> previously arranged or agreed on</p><p><b>preduvjet, pretpostavka, uvjet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an assumption on which rests the validity or effect of something else [condition, stipulation]</p><p><i>n.</i> an assumption that is taken for granted [given, presumption]</p><p><i>n.</i> a condition that is a prerequisite</p><p><i>v.</i> put into the required condition beforehand</p><p><b>preduvjet, pretpostavka (od &quot;precondition&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having already been put into a suitable condition</p><p><b>kuhati unaprijed tako da stvarna priprema neće potrajati dugo (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cook beforehand so that the actual preparation won't take long</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više masenog udjela (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> cooked partially or completely beforehand</p><p><b>za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 4. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> cooled in advance</p><p><b>ispred srca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in front of the heart</p><p><b>vanjska površina tijela koja prekriva srce i želudac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the external surface of the body overlying the heart and stomach</p><p><b>predhodnik, predkursor, predšasnik, prekurzor, preteča, prethodeći simbol, prethodnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance from which another substance is formed (especially by a metabolic reaction)</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who goes before or announces the coming of another [forerunner]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that precedes and indicates the approach of something or someone [forerunner, harbinger, herald, predecessor]</p><p><b>prethodni, uvodni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> warning of future misfortune [premonitory]</p><p><b>Lov i ubijanje drugih životinja radi hrane, Živi ili je posvećen žrtvovanju drugih za osobnu korist. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> hunting and killing other animals for food [predacious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> living by or given to victimizing others for personal gain [predacious, predatory]</p><p><b>Lov i ubijanje drugih životinja radi hrane, Živi ili je posvećen žrtvovanju drugih za osobnu korist. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> hunting and killing other animals for food [predaceous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> living by or given to victimizing others for personal gain [predaceous, predatory]</p><p><b>antedatirati, napisati raniji datum, prednjačiti, prethoditi, vrebati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be earlier in time [antecede, antedate, forego, forgo, precede]</p><p><i>v.</i> come before [precede]</p><p><i>v.</i> prey on or hunt for [prey, raven]</p><p><i>v.</i> establish something as being earlier relative to something else [antedate, foredate]</p><p><b>proždrljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an act of plundering and pillaging and marauding [depredation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of preying by a predator who kills and eats the prey</p><p><b>grabežljivac, predator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who attacks in search of booty [marauder, piranha, vulture]</p><p><i>n.</i> any animal that lives by preying on other animals [predatory animal]</p><p><b>grabežljiv, pljačkaški, razbojnički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by plundering or pillaging or marauding [marauding, raiding]</p><p><i>adj.</i> living by preying on other animals especially by catching living prey [rapacious, raptorial, ravening, vulturine, vulturous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> living by or given to victimizing others for personal gain [predaceous, predacious]</p><p><b>grabežljivac, predator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any animal that lives by preying on other animals [predator]</p><p><b>Umrijet ću prije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> die before</p><p><b>predak, prednik, prethodnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who precedes you in time (as in holding a position or office)</p><p><i>n.</i> something that precedes and indicates the approach of something or someone [forerunner, harbinger, herald, precursor]</p><p><b>Svakoga tko se preda vjerovanju da su nemoćni promijeniti svoju sudbinu., o predodređenosti ili s njom povezanim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anyone who submits to the belief that they are powerless to change their destiny [determinist, fatalist, predestinationist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to predestination</p><p><b>vjerovanje ili učenje predestinara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the belief or doctrine of predestinarians</p><p><b>predodređen božanskom voljom ili odredbom, S druge strane, u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje, to znači da se ne primjenjuje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> foreordain by divine will or decree [foreordain, predestine]</p><p><i>adj.</i> established or prearranged unalterably [foreordained, predestined]</p><p><b>predodređenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> previous determination as if by destiny or fate</p><p><i>n.</i> (theology) being determined in advance [foreordination, predetermination, preordination]</p><p><b>Svakoga tko se preda vjerovanju da su nemoćni promijeniti svoju sudbinu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anyone who submits to the belief that they are powerless to change their destiny [determinist, fatalist, predestinarian]</p><p><b>unaprijed odrediti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> decree or determine beforehand</p><p><i>v.</i> foreordain by divine will or decree [foreordain, predestinate]</p><p><i>v.</i> foreordain or determine beforehand [foreordain, preordain]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje, to znači da se ne primjenjuje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> established or prearranged unalterably [foreordained, predestinate]</p><p><b>(teologija) je unaprijed određena, mentalna odlučnost ili odlučnost unaprijed, djelo određivanja ili određivanja unaprijed onoga što će se dogoditi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (theology) being determined in advance [foreordination, predestination, preordination]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mental determination or resolve in advance</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of determining or ordaining in advance what is to take place</p><p><b>odlučiti unaprijed, unaprijed odrediti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> determine beforehand</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be biased [bias]</p><p><b>predviđeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> set in advance [preset]</p><p><b>neprijatan pol, smetnja, sumnja, teškoća, tvrđenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a situation from which extrication is difficult especially an unpleasant or trying one [plight, quandary]</p><p><b>iskaz, izricati, predikat, tvrditi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (logic) what is predicated of the subject of a proposition</p><p><i>n.</i> one of the two main constituents of a sentence [verb phrase]</p><p><i>v.</i> make the (grammatical) predicate in a proposition</p><p><i>v.</i> affirm or declare as an attribute or quality of [proclaim]</p><p><i>v.</i> involve as a necessary condition of consequence [connote]</p><p><b>sustav simboličke logike koja predstavlja pojedince i predike i kvantifikaciju nad pojedincima (kao i odnose između prijedloga) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of symbolic logic that represents individuals and predicates and quantification over individuals (as well as the relations between propositions) [functional calculus]</p><p><b>iskaz</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (logic) a declaration of something self-evident [postulation]</p><p><b>predikativ, predikativan, predikatski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of adjectives</p><p><b>predikativ, predikativan, predikatski (od &quot;predicative&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> occurring within the predicate phrase</p><p><b>izraz koji predikava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expression that predicates</p><p><b>najvaljuje, predskazati, predvidjeti, predviđati, pretkazati, proreći, proricati, provjeriti, prognozirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a prediction about [anticipate, call, forebode, foretell, prognosticate, promise]</p><p><i>v.</i> indicate, as with a sign or an omen [augur, auspicate, betoken, bode, forecast, foreshadow, foretell, omen, portend, prefigure, presage, prognosticate]</p><p><b>predvidljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being predictable</p><p><b>koje se može pretpostaviti, predvidivog, predvidljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being foretold</p><p><b>na predvidljiv način ili u predvidljivom stupnju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a predictable manner or to a predictable degree</p><p><b>predikcija, predviđanje, proricanje, proročanstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of predicting (as by reasoning about the future) [anticipation, prevision]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement made about the future [forecasting, foretelling, prognostication]</p><p><b>koji predviđa, koji pretkazuje, koji proriče, predvidljiv, proročki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to prediction [prognostic, prognosticative]</p><p><b>gatara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who makes predictions of the future (usually on the basis of special knowledge) [forecaster, prognosticator, soothsayer]</p><p><i>n.</i> information that supports a probabilistic estimate of future events</p><p><i>n.</i> a computer for controlling antiaircraft fire that computes the position of an aircraft at the instant of a shell's arrival</p><p><b>promjenljiva koja se može koristiti za predviđanje vrijednosti druge promjenljive (kao u statističkoj regresiji) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variable that can be used to predict the value of another variable (as in statistical regression)</p><p><b>prebacivanje (hrana) prije (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> digest (food) beforehand</p><p><b>S druge strane, u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvodi koji se proizvode u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka mogu biti: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> artificially partially digested as by enzymatic action</p><p><b>naklonost, osobita sklonost, predilekcija, sklonost, preferencija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a predisposition in favor of something [orientation, preference]</p><p><i>n.</i> a strong liking [penchant, preference, taste]</p><p><b>predodrediti, pridobiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make susceptible</p><p><b>učinjeno osjetljivim (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made susceptible</p><p><b>naginjanje, predispozicija, sklonost, osjetljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> susceptibility to a pathogen [sensitivity]</p><p><i>n.</i> an inclination beforehand to interpret statements in a particular way</p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition in advance to react in a particular way</p><p><b>glukokortikoid (trgovinski nazivi Pediapred ili Prelone) koji se koristi za liječenje upalnih stanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a glucocorticoid (trade names Pediapred or Prelone) used to treat inflammatory conditions [Pediapred, Prelone]</p><p><b>dehidrogenizirani analog kortizola (trgovinski nazivi Orasone ili Deltasone ili Liquid Pred ili Meticorten) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dehydrogenated analogue of cortisol (trade names Orasone or Deltasone or Liquid Pred or Meticorten) [Deltasone, Liquid Pred, Meticorten, Orasone]</p><p><b>nadmoć, prevaga, prevlast</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being predominant over others [predomination, prepotency]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being more noticeable than anything else [predomination]</p><p><b>nadmoćan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> most frequent or common [dominant, prevailing, prevalent, rife]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having superior power and influence [overriding, paramount, predominate, preponderant, preponderating]</p><p><b>pretežno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> much greater in number or influence [preponderantly]</p><p><b>gospodariti, prevladavati, dominirati, prevladati, upravljati, vladati, voditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be larger in number, quantity, power, status or importance [dominate, prevail, reign, rule]</p><p><i>v.</i> appear very large or occupy a commanding position [hulk, loom, tower]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having superior power and influence [overriding, paramount, predominant, preponderant, preponderating]</p><p><b>stanje prevladavanja nad drugima, kvaliteta da bude više primjećiv od bilo čega drugog. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being predominant over others [predominance, prepotency]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being more noticeable than anything else [predominance]</p><p><b>preeklampsija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal state of pregnancy characterized by hypertension and fluid retention and albuminuria [pre-eclampsia]</p><p><b>dijete koje je rođeno prije 37. tjedna trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infant that is born prior to 37 weeks of gestation [premature baby, premature infant, premie, preterm baby, preterm infant]</p><p><b>dominantnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> high status importance owing to marked superiority [distinction, eminence, note]</p><p><b>vodeći</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> greatest in importance or degree or significance or achievement [leading]</p><p><b>vodeći (od &quot;preeminent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a preeminent degree [pre-eminently]</p><p><b>Program obuke koji će vas pripremiti za zapošljavanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a training program to prepare you for employment</p><p><b>prisvojiti, istiskivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a high bid that is intended to prevent the opposing players from bidding [pre-empt, preemptive bid]</p><p><i>v.</i> acquire for oneself before others can do so</p><p><i>v.</i> take the place of or have precedence over [displace]</p><p><i>v.</i> gain possession of by prior right or opportunity, especially so as to obtain the right to buy (land)</p><p><i>v.</i> make a preemptive bid in the game of bridge</p><p><b>Pravni princip koji potvrđuje nadmoć savezne nad državnim zakonodavstvom o istom pitanju., pravo vlade da zaplijeni ili prisvoji nešto (kao imovinu), pravo kupnje nešto unaprijed od drugih, prethodno pripreme nečega. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the judicial principle asserting the supremacy of federal over state legislation on the same subject [pre-emption]</p><p><i>n.</i> the right of a government to seize or appropriate something (as property) [pre-emption]</p><p><i>n.</i> the right to purchase something in advance of others [pre-emption]</p><p><i>n.</i> a prior appropriation of something [pre-emption]</p><p><b>preduhitriv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> designed or having the power to deter or prevent an anticipated situation or occurrence [pre-emptive]</p><p><b>Visoka ponuda koja je namijenjena sprečavanju protivničkih igrača da ponude. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a high bid that is intended to prevent the opposing players from bidding [pre-empt, preempt]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ovog članka, poduzeća mogu imati pravo na oduzimanje akcija u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the right granting to shareholders the first opportunity to buy a new issue of stock</p><p><b>osoba koja stječe zemljište na temelju predizbora zemljišta, ponuđač u bridžu koji daje preventivnu ponudu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who acquires land by preemption [pre-emptor]</p><p><i>n.</i> a bidder in bridge who makes a preemptive bid [pre-emptor]</p><p><b>čistiti perje, udesiti, dotjerati se, dotjerivati se, lickati se, nalickati se, srediti se, sređivati se, urediti se, uređivati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> clean with one's bill [plume]</p><p><i>v.</i> pride or congratulate (oneself) for an achievement [congratulate]</p><p><i>v.</i> dress or groom with elaborate care [dress, plume, primp]</p><p><b>žlijezda koja luči ulje u podnožju repa kod većine ptica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> oil-secreting gland situated at the base of the tail in most birds [uropygial gland]</p><p><b>postoje prije ili prije određenog vremenskog razdoblja (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> exist beforehand or prior to a certain point in time</p><p><b>postojeće u ranijem stanju ili prije nečega drugog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> existing in a former state or previous to something else</p><p><b>postojanje prije ili prije nečega (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing previously or before something [pre-existent, pre-existing, preexisting]</p><p><b>prije postojanja, prvobitan, prvobitni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing previously or before something [pre-existent, pre-existing, preexistent]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a prefabricated structure</p><p><i>adj.</i> manufactured in standard sizes to be shipped and assembled elsewhere</p><p><b>za proizvodnju dijelova (zgrade), posebno u tvornici, kako bi se mogli lako transportirati i brzo sastavljati na gradilištu zgrada, S druge strane, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvođači mogu koristiti: (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to manufacture sections of (a building), especially in a factory, so that they can be easily transported to and rapidly assembled on a building site of buildings [preassemble]</p><p><i>v.</i> produce synthetically, artificially, or stereotypically and unoriginally</p><p><b>montaža, Prefabrikacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the manufacture of sections of a building at the factory so they can be easily and rapidly assembled at the building site</p><p><b>predgovor, uvod, uvesti, uvoditi, započeti, započinjati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short introductory essay preceding the text of a book [foreword, prolusion]</p><p><i>v.</i> furnish with a preface or introduction [introduce, precede, premise]</p><p><b>(od tkanine ili odjeće) koje su umjetno dobivene (izgravirane) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of fabric or clothing) having been given a faded (weathered) appearance by artificial means</p><p><b>uvodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving as an introduction or preface [introductory, prefatory]</p><p><b>uvodni, uvodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving as an introduction or preface [introductory, prefatorial]</p><p><b>prefekt, starješina, upravitelj, župan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chief officer or chief magistrate</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s prefekturom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a prefecture</p><p><b>okrug kojim upravlja prefekt (kao u Francuskoj ili Japanu ili Rimskom carstvu), Ured prefekta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the district administered by a prefect (as in France or Japan or the Roman Empire)</p><p><i>n.</i> the office of prefect</p><p><b>dati prednost, davati prednost, pogodovati, preferirati, pretpostaviti, pretpostavljati, unaprijediti, više se sviđati, više voljeti, optirati, favorizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> like better</p><p><i>v.</i> select as an alternative over another [choose, opt]</p><p><i>v.</i> promote over another [favor, favour]</p><p><i>v.</i> give preference to one creditor over another</p><p><b>bolje, bolje od, koji ima prednost, koji se preferira, poželjan, poželjniji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> more desirable than another [preferred]</p><p><b>bolje</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> more readily or willingly [rather, sooner]</p><p><b>pogodnost, povlastica, prednost, pretpostavljanje, prioritet, sklonost, veća ljubav, preferencija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strong liking [penchant, predilection, taste]</p><p><i>n.</i> a predisposition in favor of something [orientation, predilection]</p><p><i>n.</i> the right or chance to choose [druthers]</p><p><i>n.</i> grant of favor or advantage to one over another (especially to a country or countries in matters of international trade, such as levying duties)</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (b) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (b) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stock whose holders are guaranteed priority in the payment of dividends but whose holders have no voting rights [preferred shares, preferred stock]</p><p><b>-Nisam. -Nisam. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> preferred above all others and treated with partiality [best-loved, favored, favorite, favourite, pet, preferred]</p><p><b>preferencijalni, unapređenje, uživa prednost</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> manifesting partiality [discriminatory]</p><p><b>preferencijalni, unapređenje, uživa prednost (od &quot;preferential&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a preferential manner</p><p><b>davanje prednosti, prednost, unapređenje, viši</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of preferring</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making accusations</p><p><b>povlašten, prioritetan, prvenstven</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> more desirable than another [preferable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> preferred above all others and treated with partiality [best-loved, favored, favorite, favourite, pet, preferent]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (b) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (b) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stock whose holders are guaranteed priority in the payment of dividends but whose holders have no voting rights [preference shares, preferred stock]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (b) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (b) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 2. točkom (c (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stock whose holders are guaranteed priority in the payment of dividends but whose holders have no voting rights [preference shares, preferred shares]</p><p><b>primjer koji predočava ili predočava ono što će se dogoditi, Čin pružanja nejasnih unaprijed navedenog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an example that prefigures or foreshadows what is to come</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of providing vague advance indications [adumbration, foreshadowing]</p><p><b>Nejasno proročko (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> indistinctly prophetic [adumbrative, foreshadowing]</p><p><b>zamišljaj ili razmisli unaprijed, označavaju, kao što je znak ili znak (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> imagine or consider beforehand</p><p><i>v.</i> indicate, as with a sign or an omen [augur, auspicate, betoken, bode, forecast, foreshadow, foretell, omen, portend, predict, presage, prognosticate]</p><p><b>dodatni, prefiks, predmetak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an affix that is added in front of the word</p><p><i>v.</i> attach a prefix to</p><p><b>označavanje bez zagrada za stvaranje matematičkih izraza u kojima svaki operator prethodi svojim operandima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a parenthesis-free notation for forming mathematical expressions in which each operator precedes its operands [Lukasiewicz notation, Polish notation]</p><p><b>formiranje riječi pomoću prefiksa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> formation of a word by means of a prefix</p><p><b>izvesti, predoblik, stakleni štap iz kojeg se izvlači optičko vlakno</b></p><p><i>v.</i> form into a shape resembling the final, desired one</p><p><i>v.</i> form or shape beforehand or determine the shape of beforehand</p><p><b>teorija (popularna u 18. stoljeću, ali sada diskreditirana) da se osoba razvija jednostavnim uvećanjem malog potpuno oblikovanog organizma (homunculus) koji postoji u germinalnoj stanici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a theory (popular in the 18th century and now discredited) that an individual develops by simple enlargement of a tiny fully formed organism (a homunculus) that exists in the germ cell [theory of preformation]</p><p><b>prednja od čelne strukture (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> anterior to a frontal structure</p><p><b>prednji dio prednjeg režnja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the anterior part of the frontal lobe [prefrontal lobe]</p><p><b>kirurško prekidanje živčanih puteva do i iz frontalnog režnja mozga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical interruption of nerve tracts to and from the frontal lobe of the brain [frontal lobotomy, leucotomy, leukotomy, lobotomy, prefrontal leukotomy, prefrontal lobotomy]</p><p><b>kirurško prekidanje živčanih puteva do i iz frontalnog režnja mozga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical interruption of nerve tracts to and from the frontal lobe of the brain [frontal lobotomy, leucotomy, leukotomy, lobotomy, prefrontal leucotomy, prefrontal lobotomy]</p><p><b>prednji dio prednjeg režnja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the anterior part of the frontal lobe [prefrontal cortex]</p><p><b>kirurško prekidanje živčanih puteva do i iz frontalnog režnja mozga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical interruption of nerve tracts to and from the frontal lobe of the brain [frontal lobotomy, leucotomy, leukotomy, lobotomy, prefrontal leucotomy, prefrontal leukotomy]</p><p><b>bogatstvo, drugo stanje, trudnoća, značajnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being pregnant [gestation, maternity]</p><p><b>test trudnoće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a physiological test to determine whether a woman is pregnant</p><p><b>spojina koja se nalazi u urinu žena tijekom određenih faza menstrualnog ciklusa i u urinu trudnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound found in women's urine during certain phases of the menstrual cycle and in the urine of pregnant women</p><p><b>bogat, bremenit, stvaralački, trudna, trudan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> carrying developing offspring within the body or being about to produce new life</p><p><i>adj.</i> rich in significance or implication [meaning, significant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> filled with or attended with [fraught]</p><p><b>Čad koji je proboden ili uvučen u jame, ali su sva četiri ugla još uvijek povezana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chad that has been punched or dimpled but all four corners are still attached [dimple, dimpled chad]</p><p><b>predgrijati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> heat beforehand</p><p><b>Drži se. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> take hold of [clutch, seize]</p><p><b>koji se hvata</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> adapted for grasping especially by wrapping around an object</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a keen intellect</p><p><i>adj.</i> immoderately desirous of acquiring e.g. wealth [avaricious, covetous, grabby, grasping, greedy]</p><p><b>hvatanje, posezanje, uzimanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of gripping something firmly with the hands (or the tentacles) [grasping, seizing, taking hold]</p><p><b>Prednji par nogu stonoga koji su modificirani da uhvate plijen i ubrizgaju otrov od toksikognatsa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the anterior pair of legs of a centipede that are modified to seize prey and inject venom from the toxicognaths</p><p><b>prethistorijski, prethistorijsko, prethistorijskog</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to or existing in times before recorded history [prehistorical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to times before written history</p><p><i>adj.</i> no longer fashionable</p><p><b>prahistorija, prahistorijska kultura, prapovijesna kultura, prapovijest, prethistorija, prethistorijska kultura, pretpovijesna kultura, pretpovijest</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time during the development of human culture before the appearance of the written word [prehistory]</p><p><b>predhistorijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to or existing in times before recorded history [prehistoric]</p><p><b>prapovijest, prapovijesti, prahistorija, prahistorijska kultura, prapovijesna kultura, prethistorija, prethistorijska kultura, pretpovijesna kultura, pretpovijest</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time during the development of human culture before the appearance of the written word [prehistoric culture]</p><p><b>nagovještaj, predznak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that is experienced as indicating important things to come [augury, foretoken, sign]</p><p><b>skup malignih stanica koje još nisu ušle u dublje epitelno tkivo ili se proširile na druge dijelove tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cluster of malignant cells that has not yet invaded the deeper epithelial tissue or spread to other parts of the body [carcinoma in situ]</p><p><b>izolirati unaprijed (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> isolate beforehand</p><p><b>unaprijed zaključiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> judge beforehand, especially without sufficient evidence</p><p><b>U slučaju da je sud odlučio da se ne primjenjuje odredba iz članka 107. stavka 1. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment reached before the evidence is available [prejudgment]</p><p><b>prejudiciranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment reached before the evidence is available [prejudgement]</p><p><b>biti u suprotnosti, dovoditi u pitanje, narušiti, predrasuda, prejudicirati, pristranost, šteta, uštrb, utjecati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a partiality that prevents objective consideration of an issue or situation [bias, preconception]</p><p><i>v.</i> disadvantage by prejudice</p><p><i>v.</i> influence (somebody's) opinion in advance [prepossess]</p><p><b>obuzet, pristran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> emanating from a person's emotions and prejudices</p><p><i>adj.</i> being biased or having a belief or attitude formed beforehand [discriminatory]</p><p><b>škodljiv, štetan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (sometimes followed by `to') causing harm or injury [damaging, detrimental, prejudicious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to favor preconceived ideas [prejudicious]</p><p><b>sklonost da se pridržavaju predodređenih ideja, (ponekad slijedi `to') uzrokovanje štete ili ozljede (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to favor preconceived ideas [prejudicial]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (sometimes followed by `to') causing harm or injury [damaging, detrimental, prejudicial]</p><p><b>svećenici zajedno, Ured ili položaj svećenika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prelates collectively [prelature]</p><p><i>n.</i> the office or station of a prelate [prelature]</p><p><b>Od ili u vezi s vremenom prije pada Adama i Eve (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the time before the Fall of Adam and Eve</p><p><b>crkveni velik, prelat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a senior clergyman and dignitary [archpriest, hierarch, high priest, primate]</p><p><b>svećenici zajedno, Ured ili položaj svećenika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prelates collectively [prelacy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the office or station of a prelate [prelacy]</p><p><b>manju utakmicu koja prethodi glavnom događaju., ispit koji su poduzeli studenti za dobivanje diplome kako bi utvrdili njihovu sposobnost za nastavak studija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a minor match preceding the main event [preliminary]</p><p><i>n.</i> an examination taken by graduate students to determine their fitness to continue [preliminary exam, preliminary examination]</p><p><b>početni, prednatjecanje, prethodni, prethodno, prijemni ispit, pripreme, pripremni, uvodan, uvodni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a minor match preceding the main event [prelim]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that serves as a preceding event or introduces what follows [overture, prelude]</p><p><i>adj.</i> denoting an action or event preceding or in preparation for something more important</p><p><b>kolokvij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an examination taken by graduate students to determine their fitness to continue [prelim, preliminary examination]</p><p><b>ispit koji su poduzeli studenti za dobivanje diplome kako bi utvrdili njihovu sposobnost za nastavak studija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an examination taken by graduate students to determine their fitness to continue [prelim, preliminary exam]</p><p><b>Prva verzija prospekta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a first draft of a prospectus [red herring]</p><p><b>pisana stvar koja prethodi glavnom tekstu knjige (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> written matter preceding the main text of a book [front matter]</p><p><b>koji još nisu stekli sposobnost čitanja i pisanja, -Koliko je to? (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not yet having acquired the ability to read and write</p><p><i>adj.</i> used of a society that has not developed writing [nonliterate]</p><p><b>glukokortikoid (trgovinski nazivi Pediapred ili Prelone) koji se koristi za liječenje upalnih stanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a glucocorticoid (trade names Pediapred or Prelone) used to treat inflammatory conditions [Pediapred, prednisolone]</p><p><b>djelo, predigra, preludij, uvod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that serves as a preceding event or introduces what follows [overture, preliminary]</p><p><i>n.</i> music that precedes a fugue or introduces an act in an opera</p><p><i>v.</i> serve as a prelude or opening to</p><p><i>v.</i> play as a prelude</p><p><b>koji se odnose na događaje prije braka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to events before a marriage [antenuptial, prenuptial]</p><p><b>prenagljen, preran, preuranjen, preuranjeno, prijevremen, nepravodoban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> born after a gestation period of less than the normal time</p><p><i>adj.</i> too soon or too hasty [previous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> uncommonly early or before the expected time [untimely]</p><p><b>dijete koje je rođeno prije 37. tjedna trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infant that is born prior to 37 weeks of gestation [preemie, premature infant, premie, preterm baby, preterm infant]</p><p><b>ejakulacija u ranim fazama seksualnog uzbuđenja ili ubrzo nakon uvođenja penisa u vaginu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ejaculation during the early stages of sexual excitement or soon after the insertion of the penis into the vagina</p><p><b>dijete koje je rođeno prije 37. tjedna trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infant that is born prior to 37 weeks of gestation [preemie, premature baby, premie, preterm baby, preterm infant]</p><p><b>radni trenuci koji počinju prije 37. tjedna trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> labor beginning prior to the 37th week of gestation [premature labour]</p><p><b>radni trenuci koji počinju prije 37. tjedna trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> labor beginning prior to the 37th week of gestation [premature labor]</p><p><b>nepravilnost srčanog ritma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> irregularity of cardiac rhythm [PVC]</p><p><b>prenagljen, preran, preuranjen, preuranjeno, prijevremen (od &quot;premature&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (of childbirth) before the end of the normal period of gestation</p><p><i>adv.</i> too soon [untimely]</p><p><b>prenagljen, preran, preuranjen, preuranjeno, prijevremen (od &quot;premature&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being premature [prematurity]</p><p><b>stanje prijevremenog rođenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being premature [prematureness]</p><p><b>priprema za studij medicine, predhodni i priprema za studije medicine (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> preparing for the study of medicine</p><p><i>adj.</i> preceding and preparing for the study of medicine</p><p><b>unaprijed promisliti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> consider, ponder, or plan (an action) beforehand</p><p><i>v.</i> think or reflect beforehand or in advance</p><p><b>namišljen, promišljen, s predumišljajem, smišljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by deliberate purpose and some degree of planning</p><p><b>nakana, namjera, umišljaj, predumišljaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> planning or plotting in advance of acting [forethought]</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) thought and intention to commit a crime well in advance of the crime</p><p><b>prije menopauze (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> prior to menopause</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili se javljaju tijekom razdoblja neposredno prije menstruacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or occurring during the period just before menstruation</p><p><b>predmenstrualni sindrom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a syndrome that occurs in many women from 2 to 14 days before the onset of menstruation [PMS]</p><p><b>dijete koje je rođeno prije 37. tjedna trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infant that is born prior to 37 weeks of gestation [preemie, premature baby, premature infant, preterm baby, preterm infant]</p><p><b>glavni, predsjednik vlade, premijer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the person who holds the position of head of the government in the United Kingdom [PM, Prime Minister]</p><p><i>n.</i> the person who is head of government (in several countries) [chancellor, prime minister]</p><p><i>v.</i> be performed for the first time [premiere]</p><p><i>v.</i> perform a work for the first time [premiere]</p><p><i>adj.</i> first in rank or degree [prime]</p><p><i>adj.</i> preceding all others in time [premiere]</p><p><b>praizvedba, premijera, prvo prikazivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first public performance of a play or movie</p><p><i>v.</i> be performed for the first time [premier]</p><p><i>v.</i> perform a work for the first time [premier]</p><p><i>adj.</i> preceding all others in time [premier]</p><p><b>Ured premijera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the office of premier</p><p><b>premisa, pretpostavka, uvesti, uvoditi, započeti, započinjati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statement that is assumed to be true and from which a conclusion can be drawn [assumption, premiss]</p><p><i>v.</i> set forth beforehand, often as an explanation</p><p><i>v.</i> furnish with a preface or introduction [introduce, precede, preface]</p><p><i>v.</i> take something as preexisting and given [premiss]</p><p><b>prostori, prostorima</b></p><p><i>n.</i> land and the buildings on it</p><p><b>premisa, pretpostavka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statement that is assumed to be true and from which a conclusion can be drawn [assumption, premise]</p><p><i>v.</i> take something as preexisting and given [premise]</p><p><b>dar, glavna nagrada, nagrada, plaćanje, premija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> payment for insurance [insurance premium]</p><p><i>n.</i> the amount that something in scarce supply is valued above its nominal value</p><p><i>n.</i> a fee charged for exchanging currencies [agio, agiotage, exchange premium]</p><p><i>n.</i> a prize, bonus, or award given as an inducement to purchase products, enter competitions initiated by business interests, etc.</p><p><i>n.</i> payment or reward (especially from a government) for acts such as catching criminals or killing predatory animals or enlisting in the military [bounty]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or reflecting superior quality or value</p><p><b>državna obveznica koja ne nosi kamate ili kapitalne dobiti, ali nosioca uključuje u lutrije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government bond that bears no interest or capital gains but enters the holder into lotteries</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se upotrebljava u proizvodnji proizvoda iz poglavlja 3. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a commercially prepared mixture of dry ingredients [mix]</p><p><b>pretkutnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tooth having two cusps or points [bicuspid]</p><p><b>opomena, predosjećaj, slutnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of evil to come [boding, foreboding, presentiment]</p><p><i>n.</i> an early warning about a future event [forewarning]</p><p><b>služi za opomenu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> warning of future misfortune [precursory]</p><p><b>rod višegodišnjih biljaka iz Sjeverne Amerike i Azije s pinnatisect listovima male glave spuštenih žuto- do ljubičasto-crvenih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of North American and Asiatic perennial herbs having pinnatisect leaves small heads of drooping yellowish to purple flowers [genus Prenanthes]</p><p><b>biljka sjeveroistočne Sjeverne Amerike s spušteni grmovi žuto-bijelog cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herb of northeastern North America having drooping clusters of yellowish-white flowers [Nabalus alba, cankerweed, white lettuce]</p><p><b>biljka iz srednje i južne Europe s ljubičastim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herb of central and southern Europe having purple florets [rattlesnake root]</p><p><b>Obična višegodišnja biljka široko rasprostranjena u južnim i istočnim Sjedinjenim Državama s spušteni grumci ružičastih cvijeća i debelih bazalnih listova koji sugeriraju oblik lavlje noge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common perennial herb widely distributed in the southern and eastern United States having drooping clusters of pinkish flowers and thick basal leaves suggesting a lion's foot in shape [Nabalus serpentarius, gall of the earth, lion's foot]</p><p><b>koji se javljaju ili postoje prije rođenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring or existing before birth [antenatal, antepartum]</p><p><b>prenatalna dijagnostika, prenatalna dijagnoza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the diagnostic procedures used to determine whether a fetus has a genetic abnormality</p><p><b>od pridjeva (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of adjectives [attributive]</p><p><b>naučnik, šegrt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> works for an expert to learn a trade [apprentice, learner]</p><p><b>predbračni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to events before a marriage [antenuptial, premarital]</p><p><b>preokupacija, zadubljenost, zanimanje, zaokupljenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mental state of being preoccupied by something [absorption, engrossment, preoccupation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of taking occupancy before someone else does [preoccupation]</p><p><b>rasijanost, zabrinutost, preokupacija, zadubljenost, zanimanje, zaokupljenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an idea that preoccupies the mind and holds the attention</p><p><i>n.</i> the mental state of being preoccupied by something [absorption, engrossment, preoccupancy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of taking occupancy before someone else does [preoccupancy]</p><p><b>preokupiran, preopterećen, zabrinut, zaokupljen mislima</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> deeply absorbed in thought [bemused, lost]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing excessive or compulsive concern with something [haunted, obsessed, taken up]</p><p><b>brinuti o, obuzeti, prigrabiti, zaokupiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> engage or engross the interest or attention of beforehand or occupy urgently or obsessively</p><p><i>v.</i> occupy or take possession of beforehand or before another or appropriate for use in advance</p><p><b>predoperativna</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> happening or done before and in preparation for a surgical operation</p><p><b>predodređivati ili odrediti unaprijed (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> foreordain or determine beforehand [foreordain, predestine]</p><p><b>(teologija) je unaprijed određena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (theology) being determined in advance [foreordination, predestination, predetermination]</p><p><b>priprema za školovanje izvan škole (posebno kod kuće) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> preparatory school work done outside school (especially at home) [homework, preparation]</p><p><b>privatna srednja škola (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a private secondary school [preparatory school]</p><p><b>S druge vrste: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> prepared and wrapped beforehand and ready for sale [prepacked]</p><p><b>S druge vrste: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> prepared and wrapped beforehand and ready for sale [prepackaged]</p><p><b>franko, poštarina plaćena</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> used especially of mail [postpaid]</p><p><b>lijek, preparat, priprava, pripravak, pripravljanje, priprema, pripremanje, spremati se, spremnost, preparacija, spremanje, formula, planiranje, predmnijevanje, pripravnost, obuka, obučavanje, trening, treniranje, kuhanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the activity of putting or setting in order in advance of some act or purpose [readying]</p><p><i>n.</i> a substance prepared according to a formula [formulation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the cognitive process of thinking about what you will do in the event of something happening [planning, provision]</p><p><i>n.</i> the st