ntation of something [display]</p><p><i>n.</i> formally making a person known to another or to the public [intro, introduction]</p><p><i>n.</i> (obstetrics) position of the fetus in the uterus relative to the birth canal</p><p><b>predodžben</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a presentation (especially in psychology or philosophy)</p><p><b>davatelj, predlagač, prezenter, voditelj, voditeljica, donator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who presents a message of some sort (as a petition or an address or a check or a memorial etc.)</p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate who presents a person (as for an award or a degree or an introduction etc.) [sponsor]</p><p><i>n.</i> person who makes a gift of property [bestower, conferrer, donor, giver]</p><p><b>predosjećanje, slutnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of evil to come [boding, foreboding, premonition]</p><p><b>doktrinu da su proročanstva iz Apokalipse (kao u Knjizi Otkrivenja) trenutno u tijeku ispunjenja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine that the Scripture prophecies of the Apocalypse (as in the Book of Revelations) are presently in the course of being fulfilled</p><p><b>teolog koji vjeruje da se proročanstva iz Apokalipse (Knjige Otkrivenja) ispunjavaju u naše vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a theologian who believes that the Scripture prophecies of the Apocalypse (the Book of Revelation) are being fulfilled at the present time</p><p><b>odmah, smjesta, trenutno, ubrzo, uskoro</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in the near future [before long, shortly, soon]</p><p><i>adv.</i> at this time or period [currently]</p><p><b>ponašanje, predstavljane</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an accusation of crime made by a grand jury on its own initiative [notification]</p><p><i>n.</i> a document that must be accepted and paid by another person</p><p><i>n.</i> a show or display [demonstration, presentation]</p><p><b>aktuelno, današnji, dar, dosadašnji, dostaviti, glagolsko vrijeme, izvesti, nazočan, podnijeti, poklon, pokloniti, postojeći, predočiti, predstaviti, pr