s a necessary antecedent or precondition [suppose]</p><p><b>pretpostavka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of presupposing</p><p><b>u slučaju bolesti u ranoj fazi ili u vezi s njom kada točna dijagnoza nije moguća jer se simptomi bolesti još nisu pojavili. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the early phases of a disease when accurate diagnosis is not possible because symptoms of the disease have not yet appeared [preclinical]</p><p><b>predadolescentni dječak ili djevojčica (obično između 9 i 12 godina), od ili povezane s ili namijenjene djeci u dobi od 9 do 12 godina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a preadolescent boy or girl (usually between 9 and 12 years of age) [preteenager]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or designed for children between the ages of 9 and 12 [preadolescent]</p><p><b>predadolescentni dječak ili djevojčica (obično između 9 i 12 godina) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a preadolescent boy or girl (usually between 9 and 12 years of age) [preteen]</p><p><b>izgovor, lažan razlog, pravo, pretvaranje, zahtjev, himba, hinjenje, lažnost, prijetvornost, simuliranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a false or unsupportable quality [pretense, pretension]</p><p><i>n.</i> an artful or simulated semblance [guise, pretense, pretext]</p><p><i>n.</i> pretending with intention to deceive [dissembling, feigning, pretense]</p><p><i>n.</i> imaginative intellectual play [make-believe, pretense]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving a false appearance [feigning, pretending, pretense, simulation]</p><p><b>polagati pravo, pretendirati, pretvarati se, praviti se, afektirati, glumatati, glumiti, hiniti, izigravati, prenavljati se, prenemagati se, producirati se, nagađati, naslutiti, naslućivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the enactment of a pretense [make-believe]</p><p><i>v.</i> make believe with the intent to deceive [affect, dissemble, feign, sham]</p><p><i>v.</i> behave unnaturally or affectedly [act, dissemble]</p><p><i>v.</i> put forward a claim and assert right or possession of</p><p><i>v.</i> put forward, of a guess, in spite of possible refutation [guess, hazard, venture]</p><p><i>v.</i> represent fictitiously, as in a play, or pretend to be or act like [make, make believe]</p><p><i>v.</i> state insincerely [profess]</p><p><i>adj.</i> imagined as in a play [make-believe]</p><p><b>tobožnji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> adopted in order to deceive [assumed, false, fictitious, fictive, put on, sham]</p><p><b>licemjer, onaj, pretendent, hohštapler, varalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a claimant to the throne or to the office of ruler (usually without just title)</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who makes deceitful pretenses [fake, faker, fraud, imposter, impostor, pseud, pseudo, role player, sham, shammer]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who professes beliefs and opinions that he or she does not hold in order to conceal his or her real feelings or motives [dissembler, dissimulator, hypocrite, phoney, phony]</p><p><b>himba, hinjenje, lažnost, pretvaranje, prijetvornost, simuliranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving a false appearance [feigning, pretence, pretense, simulation]</p><p><b>himba, hinjenje, lažnost, pretvaranje, prijetvornost, simuliranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving a false appearance [feigning, pretence, pretending, simulation]</p><p><i>n.</i> pretending with intention to deceive [dissembling, feigning, pretence]</p><p><i>n.</i> imaginative intellectual play [make-believe, pretence]</p><p><i>n.</i> a false or unsupportable quality [pretence, pretension]</p><p><i>n.</i> an artful or simulated semblance [guise, pretence, pretext]</p><p><b>pretvaranje, traženje, zahtjev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a false or unsupportable quality [pretence, pretense]</p><p><i>n.</i> the advancing of a claim</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being pretentious (behaving or speaking in such a manner as to create a false appearance of great importance or worth) [largeness, pretentiousness]</p><p><b>pretenciozan, uobražen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> making claim to or creating an appearance of (often undeserved) importance or distinction</p><p><i>adj.</i> intended to attract notice and impress others [ostentatious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a display) tawdry or vulgar [ostentatious]</p><p><b>pretenciozno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a pretentious manner</p><p><b>pretenciozan, uobražen (od &quot;pretentious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lack of elegance as a consequence of being pompous and puffed up with vanity [inflation, ostentation, ostentatiousness, pomposity, pompousness, puffiness, splashiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being pretentious (behaving or speaking in such a manner as to create a false appearance of great importance or worth) [largeness, pretension]</p><p><b>teolog koji vjeruje da su se proročanstva iz Apokalipse (Knjiga Otkrivenja) već ispunila. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a theologian who believes that the Scripture prophecies of the Apocalypse (the Book of Revelation) have already been fulfilled</p><p><b>glagolsko vrijeme, preterit, prošlo svršeno vrijeme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a term formerly used to refer to the simple past tense [preterite]</p><p><b>izraz koji se nekada koristio za jednostavno prošlost. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a term formerly used to refer to the simple past tense [preterit]</p><p><b>sugerišući namjerno sažet tretman da je mnogo značaja izostavljeno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> suggesting by deliberately concise treatment that much of significance is omitted [paraleipsis, paralepsis, paralipsis]</p><p><b>dijete koje je rođeno prije 37. tjedna trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infant that is born prior to 37 weeks of gestation [preemie, premature baby, premature infant, premie, preterm infant]</p><p><b>dijete koje je rođeno prije 37. tjedna trudnoće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infant that is born prior to 37 weeks of gestation [preemie, premature baby, premature infant, premie, preterm baby]</p><p><b>puštanje bez najave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> letting pass without notice</p><p><b>izostaviti, izostavljati, previdjeti, previđati, propustiti, propuštati, zanemariti, zanemarivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> disregard intentionally or let pass</p><p><i>v.</i> leave undone or leave out [drop, leave out, miss, neglect, omit, overleap, overlook]</p><p><b>izvanredan, natprirodan, neobičan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> surpassing the ordinary or normal [uncanny]</p><p><i>adj.</i> existing outside of or not in accordance with nature [nonnatural, otherworldly, transcendental]</p><p><b>izvanredan, natprirodan, neobičan (od &quot;preternatural&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a supernatural manner [supernaturally]</p><p><b>izgovor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something serving to conceal plans [stalking-horse]</p><p><i>n.</i> an artful or simulated semblance [guise, pretence, pretense]</p><p><b>pretor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an annually elected magistrate of the ancient Roman Republic [praetor]</p><p><b>Grad u Transvaalu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> city in the Transvaal [capital of South Africa]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s rimskim pretorom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a Roman praetor [praetorial, praetorian, pretorian]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s rimskim pretorom, karakterističan za ili sličan vojnicima u pretorijanskoj straži u pogledu korupcije ili političke pokvarene vrijednosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a Roman praetor [praetorial, praetorian, pretorial]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of or similar to the corruptible soldiers in the Praetorian Guard with respect to corruption or political venality [Praetorian]</p><p><b>Šator starog rimskog generala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tent of an ancient Roman general [praetorium]</p><p><b>(zakonom) konferencija održana prije početka suđenja koja okuplja stranke kako bi se definirao postupak otkrivanja i utvrdili pitanja koja se trebaju suditi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a conference held before the trial begins to bring the parties together to outline discovery proceedings and to define the issues to be tried [pretrial conference]</p><p><b>(zakonom) konferencija održana prije početka suđenja koja okuplja stranke kako bi se definirao postupak otkrivanja i utvrdili pitanja koja se trebaju suditi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a conference held before the trial begins to bring the parties together to outline discovery proceedings and to define the issues to be tried [pretrial]</p><p><b>kititi, krasiti, okititi, resiti, ukrasiti, ukrašavati, uljepšati, uljepšavati, uresiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make more beautiful [beautify, embellish, fancify]</p><p><b>dosta, lijep, ljepušan, melodičan, prijatan, priličan, prilično, pristao, privlačan, sladak, zgodan, zgodno, znatan (od &quot;pretty&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a pretty manner</p><p><b>ljepota, ljupkost, privlačnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being appealing in a delicate or graceful way (of a girl or young woman) [cuteness]</p><p><b>dosta, lijep, ljepušan, melodičan, prijatan, priličan, prilično, pristao, privlačan, sladak, zgodan, zgodno, znatan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pleasing by delicacy or grace</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used ironically) unexpectedly bad</p><p><i>adv.</i> to certain extent or degree [fairly, jolly, middling, moderately, passably, reasonably, somewhat]</p><p><b>do neke mjere. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to some degree</p><p><b>posebno pazite na oblačenje, šminku itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> use special care in dressing, making-up, etc. [do up, doll up, glam up]</p><p><b>ostentativno ili neprikladno lijepo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> ostentatiously or inappropriately pretty</p><p><b>perec</b></p><p><i>n.</i> glazed and salted cracker typically in the shape of a loose knot</p><p><b>bivše kraljevstvo u sjevernoj središnjoj Europi uključujući današnju sjevernu Njemačku i sjevernu Poljsku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former kingdom in north-central Europe including present-day northern Germany and northern Poland [Prussia]</p><p><b>antiacid (trgovinski naziv Prevacid) koji potiskuje lučenje kiseline u želucu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antacid (trade name Prevacid) tha