><b>predvidjeti, proreći, predosjetiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> warn in advance or beforehand [forewarn]</p><p><i>v.</i> realize beforehand [anticipate, foreknow, foresee]</p><p><b>predviđanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a prophetic vision (as in a dream)</p><p><i>n.</i> the power to foresee the future [prescience]</p><p><i>n.</i> seeing ahead [farsightedness, foresight, prospicience]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of predicting (as by reasoning about the future) [anticipation, prediction]</p><p><b>oglas koji se sastoji od kratkih scena iz filma koji će se pojaviti u bliskoj budućnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advertisement consisting of short scenes from a motion picture that will appear in the near future [preview, trailer]</p><p><b>predratni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> existing or belonging to a time before a war</p><p><b>dekan, rektor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the head administrative officer of a college or university [president]</p><p><b>grabež, hvatati, loviti, plijen, pljačka, pljačkati, podrivati, vrebati, žrtva, lovina, ulov</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is the aim of an attack (especially a victim of ridicule or exploitation) by some hostile person or influence [fair game, quarry, target]</p><p><i>n.</i> animal hunted or caught for food [quarry]</p><p><i>v.</i> profit from in an exploitatory manner [feed]</p><p><i>v.</i> prey on or hunt for [predate, raven]</p><p><b>male mesojede ribe perkoide koje se nalaze širom svijeta u tropskim morima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small carnivorous percoid fishes found worldwide in tropical seas [family Priacanthidae]</p><p><b>tip rod Priacanthidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Priacanthidae [genus Priacanthus]</p><p><b>svjetlo obojene mesožderke ribe iz voda zapadnog Atlantika i Zapadne Indije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brightly colored carnivorous fish of western Atlantic and West Indies waters [catalufa]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) posljednji kralj Troje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the last king of Troy</p><p><b>Previše se brine o muškošću i muškarskoj seksualnosti., sliči ili je falus (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> overly concerned with masculinity and male sexuality</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling or being a phallus [phallic]</p><p><b>stanje u kojem je penis neprekidno uspravljen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> condition in which the penis is continually erect</p><p><b>Bog muške reproduktivne moći i čuvar vrtova i vinograda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (classical mythology) god of male procreative power and guardian of gardens and vineyards</p><p><b>cijena, odrediti cijenu, procijeniti, vrijednost, cijene, cijeni, novčana vrijednost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of having material worth (often indicated by the amount of money something would bring if sold) [cost, monetary value]</p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of money needed to purchase something [damage, terms]</p><p><i>n.</i> value measured by what must be given or done or undergone to obtain something [cost, toll]</p><p><i>n.</i> the high value or worth of something</p><p><i>n.</i> a monetary reward for helping to catch a criminal</p><p><i>n.</i> cost of bribing someone</p><p><i>n.</i> United States operatic soprano (born 1927) [Leontyne Price, Mary Leontyne Price]</p><p><i>v.</i> determine the price of</p><p><i>v.</i> ascertain or learn the price of</p><p><b>kategorija robe na temelju njihove cijene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a category of merchandise based on their price</p><p><b>intenzivna konkurencija u kojoj konkurenti smanjuju maloprodajne cijene kako bi dobili posao (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intense competition in which competitors cut retail prices to gain business [price war]</p><p><b>kontrola cijena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> restriction on maximum prices that is established and maintained by the government (as during periods of war or inflation)</p><p><b>smanjenje cijene robe na jednu nižu od uobičajene ili oglašavane cijene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cutting the price of merchandise to one lower than the usual or advertised price [price cutting]</p><p><b>sniženje cijena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cutting the price of merchandise to one lower than the usual or advertised price [price cut]</p><p><b>podnožje ispod kojeg cijene ne smiju pasti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> floor below which prices are not allowed to fall</p><p><b>zamrzavanje cijena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a freeze of prices at a given level</p><p><b>U slučaju da je trgovački trgovac u mogućnosti da ponudi usluge na tržištu, trgovački trgovac mora imati pristup tržišnim tržištima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pricing above the market price when no alternative retailer is available</p><p><b>rast cijena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> increase in price</p><p><b>indeks cijena, mehanizam za praćenje promjena ugovorene i tržišne</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an index that traces the relative changes in the price of an individual good (or a market basket of goods) over time [price level]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je trgovačka cijena određena u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, to znači da je trgovačka cijena određena u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an index that traces the relative changes in the price of an individual good (or a market basket of goods) over time [price index]</p><p><b>cjenik, cjenik hotelskih usluga, cjeniku</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a listing of prices for different goods or services</p><p><b>cijena ulaznice, ulaz, ulaznica, upad</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fee charged for admission [admission, admission charge, admission fee, admission price, entrance fee, entrance money]</p><p><b>pad cijena, popust</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of reducing the selling price of merchandise [deduction, discount]</p><p><b>podržavanje cijena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government subsidy used to maintain prices at a certain level</p><p><b>oznaka koja pokazuje cijenu predmeta na kojem je priložena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tag showing the price of the article it is attached to</p><p><b>intenzivna konkurencija u kojoj konkurenti smanjuju m