ion</p><p><b>Sljedeći članak, Na određeni način bez ozbiljne pažnje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> done or produced as a formality only [perfunctory]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a set manner without serious attention [perfunctorily]</p><p><b>pro rata, razmjerno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in proportion [proportionately]</p><p><b>prema potrebi (liječnici koriste PRN u pisanju recepata) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> according to need (physicians use PRN in writing prescriptions) [PRN, as needed, as required]</p><p><b>Za sada. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> for the time being [pro tempore]</p><p><i>adv.</i> for the time being [pro tempore]</p><p><b>Za sada. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> for the time being [pro tem]</p><p><i>adv.</i> for the time being [pro tem]</p><p><b>podržava Sjedinjene Države i njihove politike (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> supporting the United States and its policies</p><p><b>braniti pravo žene da kontroliše svoje tijelo (posebno njeno pravo na potražnju za pobačajem) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> advocating a woman's right to control her own body (especially her right to an induced abortion)</p><p><b>oni koji tvrde da odluku o podizanju pobačaja treba donijeti majka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> those who argue that the decision to have an induced abortion should be made by the mother</p><p><b>koji imaju tendenciju izazivati upale (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to cause inflammation [proinflammatory]</p><p><b>zalagajući se za punu pravnu zaštitu embriona i fetusa (posebno protiv legalizacije induciranih pobačaja) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> advocating full legal protection of embryos and fetuses (especially opposing the legalization of induced abortions)</p><p><b>Oni koji tvrde da je abortus ubijanje i da bi ga trebalo zabraniti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> those who argue that induced abortion is killing and should be prohibited</p><p><b>zagovornik punog pravnog zaštite embriona i fetusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of full legal protection for embryos and fetuses</p><p><b>faktor koagulacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coagulation factor [accelerator factor, factor V, prothrombin accelerator]</p><p><b>opis bilo kojeg događaja ili podražaja ili procesa koji utječe na događaje ili podražaje ili procese koji se događaju naknadno, (od politike ili osobe ili djelovanja) kontrolirati situaciju tako što će uzrokovati nešto da se dogodi umjesto da čekaju da odgovore na to nakon što se dogodi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> descriptive of any event or stimulus or process that has an effect on events or stimuli or processes that occur subsequently</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a policy or person or action) controlling a situation by causing something to happen rather than waiting to respond to it after it happens</p><p><b>Rimokatolički sustav kazuistike da kada se stručnjaci ne slažu glumac može slijediti bilo koje vjerovatno mišljenje koje želi iako je neko drugačije mišljenje vjerojatno., (filozofija) doktrina da je (pošto je sigurno neostvarljiva) vjerojatnost dovoljna osnova za vjerovanje i djelovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Roman Catholic system of casuistry that when expert opinions differ an actor can follow any solidly probable opinion that he wishes even though some different opinion might be more probable</p><p><i>n.</i> (philosophy) the doctrine that (since certainty is unattainable) probability is a sufficient basis for belief and action</p><p><b>probabilistički, vjerojatnosni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Roman Catholic philosophy of probabilism</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or based on probability</p><p><b>korištenjem teorije vjerojatnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by the use of probability theory</p><p><b>mogućnost, vjerojatnosni, vjerojatnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measure of how likely it is that some event will occur [chance]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being probable</p><p><b>matematičar koji se specijalizirao za teoriju vjerojatnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mathematician who specializes in probability theory</p><p><b>teorija vjerojatnosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of applied mathematics that deals with probabilities [theory of probability]</p><p><b>moguć, vjerodostojan, vjerojatan, vjerojatno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an applicant likely to be chosen</p><p><i>adj.</i> likely but not certain to be or become true or real [likely]</p><p><i>adj.</i> apparently destined</p><p><b>(zakonom) dokazi koji su dovoljni za uhićenje ili pretres i zaplijenu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) evidence sufficient to warrant an arrest or search and seizure</p><p><b>možda, po svoj prilici, valjda, vjerojatno, zasigurno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with considerable certainty [belike, in all likelihood, in all probability, likely]</p><p><i>adv.</i> easy to believe on the basis of available evidence [believably, credibly, plausibly]</p><p><b>sudbena potvrda oporuke, sudbeno ovjerena kopija oporuke</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a judicial certificate saying that a will is genuine and conferring on the executors the power to administer the estate [probate will]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of proving that an instrument purporting to be a will was signed and executed in accord with legal requirements</p><p><i>v.</i> put a convicted person on probation by suspending his sentence</p><p><i>v.</i> establish the legal validity of (wills and other documents)</p><p><b>sud koji je nadležan za testamente i upravljanje nasljedstvom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a court having jurisdiction over the probate of wills and the administration of estates</p><p><b>pravni certifikat koji potvrđuje da je oporuka istinita i daje izvršitelju ovlast za upravljanje ostavštinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a judicial certificate saying that a will is genuine and conferring on the executors the power to administer the estate [probate]</p><p><b>ispitivanje, kušanje, kušnja, proba, probacija, probni rok, staž, uvjetna sloboda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trial period during which your character and abilities are tested to see whether you are suitable for work or 