iv, priznanje, profesija, stalno zaposlenje, struka, struke, zanimanje, zvanje, zajednica, vokacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the body of people in a learned occupation</p><p><i>n.</i> an occupation requiring special education (especially in the liberal arts or sciences)</p><p><i>n.</i> an open avowal (true or false) of some belief or opinion [professing]</p><p><i>n.</i> affirmation of acceptance of some religion or faith</p><p><b>poznavalac, profesionalac, profesionalan, služben, stručan, zanatski, znalački, profesionalne, profesionalni, profesionalnih, profesionalnog, stručna, stručni, stručnih, stručnim, stručno, stručnog, stručnu, strukovnjak, stručnjak, učitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person engaged in one of the learned professions [professional person]</p><p><i>n.</i> an athlete who plays for pay [pro]</p><p><i>n.</i> an authority qualified to teach apprentices [master]</p><p><i>adj.</i> engaged in a profession or engaging in as a profession or means of livelihood</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or suitable as a profession</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of or befitting a profession or one engaged in a profession</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a profession</p><p><i>adj.</i> engaged in by members of a profession</p><p><b>strukovna udruga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an association of practitioners of a given profession</p><p><b>igranje bejzbola za novac. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> playing baseball for money</p><p><b>igranje košarke za novac. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> playing basketball for money</p><p><b>boksanje za novac. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> boxing for money</p><p><b>izvođač koji profesionalno pleše. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a performer who dances professionally [dancer, terpsichorean]</p><p><b>nogomet igrao za plaću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> football played for pay</p><p><b>igranje golfa za novac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> playing golf for money</p><p><b>netko tko zarađuje za život igranjem ili podučavanjem golfa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who earns a living by playing or teaching golf [golf pro]</p><p><b>Službeni radni radni staž u industriji ili trgovini ili profesionalnim djelatnostima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a career in industrial or commercial or professional activities [business life]</p><p><b>profesionalna institucija, profesionalna organizacija, stručna institucija, stručna organizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organization of and for professional people [professional organization]</p><p><b>profesionalna institucija, profesionalna organizacija, stručna institucija, stručna organizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organization of and for professional people [professional organisation]</p><p><b>strukovnjak, stručnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person engaged in one of the learned professions [professional]</p><p><b>profesionalni odnos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation that exists when one person requests and is granted professional help from a qualified source</p><p><b>igranje tenisa za novac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> playing tennis for money</p><p><b>osoba koja zarađuje za život igrajući ili poučavajući tenis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who earns a living playing or teaching tennis [tennis pro]</p><p><b>Borba za novac. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wrestling for money</p><p><b>socijalni proces kojim ljudi počinju raditi za plaću ili kao sredstvo za život (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the social process whereby people come to engage in an activity for pay or as a means of livelihood [professionalization]</p><p><b>S druge strane, ako je osoba u službi ili u službi koja je primljena u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, ona mora imati pravo na radno mjesto., S obzirom na to da je to samo jedna od glavnih razloga za to, da se (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become professional or proceed in a professional manner or in an activity for pay or as a means of livelihood [professionalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make professional or give a professional character to [professionalize]</p><p><b>profesionalizam, profesionalizma, stručnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the expertness characteristic of a professional person</p><p><b>profesionalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the social process whereby people come to engage in an activity for pay or as a means of livelihood [professionalisation]</p><p><b>S druge strane, ako je osoba u službi ili u službi koja je primljena u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, ona mora imati pravo na radno mjesto., S obzirom na to da je to samo jedna od glavnih razloga za to, da se (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become professional or proceed in a professional manner or in an activity for pay or as a means of livelihood [professionalise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make professional or give a professional character to [professionalise]</p><p><b>profesionalne, profesionalno, stručno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a professional manner</p><p><b>profesor, sveučilišni profesor, trener, prof.</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is a member of the faculty at a college or university [prof]</p><p><b>profesorski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of professors</p><p><b>profesorski (od &quot;professorial&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a professorial manner</p><p><b>profesura</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the position of professor [chair]</p><p><b>nuditi, predložiti, prijedlog, dati, davati, ponuditi, pružati, pružiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a proposal offered for acceptance or rejection [proposition, suggestion]</p><p><i>v.</i> present for acceptance or rejection [offer]</p><p><b>iskustvo, vještina, znanje, stručnost, umijeće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of having great facility and competence</p><p><i>n.</i> skillfulness in the command of fundamentals deriving from practice and familiarity [technique]</p><p><b>iskusan, poznavalac, stručnjak, vješt, dobar, tehnički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or showing knowledge and skill and aptitude [adept, expert, good, practiced, skilful, skillful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to technique or proficiency in a practical skill [technical]</p><