at depth psychologically or emotionally [deeply, intensely]</p><p><b>potpuno gluhi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> totally deaf [deaf as a post, stone-deaf, unhearing]</p><p><b>apsolutan, bezdan, dalekovidan, dubina, dubok, mudar, potpun, smišljen (od &quot;profound&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extremeness of degree</p><p><i>n.</i> wisdom that is recondite and abstruse and profound [abstruseness, abstrusity, profundity, reconditeness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the intellectual ability to penetrate deeply into ideas [astuteness, deepness, depth, profundity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being physically deep [deepness, profundity]</p><p><i>n.</i> intellectual depth [profundity]</p><p><b>dubina, ponor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wisdom that is recondite and abstruse and profound [abstruseness, abstrusity, profoundness, reconditeness]</p><p><i>n.</i> intellectual depth [profoundness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the intellectual ability to penetrate deeply into ideas [astuteness, deepness, depth, profoundness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being physically deep [deepness, profoundness]</p><p><b>bogat, darežljiv, obilan, rasipan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> produced or growing in extreme abundance [exuberant, lush, luxuriant, riotous]</p><p><b>obilan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an abundant manner [abundantly, copiously, extravagantly]</p><p><b>bogat, darežljiv, obilan, rasipan (od &quot;profuse&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being extremely abundant [cornucopia, profusion, richness]</p><p><b>bogatstvo, darežljivost, izdašnost, obilje, pretjerana raskoš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being extremely abundant [cornucopia, profuseness, richness]</p><p><b>praotac, predak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancestor in the direct line [primogenitor]</p><p><b>potomak, potomstvo, sljedbenici, učenici, izdanak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the immediate descendants of a person [issue, offspring]</p><p><b>rijetka abnormalnost obilježena preuranjenim starenjem (siva kosa i bore kože i nagnuta držanja) kod djeteta (MT)</b></p><p><