ictive, prognosticative]</p><p><b>prognozirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a prediction about [anticipate, call, forebode, foretell, predict, promise]</p><p><i>v.</i> indicate, as with a sign or an omen [augur, auspicate, betoken, bode, forecast, foreshadow, foretell, omen, portend, predict, prefigure, presage]</p><p><b>nagovješćivanje, predznak, prognoza, predviđanje, proročanstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sign of something about to happen [omen, portent, presage, prodigy, prognostic]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement made about the future [forecasting, foretelling, prediction]</p><p><i>n.</i> knowledge of the future (usually said to be obtained from a divine source) [prophecy, vaticination]</p><p><b>o predviđanju ili povezanosti s njim (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to prediction [predictive, prognostic]</p><p><b>gatara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who makes predictions of the future (usually on the basis of special knowledge) [forecaster, predictor, soothsayer]</p><p><b>nacrt, osnova rada, plan, program, programa, programirati, programski, programu, raspored, emisija, šou, kurikulum, kompjutorski program, računalni program</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a series of steps to be carried out or goals to be accomplished [plan, programme]</p><p><i>n.</i> a system of projects or services intended to meet a public need [programme]</p><p><i>n.</i> a radio or television show [broadcast, programme]</p><p><i>n.</i> a document stating the aims and principles of a political party [platform, political platform, political program]</p><p><i>n.</i> an announcement of the events that will occur as part of a theatrical or sporting event [programme]</p><p><i>n.</i> an integrated course of academic studies [course of study, curriculum, programme, syllabus]</p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a sequence of instructions that a computer can interpret and execute [computer program, computer programme, programme]</p><p><i>n.</i> a performance (or series of performances) at a public presentation [programme]</p><p><i>v.</i> arrange a program of or for [programme]</p><p><i>v.</i> write a computer program [programme]</p><p><b>biblioteka, programska biblioteka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computing) a collection of standard programs and subroutines that are stored and available for immediate use [library, subroutine library]</p><p><b>naredba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a line of code written as part of a computer program [command, instruction, statement]</p><p><b>glazbene kompozicije namijenjene podsjećanju slušatelja na događaje ili na slike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> musical compositions intended to evoke images or remind the listener of events [programme music]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, trgovački instrumenti koji se upotrebljavaju za trgovanje na tržištu u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika moraju biti: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trading technique involving large blocks of stock with trades triggered by computer programs</p><p><b>nacrt, osnova rada, plan, program, programa, programirati, programski, programu, raspored (od &quot;program&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> setting an order and time for planned events [programming, scheduling]</p><p><i>n.</i> creating a sequence of instructions to enable the computer to do something [computer programing, computer programming, programming]</p><p><b>(računalnička znanost) jezik dizajniran za programiranje računala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) a language designed for programming computers [programming language]</p><p><b>Uredba koja je javno objavljena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edict that has been publicly posted</p><p><b>emisija, program, programa, programu, kurikulum, šou, kompjutorski program, računalni program, plan, programirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an announcement of the events that will occur as part of a theatrical or sporting event [program]</p><p><i>n.</i> an integrated course of academic studies [course of study, curriculum, program, syllabus]</p><