growth or development [advancement]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of moving forward (as toward a goal) [advance, advancement, forward motion, onward motion, procession, progression]</p><p><i>n.</i> a movement forward [advance, progression]</p><p><i>v.</i> develop in a positive way [advance, come along, come on, get along, get on, shape up]</p><p><i>v.</i> move forward, also in the metaphorical sense [advance, go on, march on, move on, pass on]</p><p><i>v.</i> form or accumulate steadily [build, build up, work up]</p><p><b>izvještaj o napredovanju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a report of work accomplished during a specified time period</p><p><b>postići cilj (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> reach a goal [get to, make, reach]</p><p><b>napredovanje, prodiranje, progresija, napredak, pomak, progres</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a series with a definite pattern of advance [patterned advance]</p><p><i>n.</i> a movement forward [advance, progress]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of moving forward (as toward a goal) [advance, advancement, forward motion, onward motion, procession, progress]</p><p><b>koji raste, napredan, naprednim, postupan, progresivan, imperfekt, liberal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tense of verbs used in describing action that is on-going [continuous tense, imperfect, imperfect tense, progressive tense]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who favors a political philosophy of progress and reform and the protection of civil liberties [liberal, liberalist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> favoring or promoting progress</p><p><i>adj.</i> favoring or promoting reform (often by government action) [reform-minded, reformist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of taxes) adjusted so that the rate increases as the amount of income increases</p><p><i>adj.</i> gradually advancing in extent</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a card game or a dance) involving a series of sections for which the participants successively change place or relative position</p><p><i>adj.</i> advancing in severity</p><p><b>aspekt glagola koji izražava njegovo tekuće djelovanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the aspect of a verb that expresses its on-going action</p><p><b>(patologija) smrtonosni oblik gangrene obično uzrokovane Clostridium bakterije koje proizvode toksine koje uzrokuju smrt tkiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (pathology) a deadly form of gangrene usually caused by clostridium bacteria that produce toxins that cause tissue death [clostridial myonecrosis, emphysematous gangrene, emphysematous phlegmon, gangrenous emphysema, gas gangrene, gas phlegmon]</p><p><b>bivša politička stranka u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former political party in the United States [Bull Moose Party]</p><p><b>stil rock muzike koji se pojavio 1970-ih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a style of rock music that emerged in the 1970s [art rock]</p><p><b>Svaka porezna obveza koja se primjenjuje na određene vrste proizvoda ili usluga. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any tax in which the rate increases as the amount subject to taxation increases [graduated tax]</p><p><b>imperfekt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tense of verbs used in describing action that is on-going [continuous tense, imperfect, imperfect tense, progressive]</p><p><b>ozbiljan ili čak fatalan oblik vakcinacije koji se uglavnom javlja kod osoba s imunološkim nedostatkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a severe or even fatal form of vaccinia that occurs mainly in persons with an immunological deficiency [vaccinia gangrenosa]</p><p><b>postupno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> advancing in amount or intensity [increasingly, more and more]</p><p><b>koji raste, napredan, naprednim, postupan, progresivan (od &quot;progressive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> advancement toward better conditions or policies or methods [progressivity]</p><p><b>progresivizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the political orientation of those who favor progress toward better conditions in government and society</p><p><b>napredak prema boljim uvjetima ili politikama ili metodama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> advancement toward better conditions or policies or methods [progressiveness]</p><p