ivision of property owned or acquired by marriage partners during their marriage</p><p><b>porez na imovinu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a capital tax on property imposed by municipalities [land tax]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, poduzeća koja su u vlasništvu društva mogu imati: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> owning land or securities as a principal source of revenue [propertied]</p><p><b>od onih koji rade za plaću posebno ručni ili industrijski radnici (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of those who work for wages especially manual or industrial laborers [blue-collar, wage-earning, working-class]</p><p><b>Prvi stadij mejoze, Prvi stupanj mitoze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first stage of meiosis</p><p><i>n.</i> the first stage of mitosis</p><p><b>proročanstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> knowledge of the future (usually said to be obtained from a divine source) [prognostication, vaticination]</p><p><i>n.</i> a prediction uttered under divine inspiration [divination]</p><p><b>prorok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an authoritative person who divines the future [oracle, prophet, seer, vaticinator]</p><p><b>predskazati, proreći, propovijedati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> predict or reveal through, or as if through, divine inspiration [vaticinate]</p><p><i>v.</i> deliver a sermon [preach]</p><p><b>božji poslanik, meteorolog, prognostičar, prorok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an authoritative person who divines the future [oracle, prophesier, seer, vaticinator]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who speaks by divine inspiration</p><p><b>proročica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman prophet</p><p><b>proročanski, proročki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> foretelling events as if by supernatural intervention [prophetical]</p><p><b>predviđaju događaje kao da je to nadnaravno djelovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> foretelling events as if by supernatural intervention [prophetic]</p><p><b>na proročki način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a prophetic manner</p><p><b>Knjige proročke</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the second of three divisions of