.</i> indicating the first or earliest or original</p><p><b>Prapovijesni nepismeni jezik koji je bio predak svih indoeuropskih jezika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a prehistoric unrecorded language that was the ancestor of all Indo-European languages [PIE]</p><p><b>njemački jezik Skandinavije do oko 700. godine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Germanic language of Scandinavia up until about 700</p><p><b>normalni gen koji ima potencijal da postane onkogen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a normal gene that has the potential to become an oncogene</p><p><b>Pa, atomski broj 91, protaktinij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short-lived radioactive metallic element formed from uranium and disintegrating into actinium and then into lead [Pa, atomic number 91, protactinium]</p><p><b>Studija o ljudima prije izuma pisanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study humans prior to the invention of writing [protohistory]</p><p><b>istraživanje prapovijesnih ljudskih artefakata i ljudskih fosila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of prehistoric human artifacts and human fossils [protoarcheology]</p><p><b>istraživanje prapovijesnih ljudskih artefakata i ljudskih fosila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of prehistoric human artifacts and human fossils [protoarchaeology]</p><p><b>najprimitivniji poznati tip ptice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> most primitive avian type known</p><p><b>mali rogovi dinosaurusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small horned dinosaur</p><p><b>postupnik, pravilnik (komuniciranja), protokol, protokolizirati, zapisnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) rules determining the format and transmission of data [communications protocol]</p><p><i>n.</i> forms of ceremony and etiquette observed by diplomats and heads of state</p><p><i>n.</i> code of correct conduct</p><p><b>protist, protoktist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the unicellular protists</p><p><b>bilo koji od rodova Protoctista (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the families of Protoctista</p><p><b>bilo koji rod Protoctista (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any ge