n]</p><p><b>psihijatrijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or used in or engaged in the practice of psychiatry [psychiatric]</p><p><b>psihijatar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a physician who specializes in psychiatry [head-shrinker, shrink]</p><p><b>psihijatrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of medicine dealing with the diagnosis and treatment of mental disorders [psychological medicine, psychopathology]</p><p><b>duhovni, psihička, psihički</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person apparently sensitive to things beyond the natural range of perception</p><p><i>adj.</i> affecting or influenced by the human mind [psychical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> outside the sphere of physical science [psychical]</p><p><b>komunikacija pomoću paranormalnih sredstava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> communication by paranormal means [anomalous communication, psychical communication]</p><p><b>Svaka od sljedećih vrsta: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an actuating force or factor [mental energy]</p><p><b>parapsihologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> phenomena that appear to contradict physical laws and suggest the possibility of causation by mental processes [parapsychology, psychic phenomenon]</p><p><b>parapsihologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> phenomena that appear to contradict physical laws and suggest the possibility of causation by mental processes [parapsychology, psychic phenomena]</p><p><b>emocionalna rana ili šok koji često imaju dugotrajne posljedice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an emotional wound or shock often having long-lasting effects [trauma]</p><p><b>psihički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affecting or influenced by the human mind [psychic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> outside the sphere of physical science [psychic]</p><p><b>komunikacija pomoću paranormalnih sredstava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> communication by paranormal means [anomalous communication, psychic communication]</p><p><b>psihički (od &quot;psychical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> from a psychic point of view</p><p><b>psiho</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person afflicted with psychosis [psychotic, psychotic person]</p><p><b>utječu na um ili raspoloženje ili druge mentalne procese (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affecting the mind or mood or other mental processes [psychotropic]</p><p><b>lijek koji može izazvati promjene raspoloženja i iskrivljene percepcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that can produce mood changes and distorted perceptions [consciousness-altering drug, mind-altering drug, psychoactive substance]</p><p><b>lijek koji može izazvati promjene raspoloženja i iskrivljene percepcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that can produce mood changes and distorted perceptions [consciousness-altering drug, mind-altering drug, psychoactive drug]</p><p><b>psihoanalizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> subject to psychoanalytic treatment [analyse, analyze, psychoanalyze]</p><p><b>psihoanaliza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a set of techniques for exploring underlying motives and a method of treating various mental disorders [analysis, depth psychology]</p><p><b>psihoanalitičar, psihoanalizator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a licensed practitioner of psychoanalysis [analyst]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili uključuje metode i teoriju psihijatrijskog liječenja koji je nastao od strane Sigmunda Freuda (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or incorporating the methods and theory of psychiatric treatment originated by Sigmund Freud [psychoanalytical]</p><p><b>proces koji se pretpostavlja da se događa u psihoanalitičkoj teoriji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a process that is assumed to occur in psychoanalytic theory</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili uključuje metode i teoriju psihijatrijskog liječenja koji je nastao od strane Sigmunda Freuda (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or incorporating the methods and theory of psychiatric treatment originated by Sigmund Freud [psychoanalytic]</p><p><b>podvrgnut je psihoanalitičkom liječenju (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> subject to psychoanalytic treatment [analyse, analyze, psychoanalyse]</p><p><b>koristeći jezik pun psihološke terminologije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> using language loaded with psychological terminology</p><p><b>psihoaktivni lijek koji izaziva halucinacije ili promijenjena osjetila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a psychoactive drug that induces hallucinations or altered sensory experiences [hallucinogen, hallucinogenic drug, psychedelic drug]</p><p><b>muha iz obitelji Psychodidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fly of the family Psychodidae</p><p><b>vrlo male dvokrilate muhe s dlakavim krilima koje se razvijaju u mahovi i vlažnoj biljnoj materiji: muhe pijeska (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very small two-winged flies with hairy wings that develop in moss and damp vegetable matter: sand flies [family Psychodidae]</p><p><b>međusobnu vezu svjesnih i nesvjesnih procesa i emocija koje određuju osobnost i motivaciju, grana socijalne psihologije koja se bavi procesima i emocijama koje određuju psihologiju i motivaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the interrelation of conscious and unconscious processes and emotions that determine personality and motivation</p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of social psychology that deals with the processes and emotions that determine psychology and motivation</p><p><b>promjena električnih svojstava kože kao odgovor na stres ili anksioznost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a change in the electrical properties of the skin in response to stress or anxiety [Fere phenomenon, GSR, Tarchanoff phenomenon, electrical skin response, electrodermal response, galvanic skin response]</p><p><b>razvoj u životu pojedinca nekog poremećaja koji je uzrokovan psihološkim, a ne fiziološkim čimbenicima, Opći izraz za porijeklo i razvoj gotovo svakog aspekta uma. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the development in the life of an individual of some disorder that is caused by psychological rather than physiological factors</p><p><i>n.</i> a general term for the origin and development of almost any aspect of the mind</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s psihološkim uzrocima poremećaja, ili u vezi s poreklom i razvojem uma (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the psychological cause of a disorder [psychogenic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the origin and development of the mind</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s psihološkim uzrocima poremećaja, mentalno ili emocionalno umjesto fiziološkog porijekla (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the psychological cause of a disorder [psychogenetic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> mental or emotional rather than physiological in origin</p><p><b>Dissociativni poremećaj u kojem osoba zaboravi tko je i napusti dom da stvori novi život (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dissociative disorder in which a person forgets who they are and leaves home to create a new life [fugue]</p><p><b>Moć pomicanja nečeg razmišljanjem bez primjene fizičke sile. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the power to move something by thinking about it without the application of physical force [telekinesis]</p><p><b>Premeštanje predmeta bez očitog korištenja fizičkih sredstava (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> moving an object without apparent use of physical means</p><p><b>osoba (obično psihologa, ali ponekad i lingvista) koja proučava psihološke osnove ljudskog jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person (usually a psychologist but sometimes a linguist) who studies the psychological basis of human language</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s psihologijom jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the psychology of language</p><p><b>psiholingvistika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of cognitive psychology that studies the psychological basis of linguistic competence and performance</p><p><b>psiholog, psihološki, psihološku</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> mental or emotional as opposed to physical in nature</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or determined by psychology</p><p><b>duševno stanje, mentalno stanje, psihieko stanje, stanje uma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) a mental condition in which the qualities of a state are relatively constant even though the state itself may be dynamic [mental condition, mental state, psychological state]</p><p><b>(psihijatrija) psihološki poremećaj misli ili osjećaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychiatry) a psychological disorder of thought or emotion [disturbance, folie, mental disorder, mental disturbance]</p><p><b>psihološka karakteristika, psihološko obilježje, psihološko svojstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feature of the mental life of a living organism</p><p><b>psihijatrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of medicine dealing with the diagnosis and treatment of mental disorders [psychiatry, psychopathology]</p><p><b>Najpovoljnije vrijeme za postizanje željenog učinka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the most appropriate time for achieving a desired effect</p><p><b>Vojne akcije namijenjene utjecaju na percepciju i stavove pojedinaca, skupina i stranih vlada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> military actions designed to influence the perceptions and attitudes of individuals, groups, and foreign governments [psyop]</p><p><b>psihologija, psihološka znanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the science of mental life [psychology]</p><p><b>duševno stanje, mentalno stanje, psihieko stanje, stanje uma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) a mental condition in which the qualities of a state are relatively constant even though the state itself may be dynamic [mental condition, mental state, psychological condition]</p><p><b>Upotreba psiholoških taktika da uništi protivnički moral. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of psychological tactics to destroy the opponents' morale [war of nerves]</p><p><b>psiholog, psihološki, psihološku (od &quot;psychological&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with regard to psychology</p><p><i>adv.</i> in terms of psychology</p><p><b>psiholog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scientist trained in psychology</p><p><b>medicina, psihologija, psihološka znanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the science of mental life [psychological science]</p><p><b>Odjel za nastavno i istraživačko djelovanje u psihologiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the academic department responsible for teaching and research in psychology [department of psychology]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s psihometrijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to psychometrics</p><p><b>psihometrijski test, test</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any standardized procedure for measuring sensitivity or memory or intelligence or aptitude or personality etc [mental test, mental testing, test]</p><p><b>psihometrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any branch of psychology concerned with psychological measurements [psychometrika, psychometry]</p><p><b>psihometrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any branch of psychology concerned with psychological measurements [psychometrics, psychometry]</p><p><b>psihometrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any branch of psychology concerned with psychological measurements [psychometrics, psychometrika]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili karakteriziraju mentalne događaje koji imaju motoričke posljedice ili obrnuto (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characterizing mental events that have motor consequences or vice versa</p><p><b>postupno stjecanje vještina koje uključuju mentalnu i motoričku aktivnost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> progressive acquisition of skills involving both mental and motor activities</p><p><b>epilepsija koja se klinički karakterizira poremećajom svijesti i amnezijom za epizodu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> epilepsy characterized clinically by impairment of consciousness and amnesia for the episode [temporal lobe epilepsy]</p><p><b>neuroticizam, neuroza, psihoneuroza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mental or personality disturbance not attributable to any known neurological or organic dysfunction [neurosis, neuroticism]</p><p><b>osoba koja pati od nevroze, koji ima emocionalni poremećaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person suffering from neurosis [mental case, neurotic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> affected with emotional disorder [neurotic]</p><p><b>eksperimentalna psihologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of psychology that uses experimental methods to study psychological issues [experimental psychology]</p><p><b>psihopat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone with a sociopathic personality [sociopath]</p><p><b>psihopat (od &quot;psychopath&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suffering from an undiagnosed mental disorder [psychopathologic, psychopathological]</p><p><b>poremećaj osobnosti koji se odlikuje nemoralnošću i nedostatkom osjećaja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a personality disorder characterized by amorality and lack of affect [antisocial personality disorder, sociopathic personality]</p><p><b>koji pati od dijagnosticiranog mentalnog poremećaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suffering from an undiagnosed mental disorder [psychopathic, psychopathological]</p><p><b>koji pati od dijagnosticiranog mentalnog poremećaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suffering from an undiagnosed mental disorder [psychopathic, psychopathologic]</p><p><b>psihopatologija, psihijatrija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of psychology concerned with abnormal behavior [abnormal psychology]</p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of medicine dealing with the diagnosis and treatment of mental disorders [psychiatry, psychological medicine]</p><p><b>bilo kakve bolesti uma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any disease of the mind [mental disease, mental illness]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s psihofarmakologijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to psychopharmacology</p><p><b>Studija o lijekovima koji utječu na um (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of drugs that affect the mind</p><p><b>psiholog obučen u psihofiziku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a psychologist trained in psychophysics</p><p><b>grana psihologije koja se bavi kvantitativnim odnosima između fizičkih podražaja i njihovih psiholoških učinaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of psychology concerned with quantitative relations between physical stimuli and their psychological effects</p><p><b>grana psihologije koja se bavi fiziološkim temeljima psiholoških procesa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of psychology that is concerned with the physiological bases of psychological processes [neuropsychology, physiological psychology]</p><p><b>vodič duša u zagrobni svijet. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conductor of souls to the afterworld</p><p><b>epifitne orhideje iz Srednje i Južne Amerike koje su ranije bile uključene u rod Oncidium (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> epiphytic orchids of Central and South America formerly included in genus Oncidium [genus Psychopsis]</p><p><b>Orhideja iz Južne i Srednje Amerike s cvjetovima sličnim ali manjim od Psychopsis papilio (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orchid of South and Central America having flowers similar to but smaller than Psychopsis papilio [Oncidium papilio kramerianum]</p><p><b>Orhideja iz Južne Amerike i Trinidada s velikim žutim i crvenkasto smeđim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orchid of South America and Trinidad having large yellow and reddish-brown flowers [Oncidium papilio]</p><p><b>mentalnih ili emocionalnih stavova o seksualnosti ili odnosno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the mental or emotional attitudes about sexuality</p><p><b>(psihoanaliza) proces tijekom kojeg se osobnost i seksualno ponašanje sazrevaju kroz niz faza: prvo oralno razdoblje, zatim analno razdoblje, zatim falalno razdoblje, zatim latentno razdoblje i konačno genitalno razdoblje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychoanalysis) the process during which personality and sexual behavior mature through a series of stages: first oral stage and then anal stage and then phallic stage and then latency stage and finally genital stage</p><p><b>mentalno predstavljanje seksualnih aktivnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mental representation of sexual activities</p><p><b>psihoza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any severe mental disorder in which contact with reality is lost or highly distorted</p><p><b>psihosomatika</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> used of illness or symptoms resulting from neurosis</p><p><b>mentalni poremećaj koji uzrokuje somatske simptome (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mental disorder that causes somatic symptoms</p><p><b>Operiranje mozga kod pacijenata namijenjeno ublažavanju teških i inače neizlječivih mentalnih ili ponašanja problema (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brain surgery on human patients intended to relieve severe and otherwise intractable mental or behavioral problems</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili prakticiranje psihoterapije, emocionalno čišćenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or practicing psychotherapy</p><p><i>adj.</i> emotionally purging [cathartic]</p><p><b>odjel psihijatrije koji se bavi psihološkim metodama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of psychiatry concerned with psychological methods [mental hygiene, psychotherapy]</p><p><b>terapeut koji se bavi mentalnim i emocionalnim poremećajima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a therapist who deals with mental and emotional disorders [clinical psychologist]</p><p><b>psihoterapija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of psychiatry concerned with psychological methods [mental hygiene, psychotherapeutics]</p><p><i>n.</i> the treatment of mental or emotional problems by psychological means</p><p><b>susret ljudi u psihoterapeutske svrhe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a meeting of people for psychotherapeutic purposes</p><p><b>osoba koja boluje od psihoze, karakteristična za ili pate od psihoze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person afflicted with psychosis [psycho, psychotic person]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of or suffering from psychosis</p><p><b>zabluda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) an erroneous belief that is held in the face of evidence to the contrary [delusion]</p><p><b>stanje depresije tako teške da osoba gubi kontakt s stvarnošću i pati od različitih funkcionalnih oštećenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of depression so severe that the person loses contact with reality and suffers a variety of functional impairments</p><p><b>osoba koja boluje od psihoze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person afflicted with psychosis [psycho, psychotic]</p><p><b>tropske, uglavnom južnoameričke grmlje i drveće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical chiefly South American shrubs and trees [genus Psychotria]</p><p><b>Južnoafrička stalezelena biljka koja ima tvrdo tvrdo drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African evergreen having hard tough wood [lemon-wood, lemon-wood tree, lemonwood, lemonwood tree]</p><p><b>psihotropan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affecting the mind or mood or other mental processes [psychoactive]</p><p><b>kemijska tvar koja može utjecati na ljudsku svijest. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chemical substance that can influence human consciousness</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hygrometer consisting of a dry-bulb thermometer and a wet-bulb thermometer</p><p><b>mali aktivni insekt nalik cikadi s stražnjim nogama prilagođenim za skakanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small active cicada-like insect with hind legs adapted for leaping [jumping plant louse, psyllid]</p><p><b>mali aktivni insekt nalik cikadi s stražnjim nogama prilagođenim za skakanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small active cicada-like insect with hind legs adapted for leaping [jumping plant louse, psylla]</p><p><b>uši skakačke biljke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> jumping plant lice [Chermidae, family Chermidae, family Psyllidae]</p><p><b>Planine iz mediteranskih regija čija se sjemena otkucaju i postaju želatinska kada su vlažna i koriste se kao blagi laksativ (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plantain of Mediterranean regions whose seeds swell and become gelatinous when moist and are used as a mild laxative [Plantago psyllium, Spanish psyllium, fleawort]</p><p><b>Vojne akcije namijenjene utjecaju na percepciju i stavove pojedinaca, skupina i stranih vlada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> military actions designed to influence the perceptions and attitudes of individuals, groups, and foreign governments [psychological operation]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heavy precious metallic element [atomic number 78, platinum]</p><p><b>mali brzi, neoklopljeni i lako naoružani torpedni brod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small fast unarmored and lightly armed torpedo boat [mosquito boat, mosquito craft, motor torpedo boat]</p><p><b>glavni egipatski bog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a major Egyptian god</p><p><b>alpska kokoš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large Arctic and subarctic grouse with feathered feet and usually white winter plumage</p><p><b>malo rod ponekad uključen u rod Onoclea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus sometimes included in genus Onoclea [Matteuccia, genus Matteuccia, genus Pteretis]</p><p><b>Matteuccia struthiopteris, Onoclea struthiopteris, Pteretis struthiopteris, bujadika, peruša, smeđa stela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall fern of northern temperate regions having graceful arched fronds and sporophylls resembling ostrich plumes [Matteuccia struthiopteris, Onoclea struthiopteris, fiddlehead, ostrich fern, shuttlecock fern]</p><p><b>jedna od nekoliko obitelji u koje je obitelj Polypodiaceae podjeljena u nekim sustavima klasifikacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of a number of families into which the family Polypodiaceae has been subdivided in some classification systems [family Pteridaceae]</p><p><b>rod paprika iz obitelji Dennstaedtiaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of ferns belonging to the family Dennstaedtiaceae [genus Pteridium]</p><p><b>veliki grubi paprati često nekoliko metara visoki (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large coarse fern often several feet high [bracken, brake, pasture brake]</p><p><b>paprika iz jugoistočne Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fern of southeastern Asia [bracken]</p><p><b>za ili u vezi s proučavanjem paprika (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the study of ferns</p><p><b>stručnjak za proučavanje paprika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert in the study of ferns</p><p><b>grana botanike koja proučava paprike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of botany that studies ferns</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 g/m2 do 0,15 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> containing all the vascular plants that do not bear seeds: ferns, horsetails, club mosses, and whisk ferns [division Pteridophyta]</p><p><b>papratnjače</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plants having vascular tissue and reproducing by spores [nonflowering plant]</p><p><b>biljka izrezana iz redova Cycadofilicales (ili skupine Pteridospermae) koja proizvodi sjeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extinct seed-producing fernlike plant of the order Cycadofilicales (or group Pteridospermae) [seed fern]</p><p><b>primjenjuje se u nekim sustavima klasifikacije: skupina izumrlih fosilnih gimnosperma koestentnih s redom Cycadofilicales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used in some classification systems: a group of extinct fossil gymnosperms coextensive with the order Cycadofilicales [Pteridospermaphyta, group Pteridospermae, group Pteridospermaphyta]</p><p><b>primjenjuje se u nekim sustavima klasifikacije: skupina izumrlih fosilnih gimnosperma koestentnih s redom Cycadofilicales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used in some classification systems: a group of extinct fossil gymnosperms coextensive with the order Cycadofilicales [Pteridospermae, group Pteridospermae, group Pteridospermaphyta]</p><p><b>izumrle gimnosperme većine karbonskog do jurskog doba: semenske paprike i saveznici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct gymnosperms most of Carboniferous to Jurassic: seed ferns and allies [class Pteridospermopsida]</p><p><b>ušice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pearl oysters [family Pteriidae]</p><p><b>kraniometrijska točka u području sfenoidne fontanele (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the craniometric point in the region of the sphenoid fontanelle</p><p><b>veliki rod kopnenih paprika iz tropskih i subtropskih područja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large genus of terrestrial ferns of tropics and subtropics [genus Pteris]</p><p><b>Pteris cretica, kretski papratac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cultivated in many varieties as houseplants</p><p><b>Azijski paprikac uveden u Ameriku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic fern introduced in America [spider brake, spider fern]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fern of North Africa and Azores and Canary Islands [ribbon fern, spider fern]</p><p><b>Žabe drveće koje koplje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> burrowing tree frogs [genus Pternohyla]</p><p><b>Zemaljska žaba noćna žaba na travnatom terenu i šumovitim šumama s vrlo tvrdom gornjom površinom glave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> terrestrial burrowing nocturnal frog of grassy terrain and scrub forests having very hard upper surface of head [lowland burrowing treefrog, northern casque-headed frog]</p><p><b>rod tropskih stabala ili planinara koji obično imaju široko krilavu čunju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of tropical trees or climbers having usually broadly winged pods [genus Pterocarpus]</p><p><b>ljeplovito južnoafričko stablo s velikim lišcima s čudnim pinatima i obilnim mirisnim narandžasto-žutim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous South African tree having large odd-pinnate leaves and profuse fragrant orange-yellow flowers [bloodwood tree, kiaat]</p><p><b>drvo porijeklom iz jugoistočne Azije koje ima crvenkasto drvo s mršavim zrnom s mrljama ili prugama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree native to southeastern Asia having reddish wood with a mottled or striped black grain [amboyna, padauk, padouk]</p><p><b>Drvo iz Indije i Burme koje daje drvo slično mahagoniju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree of India and Burma yielding a wood resembling mahogany [Burma padauk, Burmese rosewood]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijsko drvo koje daje smolu ili ekstrakt koji se često koristi u medicini i na primjer u solariju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian tree yielding a resin or extract often used medicinally and in e.g. tanning [kino]</p><p><b>Drvo iz Indije i Istočne Indije koje daje tvrdo mirisno drvo cijenjeno za kabine i tamno crveno srčano drvo koje se koristi kao drvo za bojenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree of India and East Indies yielding a hard fragrant timber prized for cabinetwork and dark red heartwood used as a dyewood [red sandalwood, red sanders, red sanderswood, red saunders]</p><p><b>Uvođenje u prometni promet (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic nut trees: wing nuts [genus Pterocarya]</p><p><b>srednjo veličine, kaukasijsko veliko-zelenjeno stablo koje se razlikuje od drugih orašastih stabala svojim krilatim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized Caucasian much-branched tree distinguished from other walnut trees by its winged fruit [Caucasian walnut]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Pteroclididae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Pteroclididae [genus Pterocles]</p><p><b>Europski i afrički pšenični pastrk s izduženim srednjim repnim perjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sandgrouse of Europe and Africa having elongated middle tail feathers [pin-tailed grouse, pin-tailed sandgrouse]</p><p><b>Indijski pšenični pšenični pšeničari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sandgrouse of India [painted sandgrouse]</p><p><b>sadže</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sandgrouses [family Pteroclididae]</p><p><b>rod ptica iz obitelji Rheidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of birds of the family Rheidae [genus Pterocnemia]</p><p><b>manje od dvije visoke brze ptice koje ne lete slične nojsama ali sa tri prsta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> smaller of two tall fast-running flightless birds similar to ostriches but three-toed [nandu, rhea]</p><p><b>izumrli leteći gmizavac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct flying reptile</p><p><b>obitelj gmizavaca u redu Pterosauria (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reptile family in the order Pterosauria [family Pterodactylidae]</p><p><b>rod reptila Pterodactylidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reptile genus of Pterodactylidae [genus Pterodactylus]</p><p><b>riblje ribe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lionfishes [genus Pterois]</p><p><b>biljka iz južne Australije s pernatim dlakama oko plodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> southern Australian plant having feathery hairs surrounding the fruit [Pteropogon humboltianum]</p><p><b>biljka iz južne Australije s pernatim dlakama oko plodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> southern Australian plant having feathery hairs surrounding the fruit [pteropogon]</p><p><b>U prethodnim klasifikacijama korišteni su za sve paprike i cvjetnice i podijeljeni u tri klase Filicinae i Gymnospermae i Angiospermae. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used in former classifications to include all ferns and flowering plants and divided into the three classes Filicinae and Gymnospermae and Angiospermae [subdivision Pteropsida]</p><p><b>rod Megachiroptera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Megachiroptera [genus Pteropus]</p><p><b>različita vrsta voćnog šišmiša (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of fruit bat</p><p><b>različita vrsta voćnog šišmiša (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of fruit bat</p><p><b>izumrli gmizavac iz Jure i Krede s ptičjim kljunom i membranskim krilima podržanim vrlo dugim četvrtim prstom svakog prednjeg udova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extinct reptile of the Jurassic and Cretaceous having a bird-like beak and membranous wings supported by the very long fourth digit of each forelimb [flying reptile]</p><p><b>izumrli leteći gmizavci: pterosauri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct flying reptiles: pterosaurs [order Pterosauria]</p><p><b>rod tropskih azijskih stabala i grmlja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of tropical Asian trees and shrubs [genus Pterospermum]</p><p><b>Indijsko drvo koje ima mirisne noćne bijele cvijeće i koje daje crvenkasto drvo koje se koristi za planke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Indian tree having fragrant nocturnal white flowers and yielding a reddish wood used for planking [maple-leaved bayur, mayeng]</p><p><b>rod kopnenih orhideja iz Australije i Novog Zelanda i zapadnog Pacifika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of terrestrial orchids of Australia and New Zealand and western Pacific [genus Pterostylis]</p><p><b>vitamin B koji je bitan za rast i reprodukciju stanica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is essential for cell growth and reproduction [folacin, folate, folic acid, pteroylmonoglutamic acid, vitamin Bc, vitamin M]</p><p><b>vitamin B koji je bitan za rast i reprodukciju stanica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is essential for cell growth and reproduction [folacin, folate, folic acid, pteroylglutamic acid, vitamin Bc, vitamin M]</p><p><b>ili dva zgušena trougla sloja spojiva koja se protežu od nosne ivice oka do rožnjače. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two thickened triangular layers of conjunctiva extending from the nasal edge of the eye to the cornea</p><p><b>mišić koji silazi od sfenoidne kosti do donje vilice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> muscle descending from the sphenoid bone to the lower jaw</p><p><b>pleksus vena koji izlijevaju područje pterigodnih mišića i izlijevaju u unutarnje maksilarne i prednje faciale vene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plexus of veins draining the region of the pterygoid muscles and draining into the internal maxillary and anterior facial veins</p><p><b>dva koštana procesa koja silaze iz tijela sfenoidne kosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> two bony processes descending from the body of the sphenoid bone</p><p><b>u obliku pentala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pentails [genus Ptilocercus]</p><p><b>ljiljanke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sea lilies [genus Ptilocrinus]</p><p><b>ptice u pticama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bowerbirds [family Ptilonorhynchidae]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Ptilonorhynchidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Ptilonorhynchidae [genus Ptilonorhynchus]</p><p><b>jugoistočne Australije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of southeast Australia [satin bird, satin bowerbird]</p><p><b>rod Paradisaeidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Paradisaeidae [genus Ptloris]</p><p><b>krastavska crna australska rajska ptica sa zelenim i ljubičastim iridescencijama na glavi i repu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> velvety black Australian bird of paradise with green and purple iridescence on head and tail [riflebird]</p><p><b>uređaj koji prenosi snagu iz motora (kao što je traktor ili drugo motorno vozilo) u drugu opremu (kao što je pumpa ili čekić) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device that transfers power from an engine (as in a tractor or other motor vehicle) to another piece of equipment (as to a pump or jackhammer) [power takeoff]</p><p><b>astronom Ptolemeju ili s njim povezanim, od ili u vezi s geocentričnim Ptolemaijevim sustavom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the astronomer Ptolemy</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the geocentric Ptolemaic system</p><p><b>drevna dinastija makedonskih kraljeva koji su vladali Egiptom od 323. do 30. godine prije Krista. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient dynasty of Macedonian kings who ruled Egypt from 323 BC to 30 BC [Ptolemy]</p><p><b>(Astronomija) Ptolemajev model svemira sa Zemljom u središtu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) Ptolemy's model of the universe with the Earth at the center</p><p><b>Aleksandrijski astronom (2. stoljeća) koji je predložio geocentrični sustav astronomije koji je bio nesporan sve do kasne renesanse, drevna dinastija makedonskih kraljeva koji su vladali Egiptom od 323. do 30. godine prije Krista. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Alexandrian astronomer (of the 2nd century) who proposed a geocentric system of astronomy that was undisputed until the late Renaissance [Claudius Ptolemaeus]</p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient dynasty of Macedonian kings who ruled Egypt from 323 BC to 30 BC [Ptolemaic dynasty]</p><p><b>Egipatski kralj koji je osnovao makedonsku dinastiju u Egiptu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the king of Egypt who founded the Macedonian dynasty in Egypt</p><p><b>sin Ptolemaja I. i egipatski kralj za kojeg se tvrdi da je odgovoran za Septuagintu (oko 309-247 pr. n. e.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> son of Ptolemy I and king of Egypt who was said to be responsible for the Septuagint (circa 309-247 BC)</p><p><b>Svaka od različitih aminova (kao što su putrescin ili kadaverin) formiran od djelovanja bakterija koje se raspadaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various amines (such as putrescine or cadaverine) formed by the action of putrefactive bacteria [ptomaine]</p><p><b>Svaka od različitih aminova (kao što su putrescin ili kadaverin) formiran od djelovanja bakterija koje se raspadaju, termin za trovanje hranom koji više nije u znanstvenoj upotrebi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various amines (such as putrescine or cadaverine) formed by the action of putrefactive bacteria [ptomain]</p><p><i>n.</i> a term for food poisoning that is no longer in scientific use [ptomaine poisoning]</p><p><b>termin za trovanje hranom koji više nije u znanstvenoj upotrebi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a term for food poisoning that is no longer in scientific use [ptomaine]</p><p><b>oblak gornjeg kapka uzrokovan paralizom mišića i slabosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> drooping of the upper eyelid caused by muscle paralysis and weakness</p><p><b>anksiozni poremećaj povezan s ozbiljnim traumatičnim događajima i karakteriziran simptomima kao što su krivnja preživjelaca, ponovljena trauma u snovima, utrnulost i nedostatak uključenosti u stvarnost ili ponavljajuće misli i slike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anxiety disorder associated with serious traumatic events and characterized by such symptoms as survivor guilt, reliving the trauma in dreams, numbness and lack of involvement with reality, or recurrent thoughts and images [posttraumatic stress disorder]</p><p><b>ptijalin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an amylase secreted in saliva</p><p><b>hrakati, hraknuti, hračkati, hračnuti, ispljunuti, ispljuvati, pljunuti, pljuvati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> expel or eject (saliva or phlegm or sputum) from the mouth [ptyalize, spew, spit, spue]</p><p><b>prekomjeran protok pljuvačke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> excessive flow of saliva</p><p><b>kalcijum u pljuvačkoj žlijezdi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> calculus in a salivary gland</p><p><b>hrakati, hraknuti, hračkati, hračnuti, ispljunuti, ispljuvati, pljunuti, pljuvati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> expel or eject (saliva or phlegm or sputum) from the mouth [ptyalise, spew, spit, spue]</p><p><b>Azijske štakorske zmije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asian rat snakes [genus Ptyas]</p><p><b>ulaze u zgrade u potrazi za plijenom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enter buildings in pursuit of prey [Indian rat snake]</p