s</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of removing impurities (as from oil or metals or sugar etc.) [refinement, refining]</p><p><i>n.</i> a ceremonial cleansing from defilement or uncleanness by the performance of appropriate rites [purgation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of purging of sin or guilt</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an apparatus for removing impurities</p><p><b>čistiti, očistiti, oprati, osloboditi se, prečistiti, sprati, destilirati, pročistiti, pročišćavati, pročišćivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> remove impurities from, increase the concentration of, and separate through the process of distillation [distill, make pure, sublimate]</p><p><i>v.</i> make pure or free from sin or guilt [purge, sanctify]</p><p><i>v.</i> become clean or pure or free of guilt and sin</p><p><b>pročišćavnje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to purge or rid of sin [purgatorial, purging]</p><p><i>adj.</i> freeing from noxious matter</p><p><i>adj.</i> acting like an antiseptic [cleansing]</p><p><b>Purim</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a Jewish holy day commemorating their deliverance from massacre by Haman</p><p><b>S druge strane, od:, s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% masenog udjela, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several bases that are derivatives of purine</p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless crystalline organic base containing nitrogen</p><p><b>lijek (trgovinski naziv Purinethol) koji ometa metabolizam purina i koji se koristi za liječenje akutne limfocitne leukemije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug (trade name Purinethol) that interferes with the metabolism of purine and is used to treat acute lymphocytic leukemia [mercaptopurine]</p><p><b>purizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> scrupulous or exaggerated insistence on purity or correctness (especially in language)</p><p><b>netko tko inzistira na velikoj preciznosti i ispravnosti (posebno u korištenju riječi) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who insists on great precision and correctness (especially in the use of words)</p><p><b>član grupe engleskih protestanata koji su u 16. i 17. stoljeću smatrali da je protestantska reformacija pod Elizabetom nedovršena i zagovarali su pojednostavljenje i regulaciju oblika obožavanja, netko tko se drži strogih vjerskih načela, Osoba koja je previše zabrinuta za pristojnost i pristojnost. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a group of English Protestants who in the 16th and 17th centuries thought that the Protestant Reformation under Elizabeth was incomplete and advocated the simplification and regulation of forms of worship</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who adheres to strict religious principles</p><p><i>n.</i> a person excessively concerned about propriety and decorum [prude]</p><p><b>moralno strog i strog (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> morally rigorous and strict [blue, puritanical]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s Puritancima ili Puritanstvom, pretjerano ispravno., moralno strog i strog (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Puritans or Puritanism</p><p><i>adj.</i> exaggeratedly proper [priggish, prim, prissy, prudish, square-toed, straight-laced, straightlaced, strait-laced, straitlaced, tight-laced, victorian]</p><p><i>adj.</i> morally rigorous and strict [blue, puritanic]</p><p><b>Na prudisan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a prudish manner [prudishly]</p><p><b>vjerovanja i prakse karakteristične za puritane (od kojih su većina bili kalvinisti koji su željeli očistiti Englesku crkvu od njenih katoličkih aspekata), strogost i strogost u ponašanju i vjeri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the beliefs and practices characteristic of Puritans (most of whom were Calvinists who wished to purify the Church of England of its Catholic aspects)</p><p><i>n.</i> strictness and austerity in conduct and religion</p><p><b>čednost, čistoća, nevinost, očistiti se, vrlina, žig na uhu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> being undiluted or unmixed with extraneous material [pureness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being unsullied by sin or moral wrong [innocence, pureness, sinlessness, whiteness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a woman's virtue or chastity [honor, honour, pureness]</p><p><b>Boemski fiziolog poznat po otkriću Purkinjevih stanica i Purkinjeove mreže (1787-1869) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Bohemian physiologist remembered for his discovery of Purkinje cells and the Purkinje network (1787-1869) [Jan Evangelista Purkinje, Johannes Evangelista Purkinje]</p><p><b>veliki gusto razgranat neuron koji je karakteristična stanica cerebellarnog korteksa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large densely branching neuron that is the characteristic cell of the cerebellar cortex</p><p><b>specijalno vlakno srčanog mišića koje je dio Purkinje mreže (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialized cardiac muscle fiber that is part of the Purkinje network</p><p><b>mreža Purkinjeovih vlakana koja prenose srčani impuls iz atrioventrikularnog čvora do srčanih komora i uzrokuju ih da se skupe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a network of Purkinje fibers that carry the cardiac impulse from the atrioventricular node to the ventricles of the heart and causes them to contract [Purkinje's system, Purkinje's tissue]</p><p><b>mreža Purkinjeovih vlakana koja prenose srčani impuls iz atrioventrikularnog čvora do srčanih komora i uzrokuju ih da se skupe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a network of Purkinje fibers that carry the cardiac impulse from the atrioventricular node to the ventricles of the heart and causes them to contract [Purkinje's tissue, Purkinje network]</p><p><b>mreža Purkinjeovih vlakana koja prenose srčani impuls iz atrioventrikularnog čvora do srčanih komora i uzrokuju ih da se skupe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a network of Purkinje fibers that carry the cardiac impulse from the atrioventricular node to the ventricles of the heart and causes them to contract [Purkinje's system, Purkinje network]</p><p><b>gajtan, širit, žuborenje, kovitlati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gold or silver wire thread</p><p><i>n.</i> a basic knitting stitch made by putting the needle through the front of the stich from the righthand side [purl stitch]</p><p><i>v.</i> flow in a circular current, of liquids [eddy, swirl, whirl, whirlpool]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a murmuring sound [sough]</p><p><i>v.</i> knit with a purl stitch</p><p><i>v.</i> edge or border with gold or silver embroidery</p><p><i>v.</i> embroider with gold or silver thread</p><p><b>osnovni šav za pletenje napravljen stavljanjem igle kroz prednju stranu šavova s desne strane, Napraviti s purl šavovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a basic knitting stitch made by putting the needle through the front of the stich from the righthand side [purl]</p><p><i>v.</i> make with purl stitches</p><p><b>čestar, ivica, okolina, predgrađe, rub, šikara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an outer adjacent area of any place [environs]</p><p><b>krasti, počiniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make off with belongings of others [abstract, cabbage, filch, hook, lift, nobble, pilfer, pinch, snarf, sneak, swipe]</p><p><b>gušća od riže i piletine i malim divljem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thick stew made of rice and chicken and small game [chicken purloo, poilu]</p><p><b>carski, grimiz, grimizan, grimizna, ljubičast, ljubičasto, purpuran, raskošan, rumenilo, tamnocrven, tamnoljubičasta boja, vrlo lijep, ljubičasta, purpurna, ljubičasta boja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a purple color or pigment [purpleness]</p><p><i>n.</i> (in ancient Rome) position of imperial status [the purple]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) official dress of a cardinal [the purple]</p><p><i>v.</i> become purple</p><p><i>v.</i> color purple [empurple, purpurate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a color intermediate between red and blue [purplish, violet]</p><p><i>adj.</i> excessively elaborate or showily expressed [empurpled, over-embellished]</p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to or befitting a supreme ruler [imperial, majestic, regal, royal]</p><p><b>Visoka, blesava, tropska američka godišnja biljka s dlakavim stabljikama i dugim šiljcima obično crvenih cvijeća iznad lišća duboko crvenog ljubičastog. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall showy tropical American annual having hairy stems and long spikes of usually red flowers above leaves deeply flushed with purple [Amaranthus cruentus, Amaranthus hybridus erythrostachys, Amaranthus hybridus hypochondriacus, gentleman's-cane, prince's-feather, prince's-plume, red amaranth]</p><p><b>malo grmlje sa ljubičastim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrubby tree with purple flowers [Illicium floridanum]</p><p><b>mala hibridna marelica iz Azije i Male Azije s ljubičastom grančicom i bijelim cvijećem nakon čega slijedi inferiorno ljubičasto voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small hybrid apricot of Asia and Asia Minor having purplish twigs and white flowers following by inferior purple fruit [Prunus dasycarpa, black apricot]</p><p><b>Severnoamerička višegodišnja biljka s dlakavim bazalnim pinnatnim listovima i ljubičastim cvijećem i plodovima s vrhom s perjem, Vječna biljka iz sjeverne umjerene zone s pnomskim lišćama i nekoliko cvjetova s smeđom ljubičastim čašicom i narandžastim i ružičastim laticama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American perennial with hairy basal pinnate leaves and purple flowers and plume-tipped fruits [Geum triflorum, prairie smoke]</p><p><i>n.</i> erect perennial of north temperate zone having pinnate leaves and a few nodding flowers with a brown-purple calyx and orange and pink petals [Geum rivale, Indian chocolate, chocolate root, water avens]</p><p><b>B. B. B. B. C. D. C. D. C. D. C. D. C. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D. D (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> free-living Gram-negative pink to purplish-brown bacteria containing bacteriochlorophyll</p><p><b>vrsta europske bukove s blistavim ljubičastim ili bakarnim lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> variety of European beech with shining purple or copper-colored leaves [Fagus purpurea, Fagus sylvatica atropunicea, Fagus sylvatica purpurea, copper beech]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička biljka s okruglim lišćama i krajnjim grmovima cvijeća obaranim ljubičastim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American herb having whorled leaves and terminal clusters of flowers spotted with purple [Eupatorium purpureum, Joe-Pye weed, marsh milkweed, trumpet weed]</p><p><b>Bijeli i lavandasti do blijedo-plavi cvijeće rastu u savršenih prstenova široko raspoređenih traka oko stabljika formirajući neku vrstu pagode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white and lavender to pale-blue flowers grow in perfect rings of widely spaced bands around the stems forming a kind of pagoda [Collinsia bicolor, Collinsia heterophylla, innocense]</p><p><b>planinari sjeveroistočne Sjeverne Amerike koji imaju voskani ljubičasto-plavi cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> climber of northeastern North America having waxy purplish-blue flowers [Clematis verticillaris, mountain clematis, purple virgin's bower]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka s crveno-fijalnim do ružičastom biljkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect to decumbent short-lived perennial having red-purple to pink flowers [Trifolium pratense, red clover]</p><p><b>mala višegodišnja biljka hladnijih područja Sjeverne Amerike s ljubičastim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small perennial herb of cooler regions of North America with racemose purple flowers [Cardamine douglasii]</p><p><b>velika prelijevalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large European butterfly the male of which has wings shaded with purple [Apatura iris]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički pimpek s malinjasto crvenom glavom, grudima i guzicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American finch having a raspberry-red head and breast and rump [Carpodacus purpureus]</p><p><b>Orhideja sjeveroistočne i alpske istočne Sjeverne Amerike, bliska purpurnim orhidejama s frenzijama, ali s ružičastom-fioletskim ili ljubičastim cvijećem s denticulatnim dijelovima lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orchid of northeastern and alpine eastern North America closely related to the purple fringed orchids but having rosy-purple or violet flowers with denticulate leaf divisions [Habenaria peramoena, purple fringeless orchis]</p><p><b>Orhideja sjeveroistočne i alpske istočne Sjeverne Amerike, bliska purpurnim orhidejama s frenzijama, ali s ružičastom-fioletskim ili ljubičastim cvijećem s denticulatnim dijelovima lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orchid of northeastern and alpine eastern North America closely related to the purple fringed orchids but having rosy-purple or violet flowers with denticulate leaf divisions [Habenaria peramoena, purple fringeless orchid]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je to potrebno za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gallinules with showy purplish plumage</p><p><b>Istočni SAD-u grackle (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> eastern United States grackle [Quiscalus quiscula]</p><p><b>marakuja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Brazilian passionflower cultivated for its deep purple fruit [Passiflora edulis, granadilla]</p><p><b>Meksikanski godišnji plod naturaliziran u istočnoj Sjevernoj Americi s žutom do ljubičastim jestivim plodovima sličnim malim paradajzom, godišnji od tropske Južne Amerike s jestivim ljubičastim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mexican annual naturalized in eastern North America having yellow to purple edible fruit resembling small tomatoes [Physalis philadelphica, jamberry, miltomate, tomatillo]</p><p><i>n.</i> annual of tropical South America having edible purple fruits [Physalis peruviana, cape gooseberry]</p><p><b>američki vojni odlikovanje dodijeljeno svakom članu oružanih snaga koji je ranjen u akciji, Barbiturat dugotrajnog djelovanja koji se koristi kao sedativ (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a United States military decoration awarded to any member of the armed forces who is wounded in action [Order of the Purple Heart]</p><p><i>n.</i> a long-acting barbiturate used as a sedative [Luminal, phenobarbital, phenobarbitone, sodium thiopental]</p><p><b>poluprostrata zimzelena biljka iz zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> semi-prostrate evergreen herb of western United States [Brewer's mountain heather, Phyllodoce breweri]</p><p><b>u obliku od šipke ili od šipke do bijelog boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tufted locoweed of southwestern United States having purple or pink to white flowers [Oxytropis lambertii, purple locoweed]</p><p><b>u obliku od šipke ili od šipke do bijelog boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tufted locoweed of southwestern United States having purple or pink to white flowers [Oxytropis lambertii, purple loco]</p><p><b>močvarna biljka s dugim šiljakom ljubičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marsh herb with a long spike of purple flowers [Lythrum salicaria, spiked loosestrife]</p><p><b>Veliki sjevernoamerički martin od kojih je mužjak plavo-crni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large North American martin of which the male is blue-black [Progne subis]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka iz južne i zapadne Europe s gustim rascem purpurnih ili ljubičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of southern and western Europe having dense racemes of purple or violet flowers [Astragalus danicus]</p><p><b>Eurasijski mulin s blesavim ljubičastim ili ružičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian mullein with showy purple or pink flowers [Verbascum phoeniceum]</p><p><b>Noćni šum s srebrnim lišćem i ljubičastim ili plavim ili bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> weedy nightshade with silvery foliage and violet or blue or white flowers [Solanum elaeagnifolium, prairie berry, silver-leaved nettle, silver-leaved nightshade, silverleaf nightshade, trompillo, white horse nettle]</p><p><b>s masnim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flat mild onion having purplish tunics [red onion]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička orhideja s vrhom ljubičastog ljubičastog cvijeća pomiješanog s bijelim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American orchid having a spike of violet-purple flowers mixed with white [Orchis spectabilis, purple-hooded orchis, showy orchis]</p><p><b>Eurasijski šareni šareni s crvenkastim ili ljubičastim granama i kore bogate taninom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian osier having reddish or purple twigs and bark rich in tannin [Salix purpurea, basket willow, purple willow, red osier, red willow]</p><p><b>Prolaz pun ukrašenih i cvjetnih riječi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a passage full of ornate and flowery language</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko atraktivnih zimzelenih grmova u Australiji koji rastu zbog svojih blistavih dubokozelenih listova i cvijeća u bogatom plavom i intenzivnim ljubičastim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several attractive evergreen shrubs of Australia grown for their glossy deep green foliage and flowers in rich blues and intense violets [hovea]</p><p><b>dlakava višegodišnja biljka iz središnje SAD-a s okruglim duboko uštogljenim lištima i labavim panicama velikih crvenokrasno-fijalnih ili trešnjevih crvenih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hairy perennial of central United States having round deeply lobed leaves and loose panicles of large crimson-purple or cherry-red flowers [Callirhoe involucrata]</p><p><b>vrlo kratka plitko puzeća sjevernoamerička paprika koja obično raste na liticama ili zidovima i ima tamno blistave lisne sjekire (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very short shallowly creeping North American fern usually growing on cliffs or walls and having dark glossy leaf axes [Pellaea atropurpurea]</p><p><b>srebrno-listovita kalifornijska biljka s ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> silvery-leaved California herb with purple flowers [Salvia leucophylla, chaparral sage]</p><p><b>sanikle sjeverozapadne Sjedinjene Države i Britanske Kolumbije s žutim ili crvenim ili ljubičastim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sanicle of northwestern United States and British Columbia having yellow or red or purple flowers [Sanicula bipinnatifida]</p><p><b>biljke koje formiraju gust jastuk s svijetlom crvenkasto-lavandurnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plants forming dense cushions with bright reddish-lavender flowers [Saxifraga oppositifolia]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s ružičastom-fijazmalom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of eastern North America having pink-purple flowers [Asclepias purpurascens]</p><p><b>malo tropsko grmlje koje daje tamno crveno ovalno voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small tropical shrubby tree bearing deep red oval fruit [Psidium cattleianum, Psidium littorale longipes, cattley guava]</p><p><b>Trillium iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike koji ima loše mirisnu ružičasta do ljubičasta cvijeća i adstringentni korijen koji se koristi u narodnoj medicini posebno za olakšavanje porođaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trillium of eastern North America having malodorous pink to purple flowers and an astringent root used in folk medicine especially to ease childbirth [Trillium erectum, birthroot, red trillium]</p><p><b>Javanska biljka koja se uzgaja zbog svojih lijepih baršunastih listova s ljubičastom dlakom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Javanese foliage plant grown for their handsome velvety leaves with violet-purple hairs [Gynura aurantiaca, royal velvet plant, velvet plant]</p><p><b>planinari sjeveroistočne Sjeverne Amerike koji imaju voskani ljubičasto-plavi cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> climber of northeastern North America having waxy purplish-blue flowers [Clematis verticillaris, mountain clematis, purple clematis]</p><p><b>Eurasijski šareni šareni s crvenkastim ili ljubičastim granama i kore bogate taninom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian osier having reddish or purple twigs and bark rich in tannin [Salix purpurea, basket willow, purple osier, red osier, red willow]</p><p><b>crno obojeno ljubičastim. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of black tinged with purple [purplish-black]</p><p><b>od plave boje s ljubičastim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of blue tinged with purple [purplish-blue]</p><p><b>od crne boje, odbojene ljubičastom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of brown tinged with purple [purplish-brown]</p><p><b>s ljubičastim očnim znakom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of flowers) having a purple eyelike marking</p><p><b>s ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having purple flowers</p><p><b>Škrobna maljina istočne Sjeverne Amerike s blesavim cvjetovima od ruže do ljubičaste boje i crvenim ili narandžastim plodovima u obliku prstića (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby raspberry of eastern North America having showy rose to purplish flowers and red or orange thimble-shaped fruit [Rubus odoratus, flowering raspberry, thimbleberry]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička orhideja s grmovima mirisnih ljubičastih cvjetova s frendovima, Sjevernoamerička orhideja slična Habenaria psycodes s većim, bližijim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American orchid with clusters of fragrant purple fringed flowers [Habenaria psycodes, purple-fringed orchis]</p><p><i>n.</i> North American orchid similar to Habenaria psycodes with larger paler flowers [Habenaria fimbriata, purple-fringed orchis]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička orhideja s grmovima mirisnih ljubičastih cvjetova s frendovima, Sjevernoamerička orhideja slična Habenaria psycodes s većim, bližijim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American orchid with clusters of fragrant purple fringed flowers [Habenaria psycodes, purple-fringed orchid]</p><p><i>n.</i> North American orchid similar to Habenaria psycodes with larger paler flowers [Habenaria fimbriata, purple-fringed orchid]</p><p><b>od zelene boje, obojene ljubičastim. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of green tinged with purple [purplish-green]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička orhideja s vrhom ljubičastog ljubičastog cvijeća pomiješanog s bijelim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American orchid having a spike of violet-purple flowers mixed with white [Orchis spectabilis, purple orchis, showy orchis]</p><p><b>od lavande obojene ljubičastim (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of lavender tinged with purple [purplish-lilac]</p><p><b>od crvene boje s ljubičastim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of red tinged with purple [purpli