ting to Pythagoras or his geometry</p><p><b>Pitija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the priestess of Apollo at Delphi who transmitted the oracles [Pythoness]</p><p><b>Gljive s sporangia obično se nose uzastopno i pojedinačno na vrhovima razgranatih sporangiofora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungi having sporangia usually borne successively and singly at the tips of branching sporangiophores [family Pythiaceae]</p><p><b>Pitijske igre</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ancient Panhellenic celebration at Delphi held every four years in the third year of the Olympiad in honor of Apollo</p><p><b>Pitija (od &quot;pythia&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> friend of Damon [Phintias]</p><p><b>bilo koje gljivice iz roda Pythium (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any fungus of the genus Pythium</p><p><b>gljivice koje uzrokuju umanjkivanje bolesti u sadnicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungus causing damping off disease in seedlings [damping off fungus]</p><p><b>epitet za Apolona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> epithet for Apollo</p><p><b>piton, piton (zmija), udav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large Old World boas</p><p><i>n.</i> a soothsaying spirit or a person who is possessed by such a spirit</p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) dragon killed by Apollo at Delphi</p><p><b>vrlo veliki piton iz jugoistočne Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very large python of southeast Asia [Indian python]</p><p><b>Jugoistočne Azije i Istočne Indije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of southeast Asia and East Indies [reticulated python]</p><p><b>vrlo veliki piton iz tropske i južne Afrike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very large python of tropical and southern Africa [rock python, rock snake]</p><p><b>Australski piton s raznovrsnim uzorkom na leđima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian python with a variegated pattern on its back [Morelia spilotes variegatus, carpet snake]</p><p><b>Pitija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a witch with powers of divination</p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the priestess of Apollo at Delphi who transmitted the oracles [Pythia]</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama obitelj odvojena od Boidae koja obuhvaća Boas Starog svijeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications a family separate from Boidae comprising Old World boas [family Pythonidae]</p><p><b>Boe Starog svijeta: pitoni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World boas: pythons [subfamily Pythoninae]</p><p><b>prisutnost bijelih krvnih stanica u urinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> presence of white blood cells in the urine</p><p><b>ciborij, kutija u državnoj kovnici novca s novokovanim prim, monstranca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chest in which coins from the mint are held to await assay [pix, pix chest, pyx chest]</p><p><i>n.</i> any receptacle in which wafers for the Eucharist are kept [pix]</p><p><b>Sanduk u kojem se čuvaju novčići iz kovnice dok se ne testiraju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chest in which coins from the mint are held to await assay [pix, pix chest, pyx]</p><p><b>jedna vrsta: pixie (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one species: pyxie [genus Pyxidanthera]</p><p><b>u obliku zvijezde, s crvenim i bijelom bojom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creeping evergreen shrub having narrow overlapping leaves and early white star-shaped flowers [pixie, pixy, pyxie]</p><p><b>plodovi biljaka kao što je bananin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fruit of such plants as the plantain [pyxis]</p><p><b>u obliku zvijezde, s crvenim i bijelom bojom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creeping evergreen shrub having narrow overlapping leaves and early white star-shaped flowers [Pyxidanthera barbulata, pixie, pixy]</p><p><b>Kompas</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fruit of such plants as the plantain [pyxidium]</p><p><i>n.</i> a constellation in the southern hemisphere near Puppis and Antlia</p><p><i>n.</i> a small box used by ancient Greeks to hold medicines</p><p><b>q</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the 17th letter of the Roman alphabet</p><p><b>akutna bolest slična gripi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute disease resembling influenza</p><p><b>ezoterična ili okultna materija slična Kabali koja je tradicionalno tajna. (MT)</b></p><p><