m ljuskama na obali Atlantskog mora, jedljiva američka školjka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Atlantic coast round clams with hard shells [hard-shell clam, quahog, round clam]</p><p><i>n.</i> an edible American clam [Mercenaria mercenaria, Venus mercenaria, hard-shell clam, hard clam, quahog, round clam]</p><p><b>Okrugle školjke s tvrdim ljuskama na obali Atlantskog mora, jedljiva američka školjka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Atlantic coast round clams with hard shells [hard-shell clam, quahaug, round clam]</p><p><i>n.</i> an edible American clam [Mercenaria mercenaria, Venus mercenaria, hard-shell clam, hard clam, quahaug, round clam]</p><p><b>Ulica u Parizu duž južne obale Seine poznata po vladinim ministarstvima., Francuski ministar vanjskih poslova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the street in Paris along the south bank of the Seine known for its governmental ministries</p><p><i>n.</i> the French department in charge of foreign affairs [French Foreign Office]</p><p><b>prepelica, strepiti, uplašiti se, ustrašiti, ustuknuti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flesh of quail</p><p><i>n.</i> small gallinaceous game birds</p><p><i>v.</i> draw back, as with fear or pain [cringe, flinch, funk, recoil, shrink, squinch, wince]</p><p><b>predosjećati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> anticipate with dread or anxiety [apprehend]</p><p><b>trnasti grm s srebrno-krastavim lišćama alkalnih ravnica jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spiny shrub with silvery-scurfy foliage of alkaline plains of southwestern United States and Mexico [Atriplex lentiformis, quail bush, white thistle]</p><p><b>trnasti grm s srebrno-krastavim lišćama alkalnih ravnica jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spiny shrub with silvery-scurfy foliage of alkaline plains of southwestern United States and Mexico [Atriplex lentiformis, quail brush, white thistle]</p><p><b>čudan, izvanredan, neobičan, staromodan, zabavan, neprikladan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> strange in an interesting or pleasing way</p><p><i>adj.</i> very strange or unusual</p><p><i>adj.</i> attractively old-fashioned (but not necessarily authentic) [old-time, olde worlde]</p><p><b>čudan, izvanredan, neobičan, staromodan, zabavan, neprikladan (od &quot;quaint&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a strange but not unpleasant manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a quaint old-fashioned manner</p><p><b>dopadljivost, nastranost, staromodnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being quaint and old-fashioned</p><p><i>n.</i> strangeness as a consequence of being old fashioned</p><p><b>drhtanje, drhtavica, potres, tresti se, zemljotres</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shaking and vibration at the surface of the earth resulting from underground movement along a fault plane or from volcanic activity [earthquake, seism, temblor]</p><p><i>v.</i> shake with fast, tremulous movements [palpitate, quiver]</p><p><i>v.</i> shake with seismic vibrations [tremor]</p><p><b>kveker, protestant</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Religious Society of Friends founded by George Fox (the Friends have never called themselves Quakers) [Friend]</p><p><i>n.</i> one who quakes and trembles with (or as with) fear [trembler]</p><p><b>puška ili artiljerijski komad napravljen od drveta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dummy gun or piece of artillery made usually of wood</p><p><b>Teološka doktrina Društva prijatelja karakterizirana protivljenjem ratu i odbijanjem rituala i formalnog vjerovanja i redovnog služenja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the theological doctrine of the Society of Friends characterized by opposition to war and rejection of ritual and a formal creed and an ordained ministry</p><p><b>kveker, protestant (od &quot;quaker&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Christian sect founded by George Fox about 1660 [Religious Society of Friends, Society of Friends]</p><p><b>Vježnjak iz Starog svijeta s širokom, mnogo-ogrančanom krunom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World aspen with a broad much-branched crown [European quaking aspen, Populus tremula]</p><p><b>kvalifikacija, ograničenje, osposobljavanje, osposobljenost, predtakmičenje, pripadnost, svojstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an attribute that must be met or complied with and that fits a person for something [making]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of modifying or changing the strength of some idea</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement that limits or restricts some claim [reservation]</p><p><b>kvalificiran, kvalificirani, kvalificiranim, osposobljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> meeting the proper standards and requirements and training for an office or position or task</p><p><i>adj.</i> limited or restricted</p><p><i>adj.</i> holding appropriate documentation and officially on record as qualified to perform a specified function or practice a specified skill [certified]</p><p><i>adj.</i> restricted in meaning [restricted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> contingent on something else [dependant, dependent]</p><p><b>označni podatak, dopuna, modifikator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a contestant who meets certain requirements and so qualifies to take part in the next stage of competition</p><p><i>n.</i> a content word that qualifies the meaning of a noun or verb [modifier]</p><p><b>kvalificirati, kvalificirati se, odrediti, osposobiti, označiti, pobliže, razblažiti, razvodniti, karakterizirati, ocrtati, ocrtavati, okarakterizirati, opisati, opisivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> prove capable or fit [measure up]</p><p><i>v.</i> pronounce fit or able</p><p><i>v.</i> make more specific</p><p><i>v.</i> make fit or prepared [dispose]</p><p><i>v.</i> specify as a condition or requirement in a contract or agreement [condition, specify, stipulate]</p><p><i>v.</i> describe or portray the character or the qualities or peculiarities of [characterise, characterize]</p><p><i>v.</i> add a modifier to a constituent [modify]</p><p><b>prolaz, uspjeh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the grammatical relation that exists when a word qualifies the meaning of the phrase [limiting, modification]</p><p><i>n.</i> success in satisfying a test or requirement [pass, passing]</p><p><b>opisni pridjev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an adjective that ascribes to its noun the value of an attribute of that noun (e.g., `a nervous person' or `a musical speaking voice') [descriptive adjective]</p><p><b>kvalitativan, kvalitativna</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving distinctions based on qualities</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or involving comparisons based on qualities</p><p><b>kvalitativna analiza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of decomposing a substance into its constituent elements [chemical analysis]</p><p><b>kvalitativno, kvalitativnost</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a qualitative manner</p><p><b>kakvoća, količina, kvaliteta, kvalitetan, osobina, sposobnost, vrsnoća, bioraznolikost, kvalitativnih, kvalitet, kvalitete, kvaliteti, kvalitetni, kvalitetno, kvalitetu, karakteristika, ton</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an essential and distinguishing attribute of something or someone</p><p><i>n.</i> a degree or grade of excellence or worth [caliber, calibre]</p><p><i>n.</i> a characteristic property that defines the apparent individual nature of something [character, lineament]</p><p><i>n.</i> (music) the distinctive property of a complex sound (a voice or noise or musical sound) [timber, timbre, tone]</p><p><i>n.</i> high social status</p><p><i>adj.</i> of superior grade [choice, prime, prize, select]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of high social status</p><p><b>kontrola kvalitete, mehanizmi kontrole kvalitete, provjera kakvoće, provjera kvalitete</b></p><p><i>n.</i> maintenance of standards of quality of manufactured goods</p><p><b>kakvoća življenja, kakvoća života, kvaliteta življenja, kvaliteta života</b></p><p><i>n.</i> your personal satisfaction (or dissatisfaction) with the cultural or intellectual conditions under which you live (as distinct from material comfort)</p><p><b>klonulost, mučnina, mučnost, neodlučnost, potištenost, sumnje, utučenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> uneasiness about the fitness of an action [misgiving, scruple]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mild state of nausea [queasiness, squeamishness]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko biljaka rodova Camassia (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several plants of the genus Camassia [camas, camash, camass, camosh]</p><p><b>rod škapoznih biljaka iz Sjeverne i Južne Amerike s velikim jestivim lukama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of scapose herbs of North and South America having large edible bulbs [Camassia, genus Camassia, genus Quamassia]</p><p><b>tropska američka godišnja planinara s crvenim (ponekad bijelim) cvijećima i fino raskomadanim lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American annual climber having red (sometimes white) flowers and finely dissected leaves [Indian pink, Ipomoea quamoclit, cypress vine, star-glory]</p><p><b>Australsko stablo s jestivim mesom i jestivim sjemenom nalik orašastima, crveno australsko voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree with edible flesh and edible nutlike seed [Eucarya acuminata, Fusanus acuminatus, quandong, quandong tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> red Australian fruit [native peach, quandong, quantong]</p><p><b>neprilika, nezgodan položaj, dilema</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a situation from which extrication is difficult especially an unpleasant or trying one [plight, predicament]</p><p><i>n.</i> state of uncertainty or perplexity especially as requiring a choice between equally unfavorable options [dilemma]</p><p><b>Australsko stablo s jestivim mesom i jestivim sjemenom nalik orašastima, plodove Brisbane quandong drveta., Australsko stablo s tvrdim bijelim drvetom i sjajnim zelenim lišćama s bijelim cvijećem, a zatim s jednosemnim sjajnim plavim plodovima, crveno australsko voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree with edible flesh and edible nutlike seed [Eucarya acuminata, Fusanus acuminatus, quandang, quandong tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> the fruit of the Brisbane quandong tree [blue fig]</p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree having hard white timber and glossy green leaves with white flowers followed by one-seeded glossy blue fruit [Brisbane quandong, Elaeocarpus grandis, blue fig, quandong tree, silver quandong tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> red Australian fruit [native peach, quandang, quantong]</p><p><b>jestivo sjeme voća quandong-a nalik orašastima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> edible nutlike seed of the quandong fruit</p><p><b>Australsko stablo s jestivim mesom i jestivim sjemenom nalik orašastima, Australsko stablo s tvrdim bijelim drvetom i sjajnim zelenim lišćama s bijelim cvijećem, a zatim s jednosemnim sjajnim plavim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree with edible flesh and edible nutlike seed [Eucarya acuminata, Fusanus acuminatus, quandang, quandong]</p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree having hard white timber and glossy green leaves with white flowers followed by one-seeded glossy blue fruit [Brisbane quandong, Elaeocarpus grandis, blue fig, quandong, silver quandong tree]</p><p><b>Kvasis nevladina organizacija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a quasi nongovernmental organization [quasi-NGO]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s kvantom ili sposobne postojati u samo jednom od dva stanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a quantum or capable of existing in only one of two states [quantized]</p><p><b>homogeni polinom koji ima najmanje dvije varijable (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a homogeneous polynomial having at least two variables</p><p><b>brojivost, mjerljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being measurable [measurability]</p><p><b>mjerljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being quantified</p><p><b>mjerljivost, određivanje količine</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a limitation imposed on the variables of a proposition (as by the quantifiers `some' or `all' or `no')</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of discovering or expressing the quantity of something</p><p><b>kvantifikator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (logic) a word (such as `some' or `all' or `no') that binds the variables in a logical proposition [logical quantifier]</p><p><i>n.</i> (grammar) a word that expresses a quantity (as `fifteen' or `many')</p><p><b>kvantificirati, odrediti opseg, brojiti, izbrojiti, mjeriti, pobrojati, prebrojavati, prebrojiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> use as a quantifier</p><p><i>v.</i> express as a number or measure or quantity [measure]</p><p><b>Čin dijeljenja na kvantne ili izražavanja u smislu kvantne teorije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of dividing into quanta or expressing in terms of quantum theory [quantization]</p><p><b>Približanje (signal koji se kontinuirano mijenja u amplitudi) od strane signala čija je amplituda ograničena na propisan skup diskretnih vrijednosti, primjenjivati kvantnu teoriju na (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> approximate (a signal varying continuously in amplitude) by one whose amplitude is restricted to a prescribed set of discrete values [quantize]</p><p><i>v.</i> apply quantum theory to [quantize]</p><p><b>količinski, kvantitativan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> expressible as a quantity or relating to or susceptible of measurement</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to the measurement of quantity</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of verse) having a metric system based on relative duration of syllables</p><p><b>analiza temeljena na brojčanim podacima, kvantitativna analiza, analiza temeljena na podatcima</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chemical analysis to determine the amounts of each element in the substance [quantitative chemical analysis]</p><p><b>kemijska analiza za određivanje količine svakog elementa u tvari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chemical analysis to determine the amounts of each element in the substance [quantitative analysis]</p><p><b>kvantitavna relacija, odnos magnituda, odnos veličina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relation between magnitudes [magnitude relation]</p><p><b>kvantitativan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a quantitative manner</p><p><b>količina, kvantitet, kvantiteta, kvantiteti, množina, veličina, velika količina, iznos, mjera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> how much there is or how many there are of something that you can quantify [amount, measure]</p><p><i>n.</i> an adequate or large amount</p><p><i>n.</i> the concept that something has a magnitude and can be represented in mathematical expressions by a constant or a variable</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, "elektrana" znači električna energija koja se upotrebljava za proizvodnju električne energije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measure of the quantity of electricity (determined by the amount of an electric current and the time for which it flows) [charge unit]</p><p><b>diskretizacija kontinuirane veličine, kvantizacija, prikaz analogne veličine konačnim brojem diskretni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of dividing into quanta or expressing in terms of quantum theory [quantisation]</p><p><b>kvantiziranje</b></p><p><i>v.</i> approximate (a signal varying continuously in amplitude) by one whose amplitude is restricted to a prescribed set of discrete values [quantise]</p><p><i>v.</i> apply quantum theory to [quantise]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s kvantom ili sposobne postojati u samo jednom od dva stanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a quantum or capable of existing in only one of two states [quantal]</p><p><b>crveno australsko voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> red Australian fruit [native peach, quandang, quandong]</p><p><b>kvant, kvantna, kvantni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a discrete amount of something that is analogous to the quantities in quantum theory</p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the smallest discrete quantity of some physical property that a system can possess (according to quantum theory)</p><p><b>teorija snažnih interakcija između elementarnih čestica (uključujući interakciju koja veže protone i neutrone u jezgri) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a theory of strong interactions between elementary particles (including the interaction that binds protons and neutrons in the nucleus) [QCD]</p><p><b>relativistička kvantna teorija elektromagnetnih interakcija fotona i elektrona i miona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relativistic quantum theory of the electromagnetic interactions of photons and electrons and muons [QED]</p><p><b>kvantna teorija polja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of quantum physics that is concerned with the theory of fields</p><p><b>(fizička) nagli prijelaz elektrona ili atoma ili molekula iz jednog kvantnog stanja u drugo s emisijom ili apsorpcijom kvantnog stanja, iznenada veliki porast ili napredak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) an abrupt transition of an electron or atom or molecule from one quantum state to another with the emission or absorption of a quantum</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden large increase or advance [quantum leap]</p><p><b>iznenada veliki porast ili napredak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden large increase or advance [quantum jump]</p><p><b>kvantna mehanika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of quantum physics that accounts for matter at the atomic level</p><p><b>kvantna fizika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of physics based on quantum theory</p><p><b>kvantna teorija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a physical theory that certain properties occur only in discrete amounts (quanta)</p><p><b>planetoid otkriven 2002. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a planetoid discovered in 2002</p><p><b>član Siouan naroda doline rijeke Arkansas u Arkansasu, Dialekt Dhegiha kojim govore Quapawovi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Siouan people of the Arkansas river valley in Arkansas</p><p><i>n.</i> the Dhegiha dialect spoken by the Quapaw</p><p><b>izolacija, karantena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enforced isolation of patients suffering from a contagious disease in order to prevent the spread of disease</p><p><i>n.</i> isolation to prevent the spread of infectious disease</p><p><i>v.</i> place into enforced isolation, as for medical reasons</p><p><b>pod prisilnom izolacijom, posebno iz zdravstvenih razloga (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> under forced isolation especially for health reasons [isolated]</p><p><b>kvark</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) hypothetical truly fundamental particle in mesons and baryons</p><p><i>n.</i> fresh unripened cheese of a smooth texture made from pasteurized milk, a starter, and rennet [quark cheese]</p><p>