pire [Kechua]</p><p><i>n.</i> a community of South American Indians in Peru who were formerly the ruling class of the Incan Empire [Kechua]</p><p><i>n.</i> the language of the Quechua which was spoken by the Incas [Kechua, Kechuan, Quechuan, Quechuan language]</p><p><b>jezik Quechua koji su govorili Inci, od ili u vezi s Quechua ili njihov jezik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the language of the Quechua which was spoken by the Incas [Kechua, Kechuan, Quechua, Quechuan language]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Quechua or their language [Kechuan]</p><p><b>jezik Quechua koji su govorili Inci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the language of the Quechua which was spoken by the Incas [Kechua, Kechuan, Quechua, Quechuan]</p><p><b>test za utvrđivanje postoji li blokada kralježničnog kanala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a test to determine whether there is a blockage of the spinal canal</p><p><b>carica, dama, kraljevati, kraljica, kraljica matica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the only fertile female in a colony of social insects such as bees and ants and termites</p><p><i>n.</i> a female sovereign ruler [female monarch, queen regnant]</p><p><i>n.</i> the wife or widow of a king</p><p><i>n.</i> something personified as a woman who is considered the best or most important of her kind</p><p><i>n.</i> a competitor who holds a preeminent position [king, world-beater]</p><p><i>n.</i> offensive term for a homosexual man [fag, faggot, fagot, fairy, nance, pansy, poof, poove, pouf, queer]</p><p><i>n.</i> one of four face cards in a deck bearing a picture of a queen</p><p><i>n.</i> (chess) the most powerful piece</p><p><i>n.</i> an especially large mole rat and the only member of a colony of naked mole rats to bear offspring which are sired by only a few males [queen mole rat]</p><p><i>n.</i> female cat [tabby]</p><p><i>v.</i> promote to a queen, as of a pawn in chess</p><p><i>v.</i> become a queen</p><p><b>Daucus carota, divlja mrkva, divlji korijen, merlin, žuta mrkva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a widely natura