sch, Ragnar Frisch]</p><p><b>Norveški ekonomist poznat po svom radu u ekonometriji (1895-1973) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Norwegian economist noted for his work in econometrics (1895-1973) [Frisch, Ragnar Anton Kittil Frisch]</p><p><b>mit o konačnom uništenju bogova u borbi protiv zla. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> myth about the ultimate destruction of the gods in a battle with evil [Gotterdammerung, Twilight of the Gods]</p><p><b>dobro začinjeni gulaš od mesa i povrća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> well-seasoned stew of meat and vegetables</p><p><b>osoba koja ne zna kako se živiti, a uzima krpe iz kantu za smeće i odlagališta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unskilled person who picks up rags from trash cans and public dumps as a means of livelihood</p><p><b>oblik infekcije antraksom dobivene udisanjem prašine koja sadrži Bacillus anthracis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of anthrax infection acquired by inhalation of dust containing Bacillus anthracis [anthrax pneumonia, inhalation anthrax, pulmonary anthrax, ragsorter's disease, woolsorter's disease, woolsorter's pneumonia]</p><p><b>radnik koji razvrstava krpe i staru odjeću za nove namjene (kao u proizvodnji papira) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a worker who sorts rags and old clothing for new uses (as in papermaking)</p><p><b>oblik infekcije antraksom dobivene udisanjem prašine koja sadrži Bacillus anthracis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of anthrax infection acquired by inhalation of dust containing Bacillus anthracis [anthrax pneumonia, inhalation anthrax, pulmonary anthrax, ragpicker's disease, woolsorter's disease, woolsorter's pneumonia]</p><p><b>ološ, rulja, gomila, običan puk, svjetina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> disparaging terms for the common people [rabble, ragtag and bobtail, riffraff]</p><p><b>gomila, običan puk, rulja, svjetina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> disparaging terms for the common people [rabble, ragtag, riffraff]</p><p><b>crnački ritam, ragtime</b></p><p><i>n.</i> music with a syncopated melody (usually for the piano) [rag]<