afstalks that yield a refreshing drink of clear watery sap [ravenala, traveler's tree, traveller's tree]</p><p><b>gavran, gavrani, otimati, pljačkati, pohlepan, proždrljiv, vrana, vrebati plijen (od &quot;raven&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> living by preying on other animals especially by catching living prey [predatory, rapacious, raptorial, vulturine, vulturous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> excessively greedy and grasping [rapacious, voracious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> devouring or craving food in great quantities [edacious, esurient, rapacious, ravenous, voracious, wolfish]</p><p><b>Ravenna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a battle between the French and an alliance of Spaniards and Swiss and Venetians in 1512 [Battle of Ravenna]</p><p><b>Trava često uzgajana zbog svojih dugih bijela ribastih lišća i velikih perja koji liče na travu pampe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grass often cultivated for its long white-ribbed leaves and large plumes resembling those of pampas grass [Erianthus ravennae, wool grass]</p><p><b>gladan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> extremely hungry [esurient, famished, sharp-set, starved]</p><p><i>adj.</i> devouring or craving food in great quantities [edacious, esurient, rapacious, ravening, voracious, wolfish]</p><p><b>gladan (od &quot;ravenous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in the manner of someone who is very hungry [hungrily]</p><p><b>gladan (od &quot;ravenous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> excessive desire to eat [edacity, esurience, voraciousness, voracity]</p><p><b>bučati, buncati, govoriti, mahnitati, rave, urlati, zaneseno govoriti (od &quot;rave&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a participant in a rave dancing party</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who rants and raves [ranter]</p><p><b>Indijski sitarista koji je popularizirao klasičnu indijsku glazbu na Zapadu (rođen 1920.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Indian sitar player who popularized classical Indian music in the West (born in 1920) [Shankar]</p><p><b>Slijedeći proizvodi: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> veloute sauce seasoned with chopped chervil, chives, t