n.</i> the business of selling real estate</p><p><b>stvarno vrijeme</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to computer systems that update information at the same rate they receive information</p><p><b>obrada podataka dovoljno brzo da se može pratiti vanjski proces (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> data processing fast enough to keep up with an outside process [real-time processing]</p><p><b>obrada podataka dovoljno brzo da se može pratiti vanjski proces (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> data processing fast enough to keep up with an outside process [real-time operation]</p><p><b>rijetki mekani narandžasti mineral koji se sastoji od arsen-sulfida (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rare soft orange mineral consisting of arsenic sulphide</p><p><b>prestrojiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> align anew or better [realine]</p><p><b>Izravno ili bolje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> align anew or better [realign]</p><p><b>ostvarenje, realizacija, realiziranje, izvršenje, ostvarivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musical composition that has been completed or enriched by someone other than the composer [realization]</p><p><i>n.</i> coming to understand something clearly and distinctly [realization, recognition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sale in order to obtain money (as a sale of stock or a sale of the estate of a bankrupt person) or the money so obtained [realization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the completion or enrichment of a piece of music left sparsely notated by a composer [realization]</p><p><i>n.</i> making real or giving the appearance of reality [actualisation, actualization, realization]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that is made real or concrete [fruition, realization]</p><p><b>izvoditi, ostvariti, realizirati, doznati, prepoznati, prepoznavati, saznati, shvatiti, shvaćati, spoznati, spoznavati, znati, poimati, pojmiti, razumijevati, razumjeti, uvidjeti, uviđati, vidjeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> earn on some commercial or business transaction [bring in, clear, earn, gain, make, pull in, realize, take in]</p><p><i>v.</i> convert into cash [realize]</p><p><i>v.</i> expand or complete (a part in a piece of baroque music) by supplying the harmonies indicated in the figured bass [realize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make real or concrete [actualise, actualize, realize, substantiate]</p><p><i>v.</i> be fully aware or cognizant of [agnise, agnize, realize, recognise, recognize]</p><p><i>v.</i> perceive (an idea or situation) mentally [realize, see, understand]</p><p><b>ostvaren, ostvarena, ostvareno, ostvarenu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> successfully completed or brought to an end [accomplished, completed, realized]</p><p><b>realizam, stvarnost, pragmatizam, platonizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the attribute of accepting the facts of life and favoring practicality and literal truth [pragmatism]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being actual or real [reality, realness]</p><p><i>n.</i> (philosophy) the philosophical doctrine that physical objects continue to exist when not perceived [naive realism]</p><p><i>n.</i> an artistic movement in 19th century France [naturalism]</p><p><i>n.</i> (philosophy) the philosophical doctrine that abstract concepts exist independent of their names [Platonism]</p><p><b>realan, realist, realistički, stvaran</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a philosopher who believes that universals are real and exist independently of anyone thinking of them</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who accepts the world as it literally is and deals with it accordingly</p><p><i>n.</i> a painter who represents the world realistically and not in an idealized or romantic style</p><p><b>istinit, realan, realističan, realistički, stvaran, realističnih, stvarna</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> aware or expressing awareness of things as they really are</p><p><i>adj.</i> representing what is real [naturalistic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the philosophical doctrine of realism</p><p><b>na realističan način (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a realistic manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a realistic manner</p><p><b>istinitost, realnost, stvarnost, zbilja, zbiljom, svijet</b></p><p