egation]</p><p><b>delegiranje, dodjela dužnosti, dodjela ovlasti, ovlaštenje, ovlašćivanje, prenošenje ovlasti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> authorizing subordinates to make certain decisions [delegating, delegation, deputation, relegating]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of assigning (someone or something) to a particular class or category</p><p><i>n.</i> mild banishment</p><p><b>omekšati, popustiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give in, as to influence or pressure [soften, yield]</p><p><b>nemilosrdan, nemilostiv, neumoran, uporan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not to be placated or appeased or moved by entreaty [grim, inexorable, stern, unappeasable, unforgiving, unrelenting]</p><p><i>adj.</i> never-ceasing [persistent, unrelenting]</p><p><b>nemilosrdno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a relentless manner [unrelentingly]</p><p><b>nemilosrdan, nemilostiv, neumoran, uporan (od &quot;relentless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mercilessness characterized by an unwillingness to relent or let up [inexorability, inexorableness]</p><p><b>primjerenost, relevantnost, važnost, važnosti, bitnost, relevancija, značajnost, značenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation of something to the matter at hand [relevancy]</p><p><b>bitnost, relevancija, relevantnost, važnost, značajnost, značenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation of something to the matter at hand [relevance]</p><p><b>bitan, koji se tiče, mjerodavno, nadležan, od važnosti, odgovarajućeg, odgovarajući, odgovarajućim, odnose, relevantan, relevantna, relevantnim, svrsishodan, umjestan, važan, važeći, važećih, važno, nadležnim, važne</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a bearing on or connection with the subject at issue</p><p><b>bitan, koji se tiče, mjerodavno, nadležan, od važnosti, odgovarajućeg, odgovarajući, odgovarajućim, odnose, relevantan, relevantna, relevantnim, svrsishodan, umjestan, važan, važeći, važećih, važno, nadležnim, važne (od &quot;relevant&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with relevance</p><p><b>pouzdanost, pouzdanost sustava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being dependable or reliable [dependability, dependableness, reliableness]</p><p><b>pouzdan, siguran, vjerodostojan, pouzdane, pouzdani, pouzdano</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of reliance or trust [dependable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of being depended on [dependable, honest, true]</p><p><i>adj.</i> conforming to fact and therefore worthy of belief [authentic]</p><p><b>pouzdanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being dependable or reliable [dependability, dependableness, reliability]</p><p><b>Na vjeran način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a faithful manner [dependably, faithfully]</p><p><b>korištenje, nada, oslonac, pouzdanje, upotreba, uvjerenost, uzdanje, povjerenje, oslanjanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> certainty based on past experience [trust]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of relying on something</p><p><b>pouzdan, povjerljiv, pun samopouzdanja</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relying on another for support</p><p><b>ostatak, relikvija, trag, relikt, suvenir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antiquity that has survived from the distant past</p><p><i>n.</i> something of sentimental value [keepsake, souvenir, token]</p><p><b>organizam ili vrsta koji preživljavaju kao ostatak inače izumrle flore ili faune u okolišu u znatnoj mjeri promijenjenom od onoga u kojem su potekli, Geološki element koji je ostatak postojećeg formacije nakon što su drugi dijelovi nestali (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organism or species surviving as a remnant of an otherwise extinct flora or fauna in an environment much changed from that in which it originated</p><p><i>n.</i> geological feature that is a remnant of a pre-existing formation after other parts have disappeared</p><p><b>odmor, olakšanje, olakšica, oporavak, oslobođenje, pomoć, potpora, reljef, reljefa, smjena, utjeha, podrška, predah</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling that comes when something burdensome is removed or reduced [alleviation, assuagement]</p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of being comfortable or relieved (especially after being relieved of distress) [ease]</p><p