 točkom (a) ovog članka, "proizvodnja podataka" znači proizvodnja podataka u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> data processing in which some of the functions are performed in different places and connected by transmission facilities [distributed data processing, teleprocessing]</p><p><b>Bomba koja može biti detonirana daljinskim upravljačem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb that can be detonated by remote control</p><p><b>daljinsko upravljanje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking a crew [unmanned]</p><p><b>udaljeno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a remote manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> to a remote degree</p><p><b>zabačenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being remote [farawayness, farness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to be distant and unsympathetic in manner [aloofness, standoffishness, withdrawnness]</p><p><b>odstranjenje, odstranjivanje, uklanjanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of removing [removal]</p><p><b>Majonesni umak s okusom biljaka, senf i kapra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mayonnaise sauce flavored with herbs and mustard and capers</p><p><b>dati novi oblik, preobličiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cast again [recast, remold]</p><p><i>v.</i> give new treads to (a tire) [remold, retread]</p><p><b>kupovina konja, novi konj, opskrba novim jahaćim konjima, ponovo se popeti, popis konja, popuniti konjima, popunski konj, remont, remontski konj, svjež jahaći konj, uramiti, uzjahati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fresh horse especially (formerly) to replace one killed or injured in battle</p><p><i>v.</i> mount again</p><p><i>v.</i> mount again, as after disassembling something</p><p><i>v.</i> provide with fresh horses</p><p><b>koji se može odnijeti, koji se može odstraniti, koji se može smijeniti, koji se može svrgnuti, koji se može udaljiti, koji se može ukloniti, odstranjiv, premjestiv, promjenljiv, smijeniti, smjenjiv, svrgnuti, udaljiv, uklonjiv, zamjenljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being removed or taken away or dismissed</p><p><i>adj.</i> able to be obliterated completely [obliterable]</p><p><b>premjestivi disk, uklonjivi disk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hard disk that can be removed from the disk drive</p><p><b>odstranjenje, premještaj, premještanje, preseljavanje, selidba, seljenje, seoba, sklanjanje, udaljivanje, ukidanje, uklanjanje, odstranjivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of removing [remotion]</p><p><i>n.</i> dismissal from office</p><p><b>Poduzeće koje se bavi pomicanjem imovine obitelji ili poduzeća s jednog mjesta na drugo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a company that moves the possessions of a family or business from one site to another [mover, moving company, public mover, removal firm]</p><p><b>Poduzeće koje se bavi pomicanjem imovine obitelji ili poduzeća s jednog mjesta na drugo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a company that moves the possessions of a family or business from one site to another [mover, moving company, public mover, removal company]</p><p><b>maknuti, odnijeti, odspojiti, odstraniti, opustiti, osloboditi, premjestiti, skidati, skinuti, skloniti, smaći, udaljiti, uklanjati, ukloniti, izbaci, izbriši, skidajte, sklonite, uklanjanju, uklonite, micati, odstranjivati, povlačiti, povući, riješiti se, rješavati se, sklanjati, izostati, udaljiti se, likvidirati, pogubiti, pogubljivati, smaknuti, smicati, ubijati, ubiti, ucmekati, umoriti, usmrtiti, usmrćivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> degree of figurative distance or separation</p><p><i>v.</i> remove something concrete, as by lifting, pushing, or taking off, or remove something abstract [take, take away, withdraw]</p><p><i>v.</i> remove from a position or an office</p><p><i>v.</i> dispose of [get rid of]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to leave [move out, take out]</p><p><i>v.</i> shift the position or location of, as for business, legal, educational, or military purposes [transfer]</p><p><i>v.</i> go away or leave [absent]</p><p><i>v.</i> kill intentionally and with premeditation [bump off, dispatch, hit, murder, off, polish off, slay]</p><p><i>v.</i> get rid of something abstract [take away]</p><p><b>maknuto, udaljen, uklonjen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> separated in relationship by a given degree of descent</p><p><i>adj.</i> separate or apart in time [distant, remote]</p><p><b>otapalo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a solvent that removes a substance (usually from a surface)</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who works for a company that moves furniture</p><p><b>Stado konja iz kojeg se biraju konji koji će se koristiti sljedećeg dana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the herd of horses from which those to be used the next day are chosen</p><p><b>kompenzirati, nadoknaditi, naplatiti, platiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make payment to [compensate, recompense]</p><p><b>primanja ili ispunjavanja uvjeta za naknadu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> receiving or eligible for compensation [compensated, salaried, stipendiary]</p><p><b>nagrada, naknada, naknada za rad, plaća, plata, renumeracija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that remunerates [earnings, pay, salary, wage]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of paying for goods or services or to recompense for losses</p><p><b>koristan, nagrađen, unosan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> for which money is paid [compensable, paying, salaried, stipendiary]</p><p><i>adj.</i> producing a sizeable profit [lucrative, moneymaking]</p><p><b>platac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who pays money for something [payer]</p><p><b>(Rimska mitologija) brat blizanac Romula (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman mythology) the twin brother of Romulus</p><p><b>preporod, preporoda, renesansa, renesanse, renesansnim, renesansnog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the period of European history at the close of the Middle Ages and the rise of the modern world [Renascence]</p><p><i>n.</i> the revival of learning and culture [Renascence, rebirth]</p><p><b>Moderni učenjak koji je u stanju steći više od površnog znanja o mnogim različitim interesovanjima., učenjak tijekom renesanse koji je (zato što je znanje bilo ograničeno) mogao znati gotovo sve o mnogim temama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a modern scholar who is in a position to acquire more than superficial knowledge about many different interests [generalist]</p><p><i>n.</i> a scholar during the Renaissance who (because knowledge was limited) could know almost everything about many topics</p><p><b>bubreg, bubrežni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the kidneys [nephritic]</p><p><b>arterija koja potiče iz abdominalne aorte i opskrbljuje bubrege i nadbubrežne žlijezde i uretere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artery originating from the abdominal aorta and supplying the kidneys and adrenal glands and ureters [arteria renalis]</p><p><b>Kalcijum koji se formira u bubregu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a calculus formed in the kidney [kidney stone, nephrolith, urinary calculus]</p><p><b>oštar bol u donjem dijelu leđa koji se širi u prepone (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sharp pain in the lower back that radiates into the groin</p><p><b>Kapsula koja sadrži Bowmanovu kapsule i glomerulus na proširenom kraju nefrona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capsule that contains Bowman's capsule and a glomerulus at the expanded end of a nephron [malpighian body, malpighian corpuscle]</p><p><b>Kožni korteks bubrega koji sadrži glomerule i zakrivljene cevke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cortex of the kidney containing the glomeruli and the convoluted tubules</p><p><b>bolest bubrega (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease affecting the kidneys [kidney disease, nephropathy, nephrosis]</p><p><b>nesposobnost bubrega da izlučuju otpad i održavaju ravnotežu elektrolita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inability of the kidneys to excrete wastes and to help maintain the electrolyte balance [kidney failure]</p><p><b>Neudovoljno izlučivanje otpada bubrezima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> insufficient excretion of wastes by the kidneys</p><p><b>prisutnost bubrežnih kamenja (kalkula) u bubregu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the presence of kidney stones (calculi) in the kidney [nephrolithiasis]</p><p><b>struktura u obliku lovora u izlaznom odjelu bubrega u koju se urin izlučuje prije nego što prođe u ureter (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a structure shaped like a funnel in the outlet of the kidney into which urine is discharged before passing into the ureter [pelvis]</p><p><b>vene koje prate bubrežne arterije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> veins that accompany renal arteries [vena renalis]</p><p><b>dati drugo ime, preimenovati, preimenuj, promijeni ime, promijeniti ime, reimenovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> assign a new name to</p><p><i>v.</i> name again or anew</p><p><b>razdoblje europske povijesti na kraju srednjeg vijeka i usponom modernog svijeta, drugo ili novo rođenje., oživljavanje učenja i kulture (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the period of European history at the close of the Middle Ages and the rise of the modern world [Renaissance]</p><p><i>n.</i> a second or new birth [rebirth, reincarnation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the revival of learning and culture [Renaissance, rebirth]</p><p><b>Ponovo se uzdižu u novom životu i snagu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> rising again as to new life and vigor [resurgent]</p><p><b>Talijanski operni sopran (rođen 1922.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian operatic soprano (born in 1922) [Tebaldi]</p><p><b>iskidati, pocijepati, rascijepiti, raskinuti, razderati, parati, rasporiti, razderati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> tear or be torn violently [pull, rip, rive]</p><p><b>činiti, dati, iskazati, izvoditi, platiti, podnijeti, položiti, predočiti, prevoditi, prikazati, pružiti, topiti, učiniti, udesiti, umjetnički prikazati, uzvratiti, vratiti, žbukati, donijeti, opremati, opremiti, opskrbiti, opskrbljivati, snabdijevati, snabdjeti, davati, povratiti, vraćati, isporučiti, isporučivati, izručiti, izručivati, predati, predavati, prepustiti, prepuštati, uručiti, uručivati, prikazivati, iskazivati, izraziti, izražavati, odati, odavati, prevesti, protumačiti, tumačiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance similar to stucco but exclusively applied to masonry walls</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become</p><p><i>v.</i> give something useful or necessary to [furnish, provide, supply]