<p><i>v.</i> fail to fulfill a promise or obligation [go back on, renege on, renegue on]</p><p><b>ne ispunjava obećanje ili obvezu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> fail to fulfill a promise or obligation [go back on, renege, renegue on]</p><p><b>pregovarati ponovo., U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. stavkom 2. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> negociate anew [renegotiate]</p><p><i>v.</i> revise the terms of in order to limit or regain excess profits gained by the contractor [renegotiate]</p><p><b>pregovarati ponovo., U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. stavkom 2. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> negociate anew [renegociate]</p><p><i>v.</i> revise the terms of in order to limit or regain excess profits gained by the contractor [renegociate]</p><p><b>ne ispunjava obećanje ili obvezu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> fail to fulfill a promise or obligation [go back on, renege, renege on]</p><p><b>obnoviti, pomladiti se, uspostaviti, obnavljati, oživiti, oživljavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> reestablish on a new, usually improved, basis or make new or like new [regenerate]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to appear in a new form [reincarnate]</p><p><b>koji se može obnoviti, obnovljiv, obnovljive</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> that can be renewed or extended</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being renewed</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta prirodnog resursa (kao što su drvo ili solarna energija) koji se može prirodno nadoknaditi s vremenom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any natural resource (as wood or solar energy) that can be replenished naturally with the passage of time</p><p><b>obnova, ponavljanje, produženje, reprodukcija, obnove</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the conversion of wasteland into land suitable for use of habitation or cultivation [reclamation, rehabilitation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of renewing</p><p><i>n.</i> filling again by supplying what has been used up [refilling, replacement, replenishment]</p><p><b>obnovljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> restored to a new condition</p><p><b>obnavljanje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to impart new life and vigor to [restorative, revitalising, revitalizing, reviving]</p><p><b>(u obliku lišća ili zrna) nalik bubregu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a leaf or bean shape) resembling the shape of kidney [kidney-shaped]</p><p><b>Jednostavan list u obliku bubrega. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a simple kidney-shaped leaf</p><p><b>proteolitički enzim koji se luči kod bubrega (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a proteolytic enzyme secreted by the kidneys</p><p><b>reneta, sirište, siriti, sredstvo za kiseljenje mlijeka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance that curdles milk in making cheese and junket</p><p><b>enzim koji se nalazi u želučnom soku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an enzyme that occurs in gastric juice [chymosin]</p><p><b>grad u zapadnoj Nevadi na podnožju planina Sierra Nevada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in western Nevada at the foot of the Sierra Nevada Mountains</p><p><b>Francuski slikar impresionista (1841-1919) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French impressionist painter (1841-1919) [Pierre Auguste Renoir]</p><p><b>normalizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make normal or cause to conform to a norm or standard [normalise, normalize, renormalize]</p><p><b>normalizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make normal or cause to conform to a norm or standard [normalise, normalize, renormalise]</p><p><b>ne priznavati svojim, odbiti, odreći, odreći se, otkloniti, poreći, napustiti, dići ruke, abdicirati, dezavuirati, odricati se, zanijekati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give up, such as power, as of monarchs and emperors, or duties and obligations [abdicate]</p><p><i>v.</i> leave (a job, post, or position) voluntarily [give up, resign, vacate]</p><p><i>v.</i> turn away from [foreswear, quit, relinquish]</p><p><i>v.</i> cast off [disown, repudiate]</p><p><b>odustajanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an act (spoken or written) declaring that something is surrendered or disowned [renunciation]</p><p><b>obnoviti, renovirati, animirati, oživotvoriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> restore to a previous or better condition [restitute]</p><p><i>v.</i> make brighter and prettier [freshen up, refurbish]</p><p><i>v.</i> give new life or energy to [animate, quicken, reanimate, recreate, repair, revive, revivify, vivify]</p><p><b>adaptacija, obnavljanje, obnova, obnovu, restauriranja, urbana obnova, restauracija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of improving by renewing and restoring [overhaul, redevelopment]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being restored to its former good condition [refurbishment, restoration]</p><p><b>restaurator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skilled worker who is employed to restore or refinish buildings or antique furniture [preserver, refinisher, restorer]</p><p><b>čuvenje, glas, renome, renomiran, slava, slavan, znamenit, poštovanje, ugled, uspjeh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state or quality of being widely honored and acclaimed [celebrity, fame]</p><p><b>čuvan, glasovit, poznat, poznato, renomiranih, renomirano, slavan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> widely known and esteemed [celebrated, famed, famous, far-famed, illustrious, notable, noted]</p><p><b>vrsta mekog talka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of soft talc</p><p><b>iznajmiti, iznajmljivanja, iznajmljivanje, iznajmljivati, kirija, Najam, najamnina, poderotina, procjep, pukotina, rascjep, raskid, renta, stanarina, unajmiti, uzeti pod zakup, uzeti u najam, zakup, zakupnina, zakupiti, razderotina, rupa, najmiti, obavezati, zakupljivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a payment or series of payments made by the lessee to an owner for use of some property, facility, equipment, or service</p><p><i>n.</i> an opening made forcibly as by pulling apart [rip, snag, split, tear]</p><p><i>n.</i> the return derived from cultivated land in excess of that derived from the poorest land cultivated under similar conditions [economic rent]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of rending or ripping or splitting something [rip, split]</p><p><i>v.</i> let for money [lease]</p><p><i>v.</i> grant use or occupation of under a term of contract [lease, let]</p><p><i>v.</i> engage for service under a term of contract [charter, engage, hire, lease, take]</p><p><i>v.</i> hold under a lease or rental agreement [charter, hire, lease]</p><p><b>Osoba koja ide od kuće do kuće i skuplja stanarinu za vlasnika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who goes from house to house collecting rents for the owner</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> grant the services of or the temporary use of, for a fee [farm out, hire out]</p><p><b>(ekonomika) teorija da osoba ili tvrtka nastoji zaraditi novac manipuliranjem ekonomskim okruženjem umjesto ostvarivanja profita kroz proizvodnju ili trgovinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (economics) the theory that a person or firm seeks to make money by manipulating the economic environment rather than by making a profit through production or trade [rent-seeking]</p><p><b>iznajmljeni automobil (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rented car [car rental, hire car, self-drive, u-drive, you-drive]</p><p><b>bez najamnine</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> complimentary</p><p><i>adv.</i> without paying rent</p><p><b>povlačenje od plaće stanarine koje daje lokalna uprava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rebate on rent given by a local government authority</p><p><b>registar stanarine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a register of rents</p><p><b>(ekonomika) teorija da osoba ili tvrtka nastoji zaraditi novac manipuliranjem ekonomskim okruženjem umjesto ostvarivanja profita kroz proizvodnju ili trgovinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (economics) the theory that a person or firm seeks to make money by manipulating the economic environment rather than by making a profit through production or trade [rent seeking]</p><p><b>iznajmljiv, koji se može izdati u najam, koji se može zakupiti, zakupljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> that is able or fit be rented</p><p><b>dohodak od najma, iznajmljivanje, najam, najamnina, zakupnina, letting, unajmljeni, unajmljivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> property that is leased or rented out or let [lease, letting]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of paying for the use of something (as