ledge or pay a debt or honor a contract (especially by public authorities)</p><p><i>n.</i> the exposure of falseness or pretensions [debunking]</p><p><b>Odbijaju naglasno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> rejecting emphatically</p><p><b>da se radi o predmetu spora, sporova ili sudskih postupaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to make the subject of dispute, contention, or litigation [contend, contest]</p><p><b>gađenje, gnušanje, neskladnost, neslaganje, odvratnost, averzija, odbojnost, zazor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intense aversion [horror, repulsion, revulsion]</p><p><i>n.</i> the relation between propositions that cannot both be true at the same time [incompatibility, inconsistency, mutual exclusiveness]</p><p><b>nepodnošljiv, neprijatan, nespojiv, odvratan, proturječan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> offensive to the mind [abhorrent, detestable, obscene, repulsive]</p><p><b>odbijanje, odbijati, odbiti, odgurnuti, odreći, otkaz, otpor, suzbiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instance of driving away or warding off [rebuff, snub]</p><p><i>v.</i> force or drive back [drive back, fight off, rebuff, repel]</p><p><i>v.</i> be repellent to [repel]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to move back by force or influence [beat back, drive, force back, push back, repel]</p><p><b>antipatija, odbijanje, odvratnost, averzija, odbojnost, zazor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the force by which bodies repel one another [repulsive force]</p><p><i>n.</i> intense aversion [horror, repugnance, revulsion]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of repulsing or repelling an attack [standoff]</p><p><b>antipatičan, gadan, koji odbacuje, koji odbija, odbijajući, odbojan, odvratan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> offensive to the mind [abhorrent, detestable, obscene, repugnant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> possessing the ability to repel</p><p><i>adj.</i> so extremely ugly as to be terrifying [hideous]</p><p><b>sila kojom tijela odbijaju jedno drugo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the force by which bodies repel one another [repulsion]</p><p><b>antipatičan, gadan, koji odbacuje, koji odbija, o