T)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> sift anew</p><p><b>dati ostavku, napustiti, odlaziti, odricati se, skinuti sa sebe, dati otkaz, davati ostavku, davati otkaz, napustiti dužnost, napuštati dužnost, odstupati, odstupiti, otići, napuštati, odbaciti, odbacivati, odreći se, ostaviti, ostavljati, povlačiti se, povući se, prepustiti, prepuštati, ustupati, ustupiti, podnijeti, pomiriti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> leave (a job, post, or position) voluntarily [give up, renounce, vacate]</p><p><i>v.</i> give up or retire from a position [leave office, quit, step down]</p><p><i>v.</i> part with a possession or right [free, give up, release, relinquish]</p><p><i>v.</i> accept as inevitable [reconcile, submit]</p><p><b>ostavka, ostavke, podnošenje, rezignacija, mirenje, predaja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acceptance of despair [surrender]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving up (a claim or office or possession etc.)</p><p><i>n.</i> a formal document giving notice of your intention to resign</p><p><b>sa ostavkom i prihvaćanjem., Na beznadan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with resignation and acceptance</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a hopeless resigned manner [abjectly]</p><p><b>odbaciti, odbacivati, odreći se, odricati se, opovrgavati, opovrgnuti, opozivati, opozvati, poreći, poricati, povlačiti, povući</b></p><p><i>v.</i> pull out from an agreement, contract, statement, etc.</p><p><i>v.</i> spring back [bounce, bound, rebound, recoil, reverberate, ricochet, spring, take a hop]</p><p><i>v.</i> formally reject or disavow a formerly held belief, usually under pressure [abjure, forswear, recant, retract]</p><p><i>v.</i> return to the original position or state after being stretched or compressed</p><p><b>elastičnost, gipkost, rastegljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the physical property of a material that can return to its original shape or position after deformation that does not exceed its elastic limit [resiliency]</p><p><i>n.</i> an occurrence of rebounding or springing back [resiliency]</p><p><b>elastičnost, gipkost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an occurrence of rebounding or springing back [resilience]</p><p><i>n.</i> the physical property of a material that can return to its original shape or position after deformation that does not exceed its elastic limit [resilience]</p><p><b>elastičan, gibak, otporan, pruživ, pun života, vedar, žilav, fleksibilan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> recovering readily from adversity, depression, or the like</p><p><i>adj.</i> elastic [bouncy, live, lively, springy]</p><p><b>osmoliti, smola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a class of solid or semisolid viscous substances obtained either as exudations from certain plants or prepared by polymerization of simple molecules [rosin]</p><p><b>za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> impregnate with resin to give a special flavor to</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50% (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> impregnated or flavored with resin</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling resin in properties or texture</p><p><b>od plastike koja sadrži smole (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plastic containing resins</p><p><b>smolast</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the characteristics of pitch or tar [pitchy, resiny, tarry]</p><p><b>s karakteristikama škrga ili katrana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the characteristics of pitch or tar [pitchy, resinous, tarry]</p><p><b>ne odobravati, odolijevati, opirati se, otporan, protiviti se, pružiti otpor, uzdržati se, odupirati se, prkositi, odoljeti, oduprijeti se, usprotiviti se, buniti se, oponirati, pobuniti se, prosvjedovati, protestirati, oprijeti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> elude, especially in a baffling way [defy, refuse]</p><p><i>v.</i> stand up or offer resistance to somebody or something [hold out, stand firm, withstand]</p><p><i>v.</i> express opposition through action or words [dissent, protest]</p><p><i>v.</i> withstand the force of something [fend, stand]</p><p><i>v.</i> resist immunologically the introduction of some foreign tissue or organ [refuse, reject]</p><p><i>v.</i> refuse to comply [balk, baulk, jib]</p><p><b>izdržljivost, odupiranje, opiranje, otpor, otpornost, otpornosti, protivljenje, rezistencija, Rezistentnost, oponiranje, suprotstavljanje, imunitet, imunost, otpornik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the action of opposing something that you disapprove or disagree with [opposition]</p><p><i>n.</i> any mechanical force that tends to retard or oppose motion</p><p><i>n.</i> a material's opposition to the flow of electric current [electric resistance, electrical resistance, impedance, ohmic resistance, resistivity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the military action of resisting the enemy's advance</p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) the condition in which an organism can resist disease [immunity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the capacity of an organism to defend itself against harmful environmental agents</p><p><i>n.</i> a secret group organized to overthrow a government or occupation force [underground]</p><p><i>n.</i> the degree of unresponsiveness of a disease-causing microorganism to antibiotics or other drugs (as in penicillin-resistant bacteria)</p><p><i>n.</i> (psychiatry) an unwillingness to bring repressed feelings into conscious awareness</p><p><i>n.</i> an electrical device that resists the flow of electrical current [resistor]</p><p><i>n.</i> group action in opposition to those in power</p><p><b>Pirometar koji mjeri visoke temperature otporom u zagrijanom žicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pyrometer that measures high temperatures by the resistance in a heated wire</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thermometer that measures temperature by changes in the resistance of a spiral of platinum wire [platinum thermometer]</p><p><b>recipročni vodljivosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the reciprocal of conductance</p><p><b>izdržljiv, otporan, imun</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or conferring immunity (to disease or infection) [immune]</p><p><i>adj.</i> able to tolerate environmental conditions or physiological stress [tolerant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> impervious to being affected</p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed to or engaged in defiance of established authority [insubordinate, resistive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> incapable of absorbing or mixing with [repellent]</p><p><b>protivnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who systematically obstructs some action that others want to take [obstructer, obstructionist, obstructor, thwarter]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who offers opposition [adversary, antagonist, opponent, opposer]</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to primjena na proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 9A001., točka (a) ovog poglavlja ne vrijedi za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 9A001. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being resisted or withstood or frustrated</p><p><b>fizički napori protiv pravnog uhićenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> physical efforts to oppose a lawful arrest</p><p><b>otporan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> exhibiting or relating to electrical resistance</p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed to or engaged in defiance of established authority [insubordinate, resistant]</p><p><b>otpornost, specifičan otpor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a material's opposition to the flow of electric current [electric resistance, electrical resistance, impedance, ohmic resistance, resistance]</p><p><b>neodoljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> impossible to resist [irresistible]</p><p><i>adj.</i> offering no resistance [unresisting]</p><p><b>električni otpor, otpornik, rezistor, zavojnica otpornika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electrical device that resists the flow of electrical current [resistance]</p><p><b>mijenjati veličinu, promijeniti veličinu, promjena veličine</b></p><p><i>v.</i> change the size of</p><p><b>opet mrlja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> smudge again</p><p><b>pođoniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> put a new sole on [sole]</p><p><b>čvrst, nepokolebljiv, odlučan, odvažan, riješen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> firm in purpose or belief</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by quickness and firmness [u