teem and respect [estimable, good, honorable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> large in amount or extent or degree [goodish, goodly, healthy, hefty, sizable, sizeable, tidy]</p><p><b>u izuzetno dostojanom stupnju., na pristojan i moralno ugledan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a tolerably worthy extent [creditably]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a decent and morally reputable manner</p><p><b>cijenjen, poštovan, poštovani, štovani</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> receiving deferential regard [well-thought-of]</p><p><b>cijeniti, glede, imati obzira, obzir, obzirom, odnos, pogled, poštivanja, poštivati, poštovanje, poštovati, štovati, štujući, u pogledu, uvažavanje, uvažavati, poštovanja, poštovanju (od &quot;respect&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who respects someone or something</p><p><b>pristojan, pun poštovanja, učtiv, uljudan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of or exhibiting respect</p><p><i>adj.</i> feeling or manifesting veneration [reverential, venerating]</p><p><b>pristojan, pun poštovanja, učtiv, uljudan (od &quot;respectful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a respectful manner</p><p><b>pokornost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> courteous regard for people's feelings [deference, respect]</p><p><b>dotičan, odgovarajući, odnosan, odnosni, osobit, pojedinačan, pojedinačne, svoj, svoje, odnosna</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> considered individually [several, various]</p><p><b>odnosno, za svako posebno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in the order given [severally]</p><p><b>cijeniti, glede, imati obzira, obzir, obzirom, odnos, pogled, poštivanja, poštivati, poštovanje, poštovati, štovati, štujući, u pogledu, uvažavanje, uvažavati, poštovanja, poštovanju (od &quot;respect&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (often used with `pay') a formal expression of esteem</p><p><b>Talijanski skladatelj poznat po simfonijskim pjesmama (1879-1936) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian composer remembered for his symphonic poems (1879-1936) [Ottorino Respighi]</p><p><b>disanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the metabolic processes whereby certain organisms obtain energy from organic molecules [cellular respiration, internal respiration]</p><p><i>n.</i> a single complete act of breathing in and out</p><p><i>n.</i> the bodily process of inhalation and exhalation [breathing, external respiration, ventilation]</p><p><b>plinska maska, respirator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a breathing device for administering long-term artificial respiration [inhalator]</p><p><i>n.</i> a protective mask with a filter [gas helmet, gasmask]</p><p><b>dišne, dišni, dišnih, respiratorni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to respiration</p><p><b>acidoza uzrokovana smanjenom razmjenom plinova u plućima (kao u emfizemu ili upale pluća) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acidosis resulting from reduced gas exchange in the lungs (as in emphysema or pneumonia) [carbon dioxide acidosis]</p><p><b>alkalosi uzrokovani povećanom razmjenom plinova u plućima (kao što je hiperventilacija povezana s ekstremnom anksioznošću ili intoksikacijom aspirinom ili metaboličkom acidozom) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> alkalosis resulting from increased gas exchange in the lungs (as in hyperventilation associated with extreme anxiety or aspirin intoxication or metabolic acidosis)</p><p><b>centar u dugom mozgu i pons koji integrira osjetilne informacije o razini kisika i ugljičnog dioksida u krvi i određuje signale koji se šalju u mišiće disanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the center in the medulla oblongata and pons that integrates sensory information about the level of oxygen and carbon dioxide in the blood and determines the signals to be sent to the respiratory muscles</p><p><b>bolest dišnoga sustava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease affecting the respiratory system [respiratory disorder, respiratory illness]</p><p><b>bolest koja utječe na dišni sustav (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease affecting the respiratory system [respiratory disease, respiratory illness]</p><p><b>akutna bolest pluća novorođenčeta (posebno prevremeno rođenih) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute lung disease of the newborn (especially the pre