enovate]</p><p><b>naknada, obnavljanje, obnova, restitucija, uspostavljanje, vraćanje, povrat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sum of money paid in compensation for loss or injury [amends, damages, indemnification, indemnity, redress]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of restoring something to its original state</p><p><i>n.</i> getting something back again [regaining, restoration, return]</p><p><b>jogunast, neposlušan, nestrpljiv, samovoljan, tvrdoglav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being in a tense state [edgy, high-strung, highly strung, jittery, jumpy, nervy, overstrung, uptight]</p><p><i>adj.</i> impatient especially under restriction or delay</p><p><b>jogunast, neposlušan, nestrpljiv, samovoljan, tvrdoglav (od &quot;restive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a restive manner</p><p><b>jogunast, neposlušan, nestrpljiv, samovoljan, tvrdoglav (od &quot;restive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the anxious feeling you have when you have the jitters [jitteriness, jumpiness, nervousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> characterized by nervousness and quickness to take fright [skittishness]</p><p><b>nemiran, nespokojan, nestrpljiv, uznemiren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> worried and uneasy [ungratified, unsatisfied]</p><p><i>adj.</i> ceaselessly in motion</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking or not affording physical or mental rest [uneasy]</p><p><b>osjećaj nemira i nemira u nogama nakon što odete u krevet (ponekad uzrokuje nesanicu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feeling of uneasiness and restlessness in the legs after going to bed (sometimes causing insomnia) [Ekbom syndrome, restless legs syndrome]</p><p><b>osjećaj nemira i nemira u nogama nakon što odete u krevet (ponekad uzrokuje nesanicu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feeling of uneasiness and restlessness in the legs after going to bed (sometimes causing insomnia) [Ekbom syndrome, restless legs]</p><p><b>nemiran, nespokojan, nestrpljiv, uznemiren (od &quot;restless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a restless manner</p><p><b>nemir, unutarnji nemir, nelagoda, nelagodnost, nemirnost, nespokoj, nespokojnost, uznemirenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being ceaselessly moving or active</p><p><i>n.</i> a lack of patience [impatience]</p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of agitation expressed in continual motion [fidget, fidgetiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> inability to rest or relax or be still [queasiness, uneasiness]</p><p><b>Opet zalihe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> stock again</p><p><b>dovođenje, obnavljanje, obnova, obnova spomenika, ponovna uspostava, restaurator, restauratorskoj, restauriranja, restauriranje, sanacija, uspostavljanje, vraćanje, restauracija, povrat, maketa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the reign of Charles II in England</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of restoring something or someone to a satisfactory state</p><p><i>n.</i> getting something back again [regaining, restitution, return]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being restored to its former good condition [refurbishment, renovation]</p><p><i>n.</i> some artifact that has been restored or reconstructed</p><p><i>n.</i> a model that represents the landscape of a former geological age or that represents and extinct animal etc.</p><p><i>n.</i> the re-establishment of the British monarchy in 1660</p><p><b>povratan, sred za jačanje, okrepljujuće sredstvo, ublažujuće sredstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a medicine that strengthens and invigorates [tonic]</p><p><i>n.</i> a device for treating injury or disease [corrective]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to impart new life and vigor to [renewing, revitalising, revitalizing, reviving]</p><p><i>adj.</i> promoting recuperation [recuperative]</p><p><b>dovesti, nadoknaditi, naknaditi, obnavljanje, obnoviti, ponovno uspostaviti, ponovo uspostaviti, postaviti u početni položaj, povrat, restaurirati, u prijašnje stanje, uspostaviti, vraćanje, vraćanje u polazno stanje, vratiti, vratiti u početno stanje, obnavljati, popraviti, popravljati, povratiti, prepraviti, prepravljati, rekonstruirati, krpiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> return to its original or usable and functioning condition [reconstruct]</p><p><i>v.</i> return to life [regenerate, rejuvenate]</p><p><i>v.</i> give or bring back [restitute]</p><p><i>v.</i> restore by replacing a part or putting together what is torn or broken [bushel, doctor, fix, furbish up, mend, repair, touch on]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring back into original existence, use, function, or position [reestablish, reinstate]</p><p><b>obnavljač, popravljač, restaurator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skilled worker who is employed to restore or refinish buildings or antique furniture [preserver, refinisher, renovator]</p><p><b>često propisani benzodiazepin (trgovinski naziv Restoril) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a frequently prescribed benzodiazepine (trade name Restoril) [temazepam]</p><p><b>obuzdati, ograničiti, sprečavati, suzbiti, zadržati, zaustaviti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to close within bounds, or otherwise limit or deprive of free movement [confine, constrain, hold]</p><p><i>v.</i> restrict (someone or something) so as to make free movement difficult [cumber, encumber]</p><p><i>v.</i> prevent (someone or something) from doing something</p><p><i>v.</i> prevent the action or expression of [hold back, keep, keep back]</p><p><b>obuzdan, ograničen, prigušen, suzdržan, svladan, ublažen, umjeren, uzdržljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> cool and formal in manner [reticent, unemotional]</p><p><i>adj.</i> under restraint</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by avoidance of extravagance or extremes [moderate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not showy or obtrusive [quiet]</p><p><i>adj.</i> prudent [guarded]</p><p><b>obuzdati, ograničiti, sprečavati, suzbiti, zadržati, zaustaviti (od &quot;restrain&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chemical that is added to a photographic developer in order to retard development and reduce the amount of fog on a film</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who directs and restrains [controller]</p><p><b>obuzdavanje, ograničenje, povučenost, prepreka, smetanje, sprečavanje, stješnjavanje, strogost, suzdržavanje, svladavanje, uzdržljivost, suzdržanost, kontrola, blokada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of controlling by restraining someone or something</p><p><i>n.</i> discipline in personal and social activities [control]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being physically constrained [constraint]</p><p><i>n.</i> a rule or condition that limits freedom</p><p><i>n.</i> lack of ornamentation [chasteness, simpleness, simplicity]</p><p><i>n.</i> a device that retards something's motion [constraint]</p><p><b>Svaka djelatnost koja ima za cilj spriječiti slobodnu konkurenciju u poduzećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any act that tends to prevent free competition in business</p><p><b>Napravi se opet jakim. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make strong again</p><p><b>ograničiti, ograničiti na, ograničiti se, razgraničiti, stegnuti, potkresati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> place restrictions on [curb, curtail, cut back]</p><p><i>v.</i> place under restrictions [control]</p><p><i>v.</i> place limits on (extent or amount or access) [bound, confine, limit, throttle, trammel]</p><p><i>v.</i> prevent (information) from being circulated or disclosed</p><p><b>ograničen, ograničeno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> subject to restriction or subjected to restriction</p><p><i>adj.</i> restricted in meaning [qualified]</p><p><i>adj.</i> the lowest level of official classification for documents</p><p><b>ograničiti, ograničiti na, ograničiti se, razgraničiti, stegnuti (od &quot;restrict&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> restricting the scope or freedom of action [confining, constraining, constrictive, limiting]</p><p><b>blokiranje, ograničavanje, ograničenje, restrikcija, zadržavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a principle that limits the extent of something [limitation]</p><p><i>n.</i> an act of limiting or restricting (as by regulation) [limitation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of keeping something within specified bounds (by force if necessary) [confinement]</p><p><b>bilo koji od enzima koji režu nukleinsku kiselinu na specifičnim mjestima restrikcije i proizvode fragmente restrikcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the enzymes that cut nucleic acid at specific restriction sites and produce restriction fragments [restriction enzyme, restriction nuclease]</p><p><b>bilo koji od enzima koji režu nukleinsku kiselinu na specifičnim mjestima restrikcije i proizvode fragmente restrikcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the enzymes that cut nucleic acid at specific restriction sites and produce restriction fragments [restriction endonuclease, restriction nuclease]</p><p><b>fragment DNK koji se proizvodi dijeljenjem DNK s restrikcijskim enzimom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fragment of DNA that is produced by cleaving DNA with a restriction enzyme</p><p><b>bilo koji od enzima koji režu nukleinsku kiselinu na specifičnim mjestima restrikcije i proizvode fragmente restrikcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the enzymes that cut nucleic acid at specific restriction sites and produce restriction fragments [restriction endonuclease, restriction enzyme]</p><p><b>specifična mjesta na kojima će se enzim za ograničavanje razdvojiti DNK (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the specific sites at which a restriction enzyme will cleave DNA</p><p><b>ograničavajući, ograničen, restrikcijska, restriktivan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> serving to restrict</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of tariff) protective of national interests by restricting imports</p><p><b>podređeni stav koji ograničava ili ograničava značenje imenske fraze koju mijenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a subordinate clause that limits or restricts the meaning of the noun phrase it modifies</p><p><b>ograničavajući, ograničen, restrikcijska, restriktivan (od &quot;restrictive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a restrictive manner</p><p><b>ograničavajući, ograničen, restrikcijska, restriktivan (od &quot;restrictive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a grammatical qualification that makes the meaning more specific (`red hat' has a more specific meaning than `hat')</p><p><i>n.</i> a lack of permissiveness or indulgence and a tendency to confine behavior within certain specified limits [unpermissiveness]</p><p><b>zahod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toilet that is available to the public [comfort station, convenience, public convenience, public lavatory, public toilet, toilet facility, wash room]</p><p><b>preustroju, restrukturirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> construct or form anew or provide with a new structure [reconstitute]</p><p><b>Sublime (spojina) još jednom (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> sublime (a compound) once again</p><p><b>(informacije) ponovno dostaviti programu ili automatskom sustavu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> submit (information) again to a program or automatic system [feed back]</p><p><b>biti dobiven, biti rezultat, bodovanje, dovesti do, ishod, nalaz, nastati, posljedica, proizlaziti, proizlaziti iz, rezultat, rezultirati, učinak, uroditi, zaključan, efekt, konzekvencija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a phenomenon that follows and is caused by some previous phenomenon [consequence, effect, event, issue, outcome, upshot]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement that solves a problem or explains how to solve the problem [answer, resolution, solution, solvent]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that results [final result, outcome, resultant, termination]</p><p><i>n.</i> the semantic role of the noun phrase whose referent exists only by virtue of the activity denoted by the verb in the clause [resultant role]</p><p><i>v.</i> issue or terminate (in a specified way, state, etc.) [ensue]</p><p><i>v.</i> produce as a result or residue [lead, leave]</p><p><i>v.</i> come about or follow as a consequence</p><p><b>ishod, koji izlazi, koji rezultira, koji slijedi, rezultanta, rezultat, vektor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the final point in a process [end point]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that results [final result, outcome, result, termination]</p><p><i>n.</i> a vector that is the sum of two or more other vectors [vector sum]</p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring with or following as a consequence [accompanying, attendant, collateral, concomitant, consequent, ensuant, incidental, sequent]</p><p><b>semantička uloga imenske fraze čiji referent postoji samo na temelju aktivnosti koju označava glagol u rečenici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the semantic role of the noun phrase whose referent exists only by virtue of the activity denoted by the verb in the clause [result]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je riječ o povlačenju ili povlačenju, u slučaju da je riječ o povlačenju ili povlačenju, u slučaju da je to bilo u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili člankom 3. točkom (b) ili člankom 3. točkom (c) ili člankom 3. točkom (d) ili člankom 3. točkom (e) ili člankom 3. točkom (e) ili člankom 3. točkom (e) ili člankom 3. točkom (e) ili člankom 3. točkom (e) ili člankom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trust created by a court when it is judged that it was the intention of the parties to create a trust</p><p><b>kratki pregled, nastaviti, nastavljanje, obnoviti, ponovno zauzimanje, produžiti, rezime, rezimirati, sažetak, svesti obračun, uzeti natrag, vratiti se, životopis, pregled, skica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> short descriptive summary (of events) [sketch, survey]</p><p><i>n.</i> a summary of your academic and work history [CV, curriculum vitae]</p><p><i>v.</i> take up or begin anew [re-start, restart]</p><p><i>v.</i> return to a previous location or condition [take up]</p><p><i>v.</i> assume anew</p><p><i>v.</i> give a summary (of) [sum up, summarise, summarize]</p><p><b>nastavak, nastavak partije, nastavljanje, obnavljanje, ponovno dobivanje, postizanje, povratak, uzimanje natrag, vraćanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> beginning again [recommencement]</p><p><b>ležeći licem prema gore (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lying face upward [supine]</p><p><b>ponovno se pojavljuju na površini., pokrivanje novom površinom, opet se pojave. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> reappear on the surface</p><p><i>v.</i> cover with a new surface</p><p><i>v.</i> appear again</p><p><b>Ponovo se digni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> rise again</p><p><b>izvor, ponovno izbijanje, ponovnoga izbijanja, obnavljanje, obnova, oživljavanje, ponovni procvat, preporod, revitalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bringing again into activity and prominence [revitalisation, revitalization, revival, revivification]</p><p><b>koji oživljava, koji se oporavlja</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> rising again as to new life and vigor [renascent]</p><p><b>ponovno probuditi, ponovno uvesti, ponovo uvesti, uskrsnuti, oživjeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become alive again [raise, upraise]</p><p><i>v.</i> restore from a depressed, inactive, or unused state [revive]</p><p><i>v.</i> return from the dead [rise, uprise]</p><p><b>ponovno uvođenje, ponovo uvođenje, uskrsnuće, uspostavljanje, uskrsenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (New Testament) the rising of Christ on the third day after the Crucifixion [Christ's Resurrection, Resurrection of Christ]</p><p><i>n.</i> a revival from inactivity and disuse</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste biljaka koje se mogu upotrebljavati za proizvodnju biljaka u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje članak 3. točka (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje članak 3. točka (a) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fern growing on rocks or tree trunks and having fronds greyish and scurfy below [Polypodium polypodioides, gray polypody, grey polypody]</p><p><b>(Novi zavjet) uskrsnuće Krista trećeg dana nakon raspeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (New Testament) the rising of Christ on the third day after the Crucifixion [Christ's Resurrection, Resurrection]</p><p><b>guste tufted paprika od jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država do Perua, mala siva azijska pustinjska biljka s malenim bijelim cvijećem koja se skuplja kad suha i širi kada je vlažna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> densely tufted fern ally of southwestern United States to Peru [Selaginella lepidophylla, rose of Jericho]</p><p><i>n.</i> small grey Asiatic desert plant bearing minute white flowers that rolls up when dry and expands when moist [Anastatica hierochuntica, rose of Jericho]</p><p><b>nova anketa ili studija (MT)</