etort, riposte]</p><p><i>n.</i> the key on electric typewriters or computer keyboards that causes a carriage return and a line feed [return key]</p><p><i>n.</i> a reciprocal group action [getting even, paying back]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tennis stroke that sends the ball back to the other player</p><p><i>n.</i> (American football) the act of running back the ball after a kickoff or punt or interception or fumble</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of someone appearing again [reappearance]</p><p><i>v.</i> go or come back to place, condition, or activity where one has been before</p><p><i>v.</i> give back [render]</p><p><i>v.</i> go back to a previous state [regress, retrovert, revert, turn back]</p><p><i>v.</i> go back to something earlier [come back, hark back, recall]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring back to the point of departure [bring back, take back]</p><p><i>v.</i> return in kind</p><p><i>v.</i> make a return</p><p><i>v.</i> answer back [come back, rejoin, repay, retort, riposte]</p><p><i>v.</i> be restored [come back]</p><p><i>v.</i> pay back [give back, refund, repay]</p><p><i>v.</i> pass down [deliver, render]</p><p><i>v.</i> elect again [reelect]</p><p><i>v.</i> be inherited by [devolve, fall, pass]</p><p><i>v.</i> return to a previous position</p><p><i>v.</i> give or supply [generate, give, render, yield]</p><p><i>v.</i> submit (a report, etc.) to someone in authority</p><p><b>povratna adresa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the address of the sender of a letter or parcel indicating where it should be returned if it cannot be delivered</p><p><b>enter</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the key on electric typewriters or computer keyboards that causes a carriage return and a line feed [return]</p><p><b>(privremena) vrijednost koja se može izračunati kao vrijednost prihoda ili naknade za rad u društvu ili kao vrijednost prihoda ili naknade za rad u društvu ili kao vrijednost prihoda ili naknade za rad u društvu ili kao vrijednost prihoda ili naknade za rad u društvu ili kao vrijednost prihoda ili naknade za rad u