er of one of the tribes of Israel</p><p><i>n.</i> a hot sandwich with corned beef and Swiss cheese and sauerkraut on rye bread</p><p><b>Američki karikaturist koji je crtao složene dijagramske slike vrlo kompliciranih i nepraktičnih uređaja koji su postigli malo ili ništa (1883-1970) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States cartoonist who drew intricate diagrams of very complicated and impractical contraptions that accomplished little or nothing (1883-1970) [Goldberg, Rube Goldberg]</p><p><b>okupljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of coming together again [reunion]</p><p><b>Ujedinite se opet, kao zemlja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> unify again, as of a country [reunite]</p><p><b>ponovno sjedinjenje, sastanak, sjednica, skup, zajednički susret, okupljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a party of former associates who have come together again</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of coming together again [reunification]</p><p><b>ponovo sjediniti, ujediniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> have a reunion</p><p><i>v.</i> unify again, as of a country [reunify]</p><p><b>povrat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a process of using up or consuming again [re-uptake]</p><p><b>ponovno iskoristiv, ponovno upotrebljiv, ponovo upotrebljiv, obnovljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being used again [reclaimable, recyclable]</p><p><b>Program koji se može učitati jednom i izvršavati više puta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a program that can be loaded once and executed repeatedly</p><p><b>Uređaj koji se može učitati jednom i izvršavati više puta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a routine that can be loaded once and executed repeatedly</p><p><b>ponovno koristiti, ponovno korištenje, oporabiti, reciklirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> use again after processing [recycle, reprocess]</p><p><b>broj okreta, broj okreta stroja, dati pun gas</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rate of revolution of a motor [revolutions per minute, rpm]</p><p><i>v.</i> increase the number of rotations per minute [rev up]</p><p><b>ubrzaj., povećanje broja rotacija u minuti (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> speed up [step up]</p><p><i>v.</i> increase the number of rotations per minute [rev]</p><p><b>revalorizacija, revalvacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a new appraisal or evaluation [reappraisal, reassessment, review]</p><p><b>revalorizacija</b></p><p><i>v.</i> gain in value [appreciate, apprise, apprize]</p><p><i>v.</i> value anew</p><p><b>obnoviti, preraditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to patch up or renovate</p><p><i>v.</i> provide (a shoe) with a new vamp [vamp]</p><p><b>iznijeti na vidjelo, objaviti, objelodaniti, odati, otkriti, otkrivati, pokazati, razglasiti, pokazuju, iznijeti, iznositi, izvlačiti, izvući, objelodanjivati, prikazati, prikazivati, razotkriti, razotkrivati, objavljivati, odavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make visible [bring out, unveil]</p><p><i>v.</i> make known to the public information that was previously known only to a few people or that was meant to be kept a secret [break, bring out, disclose, discover, divulge, expose, give away, let on, let out, uncover, unwrap]</p><p><i>v.</i> disclose directly or through prophets</p><p><b>religija koja se temelji na Božjim otkrivenjima čovječanstvu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a religion founded primarily on the revelations of God to humankind</p><p><b>iz čega se puno može zaključiti, otkrivanje, razotkrivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the speech act of making something evident [disclosure, revelation]</p><p><i>adj.</i> disclosing unintentionally something concealed [telling, telltale]</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing or making known</p><p><b>budnica, uranak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (military) signal to wake up [wake-up signal]</p><p><i>n.</i> a signal to get up in the morning</p><p><b>bančiti, bučna zabava, bučno se zabavljati, gostiti, gozba, pijančiti, pijanka, raspojasati se, slavlje, terevenka, uživati u, veseliti se, veselje, zabava, zabavljati se, uživati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unrestrained merrymaking [revelry]</p><p><i>v.</i> take delight in [delight, enjoy]</p><p><i>v.</i> celebrate noisily, often indulging in drinking [jollify, make happy, make merry, make whoopie, racket, wassail, whoop it up]</p><p><b>objelodanjenje, otkriće, otkrivanje, otkrivenje, razotkrivanje, objava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the speech act of making something evident [disclosure, revealing]</p><p><i>n.</i> an enlightening or astonishing disclosure</p><p><i>n.</i> communication of knowledge to man by a divine or supernatural agency [divine revelation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the last book of the New Testament [Apocalypse, Book of Revelation, Revelation of Saint John the Divine]</p><p><b>posljednja knjiga Novog zavjeta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the last book of the New Testament [Apocalypse, Book of Revelation, Revelation]</p><p><b>(obično slijedi `of') koji jasno ukazuje ili otkriva, proročanstvo o uništenju ili konačnom uništenju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually followed by `of') pointing out or revealing clearly [indicative, indicatory, significative, suggestive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> prophetic of devastation or ultimate doom [apocalyptic, apocalyptical]</p><p><b>bančiti, bučna zabava, bučno se zabavljati, gostiti, gozba, pijančiti, pijanka, raspojasati se, slavlje, terevenka, uživati u, veseliti se, veselje, zabava, zabavljati se (od &quot;revel&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a celebrant who shares in a noisy party [merrymaker, reveller]</p><p><b>slavljenik koji učestvuje u bučnoj zabavi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a celebrant who shares in a noisy party [merrymaker, reveler]</p><p><b>bučna pijanka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unrestrained merrymaking [revel]</p><p><b>osoba koja se vraća nakon dugog odsustva, netko tko se vratio iz mrtvih., od ili u vezi s ili tipično za povratnika, Vraćam se. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who returns after a lengthy absence</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who has returned from the dead</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or typical of a revenant</p><p><i>adj.</i> coming back [recurring]</p><p><b>odmazda, osveta, osvetiti, osvetiti se, uzvraćanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> action taken in return for an injury or offense [retaliation]</p><p><i>v.</i> take revenge for a perceived wrong [avenge, retaliate]</p><p><b>osvetljiv, osvetnički, osvetoljubiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed to seek revenge or intended for revenge [vengeful, vindictive]</p><p><b>osvetljiv, osvetnički, osvetoljubiv (od &quot;revengeful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a vindictive, revengeful manner [vengefully, vindictively]</p><p><b>dohodak, porez, prihod, prihodi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the entire amount of income before any deductions are made [gross, receipts]</p><p><i>n.</i> government income due to taxation [tax income, tax revenue, taxation]</p><p><b>Obveznica koju je izdala agencija koja je zadužena za financiranje javnih radova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bond issued by an agency that is commissioned to finance public works</p><p><b>namet, oporezivanje, porez</b></p><p><i>n.</i> charge against a citizen's person or property or activity for the support of government [tax, taxation]</p><p><b>raspodjela dijela federalnih poreskih prihoda državama i općinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> distribution of part of the federal tax income to states and municipalities</p><p><b>mali komad lepljivog papira koji se stavlja na predmet kako bi se pokazalo da je državni porez plaćen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small piece of adhesive paper that is put on an object to show that a government tax has been paid [stamp]</p><p><b>tarifa uvedena za povećanje prihoda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tariff imposed to raise revenue</p><p><b>dohodak, porez, prihod, prihodi (od &quot;revenue&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government agent responsible for collecting revenue (especially one responsible for stopping bootlegging)</p><p><b>s karakterom glasnog dubokog zvuka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having the character of a loud deep sound [plangency, resonance, ringing, sonority, sonorousness, vibrancy]</p><p><b>koji odjekuje, zvonak, zvučan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a tendency to reverberate or be repeatedly reflected</p><p><b>odbiti se, odjeknuti, taliti, topiti, odjekivati, odzvanjati, oriti se, prolamati se, prolomiti se, zaoriti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> ring or echo with sound [echo, resound, ring]</p><p><i>v.</i> have a long or continuing effect</p><p><i>v.</i> be reflected as heat, sound, or light or shock waves</p><p><i>v.</i> to throw or bend back (from a surface) [reflect]</p><p><i>v.</i> spring back [bounce, bound, rebound, recoil, resile, ricochet, spring, take a hop]</p><p><i>v.</i> treat, process, heat, melt, or refine in a reverberatory furnace</p><p><b>odbiti se, odjeknuti, taliti, topiti (od &quot;reverberate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by resonance [resonant, resonating, resounding, reverberative]</p><p><b>eho, jeka, odbijanje, odjek, odražavanje, reverberacija, višestruka jeka u zatvorenom prostoru</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the repetition of a sound resulting from reflection of the sound waves [echo, replication, sound reflection]</p><p><i>n.</i> a remote or indirect consequence of some action [repercussion]</p><p><b>koji djeluje protivno, koji djeluje suprotno, koji odjekuje, koji se odražava, reverberacioni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by resonance [resonant, resonating, resounding, reverberating]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog poglavlja upotrijebi samo jedan od sljedećih materijala: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a furnace in which the material that is being treated is heated indirectly by flames that are directed at the roof and walls of the furnace</p><p><b>cijeniti, poštovati, štovati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American silversmith remembered for his midnight ride (celebrated in a poem by Longfellow) to warn the colonists in Lexington and Concord that British troops were coming (1735-1818) [Paul Revere]</p><p><i>n.</i> a lapel on a woman's garment [revers]</p><p><i>v.</i> love unquestioningly and uncritically or to excess [hero-worship, idolise, idolize, worship]</p><p><i>v.</i> regard with feelings of respect and reverence [fear, reverence, venerate]</p><p><b>duboko počastvovana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> profoundly honored [august, venerable]</p><p><b>naklonost, poštovanje, poštovati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of profound respect for someone or something [awe, fear, veneration]</p><p><i>n.</i> a reverent mental attitude</p><p><i>n.</i> an act showing respect (especially a bow or curtsy)</p><p><i>v.</i> regard with feelings of respect and reverence [fear, revere, venerate]</p><p><b>svećenik, uvaženi, velečasni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the clergy and a spiritual leader of the Christian Church [clergyman, man of the cloth]</p><p><i>n.</i> a title of respect for a clergyman</p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of adoration or reverence [sublime]</p><p><b>Engleski autor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English author [Carroll, Charles Dodgson, Charles Lutwidge Dodgson, Dodgson, Lewis Carroll]</p><p><b>pun poštovanja, smjeran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> feeling or showing profound respect or veneration</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing great reverence for god [godly, worshipful]</p><p><b>osjećaju ili pokazuju poštovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> feeling or manifesting veneration [respectful, venerating]</p><p><b>s poštovanjem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with reverence [reverently]</p><p><b>pun poštovanja, smjeran (od &quot;reverent&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with reverence [reverentially]</p><p><b>maštanje, sanjarenje, sanjaranje, snatrenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> absentminded dreaming while awake [air castle, castle in Spain, castle in the air, daydream, daydreaming, oneirism, revery]</p><p><i>n.</i> an abstracted state of absorption [revery]</p><p><b>broj okreta, broj okreta stroja, dati pun gas (od &quot;rev&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lapel on a woman's garment [revere]</p><p><b>obrat, obrtanje, poništenje, preinačenje, premještanje, preokret, preokretanje, promjena, ukidanje, okret, okretanje, prekretanje, reverzija, promjena politike, zaokret</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a change from one state to the opposite state</p><p><i>n.</i> an unfortunate happening that hinders or impedes [black eye, blow, reverse, setback]</p><p><i>n.</i> turning in an opposite direction or position [turn around]</p><p><i>n.</i> a decision to reverse an earlier decision [change of mind, flip-flop, turnabout, turnaround]</p><p><i>n.</i> a judgment by a higher court that the judgment of a lower court was incorrect and should be set aside</p><p><i>n.</i> turning in the opposite direction [reverse, reversion, turnabout, turnaround]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of reversing the order or place of [transposition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a major change in attitude or principle or point of view [about-face, policy change, volte-face]</p><p><b>invertirati, inverzni, maknut unazad, mijenjati pravac, naličje, naličju, naopak, natraške, neuspjeh, obrnut, obrnuti, okrenuti, oprečnost, poništiti, preinačiti, preokrenuti, promijeniti, revers, reverzni, stražnji, suprotan, suprotnost, ukinuti, kontrarnost, okretanje, prekretanje, reverzija, izokrenuti, izokretati, obrtati, preokretati, svrgnuti, dokinuti, lift, napustiti, opozvati, prevrnuti, ukidanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relation of direct opposition [contrary, opposite]</p><p><i>n.</i> the gears by which the motion of a machine can be reversed [reverse gear]</p><p><i>n.</i> an unfortunate happening that hinders or impedes [black eye, blow, reversal, setback]</p><p><i>n.</i> the side of a coin or medal that does not bear the principal design [verso]</p><p><i>n.</i> (American football) a running play in which a back running in one direction hands the ball to a back running in the opposite direction</p><p><i>n.</i> turning in the opposite direction [reversal, reversion, turnabout, turnaround]</p><p><i>v.</i> change to the contrary [change by reversal, turn]</p><p><i>v.</i> turn inside out or upside down [invert, turn back]</p><p><i>v.</i> rule against [override, overrule, overthrow, overturn]</p><p><i>v.</i> cancel officially [annul, countermand, lift, overturn, repeal, rescind, revoke, vacate]</p><p><i>v.</i> reverse the position, order, relation, or condition of [invert]</p><p><i>adj.</i> directed or moving toward the rear [rearward]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of the transmission gear causing backward movement in a motor vehicle</p><p><i>adj.</i> reversed (turned backward) in order or nature or effect [inverse]</p><p><b>Reversni rasjed</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a geological fault in which the upper side appears to have been pushed upward by compression [overthrust fault, thrust fault]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju električnih vozila od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the gears by which the motion of a machine can be reversed [reverse]</p><p><b>visak s rukama izduženim u leđa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hang with the arms extended in back</p><p><b>atmosferski praznici (traju 10 ms) koji pucaju sa vrha divovskih olujnih oblaka u plavim čunjama koji se šire dok bljeskaju prema gore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> atmospheric discharges (lasting 10 msec) bursting from the tops of giant storm clouds in blue cones that widen as they flash upward [blue jet, jet]</p><p><b>reverzna osmoza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) a method of producing pure water</p><p><b>obrnuta poljska notacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a parenthesis-free notation for forming mathematical expressions in which each operator follows its operands [postfix notation, suffix notation]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe primjenjuje samo na akcionare, to znači da se u slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ove Uredbe primjenjuje samo na akcionare, to znači da se u slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ove Uredbe primjenjuje samo na akcionare koji su u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ove Uredbe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a decrease in the number of outstanding shares of a corporation without changing the shareholders' equity [reverse stock split, split down]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe primjenjuje samo na akcionare, to znači da se u slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ove Uredbe primjenjuje samo na akcionare, to znači da se u slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (c) ove Uredbe primjenjuje samo na akcionare koji su u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ove Uredbe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a decrease in the number of outstanding shares of a corporation without changing the shareholders' equity [reverse split, split down]</p><p><b>polimeraza koja katalizira stvaranje DNK koristeći RNK kao predložak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a polymerase that catalyzes the formation of DNA using RNA as a template</p><p><b>antivirusni lijek koji inhibira djelovanje reverzne transkriptaze u retrovirusima kao što je HIV. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an antiviral drug that inhibits the action of reverse transcriptase in retroviruses such as HIV</p><p><b>obratni, obrnut, preokrenut, suprotan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> turned inside out and resewn</p><p><i>adj.</i> turned about in order or relation [converse, transposed]</p><p><b>invertirati, inverzni, maknut unazad, mijenjati pravac, naličje, naličju, naopak, natraške, neuspjeh, obrnut, obrnuti, okrenuti, oprečnost, poništiti, preinačiti, preokrenuti, promijeniti, revers, reverzni, stražnji, suprotan, suprotnost, ukinuti (od &quot;reverse&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an opposite way</p><p><b>kvaliteta da se može vratiti u bilo kojem smjeru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being reversible in either direction</p><p><b>koje se može okrenuti, povratni, s dva lica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a garment (especially a coat) that can be worn inside out (with either side of the cloth showing)</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of reversing or being reversed</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being reversed or used with either side out [two-sided]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being reversed</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of assuming or producing either of two states</p><p><b>Svaki proces u kojem se sustav može učiniti da prođe kroz ista stanja u obrnutom redu kada se proces obrne. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any process in which a system can be made to pass through the same states in the reverse order when the process is reversed</p><p><b>na reverzibilan način (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a reversible manner</p><p><b>termometar koji beleži temperaturu u dubokim vodama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thermometer that registers the temperature in deep waters</p><p><b>atavizam, naslijeđena osobina, obrtanje, okretanje, vraćanje, prekretanje, reverzija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) an interest in an estate that reverts to the grantor (or his heirs) at the end of some period (e.g., the death of the grantee)</p><p><i>n.</i> (genetics) a return to a normal phenotype (usually resulting from a second mutation)</p><p><i>n.</i> a reappearance of an earlier characteristic [atavism, throwback]</p><p><i>n.</i> turning in the opposite direction [reversal, reverse, turnabout, turnaround]</p><p><i>n.</i> returning to a former state [regress, regression, retrogression, retroversion]</p><p><i>n.</i> a failure to maintain a higher state [backsliding, lapse, lapsing, relapse, relapsing, reverting]</p><p><b>nasljedni, rekurzivni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or involving a reversion (especially a legal reversion)</p><p><b>nasljedna renta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an annuity payable to one person in the event that someone else is unable to receive it [survivorship annuity]</p><p><b>atavizam, naslijeđena osobina, obrtanje, okretanje, vraćanje (od &quot;reversion&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a party who is entitled to an estate in reversion</p><p><b>netko tko se povlači u prethodne neželjene obrasce ponašanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who lapses into previous undesirable patterns of behavior [backslider, recidivist]</p><p><b>koji se okreće nazad. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to be turned back [returning]</p><p><b>okrenuti, povrat na staro, povratiti se, vratiti, vratiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> go back to a previous state [regress, retrovert, return, turn back]</p><p><i>v.</i> undergo reversion, as in a mutation</p><p><b>da se vrati bivšem vlasniku ili naslednicima tog vlasnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> to be returned to the former owner or that owner's heirs</p><p><b>okrenuti, povrat na staro, povratiti se, vratiti, vratiti se (od &quot;revert&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a failure to maintain a higher state [backsliding, lapse, lapsing, relapse, relapsing, reversion]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to return to an earlier state [returning]</p><p><b>maštanje, sanjarenje, sanjarija, sanjaranje, snatrenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abstracted state of absorption [reverie]</p><p><i>n.</i> absentminded dreaming while awake [air castle, castle in Spain, castle in the air, daydream, daydreaming, oneirism, reverie]</p><p><b>obložiti, obložiti zid</b></p><p><i>v.</i> construct a revetment</p><p><i>v.</i> face with a layer of stone or concrete or other supporting material so as to retain</p><p><b>Sastav za podizanje vode (pojedino zidarstvo) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a facing (usually masonry) that supports an embankment [revetment, stone facing]</p><p><b>obloga, oplata</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a barrier against explosives</p><p><i>n.</i> a facing (usually masonry) that supports an embankment [revetement, stone facing]</p><p><b>časopis, članak, ispitati, ispitivati, izvješće, kritika, magazin, nadzirati, ocijeniti, ocjena, ocjenjivanje, osvrt, ponavljanje, ponovni pregled, ponovno ispitati, ponovno ispitivanje, ponovo ispitati, pregled, pregledati, pregledavati, pregledni, preispitati, preispitivanje, preispitivati, prikaz, prikazati, prosuditi, provjera, rasprava, razmatranje, razmotriti, recenzija, recenzirati, revidirati, revija, revizija, smotra, kontrola, sažetak, osvježavanje, usavršavanje, inspekcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a new appraisal or evaluation [reappraisal, reassessment, revaluation]</p><p><i>n.</i> an essay or article that gives a critical evaluation (as of a book or play) [critical review, critique, review article]</p><p><i>n.</i> a subsequent examination of a patient for the purpose of monitoring earlier treatment [follow-up, followup, reexamination]</p><p><i>n.</i> (accounting) a service (less exhaustive than an audit) that provides some assurance to interested parties as to the reliability of financial data [limited review]</p><p><i>n.</i> a variety show with topical sketches and songs and dancing and comedians [revue]</p><p><i>n.</i> a periodical that publishes critical essays on current affairs or literature or art</p><p><i>n.</i> a summary at the end that repeats the substance of a longer discussion [recap, recapitulation]</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a judicial reexamination of the proceedings of a court (especially by an appellate court)</p><p><i>n.</i> practice intended to polish performance or refresh the memory [brushup]</p><p><i>n.</i> a formal or official examination [inspection]</p><p><i>v.</i> look at again [reexamine]</p><p><i>v.</i> appraise critically [critique]</p><p><i>v.</i> hold a review (of troops) [go over, survey]</p><p><i>v.</i> refresh one's memory [brush up, refresh]</p><p><i>v.</i> look back upon (a period of time, sequence of events) [look back, retrospect]</p><p><b>kritika, recenzija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an essay or article that gives a critical evaluation (as of a book or play) [critical review, critique, review]</p><p><b>kopija novopublirane knjige koja se šalje piscu ili časopisu za recenziju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a copy of a newly published book that is sent for review to a writer or periodical</p><p><b>kritičar, ocjenjivač, recenzent</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who reads manuscripts and judges their suitability for publication [reader, referee]</p><p><i>n.</i> a writer who reports and analyzes events of the day [commentator]</p><p><b>stajalište s kojeg se može pregledati parada ili vojna snaga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stand from which a parade or military force can be reviewed</p><p><b>govoriti oštro, govoriti teško, izgrditi, mrziti, napadati krivim govorom, nasrtati, ukoriti govorom, ogovarati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> spread negative information about [rail, vilify, vituperate]</p><p><b>grdnja, pogrda, uvreda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rude expression intended to offend or hurt [abuse, contumely, insult, vilification]</p><p><b>ponovni pregled, revizija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of rewriting something [rescript, revise, revision]</p><p><b>ispraviti, izmijeniti, ponavljati, ponoviti, ponovno pregledati, ponovo pregled., pregled, preispitati, preraditi, promijeniti, revidirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of rewriting something [rescript, revisal, revision]</p><p><i>v.</i> make revisions in</p><p><i>v.</i> revise or reorganize, especially for the purpose of updating and improving [retool]</p><p><b>ispravljen, pregledan, promijenjen, revidirani</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> improved or brought up to date</p><p><i>adj.</i> altered or revised by rephrasing or by adding or deleting material</p><p><b>Revizija američkog Standardnog prevode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a revision of the American Standard Version</p><p><b>britanski preispitivanje Authorized Version (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a British revision of the Authorized Version</p><p><b>korektor, popravljač, revizor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who puts text into appropriate form for publication [redact, redactor, rewrite man, rewriter]</p><p><b>revizijski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> editing that involves writing something again [rewriting]</p><p><b>ispravljanje, ponavljanje, ponovni pregled, preradba, prerađeno izdanje, revision, revizija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of revising or altering (involving reconsideration and modification) [alteration]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of rewriting something [rescript, revisal, revise]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that has been written again [rescript, rewrite]</p><p><b>revizionizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any dangerous departure from the teachings of Marx</p><p><i>n.</i> a moderate evolutionary form of Marxism</p><p><b>revizionistički</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Communist who tries to rewrite Marxism to justify a retreat from the revolutionary position</p><p><b>ponovo posjetiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> visit again</p><p><b>revitalizacija, obnavljanje, obnova, oživljavanje, ponovni procvat, preporod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bringing again into activity and prominence [resurgence, revitalization, revival, revivification]</p><p><b>dati novi život ili snagu da (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give new life or vigor to [revitalize]</p><p><b>vraćen novom životu i snagu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> restored to new life and vigor [reborn, revitalized]</p><p><b>koji imaju tendenciju da daju novi život i snagu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to impart new life and vigor to [renewing, restorative, revitalizing, reviving]</p><p><b>revitalizacija, revitalizaciji, obnavljanje, obnova, oživljavanje, ponovni procvat, preporod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bringing again into activity and prominence [resurgence, revitalisation, revival, revivification]</p><p><b>oživjeti, preporoditi se, regenerirati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> restore strength [regenerate]</p><p><i>v.</i> give new life or vigor to [revitalise]</p><p><b>oživljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> restored to new life and vigor [reborn, revitalised]</p><p><b>oživjeti (od &quot;revitalize&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to impart new life and vigor to [renewing, restorative, revitalising, reviving]</p><p><b>liječnik, obnova, oporavak, oživljavanje, ponovno oživljavanje, preporod, procvat, obnavljanje, ponovni procvat, revitalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bringing again into activity and prominence [resurgence, revitalisation, revitalization, revivification]</p><p><i>n.</i> an evangelistic meeting intended to reawaken interest in religion [revival meeting]</p><p><b>skupština za propovijedanje koja je trebala probuditi interesovanje za religiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an evangelistic meeting intended to reawaken interest in religion [revival]</p><p><b>Pokušaj da se probudi evanđeoska vjera. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an attempt to reawaken the evangelical faith</p><p><b>evanđelist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a preacher of the Christian gospel [evangelist, gospeler, gospeller]</p><p><b>evanđelist (od &quot;revivalist&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characterizing revivalism</p><p><b>obnoviti, ponovno oživjeti, ponovo oživjeti, povratiti se, probuditi, uspostaviti, oživeti, oživjeti, revitalizirati, oživljavati, animirati, oživotvoriti, uskrsnuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to regain consciousness [resuscitate]</p><p><i>v.</i> give new life or energy to [animate, quicken, reanimate, recreate, renovate, repair, revivify, vivify]</p><p><i>v.</i> be brought back to life, consciousness, or strength</p><p><i>v.</i> restore from a depressed, inactive, or unused state [resurrect]</p><p><i>v.</i> return to consciousness [come to, resuscitate]</p><p><b>Vratio sam svijest ili život ili snagu., davao svjež život ili snagu ili duh (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> restored to consciousness or life or vigor</p><p><i>adj.</i> given fresh life or vigor or spirit [reanimated]</p><p><b>obnavljanje, obnova, oživljavanje, ponovni procvat, preporod, revitalizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bringing again into activity and prominence [resurgence, revitalisation, revitalization, revival]</p><p><b>animirati, oživotvoriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give new life or energy to [animate, quicken, reanimate, recreate, renovate, repair, revive, vivify]</p><p><b>obnoviti, ponovno oživjeti, ponovo oživjeti, povratiti se, probuditi, uspostaviti, oživeti, oživjeti, revitalizirati (od &quot;revive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to impart new life and vigor to [renewing, restorative, revitalising, revitalizing]</p><p><b>poništiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being revoked or annulled [revokable]</p><p><b>opoziv, opozivanje, revokacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being cancelled or annulled [annulment]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act (by someone having the authority) of annulling something previously done</p><p><b>U slučaju da se ne primjenjuje, to znači da se ne primjenjuje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being revoked or annulled [revocable]</p><p><b>obesnažiti, opozvati, pobijati, poništiti, poreći, pozvati, ukinuti, dokinuti, lift, napustiti, preokrenuti, prevrnuti, ukidanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the mistake of not following suit when able to do so [renege]</p><p><i>v.</i> fail to follow suit when able and required to do so</p><p><i>v.</i> cancel officially [annul, countermand, lift, overturn, repeal, rescind, reverse, vacate]</p><p><b>dizati bunu, gnušati se, izdići se, metež, odbijati, odmetnuti se, odvratnost, pobuna, pobuniti, pobuniti se, revolt, ustanak, ogaditi, zgaditi, zgroziti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> organized opposition to authority [insurrection, rebellion, rising, uprising]</p><p><i>v.</i> make revolution</p><p><i>v.</i> fill with distaste [disgust, gross out, repel]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause aversion in [churn up, disgust, nauseate, sicken]</p><p><b>odbijajući, odvratan, pobunjenički, ustanički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> highly offensive [disgustful, disgusting, distasteful, foul, loathly, loathsome, repellant, repellent, repelling, skanky, wicked, yucky]</p><p><b>odbijajući, odvratan, pobunjenički, ustanički (od &quot;revolting&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a disgusting manner or to a disgusting degree [disgustingly, distastefully, sickeningly]</p><p><b>jedan okret zemlje oko sunca, kružno kretanje, obrtaj, okret, okretaj, okretanje, preokret, prevrat, puč, revolucija, rotacija, zavrtaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drastic and far-reaching change in ways of thinking and behaving</p><p><i>n.</i> the overthrow of a government by those who are governed</p><p><i>n.</i> a single complete turn (axial or orbital) [gyration, rotation]</p><p><b>revolucionar, revolucionaran</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radical supporter of political or social revolution [revolutionist, subversive, subverter]</p><p><i>adj.</i> markedly new or introducing radical change [radical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic or causing an axial or orbital turn [rotatory]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or having the nature of a revolution</p><p><i>adj.</i> advocating or engaged in revolution</p><p><b>moćna i bogata teroristička organizacija osnovana 1957. kao gerilska ruka kolumbijske komunističke stranke. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a powerful and wealthy terrorist organization formed in 1957 as the guerilla arm of the Colombian communist party [FARC, Fuerzas Armadas Revolucionarios de Colombia]</p><p><b>kalendar koji je usvojila prva Francuska Republika 1793. i napušta 1805. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the calendar adopted by the first French Republic in 1793 and abandoned in 1805</p><p><b>mjesec u revolucionarnom kalendaru. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a month in the Revolutionary calendar</p><p><b>politička jedinica organizirana za promicanje revolucije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political unit organized to promote revolution</p><p><b>Šiitska teroristička organizacija sa snažnim vezama s Iranom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Shiite terrorist organization with strong ties to Iran [Hezbollah, Hizballah, Hizbollah, Hizbullah, Islamic Jihad, Islamic Jihad for the Liberation of Palestine, Lebanese Hizballah, Organization of the Oppressed on Earth, Party of God]</p><p><b>Marksističko-lenjinistička teroristička organizacija u Grčkoj koja se nasilno protivi imperijalizmu i kapitalizmu i NATO-u i Sjedinjenim Državama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Marxist-Leninist terrorist organization in Greece that is violently opposed to imperialism and capitalism and NATO and the United States [17 November]</p><p><b>Palestinska međunarodna teroristička organizacija koja se odvojila od PLO-a 1974. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Palestinian international terrorist organization that split from the PLO in 1974 [ANO, Abu Nidal Organization, Arab Revolutionary Brigades, Black September, Fatah-RC, Fatah Revolutionary Council]</p><p><b>Ekstremna marksistička teroristička organizacija u Turskoj koja se protivi NATO-u i Sjedinjenim Državama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extreme Marxist terrorist organization in Turkey that is opposed to NATO and the United States [Revolutionary People's Liberation Party]</p><p><b>Ekstremna marksistička teroristička organizacija u Turskoj koja se protivi NATO-u i Sjedinjenim Državama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extreme Marxist terrorist organization in Turkey that is opposed to NATO and the United States [Revolutionary People's Liberation Front]</p><p><b>ekstremno lijevska teroristička grupa osnovana u Grčkoj 1971. godine kako bi se suprotstavila vojnoj hunti koja je vladala Grčkom od 1967. do 1974. godine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an extreme leftist terrorist group formed in Greece in 1971 to oppose the military junta that ruled Greece from 1967 to 1974 [ELA]</p><p><b>gradski udarni odjel i gerilska grupa Komunističke partije na Filipinima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an urban hit squad and guerrilla group of the Communist Party in the Philippines [ABB, Alex Boncayao Brigade, RPA-ABB]</p><p><b>Tajna grupa ljevičarskih ekstremista koji se protive talijanskoj radnoj politici i vanjskoj politici. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a clandestine group of leftist extremists who oppose Italy's labor policies and foreign policy [NIPR, Revolutionary Proletarian Nucleus]</p><p><b>Tajna grupa ljevičarskih ekstremista koji se protive talijanskoj radnoj politici i vanjskoj politici. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a clandestine group of leftist extremists who oppose Italy's labor policies and foreign policy [NIPR, Revolutionary Proletarian Initiative Nuclei]</p><p><b>Teroristička grupa osnovana 1980-ih u Sijera Leoneu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a terrorist group formed in the 1980s in Sierra Leone [RUF]</p><p><b>pobuniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> fill with revolutionary ideas [inspire, revolutionize]</p><p><i>v.</i> change radically [overturn, revolutionize]</p><p><b>Vjerovanje u širenje revolucionarnih principa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a belief in the spread of revolutionary principles</p><p><b>revolucionar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radical supporter of political or social revolution [revolutionary, subversive, subverter]</p><p><b>pobuniti, preinačiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> change radically [overturn, revolutionise]</p><p><i>v.</i> overthrow by a revolution, of governments</p><p><i>v.</i> fill with revolutionary ideas [inspire, revolutionise]</p><p><b>brzina obrta motora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rate of revolution of a motor [rev, rpm]</p><p><b>obrtati se, okretati, okretati se, promišljati, razmišljati, rotirati, smjenjivati, kružiti, obrnuti se, okrenuti se, vrtjeti se, zavrtjeti se, kotrljati, koturati, obrnuti, obrtati, otkotrljati, otkoturati, rolati, valjati, vrtjeti, zakotrljati, zakoturati, zarolati, zarotirati, zavaljati, zavrtjeti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> turn on or around an axis or a center [go around, rotate]</p><p><i>v.</i> move in an orbit [orb, orbit]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to move by turning over or in a circular manner of as if on an axis [roll]</p><p><b>centrirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> center upon [center, center on, concentrate on, focus on, revolve around]</p><p><b>centrirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> center upon [center, center on, concentrate on, focus on, revolve about]</p><p><i>v.</i> move around in a circular motion [circle around, circle round]</p><p><b>okrenuti u krug oko osi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> turned in a circle around an axis [rotated]</p><p><b>pištolj, revolver</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pistol with a revolving cylinder (usually having six chambers for bullets) [six-gun, six-shooter]</p><p><i>n.</i> a door consisting of four orthogonal partitions that rotate about a central pivot [revolving door]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ovog članka ne primjenjuju primjene ove Uredbe, u slučaju da se primjenjuju primjene ove Uredbe, primjenjuje se sljedeći uvjet: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a charge account that does not have to be paid to zero balance</p><p><b>revolving akreditiv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a consumer credit line that can be used up to a certain limit or paid down at any time [charge account credit, open-end credit]</p><p><b>Organizacija ili institucija s visokom stopom promjena osoblja ili članstva, vrata koja se sastoje od četiri pravougaona pregrada koja se okreću oko središnjega okretača (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organization or institution with a high rate of turnover of personnel or membership</p><p><i>n.</i> a door consisting of four orthogonal partitions that rotate about a central pivot [revolver]</p><p><b>obrtni fond</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fund which, if borrowed or used, is intended to be replenished so it may be loaned or spent repeatedly</p><p><b>revija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety show with topical sketches and songs and dancing and comedians [review]</p><p><b>nagla promjena, odvratnost, preokret, averzija, odbojnost, zazor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> intense aversion [horror, repugnance, repulsion]</p><p><b>tanko elegantno stablo sa Novog Zelanda koje ima crvene cveće i daje dragocjeno crveno drvo s mrljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender elegant tree of New Zealand having racemes of red flowers and yielding valuable mottled red timber [New Zealand honeysuckle]</p><p><b>nagrada, nagraditi, naknaditi, odati priznanje, odmazda, plaća, ucjena, plata, prednost, honorirati, nagrađivati, nadoknaditi, nadoknađivati, uzvratiti, uzvraćati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a recompense for worthy acts or retribution for wrongdoing [payoff, wages]</p><p><i>n.</i> payment made in return for a service rendered</p><p><i>n.</i> an act performed to strengthen approved behavior [reinforcement]</p><p><i>n.</i> the offer of money for helping to find a criminal or for returning lost property</p><p><i>n.</i> benefit resulting from some event or action [advantage]</p><p><i>v.</i> bestow honor or rewards upon [honor, honour]</p><p><i>v.</i> strengthen and support with rewards [reinforce]</p><p><i>v.</i> act or give recompense in recognition of someone's behavior or actions [pay back, repay]</p><p><b>Nuditi ili proizvoditi nagradu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> offering or productive of reward</p><p><b>koji se isplati, koristan, vrijedan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> providing personal satisfaction</p><p><b>koji se isplati, koristan, vrijedan (od &quot;rewarding&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a rewarding manner</p><p><b>premotati, premotavanje, premotavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> wind (up) again</p><p><b>obezbediti novu žičaru (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> provide with new wiring</p><p><b>ponoviti, preformulirati, parafrazirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> express the same message in different words [paraphrase, rephrase]</p><p><b>ponoviti, preformulirati (od &quot;reword&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> changing a particular word or phrase [recasting, rephrasing]</p><p><b>adaptirati, preinačiti, prerada, preraditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> use again in altered form [make over, retread]</p><p><b>nanovo napisati, ponovno ispisati, ponovno napisati, ponovno upisati (prepisati podatke pohranjene u me, prepisati, prepisivanje, preraditi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that has been written again [rescript, revision]</p><p><i>v.</i> write differently</p><p><i>v.</i> rewrite so as to make fit to suit a new or different purpose</p><p><b>osoba koja stavlja tekst u odgovarajući oblik za objavljivanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who puts text into appropriate form for publication [redact, redactor, reviser, rewriter]</p><p><b>nanovo napisati, ponovno ispisati, ponovno napisati, ponovno upisati (prepisati podatke pohranjene u me, prepisati, prepisivanje, preraditi (od &quot;rewrite&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who puts text into appropriate form for publication [redact, redactor, reviser, rewrite man]</p><p><b>prerada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> editing that involves writing something again [revising]</p><p><b>Muški vladar. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a male sovereign [king, male monarch]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih obično rizomatnih hibridnih begonija koje potiču od istočnoindijske biljke s grubim teksturiranim listovima s masnim i bronzanim uzorcima i ljubičastom i crveno-sjedom s neopažavanim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous usually rhizomatous hybrid begonias derived from an East Indian plant having rough-textured leaves patterned in silver and bronze and purple and red-brown with inconspicuous flowers [Begonia rex, beefsteak geranium, king begonia, painted-leaf begonia]</p><p><b>Engleski glumac na pozornici i u filmovima (1908-1990) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English actor on stage and in films (1908-1990) [Harrison, Reginald Carey Harrison, Sir Rex Harrison]</p><p><b>primjena lijekova za liječenje bolesti u malim djeci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acquired encephalopathy following acute viral infections (especially influenza or chicken pox) in young children</p><p><b>Čileanski pjesnik (1904-1973) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chilean poet (1904-1973) [Neftali Ricardo Reyes, Neruda, Pablo Neruda]</p><p><b>Glavni grad i glavna luka Islanda na jugozapadnoj obali Islanda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and chief port of Iceland on the southwestern coast of Iceland [capital of Iceland]</p><p><b>konvencionalno ime za lisicu koja se koristi u pričama nakon upotrebe u starom epu `Reynard the Fox' (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conventional name for a fox used in tales following usage in the old epic `Reynard the Fox'</p><p><b>Engleski slikar portreta i prvi predsjednik Kraljevske akademije (1723-1792) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English portrait painter and first president of the Royal Academy (1723-1792) [Sir Joshua Reynolds]</p><p><b>Rf, atomski broj 104, ruthefordij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance produced by the hypothalamus that is capable of accelerating the secretion of a given hormone by the anterior pituitary gland [releasing factor, releasing hormone]</p><p><i>n.</i> a radioactive transuranic element which has been synthesized [Unq, atomic number 104, element 104, rutherfordium, unnilquadium]</p><p><i>n.</i> a complex neural network in