s of Arctic regions [woolly rhinoceros]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih velikih uglavnom tropskih bubaca s rogovima na glavi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various large chiefly tropical beetles having horns on the head</p><p><b>nosorozi, porodica Rhinocerotidae, porodica nosoroga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhinoceroses [Rhinocerotidae, family Rhinocerotidae]</p><p><b>koji ima jedan rog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having one horn [Indian rhinoceros]</p><p><b>nosorozi, porodica Rhinocerotidae, porodica nosoroga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhinoceroses [family Rhinocerotidae, rhinoceros family]</p><p><b>specijalista za bolesti uha, nosa ili grla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialist in the disorders of the ear or nose or throat [ENT man, ear-nose-and-throat doctor, otolaryngologist, otorhinolaryngologist]</p><p><b>otorinolaringologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the medical specialty that deals with diseases of the ear, nose and throat [otolaryngology, otorhinolaryngology]</p><p><b>Štakori s listnim nosom iz Starog svijeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World leaf-nosed bats [family Rhinolophidae]</p><p><b>narandžasti šišmiši potkopate (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orange horseshoe bats [genus Rhinonicteris]</p><p><b>Obični šišmiša sjeverozapadne Australije s narančastim ili žutim krznom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common bat of northwestern Australia having orange or yellow fur [orange bat, orange horseshoe bat]</p><p><b>bilo kakva bolest ili malformacija nosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any disease or malformation of the nose</p><p><b>povećanje nosa s dilatacijom folikula i crvenilo i istaknuta vaskularnost kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enlargement of the nose with dilation of follicles and redness and prominent vascularity of the skin [brandy nose, copper nose, hammer nose, hypertrophic rosacea, potato nose, rum-blossom, rum nose, toper's nose]</p><p><b>kozmetička operacija za poboljšanje izgleda nosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cosmetic surgery to improve the appearance of your nose [nose job]</p><p><