v.</i> in a rich manner [high, luxuriously]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a rich and lavish manner [extravagantly, lavishly]</p><p><b>Glavni grad države Virginia smješten u istočnom središnjem dijelu države (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capital of the state of Virginia located in the east central part of the state [capital of Virginia]</p><p><b>kardinalci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cardinals [genus Richmondena]</p><p><b>Punočastog sjevernoameričkog pimpeka s crvenim perjem u mužjaku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crested thick-billed North American finch having bright red plumage in the male [Cardinalis cardinalis, cardinal, cardinal grosbeak, redbird]</p><p><b>bogatstva, bogatstvo, jačina, plodnost, sjajnost, sočnost, imuanost, obilje, impresivnost, veličanstvenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being extremely abundant [cornucopia, profuseness, profusion]</p><p><i>n.</i> abundant wealth [affluence]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of a sensation that is rich and pleasing [fullness, mellowness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of having high intrinsic value</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of producing abundantly and sustaining vigorous and luxuriant growth [fertility, prolificacy, rankness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a strong deep vividness of hue</p><p><i>n.</i> splendid or imposing in size or appearance [grandness, impressiveness, magnificence]</p><p><b>magnitudna ljestvica, Richterova ljestvica, Richterova skala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a logarithmic scale of 1 to 10 formerly used to express the magnitude of an earthquake on the basis of the size of seismograph oscillations</p><p><b>Vječna biljka s jakim mirisom, s oštrijim i šiljatim listovima i plitkom žuto-žutih cvijeća., biljke rodova Pilea s spušteni zelenim cvjetnim grmovima i glatkim prozirnim stabljikama i lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect perennial strong-scented with serrate pointed leaves and a loose panicle of yellowish flowers [Collinsonia canadensis, horse balm, horseweed, stone-root, stone root, stoneroot]</p><p><i>n.</i> a plants of the genus Pilea having drooping green flower clusters and smooth translucent stems and leaves [Pilea pumilla, clearweed, dead nettle]</p><p><b>toksičan protein izvlačen iz ricinskog zrna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic protein extracted from castor beans [ricin toxin]</p><p><b>toksičan protein izvlačen iz ricinskog zrna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic protein extracted from castor beans [ricin]</p><p><b>uljezna masna kiselina koja se nalazi u ricinskom ulju i koristi se u sapunu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oily fatty acid found in castor oil and used in soap</p><p><b>rod biljaka koji ima samo jednu poznatu vrstu: biljka ricinskog ulja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of herb having only one known species: castor-oil plant [genus Ricinus]</p><p><b>veliki grm iz tropske Afrike i Azije s velikim palmatnim listovima i trnastima kapsulama koje sadrže sjeme koje je izvor ricinskog ulja i ricina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large shrub of tropical Africa and Asia having large palmate leaves and spiny capsules containing seeds that are the source of castor oil and ricin [castor-oil plant, castor bean plant, palma christ, palma christi]</p><p><b>plast, stog, frkati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a painful muscle spasm especially in the neck or back (`rick' and `wrick' are British) [crick, kink, wrick]</p><p><i>n.</i> a stack of hay [hayrick, haystack]</p><p><i>v.</i> pile in ricks</p><p><i>v.</i> twist suddenly so as to sprain [sprain, turn, twist, wrench, wrick]</p><p><b>Najplemenitiji američki borbeni pilot u Prvom svjetskom ratu (1890-1973) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the most decorated United States combat pilot in World War I (1890-1973) [Eddie Rickenbacker, Edward Vernon Rickenbacker]</p><p><b>kvaliteta nepostojanja stabilnog ili sigurno fiksiranog na mjestu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of not being steady or securely fixed in place [unsteadiness]</p><p><b>rahitis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> childhood disease caused by deficiency of vitamin D and sunlight associated with impaired metabolism of calcium and phosphorus [rachitis]</p><p><b>bilo koja od grupe vrlo malih šipkičastih bakterija koje žive u ugrizujućim članonožcima (kao što su krpelji i glodovi) i uzrokuju bolest kod kralježnjaka domaćina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a group of very small rod-shaped bacteria that live in biting arthropods (as ticks and mites) and cause disease in vertebrate hosts</p><p><b>mikroorganizam sličan bakteriji koji živi u tkivima članonožaka, ali je sposoban uzrokovati bolesti kod kralježnjaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> microorganism resembling bacteria inhabiting arthropod tissues but capable of causing disease in vertebrates [family Rickettsiaceae]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na ili uzrokuju riketzije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or caused by rickettsias</p><p><b>infekcijska bolest uzrokovana krpeljima ili glodama ili ušiju zaraženim reketsijalnom bakterijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> infectious disease caused by ticks or mites or body lice infected with rickettsial bacteria [rickettsiosis]</p><p><b>Plejomorfni Gram negativni mikroorganizmi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pleomorphic Gram-negative microorganisms [order Rickettsiales]</p><p><b>blage zarazne bolesti uzrokovane bakterijom rodova Rickettsia prenosi se na ljude ugrizemg mice koja živi na glodavcima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mild infectious rickettsial disease caused by a bacterium of the genus Rickettsia transmitted to humans by the bite a mite that lives on rodents</p><p><b>infekcijska bolest uzrokovana krpeljima ili glodama ili ušiju zaraženim reketsijalnom bakterijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> infectious disease caused by ticks or mites or body lice infected with rickettsial bacteria [rickettsial disease]</p><p><b>klimav, nestabilan, rahitičan, slab, trošan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined to shake as from weakness or defect [shaky, wobbly, wonky]</p><p><i>adj.</i> affected with, suffering from, or characteristic of rickets [rachitic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking bodily or muscular strength or vitality [de