ovodi primjena ovog članka, za svaki period od 1. do 2. godine, poduzeće može provesti provjeru u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the occurrence of incoming water (between a low tide and the following high tide) [flood, flood tide]</p><p><b>Jahač se diže s sedla svaki drugi korak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the rider rises from the saddle every second stride</p><p><b>izložiti se opasnosti, odlučiti se, odluke bazirane na stupnju rizika, opasnost, riskirati, rizičnost, rizik, reskirati, rizika, rizikom, riziku, rizična, rizikovati, pogibao, pogibelj, izlagati se, izložiti se, hazardirati, kockati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a source of danger [endangerment, hazard, jeopardy, peril]</p><p><i>n.</i> a venture undertaken without regard to possible loss or injury [danger, peril]</p><p><i>n.</i> the probability of becoming infected given that exposure to an infectious agent has occurred [risk of infection]</p><p><i>n.</i> the probability of being exposed to an infectious agent [risk of exposure]</p><p><i>v.</i> expose to a chance of loss or damage [lay on the line, put on the line]</p><p><i>v.</i> take a risk in the hope of a favorable outcome [adventure, chance, gamble, hazard, run a risk, take a chance, take chances]</p><p><b>arbitraža koja uključuje rizik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> arbitrage involving risk [takeover arbitrage]</p><p><b>Sredstva dostupna za ulaganje u nova ili spekulativna poduzeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wealth available for investment in new or speculative enterprises [venture capital]</p><p><b>mogućnost izloženosti zaraznom uzročniku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the probability of being exposed to an infectious agent [risk]</p><p><b>Vjerojatnost zaraze zbog izloženosti zaraznom agensu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the probability of becoming infected given that exposure to an infectious agent has occurred [risk]</p><p><b>osoba koja rizikuje gubitak ili ozljedu u nadi da će dobiti ili uzbuditi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who risks loss or injury in the hope of gain or excitement [gambler]</p><p><b>nerizičan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> thought to be devoid of risk [riskless, unhazardous]</p><p><b>rizično</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a dangerously risky manner</p><p><b>stanje opasnosti koje uključuje rizik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of danger involving risk [peril]</p><p><b>bezopasan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> thought to be devoid of risk [risk-free, unhazardous]</p><p><b>bezopasan (od &quot;riskless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> safety as a consequence of entailing no risk</p><p><b>dvosmislen, mastan, riskantan, rizičan, slan, škakljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving risk or danger [hazardous, wild]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not financially safe or secure [bad, high-risk, speculative]</p><p><b>avantura, pustolovina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wild and exciting undertaking (not necessarily lawful) [adventure, dangerous undertaking, escapade]</p><p><b>rižoto</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rice cooked with broth and sprinkled with grated cheese [Italian rice]</p><p><b>koji sugeriše seksualno neprikladnost (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suggestive of sexual impropriety [blue, gamey, gamy, juicy, naughty, racy, spicy]</p><p><b>predposljednji pleistocenski ledenjaci u Alpama i naslage koje su se nalazile u to vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the next-to-last Pleistocene glaciation in the Alps and the deposits laid down at that time</p><p><b>rod Laridae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Laridae [genus Rissa]</p><p><b>s masnim masnim tkivom od 10 kg ili više, ali ne više od 10 kg (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> minced cooked meat or fish coated in egg and breadcrumbs and fried in deep fat</p><p><b>(Glazba) postupno smanjuje tempo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (music) gradually decreasing in tempo [rallentando, ritardando, ritenuto]</p><p><b>stimulans centralnog živčanog sustava (trgovinski naziv Ritalin) koji se koristi u liječenju narkolepsije kod odraslih i poremećaja nedostatka pažnje kod djece (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> central nervous system stimulant (trade name Ritalin) used in the treatment of narcolepsy in adults and attention deficit disorder in children [methylphenidate]</p><p><b>(Glazba) postupno smanjuje tempo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (music) gradually decreasing in tempo [rallentando, rit., ritenuto]</p><p><b>običaj, obred, ritual, vjerska ceremonija, religijski obred, vjerski obred</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an established ceremony prescribed by a religion [religious rite]</p><p><i>n.</i> any customary observance or practice [ritual]</p><p><b>ritual koji se izvodi u nekim kulturama u vrijeme kada pojedinac mijenja status (kao što je od adolescencije do odraslog doba) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ritual performed in some cultures at times when an individual changes status (as from adolescence to adulthood)</p><p><b>(Glazba) postupno smanjuje tempo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (music) gradually decreasing in tempo [rallentando, rit., ritardando]</p><p><b>inhibitor proteaze (trgovinski naziv Norvir) koji se koristi u liječenju HIV-a (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a protease inhibitor (trade name Norvir) used in treating HIV [Norvir]</p><p><b>Američki astronom je rekao da je napravio prvi teleskop napravljen u Americi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States astronomer said to have built the first telescope made in America [David Rittenhouse]</p><p><b>mit, običaj, obred, obredni, ritual, ritualni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any customary observance or practice [rite]</p><p><i>n.</i> the prescribed procedure for conducting religious ceremonies</p><p><i>n.</i> stereotyped behavior</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of religious rituals</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or employed in social rites or rituals</p><p><b>ples koji je dio vjerskih rituala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dance that is part of a religious ritual [ceremonial dance, ritual dancing]</p><p><b>ples koji je dio vjerskih rituala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dance that is part of a religious ritual [ceremonial dance, ritual dance]</p><p><b>žrtvovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of killing (an animal or person) in order to propitiate a deity [sacrifice]</p><p><b>napraviti ili evoluirati u ritual (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make or evolve into a ritual [ritualize]</p><p><b>proučavanje vjerskih ili magičnih obreda i ceremonija, pretjerano naglašavanje važnosti obreda ili ritualizacije u obožavanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of religious or magical rites and ceremonies</p><p><i>n.</i> exaggerated emphasis on the importance of rites or ritualistic forms in worship</p><p><b>zagovornik strogog poštovanja ritualne forme, socijalni antropolog koji je stručnjak za obrede i ceremonije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of strict observance of ritualistic forms</p><p><i>n.</i> a social anthropologist who is expert on rites and ceremonies</p><p><b>od ili karakterizira ili se pridržava ritualizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or characterized by or adhering to ritualism</p><p><b>napraviti ili evoluirati u ritual (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make or evolve into a ritual [ritualise]</p><p><b>mit, običaj, obred, obredni, ritual, ritualni (od &quot;ritual&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a ceremonial manner [ceremonially]</p><p><b>Švicarski hotelar koji je stvorio lanac elegantnih hotela (1850-1918), ostvarenje elegancije, -Sjajan hotel. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Swiss hotelier who created a chain of elegant hotels (1850-1918) [Cesar Ritz]</p><p><i>n.</i> ostentatious display of elegance</p><p><i>n.</i> an ostentatiously elegant hotel</p><p><b>elegantan, luksuzan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> luxuriously elegant</p><p><b>konkurent, konkurirati, nadmetati se, protivnik, rival, suparnica, suparnički, suparnik, takmac, takmičar, takmičarski, takmičiti se, konkurencija, biti jednak, jednačiti, odgovarati, parirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the contestant you hope to defeat [challenger, competition, competitor, contender]</p><p><i>v.</i> be equal to in quality or ability [equal, match, touch]</p><p><i>v.</i> be the rival of