 around a pickle</p><p><b>Nordijski poglavar koji je postao prvi vojvoda Normandije (860-931) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Norse chieftain who became the first duke of Normandy (860-931) [Hrolf, Rolf]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se ne primjenjuje primjena članka 4. stavka 1. točke (b) Uredbe (EU) br. 575/2013, primjenjuje se sljedeće: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of changing the institution that invests your pension plan without incurring a tax penalty</p><p><b>(trademark) desktop rotirajući indeks kartice s uklanjivim karticama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (trademark) a desktop rotary card index with removable cards</p><p><b>debeo, niskog rasta, punačak, vrsta pudinga, zdepast</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rotund individual [butterball, fat person, fatso, fatty]</p><p><i>n.</i> pudding made of suet pastry spread with jam or fruit and rolled up and baked or steamed [roly-poly pudding]</p><p><i>adj.</i> short and plump [dumpy, podgy, pudgy, tubby]</p><p><b>svojstvo imati debelo i okruglo tijelo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of having a plump and round body [chubbiness, pudginess, tubbiness]</p><p><b>ROM, ispisna memorija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) memory whose contents can be accessed and read but cannot be changed [fixed storage, read-only memory, read-only storage]</p><p><b>Romi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a people with dark skin and hair who speak Romany and who traditionally live by seasonal work and fortunetelling [Bohemian, Gipsy, Gypsy, Romani, Romany, Rommany]</p><p><i>n.</i> capital and largest city of Italy [Eternal City, Italian capital, Rome, capital of Italy]</p><p><b>Romi (od &quot;roma&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the modern Greek vernacular [Demotic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to modern Greece or its inhabitants or its language</p><p><b>romaine</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lettuce with long dark-green leaves in a loosely packed elongated head [cos, cos lettuce, romaine lettuce]</p><p><b>zelena salata, romaine</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lettuce with long dark-green spoon-shaped leaves [Lactuca sativa longifolia, cos lettuce]</p><p><i>n.</i> lettuce with long dark-green leaves in a loosely packed elongated head [cos, cos lettuce, romaine]</p><p><b>Rimljanin, rimski, rimskog, antički, latinica, uspravna slova, rimska, rimsko, rimsku, katolik, latinski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a resident of modern Rome</p><p><i>n.</i> an inhabitant of the ancient Roman Empire</p><p><i>n.</i> a typeface used in ancient Roman inscriptions [roman letters, roman print, roman type]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic of people of Rome</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or derived from Rome (especially ancient Rome) [Romanic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of the modern type that most directly represents the type used in ancient Roman inscriptions</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or supporting Romanism [R.C., Roman Catholic, Romanist, papist, papistic, papistical, popish, romish]</p><p><b>roman u kojem su stvarne osobe i događaji prerušeni u izmišljene likove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a novel in which actual persons and events are disguised as fictional characters</p><p><b>alfabet razvijen od strane drevnih Rimljana koji služi za pisanje većine jezika zapadne Europe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the alphabet evolved by the ancient Romans which serves for writing most of the languages of western Europe [Latin alphabet]</p><p><b>okrugli luk koji je izveden iz jednog centra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a round arch drawn from a single center [semicircular arch]</p><p><b>rimska arhitektura</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the architecture of ancient Rome</p><p><b>bazilika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Roman building used for public administration [basilica]</p><p><b>rimska građevina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a building constructed by the ancient Romans</p><p><b>lunarni kalendar koji su koristili u drevnom Rimu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lunar calendar in use in ancient Rome</p><p><b>cilindrični vatromet koji projicira niz obojenih kugli vatre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cylindrical firework that projects a series of colored balls of fire</p><p><b>rimokatolički</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Roman Catholic Church</p><p><i>n.</i> the Christian Church based in the Vatican and presided over by a pope and an episcopal hierarchy [Church of Rome, Roman Catholic Church, Roman Church, Western Church]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or supporting Romanism [R.C., Roman, Romanist, papist, papistic, papistical, popish, romish]</p><p><b>Kršćanska crkva sa sjedištem u Vatikanu, koju predvodi papa i biskupska hijerarhija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Christian Church based in the Vatican and presided over by a pope and an episcopal hierarchy [Church of Rome, Roman Catholic, Roman Church, Western Church]</p><p><b>papa, pontifex</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the head of the Roman Catholic Church [Bishop of Rome, Catholic Pope, Holy Father, Vicar of Christ, pontiff, pope]</p><p><b>vjerovanja i prakse katoličke crkve sa sjedištem u Rimu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the beliefs and practices of the Catholic Church based in Rome [Romanism, papism]</p><p><b>Kršćanska crkva sa sjedištem u Vatikanu, koju predvodi papa i biskupska hijerarhija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Christian Church based in the Vatican and presided over by a pope and an episcopal hierarchy [Church of Rome, Roman Catholic, Roman Catholic Church, Western Church]</p><p><b>čvrsta bijela ovratnica bez otvora na prednjoj strani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stiff white collar with no opening in the front [clerical collar, dog collar]</p><p><b>biljka iz mediteranske regije s žarkim sjemenom koja se koristi kao i sjemena kamena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herb of the Mediterranean region having pungent seeds used like those of caraway [Nigella sativa, black caraway, nutmeg flower]</p><p><b>Bogovica koju su obožavali drevni Rimljani. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deity worshipped by the ancient Romans</p><p><b>vladar Rimskog carstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sovereign of the Roman Empire [Emperor of Rome]</p><p><