aknutim malo akvilnim mostom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nose with a prominent slightly aquiline bridge [hooknose]</p><p><b>simbol u starom rimskom znakovanju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a symbol in the old Roman notation</p><p><b>Američki lingvista (rođen u Rusiji) poznat po opisu fonoloških univerzala (1896-1982) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States linguist (born in Russia) noted for his description of the universals of phonology (1896-1982) [Jakobson, Roman Jakobson]</p><p><b>drevna rimska jedinica za dužinu (4.85 engleskih stopa) mjerena kao udaljenost od pete jednog stopala do pete iste noge kada se sljedeće dotakne zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Roman unit of length (4.85 English feet) measured as the distance from the heel of one foot to the heel of the same foot when next it touches the ground</p><p><b>tipografija koja se koristila u drevnim rimskim natpisima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a typeface used in ancient Roman inscriptions [roman, roman letters, roman type]</p><p><b>Stara rimska država od 509. godine prije Krista do Augusta koji je preuzeo vlast 27. godine prije Krista. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ancient Roman state from 509 BC until Augustus assumed power in 27 BC</p><p><b>vrijeme kada je Rim dominirao Europom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time period during which Rome dominated Europe</p><p><b>tipografija koja se koristila u drevnim rimskim natpisima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a typeface used in ancient Roman inscriptions [roman, roman letters, roman print]</p><p><b>Europski šum, glaukosa biljka sjeveroistočne Sjedinjenih Američkih Država i Kanade s labavim rascem žutih ružičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European wormwood [Artemis pontica]</p><p><i>n.</i> glaucous herb of northeastern United States and Canada having loose racemes of yellow-tipped pink flowers [Corydalis sempervirens, Fumaria sempervirens, rock harlequin]</p><p><b>umjetni jezik. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial language</p><p><b>besmislica, fantazirati, izmišljotine, pretjerivati, roman, romanca, romansa, romantična priča, sanjarenje, zanesenost, ljubavna veza, romantičan odnos, udvarati se, koketirati, očijukati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a relationship between two lovers [love affair]</p><p><i>n.</i> an exciting and mysterious quality (as of a heroic time or adventure) [romanticism]</p><p><i>n.</i> the group of languages derived from Latin [Latinian language, Romance language]</p><p><i>n.</i> a story dealing with love [love story]</p><p><i>n.</i> a novel dealing with idealized events remote from everyday life</p><p><i>v.</i> make amorous advances towards [court, solicit, woo]</p><p><i>v.</i> have a love affair with</p><p><i>v.</i> talk or behave amorously, without serious intentions [butterfly, chat up, coquet, coquette, dally, flirt, mash, philander]</p><p><i>v.</i> tell romantic or exaggerated lies</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to languages derived from Latin [Latin]</p><p><b>grupa jezika izvedenih iz latinskog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the group of languages derived from Latin [Latinian language, Romance]</p><p><b>romanika, romanike, romanička, romaničke</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a style of architecture developed in Italy and western Europe between the Roman and the Gothic styles after 1000 AD [Romanesque architecture]</p><p><b>stil arhitekture razvijen u Italiji i zapadnoj Europi između rimskog i gotičkog stila nakon 1000. godine n.e. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a style of architecture developed in Italy and western Europe between the Roman and the Gothic styles after 1000 AD [Romanesque]</p><p><b>romski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a people with dark skin and hair who speak Romany and who traditionally live by seasonal work and fortunetelling [Bohemian, Gipsy, Gypsy, Roma, Romany, Rommany]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Gypsies or their language or culture [Romany]</p><p><b>Rumunjska, Rumunjske</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic in southeastern Europe with a short coastline on the Black Sea [Roumania, Rumania]</p><p><b>Rumunj, rumunjski, Rumunjka, Rumunjski jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Romania [Rumanian]</p><p><i>n.</i> an eastern Romance language spoken in Romania [Rumanian]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of the country of Romania or its people or languages [Roumanian, Rumanian]</p><p><b>monetarna jedinica u Rumuniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Romania</p><p><b>romanike, rimski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or derived from Rome (especially ancient Rome) [Roman]</p><p><b>Pišite latinski alfabet. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> write in the Latin alphabet [Latinise, Latinize, Romanize]</p><p><b>vjerovanja i prakse katoličke crkve sa sjedištem u Rimu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the beliefs and practices of the Catholic Church based in Rome [Roman Catholicism, papism]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili podržava rimski (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or supporting Romanism [R.C., Roman, Roman Catholic, papist, papistic, papistical, popish, romish]</p><p><b>Pišite latinski alfabet. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> write in the Latin alphabet [Latinise, Latinize, Romanise]</p><p><b>član carske obitelji koja je vladala Rusijom., Ruska carska linija koja je vladala od 1613 do 1917. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the imperial family that ruled Russia [Romanov]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Russian imperial line that ruled from 1613 to 1917 [Romanov]</p><p><b>član carske obitelji koja je vladala Rusijom., Ruska carska linija koja je vladala od 1613 do 1917. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the imperial family that ruled Russia [Romanoff]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Russian imperial line that ruled from 1613 to 1917 [Romanoff]</p><p><b>Rimljani</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a New Testament book containing an exposition of the doctrines of Saint Paul [Epistle of Paul the Apostle to the Romans, Epistle to the Romans]</p><p><b>Rhaeto-romanski jezik koji se govori u jugoistočnoj Švicarskoj, od ili u vezi s romanškim jezikom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Rhaeto-