 goriva i goriva za proizvodnju električnih goriva i goriva za proizvodnju električnih goriva i goriva za proizvodnju električnih goriva i goriva za proizvodnju električnih goriva i goriva za proizvodnju električnih goriva i goriva za proizvodnju električnih goriva i goriva za proizvodnju elektri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> workplace consisting of a long narrow path or shed where rope is made [rope yard]</p><p><b>akrobat koji izvodi na užetu rastegnutom na određenoj visini iznad zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acrobat who performs on a rope stretched at some height above the ground [ropedancer]</p><p><b>prijevoz koji prevozi putnike ili teret u nosačima obješenih od kablova i podržanih nizom kula (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conveyance that transports passengers or freight in carriers suspended from cables and supported by a series of towers [aerial tramway, cable tramway, tram, tramway]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm, s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50%, (Britanski neformalni) vrlo loš kvalitet (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or resembling rope (or ropes) in being long and strong [ropy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> forming viscous or glutinous threads [ropy, stringy, thready]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (British informal) very poor in quality [ropy]</p><p><b>Ulica imena za flunitrazepan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> street names for flunitrazepan [Mexican valium, R-2, circle, forget me drug, roach, roofy, rope]</p><p><b>svojstvo da bude kohezivan i ljepljiv (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being cohesive and sticky [cohesiveness, glueyness, gluiness, gumminess, tackiness, viscidity, viscidness]</p><p><b>užad</b></p><p><i>n.</i> capturing cattle or horses with a lasso</p><p><b>ljepljiv, mizeran, nitast, slab, vlaknat, židak</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or resembling rope (or ropes) in being long and strong [ropey]</p><p><i>adj.</i> forming viscous or glutinous threads [ropey, stringy, thready]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (British informal) very poor in quality [ropey]</p><p><b>Roquefort</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French blue cheese</p><p><b>Vinaigrette s smoljanim Roquefortovim ili plavim sirom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vinaigrette containing crumbled Roquefort or blue cheese [blue cheese dressing]</p><p><b>rukola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect European annual often grown as a salad crop to be harvested when young and tender [Eruca sativa, Eruca vesicaria sativa, arugula, garden rocket, rocket, rocket salad]</p><p><b>za sve vrste iz rodova Roridula i Roridula spp. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of 2 species of the genus Roridula</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama koje su uključene u obitelj Droseraceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications included in the family Droseraceae [family Roridulaceae]</p><p><b>godišnje i višegodišnje biljke vlažnih staništa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual and perennial herbs of damp habitats [genus Rorippa]</p><p><b>višegodišnje biljke koje se nalaze na potokima i oblacima rijeka diljem Europe osim krajnjeg sjevera i Mediterana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial herb found on streams and riversides throughout Europe except extreme north and Mediterranean [Nasturtium amphibium, great yellowcress]</p><p><b>godišnji ili dvostruki krest koji raste na vlažnim mjestima ponekad se koristi u salatima ili kao biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual or biennial cress growing in damp places sometimes used in salads or as a potherb [marsh cress, yellow watercress]</p><p><b>višegodišnji evroazijski krest koji se uglavnom uzgaja u izvorima ili tekućoj vodi s mesnim oštrim listovima koji se koriste u salatima ili kao biljka ili ukras (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial Eurasian cress growing chiefly in springs or running water having fleshy pungent leaves used in salads or as a potherb or garnish [Nasturtium officinale, common watercress]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u pitanju vrsta koja se koristi za ribolov, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, mora se utvrditi da je ova vrsta ribolovna. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several baleen whales of the family Balaenopteridae having longitudinal grooves on the throat and a small pointed dorsal fin [razorback]</p><p><b>Projektivni testovi s bilateralno simetričnim mrljama mastila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a projective tests using bilaterally symmetrical inkblots [Rorschach test, inkblot test]</p><p><b>Projektivni testovi s bilateralno simetričnim mrljama mastila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a projective tests using bilaterally symmetrical inkblots [Rorschach, inkblot test]</p><p><b>rod Rosa, rod ruža, ruže</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large genus of erect or climbing prickly shrubs including roses [genus Rosa]</p><p><b>Kineska vječnozelena uzlazna ruža sa žutim ili bijelim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chinese evergreen climbing rose with yellow or white single flowers [banksia rose]</p><p><b>škrti divlji ruža sa osjetljivim ružičastom ili bijelom bezmirnom cvijetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prickly wild rose with delicate pink or white scentless flowers [dog rose]</p><p><b>Kineska ruža. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby Chinese rose [Bengal rose, China rose]</p><p><b>Velika čvrsta vrlo mirisna ružičasta ruža. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large hardy very fragrant pink rose [damask rose, summer damask rose]</p><p><b>Evroazijska ruža s bodljivim stabljikama i mirisnim lišćama i svijetlo ružičastim cvijećima s crvenim kukovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian rose with prickly stems and fragrant leaves and bright pink flowers followed by scarlet hips [briar, brier, eglantine, sweetbriar, sweetbrier]</p><p><b>Kineska plezačka ruža sa mirisnim bijelim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chinese climbing rose with fragrant white blossoms [Cherokee rose]</p><p><b>Američki sopran (1897-1981) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States soprano (1897-1981) [Ponselle, Rosa Ponselle]</p><p><b>u obliku ruže s zakrivljenim ili penjivim granama i slobodnim grmovima muskusnih cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rose native to Mediterranean region having curved or climbing branches and loose clusters of musky-scented flowers [musk rose]</p><p><b>u obliku ruže, s brojnim cvjetovima, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vigorously growing rose having clusters of numerous small flowers [Japanese rose, baby rose, multiflora, multiflora rose]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko hibridnih bušnih ruža koje potiču od kineske ruže s mirisom čaja s ružičastim ili žutim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several hybrid bush roses derived from a tea-scented Chinese rose with pink or yellow flowers [tea rose]</p><p><b>Vođa američkih građanskih prava koja je odbila dati svoje mjesto u autobusu bijelom čovjeku u Montgomeryju (Alabama) i tako pokrenula nacionalni pokret za građanska prava (rođena 1913.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States civil rights leader who refused to give up her seat on a bus to a white man in Montgomery (Alabama) and so triggered the national Civil Rights movement (born in 1913) [Parks]</p><p><b>Europska alpska ruža s crvenokrasnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European alpine rose with crimson flowers [mountain rose]</p><p><b>Američki sopran (1897-1981) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States soprano (1897-1981) [Ponselle, Rosa Melba Ponselle]</p><p><b>nizak rastovi šumovi iz južnog Oregona i Kalifornije s puzećim korijenima i obično cvjetovima korimbosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing bristly shrub of southern Oregon and California with creeping rootstocks and usually corymbose flowers [ground rose]</p><p><b>bolest kože odraslih (često žena) kod koje se krvni sudovi lica povećavaju što rezultira crvenom pojavom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skin disease of adults (more often women) in which blood vessels of the face enlarge resulting in a flushed appearance [acne rosacea]</p><p><b>velika obitelj dvostrukožnih biljaka red Rosales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large family of dicotyledonous plants of order Rosales [family Rosaceae, rose family]</p><p><b>od ili koje se odnose na ili su karakteristične za biljke iz obitelji Rosaceae, nešto ima prašnjavu ljubičasto ružičasta boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or characteristic of plants of the family Rosaceae</p><p><i>adj.</i> of something having a dusty purplish pink color [rose, roseate]</p><p><b>red Rosales</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications this category does not include Leguminosae [order Rosales]</p><p><b>lučki grad na rijeci Paran u istočnoj središnjoj Argentini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port city on the Parana River in eastern central Argentina</p><p><b>brojanice, ružičnjak, krunica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a string of beads used in counting prayers (especially by Catholics) [prayer beads]</p><p><b>krasotica, rozeta, ruža, ružičast, roze, ružičasto vino</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of many shrubs of the genus Rosa that bear roses [rosebush]</p><p><i>n.</i> pinkish table wine from red grapes whose skins were removed after fermentation began [blush wine, pink wine, rose wine]</p><p><i>n.</i> a dusty pink color [rosiness]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of something having a dusty purplish pink color [rosaceous, roseate]</p><p><b>veliki grm ili malo drvo iz istočne Sjedinjenih Država s šipkastim stabljikama i velikim grmovima ružičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large shrub or small tree of the eastern United States having bristly stems and large clusters of pink flowers [Robinia hispida, bristly locust, moss locust]</p><p><b>tropsko stablo iz Istočne Indije koje se uzgaja zbog jestivog voća, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna, odjemna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical tree of the East Indies cultivated for its edible fruit [Eugenia jambos, jambosa, rose-apple tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> fragrant oval yellowish tropical fruit used in jellies and confections</p><p><b>oleandar, Nerium oleander, oleander</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ornamental but poisonous flowering shrub having narrow evergreen leaves and clusters of fragrant white to pink or red flowers: native to East Indies but widely cultivated in warm regions [Nerium oleander, oleander]</p><p><b>cvjetni krevet u kojem rastu ruže (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flower bed in which roses are growing [bed of roses]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste bubrega u EU-u, primjenjuje se sljedeći popis: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common metallic green European beetle: larvae feed on plant roots and adults on leaves and flowers of e.g. roses [Cetonia aurata, rose chafer]</p><p><b>Uobičajena sjevernoamerička buba: ličinke se hrane korijenima, a odrasle lišća i cvijeće, npr. ružnih grmlja ili jabuka ili vinove loze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common North American beetle: larvae feed on roots and adults on leaves and flowers of e.g. rose bushes or apple trees or grape vines [Macrodactylus subspinosus, rose chafer]</p><p><b>Stara kućna vrtna biljka iz jugoistočne Europe koja se široko uzgaja zbog svojih atraktivnih bijeli vunih listova i upečatljivih crvenokrasnih cvijeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an old cottage garden plant of southeastern Europe widely cultivated for its attractive white woolly foliage and showy crimson flowers [Lychnis coronaria, dusty miller, gardener's delight, mullein pink]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste bubrega u EU-u, primjenjuje se sljedeći popis:, Uobičajena sjevernoamerička buba: ličinke se hrane korijenima, a odrasle lišća i cvijeće, npr. ružnih grmlja ili jabuka ili vinove loze. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common metallic green European beetle: larvae feed on plant roots and adults on leaves and flowers of e.g. roses [Cetonia aurata, rose beetle]</p><p><i>n.</i> common North American beetle: larvae feed on roots and adults on leaves and flowers of e.g. rose bushes or apple trees or grape vines [Macrodactylus subspinosus, rose bug]</p><p><b>lijep istočnoindijski vječnozeleni drvo koje se često sadilo kao ukras zbog svojih mirisnih bijelih cvijeća koje daju miris (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> handsome East Indian evergreen tree often planted as an ornamental for its fragrant white flowers that yield a perfume [Mesua ferrea, ironwood, ironwood tree]</p><p><b>velika obitelj dvostrukožnih biljaka red Rosales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large family of dicotyledonous plants of order Rosales [Rosaceae, family Rosaceae]</p><p><b>vrt za uzgoj ruža. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a garden for growing roses</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko južnoafričkih geranija s mirisnim trolobnim do petolobnim lištima i ružičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several southern African geraniums having fragrant three-lobed to five-lobed leaves and pink flowers [Pelargonium graveolens, sweet-scented geranium]</p><p><b>cvjetovi s duboko ružičastom ili ljubičasto-ojčanom obličju cvjetova na fleksibilnim stabljikama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> globe lily with deep rose-pink or purple egg-shaped flowers on flexuous stems [Calochortus amoenus]</p><p><b>vrlo visoko stablo u Queenslandu i Novom Južnom Walesu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very tall tree of Queensland and New South Wales [Eucalypt grandis]</p><p><b>šipak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fruit of a rose plant [hip, rosehip]</p><p><b>Sjevera američka bulbska biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American bulbous plant [Allium canadense, Canada garlic, meadow leek]</p><p><b>Američka striptiz umjetnica koja je postala poznata na Broadwayu 1930-ih (1914-1970) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States striptease artist who became famous on Broadway in the 1930s (1914-1970) [Gypsy Rose Lee, Lee]</p><p><b>sjajan grm iz solenih močvara istočne Sjedinjenih Država s velikim ružičastom bojom cvijeća, biljka s krajnjim rascemama od blesavih bijeli do ružičastih ili ljubičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> showy shrub of salt marshes of the eastern United States having large rose-colored flowers [Hibiscus moscheutos, common rose mallow, swamp mallow, swamp rose mallow]</p><p><i>n.</i> plant with terminal racemes of showy white to pink or purple flowers [Alcea rosea, Althea rosea]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (c) ovog članka, za proizvodnju proizvoda koji sadrže: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated in many varieties for its fleshy moss-like foliage and profusion of brightly colored flowers [Portulaca grandiflora, sun plant]</p><p><b>Veliki naivni azijski grm ili malo stablo s velikim jednostrukom ili dvostrukom crvenom do duboko crvenom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large showy Asiatic shrub or small tree having large single or double red to deep-red flowers [China rose, Chinese hibiscus, Hibiscus rosa-sinensis, shoe black, shoeblack plant]</p><p><b>guste tufted paprika od jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država do Perua, mala siva azijska pustinjska biljka s malenim bijelim cvijećem koja se skuplja kad suha i širi kada je vlažna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> densely tufted fern ally of southwestern United States to Peru [Selaginella lepidophylla, resurrection plant]</p><p><i>n.</i> small grey Asiatic desert plant bearing minute white flowers that rolls up when dry and expands when moist [Anastatica hierochuntica, resurrection plant]</p><p><b>Azijski grm ili malo grmlje s najozbiljnije ruže ili ljubičaste ili bijele cvijeće u obliku zvona i obično s tri lobne lišće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic shrub or small shrubby tree having showy bell-shaped rose or purple or white flowers and usually three-lobed leaves [Hibiscus syriacus]</p><p><b>u obliku od sirove ili sirove kiseline, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a volatile fragrant oil obtained from fresh roses by steam distillation [attar of roses]</p><p><b>obično uzgajana drvena biljka iz Starog svijeta s velikim ružičastim do crvenim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commonly cultivated Old World woody herb having large pinkish to red flowers [Cape periwinkle, Catharanthus roseus, Madagascar periwinkle, Vinca rosea, cayenne jasmine, old maid, periwinkle, red periwinkle]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko ružičastih cvjetova močvarne biljke istočnih Sjedinjenih Država koja liči na pravi centaury (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several pink-flowered marsh plant of the eastern United States resembling a true centaury [American centaury, Sabbatia Angularis, Sabbatia stellaris, bitter floom, marsh pink]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a translucent rose-red variety of quartz used for ornaments</p><p><b>parfem koji se sastoji od vode aromatizirane uljem ruža (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perfume consisting of water scented with oil of roses</p><p><b>rozeta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> circular window filled with tracery [rosette]</p><p><b>roze, ružičasto vino</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pinkish table wine from red grapes whose skins were removed after fermentation began [blush wine, pink wine, rose]</p><p><b>tropsko stablo iz Istočne Indije koje se uzgaja zbog jestivog voća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical tree of the East Indies cultivated for its edible fruit [Eugenia jambos, jambosa, rose apple]</p><p><b>Imajući ružičastu crvenicu zdravlja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the pinkish flush of health [flushed, rosy, rosy-cheeked]</p><p><b>koji odražava optimizam, s ružičastom bojom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> reflecting optimism [rosy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a rose color [rosy-colored]</p><p><b>blistava crna ptica s ružičastim leđima i trbuhom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> glossy black bird with pink back and abdomen [Pastor roseus, Pastor sturnus, rose-colored starling]</p><p><b>blistava crna ptica s ružičastim leđima i trbuhom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> glossy black bird with pink back and abdomen [Pastor roseus, Pastor sturnus, rose-colored pastor]</p><p><b>od lavandulje obojene ružom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of lavender tinged with rose [rose-lilac]</p><p><b>od lavandulje obojene ružom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of lavender tinged with rose [rose-lavender]</p><p><b>od ružičaste boje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of mauve tinged with rose</p><p><b>od ljubičaste sa ružičastim bojom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of purple with a rose tinge [rosy-purple]</p><p><b>od tamno malo plavocrvene boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a deep slightly bluish red color</p><p><b>Evroazijska planinska biljka s mesnatim lištima s ružičastim vrhom i gomilom žutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian mountain plant with fleshy pink-tipped leaves and a cluster of yellow flowers [Sedum rosea, midsummer-men]</p><p><b>od boje obojene ružom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a color tinged with rose [rose-tinted]</p><p><b>od boje obojene ružom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a color tinged with rose [rose-tinged]</p><p><b>nešto ima prašnjavu ljubičasto ružičasta boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of something having a dusty purplish pink color [rosaceous, rose]</p><p><b>tropski ružičasti žličak Novog svijeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical rose-colored New World spoonbill [Ajaia ajaja]</p><p><b>glavni grad i najveći grad Dominikane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Dominica</p><p><b>rododendron s kasnim proljetnim cvjetovima iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s ružičastim do ružičastog ljubičastog cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> late-spring-blooming rhododendron of eastern North America having rosy to pink-purple flowers [Rhododendron maxima]</p><p><b>Visoka sjevernoamerička višegodišnja biljka s puzećim korijenima i uskim listovima i šiljakama ružičastavičasta ljubičasta cvjetova koja se u velikoj količini nalazi u spaljenim područjima ili nedavnim čistinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall North American perennial with creeping rootstocks and narrow leaves and spikes of pinkish-purple flowers occurring in great abundance in burned-over areas or recent clearings [Epilobium angustifolium, fireweed, giant willowherb, wickup]</p><p><b>pupoljak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bud of a rose</p><p><i>n.</i> (a literary reference to) a pretty young girl</p><p><b>biljka ili stablo porijeklom iz Japana koje se uzgaja kao ukrasno bilje zbog svojih ružičastih cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub or tree native to Japan cultivated as an ornamental for its rose-pink flowers [Prunus subhirtella, winter flowering cherry]</p><p><b>Orhideja iz središnje i sjeverne Južne Amerike s 1 do 3 cvjetne stabljike velikih, navidnih ružičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orchid of central and northern South America having 1- to 3-blossomed racemes of large showy rose-colored flowers [Cleistes rosea, Pogonia rosea]</p><p><b>ruža</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of many shrubs of the genus Rosa that bear roses [rose]</p><p><b>Sjeverac Atlantika, Velike ribe sjeverne obale Atlantika Amerike i Europe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North Atlantic rockfish [ocean perch, redfish]</p><p><i>n.</i> large fish of northern Atlantic coasts of America and Europe [Sebastodes marinus, ocean perch]</p><p><b>šipak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fruit of a rose plant [hip, rose hip]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijska rijetko trnasta godišnja biljka ili višegodišnji potgrm koji se široko uzgaja zbog svojih mesnih čaša koje se koriste u pite i žele i zbog svog vlakna bast (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian sparsely prickly annual herb or perennial subshrub widely cultivated for its fleshy calyxes used in tarts and jelly and for its bast fiber [Hibiscus sabdariffa, Jamaica sorrel, red sorrel, rozelle, sorrel]</p><p><b>gljivice s glatkim peritekijom i tamnim jednobilnim askosporama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungi having smooth perithecia with dark one-celled ascospores [genus Rosellinia]</p><p><b>Sklonovi za stolove i kuhinje, od plastičnih ili sintetičkih vlakana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Scandinavian style of carved or painted decoration (as on furniture or walls or dinnerware) consisting of floral motifs</p><p><b>ružmarin, ruzmarin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated for its fragrant grey-green leaves used in cooking and in perfumery [Rosmarinus officinalis]</p><p><i>n.</i> extremely pungent leaves used fresh or dried as seasoning for especially meats</p><p><b>osip</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any red eruption of the skin [efflorescence, rash, skin rash]</p><p><b>virusna bolest dojenčadi i male djece (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a viral disease of infants and young children [exanthema subitum, pseudorubella, roseola infantum]</p><p><b>virusna bolest dojenčadi i male djece (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a viral disease of infants and young children [exanthema subitum, pseudorubella, roseola infantilis]</p><p><b>dio gravirane granitne stele koja je prvobitno bila visoka oko dva metra i postavljena je 196. godine prije Krista. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a part of an inscribed granite stela that was originally about six feet tall and was set up in 196 BC</p><p><b>rozeta, značka oblika poput ruže, značka specijalnog oblika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ornament or pattern resembling a rose that is worn as a badge of office or as recognition of having won an honor</p><p><i>n.</i> rhizoctinia disease of potatoes [little potato, russet scab, stem canker]</p><p><i>n.</i> a cluster of leaves growing in crowded circles from a common center or crown (usually at or close to the ground)</p><p><i>n.</i> circular window filled with tracery [rose window]</p><p><b>tvrdo tamno crvenkasto drvo drveta ruže s snažno obeleženim zrnom, bilo koje od onih drveća od tvrdog drveta iz roda Dalbergia koji daju rožnu drvetu - vrijedan ormarić drveće tamno crvene ili ljubičaste boje u prugama i raznolikim crnim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hard dark reddish wood of a rosewood tree having a strongly marked grain</p><p><i>n.</i> any of those hardwood trees of the genus Dalbergia that yield rosewood--valuable cabinet woods of a dark red or purplish color streaked and variegated with black [rosewood tree]</p><p><b>bilo koje od onih drveća od tvrdog drveta iz roda Dalbergia koji daju rožnu drvetu - vrijedan ormarić drveće tamno crvene ili ljubičaste boje u prugama i raznolikim crnim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of those hardwood trees of the genus Dalbergia that yield rosewood--valuable cabinet woods of a dark red or purplish color streaked and variegated with black [rosewood]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) početak svakog mjeseca u židovskom kalendaru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) the beginning of each month in the Jewish calendar [Rosh Hodesh]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) svečan židovski praznik koji se slavi 1. ili 1. i 2. mjeseca Tishri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a solemn Jewish feast day celebrated on the 1st or 1st and 2nd of Tishri [Jewish New Year, Rosh Hashanah, Rosh Hashona, Rosh Hashonah]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) svečan židovski praznik koji se slavi 1. ili 1. i 2. mjeseca Tishri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a solemn Jewish feast day celebrated on the 1st or 1st and 2nd of Tishri [Jewish New Year, Rosh Hashana, Rosh Hashona, Rosh Hashonah]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) svečan židovski praznik koji se slavi 1. ili 1. i 2. mjeseca Tishri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a solemn Jewish feast day celebrated on the 1st or 1st and 2nd of Tishri [Jewish New Year, Rosh Hashana, Rosh Hashanah, Rosh Hashonah]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) svečan židovski praznik koji se slavi 1. ili 1. i 2. mjeseca Tishri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a solemn Jewish feast day celebrated on the 1st or 1st and 2nd of Tishri [Jewish New Year, Rosh Hashana, Rosh Hashanah, Rosh Hashona]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) početak svakog mjeseca u židovskom kalendaru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) the beginning of each month in the Jewish calendar [Rosh Chodesh]</p><p><b>Član bilo koje od raznih organizacija koje su kasnije potekle iz 17. stoljeća društva, Član tajnog društva filozofa i učenjaka iz 17. stoljeća koji su bili upoznati s mističnim, metafizičkim i alhemističkim znanjem., od ili u vezi s Rosicrucians (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of any of various organizations that subsequently derived from the 17th-century society</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a secret 17th-century society of philosophers and scholars versed in mystical and metaphysical and alchemical lore</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Rosicrucians</p><p><b>teološka nauka koja obožava ružu i križ kao simbole Kristova uskrsnuća i otkupljenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the theological doctrine that venerates the rose and the cross as symbols of Christ's Resurrection and redemption</p><p><b>porodica svojte rosida</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of dicotyledonous plants</p><p><b>rod svojte rosida</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of dicotyledonous plants</p><p><b>skupina stabala i grmova i biljaka uglavnom s polipetalnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of trees and shrubs and herbs mostly with polypetalous flowers [subclass Rosidae]</p><p><b>u južnoj Kaliforniji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sneezeweed of southwestern United States especially southern California [Helenium puberulum]</p><p><b>kolofonij, smola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a class of solid or semisolid viscous substances obtained either as exudations from certain plants or prepared by polymerization of simple molecules [resin]</p><p><i>v.</i> rub rosin onto</p><p><b>vreća puna kolosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bag filled with rosin</p><p><b>ružičasta boja (posebno u obrazima) smatra se znakom dobrog zdravlja, zdrava crvenkasto-crvena boja kože, prašnjavo ružičasta boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rosy color (especially in the cheeks) taken as a sign of good health [bloom, blush, flush]</p><p><i>n.</i> a healthy reddish complexion [ruddiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a dusty pink color [rose]</p><p><b>Sjeveračka višegodišnja biljka s smolavim mirisom i žutim cvijećem, bilo koja od različitih zapadne američke biljke roda Grindelia s smočastim lišćama i stabljikama koje su ranije korištene u medicini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American perennial having a resinous odor and yellow flowers [Silphium laciniatum]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various western American plants of the genus Grindelia having resinous leaves and stems formerly used medicinally [gum plant, gumweed, tarweed]</p><p><b>uspravna biljka s malim grmovima ružičastih cvijeća u obliku trube iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect plant with small clusters of pink trumpet-shaped flowers of southwestern United States [Centaurium calycosum]</p><p><b>ružmarin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rosemary [genus Rosmarinus]</p><p><b>ružmarin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated for its fragrant grey-green leaves used in cooking and in perfumery [rosemary]</p><p><b>Škotski istraživač koji je vodio arktičke ekspedicije koje su donijele geografska otkrića u potrazi za sjeverozapadnim prolazom (1777-1856), Britanski istraživač Arktika i Antarktika, Britanski liječnik koji je otkrio da komarci prenose malariju (1857-1932), političarka iz Wyominga koja je bila prva žena guverner u Sjedinjenim Državama (1876-1977), Američka šavarica navodno je napravila prvu američku zastavu na zahtjev Georgea Washingtona (1752-1836) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Scottish explorer who led Arctic expeditions that yielded geographic discoveries while searching for the Northwest Passage (1777-1856) [John Ross, Sir John Ross]</p><p><i>n.</i> British explorer of the Arctic and Antarctic [James Clark Ross, Sir James Clark Ross]</p><p><i>n.</i> British physician who discovered that mosquitos transmit malaria (1857-1932) [Sir Ronald Ross]</p><p><i>n.</i> a politician in Wyoming who was the first woman governor in the United States (1876-1977) [Nellie Ross, Nellie Tayloe Ross]</p><p><i>n.</i> American seamstress said to have made the first American flag at the request of George Washington (1752-1836) [Betsy Griscom Ross, Betsy Ross]</p><p><b>Rossovo more</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arm of the southern Pacific Ocean in Antarctica</p><p><b>bitka u Sedmogodišnjem ratu (1757) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a battle in the Seven Year