</i> the state flower of Maryland [Rudbeckia serotina, black-eyed Susan]</p><p><b>Visoka listovita biljka s uspravnim granama koje završavaju velikim žutim glavama s zrake u obliku lukova prema dolje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall leafy plant with erect branches ending in large yellow flower heads with downward-arching rays [cutleaved coneflower]</p><p><b>vrlo visoka grana sa navidnim, mnogo udvostručenim žutim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very tall branching herb with showy much-doubled yellow flower heads [double gold, golden glow, hortensia]</p><p><b>državni cvijet Maryland (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state flower of Maryland [Rudbeckia hirta, black-eyed Susan]</p><p><b>crvenperka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European freshwater fish resembling the roach [Scardinius erythrophthalmus]</p><p><b>kormilo, krma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hinged vertical airfoil mounted at the tail of an aircraft and used to make horizontal course changes</p><p><i>n.</i> (nautical) steering mechanism consisting of a hinged vertical plate mounted at the stern of a vessel</p><p><b>vertikalno oštro na kormilu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the vertical blade on a rudder</p><p><b>oblikovan kao i služe kao kormilo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> formed like and serving like a rudder</p><p><b>hrana i riba u divljini oko Bermuda i Floride, ribama koje su naviknute slijediti brodove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> food and game fish around Bermuda and Florida [Bermuda chub, Kyphosus sectatrix]</p><p><i>n.</i> fish having the habit of following ships [Seriola zonata, banded rudderfish]</p><p><b>bez kormila, bez rukovodstva</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> aimlessly drifting [adrift, afloat, aimless, directionless, planless, undirected]</p><p><b>vertikalni stub na prednjem rubu kormira koji omogućuje kretanje kormira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vertical post at the forward edge of a rudder that enables the rudder to pivot [rudderstock]</p><p><b>vertikalni stub na prednjem rubu kormira koji omogućuje kretanje kormira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vertical post at the forward edge of a rudder that enables the rudder to pivot [rudderpost]</p><p><b>zdrava crvenkasto-crvena boja kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a healthy reddish complexion [rosiness]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,8 g/m2 do 0,8 g/m2, s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 mm, crvenilo kao da ima crvenu okersku boju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a red iron ore used in dyeing and marking [raddle, reddle]</p><p><i>v.</i> twist or braid together, interlace [raddle]</p><p><i>v.</i> redden as if with a red ocher color</p><p><b>neven</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the common European annual marigold [Calendula officinalis, Scotch marigold, common marigold, pot marigold]</p><p><b>crven, crvenkast, rumen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined to a healthy reddish color often associated with outdoor life [florid, rubicund, sanguine]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a color at the end of the color spectrum (next to orange) [blood-red, carmine, cerise, cherry, cherry-red, crimson, red, reddish, ruby, ruby-red, scarlet]</p><p><b>Crvenkasto-smeđa patka s čvrstim repom iz Sjeverne Amerike i sjeverne Južne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> reddish-brown stiff-tailed duck of North America and northern South America [Oxyura jamaicensis]</p><p><b>zujavac kamenjar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common Arctic turnstone that winters in South America and Australia [Arenaria interpres]</p><p><b>grub, iznenadan, jednostavan, nagao, neizrađen, neobrađen, neodgojen, neotesan, neuljudan, oštar, primitivan, prost, sirov, snažan, surov, uvredljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> socially incorrect in behavior [bad-mannered, ill-mannered, unmannered, unmannerly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of persons) lacking in refinement or grace [bounderish, ill-bred, lowbred, underbred, yokelish]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking civility or good manners [uncivil]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used especially of commodities) being unprocessed or manufactured using only simple or minimal processes [natural, raw]</p><p><i>adj.</i> belonging to an early stage of technical development [crude, primitive]</p><p><b>grub, iznenadan, jednostavan, nagao, neizrađen, neobrađen, neodgojen, neotesan, neuljudan, oštar, primitivan, prost, sirov, snažan, surov, uvredljiv (od &quot;rude&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in an impolite manner [discourteously, impolitely]</p><p><b>grub, iznenadan, jednostavan, nagao, neizrađen, neobrađen, neodgojen, neotesan, neuljudan, oštar, primitivan, prost, sirov, snažan, surov, uvredljiv (od &quot;rude&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a manner that is rude and insulting [discourtesy]</p><p><i>n.</i> a wild or unrefined state [crudeness, crudity, primitiveness, primitivism]</p><p><b>osnova, rudiment, začetak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the remains of a body part that was functional at an earlier stage of life</p><p><b>elementarni, nerazvijen, osnovni, rudimentaran, zakržljao, temeljan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being or involving basic facts or principles [fundamental, underlying]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being in the earliest stages of development</p><p><i>adj.</i> not fully developed in mature animals [vestigial]</p><p><b>elementarni princip, osnove, rudiment, zakržljali organ</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statement of fundamental facts or principles [basics]</p><p><i>n.</i> the elementary stages of any subject (usually plural) [ABC, ABC's, ABCs, alphabet, first principles]</p><p><b>luteranski teolog u Njemačkoj (1884-1976) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Lutheran theologian in Germany (1884-1976) [Bultmann, Rudolf Karl Bultmann]</p><p><b>Njemački inženjer (rođen u Francuskoj) koji je izumio dizel motor (1858-1913) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German engineer (born in France) who invented the diesel engine (1858-1913) [Diesel, Rudolf Diesel]</p><p><b>Njemački inženjer (rođen u Francuskoj) koji je izumio dizel motor (1858-1913) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German engineer (born in France) who invented the diesel engine (1858-1913) [Diesel, Rudolf Christian Karl Diesel]</p><p><b>Nacistički vođa koji je 1941. godine sam poletio u Škotsku u očiglednom pokuša