iki sjevernoamerički divlji trešnje s okruglim crnim kislim jestivim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large North American wild cherry with round black sour edible fruit [Prunus serotina, black cherry, black cherry tree]</p><p><b>koktel napravljen od ruma i limena ili limunovog soka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cocktail made with rum and lime or lemon juice [daiquiri]</p><p><b>povećanje nosa s dilatacijom folikula i crvenilo i istaknuta vaskularnost kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enlargement of the nose with dilation of follicles and redness and prominent vascularity of the skin [brandy nose, copper nose, hammer nose, hypertrophic rosacea, potato nose, rhinophyma, rum-blossom, toper's nose]</p><p><b>Sling napravljen od ruma. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sling made with rum</p><p><b>povećanje nosa s dilatacijom folikula i crvenilo i istaknuta vaskularnost kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enlargement of the nose with dilation of follicles and redness and prominent vascularity of the skin [brandy nose, copper nose, hammer nose, hypertrophic rosacea, potato nose, rhinophyma, rum nose, toper's nose]</p><p><b>Rumunjska</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic in southeastern Europe with a short coastline on the Black Sea [Romania, Roumania]</p><p><b>Rumunjske, Rumunj, Rumunjka, rumunjski, Rumunjski jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an eastern Romance language spoken in Romania [Romanian]</p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Romania [Romanian]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of the country of Romania or its people or languages [Romanian, Roumanian]</p><p><b>Rhaeto-romanski jezik koji se govori u jugoistočnoj Švicarskoj, od ili u vezi s romanškim jezikom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Rhaeto-Romance language spoken in southeastern Switzerland [Romansh]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Romansh language [Romansh]</p><p><b>rumba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> syncopated music in duple time for dancing the rumba [rhumba]</p><p><i>n.</i> a folk dance in duple time that originated i