ne vlade u ožujku 1917. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the coup d'etat by the Bolsheviks under Lenin in November 1917 that led to a period of civil war which ended in victory for the Bolsheviks in 1922 [October Revolution]</p><p><i>n.</i> the revolution against the czarist government which led to the abdication of Nicholas II and the creation of a provisional government in March 1917 [February Revolution]</p><p><b>rijeka u sjevernoj Kaliforniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in northern California</p><p><b>Stunt u kojem okrenete cilindar revolvera koji je naputan samo jednim metkom i onda usmjerite cijev na glavu i povučete obarač (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stunt in which you spin the cylinder of a revolver that is loaded with only one bullet and then point the muzzle at your head and pull the trigger</p><p><b>Nekada najveća sovjetska socijalistička republika u SSSR-u okupirala istočnu Europu i sjevernu Aziju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> formerly the largest Soviet Socialist Republic in the USSR occupying eastern Europe and northern Asia [Russia, Soviet Russia]</p><p><b>žuljasto-buski evroazijska biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prickly bushy Eurasian plant [Russian cactus, Russian tumbleweed, Salsola kali tenuifolia, tumbleweed]</p><p><b>žuljasto-buski evroazijska biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prickly bushy Eurasian plant [Russian cactus, Russian thistle, Salsola kali tenuifolia, tumbleweed]</p><p><b>Vječna loza s racemima mirisnih zelenkastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> twining perennial vine having racemes of fragrant greenish flowers [China fleece vine, Polygonum aubertii, silver lace vine]</p><p><b>visoka pasmina brzog kretanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall fast-moving dog breed [borzoi]</p><p><b>Sposoban komunicirati na ruskom jeziku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to communicate in Russian</p><p><b>Japanska pobjeda u ratu s Rusijom (1904-1905) dala je Japanu moć nad Korejom i Mandžurijom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Japanese victory in the war with Russia (1904-19