n]</p><p><b>daždevnjak, duh koji živi u vatri, gutač vatre, osoba koja može podnositi vrućinu, salamander, štur. daždevnjak, tava, žarač, repaši</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various typically terrestrial amphibians that resemble lizards and that return to water only to breed</p><p><i>n.</i> reptilian creature supposed to live in fire</p><p><i>n.</i> fire iron consisting of a metal rod with a handle [fire hook, poker, stove poker]</p><p><b>tip rod Salamandridae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Salamandridae [genus Salamandra]</p><p><b>ovoviviparni amfibi Alpa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ovoviviparous amphibian of the Alps [alpine salamander]</p><p><b>Europski salamander tamne kože s obično žutim mrljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European salamander having dark skin with usually yellow spots [fire salamander, spotted salamander]</p><p><b>pjegavi daždevnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of European salamander [European fire salamander]</p><p><b>uši (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> salamanders [family Salamandridae]</p><p><b>u obliku salamandre. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> shaped like a salamander</p><p><b>salama</b></p><p><i>n.</i> highly seasoned fatty sausage of pork and beef usually dried</p><p><b>sa stalnom mjesečnom plaćom, službenički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> receiving a salary</p><p><i>adj.</i> receiving or eligible for compensation [compensated, remunerated, stipendiary]</p><p><i>adj.</i> for which money is paid [compensable, paying, remunerative, stipendiary]</p><p><b>dohodak, naknada, plaća, plaća činovnika, plata, zarada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that remunerates [earnings, pay, remuneration, wage]</p><p><b>Posao smanjenja plaće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of reducing a salary [pay cut]</p><p><b>povećanje plaće, povišica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount a salary is increased [hike, raise, rise, wage hike, wage increase]</p><p><b>Drugi stub islama je molitva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the second pillar of Islam is prayer [salaah, salaat, salah]</p><p><b>aukcija, l