p><p><b>salinitet, slanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the taste experience when common salt is taken into the mouth [salt, saltiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the relative proportion of salt in a solution [brininess]</p><p><b>salinometar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hydrometer that determines the concentration of salt solutions by measuring their density</p><p><b>Glavni i najveći grad Zimbabvea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Zimbabwe [Harare, capital of Zimbabwe]</p><p><b>Mletena govedina obično sa sosom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ground beef patty usually with a sauce</p><p><b>obiteljski jezik Mosan koji se govori na sjeverozapadu Sjedinjenih Država i zapadnom dijelu Kanade., član grupe indijanaca iz Sjeverne Amerike koji govore salishanskim jezikom i žive na sjeverozapadnoj obali Sjeverne Amerike. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of Mosan language spoken in northwestern United States and western Canada [Salishan]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a group of North American Indians speaking a Salishan language and living on the northwest coast of North America</p><p><b>obiteljski jezik Mosan koji se govori na sjeverozapadu Sjedinjenih Država i zapadnom dijelu Kanade. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of Mosan language spoken in northwestern United States and western Canada [Salish]</p><p><b>pljuvačka, slina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a clear liquid secreted into the mouth by the salivary glands and mucous glands of the mouth [spit, spittle]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s pljućkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to saliva</p><p><b>kamen koji se formira u pljuvačkoj žlijezdi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stone formed in the salivary gland [sialolith]</p><p><b>kanal kroz koji pljuvačka prolazi iz pljuvačke žlijezde u usta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a duct through which saliva passes from the salivary gland into the mouth</p><p><b>bilo koji od tri para žlijezda u ustima i probavnom sustavu koji luče pljuvačku za varenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of three pairs of glands in the mouth and digestive system that secrete saliva for digestion</p><p><b>sliniti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> produce saliva</p><p><i>v.</i> be envious, desirous, eager for, or extremely happy about something [drool]</p><p><b>slinavljenje, slinjenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the secretion of saliva</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, podrijetlo za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large and widespread genus varying in size from small shrubs to large trees: willows [genus Salix]</p><p><b>Velika vrba iz Evroazije i Sjeverne Afrike s sivo-plamenim lištima i sivom kore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large willow tree of Eurasia and North Africa having greyish canescent leaves and grey bark [Huntingdon willow, white willow]</p><p><b>Eurasijska vrba s sivim lištima i uzlaznim granama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian willow tree having greyish leaves and ascending branches [cricket-bat willow]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička vrba s sivo-siljastim pubertetnim lištima koji obično postaju crni nakon sušenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American willow with greyish silky pubescent leaves that usually blacken in drying [Salix sericea, silky willow, silver willow]</p><p><b>Europska vrba s sivim lištima i žuto-narandžastom granom koja se koristi u košari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European willow having greyish leaves and yellow-orange twigs used in basketry [Salix vitellina, golden willow]</p><p><b>Vrba starog svijeta s svjetlo zelenim lišćama uzgajana za upotrebu u košari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World willow with light green leaves cultivated for use in basketry [Salix triandra, almond willow, black Hollander]</p><p><b>vrba sa lišća poput breskve ili badema (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> willow of the western United States with leaves like those of peach or almond trees [almond-leaves willow, peach-leaved willow, peachleaf willow]</p><p><b>niskokripljivi grm Arktičke Europe i Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low creeping shrub of Arctic Europe and America [arctic willow]</p><p><b>vrba s dugim spuštena grana i tanak listovi porijeklom iz Kine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> willow with long drooping branches and slender leaves native to China [Babylonian weeping willow, weeping willow]</p><p><b>Hibridna vrba obično ne plače. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hybrid willow usually not strongly weeping in habit [Salix pendulina, Salix pendulina blanda, Wisconsin weeping willow]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički grm s bijeljastim lišćama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American shrub with whitish canescent leaves [hoary willow, sage willow]</p><p><b>Vrba iz starog svijeta s velikim čvorovima i relativno velikim širokim listovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> much-branched Old World willow having large catkins and relatively large broad leaves [florist's willow, goat willow, pussy willow]</p><p><b>Eurasijska šumska vrba s bijelo-tomentoznim granama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian shrubby willow with whitish tomentose twigs [gray willow, grey willow]</p><p><b>mala vrba istočne Sjeverne Amerike s sivim lištima i svijednim mačkama koje dolaze prije lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small willow of eastern North America having greyish leaves and silky catkins that come before the leaves [pussy willow]</p><p><b>veliko vrb s čvrstima granama koje se lako lomljaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large willow tree with stiff branches that are easily broken [brittle willow, crack willow, snap willow]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjena borealna šumska vrba s djelomično podzemnim puzećim stabljikama i svijetlo zelenim blistavim lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed boreal shrubby willow with partially underground creeping stems and bright green glossy leaves [dwarf willow]</p><p><b>tanka šumovita vrba iz sušnih područja Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender shrubby willow of dry areas of North America [prairie willow]</p><p><b>šumovita vrba sa zapada Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby willow of the western United States [arroyo willow]</p><p><b>obična sjevernoamerička grmlja s blistavim lanceolatskim listovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common North American shrub with shiny lanceolate leaves [shining willow]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička šumska vrba s tamnom kore i linearnim lištima koja raste blizu potoka i jezera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American shrubby willow having dark bark and linear leaves growing close to streams and lakes [black willow, swamp willow]</p><p><b>Hibridna vrba obično ne plače. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hybrid willow usually not strongly weeping in habit [Salix blanda, Salix pendulina blanda, Wisconsin weeping willow]</p><p><b>Hibridna vrba obično ne plače. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hybrid willow usually not strongly weeping in habit [Salix blanda, Salix pendulina, Wisconsin weeping willow]</p><p><b>Europska vrba s sjajnim kožnim lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European willow tree with shining leathery leaves [bay willow, laurel willow]</p><p><b>Eurasijski šareni šareni s crvenkastim ili ljubičastim granama i kore bogate taninom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian osier having reddish or purple twigs and bark rich in tannin [basket willow, purple osier, purple willow, red osier, red willow]</p><p><b>malo grmlje u istočnoj Sjevernoj Americi čiji lišće kad se slomi, izdiše miris balzama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrubby tree of eastern North America having leaves exuding an odor of balsam when crushed [balsam willow]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, podrijetlo za proizvodnju proizvoda iz područja Unije može se upotrebljavati za proizvodnju proizvoda iz područja Unije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small trailing bush of Europe and Asia having straggling branches with silky green leaves of which several varieties are cultivated [creeping willow]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička vrba s sivo-siljastim pubertetnim lištima koji obično postaju crni nakon sušenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American willow with greyish silky pubescent leaves that usually blacken in drying [Salix alba sericea, silky willow, silver willow]</p><p><b>malo grmlje u zapadnoj Sjevernoj Americi (od Aljaske do Oregona) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small shrubby tree of western North America (Alaska to Oregon) [Sitka willow, silky willow]</p><p><b>Vrba starog svijeta s svjetlo zelenim lišćama uzgajana za upotrebu u košari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World willow with light green leaves cultivated for use in basketry [Salix amygdalina, almond willow, black Hollander]</p><p><b>vrb suha mjesta u istočnim Sjedinjenim Državama s dugim uskim lištima koje mogu rasti ispod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> willow shrub of dry places in the eastern United States having long narrow leaves canescent beneath [dwarf gray willow, dwarf grey willow, sage willow]</p><p><b>džinovski prostrati grm iz arktičkih i alpskih područja Sjeverne Amerike i Grenlanda s duboko zelenim eliptičnim listovima koji se sužavaju prema dnu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dwarf prostrate mat-forming shrub of Arctic and alpine regions of North America and Greenland having deep green elliptic leaves that taper toward the base [bearberry willow]</p><p><b>vrba s dugim fleksibilnim granama koja se koristi u košari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> willow with long flexible twigs used in basketry [common osier, hemp willow, velvet osier]</p><p><b>Europska vrba s sivim lištima i žuto-narandžastom granom koja se koristi u košari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European willow having greyish leaves and yellow-orange twigs used in basketry [Salix alba vitellina, golden willow]</p><p><b>Virolog iz Sjedinjenih Država koji je razvio Salkovu cjepivo koje se ubrizgava protiv poliomijelitisa (rođen 1914.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States virologist who developed the Salk vaccine that is injected against poliomyelitis (born 1914) [Jonas Edward Salk, Jonas Salk]</p><p><b>vakcina protiv poliovirusa koja se sastoji od inaktiviranog poliovirusa koji se ubrizgava podkožno kako bi se osigurao imunitet na poliomijelitis. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a poliovirus vaccine consisting of inactivated polio virus that is injected subcutaneously to provide immunity to poliomyelitis [IPV]</p><p><b>lagana srednjovjekovna kaciga s pukotinom za vid (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light medieval helmet with a slit for vision [salade]</p><p><b>vrba, žućkast</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several Old World shrubby broad-leaved willows having large catkins</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become sallow</p><p><i>adj.</i> unhealthy looking [sickly]</p><p><b>vrba, žućkast (od &quot;sallow&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sickly yellowish skin color</p><p><b>ispad, izljev, pokušaj proboja, šala, šetnja, vožnja, dosjetka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> witty remark [crack, quip, wisecrack]</p><p><i>n.</i> a military action in which besieged troops burst forth from their position [sortie]</p><p><i>n.</i> a venture off the beaten path [sallying forth]</p><p><b>iznenada, energično ili nasilno (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> set out in a sudden, energetic or violent manner [sally out]</p><p><b>Ravan okrugli malo slatki kolač obično se služi vruće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flat round slightly sweet teacake usually served hot</p><p><b>iznenada, energično ili nasilno, skoči iz skrovišta i iznenadi (nekoga) (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> set out in a sudden, energetic or violent manner [sally forth]</p><p><i>v.</i> jump out from a hiding place and surprise (someone) [burst forth, leap out, rush out]</p><p><b>Poduhvat izvan izbijenog puta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a venture off the beaten path [sally]</p><p><b>Nimfa koja se spojila s Hermafroditom i formirala jedno tijelo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nymph who merged with Hermaphroditus to form one body</p><p><b>asortiman, izbor, mnoštvo, plejada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collection containing a variety of sorts of things [assortment, miscellanea, miscellany, mixed bag, mixture, motley, potpourri, smorgasbord, variety]</p><p><i>n.</i> cooked meats and eggs and vegetables usually arranged in rows around the plate and dressed with a salad dressing</p><p><b>Britanski pisac romana rođen u Indiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British writer of novels who was born in India [Ahmed Salman Rushdie, Rushdie]</p><p><b>Ragout divljačke u bogatom umaku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ragout of game in a rich sauce</p><p><b>vrsta roda Salmonidae: losos i pastrva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Salmonidae: salmon and trout [genus Salmo]</p><p><b>Nalazi se u pacifičkim obalnim vodama i potokima od donje Kalifornije do Aljaske. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found in Pacific coastal waters and streams from lower California to Alaska [rainbow trout]</p><p><b>U vodama i pritokanima sjevernog obale Atlantskog mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found in northern coastal Atlantic waters or tributaries [Atlantic salmon]</p><p><b>Pstruga u europskim rijekama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> speckled trout of European rivers [brown trout, salmon trout]</p><p><b>losos, lososovo meso, ružičasto žut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various large food and game fishes of northern waters</p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Snake River in Idaho [Salmon River]</p><p><i>n.</i> flesh of any of various marine or freshwater fish of the family Salmonidae</p><p><i>n.</i> a pale pinkish orange color</p><p><i>adj.</i> of orange tinged with pink [pink-orange, pinkish-orange]</p><p><b>Mahunar s bijelim cvjetovima iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike i sjevernog Meksika s narančastom bojom u obliku prstića (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white-flowered raspberry of western North America and northern Mexico with thimble-shaped orange berries [Rubus parviflorus, salmonberry, thimbleberry]</p><p><b>riblje kruh napravljen od lososa u obilježju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fish loaf made with flaked salmon</p><p><b>masno ulje dobiveno od otpada iz konzervirane lososa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fatty oil obtained from the wastes in canning salmon</p><p><b>Američki političar i pravnik koji je bio glavni sudac Vrhovnog suda Sjedinjenih Država (1808-1873) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States politician and jurist who served as chief justice of the United States Supreme Court (1808-1873) [Chase, Salmon Portland Chase]</p><p><b>ružičasta boja sa žutom nijansom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shade of pink tinged with yellow [apricot, peach, yellowish pink]</p><p><b>Američki političar i pravnik koji je bio glavni sudac Vrhovnog suda Sjedinjenih Država (1808-1873) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States politician and jurist who served as chief justice of the United States Supreme Court (1808-1873) [Chase, Salmon P. Chase]</p><p><b>pritok rijeke Snake u Idahu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Snake River in Idaho [Salmon]</p><p><b>meso morske pastrve koja se seli iz slane u slatku vodu, Pstruga s velikim vilice u jezerima Kanade i sjevernih Sjedinjenih Država, Pstruga u europskim rijekama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flesh of marine trout that migrate from salt to fresh water [sea trout]</p><p><i>n.</i> large fork-tailed trout of lakes of Canada and the northern United States [Salvelinus namaycush, lake trout]</p><p><i>n.</i> speckled trout of European rivers [Salmo trutta, brown trout]</p><p><b>Mahunarke iz sjeverno-umjerenog područja s žutim ili narandžastom bojom, Mahunar s bijelim cvjetovima iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike i sjevernog Meksika s narančastom bojom u obliku prstića, velika uspravna maljina s crvenim cvjetovima iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s velikim ružičastom-narandžastom bojom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creeping raspberry of north temperate regions with yellow or orange berries [Rubus chamaemorus, bakeapple, baked-apple berry, cloudberry, dwarf mulberry]</p><p><i>n.</i> white-flowered raspberry of western North America and northern Mexico with thimble-shaped orange berries [Rubus parviflorus, salmon berry, thimbleberry]</p><p><i>n.</i> large erect red-flowered raspberry of western North America having large pinkish-orange berries [Rubus spectabilis]</p><p><b>Gram-negativne enterobakterije u obliku šipke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rod-shaped Gram-negative enterobacteria</p><p><b>oblik salmonele koji uzrokuje gastroenteritis kod ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of salmonella that causes gastroenteritis in humans [Gartner's bacillus]</p><p><b>oblik salmonele koji uzrokuje tifus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of salmonella that causes typhoid fever [Salmonella typhosa, typhoid bacillus]</p><p><b>oblik salmonele koji uzrokuje trovanje hranom kod ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of salmonella that causes food poisoning in humans</p><p><b>oblik salmonele koji uzrokuje tifus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of salmonella that causes typhoid fever [Salmonella typhi, typhoid bacillus]</p><p><b>salmoneloza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of food poisoning caused by eating foods contaminated with Salmonella typhimurium</p><p><b>losos, pastrvka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soft-finned fishes of cold and temperate waters</p><p><b>lososi, pastrvke, porodica Salmonidae, porodica lososa, porodica pastrvki</b></p><p><i>n.</i> salmon and trout [family Salmonidae]</p><p><b>veliki tropski američki drvo roda Cordia uzgajeno zbog svojih obilnih kremasto-bijelog cvijeća i vrijednog drveta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large tropical American tree of the genus Cordia grown for its abundant creamy white flowers and valuable wood [Cordia alliodora, Equador laurel, Spanish elm, cypre, princewood]</p><p><b>Bijeli prah s ugodnim okusom i mirisom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white powder with a pleasant taste and odor [phenyl salicylate]</p><p><b>Žena koja je plesala i nagovorila Heroda da joj da glavu Ivanom Krstiteljem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> woman whose dancing beguiled Herod into giving her the head of John the Baptist</p><p><b>Američki financijer i patriota iz Američkog rata za neovisnost koji je pomogao u financiranju vojske tijekom Američke revolucije (1740?-1785) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American financier and American Revolutionary War patriot who helped fund the army during the American Revolution (1740?-1785) [Haym Salomon]</p><p><b>salonu, uljepšavanje, salon, salon ljepote, salon za uljepšavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gallery where works of art can be displayed</p><p><i>n.</i> a shop where hairdressers and beauticians work [beauty parlor, beauty parlour, beauty salon, beauty shop]</p><p><i>n.</i> elegant sitting room where guests are received</p><p><b>lučki grad na sjeveroistoku Grčke na ulivu Egejskog mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port city in northeastern Greece on an inlet of the Aegean Sea [Salonika, Thessalonica, Thessaloniki]</p><p><b>lučki grad na sjeveroistoku Grčke na ulivu Egejskog mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port city in northeastern Greece on an inlet of the Aegean Sea [Salonica, Thessalonica, Thessaloniki]</p><p><b>bar, časnička blagavaonica na brodu, dvorana, kavana, krčma, salon, trpezarija, zatvoreni automobil, kafić, salun, točionica, limuzina, sedan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a room or establishment where alcoholic drinks are served over a counter [bar, barroom, ginmill, taproom]</p><p><i>n.</i> tavern consisting of a building with a bar and public rooms [gin mill, pothouse, pub, public house, taphouse]</p><p><i>n.</i> a car that is closed and that has front and rear seats and two or four doors [sedan]</p><p><b>vlasnik salona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the proprietor of a saloon</p><p><b>biljke iz umjerene Sjeverne i Južne Amerike: kokošja jaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herbs of temperate North and South America: cock's eggs [genus Salpichroa]</p><p><b>Argentinska loša loza s jednim bijelim cvijećem i bijelim ili žutim voćem u obliku jaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> weedy vine of Argentina having solitary white flowers followed by egg-shaped white or yellow fruit [Salpichroa rhomboidea, cock's eggs]</p><p><b>Argentinska loša loza s jednim bijelim cvijećem i bijelim ili žutim voćem u obliku jaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> weedy vine of Argentina having solitary white flowers followed by egg-shaped white or yellow fruit [Salpichroa organifolia, cock's eggs]</p><p><b>mala obitelj tunikatova iz razreda Thaliacea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small family of tunicates in the class Thaliacea [family Salpidae]</p><p><b>Svaka biljka iz roda Salpiglossis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Salpiglossis</p><p><b>Čileanska biljka s baršunastim, lovorastim žutavim ili ljubičastim cvijećima s dugim stilovima poput jezika na grlu korolje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Chilean herb having velvety funnel-shaped yellowish or violet flowers with long tonguelike styles at the corolla throat [painted tongue]</p><p><b>rod Troglodytidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Troglodytidae [genus Salpinctes]</p><p><b>Vratovi koji žive u pustinjama i mesama zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wren inhabiting badlands and mesa country of western United States and Mexico [rock wren]</p><p><b>operacija uklanjanja jedne ili obje jajovoda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical removal of one or both Fallopian tubes</p><p><b>upala jajovoda (obično posljedica infekcije koja se širi iz vagine ili maternice) ili eustahijske cijevi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of a Fallopian tube (usually the result of infection spreading from the vagina or uterus) or of a Eustachian tube</p><p><b>cijev u maternici ili uhu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tube in the uterus or the ear</p><p><b>začinjeni umak od paradajza i luka i čili paprike za pratiti meksičke namirnice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spicy sauce of tomatoes and onions and chili peppers to accompany Mexican foods</p><p><b>kozja brada, turovac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> edible root of the salsify plant [oyster plant]</p><p><i>n.</i> Mediterranean biennial herb with long-stemmed heads of purple ray flowers and milky sap and long edible root [Tragopogon porrifolius, oyster plant, vegetable oyster]</p><p><i>n.</i> either of two long roots eaten cooked</p><p><b>tropska loza s krunama od malih ljubičastih cvije