 of various samples</p><p><i>n.</i> a piece of embroidery demonstrating skill with various stitches</p><p><b>uzimanje uzorka, uzimatelj uzoraka, uzorkovanje, zahvaćanje uzorka, degustacija, ispitivanje, Sampliranje, uzorak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (statistics) the selection of a suitable sample for study</p><p><i>n.</i> items selected at random from a population and used to test hypotheses about the population [sample, sample distribution]</p><p><i>n.</i> measurement at regular intervals of the amplitude of a varying waveform (in order to convert it to digital form)</p><p><b>(telekomunikacije) učestalost uzorkovanja kontinuirano varirajućeg signala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (telecommunication) the frequency of sampling a continuously varying signal</p><p><b>brzina uzimanja uzoraka, brzina uzorkovanja, učestalost uzorkovanja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (telecommunication) the frequency of sampling per unit time</p><p><b>posmatračna stanica koja je postavljena za uzorak posmatranja nečega (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an observation station that is set up to make sample observations of something [sampler]</p><p><b>samsara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Hinduism and Buddhism) the endless cycle of birth and suffering and death and rebirth</p><p><b>(Stari zavjet) sudac Izraela koji je izvršio herkuleske podvige snage protiv Filistejaca dok mu ga nije izdala njegova ljubavnica Delilah., Veliki i jak i težak čovjek. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Old Testament) a judge of Israel who performed herculean feats of strength against the Philistines until he was betrayed to them by his mistress Delilah</p><p><i>n.</i> a large and strong and heavyset man [bruiser, bull, strapper]</p><p><b>Samuel</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Old Testament) Hebrew prophet and judge who anointed Saul as king</p><p><b>Američki revolucionarni vođa i patriota (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American Revolutionary leader and patriot [Adams, Sam Adams]</p><p><b>Američki skladatelj (1910-1981) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States composer (1910-1981) 