critically devout [sanctimoniousness]</p><p><b>dozvola, dozvoliti, odobrenje, odobriti, potvrda, potvrditi, sankcija, sankcionirati, imprimatur, odobravati, potvrđivati, pristajati, pristati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> formal and explicit approval [countenance, endorsement, imprimatur, indorsement, warrant]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mechanism of social control for enforcing a society's standards</p><p><i>n.</i> official permission or approval [authorisation, authority, authorization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of final authorization</p><p><i>v.</i> give sanction to [O.K., approve, okay]</p><p><i>v.</i> give authority or permission to</p><p><i>v.</i> give religious sanction to, such as through on oath</p><p><b>koji podrazumijeva sankciju ili služi sankciji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> implying sanction or serving to sanction [sanctioning]</p><p><b>dozvola, dozvoliti, odobrenje, odobriti, potvrda, potvrditi, sankcija, sankcionirati (od &quot;sanction&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> conforming to orthodox or recognized rules [canonic, canonical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> formally approved and invested with legal authority [ratified]</p><p><i>adj.</i> established by authority [approved]</p><p><b>dozvola, dozvoliti, odobrenje, odobriti, potvrda, potvrditi, sankcija, sankcionirati (od &quot;sanction&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> implying sanction or serving to sanction [sanctionative]</p><p><b>kvaliteta biti svet (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being holy [holiness, sanctity]</p><p><b>bogobojaznost, nepovredivost, pobožnost, svetost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being holy [holiness, sanctitude]</p><p><b>hram, svetišta, utočište, svetište, azil, sklonište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a consecrated place where sacred objects are kept</p><p><i>n.</i> a shelter from danger or hardship [asylum, refuge]</p><p><i>n.</i> area around the altar of a church for the clergy and choir [bema, chancel]</p><p><b>svetinja, svetište, sveto mjesto, vlastita radna soba, vlastiti kutak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a place of invi