ood osmotically from dissolved organic material</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of some plants or fungi) feeding on dead or decaying organic matter</p><p><b>organizam koji se hrani mrtvom organskom tvaru, posebno gljivom ili bakterijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organism that feeds on dead organic matter especially a fungus or bacterium [saprophyte]</p><p><b>(od određenih životinja) koje se hrane mrtvom ili trule životinjske materije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of certain animals) feeding on dead or decaying animal matter [saprophagous]</p><p><b>tvrdozeleni švicarski sir napravljen od odrezane mliječne pecive i okusan klinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hard green Swiss cheese made with skim-milk curd and flavored with clover</p><p><b>mali američki vještica koji se hrani sokom iz npr. jabuka i javorova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small American woodpecker that feeds on sap from e.g. apple and maple trees</p><p><b>bjelika, bjeljika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> newly formed outer wood lying between the cambium and the heartwood of a tree or woody plant</p><p><b>Grad u sjevernom Egiptu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in northern Egypt [Sakkara, Saqqarah]</p><p><b>Grad u sjevernom Egiptu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town in northern Egypt [Sakkara, Saqqara]</p><p><b>slabi inhibitor proteaze (trgovinski naziv Invirase) koji se koristi za liječenje HIV-a (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a weak protease inhibitor (trade name Invirase) used in treating HIV [Invirase]</p><p><b>Pjesnik iz Sjedinjenih Država (1884-1933) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States poet (1884-1933) [Teasdale]</p><p><b>glazba sastavljena za ples sarabanda, Veličanstveni dvorni ples iz 17. i 18. stoljeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> music composed for dancing the saraband</p><p><i>n.</i> a stately court dance of the 17th and 18th centuries</p><p><b>Saracen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (historically) a member of the nomadic people of the Syrian and Arabian deserts at the time of the Roman Empire</p><p><i>n.</i> (when used broadly) any Arab</p><p><i