. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a town of southern Ontario opposite northern Michigan</p><p><b>sauna, saunom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Finnish steam bath [sweat room]</p><p><b>besciljna šetnja, besposličiti, tumaranje, tumarati, šetuckanje, bazati, lunjati, lutati, prošetati, prošetati se, skitati, skitati se, vrludati, šetati, šetati se, šetuckati, švrljati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a careless leisurely gait</p><p><i>n.</i> a leisurely walk (usually in some public place) [amble, perambulation, promenade, stroll]</p><p><i>v.</i> walk leisurely and with no apparent aim [stroll]</p><p><b>besciljna šetnja, besposličiti, tumaranje, tumarati (od &quot;saunter&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who walks at a leisurely pace [ambler, stroller]</p><p><b>šarun</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large elongated compressed food fish of the Atlantic waters of Europe [Trachurus trachurus, horse mackerel]</p><p><i>n.</i> a California food fish [Spanish mackerel, Trachurus symmetricus, horse mackerel, jack mackerel]</p><p><b>pravi gušteri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> true lizards [Lacertilia, suborder Lacertilia, suborder Sauria]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih gmizavaca podred Sauria koji uključuje guštere, od ili u vezi s gušterima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various reptiles of the suborder Sauria which includes lizards</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to lizards [lacertilian]</p><p><b>izumrle kopnene gmizavce: teropode (mesojede) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct terrestrial reptiles: theropods (carnivorous) [order Saurischia]</p><p><b>biljjedoj ili mesojednoj dinosauriji s trostrukom zdjelicom poput krokodila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herbivorous or carnivorous dinosaur having a three-pronged pelvis like that of a crocodile [saurischian dinosaur]</p><p><b>biljjedoj ili mesojednoj dinosauriji s trostrukom zdjelicom poput krokodila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> herbivorous or carnivorous dinosaur having a three-pronged pelvis like that of a crocodile [saurischian]</p><p><b>čakvalle (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chuckwallas [genus Sauromalus]</p><p><b>biljjedjedjedni gušter koji živi među stijenama u sušnim dijelovima jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a herbivorous lizard that lives among rocks in the arid parts of southwestern United States and Mexico [chuckwalla]</p><p><b>vrlo veliki biljkojedni dinosaur iz Jure i Krede s malom glavom dugim vratom i repom i pet prstiju ekstremitetima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very large herbivorous dinosaur of the Jurassic and Cretaceous having a small head a long neck and tail and five-toed limbs [sauropod dinosaur]</p><p><b>vrlo veliki biljkojedni dinosaur iz Jure i Krede s malom glavom dugim vratom i repom i pet prstiju ekstremitetima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very large herbivorous dinosaur of the Jurassic and Cretaceous having a small head a long neck and tail and five-toed limbs [sauropod]</p><p><b>bilo koji od dinosaura sauropoda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the sauropod dinosaurs [suborder Sauropoda]</p><p><b>gigantski biljkožderi dinosauri s velikim tijelima s dugim vratom i malim glavama: Prosauropoda i Sauropoda (apatosaurus, diplodocus i titanosaurs) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gigantic herbivorous dinosaurs having huge bodies with long necks and small heads: Prosauropoda and Sauropoda (apatosaurus, diplodocus and titanosaurs) [suborder Sauropodomorpha]</p><p><b>izumrli morski gmizavci: pleziosauri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct marine reptiles: plesiosaurs [order Sauropterygia]</p><p><b>rani arhosovarski mesojed (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> early archosaurian carnivore [genus Saurosuchus]</p><p><b>obitelj višegodišnjih aromatičnih biljaka: rodovi Saururus, Anemopsis, Houttuynia (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of perennial aromatic herbs: genera Saururus, Anemopsis, Houttuynia [family Saururaceae, lizard's-tail family]</p><p><b>vrsta roda Saururaceae: gušter-rezi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Saururaceae: lizard's-tails [genus Saururus]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička biljna biljka s malom, bijelom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American herbaceous perennial of wet places having slender curled racemes of small white flowers [lizard's-tail, swamp lily, water dragon]</p><p><b>naziv raznih vrsta riba, skuša</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender long-beaked fish of temperate Atlantic waters [Scomberesox saurus, billfish]</p><p><b>aerostat, ćevap, kobasica, kobasa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> highly seasoned minced meat stuffed in casings</p><p><i>n.</i> a small nonrigid airship used for observation or as a barrage balloon [blimp, sausage balloon]</p><p><b>mali ne-tvrdi zračni brod koji se koristi za promatranje ili kao balon za zapornu letjelicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small nonrigid airship used for observation or as a barrage balloon [blimp, sausage]</p><p><b>masno kobasice oblikovanih kukulja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fat sausage-shaped curl</p><p><b>neformalni termin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> informal term [sausage hound]</p><p><b>neformalni termin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> informal term [sausage dog]</p><p><b>nadjev za kobasice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any meat that is minced and spiced and cooked as patties or used to fill sausages</p><p><b>paradajz i sira pizza s kobasicom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tomato and cheese pizza with sausage</p><p><b>Slijedeći proizvodi: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sausage meat rolled and baked in pastry</p><p><b>u obliku kobasice (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> shaped like a sausage [allantoid]</p><p><b>Švicarski lingvista i stručnjak za povijesnu lingvistiku čiji su predavanja postavila temelje sinhrone lingvistike (1857-1913) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Swiss linguist and expert in historical linguistics whose lectures laid the foundations for synchronic linguistics (1857-1913) [Ferdinand de Saussure, de Saussure]</p><p><b>rod biljaka umjerenih i hladnih regija Evroazije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of herbs of temperate and cool regions of Eurasia [genus Saussurea]</p><p><b>biljka iz istočne Himalaje (Kashmir) koja ima ljubičaste cvjetove i mirisan korijen koji daje plamljivo ulje koje se koristi u parfemiji i za konzervaciju krzna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual herb of the eastern Himalayas (Kashmir) having purple florets and a fragrant root that yields a volatile oil used in perfumery and for preserving furs [Saussurea lappa, costusroot]</p><p><b>biljka iz istočne Himalaje (Kashmir) koja ima ljubičaste cvjetove i mirisan korijen koji daje plamljivo ulje koje se koristi u parfemiji i za konzervaciju krzna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual herb of the eastern Himalayas (Kashmir) having purple florets and a fragrant root that yields a volatile oil used in perfumery and for preserving furs [Saussurea costus, costusroot]</p><p><b>na brzinu pržen u masti, pirjan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dish of sauteed food</p><p><i>v.</i> fry briefly over high heat</p><p><i>adj.</i> fried quickly in a little fat [sauteed]</p><p><b>na brzinu pržen u masti, pirjan (od &quot;saute&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> fried quickly in a little fat [saute]</p><p><b>prženje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cooking in fat or oil in a pan or griddle [frying]</p><p><b>poluslatko zlatno stolno ili desertno vino iz okoline Bordeaux u Francuskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> semisweet golden-colored table or dessert wine from around Bordeaux in France [Sauternes]</p><p><b>poluslatko zlatno stolno ili desertno vino iz okoline Bordeaux u Francuskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> semisweet golden-colored table or dessert wine from around Bordeaux in France [Sauterne]</p><p><b>Sauvignon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white wine grape grown in California</p><p><i>n.</i> a California wine</p><p><b>malo plavo-crno grožđe iz regije Medoc u Francuskoj visoko cijenjeno u proizvodnji vina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small blue-black grape of Medoc region of France highly prized in winemaking</p><p><b>baraba, barbar, divlja, divljak, divlji, grub čovjek, nenapučen, surov, urođenik, raspeti, barbarski, bezobziran, brutalan, divljački, okrutan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of an uncivilized people [barbarian]</p><p><i>n.</i> a cruelly rapacious person [beast, brute, wildcat, wolf]</p><p><i>v.</i> attack brutally and fiercely</p><p><i>v.</i> criticize harshly or violently [blast, crucify, pillory]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of persons or their actions) able or disposed to inflict pain or suffering [barbarous, brutal, cruel, fell, roughshod, vicious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> wild and menacing [feral, ferine]</p><p><i>adj.</i> without civilizing influences [barbarian, barbaric, uncivilised, uncivilized, wild]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by extreme and violent energy [ferocious, fierce, furious]</p><p><b>brutalno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a vicious manner [brutally, viciously]</p><p><i>adv.</i> wildly</p><p><b>barbarstvo, divljaštvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being untamed and ferocious [savagery]</p><p><b>svojstvo da bude neuhranjen i divlji, karakteristika ekstremne okrutnosti., Brutalni barbarski divlji čin. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being untamed and ferocious [savageness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of extreme cruelty [brutality, ferociousness, viciousness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a brutal barbarous savage act [barbarism, barbarity, brutality]</p><p><b>savana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flat grassland in tropical or subtropical regions [savannah]</p><p><b>savana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port in eastern Georgia near the mouth of the Savannah river</p><p><i>n.</i> a river in South Carolina that flows southeast to the Atlantic [Savannah River]</p><p><i>n.</i> a flat grassland in tropical or subtropical regions [savanna]</p><p><b>rijeka u Južnoj Karolini koja teče jugoistočno do Atlantika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in South Carolina that flows southeast to the Atlantic [Savannah]</p><p><b>mudrac, naučnik, učenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who has been admitted to membership in a scholarly field [initiate, learned person, pundit]</p><p><b>član Dravidskog naroda koji živi u južnoj Indiji, Dravidski jezik kojim govore Savare u jugoistočnoj Indiji (sjevera od Madrasa) (MT)</b></