ala)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being scalable</p><p><b>dostižan ljestvama, koji se ljušti, koji se menja bez deformiranja, mjerljiv na skali, podesiv, podesive veličine, razmjerljiv, skalabilan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being scaled</p><p><b>Procjena vrijednosti u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a), Skala za masno ili količinsko mjerenje ili dimenzije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> estimation of the amount of lumber in a log</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of scaling in weight or quantity or dimension</p><p><b>skalar, skalarni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variable quantity that cannot be resolved into components</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a musical scale</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a directionless magnitude (such as mass or speed etc.) that is completely specified by its magnitude</p><p><b>polje skalara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a field of scalars</p><p><b>dijagonalna matrica u kojoj su svi dijagonalni elementi jednaki (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a diagonal matrix in which all of the diagonal elements are equal</p><p><b>stvarni broj (skalar) koji je proizvod dva vektora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a real number (a scalar) that is the product of two vectors [dot product, inner product]</p><p><b>Bijeli južnjak koji je podržavao obnovu nakon američkog građanskog rata (obično zbog vlastitog interesa), Lažni i nepouzdani lopov., koji se igra i razvratno igra, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white Southerner who supported Reconstruction policies after the American Civil War (usually for self-interest) [scallywag]</p><p><i>n.</i> a deceitful and unreliable scoundrel [knave, rapscallion, rascal, rogue, scallywag, varlet]</p><p><i>n.</i> one who is playfully mischievous [imp, monkey, rapscallion, rascal, scallywag, scamp]</p><p><b>ofuriti, opariti, opekotina, oprljiti, ožeglina, skandinavska pjesma, sklad, skuhati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a burn cause by hot liquid or steam</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of burning with steam or hot water</p><p><i>v.</i> subject to harsh criticism [blister, whip]</p><p><i>v.</i> treat with boiling water</p><p><i>v.</i> heat to the boiling point</p><p><i>v.</i> burn with a hot liquid or steam</p><p><b>mlijeko zagrijeno gotovo do kuhanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> milk heated almost to boiling</p><p><b>glazbena ljestvica, kalati, kamenac, krljušt, ljestve, ljestvica, ljuska, ljuštiti, mjera, mjerilo, mjeriti, omjer, opseg, pjena, popeti se, popeti se na ljestve, procjenjivati, promjena veličine, ravnalo, razmjer, skakati, skala, skalirati, stepenice, strugati, stupanj, težiti, vaga, vagati, verati se, zdjelica vage, razini, vagati nešto, mjerna ljestvica, mjerna skala, oljuštiti, ostrugati, očistiti, čistiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ordered reference standard [graduated table, ordered series, scale of measurement]</p><p><i>n.</i> relative magnitude</p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio between the size of something and a representation of it</p><p><i>n.</i> a specialized leaf or bract that protects a bud or catkin [scale leaf]</p><p><i>n.</i> a thin flake of dead epidermis shed from the surface of the skin [exfoliation, scurf]</p><p><i>n.</i> (music) a series of notes differing in pitch according to a specific scheme (usually within an octave) [musical scale]</p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument for weighing [weighing machine]</p><p><i>n.</i> an indicator having a graduated sequence of marks</p><p><i>n.</i> a metal sheathing of uniform thickness (such as the shield attached to an artillery piece to protect the gunners) [plate, shell]</p><p><i>n.</i> a flattened rigid plate forming part of the body covering of many animals</p><p><i>v.</i> measure by or as if by a scale</p><p><i>v.</i> pattern, make, regulate, set, measure, or estimate according to some rate or standard</p><p><i>v.</i> take by attacking with scaling ladders</p><p><i>v.</i> reach the highest point of [surmount]</p><p><i>v.</i> climb up by means of a ladder</p><p><i>v.</i> remove the scales from [descale]</p><p><i>v.</i> measure with or as if with scales</p><p><i>v.</i> 