<b>đak, naučnik, stipendist, školarac, učenik, učenjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a learned person (especially in the humanities) [bookman, scholarly person, student]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone (especially a child) who learns (as from a teacher) or takes up knowledge or beliefs [assimilator, learner]</p><p><i>n.</i> a student who holds a scholarship</p><p><b>naučni, naučno, učen, znanstveno, znanstven</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic of scholars or scholarship</p><p><b>učenjak (posebno u humanističkim znanostima) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a learned person (especially in the humanities) [bookman, scholar, student]</p><p><b>dohodak, stipendija, stipendiranje, učenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> financial aid provided to a student on the basis of academic merit</p><p><i>n.</i> profound scholarly knowledge [encyclopaedism, encyclopedism, eruditeness, erudition, learnedness, learning]</p><p><b>formalan, pedantan, skolastički, skolastik, skolski, školnik, školski, učen, učiteljski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who pays more attention to formal rules and book learning than they merit [bookworm, pedant]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Scholastic philosopher or theologian</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to schools</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the philosophical doctrine of scholasticism</p><p><b>formalno, pedantno, skolastički</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to scholastic activities</p><p><b>sustav filozofije dominantni u srednjovjekovnoj Europi, ortodoksnost skolastičke vrste (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of philosophy dominant in medieval Europe</p><p><i>n.</i> orthodoxy of a scholastic variety [academicism, academism]</p><p><b>marginalna napomena koju je napisao učenjak (komentator antičke ili klasične književnosti) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a marginal note written by a scholiast (a commentator on ancient or classical literature) [scholium]</p><p><b>učenjak koji piše objašnjenja o autoru (posebno antički komentator o klasičnom autoru) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a scholar who writes explanatory notes on an author (especially an ancient commentator on a classical author)</p><p><b>marginalna napomena koju je napisao učenjak (komentator antičke ili klasične književnosti) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a marginal note written by a scholiast (a commentator on ancient or classical literature) [scholia]</p><p><b>rod tropskih američkih epifitnih orhideja s najozbiljnije cvjetove racemose (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of tropical American epiphytic orchids with showy racemose flowers [genus Schomburgkia]</p><p><b>Njemački kemičar koji je otkrio ozone i razvio vatreni pamuk kao gorivo u vatrenom oružju (1799-1868) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German chemist who discovered ozone and developed guncotton as a propellant in firearms (1799-1868) [Christian Friedrich Schonbein, Christian Schonbein]</p><p><b>Američki skladatelj i glazbeni teoretičar (rođen u Austriji) koji je razvio atonalnu kompoziciju (1874-1951) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States composer and musical theorist (born in Austria) who developed atonal composition (1874-1951) [Arnold Schoenberg, Arnold Schonberg, Schoenberg]</p><p><b>jato riba, škola, školovanje, školovati, školski, glazbena škola, školske, školskog, školska zgrada, jato, civilizirati, educirati, izobraziti, izobražavati, kultivirati, naobraziti, naobražavati, obrazovati, odgajati, prosvijetiti, rafinirati, trenirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an educational institution</p><p><i>n.</i> a building where young people receive education [schoolhouse]</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of being formally educated at a school [schooling]</p><p><i>n.</i> a body of creative artists or writers or thinkers linked by a similar style or by similar teachers</p><p><i>n.</i> the period of instruction in a school [school day, schooltime]</p><p><i>n.</i> an educational institution's faculty and students</p><p><i>n.</i> a large group of fish [shoal]</p><p><i>v.</i> educate in or as if in a school</p><p><i>v.</i> teach or refine to be discriminative in taste or judgment [civilise, civilize, cultivate, educate, train]</p><p><i>v.</i> swim in or form a large group of fish</p><p><b>školski zadatak koji učenici obavljaju kako bi zadovoljili učitelja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school task performed by a student to satisfy the teacher [schoolwork]</p><p><b>Zvono zvono najaviti početak ili kraj klase (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bell rung to announce beginning or ending of class</p><p><b>Upravni odbor za lokalne javne škole (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a board in charge of local public schools [board of education]</p><p><b>autobus koji se koristi za prevoz djece do ili iz škole (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bus used to transport children to or from school</p><p><b>pješački prijelaz gdje djeca školskog uzrasta prelaze ulicu na putu u školu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pedestrian crossing where school children cross a street on the way to school</p><p><b>svaki dan kada je škola u sjednici, razdoblje učenja u školi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any day on which school is in session</p><p><i>n.</i> the period of instruction in a school [school, schooltime]</p><p><b>Riječnik posebno napisan za one koji uče strani jezik. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dictionary specially written for those learning a foreign language [learner's dictionary]</p><p><b>samoupravna jedinica u javnom školstvu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a district whose public schools are administered together</p><p><b>novine koje su napisali i objavili studenti u školi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a newspaper written and published by students in a school [school paper]</p><p><b>fakultet koji nudi studije koje vode do stupnjeva stomatologije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graduate school offering study leading to degrees in dentistry [dental school]</p><p><b>fakultet koji nudi studije koje vode do diplome pravnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graduate school offering study leading to a law degree [law school]</p><p><b>fakultet koji nudi studije koje vode do diplome iz medicine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graduate school offering study leading to a medical degree [medical school]</p><p><b>konzervatorij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school for the study of music [music school]</p><p><b>škola za obuku medicinskih sestara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school for training nurses [nursing school]</p><p><b>doktrina, filozofija, nauk, naučavanje, teorija, škola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a belief (or system of beliefs) accepted as authoritative by some group or school [doctrine, ism, philosophical system, philosophy]</p><p><b>novine koje su napisali i objavili studenti u školi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a newspaper written and published by students in a school [school newspaper]</p><p><b>odjednom se dijete boji ići u školu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a child's sudden fear of attending school</p><p><b>ravnatelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the educator who has executive authority for a school [head, head teacher, principal]</p><p><b>brod koji se koristi za obuku studenata kao mornara (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ship used to train students as sailors [training ship]</p><p><b>Upravitelj školskog sustava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the superintendent of a school system</p><p><b>sustav školovanja, školski sistem, školski sustav</b></p><p><i>n.</i> establishment including the plant and equipment for providing education from kindergarten through high school</p><p><b>učitelj, učitelji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a teacher in a school below the college level [schoolteacher]</p><p><b>nastava, polugodište, predavanje, semestar, sjednica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time during which a school holds classes [academic session, academic term, session]</p><p><b>udžbenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a book prepared for use in schools or colleges [schoolbook, text, text edition, textbook]</p><p><b>školska godina, akademska godina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the period of time each year when the school is open and people are studying [academic year]</p><p><b>učenik, đak, školarac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a young person attending school (up through senior high school) [pupil, school