ice force in Nazi Germany founded as a personal bodyguard for Adolf Hitler in 1925 [SS]</p><p><b>Neutralni srednji samoglasnik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a neutral middle vowel [shwa]</p><p><b>Njemački fiziolog i histolog koji je 1838. i 1839. identificirao stanicu kao osnovnu strukturu biljnog i životinjskog tkiva (1810-1882) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German physiologist and histologist who in 1838 and 1839 identified the cell as the basic structure of plant and animal tissue (1810-1882) [Theodor Schwann]</p><p><b>bilo koja stanica koja pokriva živčana vlakna u perifernom živčanom sustavu i formira mijelinsku omotačicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any cell that covers the nerve fibers in the peripheral nervous system and forms the myelin sheath</p><p><b>planinski šumski region u jugozapadnom Njemačkoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hilly forest region in southwestern Germany [Black Forest]</p><p><b>Francuski filozof, liječnik i organist koji je većinu svog života proveo kao medicinski misionar u Gabonu (1875-1965) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French philosopher and physician and organist who spent most of his life as a medical missionary in Gabon (1875-1965) [Albert Schweitzer]</p><p><b>Švicarska</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked federal republic in central Europe [Suisse, Svizzera, Swiss Confederation, Switzerland]</p><p><b>obitelj koja obuhvaća jedan rod koji se do nedavno smatrao dijelom Taxodiaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family comprising a single genus that until recently was considered part of Taxodiaceae [family Sciadopityaceae]</p><p><b>vrsta i jedini rod Sciadopityaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type and sole genus of Sciadopityaceae [genus Sciadopitys]</p><p><b>Visoka zimzelena biljka s simetrično raširenoj krunom i iglama koje rastu u vrtljama koje na krajevima grančica podsećaju na kišobrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall evergreen having a symmetrical spreading crown and needles growing in whorls that resemble umbrellas at ends of twigs [Japanese umbrella pine]</p><p>