ue or white racemose flowers [squill]</p><p><b>ponekad stavljen u rod Scilla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sometimes placed in genus Scilla [Hyacinthoides nonscripta, bluebell, harebell, wild hyacinth, wood hyacinth]</p><p><b>Europska scilla s malim plavim ili ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European scilla with small blue or purple flowers [sea onion, spring squill]</p><p><b>arhipelag malih otoka kod jugozapadne obale Engleske u blizini ulaza u Kanal (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an archipelago of small islands off the southwestern coast of England near the entrance to the English Channel [Isles of Scilly]</p><p><b>kriva sablja, krivošija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a curved oriental saber</p><p><b>rod gmizavaca Scincidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reptile genus of Scincidae [genus Scincella]</p><p><b>Besplatno, okretno gušter sa smanjenim udovima i izduženim tijelom prekrivenim sjajnim ljuskama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> alert agile lizard with reduced limbs and an elongated body covered with shiny scales [scincid lizard, skink]</p><p><b>Besplatno, okretno gušter sa smanjenim udovima i izduženim tijelom prekrivenim sjajnim ljuskama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> alert agile lizard with reduced limbs and an elongated body covered with shiny scales [scincid, skink]</p><p><b>škrobovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> skinks [family Scincidae]</p><p><b>vrsta rod Scincidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of Scincidae [genus Scincus]</p><p><b>Zeleni uzorci s lepljivim korenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen climbers with adhesive adventitious roots [genus Pothos, genus Scindapsus]</p><p><b>Zeleni lijana, široko uzgajana zbog svog raznovrsnog lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen liana widely cultivated for its variegated foliage [Epipremnum aureum, golden pothos, ivy arum, pothos]</p><p><b>mrvica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tiny or scarcely detectable amount [iota, shred, smidge, smidgen, smidgeon, smidgin, tittle, whit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sparkling glittering particle</p><p><b>s kratkim blistavim točkama ili bljeskom svjetlosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having brief brilliant points or flashes of light [aglitter, coruscant, fulgid, glinting, glistering, glittering, glittery, scintillating, sparkly]</p><p><b>iskriti se, svjetlucati, treperiti, iskriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give off</p><p><i>v.</i> reflect brightly [coruscate, sparkle]</p><p><i>v.</i> emit or reflect light in a flickering manner [twinkle, winkle]</p><p><i>v.</i> physics: fluoresce momentarily when struck by a charged particle or high-energy photon</p><p><i>v.</i> be lively or brilliant or exhibit virtuosity [coruscate, sparkle]</p><p><b>iskriti se, svjetlucati, treperiti (od &quot;scintillate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> brilliantly clever</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by high spirits or excitement [bubbling, effervescent, frothy, sparkly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having brief brilliant points or flashes of light [aglitter, coruscant, fulgid, glinting, glistering, glittering, glittery, scintillant, sparkly]</p><p><b>Lokalno područje smanjenog vida obrušeno treperljivim svjetlima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a localized area of diminished vision edged by shimmering colored lights [flittering scotoma]</p><p><b>iskrenje, svjetlucanje, treperenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a flash of light that is produced in a phosphor when it absorbs a photon or ionizing particle</p><p><i>n.</i> a rapid change in brightness [sparkling, twinkle]</p><p><i>n.</i> a brilliant display of wit</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of shining with a bright reflected light [glisten, glister, glitter, sparkle]</p><p><i>n.</i> the twinkling of the stars caused when changes in the density of the earth's atmosphere produce uneven refraction of starlight</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> counter tube in which light flashes when exposed to ionizing radiation</p><p><b>Pretenziozna površnost znanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pretentious superficiality of knowledge</p><p><b>diletant</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an 