adj.</i> of the most contemptible kind [abject, low, low-down, miserable, scurvy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with scum</p><p><b>gađenje, zgaditi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strong dislike</p><p><b>meso ribe pronađeno u hladnijim vodama sjeverne obale Atlantskog mora Sjedinjenih Država, slanost ribe koja se nalazi u toplim vodama južne obale Atlantskog mora Sjedinjenih Država, Udio u ribljem prometu u Južnom Atlantiku, nalazi se u atlantskim obalnim vodama Sjeverne Amerike od Južne Karoline do Mainea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flesh of fish found in colder waters of northern Atlantic coast of the United States</p><p><i>n.</i> lean flesh of fish found in warm waters of southern Atlantic coast of the United States [porgy]</p><p><i>n.</i> porgy of southern Atlantic coastal waters of North America [Stenotomus aculeatus, southern porgy, southern scup]</p><p><i>n.</i> found in Atlantic coastal waters of North America from South Carolina to Maine [Stenotomus chrysops, northern porgy, northern scup]</p><p><b>lakomica, odljev s palube, otvor za otjecanje, palubna rupa za otjecanje, vrebati, izvrgnuti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> drain that allows water on the deck of a vessel to flow overboard</p><p><i>v.</i> wait in hiding to attack [ambuscade, ambush, bushwhack, lie in wait, lurk, waylay]</p><p><i>v.</i> put in a dangerous, disadvantageous, or difficult position [endanger, expose, peril, queer]</p><p><b>grm od južnoistočnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> amber-green muscadine grape of southeastern United States</p><p><b>kora, krasta, perut, prhut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (botany) a covering that resembles scales or bran that covers some plant parts</p><p><i>n.</i> a thin flake of dead epidermis shed from the surface of the skin [exfoliation, scale]</p><p><b>pun peruti</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or producing or covered with scurf</p><p><i>adj.</i> rough to the touch [lepidote, leprose, scabrous, scaly]</p><p><b>gruba šala, uvredljiva primjedba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> foul-mouthed or obscene abuse [billingsgate]</p><p><b>grub, podrugljiv, uvredljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> expressing offensive reproach [abusive, opprobrious]</p><p><b>grub, podrugljiv, uvredljiv (od &quot;scurrilous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a scurrilously manner</p><p><b>juriti, jurnjava, hitati, odjuriti, pohitati, pojuriti, požuriti, požuriti se, žuriti, žuriti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rushing about hastily in an undignified way [scamper, scramble]</p><p><i>v.</i> to move about or proceed hurriedly [scamper, scuttle, skitter]</p><p><b>juriti, jurnjava (od &quot;scurry&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> moving with great haste [hurrying]</p><p><b>bolest prouzročena pomanjkanjem vitamina, nizak, podao, prljav, skorbut, za preziranje (od &quot;scurvy&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a despicable, ignoble manner [basely, meanly]</p><p><b>bolest prouzročena pomanjkanjem vitamina, nizak, podao, prljav, skorbut, za preziranje, bijedan, opak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a condition caused by deficiency of ascorbic acid (vitamin C) [scorbutus]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of the most contemptible kind [abject, low, low-down, miserable, scummy]</p><p><b>Arktički krest koji se široko rasprostranjuje i za koji se smatra da ima vrijednost u liječenju ili prevenciji skorbuta, bilo koja biljka rodova Barbarea: žutocvjetna evroazijska krastavca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a widely distributed Arctic cress reputed to have value in treatment or prevention of scurvy [Cochlearia officinalis, common scurvy grass]</p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Barbarea: yellow-flowered Eurasian cresses [St. Barbara's herb, winter cress]</p><p><b>kusat repić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short erect tail</p><p><b>beznačajni, bezuspješni, dosadni, prljavi i neprijatni poslovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trivial, unrewarding, tedious, dirty, and disagreeable chores [shitwork]</p><p><b>Trailing trave porijeklom iz Europe sada kosmopolitski u toplim regijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trailing grass native to Europe now cosmopolitan in warm regions [Bahama grass, Bermuda grass, Cynodon dactylon, devil grass, doob, kweek, star grass]</p><p><b>za zaštitu od štetnih prstiju, štit. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flat protective covering (on a door or wall etc) to prevent soiling by dirty fingers [escutcheon, finger plate]</p><p><i>n.</i> a shield [escutcheon]</p><p><b>Velika kostna ili rogovita ploča kao na armadilu ili kornjači ili donjoj strani zmije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large bony or horny plate as on an armadillo or turtle or the underside of a snake</p><p><b>rod dikota koji uključuje lubanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an asterid dicot genus that includes the skullcaps [genus Scutellaria]</p><p><b>Američki mentni rastvor koji daje smolastan izlučivanje korišteno posebno u prošlosti kao antispasmodic (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an American mint that yields a resinous exudate used especially formerly as an antispasmodic [blue pimpernel, blue skullcap, mad-dog skullcap, mad-dog weed]</p><p><b>rod Scutigeridae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Scutigeridae [genus Scutigera]</p><p><b>dugonogi stonožci u vlažnim mjestima kao što su podrumovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> long-legged centipede common in damp places as e.g. cellars [house centipede]</p><p><b>vrtne stonožcice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> garden centipedes [genus Scutigerella]</p><p><b>minijaturni članonožci koji često zaraze podzemne dijelove vrtova i staklenika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> minute arthropod often infesting the underground parts of truck-garden and greenhouse crops [garden centipede, garden symphilid, symphilid]</p><p><b>porodica Chilopoda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of Chilopoda [family Scutigeridae]</p><p><b>bijeg, bježati, juriti, nagao odlazak, otvor, posuda za ugljen, potopiti brod, probušiti brod, spašavati se, žuran hod, hitati, odjuriti, pohitati, pojuriti, požuriti, požuriti se, žuriti, žuriti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> container for coal [coal scuttle]</p><p><i>n.</i> an entrance equipped with a hatch [hatchway, opening]</p><p><i>v.</i> to move about or proceed hurriedly [scamper, scurry, skitter]</p><p><b>naklapanja, ogovaranje, olajavanje, trač, tračanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a report (often malicious) about the behavior of other people [comment, gossip]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small bottom-dwelling sharks [family Scyliorhinidae]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) morska nimfa pretvorena u morsko čudovište koja je živjela na jednoj strani uskog tjesnaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) a sea nymph transformed into a sea monster who lived on one side of a narrow strait</p><p><b>režnjaci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coelenterates in which the polyp stage is absent or at least inconspicuous: jellyfishes [class Scyphozoa]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih obično slobodno plivajućih morskih koelenterata koji imaju želatinušnu meduzovsku fazu kao dominantnu fazu svog životnog ciklusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various usually free-swimming marine coelenterates having a gelatinous medusoid stage as the dominant phase of its life cycle</p><p><b>Stari grčki čaša za piće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Greek drinking cup</p><p><b>kosa, kositi, pokositi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edge tool for cutting grass</p><p><i>v.</i> cut with a scythe</p><p><b>drevno područje Evroazije koje se proteže od Crnog mora do Aralskog mora i koje su naseljeni Skiti od osmog do četvrtog stoljeća prije Krista. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient area of Eurasia extending from the Black Sea to the Aral Sea that was populated by Scythians from the eighth to the fourth century BC</p><p><b>Skit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the ancient nomadic people inhabiting Scythia</p><p><i>n.</i> the Iranian language spoken by the ancient Scythians</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the ancient Scythians or their culture or language</p><p><b>Azijski drveni paprika sa gustim spuštenim dlakama ponekad se koristi kao styptic (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Asiatic tree fern having dense matted hairs sometimes used as a styptic [Cibotium barometz]</p><p><b>država u sjeverno-srednjem dijelu Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in north central United States [Coyote State, Mount Rushmore State, S.D., South Dakota]</p><p><b>mijenjati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic nonmetallic element related to sulfur and tellurium [atomic number 34, selenium]</p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point midway between south and east [sou'-east, southeast, southeastward]</p><p><b>bedem, brana, mnoštvo, more, morski, morski val, nasip, ocean, pomorski, velika količina, masa, mora, morem, morske, morskih, morskom, moru</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a division of an ocean or a large body of salt water partially enclosed by land</p><p><i>n.</i> anything apparently limitless in quantity or volume [ocean]</p><p><i>n.</i> turbulent water with swells of considerable size</p><p><b>plutajuće olujno sidro</b></p><p><i>n.</i> restraint consisting of a canvas covered frame that floats behind a vessel [drogue]</p><p><b>morska anemona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marine polyps that resemble flowers but have oral rings of tentacles [anemone]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u ovom slučaju ne primjenjuje primjena članka 3. stavka 1. točke (a) ovog članka, točka (b) ovog članka ne primjenjuje se na sve druge vrste životinja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous animals inhabiting the sea including e.g. fishes and molluscs and many mammals [marine animal, marine creature, sea creature]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je proizvodnja proizvoda u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom ( (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small deciduous aromatic shrub (or tree) having spiny branches and yellowish flowers [Zanthoxylum americanum, Zanthoxylum fraxineum, toothache tree]</p><p><b>Obični europski aster koji raste u solnim močvarama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common European aster that grows in salt marshes [Aster tripolium, sea starwort]</p><p><b>brancin, lubin, brancini</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the lean flesh of a saltwater fish of the family Serranidae [bass]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various food and sport fishes of the Atlantic coast of the United States having an elongated body and long spiny dorsal fin</p><p><b>kupanje u moru ili oceanu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bathing in the sea or ocean</p><p><b>ptica koja često živi u obalnim vodama i otvorenom oceanu: galebovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bird that frequents coastal waters and the open ocean: gulls [seabird, seafowl]</p><p><b>vrlo tvrdi nesoljeni kolačići ili kruh (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very hard unsalted biscuit or bread [hardtack, pilot biscuit, pilot bread, ship biscuit]</p><p><b>brod koji je plovit (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a boat that is seaworthy</p><p><b>morsko dno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bottom of a sea or ocean [Davy Jones, Davy Jones's locker, ocean bottom, ocean floor, sea floor, seabed]</p><p><b>arbun</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flesh of any of various saltwater fishes of the family Sparidae or the family Bramidae [bream]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous marine percoid fishes especially (but not exclusively) of the family Sparidae [bream]</p><p><b>obalna cirkulacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cooling breeze from the sea (during the daytime)</p><p><b>kapetan, kapetan bojnog broda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an officer who is licensed to command a merchant ship [captain, master, skipper]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih morskih riba od kojih su većina usta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous marine fishes most of which are mouthbreeders</p><p><b>duboko preobrazbu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a profound transformation</p><p><b>ritmična radna pjesma koju su izvorno pjevali mornari. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rhythmical work song originally sung by sailors [chantey, chanty, shanty]</p><p><b>mornarov sanduk za pohranu osobnih stvari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sailor's storage chest for personal property</p><p><b>Ribe u školjama uglavnom iz Indijskog i zapadnog Tihog oceana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> schooling fishes mostly of Indian and western Pacific oceans</p><p><b>bitumeni ugalj u prahu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pulverized bituminous coal</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka od obalnih pijesaka i šindla sjeverne Europe i Baltičkog i Crnog mora s rascima malih bijeli cvijeće i velikih mesnih plavo-zelenih listova često se koristi kao biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of coastal sands and shingles of northern Europe and Baltic and Black Seas having racemes of small white flowers and large fleshy blue-green leaves often used as potherbs [Crambe maritima, sea kale]</p><p><b>bilo koja od dvije obitelji velikih biljnih vodenih sisavaca s repovima u obliku vesla i prednjim udovima nalik perajima, a bez stražnjih udova. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of two families of large herbivorous aquatic mammals with paddle-shaped tails and flipper-like forelimbs and no hind limbs [sirenian, sirenian mammal]</p><p><b>primitivni izduženi bilateralno simetrični morski mehurići s plaštom prekrivenom osam apnenim pločama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> primitive elongated bilaterally symmetrical marine mollusk having a mantle covered with eight calcareous plates [chiton, coat-of-mail shell, polyplacophore]</p><p><b>veliki jedljivi morski rakovi koji imaju trnasti ljusak ali nemaju velike klesnice pravih jastoga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large edible marine crustacean having a spiny carapace but lacking the large pincers of true lobsters [crawfish, crayfish, langouste, rock lobster, spiny lobster]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u ovom slučaju ne primjenjuje primjena članka 3. stavka 1. točke (a) ovog članka, točka (b) ovog članka ne primjenjuje se na sve druge vrste životinja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous animals inhabiting the sea including e.g. fishes and molluscs and many mammals [marine animal, marine creature, sea animal]</p><p><b>Echinoderma s fleksibilnim kobasičnim tijelom, pipcima oko usta i cijevama stopala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> echinoderm having a flexible sausage-shaped body, tentacles surrounding the mouth and tube feet [holothurian]</p><p><b>čvrsta biljka s cvijećem od jednog do stabla. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stout herb with flowers one to a stalk [Coreopsis maritima]</p><p><b>moreplovac, pomorac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who serves as a sailor [Jack, Jack-tar, gob, mariner, old salt, seafarer, seaman, tar]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih velikih pataka za ronjenje koje se nalaze uz obalu mora: eider (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various large diving ducks found along the seacoast: eider</p><p><b>bukoč</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large harmless hawk found worldwide that feeds on fish and builds a bulky nest often occupied for years [Pandion haliaetus, fish eagle, fish hawk, osprey]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various large eagles that usually feed on fish</p><p><b>ili od dva velika morska tjeločina bez ušiju iz sjevernog Atlantika s čipom poput debla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two large northern Atlantic earless seals having snouts like trunks [elephant seal]</p><p><b>Europski vječnozeleni eringo s iskrivljenim trnastima lištima naturaliziran na istočnoj obali Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European evergreen eryngo with twisted spiny leaves naturalized on United States east coast [Eryngium maritimum, sea holly, sea holm]</p><p><b>Koralji s kožnim skeletom u obliku stabla ili ventilatora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> corals having a treelike or fan-shaped horny skeleton</p><p><b>Koralji koji formiraju kolonije nalik perjima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> corals forming featherlike colonies</p><p><b>dno mora ili oceana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bottom of a sea or ocean [Davy Jones, Davy Jones's locker, ocean bottom, ocean floor, sea bottom, seabed]</p><p><b>Boginja koja personifikuje more i za koju se obično vjeruje da živi u moru ili da ga kontroliše. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deity that personifies the sea and is usually believed to live in or to control the sea</p><p><b>ctenofora s zaobljenim tijelom s uzdužnim redovima cilija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ctenophore having a rounded body with longitudinal rows of cilia</p><p><b>svojstvo umjerene zelene boje koja podsjeća na morske vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of a moderate green color resembling the waters of the sea</p><p><b>galeb, morski galeb</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mostly white aquatic bird having long pointed wings and short legs [gull, seagull]</p><p><b>goli morski gastropod s mekim tijelom s smanjenom unutarnjom školjkom i dva para udobnih pipaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> naked marine gastropod having a soft body with reduced internal shell and two pairs of ear-like tentacles [Aplysia punctata]</p><p><b>kotrljan, brmeč, brmak, sikavac, sikavica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European evergreen eryngo with twisted spiny leaves naturalized on United States east coast [Eryngium maritimum, sea eryngium, sea holm]</p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated southern European acanthus with whitish purple-veined flowers [Acanthus mollis, bear's breech, bear's breeches]</p><p><b>Europski vječnozeleni eringo s iskrivljenim trnastima lištima naturaliziran na istočnoj obali Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European evergreen eryngo with twisted spiny leaves naturalized on United States east coast [Eryngium maritimum, sea eryngium, sea holly]</p><p><b>Odobenus rosmarus, morž</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two large northern marine mammals having ivory tusks and tough hide over thick blubber [seahorse, walrus]</p><p><i>n.</i> small fish with horse-like heads bent sharply downward and curled tails [seahorse]</p><p><b>malo grmlje koje raste na otocima Kariba i na obali Atlantskog mora južne Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small bushy tree grown on islands of the Caribbean and off the Atlantic coast of the southern United States [Gossypium barbadense, tree cotton]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka od obalnih pijesaka i šindla sjeverne Europe i Baltičkog i Crnog mora s rascima malih bijeli cvijeće i velikih mesnih plavo-zelenih listova često se koristi kao biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of coastal sands and shingles of northern Europe and Baltic and Black Seas having racemes of small white flowers and large fleshy blue-green leaves often used as potherbs [Crambe maritima, sea cole]</p><p><b>Voditelj vikingskog gusara. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Viking pirate chief</p><p><b>(nautički) stubić koji se spušta preko strane broda za ulazak na brod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (nautical) ladder to be lowered over a ship's side for coming aboard [sea steps]</p><p><b>Veliki anadromični lampreji koji se ponekad koriste kao hrana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large anadromous lamprey sometimes used as food [Petromyzon marinus]</p><p><b>putanje na moru koje je redovito korištena ruta za plovila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lane at sea that is a regularly used route for vessels [seaway, ship route, trade route]</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka iz roda Limonium u umjereno-solnim močvarama s šiljcima bijele ili ljubičaste boje cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Limonium of temperate salt marshes having spikes of white or mauve flowers [marsh rosemary, statice]</p><p><b>morski pas</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an argumentative and contentious seaman</p><p><b>U slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka ne primjenjuje na druge vrste biljaka, to znači da se u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka ne primjenjuje na druge vrste biljaka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> seaweed with edible translucent crinkly green fronds [laver]</p><p><b>razina mora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> level of the ocean's surface (especially that halfway between mean high and low tide)</p><p><b>crinoid s osjetljivim izdajni rukama i stablo tijelo vezano za tvrdu površinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crinoid with delicate radiating arms and a stalked body attached to a hard surface</p><p><b>vrsta tuljana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several large eared seals of the northern Pacific related to fur seals but lacking their valuable coat</p><p><b>morski izopodni rakovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marine isopod crustacean [sea slater]</p><p><b>trava iz duna na pacifičkoj obali koja se koristi kao vezivač za pijesak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dune grass of the Pacific seacoast used as a sand binder [Elymus arenarius, European dune grass, Leymus arenaria]</p><p><b>sedzilo vodena životinja koja formira mahaste kolonije malih polipa s zakrivljenim ili kružnim grebenom s pipcima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sessile aquatic animal forming mossy colonies of small polyps each having a curved or circular ridge bearing tentacles [bryozoan, moss animal, polyzoan, sea moss]</p><p><b>Čarobnjak u Euroaziji i sjeveroistočnoj Sjevernoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the common gull of Eurasia and northeastern North America [Larus canus, mew, mew gull]</p><p><b>bivša britanska jedinica dužine koja se nekada koristila u plovidbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former British unit of length once used in navigation [mile]</p><p><b>mala mesna biljka uobičajena uz sjevernoameričke obale i u slane močvare s ružičastim ili bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small fleshy herb common along North American seashores and in brackish marshes having pink or white flowers [Glaux maritima, black saltwort, sea trifoly]</p><p><b>sedzilo vodena životinja koja formira mahaste kolonije malih polipa s zakrivljenim ili kružnim grebenom s pipcima, Svaka vrsta crvenih algi s gracioznim ružnim do ljubičastim lištima (npr. dulse ili carrageen) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sessile aquatic animal forming mossy colonies of small polyps each having a curved or circular ridge bearing tentacles [bryozoan, moss animal, polyzoan, sea mat]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various red algae having graceful rose to purple fronds (e.g. dulse or carrageen)</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko velikih crva s širokim ravnim tijelom s podložom grubih dlaka koje prekrivaju leđa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several large worms having a broad flattened body with a mat of coarse hairs covering the back</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) vodena nimfa koja je bila kći Okeana ili Nerea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) a water nymph who was the daughter of Oceanus or Nereus</p><p><b>zaljev Crnog mora između Rusije i Ukrajine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bay of the Black Sea between Russia and the Ukraine [Sea of Azoff, Sea of Azov]</p><p><b>zaljev Crnog mora između Rusije i Ukrajine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bay of the Black Sea between Russia and the Ukraine [Sea of Azof, Sea of Azov]</p><p><b>zaljev Crnog mora između Rusije i Ukrajine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bay of the Black Sea between Russia and the Ukraine [Sea of Azof, Sea of Azoff]</p><p><b>Zaljev zapadno od kopna Meksika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gulf to the west of the mainland of Mexico [Gulf of California]</p><p><b>Tihi okean na granici s Japanom, Korejom, Sjevernom Korejom i Rusijom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arm of the Pacific bordered by Japan, Korea, North Korea, and Russia [East Sea]</p><p><b>unutrašnje more u sjeverozapadnoj Turskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inland sea in northwestern Turkey [Marmara, Marmara Denizi, Marmora, Sea of Marmora]</p><p><b>unutrašnje more u sjeverozapadnoj Turskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inland sea in northwestern Turkey [Marmara, Marmara Denizi, Marmora, Sea of Marmara]</p><p><b>ruka Pacifika na istoku Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arm of the Pacific to the east of Asia</p><p><b>s gustima šiljcima malih bijelih cvijeća i s lukom s ljekovitim svojstvima, Europska scilla s malim plavim ili ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having dense spikes of small white flowers and yielding a bulb with medicinal properties [Urginea maritima, sea squill, squill]</p><p><i>n.</i> European scilla with small blue or purple flowers [Scilla verna, spring squill]</p><p><b>Veliki morski vidra severnopacifičkih obala s vrlo gustim tamno smeđim krznom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large marine otter of northern Pacific coasts having very thick dark brown fur [Enhydra lutris]</p><p><b>divlji grašak s obalnih područja sjeverne umjerene zone, čvrsti korijeni i ljubičasti cvijet, koristan za vezanje pijeska (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wild pea of seashores of north temperate zone having tough roots and purple flowers and useful as a sand binder [Lathyrus japonicus, Lathyrus maritimus, beach pea]</p><p><b>masno-pernate kolonije tople vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fleshy featherlike warm-water colonies</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste usmjerenih na životinje iz područja područja za koje se primjenjuje točka (a) ovog članka, za životinje iz područja za koje se primjenjuje točka (b) ovog članka, za životinje iz područja za koje se primjenjuje točka (c) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći odredbi: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tufted thrift of seacoasts and mountains of north temperate zone [Armeria maritima, cliff rose]</p><p><b>Ribe su male i vitke (do 8 inča) s tijelom prekrivenim kostnim pločama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small slender fish (to 8 inches) with body covered by bony plates [poacher, sea poker]</p><p><b>Ribe su male i vitke (do 8 inča) s tijelom prekrivenim kostnim pločama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small slender fish (to 8 inches) with body covered by bony plates [poacher, sea poacher]</p><p><b>žutocvjetna evroazijska žuljka prirodna uz pješčane obale u istočnoj Sjevernoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> yellow-flowered Eurasian glaucous herb naturalized in along sandy shores in eastern North America [Glaucium flavum, horn poppy, horned poppy, yellow horned poppy]</p><p><b>pomorska snaga, Nacija koja posjeduje strahovitu pomorsku snagu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> naval strength</p><p><i>n.</i> a nation that possesses