ies enclosed in thin spiny globular shells</p><p><b>morski vuk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> predatory black-and-white toothed whale with large dorsal fin [Orcinus orca, grampus, killer, killer whale, orca]</p><p><b>biljke zapadnih i sjevernoeuropskih obala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plants of western and northern European coasts [Artemisia maritima, Seriphidium maritimum]</p><p><b>podmorna biljka s vrlo dugim uskim listovima koja se u izobilju nalazi duž sjevernoatlantskih obala, rast morske vegetacije, posebno velikih vrsta poput kamenih trava i morskih morskih voda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> submerged marine plant with very long narrow leaves found in abundance along North Atlantic coasts [Zostera marina, eelgrass, grass wrack]</p><p><i>n.</i> growth of marine vegetation especially of the large forms such as rockweeds and kelp [wrack]</p><p><b>morska obala, obala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the shore of a sea or ocean [coast, seacoast, seashore]</p><p><b>pomorska služba na brodu na moru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> naval service aboard a ship at sea [service abroad, shipboard duty]</p><p><b>morski morski pas pronađen u blizini Kanalskih otoka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abalone found near the Channel Islands [Haliotis tuberculata, ormer]</p><p><b>boje mora. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of the color of the sea</p><p><b>biljke i grmovi iz stabala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial herbs and shrubs and lianas [Plumbaginaceae, family Plumbaginaceae, leadwort family]</p><p><b>gornje ili donje dijelove površine; (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thin flat or tubular green algae [Ulvaceae, family Ulvaceae]</p><p><b>razina mora</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lying below the normal level [low-lying]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je to potrebno za utvrđivanje vrijednosti, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, za svaku od tih vrijednosti utvrđuje se: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the atmospheric pressure reduced by a formula to the pressure at sea level</p><p><b>Podtokom u smjeru mora stvoren nakon što su val