]</p><p><i>v.</i> foam as if boiling</p><p><i>v.</i> boil vigorously [roll]</p><p><b>kipjeti, klokotati, pjeniti se, vreti (od &quot;seethe&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in constant agitation</p><p><b>Američki skulptor (rođen 1924.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States sculptor (born in 1924) [George Segal]</p><p><b>dio, duž, isječak, koluti, odjeljak, odsječak, odsječak (skupa podataka ili mreže), odvojiti na dijelove, segment, segmentima, odlomak, segmentirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of several parts or pieces that fit with others to constitute a whole object [section]</p><p><i>n.</i> one of the parts into which something naturally divides</p><p><i>v.</i> divide into segments [section]</p><p><i>v.</i> divide or split up</p><p><b>segmentni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> divided or organized into speech segments or isolable speech sounds</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the body divided into successive metameres or segments, as in earthworms or lobsters [metameric, segmented]</p><p><b>Plitki luk. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shallow arch</p><p><b>dijeljenje na odsječke, etažiranje, odvajanje, podjela programa, segmentacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (embryology) the repeated division of a fertilised ovum [cleavage]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of dividing or partitioning [division, partition, partitioning, sectionalisation, sectionalization]</p><p><b>šupljina ispunjena tekućinom unutar blastule (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fluid-filled cavity inside a blastula [blastocele, blastocoel, blastocoele, cleavage cavity]</p><p><b>dio, duž, isječak, koluti, odjeljak, odsječak, odsječak (skupa podataka ili mreže), odvojiti na dijelove, segment, segmentima (od &quot;segment&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the body divided into successive metameres or segments, as in earthworms or lobsters [metameric, segmental]</p><p><b>kolutićavac, kolutićavci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> worms with cylindrical bodies segmented both internally and externally [annelid, annelid worm]</p><p><b>(glazba) nota napisana na početku i