n, uzbudljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing intense interest, curiosity, or emotion</p><p><i>adj.</i> commanding attention [arresting, stunning]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or concerned in sensation [sensory]</p><p><b>senzacionalizam, empirizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> subject matter that is calculated to excite and please vulgar tastes</p><p><i>n.</i> the journalistic use of subject matter that appeals to vulgar tastes [luridness]</p><p><i>n.</i> (philosophy) the ethical doctrine that feeling is the only criterion for what is good [sensualism]</p><p><i>n.</i> (philosophy) the doctrine that knowledge derives from experience [empiricism, empiricist philosophy]</p><p><b>netko tko koristi pretjerane ili odvratne materijale kako bi privukao javnu pažnju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who uses exaggerated or lurid material in order to gain public attention [ballyhoo artist]</p><p><b>tipično za tabloide. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> typical of tabloids [scandalmongering, yellow]</p><p><b>senzacionalan, uzbudljiv (od &quot;sensational&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a sensational manner</p><p><b>čitanje, čitati, čulo, dojam, ispitati, ispitivanje, misao, mišljenje, naslutiti, očitavati, odrediti smjer, opažati, osjećaj, osjećanje, osjet, osjetiti, pamet, razum, saznanje, shvatiti, smisao, smjer, svijest, zdrav razum, značenje, smislu, osjetilna sposobnost, osjetilo, osjećati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a general conscious awareness</p><p><i>n.</i> the meaning of a word or expression [signified]</p><p><i>n.</i> the faculty through which the external world is apprehended [sensation, sensory faculty, sentience, sentiency]</p><p><i>n.</i> sound practical judgment [common sense, good sense, gumption, horse sense, mother wit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a natural appreciation or ability</p><p><i>v.</i> perceive by a physical sensation, e.g., coming from the skin or muscles [feel]</p><p><i>v.</i> detect some circumstance or entity automatically</p><p><i>v.</i> become aware of not through the senses but