ovements of the limbs and body [kinaesthesia, kinaesthesis, kinesthesia, kinesthesis, kinesthetics, muscle sense]</p><p><b>osobina koja ima određenu svrhu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of having a definite purpose [purposefulness]</p><p><b>svjesnost svojih obveza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an awareness of your obligations</p><p><b>savjest</b></p><p><i>n.</i> motivation deriving logically from ethical or moral principles that govern a person's thoughts and actions [conscience, moral sense, scruples]</p><p><b>motivirajuća svijest o etičkoj odgovornosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a motivating awareness of ethical responsibility [sense of duty]</p><p><b>osjetilo njuha, njuh</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the faculty that enables us to distinguish scents [olfaction, olfactory modality, smell]</p><p><b>okus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the faculty of distinguishing sweet, sour, bitter, and salty properties in the mouth [gustation, gustatory modality, taste]</p><p><b>opće suglasnosti skupine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> general agreement reached by an assembled group</p><p><b>dodir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the faculty by which external objects or forces are perceived through contact with the body (especially the hands) [cutaneous senses, skin senses, touch, touch modality]</p><p><b>osjetilni organ, osjetni receptor, receptor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organ having nerve endings (in the skin or viscera or eye or ear or nose or mouth) that respond to stimulation [receptor, sensory receptor]</p><p><b>program za označavanje čije oznake ukazuju na značenje riječi ili izraza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tagging program whose labels indicate the meanings of words or expressions</p><p><b>gras, marica, trava, vutra (od &quot;sens&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> detected by instinct or inference rather than by recognized perceptual cues [perceived]</p><p><b>besmislen, bez života, glup, mrtav, nerazuman, u nesvijesti</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not marked by the use of reason [mindless, reasonless]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unresponsive to stimulation [insensible, out of it]</p><p><i>adj.</i> serving no useful purpose [otiose, pointless, purposeless, superfluous, wasted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of especially persons) lacking sense or understanding or judgment [nitwitted, soft-witted, witless]</p><p><b>besmislen, bez života, glup, mrtav, nerazuman, u nesvijesti (od &quot;senseless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a meaningless and purposeless manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> in an unreasonably senseless manner [mindlessly]</p><p><b>besmislen, bez života, glup, mrtav, nerazuman, u nesvijesti (od &quot;senseless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> total lack of meaning or ideas [inanity, mindlessness, pointlessness, vacuity]</p><p><b>učiniti osjetljivim ili svjesnim (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make sensitive or aware [sensibilize, sensify, sensitise, sensitize]</p><p><b>osjećajnost, osjetljivost, točnost, senzibilitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mental responsiveness and awareness [aesthesia, esthesia]</p><p><i>n.</i> refined sensitivity to pleasurable or painful impressions</p><p><i>n.</i> (physiology) responsiveness to external stimuli [sensitiveness, sensitivity]</p><p><b>učiniti osjetljivim ili svjesnim (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make sensitive or aware [sensibilise, sensify, sensitise, sensitize]</p><p><b>opipljiv, osjetan, osjetljiv, pametan, razborit, razuman, svjestan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing reason or sound judgment [reasonable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> able to feel or perceive [sensitive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> readily perceived by the senses</p><p><i>adj.</i> aware intuitively or intellectually of something sensed</p><p><b>obzor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the line at which the sky and Earth appear to meet [apparent horizon, horizon, skyline, visible horizon]</p><p><b>opipljiv, osjetan, osjetljiv, pametan, razborit, razuman, svjestan (od &quot;sensible&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of showing good sense or practical judgment</p><p><b>osjetno, primjetno, razumno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with good sense or in a reasonable or intelligent manner [reasonably, sanely]</p><p><b>učiniti osjetljivim ili svjesnim (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make sensitive or aware [sensibilise, sensibilize, sensitise, sensitize]</p><p><b>očitavanje, opažanje, osjećanje, osjetni, raspoznavanje, otkrivanje, percepcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the perception that something has occurred or some state exists [detection]</p><p><i>n.</i> becoming aware of something via the senses [perception]</p><p><b>detektor, otkrivač, senzor, senzora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any device that receives a signal or stimulus (as heat or pressure or light or motion etc.) and responds to it in a distinctive manner [detector, sensor]</p><p><b>senzibilizacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being sensitive (as to an antigen) [sensitization]</p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) the process of becoming highly sensitive to specific events or situations (especially emotional events or situations) [sensitization]</p><p><i>n.</i> rendering an organism sensitive to a serum by a series of injections [sensitising, sensitization, sensitizing]</p><p><b>Razlog za osjećaj, osjetljivi na lijek ili alergen, S druge strane, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 98. točka (a) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći postupak:, učiniti osjetljivim ili svjesnim (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to sense [sensitize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make sensitive to a drug or allergen [sensitize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make (a material) sensitive to light, often of a particular colour, by coating it with a photographic emulsion [sensitize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make sensitive or aware [sensibilise, sensibilize, sensify, sensitize]</p><p><b>ako imate alergiju ili posebnu ili prekomjernu osjetljivost (posebno na određeni faktor) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an allergy or peculiar or excessive susceptibility (especially to a specific factor) [allergic, hypersensitised, hypersensitive, hypersensitized, sensitized, supersensitised, supersensitive, supersensitized]</p><p><b>(kemija) tvar koja ne uključuje katalizator i koja olakšava početak katalitičke reakcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) a substance other than a catalyst that facilitates the start of a catalytic reaction [sensitizer]</p><p><b>koji uzrokuju osjetljivost organizma na serum kroz niz injekcija, stvaranje osjetljivosti ili osjetljivosti na fizičke ili emocionalne podražaje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rendering an organism sensitive to a serum by a series of injections [sensitisation, sensitization, sensitizing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> making susceptible or sensitive to either physical or emotional stimuli [sensitizing]</p><p><b>čulan, čuvstven, emotivan, kolebljiv, osjećajan, osjetljiv, prihvatljiv, razdražljiv, senzibilan, tanan, medij, spiritist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who serves as an intermediary between the living and the dead [medium, spiritualist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> responsive to physical stimuli</p><p><i>adj.</i> being susceptible to the attitudes, feelings, or circumstances of others</p><p><i>adj.</i> able to feel or perceive [sensible]</p><p><i>adj.</i> hurting [raw, sore, tender]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to classified information or matters affecting national security</p><p><b>lijepa širi paprika istočne Sjeverne Amerike i istočne Azije naturalizirana u zapadnoj Europi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> beautiful spreading fern of eastern North America and eastern Asia naturalized in western Europe [Onoclea sensibilis, bead fern]</p><p><b>tropska američka biljka s letcima osjetljivim na dodir (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American plant having leaflets somewhat sensitive to the touch [Cassia fasciculata, Chamaecrista fasciculata, partridge pea, wild sensitive plant]</p><p><b>podstruka iz tropske Amerike i Australije, poluplješti trnasti zimzeleni grm tropske Amerike s složenim lišćama osjetljivim na svjetlost i dodir (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prostrate or semi-erect subshrub of tropical America, and Australia [Mimosa pudica, action plant, humble plant, live-and-die, shame plant, touch-me-not]</p><p><i>n.</i> semi-climbing prickly evergreen shrub of tropical America having compound leaves sensitive to light and touch [Mimosa sensitiva]</p><p><b>čulan, čuvstven, emotivan, kolebljiv, osjećajan, osjetljiv, prihvatljiv, razdražljiv, senzibilan, tanan (od &quot;sensitive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a sensitive manner</p><p><b>osjetljivost, senzitivnost, obzirnost, osjeaajnost, senzibilitet, senzibilnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sensitivity to emotional feelings (of self and others) [sensitivity]</p><p><i>n.</i> (physiology) responsiveness to external stimuli [sensibility, sensitivity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to respond to physical stimuli or to register small physical amounts or differences [sensitivity]</p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to respond to affective changes in your interpersonal environment [sensitivity]</p><p><b>osjećajnost, osjetljivost, senzibilnost, obzirnost, osjeaajnost, senzibilitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physiology) responsiveness to external stimuli [sensibility, sensitiveness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to respond to physical stimuli or to register small physical amounts or differences [sensitiveness]</p><p><i>n.</i> sensitivity to emotional feelings (of self and others) [sensitiveness]</p><p><i>n.</i> susceptibility to a pathogen [predisposition]</p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to respond to affective changes in your interpersonal environment [sensitiveness]</p><p><b>aktivacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being sensitive (as to an antigen) [sensitisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> (psychology) the process of becoming highly sensitive to specific events or situations (especially emotional events or situations) [sensitisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> rendering an organism sensitive to a serum by a series of injections [sensitisation, sensitising, sensitizing]</p><p><b>učiniti osjetljivim ili svjesnim, Razlog za osjećaj, osjetljivi na lijek ili alergen, S druge strane, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 98. točka (a) ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći postupak: (MT)