 [septet, septette]</p><p><b>sedamnaest, sedamnaesto</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cardinal number that is the sum of sixteen and one [17, XVII]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being one more than sixteen [17, xvii]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička cikada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American cicada [Magicicada septendecim, periodical cicada]</p><p><b>sedamnaesti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> position 17 in a countable series of things</p><p><i>adj.</i> coming next after the sixteenth in position [17th]</p><p><b>sedmi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> position seven in a countable series of things</p><p><i>n.</i> one part in seven equal parts [one-seventh]</p><p><i>n.</i> the musical interval between one note and another seven notes away from it</p><p><i>adj.</i> coming next after the sixth and just before the eighth in position [7th]</p><p><b>Avenue na Manhattanu koji ide sjeverno i južno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an avenue in Manhattan that runs north and south</p><p><b>trijada sa dodatkom sedme. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a triad with a seventh added</p><p><b>cranijalni živc koji opskrbljuje mišiće lica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cranial nerve that supplies facial muscles [facial, facial nerve, nervus facialis]</p><p><b>Križarski rat započeo 1248. nakon gubitka Jeruzalema 1244. i poražen 1249. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Crusade initiated in 1248 after the loss of Jerusalem in 1244 and defeated in 1249</p><p><b>blaženstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of extreme happiness [bliss, blissfulness, cloud nine, walking on air]</p><p><b>Adventisti koji su snažno protestanti i koji suče drže kao sabat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Adventism that is strongly Protestant and observes Saturday as the Sabbath</p><p><b>sedmi (od &quot;seventh&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in the seventh place</p><p><b>sedamdeset, sedamdesetak (od &quot;seventy&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the decade from 1970 to 1979 [1970s]</p><p><i>n.</i> the time of life between 70 and 80 [mid-seventies]</p><p><b>sedamdeseti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> position 70 in a countable