/i> relating to or characteristic of Shintoism [Shinto, Shintoist]</p><p><b>blistav, sjajan, sjajnu, sunčan, ulašten, vedar</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> reflecting light [glistening, glossy, lustrous, sheeny, shining]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a shiny surface or coating [glazed]</p><p><i>adj.</i> made smooth and bright by or as if by rubbing [bright, burnished, lustrous, shining]</p><p><b>sjajan zimzelena grm iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s sjajnim lištima i uglovitim granama i grmovima od ružičastih do crvenkastih cvijeća koji liče na umbel (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> showy evergreen shrub of southeastern United States with shiny leaves and angled branches and clusters of pink to reddish flowers that resemble an umbel [Lyonia lucida, fetter bush, fetterbush]</p><p><b>brod, dostava, dostaviti, jedrenjak, lađa, otpremiti, plovni objekt, poslati, poslati brodom, prevoziti lađom, slati, ukrcati, utovariti, broda, utovari u brod, ship, otposlati, otpremati, pošiljati, prenijeti, prenositi, prevažati, prevesti, prevoziti, transportirati, ukrcati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vessel that carries passengers or freight</p><p><i>v.</i> transport commercially [send, transport]</p><p><i>v.</i> hire for work on a ship</p><p><i>v.</i> go on board [embark]</p><p><i>v.</i> travel by ship</p><p><i>v.</i> place on board a ship</p><p><b>vrlo tvrdi nesoljeni kolačići ili kruh (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very hard unsalted biscuit or bread [hardtack, pilot biscuit, pilot bread, sea biscuit]</p><p><b>agent posrednik, pomorski agent posrednik u zaključivanju ugovora</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agent for the ship owner</p><p><b>stolar koji pomaže u izgradnji i ploveći drvenih brodova, Osoba koja gradi brodove kao posao. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a carpenter who helps build and launch wooden vessels [shipbuilder, shipwright]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who builds ships as a business [shipbuilder]</p><p><b>brodogradnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the construction of ships [shipbuilding]</p><p><b>brodski kanal, morski kanal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a canal large enough for seagoing vessels [shipway]</p><p><b>opskrbljivač broda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dealer in equipment and supplies for ships</p><p><b>porez koji je u Engleskoj naplaćen za nabavku brodova za nacionalnu obranu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an impost levied in England to provide money for ships for national defense</p><p><b>ratni brod namijenjen borbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a warship intended for combat [man-of-war]</p><p><b>putanje na moru koje je redovito korištena ruta za plovila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lane at sea that is a regularly used route for vessels [sea lane, seaway, trade route]</p><p><b>(nautički) svaki od osam pola sata nautičkog vremena označen udarcima brodskog zvona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (nautical) each of the eight half-hour units of nautical time signaled by strokes of a ship's bell [bell]</p><p><b>brod za komunikaciju između broda i obale (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a boat for communication between ship and shore [cutter, pinnace, tender]</p><p><b>trgovac jedrom i užadima i drugim zalihama za jedrilice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dealer in sails and ropes and other supplies for sailing ships</p><p><b>posada broda uključujući časnike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crew of a ship including the officers [company]</p><p><b>područje za pripremu hrane na brodu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the area for food preparation on a ship [caboose, cookhouse, galley]</p><p><b>časnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person authorized to serve in a position of authority on a vessel [officer]</p><p><b>brodske isprave</b></p><p><i>n.</i> official papers which a ship is legally required to have</p><p><b>izvođač koji kupuje stare brodove i razbija ih za otpad (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a contractor who buys old ships and breaks them up for scrap</p><p><b>S obzirom na to da je to sustav koji se koristi za upravljanje sustavom za praćenje i praćenje, on se ne može koristiti za praćenje i praćenje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shipboard system consisting of an acoustic detection system that is towed behind the ship</p><p><b>paluba</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> casual or ephemeral as if taking place on board a ship</p><p><b>pomorska služba na brodu na moru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> naval service aboard a ship at sea [sea-duty, service abroad]</p><p><b>član američkog mornaričkog korpusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the United States Marine Corps [Marine, devil dog, leatherneck]</p><p><b>sustav dizajniran za rad kao koherentni entitet na brodu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system designed to work as a coherent entity on board a naval ship</p><p><b>brodograditelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a carpenter who helps build and launch wooden vessels [ship builder, shipwright]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who builds ships as a business [ship builder]</p><p><i>n.</i> a business that builds and repairs ships</p><p><b>brodogradnja, brodograđevinski, brodograđevinskoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the construction of ships [ship building]</p><p><b>industrija koja gradi brodove. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industry that builds ships</p><p><b>brodski teret, brodski tovar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount of cargo that can be held by a boat or ship or a freight car [boatload, carload]</p><p><b>mornar, mornar sa istoga broda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an associate on the same ship with you</p><p><b>brodski tovar, dostava, isporuka, otprema, pošiljka, prijevoz, roba, teret, tovar, odašiljanje, slanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> goods carried by a large vehicle [cargo, consignment, freight, lading, load, loading, payload]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of sending off something [despatch, dispatch]</p><p><b>brodovlasnik, brodovlasnika, brodar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who owns a ship or a share in a ship</p><p><b>brodar, krcatelj, otpremnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who ships goods</p><p><i>n.</i> a company in the business of shipping freight</p><p><b>brodarstvo, brodovi, brodovlje, mornarica, otprema, otprema brodom, prijevoz, prijevoz vod put, trgovačke lađe, trgovačke mornar, ukrca