 southeastern United States with white flowers and small black drupaceous fruit [Bumelia lycioides, mock orange, shittim, southern buckthorn]</p><p><i>n.</i> wood of the shittah tree used to make the ark of the Hebrew Tabernacle</p><p><b>sranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the elimination of fecal waste through the anus [defecation, laxation]</p><p><b>loš, pokvaren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very bad [crappy, icky, lousy, rotten, stinking, stinky]</p><p><b>beznačajni, bezuspješni, dosadni, prljavi i neprijatni poslovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trivial, unrewarding, tedious, dirty, and disagreeable chores [scut work]</p><p><b>nož koji se koristi kao oružje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a knife used as a weapon</p><p><b>(Judaizam) razdoblje od sedam dana žalosti nakon smrti bliskog rođaka, Onaj koji je blažen. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a period of seven days of mourning after the death of close relative [shibah, shivah]</p><p><i>n.</i> the auspicious one [Siva]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) razdoblje od sedam dana žalosti nakon smrti bliskog rođaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a period of seven days of mourning after the death of close relative [shibah, shiva]</p><p><b>hinduistička sekta koja obožava Šivu., obožavanje Šive jednog od tri glavna boga hinduističkog panteona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Hindu sect worshiping Shiva [Sivaism]</p><p><i>n.</i> worship of Shiva one of the 3 chief gods of the Hindu pantheon [Sivaism]</p><p><b>obožavatelj Shive. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> worshipper of Shiva</p><p><b>bučna lažna serenada (izrada udarajući lonac i čajnik) novonaplavenom paru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a noisy mock serenade (made by banging pans and kettles) to a newly married couple [belling, callathump, callithump, charivari, chivaree]</p><p><b>cvokotanje, drhtanje, drhtati, drhtavica, krhotina, odlomak, treperiti, trijeska, zadrhtati, jeza, ježuri, srsi, trnci, žmarci, podrhtati, podrhtavati, tresti se, uzdrhtati, zatresti se, drhturiti, naježiti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reflex motion caused by cold or fear or excitement [shake, tremble]</p><p><i>n.</i> an almost pleasurable sensation of fright [chill, frisson, quiver, shudder, thrill, tingle]</p><p><i>v.</i> tremble convulsively, as from fear or excitement [shudder, thrill, throb]</p><p><i>v.</i> shake, as from cold [shudder]</p><p><b>cvokotav, drhtav, tresavice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sensation of cold that often marks the start of an infection and the development of a fever [chill]</p><p><i>adj.</i> vibrating slightly and irregularly [shaky, trembling]</p><p><b>drhtav, krhak, loman, plašljiv, treperav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> cold enough to cause shivers</p><p><i>adj.</i> provoking fear terror [chilling, scary, shuddery]</p><p><b>(Jidish) budala koji je navikao da se bavi glupostima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a dolt who is a habitual bungler [schlemiel]</p><p><b>(Jidiš) Neugodna i glupa osoba, dosadan ili težak put, hoda ili se šeta po, Povucite se jako, kao da je teško opterećenje protiv otpora. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) an awkward and stupid person [schlep, schlepper, shlepper]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tedious or difficult journey [schlep]</p><p><i>v.</i> walk or tramp about [traipse]</p><p><i>v.</i> pull along heavily, like a heavy load against a resistance [pull along, schlep]</p><p><b>(Jidiš) Neugodna i glupa osoba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) an awkward and stupid person [schlep, schlepper, shlep]</p><p><b>(Jidish) vrlo nesretna ili nesposobna osoba koja ne uspijeva u svemu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a very unlucky or inept person who fails at everything [schlimazel]</p><p><b>proizvod koji je loš ili lošiji od proizvoda koji su navedeni u Prilogu II. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> merchandise that is shoddy or inferior [dreck, schlock]</p><p><b>Trgovac koji trguje lošim robom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (slang) a merchant who deals in shoddy or inferior merchandise [schlockmeister]</p><p><b>(Jidish) pretjerana sentimentalnost u umjetnosti ili glazbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) excessive sentimentality in art or music [schmaltz, schmalz]</p><p><b>(Jidish) hrpa stvari koje idu zajedno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a batch of things that go together [schmear, schmeer]</p><p><b>(Jidish) gluposti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) baloney [schmegegge]</p><p><b>(Jidiš) kreten (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a jerk [schmo, schmuck, shmuck]</p><p><b>Pričajte na slobodan ili neobavezan način i prijateljski. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> talk idly or casually and in a friendly way [jawbone, schmoose, schmooze, shmooze]</p><p><b>(Jidiš) toplo razgovor od srca do srca, Pričajte na slobodan ili neobavezan način i prijateljski. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a warm heart-to-heart talk</p><p><i>v.</i> talk idly or casually and in a friendly way [jawbone, schmoose, schmooze, shmoose]</p><p><b>(Jidiš) kreten (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a jerk [schmo, schmuck, shmo]</p><p><b>(Jidiš) naivni glupak više da se sažali nego prezirati (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a gullible simpleton more to be pitied than despised [schnook]</p><p><b>isprositi, izmoliti, izmusti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> obtain or seek to obtain by cadging or wheedling [cadge, schnorr, scrounge]</p><p><b>isprositi, izmoliti, izmusti (od &quot;shnorr&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Yiddish) a scrounger who takes advantage of the generosity of others [schnorrer]</p><p><b>jato, jato riba, mnoštvo, pješčani sprud, plićak, pliće, sprud, pličina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sandbank in a stretch of water that is visible at low tide</p><p><i>n.</i> a stretch of shallow water [shallow]</p><p><i>n.</i> a large group of fish [school]</p><p><i>v.</i> make shallow [shallow]</p><p><i>v.</i> become shallow [shallow]</p><p><b>pun potopljenih grebena ili peska ili bazena (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of submerged reefs or sandbanks or shoals [reefy, shelfy, shelvy]</p><p><b>domaća svinja, krmče, prase, prasence, praščić, svinjče</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a young pig [piggy, piglet, shote]</p><p><b>kapija, potres, potresti, razljutiti, sudar, sudariti se, sukob, šok, šokirati, udar, udarac, udariti, uzbuditi, uzbuđenje, šokiraju, električni šok, zaprepastiti, zgranuti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling of distress and disbelief that you have when something bad happens accidentally [daze, stupor]</p><p><i>n.</i> the violent interaction of individuals or groups entering into combat [impact]</p><p><i>n.</i> a reflex response to the passage of electric current through the body [electric shock, electrical shock]</p><p><i>n.</i> (pathology) bodily collapse or near collapse caused by inadequate oxygen delivery to the cells</p><p><i>n.</i> an instance of agitation of the earth's crust [seismic disturbance]</p><p><i>n.</i> an unpleasant or disappointing surprise [blow]</p><p><i>n.</i> a pile of sheaves of grain set on end in a field to dry</p><p><i>n.</i> a bushy thick mass (especially hair)</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden jarring impact [jar, jolt, jounce]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mechanical damper [cushion, shock absorber]</p><p><i>v.</i> surprise greatly [ball over, blow out of the water, floor, take aback]</p><p><i>v.</i> strike with disgust or revulsion [appal, appall, offend, outrage, scandalise, scandalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> strike with horror or terror</p><p><i>v.</i> collide violently</p><p><i>v.</i> collect or gather into shocks</p><p><i>v.</i> subject to electrical shocks</p><p><i>v.</i> inflict a trauma upon [traumatise, traumatize]</p><p><b>amortizer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mechanical damper [cushion, shock]</p><p><b>liječenje određenih psihotičnih stanja primjenom šokova koje slijede konvulzije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> treatment of certain psychotic states by the administration of shocks that are followed by convulsions [shock treatment]</p><p><b>liječenje određenih psihotičnih stanja primjenom šokova koje slijede konvulzije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> treatment of certain psychotic states by the administration of shocks that are followed by convulsions [shock therapy]</p><p><b>Vojnici koji su posebno obučeni i naoružani za vodenje napada (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soldiers who are specially trained and armed to lead an assault</p><p><b>područje visokog tlaka koje se kreće kroz plin s velikom brzinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a region of high pressure travelling through a gas at a high velocity [blast wave]</p><p><b>s kapacitetom apsorpcije energije udarca (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the capacity to absorb the energy of an impact</p><p><b>ako imate šok (ili neredu) kose (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a shock (or untidy mass) of hair</p><p><b>koji je sposoban za šokiranje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being shocked [narrow-minded]</p><p><b>kapija, potres, potresti, razljutiti, sudar, sudariti se, sukob, šok, šokirati, udar, udarac, udariti, uzbuditi, uzbuđenje, šokiraju (od &quot;shock&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> struck with fear, dread, or consternation [aghast, appalled, dismayed]</p><p><b>kapija, potres, potresti, razljutiti, sudar, sudariti se, sukob, šok, šokirati, udar, udarac, udariti, uzbuditi, uzbuđenje, šokiraju (od &quot;shock&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shockingly bad person</p><p><i>n.</i> a sensational message (in a film or play or novel)</p><p><b>grozan, nečuvan, odvratan, potresan, sablažnjiv, strašan, šokantan, užasan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> glaringly vivid and graphic [lurid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> giving offense to moral sensibilities and injurious to reputation [disgraceful, scandalous, shameful]</p><p><b>grozan, nečuvan, odvratan, potresan, sablažnjiv, strašan, šokantan, užasan (od &quot;shocking&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> extremely</p><p><i>adv.</i> very badly</p><p><i>adv.</i> so as to shock the feelings</p><p><b>Američki fizičar (rođen u Engleskoj) koji je pridonio razvoju elektroničkog tranzistora (1910-1989) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States physicist (born in England) who contributed to the development of the electronic transistor (1910-1989) [William Bradford Shockley, William Shockley]</p><p><b>obuven</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> wearing footgear [shodden, shoed]</p><p><i>adj.</i> used of certain religious orders who wear shoes [calced]</p><p><b>obući obuću za noge (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> wearing footgear [shod, shoed]</p><p><b>bezvrijedno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a shoddy manner</p><p><b>Kvalitet jeftine imitacije nečeg boljeg., svojstvo slabosti zbog nemarne konstrukcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being cheaply imitative of something better [trashiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of weakness by virtue of careless construction [flimsiness]</p><p><b>bezvrijedan, jeftin, lažan, loš, lošeg kvaliteta, stare krpe, vještačka vuna, vještački</b></p><p><i>n.</i> reclaimed wool fiber</p><p><i>adj.</i> made of inferior workmanship and materials [cheapjack, tawdry]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unethical or dishonest [dirty, sordid]</p><p><b>cipela, kablovi spojnica, obuti, okov, omotač, papuča, papučica, pedala, peta, potkova, potkovati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> footwear shaped to fit the foot (below the ankle) with a flexible upper of leather or plastic and a sole and heel of heavier material</p><p><i>n.</i> (card games) a case from which playing cards are dealt one at a time</p><p><i>n.</i> U-shaped plate nailed to underside of horse's hoof [horseshoe]</p><p><i>n.</i> a restraint provided when the brake linings are moved hydraulically against the brake drum to retard the wheel's rotation [brake shoe, skid]</p><p><i>v.</i> furnish with shoes</p><p><b>Veliki naivni azijski grm ili malo stablo s velikim jednostrukom ili dvostrukom crvenom do duboko crvenom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large showy Asiatic shrub or small tree having large single or double red to deep-red flowers [China rose, Chinese hibiscus, Hibiscus rosa-sinensis, Rose of China, shoeblack plant]</p><p><b>eksplozivna naprava skrivena unutar pete i podloge cipele (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an explosive device concealed inside the heel and sole of a shoe</p><p><b>Šavovi koji čine rub cipele ili čizme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the stitching that forms the rim of a shoe or boot [collar]</p><p><b>industrija koja proizvodi i prodaje cipele (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industry that manufactures and sells shoes</p><p><b>pertla, vezica, špigeta, žniranac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lace used for fastening shoes [shoe string, shoelace, shoestring]</p><p><b>koža za proizvodnju cipela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leather used to make shoes</p><p><b>Sklonični materijal za proizvodnju blistave zaštitne površine na obući (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a substance used to produce a shiny protective surface on footwear [blacking]</p><p><b>Šuparski zanat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the shoemaker's trade [cobbling, shoemaking]</p><p><b>trgovina cipelama, salon cipela, trgovina cipela, trgovina obuće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shop where shoes are sold [shoe-shop, shoe store]</p><p><b>salon cipela, trgovina cipela, trgovina obuće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shop where shoes are sold [shoe-shop, shoe shop]</p><p><b>pertla, vezica, špigeta, žniranac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small amount of money [shoestring]</p><p><i>n.</i> a lace used for fastening shoes [shoe lace, shoelace, shoestring]</p><p><b>trgovina cipelama, salon cipela, trgovina cipela, trgovina obuće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shop where shoes are sold [shoe shop, shoe store]</p><p><b>balaeniceps rex</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large stork-like bird of the valley of the White Nile with a broad bill suggesting a wooden shoe [Balaeniceps rex, shoebird]</p><p><b>balaeniceps rex</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large stork-like bird of the valley of the White Nile with a broad bill suggesting a wooden shoe [Balaeniceps rex, shoebill]</p><p><b>čistač cipela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who polishes shoes and boots [bootblack]</p><p><b>Veliki naivni azijski grm ili malo stablo s velikim jednostrukom ili dvostrukom crvenom do duboko crvenom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large showy Asiatic shrub or small tree having large single or double red to deep-red flowers [China rose, Chinese hibiscus, Hibiscus rosa-sinensis, Rose of China, shoe black]</p><p><b>Svaka od ovih vrsta može se upotrebljavati za proizvodnju električnih vozila., s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a structure resembling a shoebox (as a rectangular building or a cramped room or compartment)</p><p><i>n.</i> an oblong rectangular (usually cardboard) box designed to hold a pair of shoes</p><p><b>obući obuću za noge (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> wearing footgear [shod, shodden]</p><p><b>količinu koju će obuća moći držati (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the amount that a shoe will hold</p><p><b>žlica za cipele, žlica, žlica za obuvanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device used for easing the foot into a shoe</p><p><i>v.</i> fit for a specific purpose even when not well suited</p><p><b>vezica za cipele, pertla, vezica, špigeta, žniranac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lace used for fastening shoes [shoe lace, shoe string, shoestring]</p><p><b>bez cipela. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> without shoes [barefoot, barefooted]</p><p><b>obućar, postolar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who makes or repairs shoes [cobbler]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju automobila od željeza ili električne energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> holding device shaped like a human foot that is used to fashion or repair shoes [cobbler's last, last]</p><p><b>Šuparski zanat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the shoemaker's trade [cobbling, shoe repairing]</p><p><b>cipele, mjesto, pozicija, situacija, u koži</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a particular situation [place]</p><p><b>sjajan završetak stavljen na cipele s poliranjem i poliranjem, Čin poliranja cipela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a shiny finish put on shoes with polish and buffing</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of shining shoes</p><p><b>pertla, vezica, špigeta, žniranac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lace used for fastening shoes [shoe lace, shoe string, shoelace]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small amount of money [shoe string]</p><p><b>(baseball) trčanje hvata napravljen blizu zemlje (MT)</b></