d Testament) the 2nd son of Jacob and one of the 12 patriarchs of Israel</p><p><b>(Judaizam) židovski sveti dan koji se slavi 22. ili 23. mjeseca Tishrija kako bi se proslavio završetak godišnjeg ciklusa čitanja Tore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a Jewish holy day celebrated on the 22nd or 23rd of Tishri to celebrate the completion of the annual cycle of readings of the Torah [Rejoicing in the Law, Rejoicing of the Law, Rejoicing over the Law, Shimchath Torah, Simchas Torah, Simchat Torah, Simhath Torah]</p><p><b>(Judaizam) židovski sveti dan koji se slavi 22. ili 23. mjeseca Tishrija kako bi se proslavio završetak godišnjeg ciklusa čitanja Tore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a Jewish holy day celebrated on the 22nd or 23rd of Tishri to celebrate the completion of the annual cycle of readings of the Torah [Rejoicing in the Law, Rejoicing of the Law, Rejoicing over the Law, Shimchath Torah, Simchas Torah, Simchat Torah, Simhat Torah]</p><p><b>majmun</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ape or monkey</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or resembling an ape</p><p><b>analogan, istoimeni, istovjetan, konformni, sličan, srodan, sl., slične, sličnim, nalik</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by correspondence or resemblance</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the same or similar characteristics [alike, like]</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling or similar [like]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of words) expressing closely related meanings</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of replacing or changing places with something else [exchangeable, interchangeable, standardised, standardized]</p><p><b>sličnost, sličnosti, nalikovanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being similar</p><p><i>n.</i> a Gestalt principle of organization holding that (other things being equal) parts of a stimulus field that are similar to each other tend to be perceived as belonging together as a unit [law of similarity]</p><p><b>slično</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in like or similar manner [likewise]</p><p><b>poredba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a figure of speech that express