<p><i>adj.</i> composed of one member, set, or kind</p><p><i>adj.</i> grammatical number category referring to a single item or unit</p><p><i>adj.</i> the single one of its kind [unique]</p><p><b>jednina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the form of a word that is used to denote a singleton [singular]</p><p><b>kvadratni matrica čiji je determinant nula (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a square matrix whose determinant is zero</p><p><b>razlikovati kao jednokratno (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> distinguish as singular [singularize]</p><p><b>čudo, neobičnost, singularitet, vlastitost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being one of a kind [uniqueness]</p><p><i>n.</i> strangeness by virtue of being remarkable or unusual</p><p><b>razlikovati kao jednokratno (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> distinguish as singular [singularise]</p><p><b>neponovljivo, pojedinačno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a singular manner or to a singular degree</p><p><b>(obično u množini) stanje refleksnih grčeva dijafragme praćeno brzim zatvaranjem glavice koje proizvodi čuveni zvuk (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) the state of having reflex spasms of the diaphragm accompanied by a rapid closure of the glottis producing an audible sound [hiccough, hiccup]</p><p><b>Indijski jezik koji govore ljudi na Šri Lanki., od ili u vezi s sinhalaskim jezicima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Indic language spoken by the people of Sri Lanka [Singhalese, Sinhalese]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Sinhalese languages [Singhalese, Sinhalese]</p><p><b>u Šri Lanki ili u njoj živi, Indijski jezik koji govore ljudi na Šri Lanki., od ili u vezi s sinhalaskim jezicima, od ili u vezi s Sinhalese ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Sri Lanka [Singhalese]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Indic language spoken by the people of Sri Lanka [Singhalese, Sinhala]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Sinhalese languages [Singhalese, Sinhala]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Sinhalese people [Singhalese]</p><p><b>heraldički lijevo, koban, lijevo, mračan, opak, razoran, ubitačan, zloban, zlokoban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> threatening or foreshadowing evil or tragic developments [baleful, forbidding, menacing, minacious, minatory, ominous, threatening]</p><p><i>adj.</i> stemming from evil characteristics or forces [black, dark]</p><p><i>adj.</i> on or starting from the wearer's left</p><p><b>lijevostrani, zavrnut u lije</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or on the left</p><p><i>adj.</i> preferring to use left foot or hand or eye</p><p><b>preferiranje za korištenje lijeve ruke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> preference for using the left hand [left-handedness]</p><p><b>spiralno gore od desne do lijeve (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> spiraling upward from right to left [sinistrorse]</p><p><b>spiralno gore od desne do lijeve (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> spiraling upward from right to left [sinistrorsal]</p><p><b>grupa sino-tibetanskih jezika, o ili koji se odnose na kineski narod ili njihov jezik ili kulturu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of Sino-Tibetan languages [Sinitic language]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Chinese people or their language or culture</p><p><b>grupa sino-tibetanskih jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of Sino-Tibetan languages [Sinitic]</p><p><b>četvoropol, izdubiti, izljev, lavabo, odvodni kanal, odvodnik, padati, pasti, pilo, popuštati, potonuti, potopiti, potopiti brod, prijamnik (podala ka), propadati, propasti, spuštati se, sudoper, sudoper s izljevom, tonuti, transduktor, ulegnuće, utonuti, zabiti, umivaonik, vrtača, spustiti se, potapati, potapati se, potopiti se, ulegnuti, uleći, ulijegati, legnuti, lijegati, uranjati, uroniti, uvaliti se, uvaljivati se, zalegnuti, zaleći, zalijegati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plumbing fixture consisting of a water basin fixed to a wall or floor and having a drainpipe</p><p><i>n.</i> (technology) a process that acts to absorb or remove energy or a substance from a system</p><p><i>n.</i> a depression in the ground communicating with a subterranean passage (especially in limestone) and formed by solution or by collapse of a cavern roof [sinkhole, swallow hole]</p><p><i>n.</i> a covered cistern [cesspit, cesspool, sump]</p><p><i>v.</i> fall or descend to a lower place or level [drop, drop down]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to sink</p><p><i>v.</i> pass into a specified state or condition [lapse, pass]</p><p><i>v.</i> go under [go down, go under, settle]</p><p><i>v.</i> descend into or as if into some soft substance or place [subside]</p><p><i>v.</i> appear to move downward [dip]</p><p><i>v.</i> fall heavily or suddenly [fall off, slump]</p><p><i>v.</i> fall or sink heavily [slide down, slump]</p><p><i>v.</i> embed deeply [bury]</p><p><b>postati jasan ili ući u svoju svijest ili emocije, Proći kroz (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become clear or enter one's consciousness or emotions [click, come home, dawn, fall into place, get across, get through, penetrate]</p><p><i>v.</i> pass through [filter, percolate, permeate]</p><p><b>Sposoban za potonuće (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being sunk</p><p><b>pokladnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small ring-shaped friedcake [donut, doughnut]</p><p><i>n.</i> a weight that sinks (as to hold nets or fishing lines under water)</p><p><i>n.</i> a pitch that curves downward rapidly as it approaches the plate</p><p><b>vrtača</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a depression in the ground communicating with a subterranean passage (especially in limestone) and formed by solution or by collapse of a cavern roof [sink, swallow hole]</p><p><b>autonomna pokrajina na sjeverozapadu Kine na granici s Mongolijom i Kazahstanom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an autonomous province in far northwestern China on the border with Mongolia and Kazakhstan [Xinjiang, Xinjiang Uighur Autonomous Region]</p><p><b>padanje, potapanje, potonuće, propadanje, slijeganje, spuštanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a descent as through liquid (especially through water)</p><p><i>n.</i> a slow fall or decline (as for lack of strength)</p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling caused by uneasiness or apprehension [sinking feeling]</p><p><b>osjećaj uzrokovan nemirom ili strahom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling caused by uneasiness or apprehension [sinking]</p><p><b>amortizacija kapi, postupni otkup</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fund accumulated regularly in a separate account and used to redeem debt securities</p><p><b>privremeni pad zdravlja ili vrijednosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a temporary decline in health or value</p><p><b>bezgrešan, bezgrješan, nevin</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> free from sin [impeccant, innocent]</p><p><b>bezgrešnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being unsullied by sin or moral wrong [innocence, pureness, purity, whiteness]</p><p><b>irski republikanski politički pokret osnovan 1905. godine kako bi promovirao neovisnost od Engleske i ujedinjenje Irske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Irish republican political movement founded in 1905 to promote independence from England and unification of Ireland</p><p><b>grešnica, griješnik, grješnik, grešnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who sins (without repenting) [evildoer]</p><p><b>grijeh, sagrešenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an act that is regarded by theologians as a transgression of God's will [sin]</p><p><i>adj.</i> transgressing a moral or divine law</p><p><b>rod višegodišnjih gomoljastih biljaka i grmova iz Srednje i Južne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of perennial tuberous herbs and shrubs of Central and South America [genus Sinningia]</p><p><b>Južnoamerička biljka koja se uzgaja u mnogim vrstama kao kućna biljka zbog svojih velikih lijepih listova i velikih cvjetova različitih boja u obliku zvona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South American herb cultivated in many varieties as a houseplant for its large handsome leaves and large variously colored bell-shaped flowers [Gloxinia spesiosa, florist's gloxinia]</p><p><b>rat između Kine i Japana (1894 i 1895) zbog kontrole Korejskog poluotoka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a war between China and Japan (1894 and 1895) over the control of the Korean Peninsula [Chino-Japanese War]</p><p><b>obitelj tonalnih jezika koji se govore u istočnoj Aziji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the family of tonal languages spoken in eastern Asia [Sino-Tibetan language]</p><p><b>obitelj tonalnih jezika koji se govore u istočnoj Aziji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the family of tonal languages spoken in eastern Asia [Sino-Tibetan]</p><p><b>specijalizirano tkivo srca koje kontrolira otkucaje srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a specialized bit of heart tissue that controls the heartbeat [SA node, cardiac pacemaker, pacemaker]</p><p><b>student kineske povijesti i jezika i kulture. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a student of Chinese history and language and culture</p><p><b>proučavanje kineske povijesti i jezika i kulture (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of Chinese history and language and culture</p><p><b>crveni oker koji se nekada koristio kao pigment (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a red ocher formerly used as a pigment [sinopia, sinopis]</p><p><b>crveni oker koji se nekada koristio kao pigment (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a red ocher formerly used as a pigment [sinoper, sinopis]</p><p><b>crveni oker koji se nekada koristio kao pigment (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a red ocher formerly used as a pigment [sinoper, sinopia]</p><p><b>fosilna ptica veličine vrapca iz perioda Jurskog do perioda Krede s kijelom prsne kosti i traženim repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sparrow-sized fossil bird of the Jurassic period to the Cretaceous period having a keeled breastbone and vestigial tail</p><p><b>očvrsnuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause (ores or powdery metals) to become a coherent mass by heating without melting</p><p><b>sinterirani</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> formed into a mass by heat and pressure</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, s masenim udubljenim dijelom od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> curved or curving in and out [sinuous, wiggly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a strongly waved margin alternately concave and convex</p><p><b>s krivuljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having curves [sinuousness]</p><p><b>krivudav, valovit, vijugav, zavojit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> curved or curving in and out [sinuate, wiggly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> gracefully thin and bending and moving with ease [lissom, lissome, lithe, lithesome, supple]</p><p><b>krivudav, valovit, vijugav, zavojit (od &quot;sinuous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a sinuous manner</p><p><b>krivudav, valovit, vijugav, zavojit (od &quot;sinuous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having curves [sinuosity]</p><p><b>sinus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal passage leading from a suppurating cavity to the body surface [fistula]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various air-filled cavities especially in the bones of the skull</p><p><i>n.</i> a wide channel containing blood [venous sinus]</p><p><b>ili jednog od par velikih venskih sinusa u lubanju lubanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of a pair of large venous sinuses in the cranial cavity [cavernous sinus]</p><p><b>kratak sinus koji prima većinu vena srca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short sinus receiving most of the veins of the heart [coronary sinus]</p><p><b>sinusni sinus nosne šupljine (za mostom nosa) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sinus of the meatuses of the nasal cavity (behind the bridge of the nose) [ethmoid sinus, ethmoidal sinus]</p><p><b>glavobolja uzrokovana zapćenjem ili infekcijom paranazalnih sinusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a headache resulting from congestion or infection in the paranasal sinuses</p><p><b>bilo koji od parnih sinusa u kostima lica susjednim nosnoj šupljini koje su obložene sluznicom koja je kontinuirana sa oblogom nosnih šupljina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the paired sinuses in the bones of the face adjacent to the nasal cavity that are lined with mucous membrane that is continuous with the lining of the nasal cavities [nasal sinus, paranasal sinus]</p><p><b>Neparni sinus tvrde materine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unpaired sinus of the dura mater [straight sinus, tentorial sinus]</p><p><b>S-oblik dugotrajni sinus na temporalnoj i stražnjoj kosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an S-shaped dural sinus on the temporal and occipital bones [sigmoid sinus]</p><p><b>parni sinus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a paired dural sinus [transverse sinus]</p><p><b>kružni kanal u oku koji odvodjuje vodeni humor iz prednje komore oka u prednje cilijarske vene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a circular canal in the eye that drains aqueous humor from the anterior chamber of the eye into the anterior ciliary veins [Schlemm's canal, canal of Schlemm]</p><p><b>sinusitis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of one of the paranasal sinuses</p><p><b>mali prolazi obloženi endotelom za krv u tkivu organa, krivulja y=sin x (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tiny endothelium-lined passages for blood in the tissue of an organ</p><p><i>n.</i> the curve of y=sin x [sine curve]</p><p><b>sinusni, sinusoidalan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a succession of waves or curves</p><p><b>Projekcija karte jednake površine koja prikazuje paralelne i ekvator kao ravne linije i druge meridijane kao zakrivljene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an equal-area map projection showing parallels and the equator as straight lines and other meridians as curved [Sanson-Flamsteed projection]</p><p><b>sinusni, sinusoidalan (od &quot;sinusoidal&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a sinusoidal manner</p><p><b>izvorno tvrđava koju je osvojio David (drugi kralj Izraela), Židovska republika u jugozapadnoj Aziji na istočnom kraju Mediterana, zamišljeno mjesto koje se smatra savršenim ili idealnim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> originally a stronghold captured by David (the 2nd king of the Israelites) [Zion]</p><p><i>n.</i> Jewish republic in southwestern Asia at eastern end of Mediterranean [Israel, State of Israel, Yisrael, Zion]</p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary place considered to be perfect or ideal [Utopia, Zion]</p><p><b>Sioux, Siouan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a group of North American Indian peoples who spoke a Siouan language and who ranged from Lake Michigan to the Rocky Mountains [Sioux]</p><p><i>n.</i> a family of North American Indian languages spoken by the Sioux [Siouan language]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the Sioux people or their language and culture</p><p><b>Siouan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of North American Indian languages spoken by the Sioux [Siouan]</p><p><b>Mogu komunicirati na Siouanskom jeziku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> able to communicate in a Siouan language</p><p><b>Sioux</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a group of North American Indian peoples who spoke a Siouan language and who ranged from Lake Michigan to the Rocky Mountains [Siouan]</p><p><b>Grad u sjeveroistoku Iowe gdje se Rijeka Big Sioux spoji s Missourijem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in northeastern Iowa where the Big Sioux River joins the Missouri</p><p><b>Najveći grad u Južnoj Dakoti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> largest city in South Dakota</p><p><b>gucnuti, gutljaj, mali gutljaj, pijuckati, pijucnuti, srkanje, srkati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small drink</p><p><i>v.</i> drink in sips</p><p><b>Zlobna sekta u Pakistanu koja progoni šiitske muslimane i sarađuje s Al Kaidom da napada strance i da ometa vladu Pakistana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vicious sectarian organization in Pakistan that persecutes Shiite Muslims and collaborates with al-Qaeda to attack foreigners and to disrupt the government of Pakistan</p><p><b>kriva natega, sifon, teglica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tube running from the liquid in a vessel to a lower level outside the vessel so that gravity forces the liquid through the tube [syphon]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tubular organ in an aquatic animal (especially in mollusks) through which water can be taken in or expelled [syphon]</p><p><i>v.</i> convey, draw off, or empty by or as if by a siphon [siphon off, syphon]</p><p><i>v.</i> move a liquid from one container into another by means of a siphon or a siphoning action</p><p><b>s masom od 300 g/m2 do 2000 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> convey, draw off, or empty by or as if by a siphon [siphon, syphon]</p><p><b>buhe, red Siphonaptera, red buha</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fleas [order Siphonaptera]</p><p><b>morski kolonijalni hidrozoji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marine colonial hydrozoans [order Siphonophora]</p><p><b>plutajuća ili plivajuća oceanska kolonija polipa često prozirnih ili pokazivih boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a floating or swimming oceanic colony of polyps often transparent or showily colored</p><p><b>koji pije i koji pije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drinker who sips</p><p><b>štrcaljci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> peanut worms [phylum Sipuncula]</p><p><b>mali nesegmentirani morski crv koji se, kada ga netko uznemiri, povuče u tijelo, što daje izgled kikirikija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small unsegmented marine worm that when disturbed retracts its anterior portion into the body giving the appearance of a peanut [peanut worm]</p><p><b>Meksički slikar zidnih slika koji prikazuju prosvjed i revoluciju (1896-1974) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mexican painter of murals depicting protest and revolution (1896-1974) [David Alfaro Siqueiros, David Siqueiros]</p><p><b>gospodin, gospodine, pijančiti, pijandura, Sir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> term of address for a man</p><p><i>n.</i> a title used before the name of knight or baronet</p><p><b>Engleski fiziolog koji je zajedno s Andrewom Huxleyjem otkrio ulogu atoma kalijuma i natrijuma u prijenosu živčanih impulsa (1914-1998) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English physiologist who, with Andrew Huxley, discovered the role of potassium and sodium atoms in the transmission of the nerve impulse (1914-1998) [Alan Hodgkin, Alan Lloyd Hodgkin, Hodgkin]</p><p><b>Engleski glumac pozornice i ekrana poznat po svestranosti (1914-2000) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English stage and screen actor noted for versatility (1914-2000) [Alec Guinness, Guinness]</p><p><b>Škotski bakteriolog koji je otkrio penicilin (1881-1955) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Scottish bacteriologist who discovered penicillin (1881-1955) [Alexander Fleming, Fleming]</p><p><b>Britanski filmski redatelj (rođen u Mađarskoj) (1893-1956) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British filmmaker (born in Hungary) (1893-1956) [Korda, Sandor Kellner]</p><p><b>Kanadski istraživač (rođen u Engleskoj) koji je istraživao rijeku Mackenzie i koji je prvi prešao Sjevernu Ameriku kopnom sjeverno od Meksika (1764-1820) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Canadian explorer (born in England) who explored the Mackenzie River and who was first to cross North America by land north of Mexico (1764-1820) [Mackenzie]</p><p><b>Škotski kemičar poznat po istraživanju strukture nukleinskih kiselina (rođen 1907) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Scottish chemist noted for his research into the structure of nucleic acids (born in 1907) [Lord Todd, Todd]</p><p><b>Engleski astronom koji je pionir radio astronomije (rođen 1913.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English astronomer who pioneered radio astronomy (born in 1913) [Lovell, Sir Bernard Lovell]</p><p><b>Engleski filmski redatelj poznat po svojoj vještini stvaranja napetosti (1899-1980) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English film director noted for his skill in creating suspense (1899-1980) [Alfred Hitchcock, Alfred Joseph Hitchcock, Hitchcock]</p><p><b>Engleski pisac romana i kratkih priča (1913-1991) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English writer of novels and short stories (1913-1991) [Angus Frank Johnstone Wilson, Wilson]</p><p><b>Velški filmski glumac (rođen 1937.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Welsh film actor (born in 1937) [Anthony Hopkins, Hopkins, Sir Anthony Philip Hopkins]</p><p><b>Velški filmski glumac (rođen 1937.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Welsh film actor (born in 1937) [Anthony Hopkins, Hopkins, Sir Anthony Hopkins]</p><p><b>Flamanski slikar brojnih portreta (1599-1641) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Flemish painter of numerous portraits (1599-1641) [Anthony Vandyke, Van Dyck, Vandyke]</p><p><b>Britanski pisac koji je stvorio Sherlocka Holmesa (1859-1930) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British author who created Sherlock Holmes (1859-1930) [A. Conan Doyle, Arthur Conan Doyle, Conan Doyle]</p><p><b>Britanski arheolog koji je iskopao palaču Knossos na Kreti kako bi pronašao ono što je nazvao minojskom civilizacijom (1851-1941) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British archaeologist who excavated the palace of Knossos in Crete to find what he called Minoan civilization (1851-1941) [Arthur Evans, Evans]</p><p><b>Engleski astronom poznat po popularnom objašnjenju teorije relativnosti (1882-1944) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English astronomer remembered for his popular elucidation of relativity theory (1882-1944) [Eddington]</p><p><b>Engleski kompozitor opereta koji je surađivao s libretistom Williamom Gilbertom (1842-1900) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English composer of operettas who collaborated with the librettist William Gilbert (1842-1900) [Arthur Seymour Sullivan, Arthur Sullivan, Sullivan]</p><p><b>Britanski maršal Kraljevskog zrakoplovstva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British marshal of the Royal Air Force [Bomber Harris, Harris]</p><p><b>Čisti pas koji je osvojio trostruku krunu 1919. godine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thoroughbred that won the triple crown in 1919</p><p><b>Engleski general tijekom Drugog svjetskog rata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English general during World War II [1st Viscount Montgomery of Alamein, Bernard Law Montgomery, Montgomery]</p><p><b>Engleski astronom koji je pionir radio astronomije (rođen 1913.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English astronomer who pioneered radio astronomy (born in 1913) [Lovell, Sir Alfred Charles Bernard Lovell]</p><p><b>Engleski filozof koji je oživljavao područje moralne filozofije (1929-2003) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English philosopher credited with reviving the field of moral philosophy (1929-2003) [Bernard Arthur Owen Williams, Williams]</p><p><b>Engleski arheolog koji je nadgledao iskopavanja u Uru (1880-1960) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English archaeologist who supervised the excavations at Ur (1880-1960) [Sir Leonard Woolley, Woolley]</p><p><b>Engleski fiziolog koji je radio na istraživanju refleksnog djelovanja (1857-1952) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English physiolo