nformal language consisting of words and expressions that are not considered appropriate for formal occasions [slang, slang term]</p><p><b>Neformalni jezik koji se sastoji od riječi i izraza koji se ne smatraju prikladnim za formalne prilike. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> informal language consisting of words and expressions that are not considered appropriate for formal occasions [slang, slang expression]</p><p><b>žargonski (od &quot;slangy&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with slang</p><p><b>Neobično korištenje jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> casualness in use of language</p><p><b>jezik koji se odlikuje prekomjernom upotrebom slanga ili neispravnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> language characterized by excessive use of slang or cant</p><p><b>žargonski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting or expressed in slang or given to the use of slang</p><p><b>biti nagnut, dispozicija, gledište, inklinacija, kos, kosina, nagib, nagnut, nakriviti, nakriviti se, strmen, pristranost, iskriviti, iskrivljavati, izvijati, izviti, kriviti, nagibati, naginjati, naginjati se, nagnuti, naheriti, nakositi, pregibati, presavijati, presavinuti, savijati, savinuti, svijati, svinuti, ukositi, zakositi, zakriviti, zakrivljivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a biased way of looking at or presenting something [angle]</p><p><i>n.</i> degree of deviation from a horizontal plane [pitch, rake]</p><p><i>v.</i> lie obliquely</p><p><i>v.</i> present with a bias [angle, weight]</p><p><i>v.</i> to incline or bend from a vertical position [angle, lean, tilt, tip]</p><p><i>v.</i> heel over [cant, cant over, pitch, tilt]</p><p><b>ukošen, zakrivljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an oblique or slanted direction [aslant, aslope, diagonal, slanting, sloped, sloping]</p><p><i>adj.</i> favoring one person or side over another [biased, colored, coloured, one-sided]</p><p><b>kos, kriv, nagnut, nakrivljen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an oblique or slanted direction [aslant, aslope, diagonal, slanted, sloped, sloping]</p><p><b>kos, kriv, nagnut, nakrivljen (od &quot;slanting&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with a slant [slopingly]</p><p><b>u naguljku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at a slant [slantwise]</p><p><b>iskošen, kos, koso, nakrivo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> at a slant [slantways]</p><p><b>baciti, ošamariti, pljesnuti, pljusnuti, tresnuti, udarac dlanom, ispljuskati, išamarati, išćuškati, pljuskati, ćuškati, ćušnuti, šamarati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a blow from a flat object (as an open hand) [smack]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of smacking something [smack, smacking]</p><p><i>v.</i> hit with something flat, like a paddle or the open hand</p><p><i>adv.</i> directly [bang, bolt, slapdash, smack]</p><p><b>Ne obraćaj pažnju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> apply carelessly [clap on, slam on]</p><p><b>Napravi brzo i nesmotreno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make hastily and carelessly [clap together, clap up]</p><p><b>izravno ili odmah, na nasilni ili nagli ili bučni način (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> directly or immediately</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a violent or sudden or noisy manner [slam-bang]</p><p><b>odličan, velik</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very good [bang-up, bully, corking, cracking, dandy, great, groovy, keen, neat, nifty, not bad, old, peachy, smashing, swell]</p><p><b>Označen je velikom nemarnošću., na nesmotren ili nemaran način., izravno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by great carelessness [haphazard, slipshod, sloppy]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a careless or reckless manner [slam-bang]</p><p><i>adv.</i> directly [bang, bolt, slap, smack]</p><p><b>Veseli i neodgovorno., Ošamućen od ili kao od ponavljajućih udaraca (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> cheerfully irresponsible [carefree, devil-may-care, freewheeling, happy-go-lucky, harum-scarum]</p><p><i>adj.</i> dazed from or as if from repeated blows [punch-drunk, silly]</p><p><b>udarac koji udara (obično drugu osobu) otvorenom rukom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hitter who slaps (usually another person) with an open hand [spanker]</p><p><b>brz udarac napravljen kratkim snažnim zamahom hokeja