ptied at the table [slop basin]</p><p><b>brodska kantina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commissary maintained aboard merchant ships to sell merchandise to the crew</p><p><b>veliki kantu za primanje otpadne vode iz umivaonice ili komore lonca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large pail used to receive waste water from a washbasin or chamber pot [slop pail]</p><p><b>posuda za prljavu vodu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large pail used to receive waste water from a washbasin or chamber pot [slop jar]</p><p><b>Trgovac jeftinim odjećama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dealer in cheap ready-made clothing [slopseller]</p><p><b>kosina, nagib, nagib terena, naginjati se, nagnuti, nizbrdica, obronak, padati, padina, pokos, strmina, uspon, strana, uzbrdica, nagnuti se, naheriti se, nakositi se, nakriviti se, ukositi se, zakositi se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elevated geological formation [incline, side]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property possessed by a line or surface that departs from the horizontal [gradient]</p><p><i>v.</i> be at an angle [incline, pitch]</p><p><b>kos, nagnut</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an oblique or slanted direction [aslant, aslope, diagonal, slanted, slanting, sloping]</p><p><b>kos, nagnut, spušta, strm</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an oblique or slanted direction [aslant, aslope, diagonal, slanted, slanting, sloped]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a slanting form or direction</p><p><b>kanal</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sloping channel through which things can descend [chute, slide, slideway]</p><p><b>kos, nagnut, spušta, strm (od &quot;sloping&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with a slant [slantingly]</p><p><b>jako pijan. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very drunk [besotted, blind drunk, blotto, cockeyed, crocked, fuddled, loaded, pie-eyed, pissed, pixilated, plastered, sloshed, smashed, soaked, soused, sozzled, squiffy, stiff, tight, wet]</p><p><b>aljkav, kaljav, mokar, nemaran, neuredan, prljav, traljav, vodnjikav (od &quot;sloppy&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a sloppy manner</p><p><b>nehaj, nehajnost, nemar, nemarnost, neopreznost, nepromišljenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the wetness of ground that is covered or soaked with water [muddiness, wateriness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a lack of order and tidiness [slovenliness, unkemptness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of not being careful or taking pains [carelessness]</p><p><i>n.</i> falsely emotional in a maudlin way [drippiness, mawkishness, mushiness, sentimentality, soupiness]</p><p><b>aljkav, kaljav, mokar, nemaran, neuredan, prljav, traljav, vodnjikav, močvaran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking neatness or order</p><p><i>adj.</i> wet or smeared with a spilled liquid or moist material</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of soil) soft and watery [boggy, marshy, miry, mucky, muddy, quaggy, sloughy, soggy, squashy, swampy, waterlogged]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not fitting closely [baggy, loose-fitting]</p><p><i>adj.</i> excessively or abnormally emotional [overemotional]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by great carelessness [haphazard, slapdash, slipshod]</p><p><b>goveđe meso (ne krumpir) skuhano u začinjenom umaku i posluženo na pecivu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ground beef (not a patty) cooked in a spicy sauce and served on a bun</p><p><b>prnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wet feed (especially for pigs) consisting of mostly kitchen waste mixed with water or skimmed or sour milk [pigswill, pigwash, slop, swill]</p><p><i>n.</i> cheap clothing (as formerly issued to sailors in Britain)</p><p><b>Trgovac jeftinim odjećama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dealer in cheap ready-made clothing [slop-seller]</p><p><b>trgovina koja prodaje jeftinu gotovu odjeću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a store that sells cheap ready-made clothing [slopshop]</p><p><b>trgovina koja prodaje jeftinu gotovu odjeću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a store that sells cheap ready-made clothing [slopseller's shop]</p><p><b>bljuzgavica, brčkavica, bućkuriš, glupava osjećajnost, zapljusnuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a splashing sound [slush, splash, splosh]</p><p><i>v.</i> walk through mud or mire [slop, splash, splosh, squelch, squish]</p><p><i>v.</i> spill or splash copiously or clumsily [slosh around, slush, slush around]</p><p><b>izlijevanje ili prskalica obilno ili nespretno (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> spill or splash copiously or clumsily [slosh, slush, slush around]</p><p><b>bljuzgavica, brčkavica, bućkuriš, glupava osjećajnost (od &quot;slosh&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very drunk [besotted, blind drunk, blotto, cockeyed, crocked, fuddled, loaded, pie-eyed, pissed, pixilated, plastered, slopped, smashed, soaked, soused, sozzled, squiffy, stiff, tight, wet]</p><p><b>isjek, ležište, lijevak, otvor, perorez, položaj, praznina, prazno mjesto, prorez, prorezati, pukotina, slot, urez, urezivati žljebove, utičnica, utor, uzak otvor, žlijeb, termin, vremenski termin, trag</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a position in a grammatical linguistic construction in which a variety of alternative units are interchangeable</p><p><i>n.</i> a small slit (as for inserting a coin or depositing mail)</p><p><i>n.</i> a time assigned on a schedule or agenda [time slot]</p><p><i>n.</i> a position in a hierarchy or organization</p><p><i>n.</i> the trail of an animal (especially a deer)</p><p><i>n.</i> (computer) a socket in a microcomputer that will accept a plug-in circuit board [expansion slot]</p><p><i>n.</i> a slot machine that is used for gambling [one-armed bandit]</p><p><i>v.</i> assign a time slot</p><p><b>automat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a machine that is operated by the insertion of a coin in a slot [coin machine]</p><p><b>lijenost, ljenjivac, nerad, tromost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disinclination to work or exert yourself [slothfulness]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several slow-moving arboreal mammals of South America and Central America [tree sloth]</p><p><i>n.</i> apathy and inactivity in the practice of virtue (personified as one of the deadly sins) [acedia, laziness]</p><p><b>Obični grubi medvjed sa dugim čupcem iz južno-srednje Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common coarse-haired long-snouted bear of south-central Asia [Melursus ursinus, Ursus ursinus]</p><p><b>lijen, indolentan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> disinclined to work or exertion [faineant, indolent, lazy, otiose, work-shy]</p><p><b>lijen (od &quot;slothful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disinclination to work or exert yourself [sloth]</p><p><b>pogrbljenost, spušten, šeprtlja, klonuti, pogrbiti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an incompetent person</p><p><i>n.</i> a stooping carriage in standing and walking</p><p><i>v.</i> assume a drooping posture or carriage [slump]</p><p><i>v.</i> walk slovenly</p><p><b>mekani šešir od odjeće s širokim fleksibilnim rubom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soft felt hat with a wide flexible brim [cavalier hat]</p><p><b>pogrbljenost, spušten, šeprtlja (od &quot;slouch&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who slouches</p><p><b>na nejasan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a slouchy manner</p><p><b>s naglim hodom ili držanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with a slouching gait or posture</p><p><b>nedostatak ukočenosti u obliku ili držanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking stiffness in form or posture</p><p><b>bara, depresija, glib, grinta, močvara, linjati se, mitariti se, olinjati se, presvlačiti, presvući</b></p><p><i>n.</i> necrotic tissue [gangrene, sphacelus]</p><p><i>n.</i> a hollow filled with mud</p><p><i>n.</i> a stagnant swamp (especially as part of a bayou)</p><p><i>n.</i> any outer covering that can be shed or cast off (such as the cast-off skin of a snake)</p><p><i>v.</i> cast off hair, skin, horn, or feathers [exuviate, molt, moult, shed]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička konopljana s lištima sa suvim membranskim rubovima i s dužnim krovom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American cordgrass having leaves with dry membranous margins and glumes with long awns [Spartina pectinmata, freshwater cordgrass, prairie cordgrass]</p><p><b>(formalna) ekstremna depresija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (formal) extreme depression</p><p><b>Odbaciti kao neželjeno., odvojena od okolnog živog tkiva, kao u pobačaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> discard as undesirable</p><p><i>v.</i> separate from surrounding living tissue, as in an abortion</p><p><b>klizanje, osipanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process whereby something is shed [shedding]</p><p><b>močvaran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of soil) soft and watery [boggy, marshy, miry, mucky, muddy, quaggy, sloppy, soggy, squashy, swampy, waterlogged]</p><p><b>slovački, Slovak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Slovakia</p><p><i>n.</i> the Slavic language spoken in Slovakia</p><p><b>Slovačka Republika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked republic in central Europe [Slovakia]</p><p><b>Slovačka, Slovačke</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked republic in central Europe [Slovak Republic]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Slovačku ili njezin narod ili jezik (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Slovakia or its people or language</p><p><b>monetarna jedinica u Hrvatskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Slovakia</p><p><b>aljkava osoba, lijen, neuredan, prljav, prostak, sirovina, svinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coarse obnoxious person [pig, slob, slovenly person]</p><p><b>slovenski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native of Slovenia</p><p><i>n.</i> the Slavic language of Slovenes</p><p><b>Slovenija, Slovenije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountainous republic in central Europe [Republic of Slovenia, Slovenija]</p><p><b>Slovenac, slovenski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Slovenia</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Slovenia or its people or language</p><p><b>planinska republika u srednjoj Europi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountainous republic in central Europe [Republic of Slovenia, Slovenia]</p><p><b>nedostatak reda i urednosti, obična nečistoća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lack of order and tidiness [sloppiness, unkemptness]</p><p><i>n.</i> habitual uncleanliness</p><p><b>aljkav, aljkavo, neuredan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> negligent of neatness especially in dress and person [frowsy, frowzy]</p><p><b>prostak, sirovina, svinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coarse obnoxious person [pig, slob, sloven]</p><p><b>prljava žena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dirty untidy woman [slattern, slut, trollop]</p><p><b>bez žurbe, dosadan, glup, koji zaostaje, lagan, nezanimljiv, trom, spor, sporije voziti, usporen, usporiti, polagan, polako, sporo, smanjiti brzinu, sporovozan, tup, malaksati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> lose velocity [decelerate, retard, slow down, slow up]</p><p><i>v.</i> become slow or slower [slack, slacken, slow down, slow up]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to proceed more slowly [slow down, slow up]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not moving quickly</p><p><i>adj.</i> at a slow tempo</p><p><i>adj.</i> slow to learn or understand [dense, dim, dull, dumb, obtuse]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of timepieces) indicating a time earlier than the correct time</p><p><i>adj.</i> so lacking in interest as to cause mental weariness [boring, deadening, dull, ho-hum, irksome, tedious, tiresome, wearisome]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of business) not active or brisk [dull, sluggish]</p><p><i>adv.</i> without speed (`slow' is sometimes used informally for `slowly') [easy, slowly, tardily]</p><p><i>adv.</i> of timepieces [behind]</p><p><b>usporiti, zastoj, malaksati, odmarati se, odmoriti se, opustiti se, opuštati se, relaksirati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> lose velocity [decelerate, retard, slow, slow up]</p><p><i>v.</i> become slow or slower [slack, slacken, slow, slow up]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to proceed more slowly [slow, slow up]</p><p><i>v.</i> reduce the speed of [decelerate]</p><p><i>v.</i> become less tense, rest, or take one's ease [decompress, loosen up, relax, unbend, unwind]</p><p><b>U slučaju vozila u sporom kretanju: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the traffic lane for vehicles that are moving slowly</p><p><b>čvrsti lemur iz jugoistočne Azije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stocky lemur of southeastern Asia [Nycticebus pygmaeus, Nycticebus tardigradua]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta goriva može biti upotrebljena za proizvodnju goriva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> match or fuse made to burn slowly and evenly</p><p><b>usporen, usporeno snimljen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a movie that apparently takes place at a slower than normal speed</p><p><b>(simulacija) vremenska skala koja se koristi u obradi podataka kada je faktor vremenske skale veći od jedan. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (simulation) the time scale used in data processing when the time-scale factor is greater than one [extended time scale]</p><p><b>malaksati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become slow or slower [slack, slacken, slow, slow down]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to proceed more slowly [slow, slow down]</p><p><i>v.</i> lose velocity [decelerate, retard, slow, slow down]</p><p><b>virus koji ostaje u tijelu dugo vremena prije pojave simptoma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a virus that remains dormant in the body for a long time before symptoms appear</p><p><b>kreće se sporo (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> moving slowly</p><p><b>teško shvaćati, tupoglav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> retarded in intellectual development [backward, feebleminded, half-witted]</p><p><b>kvaliteta mentalnog spora i ograničenosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being mentally slow and limited [denseness, dumbness]</p><p><b>netko tko se kreće sporo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who moves slowly [plodder, slowpoke, stick-in-the-mud]</p><p><b>smanjiti brzinu, zastoj, kašnjenje, retardacija, usporavanje, zaostajanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of slowing down or falling behind [lag, retardation]</p><p><b>sporije, sporiji</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> more slowly</p><p><b>bez žurbe, dosadan, glup, koji zaostaje, lagan, nezanimljiv, trom, spor, sporije voziti, usporen, usporiti, polagan, polako, sporo, smanjiti brzinu, sporovozan, tup (od &quot;slow&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> most slowly</p><p><b>Ne želi biti poduzetnik. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not inclined to be enterprising [unenergetic]</p><p><b>usporavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a decrease in rate of change [deceleration, retardation]</p><p><b>polagano, polako, sporo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without speed (`slow' is sometimes used informally for `slowly') [easy, slow, tardily]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in music [lento]</p><p><b>dosada, glupost, polagano shvaćanje, polaganost, sporost, zakašnjenje, zaostajanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unskillfulness resulting from a lack of training [awkwardness, clumsiness, ineptitude, ineptness, maladroitness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a rate demonstrating an absence of haste or hurry [deliberateness, deliberation, unhurriedness]</p><p><i>n.</i> lack of normal development of intellectual capacities [backwardness, mental retardation, retardation, subnormality]</p><p><b>netko tko se kreće sporo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who moves slowly [plodder, slowcoach, stick-in-the-mud]</p><p><b>mali kopalički evropski gušter bez nogu s sitnim očima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small burrowing legless European lizard with tiny eyes [Anguis fragilis, blindworm]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a caustic detergent useful for removing grease [sodium lauryl sulfate, sodium lauryl sulphate]</p><p><b>ošvarak, pretpredivo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soft lump or unevenness in a yarn [burl, knot]</p><p><b>od tekstilnih materijala (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of textiles [homespun, nubbly, nubby, tweedy]</p><p><b>blato, glib, mulj, mulja, prvi tanki led, talog, uljni talog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the precipitate produced by sewage treatment</p><p><i>n.</i> any thick, viscous matter [goo, gook, goop, guck, gunk, muck, ooze, slime]</p><p><b>okret oko ose, okret oko osi, isklizati, isklizavati, iskliznuti, klizati, kliznuti, skliznuti, zaokrenuti se, zaokretati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> turn sharply [curve, cut, sheer, slew, swerve, trend, veer]</p><p><i>v.</i> move obliquely or sideways, usually in an uncontrolled manner [skid, slew, slide, slip]</p><p><b>cjevčica, izmjeren dio tekučine ubačen u cjevovod, jezgra, komad, lijenčina, ljenčariti, matrica, metak, metalni grumen, puž balavac, redak linotipa s, slag, umetak, zrno, puščano zrn