 that burns with thick smoke but no flame [smolder]</p><p><i>v.</i> have strong suppressed feelings [smolder]</p><p><i>v.</i> burn slowly and without a flame [smolder]</p><p><b>dimiti se, pušiti se, tinjanje, tinjati, tinjava vatra (od &quot;smoulder&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing scarcely suppressed anger [smoldering]</p><p><b>sa jedva potisnutim gnjevom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with barely repressed anger [smolderingly]</p><p><b>Viši podređeni časnik u Ratnom zrakoplovstvu s činom koji je uspoređen s narednikom u vojsci. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a senior noncommissioned officer in the Air Force with a rank comparable to master sergeant in the Army [senior master sergeant]</p><p><b>četkica za miješanje, mrlja, packa, prljavština, razmazati, suharaka, tinjajuća vatra s mnogo dima, vatra od suhadi, zamazati, zamrljano mjesto, zamrljati, zaprljati, brljotina, fleka, prljavoća, razmaz, smrljotina, zmazano</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a smoky fire to drive away insects</p><p><i>n.</i> a blemish made by dirt [blot, daub, slur, smear, smirch, spot]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a smudge on [blur, smear, smutch]</p><p><b>razmaženo nečim što mrlja ili mrlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> smeared with something that soils or stains</p><p><b>filistarski uskogrudan, gladak, kičen, kićen, koji se ne zanima za sport, lijep, samodopadan, samozadovoljan, sit, student koji se ne snalazi u društvu, ubav, udoban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by excessive complacency or self-satisfaction [self-satisfied]</p><p><b>krijumčariti, prokrijumčariti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> import or export without paying customs duties</p><p><b>nelegalno distribuirana ili prodana (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> distributed or sold illicitly [black, black-market, bootleg, contraband]</p><p><b>krijumčar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who imports or exports without paying duties [contrabandist, moon-curser, moon curser, runner]</p><p><b>krijumčarenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> secretly importing prohibited goods or goods on which duty is due</p><p><b>lijepo, samodopadno, uskogrudno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a smug manner</p><p><b>filistarski uskogrudan, gladak, kičen, kićen, koji se ne zanima za sport, lijep, samodopadan, samozadovoljan, sit, student koji se ne snalazi u društvu, ubav, udoban (od &quot;smug&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an excessive feeling of self-satisfaction</p><p><b>bestidna, čađ, čađava mrlja, ljaga, nepristojne riječi, očađiti, pahuljica čađe, prljavština, prosti vicevi, riječ, svinjarija, škakljiva pripovijetka, zaprljati, čađa, snijet, pornografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a black colloidal substance consisting wholly or principally of amorphous carbon and used to make pigments and ink [carbon black, crock, lampblack, soot]</p><p><i>n.</i> destructive diseases of plants (especially cereal grasses) caused by fungi that produce black powdery masses of spores</p><p><i>n.</i> any fungus of the order Ustilaginales [smut fungus]</p><p><i>n.</i> an offensive or indecent word or phrase [dirty word, filth, obscenity, vulgarism]</p><p><i>n.</i> creative activity (writing or pictures or films etc.) of no literary or artistic value other than to stimulate sexual desire [erotica, porn, porno, pornography]</p><p><i>v.</i> make obscene</p><p><i>v.</i> stain with a dirty substance, such as soot</p><p><i>v.</i> become affected with smut</p><p><i>v.</i> affect with smut or mildew, as of a crop such as corn</p><p><b>snijet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any fungus of the order Ustilaginales [smut]</p><p><b>trava porijeklom iz Zapadne Indije, ali uobičajena u južnim Sjedinjenim Državama koja ima tufted žičane stabljike često zaražene tamnim gljivom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grass native to West Indies but common in southern United States having tufted wiry stems often infested with a dark fungus [Sporobolus poiretii, blackseed, carpet grass]</p><p><b>Napravi mrlju na (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a smudge on [blur, smear, smudge]</p><p><b>bestidna, čađ, čađava mrlja, ljaga, nepristojne riječi, očađiti, pahuljica čađe, prljavština, prosti vicevi, riječ, svinjarija, škakljiva pripovijetka, zaprljati (od &quot;smut&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South African statesman and soldier (1870-1950) [Jan Christian Smuts]</p><p><b>čađav, prljav (od &quot;smutty&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a smutty manner [vulgarly]</p><p><b>stanje prljavštine sa sokom, prostaštvo u govoru ili pisanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being dirty with soot [sootiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> obscenity in speech or writing [dirtiness]</p><p><b>čađav, prljav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by obscenity [cruddy, filthy, foul, nasty]</p><p><i>adj.</i> soiled with dirt or soot [black]</p><p><b>Izmir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port city in western Turkey [Izmir]</p><p><b>Aleksandra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Alexanders [genus Smyrnium]</p><p><b>Europska biljka pomalo slična celeru koja se široko prirodila u obalnim područjima Britanije i često se uzgaja kao biljka za uzgoj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European herb somewhat resembling celery widely naturalized in Britain coastal regions and often cultivated as a potherb [Alexander, Alexanders, black lovage, horse parsley]</p><p><b>slijepo-molahidni metalni element otporan na koroziju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a silvery malleable metallic element that resists corrosion [atomic number 50, tin]</p><p><b>dio, lagani obrok, parče, udio, užina, zakuska, zakuska na brzu ruku, zalogaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light informal meal [bite, collation]</p><p><i>v.</i> eat a snack [nosh]</p><p><b>bife, zakuska, švedski stol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> usually inexpensive bar [buffet, snack counter]</p><p><b>bife, zakuska, švedski stol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> usually inexpensive bar [buffet, snack bar]</p><p><b>grickalice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> food for light meals or for eating between meals</p><p><b>dio, lagani obrok, parče, udio, užina, zakuska, zakuska na brzu ruku, zalogaj (od &quot;snack&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who eats lightly or eats snacks between meals [nosher]</p><p><b>Jednostavna zglobna bit za konja, uhvatiti ili uhvatiti brzo i lako, Sklonite ili zadržite sa štapom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a simple jointed bit for a horse [snaffle bit]</p><p><i>v.</i> get hold of or seize quickly and easily [grab, snap up]</p><p><i>v.</i> fit or restrain with a snaffle</p><p><b>Jednostavna zglobna bit za konja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a simple jointed bit for a horse [snaffle]</p><p><b>skraćenica koju su često koristili vojnici u Drugom svjetskom ratu: situacija normalna sve je sjebano., uzrok biti u stanju potpune konfuzije, -Ne znam. -Ne znam. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acronym often used by soldiers in World War II: situation normal all fucked up</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be in a state of complete confusion</p><p><i>adj.</i> snarled or stalled in complete confusion [fucked-up]</p><p><b>greben u rijeci, kusasti, kusasti dio grane koji ostane na deblu kad se gran, kvrga, naplavljeno deblo na dnu rijeke, neočekivana zapreka, okrnjak, panj, prepreka, šiljasti panj korijen koji viri iz zemlje, škrba, zakačiti, poderotina, razderotina, rupa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sharp protuberance</p><p><i>n.</i> a dead tree that is still standing, usually in an undisturbed forest</p><p><i>n.</i> an opening made forcibly as by pulling apart [rent, rip, split, tear]</p><p><i>n.</i> an unforeseen obstacle [hang-up, hitch, rub]</p><p><i>v.</i> catch on a snag</p><p><i>v.</i> get by acting quickly and smartly</p><p><i>v.</i> hew jaggedly</p><p><b>danguba, lijenčina, puž, spirala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> freshwater or marine or terrestrial gastropod mollusk usually having an external enclosing spiral shell</p><p><i>n.</i> edible terrestrial snail usually served in the shell with a sauce of melted butter and garlic [escargot]</p><p><i>v.</i> gather snails</p><p><b>višegodišnje tropske američke loze uzgajane zbog svojih žutih i ljubičastih cvijeća s korolnom kilom navučenom poput školjke puževa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial tropical American vine cultivated for its racemes of showy yellow and purple flowers having the corolla keel coiled like a snail shell [Phaseolus caracalla, Vigna caracalla, corkscrew flower, snail-flower, snail flower, snailflower]</p><p><b>za pripremu puževa: maslac začinjen šalotom i češnjakom i peršićem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> for preparing snails: butter seasoned with shallots and garlic and parsley</p><p><b>mali puževi-jedilac perch rijeke Tennessee (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small snail-eating perch of the Tennessee River [Percina tanasi]</p><p><b>višegodišnje tropske američke loze uzgajane zbog svojih žutih i ljubičastih cvijeća s korolnom kilom navučenom poput školjke puževa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial tropical American vine cultivated for its racemes of showy yellow and purple flowers having the corolla keel coiled like a snail shell [Phaseolus caracalla, Vigna caracalla, corkscrew flower, snail-flower, snail bean, snailflower]</p><p><b>pošta (osim elektronske)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any mail that is physically delivered by the postal service</p><p><b>višegodišnje tropske američke loze uzgajane zbog svojih žutih i ljubičastih cvijeća s korolnom kilom navučenom poput školjke puževa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial tropical American vine cultivated for its racemes of showy yellow and purple flowers having the corolla keel coiled like a snail shell [Phaseolus caracalla, Vigna caracalla, corkscrew flower, snail bean, snail flower, snailflower]</p><p><b>ribe hladnovodnih vrsta u obliku golubica s zdjeličnim perajima u obliku usisača (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small tadpole-shaped cold-water fishes with pelvic fins forming a sucker [Liparis liparis, sea snail, seasnail]</p><p><b>višegodišnje tropske američke loze uzgajane zbog svojih žutih i ljubičastih cvijeća s korolnom kilom navučenom poput školjke puževa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial tropical American vine cultivated for its racemes of showy yellow and purple flowers having the corolla keel coiled like a snail shell [Phaseolus caracalla, Vigna caracalla, corkscrew flower, snail-flower, snail bean, snail flower]</p><p><b>izvijati se, tegliti, vući, zmija, zmijske</b></p><p><i>n.</i> limbless scaly elongate reptile [ophidian, serpent]</p><p><i>n.</i> a deceitful or treacherous person [snake in the grass]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Columbia River that rises in Wyoming and flows westward [Snake River]</p><p><i>n.</i> a long faint constellation in the southern hemisphere near the equator stretching between Virgo and Cancer [Hydra]</p><p><i>n.</i> something long, thin, and flexible that resembles a snake</p><p><i>n.</i> a long flexible steel coil for dislodging stoppages in curved pipes [auger, plumber's snake]</p><p><i>v.</i> move smoothly and sinuously, like a snake</p><p><i>v.</i> form a snake-like pattern</p><p><i>v.</i> move along a winding path</p><p><b>izvođač koji koristi pokrete i glazbu za kontrolu zmija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a performer who uses movements and music to control snakes</p><p><b>grupa napreduje u jednostoj vrsti serpentine staze, ceremonijalni ples (kao kod Hopija) u kojem se zmije rukuju ili pozivaju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group advancing in a single-file serpentine path</p><p><i>n.</i> a ceremonial dance (as by the Hopi) in which snakes are handled or invoked</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u pitanju krastavac, to znači da je krastavac u stanju da se odredi na određenu vrstu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender-bodied non-stinging insect having iridescent wings that are outspread at rest [darning needle, devil's darning needle, dragonfly, mosquito hawk, sewing needle, skeeter hawk, snake feeder]</p><p><b>izrazi koji se koriste kada kad se baci dva kocka i obje se pojavljuju pokazujući jedno mjesto (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> expressions used when when two dice are thrown and both come up showing one spot [craps]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u pitanju krastavac, to znači da je krastavac u stanju da se odredi na određenu vrstu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender-bodied non-stinging insect having iridescent wings that are outspread at rest [darning needle, devil's darning needle, dragonfly, mosquito hawk, sewing needle, skeeter hawk, snake doctor]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za željezničke željeznice od 8203 do 8204 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rail fence consisting of a zigzag of interlocking rails [Virginia fence, snake-rail fence, worm fence]</p><p><b>tropski paprika široko rasprostranjen u Starom svijetu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical fern widespread in Old World [Lygodium microphyllum, climbing maidenhair, climbing maidenhair fern]</p><p><b>Bog voodoo kulta afričkog porijekla koji se obožava posebno u Zapadnoj Indiji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a god of voodoo cults of African origin worshipped especially in West Indies [zombi, zombie]</p><p><b>prevarant ili izdajnik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deceitful or treacherous person [snake]</p><p><b>tropske ribe grabežljivke s izbočenim čeljustima i snažnim zubima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> predatory tropical fishes with jutting jaws and strong teeth [Gempylus serpens]</p><p><b>afrička prugasta kuna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small slender burrowing muishond with white top of the head [Poecilogale albinucha]</p><p><b>(medicinski) bilo koja od raznih tekućina prodati kao lijek (kao što je putovanje lijekovi show), ali medicinski bezvrijedan, komunikacija (pisana ili usmena) namijenjena zavaravanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) any of various liquids sold as medicine (as by a travelling medicine show) but medically worthless</p><p><i>n.</i> communication (written or spoken) intended to deceive [humbug]</p><p><b>smrdljiva pomalo mesna tropska biljka iz jugoistočne Azije uzgajana zbog svojih jestivih kormova ili u stakleniku zbog svojih velikih listova i najozbiljnijih tamno crvenih špatova koji okružuju veliki špat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> foul-smelling somewhat fleshy tropical plant of southeastern Asia cultivated for its edible corms or in the greenhouse for its large leaves and showy dark red spathe surrounding a large spadix [Amorphophallus rivieri, devil's tongue, umbrella arum]</p><p><b>bilo koje mjesto boli i nemira, Porečni izrazi za ludnicu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any place of pain and turmoil [hell, hell on earth, hellhole, inferno, the pits]</p><p><i>n.</i> pejorative terms for an insane asylum [Bedlam, booby hatch, crazy house, cuckoo's nest, funny farm, funny house, loony bin, madhouse, nut house, nuthouse, sanatorium]</p><p><b>biljka bez stabla s uskim čvrstim lišćama često uzgajana kao kućna biljka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stemless plant having narrow rigid leaves often cultivated as a houseplant [Sansevieria trifasciata, mother-in-law's tongue]</p><p><b>epifitne paprike s dugim korijenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> epiphytic ferns with long rhizomes [Microgramma-piloselloides]</p><p><b>Priloga rijeke Columbia koja izlazi u Wyomingu i teče prema zapadu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Columbia River that rises in Wyoming and flows westward [Snake]</p><p><b>otrov koji izlučuju neke zmije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> venom secreted by certain snakes</p><p><b>tropsko američko stablo s velikim peltatnim lišćama i šupljim stabljikama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American tree with large peltate leaves and hollow stems [Cecropia peltata, imbauba, trumpet-wood, trumpet tree, trumpetwood]</p><p><b>Evroazijski krugovi s višenčastim cvijećem obično su vijeni i krugovi sa ljubičastim ili smeđim na blijedom podlozi i u obliku zvona koje su nosili gubaci u srednjovjekovno doba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian checkered lily with pendant flowers usually veined and checkered with purple or maroon on a pale ground and shaped like the bells carried by lepers in medieval times [Fritillaria meleagris, checkered daffodil, guinea-hen flower, leper lily]</p><p><b>tropske ribe s velikim ustima u glavama nalik gušteru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical fishes with large mouths in lizard-like heads [lizardfish, snakefish]</p><p><b>Imaju zmije za dlake. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of monsters) having snakes for hair</p><p><b>Visoka višegodišnja biljka u močvarnim područjima istočne i središnje Sjeverne Amerike s voskovitim lanceolatičnim lištima i cvijetom s donjim dijelom kremasto bijelom i gornjim dijelom blijedo ružičastog do tamno ljubičastog boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> showy perennial of marshlands of eastern and central North America having waxy lanceolate leaves and flower with lower part creamy white and upper parts pale pink to deep purple [Chelone glabra, shell-flower, shellflower, snakehead, turtlehead]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za željezničke željeznice od 8203 do 8204 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rail fence consisting of a zigzag of interlocking rails [Virginia fence, snake fence, worm fence]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerička višegodišnja biljka s napunjenim listovima i rasemi malih bijelih cvijeća s ovalnim otrovnim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American perennial herb with alternately compound leaves and racemes of small white flowers followed by bright red oval poisonous berries [Actaea rubra, red-berry, red baneberry, redberry]</p><p><b>ptica ribolova u toplim unutarnjim vodama s dugim fleksibilnim vratom i tankim oštrim čelom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fish-eating bird of warm inland waters having a long flexible neck and slender sharp-pointed bill [anhinga, darter]</p><p><b>Ugriz od zmije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bite inflicted by a (venomous) snake</p><p><b>nalazi se u arktičkim vodama i sjevernom Atlantiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found in Arctic and northern Atlantic waters [Lumpenus lumpretaeformis]</p><p><b>tropske ribe s velikim ustima u glavama nalik gušteru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical fishes with large mouths in lizard-like heads [lizardfish, snake-fish]</p><p><b>predatorni insekt zapadne Sjeverne Amerike s dugim vratnim prothoraxom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> predatory insect of western North America having a long necklike prothorax</p><p><b>Visoka višegodišnja biljka u močvarnim područjima istočne i središnje Sjeverne Amerike s voskovitim lanceolatičnim lištima i cvijetom s donjim dijelom kremasto bijelom i gornjim dijelom blijedo ružičastog do tamno ljubičastog boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> showy perennial of marshlands of eastern and central North America having waxy lanceolate leaves and flower with lower part creamy white and upper parts pale pink to deep purple [Chelone glabra, shell-flower, shellflower, snake-head, turtlehead]</p><p><b>nalik zmiji u obliku. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling a serpent in form [serpentine, snaky]</p><p><b>biljka rod Sanicula s palmatno složenim listovima i unisexualnim cvijećem u panikiranim umbelsima s štrkovitim plodovima, bilo koja od različitih sjevernoameričkih biljaka rod Liatris s rasemi ili panicama malih diskodnih cvjetnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant of the genus Sanicula having palmately compound leaves and unisexual flowers in panicled umbels followed by bristly fruit [sanicle]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various North American plants of the genus Liatris having racemes or panicles of small discoid flower heads [blazing star, button snakeroot, gay-feather, gayfeather]</p><p><b>Igrica za djecu koja koriste kockice za pomicanje brojača gore ljestve i dolje zmije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a board game for children who use dice to move counters up ladders and down snakes</p><p><b>niskorazrastajući ljepljivi potgrm jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s uskim linearnim lištima na mnogim tankim granama i stotinama sitnih žutih cvjetnih glavaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing sticky subshrub of southwestern United States having narrow linear leaves on many slender branches and hundreds of tiny yellow flower heads [Gutierrezia sarothrae, broom snakeroot, broom snakeweed, rabbit-weed, rabbitweed, turpentine weed]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijski špiljski grm s iskrivljenim udovima i korijenima koji liče na zmije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian climbing shrub with twisted limbs and roots resembling serpents [Rauwolfia serpentina]</p><p><b>nalik zm