st, deluge, downpour, pelter, torrent, waterspout]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who drinks alcohol to excess habitually [alcoholic, alky, boozer, dipsomaniac, lush, souse]</p><p><b>močenje, nalijevanje, punjenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of becoming softened and saturated as a consequence of being immersed in water (or other liquid) [soak, soakage]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making something completely wet [drenching, souse, sousing]</p><p><i>n.</i> washing something by allowing it to soak [soak]</p><p><i>adv.</i> extremely wet [dripping, sopping]</p><p><b>(kemija) proces u kojem jedna tvar prodire u drugu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) a process in which one substance permeates another [absorption]</p><p><b>laskati, nasapunjati, sapun, novac, max, sapunati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cleansing agent made from the salts of vegetable or animal fats</p><p><i>n.</i> money offered as a bribe</p><p><i>n.</i> street names for gamma hydroxybutyrate [Georgia home boy, easy lay, goop, grievous bodily harm, liquid ecstasy, max, scoop]</p><p><i>v.</i> rub soap all over, usually with the purpose of cleaning [lather]</p><p><b>sapunski mjehur</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bubble formed by a thin soap film</p><p><b>za proizvodnju električnih vozila s motorom za vožnju na dužini od 300 mm ili više, ali ne više od 300 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bathroom or kitchen fixture for holding a bar of soap</p><p><b>razvodnik tekućeg sapuna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dispenser of liquid soap</p><p><b>film koji ostaje na predmetima nakon što su oprali sapunom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a film left on objects after they have been washed in soap</p><p><b>sapun koji je rezan u ravnice kako bi se brže odlivao (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soap that has been cut into flakes to make suds faster</p><p><b>sapunica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a serialized program usually dealing with sentimentalized family matters that is broadcast on radio or television (frequently sponsored by a company advertising soap products)</p><p>