ing soap or being covered with soap</p><p><b>od talka, mekane, teške i kompaktne vrste, sa sapunskim osjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soft heavy compact variety of talc having a soapy feel [soap-rock, soapstone, steatite]</p><p><b>steatit, talk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soft heavy compact variety of talc having a soapy feel [soap-rock, soaprock, steatite]</p><p><b>sapunica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the froth produced by soaps or detergents [lather, suds]</p><p><b>visoka drvena juka iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall arborescent yucca of southwestern United States [Yucca elata, soap-weed, soap tree]</p><p><b>biljka europskog podrijetla s ružičastim ili bijelim cvijećem i lištima koje pri rušenju daju deterdžent (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant of European origin having pink or white flowers and leaves yielding a detergent when bruised [Saponaria officinalis, bouncing Bess, bouncing Bet, hedge pink]</p><p><b>Vječna biljka iz vlažnih šuma Sjeverne Amerike s lištima i pupoljcima koji se sliče na one iz sapuna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect perennial of wet woodlands of North America having leaves and flower buds resembling those of soapwort [Gentiana saponaria]</p><p><b>laskav, sapunast, ulagivački</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling or having the qualities of soap [saponaceous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unpleasantly and excessively suave or ingratiating in manner or speech [buttery, fulsome, oily, oleaginous, smarmy, unctuous]</p><p><b>dizati se, jedrenje, jedriti, kovitlati se, lebdjeti, lebdjeti u visini, porasti, uzlijetanje, vinuti se, vinuti se u visinu, visoko letjeti, uzvinuti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of rising upward into the air [zoom]</p><p><i>v.</i> rise rapidly [soar up, soar upwards, surge, zoom]</p><p><i>v.</i> fly by means of a hang glider [hang glide]</p><p><i>v.</i> fly upwards or high in the sky</p><p><i>v.</i> go or move upward</p><p><i>v.</i> fly a plane without an engine [sailplane]</p><p><b>brzo se diže (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> rise