ijama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> take part in social activities [socialize]</p><p><i>v.</i> train for a social environment [socialize]</p><p><i>v.</i> prepare for social life [socialize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make conform to socialist ideas and philosophies [socialize]</p><p><b>pod kontrolom grupe ili vlade (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> under group or government control [socialized]</p><p><b>osoba koja sudjeluje u društvenim aktivnostima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who takes part in social activities [socializer]</p><p><b>Čin sastanka u društvene svrhe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of meeting for social purposes [socialisation, socialization, socializing]</p><p><b>socijalizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political theory advocating state ownership of industry</p><p><i>n.</i> an economic system based on state ownership of capital [socialist economy]</p><p><b>socijalist, socijalistički, socijalističkoj, socijalističkom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political advocate of socialism</p><p><i>adj.</i> advocating or following the socialist principles [socialistic]</p><p><b>ekonomski sustav zasnovan na državnom vlasništvu kapitala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an economic system based on state ownership of capital [socialism]</p><p><b>politička stranka u Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political party in the United States</p><p><b>socijalistička stranka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a political party in the United States formed in 1900 to advocate socialism</p><p><b>Socijalistička Narodna Libijska Arapska Džamahirij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a military dictatorship in northern Africa on the Mediterranean [Libya]</p><p><b>komunistička država u Indokini na Južnom kineskom moru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a communist state in Indochina on the South China Sea [Annam, Viet Nam, Vietnam]</p><p><b>socijalistički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> advocating or following the socialist principles [socialist]</p><p><b>društveno istaknuta osoba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a socially prominent person</p><p><b>društvenost</b>