/p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to both social and cultural matters</p><p><b>socioekonomski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving social as well as economic factors</p><p><b>u odnosu na socioekonomske čimbenike (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to socioeconomic factors</p><p><b>lingvista koji proučava društvene i kulturne faktore koji utječu na jezično komuniciranje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a linguist who studies the social and cultural factors that influence linguistic communication</p><p><b>sociolingvističke znanosti ili s njom povezane (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to sociolinguistics</p><p><b>u odnosu na sociolingvistiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to sociolinguistics</p><p><b>sociolingvistika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of language in relation to its sociocultural context</p><p><b>sociološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or determined by sociology</p><p><b>sociološki (od &quot;sociological&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with regard to sociology</p><p><b>sociolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a social scientist who studies the institutions and development of human society</p><p><b>sociologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study and classification of human societies</p><p><b>akademski odjel odgovoran za podučavanje i istraživanje sociologije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the academic department responsible for teaching and research in sociology [department of sociology]</p><p><b>kvantitativno proučavanje socijalnih odnosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quantitative study of social relationships</p><p><b>netko s sociopatskom osobnošću (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone with a sociopathic personality [psychopath]</p><p><b>sociopatski poremećaj osobnosti ili povezan s njim (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a sociopathic personality disorder</p><p><b>poremećaj osobnosti koji se odlikuje nemoralnošću i nedostatkom osjećaja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a personality disorder characterized by amorality and lack of affect [antisocial personality disorder, psy