ennial aromatic herb of southeastern Asia having large usually bright-colored or blotched leaves and spikes of blue-violet flowers [Coleus blumei, Joseph's coat, Solenostemon blumei, painted nettle]</p><p><b>moreuz engleskog kanala između obale Hampshirea i otoka Wight (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strait of the English Channel between the coast of Hampshire and the Isle of Wight</p><p><b>široki listoliki mišić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a broad flat muscle in the calf of the leg under the gastrocnemius muscle [soleus muscle]</p><p><b>široki listoliki mišić</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a broad flat muscle in the calf of the leg under the gastrocnemius muscle [soleus]</p><p><b>sustav solmizacije pomoću solfa slogova: do, re, mi, fa, sol, la, ti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of solmization using the solfa syllables: do, re, mi, fa, sol, la, ti [tonic solfa]</p><p><b>jedno od imena za note glazbene skale u solmiziranju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the names for notes of a musical scale in solmization</p><p><b>Pjevanje koristeći solfa slogove za označavanje note stupnjeva C major, vježba glasa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> singing using solfa syllables to denote the notes of the scale of C major [solfeggio, solmization]</p><p><i>n.</i> a voice exercise [solfeggio]</p><p><b>Pjevanje koristeći solfa slogove za označavanje note stupnjeva C major, vježba glasa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> singing using solfa syllables to denote the notes of the scale of C major [solfege, solmization]</p><p><i>n.</i> a voice exercise [solfege]</p><p><b>ružičasta boja koja je otkrivena 1859. godine, godine bitke kod Solferina., Neodlučna bitka 1859. između Francuza i Sardanaca pod Napoleonom III. i Austrijancima pod Franciskom Josifom I. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pink dye that was discovered in 1859, the year a battle was fought at Solferino [purplish pink]</p><p><i>n.</i> an indecisive battle in 1859 between the French and Sardinians under Napoleon III and the Austrians under Francis Joseph I [battle of Solferino]</p><p><b>dosađivati, izazvati, moliti, nametati se, preklinjati, tražiti, zauzimati se, snubiti, udvarati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a solicitation or entreaty for something [beg, tap]</p><p><i>v.</i> make amorous advances towards [court, romance, woo]</p><p><i>v.</i> approach with an offer of sexual favors [accost, hook]</p><p><i>v.</i> incite, move, or persuade to some act of lawlessness or insubordination</p><p><i>v.</i> make a solicitation or petition for something desired</p><p><b>dosađivanje, traženje, zahtjev, zauzimanje, prikupljanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an entreaty addressed to someone of superior status</p><p><i>n.</i> request for a sum of money [appeal, collection, ingathering]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of enticing a person to do something wrong (as an offer of sex in return for money) [allurement]</p><p><b>advokat, molitelj, odvjetnik, posrednik, zamjenik, zaštitnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a petitioner who solicits contributions or trade or votes [canvasser]</p><p><i>n.</i> a British lawyer who gives legal advice and prepares legal documents</p><p><b>službenik koji pomaže državnom odvjetniku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a law officer appointed to assist an attorney general</p><p><b>poziciju odvjetnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the position of solicitor</p><p><b>brižan, koji teži, koji želi, poklanjati pažnju, zabrinut</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of anxiety and concern</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing hovering attentiveness</p><p><b>brižan, koji teži, koji želi, poklanjati pažnju, zabrinut (od &quot;solicitous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a concerned and solicitous manner</p><p><b>brižan, koji teži, koji želi, poklanjati pažnju, zabrinut (od &quot;solicitous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of excessive concern [solicitude]</p><p><b>brige, brižnost, revnost, staranje, starenje, zabrinutost, zauzimanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of excessive concern [solicitousness]</p><p><b>bez primjesa, cjelokupan, čvrst, čvrsto tijelo, geometrijsko tijelo, iz cijela, izdržlj