itarius]</p><p><b>(fizička) kvant energije ili kvazičestice koja se može širiti kao val u nelinearnim sustavima i koja nije ni prethodna ni slijedila drugi takav poremećaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a quantum of energy or quasiparticle that can be propagated as a traveling wave in nonlinear systems and is neither preceded nor followed by another such disturbance [soliton, soliton wave]</p><p><b>(fizička) kvant energije ili kvazičestice koja se može širiti kao val u nelinearnim sustavima i koja nije ni prethodna ni slijedila drugi takav poremećaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a quantum of energy or quasiparticle that can be propagated as a traveling wave in nonlinear systems and is neither preceded nor followed by another such disturbance [solitary wave, soliton wave]</p><p><b>(fizička) kvant energije ili kvazičestice koja se može širiti kao val u nelinearnim sustavima i koja nije ni prethodna ni slijedila drugi takav poremećaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) a quantum of energy or quasiparticle that can be propagated as a traveling wave in nonlinear systems and is neither preceded nor followed by another such disturbance [solitary wave, soliton]</p><p><b>osama, pustinja, samoća, usamljenost, zabito mjesto</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of social isolation [purdah]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state or situation of being alone</p><p><i>n.</i> a solitary place</p><p><b>pustinjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who lives in solitude [hermit, recluse, solitary, troglodyte]</p><p><b>Oklop koji štiti stopalo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> armor plate that protects the foot [sabaton]</p><p><b>sustav imenovanja nota glazbene skale slojevima umjesto slova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of naming the notes of a musical scale by syllables instead of letters [solmization]</p><p><b>pjevaj po slojevima solmiziranja., Pjevaj koristeći slogove kao što su `do', `re' i `mi' kako bi predstavljali tonove skale. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> sing by the syllables of solmization</p><p><i>v.</i> sing using syllables like `do', `re' and `mi' to represent the tones of the scale</p><p><b>sustav imenovanja nota glazbene skale slojevima umjesto slova, Pjevanje koristeći solfa slogove za označavanje note stupnjeva C major (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of naming the notes of a musical scale by syllables instead of letters [solmisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> singing using solfa syllables to denote the notes of the scale of C major [solfege, solfeggio]</p><p><b>solistički, solo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any activity that is performed alone without assistance</p><p><i>n.</i> a musical composition for one voice or instrument (with or without accompaniment)</p><p><i>n.</i> a flight in which the aircraft pilot is unaccompanied</p><p><i>v.</i> fly alone, without a co-pilot or passengers</p><p><i>v.</i> perform a piece written for a single instrument</p><p><i>adj.</i> composed or performed by a single voice or instrument</p><p><i>adv.</i> without anybody else or anything else [alone, unaccompanied]</p><p><b>Domera bez trkača na bazi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a home run with no runners on base [solo homer]</p><p><b>Domera bez trkača na bazi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a home run with no runners on base [solo blast]</p><p><b>rani čovjek kasnog Pleistocena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> early man of late Pleistocene</p><p><b>solist, solista</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musician who performs a solo</p><p><b>Salomon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Old Testament) son of David and king of Israel noted for his wisdom (10th century BC)</p><p><b>Američki pisac (rođen u Kanadi) čiji su romani utjecali na američku književnost nakon Drugog svjetskog rata (1915-2005) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States author (born in Canada) whose novels influenced American literature after World War II (1915-2005) [Bellow, Saul Bellow]</p><p><b>Filantrop iz Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States philanthropist [Guggenheim]</p><p><b>Američki impresario rođen u Rusiji (1888-1974) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States impresario who was born in Russia (1888-1974) [Hurok, Sol Hurok]</p><p><b>Salamunovi Otoci, Salamunovo Otočje, Solomonski Otoci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the southern Solomon Islands that since 1978 form an independent state in the British Commonwealth</p><p><i>n.</i> the northernmost islands are part of Papua New Guinea [Solomons]</p><p><b>Šestokopta zvijezda formirana od dva jednakostrana trouglova. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a six-pointed star formed from two equilateral triangles [Magen David, Mogen David, Shield of David, Star of David]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko biljaka iz roda Polygonatum s parom spuštenih žuto-zelenih cvijeća i debelom korijenskom stabljikom s ožiljcima u obliku Solomonove pečatke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several plants of the genus Polygonatum having paired drooping yellowish-green flowers and a thick rootstock with scars shaped like Solomon's seal</p><p><b>Salomon (od &quot;solomon&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> exhibiting or requiring the wisdom of Solomon in making difficult decisions</p><p><b>Salomon (od &quot;solomon&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the northernmost islands are part of Papua New Guinea [Solomon Islands]</p><p><b>državnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who is a respected leader in national or international affairs [national leader, statesman]</p><p><b>umjetni jezik. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial language</p><p><b>solsticij, suncostaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of the two times of the year when the sun is at its greatest distance from the celestial equator</p><p><b>rastvaranja, rješivost, sposobnost, topivost, topljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quantity of a particular substance that can dissolve in a particular solvent (yielding a saturated solution)</p><p><i>n.</i> the property (of a problem or difficulty) that makes it possible to solve [solvability]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being soluble and easily dissolved in liquid</p><p><b>razjašnjiv, rješiv, topiv, topljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a substance) capable of being dissolved in some solvent (usually water)</p><p><i>adj.</i> susceptible of solution or of being solved or explained</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,05 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,05 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a viscous glass consisting of sodium silicate in solution [sodium silicate, water glass]</p><p><b>RNK molekule prisutne u stanici (u najmanje 20 vrsta, svaka vrsta sposobna za kombinaciju s određenom aminokiselinom) koje vežu pravu aminokiselinu za proteinni lanac koji se sintetizira u ribosom stanice (prema uputama kodiranim u mRNK) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> RNA molecules present in the cell (in at least 20 varieties, each variety capable of combining with a specific amino acid) that attach the correct amino acid to the protein chain that is being synthesized at the ribosome of the cell (according to directions coded in the mRNA) [acceptor RNA, tRNA, transfer RNA]</p><p><b>razjašnjiv, rješiv, topiv, topljiv (od &quot;soluble&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being dissoluble [dissolubility]</p><p><b>rastvoren</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the dissolved matter in a solution</p><p><b>otapanje, otopina, preokret, rasplet, rastvor, rješavanje, rješenja, rješenje, solucija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a homogeneous mixture of two or more substances</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement that solves a problem or explains how to solve the problem [answer, resolution, result, solvent]</p><p><i>n.</i> a method for solving a problem</p><p><i>n.</i> the set of values that give a true statement when substituted into an equation [root]</p><p><i>n.</i> the successful action of solving a problem</p><p><b>rješivost, topivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property (of a problem or difficulty) that makes it possible to solve [solubility]</p><p><b>razjašnjiv, rješiv, topiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being solved [resolvable]</p><p><b>Spoj koji se formira solvacijom (kombinacija molekula rastvarača s molekulama ili ionima rastvorenog tvari), (u) uzrokovati rastvor u (supstanci), s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 g/cm3 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound formed by solvation (the combination of solvent molecules with molecules or ions of the solute)</p><p><i>v.</i> cause a solvation in (a substance)</p><p><i>v.</i> undergo solvation or convert into a solvate</p><p><b>sredstvo koje pretvara nešto u solvat. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agent that converts something into a solvate</p><p><b>ionska solvatacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chemical process in which solvent molecules and molecules or ions of the solute combine to form a compound</p><p><b>Belgijski kemičar koji je razvio Solvayov postupak i izgradio tvornice koje ga koriste (1838-1922) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Belgian chemist who developed the Solvay process and built factories exploiting it (1838-1922) [Ernest Solvay]</p><p><b>industrijski proces za proizvodnju natrijum-karbonata iz natrijum-hlorida i amonijaka i ugljičnog dioksida (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industrial process for producing sodium carbonate from sodium chloride and ammonia and carbon dioxide</p><p><b>objasniti, razriješiti, riješiti, rješavati, odgonetnuti, razrješavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> find the solution to (a problem or question) or understand the meaning of [figure out, lick, puzzle out, work, work out]</p><p><i>v.</i> find the solution [resolve]</p><p><i>v.</i> settle, as of a debt [clear]</p><p><b>razriješeno, riješen, rješavaju, rješen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> explained or answered [resolved]</p><p><b>bonitet, likvidnost, solventnost, sposobnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ability to meet maturing obligations as they come due</p><p><b>koji rastvara, otapalo, rastvarač, solventan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a liquid substance capable of dissolving other substances [dissolvent, dissolver, dissolving agent, resolvent]</p><p><i>n.</i> a statement that solves a problem or explains how to solve the problem [answer, resolution, result, solution]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of meeting financial obligations</p><p><b>računska mašina, rastvarač, razrješivač, rješavač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thinker who focuses on the problem as stated and tries to synthesize information and knowledge to achieve a solution [convergent thinker, problem solver]</p><p><b>rješavanje, rješavanja, rješavanju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> finding a solution to a problem [resolution]</p><p><b>veliki proljak na zapadnoj obali Britanije između Engleske i Škotske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large firth on the west coast of Britain between England and Scotland</p><p><b>Sovjetski pisac i politički disident čiji su romani razotkrili brutalnost sovjetskih radnih logora (rođen 1918.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Soviet writer and political dissident whose novels exposed the brutality of Soviet labor camps (born in 1918) [Aleksandr I. Solzhenitsyn, Aleksandr Solzhenitsyn, Alexander Isayevich Solzhenitsyn]</p><p><b>osnovna jedinica novca u Uzbekistanu, osnovna jedinica novca u Kirgistanu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Uzbekistan</p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Kyrgyzstan</p><p><b>figura, građa, ljudsko tijelo, stas, tijelo, tjelesna građa, trup</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leafless East Indian vine [Sarcostemma acidum, haoma]</p><p><i>n.</i> personification of a sacred intoxicating drink used in Vedic ritual</p><p><i>n.</i> alternative names for the body of a human being [anatomy, bod, build, chassis, figure, flesh, form, frame, human body, material body, physical body, physique, shape]</p><p><b>percepcija taktičkih ili proprioceptivnih ili crijevnih osjećaja, sposobnost za percepciju tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the perception of tactual or proprioceptive or gut sensations [somatesthesia, somatic sensation, somesthesia]</p><p><i>n.</i> the faculty of bodily perception [somaesthesis, somataesthesis, somatesthesia, somatic sense, somatic sensory system, somatosensory system, somesthesia, somesthesis]</p><p><b>sposobnost za percepciju tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the faculty of bodily perception [somaesthesia, somataesthesis, somatesthesia,