e experience when vinegar or lemon juice is taken into the mouth [sourness, tartness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being acidic [acidity, sourness]</p><p><i>v.</i> go sour or spoil [ferment, turn, work]</p><p><i>v.</i> make sour or more sour [acetify, acidify, acidulate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> smelling of fermentation or staleness [rancid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a sharp biting taste</p><p><i>adj.</i> one of the four basic taste sensations</p><p><i>adj.</i> in an unpalatable state [off, turned]</p><p><i>adj.</i> inaccurate in pitch [false, off-key]</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing a brooding ill humor [dark, dour, glowering, glum, moody, morose, saturnine, sullen]</p><p><b>s masom od najmanje 10 kg, ali ne više od 10 kg (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> made with a starter of a small amount of dough in which fermentation is active [sourdough bread]</p><p><b>višnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rather small Eurasian tree producing red to black acid edible fruit [Prunus cerasus, sour cherry tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> Australian tree with sour red fruit [Eugenia corynantha]</p><p><i>n.</i> acid cherries used for pies and preserves</p><p><b>višnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rather small Eurasian tree producing red to black acid edible fruit [Prunus cerasus, sour cherry]</p><p><b>kiselo vrhnje, vrhnje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> artificially soured light cream [soured cream]</p><p><b>Europski kiseonik s velikim blago kiselim sagitatnim listovima uzgajan u sjevernoj umjerenoj zoni za salate i proljetne povrće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European sorrel with large slightly acidic sagittate leaves grown throughout north temperate zone for salad and spring greens [Rumex acetosa, garden sorrel]</p><p><b>u slučaju da je proizvodnja proizvoda u skladu s člankom 1. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe ograničena na proizvodnju proizvoda koji sadrže: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low-growing South African succulent plant having a capsular fruit containing edible pulp [Carpobrotus edulis, Hottentot's fig, Hottentot fig, Mesembryan