>n.</i> a native or resident of South Dakota</p><p><b>Dravidski jezik koji se govori uglavnom u južnoj Indiji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Dravidian language spoken primarily in southern India</p><p><b>Ekvatorijalna struja koja teče zapadno preko Pacifika južno od ekvatora. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an equatorial current that flows west across the Pacific just south of the equator</p><p><b>područje oko južnog pola: Antarktik i okolne vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the region around the south pole: Antarctica and surrounding waters [Antarctic, Antarctic Zone]</p><p><b>Najveće, ali manje naseljeno od dva glavna otoka Novog Zelanda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the larger but less populous of two main islands of New Zealand</p><p><b>Južna Koreja, Koreja (Južna)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a republic in the southern half of the Korean Peninsula [Republic of Korea]</p><p><b>Korejac iz Južne Koreje., o ili povezan s ili karakterističan za Južnu Koreju ili njen narod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Korean from South Korea</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of South Korea or its people</p><p><b>monetarna jedinica u Južnoj Koreji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in South Korea</p><p><b>osnovna jedinica novca u Južnoj Koreji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in South Korea [won]</p><p><b>Okrug u jugozapadnom Manhattanu poznat po svojim trgovinama i restoranima i galerijama i umjetničkim podnožjima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a district in southwestern Manhattan noted for its shops and restaurants and galleries and artist's lofts [SoHo]</p><p><b>taj dio Tihog oceana južno od ekvatora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> that part of the Pacific Ocean to the south of the equator</p><p><b>potokan rijeke Platte (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Platte River [South Platte River]</p><p><b>potokan rijeke Platte (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Platte River [South Platte]</p><p><b>Južni pol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the southernmost point of the Earth's axis</p><