je se primjenjuje odredba iz stavka 1. točke (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje odredba iz stavka 1. točke (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, podrijetlo se: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect or shrubby tree of Africa having ridged dark grey bark and rigid glossy medium to long leaves [Podocarpus latifolius]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog Pravilnika, poduzeća koja se nalaze u području u kojem se nalazi poduzeće mogu biti:, koji se nalazi u ili iz regije Sjedinjenih Država uključujući države donje doline Mississippija i istočno od rijeke Rio Grande (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in the southern part of a centrally located area in some geographical region</p><p><i>adj.</i> being in or of a region of the United States including the states of the lower Mississippi valley and east of the Rio Grande</p><p><b>Dravidski jezik koji se govori uglavnom u južnoj središnjoj Indiji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Dravidian language spoken primarily in south central India</p><p><b>jugoistočni, jugoistok, jugoistoku</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to, toward, or in the southeast [sou'-east, southeast]</p><p><b>na ili u blizini južnog pola (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> at or near the south pole [Antarctic]</p><p><b>pol magneta koji pokazuje prema jugu kada je magnet slobodno obješen. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the pole of a magnet that points toward the south when the magnet is suspended freely [negative magnetic pole, negative pole]</p><p><b>prema, prema ili u jugoistočnom dijelu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to, toward, or in the south southeast [sou'-sou'-east]</p><p><b>prema, prema ili u jugoj jugozapadnoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to, toward, or in the south southwest [sou'-sou'-west]</p><p><b>jugozapad, jugozapadni</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to, toward, or in the southwest [sou'west, southwest]</p><p><b>kreće se u smjeru juga</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> moving toward the south [southward]</p><p><b>jugoistok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point midway between south and east [SE, sou'-east, southeastward]</p><p><i>n.</i> the southeastern region of the United States [southeastern United States]</p><p><i>n.</i> the direction corresponding to the southeastward compass point</p><p><i>n.</i> a location in the southeastern part of a country, region, or city</p><p><i>adj.</i> coming from the southeast [southeasterly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the southeast [southeasterly, southeastern]</p><p><i>adv.</i> to, toward, or in the southeast [sou'-east, south-east]</p><p><b>geografsko podjele Azije koja uključuje Indokinu plus Indoneziju i Filipine i Singapur (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a geographical division of Asia that includes Indochina plus Indonesia and the Philippines and Singapore</p><p><b>Kompasna točka koja je jedna točka istočno od jugoistočne. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point that is one point east of southeast [SEbE]</p><p><b>Kompasna točka koja je jedna točka južno od jugoistočne (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point that is one point south of southeast [SEbS]</p><p><b>jugoistok (od &quot;southeast&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strong wind from the southeast [sou'easter]</p><p><b>Dolazi sa jugoistoka., Srednja i srednja granica (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> coming from the southeast [southeast]</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the southeast [southeast, southeastern]</p><p><b>Srednja i srednja granica, regije Sjedinjenih Država, uključujući Alabama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the southeast [southeast, southeasterly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a region of the United States generally including Alabama</p><p><b>Gopher Alabama i Georgia i Florida (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gopher of Alabama and Georgia and Florida [Geomys pinetis]</p><p><b>jugoistočni region Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the southeastern region of the United States [Southeast]</p><p><b>kompasna točka na pola puta između juga i istoka, prema jugoistoku., u smjeru sjevera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point midway between south and east [SE, sou'-east, southeast]</p><p><i>adj.</i> toward the southeast</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a southeastward direction [southeastwardly]</p><p><b>u smjeru sjevera (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a southeastward direction [southeastward]</p><p><b>južni vjetar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wind from the south [south wind, southerly]</p><p><b>južni, okrenut jugu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wind from the south [south wind, souther]</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the south [southern]</p><p><i>adj.</i> from the south [southern]</p><p><i>adv.</i> toward the south [southward, southwards]</p><p><i>adv.</i> from the south</p><p><b>južne, južni, južnog, južnoj, južnom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in or characteristic of a region of the United States south of (approximately) the Mason-Dixon line</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the south [southerly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or coming from regions of the south</p><p><i>adj.</i> from the south [southerly]</p><p><b>listovi padajući grm iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s plavo-crnim bojama i čvrstom fleksibilnom drvetom koje se nekada koristilo za izradu strela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrub of eastern North America having blue-black berries and tough pliant wood formerly used to make arrows [Viburnum dentatum, arrow wood]</p><p><b>različite vrste aster (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of aster</p><p><b>član Južne baptističke konvencije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Southern Baptist Convention</p><p><b>udruženje južnjačkih baptista (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an association of Southern Baptists</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih bukova južne hemisfere koji imaju male obično zimzelene lišće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various beeches of the southern hemisphere having small usually evergreen leaves [evergreen beech]</p><p><b>Bukić iz sjevernoameričkih šumskih područja s slame boje prugama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> beech fern of North American woodlands having straw-colored stripes [Dryopteris hexagonoptera, Phegopteris hexagonoptera, Thelypteris hexagonoptera, broad beech fern]</p><p><b>sličan plavoj zastavi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to blue flag [Iris virginica]</p><p><b>od niskih močvara i livada sjeveroistočnih i središnjih Sjedinjenih Država i južnog Kanade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of low bogs and meadows of northeastern and central United States and southern Canada [Synaptomys cooperi]</p><p><b>grmljavo trnovito listno stablo sa jugoistočnim dijelom Sjedinjenih Država s bijelim cvijećem i malim crnim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby thorny deciduous tree of southeastern United States with white flowers and small black drupaceous fruit [Bumelia lycioides, mock orange, shittim, shittimwood]</p><p><b>Česti sjevernoamerički oblik leptira kupusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common North American form of cabbage butterfly [Pieris protodice]</p><p><b>malo stablo ili grm iz jugoistočnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small tree or shrub of southeastern United States [Malus angustifolia, flowering crab]</p><p><b>južni križ</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small conspicuous constellation in the southern hemisphere in the Milky Way near Centaurus [Crux, Crux Australis]</p><p><b>obični cipres jugoistočne Sjedinjene Države s podnožjem proširenim na bazi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common cypress of southeastern United States having trunk expanded at base [Taxodium distichum, bald cypress, pond bald cypress, swamp cypress]</p><p><b>od južne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of southern North America [Rubus trivialis]</p><p><b>Pločevici (Srbija) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flounder of southern United States [Paralichthys lethostigmus]</p><p><b>mala noćna vevericara sa velikim očima iz istočnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small large-eyed nocturnal flying squirrel of eastern United States [Glaucomys volans]</p><p><b>zvonoc iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Američkih Država (od Marylanda do Georgije) s blijedoplavim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bellflower of southeastern United States (Maryland to Georgia) having pale blue flowers [Campanula divaricata]</p><p><b>polutka južno od ekvatora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the hemisphere to the south of the equator</p><p><b>Aurora južne hemisfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the aurora of the southern hemisphere [aurora australis]</p><p><b>Srednje veličine zimzelena biljka porijeklom iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike do istočne obale Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized evergreen native to eastern North America to the east coast of Mexico [Quercus virginiana]</p><p><b>uvijekzeleno stablo iz južnih Sjedinjenih Država s velikim čvrstim blistavim lišćama i velikim bijelim slatko mirisnim cvijećima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen tree of southern United States having large stiff glossy leaves and huge white sweet-smelling flowers [Magnolia grandiflora, bull bay, evergreen magnolia, large-flowering magnolia]</p><p><b>delikatna paprika s tankim sjajnim crnim stabljikama lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> delicate maidenhair fern with slender shining black leaf stalks [Adiantum capillus-veneris, Venus'-hair fern, Venus maidenhair, Venushair, common maidenhair]</p><p><b>Udio u ribljem prometu u Južnom Atlantiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> porgy of southern Atlantic coastal waters of North America [Stenotomus aculeatus, scup, southern scup]</p><p><b>ljenovnik močvarnih obalnih područja jugoistočnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> juniper of swampy coastal regions of southeastern United States [Juniperus silicicola]</p><p><b>veliko okruglo listno stablo s rasprostranjenim granama, sa uskim falcatnim lištima s duboko sinujskim režnjama i drvetom sličnim sjevernom crvenom hradu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large round-topped deciduous tree with spreading branches having narrow falcate leaves with deeply sinuate lobes and wood similar to that of northern red oaks [Quercus falcata, swamp red oak, turkey oak]</p><p><b>Republika u južnoj središnjoj Africi koja se ranije zvala Rodesija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked republic in south central Africa formerly called Rhodesia [Republic of Zimbabwe, Rhodesia, Zimbabwe]</p><p><b>Udio u ribljem prometu u Južnom Atlantiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> porgy of southern Atlantic coastal waters of North America [Stenotomus aculeatus, scup, southern porgy]</p><p><b>Ova žaba živi u jugozapadnom dijelu Sjedinjenih Država. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> this spadefoot toad lives in the southwestern United States [Scaphiopus multiplicatus]</p><p><b>vode u jugoistočnim Sjedinjenim Državama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of flowing waters of the southeastern United States [Nuphar sagittifolium]</p><p><b>grana tajskog jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a branch of the Tai languages</p><p><b>malo svjetlo sazvežđe u polarnom području južne hemisfere u blizini Circina i Apusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small bright constellation in the polar region of the southern hemisphere near Circinus and Apus [Triangulum Australe]</p><p><b>usporeno rastući srednji cedar sa istočne obale Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slow-growing medium-sized cedar of east coast of the United States [Atlantic white cedar, Chamaecyparis thyoides, coast white cedar, white cedar, white cypress]</p><p><b>veliki bor s tri igle iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s vrlo dugim iglama i čvrstom izokrenutom udom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large three-needled pine of southeastern United States having very long needles and gnarled twisted limbs [Georgia pine, Pinus palustris, longleaf pine, pitch pine]</p><p><b>južnjak, stanovnik juga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an American who lives in the South</p><p><b>Lokalizacija ili izgovor koji je karakterističan za južne Sjedinjene Države., stav karakterističan za južnjačke stanovnike (posebno u SAD-u) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a locution or pronunciation peculiar to the southern United States</p><p><i>n.</i> an attitude characteristic of Southerners (especially in the US)</p><p><b>najjužnijem, najjužniji, najnužniji, južan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated farthest south [southmost]</p><p><b>južne, južni, južnog, južnoj, južnom (od &quot;southern&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being to the south</p><p><b>šumovita europska šumovaca naturalizirana u Sjevernoj Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby European wormwood naturalized in North America [Artemisia abrotanum]</p><p><b>Engleski pjesnik i prijatelj Wordswortha i Coleridža (1774-1843) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English poet and friend of Wordsworth and Coleridge (1774-1843) [Robert Southey]</p><p><b>bilo koje područje koje se nalazi na jugu ili prema njemu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any region lying in or toward the south</p><p><b>južan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated farthest south [southernmost]</p><p><b>lijevak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a baseball pitcher who throws the ball with the left hand [left-handed pitcher, left-hander, left hander, lefthander, lefty]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who uses the left hand with greater skill than the right [left-hander, lefty]</p><p><b>južni, južno, na jug, okrenut jugu, prema jugu, jug</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the cardinal compass point that is at 180 degrees [S, due south, south]</p><p><i>adj.</i> moving toward the south [southbound]</p><p><i>adv.</i> toward the south [southerly, southwards]</p><p><b>na jug, u pravcu juga</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> toward the south [southerly, southward]</p><p><b>jugozapad</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point midway between south and west [SW, sou'-west, southwestward]</p><p><i>n.</i> the southwestern region of the United States generally including New Mexico, Arizona, Texas, California, and sometimes Utah and Colorado [southwestern United States]</p><p><i>n.</i> the direction corresponding to the southwestward compass point</p><p><i>n.</i> a location in the southwestern part of a country, region, or city</p><p><i>adj.</i> coming from the southwest [southwesterly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the southwest [southwesterly, southwestern]</p><p><i>adv.</i> to, toward, or in the southwest [sou'west, south-west]</p><p><b>Kompasna točka koja je jedna točka južno od jugozapada. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point that is one point south of southwest [SWbS]</p><p><b>Kompasna točka koja je jedna točka zapadno od jugozapada. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point that is one point west of southwest [SWbW]</p><p><b>jugozapad (od &quot;southwest&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strong wind from the southwest [sou'wester]</p><p><b>Dolazi sa jugozapada., Srednja i srednja visina (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> coming from the southwest [southwest]</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the southwest [southwest, southwestern]</p><p><b>jugozapadnom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dialect of Middle English [West Saxon]</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated in or oriented toward the southwest [southwest, southwesterly]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a region of the United States generally including New Mexico</p><p><b>Zubni paprikac iz Teksasa do Oklahome i Kolorada i Arizone i Meksika s visokim uspravnim tufted listovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lip fern of Texas to Oklahoma and Colorado and Arizona and Mexico having tall erect tufted fronds [Cheilanthes eatonii]</p><p><b>jednako bradavična čvrsta žaba iz semi-sušnih potoka jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a uniformly warty stocky toad of washes and streams of semiarid southwestern United States [Bufo microscaphus]</p><p><b>jugozapadni region Sjedinjenih Država, uključujući New Mexico, Arizona, Texas, Kaliforniju, a ponekad i Utah i Colorado (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the southwestern region of the United States generally including New Mexico, Arizona, Texas, California, and sometimes Utah and Colorado [Southwest]</p><p><b>srednji bor sjeverozapadnog Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-size pine of northwestern Mexico [Pinus strobiformis]</p><p><b>kompasna točka na pola puta između juga i zapada, prema jugozapadu., u smjeru od 0° do 0° (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the compass point midway between south and west [SW, sou'-west, southwest]</p><p><i>adj.</i> toward the southwest</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a southwestward direction [southwestwardly]</p><p><b>u smjeru od 0° do 0° (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a southwestward direction [southwestward]</p><p><b>Francuski slikar ekspresionizam (rođen u Litvi) (1893-1943) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French expressionist painter (born in Lithuania) (1893-1943) [Chaim Soutine]</p><p><b>suvenir, suvenira, uspomena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something of sentimental value [keepsake, relic, token]</p><p><i>n.</i> a reminder of past events [memento]</p><p><b>od janjetine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> made of lamb [souvlakia]</p><p><b>od janjetine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> made of lamb [souvlaki]</p><p><b>bezgraničan, djelotvoran, engleski zlatni novac, gospodar, kraljevski, monarh, neograničeni vladalac, nezavisan, nezavisna država, suveren, uspješan, viši, vladar, vrhovni</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nation's ruler or head of state usually by hereditary right [crowned head, monarch]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of political bodies) not controlled by outside forces [autonomous, independent, self-governing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> greatest in status or authority or power [supreme]</p><p><b>iznimka koja sprečava podnošenje tužbe protiv suverene vlade bez odobrenja vlade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an exemption that precludes bringing a suit against the sovereign government without the government's consent</p><p><b>državnost, nezavisnost, samostalnost, suverenitet, suvereniteta, suverenost, suverenosti, vrhovna vlast</b></p><p><i>n.</i> government free from external control</p><p><i>n.</i> royal authority [reign]</p><p><i>n.</i> the authority of a state to govern another state</p><p><b>sovjet, sovjetski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elected governmental council in a communist country (especially one that is a member of the Union of S