e, vitke noge (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having long slender legs [spindle-legged]</p><p><b>u svakom kraju suze (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tapering at each end [cigar-shaped, fusiform]</p><p><b>drveće i grmovi i drvene loze obično s plodovima svijetle boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trees and shrubs and woody vines usually having bright-colored fruits [Celastraceae, family Celastraceae, staff-tree family]</p><p><b>sve grmlje ili drvene loze iz roda Euonymus s navidnim, obično crvenkastim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any shrubby trees or woody vines of the genus Euonymus having showy usually reddish berries [spindle tree, spindleberry tree]</p><p><b>sve grmlje ili drvene loze iz roda Euonymus s navidnim, obično crvenkastim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any shrubby trees or woody vines of the genus Euonymus having showy usually reddish berries [spindle tree, spindleberry]</p><p><b>mršav osoba s dugim mršavim nogama, duge tanke noge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin person with long thin legs [spindleshanks]</p><p><i>n.</i> long thin legs [spindleshanks]</p><p><b>mršav osoba s dugim mršavim nogama, duge tanke noge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin person with long thin legs [spindlelegs]</p><p><i>n.</i> long thin legs [spindlelegs]</p><p><b>tanak kao vreteno</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> long and lean [lank]</p><p><b>prskalica koja je izduvana s površine mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spray blown up from the surface of the sea [spoondrift]</p><p><b>bodlja, drveni ukras, greben, hrbat, kičma, kralješnica, kralježnica, leđa, trn</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the series of vertebrae forming the axis of the skeleton and protecting the spinal cord [back, backbone, rachis, spinal column, vertebral column]</p><p><i>n.</i> any sharply pointed projection [acantha, spur]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small sharp-pointed tip resembling a spike on a stem or leaf [pricker, prickle, spikelet, sticker, thorn]</p><p><i>n.</i> the part of a book's cover that encloses the inner side of the book's pages and that faces outward when the book is shelved [backbone]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sharp rigid animal process or appendage</p><p><b>od biljke s vrhom s kičmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a plant tipped with a spine</p><p><b>spinel</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hard glassy mineral consisting of an oxide of magnesium and aluminum</p><p><b>Spinel koji se koristi kao dragulj (obično tamno crvena) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spinel used as a gemstone (usually dark red) [ruby spinel]</p><p><b>beskičmen, koji nema kičme, kolebljiv, nesiguran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> weak in willpower, courage or vitality [gutless, namby-pamby, wishy-washy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking a backbone or spinal column [invertebrate]</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking spiny processes</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking thorns [thornless]</p><p><b>beskičmen, koji nema kičme, kolebljiv, nesiguran (od &quot;spineless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of lacking a strong character</p><p><b>mali i kompaktno izgrađen uspravni klavir, rani model klavijatura s samo jednom strunom po noti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small and compactly built upright piano</p><p><i>n.</i> early model harpsichord with only one string per note</p><p><b>kvaliteta pokrivanja trnima ili trnima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being covered with prickly thorns or spines [bristliness, prickliness, thorniness]</p><p><b>osoba koja radi na javnim odnosima i pokušava spriječiti negativnu publicitet tako što objavljuje pozitivno tumačenje riječi ili djela tvrtke ili političke stranke ili poznate osobe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a public relations person who tries to forestall negative publicity by publicizing a favorable interpretation of the words or actions of a company or political party or famous person [spin doctor]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se upotrebljava u proizvodnji tekstilnih vlakana, to znači da se upotrebljavaju samo tekstilni vlakni. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being suitable for spinning or the capability of being spun (used of textile fibers)</p><p><b>Sposobni ili podložni utjecaju pristranosti informacija, s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50% masenog udjela (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable or susceptible to being influenced by biased information</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being spun into fibres [spinnbar]</p><p><b>veliki i obično trokutasti jedro za glavu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large and usually triangular headsail</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50% masenog udjela (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being spun into fibres [spinnable]</p><p><b>kapaciteta viskozne tekućine (posebno sluzi vrata maternice) za povlačenje u nit ili pušenje u mjehur (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capacity of a viscous liquid (especially the cervical mucus) to be drawn out into a strand or blown up into a bubble</p><p><b>pauk, prelac, prelja, preljna bradavica, stroj za predenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who spins (who twists fibers into threads) [spinster, thread maker]</p><p><i>n.</i> board game equipment that consists of a dial and an arrow that is spun to determine the next move in the game</p><p><i>n.</i> fisherman's lure</p><p><b>Kopse koji štiti divlje životinje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a copse that shelters game</p><p><b>brzo obrtanje, predenje, rotiranje, vrti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> creating thread</p><p><b>S druge dimenzije, od pregaćenih vlakana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spinning machine that draws, twists, and winds yarn</p><p><b>Rani mašin za prebacivanje s više vrenjača (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an early spinning machine with multiple spindles</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom materijala ne većim od 50 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a textile machine for spinning yarn and thread</p><p><b>s masenim udubljenjem od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fishing rod designed for casting a spinning lure</p><p><b>zvrk, čigra</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a conical child's plaything tapering to a steel point on which it can be made to spin [teetotum, top, whirligig]</p><p><b>kolovrat, kovitlac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small domestic spinning machine with a single spindle that is driven by hand or foot</p><p><b>bilo koje od nekoliko urođenih poremećaja obilježenih degeneracijom malog mozga i kičmene moždine koje dovode do spasticiteta i ataksije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several congenital disorders marked by degeneration of the cerebellum and spinal cord resulting in spasticity and ataxia</p><p><b>s trbušama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having spines</p><p><b>trnovit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having spines [spiny]</p><p><i>adj.</i> shaped like a spine or thorn [acanthoid, acanthous]</p><p><b>Nizozemski filozof koji je prihvatio panteistički sustav (1632-1677) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch philosopher who espoused a pantheistic system (1632-1677) [Baruch de Spinoza, Benedict de Spinoza, de Spinoza]</p><p><b>neudana, prelja, usidjelica, babadevojka, babadjevojka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elderly unmarried woman [old maid]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who spins (who twists fibers into threads) [spinner, thread maker]</p><p><b>stanje da je starka (obično starija neudana žena) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being a spinster (usually an elderly unmarried woman)</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama smatra se podrodom Carduelis: siskins i New World goldfinches (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications considered a subgenus of Carduelis: siskins and New World goldfinches [genus Spinus]</p><p><b>mala pfinka sjevernoameričkih iglovitih šuma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small finch of North American coniferous forests [pine finch, pine siskin]</p><p><b>Američki pfinč čiji mužjak ima žuto perje na tijelu ljeti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American finch whose male has yellow body plumage in summer [New World goldfinch, goldfinch, yellowbird]</p><p><b>bodljikav, pun trnja, trnovit</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having spines [spinous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or covered with protective barbs or quills or spines or thorns or setae etc. [barbed, barbellate, briary, briery, bristled, bristly, burred, burry, prickly, setaceous, setose, thorny]</p><p><b>U ovom slučaju, u slučaju da je to primjenjuje se na životinje koje su u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. ovog Pravilnika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a burrowing monotreme mammal covered with spines and having a long snout and claws for hunting ants and termites [anteater, echidna]</p><p><i>n.</i> a burrowing monotreme mammal covered with spines and having a long snout and claws for hunting ants and termites [anteater, echidna]</p><p><b>kostelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small bottom-dwelling dogfishes</p><p><b>pustinjski gušter koji se hrani mravima, bilo koji od brojnih gušteraca s preklapanim rebrnim šiljatim ljuskama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> desert lizard that feeds on ants [Moloch horridus, mountain devil]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous lizards with overlapping ridged pointed scales</p><p><b>jastog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> warm-water lobsters without claws [crayfish, langouste, rock lobster]</p><p><i>n.</i> large edible marine crustacean having a spiny carapace but lacking the large pincers of true lobsters [crawfish, crayfish, langouste, rock lobster, sea crawfish]</p><p><b>s visokom udubljenom površinom od oko 30 mm ili više, ali ne više od 30 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> puffers having rigid or erectile spines</p><p><b>rijeka kornjača zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s bradavičnim ljuskom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> river turtle of western United States with a warty shell [Trionyx spiniferus]</p><p><b>nizak biljka koja stvara jastuke s ružastom do crvenokrasno-mažintom cvjetom i srednjim rebrima lišća koji ostaju kao trnje kada lišće umre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low cushion-forming plant with rose to crimson-magenta flowers and leaf midribs that persist as spines when the leaves die [Talinum spinescens]</p><p><b>s leđima prekrivenim bodljima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the back covered with spines</p><p><b>s čvrstom granicom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a spiny border</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ribama s trunskim perajima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to fish with spiny fins</p><p><b>tvrdoperka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a teleost fish with fins that are supported by sharp inflexible rays [acanthopterygian]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih crva koji parazitno žive u crijevima kralježnjaka s povlačivom proboscisom prekrivenom mnogim kukom ušiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various worms living parasitically in intestines of vertebrates having a retractile proboscis covered with many hooked spines [acanthocephalan]</p><p><b>s trnastima lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having spiny leaves [spiny-leaved]</p><p><b>s trnastima lištima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having spiny leaves [spiny-leafed]</p><p><b>s trunastom stabljkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a spiny stem</p><p><b>Zapadne Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of western North America [western pipistrel]</p><p><b>Dišalo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a breathing orifice</p><p><b>japanski grm koji liči na članove roda Spiraea, Svaka biljka od roda Spiraea, u obliku od poluploče ili od poluploče (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Japanese shrub that resembles members of the genus Spiraea [Astilbe japonica, spirea]</p><p><i>n.</i> any rosaceous plant of the genus Spiraea [spirea]</p><p><i>n.</i> a dicotyledonous genus of the family Rosaceae [genus Spiraea]</p><p><b>grm s obilnim malim bijelim cvjetovima na proljeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub having copious small white flowers in spring [Saint Peter's wreath, St. Peter's wreath, bridal-wreath, bridal wreath]</p><p><b>naglo rasti, spirala, spiralan, uvojit, zavojit, zavojnica, voluta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plane curve traced by a point circling about the center but at increasing distances from the center</p><p><i>n.</i> a curve that lies on the surface of a cylinder or cone and cuts the element at a constant angle [helix]</p><p><i>n.</i> a continuously accelerating change in the economy</p><p><i>n.</i> ornament consisting of a curve on a plane that winds around a center with an increasing distance from the center [volute]</p><p><i>n.</i> a structure consisting of something wound in a continuous series of loops [coil, helix, volute, whorl]</p><p><i>n.</i> flying downward in a helical path with a large radius</p><p><i>v.</i> to wind or move in a spiral course [coil, gyrate]</p><p><i>v.</i> form a spiral</p><p><i>v.</i> move in a spiral or zigzag course [corkscrew]</p><p><i>adj.</i> in the shape of a coil [coiling, helical, spiraling, turbinate, volute, voluted, whorled]</p><p><b>s masenim udubljenjem od oko 10 mm ili više, ali ne više od 10 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oblique bandage in which successive turns overlap preceding turns</p><p><b>galaksija koja ima spiralnu strukturu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a galaxy having a spiral structure [spiral nebula]</p><p><b>galaksija koja ima spiralnu strukturu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a galaxy having a spiral structure [spiral galaxy]</p><p><b>odvijač sa čekićem (da se oštrica okreće samo u jednom smjeru) i spiralom u ručici (da se oštrica okreće) s pritiskom prema dolje na ručicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a screwdriver with a ratchet (so the blade turns in only one direction) and a spiral in the handle (so the blade rotates) with downward pressure on the handle [ratchet screwdriver]</p><p><b>Izvor koji je ranjen kao spirala. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spring that is wound like a spiral</p><p><b>s površinom od oko 5 mm ili više, ali ne više od 10 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a shell that forms a spiral</p><p><b>naglo rasti, spirala, spiralan, uvojit, zavojit, zavojnica (od &quot;spiral&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in the shape of a coil [coiling, helical, spiral, turbinate, volute, voluted, whorled]</p><p><b>spiralno, spiralan</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with spirals</p><p><b>spirant, strujnički</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a continuant consonant produced by breath moving against a narrowing of the vocal tract [fricative, fricative c