d &quot;squawk&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person given to excessive complaints and crying and whining [bellyacher, complainer, crybaby, grumbler, moaner, sniveller, whiner]</p><p><i>n.</i> the loudspeaker on an intercom or public address system [intercom speaker, squawk box]</p><p><b>Kao što je to kad kokoš škripa, posebno nakon što položi jaje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> like the cackles or squawks a hen makes especially after laying an egg [cackly]</p><p><b>Visoka biljka sa istočne strane Sjeverne Amerike i Azije koja ima plavo voće nalik bobici i debelog čvorovitog korijena koji se nekada koristio u medicini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall herb of eastern North America and Asia having blue berrylike fruit and a thick knotty rootstock formerly used medicinally [Caulophyllum thalictrioides, Caulophyllum thalictroides, blue cohosh, blueberry root, papoose root, papooseroot, squaw root]</p><p><b>cičanje, cičati, cika, izdati, kriještanje, pištanje, pištati, potkazivati, skvičanje, sretan slučaj, škripanje, škripati, cviljenje, škripa, zaškripati, zaškripiti, zaškripnuti, škripiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short high-pitched noise</p><p><i>n.</i> something achieved (or escaped) by a narrow margin [close call, close shave, narrow escape, squeaker]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a high-pitched, screeching noise [creak, screak, screech, skreak, whine]</p><p><b>Jedva da se snalaziš., pobjeći (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> manage one's existence barely [rub along, scrape along, scrape by, scratch along, squeeze by]</p><p><i>v.</i> escape [squeak through]</p><p><b>pobjeći (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> escape [squeak by]</p><p><b>cikavac, doušnik, izdajnik, mlada ptica, prokazivač, vrištavac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any artifact that makes a squeaking sound when used</p><p><i>n.</i> something achieved (or escaped) by a narrow margin [close call, close shave, narrow escape, squeak]</p><p><b>cičanje, cičati, cika, izdati, kriještanje, pištanje, pištati, potkazivati, skvičanje, sretan slučaj, škripanje, škripati (od &quot;squeak&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or making a high-pitched sound such as that made by a mouse or a rusty hinge [screaky, screechy, squeaky, squealing]</p><p><b>s visokom tonom ili visokim tonom kao što je onaj koji proizvodi miš ili hrđavi šarž (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or making a high-pitched sound such as that made by a mouse or a rusty hinge [screaky, screechy, squeaking, squealing]</p><p><b>cika, kmečati, piska, potkazivač, skvičanje, skvičati, priznati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a high-pitched howl</p><p><i>v.</i> utter a high-pitched cry, characteristic of pigs [oink]</p><p><i>v.</i> confess to a punishable or reprehensible deed, usually under pressure [confess, fink]</p><p><b>dostavljač, Sus scrofa, domaća svinja, gica, krmak, pajcek, prase, svinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who reveals confidential information in return for money [betrayer, blabber, informer, rat]</p><p><i>n.</i> domestic swine [Sus scrofa, grunter, hog, pig]</p><p><b>cika, kmečati, piska, potkazivač, skvičanje, skvičati (od &quot;squeal&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or making a high-pitched sound such as that made by a mouse or a rusty hinge [screaky, screechy, squeaking, squeaky]</p><p><b>cijeđenje, gadljiv, gužva, istiskivanje, izbirljivo, osjetljiv, otisak novca, razdražljiv, stezanje, stisak, težak položaj, ucjena</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> excessively fastidious and easily disgusted [dainty, nice, overnice, prissy]</p><p><b>gadljivo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a squeamish manner</p><p><b>izbirljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mild state of nausea [qualm, queasiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being excessively fastidious and easily shocked</p><p><b>Sastav za čistila u obliku slova T s gumenom ivicom preko vrha, brišite s perilicom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> T-shaped cleaning implement with a rubber edge across the top</p><p><i>v.</i> wipe with a squeegee</p><p><b>svojstvo da može zauzeti manje prostora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being able to occupy less space [compressibility, sponginess]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being easily compressed [compressible]</p><p><b>gnječiti, gužva, iscijediti, istisnuti, pritisnuti, stisak, stiskanje, stiskati, stisnuti, suženje, utisnuti, zgnječiti, zagrljaj, zbiti, forsirati, iznuditi, iznuđivati, nametati, nametnuti, natjerati, natjeravati, primorati, primoravati, prinuditi, prisiliti, prisiljavati, pritiskati, siliti, tjerati, mučiti, podvaliti, zavrtanje, prikliještiti, uštinuti, uštipnuti, štipati, štipkati, komprimirati, prešati, sabiti, skupiti, skupljati, stegnuti, stezati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of gripping and pressing firmly [squeezing]</p><p><i>n.</i> a state in which there is a short supply of cash to lend to businesses and consumers and interest rates are high [credit crunch, liquidity crisis]</p><p><i>n.</i> a situation in which increased costs cannot be passed on to the customer</p><p><i>n.</i> (slang) a person's girlfriend or boyfriend</p><p><i>n.</i> a twisting squeeze [wring]</p><p><i>n.</i> an aggressive attempt to compel acquiescence by the concentration or manipulation of power [power play, squeeze play]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tight or amorous embrace [clinch, hug]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of forcing yourself (or being forced) into or through a restricted space</p><p><i>v.</i> to compress with violence, out of natural shape or condition [crush, mash, squash, squelch]</p><p><i>v.</i> press firmly</p><p><i>v.</i> squeeze like a wedge into a tight space [force, wedge]</p><p><i>v.</i> to cause to do through pressure or necessity, by physical, moral or intellectual means [coerce, force, hale, pressure]</p><p><i>v.</i> obtain by coercion or intimidation [extort, gouge, rack, wring]</p><p><i>v.</i> press or force [shove, stuff, thrust]</p><p><i>v.</i> squeeze tightly between the fingers [nip, pinch, tweet, twinge, twitch]</p><p><i>v.</i> hold (someone) tightly in your arms, usually with fondness [bosom, embrace, hug]</p><p><i>v.</i> squeeze or press together [compact, compress, constrict, contract, press]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a portable box-shaped free-reed instrument [accordion]</p><p><b>Jedva da se snalaziš. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> manage one's existence barely [rub along, scrape along, scrape by, scratch along, squeak by]</p><p><b>da nekoga stisnete za novac, informacije itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> squeeze someone for money, information, etc.</p><p><b>istisnuti, ištrcati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> force out</p><p><i>v.</i> make by laborious and precarious means [eke out]</p><p><i>v.</i> extract (liquid) by squeezing or pressing [wring out]</p><p><i>v.</i> obtain with difficulty [eke out]</p><p><i>v.</i> form or shape by forcing through an opening [extrude]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to come out in a squirt [eject, force out, squirt]</p><p><b>agresivni pokušaj prisiljavanja na pristanak koncentracijom ili manipulacijom moći, igra u kojoj trkač na trećoj bazi pokušava postići gol dok udarač udara na teren (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an aggressive attempt to compel acquiescence by the concentration or manipulation of power [power play, squeeze]</p><p><i>n.</i> a baseball play in which a runner on third base tries to score as the batter bunts the pitch</p><p><b>preša</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kitchen utensil for squeezing juice from fruit</p><p><b>gnječenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of gripping and pressing firmly [squeeze]</p><p><b>blato, gacati, porazan, ušutkati, zvuk, gnječiti, zbiti, zgnječiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crushing remark [put-down, squelcher, takedown]</p><p><i>n.</i> an electric circuit that cuts off a receiver when the signal becomes weaker than the noise [squelch circuit, squelcher]</p><p><i>v.</i> suppress or crush completely [quell, quench]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a sucking sound</p><p><i>v.</i> walk through mud or mire [slop, slosh, splash, splosh, squish]</p><p><i>v.</i> to compress with violence, out of natural shape or condition [crush, mash, squash, squeeze]</p><p><b>električni krug koji isključuje prijemnik kada signal postane slabiji od buke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electric circuit that cuts off a receiver when the signal becomes weaker than the noise [squelch, squelcher]</p><p><b>blato, gacati, porazan, ušutkati, zvuk (od &quot;squelch&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> subdued or overcome [quelled, quenched]</p><p><b>blato, gacati, porazan, ušutkati, zvuk (od &quot;squelch&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crushing remark [put-down, squelch, takedown]</p><p><i>n.</i> an electric circuit that cuts off a receiver when the signal becomes weaker than the noise [squelch, squelch circuit]</p><p><b>peckanje, praskavica, zajedljiva primjedba, žabica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> firework consisting of a tube filled with powder (as a broken firecracker) that burns with a fizzing noise</p><p><b>liganj, lignja, mrkač, muzgavac, kalamar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Italian cuisine) squid prepared as food [calamari, calamary]</p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed fast-moving ten-armed cephalopod mollusk having a long tapered body with triangular tail fins</p><p><b>nakićen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very drunk [besotted, blind drunk, blotto, cockeyed, crocked, fuddled, loaded, pie-eyed, pissed, pixilated, plastered, slopped, sloshed, smashed, soaked, soused, sozzled, stiff, tight, wet]</p><p><b>kratka krivulja, Nečitljiv škriljak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short twisting line [curlicue]</p><p><i>n.</i> an illegible scrawl</p><p><b>Valovito i okretno. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> wavy and twisting</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za proizvode koji sadrže:, s gustima šiljcima malih bijelih cvijeća i s lukom s ljekovitim svojstvima, biljka iz Starog svijeta iz roda Scilla s uskim bazalnim listovima i ružičastim ili plavim ili bijelim cvjetovima racemosa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bulb of the sea squill, which is sliced, dried, and used as an expectorant</p><p><i>n.</i> having dense spikes of small white flowers and yielding a bulb with medicinal properties [Urginea maritima, sea onion, sea squill]</p><p><i>n.</i> an Old World plant of the genus Scilla having narrow basal leaves and pink or blue or white racemose flowers [scilla]</p><p><b>vrsta škampa bogoslužnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of mantis shrimp [mantis prawn]</p><p><b>rakovi koji se kopu u blatu ili ispod kamenja u plitkoj vodi duž obale mora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crustaceans that burrow in mud or under stones in shallow water along the seashore [family Squillidae]</p><p><b>ustuknuti, škiljiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small arch built across the interior angle of two walls (usually to support a spire)</p><p><i>v.</i> crouch down</p><p><i>v.</i> draw back, as with fear or pain [cringe, flinch, funk, quail, recoil, shrink, wince]</p><p><i>v.</i> cross one's eyes as if in strabismus [squint]</p><p><b>ustuknuti (od &quot;squinch&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having eyes half closed in order to see better [squinting]</p><p><b>razrok, razroko gledati, škiljav, škiljenje, škiljiti, zrikavost, žmirkanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal alignment of one or both eyes [strabismus]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of squinting</p><p><i>v.</i> cross one's eyes as if in strabismus [squinch]</p><p><i>v.</i> be cross-eyed</p><p><i>v.</i> partly close one's eyes, as when hit by direct blinding light</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used especially of glances) directed to one side with or as if with doubt or suspicion or envy [askance, askant, asquint, sidelong, squint-eyed, squinty]</p><p><b>osoba s strabismom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person with strabismus [squinter]</p><p><b>razrok, sumnjiv, zločinački, zlokoban, zrikav</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> affected by strabismus</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used especially of glances) directed to one side with or as if with doubt or suspicion or envy [askance, askant, asquint, sidelong, squint, squinty]</p><p><b>razrok, razroko gledati, škiljav, škiljenje, škiljiti, zrikavost, žmirkanje (od &quot;squint&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person with strabismus [squint-eye]</p><p><b>razrok, razroko gledati, škiljav, škiljenje, škiljiti, zrikavost, žmirkanje (od &quot;squint&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having eyes half closed in order to see better [squinched]</p><p><b>karakterizira se skretanjem očiju, (posebno za poglede) usmjereni na jednu stranu s sumnjom ili sumnjom ili zavidom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by squinting</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used especially of glances) directed to one side with or as if with doubt or suspicion or envy [askance, askant, asquint, sidelong, squint, squint-eyed]</p><p><b>gospodin, kavalir, mirovni sudac, plemić, posjednik, pratiti, štitonoša, vitezov pratitelj, vlastelin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> young nobleman attendant on a knight</p><p><i>n.</i> an English country landowner</p><p><i>n.</i> a man who attends or escorts a woman [gallant]</p><p><i>v.</i> attend upon as a squire</p><p><b>plemstvo koje posjeduje zemlju (smatra se klasom) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the gentry who own land (considered as a class) [landed gentry]</p><p><b>grčiti se, izvijati se, meškoljenje, migoljiti, previjati se, vrpoljiti se, frkati, iskobeljati se, iskoprcati se, izmigoljiti se, izviti se, izvlačiti se, izvući se, kobeljati se, koprcati se, migoljiti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of wiggling [wiggle, wriggle]</p><p><i>v.</i> to move in a twisting or contorted motion, (especially when struggling) [twist, worm, wrestle, wriggle, writhe]</p><p><b>grčiti se, izvijati se, meškoljenje, migoljiti, previjati se, vrpoljiti se (od &quot;squirm&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who can't stay still (especially a child) [wiggler, wriggler]</p><p><b>vjeverica, vjeveričje krzno, vrsta zapadnoindijske crvene ribe, veverica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of arboreal rodent having a long bushy tail</p><p><i>n.</i> the fur of a squirrel</p><p><b>čuvati za buduću upotrebu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> save up as for future use [cache, hive up, hoard, lay away, stash]</p><p><b>kavez s cilindričnim okvirom koji se okreće dok mala životinja trči unutar njega (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cage with a cylindrical framework that rotates as a small animal runs inside it</p><p><b>Američka biljka s kremastim cvijećem i gomoljastim korijenima koji liče na kukuruzna zrna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American plant with cream-colored flowers and tuberous roots resembling kernels of corn [Dicentra canadensis]</p><p><b>mali dugorepasti majmun iz Srednje i Južne Amerike sa zelenkastim krznom i crnim nosom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small long-tailed monkey of Central American and South America with greenish fur and black muzzle [Saimiri sciureus]</p><p><b>Plumeni paprika tropske Azije i Malezije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feathery fern of tropical Asia and Malaysia [Davalia bullata, Davalia bullata mariesii, Davallia Mariesii, ball fern]</p><p><b>s površinom od oko 10 mm ili više, ali ne više od 10 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having the approximate size of a squirrel</p><p><b>sličan morskoj brezi, U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za ribolov na tropskim grebenima i na plitkim vodama u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka, ribolov na tropskim grebenima može se provesti na temelju pravila o ribolovu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to sea bream [Lagodon rhomboides, pinfish, sailor's-choice]</p><p><i>n.</i> very small, brightly colored (especially red) nocturnal fishes of shallow waters or tropical reefs</p><p><b>ječam uzgojen zbog svojih visoko ukrasnih cvjetnih glavaca sa delikatnim dugim svilovitim panama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> barley grown for its highly ornamental flower heads with delicate long silky awns [Hordeum jubatum, foxtail barley, squirreltail grass]</p><p><b>ječam uzgojen zbog svojih visoko ukrasnih cvjetnih glavaca sa delikatnim dugim svilovitim panama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> barley grown for its highly ornamental flower heads with delicate long silky awns [Hord