ati kao dominikanci ili crni redovnici (oko 1170.-1221.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) Spanish priest who founded an order whose members became known as Dominicans or Black Friars (circa 1170-1221) [Domingo de Guzman, Dominic, Saint Dominic]</p><p><b>Sin Ethelred Nepripremljeni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> son of Ethelred the Unready [Edward the Confessor, Saint Edward the Confessor]</p><p><b>Kralj Engleske koji je bio sin Edgara. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> King of England who was a son of Edgar [Edward the Martyr, Saint Edward the Martyr]</p><p><b>planinski niz između Aljaske i teritorija Yukona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a range of mountains between Alaska and the Yukon territory [St. Elias Range]</p><p><b>planinski niz između Aljaske i teritorija Yukona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a range of mountains between Alaska and the Yukon territory [St. Elias Mountains]</p><p><b>električni pražnjenje uz ionizaciju okolne atmosfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electrical discharge accompanied by ionization of surrounding atmosphere [Saint Elmo's fire, Saint Elmo's light, Saint Ulmo's fire, Saint Ulmo's light, corona, corona discharge, corposant, electric glow]</p><p><b>otok na Nizozemskoj Antili (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an island in the Netherlands Antilles [Saint Eustatius]</p><p><b>(Rimska katolička crkva) talijanski i rimokatolički redovnik koji je osnovao red franjevaca (1181-1226), pritok rijeke Mississippi koja izlazi u Missouriju i teče jugoistočno kroz Arkansas (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Roman Catholic Church) an Italian and the Roman Catholic monk who founded the Franciscan order of friars (1181-1226) [Francis of Assisi, Giovanni di Bernardone, Saint Francis, Saint Francis of Assisi, St. Francis of Assisi]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Mississippi River that rises in Missouri and flows southeastward through Arkansas [Saint Francis, Saint Francis River, St. Francis River]</p><p><b>(Rimska katolička crkva) talijanski i rimokatolički redovnik koji je osnov