]</p><p><b>rana, raniti, ubod, ubosti, udarac, zabijati, zabiti, zaklati, pokušaj, bosti, probadati, probosti, ubadati, bockati, bocnuti, nabadati, nabosti, pikati, piknuti, podbadati, podbosti, rinuti, upiknuti, zabadati, zabosti, zarinuti, zariti, zarivati, čeprkati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden sharp feeling [pang, twinge]</p><p><i>n.</i> a strong blow with a knife or other sharp pointed instrument [knife thrust, thrust]</p><p><i>n.</i> informal words for any attempt or effort [shot]</p><p><i>v.</i> use a knife on [knife]</p><p><i>v.</i> stab or pierce [jab]</p><p><i>v.</i> poke or thrust abruptly [dig, jab, poke, prod]</p><p><b>netko tko ubode drugu osobu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who stabs another person</p><p><b>uzrokovanje tjelesne ili osobito psihološke povrede, bolno kao da ga je uzrokovao oštar alat (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing physical or especially psychological injury [wounding]</p><p><i>adj.</i> painful as if caused by a sharp instrument [cutting, keen, knifelike, lancinate, lancinating, piercing]</p><p><b>Slika s fiksnim jedinicama (obično iz ploče) i pričvršćena na fiksnu podlogu, (hemija, fizika, biologija) otporan na promjene, ne može se premjestiti ili nije namijenjen za premještanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sculpture having fixed units (usually constructed of sheet metal) and attached to a fixed support</p><p><i>adj.</i> (chemistry, physics, biology) resistant to change</p><p><i>adj.</i> not able or intended to be moved [immovable, immoveable, unmovable]</p><p><b>stabilizacija, stabilizacije, Sporazum o stabilizaciji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making something (as a vessel or aircraft) less likely to overturn [stabilization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of stabilizing something or making it more stable [stabilization]</p><p><b>stabiliziramo, stabilizirati, stabilizirati se, uravnotežiti se, uravnoteživati se, ustaliti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> support or hold steady and make steadfast, with or as if with a brace [brace, stabilize, steady]</p><p><i>v.</i> become stable or more stable [stabilize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make stable and keep from fluctuating or put into an equilibrium [stabilize]</p><p><b>stabiliziralo</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made stable or firm [stabilized]</p><p><b>stabiliziramo, stabilizirati (od &quot;stabilise&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device for making something stable [stabilizer]</p><p><b>stabiliziramo, stabilizirati (od &quot;stabilise&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing to become stable [stabilizing]</p><p><b>nepromjenjivost, postojanost, stabilitet, stabilnost, stabilnosti, pouzdanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality or attribute of being firm and steadfast [stableness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a stable order (especially of society)</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being enduring and free from change or variation [constancy]</p><p><b>stabilizacija, učvršćenje, ustaljenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of stabilizing something or making it more stable [stabilisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of making something (as a vessel or aircraft) less likely to overturn [stabilisation]</p><p><b>stabilizirati, uravnotežiti, ustaliti, stabilizirati se, uravnotežiti se, uravnoteživati se, ustaliti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make stable and keep from fluctuating or put into an equilibrium [stabilise]</p><p><i>v.</i> support or hold steady and make steadfast, with or as if with a brace [brace, stabilise, steady]</p><p><i>v.</i> become stable or more stable [stabilise]</p><p><b>stabilno ili čvrsto (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> made stable or firm [stabilised]</p><p><b>stabilizator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chemical that is added to a solution or mixture or suspension to maintain it in a stable or unchanging state</p><p><i>n.</i> airfoil consisting of a device for stabilizing an aircraft</p><p><i>n.</i> a device for making something stable [stabiliser]</p><p><b>čvrsta metalna šipka između prednjih i stražnjih ovjesnih ostavljača automobila i kamiona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rigid metal bar between the front suspensions and between the rear suspensions of cars and trucks [anti-sway bar]</p><p><b>stabilizirati, uravnotežiti, ustaliti (od &quot;stabilize&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing to become stable [stabilising]</p><p><b>čvrst, konjušnica, postojan, stabilan, stabilne, staja, stalan, štala, trajan, ustaljen, ustaljenim</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a farm building for housing horses or other livestock [horse barn, stalls]</p><p><i>v.</i> shelter in a stable</p><p><i>adj.</i> resistant to change of position or condition</p><p><i>adj.</i> firm and dependable</p><p><i>adj.</i> not taking part readily in chemical change</p><p><i>adj.</i> maintaining equilibrium</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing little if any change [static, unchanging]</p><p><b>Konj u staji s drugim konjem ili jednim od nekoliko konja u vlasništvu iste osobe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a horse stabled with another or one of several horses owned by the same person [stablemate]</p><p><b>Koagulacijski faktor koji se formira u bubrezima pod utjecajem vitamina K. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coagulation factor formed in the kidney under the influence of vitamin K [cothromboplastin, factor VII, proconvertin]</p><p><b>jahaća oprema, konjska oprema, oprema za konja, sedlarska roba, sedlarske potrepštine</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gear for a horse [saddlery, tack]</p><p><b>netko zaposlen u stajalištu da se brine o konjima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed in a stable to take care of the horses [groom, hostler, ostler, stableman]</p><p><b>netko zaposlen u stajalištu da se brine o konjima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed in a stable to take care of the horses [groom, hostler, ostler, stableboy]</p><p><b>Konj u staji s drugim konjem ili jednim od nekoliko konja u vlasništvu iste osobe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a horse stabled with another or one of several horses owned by the same person [stable companion]</p><p><b>postojanost, pouzdanost, stabilnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality or attribute of being firm and steadfast [stability]</p