fficulty [flounder]</p><p><i>v.</i> to arrange in a systematic order [distribute]</p><p><i>v.</i> astound or overwhelm, as with shock</p><p><b>ljeplovita grmlja od obalne ravnice istočne Sjedinjenih Država s ružičasta bijela cvjetovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrub of coastal plain of the eastern United States having nodding pinkish-white flowers [Lyonia mariana, staggerbush]</p><p><b>naslov s gornjim redom lijevo i slijedećim redovima uvučenim desno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a headline with the top line flush left and succeeding lines indented to the right [drop line, dropline, staggered head, stephead, stepped line]</p><p><b>ljeplovita grmlja od obalne ravnice istočne Sjedinjenih Država s ružičasta bijela cvjetovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrub of coastal plain of the eastern United States having nodding pinkish-white flowers [Lyonia mariana, stagger bush]</p><p><b>Upravni odbor čiji se dio članova bira svake godine umjesto da svi članovi budu birali svake godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a board of directors a portion of whose members are elected each year instead of all members being elected annually</p><p><b>naslov s gornjim redom lijevo i slijedećim redovima uvučenim desno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a headline with the top line flush left and succeeding lines indented to the right [drop line, dropline, stagger head, stephead, stepped line]</p><p><b>cikcak, poljuljati, posrtanje, posrtati, uzdrmati, zapanjiti (od &quot;stagger&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who walks unsteadily as if about to fall [reeler, totterer]</p><p><b>klimav, kolebljiv, nepostojan, nestalan, od kojega se tetura, ošamućujući, teturav, zapanjujući, začuđujući</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> so surprisingly impressive as to stun or overwhelm [astonishing, astounding, stupefying]</p><p><b>klimavo, teturavo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> extremely [enormously, hugely, tremendously]</p><p><b>cikcak, poljuljati, posrtanje, posrtati, uzdrmati, zapanjiti (od &quot;stagger&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of the central nervous system affecting especially horses and cattle [blind staggers]</p><p><b>Neobičan rast malih grana na drvetu ili grmlju uzrokovan gljivicama ili insektima ili drugim fiziološkim poremećajima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal tufted growth of small branches on a tree or shrub caused by fungi or insects or other physiological disturbance [hexenbesen, witch broom, witches' broom]</p><p><b>Veliki koral s granama koji liče na rogove. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large branching coral resembling antlers [stag's-horn coral]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih tropskih paprika rod Platycerium koji imaju velike ravne lobate lišće koje često liče na rogove jelena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various tropical ferns of the genus Platycerium having large flat lobed fronds often resembling the antlers of a stag</p><p><b>raznolikost klupskog mahova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of club moss [Lycopodium complanatum, ground cedar]</p><p><b>listovice ili istočna Sjeverna Amerika sa složenim lišćama koje postaju sjajno crvene na jesen i gusto panike zelenkasto žute cvijeće s crvenkastim kiselnim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrubby tree or eastern North America with compound leaves that turn brilliant red in fall and dense panicles of greenish yellow flowers followed by crimson acidic berries [Rhus typhina, Virginian sumac, velvet sumac, vinegar tree]</p><p><b>veliki teški pas koji se nekada koristio za lov na jelene i druge velike divlje životinje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large heavy hound formerly used in hunting stags and other large game</p><p><b>Na scenski i kazališni način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a stagy and theatrical manner [theatrically]</p><p><b>umjetna i umnožena kvaliteta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an artificial and mannered quality [theatricality]</p><p><b>režiranje, saobraćati, skele</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the production of a drama on the stage [theatrical production]</p><p><i>n.</i> a system of scaffolds [scaffolding]</p><p><i>n.</i> travel by stagecoach</p><p><i>n.</i> getting rid of a stage of a multistage rocket</p><p><b>područje gdje se prije vojne operacije okupljaju trupe i oprema u tranzitu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an area where troops and equipment in transit are assembled before a military operation</p><p><b>drevni grčki grad gdje je rođen Aristotel. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient town of Greece where Aristotle was born [Stagirus]</p><p><b>drevni grčki grad gdje je rođen Aristotel. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient town of Greece where Aristotle was born [Stagira]</p><p><b>mrtvilo, zastoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inactivity of liquids [stagnation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a state of inactivity (in business or art etc) [doldrums, stagnation]</p><p><b>mlitav, nepokretan, trom, ustajao</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not circulating or flowing [dead]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not growing or changing [moribund]</p><p><b>Anoksija koja je posljedica spore periferne cirkulacije (kao što je kongestivna srčana insuficijencija) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anoxia resulting from slow peripheral circulation (such as follows congestive cardiac failure) [ischemic anoxia]</p><p><b>hipoksija koja je posljedica spore periferne cirkulacije (kao što je kongestivna srčana insuficijencija) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hypoxia resulting from slow peripheral circulation (such as follows congestive cardiac failure) [ischemic hypoxia]</p><p><b>biti ustajao, ne otjecati, stagnirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> stand still</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to stagnate</p><p><i>v.</i> cease to flow</p><p><i>v.</i> be idle [idle, laze, slug]</p><p><b>mrtvilo, stagnacija, stagnacije, zastoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of inactivity (in business or art etc) [doldrums, stagnancy]</p><p><i>n.</i> inactivity of liquids [stagnancy]</p><p><b>koji imaju karakteristike pozornice, posebno umjetnu i obrađen kvalitet (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having characteristics of the stage especially an artificial and mannered quality [stagey]</p><p><b>razuman, smiren, staložen, trezven, uravnotežen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by dignity and propriety [sedate]</p><p><b>razuman, smiren, staložen, trezven, uravnotežen (od &quot;staid&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a grave and sober manner [gravely, soberly]</p><p><b>razuman, smiren, staložen, trezven, uravnotežen (od &quot;staid&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trait of dignified seriousness [sedateness, solemness, solemnity]</p><p><b>boja, ljaga, mrlja, obojenost, obojiti, osramotiti, ukaljati, zaprljati, umrljati, zamrljati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soiled or discolored appearance [discoloration, discolouration]</p><p><i>n.</i> (microscopy) a dye or other coloring material that is used in microscopy to make structures visible</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being covered with unclean things [dirt, filth, grease, grime, grunge, soil]</p><p><i>n.</i> a symbol of disgrace or infamy [brand, mark, stigma]</p><p><i>n.</i> an act that brings discredit to the person who does it [blot, smear, smirch, spot]</p><p><i>v.</i> color with a liquid dye or tint</p><p><i>v.</i> produce or leave stains</p><p><i>v.</i> make dirty or spotty, as by exposure to air [defile, maculate, sully, tarnish]</p><p><i>v.</i> color for microscopic study</p><p><b>(citologija) sposobnost stanica ili dijelova stanica da se obare određene boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (cytology) the capacity of cells or cell parts to stain specifically with certain dyes</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mas.% ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mas.% (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being stained (especially of cells and cell parts)</p><p><b>obojen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked or dyed or discolored with foreign matter</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a coating of stain or varnish [varnished]</p><p><b>staklo koje je bilo obojeno na neki način (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> glass that has been colored in some way</p><p><b>prozor od vitrajna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a window made of stained glass</p><p><b>boja, ljaga, mrlja, obojenost, obojiti, osramotiti, ukaljati, zaprljati (od &quot;stain&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a worker who stains (wood or fabric)</p><p><b>bojanje, bojenje, obojanost, obojenje, slikanje na staklu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (histology) the use of a dye to color specimens for microscopic study</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of spotting or staining something [maculation, spotting]</p><p><b>besprijekoran, čist, koji ne hrđa, nerđajućeg, nerđajući, neuprljan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> steel containing chromium that makes it resistant to corrosion [chromium steel, stainless steel]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of reputation) free from blemishes [unstained, unsullied, untainted, untarnished]</p><p><b>nehrđajući čelik, nerđajući čelik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> steel containing chromium that makes it resistant to corrosion [chromium steel, stainless]</p><p><b>stepenica, stepenice, stube, stuba</b></p><p><i>n.</i> support consisting of a place to rest the foot while ascending or descending a stairway [step]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strip of carpet for laying on stairs</p><p><b>šipka koja drži stepenište u kutu između dva stepena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rod that holds a stair-carpet in the angle between two steps</p><p><b>stepenice, stepenište, stubište, stube</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a way of access (upward and downward) consisting of a set of steps [stairway]</p><p><b>Platforma na vrhu stubišta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> platform at the top of a staircase</p><p><b>stepenicama, stepenice, stube, stubište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a flight of stairs or a flight of steps [steps]</p><p><b>stepenice, stube, stubište, stepenište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a way of access (upward and downward) consisting of a set of steps [staircase]</p><p><b>stubište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vertical well around which there is a stairway</p><p><b>kolac, obilježiti kolcima, poduprijeti kolcima, spaljivanje, staviti na kocku, stub, stup, učešće, udio, udjela, ulog, oznaka, oznaka kolčićima, lomača</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a right or legal share of something [interest]</p><p><i>n.</i> a pole or stake set up to mark something (as the start or end of a race track) [post]</p><p><i>n.</i> instrument of execution consisting of a vertical post that a victim is tied to for burning</p><p><i>n.</i> the money risked on a gamble [bet, stakes, wager]</p><p><i>n.</i> a strong wooden or metal post with a point at one end so it can be driven into the ground</p><p><i>v.</i> put at risk [adventure, hazard, jeopardize, venture]</p><p><i>v.</i> place a bet on [back, bet on, gage, game, punt]</p><p><i>v.</i> mark with a stake [post]</p><p><i>v.</i> tie or fasten to a stake</p><p><i>v.</i> kill by piercing with a spear or sharp pole [impale]</p><p><b>nekakav gorak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of bittern [American bittern, Botaurus lentiginosus]</p><p><b>Konjska utrka u kojoj dio nagrade daju vlasnici konja u utrci. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a horse race in which part of the prize is put up by the owners of the horses in the race</p><p><b>dionik, nositelj interesa, treća osoba kojoj je povjeren novac kod oklade, udioničar, udjelničar, vlasnik udjela, zainteresirana strana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone entrusted to hold the stakes for two or more persons betting against one another</p><p><b>nadzor nekog mjesta ili neke osobe od strane policije (kao što je očekivanje zločina) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surveillance of some place or some person by the police (as in anticipation of a crime)</p><p><b>ulog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the money risked on a gamble [bet, stake, wager]</p><p><b>stalaktit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cylinder of calcium carbonate hanging from the roof of a limestone cave</p><p><b>stalagmit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cylinder of calcium carbonate projecting upward from the floor of a limestone cave</p><p><b>banalan, bez ukusa, bljutav, izvjetrio, mokraća, neaktivan, otrcan, star, suh, ustajao, zagušljiv</b></p><p><i>v.</i> urinate, of cattle and horses</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking freshness, palatability, or showing deterioration from age</p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking originality or spontaneity [cold, dusty, moth-eaten]</p><p><b>bezizlazni položaj, ćorsokak, dovesti koga do pata, dovesti koga do zastoja, dovesti koga u bezizlazan položaj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a situation in which no progress can be made or no advancement is possible [dead end, deadlock, impasse, standstill]</p><p><i>n.</i> drawing position in chess: any of a player's possible moves would place his king in check</p><p><i>v.</i> subject to a stalemate</p><p><b>U potpunom zastoj zbog protivljenja dvije nemilosrdne sile ili frakcije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> at a complete standstill because of opposition of two unrelenting forces or factions [deadlocked]</p><p><b>otrcanost, ozljeda, ozljede, pretreniranost, upala, upale, ustajalost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unoriginality as a result of being dull and hackneyed [triteness]</p><p><i>n.</i> having lost purity and freshness as a consequence of aging</p><p><b>Staljin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Russian leader who succeeded Lenin as head of the Communist Party and created a totalitarian state by purging all opposition (1879-1953) [Iosif Vissarionovich Dzhugashvili, Joseph Stalin]</p><p><b>Najviši planinski vrh u Pamirskim planinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the highest mountain peak in the Pamir Mountains [Communism Peak, Mount Communism, Mount Garmo]</p><p><b>Glavni grad Tadžikistana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital of Tajikistan [Dusanbe, Dushanbe, Dyushambe, capital of Tajikistan]</p><p><b>Grad u europskom dijelu Rusije na Volgi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in the European part of Russia on the Volga [Tsaritsyn, Volgograd]</p><p><b>socijalni proces usvajanja (ili prisiljavanja na usvajanje) politika i praksi Josipa Stalina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> social process of adopting (or being forced to adopt) the policies and practices of Joseph Stalin [Stalinization]</p><p><b>Transformirati u skladu sa Stalinovom politikom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> transform in accordance with Stalin's policies [stalinize]</p><p><b>autoritarizam, despotizam, diktatura, staljinizam, totalitarizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of government in which the ruler is an absolute dictator (not restricted by a constitution or laws or opposition etc.) [Caesarism, absolutism, authoritarianism, despotism, dictatorship, monocracy, one-man rule, shogunate, totalitarianism, tyranny]</p><p><b>Slijednik Staljina i stalinizma., o ili u vezi s Josifom Stalinom ili njegovim vremenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a follower of Stalin and Stalinism</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to Joseph Stalin or his times</p><p><b>socijalni proces usvajanja (ili prisiljavanja na usvajanje) politika i praksi Josipa Stalina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> social process of adopting (or being forced to adopt) the policies and practices of Joseph Stalin [Stalinisation]</p><p><b>Transformirati u skladu sa Stalinovom politikom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> transform in accordance with Stalin's policies [stalinise]</p><p><b>Donjeck</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an industrial city in the Donets Basin [Donetsk, Donetske]</p><p><b>drška, klasja, prikradati se, stabljika, stabljike, stalak, struk, šuljati se, tvornički dim, vlat, ljuska, lupina, proganjati, progoniti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> material consisting of seed coverings and small pieces of stem or leaves that have been separated from the seeds [chaff, husk, shuck, straw, stubble]</p><p><i>n.</i> a slender or elongated structure that supports a plant or fungus or a plant part or plant organ [stem]</p><p><i>n.</i> a hunt for game carried on by following it stealthily or waiting in ambush [stalking, still hunt]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of following prey stealthily [stalking]</p><p><i>n.</i> a stiff or threatening gait [angry walk]</p><p><i>v.</i> walk stiffly</p><p><i>v.</i> follow stealthily or recur constantly and spontaneously to [haunt]</p><p><i>v.</i> go through (an area) in search of prey</p><p><b>drška, klasja, prikradati se, stabljika, stabljike, stalak, struk, šuljati se, tvornički dim, vlat (od &quot;stalk&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or growing on or from a peduncle or stalk [pedunculate]</p><p><b>gljiva iz roda Tulostoma koja liči na kuglu, vrsta Podaxaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mushroom of the genus Tulostoma that resembles a puffball</p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of Podaxaceae</p><p><b>lovac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who walks with long stiff strides</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who stalks game</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who prowls or sneaks about [prowler, sneak]</p><p><b>drška, klasja, prikradati se, stabljika, stabljike, stalak, struk, šuljati se, tvornički dim, vlat (od &quot;stalk&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hunt for game carried on by following it stealthily or waiting in ambush [stalk, still hunt]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of following prey stealthily [stalk]</p><p><b>Kandidat koji je izabran da podijeli opoziciju ili da prikrije pravog kandidata., Nešto što služi za skrivanje planova., ekran koji se sastoji od figure konja iza koje se lovac skriva dok proganja divlje životinje, konj iza kojeg se lovac skriva dok proganja divlje životinje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a candidate put forward to divide the Opposition or to mask the true candidate</p><p><i>n.</i> something serving to conceal plans [pretext]</p><p><i>n.</i> screen consisting of a figure of a horse behind which a hunter hides while stalking game</p><p><i>n.</i> a horse behind which a hunter hides while stalking game</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> attached directly by the base [sessile]</p><p><b>boks, kiosk, konjušnica, odjeljak u WC-u, odugovlačiti, pregrada, pregrada u staji, smicalica, šator, štala, uvijanje, zakazati, zatajiti, zaustaviti, kabina, pult, tezga, štand</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compartment in a stable where a single animal is confined and fed</p><p><i>n.</i> small area set off by walls for special use [booth, cubicle, kiosk]</p><p><i>n.</i> a booth where articles are displayed for sale [sales booth, stand]</p><p><i>n.</i