at is operated manually with a gear lever and a clutch pedal [stick shift]</p><p><b>barjaktar, zastavnik, nositelj, stjegonoša</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an outstanding leader of a political movement</p><p><i>n.</i> the soldier who carries the standard of the unit in military parades or in battle [color bearer]</p><p><b>normacija, normiranje, normizacija, standardiziranja, baždarenje, kalibracija, kalibriranje, standardizacija, standardiziranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition in which a standard has been successfully established [standardization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the imposition of standards or regulations [normalisation, normalization, standardization]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of checking or adjusting (by comparison with a standard) the accuracy of a measuring instrument [calibration, standardization]</p><p><b>normirati, standardizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> evaluate by comparing with a standard [standardize]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to conform to standard or norm [standardize]</p><p><b>U skladu s standardom, s masenim udjelom materijala od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> brought into conformity with a standard [standardized]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of replacing or changing places with something else [exchangeable, interchangeable, similar, standardized]</p><p><b>normirati, standardizirati (od &quot;standardise&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who sets a standard for things to conform to [standardizer]</p><p><b>normacija, normiranje, normizacija, Standardizacija, ujednačavanje, baždarenje, kalibracija, kalibriranje, standardiziranje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition in which a standard has been successfully established [standardisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the imposition of standards or regulations [normalisation, normalization, standardisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of checking or adjusting (by comparison with a standard) the accuracy of a measuring instrument [calibration, standardisation]</p><p><b>normirati, prilagoditi propisima, prilagođeno mjerilu, standardizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to conform to standard or norm [standardise]</p><p><i>v.</i> evaluate by comparing with a standard [standardise]</p><p><b>standardiziran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> brought into conformity with a standard [standardised]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of replacing or changing places with something else [exchangeable, interchangeable, similar, standardised]</p><p><b>normirati, prilagoditi propisima, prilagođeno mjerilu, standardizirati (od &quot;standardize&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who sets a standard for things to conform to [standardiser]</p><p><b>pasivno stanje, pomoćni, pričuvni, rezervni, zamjenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something that can be relied on when needed</p><p><i>n.</i> an actor able to replace a regular performer when required [understudy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> ready for emergency use</p><p><b>U slučaju da je osoba u stanju uzbune ili pripravnosti, ona se može vratiti u stanje uzbune ili pripravnosti., (vojna) privremeni prekid ofanzivne vojne akcije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a suspension and relaxation from an alert state or a state of readiness [stand-down]</p><p><i>n.</i> (military) a temporary stop of offensive military action [stand-down]</p><p><b>osoba koja stoji na mjestu gdje bi inače mogla sjediti (kao gledatelj koji koristi stojeći prostor u kazalištu ili putnik u gužvom autobusu ili vlaku), kartonski rez (obično slavne osobe) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who stands in a place where one might otherwise sit (as a spectator who uses standing room in a theater or a passenger on a crowded bus or train)</p><p><i>n.</i> a lifesize cardboard cutout (usually of a celebrity)</p><p><b>koji ostaje, onaj koji stoji, stajalac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organism (person or animal) that stands</p><p><b>položaj, poziv, regularan, stajanje, stalan, stalež, stanovište, stojeći, trajanje, uobičajen, uspravljen, ustaljen, zanimanje, renome, ugled</b></p><p><i>n.</i> social or financial or professional status or reputation</p><p><i>n.</i> an ordered listing of scores or results showing the relative positions of competitors (individuals or teams) in a sporting event</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of assuming or maintaining an erect upright position</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a supporting base</p><p><i>adj.</i> not created for a particular occasion</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of fluids) not moving or flowing</p><p><i>adj.</i> executed in or initiated from a standing position</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of persons) on the feet</p><p><i>adj.</i> permanent</p><p><b>Stalna vojska plaćenih vojnika. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a permanent army of paid soldiers</p><p><b>stalni odbor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a permanent committee</p><p><b>Provedba koja se redovito slijedi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a prescribed procedure to be followed routinely [SOP, standard operating procedure, standard procedure]</p><p><b>trajni nalog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rule of order permanently in force</p><p><b>ovacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enthusiastic recognition (especially one accompanied by loud applause) [ovation]</p><p><b>veliki štamparski aparat koji vrši pritisak vertikalno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large printing press that exerts pressure vertically</p><p><b>U slučaju da je proizvod proizveden od mesa (goveđe ili jelenje), u kojem je bilo više rebara, u kojem je meso smješteno uzduž vanjske strane rebara, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cut of meat (beef or venison) including more than one rib and the meat located along the outside of the ribs [rib roast]</p><p><b>prostor za stojanje putnika ili gledatelja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> room for passengers or spectators to stand</p><p><b>visoki uspravni megalith (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tall upright megalith [menhir]</p><p><b>stojni val</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wave (as a sound wave in a chamber or an electromagnetic wave in a transmission line) in which the ratio of its instantaneous amplitude at one point to that at any other point does not vary with time [stationary wave]</p><p><b>Engleski kolonist u Americi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English colonist in America [Miles Standish, Myles Standish]</p><p><b>izjednačenje, neodlučen ishod, remi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the finish of a contest in which the score is tied and the winner is undecided [draw, tie]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of repulsing or repelling an attack [repulsion]</p><p><b>Nedostatak srdačnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking cordiality [offish]</p><p><b>na odmaknut način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a standoffish manner</p><p><b>sklonost da bude udaljen i nesimpatičan na način (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to be distant and unsympathetic in manner [aloofness, remoteness, withdrawnness]</p><p><b>Staroumno i zastarelo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> old-fashioned and out of date [fusty, nonprogressive, unprogressive]</p><p><b>cijevni nastavak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vertical pipe</p><p><b>gledište, način mišljenja, stajalište, stanovište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mental position from which things are viewed [point of view, stand, viewpoint]</p><p><b>mirovanje, nerad, odmor, prekid, zaostatak, zastoj, zatišje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a situation in which no progress can be made or no advancement is possible [dead end, deadlock, impasse, stalemate]</p><p><i>n.</i> an interruption of normal activity [stand, tie-up]</p><p><b>komičar koji koristi šale. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a comedian who uses gags [gagman]</p><p><b>Izvršni direktor američke željeznice i osnivač Sveučilišta Stanford (1824-1893), Sveučilište u Kaliforniji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States railroad executive and founder of Stanford University (1824-1893) [Leland Stanford]</p><p><i>n.</i> a university in California [Stanford University]</p><p><b>Sveučilište u Kaliforniji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a university in California [Stanford]</p><p><b>Američki arhitekt (1853-1906) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States architect (1853-1906) [White]</p><p><b>revizija Binet-Simonove skale (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> revision of the Binet-Simon Scale</p><p><b>lak otvoreni konjski voz s dva i