73) [S. Smith Stevens, Smitty Stevens, Stevens]</p><p><b>automobil na parnu pogon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a steam-powered automobile</p><p><b>Knezovo perje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prince's plume [genus Stanleya]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s kožnim plavo-zeleno pinnatifidnim listovima i debelim plemenastim šiljcima žutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of southwestern United States having leathery blue-green pinnatifid leaves and thick plumelike spikes of yellow flowers [Cleome pinnata, desert plume, prince's-plume]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili sadržavaju cink (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or containing tin [stannous]</p><p><b>bezbožna kaustična tekućina proizvedena tretiranjem cimena s hlorom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless caustic liquid made by treating tin with chlorine</p><p><b>žuti pigment ponekad suspendiran u lakatu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a yellow pigment sometimes suspended in lacquer [mosaic gold]</p><p><b>tamno sivi mineral s metalnim sjajom koji je izvor cimena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dark grey mineral with a metallic luster that is a source of tin [tin pyrites]</p><p><b>koji sadržava kositar, kositren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or containing tin [stannic]</p><p><b>bijeli prah koji se koristi za fluoriranje zubepasta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white powder that is used to fluoridate toothpaste</p><p><b>Sufražistkinja i feministkinja Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States suffragist and feminist [Elizabeth Cady Stanton]</p><p><b>kitica, strofa, stanca, stih</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fixed number of lines of verse forming a unit of a poem</p><p><b>operacija uklanjanja štapova srednjeg uha (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical removal of the stapes of the middle ear</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka iz roda Stapelia koja ima sočne bezlistne stabljike s zubima nalik kaktusu i velike smrdljive (često zvijezdane) cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Stapelia having succulent leafless toothed stems resembling cacti and large foul-smelling (often star-shaped) flowers [carrion flower, starfish flower]</p><p><b>Stapelia Cape Province s uglavnom tamnocrvenokamenim cvijećem s ravnim zvijezdastom korolom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stapelia of Cape Province having mostly dark red-brown flowers with flat starlike corollas</p><p><b>stremen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the stirrup-shaped ossicle that transmits sound from the incus to the cochlea [stirrup]</p><p><b>sferične Gram-pozitivne parazitske bakterije koje imaju tendenciju formiranja nepravilnih kolonija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spherical Gram-positive parasitic bacteria that tend to form irregular colonies [staphylococci, staphylococcus]</p><p><b>porodica dvostrukožnih biljaka redom Sapindales uglavnom se nalazi u sjevernoj umjerenoj zoni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of dicotyledonous plants of order Sapindales found mostly in the north temperate zone [bladdernut family, family Staphylaceae]</p><p><b>rod malih stabala ili grmova iz obitelji Staphylaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of small trees or shrubs of the family Staphylaceae [genus Staphylea]</p><p><b>Bjelančevi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rove beetles [family Staphylinidae]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s bakterijama stafilokokusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the staphylococcus bacteria</p><p><b>raztopni egzotoksin koji nastaje od strane nekih sojeva stafilokokusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soluble exotoxin produced by some strains of staphylococcus</p><p><b>oblik enterotoksina od stafilokokova koji se koristi kao invalidan sredstvo u biološkom ratu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of staphylococcal enterotoxin that has been used as an incapacitating agent in biological warfare [SEB]</p><p><b>infekcija bakterijom stafilokokusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infection with staphylococcus bacteria</p><p><b>sferične Gram-pozitivne parazitske bakterije koje imaju tendenciju formiranja nepravilnih kolonija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spherical Gram-positive parasitic bacteria that tend to form irregular colonies [staph, staphylococcus]</p><p><b>sferične Gram-pozitivne parazitske bakterije koje imaju tendenciju formiranja nepravilnih kolonija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spherical Gram-positive parasitic bacteria that tend to form irregular colonies [staph, staphylococci]</p><p><b>glavna osobina, glavni proizvod, gvozdena spona, osnovna crta, pričvrstiti, skoba, spajalica, spojnica, stovarište, neobrađeni materijal, neprerađeni materijal, sirovina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (usually in the plural) a necessary commodity for which demand is constant [basic]</p><p><i>n.</i> a natural fiber (raw cotton, wool, hemp, flax) that can be twisted to form yarn [staple fiber, staple fibre]</p><p><i>n.</i> material suitable for manufacture or use or finishing [raw material]</p><p><i>n.</i> a short U-shaped wire nail for securing cables</p><p><i>n.</i> paper fastener consisting of a short length of U-shaped wire that can fasten papers together</p><p><i>v.</i> secure or fasten with a staple or staples</p><p><i>adj.</i> necessary or important, especially regarding food or commodities</p><p><b>od vlakana od čelika ili čelika, s masenim udjelom čelika od najmanje 0,05 mm, ali ne većim od 0,05 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a natural fiber (raw cotton, wool, hemp, flax) that can be twisted to form yarn [staple, staple fibre]</p><p><b>sortirano vlakno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a natural fiber (raw cotton, wool, hemp, flax) that can be twisted to form yarn [staple, staple fiber]</p><p><b>ručni stroj za vođenje spona kući (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hand-held machine for driving staples home [staplegun, tacker]</p><p><b>ručni stroj za vođenje spona kući (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hand-held machine for driving staples home [staple gun, tacker]</p><p><b>klamanje, klamerica, koji razvrstava pamuk, koji razvrstava vunu, naprava za spajanje, pamuk, spajalica, trgovac vunom na veliko, vunu, klamer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a machine that inserts staples into sheets of paper in order to fasten them together [stapling machine]</p><p><b>klamer, klamerica, spajalica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a machine that inserts staples into sheets of paper in order to fasten them together [stapler]</p><p><b>igrati glavnu ulogu, iteracija, sudbina, udes, usud, znamenitost, zvijezda, zvjezdan, zvjezdica, zvijezdu, zvezda, adept, genij, majstor, virtuoz, vunderkind</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) a celestial body of hot gases that radiates energy derived from thermonuclear reactions in the interior</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is dazzlingly skilled in any field [ace, adept, champion, genius, hotshot, maven, mavin, sensation, superstar, virtuoso, whiz, whizz, wiz, wizard]</p><p><i>n.</i> any celestial body visible (as a point of light) from the Earth at night</p><p><i>n.</i> an actor who plays a principal role [lead, principal]</p><p><i>n.</i> a plane figure with 5 or more points</p><p><i>n.</i> a performer who receives prominent billing [headliner]</p><p><i>n.</i> a star-shaped character * used in printing [asterisk]</p><p><i>n.</i> the topology of a network whose components are connected to a hub [star topology]</p><p><i>v.</i> feature as the star</p><p><i>v.</i> be the star in a performance</p><p><i>v.</i> mark with an asterisk [asterisk]</p><p><i>adj.</i> indicating the most important performer or role [leading, prima, starring, stellar]</p><p><b>zvjezdani anis, zvjezdasti anis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small tree of China and Vietnam bearing anise-scented star-shaped fruit used in food and medicinally as a carminative [Chinese anise, Illicium verum]</p><p><i>n.</i> small shrubby tree of Japan and Taiwan [Illicium anisatum]</p><p><i>n.</i> anise-scented star-shaped fruit or seed used in Asian cooking and medicine [Chinese anise, star aniseed]</p><p><b>zvjezdani anis, zvjezdasti anis</b></p><p><i>n.</i> anise-scented star-shaped fruit or seed used in Asian cooking and medicine [Chinese anise, star anise]</p><p><b>zeleno drvo iz Zapadne Indije i Srednje Amerike s jestivim ljubičastim plodovima u obliku zvijezde u poprečnom presjeku i tamnozelena lišća s zlatnim svilovitim donjim dijelovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen tree of West Indies and Central America having edible purple fruit star-shaped in cross section and dark green leaves with golden silky undersides [Chrysophyllum cainito, caimito]</p><p><b>Rizomatous begonia s lištima s šiljatim režnjevima koji podsjećaju na zvijezde i ružičaste cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rhizomatous begonia having leaves with pointed lobes suggestive of stars and pink flowers [Begonia heracleifolia, star-leaf begonia]</p><p><b>Bivši engleski sud koji je postao poznat po svojim proizvoljnim metodama i teškim kaznama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former English court that became notorious for its arbitrary methods and severe punishments</p><p><b>grafikon koji prikazuje relativne položaje zvijezda u određenom dijelu neba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chart showing the relative positions of the stars in a particular part of the sky</p><p><b>astrologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pseudoscience claiming divination by the positions of the planets and sun and moon [astrology]</p><p><b>čelična bušilica za stijene sa vrhom u obliku zvijezde koja se koristi za pravljenje rupa u kamenu ili zidarstvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a steel rock drill with a star-shaped point that is used for making holes in stones or masonry</p><p><b>Zemljina kugla glatke gornje površine koja je u početku zakopana u pijesak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an earthball with a smooth upper surface that is at first buried in sand [Scleroderma flavidium]</p><p><b>tropsko voće sa dubokim žutom-sjedom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deeply ridged yellow-brown tropical fruit [carambola]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko višegodišnjih biljaka iz roda Aletris s lištima nalik travi i gorkim korijenima za koje se smatra da liječe kolike, biljka iz roda Hypoxis s dugim lišćama poput trave i žutim cvjetovima u obliku zvijezde: Afrika, Trailing trave porijeklom iz Europe sada kosmopolitski u toplim regijama, višegodišnja australijska trava s brojnim dugim šiljcima raspoređenim poput vetrenog mlina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several perennials of the genus Aletris having grasslike leaves and bitter roots reputed to cure colic [colic root, colicroot, crow corn, unicorn root]</p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Hypoxis having long grasslike leaves and yellow star-shaped flowers: Africa</p><p><i>n.</i> trailing grass native to Europe now cosmopolitan in warm regions [Bahama grass, Bermuda grass, Cynodon dactylon, devil grass, doob, kweek, scutch grass]</p><p><i>n.</i> perennial Australian grass having numerous long spikes arranged like the vanes of a windmill [Chloris truncata, creeping windmill grass, windmill grass]</p><p><b>biljka s crvenim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual herb having scarlet flowers [Ipomoea coccinea, red morning-glory]</p><p><b>Zeleni kineski drveni planinari s sjajnim tamnozelenim lišćama i intenzivno mirisnim bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen Chinese woody climber with shiny dark green leaves and intensely fragrant white flowers [Trachelospermum jasminoides, confederate jasmine]</p><p><b>ljeplovita magnolija iz Japana koja ima mirisne bijele zvijezdane cvijeće koje cvjetaju prije nego se listovi razotknu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrubby magnolia from Japan having fragrant white starlike flowers blooming before leaves unfold [Magnolia stellata]</p><p><b>Šestokopta zvijezda formirana od dva jednakostrana trouglova. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a six-pointed star formed from two equilateral triangles [Magen David, Mogen David, Shield of David, Solomon's seal]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko južnoafričkih biljaka koje se uzgajaju zbog obilja obično žutih cvjetova nalik maramurici i gomila aromatičnog lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several South African plants grown for the profusion of usually yellow