ignal]</p><p><i>n.</i> the advantage gained by beginning early (as in a race) [head start]</p><p><i>v.</i> take the first step or steps in carrying out an action [begin, commence, get, get down, set about, set out, start out]</p><p><i>v.</i> set in motion, cause to start [begin, commence, lead off]</p><p><i>v.</i> leave [depart, part, set forth, set off, set out, start out, take off]</p><p><i>v.</i> have a beginning, in a temporal, spatial, or evaluative sense [begin]</p><p><i>v.</i> bring into being [initiate, originate]</p><p><i>v.</i> get off the ground [commence, embark on, start up]</p><p><i>v.</i> move or jump suddenly, as if in surprise or alarm [jump, startle]</p><p><i>v.</i> get going or set in motion [start up]</p><p><i>v.</i> begin or set in motion [get going, go]</p><p><i>v.</i> begin work or acting in a certain capacity, office or job [take up]</p><p><i>v.</i> play in the starting lineup</p><p><i>v.</i> have a beginning characterized in some specified way [begin]</p><p><i>v.</i> begin an event that is implied and limited by the nature or inherent function of the direct object [begin]</p><p><i>v.</i> bulge outward [bug out, bulge, bulge out, come out, pop, pop out, protrude]</p><p><b>početi raditi, započeti karijeru, krenuti, kretati, početi, počinjati, startati, stati, započeti, započinjati, začeti, začinjati, odlaziti, otići, otputovati, polaziti, poći, putovati, uputiti se, zaputiti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> take the first step or steps in carrying out an action [begin, commence, get, get down, set about, set out, start]</p><p><i>v.</i> leave [depart, part, set forth, set off, set out, start, take off]</p><p><b>početno pokretanje, pojaviti se, pokrenuti, pokrenuti računalo, pokretanje, krenuti, kretati, otpočeti, otpočinjati, pokretati, početi, počinjati, započeti, započinjati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> get going or set in motion [start]</p><p><i>v.</i> get off the ground [commence, embark on, start]</p><p><b>krenuti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a start given to contest