ext in manuscript form) on the basis of relations between the various surviving manuscripts (sometimes using cladistic analysis) [stemmatics]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više masenog udjela, ali ne više od 50% masenog udjela,, (biljaka) koje proizvode dobro razvijenu stabljku iznad zemlje, s uklanjanjem stabljika (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a stem or stems or having a stem as specified</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of plants) producing a well-developed stem above ground [caulescent, cauline]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the stem removed</p><p><b>radnik koji odvaja stabljike od vlažnih listova duhana i veže listove zajedno u knjige, radnik koji proizvodi ili nanosi stabljike za umjetne cvijeće, algoritam za uklanjanje skretnih i izvedenih završetaka kako bi se riječi smanjile na zajednički korijen, rudarski čep za udaranje u pakiranje preko eksplozivnog naboja, uređaj za uklanjanje stabljika od voća (kao što su grožđe ili jabuke) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a worker who strips the stems from moistened tobacco leaves and binds the leaves together into books [sprigger, stripper]</p><p><i>n.</i> a worker who makes or applies stems for artificial flowers</p><p><i>n.</i> an algorithm for removing inflectional and derivational endings in order to reduce word forms to a common stem [stemming algorithm]</p><p><i>n.</i> a miner's tamping bar for ramming packing in over a blasting charge</p><p><i>n.</i> a device for removing stems from fruit (as from grapes or apples)</p><p><b>algoritam za uklanjanje skretnih i izvedenih završetaka kako bi se riječi smanjile na zajednički korijen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an algorithm for removing inflectional and derivational endings in order to reduce word forms to a common stem [stemmer]</p><p><b>lagan britanski mitraljez. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lightweight British submachine gun</p><p><b>smrad, vonj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a distinctive odor that is offensively unpleasant [fetor, foetor, malodor, malodour, mephitis, reek, stink]</p><p><b>mala