azi se u atlantskim obalnim vodama Sjeverne Amerike od Južne Karoline do Mainea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found in Atlantic coastal waters of North America from South Carolina to Maine [northern porgy, northern scup, scup]</p><p><b>rod zapadnoameričkih niskih zimzelenih grmova koji rastu u gustim tuftovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of western North American low evergreen shrubs growing in dense tufts [genus Stenotus]</p><p><b>tamnozelena uspravna biljka sjeverozapadne Sjedinjenih Država i jugozapadne Kanade s čvrstima lišcima u gustim tuftovima i žutim cvjetnim glavama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dark green erect herb of northwestern United States and southwestern Canada having stiff leaves in dense tufts and yellow flower heads [Haplopappus acaulis, stemless golden weed]</p><p><b>stent</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slender tube inserted inside a tubular body part (as a blood vessel) to provide support during and after surgical anastomosis</p><p><b>govornik s neuobičajeno glasnim glasom, mitološki grčki ratnik s neuobičajeno glasnim glasom koji je umro nakon što je izgubio natjecanje u vikanju s Hermesom., bilo koji od nekoliko cilijatskih protozoja u obliku truba koje su članovi roda Stentor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a speaker with an unusually loud voice</p><p><i>n.</i> the mythical Greek warrior with an unusually loud voice who died after losing a shouting contest with Hermes</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several trumpet-shaped ciliate protozoans that are members of the genus Stentor</p><p><b>gromak, gromoglasan, prodoran, zvučan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of the voice or sound) deep and resonant [booming]</p><p><b>čin, koračati, koračni, korak, kročiti, mjera, papuča, postupak, prag, stepenica, zvanje, koraci, koraknuti, sredstvo, stopa, stuba, razred, stepen, stupanj, sekunda, plesni korak, gaziti, nagaziti, stupati, stupiti, zagaziti, zakoraknuti, zakoračiti, zakročiti, maltretirati, zlorabiti, zlostavljati, zloupotrijebiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any maneuver made as part of progress toward a goal [measure]</p><p><i>n.</i> the distance covered by a step [footstep, pace, stride]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of changing location by raising the foot and setting it down</p><p><i>n.</i> support consisting of a place to rest the foot while ascending or descending a stairway [stair]</p><p><i>n.</i> relative position in a graded series [gradation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a short distance [stone's throw]</p><p><i>n.</i> the sound of a step of someone walking [footfall, footstep]</p><p><i>n.</i> a musical interval of two semitones [tone, whole step, whole tone]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mark of a foot or shoe on a surface [footmark, footprint]</p><p><i>n.</i> a solid block joined to the beams in which the heel of a ship's mast or capstan is fixed</p><p><i>n.</i> a sequence of foot movements that make up a particular dance [dance step]</p><p><i>v.</i> shift or move by taking a step</p><p><i>v.</i> put down or press the foot, place the foot [tread]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause (a computer) to execute a single command</p><p><i>v.</i> treat badly [abuse, ill-treat, ill-use, maltreat, mistreat]</p><p><i>v.</i> furnish with steps</p><p><i>v.</i> move with one's feet in a specific manner</p><p><i>v.</i> walk a short distance to a specified place or in a specified manner</p><p><i>v.</i> place (a ship's mast) in its step</p><p><i>v.</i> measure (distances) by pacing [pace]</p><p><i>v.</i> move or proceed as if by steps into a new situation</p><p><b>konačni sustav, korak po korak, postupno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a gradual manner [bit by bit, gradually]</p><p><i>adv.</i> proceeding in steps [stepwise]</p><p><b>plesanje stepa, step, stepanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dancing in which the steps are more important than gestures or postures [hoofing]</p><p><b>sići, spustiti se, dati ostavku, dati otkaz, davati ostavku, davati otkaz, napustiti dužnost, napuštati dužnost, odlaziti, odstupati, odstupiti, otići</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give up or retire from a position [leave office, quit, resign]</p><