n.</i> the dead body of a human being [cadaver, clay, corpse, remains]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not moving or operating freely</p><p><i>adj.</i> powerful</p><p><i>adj.</i> rigidly formal [buckram, starchy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a strong physiological or chemical effect [potent, strong]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by firm determination or resolution [firm, steadfast, steady, unbendable, unfaltering, unshakable, unwavering]</p><p><i>adj.</i> incapable of or resistant to bending [rigid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> very drunk [besotted, blind drunk, blotto, cockeyed, crocked, fuddled, loaded, pie-eyed, pissed, pixilated, plastered, slopped, sloshed, smashed, soaked, soused, sozzled, squiffy, tight, wet]</p><p><i>adv.</i> extremely</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a stiff manner [stiffly]</p><p><b>žičasta višegodišnja biljka sa čvrstih, uspravnih, grubih stabljika, linearnih lišća i velikih ljubičastih cvijeća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wiry tufted perennial of the eastern United States with stiff erect rough stems, linear leaves and large violet flowers [Aster linarifolius]</p><p><b>Gentijan iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s grmovima čvrstih plavih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gentian of eastern North America having clusters of bristly blue flowers [Gentiana quinquefolia, Gentianella quinquefolia, ague weed, agueweed, five-flowered gentian]</p><p><b>samokontrola u izražavanju emocija (posebno strah ili tuga) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> self-restraint in the expression of emotion (especially fear or grief)</p><p><b>imaš ukočen leđa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a stiff back</p><p><b>s čvrstim granama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having stiff branches</p><p><b>ima tvrdu kosu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having stiff hair</p><p><b>tvrdoglav, uporan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> haughtily stubborn</p><p><b>ima čvrst rep (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a stiff tail</p><p><b>otvrdnuti, pojačati se, ukrutiti se, zgusnuti se, kočiti se, otvrdnjivati, skrutiti se, skrućivati se, stiskati se, stisnuti se, stvrdnjivati se, stvrdnuti se, ukočiti se, ukrućivati se, skrutiti, skrućivati, stiskati, stisnuti, stvrdnjivati, stvrdnuti, ukočiti, ukrutiti, ukrućivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become stiff or stiffer</p><p><i>v.</i> make stiff or stiffer</p><p><i>v.</i> severely restrict in scope or extent [constrain, tighten, tighten up]</p><p><b>armatura, element ukrućenja, krutilo, ojačanje, sredstvo za ukrućivanje, štirka, ukrepa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> material used for stiffening something</p><p><b>krućenje, nešto kruto, sredstvo za ukrućivanje, štirkanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of becoming stiff</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of becoming stiff or rigid [rigidification, rigidifying]</p><p><b>čovjek, gust, jak, krut, naporan, nesavitljiv, odlučan, sputan, strm, težak, tvrd, tvrdoglav, ukočen, uporan, usiljen, vezan, visok (od &quot;stiff&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a stiff manner [stiff]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a rigid manner [bolt, rigidly]</p><p><b>krutost, ukočenost, krutosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the physical property of being inflexible and hard to bend</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of moving with pain or difficulty</p><p><i>n.</i> firm resoluteness in purpose or opinion or action</p><p><i>n.</i> the inelegance of someone stiff and unrelaxed (as by embarrassment) [awkwardness, clumsiness, gracelessness]</p><p><i>n.</i> excessive sternness [hardness, harshness, inclemency, rigor, rigorousness, rigour, rigourousness, severeness, severity]</p><p><b>gubiti dah, obuzdati, prigušiti, ugasiti, ugušiti, zataškati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> joint between the femur and tibia in a quadruped [knee]</p><p><i>v.</i> suppress in order to conceal or hide [muffle, repress, smother, strangle]</p><p><i>v.</i> suppress or constrain so as to lessen in intensity [dampen]</p><p><i>v.</i> impair the respiration of or obstruct the air passage of [asphyxiate, choke, suffocate]</p><p><i>v.</i> be asphyxiated [asphyxiate, suffocate]</p><p><b>Složeno s poteškoćama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> held in check with difficulty [smothered, strangled, suppressed]</p><p><b>gubiti dah, obuzdati, prigušiti, ugasiti, ugušiti, zataškati (od &quot;stifle&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who stifles or smothers or suppresses [smotherer]</p><p><b>zagušljiv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> forceful prevention [crushing, quelling, suppression]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by oppressive heat and humidity [sulfurous, sulphurous, sultry]</p><p><b>ljaga, sramota, stigma, žig na uhu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the apical end of the style where deposited pollen enters the pistil</p><p><i>n.</i> a symbol of disgrace or infamy [brand, mark, stain]</p><p><i>n.</i> an external tracheal aperture in a terrestrial arthropod</p><p><i>n.</i> a skin lesion that is a diagnostic sign of some disease</p><p><b>stigma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> marks resembling the wounds on the crucified body of Christ</p><p><b>osoba čije tijelo je obilježeno religijskim stigmatama (kao što su oznake koje podsećaju na rane raspetog Krista), koji se odnose na ili sliče na ili imaju stigme, s masom od 300 mm ili većom, ali ne većom od 300 mm,, ne astigmatični (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person whose body is marked by religious stigmata (such as marks resembling the wounds of the crucified Christ) [stigmatist]</p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to or resembling or having stigmata</p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to a lens or lens system free of astigmatism (able to form point images) [anastigmatic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not astigmatic [anastigmatic]</p><p><b>Stigmatizacija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of stigmatizing [branding, stigmatization]</p><p><b>optužiti ili osuditi ili otvoreno ili formalno ili označiti kao sramotno, oznaka s stigmom ili stigmatama (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to accuse or condemn or openly or formally or brand as disgraceful [brand, denounce, mark, stigmatize]</p><p><i>v.</i> mark with a stigma or stigmata [stigmatize]</p><p><b>stanje imati ili biti označen stigmatima, (optika) stanje optičkog sustava (kao sočiva) u kojem svjetlosni zrake iz jedne točke 