reater or the full length [extend, stretch, unfold]</p><p><i>v.</i> lie down comfortably [stretch]</p><p><i>v.</i> thrust or extend out [exsert, extend, hold out, put out, stretch forth]</p><p><i>v.</i> extend one's body or limbs [stretch]</p><p><i>v.</i> stretch (the neck) so as to see better [crane]</p><p><b>od tkanine od pređe od 50 mm ili više, ali ne više od 50 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> trousers made of a stretchy fabric</p><p><b>receptor u mišiću koji reagira na istezanje mišićnog tkiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a receptor in a muscle that responds to stretching of the muscle tissue</p><p><b>Refleksna kontrakcija mišića kada se povuče vezana tetiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> reflex contraction of a muscle when an attached tendon is pulled [myotactic reflex]</p><p><b>sposobnost za istezanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capacity for being stretched [stretch, stretchiness]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being easily stretched and resuming former size or shape [stretchy]</p><p><b>odsjek, parcela, protezanje, protezati se, pružati se, rastegnuti se, rastezanje, rastezljiv, razapeti, prostiru, protežu (od &quot;stretch&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of muscles) relieved of stiffness by stretching</p><p><i>adj.</i> extended or spread over a wide area or distance</p><p><b>nosila</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wooden framework on which canvas is stretched and fixed for oil painting</p><p><i>n.</i> a mechanical device used to make something larger (as shoes or gloves) by stretching it</p><p><i>n.</i> a litter for transporting people who are ill or wounded or dead</p><p><i>n.</i> a stone that forms the top of wall or building [capstone, copestone, coping stone]</p><p><b>grupa ljudi s nosilacima za nošenje ozlijeđene osobe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a party of people with stretchers to carry an injured person</p><p><b>onaj koji pomaže nositi nosilec (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who helps carry a stretcher [litter-bearer]</p><p><b>sposobnost za istezanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capacity for being stretched [stretch, stretchability]</p><p><b>istezanje, prostire, proteže, statičko istezanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> act of expanding by lengthening or widening</p><p><i>n.</i> exercise designed to extend the limbs and muscles to their full extent [stretch]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being easily stretched and resuming former size or shape [stretchable]</p><p><b>Pjesma s vrhom od strusela, krhko obloženje za pecivo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pastry with a topping of streusel</p><p><i>n.</i> a crumbly topping for a pastry</p><p><b>posuti, rasuti, zasuti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> spread by scattering ("straw" is archaic) [straw]</p><p><i>v.</i> cover</p><p><b>posuti, rasuti, zasuti (od &quot;strew&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of scattering [scatter, scattering]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko malih paralelnih žlijezda kao što su: ogrebotine koje je glečer ostavio na stijenama ili pruge ili grebene u mišićnom tkivu, s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a number of tiny parallel grooves such as: the scratches left by a glacier on rocks or the streaks or ridges in muscle tissue [striation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a stripe or stripes of contrasting color [band, banding, striation]</p><p><b>prugast</b></p><p><i>v.</i> mark with striae or striations</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked with stria or striations</p><p><b>dio okcipitalnog kora koji prima vlakna optičkog zračenja iz bočnog genikularnog tijela i glavni je receptor vidnog područja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of the occipital cortex that receives the fibers of the optic radiation from the lateral geniculate body and is the primary receptive area for vision [Brodmann's area 17, area 17 of Brodmann, first visual area, striate cortex]</p><p><b>Pjesna masa bijele i sive tvari smještena ispred talamusa u svakoj moždanoj hemisferi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a striped mass of white and grey matter located in front of the thalamus in each cerebral hemisphere [corpus striatum, striatum]</p><p><b>dio okcipitalnog kora koji prima vlakna optičkog zračenja iz bočnog genikularnog tijela i glavni je receptor vidnog područja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the part of the occipital cortex that receives the fibers of the optic radiation from the lateral geniculate body and is the primary receptive area for vision [Brodmann's area 17, area 17 of Brodmann, first visual area, striate area]</p><p><b>Priloga bazalnoj veni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tributaries to the basal vein [inferior thalamostriate vein]</p><p><b>mišić koji je povezan na jednom ili oba kraja s kosom i tako pomakne dijelove kostura (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a muscle that is connected at either or both ends to a bone and so move parts of the skeleton [skeletal muscle]</p><p><b>izdužena kontraktilna stanica u prugavom mišićnom tkivu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elongated contractile cell in striated muscle tissue [striated muscle fiber]</p><p><b>izdužena kontraktilna stanica u prugavom mišićnom tkivu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an elongated contractile cell in striated muscle tissue [striated muscle cell]</p><p><b>mišićno tkivo koje karakteriziraju poprečne prugama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> muscle tissue characterized by transverse stripes</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko malih paralelnih žlijezda kao što su: ogrebotine koje je glečer ostavio na stijenama ili pruge ili grebene u mišićnom tkivu, s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a number of tiny parallel grooves such as: the scratches left by a glacier on rocks or the streaks or ridges in muscle tissue [stria]</p><p><i>n.</i> a stripe or stripes of contrasting color [band, banding, stria]</p><p><b>Pjesna masa bijele i sive tvari smještena ispred talamusa u svakoj moždanoj hemisferi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a striped mass of white and grey matter located in front of the thalamu