tanding a subject (especially by reading) [work]</p><p><i>n.</i> a written document describing the findings of some individual or group [report, written report]</p><p><i>n.</i> a state of deep mental absorption</p><p><i>n.</i> a room used for reading and writing and studying</p><p><i>n.</i> a branch of knowledge [bailiwick, discipline, field, field of study, subject, subject area, subject field]</p><p><i>n.</i> preliminary drawing for later elaboration [sketch]</p><p><i>n.</i> attentive consideration and meditation [cogitation]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who memorizes quickly and easily (as the lines for a part in a play)</p><p><i>n.</i> a composition intended to develop one aspect of the performer's technique</p><p><i>v.</i> consider in detail and subject to an analysis in order to discover essential features or meaning [analyse, analyze, canvass, examine]</p><p><i>v.</i> be a student</p><p><i>v.</i> give careful consideration to [consider]</p><p><i>v.</i> be a student of a certain subject [learn, read, take]</p><p><i>v.</i> learn by reading books [hit the books]</p><p><i>v.</i> think intently and at length, as for spiritual purposes [contemplate, meditate]</p><p><b>vrijeme tijekom školskog dana koje je izdvojeno za proučavanje, Učionica namijenjena za učenje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a period of time during the school day that is set aside for study</p><p><i>n.</i> a classroom reserved for study</p><p><b>studij, učeći</b></p><p><i>n.</i> reading carefully with intent to remember [perusal, perusing, poring over]</p><p><b>građa, ispuniti, kljukati, materijal, nadjenuti, natrpati, popuniti, predmet, puniti, roba, stvar, stvari, sukno, štof, tvar, začepiti, sirovina, ispunjavati, nadijevati, popunjavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tangible substance that goes into the makeup of a physical object [material]</p><p><i>n.</i> miscellaneous unspecified objects</p><p><i>n.</i> informal terms for personal possessions [clobber]</p><p><i>n.</i> senseless talk [hooey, poppycock, stuff