ratus intended for use under water</p><p><i>n.</i> a warship designed to operate under water [submersible warship]</p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being immersed in water or functioning while submerged [submergible]</p><p><b>podmornica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a warship designed to operate under water [submersible]</p><p><b>potapanje, uronjenje, zaronjivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sinking until covered completely with water [immersion, submergence, submerging]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of wetting something by submerging it [dousing, ducking, immersion]</p><p><b>davanje na uvid, podčinjenost, podnošenje, pokornost, prijavak, prijavka, prijava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something (manuscripts or architectural plans and models or estimates or works of art of all genres etc.) submitted for the judgment of others (as in a competition) [entry]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of submitting [compliance]</p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of having submitted to control by someone or something else</p><p><i>n.</i> the feeling of patient, submissive humbleness [meekness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a legal document summarizing an agreement between parties in a dispute to abide by the decision of an arbiter</p><p><i>n.</i> an agreement between parties in a dispute to abide by the decision of an arbiter</p><p><i>n.</i> (law) a contention presented by a lawyer to a judge or jury as part of the case he is arguing</p><p><b>krotak, odan, podložan, pokoran, ponizan, smjeran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inclined or willing to submit to orders or wishes of others or showing such inclination</p><p><i>adj.</i> abjectly submissive [slavish, subservient]</p><p><b>krotko, odano, pokorno, ponizno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a servile manner [deferentially]</p><p><b>pokornost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being willing to yield to the will of another person or a superior force etc.</p><p><b>dimenzionirati, dostaviti, izložiti, podčiniti, podjarmiti, podnijeti, podnositi, podvrgnuti, pokoriti, ponuda, predaju, predati se, predočiti, predati, pomiriti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> refer for judgment or consideration</p><p><i>v.</i> put before [posit, put forward, state]</p><p><i>v.</i> yield to the control of another</p><p><i>v.</i> hand over formally [present]</p><p><i>v.</i> refer to another person for decision or judgment [pass on, relegate]</p><p><i>v.</i> yield to another's wish or opinion [accede, bow, defer, give in]</p><p><i>v.</i> accept or undergo, often unwillingly [take]</p><p><i>v.</i> make an application as for a job or funding [put in]</p><p><i>v.</i> make over as a return [render]</p><p><i>v.</i> accept as inevitable [reconcile, resign]</p><p><b>podnositelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who yields to the will of another person or force</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who submits something (as an application for a job or a manuscript for publication etc.) for the judgment of others</p><p><b>vezivno tkivo ispod sluznice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the connective tissue beneath mucous membrane</p><p><b>osoba s nižom inteligencijom od normalne, ispod normalnog ili prosječnog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person of less than normal intelligence</p><p><i>adj.</i> below normal or average</p><p><b>stanje manje nego normalno (posebno u pogledu inteligencije), nedostatak normalnog razvoja intelektualnih sposobnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being less than normal (especially with respect to intelligence)</p><p><i>n.</i> lack of normal development of intellectual capacities [backwardness, mental retardation, retardation, slowness]</p><p><b>formiran ili smješten ili se javlja ispod oceana ili oceanskog dna (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> formed or situated or occurring beneath the ocean or the ocean bed [suboceanic]</p><p><b>formiran ili smješten ili se javlja ispod oceana ili oceanskog dna (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> formed or situated or occurring beneath the ocean or the ocean bed [subocean]</p><p><b>na podu oka ili ispod njega (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> situated on or below the floor of the eye socket [suborbital]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm,, na podu oka ili ispod njega (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having or involving a trajectory of less than one orbit</p><p><i>adj.</i> situated on or below the floor of the eye socket [subocular]</p><p><b>(biologija) taksonomska skupina koja je poddijeljenje reda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) taxonomic group that is a subdivision of an order</p><p><b>od kojih su mekani koralji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comprising the soft corals [Alcyonacea]</p><p><b>uši (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dragonflies [Anisoptera]</p><p><b>korišten u nekim posebno starijim klasifikacijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used in some especially older classifications [Anseres]</p><p><b>majmuni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monkeys [Anthropoidea]</p><p><b>ščurci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cockroaches [Blattaria, Blattodea, suborder Blattodea]</p><p><b>ščurci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cockroaches [Blattaria, Blattodea, suborder Blattaria]</p><p><b>kratkorepci, podred Brachyura, podred kratkorepaca, rakovi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an order of crustaceans (including true crabs) having a reduced abdomen folded against the ventral surface [Brachyura]</p><p><b>najveće mesožderske kopnene životinje ikad poznate (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> largest carnivorous land animals ever known [Carnosaura]</p><p><b>izumrla skupina oklopnih ribljaka-liknih kralježnjaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct group of armored fish-like vertebrates [Cephalaspida, Osteostraci, suborder Osteostraci]</p><p><b>dinosauri sa rogovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> horned dinosaurs [Ceratopsia]</p><p><b>primitivni dinosauri saurischian (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> primitive saurischian dinosaurs</p><p><b>Ptica: ptičica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shorebirds: plovers [Charadrii]</p><p><b>upotrebljava se u nekim sustavima klasifikacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> used in some classification systems [Clamatores]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjena skupina uključujući dinosaure s patkom i njihove rane rođake (hadrosau