, debauch, demoralise, demoralize, deprave, misdirect, pervert, profane, vitiate]</p><p><i>v.</i> destroy property or hinder normal operations [counteract, countermine, sabotage, undermine, weaken]</p><p><i>v.</i> destroy completely</p><p><b>revolucionar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radical supporter of political or social revolution [revolutionary, revolutionist, subversive]</p><p><b>artikuliraju bez stvaranja zvučnih zvukova (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> articulate without making audible sounds [subvocalize]</p><p><b>netko tko izražava govor bez izgovaranja zvukova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who articulates speech without uttering sounds [subvocalizer]</p><p><b>artikuliraju bez stvaranja zvučnih zvukova (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> articulate without making audible sounds [subvocalise]</p><p><b>netko tko izražava govor bez izgovaranja zvukova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who articulates speech without uttering sounds [subvocaliser]</p><p><b>podvožnjak, podzemna željeznica, podzemni hodnik, metro, pothodnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electric railway operating below the surface of the ground (usually in a city) [metro, subway system, tube, underground]</p><p><i>n.</i> an underground tunnel or passage enabling pedestrians to cross a road or railway [underpass]</p><p><b>cijena vožnje vlakom podzemne željeznice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fare charged for riding a subway train</p><p><b>terminal gdje podzemna željeznica utovari i istovari putnike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a terminal where subways load and unload passengers</p><p><b>metro, podzemna željeznica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electric railway operating below the surface of the ground (usually in a city) [metro, subway, tube, underground]</p><p><b>žeton</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a token that is used to pay for entry to the subway system</p><p><b>vlak koji ide u podzemnoj željeznici. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a train that runs in a subway system</p><p><b>zvučnik koji je dizajniran za reprodukciju vrlo niskih basnih frekvencija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loudspeaker that is designed to reproduce very low bass frequencies</p><p><b>Voće kuhano u šećernom sirupu i okrašeno šećernim kristalima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fruit cooked in sugar syrup and encrusted with a sugar crystals [candied fruit, crystallized fruit]</p><p><b>(medicinski lijek) nešto što se može koristiti kao zamjena (posebno bilo koji lijek koji se može uzimati umjesto drugog) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) something that can be used as a substitute (especially any medicine that may be taken in place of another)</p><p><b>dolaziti nakon, naslijediti, slijediti, sljedovati, uspeti, uspijevati, uspio, uspjeti, pobijediti, pobjeđivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> attain success or reach a desired goal [bring home the bacon, come through, deliver the goods, win]</p><p><i>v.</i> be the successor (of) [come after, follow]</p><p><b>dolaziti nakon, naslijediti, slijediti, sljedovati, uspeti, uspijevati, uspio, uspjeti (od &quot;succeed&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person with a record of successes [achiever, success, winner]</p><p><b>idući, naredni, sljedeći, sukcesivan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> coming after or following</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of elected officers) elected but not yet serving [future, next]</p><p><b>uspjeh, uspješnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that accomplishes its intended purpose</p><p><i>n.</i> an attainment that is successful</p><p><i>n.</i> a state of prosperity or fame</p><p><i>n.</i> a person with a record of successes [achiever, succeeder, winner]</p><p><b>uspio, uspješan, uspješne, uspješni, uspješnu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having succeeded or being marked by a favorable outcome</p><p><b>uspješno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with success</p><p><b>uspio, uspješan, uspješne, uspješni, uspješnu (od &quot;successful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of prospering [prosperity]</p><p><b>nasljeđivanje, uzastopnost, secesija, slijeđenje, sukcesija, neprekidni niz, slijed, niz, red, redoslijed, ekološka sukcesija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a following of one thing after another in time [chronological sequence, chronological succession, sequence, successiveness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a group of people or things arranged or following in order</p><p><i>n.</i> the action of following in order [sequence]</p><p><i>n.</i> (ecology) the gradual and orderly process of change in an ecosystem brought about by the progressive replacement of one community by another until a stable climax is established [ecological succession]</p><p><i>n.</i> acquisition of property by descent or by will [taking over]</p><p><b>slijedeći, sukcesivan, susljedan, uzastopan, uzastopni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> in regular succession without gaps [consecutive, sequent, sequential, serial]</p><p><b>sukcesivno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in proper order or sequence [in turn]</p><p><b>uzastopnost, slijed</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a following of one thing after another in time [chronological sequence, chronological succession, sequence, succession]</p><p><b>baštinik, nasljednik, sljednik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who follows next in order [replacement]</p><p><i>n.</i> a thing or person that immediately replaces something or someone</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who inherits some title or office [heir]</p><p><b>kratak, sažet</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> briefly giving the gist of something [compact, compendious, summary]</p><p><b>jezgrovito, sažeto</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with concise and precise brevity [compactly]</p><p><b>kratak, sažet (od &quot;succinct&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> terseness and economy in writing and speaking achieved by expressing a great deal in just a few words [conciseness, concision, pithiness]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili dobivene od jantarne boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or obtained from amber</p><p><b>Dicarboksilna kiselina (C4H6O4) aktivna u metaboličkim procesima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dicarboxylic acid (C4H6O4) active in metabolic processes</p><p><b>mišični relaksant za strijatne mišiće koji se koristi kao dodatak aneste