 tolerirati, bolovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> undergo or be subjected to [endure]</p><p><i>v.</i> undergo (as of injuries and illnesses) [get, have, sustain]</p><p><i>v.</i> experience (emotional) pain</p><p><i>v.</i> put up with something or somebody unpleasant [abide, bear, brook, digest, endure, put up, stand, stick out, stomach, support, tolerate]</p><p><i>v.</i> get worse</p><p><i>v.</i> feel pain or be in pain [hurt]</p><p><i>v.</i> feel physical pain [ache, hurt]</p><p><i>v.</i> feel unwell or uncomfortable</p><p><i>v.</i> be given to</p><p><i>v.</i> undergo or suffer [meet]</p><p><i>v.</i> be set at a disadvantage [lose]</p><p><b>Sposoban da se nosi iako neprijatno (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being borne though unpleasant [bearable, endurable, supportable]</p><p><b>trpljenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> patient endurance especially of pain or distress</p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to tolerate or accept people or situations [acceptance, toleration]</p><p><b>mučenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person suffering from an illness [diseased person, sick person]</p><p><i>n.</i> one who suffers for the sake of principle [martyr]</p><p><b>patnja, trpljenje, bol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of acute pain [agony, excruciation]</p><p><i>n.</i> misery resulting from affliction [woe]</p><p><i>n.</i> psychological suffering [distress, hurt]</p><p><i>n.</i> feelings of mental or physical pain [hurt]</p><p><i>adj.</i> troubled by pain or loss</p><p><i>adj.</i> very unhappy [miserable, wretched]</p><p><b>biti dovoljan, dostajati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be sufficient [answer, do, serve]</p><p><b>dostatnost, dovoljnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sufficient resources to provide comfort and meet obligations</p><p><i>n.</i> an adequate quantity [enough]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being sufficient for the end in view [adequacy]</p><p><b>dostatan, dovoljan, dovoljno, opravdan, umiješan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a quantity that can fulfill a need or requirement but without being abundant</p><p><b>dostatno, dovoljno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a sufficient degree</p><p><b>dodatak, dometak, predmetak, riječca ili slog koji se stavlja na kraju rijeci, sufiks, tvorbeni nastavak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an affix that is added at the end of the word [postfix]</p><p><i>v.</i> attach a suffix to</p><p><b>obrnuta poljska notacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a parenthesis-free notation for forming mathematical expressions in which each operator follows its operands [postfix notation, reverse Polish notation]</p><p><b>formiranje riječi pomoću sufiksa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> formation of a word by means of a suffix</p><p><b>gušiti, gušiti se, udaviti, ugušiti, zagušiti se, daviti, prigušiti, zadaviti, zagušiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> deprive of oxygen and prevent from breathing [asphyxiate, smother]</p><p><i>v.</i> impair the respiration of or obstruct the air passage of [asphyxiate, choke, stifle]</p><p><i>v.</i> become stultified, suppressed, or stifled [choke]</p><p><i>v.</i> suppress the development, creativity, or imagination of [choke]</p><p><i>v.</i> be asphyxiated [asphyxiate, stifle]</p><p><i>v.</i> feel uncomfortable for lack of fresh air</p><p><i>v.</i> struggle for breath [choke, gag, strangle]</p><p><b>izaziva gušenje</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing difficulty in breathing especially through lack of fresh air and presence of heat [smothering, suffocative]</p><p><b>davljenje, gušenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> killing by depriving of oxygen [asphyxiation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the condition of being deprived of oxygen (as by having breathing stopped) [asphyxiation]</p><p><b>uzrokovanje poteškoća u disanju, posebno zbog nedostatka svježeg zraka i prisutnosti toplote (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing difficulty in breathing especially through lack of fresh air and presence of heat [smothering, suffocating]</p><p><b>pomoćnik ili podređeni biskup biskupije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an assistant or subordinate bishop of a diocese [suffragan bishop]</p><p><b>pomoćnik ili podređeni biskup biskupije (MT)