ine carbohydrate used as a sweetener and preservative [refined sugar]</p><p><i>n.</i> an essential structural component of living cells and source of energy for animals [carbohydrate, saccharide]</p><p><i>n.</i> informal terms for money [boodle, bread, cabbage, clams, dinero, dough, gelt, kale, lettuce, lolly, loot, lucre, moolah, pelf, scratch, shekels, simoleons, wampum]</p><p><i>v.</i> sweeten with sugar [saccharify]</p><p><b>slatko pulpno tropsko voće s guskom ljuskom i blistavim crnim sjemenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sweet pulpy tropical fruit with thick scaly rind and shiny black seeds [annon, sweetsop]</p><p><b>šećerna repa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> form of the common beet having a sweet white root from which sugar is obtained</p><p><i>n.</i> white-rooted beet grown as a source of sugar</p><p><b>posudica za šećer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dish in which sugar is served</p><p><b>Proizvodi se kuhanjem čiste šećere dok ne zatvrdi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> made by boiling pure sugar until it hardens</p><p><b>šećerna trska</b></p><p><i>n.</i> juicy canes whose sap is a source of molasses and commercial sugar [sugarcane]</p><p><i>n.</i> tall tropical southeast Asian grass having stout fibrous jointed stalks [Saccharum officinarum, sugarcane]</p><p><b>Piškotci posut granulatnim šećerom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cookies sprinkled with granulated sugar</p><p><b>biljka kukuruza razvijena kako bi imala mlade uši koje su slatke i pogodne za jelo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a corn plant developed in order to have young ears that are sweet and suitable for eating [Zea mays rugosa, Zea saccharata, green corn, sweet corn, sweet corn plant]</p><p><b>Bogati stariji čovjek koji daje skupo darove mladom čovjeku u zamjenu za prijateljstvo ili bliskost. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wealthy older man who gives a young person expensive gifts in return for friendship or intimacy</p><p><b>veliki konusni kruh koncentriranog rafiniranog šećera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large conical loaf of concentrated refined sugar [loaf sugar, sugarloaf]</p><p><b>Kravlje iz istočne i središnje Sjeverne Amerike s tri- do pet-lobed lišća i tvrdo blizu zrnasta drvo često se koristi za rad ormarića posebno kovrčasti zrnasti oblik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> maple of eastern and central North America having three-lobed to five-lobed leaves and hard close-grained wood much used for cabinet work especially the curly-grained form [Acer saccharum, rock maple]</p><p><b>odjemna voda (Pb[CH3CO]2) koja se koristi za bojenje pamuka i proizvodnju emajla i lakova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a poisonous white solid (Pb[CH3CO]2) used in dyeing cotton and in making enamels and varnishes [lead acetate]</p><p><b>Malezijska palma s plemena s podnožjem gusto prekrivenom vlaknima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Malaysian feather palm with base densely clothed with fibers [Arenga pinnata, gomuti, gomuti palm]</p><p><b>vrsta graška koja proizvodi grašak s tankim ravnim jestivim čunjama, Zeleni grašak s ravnim jestivim čunjama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> variety of pea plant producing peas having thin flat edible pods [snow pea]</p><p><i>n.</i> green peas with flat edible pods [snow pea]</p><p><b>Američki borca koji je osvojio svjetsko prvenstvo u srednjoj kategoriji pet puta i svjetsko prvenstvo u welter kategoriji jednom (1921-1989) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States prizefighter who won the world middleweight championship five times and the world welterweight championship once (1921-1989) [Ray Robinson, Robinson, Walker Smith]</p><p><b>šećerana, rafinerija šećera, tvornica šećera</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a refinery for sugar</p><p><b>žlica za serviranje šećera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spoon for serving sugar [sugar spoon]</p><p><b>vrsta graška koja proizvodi grašak s krhkim okruglim jestivim čunjama, Zeleni grašak s jestivim čunjama koji su vrlo hrskavi i nisu ravni (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> variety of pea plant producing peas having crisp rounded edible pods [snap pea]</p><p><i>n.</i> green peas with edible pods that are very crisp and not flat</p><p><b>Svaka od nekoliko sorgoima uzgajanih kao izvor sirup (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several sorghums cultivated as a source of syrup [sorgho, sorgo, sweet sorghum]</p><p><b>žlica za serviranje šećera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spoon for serving sugar [sugar shell]</p><p><b>Zastozelena grmlja iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s šiljcima crvenkasto žutih cvijeća i žlezdavih dlakavih plodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen shrub of southeastern United States with spikes of reddish yellow flowers and glandular hairy fruits [Rhus ovata, sugar-bush]</p><p><b>šećer i voda i ponekad kukuruzni sirup skuhani zajedno (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sugar and water and sometimes corn syrup boiled together</p><p><b>voda zaslađena šećerom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> water sweetened with sugar</p><p><b>Zastozelena grmlja iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s šiljcima crvenkasto žutih cvijeća i žlezdavih dlakavih plodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> evergreen shrub of southeastern United States with spikes of reddish yellow flowers and glandular hairy fruits [Rhus ovata, sugar sumac]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom šećera ili siropa (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> encrusted with sugar or syrup [candied]</p><p><b>lišće lišće s malim crnim bojama, mala jestiva tamno ljubičasta do crna bobica s velikim jamama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shade tree with small black berries [Celtis laevigata]</p><p><i>n.</i> small edible dark purple to black berry with large pits [hackberry]</p><p><b>Slastične trske čiji sok služi kao izvor melase i komercijalnog šećera, Visoka tropska jugoistočna azijska trava s čvrstima vlaknastom spojenim stabljikama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> juicy canes whose sap is a source of molasses and commercial sugar [sugar cane]</p><p><i>n.</i> tall tropical southeast Asian grass having stout fibrous jointed stalks [Saccharum officinarum, sugar cane]</p><p><b>glazirati, kandirati, ušećeriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> coat with something sweet, such as a hard sugar glaze [candy, glaze]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to appear more pleasant or appealing</p><p><b>šećer, šećerni, zasladiti, sećer, šećerom (od &quot;sugar&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> with sweetening added [sweet, sweet-flavored, sweetened]</p><p><b>okusni osjećaj kada se šećer rastvori u ustima, slatkoća šećera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the taste experience when sugar dissolves in the mouth [sweet, sweetness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the sweetness of sugar</p><p><b>ne sadržavaju šećer (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> not containing sugar [nonsweet]</p><p><b>veliki konusni kruh koncentriranog rafiniranog šećera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large conical loaf of concentrated refined sugar [loaf sugar, sugar loaf]</p><p><b>Svakakav od različitih malih slatkiša s šećerom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various small sugary candies</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom šećera (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing sugar</p><p><b>nagovijestiti, natuknuti, navesti, podsjećati, predlagati, predložiti, preporučiti, pretpostaviti, sugerirati, zahtijevati, predloži, sugeriraju, savjetovati, dočarati, evocirati, naslikati sliku</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make a proposal, declare a plan for something [advise, propose]</p><p><i>v.</i> drop a hint [hint]</p><p><i>v.</i> imply as a possibility [intimate]</p><p><i>v.</i> call to mind [evoke, paint a picture]</p><p><b>nagovijestiti, natuknuti, navesti, podsjećati, predlagati, predložiti, preporučiti, pretpostaviti, sugerirati, zahtijevati, predloži, sugeriraju (od &quot;suggest&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who advances a suggestion or proposal [proposer]</p><p><b>osjetljivost ili odzivnost na sugestije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> susceptibility or responsiveness to suggestion</p><p><b>osjetljiv ili reagira na sugestije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> susceptible or responsive to suggestion</p><p><b>nagovještenje, prijedlog, savjet, sugestija, uputa, trag</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an idea that is suggested</p><p><i>n.</i> a proposal offered for acceptance or rejection [proffer, proposition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a just detectable amount [hint, tint, trace]</p><p><i>n.</i> persuasion formulated as a suggestion [prompting]</p><p><i>n.</i> the sequential mental process in which one thought leads to another by association</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of inducing hypnosis [hypnotism, mesmerism]</p><p><b>koji nagovještava, sugestivan, sugestivnom</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to suggest or imply [implicative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually followed by `of') pointing out or revealing clearly [indicative, indicatory, revelatory, significative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to suggest something improper or indecent</p><p><b>koji nagovještava, sugestivan, sugestivnom (od &quot;suggestive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a suggestive manner</p><p><b>Visoka zimzelena stabla iz Japana i Kine koja daju vrijedno mekano drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall evergreen of Japan and China yielding valuable soft wood [Cryptomeria japonica, Japan cedar, Japanese cedar]</p><p><b>Suharto</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Indonesian statesman who seized power from Sukarno in 1967 (born in 1921)</p><p><b>koji predstavljaju vlastitu klasu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting a class of its own</p><p><b>poguban, smrtonosan, ubitačan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> dangerous to yourself or your interests [self-destructive]</p><p><b>samoubojstvo, ubiti se, samoubistvo, suicid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of killing yourself [self-annihilation, self-destruction]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who kills himself intentionally [felo-de-se]</p><p><b>bombaš samoubojica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a terrorist who blows himself up in order to kill or injure other people</p><p><b>teroristički napad koji je izvršio netko tko ne nada da će preživjeti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a terrorist bombing carried out by someone who does not hope to survive it</p><p><b>Ubijanje ili ozlijeđivanje drugih dok se uništavaš (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> killing or injuring others while annihilating yourself [martyr operation, sacrifice operation]</p><p><b>dogovor između dvoje ili više ljudi da počine samoubojstvo zajedno na određenom mjestu i u određenom vremenu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agreement by two or more people to commit suicide together at a given place and time</p><p><b>otrovna pilula s potencijalno katastrofalnim posljedicama za tvrtku koju je namijenjena zaštiti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a poison pill with potentially catastrophic implications for the company it is intended to protect</p><p><b>trkač na trećoj bazi počinje kući dok bacač isporučuje loptu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the runner on third base starts home as the pitcher delivers the ball [suicide squeeze play]</p><p><b>trkač na trećoj bazi počinje kući dok bacač isporučuje loptu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the runner on third base starts home as the pitcher delivers the ball [suicide squeeze]</p><p><b>svinjske vrste (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pigs [family Suidae]</p><p><b>rod gljiva iz obitelji Boletaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of fungi belonging to the family Boletaceae [genus Suillus]</p><p><b>kratka hronična gljiva s crvenkasto smeđom kapačkom i bijelom stabljkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a short squat edible fungus with a reddish brown cap and white stalk</p><p><b>Švicarska</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked federal republic in central Europe [Schweiz, Svizzera, Swiss Confederation, Switzerland]</p><p><b>biti podesan, biti prikladan, kombinezon, kostim, odgovarati, odgovarati kome, odijelo, odjeća, parnica, po mjeri, prilagoditi, pristajati, prosidba, serija, tužba, udesiti se, ugađanje, ugoditi, slučaj, pasati, zadovoljavati, zadovoljiti, dolikovati, doličiti, priličiti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a set of garments (usually including a jacket and trousers or skirt) for outerwear all of the same fabric and color [suit of clothes]</p><p><i>n.</i> a comprehensive term for any proceeding in a court of law whereby an individual seeks a legal remedy [case, causa, cause, lawsuit]</p><p><i>n.</i> (slang) a businessman dressed in a business suit</p><p><i>n.</i> a man's courting of a woman [courting, courtship, wooing]</p><p><i>n.</i> a petition or appeal made to a person of superior status or rank</p><p><i>n.</i> playing card in any of four sets of 13 cards in a pack</p><p><i>v.</i> be agreeable or acceptable to [accommodate, fit]</p><p><i>v.</i> be agreeable or acceptable</p><p><i>v.</i> accord or comport with [befit, beseem]</p><p><i>v.</i> enhance the appearance of [become]</p><p><b>oklop koji štiti cijelo tijelo nosioca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> armor that protects the wearer's whole body [body armor, body armour, cataphract, coat of mail, suit of armour]</p><p><b>oklop koji štiti cijelo tijelo nosioca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> armor that protects the wearer's whole body [body armor, body armour, cataphract, coat of mail, suit of armor]</p><p><b>odijelo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a set of garments (usually including a jacket and trousers or skirt) for outerwear all of the same fabric and color [suit]</p><p><b>podobnost, prikladnost, primjerenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of having the properties that are right for a specific purpose [suitableness]</p><p><b>odgovarajući, podesan, podesnog, podoban, pogodan, pogodno, prikladan, prikladnih, prilagođen, primjereno, zgodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> meant or adapted for an occasion or use [suited]</p><p><i>adj.</i> worthy of being chosen especially as a spouse [desirable, worthy]</p><p><b>podobnost, prikladnost, primjerenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of having the properties that are right for a specific purpose [suitability]</p><p><b>U skladu s onim što je prikladno ili prikladno za okolnosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in accordance with what is appropriate or suitable for the circumstances [appropriately, befittingly, duly, fitly, fittingly, properly]</p><p><b>kofer, kovčeg, putna torba, ručni kovčeg, koveeg, kufer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a portable rectangular container for carrying clothes [bag, grip, traveling bag, travelling bag]</p><p><b>apartman, nastavak, odijelo, pratnja, soba, svita, suita, sobe</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musical composition of several movements only loosely connected</p><p><i>n.</i> apartment consisting of a series of connected rooms used as a living unit (as in a hotel) [rooms]</p><p><i>n.</i> the group following and attending to some important person [cortege, entourage, retinue]</p><p><i>n.</i> a matching set of furniture</p><p><b>podesan, pogodan, prikladan, snabdjeven, zgodan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> meant or adapted for an occasion or use [suitable]</p><p><i>adj.</i> outfitted or supplied with clothing</p><p><b>podešavanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fabric used for suits</p><p><b>molilac, parničar, prosilac, tužitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man who courts a woman [suer, wooer]</p><p><b>Sukarno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Indonesian statesman who obtained the independence of Indonesia from the Netherlands in 1949 and served as president until ousted by Suharto in a coup d'etat (1901-1970) [Achmad Sukarno]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je proizvod proizveden u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvedena je od: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thin beef strips (or chicken or pork) cooked briefly at the table with onions and greens and soy sauce</p><p><b>Židovski veliki praznik koji počinje uoči 15. dana Tisrija i koji se obilježava u znak sjećanja na utočište koje su Izraelci imali tijekom 40 godina u pustinji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a major Jewish festival beginning on the eve of the 15th of Tishri and commemorating the shelter of the Israelites during their 40 years in the wilderness [Feast of Booths, Feast of Tabernacles, Succos, Succoth, Tabernacles]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko američkih biljaka rodova Suksdorfia s orbicularnim ili bubrežnim lišćama i bijelima ili ružnim ili ljubičastim cvijećima u krajnjim panicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several American plants of the genus Suksdorfia having orbicular to kidney-shaped somewhat succulent leaves and white or rose or violet flowers in terminal panicles</p><p><b>tanka delikatna biljka s širokim okruglim duboko uštogljenim lišćama i tamno ružičastim do ljubičastim cvjetovima u obliku lovora (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender delicate plant with wide roundish deeply lobed leaves and deep pink to violet funnel-shaped flowers [violet suksdorfia]</p><p><b>Sukur, Sukur jezik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Chadic language spoken south of Lake Chad</p><p><b>vrsta rod Sulidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Sulidae [genus Sula]</p><p><b>bluna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very large white gannet with black wing tips [solan, solan goose, solant goose]</p><p><b>sulfonamid (trgovinski naziv Sulamyd) za liječenje infekcija očiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a topical sulfonamide (trade name Sulamyd) used to treat eye infections [sulfacetamide]</p><p><b>Celebes, Sulawesi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mountainous island in eastern Indonesia [Celebes]</p><p><b>s masenim udubljenim dijelom, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having deep narrow furrows or grooves</p><p><b>(anatomija) bilo koji od uskih žlijezda u tijelu ili tkivu, posebno one koje označavaju konvulzije na površini mozga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (anatomy) any of the narrow grooves in an organ or tissue especially those that mark the convolutions on the surface of the brain</p><p><b>pukotina mozga koja se proteže prema gore na bočnoj površini obje hemisfere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brain fissure extending upward on the lateral surface of both hemispheres [Rolando's fissure, central sulcus, fissure of Rolando]</p><p><b>Najdublje i najistaknutije pukotine kortikalne šupljine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the deepest and most prominent of the cortical fissures [Sylvian fissure, fissure of Sylvius, lateral cerebral sulcus]</p><p><b>Protibakterijski lijek koji se sastoji od bilo kojeg od nekoliko sintetičkih organskih spojeva koji su sposobni inhibirati rast bakterija koje zahtijevaju PABA (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antibacterial consisting of any of several synthetic organic compounds capable of inhibiting the growth of bacteria that require PABA [sulfa drug, sulfonamide, sulpha]</p><p><b>Protibakterijski lijek koji se sastoji od bilo kojeg od nekoliko sintetičkih organskih spojeva koji su sposobni inhibirati rast bakterija koje zahtijevaju PABA (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antibacterial consisting of any of several synthetic organic compounds capable of inhibiting the growth of bacteria that require PABA [sulfa, sulfonamide, sulpha]</p><p><b>sulfonamid (trgovinski naziv Sulamyd) za liječenje infekcija očiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a topical sulfonamide (trade name Sulamyd) used to treat eye infections [Sulamyd]</p><p><b>sulfovi lijekovi koji se koriste za liječenje meningitisa i upale pluća i drugih infekcija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sulfa drug used in treating meningitis and pneumonia and other infections</p><p><b>sulfovir koji se koristi kao sulfadiazin i u veterinarskoj medicini. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sulfa drug used like sulfadiazine and also in veterinary medicine [sulfamezathine]</p><p><b>sulfonamid (trgovinski naziv Gantanol) koji se koristi za liječenje infekcija (posebno infekcija mokraćnih puteva) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sulfonamide (trade name Gantanol) used to treat infections (especially infections of the urinary tract) [Gantanol]</p><p><b>sulfovir koji se koristi kao sulfadiazin i u veterinarskoj medicini. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sulfa drug used like sulfadiazine and also in veterinary medicine [sulfamethazine]</p><p><b>bjelokritični bezmirni sulf-drog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a white odorless crystalline sulfa drug</p><p><b>kristalna kiselina od anilina koja se koristi kao boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crystalline acid made from aniline and used as a dye [sulphanilic acid]</p><p><b>Sulfovir iz piridina i sulfanilamida (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sulfa drug derived from pyridine and sulfanilamide</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5%, pretvoriti u sulfat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt or ester of sulphuric acid [sulphate]</p><p><i>v.</i> convert into a sulfate</p><p><b>sulfid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound of sulphur and some other element that is more electropositive [sulphide]</p><p><b>sulfonamid (trgovinski naziv Gantrisin) koji se koristi za liječenje infekcija mokraćnih puteva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sulfonamide (trade name Gantrisin) used to treat infections of the urinary tract [Gantrisin]</p><p><b>Protibakterijski lijek koji se sastoji od bilo kojeg od nekoliko sintetičkih organskih spojeva koji su sposobni inhibirati rast bakterija koje zahtijevaju PABA (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antibacterial consisting of any of several synthetic organic compounds capable of inhibiting the growth of bacteria that require PABA [sulfa, sulfa drug, sulpha]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt of sulphonic acid</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% masenog udjela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acid derived from sulphuric acid [sulphonic acid]</p><p><b>lijek protiv dijabetesa koji se sastoji od bilo kojeg od nekoliko lijekova koji smanjuju razinu glukoze u krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antidiabetic consisting of any of several drugs that reduce the level of glucose in the blood</p><p><b>sumpor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abundant tasteless odorless multivalent nonmetallic element [S, atomic number 16, sulphur]</p><p><i>v.</i> treat with sulphur in order to preserve [sulphur]</p><p><b>bilo koji bakterija iz roda Thiobacillus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any bacterium of the genus Thiobacillus [sulphur bacteria, thiobacteria]</p><p><b>Najveći sisar ikada poznat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> largest mammal ever known [Balaenoptera musculus, blue whale]</p><p><b>bilo koji od brojnih žutih ili narandžastih leptira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous yellow or orange butterflies [sulphur butterfly]</p><p><b>bezbojan toksični plin (SO2) koji se nalazi u plinovima iz vulkana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless toxic gas (SO2) that occurs in the gases from volcanoes [sulphur dioxide]</p><p><b>bezbojan plin koji je rastvoran u alkoholu i etru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless gas that is soluble in alcohol and ether [sulphur hexafluoride]</p><p><b>rudnik u kojem se sumpor iskopava iz zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mine where sulphur is dug from the ground [sulphur mine]</p><p><b>Toxicni ratni plin s sulfidnim spojevima koji stvara mjehuriće i napada oči i pluća. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a toxic war gas with sulfide based compounds that raises blisters and attacks the eyes and lungs [blistering agent, dichloroethyl sulfide, mustard agent, mustard gas]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom ugljika od 0,05 do 0,05 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several oxides of sulphur [sulphur oxide]</p><p><b>biljka vlažnih visoravničkih livada s razbijenim grmovima blijedožutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant of moist highland meadows having ragged clusters of pale yellow flowers [Castilleja sulphurea]</p><p><b>od nečeg što ima žutu boju sumpora (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of something having the yellow color of sulfur [sulphur-yellow]</p><p><b>kombinirati s sumporom (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> combine with sulfur [sulphurette]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50% (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> treated or impregnated with sulfur [sulfurized, sulphuretted]</p><p><b>sumpor (od &quot;sulfur&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or containing sulfur [sulphuric]</p><p><b>(H2SO4) vrlo korozivna kiselina napravljena od sumpor dioksida (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (H2SO4) a highly corrosive acid made from sulfur dioxide [oil of vitriol, sulphuric acid, vitriol]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50% (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> treated or impregnated with sulfur [sulfuretted, sulphuretted]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s sumporom ili ga sadrže ili su izvedene iz sumpora, od strane proizvođača:, karakterizira se oštrim toplinom i vlažnošću. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or related to or containing sulfur or derived from sulfur [sulphurous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> harsh or corrosive in tone [acerb, acerbic, acid, acrid, bitter, blistering, caustic, sulphurous, virulent, vitriolic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by oppressive heat and humidity [stifling, sulphurous, sultry]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> gannets and boobies [family Sulidae]</p><p><b>ne-steroidni protuupalni lijek (trgovinski naziv Clinoril) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (trade name Clinoril) [Clinoril]</p><p><b>zlovolja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mood or display of sullen aloofness or withdrawal [sulkiness]</p><p><i>v.</i> be in a huff and display one's displeasure [brood, pout]</p><p><b>natmuren, zlovoljan (od &quot;sulky&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a sulky manner</p><p><b>raspoloženje ili izraz mrzovoljnog odstupnosti ili povlačenja, osjećaj mrzovoljnog mržnje., -Bezobrazan, ljut. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mood or display of sullen aloofness or withdrawal [sulk]</p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of sulky resentment [huffishness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sullen moody resentful disposition [moroseness, sourness, sullenness]</p><p><b>natmuren, zlovoljan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a light two-wheeled vehicle for one person</p><p><i>adj.</i> sullen or moody [huffish]</p><p><i>adj.</i> moving slowly [sluggish]</p><p><i>adj.</i> depressingly dark [gloomful, glooming, gloomy]</p><p><b>Sula</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of southern Europe cultivated for forage and for its nectar-rich pink flowers that make it an important honey crop [French honeysuckle, Hedysarum coronarium]</p><p><i>n.</i> Roman general and dictator (138-78 BC) [Lucius Cornelius Sulla Felix]</p><p><b>mrk, natmuren, potišten, sumoran, zagasitim</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing a brooding ill humor [dark, dour, glowering, glum, moody, morose, saturnine, sour]</p><p><i>adj.</i> darkened by clouds [heavy, lowering, threatening]</p><p><b>mrk, natmuren, potišten, sumoran, zagasitim (od &quot;sullen&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a sullen manner [dourly, glumly]</p><p><b>mračnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gloomy ill-tempered feeling [glumness, moroseness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a sullen moody resentful disposition [moroseness, sourness, sulkiness]</p><p><b>Američki arhitekt poznat po svojim neboderacima s čeličnim okvirima i zbog izmišljanja fraze "form slijedi funkciju" (1856-1924), Psihijatar iz Sjedinjenih Država (1892-1949), Američki voditelj na poznatom televizijskom varijetetu (1902-1974), Američka učiteljica i životna pratnja Helen Keller (1866-1936), Engleski kompozitor opereta koji je surađivao s libretistom Williamom Gilbertom (1842-1900) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States architect known for his steel framed skyscrapers and for coining the phrase `form follows function' (1856-1924) [Louis Henri Sullivan, Louis Henry Sullivan, Louis Sullivan]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States psychiatrist (1892-1949) [Harry Stack Sullivan]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States host on a well known television variety show (1902-1974) [Ed Sullivan, Edward Vincent Sullivan]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States educator who was the teacher and lifelong companion of Helen Keller (1866-1936) [Anne Mansfield Sullivan, Anne Sullivan]</p><p><i>n.</i> English composer of operettas who collaborated with the librettist William Gilbert (1842-1900) [Arthur Seymour Sullivan, Arthur Sullivan, Sir Arthur Sullivan]</p><p><b>prljati, ukaljati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States painter (born in England) of portraits and historical scenes (1783-1872) [Thomas Sully]</p><p><i>n.</i> French statesman (1560-1641) [Duc de Sully, Maxmilien de Bethune]</p><p><i>v.</i> place under suspicion or cast doubt upon [cloud, corrupt, defile, taint]</p><p><i>v.</i> make dirty or spotty, as by exposure to air [defile, maculate, stain, tarnish]</p><p><i>v.</i> charge falsely or with malicious intent [asperse, besmirch, calumniate, defame, denigrate, slander, smear, smirch]</p><p><b>Protibakterijski lijek koji se sastoji od bilo kojeg od nekoliko sintetičkih organskih spojeva koji su sposobni inhibirati rast bakterija koje zahtijevaju PABA (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> antibacterial consisting of any of several synthetic organic compounds capable of inhibiting the growth of bacteria that require PABA [sulfa, sulfa drug, sulfonamide]</p><p><b>kristalna kiselina od anilina koja se koristi kao boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crystalline acid made from aniline and used as a dye [sulfanilic acid]</p><p><b>sol sumporne kiseline</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt or ester of sulphuric acid [sulfate]</p><p><b>sulfid</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound of sulphur and some other element that is more electropositive [sulfide]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% masenog udjela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acid derived from sulphuric acid [sulfonic acid]</p><p><b>sumpor, sumpur</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abundant tasteless odorless multivalent nonmetallic element [S, atomic number 16, sulfur]</p><p><i>v.</i> treat with sulphur in order to preserve [sulfur]</p><p><b>bilo koji bakterija iz roda Thiobacillus (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any bacterium of the genus Thiobacillus [sulfur bacteria, thiobacteria]</p><p><b>bilo koji od brojnih žutih ili narandžastih leptira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous yellow or orange butterflies [sulfur butterfly]</p><p><b>bezbojan toksični plin (SO2) koji se nalazi u plinovima iz vulkana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless toxic gas (SO2) that occurs in the gases from volcanoes [sulfur dioxide]</p><p><b>bezbojan plin koji je rastvoran u alkoholu i etru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless gas that is soluble in alcohol and ether [sulfur hexafluoride]</p><p><b>rudnik u kojem se sumpor iskopava iz zemlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mine where sulphur is dug from the ground [sulfur mine]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom ugljika od 0,05 do 0,05 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several oxides of sulphur [sulfur oxide]</p><p><b>Bijeli kakadu sa žutom erektilnom grebenom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> white cockatoo with a yellow erectile crest [Cacatua galerita, Kakatoe galerita]</p><p><b>od nečeg što ima žutu boju sumpora (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of something having the yellow color of sulfur [sulfur-yellow]</p><p><b>kombinirati s sumporom (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> combine with sulfur [sulfurette]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 50% (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> treated or impregnated with sulfur [sulfuretted, sulfurized]</p><p><b>sumporni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or containing sulfur [sulfuric]</p><p><b>sumporna kiselina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (H2SO4) a highly corrosive acid made from sulfur dioxide [oil of vitriol, sulfuric acid, vitriol]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s sumporom ili ga sadrže ili su izvedene iz sumpora, od strane proizvođača:, karakterizira se oštrim toplinom i vlažnošću. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or related to or containing sulfur or derived from sulfur [sulfurous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> harsh or corrosive in tone [acerb, acerbic, acid, acrid, bitter, blistering, caustic, sulfurous, virulent, vitriolic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by oppressive heat and humidity [stifling, sulfurous, sultry]</p><p><b>sultan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ruler of a Muslim country (especially of the former Ottoman Empire) [grand Turk]</p><p><b>George Herman Ruth</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States professional baseball player famous for hitting home runs (1895-1948) [Babe Ruth, George Herman Ruth, Ruth]</p><p><b>u obliku zrna ili u obliku vina, sušeno grožđe bez sjemenki (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pale yellow seedless grape used for raisins and wine</p><p><i>n.</i> dried seedless grape [seedless raisin]</p><p><b>zemlja ili teritorij kojim vlada sultan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> country or territory ruled by a sultan</p><p><b>Sultanat Oman</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strategically located monarchy on the southern and eastern coasts of the Arabian Peninsula [Muscat an