 km (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Swedish unit of length equivalent to 10 km [mil, mile]</p><p><b>švedska novčana jedinica, švedska valuta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Sweden</p><p><b>Švedska sopranistkinja koja je obišla Sjedinjene Države pod vodstvom P. T. Barnuma (1820-1887) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Swedish soprano who toured the United States under the management of P. T. Barnum (1820-1887) [Jenny Lind, Lind]</p><p><b>Hladni aromatični kruh od kvasca od brašna i melase i pomorandžine kore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a moist aromatic yeast-raised bread made with rye flour and molasses and orange rind [Swedish rye bread]</p><p><b>Hladni aromatični kruh od kvasca od brašna i melase i pomorandžine kore (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a moist aromatic yeast-raised bread made with rye flour and molasses and orange rind [Swedish rye]</p><p><b>križastog biljka s gustim žutih korijena, veliki žuti korijen biljke rutabaga koja se koristi kao hrana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cruciferous plant with a thick bulbous edible yellow root [Brassica napus napobrassica, rutabaga, rutabaga plant, swede, turnip cabbage]</p><p><i>n.</i> the large yellow root of a rutabaga plant used as food [rutabaga, swede, yellow turnip]</p><p><b>izmišljeni lik u predstavi Georgea Pitta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fictional character in a play by George Pitt [Todd]</p><p><b>brisati, čišćenje, domet, doseg, mesti, pomesti, zamah, prelaziti, prijeći, prolaziti, pronijeti se, pronositi se, proći, doploviti, lebdjeti, odjedriti, ploviti, pometati, dovući, protezati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wide scope [expanse]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who cleans soot from chimneys [chimneysweep, chimneysweeper]</p><p><i>n.</i> winning all or all but one of the tricks in bridge [slam]</p><p><i>n.</i> a long oar used in an open boat [sweep oar]</p><p><i>n.</i> (American football) an attempt to advance the ball by running around the end of the line [end run]</p><p><i>n.</i> a movement in an arc</p><p><i>v.</i> sweep across or over 