i>v.</i> take up the cause, ideology, practice, method, of someone and use it as one's own [adopt, embrace, espouse]</p><p><b>drugi kazalj koji je postavljen na istom središtu kao sat i minut kazalj i čitan je na minutama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a second hand that is mounted on the same center as the hour and minute hand and is read on the minutes [sweep hand]</p><p><b>minolovac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an employee who sweeps (floors or streets etc.)</p><p><i>n.</i> a cleaning implement with revolving brushes that pick up dirt as the implement is pushed over a carpet [carpet sweeper]</p><p><i>n.</i> little-known nocturnal fish of warm shallow seas with an oblong compressed body</p><p><b>brisanje, čišćenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of cleaning with a broom</p><p><i>adj.</i> taking in or moving over (or as if over) a wide area</p><p><i>adj.</i> ignoring distinctions [wholesale]</p><p><b>brisanje, čišćenje (od &quot;sweeping&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a sweeping manner</p><p><b>klađenje, nagrada od uloga, oklada</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lottery in which the prize consists of the money paid by the participants</p><p><b>bombon, milina, sladak, slatkiš, slatkoća, slatkost, ugodan, slatkim, slatko, desert, dezert, slastica, poslastica, slastičarki proizvodi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English phonetician [Henry Sweet]</p><p><i>n.</i> a dish served as the last course of a meal [afters, dessert]</p><p><i>n.</i> a food rich in sugar [confection]</p><p><i>n.</i> the taste experience when sugar dissolves in the mouth [sugariness, sweetness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of tasting as if it contains sugar [sweetness]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or denoting the characteristic taste of sugar</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a sweet nature befitting an angel or cherub [angelic, angelical, cherubic, seraphic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> pleasing to the ear [dulcet, honeyed, mellifluous, mellisonant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> pleasing to the senses</p><p><i>adj.</i> pleasing to the mind or feeling [gratifying]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a natural fragrance [odoriferous, odorous, perfumed, scented, sweet-scented, sweet-smelling]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of wines) having a high residual sugar content</p><p><i>adj.</i> not containing or composed of salt water [fresh]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not soured or preserved [fresh, unfermented]</p><p><i>adj.</i> with sweetening added [sugared, sweet-flavored, sweetened]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in an affectionate or loving manner (`sweet' is sometimes a poetic or informal variant of `sweetly') [sweetly]</p><p><b>tropski američki trnasti grm ili drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American thorny shrub or small tree [Acacia farnesiana, cassie, flame tree, huisache, mimosa bush, scented wattle, sweet wattle]</p><p><b>višegodišnja europska biljka s grmovima malih mirisnih cvijeća obično bijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial European plant having clusters of small fragrant usually white flowers [Lobularia maritima, sweet alyssum]</p><p><b>slatki badem</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small bushy deciduous tree native to Asia and North Africa having pretty pink blossoms and highly prized edible nuts enclosed in a hard green hull [Amygdalus communis, Prunus amygdalus, Prunus dulcis, almond]</p><p><b>Blisko žuto masno ulje iz slatkih ili gorkih badema (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pale yellow fatty oil expressed from sweet or bitter almonds [almond oil, expressed almond oil]</p><p><b>višegodišnja europska biljka s grmovima malih mirisnih cvijeća obično bijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial European plant having clusters of small fragrant usually white flowers [Lobularia maritima, sweet alison]</p><p><b>Bliski višegodišnji biljci starog svijeta s malom bijelom ili žutošću cvijeća i mirisnim lištima okusa limuna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bushy perennial Old World mint having small white or yellowish flowers and fragrant lemon-flavored leaves [Melissa officinalis, bee balm, beebalm, garden balm, lemon balm]</p><p><b>bosilja, bosiljak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual or perennial of tropical Asia having spikes of small white flowers and aromatic leaves [Ocimum basilicum, common basil]</p><p><i>n.</i> leaves of the common basil [basil]</p><p><b>grm ili drvo s prilično malim mirisnim bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub or small tree having rather small fragrant white flowers [Magnolia virginiana, swamp bay, swamp laurel]</p><p><b>grmasti listovit grm sa dugim cvetovima ružičastih cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bushy deciduous shrub of the eastern United States with long racemes of pinkish flowers [Leucothoe racemosa]</p><p><b>uobičajena breza istočne Sjedinjenih Država s začinjenim smeđom koreom koja daje nestabilno ulje i tvrdo tamno drvo koje se koristi za namještaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common birch of the eastern United States having spicy brown bark yielding a volatile oil and hard dark wood used for furniture [Betula lenta, black birch, cherry birch]</p><p><b>visoka i često uzgajana buckeye iz središnje Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tall and often cultivated buckeye of the central United States</p><p><b>Zapadnoindijski cvijet strast s jestivim plodovima veličine jabuke, voće strasti veličine jabuke iz Zapadne Indije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> West Indian passionflower with edible apple-sized fruit [Passiflora maliformis]</p><p><i>n.</i> apple-sized passion fruit of the West Indies</p><p><b>iđirot</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial marsh plant having swordlike leaves and aromatic roots [Acorus calamus, calamus, flagroot, myrtle flag, sweet flag]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste biljaka koje se upotrebljavaju u proizvodnji hrane za životinje, za koje se primjenjuje sljedeći popis: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South American plant with roots used as a vegetable and herbage used for stock feed [Manihot dulcis]</p><p><b>divlja trešnja, Trešnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large Eurasian tree producing small dark bitter fruit in the wild but edible sweet fruit under cultivation [Prunus avium]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several fruits of cultivated cherry trees that have sweet flesh [black cherry]</p><p><b>pitomi kesten</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wild or cultivated throughout southern Europe, northwestern Africa and southwestern Asia [Castanea sativa, European chestnut, Spanish chestnut]</p><p><b>Europska biljka s mekanim lišćama i bijelim cvijećem, aromatska smola koja se gori kao tamjan i koristi u parfemima, Sljedeći članci: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European herb with soft ferny leaves and white flowers [Myrrhis odorata]</p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic resin that is burned as incense and used in perfume [gum myrrh, myrrh]</p><p><i>n.</i> fresh ferny leaves and green seeds used as garnish in salads and cold vegetables</p><p><b>nefermentirani jabukovci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unfermented cider</p><p><b>uzgajanje jednogodišnje ili dvostruke biljke koja se široko uzgaja posebno za sijeno i poboljšanje tla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect annual or biennial plant grown extensively especially for hay and soil improvement [melilot, melilotus]</p><p><b>Slatko-aromatična biljka iz Amerike, Europska biljka s bijelo-ružičastim cvijećima u mirisu vanilije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American sweet-scented herb [Petasites sagitattus]</p><p><i>n.</i> European herb with vanilla-scented white-pink flowers [Petasites fragrans, winter heliotrope]</p><p><b>kukuruz</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a corn plant developed in order to have young ears that are sweet and suitable for eating [Zea mays rugosa, Zea saccharata, green corn, sugar corn, sweet corn plant]</p><p><i>n.</i> corn that can be eaten as a vegetable while still young and soft [green corn]</p><p><b>biljka kukuruza razvijena kako bi imala mlade uši koje su slatke i pogodne za jelo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a corn plant developed in order to have young ears that are sweet and suitable for eating [Zea mays rugosa, Zea saccharata, green corn, sugar corn, sweet corn]</p><p><b>jedno žuto voće Jamajke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the edible yellow fruit of the Jamaica honeysuckle [bell apple, water lemon, yellow granadilla]</p><p><b>uobičajena starina iz središnje i istočne Sjeverne Amerike koja nosi ljubičaste crne bobice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common elder of central and eastern North America bearing purple-black berries [American elder, Sambucus canadensis, black elderberry]</p><p><b>kamilica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual Eurasian herb similar in fragrance and medicinal uses to chamomile though taste is more bitter and effect is considered inferior [German chamomile, Matricaria chamomilla, Matricaria recutita, wild chamomile]</p><p><b>Malo ili ništa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> little or nothing at all [Fanny Adams, bugger all, fuck all]</p><p><b>Polypodium vulgare, lezibaba, obični oslad, slatka bujad, slatki korijen</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mat-forming lithophytic or terrestrial fern with creeping rootstocks and large pinnatifid fronds found throughout North America and Europe and Africa and east Asia [Polypodium vulgare, adder's fern, common polypody, golden maidenhair, golden polypody, wall fern]</p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrub of eastern North America with sweet scented fernlike leaves and tiny white flowers [Comptonia asplenifolia, Comptonia peregrina]</p><p><b>iđirot</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial marsh plant having swordlike leaves and aromatic roots [Acorus calamus, calamus, flagroot, myrtle flag, sweet calamus]</p><p><b>ljeploviti divlji cvijet s mirisnim vitkim ili blijedo ružičastim cvijećem u obliku trube (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leafy wildflower having fragrant slender white or pale pink trumpet-shaped flowers [Mirabilis longiflora, maravilla]</p><p><b>Blagorje u sjevernoj umjerenoj zoni s gorkim okusom mirisnih lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bog shrub of north temperate zone having bitter-tasting fragrant leaves [Myrica gale, Scotch gale]</p><p><b>s aromatičnim lištima od kojih se pravi ljekoviti čaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> goldenrod of eastern America having aromatic leaves from which a medicinal tea is made [Blue Mountain tea, Solidago odora]</p><p><b>smatra se najboljim za voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> considered best for fruit [Passiflora ligularis, granadilla]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko vlažnih trava iz roda Glyceria s slatkim okusom ili mirisom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several moisture-loving grasses of the genus Glyceria having sweet flavor or odor [manna grass]</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka ne primjenjuje druga pravila iz članka 4. stavka 1. točaka (a) i (b) ovog članka, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije II., aromatični izlučik iz drveta slatke guma, Sjevernoameričko stablo rod Liquidambar s trunastima sfernim plodovima i mirisnim sokom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> reddish-brown wood and lumber from heartwood of the sweet gum tree used to make furniture [hazelwood, red gum, satin walnut]</p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic exudate from the sweet gum tree [liquidambar]</p><p><i>n.</i> a North American tree of the genus Liquidambar having prickly spherical fruit clusters and fragrant sap [American sweet gum, Liquidambar styraciflua, bilsted, red gum, sweet gum tree]</p><p><b>Sjevernoameričko stablo rod Liquidambar s trunastima sfernim plodovima i mirisnim sokom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a North American tree of the genus Liquidambar having prickly spherical fruit clusters and fragrant sap [American sweet gum, Liquidambar styraciflua, bilsted, red gum, sweet gum]</p><p><b>Limunovo drvo s plodovima s pomalo neukusnom slatko-slatkom pulpom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lemon tree having fruit with a somewhat insipid sweetish pulp [Citrus limetta, sweet lime]</p><p><b>Limunovo drvo s plodovima s pomalo neukusnom slatko-slatkom pulpom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lemon tree having fruit with a somewhat insipid sweetish pulp [Citrus limetta, sweet lemon]</p><p><b>aromatska europska biljka porijeklom iz Sredozemlja i Turske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic European plant native to Mediterranean and Turkey [Majorana hortensis, Origanum majorana, knotted marjoram]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko sorti grožđa čiji plodovi imaju mrežnu kožu i jestivo meso te miris muška, od voća muskmelonove loze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several varieties of vine whose fruit has a netted rind and edible flesh and a musky smell [Cucumis melo, muskmelon, sweet melon vine]</p><p><i>n.</i> the fruit of a muskmelon vine [muskmelon]</p><p><b>bilo koja od nekoliko sorti grožđa čiji plodovi imaju mrežnu kožu i jestivo meso te miris muška (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several varieties of vine whose fruit has a netted rind and edible flesh and a musky smell [Cucumis melo, muskmelon, sweet melon]</p><p><b>neobavezne izraze ljubavi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inconsequential expressions of affection [honeyed words]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se upotrebljava kao hrana, blago biljno ulje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mild vegetable oil when used as food</p><p><b>narandža s slatkom sokovitom pulpom, vjerojatno porijeklom iz južne Kine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> orange with sweet juicy pulp</p><p><i>n.</i> probably native to southern China [Citrus sinensis, sweet orange tree]</p><p><b>vjerojatno porijeklom iz južne Kine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> probably native to southern China [Citrus sinensis, sweet orange]</p><p><b>biljka za uzlazak u vrt s mirisnim pastelnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> climbing garden plant having fragrant pastel-colored flowers [Lathyrus odoratus, sweetpea]</p><p><b>biljka s velikim blagim debelim zidovima obično zvonoličnim plodovima, Veliki blagi, hrskavi, debeloparti paprike obično zvonolični ili pomalo dugolični (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant bearing large mild thick-walled usually bell-shaped fruits [Capsicum annuum grossum, bell pepper, paprika, pimento, pimiento, sweet pepper plant]</p><p><i>n.</i> large mild crisp thick-walled capsicum peppers usually bell-shaped or somewhat oblong</p><p><b>biljka s velikim blagim debelim zidovima obično zvonoličnim plodovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant bearing large mild thick-walled usually bell-shaped fruits [Capsicum annuum grossum, bell pepper, paprika, pimento, pimiento, sweet pepper]</p><p><b>grm istočne i južne obale Sjedinjenih Država koji ima lijepe raseme bijelih cvijeća mirisnih začina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub of eastern and southern coastal United States having beautiful racemes of spice-scented white flowers [Clethra alnifolia, pepper bush, summer sweet, white alder]</p><p><b>Svinja, slijepa, slijepa i slijepa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pickle cured in brine and preserved in sugar and vinegar</p><p><b>batat, slatki krumpir, okarina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pantropical vine widely cultivated in several varieties for its large sweet tuberous root with orange flesh [Ipomoea batatas, sweet potato vine]</p><p><i>n.</i> the edible tuberous root of the sweet potato vine which is grown widely in warm regions of the United States</p><p><i>n.</i> egg-shaped terra cotta wind instrument with a mouthpiece and finger holes [ocarina]</p><p><b>batat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pantropical vine widely cultivated in several varieties for its large sweet tuberous root with orange flesh [Ipomoea batatas, sweet potato]</p><p><b>Sredozemna drvena godišnja biljka široko uzgajana zbog svojih gustoga vrha poput šiljaka zelenavi ili žutičasti bijeli cvijeće s intenzivnim začinjenim mirisom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mediterranean woody annual widely cultivated for its dense terminal spikelike clusters greenish or yellowish white flowers having an intense spicy fragrance [Reseda odorata, mignonette]</p><p><b>duge biljke s cvijećem čiji je miris izraženiji navečer (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> long cultivated herb having flowers whose scent is more pronounced in the evening [Dame's violet, Hesperis matronalis, damask violet]</p><p><b>Slatki kolačići od kvasca bez grožđa, orašastih plodova ili začina ili glazure (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous yeast-raised sweet rolls with our without raisins or nuts or spices or a glaze [coffee roll]</p><p><b>veći od Abronia elliptica i s noćnim cvjetovima, biljka s glavama mirisnih bijeli truba u obliku cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> taller than Abronia elliptica and having night-blooming flowers [Abronia fragrans]</p><p><i>n.</i> plant having heads of fragrant white trumpet-shaped flowers [Abronia elliptica, snowball]</p><p><b>Godisnje biljke starog svijeta koje imaju mirisne ljubičaste do duboko crvenokrasne vrhove cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World annual having fragrant purple to deep crimson flower heads [Scabiosa atropurpurea, mournful widow, pincushion flower]</p><p><b>čvrsta grmljava stabla iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država koja imaju drvo koje miriše na klinčeve i mirisne crveno-smeđe cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hardy shrub of southeastern United States having clove-scented wood and fragrant red-brown flowers [Calycanthus floridus, Carolina allspice, strawberry bush, strawberry shrub]</p><p><b>Svaka od nekoliko sorgoima uzgajanih kao izvor sirup (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several sorghums cultivated as a source of syrup [sorgho, sorgo, sugar sorghum]</p><p><b>godišnji od mediteranskih do portugalskih stabljika s dlakavim stabljikama i lištima s malo trnjavim zubima i velikim glavama žutih cvijeća, višegodišnja biljka planina Irana i Iraka, Azijska biljka koja se široko uzgaja zbog svojih slatko mirisnih ružičastih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual of Mediterranean to Portugal having hairy stems and minutely spiny-toothed leaves and large heads of yellow flowers [Cnicus benedictus, blessed thistle]</p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of mountains of Iran and Iraq [Centaurea imperialis]</p><p><i>n.</i> Asian plant widely grown for its sweetly fragrant pink flowers [Amberboa moschata, Centaurea moschata]</p><p><b>laskanje namijenjeno dobivanju naklonosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flattery designed to gain favor [blarney, coaxing, soft soap]</p><p><b>Neko s sigurnim i ugodnim ponašanjem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone with an assured and ingratiating manner [charmer, smoothie, smoothy]</p><p><b>snažan apetit za slatkom hranom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strong appetite for sweet food</p><p><b>biljka iz roda Proboscidea (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a herbaceous plant of the genus Proboscidea [Martynia fragrans, Proboscidea fragrans]</p><p><b>slatka tamno-žutica sorta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sweet dark amber variety [Italian vermouth]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka sa cvetnim cvetovima od ružičaste do ljubičaste boje, a zatim s ravnim čunjama koji se odvajaju u gotovo orbicularne zglobove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of western United States having racemes of pink to purple flowers followed by flat pods that separate into nearly orbicular joints [Hedysarum boreale]</p><p><b>Europska ljubičasta s ljubičastom do bijelom bojom cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European violet typically having purple to white flowers [English violet, Viola odorata, garden violet]</p><p><b>tropski američki trnasti grm ili drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American thorny shrub or small tree [Acacia farnesiana, cassie, flame tree, huisache, mimosa bush, scented wattle, sweet acacia]</p><p><b>kratko-stena violeta iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s mirisnim bijeli cvijeće purpurne žile (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> short-stemmed violet of eastern North America having fragrant purple-veined white flowers [Viola blanda, white violet, woodland white violet]</p><p><b>Evroazijska ruža koja se široko uzgaja zbog svojih gostih grama različitih cvjetova s ravnim vrhom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian pink widely cultivated for its flat-topped dense clusters of varicolored flowers [Dianthus barbatus]</p><p><b>lazarkinja, mirisna lazarkinja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World fragrant stoloniferous perennial having small white flowers and narrow leaves used as flavoring and in sachets [Asperula odorata, Galium odoratum, fragrant bedstraw, waldmeister, woodruff]</p><p><i>n.</i> fragrant dark green leaves used to flavor May wine [waldmeister]<