 parts of truck-garden and greenhouse crops [Scutigerella immaculata, garden centipede, garden symphilid]</p><p><b>simfonijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or characteristic or suggestive of a symphony</p><p><i>adj.</i> harmonious in sound [symphonious]</p><p><b>simfonija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long and complex sonata for symphony orchestra [symphony]</p><p><b>orkestarska kompozicija zasnovana na književnosti ili narodnim pričama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an orchestral composition based on literature or folk tales [tone poem]</p><p><b>harmoničan u zvuku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> harmonious in sound [symphonic]</p><p><b>svirati ili zvučati zajedno, u harmoniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> play or sound together, in harmony [symphonize]</p><p><b>kompozitor simfonija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a composer of symphonies</p><p><b>svirati ili zvučati zajedno, u harmoniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> play or sound together, in harmony [symphonise]</p><p><b>simfonija, simfonijski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long and complex sonata for symphony orchestra [symphonic music]</p><p><i>n.</i> a large orchestra [philharmonic, symphony orchestra]</p><p><b>simfonijskog orkestra</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large orchestra [philharmonic, symphony]</p><p><b>ljeploviti grmovi Sjeverne i Srednje Amerike i Kine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrubs of North America and Central America and China [genus Symphoricarpos]</p><p><b>Symphoricarpos albus, bijeli biserak, grozdovita pamela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrub of western North America having spikes of pink flowers followed by round white berries [common snowberry, snowberry, waxberry]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički listnat grm koji se uzgaja zbog obilne gomile koralno crvenih bobica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American deciduous shrub cultivated for it abundant clusters of coral-red berrylike fruits [Indian currant, coralberry]</p><p><b>mala klasa sitnih članonožnih životinja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small class of minute arthropods [class Symphyla]</p><p><b>Neobična adhezija dvije ili više struktura, Sastavljanje dijelova ili struktura (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an abnormal adhesion of two or more structures</p><p><i>n.</i> a growing together of parts or structures</p><p><b>slijepa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> comfrey [genus Symphytum]</p><p><b>Europska biljka s malim bijelim, ružičastim ili ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European herb having small white, pink or purple flowers [boneset, common comfrey]</p><p><b>dvostrukožci iz reda Ebenales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a dicotyledonous family of order Ebenales [family Symplocaceae, sweetleaf family]</p><p><b>jedna vrsta: zelena zelena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one species: skunk cabbage [genus Symplocarpus]</p><p><b>višegodišnja listovita nisko rastuća smrdljiva močvarna biljka iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s malenim cvijećem zatvorenim u mrljano zeleno ili ljubičasto spathe u obliku kapulja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous perennial low-growing fetid swamp plant of eastern North America having minute flowers enclosed in a mottled greenish or purple cowl-shaped spathe [foetid pothos, polecat weed, skunk cabbage]</p><p><b>ponavljanje riječi ili fraze na početku i na kraju uzastopnih stavaka, tj. istodobna upotreba anafore i epistrophe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> repetition of a word or phrase at the beginning and another at the end of successive clauses, i.e., simultaneous use of anaphora and epistrophe</p><p><b>vrsta i jedini rod Symplocaceae uključujući slatko listove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type and sole genus of Symplocaceae including sweetleaf [genus Symplocus]</p><p><b>listovice iz istočne Azije koje nose ukrasno svijetlo plavo voće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrub of eastern Asia bearing decorative bright blue fruit [Asiatic sweetleaf, sapphire berry]</p><p><b>malo žuto drvo iz južnih Sjedinjenih Država koje ima male mirisne bijele cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small yellowwood tree of southern United States having small fragrant white flowers [sweetleaf]</p><p><b>osoba koja predlaže zdravicu i upoznaje govornike na banketu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the person who proposes toasts and introduces speakers at a banquet [toastmaster]</p><p><b>osoba koja sudjeluje u simpozijumu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who participates in a symposium</p><p><b>gozba, gozba u staroj Grčkoj, simpozij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a meeting or conference for the public discussion of some topic especially one in which the participants form an audience and make presentations</p><p><b>simptom</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) any sensation or change in bodily function that is experienced by a patient and is associated with a particular disease</p><p><i>n.</i> anything that accompanies X and is regarded as an indication of X's existence</p><p><b>karakteristična ili pokazatelj bolesti, koji se odnose na ili u skladu s simptomom ili simptomima ili koji utječu na njih (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> characteristic or indicative of a disease [diagnostic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or according to or affecting a symptom or symptoms</p><p><b>po simptomima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by symptoms</p><p><b>koji nemaju simptome bolesti ili bolesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having no symptoms of illness or disease [asymptomatic]</p><p><b>Suzbijanje dva samoglasnika u diftong., odvojenost tekućine od gela koja je uzrokovana kontrakcijom (kao u proizvodnji sira) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the contraction of two vowels into a diphthong [syneresis]</p><p><i>n.</i> the separation of liquid from a gel that is caused by contraction (as in cheese making) [syneresis]</p><p><b>sinestezija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sensation that normally occurs in one sense modality occurs when another modality is stimulated [synesthesia]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na sinesteziju ili su u njoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or experiencing synesthesia [synesthetic]</p><p><b>sinagoga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) the place of worship for a Jewish congregation [tabernacle, temple]</p><p><b>rod Serranidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Serranidae [genus Synagrops]</p><p><b>Ribe s crnim ustima i žlijezdnim šupljinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small marine fish with black mouth and gill cavity [blackmouth bass]</p><p><b>riblje ribe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stonefishes [genus Synanceja]</p><p><b>Trupna morska riba koja liči na komad stijene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> venomous tropical marine fish resembling a piece of rock [stonefish]</p><p><b>sinapsa, sinapse</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the junction between two neurons (axon-to-dendrite) or between a neuron and a muscle</p><p><b>izumrli gmizavac s jednim parom bočnih privremenih otvora u lubanji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct reptile having a single pair of lateral temporal openings in the skull [synapsid reptile]</p><p><b>izumrli gmizavac s jednim parom bočnih privremenih otvora u lubanji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct reptile having a single pair of lateral temporal openings in the skull [synapsid]</p><p><b>izumrli gmizavci iz Perma do Jure koji se smatraju predcima sisavaca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct reptiles of the Permian to Jurassic considered ancestral to mammals [subclass Synapsida]</p><p><b>U slučaju da se primjenjuje primjena ovog članka, to znači da se primjenjuje primjena ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the side by side pairing of homologous maternal and paternal chromosomes at the start of meiosis</p><p><b>sinaptičan, sinaptična</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (neuroscience) of or involving synapses</p><p><b>Blagovišni lemingi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> bog lemmings [genus Synaptomys]</p><p><b>u mokrim alpskim i subalpskim livama Kanade i Aljaske (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of wet alpine and subalpine meadows of Canada and Alaska [northern bog lemming]</p><p><b>od niskih močvara i livada sjeveroistočnih i središnjih Sjedinjenih Država i južnog Kanade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> of low bogs and meadows of northeastern and central United States and southern Canada [southern bog lemming]</p><p><b>harmonizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make synchronous and adjust in time or manner [synchronise, synchronize]</p><p><b>Voće koje se sastoji od mnogih pojedinačnih malih plodova ili drup dobivenih iz odvojenih jajnika u zajedničkom spremniku: npr. borovnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fruit consisting of many individual small fruits or drupes derived from separate ovaries within a common receptacle: e.g. blackberry [aggregate fruit, multiple fruit]</p><p><b>(od jajnika cvjetnica) koje se sastoje od ujedinjenih karpela (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of ovaries of flowering plants) consisting of united carpels</p><p><b>sinkategorematski izraz (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a syncategorematic expression [syncategoreme]</p><p><b>Izraz koji ne može biti subjekt ili (posebno) predikat prijedloga, ali se mora koristiti zajedno s drugim izrazima (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a term that cannot stand as the subject or (especially) the predicate of a proposition but must be used in conjunction with other terms</p><p><b>sinkategorematski izraz (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a syncategorematic expression [syncategorem]</p><p><b>Sastav koji se sastoji od generatora i motora koji su povezani tako da motor zauzima istu relativnu poziciju kao i generator (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system consisting of a generator and a motor so connected that the motor will assume the same relative position as the generator [selsyn]</p><p><b>ciklotron koji postiže relativističke brzine moduliranjem frekvencije ubrzanog električnog polja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cyclotron that achieves relativistic velocities by modulating the frequency of the accelerating electric field</p><p><b>uređaj za sinhronizaciju vrha bljeska s otvaranjem zatvarača kamere (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device used in photography to synchronize the peak of a flash with the opening of the camera shutter</p><p><b>Automobilski sustav za pomicanje zupčanika u kojem se zupčanici okreću istom brzinom i tako se glatko pomicanju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an automotive system for shifting gears in which the gears revolve at the same speed and so shift smoothly</p><p><b>koji se javljaju ili postoje u isto vrijeme ili imaju isto razdoblje ili fazu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring or existing at the same time or having the same period or phase [synchronic, synchronous]</p><p><b>sinkronicitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation that exists when things occur at the same time [synchronicity, synchronisation, synchronism, synchronization, synchronizing, synchrony]</p><p><b>sinkronijsko</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring or existing at the same time or having the same period or phase [synchronal, synchronous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with phenomena (especially language) at a particular period without considering historical antecedents</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of taxa) occurring in the same period of geological time</p><p><b>proučavanje jezika bez pomaka na njegov povijesni kontekst (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of a language without reference to its historical context</p><p><b>sinkronija, sinkronicitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation that exists when things occur at the same time [synchroneity, synchronisation, synchronism, synchronization, synchronizing, synchrony]</p><p><b>sinkronicitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation that exists when things occur at the same time [synchroneity, synchronicity, synchronism, synchronization, synchronizing, synchrony]</p><p><i>n.</i> an adjustment that causes something to occur or recur in unison [synchronising, synchronization, synchronizing]</p><p><i>n.</i> coordinating by causing to indicate the same time [synchronization, synchronizing]</p><p><b>događaju se u isto vrijeme, napraviti (zvuci filma) točno istovremeno s akcijom, organizira ili predstavlja događaje tako da se događaju istovremeno, istovremeno djeluju, uzrok da se navede isto vrijeme ili stopa, Sinkronizirati i prilagoditi u vremenu ili na način (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> happen at the same time [contemporise, contemporize, synchronize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make (motion picture sound) exactly simultaneous with the action [synchronize]</p><p><i>v.</i> arrange or represent events so that they co-occur [contemporise, contemporize, synchronize]</p><p><i>v.</i> operate simultaneously [synchronize]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to indicate the same time or rate [synchronize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make synchronous and adjust in time or manner [sync, synchronize]</p><p><b>radi u unisonu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> operating in unison [synchronized]</p><p><b>Instrument koji pokazuje jesu li dva periodična kretanja sinhrona (posebno instrument koji omogućuje pilota da sinhronizira propelere aviona koji ima dva ili više motora) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instrument that indicates whether two periodic motions are synchronous (especially an instrument that enables a pilot to synchronize the propellers of a plane that has two or more engines) [synchronizer, synchronoscope, synchroscope]</p><p><b>prilagodba koja uzrokuje da se nešto dogodi ili ponavlja u unisonu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an adjustment that causes something to occur or recur in unison [synchronisation, synchronization, synchronizing]</p><p><b>sinkronicitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation that exists when things occur at the same time [synchroneity, synchronicity, synchronisation, synchronization, synchronizing, synchrony]</p><p><b>sinkronizacija, usklađivanje, sinkronicitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation that exists when things occur at the same time [synchroneity, synchronicity, synchronisation, synchronism, synchronizing, synchrony]</p><p><i>n.</i> an adjustment that causes something to occur or recur in unison [synchronisation, synchronising, synchronizing]</p><p><i>n.</i> coordinating by causing to indicate the same time [synchronisation, synchronizing]</p><p><b>sinkronizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make synchronous and adjust in time or manner [sync, synchronise]</p><p><i>v.</i> happen at the same time [contemporise, contemporize, synchronise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make (motion picture sound) exactly simultaneous with the action [synchronise]</p><p><i>v.</i> arrange or represent events so that they co-occur [contemporise, contemporize, synchronise]</p><p><i>v.</i> operate simultaneously [synchronise]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to indicate the same time or rate [synchronise]</p><p><b>usklađen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> operating in unison [synchronised]</p><p><b>sinkronizirati (od &quot;synchronize&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instrument that indicates whether two periodic motions are synchronous (especially an instrument that enables a pilot to synchronize the propellers of a plane that has two or more engines) [synchroniser, synchronoscope, synchroscope]</p><p><b>sinkronicitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation that exists when things occur at the same time [synchroneity, synchronicity, synchronisation, synchronism, synchronization, synchrony]</p><p><i>n.</i> an adjustment that causes something to occur or recur in unison [synchronisation, synchronising, synchronization]</p><p><i>n.</i> coordinating by causing to indicate the same time [synchronisation, synchronization]</p><p><b>Instrument koji pokazuje jesu li dva periodična kretanja sinhrona (posebno instrument koji omogućuje pilota da sinhronizira propelere aviona koji ima dva ili više motora) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instrument that indicates whether two periodic motions are synchronous (especially an instrument that enables a pilot to synchronize the propellers of a plane that has two or more engines) [synchroniser, synchronizer, synchroscope]</p><p><b>istodoban, istovremen, sinkron, usklađen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring or existing at the same time or having the same period or phase [synchronal, synchronic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (digital communication) pertaining to a transmission technique that requires a common clock signal (a timing reference) between the communicating devices in order to coordinate their transmissions</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom energije od 1,15 kVA ili više, ali ne više od 2,15 kVA, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electrical converter consisting of a synchronous machine that converts alternating to direct current or vice versa [rotary, rotary converter]</p><p><b>sinkroni stroj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electric motor in which the speed of rotation is proportional to the frequency of the A.C. power</p><p><b>operacije koje se predvidivo pokreću satom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> operations that are initiated predictably by a clock</p><p><b>istodoban, istovremen, sinkron, usklađen (od &quot;synchronous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in synchrony</p><p><b>sinkronija, sinkronicitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the relation that exists when things occur at the same time [synchroneity, synchronicity, synchronisation, synchronism, synchronization, synchronizing]</p><p><b>Instrument koji pokazuje jesu li dva periodična kretanja sinhrona (posebno instrument koji omogućuje pilota da sinhronizira propelere aviona koji ima dva ili više motora) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instrument that indicates whether two periodic motions are synchronous (especially an instrument that enables a pilot to synchronize the propellers of a plane that has two or more engines) [synchroniser, synchronizer, synchronoscope]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom energije od 1,15 kVA ili većim od 2,25 kVA, ali ne većim od 2,15 kVA, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cyclotron in which the electric field is maintained at a constant frequency</p><p><b>Članovi obitelji gljiva red Chytridiales (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus family of order Chytridiales [family Synchytriaceae]</p><p><b>Jednostavne parazitske gljive uključujući parazite iz ribolovnih jezera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> simple parasitic fungi including pond scum parasites [genus Synchytrium]</p><p><b>gljivica koja uzrokuje bolest bradavica u gomoljima krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungus causing potato wart disease in potato tubers [potato wart fungus]</p><p><b>sinklinala</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> sloping downward toward each other to create a trough</p><p><b>izostaviti zvuk ili slovo u riječi, promijeniti ritam naglašavajući ili naglaskom slab ritam (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> omit a sound or letter in a word</p><p><i>v.</i> modify the rhythm by stressing or accenting a weak beat</p><p><b>naglašavajući normalno slab otkucaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> stressing a normally weak beat</p><p><b>(fonologija) gubitak zvukova unutar riječi (kao u `fo'c'sle' za `forcastle'), glazbeni ritam koji naglašava obično slab ritam, glazba (posebno plesna glazba) koja ima sinkopirani ritam (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (phonology) the loss of sounds from within a word (as in `fo'c'sle' for `forecastle') [syncope]</p><p><i>n.</i> a musical rhythm accenting a normally weak beat</p><p><i>n.</i> music (especially dance music) that has a syncopated rhythm</p><p><b>glazbenik koji svira sinkopiranu jazz glazbu (obično u plesnom sastavu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musician who plays syncopated jazz music (usually in a dance band)</p><p><b>sinkopa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spontaneous loss of consciousness caused by insufficient blood to the brain [deliquium, faint, swoon]</p><p><i>n.</i> (phonology) the loss of sounds from within a word (as in `fo'c'sle' for `forecastle') [syncopation]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na povijesnu tendenciju jezika da smanji upotrebu nagibanja, od ili karakteriziran sinkretizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a historical tendency for a language to reduce its use of inflections [syncretical, syncretistic, syncretistical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or characterized by syncretism [syncretical, syncretistic, syncretistical]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na povijesnu tendenciju jezika da smanji upotrebu nagibanja, od ili karakteriziran sinkretizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a historical tendency for a language to reduce its use of inflections [syncretic, syncretistic, syncretistical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or characterized by syncretism [syncretic, syncretistic, syncretistical]</p><p><b>postati spojeni., Ujedinjenje (suprotstavljanje ili suprotstavljanje načela) (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become fused [syncretize]</p><p><i>v.</i> unite (beliefs or conflicting principles) [syncretize]</p><p><b>sinkretizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the union (or attempted fusion) of different systems of thought or belief (especially in religion or philosophy)</p><p><i>n.</i> the fusion of originally different inflected forms (resulting in a reduction in the use of inflections)</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na povijesnu tendenciju jezika da smanji upotrebu nagibanja, od ili karakteriziran sinkretizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a historical tendency for a language to reduce its use of inflections [syncretic, syncretical, syncretistical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or characterized by syncretism [syncretic, syncretical, syncretistical]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na povijesnu tendenciju jezika da smanji upotrebu nagibanja, od ili karakteriziran sinkretizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to a historical tendency for a language to reduce its use of inflections [syncretic, syncretical, syncretistic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or characterized by syncretism [syncretic, syncretical, syncretistic]</p><p><b>postati spojeni., Ujedinjenje (suprotstavljanje ili suprotstavljanje načela) (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become fused [syncretise]</p><p><i>v.</i> unite (beliefs or conflicting principles) [syncretise]</p><p><b>masa citoplazme koja sadrži nekoliko jezgara i zatvorena je u membranu, ali nema unutarnjih staničnih granica (kao u mišićnim vlaknima) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mass of cytoplasm containing several nuclei and enclosed in a membrane but no internal cell boundaries (as in muscle fibers)</p><p><b>Rođeni defekt u kojem postoji djelomično ili potpuno vezanje dva ili više prstiju ili prstiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> birth defect in which there is partial or total webbing connecting two or more fingers or toes [syndactyly]</p><p><b>Rođeni defekt u kojem postoji djelomično ili potpuno vezanje dva ili više prstiju ili prstiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> birth defect in which there is partial or total webbing connecting two or more fingers or toes [syndactylism]</p><p><b>povezano spojnicom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> connected by a conjunction</p><p><b>osoba imenovana da predstavlja grad ili sveučilište ili korporaciju u poslovnim transakcijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one appointed to represent a city or university or corporation in business transactions</p><p><b>radikalni politički pokret koji se zalaže za stavljanje industrije i vlade pod kontrolu sindikata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radical political movement that advocates bringing industry and government under the control of labor unions</p><p><b>anarhist</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of anarchism [anarchist, nihilist]</p><p><b>sindikat, konzorcij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loose affiliation of gangsters in charge of organized criminal activities [crime syndicate, family, mob]</p><p><i>n.</i> an association of companies for some definite purpose [consortium, pool]</p><p><i>n.</i> a news agency that sells features or articles or photographs etc. to newspapers for simultaneous publication</p><p><i>v.</i> join together into a syndicate</p><p><i>v.</i> organize into or form a syndicate</p><p><i>v.</i> sell articles, television programs, or photos to several publications or independent broadcasting stations</p><p><b>spajanje u sindikat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> organizing into or administering as a syndicate</p><p><i>n.</i> selling (an article or cartoon) for publication in many magazines or newspapers at the same time</p><p><b>Poslovnik koji formira sindikat. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a businessman who forms a syndicate</p><p><b>sindrom, sindroma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a complex of concurrent things</p><p><i>n.</i> a pattern of symptoms indicative of some disease</p><p><b>sinegdoha</b></p><p><i>n.</i> substituting a more inclusive term for a less inclusive one or vice versa</p><p><b>korištenje imena dijela za ono od cjeline ili cjeline za dio (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> using the name of a part for that of the whole or the whole for the part [synecdochical]</p><p><b>korištenje imena dijela za ono od cjeline ili cjeline za dio (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> using the name of a part for that of the whole or the whole for the part [synecdochic]</p><p><b>Adhezije između iris i leće ili rožnjače koje su posljedica traume ili operacije oka ili komplikacije glaukoma ili katarakte (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> adhesions between the iris and the lens or cornea resulting from trauma or eye surgery or as a complication of glaucoma or cataract</p><p><b>red ribe bez kralježnica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> order of fishes having spineless fins [order Synentognathi]</p><p><b>veliki, često divlji bizon južne Afrike s gorenim zakrivljenim rogovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large often savage buffalo of southern Africa having upward-curving horns [Cape buffalo]</p><p><b>Suzbijanje dva samoglasnika u diftong., odvojenost tekućine od gela koja je uzrokovana kontrakcijom (kao u proizvodnji sira) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the contraction of two vowels into a diphthong [synaeresis]</p><p><i>n.</i> the separation of liquid from a gel that is caused by contraction (as in cheese making) [synaeresis]</p><p><b>sinergetski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> working together [synergistic]</p><p><b>sinergistički, sinergistični, sinergizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the working together of two things (muscles or drugs for example) to produce an effect greater than the sum of their individual effects [synergy]</p><p><i>n.</i> the theological doctrine that salvation results from the interaction of human will and divine grace</p><p><b>lijek koji povećava aktivnost drugog lijeka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug that augments the activity of another drug</p><p><b>sinergistički, sinergizam, interaktivni, sinergijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> used especially of drugs or muscles that work together so the total effect is greater than the sum of the two (or more) [interactive]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the theological doctrine of synergism</p><p><i>adj.</i> working together [synergetic]</p><p><b>(grupi) na sinergijski ili kooperativni način, (droge ili mišića) na sinergijski ili interaktivni način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (of group) in a synergistic or cooperative manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> (of drugs or muscles) in a synergistic or interactive manner</p><p><b>sinergiju</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the working together of two things (muscles or drugs for example) to produce an effect greater than the sum of their individual effects [synergism]</p><p><b>sinestezija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sensation that normally occurs in one sense modality occurs when another modality is stimulated [synaesthesia]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na sinesteziju ili su u njoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or experiencing synesthesia [synaesthetic]</p><p><b>Metafora koja iskorištava sličnost između iskustava u različitim smjerovima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a metaphor that exploits a similarity between experiences in different sense modalities</p><p><b>Smanjenje hromatina prema jednoj strani jezgre tijekom profaze mejoze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the contraction of chromatin towards one side of the nucleus during the prophase of meiosis [synizesis]</p><p><b>Irski pjesnik i dramaturg čije su drame zasnovane na ruralnom irskom životu (1871-1909) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Irish poet and playwright whose plays are based on rural Irish life (1871-1909) [Edmund John Millington Synge, J. M. Synge, John Millington Synge]</p><p><b>riblje ribe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pipefishes [family Syngnathidae]</p><p><b>vrsta rod porodice Syngnathidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the family Syngnathidae [genus Syngnathus]</p><p><b>mala (4 inča) riba pronađena kod obale Florida zaliva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small (4 inches) fish found off the Florida Gulf Coast [dwarf pipefish]</p><p><b>epifitični ili kopneni penjivi grmovi iz Srednje i Južne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> epiphytic or terrestrial climbing shrubs of Central and South America [genus Syngonium]</p><p><b>Smanjenje hromatina prema jednoj strani jezgre tijekom profaze mejoze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the contraction of chromatin towards one side of the nucleus during the prophase of meiosis [synezesis]</p><p><b>sabori, sinod, koncil</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a council convened to discuss ecclesiastical business</p><p><b>lunarni mjesec, mjesec, sinodički mjesec</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the period between successive new moons (29.531 days) [lunar month, lunation, moon]</p><p><b>riblje vrste (Solea spp.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> soft-finned bottom-dwelling fishes [family Synodontidae]</p><p><b>s muškim i ženskim reproduktivnim organima pomiješanim u istom gametoecium (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having male and female reproductive organs mixed in the same gametoecium [synoicous]</p><p><b>s muškim i ženskim reproduktivnim organima pomiješanim u istom gametoecium (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having male and female reproductive organs mixed in the same gametoecium [synoecious]</p><p><b>sinonim, bliskoznačnica, istoznačnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> two words that can be interchanged in a context are said to be synonymous relative to that context [equivalent word]</p><p><b>tezaurus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a book containing a classified list of synonyms [thesaurus]</p><p><b>Student sinonimima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a student of synonyms</p><p><b>bliskoznačnost, istoznačnost, sinonimija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the semantic relation that holds between two words that can (in a given context) express the same meaning [synonymousness, synonymy]</p><p><b>istoznačan, sinoniman, srodan po značenju</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of words) meaning the same or nearly the same</p><p><b>istoznačan, sinoniman, srodan po značenju (od &quot;synonymous&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a synonymous manner</p><p><b>bliskoznačnost, istoznačnost, sinonimija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the semantic relation that holds between two words that can (in a given context) express the same meaning [synonymity, synonymy]</p><p><b>bliskoznačnost, istoznačnost, sinonimija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the semantic relation that holds between two words that can (in a given context) express the same meaning [synonymity, synonymousness]</p><p><b>kratki sadržaj, pregled, sinopsis, sažetak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sketchy summary of the main points of an argument or theory [abstract, outline, precis]</p><p><b>pregledan, sinoptičan, sinoptički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> presenting a summary or general view of a whole</p><p><i>adj.</i> presenting or taking the same point of view [synoptical]</p><p><b>prva tri evanđelja koja opisuju događaje u životu Krista s sličnog gledišta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first three Gospels which describe events in Christ's life from a similar point of view [Synoptics]</p><p><b>koji predstavljaju ili imaju isti stav (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> presenting or taking the same point of view [synoptic]</p><p><b>pregledan, sinoptičan, sinoptički (od &quot;synoptic&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the first three Gospels which describe events in Christ's life from a similar point of view [Synoptic Gospels]</p><p><b>Viskidna lubrikantna tekućina izlučena membranskim oblozima i sluznicama tetiva itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> viscid lubricating fluid secreted by the membrane lining joints and tendon sheaths etc. [synovial fluid]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na sinoviju ili je luče (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or secreting synovia</p><p><b>Viskidna lubrikantna tekućina izlučena membranskim oblozima i sluznicama tetiva itd. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> viscid lubricating fluid secreted by the membrane lining joints and tendon sheaths etc. [synovia]</p><p><b>articulatio synovialis, diarthrosis, diartroza, juncura synovialis, pokretni zglob, pravi zglob, sinovijalni zglob</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a joint so articulated as to move freely [articulatio synovialis, diarthrosis]</p><p><b>tanka membrana u sinovijalnim zglobovima koja obložava kapsulnu zglob i izlučuje sinovijalnu tekućinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin membrane in synovial (freely moving) joints that lines the joint capsule and secretes synovial fluid [synovium]</p><p><b>upal sinovijalne membrane koja obložava sinovijalni zglob (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the synovial membrane that lines a synovial joint</p><p><b>tanka membrana u sinovijalnim zglobovima koja obložava kapsulnu zglob i izlučuje sinovijalnu tekućinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thin membrane in synovial (freely moving) joints that lines the joint capsule and secretes synovial fluid [synovial membrane]</p><p><b>riječi ili fraze koja ima smisao samo kada se pojavljuje u društvu drugih riječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a word or phrase meaningful only when it occurs in the company of other words</p><p><b>skup jednog ili više sinonimova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a set of one or more synonyms</p><p><b>sintaktički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or conforming to the rules of syntax [syntactical]</p><p><b>gramatička kategorija, sintaktička kategorija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (grammar) a category of words having the same grammatical properties [grammatical category]</p><p><b>sintatkički, sintaktički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or conforming to the rules of syntax [syntactic]</p><p><b>sintaktički</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to syntax</p><p><b>lingvista koji se specijalizira za proučavanje gramatike i sintakse (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a linguist who specializes in the study of grammar and syntax [grammarian]</p><p><b>sintagma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a syntactic string of words that forms a part of some larger syntactic unit [syntagma]</p><p><b>sintagma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a syntactic string of words that forms a part of some larger syntactic unit [syntagm]</p><p><b>povezane kao članovi sintagme (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> related as members of a syntagma</p><p><b>gramatika, morfologija, sintaksa, skladnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the grammatical arrangement of words in sentences [phrase structure, sentence structure]</p><p><i>n.</i> a systematic orderly arrangement</p><p><i>n.</i> studies of the rules for forming admissible sentences</p><p><b>Program za provjeru sintakse prirodnog jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a program to check natural language syntax</p><p><b>pogreška u programu nastala povredom pravila progr, sintaktička pogreška</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an error of language resulting from code that does not conform to the syntax of the programming language</p><p><b>jezik koji se koristi za opisivanje sintakse drugog jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a language used to describe the syntax of another language</p><p><b>sinteza, dedukcija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of producing a chemical compound (usually by the union of simpler chemical compounds)</p><p><i>n.</i> the combination of ideas into a complex whole [synthetic thinking]</p><p><i>n.</i> reasoning from the general to the particular (or from cause to effect) [deduction, deductive reasoning]</p><p><b>sintetizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> combine so as to form a more complex, product [synthesize]</p><p><b>sintesajzer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an intellectual who synthesizes or uses synthetic methods [synthesist, synthesizer]</p><p><i>n.</i> (music) an electronic instrument (usually played with a keyboard) that generates and modifies sounds electronically and can imitate a variety of other musical instruments [synthesizer]</p><p><b>intelektualci koji sintetiziraju ili koriste sintetičke metode. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an intellectual who synthesizes or uses synthetic methods [synthesiser, synthesizer]</p><p><b>sastaviti, sintetizirao, sintetizirati, spajati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> combine so as to form a more complex, product [synthesise]</p><p><i>v.</i> combine and form a synthesis</p><p><b>sintesajzer, sintetizator</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an intellectual who synthesizes or uses synthetic methods [synthesiser, synthesist]</p><p><i>n.</i> (music) an electronic instrument (usually played with a keyboard) that generates and modifies sounds electronically and can imitate a variety of other musical instruments [synthesiser]</p><p><b>sintetičan, sintetički, sintetske, sintetski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound made artificially by chemical reactions [synthetic substance]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not of natural origin [man-made, semisynthetic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> involving or of the nature of synthesis (combining separate elements to form a coherent whole) as opposed to analysis [synthetical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> systematic combining of root and modifying elements into single words</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a proposition whose truth value is determined by observation or facts [synthetical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> artificial as if portrayed in a film [celluloid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> not genuine or natural</p><p><b>Kasna faza kubizma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the late phase of cubism</p><p><b>Sastav za proizvodnju vlakana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fiber created from natural materials or by chemical processes [man-made fiber]</p><p><b>sintetički narkotni lijek sličan morfiju, ali manje navikavajući (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> synthetic narcotic drug similar to morphine but less habit-forming [dolophine hydrochloride, fixer, methadon, methadone, methadone hydrochloride]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od 99,99% ili više, ali ne više od 99,99% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a resin having a polymeric structure</p><p><b>sintetička guma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various synthetic elastic materials whose properties resemble natural rubber [rubber]</p><p><b>Spoj koji se umjetno proizvodi kemijskim reakcijama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a compound made artificially by chemical reactions [synthetic]</p><p><b>sinteza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the combination of ideas into a complex whole [synthesis]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) Uredbe (EZ) br., tvrdnje čija je vrijednost istine određena promatranjem ili činjenicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving or of the nature of synthesis (combining separate elements to form a coherent whole) as opposed to analysis [synthetic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a proposition whose truth value is determined by observation or facts [synthetic]</p><p><b>sintezom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by synthesis</p><p><b>sintetizam</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genre of French painting characterized by bright flat shapes and symbolic treatments of abstract ideas</p><p><b>uobičajena venerična bolest uzrokovana treponemom pallidum spirochetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common venereal disease caused by the treponema pallidum spirochete [lues, lues venerea, pox, syphilis]</p><p><b>uobičajena venerična bolest uzrokovana treponemom pallidum spirochetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common venereal disease caused by the treponema pallidum spirochete [lues, lues venerea, pox, syph]</p><p><b>osoba koja boluje od sifilisa, od ili povezane s ili zaražene sifilisom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person suffering from syphilis</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or infected with syphilis</p><p><b>sifon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tube running from the liquid in a vessel to a lower level outside the vessel so that gravity forces the liquid through the tube [siphon]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tubular organ in an aquatic animal (especially in mollusks) through which water can be taken in or expelled [siphon]</p><p><i>v.</i> convey, draw off, or empty by or as if by a siphon [siphon, siphon off]</p><p><b>Syracuse</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in central New York</p><p><i>n.</i> a city in southeastern Sicily that was founded by Corinthians in the 8th century BC [Siracusa]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Roman siege of Syracuse (214-212 BC) was eventually won by the Romans who sacked the city (killing Archimedes) [siege of Syracuse]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Athenian siege of Syracuse (415-413 BC) was eventually won by Syracuse [siege of Syracuse]</p><p><b>Sirija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an Asian republic in the Middle East at the east end of the Mediterranean [Syrian Arab Repu