gence that is required for the planning and conduct of tactical operations [combat intelligence]</p><p><b>manevar, taktički potez</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a move made to gain a tactical end [maneuver, manoeuvre, tactical manoeuvre]</p><p><b>manevar, taktički potez</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a move made to gain a tactical end [maneuver, manoeuvre, tactical maneuver]</p><p><b>(vojni) upozorenje nakon početka neprijateljskog čina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (military) a warning after the initiation of a hostile act</p><p><b>taktičan, taktički (od &quot;tactical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with regard to tactics</p><p><b>taktičar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is skilled at planning tactics</p><p><b>taktika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of military science dealing with detailed maneuvers to achieve objectives set by strategy</p><p><i>n.</i> a plan for attaining a particular goal [maneuver, manoeuvre, tactic]</p><p><b>dodirni, opipljiv, osjetan, taktilan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or proceeding from the sense of touch [haptic, tactual]</p><p><i>adj.</i> producing a sensation of touch [tactual]</p><p><b>gubitak sposobnosti prepoznavanja predmeta prilikom rukovanja njima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loss of the ability to recognize objects by handling them [astereognosis]</p><p><b>opip, taktilno svojstvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a property perceived by touch [feel]</p><p><b>dodir, osjet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sensation produced by pressure receptors in the skin [feeling, tactual sensation, touch, touch sensation]</p><p><b>opipljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the faculty of perceiving (via the skin) pressure or heat or pain [skin perceptiveness, tactual sensation, touch perception]</p><p><b>bez takta, netaktičan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> lacking or showing a lack of what is fitting and considerate in dealing with others [untactful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> revealing lack of perceptiveness or judgment or finesse [inept]</p><p><b>bez takta, netaktičan (od &quot;tactless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> without tact</p><p><b>bez takta, manjak takta, neobaziranje, neobzirnost, netaktienost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of lacking tact</p><p><b>taktilan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or proceeding from the sense of touch [haptic, tactile]</p><p><i>adj.</i> producing a sensation of touch [tactile]</p><p><b>metoda ispitivanja u kojoj ispitivač osjeća veličinu ili oblik ili čvrstoću ili mjesto nečega (delova tijela ako je ispitivač zdravstveni radnik) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a method of examination in which the examiner feels the size or shape or firmness or location of something (of body parts when the examiner is a health professional) [palpation]</p><p><b>dodir, osjet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sensation produced by pressure receptors in the skin [feeling, tactile sensation, touch, touch sensation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the faculty of perceiving (via the skin) pressure or heat or pain [skin perceptiveness, tactility, touch perception]</p><p><b>taktilan (od &quot;tactual&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by touch [haptically]</p><p><b>malo ili stepen razlike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slight amount or degree of difference [shade]</p><p><b>lijek za povećanje viriliteta (trgovinski naziv Cialis) koji se koristi za liječenje erektilne disfunkcije kod muškaraca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> virility drug (trade name Cialis) used to treat erectile dysfunction in men [Cialis]</p><p><b>Štakori s slobodnim repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> freetail bats [genus Tadarida]</p><p><b>Obični šišmiša s slobodnim repom iz južnih Sjedinjenih Država s kratkim baršunastim krznom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the common freetail bat of southern United States having short velvety fur [Mexican freetail bat, guano bat]</p><p><b>Švicarski kemičar rođen u Poljskoj. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Swiss chemist born in Poland [Reichstein]</p><p><b>Poljski patriota i vojnik koji se borio s Amerikancima u Američkoj revoluciji (1746-1817) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Polish patriot and soldier who fought with Americ