hority and possibly with force [arrogate, assume, seize, usurp]</p><p><i>v.</i> take on titles, offices, duties, responsibilities [adopt, assume, take on]</p><p><i>v.</i> free someone temporarily from his or her obligations [relieve]</p><p><i>v.</i> take on as one's own the expenses or debts of another person [accept, assume, bear]</p><p><i>v.</i> take over ownership of [buy out, buy up]</p><p><i>v.</i> do over [repeat]</p><p><i>v.</i> take up and practice as one's own [adopt, borrow, take up]</p><p><i>v.</i> take up, as of debts or payments [absorb]</p><p><b>posebno se potruditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> try very hard to do something [be at pains]</p><p><b>sudjelovanja, sudjelovati, participirati, učestvovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> share in something [participate]</p><p><b>desiti se, dešavati se, održava se, odvijati se, sjedati, događati se, dogoditi se, odigrati se, odigravati se, održati se, održavati se, odviti se, zbiti se, zbivati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come to pass [come about, fall out, go on, hap, happen, occur, pass, pass off]</p><p><b>biti ponosan na (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> feel proud of [pride oneself]</p><p><b>smiriti se, smjestiti se, snaći se, uklopiti se, ukorijeniti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become settled or established and stable in one's residence or life style [root, settle, settle down, steady down]</p><p><b>razviti u prepoznatljiv entitet (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> develop into a distinctive entity [form, spring, take form]</p><p><b>podržati nekoga (kao u raspravi) (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> support someone (as in an argument) [take someone's side]</p><p><b>podržati nekoga (kao u raspravi) (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> support someone (as in an argument) [take sides with]</p><p><b>Privući pažnju na sebe. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> attract attention onto oneself [take the stage]</p><p><b>ispitati, ispitivati, protresati, protresti, proučavati, proučiti, razmatrati, razmotriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to look at critically or searchingly, or in minute detail [scrutinise,