b>bez talenta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> devoid of talent [untalented]</p><p><b>Nedostatak talenta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lack of talent</p><p><b>dostavljač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who gossips indiscreetly [blabbermouth, talebearer, tattler, tattletale, telltale]</p><p><b>fundamentalistička islamska milicija. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fundamentalist Islamic militia [Taleban]</p><p><b>luka i brodogradni centar na sjeveroistoku Kine na poluotoku Liaodong (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a port and shipbuilding center in northeastern China on the Liaodong Peninsula [Dairen, Dalian]</p><p><b>rod uglavnom američkih više-manje sočnih biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of mainly American more-or-less succulent herbs [genus Talinum]</p><p><b>sličan Talinum aurantiacum, ali sa uskim listovima i žuto-narandžastom cvjetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> similar to Talinum aurantiacum but with narrower leaves and yellow-orange flowers [narrow-leaved flame flower]</p><p><b>biljka s mesnatim korijenima i uspravnim stabljikama s uskim sočnim lištima i jednim crvenkasto-narandžastim cvijetom u svakoj gornjoj oslozi lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant with fleshy roots and erect stems with narrow succulent leaves and one reddish-orange flower in each upper leaf axil [flame-flower, flame flower, flameflower]</p><p><b>niska biljka sa guštim uskim sočnim lišcima i prilično velikim duboko ružičastim oslinskim cvijećima koji izgledaju kao da sjede na zemlji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low plant with crowded narrow succulent leaves and fairly large deep pink axillary flowers that seem to sit on the ground [pigmy talinum]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka s ružičastim cvjetovima iz stjenovitih regija zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pink-flowered perennial of rocky regions of western United States [rock pink]</p><p><b>uspravna biljka s gomoljastim korijenima i krajnjim panicama crvenih do žutih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect plant with tuberous roots and terminal panicles of red to yellow flowers [jewels-of-opar]</p><p><b>nizak biljka koja stvara jastuke s ružastom do crvenokrasno-mažintom cvjetom i srednjim rebrima lišća koji ostaju kao trnje kada lišće umre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> low cushion-forming plant with rose to crimson-magenta flowers and leaf midribs that persist as spines when the leaves die [spiny talinum]</p><p><b>s deformiranom stopom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a deformed foot [clubfooted]</p><p><b>urodna deformacija stopala obično obilježena zakrivljenim oblikom ili iskrivljenim položajem gležnja i pete i prstiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> congenital deformity of the foot usually marked by a curled shape or twisted position of the ankle and heel and toes [clubfoot]</p><p><b>talipes u kojima su prsti na nogama upućeni prema gore i osoba hoda na pete stopala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> talipes in which the toes are pointed upward and the person walks on the heel of the foot</p><p><b>talipes u kojima su prsti upereni prema dolje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> talipes in which the toes are pointed downward</p><p><b>deformacija stopala u kojoj je stopala iskrivljena prema van (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deformity of the foot in which the foot is twisted outward</p><p><b>visoka palma južne Indije i Šri Lanke s ogromnim listovima koji se koriste kao kišobrani i ventilatori ili se režu u trake za pisanje papira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall palm of southern India and Sri Lanka with gigantic leaves used as umbrellas and fans or cut into strips for writing paper [Corypha umbraculifera, talipot palm]</p><p><b>visoka palma južne Indije i Šri Lanke s ogromnim listovima koji se koriste kao kišobrani i ventilatori ili se režu u trake za pisanje papira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall palm of southern India and Sri Lanka with gigantic leaves used as umbrellas and fans or cut into strips for writing paper [Corypha umbraculifera, talipot]</p><p><b>talisman, amulet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trinket or piece of jewelry usually hung about the neck and thought to be a magical protection against evil or disease [amulet]</p><p><b>talisman (od &quot;talisman&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> possessing or believed to possess magic power especially protective power</p><p><b>brbljati, diskusija, ekspoze, govor, govoriti, odgovarati, pričati, razgovarati, razgovor, razgovarati se, konverzacija, predavanje, ispričati, izgovarati, izgovoriti, izreći, izricati, kazati, kazivati, prozboriti, reći, verbalizirati, zboriti, predavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an exchange of ideas via conversation [talking]</p><p><i>n.</i> discussion</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of giving a talk to an audience</p><p><i>n.</i> a speech that is open to the public [lecture, public lecture]</p><p><i>n.</i> idle gossip or rumor [talk of the town]</p><p><i>v.</i> exchange thoughts [speak]</p><p><i>v.</i> express in speech [mouth, speak, utter, verbalise, verbalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> use language [speak]</p><p><i>v.</i> reveal information [spill]</p><p><i>v.</i> divulge confidential information or secrets [babble, babble out, blab, blab out, let the cat out of the bag, peach, sing, spill the beans, tattle]</p><p><i>v.</i> deliver a lecture or talk [lecture]</p><p><b>ispričati, raspravljati, diskutirati, divaniti, govoriti, raspredati, razglabati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to consider or examine in speech or writing [discourse, discuss]</p><p><i>v.</i> discuss or mention [talk of]</p><p><b>Smanjivanje kroz razgovor., Govori ponizno, kao da si s djetetom, Upravljanje zrakoplovom (plet zrakoplova tijekom slijetanja) putem radija (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> belittle through talk</p><p><i>v.</i> speak in a condescending manner, as if to a child</p><p><i>v.</i> direct and control (the flight of an airplane during landing) via radio</p><p><b>nagovoriti, nagovarati, potaknuti, potaći, poticati, privoljeti, uvjeravati, uvjeriti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> persuade somebody to do something</p><p><b>diskutirati, divaniti, govoriti, raspredati, razglabati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> discuss or mention [talk about]</p><p><b>beskorisni tračevi ili glasine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> idle gossip or rumor [talk]</p><p><b>odgovarati, odgovoriti, odvratiti, odvraćati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> persuade someone not to do something</p><p><b>pretresti, raspravljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> speak with others about (something) [discuss, hash out]</p><p><b>Razgovarajte o stvarima vezanih uz posao. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> discuss matters that are related to work</p><p><b>Program u kojem poznati ljudi raspravljaju o temi ili odgovore na pitanja koja slušatelji postavljaju telefonom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a program during which well-known people discuss a topic or answer questions telephoned in by the audience [chat show]</p><p><b>dogovarati, dogovoriti, pregovarati, sporazumijevati se, sporazumjeti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> discuss the terms of an arrangement [negociate, negotiate]</p><p><b>govori neiskreno ili bez obzira na činjenice ili istine (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> speak insincerely or without regard for facts or truths [bull, bullshit, fake]</p><p><b>otvoreno razgovarate, često u poslovnom kontekstu (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> discuss frankly, often in a business context</p><p><b>brbljav, brbljiv, pričljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of trivial conversation [chatty, gabby, garrulous, loquacious, talky]</p><p><i>adj.</i> unwisely talking too much [bigmouthed, blabbermouthed, blabby]</p><p><i>adj.</i> friendly and open and willing to talk [expansive]</p><p><b>brbljav (od &quot;talkative&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a chatty loquacious manner [garrulously, loquaciously, talkily]</p><p><b>brbljav (od &quot;talkative&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being wordy and talkative [garrulity, garrulousness, loquaciousness, loquacity]</p><p><b>govornik, pošiljatelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who expresses in language [speaker, utterer, verbaliser, verbalizer]</p><p><b>identifikacija osobe po glasu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> identification of a person from the sound of their voice [speaker