ijena smolom i prekrivena perjem kao kazna. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> smeared with tar and covered with feathers as a punishment</p><p><b>Čin zadržavanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of tarrying [lingering]</p><p><b>mali rod drveća iz istočne Azije i Australije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small genus of east Asian and Australian timber trees [genus Tarrietia]</p><p><b>Australsko drvo (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Australian timber tree [silver tree]</p><p><b>namazan katranom, odugovlačiti, bazati, dangubiti, džabalebariti, tumarati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be about [footle, hang around, lallygag, linger, loaf, loiter, lollygag, lounge, lurk, mess about, mill about, mill around]</p><p><i>v.</i> leave slowly and hesitantly [linger]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the characteristics of pitch or tar [pitchy, resinous, resiny]</p><p><b>bilo koja kost tarsa, od ili u vezi s ili u blizini tarsa stopala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any bone of the tarsus [tarsal bone]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or near the tarsus of the foot</p><p><b>bilo koja kost tarsa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any bone of the tarsus [tarsal]</p><p><b>dugačka lojna žlijezda koja podmazuje kapke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long sebaceous gland that lubricates the eyelids [Meibomian gland]</p><p><b>avetnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nocturnal arboreal primate of Indonesia and the Philippines having huge eyes and digits ending in pads to facilitate climbing</p><p><b>Koekstenzivni s rodom Tarsius: tarsieri (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> coextensive with the genus Tarsius: tarsiers [family Tarsiidae]</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama dodijeljenim podredu Prosimii (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications assigned to the suborder Prosimii [suborder Tarsioidea]</p><p><b>upale kapaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of the eyelid</p><p><b>vrsta i jedini rod obitelji Tarsiidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type and sole genus of the family Tarsiidae [genus Tarsius]</p><p><b>različite vrste tarsija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variet