artaric acid</p><p><b>Tartu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city of southeastern Estonia that was a member of the Hanseatic League</p><p><b>Tartuffe</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hypocrite who pretends to religious piety (after the protagonist in a play by Moliere) [Tartuffe]</p><p><b>Tartuffe</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hypocrite who pretends to religious piety (after the protagonist in a play by Moliere) [Tartufe]</p><p><b>Svaka od različitih smočastih žlijezdastih biljaka rodova Madia, bilo koja od različitih zapadne američke biljke roda Grindelia s smočastim lišćama i stabljikama koje su ranije korištene u medicini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various resinous glandular plants of the genus Madia</p><p><i>n.</i> any of various western American plants of the genus Grindelia having resinous leaves and stems formerly used medicinally [gum plant, gumweed, rosinweed]</p><p><b>Šumovi iz Novog Zelanda, Novi Zeland srebrni bor sa konicnim oblikom i dugim vitkim, fleksibilnim granama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> New Zealand shrub [Dacrydium bidwilli, Halocarpus bidwilli, New Zealand mountain pine, tar-wood]</p><p><i>n.</i> New Zealand silver pine of conical habit with long slender flexuous branches [Dacrydium colensoi, tar-wood]</p><p><b>Tarzan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (sometimes used ironically) a man of great strength and agility (after the hero of a series of novels by Edgar Rice Burroughs)</p><p><i>n.</i> a man raised by apes who was the hero of a series of novels by Edgar Rice Burroughs [Tarzan of the Apes]</p><p><b>Tarzan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a man raised by apes who was the hero of a series of novels by Edgar Rice Burroughs [Tarzan]</p><p><b>Taškent</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital of Uzbekistan [Taskent, capital of Uzbek]</p><p><b>Nabuov suprug (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> consort of Nabu [Tashmitum]</p><p><b>Nabuov suprug (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> consort of Nabu [Tashmit]</p><p><b>Ludi Konj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chief of the Sioux who resisted the invasion of the Black Hills and joined Sitting Bull