> characterizing or showing skill in or specialized knowledge of applied arts and sciences</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a practical subject that is organized according to scientific principles [technological]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or concerned with machinery or tools [mechanical, mechanically skillful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> according to strict interpretation of the law or set of rules</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or requiring special knowledge to be understood [expert]</p><p><i>adj.</i> resulting from or dependent on market factors rather than fundamental economic considerations</p><p><b>tehnička analiza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (stock exchange) analysis of past price changes in the hope of forecasting future price changes [technical analysis of stock trends]</p><p><b>(borza) analiza prošlih promjena cijena u nadi da će se predvidjeti buduće promjene cijena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (stock exchange) analysis of past price changes in the hope of forecasting future price changes [technical analysis]</p><p><b>analitičar na berzi koji pokušava predvidjeti tržišne trendove na temelju grafikona nedavnih cijena vrijednosnih papira. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stock market analyst who tries to predict market trends from graphs of recent prices of securities [chartist]</p><p><b>tehnička greška</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (basketball) a foul that can be assessed on a player or a coach or a team for unsportsmanlike conduct [technical]</p><p><b>sadrže male količine drugih kemikalija, stoga su blago nečiste (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing small amounts of other chemicals, hence slightly impure [technical-grade]</p><p><b>KO koji je proglasio sudac koji je odlučio da jedan boksač ne može nastaviti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a knockout declared by the referee who judges one boxer unable to continue [TKO]</p><p><b>tehnička škola</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a school teaching mechanical and industrial arts and the applied sciences [tech]</p><p><b>podčuvnik nižeg ranga od narednika u zrakoplovstvu ili mornarici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a noncommissioned officer ranking below a master sergeant in the air force or marines</p><p><b>sadrže male količine drugih kemikalija, stoga su blago nečiste (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> containing small amounts of other chemicals, hence slightly impure [technical grade]</p><p><b>propis, tehnička priroda, tehnička svojstva</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being technical as in the use of technical terms or methods</p><p><i>n.</i> a specific detail in a set of rules or terms belonging to a particular field</p><p><b>stručno, tehnički</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with regard to technique</p><p><i>adv.</i> with regard to technical skill and the technology available</p><p><i>adv.</i> according to the exact meaning</p><p><b>tehničar, tehnički stručnjak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone whose occupation involves training in a specific technical process</p><p><i>n.</i> someone known for high skill in some intellectual or artistic technique</p><p><b>S druge strane, u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje druga metoda, to znači da se ne primjenjuje druga metoda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a trademarked method of making color motion pictures</p><p><b>metoda, metoda rada, način izvođenja, postupak, tehnika, vještina, stručnost, umijeće</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a practical method or art applied to some particular task</p><p><i>n.</i> skillfulness in the command of fundamentals deriving from practice and familiarity [proficiency]</p><p><b>techno</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a style of fast heavy electronic dance music usually without vocals</p><p><b>tehnički žargoni iz računalstva i drugih visokotehnoloških predmeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> technical jargon from computing and other high-tech subjects</p><p><b>tehnokracija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of government in which scientists and technical experts are in control</p><p><b>stručnjak koji je član visoko kvalificirane elitne skupine., zagovornik tehnokratije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expert who is a member of a highly skilled elite group</p><p><i>n.</i> an advocate of technocracy</p><p><b>tehnološka, tehnološki, tehnički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> based in scientific and industrial progress</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a practical subject that is organized according to scientific principles [technical]</p><p><b>industrijska revolucija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the transformation from an agricultural to an industrial nation [Industrial Revolution]</p><p><b>tehnološka, tehnološki (od &quot;technological&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by means of technology</p><p><b>tehnolog, inženjer, tehničar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who uses scientific knowledge to solve practical problems [applied scientist, engineer]</p><p><b>inženjerstvo, tehnika, tehnologija, tehnološki, tehnologije, tehnologiju, tehničko-tehnološka znanost, tehnološka znanost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the application of the knowledge and usage of tools (such as machines or utensils) and techniques to control one's environment</p><p><i>n.</i> the discipline dealing with the art or science of applying scientific knowledge to practical problems [applied science, engineering, engineering science]</p><p><i>n.</i> machinery and equipment developed from engineering or other applied sciences</p><p><b>Agencija u Ministarstvu trgovine koja radi s industrijama Sjedinjenih Država za promicanje konkurentnosti i maksimiziranje utjecaja tehnologije na gospodarski rast. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agency in the Department of Commerce that works with United States industries to promote competitiveness and maximize the impact of technology on economic growth</p><p><b>osoba koja je oduševljena novom tehnologijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is enthusiastic about new technology</p><p><b>entuzijazam za nove tehnologije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> enthusiasm for new technology</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili pokazuju tehnofiliju (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or showing technophilia</p><p><b>osoba koja ne voli ili izbjegava nove 