o pogodak (1918-2002) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States baseball player noted as a hitter (1918-2002) [Ted Williams, Williams]</p><p><b>Posljednji car ujedinjenog Rimskog carstva, preuzeo je kontrolu nad istočnim carstvom i okončao rat sa Vizigotima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the last emperor of a united Roman Empire, he took control of the eastern empire and ended the war with the Visigoths [Flavius Theodosius, Theodosius I, Theodosius the Great]</p><p><b>Posljednji car ujedinjenog Rimskog carstva, preuzeo je kontrolu nad istočnim carstvom i okončao rat sa Vizigotima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the last emperor of a united Roman Empire, he took control of the eastern empire and ended the war with the Visigoths [Flavius Theodosius, Theodosius, Theodosius the Great]</p><p><b>Posljednji car ujedinjenog Rimskog carstva, preuzeo je kontrolu nad istočnim carstvom i okončao rat sa Vizigotima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the last emperor of a united Roman Empire, he took control of the eastern empire and ended the war with the Visigoths [Flavius Theodosius, Theodosius, Theodosius I]</p><p><b>teogonija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the study of the origins and genealogy of the gods</p><p><b>bogoslov, teolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is learned in theology or who speculates about theology [theologiser, theologist, theologizer]</p><p><b>teološki</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or concerning theology</p><p><b>nauku jedne vjerske skupine. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the doctrine of a religious group</p><p><b>bogoslovlje, teologija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a particular system or school of religious beliefs and teachings [theology]</p><p><b>duhovna vrlina, teološka vrlina, vjerska vrlina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> according to Christian ethics: one of the three virtues (faith, hope, and charity) created by God to round out the natural virtues [supernatural virtue]</p><p><b>teološki (od &quot;theological&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> as regards theology</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a theological manner</p><p><b>tretirati iz teološkog stajališta ili dati teološki karakter, da se radi o teorijskim spekulacijama o teologiji ili raspravlja o teološkim temama (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> treat from a theological viewpoint or render theological in character [theologize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make theoretical speculations about theology or discuss theological subjects [theologize]</p><p><b>bogoslov, teolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is learned in theology or who speculates about theology [theologian, theologist, theologizer]</p><p><b>bogoslov, teolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is learned in theology or who speculates about theology [theologian, theologiser, theologizer]</p><p><b>tretirati iz teološkog stajališta ili dati teološki karakter, da se radi o teorijskim spekulacijama o teologiji ili raspravlja o teološkim temama (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> treat from a theological viewpoint or render theological in character [theologise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make theoretical speculations about theology or discuss theological subjects [theologise]</p><p><b>bogoslov, teolog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is learned in theology or who speculates about theology [theologian, theologiser, theologist]</p><p><b>bogoslovlje, teologija, teologije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the rational and systematic study of religion and its influences and of the nature of religious truth [divinity]</p><p><i>n.</i> a particular system or school of religious beliefs and teachings [theological system]</p><p><i>n.</i> the learned profession acquired by specialized courses in religion (usually taught at a college or seminary)</p><p><b>vidljiva (ali ne nužno materijalna) manifestacija božanstva ljudskoj osobi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a visible (but not necessarily material) manifestation of a deity to a human person</p><p><b>obitelj uglavnom tropskih američkih stabala i grmova sličnih onima iz Myrsinaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of mainly tropical American trees and shrubs similar to those of the Myrsinaceae [family Theophrastaceae]</p><p><b>Grčki filozof koji je bio učenik Aristotela i koji je naslijedio Aristotela kao vođa Peripatetika (371-287 pr. n. e.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek philosopher who was a student of Aristotle and who succeeded Aristotle as the leader of the Peripatetics (371-287 BC)</p><p><b>Švicarski liječnik koji je na temelju svojih promatranja i iskustva uveo tretmane za određene bolesti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Swiss physician who introduced treatments of particular illnesses based on his observation and experience [Paracelsus, Philippus Aureolus Paracelsus]</p><p><b>bezbojni kristalni alkaloid dobiven od čajnih listova ili sintetički proizveden (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless crystalline alkaloid derived from tea leaves or made synthetically [Elixophyllin, Slo-Bid, Theobid]</p><p><b>pravilo, teorem, teorema, tvrdnja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a proposition deducible from basic postulates</p><p><i>n.</i> an idea accepted as a demonstrable truth</p><p><b>čisto misaoni, teorijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned primarily with theories or hypotheses rather than practical considerations [theoretical]</p><p><b>teorijske, teorijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned primarily with theories or hypotheses rather than practical considerations [theoretic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with theories rather than their practical applications</p><p><b>model</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hypothetical description of a complex entity or process [framework, model]</p><p><b>teorijski</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in theory</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a theoretical manner</p><p><b>teoretičar, teoretik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who theorizes (especially in science or art) [idealogue, theoriser, theorist, theorizer]</p><p><b>proizvodnja ili korištenje teorija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the production or use of theories [theorization]</p><p><b>filozofirati, pretpostaviti, pretpostavljati, spekulirati, teoretizirati, umovati, vjerovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to believe especially on uncertain or tentative grounds [conjecture, hypothecate, hypothesise, hypothesize, speculate, suppose, theorize]</p><p><b>teoretik, teoretičar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who theorizes (especially in science or art) [idealogue, theoretician, theorist, theorizer]</p><p><b>teoretik, teoretičar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who theorizes (especially in science or art) [idealogue, theoretician, theoriser, theorizer]</p><p><b>proizvodnja ili korištenje teorija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the production or use of theories [theorisation]</p><p><b>filozofirati, pretpostaviti, pretpostavljati, spekulirati, teoretizirati, umovati, vjerovati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> to believe especially on uncertain or tentative grounds [conjecture, hypothecate, hypothesise, hypothesize, speculate, suppose, theorise]</p><p><i>v.</i> construct a theory about</p><p><i>v.</i> form or construct theories</p><p><b>teoretik, teoretičar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who theorizes (especially in science or art) [idealogue, theoretician, theoriser, theorist]</p><p><b>teorija, teorije, teoriji</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a well-substantiated explanation of some aspect of the natural world</p><p><i>n.</i> a tentative insight into the natural world [hypothesis, possibility]</p><p><i>n.</i> a belief that can guide behavior</p><p><b>(hemija) teorija koja opisuje vodene rastvore u smislu kiselina (koji se disoziiraju da daju vodikove ione) i baza (koji se disoziiraju da daju hidroksilne ione) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) theory that describes aqueous solutions in terms of acids (which dissociate to give hydrogen ions) and bases (which dissociate to give hydroxyl ions) [Arrhenius theory of dissociation, theory of electrolytic dissociation]</p><p><b>(hemija) teorija koja opisuje vodene rastvore u smislu kiselina (koji se disoziiraju da daju vodikove ione) i baza (koji se disoziiraju da daju hidroksilne ione) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) theory that describes aqueous solutions in terms of acids (which dissociate to give hydrogen ions) and bases (which dissociate to give hydroxyl ions) [Arrhenius theory of dissociation, theory of dissociation]</p><p><b>(biologija) znanstvena teorija o podrijetlu vrsta biljaka i životinja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) a scientific theory of the origin of species of plants and animals [evolutionism, theory of organic evolution]</p><p><b>(ekonomika) teorija natjecanja izražena u smislu dobitaka i gubitaka među protivničkim igračima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (economics) a theory of competition stated in terms of gains and losses among opposing players [game theory]</p><p><b>(fizička) teorija da se bilo koje dvije čestice materije međusobno privlače silom koja je direktno proporcionalna sa proizvodom njihovih masa i obrnuto proporcionalna kvadratu udaljenosti između njih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the theory that any two particles of matter attract one another with a force directly proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them [Newton's theory of gravitation, gravitational theory, theory of gravity]</p><p><b>(fizička) teorija da se bilo koje dvije čestice materije međusobno privlače silom koja je direktno proporcionalna sa proizvodom njihovih masa i obrnuto proporcionalna kvadratu udaljenosti između njih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the theory that any two particles of matter attract one another with a force directly proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them [Newton's theory of gravitation, gravitational theory, theory of gravitation]</p><p><b>(hemija) teorija da su svi indikatori ili slabe kiseline ili slabe baze u kojima je boja ionizirane forme različita od boje prije disocijacije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (chemistry) the theory that all indicators are either weak acids or weak bases in which the color of the ionized form is different from the color before dissociation [Ostwald's theory of indicators]</p><p><b>(biologija) teorija kako se karakteristike jedne generacije izvode iz ranijih generacija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) a theory of how characteristics of one generation are derived from earlier generations</p><p><b>(biologija) znanstvena teorija o podrijetlu vrsta biljaka i životinja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) a scientific theory of the origin of species of plants and animals [evolutionism, theory of evolution]</p><p><b>teorija (popularna u 18. stoljeću, ali sada diskreditirana) da se osoba razvija jednostavnim uvećanjem malog potpuno oblikovanog organizma (homunculus) koji postoji u germinalnoj stanici (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a theory (popular in the 18th century and now discredited) that an individual develops by simple enlargement of a tiny fully formed organism (a homunculus) that exists in the germ cell [preformation]</p><p><b>teorija vjerojatnosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of applied mathematics that deals with probabilities [probability theory]</p><p><b>teorija evolucije koja tvrdi da su evolucijske promjene u fosilnim zapisima počele u trenutku umjesto u stalnom procesu sporih promjena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a theory of evolution holding that evolutionary change in the fossil record came in fits and starts rather than in a steady process of slow change [punctuated equilibrium]</p><p><b>teorija relativnosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (physics) the theory that space and time are relative concepts rather than absolute concepts [Einstein's theory of relativity, relativity, relativity theory]</p><p><b>zasnovana na teoriji, a ne na eksperimentu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> based in theory rather than experiment</p><p><b>o ili u vezi s teozofijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to theosophy</p><p><b>vjerovanje u teozofiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> belief in theosophy</p><p><b>Vjernik u teozofiju. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a believer in theosophy</p><p><b>teozofija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system of belief based on mystical insight into the nature of God and the soul</p><p><b>terorizam u vjersku svrhu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> terrorism for a religious purpose</p><p><b>ljekovit, terapeutski, terapijski, lijek</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a medicine or therapy that cures disease or relieve pain [curative, cure, remedy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> tending to cure or restore to health [alterative, curative, healing, remedial, sanative]</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or involved in therapy [therapeutical]</p><p><b>pobačaj iz zdravstvenih razloga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a legally induced abortion for medical reasons (as when the mother's life is threatened)</p><p><b>Prenašanje nuklearne stanice pacijenta kako bi se stvorio oocit iz kojeg se mogu dobiti stanice koje su kompatibilne s imunološkim sustavom (posebno matične stanice) za transplantaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> nuclear transplantation of a patient's own cells to make an oocyte from which immune-compatible cells (especially stem cells) can be derived for transplant [biomedical cloning]</p><p><b>pružanje pomoći osobama s invaliditetom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> providing help for disabled persons [physical rehabilitation, physical restoration]</p><p><b>terapijski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or involved in therapy [therapeutic]</p><p><b>terapijski (od &quot;therapeutical&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> for therapeutic purposes</p><p><b>terapeutika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> branch of medicine concerned with the treatment of disease</p><p><b>veliki tropski paukovi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large tropical spiders [family Theraphosidae]</p><p><b>terapeut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person skilled in a particular type of therapy [healer]</p><p><b>Vjerojatno toplo-krvnih. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> probably warm-blooded [protomammal]</p><p><b>izumrli gmizavci slični sisarima koji su naseljeni na svim kontinentima od srednjeg Perma do kasnog Triasa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extinct mammal-like reptiles found inhabiting all continents from the mid Permian to late Triassic [order Therapsida]</p><p><b>liječenje, terapija, terapija bolesti jetre</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) the act of caring for someone (as by medication or remedial training etc.)</p><p><b>Jedna od dvije velike škole budističke doktrine koja naglašava osobno spasenje kroz vlastite napore. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of two great schools of Buddhist doctrine emphasizing personal salvation through your own efforts [Theravada Buddhism]</p><p><b>Jedna od dvije velike škole budističke doktrine koja naglašava osobno spasenje kroz vlastite napore. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of two great schools of Buddhist doctrine emphasizing personal salvation through your own efforts [Theravada]</p><p><b>da, drugdje, gle, onamo, ondje, onuda, tamo, tu, evo, onde</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a location other than here</p><p><i>adv.</i> in or at that place or location</p><p><i>adv.</i> in that matter</p><p><i>adv.</i> to or toward that place [thither]</p><p><b>tu</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> near that time or date [thereabouts]</p><p><i>adv.</i> near that place [thereabouts]</p><p><b>tu blizu, u blizini</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> near that time or date [thereabout]</p><p><i>adv.</i> near that place [thereabout]</p><p><b>nakon, nakon toga, od tada, od toga doba, odonda, otada, poslije toga, potom, prema tome, zatim</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> from that time on [thenceforth]</p><p><b>na taj način, otuda, pomoću toga, pri tom, stoga, tako, time, u vezi s tim</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by that means or because of that</p><p><b>za to, za tu svrhu</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (in formal usage, especially legal usage) for that or for it</p><p><b>dakle, pa, prema tome, radi toga, stoga, tako, u tu svrhu, zato, zbog toga</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (used to introduce a logical conclusion) from that fact or reason or as a result [hence, so, thence, thus]</p><p><i>adv.</i> as a consequence [consequently]</p><p><b>odatle, otuda</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> from that circumstance or source [thence, thereof]</p><p><i>adv.</i> from that place or from there [thence]</p><p><b>onda, ovdje, tamo, u tom, u tome, unutra</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> (formal) in or into that thing or place [in that, in this]</p><p><b>u sljedećem dijelu određenog pitanja, kao u dokumentu ili govoru (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in the following part of a given matter, as in a document or speech</p><p><b>električni glazbeni instrument (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electronic musical instrument</p><p><b>da, drugdje, gle, onamo, ondje, onuda, tamo, tu, evo, onde (od &quot;there&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> real existence</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being there--not here--in position</p><p><b>iz toga, o čemu, o tome, od ovog, od tog, od toga, od tud, sadržajem</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> of or concerning this or that</p><p><i>adv.</i> from that circumstance or source [thence, therefrom]</p><p><b>na ovo, na to, na tome</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> on that [on it, on that]</p><p><b>Indijska časna sestra i misionarka u rimokatoličkoj crkvi (rođena albanskim roditeljima u današnjoj Makedoniji) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Indian nun and missionary in the Roman Catholic Church (born of Albanian parents in what is now Macedonia) [Agnes Gonxha Bojaxhiu, Mother Teresa, Mother Theresa, Teresa]</p><p><b>k ovom, k tome, na ovo, na to</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to that [to it, to that]</p><p><b>Do tog vremena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> up to that time</p><p><b>pored toga, s ovim, s tim, time</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with that or this or it</p><p><b>zajedno sa svim tim. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> together with all that</p><p><b>pauk s hromom poput čireva na svakoj stražnjoj nozi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> spider having a comb-like row of bristles on each hind foot [comb-footed spider]</p><p><b>obitelj čipkica s čepom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of comb-footed spiders [family Theridiidae]</p><p><b>jedinica toplo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of heat equal to 100,000 British thermal units</p><p><b>termalan, termalni, termalno, termički, termoenergetskih, topao, toplinskom, toplinsku, toplotni, termička, termičko, toplinski</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rising current of warm air</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or associated with heat [caloric, thermic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a hot spring</p><p><i>adj.</i> caused by or designed to retain heat</p><p><b>ograničenje leta velikom brzinom koje je nametnuto aerodinamičkim zagrijavanjem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a limit to high speed flight imposed by aerodynamic heating [heat barrier]</p><p><b>emisija elektrona iz vrlo vrućih tvari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the emission of electrons from very hot substances [thermionic emission]</p><p><b>stanje u kojem su svi dijelovi sustava na istoj temperaturi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state in which all parts of a system are at the same temperature</p><p><b>toplinsko zagađenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> harm to lakes and rivers resulting from the release of excessive waste heat into them</p><p><b>termalni pisač, toplinski pisač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a printer that produces characters by applying heat to special paper that is sensitive to heat</p><p><b>nuklearni reaktor u kojem su nuklearne fisije uzrokovane neutronima koji su usporeni moderatorom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear reactor in which nuclear fissions are caused by neutrons that are slowed down by a moderator</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom materijala od 0,01 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a semiconductor device made of materials whose resistance varies as a function of temperature [thermistor]</p><p><b>s temperaturom od 70 F ili više (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a natural spring of water at a temperature of 70 F or above [hot spring]</p><p><b>bol uzrokovana toplinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pain caused by heat</p><p><b>termički</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> by means of heat or with respect to thermal properties</p><p><b>električni termometar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thermometer that uses thermoelectric current to measure temperature [electric thermometer, thermoelectric thermometer]</p><p><b>termički, toplinski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or associated with heat [caloric, thermal]</p><p><b>insolacija, sunčanica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sudden prostration due to exposure to the sun or excessive heat [insolation, siriasis, sunstroke]</p><p><b>jedanaesti mjesec revolucionarnog kalendara (svibanj i kolovoz) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> eleventh month of the Revolutionary calendar (July and August)</p><p><b>Električno napunjena čestica (elektron ili ion) koju emitira tvar na visokom nivou temperature (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electrically charged particle (electron or ion) emitted by a substance at a high temperature</p><p><b>cijevni, termoelektronski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of thermions</p><p><b>električna struja proizvedena između dvije elektrode kao rezultat elektrona emitiranih termoonskom emisijom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an electric current produced between two electrodes as a result of electrons emitted by thermionic emission</p><p><b>emisija elektrona iz vrlo vrućih tvari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the emission of electrons from very hot substances [thermal emission]</p><p><b>cijev, elektron cijev, elektronska cijev, katodna cijev, vakumska cijev, vakuumska cijev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electronic device consisting of a system of electrodes arranged in an evacuated glass or metal envelope [electron tube, thermionic vacuum tube, thermionic valve, tube, vacuum tube]</p><p><b>cijev, elektron cijev, elektronska cijev, katodna cijev, vakumska cijev, vakuumska cijev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electronic device consisting of a system of electrodes arranged in an evacuated glass or metal envelope [electron tube, thermionic tube, thermionic valve, tube, vacuum tube]</p><p><b>cijev, elektron cijev, elektronska cijev, katodna cijev, vakumska cijev, vakuumska cijev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electronic device consisting of a system of electrodes arranged in an evacuated glass or metal envelope [electron tube, thermionic tube, thermionic vacuum tube, tube, vacuum tube]</p><p><b>cijevni, termoelektronski (od &quot;thermionic&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of electronics dealing with thermionic phenomena (especially thermionic vacuum tubes)</p><p><b>termorezistor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a semiconductor device made of materials whose resistance varies as a function of temperature [thermal resistor]</p><p><b>Arheobacteriaceae koje rastu u vrlo kiselom okruženju pri visokim temperaturama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> archaebacteria that thrive in strongly acidic environments at high temperatures</p><p><b>bomba koja koristi eksploziv gorivo-vazduh (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb that uses a fuel-air explosive [aerosol bomb, fuel-air bomb, vacuum bomb, volume-detonation bomb]</p><p><b>rod Lepismatidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Lepismatidae [genus Thermobia]</p><p><b>Živi u toplim vlažnim područjima, npr. oko peći. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> lives in warm moist areas e.g. around furnaces [firebrat]</p><p><b>u slučaju da se ne primjenjuje primjena ovog članka, primjenjuje se sljedeći postupak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cautery (destruction of tissue) by heat</p><p><b>termokemija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of chemistry that studies the relation between chemical action and the amount of heat absorbed or generated</p><p><b>Tkivo se smrzava toplinom (kao što je struja) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> congealing tissue by heat (as by electric current)</p><p><b>termoelement</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of thermometer consisting of two wires of different metals that are joined at both ends [thermocouple junction]</p><p><b>vrsta termometra koji se sastoji od dvije žice različitih metala koje su spojene na oba kraja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of thermometer consisting of two wires of different metals that are joined at both ends [thermocouple]</p><p><b>termodinamički</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or concerned with thermodynamics [thermodynamical]</p><p><b>Termodinamički sustav (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or concerned with thermodynamics [thermodynamic]</p><p><b>termodinamički</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with respect to thermodynamics</p><p><b>termodinamika, Termotehnika</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of physics concerned with the conversion of different forms of energy</p><p><b>aspekt termodinamike koji se odnosi na toplinsku ravnotežu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the aspect of thermodynamics concerned with thermal equilibrium [thermostatics]</p><p><b>termoelektrični</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving or resulting from thermoelectricity [thermoelectrical]</p><p><b>Termometar koji koristi termoelektričnu struju za mjerenje temperature (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thermometer that uses thermoelectric current to measure temperature [electric thermometer, thermel]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> involving or resulting from thermoelectricity [thermoelectric]</p><p><b>Električna energija proizvedena toplinom (kao u termoparu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> electricity produced by heat (as in a thermocouple)</p><p><b>termogram</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a graphical record produced by a thermograph</p><p><b>termograf</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medical instrument that uses an infrared camera to reveal temperature variations on the surface of the body</p><p><i>n.</i> a thermometer that records temperature variations on a graph as a function of time [thermometrograph]</p><p><b>termografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> diagnostic technique using a thermograph to record the heat produced by different parts of the body</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hydrometer that includes a thermometer [thermohydrometer]</p><p><b>za proizvodnju električnih goriva ili električne energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to thermal hydrometry [thermohydrometric]</p><p><b>mjerenje promjena u masi u funkciji promjena u temperaturi koje se koristi kao tehnika kemijske analize tvari (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the measurement of changes in weight as a function of changes in temperature used as a technique of chemically analyzing substances</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm, ali ne više od 0,01 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hydrometer that includes a thermometer [thermogravimeter]</p><p><b>za proizvodnju električnih goriva ili električne energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to thermal hydrometry [thermogravimetric]</p><p><b>termospoj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a junction between two dissimilar metals across which a voltage appears</p><p><b>nepostojan na toplinu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (chemistry, physics, biology) readily changed or destroyed by heat</p><p><b>termometar, toplomjer</b></p><p><i>n.</i> measuring instrument for measuring temperature</p><p><b>termometarski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to thermometry</p><p><b>Termometar koji bilježi promjene temperature na grafikonu kao funkciju vremena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thermometer that records temperature variations on a graph as a function of time [thermograph]</p><p><b>mjerenje temperature (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the measurement of temperature</p><p><b>termonuklearni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> using nuclear weapons based on fusion as distinguished from fission</p><p><b>nuklearnog oružja koje oslobađa atomsku energiju spajanjem lakih (vodoničnih) jezgara na visokim temperaturama kako bi se formirao helijum (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear weapon that releases atomic energy by union of light (hydrogen) nuclei at high temperatures to form helium [H-bomb, fusion bomb, hydrogen bomb]</p><p><b>nuklearna fuzijska reakcija koja se odvija na vrlo visokim temperaturama (kao što je Sunce) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear fusion reaction taking place at very high temperatures (as in the sun)</p><p><b>nuklearni reaktor koji koristi kontroliranu fuziju za proizvodnju energije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nuclear reactor that uses controlled nuclear fusion to generate energy [fusion reactor]</p><p><b>borbena glava rakete dizajnirana za isporuku atomske bombe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the warhead of a missile designed to deliver an atom bomb [atomic warhead, nuclear warhead, nuke]</p><p><b>termički stup, termo element</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kind of thermometer for measuring heat radiation</p><p><b>termoplastični</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a material that softens when heated and hardens again when cooled [thermoplastic resin]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having the property of softening or fusing when heated and of hardening and becoming rigid again when cooled</p><p><b>materijal koji se omekšava pri zagrevanju i opet tvrdi pri hlađenju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a material that softens when heated and hardens again when cooled [thermoplastic]</p><p><b>rod američkih i azijskih izuzetno izuzetnih biljaka: grašak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of American and Asiatic showy rhizomatous herbs: bush peas [genus Thermopsis]</p><p><b>Zapadna Sjedinjene Države grmljava biljka s žutim grašak-ličnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> western United States bushy herb having yellow pea-like flowers [false lupine, golden pea, yellow pea]</p><p><b>Istočni dio Sjedinjenih Američkih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> eastern United States bush pea [Carolina lupine]</p><p><b>Slavna bitka 480 pne. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a famous battle in 480 BC [battle of Thermopylae]</p><p><b>Osjetni receptor koji reagira na toplinu i hladnoću. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sensory receptor that responds to heat and cold</p><p><b>termoregulator, termostat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a regulator for automatically regulating temperature by starting or stopping the supply of heat [thermostat]</p><p><b>termos</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vacuum flask that preserves temperature of hot or cold drinks [thermos bottle, thermos flask]</p><p><b>S druge strane, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz poglavlja 98. točka (a) ovog članka ne vrijedi: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vacuum flask that preserves temperature of hot or cold drinks [thermos, thermos flask]</p><p><b>termos-boca, termosica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vacuum flask that preserves temperature of hot 