ljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> careful and diligent in the use of resources</p><p><i>adj.</i> mindful of the future in spending money [careful]</p><p><b>drhtanje, jeza, oduševiti, oduševljenje, ushititi, uzbuditi se, uzbudljivost, uzbuđenje, užitka, zadrhtati, zatreperiti, ježuri, srsi, trnci, žmarci, drhtati, podrhtati, podrhtavati, tresti se, uzdrhtati, zatresti se, uznijeti, zgroziti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the swift release of a store of affective force [bang, boot, charge, flush, kick, rush]</p><p><i>n.</i> an almost pleasurable sensation of fright [chill, frisson, quiver, shiver, shudder, tingle]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that causes you to experience a sudden intense feeling or sensation</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to be thrilled by some perceptual input</p><p><i>v.</i> feel sudden intense sensation or emotion [tickle, vibrate]</p><p><i>v.</i> tremble convulsively, as from fear or excitement [shiver, shudder, throb]</p><p><i>v.</i> fill with sublime emotion [beatify, exalt, exhilarate, inebriate, tickle pink]</p><p><b>drhtanje, jeza, oduševiti, oduševljenje, ushititi, uzbuditi se, uzbudljivost, uzbuđenje, užitka, zadrhtati, zatreperiti (od &quot;thrill&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> feeling intense pleasurable excitement</p><p><b>glazba koja uzbuđuje, jezovit, knjiga ili film kriminalističkog sadržaja, krimić, senzacionalan film, senzacionalan roman, triler</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a suspenseful adventure story or play or movie</p><p><b>pun uzbuđenja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> full of excitement</p><p><b>koji dira, koji ima elemente trilera, koji izaziva grozu, koji izaziva jezu, koji obuzima, koji potresa, koji prodire, koji uzrujava, napet, senzacionalan, uzbudljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing a surge of emotion or excitement [electrifying]</p><p><i>adj.</i> causing quivering or shivering as by cold or fear or electric shock</p><p><b>Srednja i mala palma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small to medium-sized fan palms [genus Thrinax]</p><p><b>mala čvrsta palma od južnog Floride i Kube (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small stocky fan palm of southern Florida and Cuba [Thrinax microcarpa, Thrinax morrisii, key palm, silver thatch, silvertop palmetto]</p><p><b>mala čvrsta palma od južnog Floride i Kube (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small stocky fan palm of southern Florida and Cuba [Thrinax keyensis, Thrinax morrisii, key palm, silver thatch, silvertop palmetto]</p><p><b>mala čvrsta palma od južnog Floride i Kube (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small stocky fan palm of southern Florida and Cuba [Thrinax keyensis, Thrinax microcarpa, key palm, silver thatch, silvertop palmetto]</p><p><b>mala palma iz južne Floride i Zapadne Indije koja se vrlo sliči na palmettu s srebrnim vrhom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small palm of southern Florida and West Indies closely resembling the silvertop palmetto [broom palm, silver thatch, thatch palm, thatch tree]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih malih do sitnih sisajućih insekata s uskim pernatim krilima ako ih ima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various small to minute sucking insects with narrow feathery wings if any [thripid, thrips]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih malih do sitnih sisajućih insekata s uskim pernatim krilima ako ih ima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various small to minute sucking insects with narrow feathery wings if any [thrip, thrips]</p><p><b>trips (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thrips [family Thripidae]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih malih do sitnih sisajućih insekata s uskim pernatim krilima ako ih ima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various small to minute sucking insects with narrow feathery wings if any [thrip, thripid]</p><p><b>Štetno za biljke luka i ponekad duhana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> injurious to onion plants and sometimes tobacco [onion louse, onion thrips]</p><p><b>napredovati, rasti, uspijevati, bujati, cvasti, cvjetati, ekspandirati, jačati, narasti, ojačati, procvasti, procvjetati, prosperirati, razgranati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> grow vigorously [boom, expand, flourish]</p><p><i>v.</i> make steady progress [flourish, fly high, prosper]</p><p><b>napredan, uspješan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> very lively and profitable [booming, flourishing, palmy, prospering, prosperous, roaring]</p><p><b>grkljan, grlo, lijevak, otvor, prolaz, vrat, naglavak cipele</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the passage to the stomach and lungs [pharynx]</p><p><i>n.</i> an opening in the vamp of a shoe at the instep</p><p><i>n.</i> a passage resembling a throat in shape or function</p><p><i>n.</i> the part of an animal's body that corresponds to a person's throat</p><p><b>infekcija usne grlice i tonzila od strane streptokokusa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an infection of the oral pharynx and tonsils by streptococcus [septic sore throat, strep throat, streptococcal sore throat, streptococcus tonsilitis]</p><p><b>zaštitna odjeća koju nose hokejski golmen i hvatač u bejzbolu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> protective garment worn by hockey goalkeeper and catcher in baseball</p><p><b>Hrana za uzgoj i uzgoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> edible thymus gland of an animal [neck sweetbread]</p><p><b>grkljan, grlo, lijevak, otvor, prolaz, vrat (od &quot;throat&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a throat as specified</p><p><b>Europski zvončanica s plavo-fijalko do lilaka cvijeća ranije se koristi za liječenje bolova u grlu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European bellflower with blue-purple to lilac flowers formerly used to treat sore throat [Campanula trachelium, nettle-leaved bellflower]</p><p><b>zvuči kao da je izražen nisko u grlu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> sounding as if pronounced low in the throat</p><p><b>bilo, lupati, pulsiranje, udaranje, udariti, vibrirati, drhtati, podrhtati, podrhtavati, tresti se, uzdrhtati, zadrhtati, zatresti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a deep pulsating type of pain</p><p><i>n.</i> an instance of rapid strong pulsation (of the heart) [pounding, throbbing]</p><p><i>v.</i> pulsate or pound with abnormal force</p><p><i>v.</i> expand and contract rhythmically [pulsate, pulse]</p><p><i>v.</i> tremble convulsively,