nd in order to raise crops</p><p><b>kosina, nagib, nagibati se, nagnuti, nagnuti se, nakriviti se, podrezivati, strmina, škljocati, zaklopiti, zakositi, zakošenje, nagnutost, nakrivljenost, neravnost, iskriviti, iskrivljavati, izvijati, izviti, kriviti, nagibati, naginjati, naginjati se, naheriti, nakositi, nakriviti, pregibati, presavijati, presavinuti, savijati, savinuti, svijati, svinuti, ukositi, zakriviti, zakrivljivati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a combat between two mounted knights tilting against each other with blunted lances [joust]</p><p><i>n.</i> a contentious speech act [arguing, argument, contention, contestation, controversy, disceptation, disputation]</p><p><i>n.</i> a slight but noticeable partiality</p><p><i>n.</i> the property possessed by a line or surface that departs from the vertical [inclination, lean, leaning, list]</p><p><i>n.</i> pitching dangerously to one side [careen, rock, sway]</p><p><i>v.</i> to incline or bend from a vertical position [angle, lean, slant, tip]</p><p><i>v.</i> heel over [cant, cant over, pitch, slant]</p><p><i>v.</i> move sideways or in an unsteady way [careen, shift, wobble]</p><p><i>v.</i> charge with a tilt</p><p><b>kut koji raketa čini s vertikalom dok se zakriva duž svoje putanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the angle a rocket makes with the vertical as it curves along its trajectory</p><p><b>za proizvodnju električnih vozila s motorom za vožnju na brzinu od 300 km/h do 300 km/h (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pedestal table whose top is hinged so that it can be tilted to a vertical position [tip-top table, tip table]</p><p><b>nagnut</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> departing or being caused to depart from the true vertical or horizontal [atilt, canted, leaning, tipped]</p><p><b>kosina, nagib, nagibati se, nagnuti, nagnuti se, nakriviti se, podrezivati, strmina, škljocati, zaklopiti, zakositi, zakošenje (od &quot;tilt&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who engages in a tilt or joust</p><p><i>n.</i> a device for emptying a cask by tilting it without disturbing the dregs</p><p><b>njiva, obrada zemlje, oranica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of aggregation of soil and its condition for supporting plant growth</p><p><i>n.</i> arable land that is worked by plowing and sowing and raising crops [cultivated land, farmland, ploughland, plowland, tillage, tilled land]</p><p><b>igračka koja se sastoji od ploče koja je uravnotežena na uporištu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plaything consisting of a board balanced on a fulcrum [dandle board, seesaw, teeter, teeter-totter, teeterboard, teetertotter]</p><p><b>(bivši) zatvoreno polje za nagibanje natjecanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (formerly) an enclosed field for tilting contests</p><p><b>Američki psiholog koji je eksperimentirao s psihoaktivnim drogama (uključujući LSD) i postao poznat zagovornik njihove upotrebe (1920-1996) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States psychologist who experimented with psychoactive drugs (including LSD) and became a well-known advocate of their use (1920-1996) [Leary, Timothy Francis Leary, Timothy Leary]</p><p><b>tip rod Timaliidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Timaliidae [genus Timalia]</p><p><b>šaputanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> babblers [family Timaliidae]</p><p><b>pojedinačna porcija mletog mesa ili ribe u bogatom kremastošću i pečenom u malom obliku za pecivo ili u školjci od timbale, Slastice za proizvodnju hrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> individual serving of minced e.g. meat or fish in a rich creamy sauce baked in a small pastry mold or timbale shell</p><p><i>n.</i> small pastry shell for creamy mixtures of minced foods [timbale case]</p><p><b>Slastice za proizvodnju hrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small pastry shell for creamy mixtures of minced foods [timbale]</p><p><b>deblo, drven, drvena građa, drvo, drvo za gradnju, greda, tesati, drvni materijal, šuma, ton</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the wood of trees cut and prepared for use as building material [lumber]</p><p><i>n.</i> a beam made of wood</p><p><i>n.</i> a post made of wood</p><p><i>n.</i> land that is covered with trees and shrubs [forest, timberland, woodland]</p><p><i>n.</i> (music) the distinctive property of a complex sound (a voice or noise or musical sound) [quality, timbre, tone]</p><p><b>čvrstoće koja se koristi za vezanje užeta za deblo ili špar. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hitch used to secure a rope to a log or spar</p><p><b>linija koja označava gornju granicu rasta stabala u planinama ili sjevernim širinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> line marking the upper limit of tree growth in mountains or northern latitudes [timberline, tree line]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjen u grubim zemljama istočnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed in rugged ground of eastern United States [Crotalus horridus horridus, banded rattlesnake]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta drveta koja se cijeni kao izvor drveta ili drveta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any tree that is valued as a source of lumber or timber</p><p><b>vuk s mrljano sivim plaštom koji živi u šumovitim sjevernim područjima Sjeverne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wolf with a brindled grey coat living in forested northern regions of North America [Canis lupus, gray wolf, grey wolf]</p><p><b>u okviru izloženog drveta (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> framed by exposed timbers</p><p><b>deblo, drven, drvena građa, drvo, drvo za gradnju, greda, tesati (od &quot;timber&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> furnished with or made of wood or timbers</p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with growing timber</p><p><b>šuma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> land that is covered with trees and shrubs [forest, timber, woodland]</p><p><b>linija koja označava gornju granicu rasta stabala u planinama ili sjevernim širinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> line marking the upper limit of tree growth in mountains or northern latitudes [timber line, tree line]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, poduzeća koja se bave proizvodnjom drveta mogu biti: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an owner or manager of a company that is engaged in lumbering</p><p><b>boja glasa, boja zvuka, vrsta tona, ton</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (music) the distinctive property of a complex sound (a voice or noise or musical sound) [quality, timber, tone]</p><p><b>tamburin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small hand drum similar to a tambourine</p><p><b>Grad u središnjem Maliu blizu rijeke Niger (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a city in central Mali near the Niger river</p><p><b>čas, doba, epoha, istovremeno, kratko vrijeme, moment vremena, na vrijeme, nekoć, pravodobno, put, razdoblje, sinkronizirati, takt, tempo, trenutak, vremenski, vrijeme, odredi vrijeme, puta, vremena, vremenu, vreme, prigoda, sat, ura, kazna, izmjeriti, mjeriti, štopati, tempirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instance or single occasion for some event [clip]</p><p><i>n.</i> a period of time considered as a resource under your control and sufficient to accomplish something</p><p><i>n.</i> an indefinite period (usually marked by specific attributes or activities)</p><p><i>n.</i> a suitable moment</p><p><i>n.</i> the continuum of experience in which events pass from the future through the present to the past</p><p><i>n.</i> a person's experience on a particular occasion</p><p><i>n.</i> a reading of a point in time as given by a clock [clock time]</p><p><i>n.</i> the fourth coordinate that is required (along with three spatial dimensions) to specify a physical event [fourth dimension]</p><p><i>n.</i> rhythm as given by division into parts of equal duration [meter, metre]</p><p><i>n.</i> the period of time a prisoner is imprisoned [prison term, sentence]</p><p><i>v.</i> measure the time or duration of an event or action or the person who performs an action in a certain period of time [clock]</p><p><i>v.</i> assign a time for an activity or event</p><p><i>v.</i> set the speed, duration, or execution of</p><p><i>v.</i> regulate or set the time of</p><p><i>v.</i> adjust so that a force is applied and an action occurs at the desired time</p><p><b>stopa plaće koja je 1,5 puta veća od redovne stope (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rate of pay that is 1.5 times the regular rate</p><p><b>ponavljajuće (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> repeatedly [again and again, over and over, over and over again, time and time again]</p><p><b>analiza određenog posla u nastojanju da se pronađe najefikasnija metoda u smislu vremena i truda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an analysis of a specific job in an effort to find the most efficient method in terms of time and effort [motion study, time-and-motion study, time-motion study, time study, work study]</p><p><b>ponavljajuće (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> repeatedly [again and again, over and over, over and over again, time and again]</p><p><b>-Sadašnji trenutak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the present occasion [nonce]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a draft payable at a specified future date [time draft]</p><p><b>problematična situacija koja će na kraju postati opasna ako se ne riješi, bomba koja ima mehanizam za detonaciju koji se može postaviti da eksplodira u određeno vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a problematic situation that will eventually become dangerous if not addressed [ticking bomb]</p><p><i>n.</i> a bomb that has a detonating mechanism that can be set to go off at a particular time [infernal machine]</p><p><b>Kontejner za čuvanje povijesnih zapisa koji će biti otkriveni u neko vrijeme u budućnosti. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> container for preserving historical records to be discovered at some future time</p><p><b>sat koji se koristi za bilježenje sati koje ljudi rade (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> clock used to record the hours that people work</p><p><b>(elektronika) vrijeme potrebno za struju ili napon u krugu da se poveća ili smanji eksponencijalno kroz približno 63% njegove amplitude, odnos induktivnosti kola u henzima prema otporu u ohmima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (electronics) the time required for the current or voltage in a circuit to rise or fall exponentially through approximately 63 per cent of its amplitude</p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio of the inductance of a circuit in henries to its resistance in ohms</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (b) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a certificate of deposit from which withdrawals can be made only after advance notice or at a specified future date</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 2. stavkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (b) ove Uredbe, u skladu s člankom 3. stavkom (c) ove Uredbe, u skladu s član (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a savings account in which the deposit is held for a fixed term or in which withdrawals can be made only after giving notice or with loss of interest [deposit account]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a draft payable at a specified future date [time bill]</p><p><b>fotografija napravljena s relativno dugim vremenskim izlaganjem, U slučaju da se ne primjenjuje određeni regulatorni regulator, to se može učiniti na temelju sljedećih uvjeta: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a photograph produced with a relatively long exposure time</p><p><i>n.</i> exposure of a film for a relatively long time (more than half a second)</p><p><b>vremenski okvir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a time period during which something occurs or is expected to occur</p><p><b>Dalekom prošlosti izvan sjećanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the distant past beyond memory [time out of mind]</p><p><b>interval, period vremena, vremenski interval, vremenski razmak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a definite length of time marked off by two instants [interval]</p><p><b>vrijeme kašnjenja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> time during which some action is awaited [delay, hold, postponement, wait]</p><p><b>vremenska granica, vremensko ograničenje, rok, vremenski rok</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a time period within which something must be done or completed</p><p><b>zajam koji se isplaćuje na ili prije određenog datuma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a loan that is payable on or before a specified date</p><p><b>vremeplov</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a science fiction machine that is supposed to transport people or objects into the past or the future</p><p><b>U slučaju da je u pitanju kreditna kartica, u skladu s člankom 6. stavkom 2. točkom (a) ili (b) ovog članka, kreditna kartica može se koristiti za plaćanje novčanih sredstava. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a note that specifies the time (or times) of repayment</p><p><b>vrijeme kada se javni prijevoz planira stići na određenu destinaciju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time at which a public conveyance is scheduled to arrive at a given destination [arrival time]</p><p><b>dnevno vrijeme, vrijeme od 24 h, doba dana, sat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> clock time [hour]</p><p><b>vrijeme kada je planirano da javni prijevoz krene s određene točke podrijetla (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time at which a public conveyance is scheduled to depart from a given point of origin [departure time]</p><p><b>doba života, faza života, životna dob, životna faza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a period of time during which a person is normally in a particular life state</p><p><b>Starija vina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the oldness of wines [vintage]</p><p><b>godišnje doba, sezona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the natural periods into which the year is divided by the equinoxes and solstices or atmospheric conditions [season]</p><p><b>slobodno vrijeme, slobodan dan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a time period when you are not required to work</p><p><b>minuta odmora, odmor, prekid, vremenska granica, pauza, predah, tajm-aut, kratak odmor, time-out</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pause from doing something (as work) [break, recess, respite]</p><p><b>Dalekom prošlosti izvan sjećanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the distant past beyond memory [time immemorial]</p><p><b>razdoblje, period</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an amount of time [period, period of time]</p><p><b>sustav plaćanja za robu u ratama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a system for paying for goods by installments [installment buying, installment plan]</p><p><b>mjera za vrijeme</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arrangement of events used as a measure of duration</p><p><b>vremenski nizovi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a series of values of a variable at successive times</p><p><b>paralelan rad, dijeljenje vremena, time-sharing</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (computer science) the use of a central computer by many users simultaneously</p><p><b>vremenska tablica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a record of the hours worked by employees</p><p><b>Snimak (posebno elektronički ili radio) koji pokazuje točno pravo vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a signal (especially electronic or by radio) indicating the precisely correct time</p><p><b>glazbena notacija koja označava broj otkucaja na mjerilo i vrstu note koja uzima otkucaj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a musical notation indicating the number of beats to a measure and kind of note that takes a beat [musical time signature]</p><p><b>vremenski odsječak, termin, vremenski termin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a time assigned on a schedule or agenda [slot]</p><p><b>analiza određenog posla u nastojanju da se pronađe najefikasnija metoda u smislu vremena i truda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an analysis of a specific job in an effort to find the most efficient method in terms of time and effort [motion study, time-and-motion study, time-motion study, time and motion study, work study]</p><p><b>buduća vremena, budućnost, sutra, sutrašnjica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time yet to come [future, futurity, hereafter]</p><p><b>jedinica vremena, vremenska jedinica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit for measuring time periods [unit of time]</p><p><b>(glazba) relativno trajanje glazbene note (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (music) the relative duration of a musical note [note value, value]</p><p><b>vremenska zona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of the 24 regions of the globe (loosely divided by longitude) throughout which the same standard time is used</p><p><b>analiza određenog posla u nastojanju da se pronađe najefikasnija metoda u smislu vremena i truda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an analysis of a specific job in an effort to find the most efficient method in terms of time and effort [motion study, time-motion study, time and motion study, time study, work study]</p><p><b>loptica koja se klizi niz štap kako bi pokazala fiksno vrijeme (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a ball that slides down a staff to show a fixed time</p><p><b>dugog trajanja</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a task that takes time and patience</p><p><b>chronoscope za mjerenje vremenske razlike između dva događaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chronoscope for measuring the time difference between two events [time-delay measuring system]</p><p><b>chronoscope za mjerenje vremenske razlike između dva događaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chronoscope for measuring the time difference between two events [time-delay measuring instrument]</p><p><b>Siguran je napravljen da gori određeno vrijeme (posebno da eksplodira bomba) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fuse made to burn for a given time (especially to explode a bomb)</p><p><b>prihvatljivo za dugo vremena, Poštovani zbog starosti ili dugog korištenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> acceptable for a long time [time-honoured]</p><p><i>adj.</i> honored because of age or long usage [time-honoured]</p><p><b>prihvatljivo za dugo vremena, Poštovani zbog starosti ili dugog korištenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> acceptable for a long time [time-honored]</p><p><i>adj.</i> honored because of age or long usage [time-honored]</p><p><b>analiza određenog posla u nastojanju da se pronađe najefikasnija metoda u smislu vremena i truda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an analysis of a specific job in an effort to find the most efficient method in terms of time and effort [motion study, time-and-motion study, time and motion study, time study, work study]</p><p><b>minuta odmora, odmor, prekid, vremenska granica, pauza, predah, tajm-aut</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brief suspension of play</p><p><b>Od ili povezan s pripravkom koji postupno oslobađa aktivnu tvar (posebno lijek) tijekom vremenskog razdoblja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to a preparation that gradually releases an active substance (especially a drug) over a period of time</p><p><b>U slučaju da je to potrebno za provedbu simulacije, u slučaju da je to potrebno za provedbu simulacije, u slučaju da je to potrebno za provedbu simulacije, u slučaju da je to potrebno za provedbu simulacije, u slučaju da je to potrebno za provedbu simulacije, u slučaju da je to potrebno za provedbu simulacije, u slučaju da je to potrebno za provedbu simulacije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the ratio of the simulation time to the time of the real process</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom energije od 1,15 kVA ili većim od 2,25 kVA (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a switch set to operate at a desired time</p><p><b>testiran i dokazano pouzdan (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tested and proved to be reliable [tested, tried, tried and true]</p><p><b>Kartica s zapisom početka i završetka svakog radnog dana zaposlenika, Kartica koja se koristi s satom za zapis vremena početka i završetka svakog dana zaposlenika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a card recording an employee's starting and quitting times each work day</p><p><i>n.</i> a card used with a time clock to record an employee's starting and quitting times each day</p><p><b>sinkroniziran, tempiran, vremenski određen, vremenski reguliran, vremenski ugođen, vremenski usklađen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> regularly spaced in time</p><p><b>kronometar, mjeritelj vremena, sat, štoperica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (sports) an official who keeps track of the time elapsed [timer]</p><p><i>n.</i> a clerk who keeps track of the hours worked by employees</p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument or device for keeping time [horologe, timepiece]</p><p><b>Čin ili postupak određivanja vremena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act or process of determining the time</p><p><b>beskonačan, bezvremen, koji nije vezan na vrijeme, vječan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> unaffected by time [dateless]</p><p><b>stanje vječnog postojanja vjeruje u nekim religijama da karakteriše život poslije smrti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of eternal existence believed in some religions to characterize the afterlife [eternity, timelessness]</p><p><b>bezvremenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a state of eternal existence believed in some religions to characterize the afterlife [eternity, timeless existence]</p><p><b>vremenska skala</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sequence of related events arranged in chronological order and displayed along a line (usually drawn left to right or top to bottom)</p><p><b>pravodobnost, pravovremenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> being at the right time [seasonableness]</p><p><i>n.</i> timely convenience [opportuneness, patness]</p><p><b>blagovremen, kada treba, na vrijeme, pravodoban, pravovremen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> before a time limit expires</p><p><i>adj.</i> done or happening at the appropriate or proper time [seasonable, well-timed, well timed]</p><p><i>adv.</i> at an opportune time [apropos, seasonably, well-timed]</p><p><b>sat, kronometar, štoperica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument or device for keeping time [horologe, timekeeper]</p><p><b>davatelj vremena, programator, sat u računalu, tajmer, vremenski relej, vremenski sklop, kronometar, štoperica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a timepiece that measures a time interval and signals its end</p><p><i>n.</i> (sports) an official who keeps track of the time elapsed [timekeeper]</p><p><i>n.</i> a regulator that activates or deactivates a mechanism at set times</p><p><b>doba, navrat, navrata, puta, umnožak, vremena, vremenima</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a more or less definite period of time now or previously present</p><p><i>n.</i> an arithmetic operation that is the inverse of division [multiplication]</p><p><b>područje Manhattana oko raskrižja Broadwaya i Sedme avenije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the area of Manhattan around the intersection of Broadway and Seventh Avenue</p><p><b>osoba koja se prilagođava trenutnim načinom i mišljenjima radi osobne koristi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who conforms to current ways and opinions for personal advantage</p><p><b>Izvješće o postupku za odlazak iz države članice u koju se upućuje zahtjev za odlazak iz države članice u koju se upućuje zahtjev za odlazak iz države članice u koju se upućuje zahtjev za odlazak iz države članice u koju se upućuje zahtjev za odlazak iz države članice u koju se upućuje zahtjev za odlazak iz države članice u koju se upućuje zahtjev za odlazak iz države članice u koju se upućuje zahtjev za odlazak iz države članice u koju se nalazi zahtjev za odlazak iz države članice u koju se nalazi zahtjev za odlazak iz (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> taking immediate advantage, often unethically, of any circumstance of possible benefit [opportunist, opportunistic]</p><p><b>raspored, red letenja, red vožnje, vozni red</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a schedule listing events and the times at which they will take place</p><p><i>n.</i> a schedule of times of arrivals and departures</p><p><b>rad plaćen po stopama po jedinici vremena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> work paid for at a rate per unit of time</p><p><b>Prečesto ponavljanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> repeated too often [banal, commonplace, hackneyed, old-hat, shopworn, stock, threadbare, tired, trite, well-worn]</p><p><b>drevni grad koji su osnovali Rimljani. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient town founded by the Romans</p><p><b>