ina, tkivno, tkivo, staničje, papirnata maramica, isplesti, istkati, plesti, satkati, tkati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> part of an organism consisting of an aggregate of cells having a similar structure and function</p><p><i>n.</i> a soft thin (usually translucent) paper [tissue paper]</p><p><i>v.</i> create a piece of cloth by interlacing strands of fabric, such as wool or cotton [weave]</p><p><b>membrana, opna, ovojnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pliable sheet of tissue that covers or lines or connects the organs or cells of animals or plants [membrane]</p><p><b>karbon papir, maramica, papirnata maramica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a soft thin (usually translucent) paper [tissue]</p><p><b>trombolitički sredstvo (trgovinski naziv Activase) koje uzrokuje fibrinolizu na mjestu krvnog ugruška (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a thrombolytic agent (trade name Activase) that causes fibrinolysis at the site of a blood clot [Activase]</p><p><b>niz dijagnostičkih ispitivanja prije transplantacije organa kako bi se utvrdilo jesu li tkiva donatora i primatelja kompatibilna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a series of diagnostic tests before an organ transplant to determine whether the tissues of a donor and recipient are compatible</p><p><b>bradavica, bradavica na grudima, sjenica, sjenica (ptica), slavuj, dojka, sjenice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of two soft fleshy milk-secreting glandular organs on the chest of a woman [boob, bosom, breast, knocker, titty]</p><p><i>n.</i> the small projection of a mammary gland [mamilla, mammilla, nipple, pap, teat]</p><p><i>n.</i> small insectivorous birds [titmouse]</p><p><b>ekvivalent koji se daje u zamjenu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an equivalent given in return</p><p><b>igra u kojoj dva igrača napunjuju križeve i krugove u jedan od odjeljaka kvadratne mreže od devet mjesta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a game in which two players alternately put crosses and circles in one of the compartments of a square grid of nine spaces [noughts and crosses, tic-tac-toe, tick-tack-toe, tickta