n sunflower]</p><p><b>stablo niskoližnih obalnih područja jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s sjajnim lištima i rasemi mirisnih bijelih cvijeća, ljeplovita grmljava stabla iz istočne Sjeverne Amerike s duboko rascjepljenom kore i sprejima malih mirisnih bijelih cvijeća i kiselog ukusa lišća, Mali južnoamerički majmuni s dugim lijepim krznom i dugim neosjetljivim repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tree of low-lying coastal areas of southeastern United States having glossy leaves and racemes of fragrant white flowers [Cliftonia monophylla, buckwheat tree]</p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrubby tree of eastern North America having deeply fissured bark and sprays of small fragrant white flowers and sour-tasting leaves [Oxydendrum arboreum, sorrel tree, sourwood]</p><p><i>n.</i> small South American monkeys with long beautiful fur and long nonprehensile tail [titi monkey]</p><p><b>biljke i stabla s kožnim lišćama i malim bijelim cvijećima u rasemi: rodovi Cyrilla i Cliftonia (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubs and trees with leathery leaves and small white flowers in racemes: genera Cyrilla and Cliftonia [Cyrilliaceae, cyrilla family, family Cyrilliaceae]</p><p><b>Mali južnoamerički majmuni s dugim lijepim krznom i dugim neosjetljivim repom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small South American monkeys with long beautiful fur and long nonprehensile tail [titi]</p><p><b>Tizian</b></p><p><i>n.</i> old master of the Venetian school (1490-1576) [Tiziano Vecellio]</p><p><b>prijatno uzbuđenje, škakljati, zagolicati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> touch (a body part) lightly so as to excite the surface nerves and cause uneasiness, laughter, or spasmodic movements [tickle, vellicate]</p><p><i>v.</i> excite pleasurably or erotically</p><p><b>Osjećaj blage ugodne uzbuđenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> feeling mild pleasurable excitement [teased]</p><p><b>prijatno uzbuđenje, škakljati, zagolicati (od &quot;titillate&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> pleasantly and superficially exciting</p><p><i>adj.</i> giving sexual pleasure [erotic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> exciting by touching lightly so as to cause laughter or twitching movements [tickling, tingling]</p><p><b>prskanje od uzbuđenja (kao od drkanja ili škaklja), ugodna uzbuđenja, Čin škakljanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tingling feeling of excitement (as from teasing or tickling)</p><p><i>n.</i> an agreeable arousal</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of tickling [tickle, tickling]</p><p><b>dotjerati se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make neat, smart, or trim [slick up, smarten up, spiff up, spruce, spruce up, tittivate]</p><p><b>-Pokretanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sprucing up [tittivation]</p><p><b>ptica koja živi uglavnom na zemlji u otvorenom području. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a songbird that lives mainly on the ground in open country [lark, pipit]</p><p><b>glava, ime, naslov, natpis, naziv, osloviti, položaj, titl, titlovati, titula, titulirati, vlasništvo, zaglavljen, imenom, naslova, zaposlenost, isprava, pravo, nasloviti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heading that names a statute or legislative bill [rubric, statute title]</p><p><i>n.</i> the name of a work of art or literary composition etc.</p><p><i>n.</i> a general or descriptive heading for a section of a written work</p><p><i>n.</i> the status of being a champion [championship]</p><p><i>n.</i> a legal document signed and sealed and delivered to effect a transfer of property and to show the legal right to possess it [deed, deed of conveyance]</p><p><i>n.</i> an identifying appellation signifying status or function: e.g. `Mr.' or `General' [form of address, title of respect]</p><p><i>n.</i> an established or recognized right [claim]</p><p><i>n.</i> (usually plural) written material introduced into a movie or TV show to give credits or represent dialogue or explain an action</p><p><i>n.</i> an appellation signifying nobility</p><p><i>n.</i> an informal right to something [claim]</p><p><i>v.</i> give a title to [entitle]</p><p><i>v.</i> designate by an identifying term [style]</p><p><b>naslovna traka, naslovni