olerancija, tolerancije, tolerantnost, toleriranje, trpeljivost, vrijednosti, podnošenje, snošljivost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the power or capacity of an organism to tolerate unfavorable environmental conditions</p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to allow freedom of choice and behavior [permissiveness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of tolerating something</p><p><i>n.</i> willingness to recognize and respect the beliefs or practices of others</p><p><i>n.</i> a permissible difference [allowance, leeway, margin]</p><p><b>dopušten, dozvoljen, popustljiv, snošljiv, strpljiv, tolerantan, trpeljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> showing respect for the rights or opinions or practices of others</p><p><i>adj.</i> tolerant and forgiving under provocation [kind]</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing or characterized by broad-mindedness [broad, large-minded, liberal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> able to tolerate environmental conditions or physiological stress [resistant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing the capacity for endurance [patient of]</p><p><b>dopušten, dozvoljen, popustljiv, snošljiv, strpljiv, tolerantan, trpeljiv (od &quot;tolerant&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a tolerant manner</p><p><b>dopuštati, dozvoliti, podnositi, tolerirati, trpjeti, durati, izdržati, izdržavati, izdurati, otrpjeti, podnašati, podnijeti, probaviti, probavljati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> put up with something or somebody unpleasant [abide, bear, brook, digest, endure, put up, stand, stick out, stomach, suffer, support]</p><p><i>v.</i> recognize and respect (rights and beliefs of others)</p><p><i>v.</i> have a tolerance for a poison or strong drug or pathogen or environmental condition</p><p><i>v.</i> allow the presence of or allow (an activity) without opposing or prohibiting [allow, permit]</p><p><b>dozvoljavanje, podnošenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disposition to tolerate or accept people or situations [acceptance, sufferance]</p><p><i>n.</i> official recognition of the right of individuals to hold dissenting opinions (especially in religion)</p><p><b>lijek (trgovinski naziv Tolinaza) koji se koristi za liječenje stabilnog dijabetesa u odraslih osoba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a drug (trade name Tolinase) used in treating stable adult-onset diabetes mellitus [tolazamide]</p><p><b>Tolkin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British philologist and writer of fantasies (born in South Africa) (1892-1973) [J.R.R. Tolkien, John Ronald Reuel Tolkien]</p><p><b>carina, cestarina, davanje, gubitak, međumjesni, putarina, taksa, trošarina, zvonjenje, cijena, zvon, zvonjava</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fee levied for the use of roads or bridges (used for maintenance)</p><p><i>n.</i> value measured by what must be given or done or undergone to obtain something [cost, price]</p><p><i>n.</i> the sound of a bell being struck [bell]</p><p><i>v.</i> ring slowly</p><p><i>v.</i> charge a fee for using</p><p><b>osoba koja je zaposlena za naplatu putnih pristojbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed to collect tolls [toll collector, toll taker, toller, tollgatherer, tollkeeper, tollman]</p><p><b>most na kojem se naplaćuje putna pristojba za prelazak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bridge where toll is charged for crossing</p><p><b>međumjesni poziv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long-distance telephone call at charges above a local rate</p><p><b>osoba koja je zaposlena za naplatu putnih pristojbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed to collect tolls [toll agent, toll taker, toller, tollgatherer, tollkeeper, tollman]</p><p><b>kolačići koji sadrže čokoladne čipse (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cookies containing chocolate chips [chocolate chip cookie]</p><p><b>Telefoni za daljinski pozivi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a telephone line for long-distance calls</p><p><b>područje gdje se nalaze putovnice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an area where tollbooths are located</p><p><b>cestarina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an expressway on which tolls are collected [turnpike]</p><p><b>osoba koja je zaposlena za naplatu putnih pristojbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed to collect tolls [toll agent, toll collector, toller, tollgatherer, tollkeeper, tollman]</p><p><b>s masom od 300 g/m2 ili većom od 300 g/m2 (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having no toll levied for its use</p><p><b>vrata ili šipke preko mosta ili puta s naplatom koji se podižu kada se plaća naplata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gate or bar across a toll bridge or toll road which is lifted when the toll is paid [tollgate]</p><p><b>gradski zatvor, mitnica, stražarnica za ubiranje gradske maltarine</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a booth at a tollgate where the toll collector collects tolls [tolbooth, tollhouse]</p><p><b>zvončara</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who rings church bells (as for summoning the congregation) [bell ringer, ringer]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed to collect tolls [toll agent, toll collector, toll taker, tollgatherer, tollkeeper, tollman]</p><p><b>vrata ili šipke preko mosta ili puta s naplatom koji se podižu kada se plaća naplata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gate or bar across a toll bridge or toll road which is lifted when the toll is paid [tollbar]</p><p><b>osoba koja je zaposlena za naplatu putnih pristojbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed to collect tolls [toll agent, toll collector, toll taker, toller, tollkeeper, tollman]</p><p><b>stanica na cestovnom prolazu gdje cestovnik skuplja cestovnice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a booth at a tollgate where the toll collector collects tolls [tolbooth, tollbooth]</p><p><b>osoba koja je zaposlena za naplatu putnih pristojbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed to collect tolls [toll agent, toll collector, toll taker, toller, tollgatherer, tollman]</p><p><b>osoba koja je zaposlena za naplatu putnih pristojbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed to collect tolls [toll agent, toll collector, toll taker, toller, tollgatherer, tollkeeper]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za proizvodnju proizvoda iz kategorije "Korišćenje" u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, proizvođač proizvodi proizvode iz kategorije "Korišćenje" u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ornamental evergreen treelike shrub of the Pacific coast of the United States having large white flowers and red berrylike fruits [Christmas berry, Christmasberry, Heteromeles arbutifolia, Photinia arbutifolia, toyon]</p><p><b>ne-steroidni protuupalni lijek (trgovinski naziv Tolectin) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (trade name Tolectin) [Tolectin]</p><p><b>jedna vrsta: biljka za uzimanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one species: pickaback plant [genus Tolmiea]</p><p><b>Vježnija višegodišnja biljka s cvjetovima u uspravnim stabljikama i mladim biljkama koje se razvijaju na spoju listne listine i listnog stuba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vigorous perennial herb with flowers in erect racemes and having young plants develop at the junction of a leaf blade and the leafstalk [pickaback plant, piggyback plant, youth-on-age]</p><p><b>Ruski pisac poznat po dva velika romana (1828-1910) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Russian author remembered for two great novels (1828-1910) [Count Lev Nikolayevitch Tolstoy, Leo Tolstoy]</p><p><b>član naroda koji govori nahuatl u središnjem i južnom Meksiku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Nahuatl speaking people of central and southern Mexico</p><p><b>aromatični žuto-smeđi balzam iz drveta tolu balzam koji se koristi posebno u sirupu za kašalj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic yellowish brown balsam from the tolu balsam tree used especially in cough syrups [balsam of tolu, tolu balsam]</p><p><b>aromatični žuto-smeđi balzam iz drveta tolu balzam koji se koristi posebno u sirupu za kašalj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic yellowish brown balsam from the tolu balsam tree used especially in cough syrups [balsam of tolu, tolu]</p><p><b>srednjo veličine tropsko američko drvo koje daje tolu balzam i mirisno tvrdo drvo koje se koristi za visoko kvalitetan namještaj i ormariće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized tropical American tree yielding tolu balsam and a fragrant hard wood used for high-grade furniture and cabinetwork [Myroxylon balsamum, Myroxylon toluiferum, tolu tree]</p><p><b>srednjo veličine tropsko američko drvo koje daje tolu balzam i mirisno tvrdo drvo koje se koristi za visoko kvalitetan namještaj i ormariće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> medium-sized tropical American tree yielding tolu balsam and a fragrant hard wood used for high-grade furniture and cabinetwork [Myroxylon balsamum, Myroxylon toluiferum, tolu balsam tree]</p><p><b>toluol</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless flammable liquid obtained from petroleum or coal tar [methylbenzene]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena od 1,5% ili više, ali ne više od 2,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an isomeric acid derived from toluene</p><p><b>rod Dasypodidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Dasypodidae [genus Tolypeutes]</p><p><b>Južnoamerički armadillo s tri trake kostnih ploča (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> South American armadillo with three bands of bony plates [apar, three-banded armadillo]</p><p><b>mačor, mačak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> male cat [tomcat]</p><p><i>n.</i> male turkey [gobbler, tom turkey, turkey cock]</p><p><b>topli rum s udarenim jajima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hot rum toddy with a beaten egg</p><p><b>Američki političar koji je izabran za prvog crnog gradonačelnika Los Angelesa (1917-1998) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States politician who was elected the first black mayor of Los Angeles (1917-1998) [Bradley, Thomas Bradley]</p><p><b>Visoki ledeni napitak od alkohola (obično gin) s voćnim sokom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall iced drink of liquor (usually gin) with fruit juice [collins]</p><p><b>Američki filmski glumac (rođen 1956) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States film actor (born in 1956) [Hanks, Thomas J. Hanks]</p><p><b>Američki revolucionarni vođa i pamfletist (rođen u Engleskoj) koji je podržao borbu američkih kolonista za neovisnost i podržao Francusku revoluciju (1737-1809) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American Revolutionary leader and pamphleteer (born in England) who supported the American colonist's fight for independence and supported the French Revolution (1737-1809) [Paine, Thomas Paine]</p><p><b>dječak junak iz romana Marka Twaina. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the boy hero of a novel by Mark Twain</p><p><b>Britanski dramaturg (rođen u Čehoslovačkoj 1937.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British dramatist (born in Czechoslovakia in 1937) [Sir Tom Stoppard, Stoppard, Thomas Straussler]</p><p><b>zamišljeni junak engleskog folklora koji nije bio viši od očevog palca., vrlo mala osoba. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an imaginary hero of English folklore who was no taller than his father's thumb</p><p><i>n.</i> a very small person</p><p><b>muškog purana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> male turkey [gobbler, tom, turkey cock]</p><p><b>Američki pisac koji je puno pisao o američkoj kulturi (rođen 1931.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer who has written extensively on American culture (born in 1931) [Thomas Kennerly Wolfe Jr., Thomas Wolfe, Wolfe]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 mm ili većim od 0,01 mm, ali ne većim od 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various drums with small heads [tenor drum]</p><p><b>bojna sjekira sjevernoameričkih Indijanaca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> weapon consisting of a fighting ax [hatchet]</p><p><i>v.</i> cut with a tomahawk</p><p><i>v.</i> kill with a tomahawk</p><p><b>Hladna zelenkasta tvar u kuhanom jastogu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> edible greenish substance in boiled lobster</p><p><b>Španjol koji je kao veliki inkvizitor bio odgovoran za smrt tisuća Židova i osumnjičenih vještica tijekom španjolske inkvizicije (1420-1498) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the Spaniard who as Grand Inquisitor was responsible for the death of thousands of Jews and suspected witches during the Spanish Inquisition (1420-1498) [Torquemada]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1447. do 1455. koji je osnovao vatikansku knjižnicu (1397.-1455.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1447 to 1455 who founded the Vatican library (1397-1455) [Nicholas V]</p><p><b>Meksikanski godišnji plod naturaliziran u istočnoj Sjevernoj Americi s žutom do ljubičastim jestivim plodovima sličnim malim paradajzom, godišnje od Meksika i južnih Sjedinjenih Država koje imaju jestivo ljubičasto viskozno voće slično malim paradajzom, malo jestivo žuto do ljubičasto voće nalik paradajzu zatvoreno u ljusku nalik mjehuru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mexican annual naturalized in eastern North America having yellow to purple edible fruit resembling small tomatoes [Physalis philadelphica, jamberry, miltomate, purple ground cherry]</p><p><i>n.</i> annual of Mexico and southern United States having edible purplish viscid fruit resembling small tomatoes [Mexican husk tomato, Physalis ixocarpa, jamberry]</p><p><i>n.</i> small edible yellow to purple tomato-like fruit enclosed in a bladderlike husk [Mexican husk tomato, husk tomato]</p><p><b>paradajz, patlidžan, rajčica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mildly acid red or yellow pulpy fruit eaten as a vegetable</p><p><i>n.</i> native to South America [Lycopersicon esculentum, love apple, tomato plant]</p><p><b>bolest biljaka paradajza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of tomato plants [tomato yellows]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15% ili većim od 0,15% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a concentrated form of tomatoes</p><p><b>larva noctitudnog molja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> larva of a noctuid moth [Heliothis zia, corn earworm, cotton bollworm, tobacco budworm, vetchworm]</p><p><b>Larva velikog zelenog bijelacasta jastogova koji se hrani biljkama paradajza i krompira (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large green white-striped hawkmoth larva that feeds on tomato and potato plants [Manduca quinquemaculata, potato worm]</p><p><b>sok od rajčica, sok od rajčice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the juice of tomatoes (usually bottled or canned)</p><p><b>gusto začinjeno umak od paradajza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thick spicy sauce made from tomatoes [catsup, cetchup, ketchup]</p><p><b>koncentrat, pašteta od rajčice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thick concentrated tomato puree</p><p><b>izvorno iz Južne Amerike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> native to South America [Lycopersicon esculentum, love apple, tomato]</p><p><b>rajčica umak, umak od rajčice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sauce made with a puree of tomatoes (or strained tomatoes) with savory vegetables and other seasonings</p><p><b>bolest široke palete biljaka (paradižana, krumpira, graška) koja je posljedica mješovite infekcije krumpira i mozaika od paradajza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> disease of a wide range of plants (tomatoes, potatoes, peas) resulting from a mixed infection of potato and tomato mosaic</p><p><b>Larva velikog zelenog bijelacasta s crvenim prugama koja se hrani duhanom i srodnim biljkama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large green white-striped hawkmoth larva that feeds on tobacco and related plants [Manduca sexta, tobacco hornworm]</p><p><b>bolest biljaka paradajza (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a disease of tomato plants [tomato blight]</p><p><b>grob, grobnica, sahraniti, grobnice</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a place for the burial of a corpse (especially beneath the ground and marked by a tombstone) [grave]</p><p><b>legura bakra i cinka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alloy of copper and zinc (and sometimes arsenic) used to imitate gold in cheap jewelry and for gilding [tambac, tombak]</p><p><b>legura bakra i cinka (a ponekad i arzenika) koja se koristi za imitaciju zlata u jeftinim nakitima i za pozlaćivanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an alloy of copper and zinc (and sometimes arsenic) used to imitate gold in cheap jewelry and for gilding [tambac, tombac]</p><p><b>Američki astronom koji je otkrio planet Pluton (1906-1997) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States astronomer who discovered the planet Pluto (1906-1997) [Clyde Tombaugh, Clyde William Tombaugh]</p><p><b>rijeka koja izlazi na sjeveroistoku Mississippija i teče prema jugu kroz zapadnu Alabamu da se pridruži rijeci Alabama i formira rijeku Mobile (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river that rises in northeastern Mississippi and flows southward through western Alabama to join the Alabama River and form the Mobile River [Tombigbee River]</p><p><b>rijeka koja izlazi na sjeveroistoku Mississippija i teče prema jugu kroz zapadnu Alabamu da se pridruži rijeci Alabama i formira rijeku Mobile (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river that rises in northeastern Mississippi and flows southward through western Alabama to join the Alabama River and form the Mobile River [Tombigbee]</p><p><b>lutrija u kojoj se karte izvlače iz vrtoglavog bubnja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lottery in which tickets are drawn from a revolving drum</p><p><b>djevojče</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a girl who behaves in a boyish manner [hoyden, romp]</p><p><b>korištena za djevojke (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> used of girls [hoydenish]</p><p><b>muškost kod žena (posebno kod djevojaka i mladih žena) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> masculinity in women (especially in girls and young women) [hoydenism]</p><p><b>nadgrobni reljef, nadgrobni kamen, nadgrobni spomenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stone that is used to mark a grave [gravestone, headstone]</p><p><b>mačak, mačor</b></p><p><i>n.</i> male cat [tom]</p><p><b>svezak, tom, velika knjiga, knjiga (velika), sveska</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a (usually) large and scholarly book</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 85%, guste krpe od kratkih, čvrstih dlakavih dlaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with densely matted filaments</p><p><i>adj.</i> densely covered with short matted woolly hairs [tomentous]</p><p><b>guste krpe od kratkih, čvrstih dlakavih dlaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> densely covered with short matted woolly hairs [tomentose]</p><p><b>vještački rast poput dlake na biljci, mreža sitnih krvnih žila između moždane površine pia mater i moždanog korteksa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> filamentous hairlike growth on a plant [fuzz, hair]</p><p><i>n.</i> a network of tiny blood vessels between the cerebral surface of the pia mater and the cerebral cortex [tomentum cerebri]</p><p><b>mreža sitnih krvnih žila između moždane površine pia mater i moždanog korteksa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a network of tiny blood vessels between the cerebral surface of the pia mater and the cerebral cortex [tomentum]</p><p><b>budala, lakrdijaš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who lacks good judgment [fool, muggins, sap, saphead]</p><p><b>glupo ili besmisleno ponašanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> foolish or senseless behavior [craziness, folly, foolery, indulgence, lunacy]</p><p><b>rod malajskih krokodila (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a genus of Malayan crocodiles [genus Tomistoma]</p><p><b>krokodil iz jugoistočne Azije sličan, ali manji od gavijala (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> crocodile of southeast Asia similar to but smaller than the gavial [false gavial]</p><p><b>vrsta automata, Thompson</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a .45-caliber submachine gun [Thompson submachine gun]</p><p><b>Pretenziozno ili glupo govor ili pisanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pretentious or silly talk or writing [baloney, bilgewater, boloney, bosh, drool, humbug, taradiddle, tarradiddle, tosh, twaddle]</p><p><b>Röntgenski stroj u kojem računalnik izgrađuje detaljnu sliku određene ravni kroz objekt iz višestrukih röntgenskih mjerenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> X-ray machine in which a computer builds a detailed image of a particular plane through an object from multiple X-ray measurements</p><p><b>(medicina) dobivanje slika unutrašnjosti tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) obtaining pictures of the interior of the body [imaging]</p><p><b>sutra, sutrašnje, sutradan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the day after today</p><p><i>n.</i> the near future</p><p><i>adv.</i> the next day, the day after, following the present day</p><p><b>utikač za dupe pištolja da bi se izbjegla prašina i vlažnost (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plug for the muzzle of a gun to keep out dust and moisture [tampion]</p><p><b>Nađen je u zapadnoj Indiji i Floridi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found off the West Indies and Florida [Haemulon aurolineatum]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjeni europski titmouse s svijetlom kobaltom plavim krilima i repom i krunom glave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely distributed European titmouse with bright cobalt blue wings and tail and crown of the head [Parus caeruleus, blue tit]</p><p><b>naglasak, teret, težina, ton, tona, zvuk</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a United States unit of weight equivalent to 2000 pounds [net ton, short ton]</p><p><i>n.</i> a British unit of weight equivalent to 2240 pounds [gross ton, long ton]</p><p><b>zvučni, tonski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> employing variations in pitch to distinguish meanings of otherwise similar words [tonic]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having tonality</p><p><b>jezik u kojem različiti tonovi razlikuju različita značenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a language in which different tones distinguish different meanings [tone language]</p><p><b>percepcija ugodnih aranžmana glazbenih nota (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the perception of pleasant arrangements of musical notes [melody]</p><p><b>sustav tonova koji se koristi u određenom jeziku ili dijalektu tonog jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the system of tones used in a particular language or dialect of a tone language [tone system]</p><p><b>ključ, tonalitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of 24 major or minor diatonic scales that provide the tonal framework for a piece of music [key]</p><p><b>boja, glas, nijansa, nota, prizvuk, ton, zvučan, zvuk, atmosfera, duh, raspoloženje, preliv, preljev, sekunda, skandirati, modulirati, konsolidirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of a person's voice [tone of voice]</p><p><i>n.</i> (linguistics) a pitch or change in pitch of the voice that serves to distinguish words in tonal languages</p><p><i>n.</i> (music) the distinctive property of a complex sound (a voice or noise or musical sound) [quality, timber, timbre]</p><p><i>n.</i> the general atmosphere of a place or situation and the effect that it has on people [feel, feeling, flavor, flavour, look, smell, spirit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a quality of a given color that differs slightly from another color [shade, tincture, tint]</p><p><i>n.</i> a notation representing the pitch and duration of a musical sound [musical note, note]</p><p><i>n.</i> a steady sound without overtones [pure tone]</p><p><i>n.</i> the elastic tension of living muscles, arteries, etc. that facilitate response to stimuli [tonicity, tonus]</p><p><i>n.</i> a musical interval of two semitones [step, whole step, whole tone]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of something (an act or a piece of writing) that reveals the attitudes and presuppositions of the author</p><p><i>v.</i> utter monotonously and repetitively and rhythmically [chant, intone]</p><p><i>v.</i> vary the pitch of one's speech [inflect, modulate]</p><p><i>v.</i> change the color or tone of</p><p><i>v.</i> change to a color image</p><p><i>v.</i> give a healthy elasticity to [strengthen, tone up]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mechanical device consisting of a light balanced arm that carries the cartridge [pickup, pickup arm]</p><p><b>nesposobnost razlikovanja razlikovanja u visini glasa (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an inability to distinguish differences in pitch [tin ear]</p><p><b>prigušiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> deaden (a sound or noise), especially by wrapping [damp, dampen, dull, muffle, mute]</p><p><i>v.</i> make less strong or intense [moderate, tame]</p><p><b>(glazba) čin ili način završetka glazbene fraze ili tona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (music) the act or manner of terminating a musical phrase or tone [release]</p><p><b>jezik u kojem različiti tonovi razlikuju različita značenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a language in which different tones distinguish different meanings [tonal language]</p><p><b>ton</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of a person's voice [tone]</p><p><b>orkestarska kompozicija zasnovana na književnosti ili narodnim pričama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an orchestral composition based on literature or folk tales