, crosspiece, traverse]</p><p><b>hod, kretanje, kretati se, mobilna, put, putovanje, putovati, putuje, voziti se, pokretanje, pokretljivost, otputovati, odlaziti na izlet, otići na izlet, proputovati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of going from one place to another [traveling, travelling]</p><p><i>n.</i> a movement through space that changes the location of something [change of location]</p><p><i>n.</i> self-propelled movement [locomotion]</p><p><i>v.</i> change location [go, locomote, move]</p><p><i>v.</i> undertake a journey or trip [journey]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a trip for pleasure [jaunt, trip]</p><p><i>v.</i> travel upon or across [journey]</p><p><i>v.</i> undergo transportation as in a vehicle</p><p><i>v.</i> travel from place to place, as for the purpose of finding work, preaching, or acting as a judge [move around]</p><p><b>putnička agencija, turistička agencija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agency that arranges personal travel</p><p><b>turistička agencija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who sells or arranges trips or tours for customers</p><p><b>iznos odobren za putovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sum allowed for travel [travel reimbursement]</p><p><b>pratiti, slijediti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> travel along a certain course [follow]</p><p><b>Račun na koji prodavači ili rukovodioci mogu naplatiti troškove putovanja i zabave (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an account to which salespersons or executives can charge travel and entertainment expenses [expense account]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) Uredbe (EU) br. 651/2014 Komisija je odlučila da se u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) Uredbe (EU) br. 651/2014 primjenjuje sljedeći uvjet: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bargain rate for travellers on commercial routes (usually air routes)</p><p><b>prolaziti, proći</b></p><p><i>v.</i> move past [go by, go past, pass, pass by, surpass]</p><p><b>(često u množini) troškovi koje zaposlenik ima za obavljanje posla i koje obično nadoknađuje poslodavac (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (frequently plural) expenses incurred by an employee in the performance of the job and usually reimbursed by the employer</p><p><b>vodič za putnike (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a guidebook for travelers [itinerary]</p><p><b>Mali lagani željezni stroj koji se može nositi dok putujete. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small lightweight iron that can be carried while traveling</p><p><b>Sestav za nošenje toaletnih predmeta tijekom putovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a kit for carrying toilet articles while traveling [toilet kit]</p><p><b>predviđena putna ruta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a proposed route of travel [itinerary]</p><p><b>putovanje voljno i u određenom smjeru s određenim ciljem (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> travel volitionally and in a certain direction with a certain goal</p><p><b>jurcati, juriti, jurišati, letjeti, projuriti, proletjeti, prozujati, prošišati, zujati, šišati, žuriti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> move very fast [hurry, speed, zip]</p><p><b>iznos odobren za putovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sum allowed for travel [travel allowance]</p><p><b>vrijeme kretanja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a period of time spent traveling</p><p><b>posjetiti, posjećivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> go to certain places as for sightseeing [visit]</p><p><b>Prljav od putovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> soiled from travel [travel-stained]</p><p><b>Prljav od putovanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> soiled from travel [travel-soiled]</p><p><b>Umoran od putovanja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tired by travel</p><p><b>koji je sposoban za prelazak (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> capable of being traversed [traversable]</p><p><b>hod, kretanje, kretati se, mobilna, put, putovanje, putovati, putuje, voziti se (od &quot;travel&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> traveled over or through</p><p><i>adj.</i> familiar with many parts of the world [travelled]</p><p><b>putnik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who changes location [traveller]</p><p><b>"Kreditno pismo" znači akreditiv izdan od strane banke ili ekspresne tvrtke koji se plaća na prijenos