g, swinging, swingy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> moving easily and quickly [light, lightsome]</p><p><b>automatsko otvaranje, okidanje, uključivanje (od &quot;tripping&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> moving with quick light steps [lightsomely]</p><p><b>triptihu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> art consisting of a painting or carving (especially an altarpiece) on three panels (usually hinged together)</p><p><b>trokutasta kost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wrist bone that articulates with the pisiform and hamate and lunate bones [cuneiform bone, os triquetrum, pyramidal bone, triquetral bone]</p><p><b>trokutasta kost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wrist bone that articulates with the pisiform and hamate and lunate bones [cuneiform bone, os triquetrum, pyramidal bone, triquetral]</p><p><b>Europski por u Velikoj Britaniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European leek naturalized in Great Britain [Allium triquetrum, three-cornered leek]</p><p><b>Stari grčki ili rimski galerijski ili ratni brod s tri stupnja vesla s svake strane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ancient Greek or Roman galley or warship having three tiers of oars on each side</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta ugljikohidrata koja daje tri molekula monosaharida na potpunu hidrolizu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a variety of carbohydrates that yield three monosaccharide molecules on complete hydrolysis</p><p><b>dijeliti na 3</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cut in three</p><p><b>Morbidni strah od broja 13 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a morbid fear of the number 13</p><p><b>koji pati od triskaidekaphobie (abnormalnog straha od broja 13) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suffering from triskaidekaphobia (abnormal fear of the number 13)</p><p><b>figura koja se sastoji od tri stilizirane ljudske ruke ili noge (ili tri savijene linije) koje zrače iz središta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a figure consisting of three stylized human arms or legs (or three bent lines) radiating from a center [triskelion]</p><p><b>figura koja se sastoji od tri stilizirane ljudske ruke ili noge (ili tri savijene linije) koje zrače iz središta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a figure consisting of three stylized human arms or legs (or three bent lines) radiating from a center [triskele]</p><p><b>dugotrajan grč mišića vilice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> prolonged spasm of the jaw muscles</p><p><b>Tercijarni natrijev fosfat koji se koristi kao gradivač u sapunima i deterdžentima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tertiary phosphate of sodium used as a builder in soaps and detergents [tribasic sodium phosphate, trisodium phosphate]</p><p><b>Tercijarni natrijev fosfat koji se koristi kao gradivač u sapunima i deterdžentima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the tertiary phosphate of sodium used as a builder in soaps and detergents [tribasic sodium phosphate, trisodium orthophosphate]</p><p><b>kromosomska abnormalnost u kojoj je u stanici jedan hromozom više od normalnog broja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chrosomal abnormality in which there is one more than the normal number of chromosomes in a cell</p><p><b>urođeni poremećaj uzrokovan dodatnim 21. hromozomom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a congenital disorder caused by having an extra 21st chromosome [Down's syndrome, Down syndrome, mongolianism, mongolism]</p><p><b>(Srednji vijek) nećak kralja Cornwalla koji se (prema legendi) zaljubio u nevestu svog ujaka (Iseult) nakon što su greškom popili ljubavni napitak koji ih je ostavio vječno zaljubljene jedni u druge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Middle Ages) the nephew of the king of Cornwall who (according to legend) fell in love with his uncle's bride (Iseult) after they mistakenly drank a love potion that left them eternally in love with each other [Tristram]</p><p><b>Francuski pjesnik (rođen u Rumunjskoj) koji je bio jedan od osnivača pokreta dada (1896-1963) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French poet (born in Romania) who was one of the cofounders of the dada movement (1896-1963) [Samuel Rosenstock, Tzara]</p><p><b>triglicerid stearinske kiseline (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a triglyceride of stearic acid [glycerol tristearate]</p><p><b>(Srednji vijek) nećak kralja Cornwalla koji se (prema legendi) zaljubio u nevestu svog ujaka (Iseult) nakon što su greškom popili ljubavni napitak koji ih je ostavio vječno zaljubljene jedni u druge (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Middle Ages) the nephew of the king of Cornwall who (according to legend) fell in love with his uncle's bride (Iseult) after they mistakenly drank a love potion that left them eternally in love with each other [Tristan]</p><p><b>riječ koja ima tri sloja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a word having three syllables</p><p><b>rijetka forma dikromacije koju karakterizira smanjena osjetljivost na plavu svjetlost koja rezultira nemogućnošću razlikovanja plave i žute svjetlosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> rare form of dichromacy characterized by a lowered sensitivity to blue light resulting in an inability to distinguish blue and yellow [blue-blindness]</p><p><b>nemogućnost da se vidi plava boja ili da se razlikuju plava i žuta boja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> inability to see the color blue or to distinguish the colors blue and yellow [blue-blind]</p><p><b>banalan, običan, otrcan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> repeated too often [banal, commonplace, hackneyed, old-hat, shopworn, stock, threadbare, timeworn, tired, well-worn]</p><p><b>banalan, običan, otrcan (od &quot;trite&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a trite manner</p><p><b>banalan, običan, otrcan (od &quot;trite&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> unoriginality as a result of being dull and hackneyed [staleness]</p><p><b>(Kršćanstvo) heretičko vjerovanje da su Otac, Sin i Sveti Duh tri odvojena boga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Christianity) the heretical belief that the Father and the Son and the Holy Spirit are three separate gods</p><p><b>netko (ne pravoslavni kršćanin) koji vjeruje da su Otac, Sin i Sveti Duh tri odvojena boga (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone (not an orthodox Christian) who believes that the Father and Son and Holy Ghost are three separate gods</p><p><b>godišnje žitnice iz područja Mediterana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annual cereal grasses from Mediterranean area [genus Triticum]</p><p><b>Uobičajeno uzgaja se u umjerenoj regiji u mnogim sortama zbog svog komercijalno važnog žitarica. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> widely cultivated in temperate regions in many varieties for its commercially important grain [common wheat]</p><p><b>pir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hardy wheat grown mostly in Europe for livestock feed [Triticum spelta, spelt]</p><p><b>tvrda crvena pšenica koja se uglavnom uzgaja u Rusiji i Njemačkoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hard red wheat grown especially in Russia and Germany [emmer, starch wheat, two-grain spelt]</p><p><b>pronađen divlje u Palestini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found wild in Palestine [wild emmer, wild wheat]</p><p><b>pšenica s tvrdim tamnim zrnama s visokim sadržajem glutena i koja se koristi za kruh i tjesteninu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wheat with hard dark-colored kernels high in gluten and used for bread and pasta [Triticum turgidum, durum, durum wheat, hard wheat, macaroni wheat]</p><p><b>pir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hardy wheat grown mostly in Europe for livestock feed [Triticum aestivum spelta, spelt]</p><p><b>pšenica s tvrdim tamnim zrnama s visokim sadržajem glutena i koja se koristi za kruh i tjesteninu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wheat with hard dark-colored kernels high in gluten and used for bread and pasta [Triticum durum, durum, durum wheat, hard wheat, macaroni wheat]</p><p><b>tritij</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a radioactive isotope of hydrogen</p><p><b>biljka iz roda Kniphofia s dugim lišćama poput trave i visokim štapovima crvenih ili žutih spuštenih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant of the genus Kniphofia having long grasslike leaves and tall scapes of red or yellow drooping flowers [flame-flower, flame flower, flameflower, kniphofia]</p><p><b>jezgra tritija, Triton</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) a sea god</p><p><i>n.</i> the largest moon of Neptune</p><p><i>n.</i> tropical marine gastropods having beautifully colored spiral shells</p><p><i>n.</i> small usually bright-colored semiaquatic salamanders of North America and Europe and northern Asia [newt]</p><p><b>uglavnom vodene salamandre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> chiefly aquatic salamanders [genus Triturus]</p><p><b>Sljedeći članak: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small semiaquatic salamander [common newt]</p><p><b>pobjeda, trijumf, trijumfirati, likovati, radovati se, veseliti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a successful ending of a struggle or contest [victory]</p><p><i>n.</i> the exultation of victory</p><p><i>v.</i> prove superior [prevail]</p><p><i>v.</i> be ecstatic with joy [rejoice, wallow]</p><p><i>v.</i> dwell on with satisfaction [crow, gloat]</p><p><i>v.</i> to express great joy [exuberate, exult, jubilate, rejoice]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na ili slavi trijumf, radosni i ponosni posebno zbog trijumfa ili uspjeha (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or celebrating a triumph</p><p><i>adj.</i> joyful and proud especially because of triumph or success [exultant, exulting, jubilant, prideful, rejoicing, triumphant]</p><p><b>monumentalni luk. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a monumental archway</p><p><b>pobjedonosan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> joyful and proud especially because of triumph or success [exultant, exulting, jubilant, prideful, rejoicing, triumphal]</p><p><i>adj.</i> experiencing triumph [victorious]</p><p><b>pobjedonosan (od &quot;triumphant&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a triumphant manner</p><p><b>jedan od tri grupe koje dijele javnu upravu ili civilnu vlast posebno u starom Rimu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of a group of three sharing public administration or civil authority especially in ancient Rome</p><p><b>trijumvirat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a group of three men responsible for public administration or civil authority</p><p><b>trojstvo</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being three in one</p><p><b>trovalentni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a valence of three</p><p><b>oralna cjepiva (koja sadrže živ ali oslabljeni poliovirus) koja se daju kako bi se osigurao imunitet na poliomijelitis (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oral vaccine (containing live but weakened poliovirus) that is given to provide immunity to poliomyelitis [OPV, Sabin vaccine, TOPV, oral poliovirus vaccine]</p><p><b>podmetač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a three-legged metal stand for supporting a cooking vessel in a hearth</p><p><i>n.</i> a stand with short feet used under a hot dish on a table</p><p><b>sitnice, trivijalnosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something of small importance [small beer, trifle, triviality]</p><p><b>beznačajan, elementaran, nevažan, običan, prost, svakidašnji, trivijalan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (informal) small and of little importance [fiddling, footling, lilliputian, little, niggling, petty, picayune, piddling, piffling]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of little substance or significance [superficial]</p><p><i>adj.</i> concerned with trivialities</p><p><b>učiniti trivijalno ili nevažno (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make trivial or insignificant [trivialize]</p><p><b>beznačajnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being unimportant and petty or frivolous [pettiness, puniness, slightness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a detail that is considered insignificant [trifle]</p><p><i>n.</i> something of small importance [small beer, trifle, trivia]</p><p><b>učiniti trivijalno ili nevažno (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make trivial or insignificant [trivialise]</p><p><b>beznačajno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with little effort</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a frivolously trivial manner</p><p><b>(Srednji vijek) uvodni nastavni program na srednjovjekovnom sveučilištu koji uključuje gramatiku, logiku i retoriku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Middle Ages) an introductory curriculum at a medieval university involving grammar and logic and rhetoric</p><p><b>maksimalni period slanja RM ćelija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the coordinated universal time when a transmission is sent from Earth to a spacecraft or other celestial body [transmission time]</p><p><b>RNK molekule prisutne u stanici (u najmanje 20 vrsta, svaka vrsta sposobna za kombinaciju s određenom aminokiselinom) koje vežu pravu aminokiselinu za proteinni lanac koji se sintetizira u ribosom stanice (prema uputama kodiranim u mRNK) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> RNA molecules present in the cell (in at least 20 varieties, each variety capable of combining with a specific amino acid) that attach the correct amino acid to the protein chain that is being synthesized at the ribosome of the cell (according to directions coded in the mRNA) [acceptor RNA, soluble RNA, transfer RNA]</p><p><b>izlučuju krik koji je namijenjen privlačenju drugih životinja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> emit a cry intended to attract other animals</p><p><b>od ili sastavljen od troketa (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or consisting of trochees</p><p><b>jedan od kostiju izbočine razvijen u blizini gornjeg kraja bedrene kosti na koju su mišići povezani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the bony prominences developed near the upper extremity of the femur to which muscles are attached</p><p><b>lijek za umirujuće krilo. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a medicated lozenge used to soothe the throat [cough drop, pastil, pastille]</p><p><b>metrička jedinica s naglaskom-nenaglaskom slogova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a metrical unit with stressed-unstressed syllables</p><p><b>kolibri, kolibrići, porodica Trochilidae, porodica kolibrića</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hummingbirds [family Trochilidae]</p><p><b>jedan od dva lubanjna živca na obje strane koji kontroliraju gornje nagibne mišiće očiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of the two cranial nerves on either side that control the superior oblique muscles of the eyes [fourth cranial nerve, trochlear nerve, trochlearis]</p><p><b>jedan od dva lubanjna živca na obje strane koji kontroliraju gornje nagibne mišiće očiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> either of the two cranial nerves on either side that control the superior oblique muscles of the eyes [fourth cranial nerve, trochlear, trochlearis]</p><p><b>jedan od dva lubanjna živca na obje strane koji kontroliraju gornje nagibne mišiće oči