></p><p><i>adj.</i> short and plump [dumpy, podgy, pudgy, roly-poly]</p><p><b>bužir, cijev, epruveta, lampa, podzemna željeznica, proba, tuba, valjak, cev, elektron cijev, elektronska cijev, katodna cijev, vakumska cijev, vakuumska cijev, metro</b></p><p><i>n.</i> conduit consisting of a long hollow object (usually cylindrical) used to hold and conduct objects or liquids or gases [tubing]</p><p><i>n.</i> electronic device consisting of a system of electrodes arranged in an evacuated glass or metal envelope [electron tube, thermionic tube, thermionic vacuum tube, thermionic valve, vacuum tube]</p><p><i>n.</i> a hollow cylindrical shape [pipe]</p><p><i>n.</i> (anatomy) any hollow cylindrical body structure [tube-shaped structure]</p><p><i>n.</i> an electric railway operating below the surface of the ground (usually in a city) [metro, subway, subway system, underground]</p><p><i>v.</i> provide with a tube or insert a tube into</p><p><i>v.</i> convey in a tube</p><p><i>v.</i> ride or float on an inflated tube</p><p><i>v.</i> place or enclose in a tube</p><p><b>probojni cijevasti proces većine eginodermi (morske zvijezde i jezerci i holoturijanci) koji imaju sisalo na kraju i koriste se npr. za kretanje i disanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tentacular tubular process of most echinoderms (starfish and sea urchins and holothurians) having a sucker at the end and used for e.g. locomotion and respiration</p><p><b>bunar napravljen pogonom cijevi u zemlju do sloja koji nosi vodu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a well made by driving a tube into the earth to a stratum that bears water [driven well]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> adjustable wrench for gripping and turning a pipe [pipe wrench]</p><p><b>s cijevastom nosom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a tubular nose</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih plodnih šišmiša rodova Nyctimene koji se razlikuju nosnicama koje se izvlače u različite cijevi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various fruit bats of the genus Nyctimene distinguished by nostrils drawn out into diverging tubes [harpy, harpy bat, tube-nosed fruit bat]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih plodnih šišmiša rodova Nyctimene koji se razlikuju nosnicama koje se izvlače u različite cijevi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various fruit bats of the genus Nyctimene distinguished by nostrils drawn out into diverging tubes [harpy, harpy bat, tube-nosed bat]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting a tube [cannular, tubelike, tubular, vasiform]</p><p><b>cijev</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (anatomy) any hollow cylindrical body structure [tube]</p><p><b>bačva, čabar, izvlačna kutija, kada, kada za kupanje, kupati se, vedro (od &quot;tub&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of a tire</p><p><b>bescijevni, bez unutra gume</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pneumatic tire not needing an inner tube to be airtight [tubeless tire]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a tire</p><p><b>pneumatske gume koje ne trebaju unutarnju cijev da bi bile hermetične (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> pneumatic tire not needing an inner tube to be airtight [tubeless]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting a tube [cannular, tube-shaped, tubular, vasiform]</p><p><b>gomolj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fleshy underground stem or root serving for reproductive and food storage</p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Tuberaceae: fungi whose fruiting bodies are typically truffles [genus Tuber]</p><p><b>Vječna biljka iz istočne i južne Sjedinjenih Država s sjajnim narandžastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> erect perennial of eastern and southern United States having showy orange flowers [Asclepias tuberosa, Indian paintbrush, butterfly weed, chigger flower, chiggerflower, orange milkweed, pleurisy root]</p><p><b>obitelj gljiva čiji askocarps sličan gomolji i razlikuju se u veličini od žulje do velike jabukove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> family of fungi whose ascocarps resemble tubers and vary in size from that of an acorn to that of a large apple [family Tuberaceae]</p><p><b>mali red gljiva koji pripadaju podpodručiju Ascomycota i imaju zatvorene podzemne askocarpe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small order of fungi belonging to the subdivision Ascomycota having closed underground ascocarps [order Tuberales]</p><p><b>oteklina koja je karakteristična za tuberkulozu, mala okrugla izbočina na biljci, izbočina na kosti posebno za vezanje mišića ili ligamenta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a swelling that is the characteristic lesion of tuberculosis</p><p><i>n.</i> small rounded wartlike protuberance on a plant [nodule]</p><p><i>n.</i> a protuberance on a bone especially for attachment of a muscle or ligament [eminence, tuberosity]</p><p><b>uzrok tuberkuloze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cause of tuberculosis [Mycobacterium tuberculosis]</p><p><b>osoba s plućnom tuberkulozom, u kojima se nalazi tuberkulozni otpad ili tuberkulozni bubreg, koji se odnosi na ili je prirodne prirode normalne tuberoznosti ili tuberkulacije, koji se odnose na tuberkulozu ili one koji pate od nje, koji predstavljaju ili boluju od tuberkuloze ili tuberkulogasa ili ih uzrokuje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person with pulmonary tuberculosis [consumptive, lunger]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by the presence of tuberculosis lesions or tubercles</p><p><i>adj.</i> pertaining to or of the nature of a normal tuberosity or tubercle</p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to tuberculosis or those suffering from it</p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting or afflicted with or caused by tuberculosis or the tubercle bacillus [tuberculous]</p><p><b>vrsta roda Tuberculariaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Tuberculariaceae [genus Tubercularia]</p><p><b>velika obitelj uglavnom saprofitnih imperfektnih gljiva (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large family of mainly saprophytic imperfect fungi [family Tuberculariaceae]</p><p><b>prekrivena tuberkulama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> covered with tubercles</p><p><b>sterična tekućina koja sadrži pročišćen protein derivat bakterije tuberkuloze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sterile liquid containing a purified protein derivative of the tuberculosis bacterium</p><p><b>kožni test za utvrđivanje prošle ili sadašnje infekcije bakterijom tuberkuloze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skin test to determine past or present infection with the tuberculosis bacterium [tuberculin test]</p><p><b>kožni test za utvrđivanje prošle ili sadašnje infekcije bakterijom tuberkuloze (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a skin test to determine past or present infection with the tuberculosis bacterium [tuberculin skin test]</p><p><b>koji podsjećaju na tuberkulozu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling tuberculosis</p><p><b>lepra obilježena tumorom na koži i kožnim živcima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> leprosy characterized by tumors in the skin and cutaneous nerves</p><p><b>tuberkuloza, tuberkuloze</b></p><p><i>n.</i> infection transmitted by inhalation or ingestion of tubercle bacilli and manifested in fever and small lesions (usually in the lungs but in various other parts of the body in acute stages) [T.B., TB]</p><p><b>tuberkulozan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> constituting or afflicted with or caused by tuberculosis or the tubercle bacillus [tubercular]</p><p><b>tuberoza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tuberous Mexican herb having grasslike leaves and cultivated for its spikes of highly fragrant lily-like waxy white flowers [Polianthes tuberosa]</p><p><b>izbočina na kosti posebno za vezanje mišića ili ligamenta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a protuberance on a bone especially for attachment of a muscle or ligament [eminence, tubercle]</p><p><b>od ili povezane s ili nalik gomolji (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or resembling a tuber</p><p><b>bilo koji od brojnih begonija s velikim gomoljastim korijenima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous begonias having large tuberous roots</p><p><b>biljka koja raste iz gomolja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant growing from a tuber</p><p