/p><p><i>n.</i> (medicine) the chemical analysis of urine (for medical diagnosis) [urinalysis]</p><p><b>Uranija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the Muse of astronomy</p><p><i>n.</i> goddess of love [Venus]</p><p><b>mineral koji se sastoji od uranijuma oksida i u tragovima radija i torija i polonija i olova i helija (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mineral consisting of uranium oxide and trace amounts of radium and thorium and polonium and lead and helium [pitchblende]</p><p><b>uranij, uran</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heavy toxic silvery-white radioactive metallic element [U, atomic number 92]</p><p><b>s masenim brojem 235 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a uranium isotope with mass number 235</p><p><b>najčešći izotop uranijuma (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the commonest isotope of uranium</p><p><b>Svaka ruda iz koje se može ekstrahirati uran (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any ore from which uranium can be extracted</p><p><b>astronom, zvjezdoznanac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a physicist who studies astronomy [astronomer, stargazer]</p><p><b>astronomija, zvjezdoznanstvo, zvjezdoznastvo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of physics that studies celestial bodies and the universe as a whole [astronomy]</p><p><b>operacija za popravak oštećenja nepca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> surgical correction of a defect of the palate</p><p><b>Zvezda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> stargazers [family Uranoscopidae]</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) bog nebesa, džinovski planet s prstenom ledenih čestica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) god of the heavens [Ouranos]</p><p><i>n.</i> a giant planet with a ring of ice particles</p><p><b>bivalentni radikal UO2 koji formira soli s kiselinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bivalent radical UO2 which forms salts with acids [uranyl group, uranyl radical]</p><p><b>bivalentni radikal UO2 koji formira soli s kiselinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bivalent radical UO2 which forms salts with acids [uranyl, uranyl radical]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,5% ili više, ali ne više od 0,5% (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a yellow salt obtained by the reaction of uranium salts with nitric acid</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom polipropilena (CAS RN 1344-26-8) i (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt obtained by the reaction of uranium salts with oxalic acid</p><p><b>bivalentni radikal UO2 koji formira soli s kiselinama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the bivalent radical UO2 which forms salts with acids [uranyl, uranyl group]</p><p><b>giht</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a painful inflammation of the big toe and foot caused by defects in uric acid metabolism resulting in deposits of the acid and its salts in the blood and joints [gout, gouty arthritis]</p><p><b>sol mokraćne kiseline (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a salt of uric acid</p><p><b>prisutnost abnormalnih količina soli mokraćne kiseline u krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> presence of abnormal amounts of uric acid salts in the blood</p><p><b>prisutnost neuobičajeno velike količine mokraćne kiseline u urinu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> presence of abnormally large amounts of uric acid in the urine</p><p><b>gradski, urbani, urbanistička, urbanistički, urbanističkoj, urbanog, urbane, urbano, urbanu, urban</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or concerned with a city or densely populated area</p><p><i>adj.</i> located in or characteristic of a city or city life</p><p><b>gradsko područje, urbana sredina, urbano područje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a geographical area constituting a city or town [populated area]</p><p><b>Veliki i gusto naseljeni gradski prostor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large and densely populated urban area [city, metropolis]</p><p><b>Geriljan koji se bori samo u gradovima i gradovima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a guerrilla who fights only in cities and towns</p><p><b>Francuski papa od 1088. do 1099. čije propovijedi pozivaju na Prvi križarski rat (1042-1099) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French pope from 1088 to 1099 whose sermons called for the First Crusade (1042-1099) [Odo, Odo of Lagery, Otho, Otho of Lagery]</p><p><b>Priča koja se pojavljuje misteriozno i širi se spontano u različitim oblicima i obično je lažna. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a story that appears mysteriously and spreads spontaneously in various forms and is usually false</p><p><b>urbanizam, urbanističko planiranje, urbanizma</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the branch of architecture dealing with the design and organization of urban space and activities</p><p><i>n.</i> determining and drawing up plans for the future physical arrangement and condition of a community [city planning, town planning]</p><p><b>gradska obnova</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the clearing and rebuilding and redevelopment of urban slums</p><p><b>konurbacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an aggregation or continuous network of urban communities [conurbation, sprawl]</p><p><b>akutna infekcija uzrokovana riketsijom i prenosi se ugrizem zaražene buhe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> acute infection caused by rickettsia and transmitted by the bite of an infected flea [endemic typhus, murine typhus, rat typhus]</p><p><b>Francuski papa od 1362. do 1370. koji je pokušao ponovno uspostaviti papinstvo u Rimu ali se 1367. vratio u Avignon u nadi da će okončati rat između Francuske i Engleske. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French pope from 1362 to 1370 who tried to reestablish the papacy in Rome but in 1367 returned to Avignon hoping to end the war between France and England [Guillaume de Grimoard]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1378. do 1389. čiji je sporni izbor započeo Veliki raskol (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1378 to 1389 whose contested election began the Great Schism [Bartolomeo Prignano]</p><p><b>Talijanski papa od 1623. do 1644. koji je odobrio osudu Galileja, ali ga je kasnije oslobodio (1568-1644) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Italian pope from 1623 to 1644 who sanctioned the condemnation of Galileo but later freed him (1568-1644) [Maffeo Barberini]</p><p><b>Univerzitet u istočnom središnjem Illinoisu susjednom Champaignu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a university town in east central Illinois adjoining Champaign</p><p><b>l