recommend]</p><p><i>v.</i> spur on or encourage especially by cheers and shouts [barrack, cheer, exhort, inspire, pep up, root on, urge on]</p><p><b>inkontinencija mokraćnog trakta koja se obično može pripisati nesvjesnim kontrakcijama mišića mjehura, što rezultira hitnom potrebom za mokrenjem uz iznenadni gubitak mokraće. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> urinary incontinence that is generally attributable to involuntary contracts of the bladder muscle resulting in an urgent need to urinate accompanied by a sudden loss of urine</p><p><b>bodriti, obodriti, forsirati, nagnati, natjerati, natjeravati, navaljivati, navesti, navoditi, prešati, tjerati, urgirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> spur on or encourage especially by cheers and shouts [barrack, cheer, exhort, inspire, pep up, root on, urge]</p><p><i>v.</i> force or impel in an indicated direction [exhort, press, urge]</p><p><b>hitnost, nametljivost, nužda, žurba, žurnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being urgent</p><p><i>n.</i> pressing importance requiring speedy action</p><p><i>n.</i> an urgent situation calling for prompt action</p><p><i>n.</i> insistent solicitation and entreaty [importunity, urging]</p><p><b>hitan, hitno, imperativan, nametljiv, nasrtljiv, neodložan, nužan, uporan, urgentan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> compelling immediate action [pressing]</p><p><b>hitno, očajnički</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with great urgency [desperately]</p><p><b>Sredozemski lilijani (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Mediterranean liliaceous plants [genus Urginea]</p><p><b>s gustima šiljcima malih bijelih cvijeća i s lukom s ljekovitim svojstvima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having dense spikes of small white flowers and yielding a bulb with medicinal properties [sea onion, sea squill, squill]</p><p><b>bodriti, nagovarati, navaljivati, pozivati, požurivati, tjerati, ubrzavati, zahtijevati (od &quot;urge&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a verbalization that encourages you to attempt something [goad, goading, prod, prodding, spur, spurring]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of