ne posjetitelje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the United States intelligence agency that protects current and former presidents and vice presidents and their immediate families and protects distinguished foreign visitors [SS, Secret Service, US Secret Service, United States Secret Service]</p><p><b>gljivice iz obitelji los-smutova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fungus family of loose smuts [family Ustilaginaceae]</p><p><b>parazitske gljivice koje uzrokuju smuts (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> parasitic fungi causing smuts [order Ustilaginales]</p><p><b>rod nesposobnih gljiva koji uzrokuju bolesti biljaka kao što je mršavljenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of imperfect fungi causing plant diseases like smut [genus Ustilaginoidea]</p><p><b>gljivica koja uzrokuje zelenu prljavštinu u rižu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fungus causing green smut in rice [green smut fungus]</p><p><b>tip rod Ustilaginaceae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus of the Ustilaginaceae [genus Ustilago]</p><p><b>mjehurasta snijet kukuruza</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common smut attacking Indian corn causing greyish white swellings that rupture to expose a black spore mass [boil smut]</p><p><b>Britanski glumac i dramaturg (1921-2004) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> British actor and playwright (1921-2004) [Peter Alexander Ustinov, Sir Peter Ustinov]</p><p><b>običan, redovan, redovit, uobičajen, uobičajeni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> occurring or encountered or experienced or observed frequently or in accordance with regular practice or procedure</p><p><i>adj.</i> commonly encountered [common]</p><p><b>obično, redovito, u pravilu, uglavnom, uobičajeno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> under normal conditions [commonly, normally, ordinarily, unremarkably]</p><p><b>običan, redovan, redovit, uobičajen, uobičajeni (od &quot;usual&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> commonness by virtue of not being unusual</p><p><b>plodouživanje, uživanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a legal right to use and derive profit from property belonging to someone else provided that the property itself is not injured in any way</p><p><b>osoba koja posjeduje imovinu po korisničkom pravu, o ili povezan s prirodom korisničkog prava (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who holds property by usufruct</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the nature of a usufruct</p><p><b>vjerski pokret perzijskih šiitskih muslimana u 17. stoljeću u Iranu koji se protivi Akhbariju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a religious movement by Persian Shiite Muslims in 17th century Iran that is opposed to the Akhbari</p><p><b>Bujumbura</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Burundi [Bujumbura, capital of Burundi]</p><p><b>lihvar, pijavica, zelenaš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who lends money at excessive rates of interest [loan shark, moneylender, shylock]</p><p><b>zelenaški</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> greatly exceeding bounds of reason or moderation [exorbitant, extortionate, outrageous, steep, unconscionable]</p><p><b>zelenaški (od &quot;usurious&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to an exorbitant degree [exorbitantly, extortionately]</p><p><b>oteti, preoteti, prisvojiti, uzeti, uzurpirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> seize and take control without authority and possibly with force [arrogate, assume, seize, take over]</p><p><i>v.</i> take the place of</p><p><b>prisvajanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> entry to another's property without right or permission [encroachment, intrusion, trespass, violation]</p><p><i>n.</i> wrongfully seizing and holding (an office or powers) by force (especially the seizure of a throne or supreme authority)</p><p><b>oteti, preoteti, prisvojiti, uzeti, uzurpirati (od &quot;usurp&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who wrongfully or illegally seizes and holds the place of another [supplanter]</p><p><b>lihvarenje, lihvarstvo, zelenaš kamate, zelenaštvo, kamatarenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an exorbitant or unlawful rate of interest [vigorish]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of lending money at an exorbitant rate of interest</p><p><b>lokalno vrijeme na 0 meridijanu koji prolazi kroz Greenwich, Engleska, dr