 ženu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (legal terminology) the Latin word for wife [ux.]</p><p><b>Pripada ili karakteristika žene (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> befitting or characteristic of a wife [wifelike, wifely]</p><p><b>Muž koji ubija svoju ženu., Ubojstvo supruge od strane njenog muža. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a husband who murders his wife</p><p><i>n.</i> the murder of a wife by her husband</p><p><b>glupo voljeti ili biti podređen svojoj ženi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> foolishly fond of or submissive to your wife</p><p><b>Na ljubazan i uzvišeni način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a loving and uxorious manner</p><p><b>glupo ljubljenje ili pretjerano podložnost svojoj ženi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> foolish fondness for or excessive submissiveness to one's wife</p><p><b>pripadnik naroda koji govori ujgur i živi u Sinđijangu i susjednim područjima, Turkijski jezik kojim govori oko 7.000.000 Ujgura na sjeverozapadu Kine., pisac (iz aramejskog) koji se koristio za pisanje ujgurskog jezika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a people who speak Uighur and live in Xinjiang and adjacent areas [Uighur, Uigur]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Turkic language spoken by approximately 7,000,000 Uighur in extreme northwestern China [Uighur, Uigur]</p><p><i>n.</i> the script (derived from Aramaic) used to write the Uighur language [Uighur, Uigur]</p><p><b>Uzbeci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a Turkic people of Uzbekistan and neighboring areas [Usbeg, Usbek, Uzbeg, Uzbek]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Turkic language spoken by the Uzbek [Usbeg, Usbek, Uzbeg, Uzbek]</p><p><b>Uzbeci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a Turkic people of Uzbekistan and neighboring areas [Usbeg, Usbek, Uzbak, Uzbek]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Turkic language spoken by the Uzbek [Usbeg, Usbek, Uzbak, Uzbek]</p><p><b>Uzbeci</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a Turkic people of Uzbekistan and neighboring areas [Usbeg, Usbek, Uzbak, Uzbeg]</p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked republic in west central Asia [Republic of Uzbekistan, Uzbekistan]</p><p><i>n.</i> the Turkic language spoken by the Uzbek [Usbeg, Usbek, Uzbak, Uzbeg]</p><p><b>Republika bez izlaza na more u zapadnoj središnjoj Aziji. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked republic in west central Asia [Republic of Uzbekistan, Uzbek]</p><p><b>od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Uzbekistan ili njegov narod ili kulturu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Uzbekistan or its people or culture</p><p><b>novčana jedinica u Uzbekistanu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monetary unit in Uzbekistan</p><p><b>Uzi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a type of submachine gun that is designed and manufactured in Israel</p><p><b>pet, v</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of potential equal to the potential difference between two points on a conductor carrying a current of 1 ampere when the power dissipated between the two points is 1 watt [volt]</p><p><i>n.</i> a soft silvery white toxic metallic element used in steel alloys [atomic number 23, vanadium]</p><p><i>n.</i> the cardinal number that is the sum of four and one [5, Little Phoebe, Phoebe, cinque, fin, five, fivesome, pentad, quint, quintet, quintuplet]</p><p><i>n.</i> the 22nd letter of the Roman alphabet</p><p><i>adj.</i> being one more than four [5, five]</p><p><b>vrat odjeće ima oblik slova V. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the neck of a garment has the shape of the letter V</p><p><b>znak (za pobjedu) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sign (for victory)</p><p><b>mala krila koja nosi bombu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small jet-propelled winged missile that carries a bomb [buzz bomb, doodlebug, flying bomb, robot bomb]</p><p><b>oznaka za konzervirane mješovite povrćne sokove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brand name for canned mixed vegetable juices</p><p><b>dan pobjede</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the day of a victory [Victory Day]</p><p><b>datum pobjede saveznika u Europi, Drugi svjetski rat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the date of Allied victory in Europe, World War II [8 May 1945]</p><p><b>datum pobjede Saveznika nad Japanom, Drugi svjetski rat