re, value]</p><p><b>cijena, normiranje, određivanje, određivanje vrijednosti, procjena, procjenjivanje, valorizacija, vrednovanje, vrijednost, evaluacija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an appraisal of the value of something [evaluation, rating]</p><p><i>n.</i> assessed price</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, "skupna imovina" znači imovina koja se koristi za upravljanje poslovnim gospodarstvom u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reserve fund created by a charge against profits in order to provide for changes in the value of a company's assets [allowance, allowance account, valuation reserve]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 4. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, "skupna imovina" znači imovina koja se koristi za upravljanje poslovnim gospodarstvom u skladu s člankom 4. točkom (a) ovog članka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a reserve fund created by a charge against profits in order to provide for changes in the value of a company's assets [allowance, allowance account, valuation account]</p><p><b>osoba koja službeno procjenjuje vrijednost ili vrijednost ili kvalitetu stvari. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who estimates officially the worth or value or quality of things [appraiser]</p><p><b>cijena, cijeniti, korisnost, korist, poštovati, procijeniti, veličina, vrijednost, veličine, vrijednosti, vrijednošću, vrednost, vridnost, kvaliteta, uvažavati, štovati, bodovati, procjenjivati, valorizirati, vrednovati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a numerical quantity measured or assigned or computed</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality (positive or negative) that renders something desirable or valuable</p><p><i>n.</i> the amount (of money or goods or services) that is considered to be a fair equivalent for something else [economic value]</p><p><i>n.</i> relative darkness or lightness of a color</p><p><i>n.</i> (music) the relative duration of a musical note [note value, time value]</p><p><i>n.</i> an ideal accepted by some individual or group</p><p><i>v.</i> fix or determine the value of</p><p><i>v.</i> hold dear [appreciate, prize, treasure]</p><p><i>v.</i> regard highly [esteem, prise, prize, respect]</p><p><i>v.</i> evaluate or estimate the nature, quality, ability, extent, or significance of [appraise, assess, evaluate, measure, valuate]</p><p><i>v.</i> estimate the value of [rate]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je osoba koja je podložna ocjeni u skladu s člankom 5. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, ona mora imati pravo na određene informacije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an assessment that reveals more about the values of the person making the assessment than about the reality of what is assessed [value judgment]</p><p><b>U slučaju da je osoba koja je podložna ocjeni u skladu s člankom 5. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ili (b) ove Uredbe, ona mora imati pravo na određene informacije. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an assessment that reveals more about the values of the person making the assessment than about the reality of what is assessed [value judgement]</p><p><b>vrijednosne orijentacije</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principles of right and wrong that are accepted by an individual or a social group [ethic, moral principle, value-system]</p><p><b>Izjava o poželjnosti nečega. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a statement of the desirability of something</p><p><b>porez na dodanu vrijednost, porez na promet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tax levied on the difference between a commodity's price before taxes and its cost of production [VAT, ad valorem tax]</p><p><b>načela dobra i zla koja su prihvaćena od strane pojedinca ili društvene skupine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the principles of right and wrong that are accepted by an individual or a social group [ethic, moral principle, value orientation]</p><p><b>procijeniti, utvrđivati vrijednosti</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (usually used in combination) having value of a specified kind</p><p><i>adj.</i> held in great esteem for admirable qualities especially of an intrinsic nature [precious]</p><p><b>bez značaja, bezvrijedan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of no value</p><p><b>bez značaja, bezvrijedan (od &quot;valueless&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having none of the properties that endow something with value</p><p><b>procjenitelj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who assesses the monetary worth of possessions</p><p><b>vrijednosti, vrijednostima, političko ponašanje, VREDNOTE, stavovi, uvjerenja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> beliefs of a person or social group in which they have an emotional investment (either for or against something)</p><p><b>elektron cijev, kapak, klip, krilo, razvodnik, ventil, ventilima, zalistak (srce), zasun, oduška, zaklopac, zapornica, zatvarač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a structure in a hollow organ (like the heart) with a flap to insure one-way flow of fluid through it</p><p><i>n.</i> device in a brass wind instrument for varying the length of the air column to alter the pitch of a tone</p><p><i>n.</i> control consisting of a mechanical device for controlling the flow of a fluid</p><p><i>n.</i> the entire one-piece shell of a snail and certain other molluscs</p><p><i>n.</i> one of the paired hinged shells of certain molluscs and of brachiopods</p><p><b>polugom koja se okreće u središtu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lever pivoted at the center [rocker arm]</p><p><b>motor s unutarnjim sagorevanjem s ulaznim i izduvnim ventilima smještena u glavu cilindra (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> internal-combustion engine having both inlet and exhaust valves located in the cylinder head</p><p><b>S druge konstrukcije od metala ili od gume ili gume (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of brass instruments) having valves</p><p><b>mali ventil (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small valve [valvula, valvule]</p><p><b>rez u stenozni srčani ventil za ublažavanje začepljenosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> incision into a stenosed cardiac valve to relieve the obstruction [valvulotomy]</p><p><b>mali ventil (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small valve [valvelet, valvule]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,15 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or operating by means of valves</p><p><b>srčane bolesti uzrokovane stenozom srčanih zalisaka i ometanim protokom krvi ili uzrokovane degeneracijom i regurgitacijom krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> heart disease caused by stenosis of the cardiac valves and obstructed blood flow or caused by degeneration and blood regurgitation</p><p><b>nesposobnost zatvaranja tjelesnog ventila u potpunosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inability of a bodily valve to close completely</p><p><b>mali ventil (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small valve [valvelet, valvula]</p><p><b>upale zaliska (posebno srčanog zaliska zbog reumatske groznice) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammation of a valve (especially of a cardiac valve as a consequence of rheumatic fever)</p><p><b>rez u stenozni srčani ventil za ublažavanje začepljenosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> incision into a stenosed cardiac valve to relieve the obstruction [valvotomy]</p><p><b>top od oklopa štiteći podlaktu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> cannon of plate armor protecting the forearm [lower cannon]</p><p><b>Odjednom odem. (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> leave suddenly [decamp, skip]</p><p><b>koketa, vamp, zakrpa, zavoditi, zavodnica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a seductive woman who uses her sex appeal to exploit men [coquette, flirt, minx, prickteaser, tease, vamper]</p><p><i>n.</i> an improvised musical accompaniment</p><p><i>n.</i> piece of leather forming the front part of the upper of a shoe</p><p><i>v.</i> make up [vamp up]</p><p><i>v.</i> piece (something old) with a new part [vamp up]</p><p><i>v.</i> act seductively with (someone)</p><p><i>v.</i> provide (a shoe) with a new vamp [revamp]</p><p><b>-Pokupiti., komad (nešto staro) s novim dijelom (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> make up [vamp]</p><p><i>v.</i> piece (something old) with a new part [vamp]</p><p><b>koketa, vamp, zakrpa, zavoditi, zavodnica (od &quot;vamp&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a seductive woman who uses her sex appeal to exploit men [coquette, flirt, minx, prickteaser, tease, vamp]</p><p><b>vampir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (folklore) a corpse that rises at night to drink the blood of the living [lamia]</p><p><b>bilo koji od različitih tropskih američkih šišmiša iz obitelji Desmodontidae koji grize sisare i ptice kako bi se hranili njihovom krvlju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various tropical American bats of the family Desmodontidae that bite mammals and birds to feed on their blood [true vampire bat]</p><p><b>Vjerovanje u postojanje vampira., Vampirske postupke ili prakse. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> belief in the existence of vampires</p><p><i>n.</i> the actions or practices of a vampire</p><p><b>furgon, kombi, natkrivena kola za prijevoz robe, prethodnica, prikolica, teretna kola, Van, avangarda</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any creative group active in the innovation and application of new concepts and techniques in a given field (especially in the arts) [avant-garde, new wave, vanguard]</p><p><i>n.</i> the leading units moving at the head of an army [vanguard]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Great Britain) a closed railroad car that carries baggage or freight</p><p><i>n.</i> a camper equipped with living quarters [caravan]</p><p><i>n.</i> a truck with an enclosed cargo space</p><p><b>Američki fizičar koji je otkrio dva pojasa napunjenih čestica iz sunčevog vjetra zarobljenih Zemljinim magnetnim poljem (rođen 1914.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States physicist who discovered two belts of charged particles from the solar wind trapped by the Earth's magnetic field (born in 1914) [James Alfred Van Allen]</p><p><b>pojas naelektrisanih čestica (iz kosmičkih zraka) iznad Zemlje zarobljen Zemljinim magnetnim poljem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a belt of charged particles (resulting from cosmic rays) above the Earth trapped by the Earth's magnetic field</p><p><b>Njemački skladatelj instrumentalne glazbe (posebno simfonijske i komorne glazbe) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German composer of instrumental music (especially symphonic and chamber music) [Beethoven, Ludwig