, zanemariv</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden or mysterious disappearance</p><p><i>n.</i> a sudden disappearance from sight</p><p><b>Krema koja se koristi u kozmetičkim svrhama (uglavnom od strane žena) za omekšavanje i čišćenje kože. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cream used cosmetically (mostly by women) for softening and cleaning the skin [cold cream, coldcream, face cream]</p><p><b>točka nestajanja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the point beyond which something disappears or ceases to exist</p><p><i>n.</i> the appearance of a point on the horizon at which parallel lines converge</p><p><b>nestajanje, zamiranje, zanemariv (od &quot;vanishing&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> so as to disappear or approach zero</p><p><b>ispraznost, samodopadanje, sujeta, taština, uobraženost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> feelings of excessive pride [amour propre, conceit, self-love]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being valueless or futile [emptiness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being unduly vain and conceited [conceit, conceitedness]</p><p><i>n.</i> low table with mirror or mirrors where one sits while dressing or applying makeup [dresser, dressing table, toilet table]</p><p><b>uzaludan i bezobziran život, posebno u velikim gradovima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vain and frivolous lifestyle especially in large cities</p><p><b>Američki elektroinženjer koji je dizajnirao rani analogni kompjuter i koji je vodio znanstveni program Sjedinjenih Država tijekom Drugog svjetskog rata (1890-1974) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States electrical engineer who designed an early analogue computer and who led the scientific program of the United States during World War II (1890-1974) [Bush]</p><p><b>pobijediti, pokoriti, shrvati, istući</b></p><p><i>v.</i> come out better in a competition, race, or conflict [beat, beat out, crush, shell, trounce]</p><p><b>Moguće da će biti poraženi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> susceptible to being defeated [beatable, vincible]</p><p><b>osvajač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who is victorious by force