ue [evaporate, vaporize]</p><p><b>evaporirati, hlapiti, hlapjeti, ishlapiti, ishlapjeti, isparavati, ispariti, vaporizirati (od &quot;vaporise&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device that puts out a substance in the form of a vapor (especially for medicinal inhalation) [vaporizer]</p><p><b>koji podsećaju na par ili imaju karakteristike pare (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling or characteristic of vapor [vaporific, vaporous, vapourific, vapourish, vapourous]</p><p><b>isparljiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (used of substances) capable of being volatilized [evaporable, vaporific, vapourific, vapourisable, volatilisable, volatilizable]</p><p><b>isparavanje, hlapljenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> annihilation by vaporizing something [vaporisation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of becoming a vapor [evaporation, vapor, vaporisation, vapour]</p><p><b>ishlapiti, isparavati, evaporirati, hlapiti, hlapjeti, ishlapjeti, ispariti, vaporizirati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> kill with or as if with a burst of gunfire or electric current or as if by shooting [zap]</p><p><i>v.</i> turn into gas [aerify, gasify, vaporise]</p><p><i>v.</i> lose or cause to lose liquid by vaporization leaving a more concentrated residue [evaporate, vaporise]</p><p><i>v.</i> decrease rapidly and disappear [fly, vanish]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,15 do 0,15 g/cm3 (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> converted into a gas or vapor [gasified, vapourised, volatilised, volatilized]</p><p><b>isparivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a device that puts out a substance in the form of a vapor (especially for medicinal inhalation) [vaporiser]</p><p><b>parni, pun pare, sličan pari, zamagljen, proziran</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> so thin as to transmit light [cobwebby, diaphanous, filmy, gauze-like, gauzy, gossamer, see-through, sheer, transparent, vapourous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling or characteristic of vapor [vaporific, vaporish, vapourific, vapourish, vapourous]</p><p><i>adj.</i> filled with vapor [miasmal, miasmic, vapourous]</p><p><b>parni, pun pare, sličan p