roup [division]</p><p><i>n.</i> the second moment around the mean</p><p><i>n.</i> a difference between conflicting facts or claims or opinions [disagreement, discrepancy, divergence]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being subject to variation [variability, variableness]</p><p><i>n.</i> an official dispensation to act contrary to a rule or regulation (typically a building regulation)</p><p><i>n.</i> an activity that varies from a norm or standard [variation]</p><p><b>dopunski, drugi način, drugi oblik, promjenjiv, različit, rezervni, varijacija, varijanta, inačica, verzija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an event that departs from expectations [discrepancy, variance]</p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) a group of organisms within a species that differ in trivial ways from similar groups [form, strain, var.]</p><p><i>n.</i> a variable quantity that is random [chance variable, random variable, stochastic variable, variate]</p><p><i>n.</i> something a little different from others of the same type [edition, variation, version]</p><p><i>adj.</i> differing from a norm or standard</p><p><i>adj.</i> exhibiting variation and change</p><p><b>mijenjati, slučajna varijabla, slučajna vrijednost, varirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variable quantity that is random [chance variable, random variable, stochastic variable, variant]</p><p><b>kolebanje, odstupanje, oscilacija, preinaka, promjena, rasipanje, razlika, varijacija, varijanta, variranje, inačica, verzija, mutant</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an instance of change [fluctuation]</p><p><i>n.</i> an activity that varies from a norm or standard [variance]</p><p><i>n.</i> a repetition of a musical theme in which it is modified or embellished</p><p><i>n.</i> something a little different from others of the same type [edition, variant, version]</p><p><i>n.</i> an artifact that deviates from a norm or standard</p><p><i>n.</i> the angle (at a particular location) between magnetic north and true north [magnetic declination, magnetic variation]</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of varying or being varied</p><p><i>n.</i> (astronomy) any perturbation of the mean motion or orbit of a planet or satellite (especially a perturbation of the earth's moon)</p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) an organism that has characteristics resulting from chromosomal alteration [mutant, mutation, sport]</p><p><i>n.</i> (ballet) a solo dance or dance figure [pas seul]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of changing or altering something slightly but noticeably from the norm or standard</p><p><b>varičele</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an acute contagious disease caused by herpes varicella zoster virus [chickenpox]</p><p><b>član obitelji herpes virusa koji je odgovoran za boginja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the member of the herpes virus family that is responsible for chickenpox</p><p><b>koji sliči na osip kišne boginja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> resembling the rash of chickenpox</p><p><b>varikokela</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dilatation of the veins associated with the spermatic cord in the testes</p><p><b>šaren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a variety of colors [varicoloured, variegated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having sections or patches colored differently and usually brightly [calico, motley, multi-color, multi-colored, multi-colour, multi-coloured, multicolor, multicolored, multicolour, multicoloured, painted, particolored, particoloured, piebald, pied, varicoloured]</p><p><b>šaren</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a variety of colors [varicolored, variegated]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having sections or patches colored differently and usually brightly [calico, motley, multi-color, multi-colored, multi-colour, multi-coloured, multicolor, multicolored, multicolour, multicoloured, painted, particolored, particoloured, piebald, pied, varicolored]</p><p><b>koji se odnosi na proširenje vena, koji se tiče vena, koji trpi od proširenja vena, nabreknut kao proširena vena, varikozan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> abnormally swollen or knotty</p><p><b>vena koja je trajno proširena (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vein that is permanently dilated</p>