irusa boginja s smrtnom stopom do 25 posto (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a highly contagious viral disease characterized by fever and weakness and skin eruption with pustules that form scabs that slough off leaving scars [smallpox, variola]</p><p><i>n.</i> a type of smallpox virus that has a fatality rate of up to 25 percent [variola major virus]</p><p><b>vrsta virusa boginja s smrtnom stopom do 25 posto (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a type of smallpox virus that has a fatality rate of up to 25 percent [variola major]</p><p><b>blagi oblik boginja uzrokovan manje virulentnim oblikom virusa, vrsta virusa boginja s smrtnom stopom od oko 1 posto (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mild form of smallpox caused by a less virulent form of the virus [Cuban itch, Kaffir pox, West Indian smallpox, alastrim, milk pox, pseudosmallpox, pseudovariola, white pox]</p><p><i>n.</i> a type of smallpox virus that has a fatality rate of about 1 percent [variola minor virus]</p><p><b>vrsta virusa boginja s smrtnom stopom od oko 1 posto (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a type of smallpox virus that has a fatality rate of about 1 percent [variola minor]</p><p><b>lokalna infekcija izazvana kod ljudi cijepljenjem virusa koji uzrokuje boginje krava kako bi se osigurala otpornost na boginje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a local infection induced in humans by inoculation with the virus causing cowpox in order to confer resistance to smallpox [vaccina, vaccinia, variola vaccine, variola vaccinia]</p><p><b>lokalna infekcija izazvana kod ljudi cijepljenjem virusa koji uzrokuje boginje krava kako bi se osigurala otpornost na boginje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a local infection induced in humans by inoculation with the virus causing cowpox in order to confer resistance to smallpox [vaccina, vaccinia, variola vaccina, variola vaccinia]</p><p><b>lokalna infekcija izazvana kod ljudi cijepljenjem virusa koji uzrokuje boginje krava kako bi se osigurala otpornost na boginje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a local infection induced in humans by inoculation with the virus causing cowpox in order to confer resistance to smallpox [vaccina, vaccinia, variola vaccina, variola vaccine]</p><p><b>virus koji uzrokuje boginje kod ljudi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the virus that causes smallpox in humans [smallpox virus]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na boginje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to small pox [variolic, variolous]</p><p><b>Stariji postupak cijepljenja osjetljive osobe materijalom preuzetim iz mjehurice osobe koja ima boginje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the obsolete process of inoculating a susceptible person with material taken from a vesicle of a person who has smallpox [variolization]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na boginje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to small pox [variolar, variolous]</p><p><b>Stariji postupak cijepljenja osjetljive osobe materijalom preuzetim iz mjehurice osobe koja ima boginje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the obsolete process of inoculating a susceptible person with material taken from a vesicle of a person who has smallpox [variolation]</p><p><b>koji se odnose na boginje (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to small pox [variolar, variolic]</p><p><b>variometar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a measuring instrument for measuring variations in a magnetic field</p><p><b>izdanje koje sadrži različite verzije teksta ili bilješke različitih znanstvenika ili urednika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edition containing various versions of a text or notes by various scholars or editors [variorum edition]</p><p><b>izdanje koje sadrži različite verzije teksta ili bilješke različitih znanstvenika ili urednika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an edition containing various versions of a text or notes by various scholars or editors [variorum]</p><p><b>mnogostran, različit, različiti, razni, razno, raznoliki, raznovrstan, šarolik, različite, različitih, različitim, raznih, raznim, raznovrsne, raznovrsnih</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of many different kinds purposefully arranged but lacking any uniformity [assorted]</p><p><i>adj.</i> cons