lt]</p><p><i>n.</i> a strongroom or compartment (often made of steel) for safekeeping of valuables [bank vault]</p><p><i>n.</i> an arched brick or stone ceiling or roof</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of jumping over an obstacle [hurdle]</p><p><i>v.</i> jump across or leap over (an obstacle) [overleap]</p><p><i>v.</i> bound vigorously</p><p><b>nebeski svod, nebo</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the apparent surface of the imaginary sphere on which celestial bodies appear to be projected [celestial sphere, empyrean, firmament, heavens, sphere, welkin]</p><p><b>zasvođen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having a hemispherical vault or dome [domed]</p><p><b>luk, podrum, sef, strop, svod, trezor (od &quot;vault&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an athlete who jumps over a high crossbar with the aid of a long pole [pole jumper, pole vaulter]</p><p><b>svod, svodovi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (architecture) a vaulted structure</p><p><i>n.</i> a light leap by a horse in which both hind legs leave the ground before the forelegs come down [curvet]</p><p><i>adj.</i> revealing excessive self-confidence [overreaching]</p><p><b>gimnastički konj bez pommelsa i s jednim krajem izduženim (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gymnastic horse without pommels and with one end elongated [buck, long horse]</p><p><b>hvalisanje, hvalisati se, hvastati se, producirati se, razmetati se, šepiriti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extravagant self-praise</p><p><i>v.</i> show off [blow, bluster, boast, brag, gas, gasconade, shoot a line, swash, tout]</p><p><b>hvalisanje, hvalisati se (od &quot;vaunt&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a very boastful and talkative person [blowhard, boaster, braggart, bragger, line-shooter]</p><p><b>Na hvalisan način. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a boastful manner [big, boastfully, large]</p><p><b>Američki pejzažni arhitekta (rođen u Engleskoj) koji je dizajnirao Central Park (1824-1895) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States landscape architect (born in England) who designed Central Park (1824-1895) [Calvert Vaux]</p><p><b>Hinduistički 