tory]</p><p><i>adj.</i> providing justification [justificative, justificatory]</p><p><b>osvetoljubiv</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed to seek revenge or intended for revenge [revengeful, vengeful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> showing malicious ill will and a desire to hurt [despiteful, spiteful]</p><p><b>osvetoljubiv (od &quot;vindictive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a vindictive, revengeful manner [revengefully, vengefully]</p><p><b>osvetoljubiv (od &quot;vindictive&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a malevolent desire for revenge [vengefulness]</p><p><b>čokot, loza, trs, vinova loza, povijuša, puzavica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a plant with a weak stem that derives support from climbing, twining, or creeping along a surface</p><p><b>pustinjski grm jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika koji ima tanke gole trnjeve grane koje nakon kišne sezone izlaze listovima i grmovima crvenih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> desert shrub of southwestern United States and Mexico having slender naked spiny branches that after the rainy season put forth foliage and clusters of red flowers [Fouquieria splendens, Jacob's staff, coachwhip, ocotillo]</p><p><b>mala klovna s sjeverozapadne Sjeverne Amerike koja ima prostirane stabljike koje slobodno korene i formiraju gusto grmlje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small maple of northwestern North America having prostrate stems that root freely and form dense thickets [Acer circinatum]</p><p><b>tanka drvena zmija koja se nalazi od južne Arizone do Bolivije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slender arboreal snake found from southern Arizona to Bolivia</p><p><b>kvasina, ocat, vinski ocat, zakiseliti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sour-tasting liquid produced usually by oxidation of the alcohol in wine or cider and used as a condiment or food preservative [acetum]</p><p><i>n.</i> dilute acetic acid</p><p><b>U ovom članku se navode primjerice: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> minute eelworm that feeds on organisms that cause fermentation in e.g. vinegar [Anguillula aceti, Turbatrix aceti, vinegar worm]</p><p><b>muhe čije se ličinke hrane krastavcima i nesavršeno zapečaćenim konzervama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flies whose larvae feed on pickles and imperfectly sealed preserves</p><p><b>General Sjedinjenih Država koji je zapovijedao savezničkim snagama u Kini, Burmi i Indiji tijekom Drugog svjetskog rata (1883-1946) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States general who commanded the Allied forces in China and Burma and India during World War II (1883-1946) [Joseph Warren Stilwell, Stilwell, Uncle Joe]</p><p><b>listovice ili istočna Sjeverna Amerika sa složenim lišćama koje postaju sjajno crvene na jesen i gusto panike zelenkasto žute cvijeće s crvenkastim kiselnim bojama, Česta neotrovna grmlja istočne Sjeverne Amerike s voskovitim složenim listovima i zelenim paniculate cvijeće slijede crvene bobice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous shrubby tree or eastern North America with compound leaves that turn brilliant red in fall and dense panicles of greenish yellow flowers followed by crimson acidic berries [Rhus typhina, Virginian sumac, staghorn sumac, velvet sumac]</p><p><i>n.</i> common nonpoisonous shrub of eastern North America with waxy compound leaves and green paniculate flowers followed by red berries [Rhus glabra, scarlet sumac, smooth sumac]</p><p><b>U ovom članku se navode primjerice: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> minute eelworm that feeds on organisms that cause fermentation in e.g. vinegar [Anguillula aceti, Turbatrix aceti, vinegar eel]</p><p><b>Kurva kao kisel ocat. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sourness resembling that of vinegar [vinegarishness]</p><p><b>ukus ili miris octa, koji je mrzovoljan. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> tasting or smelling like vinegar [acetose, acetous, vinegary]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having a sour disposition [vinegary]</p><p><b>Kurva kao kisel ocat. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sourness resembling that of vinegar [vinegariness]</p><p><b>veliki bič-škorpija iz Meksika i južnih Sjedinjenih Država koji emitira miris sirćeta kada se uznemiri (MT)