porodica lozica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of vines belonging to order Rhamnales [Vitidaceae, family Vitaceae, grapevine family]</p><p><b>bitan, egzistencijalnog, ključan, neophodan, suštinski, vitalan, vitalno, životni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> urgently needed [critical]</p><p><i>adj.</i> performing an essential function in the living body [life-sustaining]</p><p><i>adj.</i> full of spirit [lively]</p><p><i>adj.</i> manifesting or characteristic of life</p><p><b>vitalni kapacitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the maximum amount of air that can be exhaled after a maximum inhalation (usually tested with a spirometer)</p><p><b>(biologija) hipotetička sila (ne fizička ili kemijska) za koju je Henri Bergson jednom mislio da uzrokuje evoluciju i razvoj organizama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) a hypothetical force (not physical or chemical) once thought by Henri Bergson to cause the evolution and development of organisms [elan vital, life force, vitality]</p><p><b>vitalni organ, vitalni organi</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bodily organ that is essential for life [vitals]</p><p><b>vis vitalis, životna energija, životna sila</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a hypothetical force to which the functions and qualities peculiar to living things are sometimes ascribed [life principle]</p><p><b>znak života (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> sign of life</p><p><b>podaci o rođenju i smrti te zdravlju i bolestima i brakovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> data relating to births and deaths and health and diseases and marriages</p><p><b>stanje biti vitaliziran i ispunjen životom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being vitalized and filled with life [vitalization]</p><p><b>Dajem život..., učiniti življi ili energičniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give life to [vitalize]</p><p><i>v.</i> make more lively or vigorous [vitalize]</p><p><b>netko tko daje energiju i vitalnost i duh drugim ljudima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who imparts energy and vitality and spirit to other people [animator, energiser, energizer, vitalizer]</p><p><b>(filozofija) doktrina da je život vitalni princip koji se razlikuje od fizike i kemije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (philosophy) a doctrine that life is a vital principle distinct from physics and chemistry</p><p><b>Onaj koji vjeruje u vitalizam. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who believes in vitalism</p><p><b>vitalnost, životna snaga, životne snage, životnost, vitalitet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an energetic style [verve]</p><p><i>n.</i> a healthy capacity for vigorous activity [energy, vim]</p><p><i>n.</i> (biology) a hypothetical force (not physical or chemical) once thought by Henri Bergson to cause the evolution and development of organisms [elan vital, life force, vital force]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being able to survive and grow [animation]</p><p><b>stanje biti vitaliziran i ispunjen životom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being vitalized and filled with life [vitalisation]</p><p><b>Dajem život..., učiniti življi ili energičniji (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> give life to [vitalise]</p><p><i>v.</i> make more lively or vigorous [vitalise]</p><p><b>netko tko daje energiju i vitalnost i duh drugim ljudima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who imparts energy and vitality and spirit to other people [animator, energiser, energizer, vitaliser]</p><p><b>davanje ili imati moć davanja života i duha (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> giving or having the power to give life and spirit [life-giving]</p><p><b>bitan, egzistencijalnog, ključan, neophodan, suštinski, vitalan, vitalno, životni (od &quot;vital&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to a vital degree</p><p><b>bitan, egzistencijalnog, ključan, neophodan, suštinski, vitalan, vitalno, životni (od &quot;vital&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality possessed by something that you cannot possibly do without [indispensability, indispensableness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of being essential to maintain life</p><p><b>suština, vitalni organi, vitalni organ</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bodily organ that is essential for life [vital organ]</p><p><b>vitamin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a group of organic substances essential in small quantities to normal metabolism</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko rastopnih vitamina bitnih za normalno vidovanje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several fat-soluble vitamins essential for normal vision [A, antiophthalmic factor, axerophthol]</p><p><b>retinol, vitamin A1</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an unsaturated alcohol that occurs in marine fish-liver oils and is synthesized biologically from carotene [retinol]</p><p><b>viskozni alkohol koji je manje aktivan kod sisavaca od vitamina A1 (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a viscous alcohol that is less active in mammals than is vitamin A1 [dehydroretinol]</p><p><b>B-kompleks</b></p><p><i>n.</i> originally thought to be a single vitamin but now separated into several B vitamins [B, B-complex vitamin, B complex, B vitamin, vitamin B complex]</p><p><b>B-kompleks</b></p><p><i>n.</i> originally thought to be a single vitamin but now separated into several B vitamins [B, B-complex vitamin, B complex, B vitamin, vitamin B]</p><p><b>vitamin B koji sprečava beriberi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that prevents beriberi [aneurin, antiberiberi factor, thiamin, thiamine]</p><p><b>vitaminB12</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is used to treat pernicious anemia [antipernicious anemia factor, cobalamin, cyanocobalamin]</p><p><b>vitamin b2</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that prevents skin lesions and weight loss [hepatoflavin, lactoflavin, ovoflavin, riboflavin, vitamin G]</p><p><b>vitamin B koji je bitan za metabolizam aminokiselina i skroba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is essential for metabolism of amino acids and starch [adermin, pyridoxal, pyridoxamine, pyridoxine]</p><p><b>vitamin B koji je bitan za rast i reprodukciju stanica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is essential for cell growth and reproduction [folacin, folate, folic acid, pteroylglutamic acid, pteroylmonoglutamic acid, vitamin M]</p><p><b>C vitamin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vitamin found in fresh fruits (especially citrus fruits) and vegetables [C, ascorbic acid]</p><p><b>kalciferol, kolekalciferol, vitamin D</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fat-soluble vitamin that prevents rickets [D, calciferol, cholecalciferol, ergocalciferol, viosterol]</p><p><b>vitamin e</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fat-soluble vitamin that is essential for normal reproduction [E, tocopherol]</p><p><b>vitamin b2</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that prevents skin lesions and weight loss [hepatoflavin, lactoflavin, ovoflavin, riboflavin, vitamin B2]</p><p><b>biotin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that aids in body growth [biotin]</p><p><b>vitamin rastvorljiv u mastima koji pomaže u zgrušavanju krvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fat-soluble vitamin that helps in the clotting of blood [antihemorrhagic factor, naphthoquinone]</p><p><b>oblik vitamina K. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of vitamin K [phylloquinone, phytonadione]</p><p><b>oblik vitamina K. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a form of vitamin K [menadione]</p><p><b>vitamin B koji je bitan za rast i reprodukciju stanica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a B vitamin that is essential for cell growth and reproduction [folacin, folate, folic acid, pteroylglutamic acid, pteroylmonoglutamic acid, vitamin Bc]</p><p><b>vitamin koji održava otpornost staničnih i kapilarnih zidova na prodiranje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vitamin that maintains the resistance of cell and capillary walls to permeation [bioflavinoid, citrin]</p><p><b>Tablete koje sadrže jedan ili više vitamina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a pill containing one or more vitamins</p><p><b>Dijeta namijenjena pacijentima s nedostatkom vitamina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a diet designed to patients with vitamin deficiencies [high-vitamin diet]</p><p><b>dodati vitamine kao dodatak (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> add vitamins as a supplement [vitaminize]</p><p><b>dodati vitamine kao dodatak (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> add vitamins as a supplement [vitaminise]</p><p><b>cirkulacija krvi između embriona i žumančevo