ity, voraciousness]</p><p><b>kovitlac, vihor, vir, vrtlog</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the shape of something rotating rapidly [convolution, swirl, whirl]</p><p><i>n.</i> a powerful circular current of water (usually the result of conflicting tides) [maelstrom, whirlpool]</p><p><b>vena koju čine grane s stražnje površine oka i cilijarijskog tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vein formed by branches from the back surface of the eye and the ciliary body [vena vorticosum, vorticose vein]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta protozoa s prozirnim kožnim tijelom s povlačivom stabljkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various protozoa having a transparent goblet-shaped body with a retractile stalk</p><p><b>vena koju čine grane s stražnje površine oka i cilijarijskog tijela (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vein formed by branches from the back surface of the eye and the ciliary body [vena vorticosum, vortex vein]</p><p><b>poklonik, redovnik, sljedbenik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one bound by vows to a religion or life of worship or service</p><p><i>n.</i> a priest or priestess (or consecrated worshipper) in a non-Christian religion or cult</p><p><i>n.</i> a devoted (almost religiously so) adherent of a cause or person or activity</p><p><b>glas, glasanje, glasati, glasovanje, glasovanjem, glasovati, izbor, izglasati, odobriti, glasači, birati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a choice that is made by counting the number of people in favor of each alternative [ballot, balloting, voting]</p><p><i>n.</i> the opinion of a group as determined by voting</p><p><i>n.</i> a legal right guaranteed by the 15th amendment to the US Constitution [right to vote, suffrage]</p><p><i>n.</i> a body of voters who have the same interests</p><p><i>n.</i> the total number of voters who participated [voter turnout]</p><p><i>v.</i> express one's preference for a candidate or for a measure or resolution</p><p><i>v.</i> express one's choice or preference by vote</p><p><i>v.</i> express a choice or opinion</p><p><i>v.</i> be guided by in voting</p><p><i>v