aitress in a restaurant [waitress]</p><p><b>dvoriti, služiti, asistirati, poslužiti, posluživati, raditi</b></p><p><i>v.</i> work for or be a servant to [assist, attend, attend to, serve]</p><p><b>Američki pravnik koji je 1874. godine imenovan glavnim sudijom Vrhovnog suda Sjedinjenih Država od strane predsjednika Granta (1816-1888) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States jurist who was appointed chief justice of the United States Supreme Court in 1874 by President Grant (1816-1888) [Morrison R. Waite, Morrison Remick Waite, Morrison Waite]</p><p><b>kelner, konobar, konobarica, sluga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person whose occupation is to serve at table (as in a restaurant) [server]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who waits or awaits</p><p><b>Redatelj restorana koji postavlja stolove i pomaže konobarima i briše prljavo posuđe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a restaurant attendant who sets tables and assists waiters and clears away dirty dishes [busboy]</p><p><b>čekajući, čekanje, iščekivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of waiting (remaining inactive in one place while expecting something) [wait]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being and remaining ready and available for use [ready and waiting]</p><p><b>čekaonica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a room (as in a hotel or airport) with seating where people can wait [lounge, waiting room]</p><p><b>strategija kašnjenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strategy of delay</p><p><b>red</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a line of people or vehicles waiting for something [queue]</p><p><b>Popis onih koji čekaju da dobiju nešto. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a roster of those waiting to obtain something</p><p><b>čekaonica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a room (as in a hotel or airport) with seating where people can wait [lounge, waiting area]</p><p><b>kelnerica, konobarica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman waiter</p><p><i>v.</i> serve as a waiter or waitress in a restaurant [wait]</p><p><b>odreći, odreći se, gubiti, izgubiti, odricati se, uskratiti si, uskraćivati si</b></p><p><i>v.</i> do without or cease to hold 