ouse, awaken, rouse, wake up, waken]</p><p><b>ploveća daska (slična deski za surfovanje) koja se koristi za vožnju preko vode dok se vuče iza motornog čamca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a buoyant board (resembling a surfboard) that is used to ride over water while being pulled behind a motorboat [wakeboard]</p><p><b>Otok Wake</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an island in the western Pacific between Guam and Hawaii [Wake]</p><p><b>buditi, probuditi, probuditi se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become awake or conscious [arouse, awaken, rouse, wake, waken]</p><p><i>v.</i> stop sleeping [arouse, awake, awaken, come alive, wake, waken]</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka lilijastica iz roda Trillium koja ima vrh od tri lista na vrhu stabla s jednim cvetom s tri latica, obična američka biljka s proljetnim cvjetovima koja ima listove za pokrivanje i uspravnu štapovsku spadix s sveobuhvatnim zelenim i ljubičastim spatheom koji proizvodi crvene bobice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any liliaceous plant of the genus Trillium having a whorl of three leaves at the top of the stem with a single three-petaled flower [trillium, wood lily]</p><p><i>n.</i> common American spring-flowering woodland herb having sheathing leaves and an upright club-shaped spadix with overarching green and purple spathe producing scarlet berries [Arisaema atrorubens, Arisaema triphyllum, Indian turnip, jack-in-the-pulpit]</p><p><b>buđenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a warning to take action concerning something that was overlooked or neglected</p><p><i>n.</i> a telephone call that you request be made a specific time in order to wake you up at that time (especially in hotels)</p><p><b>(vojni) signal za buđenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (military) signal to wake up [reveille]</p><p><b>ploveća daska (slična deski za surfovanje) koja se koristi za vožnju preko vode dok se vuče iza motornog čamca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a buoyant board (resembling a surfboard) that is used to ride over water while being pulled behind a motorboat [wake board]</p><p><b>besan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> carefully observant or attentive [argus-eyed, open-eyed, vigilant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of sleep) easily disturbed [light]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by full consciousness or alertness [waking]</p><p><b>budnost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a periodic state during which you are conscious and aware of the world</p><p><i>n.</i> a temporary state in which you are unable (or unwilling) to sleep [sleeplessness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the process of paying close and continuous attention [alertness, vigilance, watchfulness]</p><p><b>Dubok, pun. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of sleep) deep and complete [heavy, profound, sound]</p><p><b>bdjeti, probuditi, probuditi se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> cause to become awake or conscious [arouse, awaken, rouse, wake, wake up]</p><p><i>v.</i> stop sleeping [arouse, awake, awaken, come alive, wake, wake up]</p><p><b>bdjeti, probuditi, probuditi se (od &quot;waken&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of waking [awakening, waking up]</p><p><b>bdijenje, bdjenje, bdjeti, biti budan, brazda za brodom, buditi, buđenje, čuvati, java, nespavanje, pobuditi, potaknuti, probuditi, probuditi se, razbudjeti se, stražarenje, sustrujanje, trag, vodena brazda (od &quot;wake&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who rouses others from sleep [arouser, rouser]</p><p><i>n.</i> a person who awakes</p><p><b>bdijenje, bdjenje, bdjeti, biti budan, brazda za brodom, buditi, buđenje, čuvati, java, nespavanje, pobuditi, potaknuti, probuditi, probuditi se, razbudjeti se, stražarenje, sustrujanje, trag, vodena brazda (od &quot;wake&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the state of remaining awake</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by full consciousness or alertness [wakeful]</p><p><b>Čin buđenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of waking [awakening, wakening]</p><p><b>član severnamjerskog naroda koji je nekada živio u dolini rijeke Colorado u Arizoni, Yuman jezik kojim govore Walapai (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of a North American people formerly living in the Colorado river valley i