ni brod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government ship that is available for waging war [combat ship, warship]</p><p><b>vrisak namijenjen okupljanju grupe vojnika u borbi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a yell intended to rally a group of soldiers in battle [battle cry, rallying cry, war cry]</p><p><b>Žena čiji je muž poginuo u ratu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a woman whose husband has died in war</p><p><b>borbena zona u kojoj se koordiniraju vojne operacije (posebno određeno područje u međunarodnim vodama gdje države u ratu ne poštuju prava neutralnih država) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a combat zone where military operations are coordinated (especially a designated area in international waters where the rights of neutrals are not respected by nations at war)</p><p><b>U ratu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> engaged in war [belligerent, militant, warring]</p><p><b>koji je oštećen u ratu</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> laid waste by war [war-worn]</p><p><b>razorena ratom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> laid waste by war [war-torn]</p><p><b>Škrgajući grm sa uskim lišćama i vidljivim crvenim cvijećima u gustim kuglatim rascima, visoki grm istočne Australije koji ima oblanceolate do obovate lišće i crvene cvijeće u kompaktnim rascemama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> straggling shrub with narrow leaves and conspicuous red flowers in dense globular racemes [Telopea speciosissima]</p><p><i>n.</i> tall shrub of eastern Australia having oblanceolate to obovate leaves and red flowers in compact racemes [Telopea Oreades]</p><p><b>cvrkutanje, cvrkutati, ćurlikati, drhtati tonom, treperenje, treperiti, treperiti glas, triler, tremolirati, trilirati, vibrirati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a lumpy abscess under the hide of domestic mammals caused by larvae of a botfly or warble fly</p><p><i>v.</i> sing or play with trills, alternating with the half note above or below [quaver, trill]</p><p><i>v.</i> sing by changing register [descant, yodel]</p><p><b>muha poput pčele čije ličinke proizvode grudične apscese (grupacije) ispod kože goveda (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> hairy bee-like fly whose larvae produce lumpy abscesses (warbles) under the skin of cattle</p><p><b>modul s frekvencijom c</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a singer</p><p><i>n.</i> a small active songbird</p><p><b>Njemački biohemičar koji je bio pionir u korištenju kemijskih tehnika u biološkim istraživanjima, Njemački povjesničar umjetnosti (1866-1929) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German biochemist who pioneered the use of chemical techniques in biological investigations [Otto Heinrich Warburg]</p><p><i>n.</i> German art historian (1866-1929) [Aby Moritz Warburg, Aby Warburg]</p><p><b>bolnička soba, odbiti, starateljstvo, suzbiti, štićenik, štititi, tutorstvo, zaštita, zatvorska ćelija, dvorištem, štićenica, gradska izborna jedinica, bolnički odjel, blok, odjel, zatvorski blok, zatvorski odjel</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is under the protection or in the custody of another</p><p><i>n.</i> a district into which a city or town is divided for the purpose of administration and elections</p><p><i>n.</i> block forming a division of a hospital (or a suite of rooms) shared by patients who need a similar kind of care [hospital ward]</p><p><i>n.</i> English economist and conservationist (1914-1981) [Barbara Ward, Baroness Jackson of Lodsworth]</p><p><i>n.</i> English writer of novels who was an active opponent of the women's suffrage movement (1851-1920) [Mary Augusta Arnold Ward, Mrs. Humphrey Ward]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States businessman who in 1872 established a successful mail-order business (1843-1913) [Aaron Montgomery Ward, Montgomery Ward]</p><p><i>n.</i> a division of a prison (usually consisting of several cells) [cellblock]</p><p><i>v.</i> watch over or shield from danger or harm [guard]</p><p><b>obraniti se</b></p><p><i>v.</i> prevent the occurrence of [avert, avoid, debar, deflect, fend off, forefend, forfend, head off, obviate, stave off]</p><p><i>v.</i> avert, turn away, or repel</p><p><b>političar koji pripada malom kliku koja kontrolira poli