vanje robe dok se ne plate sve naknade za skladištenje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> right of a warehouseman to retain goods until all storage charges have been paid</p><p><b>magazin, skladišta, skladište, skladištenje, spremište, staviti u maga, stovarište, uskladištiti (od &quot;warehouse&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a workman who manages or works in a warehouse [warehouseman]</p><p><b>skladišno poslovanje, skladištenje, stavljati u magazin, uskladištenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> depositing in a warehouse [repositing, reposition, storage]</p><p><b>rat, ratovanje, boj, vojna</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the waging of armed conflict against an enemy [war]</p><p><i>n.</i> an active struggle between competing entities [war]</p><p><b>antikoagulansa (trgovinski naziv Coumadin) koji se koristi za sprečavanje i liječenje tromba ili embola (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an anticoagulant (trade name Coumadin) use to prevent and treat a thrombus or embolus [Coumadin]</p><p><b>bojeva glava, eksplozivno punjenje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the front part of a guided missile or rocket or torpedo that carries the nuclear or explosive charge or the chemical or biological agents [load, payload]</p><p><b>Američki umjetnik koji je bio vođa pokreta Pop Art (1930-1987) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States artist who was a leader of the Pop Art movement (1930-1987) [Andy Warhol]</p><p><b>umjetničko djelo (kompozicija ili drama) koje je dio standardnog repertoara, ali je postalo razmazano zbog velikog ponavljanja, Iskusan čovjek koji je prošao kroz mnoge bitke., Konj koji se koristi u ratu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a work of art (composition or drama) that is part of the standard repertory but has become hackneyed from much repetition</p><p><i>n.</i> an experienced person who has been through many battles [old-timer, old hand, old stager, oldtimer, stager, veteran]</p><p><i>n.</i> horse used in war</p><p><b>oprezno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a wary manner</p><p><b>osobina da bude oprezan i budan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being cautious and watchful [chariness]</p><p><b>jezikom Čad koji se govori u sjevernoj Nigeriji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Chadic language spoken in northern Nigeria</p><p><b>borben, ratnički, ratoboran, vojni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> disposed to warfare or hard-line policies [hawkish, militant]</p><p><i>adj.</i> suggesting war or military life [martial]</p><p><b>vještac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a male witch or demon</p><p><b>gospodar rata, ratni vođa, vođa, vojskovođa</b></p><p><i>n.</i> supreme military leader exercising civil power in a region especially one accountable to nobody when the central government is weak</p><p><b>jezik australijskih Aboridžina (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a language of Australian aborigines [Walbiri]</p><p><b>grijati, topao, ugrijati, usrdan, zagrijati, zagrijati se, topla, tople, toplim, toplo, toplom, grijati se, ugrijati se, ugrijavati se, zagrijavati se, zgrijati se, zgrijavati se, ugrijavati, zagrijavati, zgrijati, zgrijavati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> get warm or warmer [warm up]</p><p><i>v.</i> make warm or warmer</p><p><i>adj.</i> having or producing a comfortable and agreeable degree of heat or imparting or maintaining heat</p><p><i>adj.</i> psychologically warm</p><p><i>adj.</i> inducing the impression of warmth</p><p><i>adj.</i> freshly made or left [strong]</p><p><i>adj.</i> easily aroused or excited [quick]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by strong enthusiasm [ardent]</p><p><i>adj.</i> characterized by liveliness or excitement or disagreement</p><p><i>adj.</i> uncomfortable because of possible danger or trouble</p><p><i>adj.</i> of a seeker</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a warm manner [warmly]</p><p><b>topla fronta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the front of an advancing mass of warmer air</p><p><b>biti van igre (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> be out of the game [ride the bench]</p><p><b>biti uzbuđen o (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> become excited about</p><p><b>podgrijati, zagrijavanje, zagrijavati, grijati se, ugrijati se, ugrijavati se, zagrijati se, zagrijavati se, zgrijati se, zgrijavati se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> performing mild exercises to prepare for some more strenuous activity</p><p><i>v.</i> run until the normal working temperature is reached</p><p><i>v.</i> become more friendly or open</p><p><i>v.</i> get warm or warmer [warm]</p><p><i>v.</i> cause to do preliminary exercises so as to stretch the muscles</p><p><i>v.</i> make one's body limber or suppler by stretching, as if to prepare for strenuous physical activity [limber up, loosen up]</p><p><b>(u životinja čija je tjelesna temperatura unutarnje regulisana) (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having warm blood (in animals whose body temperature is internally regulated)</p><p><b>korištenje glazbe (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> used of music</p><p><b>podgrijati, zagrijavanje, zagrijavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> exercising in preparation for strenuous activity [prolusion, tune-up]</p><p><b>grijati, topao, ugrijati, usrdan, zagrijati, zagrijati se, topla, tople, toplim, toplo, toplom (od &quot;warm&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having been warmed up</p><p><b>grijalica, grijač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> device that heats water or supplies warmth to a room [heater]</p><p><b>Označen toplinom osjećaja kao što su dobrota i suosjećanje i velikodušnost. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by warmth of feeling like kindness and sympathy and generosity</p><p><b>toplina, blagost, dragost, naklonost, nježnost, privrženost, sklonost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a warmhearted feeling [warmth]</p><p><i>n.</i> a positive feeling of liking [affection, affectionateness, fondness, heart, philia, tenderness, warmness]</p><p><b>grijanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the process of becoming warmer [heating]</p><p><i>n.</i> warm weather following a freeze [thaw, thawing]</p><p><i>adj.</i> imparting heat</p><p><i>adj.</i> producing the sensation of heat when applied to the body [calefacient]</p><p><b>tanjir s dugim rukom koji drži ugljen kako bi se zagrijao krevet (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a long-handled covered pan holding live coals to warm a bed</p><p><b>srdačno, toplo</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a hearty manner [cordially, heartily]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a warm manner [warm]</p><p><b>blagost, dragost, naklonost, nježnost, privrženost, sklonost, toplina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a positive feeling of liking [affection, affectionateness, fondness, heart, philia, tenderness, warmheartedness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of having a moderate degree of heat [warmth]</p><p><b>ratni huškač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who advocates war or warlike policies [militarist]</p><p><b>huškanje na rat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a policy of advocating war [war advocacy]</p><p><b>srdačnost, toplina, topline, toplinu, toplota, strastvenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sensation caused by heat energy [heat]</p><p><i>n.</i> a warmhearted feeling [warmheartedness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the quality of having a moderate degree of heat [warmness]</p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being intensely emotional [heat, passion]</p><p><i>n.</i> a quality proceeding from feelings of affection or love [affectionateness, fondness, lovingness]</p><p><b>nagovijestiti, obavijestiti, opomenuti, skrenuti pažnju, upozorenje, upozorite, upozoriti, opominjati, upozoravati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> notify of danger, potential harm, or risk</p><p><i>v.</i> advise or counsel in terms of someone's behavior [admonish, discourage, monish]</p><p><i>v.</i> ask to go away</p><p><i>v.</i> notify, usually in advance</p><p><b>indikator metana</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States filmmaker who with his brothers founded the movie studio that produced the first talking picture (1881-1958) [Charles Dudley Warner]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who gives a warning to others</p><p><b>detekcija, opomena, otkrivanje, prethodnih naznaka, upozorenje, znak opasnosti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a message informing of danger</p><p><i>n.</i> cautionary advice about something imminent (especially imminent danger or other unpleasantness) [admonition, monition, word of advice]</p><p><i>n.</i> notification of something,