.</i> something forming a web (as between the toes of birds)</p><p><i>n.</i> a narrow closely woven tape</p><p><i>n.</i> a strong fabric woven in strips</p><p><b>molj koji stvara mrežu u kojoj živi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> moth that forms a web in which it lives [Tineola bisselliella, webbing moth]</p><p><b>molj koji stvara mrežu u kojoj živi. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> moth that forms a web in which it lives [Tineola bisselliella, webbing clothes moth]</p><p><b>s otvorenim rastopanjima ili sličnim mrežama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having open interstices or resembling a web [lacy, netlike, netted, webbed, weblike]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom materijala od 0,01 mm ili više, ali ne više od 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a digital camera designed to take digital photographs and transmit them over the internet</p><p><b>veber</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of magnetic flux equal to 100,000,000 maxwells [Wb]</p><p><i>n.</i> German physicist and brother of E. H. Weber [Wilhelm Eduard Weber]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States abstract painter (born in Russia) (1881-1961) [Max Weber]</p><p><i>n.</i> German sociologist and pioneer of the analytic method in sociology (1864-1920) [Max Weber]</p><p><i>n.</i> German conductor and composer of romantic operas (1786-1826) [Baron Karl Maria Friedrich Ernst von Weber, Carl Maria von Weber]</p><p><i>n.</i> German physiologist who studied sensory responses to stimuli and is considered the father of psychophysics (1795-1878) [E. H. Weber, Ernst Heinrich Weber]</p><p><b>(psihofizici) koncept da je samo-značajna razlika u podražaju proporcionalna veličini prvobitnog podražaja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychophysics) the concept that a just-noticeable difference in a stimulus is proportional to the magnitude of the original stimulus</p><p><b>(psihofizički) koncept da se veličina subjektivne senzacije povećava proporcionalno logaritmu intenziteta podražaja. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (psychophysics) the concept that the magnitude of a subjective sensation increases proportional to the logarithm of the stimulus intensity [Fechner's law]</p><p><b>stopala s prstima spojenim sa prepukotinama kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a foot having the toes connected by folds of skin</p><p><b>s otvorenim rastopanjima ili sličnim mrežama (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having open interstices or resembling a web [lacy, netlike, netted, webbed, webby]</p><p><b>webmaster</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a technician who designs or maintains a website</p><p><b>dokument povezan s World Wide Webom i koji može pogledati svatko s internetom koji ima web preglednik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a document connected to the World Wide Web and viewable by anyone connected to the internet who has a web browser [web page]</p><p><b>internetska stranica, web stranici, stranica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a computer connected to the internet that maintains a series of web pages on the World Wide Web [internet site, site, web site]</p><p><b>Engleski dramaturg (1580-1625), Američki političar i govornik (1782-1817), Američki leksikograf (1758-1843) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English playwright (1580-1625) [John Webster]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States politician and orator (1782-1817) [Daniel Webster]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States lexicographer (1758-1843) [Noah Webster]</p><p><b>nekoliko larvi skupnih molova koje se previjaju preko lišća na kojem se hrane (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> several gregarious moth larvae that spin webs over foliage on which they feed</p><p><b>raznolikost molja koji pređe mrežu u kojoj živi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of moth that spins a web in which it lives</p><p><b>oplesti, oženiti se, sjediniti, udati se, vjenčati se, udavati se, vjenčavati se, ženiti, ženiti se, oženiti, vjenčati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fourth day of the week [Midweek, Wednesday]</p><p><i>v.</i> take in marriage [conjoin, espouse, get hitched with, get married, hook up with, marry]</p><p><i>v.</i> perform a marriage ceremony [marry, splice, tie]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having been taken