ed as a source of yellow dye [Reseda luteola, dyer's mignonette, dyer's rocket]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States abolitionist (1803-1895) [Theodore Dwight Weld]</p><p><i>n.</i> a metal joint formed by softening with heat and fusing or hammering together</p><p><i>v.</i> join together by heating</p><p><i>v.</i> unite closely or intimately</p><p><b>zavarivač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> joins pieces of metal by welding them together</p><p><b>masku koju nosite za zaštitu prilikom varenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mask that you wear for protection when doing welding</p><p><b>varenje, zavarivanja, zavarivanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fastening two pieces of metal together by softening with heat and applying pressure</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 10 kg ili više, ali ne više od 10 kg (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an assembly of parts welded together</p><p><b>blagostanje, dobro, dobrobit, napredak, skrb, skrbi, socijalna skrb, socijalna pomoć, korist, boljitak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> governmental provision of economic assistance to persons in need [public assistance, social welfare]</p><p><i>n.</i> something that aids or promotes well-being [benefit]</p><p><i>n.</i> a contented state of being happy and healthy and prosperous [eudaemonia, eudaimonia, upbeat, well-being, wellbeing]</p><p><b>Slučaj za socijalnog radnika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a case for a welfare worker [charity case]</p><p><b>socijalna država</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a government that undertakes responsibility for the welfare of its citizens through programs in public health and public housing and pensions and unemployment compensation etc.</p><p><b>organizacija za poboljšanje stanja siromašnih u društvu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an organized activity to improve the condition of disadvantaged people in society [social service]</p><p><b>osoba koja je zaposlena za pružanje socijalnih usluga (posebno za ugrožene osobe) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone employed to provide social services (especially to the disadvantaged) [caseworker, social w