n in Germany where he designed a missile used against England) [Braun, Wernher Magnus Maximilian von Braun, von Braun]</p><p><b>Njemački neurolog poznat po studijama afazije (1848-1905) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German neurologist best known for his studies of aphasia (1848-1905) [Karl Wernicke]</p><p><b>Afazija karakterizirana tečnim, ali beznačajnim govorom i ozbiljnim oštećenjem sposobnosti razumijevanja govorenih ili pisanih riječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aphasia characterized by fluent but meaningless speech and severe impairment of the ability understand spoken or written words [fluent aphasia, impressive aphasia, receptive aphasia, sensory aphasia]</p><p><b>slušni centar riječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the auditory word center [Wernicke's center]</p><p><b>slušni centar riječi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the auditory word center [Wernicke's area]</p><p><b>upalna degenerativna bolest mozga uzrokovana nedostatkom tiamina koja je obično povezana s alkoholizmom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inflammatory degenerative disease of the brain caused by thiamine deficiency that is usually associated with alcoholism</p><p><b>Weser</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in northwestern Germany that flows northward to the North Sea near Bremerhaven [Weser River]</p><p><b>Weser</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a river in northwestern Germany that flows northward to the North Sea near Bremerhaven [Weser]</p><p><b>Engleski svećenik i brat Johna Wesleya koji je napisao mnoge himne (1707-1788), Engleski svećenik i osnivač metodizma (1703-1791) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English clergyman and brother of John Wesley who wrote many hymns (1707-1788) [Charles Wesley]</p><p><i>n.</i> English clergyman and founder of Methodism (1703-1791) [John Wesley]</p><p><b>sljedbenik Wesleyanism, od ili se odnosi na ili karakteristično za granu protestantizma koji se pridržava gledišta Wesleyja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a follower of Wesleyanism</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or pertaining to or characteristic of the branch of Protestantism