n the wind [rustle, rustling, whisper]</p><p><i>n.</i> speaking softly without vibration of the vocal cords [susurration, voicelessness, whisper]</p><p><i>adj.</i> making a low continuous indistinct sound [murmuring, susurrant]</p><p><b>viscidna biljka iz sušnih ili pustinjskih staništa jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država s višenastvenim žutim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> viscid herb of arid or desert habitats of southwestern United States having pendulous yellow flowers [California yellow bells, Emmanthe penduliflora, yellow bells]</p><p><b>organizirano širenje pogrdnih glasina namijenjenih diskreditiranju kandidata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the organized dissemination of derogatory rumors designed to discredit a candidate</p><p><b>prostor ispod kupole ili luka u kojem su zvukovi proizvedeni u određenim točkama jasno čuvljivi u određenim udaljenim točkama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a space beneath a dome or arch in which sounds produced at certain points are clearly audible at certain distant points [whispering gallery]</p><p><b>prostor ispod kupole ili luka u kojem su zvukovi proizvedeni u određenim točkama jasno čuvljivi u određenim udaljenim točkama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a space beneath a dome or arch in which sounds produced at certain points are clearly audible at certain distant points [whispering dome]</p><p><b>Kartačka igra za četiri igrača koji čine dva partnerstva. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a card game for four players who form two partnerships [long whist, short whist]</p><p><b>Progresivna whist stranka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a progressive whist party</p><p><b>fijukati, pištaljka, pištanje, pištati, zviznuti, zviždaljka, zviždanje, zviždati, zvižduk, zvuk, fićukati, fućkati, zviždukati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the sound made by something moving rapidly or by steam coming out of a small aperture [whistling]</p><p><i>n.</i> the act of signalling (e.g., summoning) by whistling or blowing a whistle [whistling]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small wind instrument that produces a whistling sound by blowing into it</p><p><i>n.</i> acoustic device that forces air or steam against an edge or into a cavity and so produces a loud shrill sound</p><p><i>n.</i> an inexpensive fipple flute [pennywhistle, tin whistle]</p><p><i>v.</i> make whistling sounds</p><p><i>v.</i> move with, or as with, a whistling sound</p><p><i>v.</i> utter or express by whistling</p><p><i>v.</i> move, send, or bring as if by whistling</p><p><i>v.</i> make a whining, ringing, or whistling sound [sing]</p><p><i>v.</i> give a signal by whistling</p><p><b>cinkaroš, onaj tko alarmira, onaj tko upozorava, zviždač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an informant who exposes wrongdoing within an organization in the hope of stopping it [whistle-blower, whistleblower]</p><p><b>Boja koja puši zvuk zvižduka. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a buoy that makes a whistling noise [whistling buoy]</p><p><b>cinkaroš, onaj tko alarmira, onaj tko upozorava, zviždač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an informant who exposes wrongdoing within an organization in the hope of stopping it [whistle blower, whistleblower]</p><p><b>obilazak kandidata u okviru političke kampanje u kojoj se posjeti niz malih gradova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tour by a candidate as part of a political campaign in which a series of small towns are visited</p><p><b>zviždač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an informant who exposes wrongdoing within an organization in the hope of stopping it [whistle-blower, whistle blower]</p><p><b>atmosferske smetnje, pištanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States painter (1834-1903) [James Abbott McNeill Whistler]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who makes a loud high sound</p><p><i>n.</i> large North American mountain marmot [Marmota caligata, hoary marmot, whistling marmot]</p><p><i>n.</i> large-headed swift-flying diving duck of Arctic regions [Bucephela clangula, goldeneye]</p><p><i>n.</i> Australian and southeastern Asian birds with a melodious whistling call [thickhead]</p><p><b>obići zemlju kako bi se prikupili glasovi za izbore. (MT)</b