ited States writer noted for his humorous essays (1899-1985) [E. B. White, Elwyn Brooks White]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States educator who in 1865 (with Ezra Cornell) founded Cornell University and served as its first president (1832-1918) [Andrew D. White, Andrew Dickson White]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tributary of the Mississippi River that flows southeastward through northern Arkansas and southern Missouri [White River]</p><p><i>n.</i> the white part of an egg [albumen, egg white, ovalbumin]</p><p><i>n.</i> (board games) the lighter pieces</p><p><i>n.</i> (usually in the plural) trousers made of flannel or gabardine or tweed or white cloth [flannel, gabardine, tweed]</p><p><i>v.</i> turn white [whiten]</p><p><i>adj.</i> being of the achromatic color of maximum lightness</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or belonging to a racial group having light skin coloration</p><p><i>adj.</i> free from moral blemish or impurity</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by the presence of snow [snowy]</p><p><i>adj.</i> restricted to whites only [lily-white]</p><p><i>adj.</i> glowing white with heat [white-hot]</p><p><i>adj.</i> benevolent</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a surface) not written or printed on [blank, clean]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of coffee) having cream or milk added</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of hair) having lost its color [whitened]</p><p><i>adj.</i> anemic looking from illness or emotion [ashen, blanched, bloodless, livid]</p><p><i>adj.</i> of summer nights in northern latitudes where the sun barely sets</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički leptir s plavo-crnim krilima koje prekriva širok bijeli pojas, Euroazijski leptir s smeđim krilima i bijelim oznakama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American butterfly with blue-black wings crossed by a broad white band [Limenitis arthemis, banded purple]</p><p><i>n.</i> Eurasian butterfly with brown wings and white markings [Limenitis camilla]</p><p><b>stablo zapadnih Sjedinjenih Država, grm istočne i južne obale Sjedinjenih Država koji ima lijepe raseme bijelih cvijeća mirisnih začina (MT)</