ama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> North American herb with white poisonous berries [Actaea alba, doll's eyes, white baneberry, white bead]</p><p><b>krvne stanice koje prožimaju i probavljaju bakterije i gljivice (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> blood cells that engulf and digest bacteria and fungi [WBC, leucocyte, leukocyte, white blood cell, white blood corpuscle, white cell]</p><p><b>-Bila je to bela govna. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a crappie that is white [Pomoxis annularis]</p><p><b>Srebro- i plavo-blueish drumfish od plitkih kalifornijskih obalnih voda, mala srebrna morska hrana riba pronađena u blizini Kalifornije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> silvery and bluish drumfish of shallow California coastal waters [Seriphus politus, queenfish]</p><p><i>n.</i> small silvery marine food fish found off California [Genyonemus lineatus, chenfish, kingfish]</p><p><b>Bjelančevine s malim bijelim bobicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> garden currant bearing small white berries [Ribes sativum]</p><p><b>usporeno rastući srednji cedar sa istočne obale Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> slow-growing medium-sized cedar of east coast of the United States [Atlantic white cedar, Chamaecyparis thyoides, coast white cedar, southern white cedar, white cedar]</p><p><b>malo stablo ili grm iz južne Australije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small tree or shrub of southern Australia [Callitris glauca, Callitris glaucophylla]</p><p><b>Visoka ljeplovita višegodišnja biljka s bijelim cvjetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall leafy-stemmed Eurasian perennial with white flowers [Chrysanthemum leucanthemum, Leucanthemum vulgare, marguerite, moon daisy, ox-eyed daisy, oxeye daisy]</p><p><b>Europska mrtva kopriva s bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European dead nettle with white flowers [Lamium album]</p><p><b>šumski planinari s sjajnim lišćama i bijelim cvjetovima u obliku lovora s žutim grlom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrubby climber having glossy leaves and white funnel-shaped flowers with yellow throats [Dip