ičar koji je surađivao s Bertrandom Russellem (1861-1947), mala bijelkasta kvrga u koži zbog začepljene lojne žlijezde (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English philosopher and mathematician who collaborated with Bertrand Russell (1861-1947) [Alfred North Whitehead]</p><p><i>n.</i> a small whitish lump in the skin due to a clogged sebaceous gland [milium]</p><p><b>Glavni grad pokrajine teritorija Yukon (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the provincial capital of the Yukon Territory</p><p><b>Odgovor bijelaca rasista protiv napredovanja crnaca u građanskim pravima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> backlash by white racists against black civil rights advances [white backlash]</p><p><b>Zajednička europska višegodišnja biljka naturalizirana širom svijeta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common European perennial naturalized worldwide [Plantago major, broad-leaved plantain, cart-track plant, common plantain, white-man's foot]</p><p><b>bijeliti, krečiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> turn white [white]</p><p><b>bijeliti, krečiti (od &quot;whiten&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of hair) having lost its color [white]</p><p><b>bijeliti, krečiti (od &quot;whiten&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an agent that makes things white or colorless [blanching agent, bleach, bleaching agent]</p><p><b>bjelina, bijela, bijela boja</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the quality or state of the achromatic color of greatest lightness (bearing the least resemblance to black) [white]</p><p><i>n.</i> the state of being unsullied by sin or moral wrong [innocence, pureness, purity, sinlessness]</p><p><i>n.</i> lightness or fairness of complexion</p><p><b>bijeliti, krečiti (od &quot;whiten&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> changing to a lighter color [lightening]</p><p><b>Arktički atmosferski uvjeti s oblacima iznad snijega stvaraju jednaku bijelu boju i teško se vide predmeti., zalijevanje tečnošću za korekciju, gubitak vidljivosti svjetlosti tijekom dana u gorućoj magli, snijegu ili kiši (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an arctic atmospheric condition with clouds over snow produce a uniform whiteness and objects are difficult to see</p><p><i>v.</i> cover up with a liquid correction fluid [white out]</p><p><i>v.</i> lose daylight visibility in heavy fog, snow, or rain [white-out]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički jelen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common North American deer [Odocoileus Virginianus, Virginia deer, white-tailed deer, white tail, whitetail deer]</p><p><b>mala vjevericka sa zapada Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small ground squirrel of western United States [Citellus leucurus, antelope chipmunk, antelope squirrel]</p><p><b>Sjevernoamerički jelen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common North American deer [Odocoileus Virginianus, Virginia deer, white-tailed deer, white tail, whitetail]</p><p><b>Najveći zec sjevernih ravnica i zapadnih planina Sjedinjenih Država (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> largest hare of northern plains and western mountains of United States [Lepus townsendi, white-tailed jackrabbit]</p><p><b>rep je bijeli vrh (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tail is white tipped [Cynomys gunnisoni]</p><p><b>trnasti evroazijski grm od malog stabla s gustim grmovima bijele do crvene boje cvijeća s duboko crvenim bojama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> thorny Eurasian shrub of small tree having dense clusters of white to scarlet flowers followed by deep red berries [Crataegus laevigata, Crataegus oxycantha, English hawthorn, may]</p><p><b>obična grmuša</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Old World warbler similar to the greater whitethroat but smaller [Sylvia curruca, lesser whitethroat]</p><p><i>n.</i> greyish-brown Old World warbler with a white throat and underparts [Sylvia communis, greater whitethroat]</p><p><i>n.</i> common North American finch with a white patch on the throat and black-and-white striped crown [Zonotrichia albicollis, white-throated sparrow]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 2. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste ribara u području Unije, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje odjeljak 1. točka (a) ovog članka, za koje se primjenjuje odjeljak 1. točka (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, za sve vrste ribara u području Unije, u skladu s člankom 2. točkom (a) ovog članka, u skladu s člankom 3. točkom (a) ovog članka,, Velika duboka morska riba s bijelim dorsnim perajem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> smooth dogfish of Pacific and Indian Oceans and Red Sea having white-tipped dorsal and caudal fins [Triaenodon obseus, reef whitetip shark]</p><p><i>n.</i> large deep-water shark with white-tipped dorsal fin [Carcharinus longimanus, oceanic whitetip shark, white-tipped shark]</p><p><b>bijeljenje, kreč, krečiti, obijeliti, okrečiti, vapnena voda, vapno, bijeliti, pobijeliti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a defeat in which the losing person or team fails to score</p><p><i>n.</i> wash consisting of lime and size in water</p><p><i>n.</i> a specious or deceptive clearing that attempts to gloss over failings and defects</p><p><i>v.</i> cover up a misdemeanor, fault, or error [gloss over, hush up, sleek over]</p><p><i>v.</i> cover with whitewash</p><p><i>v.</i> exonerate by means of a perfunctory investigation or through biased presentation of data</p><p><b>bijeljenje, kreč, krečiti, obijeliti, okrečiti, vapnena voda, vapno (od &quot;whitewash&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> coated with whitewash</p><p><b>pjenasta voda kao u brzicima ili vodopadima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> frothy water as in rapids or waterfalls [white water]</p><p><b>lakše obrađivano drvo tulipana (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> light easily worked wood of a tulip tree [true tulipwood, tulipwood, white poplar, yellow poplar]</p><p><b>(Slang) uvredljiva imena za bijelca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (slang) offensive names for a White man [honkey, honkie, honky]</p><p><b>pišmolj</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flesh of a cod-like fish of the Atlantic waters of Europe</p><p><i>n.</i> flesh of any of a number of slender food fishes especially of Atlantic coasts of North America</p><p><i>n.</i> a small fish of the genus Sillago</p><p><i>n.</i>