im cvetovima (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European teasel with white to pink flowers [Dipsacus sylvestris]</p><p><b>aromatični patuljasti grm uobičajen na obroncima i obroncima u Europi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> aromatic dwarf shrub common on banks and hillsides in Europe [Thymus serpyllum, creeping thyme]</p><p><b>Tabakovna biljka Južne Amerike i Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tobacco plant of South America and Mexico [Indian tobacco, Nicotiana rustica]</p><p><b>višegodišnja biljka iz jugoistočne Sjedinjenih Država s lišćama koje imaju miris vanilije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> perennial of southeastern United States with leaves having the fragrance of vanilla [Trilisa odoratissima]</p><p><b>tropski američki cvijet strasti s fino raskomadanim bractama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tropical American passion flower with finely dissected bracts [Passiflora foetida, love-in-a-mist, running pop]</p><p><b>Zapadni Sjedinjene Države tijekom svog graničnog razdoblja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the western United States during its frontier period</p><p><b>spektakularno prikazivanje koje je 1883. godine organizovao William F. Cody koje je uključivalo jahanje konja i strijeljenje na velikoj razini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a spectacular show organized in 1883 by William F. Cody that featured horseback riding and marksmanship on a large scale [Buffalo Bill's Wild West Show]</p><p><b>pronađen divlje u Palestini (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> found wild in Palestine [Triticum dicoccum dicoccoides, wild emmer]</p><p><b>larva saturnidnog molja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> larva of a saturniid moth [giant silkworm, silkworm]</p><p><b>Zimična jednogodišnja biljka s slabim stablom koja je izvorno iz mediteranske regije i dugo se nalazi na jugu Sjedinjenih Država. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a weak-stemmed winter annual native to Mediterranean region for long established in southern United States [Caley pea, Lathyrus hirsutus, rough pea, singletary pea]</p><p><b>s rizomom koja je prethodno sušena i koja se koristi za liječenje reuma ili bolesti jetre (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> having a rhizome formerly dried and used to treat rheumatism or liver disorders [Dioscorea paniculata]</p><p><b>obična lilija istočne Sjedinjenih Država s žutim ili crvenkastim cvjetovima s smeđim mrljama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> common lily of the eastern United States having nodding yellow or reddish flowers spotted with brown [Canada lily, Lilium canadense, meadow lily, wild meadow lily]</p><p><b>Izgledaju izuzetno uznemireni., Ne razumno u praktičnim stvarima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> appearing extremely agitated</p><p><i>adj.</i> not sensible about practical matters [quixotic, romantic]</p><p><b>beskorisno traženje nečeg nedostupnog (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the fruitless pursuit of something unattainable</p><p><b>divlja mačka, nesiguran</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an exploratory oil well drilled in land not known to be an oil field [wildcat well]</p><p><i>n.</i> a cruelly rapacious person [beast, brute, savage, wolf]</p><p><i>n.</i> any small or medium-sized cat resembling the domestic cat and living in the wild</p><p><i>adj.</i> outside the bounds of legitimate or ethical business practices</p><p><i>adj.</i> without official authorization [unauthorised, unauthorized]</p><p><i>adj.</i> (of a mine or oil well) drilled speculatively in an area not known to be productive</p><p><b>Štrajk koji su poduzeli radnici bez odobrenja službenika svog sindikata (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a strike undertaken by workers without approval from the officials of their union</p><p><b>istraživanje nafte na zemljištu za koje se ne zna da je naftno polje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an exploratory oil well drilled in land not known to be an oil field [wildcat]</p><p><b>naftar koji buši istraživačke bušotine na području za koje se ne zna da je naftno polje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an oilman who drills exploratory wells in territory not known to be an oil field</p><p><b>Irski pisac i duh (1854-1900) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Irish writer and wit (1854-1900) [Oscar Fingal O'Flahertie Wills Wilde, Oscar Wilde]</p><p><b>relativno netoksična južnoafrička biljka pušena kao duhan (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> relatively nontoxic South African herb smoked like tobacco [Cape dagga, Leonotis leonurus, dagga, red dagga]</p><p><b>gnu</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large African antelope having a head with horns like an ox and a long tufted tail [gnu]</p><p><b>divalj, divlje, divlji, divljim, divljina, mahnit, makar kako, neobuzdan, otkačen, pust, pustoš, razuzdan, razvratan, divljački (od &quot;wild&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer and dramatist (1897-1975) [Thornton Niven Wilder, Thornton Wilder]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States filmmaker (born in Austria) whose dark humor infused many of the films he made (1906-2002) [Billy Wilder, Samuel Wilder]</p><p><b>divljina, pustara, pustoš</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (politics) a state of disfavor</p><p><i>n.</i> a wooded region in northeastern Virginia near Spotsylvania where bloody but inconclusive battles were fought in the American Civil War</p><p><i>n.</i> a wild and uninhabited area left in its natural condition [wild]</p><p><i>n.</i> a bewildering profusion</p><p><b>Američki građanski rat (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> American Civil War</p><p><b>munjevito</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a raging and rapidly spreading conflagration</p><p><b>divlji cvijet</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wild or uncultivated flowering plant [wild flower]</p><p><b>meso bilo koje od nekoliko divljih divljih ptica pogodnih za hranu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> flesh of any of a number of wild game birds suitable for food</p><p><b>divlja biljka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a wild uncultivated plant (especially a wild apple or crabapple tree)</p><p><i>n.</i> an outrageous rampage usually involving sexual attacks by men on women</p><p><b>biljni i životinjski svijet, divljač, divlje životinje, divljina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> all living things (except people) that are undomesticated</p><p><b>divlje, znatno, mahnit</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> to an extreme or greatly exaggerated degree</p><p><i>adv.</i> in an uncontrolled or unrestrained manner</p><p><i>adv.</i> with violent and uncontrollable passion</p><p><b>divljaštvo, divljina, divljine</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a feeling of extreme emotional intensity [abandon]</p><p><i>n.</i> the property of being wild or turbulent [ferocity, fierceness, furiousness, fury, vehemence, violence]</p><p><i>n.</i> an unruly disposition to do as one pleases</p><p><i>n.</i> an intractably barbarous or uncultivated state of nature</p><p><b>prevariti, prijevara, smicalica, trik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the use of tricks to deceive someone (usually to extract money from them) [chicane, chicanery, guile, shenanigan, trickery]</p><p><b>Američki avijator koji je 1933. godine prvi sam letovao oko svijeta (1899-1935) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States aviator who in 1933 made the first solo flight around the world (1899-1935) [Post]</p><p><b>hotimičan, svojevoljan, uporan</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> done by design [willful]</p><p><i>adj.</i> habitually disposed to disobedience and opposition [froward, headstrong, self-willed, willful]</p><p><b>namjerno</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a willful manner [willfully]</p><p><b>hotimičan, svojevoljan, uporan (od &quot;wilful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the trait of being prone to disobedience and lack of discipline [fractiousness, unruliness, willfulness]</p><p><b>Francuski pjesnik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> French poet [Apollinaire, Guillaume Apollinaire]</p><p><b>Njemački fizičar i brat E. H. Webera (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German physicist and brother of E. H. Weber [Weber]</p><p><b>Wilhelm Grimm</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the younger of the two Grimm brothers remembered best for their fairy stories (1786-1859) [Grimm, Wilhelm Karl Grimm]</p><p><b>unuk kraljice Viktorije i njemačkog cara od 1888. do 1918. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> grandson of Queen Victoria and Kaiser of Germany from 1888 to 1918 [Kaiser Bill, Kaiser Wilhelm]</p><p><b>Wilhelm Grimm</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the younger of the two Grimm brothers remembered best for their fairy stories (1786-1859) [Grimm, Wilhelm Grimm]</p><p><b>Njemački fizičar koji je otkrio rendgenske zrake i razvio rendgenografiju (1845-1923) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German physicist who discovered x-rays and developed roentgenography (1845-1923) [Roentgen, Rontgen, Wilhelm Konrad Rontgen]</p><p><b>Njemački fizičar koji je otkrio rendgenske zrake i razvio rendgenografiju (1845-1923) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German physicist who discovered x-rays and developed roentgenography (1845-1923) [Roentgen, Rontgen, Wilhelm Konrad Roentgen]</p><p><b>Njemački kemičar (1853-1932) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German chemist (1853-1932) [Ostwald]</p><p><b>Austrijski psihoanalitičar koji je živio u Sjedinjenim Državama. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Austrian born psychoanalyst who lived in the United States [Reich]</p><p><b>Njemački kompozitor opera i izumitelj glazbene drame u kojoj se drama, spektakl i glazba spajaju (1813-1883) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German composer of operas and inventor of the musical drama in which drama and spectacle and music are fused (1813-1883) [Richard Wagner, Wagner]</p><p><b>Opel</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German industrialist who was the first in Germany to use an assembly line in manufacturing automobiles (1871-1948) [Opel]</p><p><b>lukavost, lukavstvo, prepredenost</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrewdness as demonstrated by being skilled in deception [craft, craftiness, cunning, foxiness, guile, slyness]</p><p><b>Engleski reformator koji je objavio napade na Georgea III. i podržao prava američkih kolonista (1727-1797), Američki istraživač Antarktika (1798-1877) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English reformer who published attacks on George III and supported the rights of the American colonists (1727-1797) [John Wilkes]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States explorer of Antarctica (1798-1877) [Charles Wilkes]</p><p><b>obalni region Antarktika na Indijskom oceanu južno od Australije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a coastal region of Antarctica on the Indian Ocean to the south of Australia</p><p><b>Engleski pisac poznat po ranoj detektivskoj knjizi (1824-1889) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English writer noted for early detective novels (1824-1889) [Collins, William Wilkie Collins]</p><p><b>Vođa američkih građanskih prava (1901-1981), Australac koji je prvi istražio Arktik avionom (1888-1958), Engleski biohemičar koji je pomogao u otkrivanju strukture DNK (1916-2004) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States civil rights leader (1901-1981) [Roy Wilkins]</p><p><i>n.</i> Australian who was the first to explore the Arctic by airplane (1888-1958) [George Hubert Wilkins]</p><p><i>n.</i> English biochemist who helped discover the structure of DNA (1916-2004) [Maurice Hugh Frederick Wilkins, Maurice Wilkins]</p><p><b>izmišljeni lik kojeg je stvorio Charles Dickens (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fictional character created by Charles Dickens [Micawber]</p><p><b>Engleski kemičar nagrađen za istraživanje zagađivača u izduvnim plinovima automobila (rođen 1921.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English chemist honored for his research on pollutants in car exhausts (born in 1921) [Sir Geoffrey Wilkinson]</p><p><b>će, ćemo, ćete, htijenje, htjeti, oporuka, volja, želja, hoće, hoćeš, hoću, volje, hteti, oporučiti, oporučivati, oporučno ostaviti, oporučno ostavljati, ostaviti, zavještati, zavještavati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capability of conscious choice and decision and intention [volition]</p><p><i>n.</i> a fixed and persistent intent or purpose</p><p><i>n.</i> a legal document declaring a person's wishes regarding the disposal of their property when they die [testament]</p><p><i>v.</i> decree or ordain</p><p><i>v.</i> determine by choice</p><p><i>v.</i> leave or give by will after one's death [bequeath, leave]</p><p><b>Američki povjesničar (1885-1981) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States historian (1885-1981) [Durant, William James Durant]</p><p><b>Američki odvjetnik i političar koji je formulirao proizvodni kodeks koji