ago. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Siouan-speaking people formerly living in eastern Wisconsin south of Green Bay</p><p><i>n.</i> the Siouan language spoken by the Winnebago</p><p><b>dobitnik, pobjednik</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the contestant who wins the contest [victor]</p><p><i>n.</i> a gambler who wins a bet</p><p><i>n.</i> a person with a record of successes [achiever, succeeder, success]</p><p><b>malo područje na trkalištu gdje se nagrade dodjeljuju vlasnicima dobitnika konja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a small area at a racecourse where awards are given to the owners of winning horses</p><p><b>dobitnički, pobjeda, pobjednički, pobjedonosan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> succeeding with great difficulty</p><p><i>adj.</i> having won [victorious]</p><p><i>adj.</i> very attractive [fetching, taking]</p><p><b>post na kraju trkališta. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the post at the end of a racecourse</p><p><b>niz pobjeda. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a streak of wins</p><p><b>dobitak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> something won (especially money) [profits, win]</p><p><b>Winnipeg</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the capital and largest city of Manitoba</p><p><i>n.</i> a lake in southern Canada in Manitoba [Lake Winnipeg]</p><p><b>izdvojiti, odvojiti, razbacati, rešetati, vijati, vijati (žito)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of separating grain from chaff [sifting, winnowing]</p><p><i>v.</i> separate the chaff from grain by using air currents</p><p><i>v.</i> blow on</p><p><i>v.</i> select desirable parts from a group or list [cull out]</p><p><i>v.</i> blow away or off with a current of air [fan]</p><p><b>eliminirati, isključiti, isključivati</b></p><p><i>v.</i> dismiss from consideration or a contest [eliminate, reject, rule out]</p><p><b>izdvojiti, odvojiti, razbacati, rešetati, vijati, vijati (žito) (od &quot;winnow&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of separating grain from chaff [sifting, winnow]</p><p><b>kronični pijanic. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a chronic drinker [drunk, drunkard, inebriate, rummy, sot]</p