mon sole]</p><p><i>n.</i> important American food fish in the winter [Pseudopleuronectes americanus, blackback flounder, lemon sole]</p><p><b>biljka ili stablo porijeklom iz Japana koje se uzgaja kao ukrasno bilje zbog svojih ružičastih cvjetova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> shrub or tree native to Japan cultivated as an ornamental for its rose-pink flowers [Prunus subhirtella, rosebud cherry]</p><p><b>bilo koji od nekoliko azijskih listnatog grma uzgojenih zbog svojih gnušavih žutih cvijeća koji se pojavljuju prije lišća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several Asiatic deciduous shrubs cultivated for their nodding racemes of yellow flowers that appear before the leaves [flowering hazel]</p><p><b>džinovski europski grm s vrlo rano cvjetanjem crvenih cvjetova u obliku zvona (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dwarf European shrub with very early blooming bell-shaped red flowers [Erica carnea, spring heath]</p><p><b>Europska biljka s bijelo-ružičastim cvijećima u mirisu vanilije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> European herb with vanilla-scented white-pink flowers [Petasites fragrans, sweet coltsfoot]</p><p><b>Blomovi iz stabla, u obliku stabla, u obliku žutih cvjetova. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> deciduous rambling shrub widely cultivated for its winter-blooming yellow flowers [Jasminum nudiflorum]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta vinove loze od lubenice koja ima plodove glatke bele kore i bijelo ili zelenkasto meso koje nema miris muške, plodovi zimske paljbe (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a variety of muskmelon vines having fruit with a smooth white rind and white or greenish flesh that does not have a musky smell [Cucumis melo inodorus, Persian melon, honeydew melon, winter melon vine]</p><p><i>n.</i> the fruit of the winter melon vine</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta vinove loze od lubenice koja ima plodove glatke bele kore i bijelo ili zelenkasto meso koje nema miris muške (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a variety of muskmelon vines having fruit with a smooth white rind and white or greenish flesh that does not 