</p><p><i>n.</i> common violet of the eastern United States with large pale blue or purple flowers resembling pansies [Johnny-jump-up, Viola pedata, bird's-foot violet, pansy violet]</p><p><b>čvorovi s čeljustima koji su podložni kako bi se drvo držalo bez izbočenja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a vise with jaws that are padded in order to hold lumber without denting it [shoulder vise, woodworking vise]</p><p><b>šumski zviždak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small bright-colored American songbird with a weak unmusical song [New World warbler]</p><p><i>n.</i> European woodland warbler with dull yellow plumage [Phylloscopus sibilatrix]</p><p><b>karolinka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> showy North American duck that nests in hollow trees [Aix sponsa, summer duck, wood duck]</p><p><b>Sastav koji se može spojiti s poluproizvodom bizmuta plus olovo, cink i kadmijum (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fusible alloy that is half bismuth plus lead, tin, and cadmium [Wood's metal]</p><p><b>Sastav koji se može spojiti s poluproizvodom bizmuta plus olovo, cink i kadmijum (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fusible alloy that is half bismuth plus lead, tin, and cadmium [Wood's alloy]</p><p><b>na drvetu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> fueled by wood [wood-fired]</p><p><b>bilo koja od brojnih ptica u Južnoj i Srednjoj Americi sa zakrivljenim kljunom i tvrdim repnim perjem koje se penju i hrane kao vještice. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of numerous South American and Central American birds with a curved bill and stiffened tail feathers that climb and feed like woodpeckers [tree creeper, woodcreeper, woodhewer]</p><p><b>Svaka vrsta ptica iz rodova Dryopteris (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various ferns of the genus Dryopteris [wood fern, woodfern]</p><p><b>na drvetu (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> fueled by wood [wood-burning]</p><p><b>široko rasprostranjena svjetlo smeđa žaba vlažnih šumskih područja Sjeverne Amerike, posebno smrke (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wide-ranging light-brown frog of moist North American woodlands especially spruc