je</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the remaining parts of something that has been wrecked</p><p><b>razoren, uništen</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> destroyed in an accident</p><p><b>obalni kradljivac, razbijač, šlep auto</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who demolishes or dismantles buildings as a job</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who commits sabotage or deliberately causes wrecks [diversionist, saboteur]</p><p><i>n.</i> a truck equipped to hoist and pull wrecked cars (or to remove cars from no-parking zones) [tow car, tow truck]</p><p><b>Crne ribe iz Atlantskog i Sredozemnog mora pronađene oko stijena i olupina brodova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> brown fish of the Atlantic and Mediterranean found around rocks and shipwrecks [Polyprion americanus, stone bass]</p><p><b>brodolom, olupina, pretrpjeti brodolom, propast, razbiti, razbiti brod, razoriti, slupati, udes, uništiti, upropastiti (od &quot;wreck&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the event of a structure being completely demolished and leveled [razing]</p><p><i>n.</i> destruction achieved by causing something to be wrecked or ruined [laying waste, ruin, ruination, ruining]</p><p><b>ćuskija, željezna poluga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a heavy iron lever with one end forged into a wedge [crowbar, pry, pry bar]</p><p><b>carić, strež</b></p><p><i>n.</i> English architect who designed more than fifty London churches (1632-1723) [Sir Christopher Wren]</p><p><i>n.</i> any of several small active brown birds of the northern hemisphere with short upright tails [jenny wren]</p><p><b>mala azijska i afrička ptica (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small Asiatic and African bird</p><p><b>mala smeđa ptica iz Kalifornije koja liči na vrtača (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> small brown bird of California resembling a wren [Chamaea fasciata]</p><p><b>blokirati, francuski ključ, iščašenje, iščašiti, izvijanje, jako trzanje, ključ, ključ za odvij, odvrnuti, odvrtanje, snažno povući, tuga, uganuće, uganuti, viljuškasti ključ, uvijanje, frkati</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a sharp strain on muscles or ligaments [pull, twist]</p><p><i>n.</i> a jerky pulling movement [twist]</p><p><i>n.</i> a hand tool that is used to hold or twist a nut or bolt [spanner]</p><p><i>v.</i> twist or pull violently or suddenly, especially so as to remove (something) from that to which it is attached or from where it originates [twist]</p><p><i>v.</i> make a sudden twisting motion</p><p><i>v.</i> twist and compress, as if in pain or anguish [wring]</p><p><i>v.</i> twist suddenly so as to sprain [rick, sprain, turn, twist, wrick]</p><p><b>blokirati, francuski ključ, iščašenje, iščašiti, izvijanje, jako trzanje, ključ, ključ za odvij, odvrnuti, odvrtanje, snažno povući, tuga, uganuće, uganuti, viljuškasti ključ (od &quot;wrench&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> causing great physical or mental suffering [racking]</p><p><b>istrgnuti, izopačiti</b></p><p><i>v.</i> obtain by seizing forcibly or violently, also metaphorically</p><p><b>istrgnuti, izopačiti (od &quot;wrest&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> someone who obtains something by pulling it violently with twisting movements</p><p><b>boriti se, hrvati se, rvati se, hrvanje, frkati, iskobeljati se, iskoprcati se, izmigoljiti se, izvijati se, izviti se, izvlačiti se, izvući se, kobeljati se, koprcati se, migoljiti se</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of engaging in close hand-to-hand combat [grapple, grappling, hand-to-hand struggle, wrestling]</p><p><i>v.</i> combat to overcome an opposing tendency or force</p><p><i>v.</i> engage in deep thought, consideration, or debate</p><p><i>v.</i> to move in a twisting or contorted motion, (especially when struggling) [squirm, twist, worm, wriggle, writhe]</p><p><i>v.</i> engage in a wrestling match</p><p><b>hrvač, rvač</b></p><p><i>n.</i> combatant who tries to throw opponent to the ground [grappler, matman]</p><p><b>hrvanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the act of engaging in close hand-to-hand combat [grapple, grappling, hand-to-hand struggle, wrestle]</p><p><i>n.</i> the sport of hand-to-hand struggle between unarmed contestants w