move in a twisting or contorted motion, (especially when struggling) [squirm, twist, worm, wrestle, writhe]</p><p><b>krivudati, migoljiti, probijati se, provlačiti se, vijuganje, vijugati, vrtjeti se, zaokret, zavoj (od &quot;wriggle&quot;)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one who can't stay still (especially a child) [squirmer, wiggler]</p><p><i>n.</i> larva of a mosquito [wiggler]</p><p><b>krivudati, migoljiti, probijati se, provlačiti se, vijuganje, vijugati, vrtjeti se, zaokret, zavoj (od &quot;wriggle&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> moving in a twisting or snake-like or wormlike fashion [wiggly, wriggly, writhing]</p><p><b>kretanje u okretanju ili zmijskom ili crvljićem obliku (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> moving in a twisting or snake-like or wormlike fashion [wiggly, wriggling, writhing]</p><p><b>gaditelj, graditelj, obrtnik, pisac, radnik, radnik obrtnik, tvorac</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer of detective novels (1888-1939) [S. S. Van Dine, Willard Huntington Wright]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States writer whose work is concerned with the oppression of African Americans (1908-1960) [Richard Wright]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States aviation pioneer who (with his brother Orville Wright) invented the airplane (1867-1912) [Wilbur Wright]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States aviation pioneer who (with his brother Wilbur Wright) invented the airplane (1871-1948) [Orville Wright]</p><p><i>n.</i> influential United States architect (1869-1959) [Frank Lloyd Wright]</p><p><i>n.</i> United States early feminist (born in Scotland) (1795-1852) [Fanny Wright, Frances Wright]</p><p><i>n.</i> someone who makes or repairs something (usually used in combination)</p><p><b>cijediti, cijeđenje, sažimanje, stezanje, stiskanje, zavrtanje, zavrtati, iscijediti, izvitoperiti, iznuditi, mučiti, podvaliti</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a twisting squeeze [squeeze]</p><p><i>v.</i> twist and press out of shape [contort, deform, distort]</p><p><i>v.</i> twist and compress, as if in pain or anguish [wrench]</p><p><i>v.</