an ninety [91, ninety-one]</p><p><b>biti dva više od devedeset (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being two more than ninety [92, ninety-two]</p><p><b>biti tri više od devedeset (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being three more than ninety [93, ninety-three]</p><p><b>Četiri više od devedeset. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being four more than ninety [94, ninety-four]</p><p><b>što je deset više od sto osamdeset (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being ten more than one hundred eighty [190, one hundred ninety]</p><p><b>biti pet više od devedeset (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being five more than ninety [95, ninety-five]</p><p><b>da je šest više od devedeset. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being six more than ninety [96, ninety-six]</p><p><b>biti sedam više od devedeset (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being seven more than ninety [97, ninety-seven]</p><p><b>biti osam više od devedeset (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being eight more than ninety [98, ninety-eight]</p><p><b>Xe, atomski broj 54, ksenon</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless odorless inert gaseous element occurring in the earth's atmosphere in trace amounts [atomic number 54, xenon]</p><p><b>pasanci, porodica Dasypodidae, porodica pasanaca</b></p><p><i>n.</i> armadillos [suborder Xenarthra]</p><p><b>Alternativna imena za obitelj koja obuhvaća novozelandske vrene (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> alternative names for the family comprising the New Zealand wrens [Acanthisittidae, family Acanthisittidae, family Xenicidae]</p><p><b>tip rod za Xenicidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type genus for the Xenicidae [genus Xenicus]</p><p><b>ptica s kratkim repom koja liči na ptičju ptičicu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> short-tailed bird resembling a wren [rock wren]</p><p><b>koji označavaju ili se odnose na stanice ili tkiva pojedinaca različitih vrsta (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> denoting or relating to cells or tissues from individuals belonging to different species</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 3. stavkom 1. točkom (a) ovog članka, "sastavljanje" znači: (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the alternation of two or more different forms in the life cycle of a plant or animal [alternation of generations, heterogenesis]</p><p><b>Tkivo iz životinje jedne vrste koje se koristi kao privremeni presadak (kao u slučajevima teških opekotina) na pojedinca druge vrste (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tissue from an animal of one species used as a temporary graft (as in cases of severe burns) on an individual of another species [heterograft]</p><p><b>(geologija) komad stijene različitog podrijetla od magmatske stijene u kojoj je ugrađen (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (geology) a piece of rock of different origin from the igneous rock in which it is embedded</p><p><b>ksenon, Xe, atomski broj 54</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a colorless odorless inert gaseous element occurring in the earth's atmosphere in trace amounts [Xe, atomic number 54]</p><p><b>Ksenofan</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek philosopher (560-478 BC)</p><p><b>ksenofobija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a fear of foreigners or strangers</p><p><b>koji pate od ksenofobije (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suffering from xenophobia</p><p><b>Grčki general i povjesničar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Greek general and historian</p><p><b>u nekim klasifikacijama obitelj roda Xenopus koji je inače uključen u obitelj Pipidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> in some classifications the family of the genus Xenopus which is otherwise included in the family Pipidae [family Xenopodidae]</p><p><b>afrička žaba sa kandžama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an African clawed frog [genus Xenopus]</p><p><b>Žaba bez jezika porijeklom iz Afrike. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a tongueless frog native to Africa [African clawed frog]</p><p><b>Istočnoindijski i australijski bobići (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> East Indian and Australian storks [genus Xenorhyncus]</p><p><b>veliki uglavnom bijeli australijski čvor (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> large mostly white Australian stork [black-necked stork, jabiru, policeman bird]</p><p><b>monotipno obitelji meksičkih gušteraca (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> monotypic family of Mexican lizards [family Xenosauridae]</p><p><b>vrsta i jedini rod Xenosauridae: meksički gušteri vitkog tijela čija je gornja površina prekrivena sitnim granulima i gomoljicama (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> type and sole genus of Xenosauridae: slender-bodied Mexican lizards having the upper surface covered with tiny granules and tubercles [genus Xenosaurus]</p><p><b>mineral od smeđe do žute boje koji je fosfat itrija u kristalnom obliku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a brown-to-yellow mineral that is a phosphate of yttrium in crystalline form</p><p><b>operacija kojom se tkivo ili cijeli organ prenose s jedne vrste na drugu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a surgical procedure in which tissue or whole organs are transfered from one species to another species [xenotransplantation]</p><p><b>operacija kojom se tkivo ili cijeli organ prenose s jedne vrste na drugu. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a surgical procedure in which tissue or whole organs are transfered from one species to another species [xenotransplant]</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka rod Xeranthemum porijeklom iz južne Europe s plamenastom ili srebrnom cvjetnom glavom s ljubičastim cijevičnim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any plant of the genus Xeranthemum native to southern Europe having chaffy or silvery flower heads with purplish tubular flowers</p><p><b>uglavnom široko uzgajane vrste vječnih cvijeća s obično ljubičastim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mostly widely cultivated species of everlasting flowers having usually purple flowers [immortelle]</p><p><b>nedostatak vlage (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> being deficient in moisture</p><p><b>Mogući novi rod za pustinjske i teksaške kornjače na temelju nedavnih istraživanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> possible new genus for desert and Texas tortoises based on recent research [genus Xerobates]</p><p><b>lak oblik ihtioze karakteriziran abnormalnom suhošću i grubošću kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mild form of ichthyosis characterized by abnormal dryness and roughness of the skin [xerodermia]</p><p><b>rijetko genetsko stanje koje se karakterizira izbijanjem izloženog kože u djetinjstvu i fotosenzitivnošću s teškim opekotinama od sunca. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rare genetic condition characterized by an eruption of exposed skin occurring in childhood and photosensitivity with severe sunburn</p><p><b>lak oblik ihtioze karakteriziran abnormalnom suhošću i grubošću kože (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a mild form of ichthyosis characterized by abnormal dryness and roughness of the skin [xeroderma]</p><p><b>kserografski</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to xerography</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom materijala od 85% ili više, ali ne više od 85%, (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a duplicator (trade mark Xerox) that copies graphic matter by the action of light on an electrically charged photoconductive insulating surface in which the latent image is developed with a resinous powder [Xerox, Xerox machine]</p><p><b>štampač stranica koji koristi xerografski proces (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a page printer that uses the xerographic process</p><p><b>kserografija</b></p><p><i>n.</i> forming an image by the action of light on a specially coated charged plate</p><p><b>neuobičajeno suvoća konjunktiva i rožnice očiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal dryness of the conjunctiva and cornea of the eyes [conjunctivitis arida, xerophthalmia, xerophthalmus]</p><p><b>biljka prilagođena životu s ograničenim zalihom vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant adapted for life with a limited supply of water [desert plant, xerophilous plant, xerophyte, xerophytic plant]</p><p><b>biljka prilagođena životu s ograničenim zalihom vode (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant adapted for life with a limited supply of water [desert plant, xerophile, xerophyte, xerophytic plant]</p><p><b>neuobičajeno suvoća konjunktiva i rožnice očiju (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> abnormal dryness of the conjunctiva and cornea of the eyes [conjunctivitis arida, xeroma, xerophthalmus]</p><p><b>neuobičajeno suvoća konjunktiva i rožnice očiju (MT)<