lni momak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cruel and brutal fellow [bully, hooligan, roughneck, rowdy, ruffian, tough, yobbo, yobo]</p><p><b>okrutni i brutalni momak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cruel and brutal fellow [bully, hooligan, roughneck, rowdy, ruffian, tough, yob, yobo]</p><p><b>jedinica informacija jednaka 1024 zebibita ili 2^80 bita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of information equal to 1024 zebibits or 2^80 bits [Yibit]</p><p><b>Jedinica informacija jednaka 1024 zebibajta ili 2^80 bajta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of information equal to 1024 zebibytes or 2^80 bytes [YB, YiB, yottabyte]</p><p><b>okrutni i brutalni momak. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a cruel and brutal fellow [bully, hooligan, roughneck, rowdy, ruffian, tough, yob, yobbo]</p><p><b>Pjesniški krik u kojem glas brzo varira između normalnog glasa i falseta., Pjevaj mijenjanjem registra. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a songlike cry in which the voice fluctuates rapidly between the normal voice and falsetto</p><p><i>v.</i> sing by changing register [descant, warble]</p><p><b>jodlanje</b></p><p><i>n.</i> singing by changing back and forth between the chest voice and a falsetto</p><p><b>pjevač koji brzo mijenja register (popularna su švicarska narodna pjesma) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a singer who changes register rapidly (popular is Swiss folk songs)</p><p><b>jod</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the 10th letter of the Hebrew alphabet</p><p><b>joga</b></p><p><i>n.</i> discipline aimed at training the consciousness for a state of perfect spiritual insight and tranquility that is achieved through the three paths of actions and knowledge and devotion</p><p><i>n.</i> a system of physical, breathing and meditation exercises practiced to promote control of the body and mind</p><p><b>jedna od glavnih tradicija budizma Mahayana. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of the main traditions of Mahayana Buddhism</p><p><b>jogurt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a custard-like food made from curdled milk [yoghurt, yogurt]</p><p><b>jogurt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a custard-like food made from curdled milk [yoghourt, yogurt]</p><p><b>Američki bejzbolista (rođen 1925), Onaj koji prakticira jogu i postigao je visoki nivo duhovnog uvida. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States baseball player (born 1925) [Berra, Lawrence Peter Berra, Yogi Berra]</p><p><i>n.</i> one who practices yoga and has achieved a high level of spiritual insight</p><p><b>Američki bejzbolista (rođen 1925) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States baseball player (born 1925) [Berra, Lawrence Peter Berra, Yogi]</p><p><b>o ili u vezi s jogom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to yoga [yogistic]</p><p><b>o ili u vezi s jogom (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to yoga [yogic]</p><p><b>jogurt</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a custard-like food made from curdled milk [yoghourt, yoghurt]</p><p><b>armatura magneta, dvokraka poluga, jaram, obruč, otklonski sustav, otklonski svitak, podjarmiti, škopac, par, jaremica, obremica</b></p><p><i>n.</i> fabric comprising a fitted part at the top of a garment</p><p><i>n.</i> an oppressive power</p><p><i>n.</i> two items of the same kind [brace, couple, couplet, distich, duad, duet, duo, dyad, pair, span, twain, twosome]</p><p><i>n.</i> a pair of draft animals joined by a yoke</p><p><i>n.</i> support consisting of a wooden frame across the shoulders that enables a person to carry buckets hanging from each end</p><p><i>n.</i> a connection (like a clamp or vise) between two things so they move together [coupling]</p><p><i>n.</i> stable gear that joins two draft animals at the neck so they can work together as a team</p><p><i>v.</i> become joined or linked together</p><p><i>v.</i> link with or as with a yoke [link]</p><p><i>v.</i> put a yoke on or join with a yoke</p><p><b>prostak, seljačina</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a person who is not very intelligent or interested in culture [bumpkin, chawbacon, hayseed, hick, rube, yahoo]</p><p><b>Glupi i neobrazljivi kao ruralni stanovnici. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> stupid and ignorant like proverbial rural inhabitants</p><p><b>koji nisu ni čvrsti ni ugledni, (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> (of persons) lacking in refinement or grace [bounderish, ill-bred, lowbred, rude, underbred]</p><p><b>Američki glazbenik (rođen u Japanu) koji se oženio Johnom Lennonom i surađivao s njim na snimcima (rođen 1933) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States musician (born in Japan) who married John Lennon and collaborated with him on recordings (born in 1933) [Ono]</p><p><b>Yokohama</b></p><p><i>n.</i> port city on southeastern Honshu in central Japan</p><p><b>Penutski jezik koji govore Yokuti u dolini San Joaquin, član sjevernoameričkog indijanskog naroda doline San Joaquin (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Penutian language spoken by the Yokuts in the San Joaquin Valley [Mariposan]</p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the North American Indian people of the San Joaquin Valley</p><p><b>žumance, žumanjak, vitellus</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the yellow spherical part of an egg that is surrounded by the albumen [egg yolk]</p><p><i>n.</i> nutritive material of an ovum stored for the nutrition of an embryo (especially the yellow mass of a bird or reptile egg) [vitellus]</p><p><b>membranska struktura koja funkcioniše kao cirkulacijski sustav u embrionima sisavaca dok srce ne postane funkcionalno, membranska struktura koja okružuje žumance kod ptica, gmizavaca, marsipa i nekih riba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> membranous structure that functions as the circulatory system in mammalian embryos until the heart becomes functional [umbilical vesicle, vesicula umbilicus, vitelline sac]</p><p><i>n.</i> membranous structure enclosing the yolk of eggs in birds, reptiles, marsupials, and some fishes</p><p><b>(Judaizam) svečan i veliki dan posta na židovskom kalendaru (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Judaism) a solemn and major fast day on the Jewish calendar [Day of Atonement]</p><p><b>Egipat i Sirija napali su Izrael u listopadu 1973. (na Jom Kipur) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Egypt and Syria attacked Israel in October 1973 (on Yom Kippur) [Arab-Israeli War]</p><p><b>onaj, tamo, tamošnji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> distant but within sight (`yon' is dialectal) [yonder]</p><p><i>adv.</i> at or in an indicated (usually distant) place (`yon' is archaic and dialectal) [yonder]</p><p><b>onamo, tamo, tamošnji</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> distant but within sight (`yon' is dialectal) [yon]</p><p><i>adv.</i> at or in an indicated (usually distant) place (`yon' is archaic and dialectal) [yon]</p><p><b>stara vremena</b></p><p><i>n.</i> time long past</p><p><b>engleska kraljevska kuća (odjel Plantagenetove linije) koja je vladala od 1461. do 1485. godine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the English royal house (a branch of the Plantagenet line) that reigned from 1461 to 1485 [House of York]</p><p><b>Nekadašnji veliki grofovija u sjevernoj Engleskoj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a former large county in northern England</p><p><b>Visoka europska višegodišnja trava s baršunastom stabljkom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall European perennial grass having a velvety stem [Holcus lanatus, velvet grass]</p><p><b>lagano pufno kruh napravljeno od pufne mase i tradicionalno pečeno u lonacu s pečenom govedinom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> light puffy bread made of a puff batter and traditionally baked in the pan with roast beef</p><p><b>vrlo mala rasa s dugim sjajnim plavom plavušasta i smeđom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> very small breed having a long glossy coat of bluish-grey and tan</p><p><b>povijesno selo u jugoistočnoj Virginiji sjeverno od Newport Neusa, 1781. Britanci pod Cornwallisom predaju se nakon tri tjedna opsade američkih i francuskih trupa. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a historic village in southeastern Virginia to the north of Newport News</p><p><i>n.</i> in 1781 the British under Cornwallis surrendered after a siege of three weeks by American and French troops [siege of Yorktown]</p><p><b>pripadnik zapadnoafričkog naroda koji živi uglavnom u jugozapadnoj Nigeriji., Kwa jezik koji govore Jorube u jugozapadnoj Nigeriji (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.