>n.</i> early maturity</p><p><i>n.</i> an early period of development [early days]</p><p><i>n.</i> the freshness and vitality characteristic of a young person [juvenility, youthfulness]</p><p><b>politički ili vjerski ili društveni reformski pokret ili agitacija koji se uglavnom sastoji od mladih (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> political or religious or social reform movement or agitation consisting chiefly of young people [youth movement]</p><p><b>Mladi odrasli (generacijska jedinica) smatraju se kulturnom klasom ili subkulturom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> young adults (a generational unit) considered as a cultural class or subculture</p><p><b>bandi čiji su članovi tinejdžeri. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a gang whose members are teenagers</p><p><b>prenoćište za mladež, hostel, pansion, prenoćište</b></p><p><i>n.</i> inexpensive supervised lodging (especially for youths on bicycling trips) [hostel, student lodging]</p><p><b>pokret mladeži</b></p><p><i>n.</i> political or religious or social reform movement or agitation consisting chiefly of young people [youth crusade]</p><p><b>Mladička kultura manjine čija je posebnost u velikoj mjeri ovisila o društvenoj klasi i etničkom porijeklu njenih članova (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a minority youth culture whose distinctiveness depended largely on the social class and ethnic background of its members</p><p><b>Vježnija višegodišnja biljka s cvjetovima u uspravnim stabljikama i mladim biljkama koje se razvijaju na spoju listne listine i listnog stuba (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vigorous perennial herb with flowers in erect racemes and having young plants develop at the junction of a leaf blade and the leafstalk [Tolmiea menziesii, pickaback plant, piggyback plant]</p><p><b>mlad, mladenački, mladićki, mladolik, mlađahan, snažan, svjež</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> suggestive of youth [vernal, young]</p><p><b>mlad, mladenački, mladićki, mladolik, mlađahan, snažan, svjež (od &quot;youthful&quot;)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> in a youthful manner</p><p><b>mlad, m