n the Bay of Campeche and the Caribbean Sea [Yucatan Peninsula]</p><p><b>Yucatán</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a peninsula in Central America extending into the Gulf of Mexico between the Bay of Campeche and the Caribbean Sea [Yucatan]</p><p><b>pripadnik naroda Maja na poluotoku Jukatanu u Meksiku., jezik Maja kojim govore Yukateci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Mayan people of the Yucatan peninsula in Mexico [Yucateco]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Mayan language spoken by the Yucatec [Yucateco]</p><p><b>pripadnik naroda Maja na poluotoku Jukatanu u Meksiku., jezik Maja kojim govore Yukateci (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a member of the Mayan people of the Yucatan peninsula in Mexico [Yucatec]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Mayan language spoken by the Yucatec [Yucatec]</p><p><b>juka</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of several evergreen plants of the genus Yucca having usually tall stout stems and a terminal cluster of white flowers</p><p><b>tvrda juka s kratkim deblom (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a stiff yucca with a short trunk [Spanish bayonet]</p><p><b>visoka juka iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i Meksika s drvenastom stabljikom i čvrstima šiljatim lištima nalik maču i velikim gromom bijelih cvijeća (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> tall yucca of the southwestern United States and Mexico having a woody stem and stiff swordlike pointed leaves and a large cluster of white flowers [Spanish bayonet]</p><p><b>veliki granatasti drveni yucca sa jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država koji ima kratke lišće i zelenilave bijele cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large branched arborescent yucca of southwestern United States having short leaves and clustered greenish white flowers [Joshua tree]</p><p><b>drvena juka iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država i sjevernog Meksika s lišćama u obliku mača i bijelim cvijećem (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> arborescent yucca of southwestern United States and northern Mexico with sword-shaped leaves and white flowers [Spanish dagger]</p><p><b>visoka drvena juka iz jugozapadnih Sjedinjenih Država (MT)