]</p><p><b>z</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the 26th letter of the Roman alphabet [Z, ezed, izzard, z, zed]</p><p><b>Holandski fizičar nagrađen za istraživanje utjecaja magnetizma na zračenje koje je pokazalo da se svjetlost zrači kretanjem naelektrisanih čestica u atomu (1865-1943) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> Dutch physicist honored for his research on the influence of magnetism on radiation which showed that light is radiated by the motion of charged particles in an atom (1865-1943) [Pieter Zeeman]</p><p><b>obitelj riba u redu Zeomorphi (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a family of fish in the order Zeomorphi [family Zeidae]</p><p><b>duh vremena. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the spirit of the time</p><p><b>Američki lingvista (rođen u Ukrajini) koji je razvio matematičku lingvistiku i tumačio govor i pisanje u društvenom kontekstu (1909-1992) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States linguist (born in Ukraine) who developed mathematical linguistics and interpreted speech and writing in a social context (1909-1992) [Harris, Zellig Sabbatai Harris]</p><p><b>Američki lingvista (rođen u Ukrajini) koji je razvio matematičku lingvistiku i tumačio govor i pisanje u društvenom kontekstu (1909-1992) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States linguist (born in Ukraine) who developed mathematical linguistics and interpreted speech and writing in a social context (1909-1992) [Harris, Zellig Harris]</p><p><b>škola Mahayana budizma tvrdeći da prosvjetljenje može doći kroz meditaciju i intuiciju umjesto vjere, Budistička doktrina da se prosvjetljenje može postići kroz direktno intuitivno uvid., Naziv ulice za lisergnu kiselinu dietilamid (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> school of Mahayana Buddhism asserting that enlightenment can come through meditation and intuition rather than faith [Zen Buddhism]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Buddhist doctrine that enlightenment can be attained through direct intuitive insight [Zen Buddhism]</p><p><i>n.</i> street name for lysergic acid diethylamide [Elvis, Lucy in the sky with diamonds, acid, back breaker, battery-acid, dose, dot, loony toons, pane, superman, window pane]</p><p><b>škola Mahayana budizma tvrdeći da prosvjetljenje može doći kroz meditaciju i intuiciju umjesto vjere, Budistička doktrina da se prosvjetljenje može postići kroz direktno intuitivno uvid. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> school of Mahayana Buddhism asserting that enlightenment can come through meditation and intuition rather than faith [Zen]</p><p><i>n.</i> a Buddhist doctrine that enlightenment can be attained through direct intuitive insight [Zen]</p><p><b>pristalica doktrina zen budizma. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an adherent of the doctrines of Zen Buddhism</p><p><b>žalosne golubove (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> mourning doves [genus Zenaidura]</p><p><b>Divlja golubica iz Sjedinjenih Država koja ima tužan poziv. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> wild dove of the United States having a mournful call [mourning dove]</p><p><b>drevni iranski jezik (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ancient Iranian language [Avestan]</p><p><b>Avesta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a collection of Zoroastrian texts gathered during the 4th or 6th centuries [Avesta]</p><p><b>najviša točka, vrhunac, zenit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the point above the observer that is directly opposite the nadir on the imaginary sphere against which celestial bodies appear to be projected</p><p><b>zenitni</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> relating to or located at or near the zenith</p><p><b>Stari grčki filozof koji je formulisao paradokse koji su branili vjerovanje da su kretanje i promjena iluzije (oko 495-430 p.n.e.), Stari grčki filozof koji je osnovao stoičku školu (oko 335-263 pr. n. e.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ancient Greek philosopher who formulated paradoxes that defended the belief that motion and change are illusory (circa 495-430 BC) [Zeno of Elea]</p><p><i>n.</i> ancient Greek philosopher who founded the Stoic school (circa 335-263 BC) [Zeno of Citium]</p><p><b>Stari grčki filozof koji je osnovao stoičku školu (oko 335-263 pr. n. e.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ancient Greek philosopher who founded the Stoic school (circa 335-263 BC) [Zeno]</p><p><b>Stari grčki filozof koji je formulisao paradokse koji su branili vjerovanje da su kretanje i promjena iluzije (oko 495-430 p.n.e.) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> ancient Greek philosopher who formulated paradoxes that defended the belief that motion and change are illusory (circa 495-430 BC) [Zeno]</p><p><b>zeoliti, zeolitski tuf</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of a family of glassy minerals analogous to feldspar containing hydrated aluminum silicates of calcium or sodium or potassium</p><p><b>dorije (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> dories [order Zeomorphi]</p><p><b>veliki sendvič od duge krastavke podijeljene dužinom i ispunjene mesom i sirom (i rajčica i luk i salata i začini) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a large sandwich made of a long crusty roll split lengthwise and filled with meats and cheese (and tomato and onion and lettuce and condiments) [Cuban sandwich, Italian sandwich, bomber, grinder, hero, hero sandwich, hoagie, hoagy, poor boy, sub, submarine, submarine sandwich, torpedo, wedge]</p><p><b>hebrejski mali prorok iz kasnog 7. stoljeća prije Krista., Stari zavjet knjiga koja govori proročanstva Zefanije koja se uglavnom odnose na približavanje Božje presude na grešnike Judeje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a Hebrew minor prophet of the late 7th century BC [Sophonias]</p><p><i>n.</i> an Old Testament book telling the prophecies of Zephaniah which are concerned mainly with the approaching judgment by God upon the sinners of Judah [Book of Zephaniah, Sophonias]</p><p><b>lahor, povjetarac, tanka majica, zapadni vjetar, zefir</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a slight wind (usually refreshing) [air, breeze, gentle wind]</p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the Greek god of the west wind</p><p><b>cepelin</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German inventor who designed and built the first rigid motorized dirigible (1838-1917) [Count Ferdinand von Zeppelin]</p><p><i>n.</i> a large rigid dirigible designed to carry passengers or bombs [Graf Zeppelin]</p><p><b>Američki komičar (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> United States comedian [Herbert Marx, Marx]</p><p><b>ništica, nula, nulta informacija, nulta točka, nulte, nulti, nultog, postaviti na nulu, postaviti na 0, figa, friška figa, ništa, pišljivi bob, šipak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a quantity of no importance [aught, cipher, cypher, goose egg, nada, naught, nil, nix, nothing, null, zilch, zip, zippo]</p><p><i>n.</i> a mathematical element that when added to another number yields the same number [0, cipher, cypher, nought]</p><p><i>n.</i> the point on a scale from which positive or negative numerical quantities can be measured [zero point]</p><p><i>n.</i> the sight setting that will cause a projectile to hit the center of the target with no wind blowing</p><p><i>v.</i> adjust (an instrument or device) to zero value</p><p><i>v.</i> adjust (as by firing under test conditions) the zero of (a gun) [zero in]</p><p><i>adj.</i> indicating the absence of any or all units under consideration [0]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having no measurable or otherwise determinable value</p><p><i>adj.</i> indicating an initial point or origin</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to the null set (a set with no members)</p><p><b>obveznica bez kupona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bond that is issued at a deep discount from its value at maturity and pays no interest during the life of the bond [zero-coupon bond]</p><p><b>vrijednosni papir koji ne plaća kamate, već se umjesto toga prodaje s velikim popustom od njegove nominalne vrijednosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a security that makes no interest payments but instead is sold at a deep discount from its face value [zero-coupon security]</p><p><b>U skladu s člankom 21. stavkom 1. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the time set for the start of an action or operation</p><p><b>direktno na točku ili metu, posebno pomoću automatskog navigacijskog uređaja, (kao što je pucanje u uvjetima ispitivanja) prilagoditi nuli (puška) (MT)</b></p><p><i>v.</i> direct onto a point or target, especially by automatic navigational aids [home in, range in]</p><p><i>v.</i> adjust (as by firing under test conditions) the zero of (a gun) [zero]</p><p><b>točka na skali iz koje se mogu mjeriti pozitivne ili negativne numeričke veličine (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the point on a scale from which positive or negative numerical quantities can be measured [zero]</p><p><b>ekstremna netolerancija antisocijalnog ponašanja (obično bezkompromisnom primjenom zakona) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> extreme intolerance of antisocial behavior (usually by an uncompromising application of the law)</p><p><b>obveznica bez kupona</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a bond that is issued at a deep discount from its value at maturity and pays no interest during the life of the bond [zero coupon bond]</p><p><b>vrijednosni papir koji ne plaća kamate, već se umjesto toga prodaje s velikim popustom od njegove nominalne vrijednosti (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a security that makes no interest payments but instead is sold at a deep discount from its face value [zero coupon security]</p><p><b>igra u kojoj je ukupni iznos svih dobitaka i gubitaka nula. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a game in which the total of all the gains and losses is zero</p><p><b>bilo koja politika koja ne dopušta iznimku (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any policy that allows no exception</p><p><b>Prije nego što je čak i prvi (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> preceding even the first</p><p><b>Zakona da ako su dva tijela u toplotnoj ravnoteži s trećim tijelom onda su prva dva tijela u toplotnoj ravnoteži jedni s drugima. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the law that if two bodies are in thermal equilibrium with a third body then the first two bodies are in thermal equilibrium with each other</p><p><b>oduševljenje, oštrina, polet, privlačnost, uživanje, začin, začiniti, zamah, žar</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vigorous and enthusiastic enjoyment [gusto, relish, zestfulness]</p><p><i>n.</i> a tart spicy quality [nip, piquance, piquancy, piquantness, tang, tanginess]</p><p><i>v.</i> add herbs or spices to [spice, spice up]</p><p><b>Oznaka živopisnog uživanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by spirited enjoyment [barmy, yeasty, zesty]</p><p><b>s žutom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with zest [zestily]</p><p><b>snažno i uzbuđeno uživanje. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> vigorous and enthusiastic enjoyment [gusto, relish, zest]</p><p><b>s žutom. (MT)</b></p><p><i>adv.</i> with zest [zestfully]</p><p><b>lizinopril</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an ACE inhibiting drug (trade names Prinival or Zestril) administered as an antihypertensive and after heart attacks [Prinival, lisinopril]</p><p><b>s ugodno oštrim okusom, Oznaka živopisnog uživanja (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having an agreeably pungent taste [piquant, savory, savoury]</p><p><i>adj.</i> marked by spirited enjoyment [barmy, yeasty, zestful]</p><p><b>zeta</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the 6th letter of the Greek alphabet</p><p><b>Arhipelag od oko 100 otoka u Sjevernom Atlantiku uz sjevernu obalu Škotske. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an archipelago of about 100 islands in the North Atlantic off the north coast of Scotland [Shetland, Shetland Islands]</p><p><b>Jedinica informacija jednaka 1000 eksabita ili 10^21 bita (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of information equal to 1000 exabits or 10^21 bits [Zb, Zbit]</p><p><b>Jedinica informacija jednaka 1000 eksabajta ili 10^21 bajta, jedinica informacija jednaka 1024 eksbibajta ili 2 ^ 70 bajta (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of information equal to 1000 exabytes or 10^21 bytes [ZB]</p><p><i>n.</i> a unit of information equal to 1024 exbibytes or 2^70 bytes [ZB, ZiB, zebibyte]</p><p><b>Upotreba glagola s dva ili više komplementa, igrajući se na polizemskom obliku glagola, za humoristički učinak (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> use of a verb with two or more complements, playing on the verb's polysemy, for humorous effect</p><p><b>(grčka mitologija) vrhovni bog drevne grčke mitologije, vrsta rod porodice Zeidae (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> (Greek mythology) the supreme god of ancient Greek mythology</p