r noted for a series of extravagant revues known as the Ziegfeld Follies (1869-1932) [Flo Ziegfeld, Florenz Ziegfeld]</p><p><b>seriju ekstravagantnih revija koje je producirao Flo Ziegfeld. (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a series of extravagant revues produced by Flo Ziegfeld</p><p><b>Njemački kemičar nagrađen za istraživanje polimera (1898-1973) (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> German chemist honored for his research on polymers (1898-1973) [Karl Waldemar Ziegler]</p><p><b>s masenim udjelom od 0,01 do 0,01 mm (MT)</b></p><p><i>adj.</i> having short sharp turns or angles [zigzag]</p><p><b>bilo koja biljka iz roda Zigadenus s glaukznim listovima i krajnjim rascima uglavnom bijeli cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> any of various plants of the genus Zigadenus having glaucous leaves and terminal racemes of mostly white flowers [death camas]</p><p><b>rod uglavnom sjevernoameričkih otrovnih biljaka (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> genus of mostly North American poisonous plants [genus Zigadenus]</p><p><b>biljka iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike koja ima lišće poput trave i zelenkasto-bijele cvijeće (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant of western North America having grasslike leaves and greenish-white flowers [alkali grass]</p><p><b>biljka iz istočne i središnje Sjeverne Amerike s kremastima bijelim cvijećima obojenim u smeđe ili ljubičaste boje (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant of eastern and central North America having creamy white flowers tinged with brown or purple [white camas]</p><p><b>Obična višegodišnja smrtna kamna (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a common perennial death camas [poison camas]</p><p><b>biljka iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike do Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant of western North America to Mexico [Zigadenus venenosus gramineus, grassy death camas]</p><p><b>biljka iz zapadne Sjeverne Amerike do Meksika (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> plant of western North America to Mexico [Zigadenus venenosus, grassy death camas]</p><p><b>zigurat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rectangular tiered temple or terraced mound erected by the ancient Assyrians and Babylonians [zikkurat, zikurat]</p><p><b>cik cak, cikcak, krivudati, vijugav, zavojit</b></p><p><i>n.</i> an angular shape characterized by sharp turns in alternating directions [zag, zig]</p><p><i>v.</i> travel along a zigzag path [crank]</p><p><i>adj.</i> having short sharp turns or angles [zig-zag]</p><p><i>adv.</i> in a zigzag course or on a zigzag path</p><p><b>različita vrsta zlatne trake (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a variety of goldenrod [broad leaved goldenrod]</p><p><b>zigurat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rectangular tiered temple or terraced mound erected by the ancient Assyrians and Babylonians [ziggurat, zikurat]</p><p><b>zigurat</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a rectangular tiered temple or terraced mound erected by the ancient Assyrians and Babylonians [ziggurat, zikkurat]</p><p><b>figa, friška figa, ništa, ništica, nula, pišljivi bob, šipak</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a quantity of no importance [aught, cipher, cypher, goose egg, nada, naught, nil, nix, nothing, null, zero, zip, zippo]</p><p><b>jedan od para malih metalnih cimbala koji se nose na palcu i srednjem prstu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> one of a pair of small metallic cymbals worn on the thumb and middle finger</p><p><b>vrlo veliki neodređeni broj (obično hiperbola), vrlo veliki neodređeni broj (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a very large indefinite number (usually hyperbole) [bazillion, billion, gazillion, jillion, million, trillion]</p><p><i>adj.</i> very large indeterminate number</p><p><b>Zimbabve</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a landlocked republic in south central Africa formerly called Rhodesia [Republic of Zimbabwe, Rhodesia, Southern Rhodesia]</p><p><b>rodom ili stanovnikom Zimbabvea, od ili u vezi s ili karakteristično za Zimbabwe ili njegov narod (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> a native or inhabitant of Zimbabwe</p><p><i>adj.</i> of or relating to or characteristic of Zimbabwe or its people</p><p><b>osnovna jedinica novca u Zimbabveu (MT)</b></p><p><i>n.</i> the basic unit of money in Zimbabwe</p><p><b>V